  ('lake-naivasha', 31, '7-nights-8-days-luxury-safari-itinerary', '7 Nights / 8 Days Luxury Safari Itinerary', 'Day 7 – Masai Mara → Nairobi', NULL, '', 281),
  ('lake-naivasha', 31, '7-nights-8-days-luxury-safari-itinerary', '7 Nights / 8 Days Luxury Safari Itinerary', 'Day 8 – Nairobi Departure', NULL, '', 282),
  ('lake-naivasha', 32, 'travel-agent-insights', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS', 'Lake Naivasha', NULL, '### What inexperienced planners often do wrong ### What an experienced planner does differently', 283),
  ('lake-naivasha', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', NULL, NULL, 'IF: `trip_length <= 3 nights` THEN: Do not add Naivasha, Elementeita, or Mara by default. Reason: Short Rift Valley trips work best when time is concentrated on core lake experiences (boat rides, Crescent Island, Hell’s Gate) rather than spread across multiple parks. IF: `trip_type == HONEYMOON` THEN: `romance_weight += 30%`, `privacy_weight += 20%`, `free_time_weight += 20%`, `activity_density -= 20%` Reason: Naivasha honeymoon value comes from private boat rides, lakeside scenery, and relaxed lodge time rather than maximum activity coverage. IF: `traveler_type == FAMILY` **AND** `children_age <= 6` THEN: `walking_intensity_target -= 20%`, `downtime += 20%`, prefer short transfers and predictable meal breaks. Reason: Young children handle Naivasha better with short boat rides, pool time, and fewer long vehicle days. IF: `hotel_is_far_from_main_jetties_and_boat_areas` **AND** `hotel_saving < additional_transport_cost + value_of_lost_time` THEN: Prefer central/lakeside lodge. Reason: A cheaper lodge far from main boat jetties often creates worse overall trip value in Naivasha. IF: `trip_length <= 3 nights` THEN: Prefer one lodge. Reason: Lodge changes consume valuable activity time on a short Naivasha trip. IF: `trip_length >= 5 nights` **AND** `traveler_interest == RELAXATION` THEN: Consider Lake Nakuru/Elementaita add-on. Reason: Longer stays make a slower scenic or multi-lake extension more practical and rewarding. IF: `traveler_type == LUXURY` THEN: Prefer private transfer **AND** high-service lodge **AND** exclusive/private experiences. Reason: Luxury value in Naivasha is created through comfort, privacy, and service (private boats, lakeside dining) rather than more activities. IF: `traveler_type == BUDGET` THEN: Prefer shared transfer/group activities **AND** high-value lodge location **AND** mix free/paid attractions. Reason: Naivasha offers strong value when the itinerary uses core lake circuits, simple lodge meals, and fewer paid extras. IF: `trip_type == FIRST_TIME_VISITOR` THEN: Anchor trip around: boat safari, Crescent Island walk, Hell’s Gate excursion **AND** include one sunrise/sunset photography session. Reason: These elements give the clearest first impression of Naivasha’s wildlife, landscapes, and Rift Valley scenery. IF: `trip_type == FAMILY` THEN: Limit major activities/day to 2 **AND** include one leisure block daily. Reason: Naivasha family trips work best when the pace stays relaxed with predictable rest and meal times. IF: `trip_type == HONEYMOON` THEN: Schedule premium lakeside dinner or sundowner. Reason: Naivasha is strongest at sunset, on the water, and during quiet, private wildlife and landscape experiences. IF: `weather == LONG_RAINS (March–May)` THEN: Reduce outdoor walking **AND** increase lodge/photography time. Reason: Heavy rain and muddy roads make a slower, more flexible Naivasha plan perform better. IF: `traveler_interest == WILDLIFE OR PHOTOGRAPHY` THEN: Combine morning and late-afternoon boat rides/excursions on the same day. Reason: These time blocks cluster well around animal activity and light, creating a more coherent nature experience. IF: `traveler_type == SENIOR` THEN: Prefer lodge near main jetties/town **AND** use private 4×4 when helpful **AND** avoid multiple long activities in one day. Reason: Naivasha’s wildlife and views are rewarding, but easier when movement, heat, and rough roads are controlled. IF: `trip_length >= 4 nights` THEN: Add one flexible half-day. Reason: Naivasha benefits from breathing room for extra photography, lodge relaxation, or weather adjustments.', 284),
  ('lake-naivasha', 34, 'destination-scoring', 'DESTINATION SCORING', NULL, NULL, '| Factor | Score | | ------------------ | ----- | | Family | 84 | | Honeymoon | 86 | | Luxury | 84 | | Budget | 78 | | Adventure | 76 | | Culture | 62 | | Food | 68 | | Shopping | 48 | | Nightlife | 35 | | Relaxation | 68 | | Nature | 86 | | Accessibility | 65 | | Senior travelers | 82 | | First-time visitor | 83 | | Photography | 89 |', 285),
  ('lake-naivasha', 35, 'final-travel-agent-verdict', 'FINAL TRAVEL AGENT VERDICT', NULL, NULL, 'Best traveler profiles: Honeymoon Romantic couple First-time safari-goer Luxury traveler Wildlife & photography enthusiast Family with appropriate pacing Best duration: 2–3 nights Best season: June–October, January–February Best hotel strategy: Well-located lakeside lodge or quiet southern-shore resort; prioritize proximity to main jetties and boat areas over remote budget options. Best transportation: Private 4×4 from Nairobi; shared transfers acceptable for budget travelers. Private transfer for: Honeymoon Luxury Family convenience Senior travelers Must-do for first-time visitor: One Lake Naivasha boat safari (hippos & birds) One Crescent Island guided walking safari One Hell’s Gate excursion (cycling/hiking) One sunrise/sunset photography session by the lake One relaxed lodge day with pool/scenery Don’t-do: Do not overpack every day with long activities. Do not change lodges unnecessarily on short trips. Do not underestimate heat, boat safety, and rough roads. Do not treat Naivasha like a checklist destination; it’s a relaxed nature-and-lake experience. Biggest advantage: Outstanding lake scenery, hippos, birdlife, and easy access to Crescent Island and Hell’s Gate within a compact, Nairobi-friendly destination. Biggest disadvantage: Limited high-adrenaline adventure, shopping, and nightlife; boat quality and accessibility vary by operator and lodge. Overall destination score: 86/100', 286),
  ('lake-naivasha', 36, 'data-quality', 'DATA QUALITY', NULL, NULL, 'information_completeness: 85/100 last_updated: 2026-08-23 last_verified: NOT_LIVE_VERIFIED verified_by: TRAVEL_ENGINE_INITIAL_DATASET sources: IMPORTANT: Prices, opening hours, schedules, visa requirements, availability, accessibility and operational conditions must NOT be treated as permanently valid from this document. These must be sourced from structured, refreshable data.', 287),
  ('masaimara', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Long Dry Season', NULL, 'months: June–October, January–February weather: Dry, sunny, and comfortable; cool mornings and warm afternoons. crowd_level: MEDIUM → HIGH price_level: MEDIUM → HIGH overall_score: 86–92 recommended: true reason: Best for boat rides, birding, wildlife viewing, and clear photography, though peak periods cost more.', 288),
  ('masaimara', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Short Rains', NULL, 'months: November–December weather: Warm with occasional showers and greener surroundings. crowd_level: LOW → MEDIUM price_level: LOW → MEDIUM overall_score: 82–87 recommended: true reason: A good-value period with pleasant scenery, fewer crowds, and generally suitable conditions for lake activities.', 289),
  ('masaimara', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Long Rains', NULL, 'months: March–May weather: Frequent showers, cloudy periods, lush scenery, and occasionally muddy roads. crowd_level: LOW price_level: LOW overall_score: 68–76 recommended: true reason: Best for budget travelers, birders, and photographers seeking green landscapes and dramatic skies; outdoor plans may need flexibility.', 290),
  ('masaimara', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Shoulder Transition', NULL, 'months: October–November weather: Mostly warm and sunny with brief scattered showers. crowd_level: LOW → MEDIUM price_level: LOW → MEDIUM overall_score: 80–85 recommended: true reason: Offers a useful balance of weather, wildlife, scenery, and value, with manageable visitor levels.', 291),
  ('masaimara', 10, 'budget-strategy', 'BUDGET STRATEGY', NULL, NULL, 'Where saving money is not recommended: Travel-agent rule: Masai Mara offers best value through **shared safaris, strategically located camps, and off-peak travel**; never compromise on vehicle safety, guide quality, park access, or camp standards.', 292),
  ('masaimara', 12, 'airport-transfer-logic', 'AIRPORT TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Family', 'family', 'Pre-booked private 4×4 or van from Nairobi’s JKIA/Wilson Airport directly to the camp; safest and easiest with children and luggage.', 293),
  ('masaimara', 12, 'airport-transfer-logic', 'AIRPORT TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Honeymoon', 'honeymoon', 'Private 4×4 or scenic flight to the Mara; offers comfort, privacy, and a smooth arrival. Reason: Door-to-door or fly-in transfers save time and create a relaxed start.', 294),
  ('masaimara', 12, 'airport-transfer-logic', 'AIRPORT TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Luxury', 'luxury', 'Private charter flight from Nairobi or chauffeured 4×4 to an exclusive camp; ideal for comfort and convenience.', 295),
  ('masaimara', 12, 'airport-transfer-logic', 'AIRPORT TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Budget', 'budget', 'Shared safari vehicle or scheduled shuttle from Nairobi; most affordable, but fixed timings and longer road travel apply. Transfer note: Confirm whether the camp is inside the reserve, near a specific gate, or in a conservancy, as transfer time and access conditions vary. Primary airports are **JKIA (NBO)** and **Wilson Airport (WIL)**; local airstrips may offer faster camp access.', 296),
  ('masaimara', 18, 'family-travel', 'FAMILY TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'child_friendly_score: 86 best_ages: Rules: For young children: Prefer: Avoid:', 297),
  ('masaimara', 19, 'honeymoon-travel', 'HONEYMOON TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'honeymoon_score: 96 romance_score: 98 privacy_score: 90 luxury_score: 95 Recommended: Itinerary rule: Limit to **2 major activities per day**. Prefer: One memorable safari experience + free time. Over: Three or four rushed activities. Recommended areas:', 298),
  ('masaimara', 20, 'luxury-travel', 'LUXURY TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'luxury_score: 97 Recommended: Luxury should increase: Comfort, privacy, service, convenience, and exclusivity—not simply the number of activities. Recommended areas:', 299),
  ('masaimara', 21, 'adventure', 'ADVENTURE', NULL, NULL, 'adventure_score: 82 Masai Mara is ideal for **wildlife-based adventure**, rather than high-adrenaline activities. Top experiences: Recommended areas: Best for:', 300),
  ('masaimara', 22, 'senior-travel', 'SENIOR TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'senior_suitability: 86 walking_intensity: LOW → MEDIUM (mostly vehicle-based) Rules: Prefer: Avoid:', 301),
  ('masaimara', 23, 'accessibility', 'ACCESSIBILITY', NULL, NULL, 'wheelchair_accessibility: PARTIAL_TO_GOOD depending on attraction and transport public_transport_accessibility: VARIABLE hotel_accessibility: MUST_BE_VERIFIED_PER_HOTEL attraction_accessibility: MUST_BE_VERIFIED_PER_ATTRACTION Rule: Never infer accessibility from destination-level accessibility. Each hotel and attraction must carry its own accessibility data.', 302),
  ('masaimara', 24, 'food', 'FOOD', NULL, NULL, 'food_score: 68 Masai Mara is primarily a safari destination, with dining centred on lodge and camp restaurants. Food experiences: Best for: Travel-agent note: Food variety is limited inside the Mara; prioritise meal plans, dietary confirmation, and camp quality over restaurant-hopping.', 303),
  ('masaimara', 25, 'shopping', 'SHOPPING', NULL, NULL, 'shopping_score: 40 Masai Mara is not a shopping destination. Best buys: Prefer: Avoid: Best for: Meaningful cultural souvenirs and quick purchases, rather than shopping excursions.', 304),
  ('masaimara', 26, 'nightlife', 'NIGHTLIFE', NULL, NULL, 'nightlife_level: 25 Masai Mara has virtually no conventional nightlife; evenings focus on camp dinners, sundowners, stargazing, and storytelling. Best for: Prefer: Avoid: Travel-agent note: For nightlife, add Nairobi before or after the safari; in the Mara, sell the evening experience as peaceful, scenic, and exclusive.', 305),
  ('masaimara', 28, 'sample-itinerary-patterns', 'SAMPLE ITINERARY PATTERNS', '3 NIGHTS – MASAI MARA', NULL, 'Day 1: Arrival → Transfer to safari camp → Afternoon game drive → Dinner at camp Day 2: Morning: Early game drive – Big Five & predators Afternoon: Lodge rest / pool time Evening: Sunset game drive or sundowner Day 3: Morning: Full-day game drive with picnic lunch Afternoon: Mara River or migration area visit, if seasonal Evening: Bush dinner / campfire Day 4: Breakfast → Final short game drive → Nairobi transfer or flight → Departure', 306),
