  ('nairobi', 32, 'travel-agent-insights', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS', 'Nairobi', NULL, '#### What inexperienced planners often do wrong #### What an experienced planner does differently', 371),
  ('nairobi', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', NULL, NULL, 'IF: `trip_length <= 1 night` THEN: Use Nairobi as a transit stop; focus on one nearby activity or hotel-based rest. Reason: Limited time and airport transfers make a packed itinerary impractical. IF: `trip_length == 2 nights` THEN: Combine Nairobi National Park, Karen, and one dining or cultural experience. Reason: Two nights allow the city’s main highlights without excessive travel. IF: `trip_length >= 3 nights` THEN: Add museums, shopping, Karura Forest, or a second food and cultural experience. Reason: Longer stays allow deeper exploration at a relaxed pace. IF: `trip_type == FIRST_TIME_VISITOR` THEN: Prioritize Nairobi National Park, Giraffe Centre, Karen Blixen Museum, and local cuisine. Reason: These provide a balanced introduction to Nairobi’s wildlife, culture, and food. IF: `trip_type == HONEYMOON` THEN: Choose Karen, Gigiri, or Riverside, with private transfers, premium dining, and relaxed activities. Reason: Nairobi is best used as a comfortable luxury stop before or after a safari. IF: `traveler_type == FAMILY` THEN: Plan 1–2 activities daily, include rest time, and choose family-friendly hotels and transport. Reason: Short activities and minimal traffic exposure improve comfort. IF: `traveler_type == LUXURY` THEN: Prefer a five-star hotel, chauffeur, private guide, fine dining, and a private park experience. Reason: Luxury value comes from comfort, privacy, service, and convenience. IF: `traveler_type == BUDGET` THEN: Choose a well-located guesthouse, local restaurants, ride-hailing, and shared tours. Reason: Location and safe transport matter more than small accommodation savings. IF: `traveler_interest == CULTURE` THEN: Focus on museums, Karen Blixen Museum, Bomas of Kenya, markets, and local crafts. Reason: Nairobi offers strong cultural and historical experiences. IF: `traveler_interest == FOOD` THEN: Add Kenyan cuisine, nyama choma, cafés, and one recommended restaurant. Reason: Nairobi has a wide range of local and international dining. IF: `traveler_interest == SHOPPING` THEN: Visit Maasai Market, Village Market, Karen boutiques, or Westlands malls. Reason: Nairobi provides greater shopping variety than safari areas. IF: `traveler_interest == NATURE` THEN: Choose Nairobi National Park, Karura Forest, or Ngong Hills according to walking ability. Reason: Each offers a different level of wildlife and outdoor activity. IF: `traveler_type == SENIOR` THEN: Use private transfers, accessible hotels, short activities, and a relaxed schedule. Reason: This reduces traffic stress, walking demands, and physical strain. IF: `traveler_type == TRANSIT` THEN: Stay near JKIA and avoid distant city attractions unless sufficient transfer time is available. Reason: Airport proximity reduces the risk of delays. IF: `trip_length >= 4 nights` THEN: Consider adding a safari or nearby destination rather than repeating city activities. Reason: Nairobi is generally strongest as a 1–3 night city stop.', 372),
  ('nairobi', 34, 'destination-scoring', 'DESTINATION SCORING', NULL, NULL, '| Factor | Score | | ------------------ | ----- | | Family | 84 | | Honeymoon | 86 | | Luxury | 84 | | Budget | 78 | | Adventure | 76 | | Culture | 82 | | Food | 84 | | Shopping | 82 | | Nightlife | 76 | | Relaxation | 68 | | Nature | 86 | | Accessibility | 70 | | Senior travelers | 82 | | First-time visitor | 83 | | Photography | 84 |', 373),
  ('nairobi', 35, 'final-travel-agent-verdict', 'FINAL TRAVEL AGENT VERDICT', NULL, NULL, 'Best for: First-time visitors, business travelers, culture travelers, foodies, shoppers, families, photographers, and safari stopovers. Best duration: 2–3 nights Best season: June–October; January–February Best stay: Well-located hotel in Karen, Westlands, Gigiri, Riverside, or near the airport. Best transport: Private transfers, ride-hailing, or licensed taxis. Must-do: Avoid: Biggest advantage: A unique combination of city life, culture, dining, shopping, business facilities, and nearby wildlife. Biggest disadvantage: Heavy traffic, variable accessibility, safety considerations, and limited relaxation compared with a dedicated resort destination. Overall destination score: **83/100**', 374),
  ('nairobi', 36, 'data-quality', 'DATA QUALITY', NULL, NULL, 'information_completeness: 88/100 last_updated: 2026-08-24 last_verified: NOT_LIVE_VERIFIED verified_by: TRAVEL_ENGINE_INITIAL_DATASET sources: IMPORTANT: Prices, opening hours, schedules, visa requirements, availability, accessibility and operational conditions must NOT be treated as permanently valid from this document. These must be sourced from structured, refreshable data.', 375),
  ('port-louis', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Long Dry Season', NULL, 'months: June–October, January–February weather: Dry, sunny, and comfortable. crowd_level: MEDIUM → HIGH price_level: MEDIUM → HIGH overall_score: 86–92 recommended: true reason: Best for sightseeing, photography, and outdoor activities.', 376),
  ('port-louis', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Short Rains', NULL, 'months: November–December weather: Warm with occasional showers and greener scenery. crowd_level: LOW → MEDIUM price_level: LOW → MEDIUM overall_score: 82–87 recommended: true reason: Good value with fewer crowds and pleasant conditions.', 377),
  ('port-louis', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Long Rains', NULL, 'months: March–May weather: Frequent showers, cloudy skies, and lush surroundings. crowd_level: LOW price_level: LOW overall_score: 68–76 recommended: true reason: Suitable for budget travel and green-season photography; keep plans flexible.', 378),
  ('port-louis', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Shoulder Season', NULL, 'months: October–November weather: Warm and mostly sunny with brief showers. crowd_level: LOW → MEDIUM price_level: LOW → MEDIUM overall_score: 80–85 recommended: true reason: Balanced weather, manageable crowds, and good value.', 379),
  ('port-louis', 10, 'budget-strategy', 'BUDGET STRATEGY', NULL, NULL, 'Where saving money is not recommended: Travel-agent rule: Port Louis offers the best value through **well-located mid-range stays, local dining, shared tours, and planned transport**.', 380),
  ('port-louis', 18, 'family-travel', 'FAMILY TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'child_friendly_score: 86 best_ages: Rules: For young children: Prefer: Avoid:', 381),
  ('port-louis', 19, 'honeymoon-travel', 'HONEYMOON TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'honeymoon_score: 76 romance_score: 75 privacy_score: 70 luxury_score: 80 Recommended: Itinerary rule: Limit to **2 major activities per day**. Prefer: One memorable beach, sea, or dining experience + free time. Over: Three or four rushed activities, long cross-island journeys, or excessive hotel changes. Recommended areas:', 382),
  ('port-louis', 20, 'luxury-travel', 'LUXURY TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'luxury_score: 80 Recommended: Luxury should increase: Comfort, privacy, service, convenience, and exclusivity—not simply the number of activities. Prefer: One private sea, cultural, or dining experience + premium relaxation. Over: Crowded group tours, poorly located hotels, peak-hour traffic, and overly busy itineraries. Recommended areas:', 383),
  ('port-louis', 21, 'adventure', 'ADVENTURE', NULL, NULL, 'adventure_score: 68 Port Louis offers **urban, cultural, and nature-based adventure**, rather than extreme high-adrenaline activities. The city is best used as a base for nearby landscapes, water activities, and island excursions. Top experiences: Recommended areas: Best for: Avoid expecting:', 384),
  ('port-louis', 22, 'senior-travel', 'SENIOR TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'senior_suitability: 78 walking_intensity: LOW → MEDIUM (mostly vehicle-based) Rules: Prefer: Avoid:', 385),
  ('port-louis', 23, 'accessibility', 'ACCESSIBILITY', NULL, NULL, 'wheelchair_accessibility: PARTIAL_TO_GOOD depending on attraction and transport public_transport_accessibility: VARIABLE hotel_accessibility: MUST_BE_VERIFIED_PER_HOTEL attraction_accessibility: MUST_BE_VERIFIED_PER_ATTRACTION Rule: Never infer accessibility from destination-level accessibility. Each hotel and attraction must carry its own accessibility data.', 386),
  ('port-louis', 24, 'food', 'FOOD', NULL, NULL, 'food_score: 86 Port Louis is an excellent food destination, offering Mauritian, Indian, Creole, Chinese, French, and international cuisine. Food choices are widely available across Caudan Waterfront, CBD, Chinatown, and premium hotels. Food experiences: Best for: Recommended areas: Travel-agent note: Port Louis offers greater food variety than most Mauritius resort areas, so food-focused travelers should allow at least one dedicated restaurant or local-cuisine experience. Confirm dietary requirements, restaurant opening times, reservations, and transport arrangements before booking.', 387),
  ('port-louis', 25, 'shopping', 'SHOPPING', NULL, NULL, 'shopping_score: 82 Port Louis is a strong shopping destination, offering waterfront malls, artisan markets, crafts, souvenirs, fashion, local products, and premium retail. It is far better suited to dedicated shopping than Mauritius’s resort beaches. Best buys: Prefer: Avoid: Best for: Recommended areas:', 388),
  ('port-louis', 26, 'nightlife', 'NIGHTLIFE', NULL, NULL, 'nightlife_level: 65 Port Louis offers modest nightlife, centered on waterfront restaurants, hotel bars, lounges, and occasional live music or cultural performances. The city is not a late-night party destination; evenings are best enjoyed through dining, sundowners, and relaxed entertainment. Best for: Prefer: Recommended areas: Best evening experiences: Avoid:', 389),
  ('port-louis', 28, 'sample-itinerary-patterns', 'SAMPLE ITINERARY PATTERNS', 'PORT LOUIS, MAURITIUS', NULL, 'Below are ready-to-use itinerary patterns for Port Louis, modelled on your Nairobi examples and aligned with Port Louis’s strengths as a 1–3 night city stop for culture, food, shopping, and waterfront experiences. ### 2 NIGHTS – PORT LOUIS HIGHLIGHTS Day 1: Arrival at MRU (Sir Seewoosagur Ramgoolam Airport) → Private transfer to hotel in Caudan or CBD → Check-in and rest → Dinner at Caudan Waterfront or in Chinatown Day 2: Morning: Central Market (Port Louis Market) for spices, crafts, and local life → Aapravasi Ghat (UNESCO World Heritage Site) Afternoon: Lunch in CBD or Caudan → Blue Penny Museum or Natural History Museum Evening: Waterfront promenade and sunset views → Relaxed dinner at Caudan Day 3: Morning: Citadel Fort (Fort Adelaide) for panoramic views → Optional short visit to Jummah Mosque or Chinatown cultural walk Afternoon: Final shopping at Caudan Waterfront or Central Market → Transfer to MRU airport or onward to a beach resort (Grand Bay, Flic-en-Flac, or Le Morne) ### 3 NIGHTS – PORT LOUIS CULTURE, FOOD & SHOPPING Day 1: Arrival at MRU → Transfer to hotel in Caudan or CBD → Relaxed lunch → Evening waterfront dinner or hotel dining Day 2: Morning: Central Market and local craft shopping → Aapravasi Ghat and Blue Penny Museum Afternoon: Lunch in Chinatown or CBD → Guided city heritage walk (colonial sites, Jummah Mosque area) Evening: Mauritian Creole or Indian-inspired dinner → Optional live sega music or cultural performance (where available) Day 3: Morning: Citadel Fort (Fort Adelaide) for views and photography → Optional visit to Natural History Museum or Photography Museum Afternoon: Lunch at Caudan Waterfront → Boutique shopping or gallery visit in Caudan Evening: Rooftop or waterfront sundowner → Relaxed dinner Day 4: Morning: Optional half-day excursion to Pamplemousses Botanical Garden → Or relaxed morning and final shopping → Airport transfer or onward to a beach/nature area ### 3 NIGHTS – FAMILY PORT LOUIS Day 1: Arrival at MRU → Private family transfer to hotel (Caudan or CBD) → Check-in and rest → Early child-friendly dinner at Caudan Waterfront Day 2: Morning: Short city sightseeing: Central Market and waterfront promenade Afternoon: Hotel pool and downtime → Optional visit to a family-friendly mall or park Evening: Early dinner at a waterfront restaurant Day 3: Morning: Aapravasi Ghat (short, supervised visit) and Blue Penny Museum Afternoon: Lunch in Caudan → Relaxed shopping or cinema at Caudan Waterfront Evening: Relaxed meal near the hotel Day 4: Breakfast → Final short activity (waterfront walk or park) if time allows → Airport transfer or onward to a beach resort ### 2 NIGHTS – LUXURY PORT LOUIS Day 1: Arrival at MRU → Chauffeured private transfer to a five-star hotel in Caudan or Port Louis → Luxury hotel check-in → Spa or private relaxation → Fine-dining dinner at a premium waterfront or hotel restaurant Day 2: Morning: Private guided city tour (Central Market, Aapravasi Ghat, Blue Penny Museum, Citadel Fort) Afternoon: Hotel lunch and spa time → Optional private art or shopping tour in Caudan Evening: Rooftop sundowner or private waterfront dinner Day 3: Morning: Private cultural or heritage experience (e.g., curated museum visit, Chinatown walk with a guide) → Concierge-arranged airport transfer or scenic drive to a luxury beach resort (Le Morne, Grand Bay, or Flic-en-Flac) ### 3 NIGHTS – HONEYMOON PORT LOUIS (CITY STOP BEFORE BEACH) Day 1: Arrival at MRU → Private airport transfer to a boutique or luxury hotel in Caudan/Port Louis → Couples’ spa or relaxed hotel time → Romantic dinner at a waterfront or premium restaurant Day 2: Morning: Private city tour or heritage trail (Aapravasi Ghat, Blue Penny Museum, Citadel Fort) Afternoon: Leisurely lunch and downtime → Optional couples’ spa or wellness experience Evening: Sunset waterfront dinner or rooftop sundowner Day 3: Morning: Relaxed cultural walk (Chinatown, Jummah Mosque area) or boutique shopping in Caudan Afternoon: Private art tour or gallery visit → Late check-out and transfer to a beach resort (Grand Bay, Flic-en-Flac, or Le Morne) for the main honeymoon stay Evening: Private dining or relaxed hotel evening at the beach resort Day 4: Breakfast at the beach resort → Continue honeymoon with beach, catamaran cruise, or spa experiences ### 1 NIGHT – TRANSIT STOP (PORT LOUIS / AIRPORT AREA) Day 1: Arrival at MRU → Transfer to airport-area hotel or Caudan hotel (depending on flight times) → Check-in and rest → Dinner at the hotel or nearby waterfront restaurant Day 2: Breakfast → Complimentary or private shuttle to MRU → Continue to the next destination (beach resort or onward flight) ### 4 NIGHTS – DEEPER PORT LOUIS & NEARBY EXPLORATION Day 1: Arrival at MRU → Hotel transfer to Caudan or CBD → Check-in and rest → Dinner nearby (waterfront or local restaurant) Day 2: Morning: Central Market and Aapravasi Ghat Afternoon: Blue Penny Museum and colonial heritage walk Evening: Mauritian dining experience in Chinatown or Caudan Day 3: Morning: Citadel Fort (Fort Adelaide) and panoramic photography Afternoon: Lunch and boutique shopping in Caudan Evening: Relaxed waterfront dinner or live music (where available) Day 4: Morning: Half-day excursion to Pamplemousses Botanical Garden Afternoon: Return to Port Louis; optional visit to Natural History Museum or Photography Museum Evening: Rooftop dining or hotel lounge sundowner Day 5: Morning: Final shopping at Caudan Waterfront or Central Market → Optional short visit to a local craft cooperative → Airport transfer or onward to a beach/nature area', 390),
  ('port-louis', 29, '4-nights-5-days-honeymoon-pattern', '4 NIGHTS / 5 DAYS – HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'PORT LOUIS, MAURITIUS', NULL, '**Day 1 – Arrival & Rest** Arrival at Sir Seewoosagur Ramgoolam International Airport (MRU) → Private airport transfer to hotel in Caudan Waterfront or Port Louis → Check-in and day at rest to recover from travel → Relaxed dinner at the hotel or nearby waterfront restaurant **Day 2 – Full Day Île aux Cerfs Tour** After breakfast: → Private or shared transfer to the departure point for Île aux Cerfs → Full-day island tour with: Evening: → Return to hotel → Romantic dinner at Caudan Waterfront or a premium restaurant **Day 3 – South Island Tour (incl. Vallée des Couleurs)** After breakfast: → Full-day South Tour with private or shared vehicle, including: → Lunch at a scenic restaurant en route (e.g., Chamarel or Rivière Noire) Evening: → Return to hotel → Relaxed dinner or couples’ spa time **Day 4 – Check-out & Departure** After breakfast: → Check-out from hotel at 12:00 → Private transfer to MRU airport at noon (or as per flight schedule) → Tour ends with sweet happy memories of the journey', 391),
  ('port-louis', 30, '4-nights-5-days-family-itinerary', '4 NIGHTS / 5 DAYS – FAMILY Itinerary', NULL, NULL, '**Day 1 – Arrival & Rest** Arrival at Sir Seewoosagur Ramgoolam International Airport (MRU) → Private family transfer to hotel in Caudan Waterfront or Port Louis → Check-in and day at rest to recover from travel → Early child-friendly dinner at the hotel or nearby waterfront restaurant **Day 2 – Full Day Île aux Cerfs Tour** After breakfast: → Private or shared transfer to the departure point for Île aux Cerfs → Full-day island tour with: Evening: → Return to hotel → Relaxed family dinner at Caudan Waterfront or a kid-friendly restaurant **Day 3 – South Island Tour (incl. Vallée des Couleurs)** After breakfast: → Full-day South Tour with private or shared vehicle, including: → Lunch at a scenic restaurant en route (e.g., Chamarel or Rivière Noire) Evening: → Return to hotel → Early relaxed dinner; optional short stroll along the waterfront if energy allows **Day 4 – Check-out & Departure** After breakfast: → Check-out from hotel at 12:00 → Private transfer to MRU airport at noon (or as per flight schedule) → Tour ends with sweet happy memories of the journey', 392),
  ('port-louis', 31, '4-nights-5-days-luxury-itinerary', '4 Nights / 5 Days – Luxury Itinerary', 'Day 1 – Arrival & Rest', NULL, '', 393),
  ('port-louis', 31, '4-nights-5-days-luxury-itinerary', '4 Nights / 5 Days – Luxury Itinerary', 'Day 2 – Full‑Day Île aux Cerfs Luxury Tour', 'luxury', '', 394),
  ('port-louis', 31, '4-nights-5-days-luxury-itinerary', '4 Nights / 5 Days – Luxury Itinerary', 'Day 3 – Full‑Day South Island Tour (incl. Vallée des Couleurs)', NULL, '', 395),
  ('port-louis', 31, '4-nights-5-days-luxury-itinerary', '4 Nights / 5 Days – Luxury Itinerary', 'Day 4 – Check‑out & Departure', NULL, '', 396),
  ('port-louis', 32, 'travel-agent-insights', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS', 'Port Louis', NULL, '#### What inexperienced planners often do wrong #### What an experienced planner does differently', 397),
  ('port-louis', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', NULL, NULL, 'IF: `trip_length <= 1 night` THEN: Use Port Louis as a transit stop; focus on one nearby activity or hotel-based rest. Reason: Limited time and airport transfers make a packed itinerary impractical. IF: `trip_length == 2 nights` THEN: Combine Caudan Waterfront, Central Market, Aapravasi Ghat, and one dining or cultural experience. Reason: Two nights allow the city’s main highlights without excessive travel. IF: `trip_length >= 3 nights` THEN: Add museums, shopping, Citadel Fort, or a second food and cultural experience. Reason: Longer stays allow deeper exploration at a relaxed pace. IF: `trip_type == FIRST_TIME_VISITOR` THEN: Prioritize Caudan Waterfront, Central Market, Aapravasi Ghat, Blue Penny Museum, and local Mauritian cuisine. Reason: These provide a balanced introduction to Port Louis’s culture, history, and food. IF: `trip_type == HONEYMOON` THEN: Choose Caudan, Grand Bay, or Le Morne, with private transfers, premium dining, and relaxed activities. Reason: Port Louis is best used as a comfortable luxury stop before or after a beach honeymoon. IF: `traveler_type == FAMILY` THEN: Plan 1–2 activities daily, include rest time, and choose family-friendly hotels and transport. Reason: Short activities and minimal traffic exposure improve comfort. IF: `traveler_type == LUXURY` THEN: Prefer a five-star hotel, chauffeur, private guide, fine dining, and a private island or sea experience. Reason: Luxury value comes from comfort, privacy, service, and convenience. IF: `traveler_type == BUDGET` THEN: Choose a well-located guesthouse, local restaurants, ride-hailing, and shared tours. Reason: Location and safe transport matter more than small accommodation savings. IF: `traveler_interest == CULTURE` THEN: Focus on Aapravasi Ghat, Blue Penny Museum, Central Market, Chinatown, and Jummah Mosque. Reason: Port Louis offers strong multicultural and historical experiences. IF: `traveler_interest == FOOD` THEN: Add Mauritian Creole, Indian, Chinese, and French-inspired cuisine, plus local markets and cafés. Reason: Port Louis has a wide range of local and international dining. IF: `traveler_interest == SHOPPING` THEN: Visit Central Market, Caudan Waterfront, Bagatelle Mall, or Cascavelle Shopping Mall. Reason: Port Louis provides greater shopping variety than Mauritius’s resort beaches. IF: `traveler_interest == NATURE` THEN: Choose Pamplemousses Botanical Garden, Vallée des Couleurs, or nearby coastal excursions according to walking ability. Reason: Each offers a different level of wildlife and outdoor activity. IF: `traveler_type == SENIOR` THEN: Use private transfers, accessible hotels, short activities, and a relaxed schedule. Reason: This reduces traffic stress, walking demands, and physical strain. IF: `traveler_type == TRANSIT` THEN: Stay near MRU airport or Caudan and avoid distant island attractions unless sufficient transfer time is available. Reason: Airport or waterfront proximity reduces the risk of delays. IF: `trip_length >= 4 nights` THEN: Consider adding a beach or nature destination (e.g., Grand Bay, Flic-en-Flac, Le Morne) rather than repeating city activities. Reason: Port Louis is generally strongest as a 1–3 night city stop within a wider Mauritius holiday.', 398),
  ('port-louis', 34, 'destination-scoring', 'DESTINATION SCORING', NULL, NULL, '| Factor | Score | | ------------------ | ----- | | Family | 84 | | Honeymoon | 76 | | Luxury | 80 | | Budget | 82 | | Adventure | 68 | | Culture | 90 | | Food | 86 | | Shopping | 85 | | Nightlife | 65 | | Relaxation | 62 | | Nature | 68 | | Accessibility | 68 | | Senior travelers | 78 | | First-time visitor | 86 | | Photography | 84 |', 399);
INSERT INTO destination_guidance (place_id, section, topic, section_title, heading, audience, body, position) VALUES
  ('port-louis', 35, 'final-travel-agent-verdict', 'FINAL TRAVEL AGENT VERDICT', NULL, NULL, 'Best for: First-time visitors, business travelers, culture travelers, foodies, shoppers, families, photographers, and beach-and-city combination holidays. Best duration: 2–3 nights Best season: June–October; January–February Best stay: Well-located hotel in Caudan Waterfront, CBD / City Centre, or near the airport (MRU). Best transport: Private transfers, ride-hailing, or licensed taxis. Must-do: Avoid: Biggest advantage: A compact capital with strong multicultural heritage, excellent food, waterfront shopping, and convenient access to Mauritius’s top nature and beach attractions. Biggest disadvantage: Busy urban setting with traffic, limited deep relaxation, and variable accessibility compared with dedicated beach-resort destinations. Overall destination score: **82/100**', 400),
  ('port-louis', 36, 'data-quality', 'DATA QUALITY', NULL, NULL, 'information_completeness: 90/100 last_updated: 2026-08-24 last_verified: NOT_LIVE_VERIFIED verified_by: TRAVEL_ENGINE_INITIAL_DATASET sources: IMPORTANT: Prices, opening hours, schedules, visa requirements, availability, accessibility and operational conditions must NOT be treated as permanently valid from this document. These must be sourced from structured, refreshable data.', 401),
  ('ile-aux-cerfs', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Long Dry Season', NULL, 'months: June–October, January–February weather: Dry, sunny, and comfortable. crowd_level: MEDIUM → HIGH price_level: MEDIUM → HIGH overall_score: 90–96 recommended: true reason: Best for beach time, snorkeling, water activities, and photography.', 402),
  ('ile-aux-cerfs', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Short Rains', NULL, 'months: November–December weather: Warm with occasional showers and greener scenery. crowd_level: LOW → MEDIUM price_level: LOW → MEDIUM overall_score: 82–88 recommended: true reason: Good value with fewer crowds and pleasant island conditions.', 403),
  ('ile-aux-cerfs', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Long Rains', NULL, 'months: March–May weather: More frequent showers, cloudy skies, and lush surroundings. crowd_level: LOW price_level: LOW overall_score: 70–78 recommended: true reason: Suitable for budget travel and relaxed beach visits, but keep plans flexible.', 404),
  ('ile-aux-cerfs', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Shoulder Season', NULL, 'months: October–November weather: Warm and mostly sunny with brief showers. crowd_level: LOW → MEDIUM price_level: LOW → MEDIUM overall_score: 84–89 recommended: true reason: Balanced weather, manageable crowds, and strong value for a Mauritius island add-on.', 405),
  ('ile-aux-cerfs', 10, 'budget-strategy', 'BUDGET STRATEGY', NULL, NULL, 'Where saving money is not recommended: Travel-agent rule: Île aux Cerfs offers the best value through **shared boat access, packaged day tours, and a short stay format**, while premium pricing is justified only for private transfers, exclusive beach setups, and luxury sea experiences.', 406),
  ('ile-aux-cerfs', 18, 'family-travel', 'FAMILY TRAVEL', 'Family rating format', 'family', 'child_friendly_score: 86 best_ages: Rules:', 407),
  ('ile-aux-cerfs', 19, 'honeymoon-travel', 'HONEYMOON TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'Best areas: Grand Bay / Nord: best for beaches, restaurants, nightlife, and shopping. Flic-en-Flac: best for long beach stays, resorts, and relaxed dining. Le Morne / Bel Ombre: best for luxury resorts, privacy, and scenic settings. Port Louis / Caudan: best for a short culture-and-dining stop before moving to the beach. MRU / Airport area: best for a comfortable final night before departure. Honeymoon rules: Prefer one special experience plus free time. Overpacked days and long transfers reduce the romantic feel. Private transfers and a well-located hotel matter more than squeezing in extra activities.', 408),
  ('ile-aux-cerfs', 20, 'luxury-travel', 'LUXURY TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'luxury_score: 80 Best-value luxury pattern Stay in a five-star or boutique property on the east coast or in a premium Mauritius base. Use private airport and island transfers. Spend one full day on Île aux Cerfs with a private cruise, beach time, and a premium lunch. Add one relaxed evening with a waterfront dinner or spa session. Luxury rules: Keep the itinerary light and avoid overpacking the day. Prefer comfort, privacy, service, convenience, and exclusivity over doing more activities. Avoid crowded group tours, poorly located hotels, peak-hour traffic, and unnecessary hotel changes. For Île aux Cerfs, a day trip or 1-night luxury add-on is usually enough.', 409),
  ('ile-aux-cerfs', 21, 'adventure', 'ADVENTURE', NULL, NULL, 'adventure_score: 81 Île aux Cerfs is a strong water-based adventure destination, best known for lagoon activities, boat access, snorkeling, and scenic island experiences rather than extreme adrenaline. It is best treated as a day trip or short 1-night add-on because the island itself is mainly built around beach and sea activities. Top experiences: Recommended areas: Best for:', 410),
  ('ile-aux-cerfs', 22, 'senior-travel', 'SENIOR TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'senior_suitability: 78 walking_intensity: LOW → MEDIUM (mostly vehicle-based) Île aux Cerfs is a good fit for senior travelers if mobility is considered in advance and the trip is kept relaxed. The island is best enjoyed as a pre-arranged day trip with private transfers, limited walking, and frequent rest breaks. Rules: Prefer: Avoid:', 411),
  ('ile-aux-cerfs', 23, 'accessibility', 'ACCESSIBILITY', NULL, NULL, 'wheelchair_accessibility: PARTIAL_TO_GOOD depending on attraction and transport public_transport_accessibility: VARIABLE hotel_accessibility: MUST_BE_VERIFIED_PER_HOTEL attraction_accessibility: MUST_BE_VERIFIED_PER_ATTRACTION Rule: Never infer accessibility from destination-level accessibility. Each hotel and attraction must carry its own accessibility data.', 412),
  ('ile-aux-cerfs', 24, 'food', 'FOOD', NULL, NULL, 'food_score: 68 Île aux Cerfs has limited food variety compared with Mauritius’s main city and resort hubs, so it works better for a beach day with a planned meal than as a food destination. Most dining here is tied to beach clubs, island lunch stops, or nearby east-coast transfer points. Food experiences: Best for: Recommended areas:', 413),
  ('ile-aux-cerfs', 25, 'shopping', 'SHOPPING', NULL, NULL, 'shopping_score: 31 Île aux Cerfs has very limited shopping, so it is not a shopping destination in itself. It is best for a beach day with only light souvenir or resort-retail browsing nearby. Best buys: Prefer: Avoid: Best for:', 414),
  ('ile-aux-cerfs', 26, 'nightlife', 'NIGHTLIFE', NULL, NULL, 'nightlife_level: 18 Île aux Cerfs has very limited nightlife and is mainly a daytime beach-and-lagoon destination. Evenings are usually quiet, with the best options being relaxed dinners on the east coast or at resort hotels nearby. Best for: Prefer: Avoid: Best evening areas:', 415),
  ('ile-aux-cerfs', 28, 'sample-itinerary-patterns', 'SAMPLE ITINERARY PATTERNS', '2 NIGHTS – ÎLE AUX CERFS HIGHLIGHTS', NULL, 'Day 1: Arrival at MRU → Transfer to east coast hotel or Trou d’Eau Douce area → Check-in and rest → Dinner at resort or beachside restaurant Day 2: Morning: Boat transfer to Île aux Cerfs → Beach time, snorkeling, and lagoon activities Afternoon: BBQ lunch or island dining → Relaxed swimming and photography Evening: Return to hotel → Quiet dinner and rest Day 3: Morning: Optional second boat trip or relaxed east coast beach time → Transfer to MRU or onward to another Mauritius beach area', 416),
  ('ile-aux-cerfs', 28, 'sample-itinerary-patterns', 'SAMPLE ITINERARY PATTERNS', '3 NIGHTS – ÎLE AUX CERFS BEACH & LAGOON', NULL, 'Day 1: Arrival at MRU → Transfer to east coast hotel → Check-in and rest → Sunset dinner Day 2: Morning: Île aux Cerfs full-day tour → Speedboat or catamaran transfer Afternoon: Snorkeling, beach relaxation, and water activities Evening: Return to hotel → Dinner and downtime Day 3: Morning: Belle Mare or East Coast beach relaxation → Optional spa or light coastal walk Afternoon: Leisure lunch and rest Evening: Romantic or family dinner by the sea Day 4: Breakfast → Airport transfer or onward beach stay', 417),
  ('ile-aux-cerfs', 28, 'sample-itinerary-patterns', 'SAMPLE ITINERARY PATTERNS', '4 NIGHTS – ÎLE AUX CERFS + EAST COAST STAY', NULL, 'Day 1: Arrival at MRU → Transfer to east coast base → Check-in and rest → Dinner near the resort Day 2: Morning: Île aux Cerfs day trip Afternoon: Beach time, snorkeling, and lunch Evening: Return to hotel and relax Day 3: Morning: East coast beach leisure or Belle Mare relaxation Afternoon: Optional Flacq visit for practical shopping Evening: Dinner at resort Day 4: Morning: Optional second lagoon excursion or catamaran cruise Afternoon: Free time and photography Evening: Final seaside dinner Day 5: Breakfast → MRU transfer or onward travel', 418),
  ('ile-aux-cerfs', 28, 'sample-itinerary-patterns', 'SAMPLE ITINERARY PATTERNS', '1 NIGHT – TRANSIT / SHORT ADD-ON', NULL, 'Day 1: Arrival at MRU → Transfer to east coast hotel → Check-in and rest → Dinner Day 2: Breakfast → Short Île aux Cerfs visit or direct airport transfer depending on timing', 419),
  ('ile-aux-cerfs', 29, '4-nights-5-days-honeymoon-pattern', '4 NIGHTS / 5 DAYS – HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'PORT LOUIS, MAURITIUS', NULL, '**Day 1 – Arrival & Rest** Arrival at Sir Seewoosagur Ramgoolam International Airport (MRU) → Private airport transfer to hotel in Caudan Waterfront or Port Louis → Check-in and day at rest to recover from travel → Relaxed dinner at the hotel or nearby waterfront restaurant **Day 2 – Full Day Île aux Cerfs Tour** After breakfast: → Private or shared transfer to the departure point for Île aux Cerfs → Full-day island tour with: Evening: → Return to hotel → Romantic dinner at Caudan Waterfront or a premium restaurant **Day 3 – South Island Tour (incl. Vallée des Couleurs)** After breakfast: → Full-day South Tour with private or shared vehicle, including: → Lunch at a scenic restaurant en route (e.g., Chamarel or Rivière Noire) Evening: → Return to hotel → Relaxed dinner or couples’ spa time **Day 4 – Check-out & Departure** After breakfast: → Check-out from hotel at 12:00 → Private transfer to MRU airport at noon (or as per flight schedule) → Tour ends with sweet happy memories of the journey', 420),
  ('ile-aux-cerfs', 30, '4-nights-5-days-family-itinerary', '4 NIGHTS / 5 DAYS – FAMILY Itinerary', NULL, NULL, '**Day 1 – Arrival & Rest** Arrival at Sir Seewoosagur Ramgoolam International Airport (MRU) → Private family transfer to hotel in Caudan Waterfront or Port Louis → Check-in and day at rest to recover from travel → Early child-friendly dinner at the hotel or nearby waterfront restaurant **Day 2 – Full Day Île aux Cerfs Tour** After breakfast: → Private or shared transfer to the departure point for Île aux Cerfs → Full-day island tour with: Evening: → Return to hotel → Relaxed family dinner at Caudan Waterfront or a kid-friendly restaurant **Day 3 – South Island Tour (incl. Vallée des Couleurs)** After breakfast: → Full-day South Tour with private or shared vehicle, including: → Lunch at a scenic restaurant en route (e.g., Chamarel or Rivière Noire) Evening: → Return to hotel → Early relaxed dinner; optional short stroll along the waterfront if energy allows **Day 4 – Check-out & Departure** After breakfast: → Check-out from hotel at 12:00 → Private transfer to MRU airport at noon (or as per flight schedule) → Tour ends with sweet happy memories of the journey', 421),
  ('ile-aux-cerfs', 31, '4-nights-5-days-luxury-itinerary', '4 Nights / 5 Days – Luxury Itinerary', 'Day 1 – Arrival & Rest', NULL, '', 422),
  ('ile-aux-cerfs', 31, '4-nights-5-days-luxury-itinerary', '4 Nights / 5 Days – Luxury Itinerary', 'Day 2 – Full‑Day Île aux Cerfs Luxury Tour', 'luxury', '', 423),
  ('ile-aux-cerfs', 31, '4-nights-5-days-luxury-itinerary', '4 Nights / 5 Days – Luxury Itinerary', 'Day 3 – Full‑Day South Island Tour (incl. Vallée des Couleurs)', NULL, '', 424),
  ('ile-aux-cerfs', 31, '4-nights-5-days-luxury-itinerary', '4 Nights / 5 Days – Luxury Itinerary', 'Day 4 – Check‑out & Departure', NULL, '', 425),
  ('ile-aux-cerfs', 32, 'travel-agent-insights', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS', 'What inexperienced planners often do wrong', NULL, '', 426),
  ('ile-aux-cerfs', 32, 'travel-agent-insights', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS', 'What an experienced planner does differently', NULL, '', 427),
  ('ile-aux-cerfs', 32, 'travel-agent-insights', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS', 'Best planning rule', NULL, '', 428),
  ('ile-aux-cerfs', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', NULL, NULL, 'IF: `trip_length <= 1 night` THEN: Use Île aux Cerfs as a quick day trip or transit-style add-on. Reason: The island is best for short beach time, not a packed multi-day base. IF: `trip_length == 2 nights` THEN: Pair Île aux Cerfs with Belle Mare or another east-coast beach stay. Reason: Two nights are enough for one island day plus relaxed coastal downtime. IF: `trip_length >= 3 nights` THEN: Add another Mauritius region instead of repeating island activities. Reason: Île aux Cerfs works best as part of a broader Mauritius itinerary. IF: `trip_type == FIRST_TIME_VISITOR` THEN: Prioritize Île aux Cerfs lagoon time, boat transfer, snorkeling, and beach relaxation. Reason: These give the clearest classic Mauritius experience. IF: `trip_type == HONEYMOON` THEN: Choose private transfer, premium boat access, and quiet beach time. Reason: The island is very strong for romantic lagoon experiences. IF: `traveler_type == FAMILY` THEN: Plan 1–2 activities daily, include rest time, and keep the schedule easy. Reason: Short, calm outings work best for children and parents. IF: `traveler_type == LUXURY` THEN: Prefer a private cruise, high-end resort base, and curated island lunch. Reason: Luxury value comes from comfort and exclusivity. IF: `traveler_type == BUDGET` THEN: Use shared boat transfers, simple meals, and a short day-trip format. Reason: The island is still affordable if you avoid private upgrades. IF: `traveler_interest == NATURE` THEN: Focus on lagoon scenery, swimming, and coastal relaxation. Reason: Nature is one of the island’s strongest selling points. IF: `traveler_interest == FOOD` THEN: Keep food expectations simple and plan one mainland meal stop if needed. Reason: Île aux Cerfs is not a major food destination. IF: `traveler_interest == SHOPPING` THEN: Do shopping on the mainland, especially in Flacq or other east-coast stops. Reason: Shopping on the island itself is very limited. IF: `traveler_type == SENIOR` THEN: Use private transfers, short activities, and an east-coast base. Reason: This reduces walking and transfer stress. IF: `traveler_type == TRANSIT` THEN: Stay near MRU or the east coast and avoid unnecessary extra movement. Reason: Convenience matters more than trying to fit in too much. IF: `trip_length >= 4 nights` THEN: Combine Île aux Cerfs with a beach or city segment elsewhere in Mauritius. Reason: The island is strongest as one highlight within a larger holiday.', 429),
  ('ile-aux-cerfs', 34, 'destination-scoring', 'DESTINATION SCORING', NULL, NULL, '| Factor | Score | | ------------------ | ----- | | Family | 92 | | Honeymoon | 95 | | Luxury | 90 | | Budget | 62 | | Adventure | 81 | | Culture | 34 | | Food | 68 | | Shopping | 31 | | Nightlife | 18 | | Relaxation | 97 | | Nature | 96 | | Accessibility | 58 | | Senior travelers | 83 | | First-time visitor | 90 | | Photography | 95 |', 430),
  ('ile-aux-cerfs', 35, 'final-travel-agent-verdict', 'FINAL TRAVEL AGENT VERDICT', NULL, NULL, 'Best for: Families, honeymooners, photographers, nature lovers, first-time visitors, and travelers who want a classic Mauritius beach-and-lagoon experience. Best duration: 1 day / 1 night Best season: June–October; January–February Best stay: East Coast Resort Corridor, Belle Mare, or near Trou d’Eau Douce / the boat departure point. Best transport: Pre-arranged private transfers, licensed taxis, or hotel transfers, followed by a boat to the island. Must-do: Avoid: Biggest advantage: A stunning lagoon setting with excellent beach relaxation, water activities, and romantic scenery. Biggest disadvantage: Limited cultural depth, limited shopping and nightlife, and logistics that depend on boat timing and weather. Overall destination score: **92/100**', 431),
  ('ile-aux-cerfs', 36, 'data-quality', 'DATA QUALITY', NULL, NULL, 'information_completeness: 90/100 last_updated: 2026-08-25 last_verified: NOT_LIVE_VERIFIED verified_by: TRAVEL_ENGINE_INITIAL_DATASET sources: IMPORTANT: Prices, opening hours, schedules, visa requirements, availability, accessibility and operational conditions must NOT be treated as permanently valid from this document. These must be sourced from structured, refreshable data.', 432),
  ('south-islands', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Long Dry Season', NULL, 'months: May–September weather: Coolest, driest period with strong trade winds; mild temperatures (20–25°C) and clear skies. crowd_level: MEDIUM → HIGH price_level: MEDIUM → HIGH overall_score: 85–92 recommended: true reason: Ideal for coastal exploring, hiking in Black River Gorges, and lower humidity, though trade winds heavily affect southern beaches.', 433),
  ('south-islands', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Short Rains', NULL, 'months: October–December weather: Warm, transition period with rising temperatures, low rainfall, and light winds. crowd_level: MEDIUM → HIGH price_level: HIGH overall_score: 90–96 recommended: true reason: Excellent ocean visibility for diving/snorkeling, calm seas in the south, and pleasant beach weather before peak summer heat.', 434),
  ('south-islands', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Long Rains', NULL, 'months: January–April weather: Hot, highly humid, heavy rainfall, and risk of tropical cyclones (peaks Jan–Mar). crowd_level: LOW → MEDIUM price_level: LOW → MEDIUM overall_score: 70–78 recommended: false reason: Tropical storms can disrupt water activities and outdoor itineraries, though prices drop and landscape is lush.', 435),
  ('south-islands', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Shoulder Season', NULL, 'months: April–May weather: Warm temperatures fading into milder winter conditions, dropping rainfall, and decreasing humidity. crowd_level: LOW → MEDIUM price_level: LOW → MEDIUM overall_score: 84–88 recommended: true reason: Calmer weather, competitive resort rates, and comfortable conditions for sightseeing around Le Morne and Chamarel.', 436),
  ('south-islands', 10, 'budget-strategy', 'BUDGET STRATEGY', NULL, NULL, 'Where saving money is not recommended:', 437),
  ('south-islands', 18, 'family-travel', 'FAMILY TRAVEL', 'Family rating format', 'family', 'child_friendly_score: 88 best_ages: Rules:', 438),
  ('south-islands', 19, 'honeymoon-travel', 'HONEYMOON TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'Best areas: Le Morne Peninsula: best for dramatic mountain scenery, iconic beach settings, and romantic luxury resorts. Bel Ombre: best for secluded five-star sanctuaries, golf, fine dining, and pristine nature reserves. Pointe d’Esny: best for quiet turquoise lagoon stays, boutique boutique luxury, and uncrowded beaches. Chamarel Highlands: best for intimate eco-luxury lodges, cooler mountain air, rum tasting, and scenic views. Mahébourg / Airport area: best for effortless, short transfers and seamless arrival or departure transit. Honeymoon rules: Prefer one special experience plus free time. Overpacked days and long transfers reduce the romantic feel. Private transfers and a well-located hotel matter more than squeezing in extra activities.', 439),
  ('south-islands', 20, 'luxury-travel', 'LUXURY TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'luxury_score: 95 Best-value luxury pattern Stay in an ultra-exclusive resort sanctuary in Bel Ombre or Le Morne Peninsula. Use private helicopter transfers from the airport directly to resort helipads, combined with chauffeured luxury SUVs for local touring. Charter a private catamaran or luxury yacht to explore Le Morne lagoon, pristine snorkeling spots, and the wild southern coastline. Enjoy fine dining at historical estate venues like Le Château de Bel Ombre, private beachside dinners, and wellness retreats at five-star spas. Luxury rules: Keep the itinerary light and avoid overpacking the day. Prefer comfort, privacy, service, convenience, and exclusivity over doing more activities. Avoid crowded group tours, poorly located hotels, peak-hour traffic, and unnecessary hotel changes. For South Mauritius, a dedicated 4 to 7-night resort stay provides the ideal balance of scenic nature, privacy, and world-class hospitality.', 440),
  ('south-islands', 21, 'adventure', 'ADVENTURE', NULL, NULL, 'adventure_score: 92 South Mauritius is a premier outdoor and landscape adventure destination, renowned for mountain trekking, coastal waterfall exploration, wild sea-cliff views, and world-class lagoon wind sports rather than purely artificial attractions. It is best explored via a self-drive road trip or dedicated nature-focused base because the region encompasses vast nature reserves, national parks, and dramatic coastal terrain. Top experiences: Recommended areas: Best for:', 441),
  ('south-islands', 22, 'senior-travel', 'SENIOR TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'senior_suitability: 84 walking_intensity: LOW → MEDIUM (mostly vehicle-based) South Mauritius is a very good fit for senior travelers when itineraries prioritize comfortable vehicle transport, scenic drives, and gentle coastal exploration. The region''s top natural highlights can be comfortably appreciated through panoramic viewpoints, accessible nature spots, and scenic resort stays without demanding rigorous physical exertion. Rules: Prefer: Avoid:', 442),
  ('south-islands', 23, 'accessibility', 'ACCESSIBILITY', NULL, NULL, 'wheelchair_accessibility: PARTIAL_TO_GOOD depending on attraction and transport public_transport_accessibility: VARIABLE hotel_accessibility: MUST_BE_VERIFIED_PER_HOTEL attraction_accessibility: MUST_BE_VERIFIED_PER_ATTRACTION Rule: Never infer accessibility from destination-level accessibility. Each hotel and attraction must carry its own accessibility data.', 443),
  ('south-islands', 24, 'food', 'FOOD', NULL, NULL, 'food_score: 82 South Mauritius is a rich culinary hub known for authentic Creole flavors, fresh seafood, sugarcane rum tastings, and local street food. Dining here ranges from vibrant local markets in Mahébourg to fine dining on historic colonial estates and panoramic mountain restaurants overlooking the coast. Food experiences: Best for: Recommended areas:', 444),
  ('south-islands', 25, 'shopping', 'SHOPPING', NULL, NULL, 'shopping_score: 68 South Mauritius offers an authentic and culturally rich shopping experience, centered around traditional town markets, artisanal craft workshops, local rum distilleries, and tea estates rather than large modern commercial shopping malls. Best buys: Prefer: Avoid: Best for:', 445),
  ('south-islands', 26, 'nightlife', 'NIGHTLIFE', NULL, NULL, 'nightlife_level: 25 South Mauritius has very quiet, low-key nightlife and is primarily a daytime nature and beach destination. Evenings revolve around relaxed oceanfront dining, hotel lounges, sunset cocktails, and quiet local town taverns rather than vibrant clubs or late-night entertainment. Best for: Prefer: Avoid: Best evening areas:', 446),
  ('south-islands', 28, 'sample-itinerary-patterns', 'SAMPLE ITINERARY PATTERNS', '2 NIGHTS – SOUTH MAURITIUS HIGHLIGHTS', NULL, 'Day 1: Arrival at MRU → Short transfer to Bel Ombre, Le Morne, or Pointe d’Esny hotel → Check-in and rest → Sunset cocktails and dinner at resort or beach restaurant Day 2: Morning: Scenic coastal drive to Chamarel Seven Colored Earth and Waterfall → Rhumerie de Chamarel visit and rum tasting Afternoon: Gourmet Creole lunch in Chamarel → Drive down to Le Morne public beach for afternoon relaxation and photography Evening: Return to hotel → Quiet seaside dinner Day 3: Morning: Blue Bay Marine Park glass-bottom boat tour and snorkeling → Quick visit to Mahébourg waterfront or Gris Gris sea cliffs → Transfer to MRU or onward to another Mauritius region', 447),
  ('south-islands', 28, 'sample-itinerary-patterns', 'SAMPLE ITINERARY PATTERNS', '3 NIGHTS – NATURE, MOUNTAINS & LAGOON', NULL, 'Day 1: Arrival at MRU → Transfer to Le Morne or Bel Ombre resort → Check-in and downtime → Relaxed beachfront dinner Day 2: Morning: Guided morning hike at Le Morne Brabant mountain Afternoon: Relaxed beach recovery time at Le Morne lagoon or Pointe d’Esny → Beachside lunch Evening: Sunset catamaran cruise or seaside dinner Day 3: Morning: Scenic tour of Chamarel, Black River Gorges viewpoints, and Alexandra Falls Afternoon: Lunch in Chamarel → Visit Gris Gris wild sea cliffs and Rochester Falls Evening: Fine dining at a historical venue like Le Château de Bel Ombre Day 4: Breakfast → Final beach stroll → Airport transfer or onward resort stay', 448),
  ('south-islands', 28, 'sample-itinerary-patterns', 'SAMPLE ITINERARY PATTERNS', '4 NIGHTS – ULTIMATE SOUTH MAURITIUS DISCOVERY', NULL, 'Day 1: Arrival at MRU → Transfer to south coast hotel base → Check-in, resort relaxation, and sunset views → Welcome dinner Day 2: Morning: Chamarel Seven Colored Earth, Waterfall, and Rhumerie de Chamarel tour Afternoon: Black River Gorges National Park viewpoints and nature walks Evening: Return to hotel and relax Day 3: Morning: Blue Bay Marine Park snorkeling and boat trip to Île aux Aigrettes nature sanctuary Afternoon: Explore historic Mahébourg town and local waterfront market Evening: Fresh seafood dinner in Mahébourg or Pointe d’Esny Day 4: Morning: Quad biking or safari tour in Bel Ombre Nature Reserve Afternoon: Free leisure afternoon at Le Morne beach or hotel spa Evening: Farewell fine-dining experience Day 5: Breakfast → Short transfer to MRU or onward travel', 449),
  ('south-islands', 28, 'sample-itinerary-patterns', 'SAMPLE ITINERARY PATTERNS', '1 NIGHT – TRANSIT / SHORT ADD-ON', NULL, 'Day 1: Arrival at MRU → Short transfer to Pointe d’Esny or Mahébourg hotel → Check-in and rest → Visit Gris Gris cliffs or Blue Bay beach for sunset → Casual seafood dinner Day 2: Breakfast → Morning swim or glass-bottom boat tour at Blue Bay Marine Park → Direct airport transfer depending on flight timing.', 450),
  ('south-islands', 29, '4-nights-5-days-honeymoon-pattern', '4 NIGHTS / 5 DAYS – HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'PORT LOUIS, MAURITIUS', NULL, '**Day 1 – Arrival & Rest** Arrival at Sir Seewoosagur Ramgoolam International Airport (MRU) → Private airport transfer to hotel in Caudan Waterfront or Port Louis → Check-in and day at rest to recover from travel → Relaxed dinner at the hotel or nearby waterfront restaurant **Day 2 – Full Day Île aux Cerfs Tour** After breakfast: → Private or shared transfer to the departure point for Île aux Cerfs → Full-day island tour with: Evening: → Return to hotel → Romantic dinner at Caudan Waterfront or a premium restaurant **Day 3 – South Island Tour (incl. Vallée des Couleurs)** After breakfast: → Full-day South Tour with private or shared vehicle, including: → Lunch at a scenic restaurant en route (e.g., Chamarel or Rivière Noire) Evening: → Return to hotel → Relaxed dinner or couples’ spa time **Day 4 – Check-out & Departure** After breakfast: → Check-out from hotel at 12:00 → Private transfer to MRU airport at noon (or as per flight schedule) → Tour ends with sweet happy memories of the journey', 451),
  ('south-islands', 30, '4-nights-5-days-family-itinerary', '4 NIGHTS / 5 DAYS – FAMILY Itinerary', NULL, NULL, '**Day 1 – Arrival & Rest** Arrival at Sir Seewoosagur Ramgoolam International Airport (MRU) → Private family transfer to hotel in Caudan Waterfront or Port Louis → Check-in and day at rest to recover from travel → Early child-friendly dinner at the hotel or nearby waterfront restaurant **Day 2 – Full Day Île aux Cerfs Tour** After breakfast: → Private or shared transfer to the departure point for Île aux Cerfs → Full-day island tour with: Evening: → Return to hotel → Relaxed family dinner at Caudan Waterfront or a kid-friendly restaurant **Day 3 – South Island Tour (incl. Vallée des Couleurs)** After breakfast: → Full-day South Tour with private or shared vehicle, including: → Lunch at a scenic restaurant en route (e.g., Chamarel or Rivière Noire) Evening: → Return to hotel → Early relaxed dinner; optional short stroll along the waterfront if energy allows **Day 4 – Check-out & Departure** After breakfast: → Check-out from hotel at 12:00 → Private transfer to MRU airport at noon (or as per flight schedule) → Tour ends with sweet happy memories of the journey', 452),
  ('south-islands', 31, '4-nights-5-days-luxury-itinerary', '4 Nights / 5 Days – Luxury Itinerary', 'Day 1 – Arrival & Rest', NULL, '', 453),
  ('south-islands', 31, '4-nights-5-days-luxury-itinerary', '4 Nights / 5 Days – Luxury Itinerary', 'Day 2 – Full‑Day Île aux Cerfs Luxury Tour', 'luxury', '', 454),
  ('south-islands', 31, '4-nights-5-days-luxury-itinerary', '4 Nights / 5 Days – Luxury Itinerary', 'Day 3 – Full‑Day South Island Tour (incl. Vallée des Couleurs)', NULL, '', 455),
  ('south-islands', 31, '4-nights-5-days-luxury-itinerary', '4 Nights / 5 Days – Luxury Itinerary', 'Day 4 – Check‑out & Departure', NULL, '', 456),
  ('south-islands', 32, 'travel-agent-insights', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS', 'What inexperienced planners often do wrong', NULL, '', 457),
  ('south-islands', 32, 'travel-agent-insights', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS', 'What an experienced planner does differently', NULL, '', 458),
  ('south-islands', 32, 'travel-agent-insights', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS', 'Best planning rule', NULL, '', 459),
  ('south-islands', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', NULL, NULL, 'IF: `trip_length <= 1 night` THEN: Focus on Pointe d’Esny, Mahébourg waterfront, or Blue Bay Marine Park near MRU airport. Reason: Southern highlights near the airport maximize scenic downtime and minimize transfer delays. IF: `trip_length == 2 nights` THEN: Base in Le Morne, Bel Ombre, or Pointe d’Esny and cover Chamarel and Gris Gris. Reason: Two nights allow for one dedicated coastal drive day and one relaxed beach day. IF: `trip_length >= 3 nights` THEN: Explore the full South Coast Corridor before moving to northern or western Mauritius. Reason: Three or more nights allow you to combine mountain hikes, nature reserves, and lagoon relaxation without rushing. IF: `trip_type == FIRST_TIME_VISITOR` THEN: Prioritize Le Morne Brabant, Chamarel Seven Colored Earth, Gris Gris sea cliffs, and Blue Bay snorkeling. Reason: These iconic southern landmarks provide the most dramatic introduction to Mauritius''s natural diversity. IF: `trip_type == HONEYMOON` THEN: Choose a private villa in Bel Ombre or Le Morne, paired with a helicopter tour or private catamaran cruise. Reason: The dramatic mountain backdrop and secluded luxury sanctuaries create an ideal romantic setting. IF: `traveler_type == FAMILY` THEN: Include La Vanille Nature Park, Blue Bay glass-bottom boat tours, and Rochester Falls. Reason: Gentle wildlife encounters and calm lagoon swimming are safe and engaging for all ages. IF: `traveler_type == LUXURY` THEN: Base in Bel Ombre or Le Morne Peninsula with private helicopter transfers and fine dining at estate venues. Reason: Five-star integrated resort sanctuaries offer world-class golf, spas, and butler service. IF: `traveler_type == BUDGET` THEN: Base in Mahébourg or Souillac, use public buses or a rental car, and enjoy free public beaches. Reason: Southeast guesthouses and local street food deliver high value without resort markups. IF: `traveler_interest == NATURE` THEN: Trek in Black River Gorges National Park, explore Chamarel, and tour Île aux Aigrettes sanctuary. Reason: South Mauritius contains the island''s highest concentration of native flora, fauna, and national parks. IF: `traveler_interest == FOOD` THEN: Pair Mahébourg street food markets with rum tasting at Rhumerie de Chamarel and heritage estate dining. Reason: The South offers an authentic blend of local Creole street food, colonial estate cuisine, and artisanal spirits. IF: `traveler_interest == SHOPPING` THEN: Focus on Mahébourg Market, Bois Chéri Tea Estate, and local rum distilleries. Reason: Shopping in the South centers around authentic local spices, artisanal crafts, tea, and rum rather than modern malls. IF: `traveler_type == SENIOR` THEN: Use private chauffeured transfers, focus on panoramic drive-up lookouts, and stay in accessible coastal resorts. Reason: Viewing Chamarel and Gris Gris via vehicle-accessible points avoids strenuous walking or steep trails. IF: `traveler_type == TRANSIT` THEN: Stay in Mahébourg or Pointe d’Esny for a 10–15 minute airport transfer. Reason: Close proximity to MRU airport avoids long cross-island drives before or after flights. IF: `trip_length >= 4 nights` THEN: Split the stay between a South nature/resort base and a North/West beach and nightlife hub.', 460),
  ('south-islands', 34, 'destination-scoring', 'DESTINATION SCORING', NULL, NULL, '| Factor | Score | | --- | --- | | Family | 88 | | Honeymoon | 94 | | Luxury | 92 | | Budget | 65 | | Adventure | 92 | | Culture | 78 | | Food | 72 | | Shopping | 42 | | Nightlife | 25 | | Relaxation | 95 | | Nature | 98 | | Accessibility | 65 | | Senior travelers | 84 | | First-time visitor | 96 | | Photography | 98 |', 461),
  ('south-islands', 35, 'final-travel-agent-verdict', 'FINAL TRAVEL AGENT VERDICT', NULL, NULL, 'Best for: Honeymooners, nature enthusiasts, photographers, road-trippers, adventure seekers, and luxury travelers looking for a dramatic, landscape-focused Mauritius experience. Best duration: 3–4 days / 3–4 nights Best season: May–November; December–April Best stay: Bel Ombre, Le Morne Peninsula, or Pointe d’Esny / Mahébourg Best transport: Pre-arranged private transfers, chauffeured drivers, or rental cars for scenic coastal drives Must-do: Avoid: Biggest advantage: Breathtaking, untamed natural scenery featuring iconic mountains, national parks, wild ocean cliffs, and pristine luxury resort sanctuaries. Biggest disadvantage: Quiet and limited nightlife, minimal commercial shopping, and strong trade winds/currents along certain un-reefed stretches of the southern coast. Overall destination score: **96/100**', 462),
  ('south-islands', 36, 'data-quality', 'DATA QUALITY', NULL, NULL, 'information_completeness: 94/100 last_updated: 2026-08-25 last_verified: NOT_LIVE_VERIFIED verified_by: TRAVEL_ENGINE_INITIAL_DATASET sources: IMPORTANT: Prices, opening hours, schedules, visa requirements, availability, accessibility and operational conditions must NOT be treated as permanently valid from this document. These must be sourced from structured, refreshable data.', 463),
  ('mahe-island', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Spring', NULL, 'months: March April May weather: Warm and tropical throughout. March remains humid with occasional heavy showers, while April and early May are among the calmest transition periods, with temperatures generally around 24–32°C and particularly favourable sea conditions. crowd_level: MEDIUM price_level: MEDIUM → HIGH overall_score: 84–93 recommended: true reason: One of the strongest periods for Mahé, especially April–May, combining calm seas, beach time, snorkelling, diving, hiking, photography, and island exploration. Best for: Official Seychelles tourism guidance identifies April and May among the best overall months, with relatively calm winds and excellent conditions for sunbathing, wildlife, diving, and marine activities.', 464),
  ('mahe-island', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Summer', NULL, 'months: June July August weather: Warm, relatively cooler, less humid, and generally drier under the southeast trade winds. Temperatures normally remain tropical, but winds become noticeably stronger and seas can be rougher, particularly along exposed southern and southeastern parts of Mahé. crowd_level: MEDIUM → HIGH price_level: MEDIUM → HIGH overall_score: 75–84 recommended: true reason: Excellent for: This is a strong season for hiking and outdoor exploration because conditions are generally drier and less humid. However, southeast trade winds from May to September can create rougher seas on exposed coasts, so beach choice becomes important for swimming and boat activities.', 465),
  ('mahe-island', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Autumn', NULL, 'months: September October November weather: September remains influenced by the southeast trade winds. October is a major transition month with lighter winds and calmer seas, while November becomes warmer and more humid as the northwest-wind season develops. crowd_level: MEDIUM price_level: MEDIUM → HIGH overall_score: 82–94 recommended: true reason: October and early November form one of Mahé''s premier periods for beaches, snorkelling, diving, marine excursions, hiking, photography, and romantic travel. Best for: Official Tourism Seychelles identifies October–November among the periods with the calmest seas and strongest underwater visibility, making them especially attractive for snorkelling and diving.', 466),
  ('mahe-island', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Winter', NULL, 'months: December January February weather: Hot, humid, and wetter under the northwest trade-wind pattern. January and February traditionally receive the most rainfall, although showers are often tropical and intermittent rather than continuous all-day rain. Seas are generally calmer than during the southeast trade-wind period. crowd_level: MEDIUM → HIGH price_level: HIGH → VERY_HIGH overall_score: 68–80 recommended: true reason: Excellent for: Mahé remains a viable year-round tropical destination, but December–February scores lower because of greater humidity, rainfall, holiday demand, and premium festive-season accommodation rates. January and February are traditionally the wettest period, while Seychelles'' temperatures generally remain between approximately 24°C and 32°C year-round.', 467),
  ('mahe-island', 10, 'budget-strategy', 'BUDGET STRATEGY', NULL, NULL, 'Where money can be saved: Where saving money is usually NOT recommended: Travel-agent rule: On Mahé Island, **SPTC_BUSES_OR_COMPACT_CAR_RENTAL + CREOLE_TAKEAWAYS + SELF_CATERING_OR_GUESTHOUSE + FREE_BEACHES_AND_TRAILS should be evaluated together**. For short stays, prioritize **BEAU_VALLON_OR_SOUTH_MAHE_BASE + VICTORIA_MARKET_AND_CLOCKTOWER_WALK + SAINTE_ANNE_MARINE_PARK_TRIP**. For longer stays, add **MORNE_SEYCHELLOIS_HIKE + TAKAMAKA_RUM_DISTILLERY_TASTING + ANSE_INTENDANCE_AND_PETITE_ANSE_BEACH_HOPPING** rather than switching accommodations between different parts of Mahé frequently.', 468),
  ('mahe-island', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Family', 'family', 'Mahé Island’s primary entry point is Seychelles International Airport (SEZ) at Pointe La Rue, along with the Inter Island Ferry Terminal (Cat Cocos) at the Commercial Port in Victoria. For families arriving with young children and multiple pieces of luggage, pre-booked resort minivans, private chauffeured transfers, or compact rental car pickups directly at the airport arrivals terminal provide the smoothest transition across winding island roads to Beau Vallon, Anse Royale, or southern resort bays. When traveling from Hong Kong, Europe, or Middle Eastern hubs, international flights disembark directly on Mahé, where pre-arranged transfers avoid long queues at peak arrival windows and navigate narrow coastal passes effortlessly.', 469),
  ('mahe-island', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Honeymoon', 'honeymoon', 'Opt for pre-arranged luxury private transfers (e.g., chauffeured SUVs or luxury sedans) directly from airport arrivals or the Victoria Ferry Terminal to luxury hillside villed resorts along Petite Anse, Intendance Bay, or Port Launay. For multi-island honeymoon itineraries, combine: PRIVATE_AIRPORT_OR_FERRY_TRANSFER + CAT_COCOS_CATAMARAN_PREMIUM_CLASS (Mahé–Praslin–La Digue corridor) + PRIVATE_CHAUFFEUR_FOR_SOUTHERN_MAHE_COVES_AND_LUXURY_HILLSIDE_RESORTS.', 470),
  ('mahe-island', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Luxury', 'luxury', 'Utilize pre-booked private chauffeured transfers directly from Seychelles International Airport arrivals, private jet terminals (Zil Air VIP Helipad), or yacht marinas at Eden Island. For complex luxury Seychelles circuits, combine: VIP_AIRPORT_MEET_AND_GREET + PRIVATE_LUXURY_SUV_TRANSFERS + CHARTERED_HELICOPTER_FLIGHTS_TO_OUTER_RESORTS + PRIVATE_CREOLE_YACHT_CHARTERS_AND_RESORT_VIP_CONCIERGE_SERVICES.', 471),
  ('mahe-island', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Budget', 'budget', 'Take advantage of Mahé’s affordable public infrastructure and self-catering options connecting entry ports across the island: For onward travel to isolated southern coves (like Anse Intendance), utilize public buses (e.g., Routes 5, 6, 9) or a small rental car.', 472),
  ('mahe-island', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Senior', 'senior', 'Prioritize door-to-door pre-booked taxi transfers or hotel shuttles directly at terminal drop-offs to avoid extensive walking on uneven ground or waiting for buses under intense tropical heat. When using inter-island ferries or island excursion catamarans, book VIP/First-Class air-conditioned upper deck seats, utilize pier luggage assistance services, and select central accommodations near ground-level coastal roads.', 473),
  ('mahe-island', 18, 'family-travel', 'FAMILY TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'child_friendly_score: 91 best_ages: Rules: For young children: Prefer: Avoid:', 474),
  ('mahe-island', 19, 'honeymoon-travel', 'HONEYMOON TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'honeymoon_score: 98 romance_score: 97 privacy_score: 95 luxury_score: 97 Recommended: Honeymoon itineraries should generally stay at: 2–3 major experiences/day. Prefer: LUXURY_HILLSIDE_SUITES + PRIVATE_BEACH_COVES + RESORT_SPA_RELAXATION + FINE_CREOLE_DINING + SUNSET_CATAMARAN_CRUISE + FREE_TIME over: Constant hotel changes and rushed daily island hopping.', 475),
  ('mahe-island', 20, 'luxury-travel', 'LUXURY TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'luxury_score: 97 Recommended:', 476),
  ('mahe-island', 21, 'adventure', 'ADVENTURE', NULL, NULL, 'adventure_score: 88 Mahé offers dynamic tropical marine and mountain adventure across trail trekking, scuba diving, zip-lining, and ocean kayaking. Adventure experiences: Best regions: MORNE_SEYCHELLOIS_HIKE_ZONE + SAINTE_ANNE_MARINE_PARK + PORT_LAUNAY_ADVENTURE_HUB + SOUTH_MAHE_COASTAL_TRAILS', 477),
  ('mahe-island', 22, 'senior-travel', 'SENIOR TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'senior_suitability: 86 walking_intensity: LOW–MEDIUM for Victoria town walks, market strolls, Eden Island boardwalks, and flat resort beach paths MEDIUM–HIGH for full Morne Seychellois forest hikes, steep granite trail steps, and unpaved beach inclines Rules: Mahé works exceptionally well for seniors as an: UNTOUCHED_NATURAL_BEAUTY + CREOLE_GASTRONOMY + LUXURY_RESORT_COMFORT + SCENIC_COASTAL_DRIVES + PEACEFUL_RELAXATION destination.', 478),
  ('mahe-island', 23, 'accessibility', 'ACCESSIBILITY', NULL, NULL, 'wheelchair_accessibility: HIGH IN SEYCHELLES INTERNATIONAL AIRPORT, EDEN ISLAND MARINA, AND MODERN LUXURY RESORTS VARIABLE TO LIMITED IN HISTORIC VICTORIA STREETS, NATURAL MOUNTAIN TRAILS, AND UNPAVED BEACHES public_transport_accessibility: MODERATE TO LIMITED on public SPTC buses due to high steps and lack of dedicated wheelchair ramps hotel_accessibility: MUST_BE_VERIFIED_PER_HOTEL attraction_accessibility: MUST_BE_VERIFIED_PER_ATTRACTION Rule: Never assume universal step-free access across natural beach sand, granite boulder paths, and historic plantation steps. Additional notes:', 479),
  ('mahe-island', 24, 'food', 'FOOD', NULL, NULL, 'Mahé is particularly strong for: Food experiences: Family: Prioritize grilled fish, octopus curry, breadfruit chips, coconut smoothies, fresh fruit, and local ice cream. Honeymoon: Choose romantic hillside resort dining, private beach candlelit dinners, and oceanfront craft cocktail pairings. Luxury: Include multi-course Creole-fusion fine dining, private chef villa banquets, and world-class wine-pairing dinners. Budget: Use local takeaway stalls (*takeaways*), beachside fish shacks, neighborhood Creole cafes, and Victoria market food stalls.', 480),
  ('mahe-island', 25, 'shopping', 'SHOPPING', NULL, NULL, 'Strong categories: Luxury shopping: Prefer: Budget: Prefer: Travel-agent rule: Use EDEN_ISLAND_PLAZA / RESORT_BOUTIQUES for HIGH_END_ART_AND_FASHION, VICTORIA_MARKET / CRAFT_VILLAGE for LOCAL_HANDICRAFTS_SPICES_AND_SOUVENIRS, and LOCAL_SUPERMARKETS / TAKAMAKA_DISTILLERY for RUM_TEAS_AND_EDIBLE_GIFTS.', 481),
  ('mahe-island', 26, 'nightlife', 'NIGHTLIFE', NULL, NULL, 'nightlife_level: 70 Suitable for: Best areas: Evening activities: Mahé offers a relaxed, nature-centric evening atmosphere focused on sunset drinks, seaside resort lounges, authentic Creole music, and quiet oceanfront dining rather than late-night clubbing. Honeymoon travelers should generally prefer: HILLSIDE_SUNSET_COCKTAILS + SECLUDED_BEACH_DINING + RESORT_LOUNGES + LIVE_CREOLE_ACOUSTIC_MUSIC over: Crowded late-night dance clubs. Travel-agent rule: Position Mahé as a **RELAXED_SUNSET_COCKTAILS + CREOLE_GASTRONOMY + MARINA_LOUNGES + PEACEFUL_OCEANFRONT_NIGHTS DESTINATION**, with serene evening relaxation serving as a primary highlights pillar.', 482),
  ('mahe-island', 28, 'sample-itinerary-patterns', 'SAMPLE ITINERARY PATTERNS', '3 NIGHTS', NULL, '### Day 1 Arrival at Seychelles International Airport (SEZ), Mahé Island → Private transfer / resort transfer to beachfront hotel → Hotel check-in & relax after arrival Afternoon: → Explore Victoria, the compact capital of Seychelles → Visit the Clock Tower & Sir Selwyn Selwyn-Clarke Market → Scenic drive through Mahé''s lush tropical landscapes → Continue towards Beau Vallon Beach for swimming, relaxation & golden-hour views Evening: → Welcome dinner featuring Seychellois Creole cuisine & fresh seafood → Sunset walk along Beau Vallon Beach → Beachfront cocktails / relaxed resort evening → Hotel SEZ on Mahé Island serves as the principal international gateway to Seychelles and provides convenient connections to Praslin Island by domestic flight or ferry, with onward ferry connections making La Digue easily accessible. ### Day 2 Morning: Breakfast → Scenic Mahé Island exploration → Visit Mission Lodge viewpoint for panoramic mountain & coastal scenery → Explore the tropical landscapes of Morne Seychellois National Park → Scenic coastal drive through Mahé Afternoon: → Beach hopping along Mahé''s picturesque coastline → Anse Intendance / Anse Takamaka → Swimming & tropical beach relaxation → Creole seafood lunch Evening: → Return to the resort → Sunset beach experience → Creole / international dinner → Hotel ### Day 3 Recommended first-time option: → Early transfer to Mahé ferry terminal / SEZ domestic terminal → Ferry or domestic flight to Praslin Island → Explore Vallée de Mai Nature Reserve → Tropical forest walk through the famous coco de mer palm landscape Afternoon: → Continue to Anse Lazio → Beach relaxation, swimming & photography → Ferry from Praslin to La Digue Island → Explore La Digue by bicycle / island transport → Visit L''Union Estate → Continue to iconic Anse Source d''Argent → Granite boulders, turquoise water & tropical beach scenery Evening: → Return by ferry towards Praslin / Mahé according to connection schedule → Relaxed dinner → Hotel Optional alternative instead of covering BOTH Praslin & La Digue in one day: PRASLIN_ISLAND: → Vallée de Mai Nature Reserve → Anse Lazio → Anse Georgette / scenic coastal exploration → Relaxed island lunch & beach experience LA_DIGUE_ISLAND: → Bicycle exploration around La Digue → L''Union Estate → Anse Source d''Argent → Grand Anse / Petite Anse → Traditional island village experience SPA & WELLNESS: → Luxury beachfront resort spa → Couple / wellness treatments → Private beach relaxation → Sunset yoga or tropical wellness experience NATURE: → Morne Seychellois National Park → Botanical Garden exploration → Tropical hiking & panoramic viewpoints → Marine / snorkelling experience FAMILY: → Beau Vallon Beach activities → Seychelles National Botanical Gardens → Praslin nature experience → La Digue bicycle / island exploration HONEYMOON: → Private sunset sailing experience around Mahé → Romantic Anse Source d''Argent photography on La Digue → Couple spa & private beachfront dinner FOOD: → Seychellois Creole culinary experience → Fresh grilled fish & seafood → Tropical fruits & local market exploration → Beachfront Creole dinner For only 3 nights, prioritize: MAHE_ISLAND_AND_BEAU_VALLON + PRASLIN_VALLEE_DE_MAI_AND_ANSE_LAZIO + LA_DIGUE_AND_ANSE_SOURCE_DARGENT OR MAHE_ISLAND_EXPLORATION + PRASLIN_ISLAND + LA_DIGUE_ISLAND rather than trying to include too many additional Seychelles islands within a short stay. ### Day 4 Breakfast → Leisurely morning beach walk / resort relaxation → Souvenir shopping for local crafts, spices, vanilla & coconut products → Hotel checkout → Private transfer / resort transfer to Seychelles International Airport (SEZ) → Departure', 483),
  ('mahe-island', 29, 'seven-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'SEVEN-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 1', NULL, 'Arrival at Mahé Island – Seychelles International Airport (SEZ) → Private airport transfer → Romantic beachfront resort check-in → Relax and refresh Evening: → Beachfront sunset walk → Welcome romantic dinner → Overnight at Mahé Island', 484),
  ('mahe-island', 29, 'seven-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'SEVEN-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 2', NULL, 'Breakfast at the hotel Morning: → Mahé Island scenic tour → Victoria → Clock Tower → Local market Afternoon: → Beau Vallon Beach → Scenic coastal viewpoints → Couple photography Evening: → Sunset by the beach → Romantic dinner → Overnight at Mahé Island', 485),
  ('mahe-island', 29, 'seven-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'SEVEN-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 3', NULL, 'Breakfast → Leisure & beach day Choose ONE: ROMANTIC_LEISURE → Beach relaxation → Couple spa → Sunset experience ISLAND_EXPLORATION → Scenic coastal drive → Tropical gardens → Hidden beaches Evening: → Private / beachfront dinner → Overnight at Mahé Island', 486),
  ('mahe-island', 29, 'seven-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'SEVEN-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 4', NULL, 'Breakfast → Hotel checkout → Ferry / domestic flight to Praslin Island → Romantic resort check-in Afternoon: → Vallée de Mai Nature Reserve → Tropical nature walk → Couple photography Evening: → Beach leisure → Romantic dinner → Overnight at Praslin Island', 487),
  ('mahe-island', 29, 'seven-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'SEVEN-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 5', NULL, 'Breakfast → Praslin Island exploration → Anse Lazio → Beach relaxation → Swimming & leisure → Scenic couple photography Afternoon: → Anse Georgette / resort leisure → Sunset experience Evening: → Romantic dinner → Overnight at Praslin Island', 488),
  ('mahe-island', 29, 'seven-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'SEVEN-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 6', NULL, 'Breakfast → Day excursion to La Digue Island → Bicycle / private island exploration → L''Union Estate → Anse Source d''Argent → Granite rock formations → Couple photography Afternoon: → Beach relaxation → Leisure around La Digue Evening: → Return to Praslin → Overnight at Praslin Island', 489),
  ('mahe-island', 29, 'seven-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'SEVEN-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 7', NULL, 'Breakfast → Ferry / domestic flight to Mahé Island → Romantic resort check-in Afternoon: → Beach leisure → Couple spa / relaxation → Souvenir shopping Evening: → Sunset experience → Farewell romantic dinner → Overnight at Mahé Island', 490),
  ('mahe-island', 29, 'seven-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'SEVEN-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 8', NULL, 'Breakfast → Leisure morning → Hotel checkout → Private transfer to Seychelles International Airport (SEZ) → Departure', 491),
  ('mahe-island', 30, 'seven-nights-family-pattern', 'SEVEN-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 1', NULL, 'Arrival at Mahé Island – Seychelles International Airport (SEZ) → Airport transfer → Family resort check-in → Relax and refresh Evening: → Beachfront walk → Family dinner → Overnight at Mahé Island', 492),
  ('mahe-island', 30, 'seven-nights-family-pattern', 'SEVEN-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 2', NULL, 'Breakfast at the hotel Morning: → Mahé Island sightseeing → Victoria → Clock Tower → Local market Afternoon: → Beau Vallon Beach → Swimming & beach activities → Family photography Evening: → Leisure time → Family dinner → Overnight at Mahé Island', 493),
  ('mahe-island', 30, 'seven-nights-family-pattern', 'SEVEN-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 3', NULL, 'Breakfast → Family leisure day Choose ONE: FAMILY_FUN → Beach activities → Swimming → Snorkelling NATURE → Tropical gardens → Scenic coastal drive → Nature exploration Evening: → Beachfront leisure → Family dinner → Overnight at Mahé Island', 494),
  ('mahe-island', 30, 'seven-nights-family-pattern', 'SEVEN-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 4', NULL, 'Breakfast → Hotel checkout → Ferry / domestic flight to Praslin Island → Family resort check-in Afternoon: → Vallée de Mai Nature Reserve → Tropical nature trails → Family exploration Evening: → Beach leisure → Family dinner → Overnight at Praslin Island', 495),
  ('mahe-island', 30, 'seven-nights-family-pattern', 'SEVEN-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 5', NULL, 'Breakfast → Praslin Island exploration → Anse Lazio → Swimming & beach activities → Family photography Afternoon: → Beach / resort leisure → Family activities Evening: → Relaxed family dinner → Overnight at Praslin Island', 496),
  ('mahe-island', 30, 'seven-nights-family-pattern', 'SEVEN-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 6', NULL, 'Breakfast → Day excursion to La Digue Island → Bicycle / island exploration → L''Union Estate → Anse Source d''Argent → Granite formations → Family photography Afternoon: → Beach relaxation → Leisure around La Digue Evening: → Return to Praslin → Overnight at Praslin Island', 497),
  ('mahe-island', 30, 'seven-nights-family-pattern', 'SEVEN-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 7', NULL, 'Breakfast → Ferry / domestic flight to Mahé Island → Family resort check-in Afternoon: → Beach leisure → Shopping / souvenir time → Family relaxation Evening: → Farewell family dinner → Overnight at Mahé Island', 498),
  ('mahe-island', 30, 'seven-nights-family-pattern', 'SEVEN-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 8', NULL, 'Breakfast → Leisure morning → Hotel checkout → Transfer to Seychelles International Airport (SEZ) → Departure', 499),
  ('mahe-island', 31, 'seven-nights-luxury-pattern', 'SEVEN-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 1', NULL, 'Arrival at Mahé Island – Seychelles International Airport (SEZ) → Private luxury airport transfer → Premium beachfront resort check-in → Relax and refresh Evening: → Private sunset experience → Fine-dining dinner → Overnight at Mahé Island', 500),
  ('mahe-island', 31, 'seven-nights-luxury-pattern', 'SEVEN-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 2', NULL, 'Breakfast at the hotel Morning: → Private Mahé Island tour → Victoria → Local market → Scenic island viewpoints Afternoon: → Beau Vallon → Private beach experience → Scenic photography Evening: → Sunset cocktails → Fine dining → Overnight at Mahé Island', 501),
  ('mahe-island', 31, 'seven-nights-luxury-pattern', 'SEVEN-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 3', NULL, 'Breakfast → Luxury leisure day Choose ONE: LUXURY_LEISURE → Private beach cabana → Spa & wellness → Premium afternoon experience PRIVATE_EXPERIENCE → Private yacht / sailing experience → Snorkelling → Secluded beach stop Evening: → Private beachfront dinner → Overnight at Mahé Island', 502),
  ('mahe-island', 31, 'seven-nights-luxury-pattern', 'SEVEN-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 4', NULL, 'Breakfast → Hotel checkout → Premium ferry / private transfer to Praslin Island → Luxury resort check-in Afternoon: → Private Vallée de Mai experience → Tropical nature exploration → Scenic photography Evening: → Resort spa / leisure → Fine dining → Overnight at Praslin Island', 503),
  ('mahe-island', 31, 'seven-nights-luxury-pattern', 'SEVEN-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 5', NULL, 'Breakfast → Private Praslin Island experience → Anse Lazio → Secluded beach leisure → Swimming & snorkelling Afternoon: → Anse Georgette → Premium resort experience → Spa / wellness Evening: → Sunset experience → Fine dining → Overnight at Praslin Island', 504),
  ('mahe-island', 31, 'seven-nights-luxury-pattern', 'SEVEN-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 6', NULL, 'Breakfast → Private excursion to La Digue Island → Private island exploration → L''Union Estate → Anse Source d''Argent → Granite rock formations → Scenic photography Afternoon: → Secluded beach experience → Private leisure / yacht experience Evening: → Return to Praslin → Premium dinner → Overnight at Praslin Island', 505),
