  ('cape-town', 30, '10-day-9-night-south-africa-family-itinerary', '10-DAY / 9-NIGHT SOUTH AFRICA FAMILY ITINERARY', 'DAY 6: OUDTSHOORN DAY TOUR (CAVES, WILDLIFE & OSTRICH FARM)', NULL, '', 600),
  ('cape-town', 30, '10-day-9-night-south-africa-family-itinerary', '10-DAY / 9-NIGHT SOUTH AFRICA FAMILY ITINERARY', 'DAY 7: OUDTSHOORN TO CAPE TOWN', NULL, '', 601),
  ('cape-town', 30, '10-day-9-night-south-africa-family-itinerary', '10-DAY / 9-NIGHT SOUTH AFRICA FAMILY ITINERARY', 'DAY 8: CAPE TOWN CITY TOUR, TABLE MOUNTAIN & GOLD RESTAURANT', NULL, '', 602),
  ('cape-town', 30, '10-day-9-night-south-africa-family-itinerary', '10-DAY / 9-NIGHT SOUTH AFRICA FAMILY ITINERARY', 'DAY 9: FULL-DAY CAPE PENINSULA TOUR & SEAL ISLAND CRUISE', NULL, '', 603),
  ('cape-town', 30, '10-day-9-night-south-africa-family-itinerary', '10-DAY / 9-NIGHT SOUTH AFRICA FAMILY ITINERARY', 'DAY 10: CAPE TOWN DEPARTURE', NULL, '', 604),
  ('cape-town', 31, '10-days-and-9-nights-luxury-itinerary', '10 DAYS & 9 NIGHTS LUXURY ITINERARY', 'DAY 1 – ARRIVAL IN JOHANNESBURG & EMPERORS PALACE IMMERSION', NULL, 'Morning / Afternoon: Upon landing at O.R. Tambo International Airport (JNB), pass through customs and clear arrival formalities. → Collect your luggage and head to the designated terminal exit to board the **Peermont Complimentary Airport Shuttle** for a quick 5-minute transfer to the resort complex. → Check into **Peermont Metcourt Suites at Emperors Palace** (Classic Room), taking time to unpack, refresh, and settle into your resort accommodations. → Spend your afternoon relaxing by the outdoor resort pool or exploring the grand casino complex and entertainment concourses. **Lunch & Dinner** Indulge in authentic Indian flavors at **Taste of Mumbai**, conveniently located within the Emperors Palace hotel complex.', 605),
  ('cape-town', 31, '10-days-and-9-nights-luxury-itinerary', '10 DAYS & 9 NIGHTS LUXURY ITINERARY', 'DAY 2 – GOLD MINING HERITAGE & JOHANNESBURG EXPLORATION', NULL, 'Morning: Enjoy a fresh buffet breakfast at the hotel''s main dining hall. → Meet your private guide in the lobby and step into your 7-seater vehicle for a half-day **Gold Reef City Tour**. → Explore the surface grounds of the historic 19th-century Witwatersrand gold mine, witnessing a live molten gold pour and viewing historic mining displays. → *(Optional)* Experience the theme park’s thrill rides or arrange an optional underground mine shaft tour (for your own account). Lunch: Savor a traditional North Indian meal at **The Raj Restaurant**, located right within the Gold Reef City complex. **Afternoon & Evening** Transfer back to Emperors Palace in your private vehicle for a relaxed afternoon at leisure. → Walk through the manicured gardens, visit the resort spa, or enjoy high-stakes gaming inside the casino. → Dine on gourmet North and South Indian specialties for dinner back at **Taste of Mumbai**.', 606),
  ('cape-town', 31, '10-days-and-9-nights-luxury-itinerary', '10 DAYS & 9 NIGHTS LUXURY ITINERARY', 'DAY 3 – SCENIC OVERLAND TRANSFER TO SUN CITY RESORT', NULL, 'Morning: Following breakfast, check out of Peermont Metcourt Suites. → Meet your private chauffeur for a comfortable overland transfer (~2.5 to 3 hours) in a 7-seater vehicle heading northwest to **Sun City Resort**. → Pass through the rolling landscapes of the North West Province before arriving at the world-famous luxury entertainment complex. → Check into the **Sun City Hotel** (Luxury Room), receiving your complimentary access passes to the resort''s iconic water park. Lunch: Enjoy a vibrant, spice-infused lunch at **The Raj Restaurant** inside the Sun City complex. **Afternoon & Evening** Spend your afternoon utilizing your included access to the **Valley of Waves**, riding the Roaring Lagoon wave pool or relaxing along the tropical artificial beach. → Make use of the complimentary resort shuttles to explore the Gary Player Golf Course, the Lost City gardens, or the casino concourse. → Enjoy a fine Indian dining experience for dinner at **The Raj Restaurant**, followed by evening entertainment around the resort.', 607),
  ('cape-town', 31, '10-days-and-9-nights-luxury-itinerary', '10 DAYS & 9 NIGHTS LUXURY ITINERARY', 'DAY 4 – PILANESBERG BIG FIVE SAFARI & RESORT LEISURE', NULL, 'Morning / Afternoon: Venture out on an exciting **Game Drive in Pilanesberg National Park**, situated in an extinct volcanic crater directly bordering Sun City. → Board an open 4x4 safari vehicle with a professional game ranger to track Africa''s "Big Five" (lion, leopard, elephant, rhino, and buffalo), along with giraffes, zebras, and diverse birdlife. → Return to the resort to relax, catch up on downtime by the pool, or explore the maze at the Lost City. **Lunch & Dinner** Enjoy both your lunch and evening dinner at **The Raj Restaurant** inside Sun City, sampling regional curries, tandoori grills, and fresh naan.', 608),
  ('cape-town', 31, '10-days-and-9-nights-luxury-itinerary', '10 DAYS & 9 NIGHTS LUXURY ITINERARY', 'DAY 5 – COASTAL ESCAPE TO KNYSNA & THE HEADS CRUISE', NULL, 'Morning: Enjoy breakfast, check out of the Sun City Hotel, and transfer via private 7-seater vehicle back to Johannesburg International Airport (JNB). → Board your short domestic flight (booked separately) across South Africa to **George Airport (GRJ)** on the Garden Route. → Meet your private driver upon landing at George Airport for a scenic coastal transfer along the Garden Route toward **Knysna**. Afternoon: Check into the **Knysna Log-Inn**, ideally located near the waterfront. → Board the iconic **John Benn Cruise** for a scenic voyage across the Knysna Lagoon, sailing past featherbed nature reserves toward the dramatic sandstone cliffs of the **Knysna Heads**. **Lunch & Dinner** Savor delicious Indian dishes for both lunch and dinner at **The Raasoie Restaurant** in Knysna.', 609),
  ('cape-town', 31, '10-days-and-9-nights-luxury-itinerary', '10 DAYS & 9 NIGHTS LUXURY ITINERARY', 'DAY 6 – OUDTSHOORN HERITAGE & CANGO WILDLIFE EXPLORATION', NULL, 'Morning: Meet your registered Cape tourist guide for a full-day private excursion through the majestic Outeniqua Pass into the semi-arid Klein Karoo region. → Tour the ancient **Cango Caves**, marveling at towering dripstone formations and vast subterranean limestone chambers. → Visit the **Cango Wildlife Ranch** for an up-close educational tour highlighting cheetahs, crocodiles, and endangered wildlife. Lunch: Stop at the **Safari Ostrich Farm** for a guided classic tour of a working ostrich estate, followed by a specially prepared 4-course **Eastern Lunch (Menu 3)**. **Afternoon & Evening** Check into the **Oudtshoorn Inn** in the heart of the ostrich capital of the world. → Spend a quiet late afternoon swimming or relaxing on the hotel grounds. → Enjoy a formal sit-down dinner hosted inside the **Oudtshoorn Inn** hotel complex.', 610),
  ('cape-town', 31, '10-days-and-9-nights-luxury-itinerary', '10 DAYS & 9 NIGHTS LUXURY ITINERARY', 'DAY 7 – FLIGHT TO CAPE TOWN & CITY ARRIVAL', NULL, 'Morning: Enjoy breakfast at the hotel before checking out. → Meet your private 7-seater vehicle for your transfer from Oudtshoorn back through the mountain passes to **George Airport (GRJ)**. → Board your domestic flight (booked separately) to **Cape Town International Airport (CPT)**. Afternoon: Arrive in Cape Town, where your private full-day vehicle and driver will meet you at arrivals for your transfer into the city center. → Check into **The Capetonian Hotel** (Superior Room), located centrally near the V&A Waterfront and City Bowl. **Lunch & Dinner** Indulge in authentic Indian cuisine for both lunch and dinner at a recommended fine-dining **Indian Restaurant in Cape Town**.', 611),
  ('cape-town', 31, '10-days-and-9-nights-luxury-itinerary', '10 DAYS & 9 NIGHTS LUXURY ITINERARY', 'DAY 8 – TABLE MOUNTAIN & CULTURAL DJEMBE DINNER', NULL, 'Morning: Embark on a private half-day **Cape Town City Tour** in your 7-seater vehicle. → Take the revolving **Table Mountain Aerial Cableway** to the summit, enjoying 360-degree views over Table Bay, Camp''s Bay, and Lion''s Head during the ascent. → Walk the summit pathways before descending into the historic city center to view Greenmarket Square and the colorful Bo-Kaap neighborhood. Lunch: Enjoy lunch at a selected **Indian Restaurant in Cape Town**. Evening: Experience an immersive African culinary journey at **GOLD Restaurant**. → Participate in an interactive **Djembe drumming session** led by master drummers. → Savor a multi-course tasting menu of pan-African cuisine served directly to your table, accompanied by live performance artists, tall Mali puppets, and traditional singers.', 612),
  ('cape-town', 31, '10-days-and-9-nights-luxury-itinerary', '10 DAYS & 9 NIGHTS LUXURY ITINERARY', 'DAY 9 – CAPE PENINSULA COASTAL LOOP & SEAL ISLAND', NULL, 'Morning: Depart on a private, full-day **Cape Peninsula Tour** along one of the world''s most scenic coastal drives. → Travel through the Atlantic Seaboard coves to Hout Bay Harbor; board the **Nauticat Catamaran** for a cruise to Duiker Island (Seal Island) to view thousands of wild Cape fur seals. → Continue along the dramatic cliffside curves of **Chapman''s Peak Drive**, passing through Noordhoek toward Table Mountain National Park. Afternoon: Arrive at **Cape Point**; ride the Flying Dutchman Funicular up to the historic lighthouse before visiting the landmark sign at the **Cape of Good Hope**. → Stop at **Boulders Beach** in Simon''s Town to walk along the wooden boardwalks alongside a wild colony of African Penguins. **Lunch & Dinner** Refuel with Indian cuisine during your day’s outing and return to central Cape Town for dinner at an **Indian Restaurant in Cape Town**.', 613),
  ('cape-town', 31, '10-days-and-9-nights-luxury-itinerary', '10 DAYS & 9 NIGHTS LUXURY ITINERARY', 'DAY 10 – DEPARTURE FROM CAPE TOWN', NULL, 'Morning: Enjoy a final breakfast at The Capetonian Hotel and complete check-out procedures. → Meet your private 7-seater driver in the hotel lobby for your direct transfer to **Cape Town International Airport (CPT)** for your onward international flight home.', 614),
  ('cape-town', 32, 'travel-agent-insights', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS', 'What inexperienced planners often do wrong', NULL, '', 615),
  ('cape-town', 32, 'travel-agent-insights', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS', 'What an experienced planner does differently', NULL, '', 616),
  ('cape-town', 32, 'travel-agent-insights', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS', 'Best planning rule', NULL, '', 617),
  ('cape-town', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', NULL, NULL, 'IF: `trip_length <= 0.5 days` THEN: Choose a focused excursion taking the **Table Mountain Aerial Cableway** to the summit for 360-degree views of the Mother City, followed by a quick stroll through the colorful historic streets of **Bo-Kaap** and a traditional Cape Malay snack before returning to Cape Town International Airport (CPT). Reason: Half-day layovers require efficient, high-impact scheduling near the city center; prioritizing Table Mountain and Bo-Kaap delivers Cape Town''s most iconic natural landmark and vibrant cultural heritage without risking missed flight connections. IF: `trip_length == 1 day` THEN: Ascend **Table Mountain** early via cableway in the morning, explore the colorful streets of **Bo-Kaap** and historic **Greenmarket Square** for lunch, take an afternoon trip to the **V&A Waterfront** and **Zeitz MOCAA**, and enjoy an oceanfront seafood dinner along the **Camps Bay Strip** at sunset. Reason: A single full day allows energetic travelers to experience Cape Town''s striking contrast between dramatic mountain landscapes, historic Cape Malay culture, world-class modern art, and vibrant Atlantic coastal dining. IF: `trip_length >= 2 days` THEN: Spend day one exploring central highlights including **Table Mountain**, **Bo-Kaap**, the **V&A Waterfront**, and **Zeitz MOCAA**; spend day two taking a full-day coastal road trip down the **Cape Peninsula**, traveling via **Chapman’s Peak Drive** to **Cape Point**, **Cape of Good Hope**, and the **Boulders Beach Penguin Colony**. Reason: Multi-day stays allow travelers to balance Cape Town''s central urban landmarks and cultural museums with a world-famous coastal drive through marine reserves and wild penguin habitats. IF: `trip_type == FIRST_TIME_VISITOR` THEN: Focus on quintessential city highlights—ascending **Table Mountain**, taking a full-day **Cape Peninsula** trip (**Chapman’s Peak Drive**, **Cape Point**, **Boulders Beach Penguins**), visiting the historic **Robben Island** prison museum, exploring **Bo-Kaap**, and dining at the **V&A Waterfront**. Reason: Combining iconic natural wonder peaks, wild African penguin colonies, historic apartheid heritage sites, and harbor dining delivers a complete, unforgettable first-time overview of Cape Town. IF: `trip_type == HONEYMOON` THEN: Book a luxury ocean-facing suite in **Camps Bay** or a historic wine estate room in **Constantia**, schedule a private sunset catamaran cruise from the **V&A Waterfront**, charter a private vintage sidecar along **Chapman’s Peak Drive**, and indulge in fine-dining wine-pairing tasting menus in the **Cape Winelands**. Reason: Pairing dramatic Atlantic oceanfront views and boutique vineyard luxury with private sunset cruises, scenic cliffside drives, and acclaimed culinary estates creates a romantic getaway. IF: `traveler_type == FAMILY` THEN: Visit the **Two Oceans Aquarium** at the V&A Waterfront, ride the **Table Mountain Aerial Cableway**, walk among wild penguins on wooden boardwalks at **Boulders Beach**, cross the elevated "Boomslang" Tree Canopy Walkway at **Kirstenbosch Botanical Garden**, and ride the **Cape Wheel**. Reason: Interactive marine touch pools, revolving cable cars, accessible penguin boardwalks, and wide botanical garden lawns keep children entertained without physical strain. IF: `traveler_type == LUXURY` THEN: Book 5-star suites at iconic properties like *The Silo Hotel*, *One&Only Cape Town*, *Mount Nelson*, or *The Twelve Apostles Hotel & Spa*, hire private chauffeured vehicles, take a scenic helicopter flight over the Cape Peninsula, and enjoy private cellar tastings and tasting menus in **Constantia** and **Franschhoek**. Reason: World-class waterfront luxury hotels, private aerial transport, exclusive estate wine tastings, and internationally acclaimed culinary tables provide high-end comfort and service. IF: `traveler_type == BUDGET` THEN: Stay in central hostels or guesthouses around **Long Street** or **Green Point**, hike up **Lion''s Head** or **Table Mountain** via Platteklip Gorge for free, photograph **Bo-Kaap** on foot, browse local craft markets at **Greenmarket Square** and **The Watershed**, and spend low-cost days on **Clifton** and **Camps Bay public beaches**. Reason: Cape Town offers extensive zero-cost outdoor mountain hikes, vibrant craft markets, free public beaches, and low-cost self-guided cultural walks for price-conscious travelers. IF: `traveler_interest == NATURE` THEN: Explore the native fynbos flora and canopy walkway at **Kirstenbosch National Botanical Garden**, trek the wilderness trails inside **Table Mountain National Park**, spot marine life and Cape fur seals in **Hout Bay**, view wild African penguins at **Boulders Beach**, and visit the dramatic cliffside landscapes of **Cape Point**. Reason: Cape Town is situated within the unique Cape Floral Kingdom, offering unparalleled access to biodiverse botanical gardens, endemic marine life, and coastal nature reserves. IF: `traveler_interest == FOOD` THEN: Embark on a rich culinary journey—sampling traditional Cape Malay curries in **Bo-Kaap**, exploring third-wave coffee shops and trendy bistros along **Bree Street**, savoring fresh seafood at the **V&A Waterfront**, eating gourmet street food at the weekend **Bay Harbour Market**, and experiencing fine-dining open-fire gastronomy and wine pairings in **Constantia**. Reason: Cape Town is Africa''s premier culinary destination, blending indigenous South African braai traditions, historic Cape Malay spices, fresh Atlantic seafood, and modern fine-dining techniques. IF: `traveler_interest == ADVENTURE` THEN: Paraglide tandem off **Signal Hill** landing in Sea Point, abseil 112 meters down the cliff face of **Table Mountain**, snorkel with wild Cape fur seals off **Hout Bay**, surf the swells at **Muizenberg Beach**, and hike the steep knife-edge ridges of **Lion''s Head** or **India Venster**. Reason: Adrenaline seekers can turn Cape Town''s dramatic topography into a playground for ocean water sports, high-altitude cliff rappelling, mountain ridge treks, and tandem aerial paragliding. IF: `traveler_type == SENIOR` THEN: Stay at step-free luxury properties along the flat **V&A Waterfront** or **Sea Point Promenade**, utilize private chauffeured transfers, take the **Table Mountain Aerial Cableway**, stroll accessible wooden boardwalks at **Boulders Beach**, take a golf-cart tour of **Kirstenbosch Botanical Garden**, and enjoy scenic drives along **Chapman''s Peak Drive**. Reason: Revolving cable cars, flat harbor promenades, wheelchair-accessible wooden boardwalks, and scenic vehicle drives allow mature travelers to experience Cape Town''s beauty comfortably. IF: `traveler_type == TRANSIT` THEN: Take a 20-to-30 minute taxi or ride-share from Cape Town International Airport (CPT) directly to the **V&A Waterfront**, enjoy a relaxed meal of fresh seafood or South African cuisine, browse artisanal crafts at **The Watershed**, take in Table Mountain views across the harbor, and return directly to the terminal. Reason: High accessibility between CPT Airport and the self-contained V&A Waterfront allows layover passengers to sample local food, shop for authentic crafts, and enjoy mountain views without transit complications. IF: `trip_length >= 3 days` THEN: Divide your stay between 1 full day of city core highlights (**Table Mountain**, **Bo-Kaap**, **V&A Waterfront**, **Robben Island**), 1 full day along the coastal **Cape Peninsula** (**Chapman''s Peak Drive**, **Cape Point**, **Boulders Beach Penguins**), and 1 full day exploring the historic wine estates and fine dining of **Constantia**, **Stellenbosch**, or **Franschhoek**. Reason: A comprehensive multi-day itinerary bridges Cape Town''s iconic urban mountain landmarks and marine wildlife reserves with world-renowned wine valleys and heritage estates nearby.', 618),
  ('cape-town', 34, 'destination-scoring', 'DESTINATION SCORING', NULL, NULL, '| Factor | Score | | --- | --- | | Family | 94 | | Honeymoon | 98 | | Luxury | 96 | | Budget | 82 | | Adventure | 98 | | Culture | 92 | | Food | 98 | | Shopping | 88 | | Nightlife | 88 | | Relaxation | 92 | | Nature | 90 | | Accessibility | 76 | | Senior travelers | 84 | | First-time visitor | 94 | | Photography | 98 |', 619),
  ('cape-town', 35, 'final-travel-agent-verdict', 'FINAL TRAVEL AGENT VERDICT', NULL, NULL, 'Best for: Nature lovers, ocean enthusiasts, food and wine connoisseurs, luxury travelers, adventure seekers, photographers, and history buffs looking for an extraordinary blend of dramatic mountain landscapes, marine wildlife encounters, rich Cape Malay heritage, world-class gastronomy, and picturesque coastal drives. Best duration: 3 to 5 days for a dedicated Cape Town trip covering city highlights, Table Mountain, historic museums, wine valleys, and the coastal Cape Peninsula; or 7 to 10 days when using Cape Town as an anchor point to explore the broader Western Cape, including the Garden Route and nearby safari game reserves. Best season: November to March (the dry summer season, offering long sunny days, warm temperatures, clear skies ideal for Table Mountain views, and outdoor beach activities); June to August brings cool temperatures, wind, and winter rainfall, though it offers great conditions for indoor wine tasting, lower hotel rates, and whale watching along the coast. Best stay: Split-stay strategy—2 to 3 nights in a waterfront or central luxury property (e.g., The Silo Hotel or One&Only Cape Town at the V&A Waterfront) for walking access to harbor shopping, fine-dining restaurants, and museum tours, paired with 2 nights in a coastal strip resort (e.g., The Twelve Apostles Hotel & Spa or a Camps Bay boutique hotel) or a historic wine estate in Constantia (e.g., Steenberg Hotel & Spa) for scenic luxury, vineyard views, and ocean sunsets. Best transport: International arrival via Cape Town International Airport (CPT); Uber ride-hailing service for safe, easy, and affordable point-to-point urban transit; private air-conditioned vehicle transfers or rental cars for day trips around the Cape Peninsula and Winelands; and the Hop-On Hop-Off Sightseeing Bus for convenient access to major tourist hubs across the city. Must-do: Avoid: Biggest advantage: Unrivaled natural beauty and variety—Cape Town seamlessly blends a cosmopolitan international city center with dramatic ocean scenery, towering mountain peaks, biodiverse botanical gardens, endemic marine wildlife, and world-renowned wine valleys all within a short driving radius. Biggest disadvantage: Unpredictable coastal weather and strong seasonal winds (the "Cape Doctor"), along with economic safety disparities that require travelers to exercise constant urban vigilance and rely on secure vehicle transport after dark. Overall destination score: **94/100**', 620),
  ('cape-town', 36, 'data-quality', 'DATA QUALITY', NULL, NULL, 'information_completeness: 92/100 last_updated: 2026-09-01 last_verified: NOT_LIVE_VERIFIED verified_by: TRAVEL_ENGINE_INITIAL_DATASET sources: IMPORTANT: Prices, opening hours, schedules, visa requirements, availability, accessibility and operational conditions must NOT be treated as permanently valid from this document. These must be sourced from structured, refreshable data.', 621),
  ('tbilisi', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Spring', NULL, 'months: March April May weather: Cool to mild in March, becoming pleasantly warm through April and May. Spring brings increasing sunshine, blooming gardens, and comfortable conditions for walking and sightseeing, although March can still have chilly days and occasional rain. crowd_level: MEDIUM → HIGH price_level: MEDIUM → HIGH overall_score: 88-93 recommended: true reason: One of the best periods for Tbilisi sightseeing, particularly for Old Tbilisi walks, historic landmarks, viewpoints, museums, parks, cafés, and outdoor dining. April and May generally provide increasingly pleasant conditions before the hotter summer period, while visitor demand gradually rises.', 622),
  ('tbilisi', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Summer', NULL, 'months: June July August weather: Warm to hot and generally sunny, with July and August being the hottest months. Rain and thunderstorms can occur, but prolonged rainfall is less typical than in spring or autumn. Daytime heat can make extended walking uncomfortable, particularly in July and August. crowd_level: HIGH price_level: HIGH overall_score: 82-89 recommended: true reason: Good for travelers who enjoy warm weather, outdoor cafés, nightlife, evening walks, viewpoints, and city sightseeing. The hottest parts of the day are better reserved for museums, restaurants, shopping, or hotel relaxation, while outdoor sightseeing is more comfortable in the morning and evening.', 623),
  ('tbilisi', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Autumn', NULL, 'months: September October November weather: Warm and pleasant in September, gradually becoming cooler through October and November. Autumn brings comfortable sightseeing conditions, changing foliage, and generally favorable temperatures, although rainfall becomes more frequent later in the season. crowd_level: MEDIUM → LOW price_level: MEDIUM → LOW overall_score: 92-96 recommended: true reason: One of the strongest seasons for Tbilisi, combining comfortable temperatures with excellent conditions for Old Town exploration, photography, food and wine experiences, museums, parks, and day trips. September and October are particularly attractive for travelers combining Tbilisi with Georgia''s wine regions and countryside. November is cooler and quieter but remains suitable for city sightseeing.', 624),
  ('tbilisi', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Winter', NULL, 'months: December January February weather: Cold to cool, with chilly mornings and evenings and occasional snowfall. Daytime temperatures are generally manageable for city sightseeing, although winter weather can make outdoor walks less comfortable. January is typically among the coldest months. crowd_level: MEDIUM → LOW price_level: LOW → MEDIUM overall_score: 80-87 recommended: true reason: A good period for travelers interested in Tbilisi''s historic atmosphere, museums, cafés, Georgian cuisine, wine, sulfur baths, shopping, and winter city experiences. Visitor numbers are generally lower outside the Christmas and New Year period, while festive dates can bring increased demand. Warm clothing is recommended, particularly for evening walks and hilltop viewpoints.', 625),
  ('tbilisi', 10, 'budget-strategy', 'BUDGET STRATEGY', NULL, NULL, 'Where money can be saved: Where saving money is usually NOT recommended: Travel-agent rule: A slightly more expensive but clean, well-reviewed and reasonably central hotel in Tbilisi usually delivers better total value than a cheaper property far outside the centre once you factor in daily transport costs, travel time, sightseeing convenience, and access to restaurants and attractions. Tbilisi has extensive metro and bus coverage, making a well-located hotel especially valuable for budget travelers.', 626),
  ('tbilisi', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Family', 'family', 'Pre-booked private car / MPV or reliable airport taxi from Tbilisi International Airport; door-to-door service, sufficient luggage space, and convenient for children. Tbilisi International Airport is approximately 17 km southeast of central Tbilisi, with direct road access into the city. A private transfer is generally the most convenient family option, particularly with children and luggage.', 627),
  ('tbilisi', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Honeymoon', 'honeymoon', 'Pre-booked private car with direct hotel drop-off; comfortable and convenient for couples arriving at Tbilisi International Airport. A private transfer is especially suitable for couples carrying luggage and wanting a relaxed start to their city stay. reason: Tbilisi International Airport is the city''s main airport and is well connected with central Tbilisi by road. Official airport information lists municipal buses and airport taxis as direct city-transfer options, while the relatively short airport-to-centre journey makes private transfers practical for couples and other travelers prioritizing convenience.', 628),
  ('tbilisi', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Luxury', 'luxury', 'Chauffeured premium SUV / MPV or private luxury car from Tbilisi International Airport; personalized pickup, luggage assistance, comfortable direct transfer, and hotel drop-off suitable for luxury hotels, boutique properties, and premium stays.', 629),
  ('tbilisi', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Budget', 'budget', 'Municipal bus from Tbilisi International Airport; route #337 connects the airport with central Tbilisi and operates between the airport and the city centre. The official airport lists the municipal bus as a low-cost public transport option, making it the preferred choice for budget travelers comfortable with a longer and less personalized transfer. Airport taxi is another practical option for travelers prioritizing convenience. Official airport taxis operate 24 hours outside the terminal, with the journey to central Tbilisi generally taking around 20–30 minutes depending on traffic.', 630),
  ('tbilisi', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Senior', 'senior', 'Pre-booked private car or official airport taxi with minimal transfers and direct hotel drop-off; prioritize comfortable seating, luggage assistance, and avoiding unnecessary changes between airport, bus, and city transport. A direct road transfer is generally preferable for seniors, particularly when arriving with luggage or staying in central Tbilisi areas with hilly or uneven streets.', 631),
  ('tbilisi', 18, 'family-travel', 'FAMILY TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'child_friendly_score: 91 best_ages: Rules: For young children: Prefer: Avoid:', 632),
  ('tbilisi', 19, 'honeymoon-travel', 'HONEYMOON TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'honeymoon_score: 92 romance_score: 94 privacy_score: 78 luxury_score: 82 Recommended: Honeymoon itinerary should NOT contain more than: 2–3 major activities/day. Prefer: One memorable scenic, cultural, culinary, or wellness experience + free time over: Three or four attractions. Recommended hotel areas: Tbilisi works particularly well for a romantic honeymoon because of its historic Old Town, atmospheric streets, river views, hilltop viewpoints, distinctive architecture, Georgian cuisine and wine culture, sulfur baths, cafés, and vibrant evening atmosphere. Old Tbilisi, Narikala Fortress, the Bridge of Peace, Mtatsminda, Abanotubani, and scenic city viewpoints can each provide memorable couple experiences, but they should be spread across the itinerary rather than packed into a single day. Private transport is recommended for couples who want flexibility and comfort, especially when visiting Mtskheta, Jvari, Kakheti, or other destinations outside central Tbilisi. Central Tbilisi is highly walkable in many areas and well served by public transport, but hilly streets, cobblestones, stairs, and longer regional journeys can make private transport more comfortable for selected experiences. Tbilisi is particularly well suited to couples seeking a romantic combination of historic streets, Georgian food and wine, architecture, scenic viewpoints, wellness, cafés, cultural experiences, and lively evenings. It is less suited to couples seeking an isolated resort-style honeymoon with beaches, private villas, or a completely secluded natural setting.', 633),
  ('tbilisi', 20, 'luxury-travel', 'LUXURY TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'luxury_score: 82 Recommended: Tbilisi luxury travel should focus on: Luxury travelers should not simply be given more activities. Luxury in Tbilisi should primarily increase:', 634),
  ('tbilisi', 21, 'adventure', 'ADVENTURE', NULL, NULL, 'adventure_score: 78 Tbilisi is primarily a cultural, historical, and urban destination, but it also offers a good range of outdoor and moderate adventure experiences in and around the city. Hiking around Mtatsminda, Turtle Lake, Tbilisi National Park, Kojori, cycling, funicular and cable-car rides, nature walks, and scenic exploration are among its notable outdoor activities. Adventure experiences should be interpreted as:', 635),
  ('tbilisi', 22, 'senior-travel', 'SENIOR TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'senior_suitability: 86 walking_intensity: MEDIUM unless carefully managed Rules:', 636),
  ('tbilisi', 23, 'accessibility', 'ACCESSIBILITY', NULL, NULL, 'wheelchair_accessibility: PARTIAL; varies significantly by hotel, attraction, historic area, terrain and transport public_transport_accessibility: VARIABLE; taxis and private vehicles are often more practical for travelers with significant mobility requirements, particularly for hilly or historic areas hotel_accessibility: MUST_BE_VERIFIED_PER_HOTEL attraction_accessibility: MUST_BE_VERIFIED_PER_ATTRACTION Rule: Never infer accessibility from Tbilisi''s overall accessibility. Each hotel and attraction must carry its own accessibility data. Additional notes:', 637),
  ('tbilisi', 24, 'food', 'FOOD', NULL, NULL, 'Tbilisi is particularly strong for: Food experiences: Family: Prioritize clean, family-friendly Georgian restaurants with vegetarian options, familiar dishes, mild food choices, bakeries, khachapuri, soups, grilled dishes, and flexible menus. Honeymoon: A traditional Georgian restaurant, wine-focused dinner, Old Tbilisi dining experience, or scenic restaurant is recommended, with a relaxed evening after sightseeing. Luxury: Premium Georgian restaurants, wine-pairing dinners, private dining, curated wine tastings, boutique restaurants, chef-led experiences, and high-quality Georgian cuisine can be included. Tbilisi has a strong premium dining and wine scene. Budget: Mix local Georgian restaurants, bakeries, casual khinkali restaurants, cafés, food markets, and traditional eateries for affordable meals. Khinkali, khachapuri, lobio, soups, and bakery foods can provide good-value local dining.', 638),
  ('tbilisi', 25, 'shopping', 'SHOPPING', NULL, NULL, 'Strong categories: Luxury shopping: Prefer established wine boutiques, artisan studios, designer boutiques, specialty food shops, and curated Georgian craft stores around Old Tbilisi, Rustaveli Avenue, Freedom Square, and creative districts such as Fabrika for premium wine, jewellery, ceramics, textiles, artwork, designer products, and locally produced gourmet goods. Budget: Prefer: Tbilisi is particularly known for Georgian wine, churchkhela, spices, Svanetian salt, honey, jams, dried fruits, ceramics, minankari enamel jewellery, textiles, carpets, handicrafts, and traditional wine accessories. Travel-agent rule: Prioritize authentic Georgian-made products over generic tourist merchandise. For wine, spices, churchkhela, honey, ceramics, jewellery, and handicrafts, compare quality and provenance before purchasing and prefer established producers, specialist shops, artisan workshops, or reputable markets where authenticity and product quality are easier to verify.', 639),
  ('tbilisi', 26, 'nightlife', 'NIGHTLIFE', NULL, NULL, 'nightlife_level: 82 Suitable for: Best areas: Not a primary requirement for: Evening activities are better suited to: Honeymoon travelers should generally prefer: Romantic Old Tbilisi evening over: Late-night club itinerary unless nightlife is explicitly requested. For couples seeking a more atmospheric evening, prioritize a rooftop dinner, Georgian wine experience, Old Tbilisi walk, live-music venue, scenic Mtatsminda experience, cozy café, or elegant cocktail bar rather than building the itinerary entirely around late-night partying. Travel-agent rule: Position Tbilisi as a destination with strong and varied nightlife rather than a quiet-only evening destination. Its nightlife appeal combines Georgian restaurants, wine bars, cafés, live music, rooftop venues, cultural entertainment, cocktail bars, and late-evening social areas, particularly around Old Tbilisi, Shardeni, Rustaveli, Fabrika, Vera, and Marjanishvili.', 640),
  ('tbilisi', 28, 'sample-itinerary-patterns', 'SAMPLE ITINERARY PATTERNS', '3 NIGHTS', NULL, '### Day 1 Arrival at Tbilisi International Airport → Airport transfer to Tbilisi city → Hotel check-in → Freedom Square → Rustaveli Avenue → Evening walk / café experience → Georgian dinner → Hotel ### Day 2 Morning: Old Tbilisi → Meidan Square → Abanotubani → Sulfur Baths area → Sioni Cathedral → Metekhi Church Afternoon: Rike Park → Bridge of Peace → Cable Car to Narikala Fortress → Mother of Georgia → Tbilisi Botanical Garden Evening: Shardeni Street → Georgian wine / café experience → Dinner → Hotel ### Day 3 Morning: Sameba Holy Trinity Cathedral → Dry Bridge Market → Marjanishvili / Fabrika area Afternoon: Mtatsminda Funicular → Mtatsminda Park → Tbilisi panoramic views Evening: Rustaveli Avenue → Georgian restaurant / wine bar → Relaxed evening in Tbilisi ### Day 4 Breakfast → Hotel checkout → Airport transfer → Tbilisi International Airport → Departure', 641),
  ('tbilisi', 29, 'four-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'FOUR-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 1', NULL, 'Arrival at Tbilisi International Airport → Private transfer to Tbilisi → Romantic hotel check-in → Relax and enjoy the hotel → Evening walk through Old Tbilisi → Romantic Georgian dinner → Overnight at Tbilisi', 642),
  ('tbilisi', 29, 'four-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'FOUR-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 2', NULL, 'Morning: Private Tbilisi sightseeing → Freedom Square → Rustaveli Avenue → Old Tbilisi → Meidan Square → Abanotubani Afternoon: Private lunch → Sioni Cathedral → Metekhi Church → Rike Park → Bridge of Peace Evening: Cable car to Narikala Fortress → Panoramic Tbilisi views → Romantic dinner', 643),
  ('tbilisi', 29, 'four-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'FOUR-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 3', NULL, 'Breakfast → Private excursion from Tbilisi to Mtskheta → Jvari Monastery → Scenic views over the Aragvi and Mtkvari rivers → Svetitskhoveli Cathedral → Explore historic Mtskheta Afternoon: Private Georgian lunch → Return to Tbilisi → Hotel relaxation Evening: Mtatsminda Funicular → Panoramic sunset views → Special honeymoon dinner', 644),
  ('tbilisi', 29, 'four-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'FOUR-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 4', NULL, 'Breakfast → Private excursion from Tbilisi towards Ananuri → Ananuri Fortress → Zhinvali Reservoir viewpoint → Scenic Georgian Military Road → Gudauri Afternoon: Private lunch → Mountain scenery and couple photography → Relaxed return journey to Tbilisi Evening: Free time → Romantic café / wine experience → Special Georgian dinner → Overnight at Tbilisi', 645),
  ('tbilisi', 29, 'four-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'FOUR-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 5', NULL, 'Breakfast → Leisure morning → Hotel checkout → Private transfer to Tbilisi International Airport → Departure', 646),
  ('tbilisi', 30, 'four-nights-family-pattern', 'FOUR-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 1', NULL, 'Arrival at Tbilisi International Airport → Private family transfer to Tbilisi → Hotel check-in → Rest and refresh Evening: → Easy walk around Freedom Square → Bridge of Peace → Rike Park → Family-friendly dinner → Overnight at Tbilisi', 647),
  ('tbilisi', 30, 'four-nights-family-pattern', 'FOUR-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 2', NULL, 'Morning: Private Tbilisi sightseeing → Old Tbilisi → Meidan Square → Sioni Cathedral → Abanotubani Afternoon: Family lunch → Tbilisi Cable Car → Narikala Fortress → Mother of Georgia viewpoint Evening: → Relaxed café / dessert experience → Dinner → Overnight at Tbilisi', 648),
  ('tbilisi', 30, 'four-nights-family-pattern', 'FOUR-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 3', NULL, 'Breakfast → Private day trip to Mtskheta → Jvari Monastery → Scenic viewpoints → Svetitskhoveli Cathedral → Explore historic Mtskheta Afternoon: → Family lunch → Return to Tbilisi → Hotel rest Evening: → Mtatsminda Funicular → Mtatsminda Park → Family leisure time → Dinner → Overnight at Tbilisi', 649),
  ('tbilisi', 30, 'four-nights-family-pattern', 'FOUR-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 4', NULL, 'Breakfast → Private excursion towards Ananuri → Ananuri Fortress → Zhinvali Reservoir → Scenic Georgian Military Road → Gudauri Afternoon: → Family lunch → Mountain scenery and photography → Return to Tbilisi Evening: → Free time → Family dinner → Overnight at Tbilisi', 650),
  ('tbilisi', 30, 'four-nights-family-pattern', 'FOUR-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 5', NULL, 'Breakfast → Hotel checkout → Free time depending on flight schedule → Private transfer to Tbilisi International Airport → Departure', 651),
  ('tbilisi', 31, 'four-nights-luxury-pattern', 'FOUR-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 1', NULL, 'Arrival at Tbilisi International Airport → Premium private airport transfer → Luxury hotel check-in → Welcome drink and leisure time → Relax at the hotel Evening: → Private Old Tbilisi walk → Bridge of Peace → Rike Park → Premium Georgian dinner → Overnight at Tbilisi', 652),
  ('tbilisi', 31, 'four-nights-luxury-pattern', 'FOUR-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 2', NULL, 'Morning: Private chauffeur-driven Tbilisi sightseeing → Freedom Square → Rustaveli Avenue → Old Tbilisi → Sioni Cathedral → Abanotubani Afternoon: → Premium Georgian lunch → Private cable-car ride to Narikala Fortress → Mother of Georgia → Tbilisi Botanical Garden Evening: → Mtatsminda Funicular → Panoramic sunset views over Tbilisi → Fine-dining experience → Overnight at Tbilisi', 653),
  ('tbilisi', 31, 'four-nights-luxury-pattern', 'FOUR-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 3', NULL, 'Breakfast → Private chauffeur-driven excursion to Mtskheta → Jvari Monastery → Panoramic views → Svetitskhoveli Cathedral → Private guided heritage experience Afternoon: → Premium Georgian lunch → Continue towards Ananuri Fortress → Zhinvali Reservoir → Scenic Georgian Military Road Evening: → Return to Tbilisi → Luxury hotel relaxation → Private dinner → Overnight at Tbilisi', 654),
  ('tbilisi', 31, 'four-nights-luxury-pattern', 'FOUR-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 4', NULL, 'Breakfast → Private excursion to Kakheti → Scenic vineyard landscapes → Premium winery experience → Private wine tasting → Traditional Georgian cultural experience Afternoon: → Gourmet Georgian lunch at a selected winery → Leisurely countryside experience → Return to Tbilisi Evening: → Spa / wellness experience → Premium dinner → Relaxed evening at the hotel → Overnight at Tbilisi', 655),
  ('tbilisi', 31, 'four-nights-luxury-pattern', 'FOUR-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 5', NULL, 'Breakfast → Luxury hotel checkout → Private airport transfer → Tbilisi International Airport → Departure', 656),
  ('tbilisi', 32, 'travel-agent-insights', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS', 'What inexperienced planners often do wrong', NULL, '', 657),
  ('tbilisi', 32, 'travel-agent-insights', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS', 'What an experienced planner does differently', NULL, '', 658),
  ('tbilisi', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', NULL, NULL, 'IF: trip_length <= 2 nights THEN: do not recommend Gori + Uplistsikhe, Ananuri + Gudauri, or Kakheti day trips as default additions. Reason: The additional road travel can make a short Tbilisi stay unnecessarily rushed. IF: trip_type == HONEYMOON THEN: increase_romance_weight by 20% increase_privacy_weight by 15% increase_free_time_weight by 25% decrease_activity_density by 20% Reason: The objective is a relaxed and romantic city experience with scenic views, Georgian dining, cafés, and quality couple time rather than maximum sightseeing. IF: traveler_type == FAMILY AND: children_age <= 6 THEN: reduce_travel_intensity_target by 20% increase_downtime by 20% prefer_short_sightseeing + parks + cable_car + family_friendly_experiences Reason: Young children can find long walking routes, crowded historic areas, mountain-road transfers, and excessive sightseeing tiring. IF: hotel_is_far_from_central_TBILISI AND: hotel_saving < additional_transport_cost + value_of_lost_time THEN: prefer_hotel_near_CENTRAL_TBILISI Reason: A cheaper hotel may not provide better total value once daily taxi costs, traffic, travel time, and sightseeing convenience are considered. IF: trip_length <= 4 nights THEN: prefer_one_hotel Reason: Hotel changes consume valuable short-trip time and reduce time available for sightseeing, dining, shopping, and relaxation. IF: trip_length >= 4 nights AND: traveler_interest == HISTORY_AND_SCENIC_EXPLORATION THEN: consider_TBILISI + NEARBY_GEORGIAN_DESTINATIONS Reason: A longer stay makes it practical to explore Tbilisi''s core attractions along with Mtskheta, Gori, Uplistsikhe, Ananuri, Gudauri, or Kakheti. IF: traveler_type == LUXURY THEN: prefer_private_transfer AND: prefer_high_service_hotel AND: prefer_private_or_personalized_experiences Reason: Luxury value in Tbilisi is primarily created through premium accommodation, private transfers, personalized tours, fine dining, spa experiences, wine experiences, and convenient sightseeing. IF: traveler_type == BUDGET THEN: prefer_central_hotel_location AND: use_metro_or_local_bus_where_practical AND: mix_free_and_paid_attractions Reason: Maintain sightseeing quality while reducing unnecessary transportation and accommodation costs. IF: traveler_interest == CULTURE_AND_RELAXATION THEN: prefer_OLD_TBILISI AND: group_OLD_TBILISI + FREEDOM_SQUARE + RUSTAVELI_AVENUE + RIVERSIDE_EXPERIENCES Reason: Central Tbilisi provides convenient access to historic streets, churches, restaurants, cafés, cultural attractions, shopping, and relaxed city experiences. IF: traveler_interest == SCENIC_AND_PHOTOGRAPHY THEN: prefer_MTATSMINDA_AND_NARIKALA AND: group_panorama_views + OLD_TBILISI + RIVER_VIEWS + CITYSCAPES Reason: Mtatsminda, Narikala Fortress, the Tbilisi Cable Car, and Old Tbilisi provide some of the city''s strongest panoramic and photographic experiences. IF: traveler_interest == ADVENTURE_AND_OUTDOORS THEN: prefer_TBILISI_SURROUNDINGS AND: group_hiking + MOUNTAIN_VIEWS + SCENIC_ROADS + NATURE_EXPERIENCES Reason: The areas surrounding Tbilisi provide opportunities for hiking, scenic drives, mountain viewpoints, and nature-focused excursions. IF: traveler_interest == HISTORY_AND_CULTURE THEN: prefer_OLD_TBILISI AND: group_NARIKALA + ABANOTUBANI + SIONI_CATHEDRAL + GEORGIAN_HERITAGE_EXPERIENCES Reason: These experiences showcase Tbilisi''s historic architecture, religious heritage, traditional neighborhoods, baths, and Georgian cultural character. IF: traveler_interest == HISTORY + DAY_TRIPS THEN: consider_MTSKHETA_AND_GORI_UPLISTSIKHE AND: group_ancient_sites + churches + museums + archaeological_landscapes Reason: Mtskheta, Gori, and Uplistsikhe provide strong opportunities to experience Georgia''s religious, historical, archaeological, and cultural heritage beyond Tbilisi. IF: trip_length >= 4 nights AND: traveler_interest == MOUNTAINS + SCENIC_EXPLORATION THEN: consider_split_itinerary BETWEEN: CENTRAL_TBILISI + ANANURI/GUDAURI Reason: Separating central Tbilisi sightseeing from longer mountain excursions reduces unnecessary backtracking and keeps the itinerary comfortable. IF: traveler_interest == WINE_AND_GASTRONOMY THEN: consider_KAKHETI AND: group_winery_visits + WINE_TASTING + GEORGIAN_FOOD + COUNTRYSIDE_EXPERIENCES Reason: Kakheti is Georgia''s principal wine region and provides a strong combination of wine, food, countryside, and cultural experiences. IF: weather == HEAVY_RAIN OR: visibility == LOW THEN: reduce_mountain_and_remote_outdoor_activities AND: prefer_CENTRAL_TBILISI AND: increase_flexible_indoor_or_hotel_time Reason: Rain, fog, snow, and poor visibility can reduce the value and safety of viewpoints, mountain excursions, and longer road journeys. IF: traveler_interest == ROMANTIC_RELAXATION THEN: prefer_OLD_TBILISI + MTATSMINDA + RIVERSIDE_EXPERIENCES AND: decrease_activity_density_by_20_percent Reason: Couples generally benefit more from scenic walks, panoramic views, Georgian dining, cafés, spa experiences, and free time than from packing multiple distant destinations into one day.', 659),
  ('tbilisi', 34, 'destination-scoring', 'DESTINATION SCORING', NULL, NULL, '| Factor | Score | | ------------------ | ----: | | Family | 91 | | Honeymoon | 93 | | Luxury | 86 | | Budget | 89 | | Adventure | 78 | | Culture | 98 | | Food | 97 | | Shopping | 88 | | Nightlife | 92 | | Relaxation | 88 | | Nature | 79 | | Accessibility | 82 | | Safety | 89 | | First-time visitor | 97 | | Photography | 96 |', 660),
  ('tbilisi', 35, 'final-travel-agent-verdict', 'FINAL TRAVEL AGENT VERDICT', NULL, NULL, 'Best traveler profiles: 1. Culture / heritage traveler 2. First-time international traveler 3. Honeymoon / romantic traveler 4. Food / wine traveler 5. Family traveler 6. Photography traveler 7. History traveler 8. Luxury / leisure traveler 9. Budget traveler 10. Adventure / outdoor traveler Best duration: 3–4 nights Best season: May–October May–June for pleasant weather, sightseeing, outdoor activities, and comfortable city exploration September–October for mild temperatures, cultural experiences, food, wine, and scenic day trips July–August for travelers comfortable with hotter weather and higher seasonal demand Best hotel strategy: Choose a clean, well-reviewed hotel, boutique property, heritage-style stay, or luxury hotel based on proximity to Old Tbilisi, Freedom Square, Rustaveli Avenue, Mtatsminda, public transport, restaurants, and the main purpose of the trip. Best transportation: Walking, metro, buses, taxis, private cars, guided tours, cable cars, and local transport depending on distance, budget, comfort, and itinerary. Private transport for: Must-do for first-time visitor: Don''t-do: Biggest advantage: Exceptional combination of historic Old Tbilisi, Georgian culture and heritage, distinctive architecture, traditional cuisine and wine, scenic viewpoints, sulfur baths, museums, cafés, nightlife, shopping, and convenient access to major Georgian destinations. Biggest disadvantage: Hot summer periods, occasional traffic congestion, hilly and uneven streets in historic areas, variable accessibility at older attractions, and longer travel times for mountain and regional excursions outside Tbilisi. Overall destination score: 93/100', 661),
  ('tbilisi', 36, 'data-quality', 'DATA QUALITY', NULL, NULL, 'information_completeness: 91/100 last_updated: 2026-08-17 last_verified: PARTIALLY_WEB_VERIFIED verified_by: OFFICIAL GEORGIAN NATIONAL TOURISM ADMINISTRATION_AND_TBILISI_CITY_HALL_AND_GEORGIA_TRAVEL_SOURCES sources: IMPORTANT: Prices, opening hours, ticket prices, cable-car schedules, museum timings, attraction operating conditions, accessibility, transport schedules, road conditions, weather conditions and other operational details must NOT be treated as permanently valid from this document. Tbilisi Cable Car, museums, sulfur baths, Mtatsminda attractions and other visitor facilities should be checked against the latest official information before travel. Attraction opening hours, ticket prices, public transport availability, cable-car schedules and accessibility should be sourced from structured, refreshable data. Mtskheta, Gori, Uplistsikhe, Ananuri, Gudauri, Kakheti and other regional excursions may be affected by weather, road conditions, traffic, seasonal restrictions, attraction schedules and local administrative decisions. Tbilisi travel conditions can vary significantly during summer periods, weekends, public holidays, festivals, major cultural events and peak tourism periods. Road travel times outside Tbilisi should be treated as variable because traffic, weather, road conditions, mountain routes and seasonal congestion can affect journey duration. Mountain destinations such as Gudauri and routes along the Georgian Military Highway should have current road and weather conditions verified before inclusion in an itinerary. Uplistsikhe and other archaeological or heritage attractions may have uneven terrain, stairs and exposed walking areas, so practical accessibility should be verified before travel. Accessibility must be verified separately for each hotel, attraction, transport service and activity because Tbilisi''s historic streets, hills, stairs, older buildings and surrounding nature destinations can create significant differences in practical accessibility. Weather information should be treated as a planning guide rather than a guarantee. Regional destinations such as Gori, Uplistsikhe, Mtskheta, Ananuri, Gudauri and Kakheti should not be assumed to have the same accessibility, transport availability or operating conditions as central Tbilisi. Tbilisi''s tourism infrastructure, public transport, attraction operations and visitor conditions may change seasonally or through local administrative decisions. This dataset should be refreshed regularly before production use.', 662),
  ('batumi', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Spring', NULL, 'months: March April May weather: Mild and increasingly warm, with blooming gardens, comfortable sightseeing conditions, and frequent rainfall. May is especially attractive for coastal activities as the weather becomes warmer. crowd_level: MEDIUM → HIGH price_level: MEDIUM → HIGH overall_score: 90-94 recommended: true reason: One of the best periods for Batumi, particularly for Old Batumi, Batumi Boulevard, Botanical Garden, photography, nature excursions, and comfortable city exploration. May also marks the beginning of the stronger beach season.', 663),
  ('batumi', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Summer', NULL, 'months: June July August weather: Warm to hot, humid, and generally suitable for beach and coastal activities. Summer is the busiest period, while rainfall and occasional heavy showers remain possible. crowd_level: HIGH price_level: HIGH overall_score: 87-92 recommended: true reason: Best for beach holidays, swimming, water activities, seaside walks, nightlife, and outdoor entertainment. July and August bring the highest visitor demand, so accommodation prices and crowd levels can increase.', 664),
  ('batumi', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Autumn', NULL, 'months: September October November weather: Warm and pleasant in September and October, gradually becoming cooler and wetter in November. September and October can provide excellent sea conditions and comfortable sightseeing. crowd_level: MEDIUM → LOW price_level: MEDIUM → LOW overall_score: 93-96 recommended: true reason: One of the strongest periods for Batumi, combining pleasant coastal weather with fewer crowds than peak summer. September and October are particularly good for beaches, photography, nature, wine tourism, and exploring wider Adjara.', 665),
  ('batumi', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Winter', NULL, 'months: December January February weather: Mild but frequently rainy and humid, with cool temperatures and occasional snow. Snow is rare in coastal Batumi and usually melts quickly. crowd_level: LOW → MEDIUM price_level: LOW → MEDIUM overall_score: 78-84 recommended: true reason: Suitable for travelers interested in Old Batumi, cafés, restaurants, museums, shopping, nightlife, wellness, and quieter city experiences. Winter is less suitable for a traditional beach holiday, although wider Adjara offers mountain and winter activities.', 666),
  ('batumi', 10, 'budget-strategy', 'BUDGET STRATEGY', NULL, NULL, 'Where money can be saved: Where saving money is usually NOT recommended: Travel-agent rule: A slightly more expensive but clean, well-reviewed and centrally located hotel in Batumi usually provides better total value than a cheaper property far outside the centre once daily transport, travel time, sightseeing convenience, and access to beaches, restaurants, and attractions are considered.', 667),
  ('batumi', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Family', 'family', 'Pre-booked private car / MPV or reliable airport taxi from Batumi International Airport; door-to-door service, sufficient luggage space, and convenient for children. Batumi International Airport is located very close to Batumi, and the airport lists taxi travel to the city centre at approximately 10–15 minutes. A private transfer is generally the most convenient family option.', 668),
  ('batumi', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Honeymoon', 'honeymoon', 'Pre-booked private car with direct hotel drop-off; comfortable and convenient for couples arriving at Batumi International Airport. A private transfer is especially suitable for couples carrying luggage and wanting a relaxed start to their coastal stay. reason: Batumi International Airport is the city''s main airport and is conveniently connected to central Batumi. Municipal bus No. 10 provides a low-cost connection to the city centre, while taxis are available directly outside the terminal.', 669),
  ('batumi', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Luxury', 'luxury', 'Chauffeured premium SUV / MPV or private luxury car from Batumi International Airport; personalized pickup, luggage assistance, comfortable direct transfer, and hotel drop-off suitable for luxury hotels, beachfront properties, and premium resorts.', 670),
  ('batumi', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Budget', 'budget', 'Municipal bus No. 10 from Batumi International Airport; the bus stop is directly in front of the terminal and the journey to Batumi city centre takes approximately 20 minutes. It is the preferred option for budget travelers comfortable with public transport. Airport taxi is another practical option for travelers prioritizing convenience. Taxis are available directly outside the terminal, with the airport stating an approximately 10–15 minute drive to the city centre.', 671),
  ('batumi', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Senior', 'senior', 'Pre-booked private car or airport taxi with minimal transfers and direct hotel drop-off; prioritize comfortable seating, luggage assistance, and avoiding unnecessary changes between airport, bus, and city transport. A direct road transfer is generally preferable for seniors, particularly when arriving with luggage.', 672),
  ('batumi', 18, 'family-travel', 'FAMILY TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'child_friendly_score: 94 best_ages: Rules: For young children: Prefer: Avoid:', 673),
  ('batumi', 19, 'honeymoon-travel', 'HONEYMOON TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'honeymoon_score: 94 romance_score: 95 privacy_score: 82 luxury_score: 84 Recommended: Honeymoon itinerary should NOT contain more than: 2–3 major activities/day. Prefer: One memorable scenic, coastal, cultural, culinary, or wellness experience + free time over: Three or four attractions. Recommended hotel areas: Batumi works particularly well for a romantic honeymoon because of its Black Sea coastline, historic Old Batumi, long seaside boulevard, sunset views, distinctive architecture, cafés, restaurants, Georgian and Ajarian cuisine, nightlife, and relaxed coastal atmosphere. Batumi Boulevard, Ali & Nino, Miracle Park, Europe Square, Piazza, the Argo Cable Car, and the Botanical Garden can each provide memorable couple experiences, but they should be spread across the itinerary rather than packed into a single day. Private transport is recommended for couples who want flexibility and comfort, especially when visiting Batumi Botanical Garden, Mtirala National Park, Gonio Fortress, mountain villages, waterfalls, or other destinations outside central Batumi. Central Batumi is relatively compact and easy to explore on foot, while taxis and private cars provide greater comfort for longer excursions. Batumi is particularly well suited to couples seeking a romantic combination of seaside relaxation, scenic walks, sunsets, Georgian and Ajarian food, architecture, cafés, wellness, photography, and lively evenings. It is less suited to couples seeking a completely secluded honeymoon away from urban activity, as Batumi is an active coastal city and can become busy during the summer season.', 674),
  ('batumi', 20, 'luxury-travel', 'LUXURY TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'luxury_score: 88 Recommended: Batumi luxury travel should focus on: Luxury travelers should not simply be given more activities. Luxury in Batumi should primarily increase:', 675),
  ('batumi', 21, 'adventure', 'ADVENTURE', NULL, NULL, 'adventure_score: 82 Batumi is primarily a coastal, leisure, and cultural destination, but it also offers a strong range of outdoor and moderate-to-challenging adventure experiences in and around Adjara. Hiking, cycling, canyon and waterfall exploration, cable-car rides, kayaking/boating, nature walks, coastal exploration, and mountain excursions are among its notable outdoor activities. Adventure experiences should be interpreted as:', 676),
  ('batumi', 22, 'senior-travel', 'SENIOR TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'senior_suitability: 88 walking_intensity: LOW–MEDIUM unless carefully managed Rules:', 677),
  ('batumi', 23, 'accessibility', 'ACCESSIBILITY', NULL, NULL, 'wheelchair_accessibility: PARTIAL → GOOD IN SELECTED AREAS; varies by hotel, attraction, beach, historic area, terrain and transport public_transport_accessibility: GOOD ON MANY MUNICIPAL BUS ROUTES; Batumi''s modern municipal buses are adapted for people with disabilities, although accessibility should still be confirmed for the specific route and stop hotel_accessibility: MUST_BE_VERIFIED_PER_HOTEL attraction_accessibility: MUST_BE_VERIFIED_PER_ATTRACTION Rule: Never infer accessibility from Batumi''s overall accessibility. Each hotel and attraction must carry its own accessibility data. Additional notes:', 678),
  ('batumi', 24, 'food', 'FOOD', NULL, NULL, 'Batumi is particularly strong for: Batumi''s food identity is strongly connected with Adjara''s combination of Black Sea and mountain culinary traditions, with fish, dairy products, vegetables, meat, corn-based dishes, local cheeses, wine and distinctive Ajarian recipes playing an important role. Food experiences: Family: Prioritize clean, family-friendly Georgian and Ajarian restaurants with vegetarian options, familiar dishes, mild food choices, khachapuri, soups, grilled dishes, seafood options, bakeries, and flexible menus. Honeymoon: A romantic seaside restaurant, traditional Ajarian restaurant, wine-focused dinner, or scenic Old Batumi dining experience is recommended, with time for a relaxed evening along the Batumi Boulevard after sightseeing. Luxury: Premium Georgian and Ajarian restaurants, seafood dining, wine-pairing dinners, private culinary experiences, curated wine tastings, boutique restaurants, chef-led experiences, and premium seaside dining can be included. Batumi offers a growing premium food and hospitality scene alongside its traditional cuisine. Budget: Mix local Georgian restaurants, bakeries, casual khachapuri restaurants, cafés, food markets, and traditional eateries for affordable meals. Adjarian khachapuri, mchadi, lobio, soups, bakery foods, and other local dishes can provide good-value dining while experiencing Batumi''s regional cuisine.', 679),
  ('batumi', 25, 'shopping', 'SHOPPING', NULL, NULL, 'Strong categories: Luxury shopping: Prefer established wine boutiques, gourmet shops, artisan studios, designer boutiques, specialty food stores, and curated Georgian craft outlets around Old Batumi, Europe Square, Batumi Boulevard, and major shopping centres for premium Georgian wine, chacha, tea, jewellery, ceramics, artwork, designer products, and locally produced gourmet goods. Budget: Prefer: Batumi is particularly known for Ajarian tea, Georgian wine, chacha, local honey, churchkhela, spices, dried fruits, handmade crafts, ceramics, textiles, jewellery, artwork, and regional food products. Adjara''s tea-growing tradition also makes locally produced tea a distinctive souvenir category. Travel-agent rule: Prioritize authentic Georgian and Ajarian products over generic tourist merchandise. For wine, tea, honey, spices, churchkhela, ceramics, jewellery, handicrafts, and other consumables, compare quality and provenance before purchasing and prefer established producers, specialist shops, artisan workshops, or reputable markets where authenticity and product quality are easier to verify.', 680),
  ('batumi', 26, 'nightlife', 'NIGHTLIFE', NULL, NULL, 'nightlife_level: 80 Suitable for: Best areas: Not a primary requirement for: Evening activities are better suited to: Honeymoon travelers should generally prefer: Romantic Batumi Boulevard / Black Sea evening over: Late-night club itinerary unless nightlife is explicitly requested. For couples seeking a more atmospheric evening, prioritize a seaside dinner, Georgian wine experience, Batumi Boulevard sunset walk, Piazza Square, live-music venue, rooftop restaurant, cozy café, or elegant cocktail bar rather than building the itinerary entirely around late-night partying. Travel-agent rule: Position Batumi as a destination with a strong and varied coastal nightlife scene rather than a quiet-only evening destination. Its nightlife appeal combines Georgian and Ajarian restaurants, wine bars, cafés, beachfront venues, rooftop bars, live music, casinos, cocktail bars, and late-evening social areas, particularly around Old Batumi, Piazza, Europe Square, Batumi Boulevard, and the central waterfront.', 681),
  ('batumi', 28, 'sample-itinerary-patterns', 'SAMPLE ITINERARY PATTERNS', '3 NIGHTS', NULL, '### Day 1 Arrival at Batumi International Airport → Airport transfer to Batumi city → Hotel check-in → Batumi Boulevard → Europe Square → Piazza Square → Evening walk → Georgian / Adjara dinner → Hotel ### Day 2 Morning: Batumi Boulevard → Alphabet Tower → Ali & Nino Statue → Miracle Park → Batumi Old Town Afternoon: Batumi Botanical Garden → Scenic Black Sea viewpoints → Return to Batumi city Evening: Piazza Square → Old Town cafés / restaurants → Batumi nightlife or relaxed evening → Hotel ### Day 3 Morning: Gonio Fortress → Gonio / Kvariati coastal area Afternoon: Batumi Cable Car → Anuria Mountain viewpoints → Panoramic Batumi and Black Sea views Evening: Europe Square → Batumi Boulevard sunset → Georgian / Adjara dinner → Hotel ### Day 4 Breakfast → Hotel checkout → Airport transfer → Batumi International Airport → Departure', 682),
  ('batumi', 29, 'four-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'FOUR-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 1', NULL, 'Arrival at Tbilisi International Airport → Private transfer to Tbilisi → Romantic hotel check-in → Relax and enjoy the hotel → Evening walk through Old Tbilisi → Romantic Georgian dinner → Overnight at Tbilisi', 683),
  ('batumi', 29, 'four-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'FOUR-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 2', NULL, 'Morning: Private Tbilisi sightseeing → Freedom Square → Rustaveli Avenue → Old Tbilisi → Meidan Square → Abanotubani Afternoon: Private lunch → Sioni Cathedral → Metekhi Church → Rike Park → Bridge of Peace Evening: Cable car to Narikala Fortress → Panoramic Tbilisi views → Romantic dinner', 684),
  ('batumi', 29, 'four-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'FOUR-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 3', NULL, 'Breakfast → Private excursion from Tbilisi to Mtskheta → Jvari Monastery → Scenic views over the Aragvi and Mtkvari rivers → Svetitskhoveli Cathedral → Explore historic Mtskheta Afternoon: Private Georgian lunch → Return to Tbilisi → Hotel relaxation Evening: Mtatsminda Funicular → Panoramic sunset views → Special honeymoon dinner', 685),
  ('batumi', 29, 'four-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'FOUR-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 4', NULL, 'Breakfast → Private excursion from Tbilisi towards Ananuri → Ananuri Fortress → Zhinvali Reservoir viewpoint → Scenic Georgian Military Road → Gudauri Afternoon: Private lunch → Mountain scenery and couple photography → Relaxed return journey to Tbilisi Evening: Free time → Romantic café / wine experience → Special Georgian dinner → Overnight at Tbilisi', 686),
  ('batumi', 29, 'four-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'FOUR-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 5', NULL, 'Breakfast → Leisure morning → Hotel checkout → Private transfer to Tbilisi International Airport → Departure', 687),
  ('batumi', 30, 'four-nights-family-pattern', 'FOUR-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 1', NULL, 'Arrival at Tbilisi International Airport → Private family transfer to Tbilisi → Hotel check-in → Rest and refresh Evening: → Easy walk around Freedom Square → Bridge of Peace → Rike Park → Family-friendly dinner → Overnight at Tbilisi', 688),
  ('batumi', 30, 'four-nights-family-pattern', 'FOUR-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 2', NULL, 'Morning: Private Tbilisi sightseeing → Old Tbilisi → Meidan Square → Sioni Cathedral → Abanotubani Afternoon: Family lunch → Tbilisi Cable Car → Narikala Fortress → Mother of Georgia viewpoint Evening: → Relaxed café / dessert experience → Dinner → Overnight at Tbilisi', 689),
  ('batumi', 30, 'four-nights-family-pattern', 'FOUR-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 3', NULL, 'Breakfast → Private day trip to Mtskheta → Jvari Monastery → Scenic viewpoints → Svetitskhoveli Cathedral → Explore historic Mtskheta Afternoon: → Family lunch → Return to Tbilisi → Hotel rest Evening: → Mtatsminda Funicular → Mtatsminda Park → Family leisure time → Dinner → Overnight at Tbilisi', 690),
  ('batumi', 30, 'four-nights-family-pattern', 'FOUR-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 4', NULL, 'Breakfast → Private excursion towards Ananuri → Ananuri Fortress → Zhinvali Reservoir → Scenic Georgian Military Road → Gudauri Afternoon: → Family lunch → Mountain scenery and photography → Return to Tbilisi Evening: → Free time → Family dinner → Overnight at Tbilisi', 691),
  ('batumi', 30, 'four-nights-family-pattern', 'FOUR-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 5', NULL, 'Breakfast → Hotel checkout → Free time depending on flight schedule → Private transfer to Tbilisi International Airport → Departure', 692),
  ('batumi', 31, 'four-nights-luxury-pattern', 'FOUR-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 1', NULL, 'Arrival at Tbilisi International Airport → Premium private airport transfer → Luxury hotel check-in → Welcome drink and leisure time → Relax at the hotel Evening: → Private Old Tbilisi walk → Bridge of Peace → Rike Park → Premium Georgian dinner → Overnight at Tbilisi', 693),
  ('batumi', 31, 'four-nights-luxury-pattern', 'FOUR-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 2', NULL, 'Morning: Private chauffeur-driven Tbilisi sightseeing → Freedom Square → Rustaveli Avenue → Old Tbilisi → Sioni Cathedral → Abanotubani Afternoon: → Premium Georgian lunch → Private cable-car ride to Narikala Fortress → Mother of Georgia → Tbilisi Botanical Garden Evening: → Mtatsminda Funicular → Panoramic sunset views over Tbilisi → Fine-dining experience → Overnight at Tbilisi', 694),
  ('batumi', 31, 'four-nights-luxury-pattern', 'FOUR-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 3', NULL, 'Breakfast → Private chauffeur-driven excursion to Mtskheta → Jvari Monastery → Panoramic views → Svetitskhoveli Cathedral → Private guided heritage experience Afternoon: → Premium Georgian lunch → Continue towards Ananuri Fortress → Zhinvali Reservoir → Scenic Georgian Military Road Evening: → Return to Tbilisi → Luxury hotel relaxation → Private dinner → Overnight at Tbilisi', 695),
  ('batumi', 31, 'four-nights-luxury-pattern', 'FOUR-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 4', NULL, 'Breakfast → Private excursion to Kakheti → Scenic vineyard landscapes → Premium winery experience → Private wine tasting → Traditional Georgian cultural experience Afternoon: → Gourmet Georgian lunch at a selected winery → Leisurely countryside experience → Return to Tbilisi Evening: → Spa / wellness experience → Premium dinner → Relaxed evening at the hotel → Overnight at Tbilisi', 696),
  ('batumi', 31, 'four-nights-luxury-pattern', 'FOUR-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 5', NULL, 'Breakfast → Luxury hotel checkout → Private airport transfer → Tbilisi International Airport → Departure', 697),
  ('batumi', 32, 'travel-agent-insights', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS', 'What inexperienced planners often do wrong', NULL, '', 698),
  ('batumi', 32, 'travel-agent-insights', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS', 'What an experienced planner does differently', NULL, '', 699),
  ('batumi', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', NULL, NULL, 'IF: trip_length <= 2 nights THEN: do not recommend Mtirala National Park + waterfalls, Batumi Botanical Garden + mountain excursions, or multiple Adjara day trips as default additions. Reason: Additional road travel can make a short Batumi stay unnecessarily rushed. IF: trip_type == HONEYMOON THEN: increase_romance_weight by 20% increase_privacy_weight by 15% increase_free_time_weight by 25% decrease_activity_density by 20% Reason: The objective is a relaxed coastal experience with beach time, scenic walks, sunsets, Georgian dining, cafés, and quality couple time rather than maximum sightseeing. IF: traveler_type == FAMILY AND: children_age <= 6 THEN: reduce_travel_intensity_target by 20% increase_downtime by 20% prefer_short_sightseeing + BEACH + PARKS + BOULEVARD + FAMILY_FRIENDLY_EXPERIENCES Reason: Young children can find long walking routes, crowded areas, extended road journeys, and excessive sightseeing tiring. IF: hotel_is_far_from_CENTRAL_BATUMI AND: hotel_saving < additional_transport_cost + value_of_lost_time THEN: prefer_hotel_near_CENTRAL_BATUMI Reason: A cheaper hotel may not provide better total value once daily taxi costs, traffic, travel time, and sightseeing convenience are considered. IF: trip_length <= 4 nights THEN: prefer_one_hotel Reason: Hotel changes consume valuable short-trip time and reduce time available for sightseeing, beach relaxation, dining, shopping, and leisure. IF: trip_length >= 4 nights AND: traveler_interest == NATURE_AND_SCENIC_EXPLORATION THEN: consider_BATUMI + ADJARA_DESTINATIONS Reason: A longer stay makes it practical to combine Batumi''s core attractions with the Botanical Garden, Gonio, Mtirala National Park, waterfalls, and other Adjara experiences. IF: traveler_type == LUXURY THEN: prefer_private_transfer AND: prefer_high_service_hotel AND: prefer_private_or_personalized_experiences Reason: Luxury value in Batumi is primarily created through premium accommodation, private transfers, personalized tours, fine dining, spa experiences, seaside experiences, and convenient sightseeing. IF: traveler_type == BUDGET THEN: prefer_central_hotel_location AND: use_city_bus_or_local_transport_where_practical AND: mix_free_and_paid_attractions Reason: Maintain sightseeing quality while reducing unnecessary transportation and accommodation costs. IF: traveler_interest == CULTURE_AND_RELAXATION THEN: prefer_OLD_BATUMI AND: group_OLD_BATUMI + EUROPE_SQUARE + BATUMI_BOULEVARD + SEASIDE_EXPERIENCES Reason: Central Batumi provides convenient access to historic streets, architecture, restaurants, cafés, parks, the waterfront, and relaxed city experiences. IF: traveler_interest == SCENIC_AND_PHOTOGRAPHY THEN: prefer_BATUMI_BOULEVARD_AND_ALI_NINO AND: group_SEA_VIEWS + OLD_BATUMI + MIRACLE_PARK + PANORAMIC_CITYSCAPES Reason: Batumi Boulevard, the Black Sea waterfront, Ali & Nino, Miracle Park, and the surrounding cityscape provide strong sunset and photography opportunities. IF: traveler_interest == ADVENTURE_AND_OUTDOORS THEN: prefer_BATUMI_SURROUNDINGS AND: group_HIKING + WATERFALLS + MOUNTAIN_VIEWS + NATURE_EXPERIENCES Reason: The wider Adjara region provides opportunities for hiking, waterfalls, forest experiences, scenic mountain roads, and outdoor activities. IF: traveler_interest == HISTORY_AND_CULTURE THEN: prefer_OLD_BATUMI AND: group_EUROPE_SQUARE + GONIO_FORTRESS + BATUMI_ARCHITECTURE + ADJARAN_CULTURAL_EXPERIENCES Reason: These experiences showcase Batumi''s historic architecture, ancient heritage, multicultural character, and Adjara''s cultural identity. IF: traveler_interest == HISTORY + DAY_TRIPS THEN: consider_GONIO_FORTRESS + ADJARA_HISTORIC_SITES AND: group_ANCIENT_SITES + FORTRESS + CULTURAL_EXPERIENCES + REGIONAL_LANDSCAPES Reason: Gonio and other historic sites around Adjara provide opportunities to experience the region''s ancient, Georgian, and multicultural heritage beyond central Batumi. IF: trip_length >= 4 nights AND: traveler_interest == MOUNTAINS + SCENIC_EXPLORATION THEN: consider_split_itinerary BETWEEN: CENTRAL_BATUMI + MTIRALA_OR_ADJARA_MOUNTAIN_EXCURSIONS Reason: Separating central Batumi sightseeing from longer mountain excursions reduces unnecessary backtracking and keeps the itinerary comfortable. IF: traveler_interest == FOOD_AND_GASTRONOMY THEN: consider_ADJARAN_CUISINE AND: group_ADJARULI_KHACHAPURI + GEORGIAN_FOOD + LOCAL_MARKETS + WINE_EXPERIENCES Reason: Batumi provides strong access to Georgian and Adjara cuisine, seafood, cafés, restaurants, wine experiences, and regional culinary traditions. IF: weather == HEAVY_RAIN OR: visibility == LOW THEN: reduce_MOUNTAIN_AND_REMOTE_OUTDOOR_ACTIVITIES AND: prefer_CENTRAL_BATUMI AND: increase_FLEXIBLE_INDOOR_OR_HOTEL_TIME Reason: Heavy rain, fog, and poor visibility can reduce the value and practicality of beaches, viewpoints, mountain excursions, hiking, and longer road journeys. IF: traveler_interest == ROMANTIC_RELAXATION THEN: prefer_BATUMI_BOULEVARD + OLD_BATUMI + SEASIDE_SUNSETS AND: decrease_activity_density_by_20_percent Reason: Couples generally benefit more from seaside walks, sunsets, cafés, Georgian dining, spa experiences, beach time, and free time than from packing multiple distant destinations into one day.', 700),
  ('batumi', 34, 'destination-scoring', 'DESTINATION SCORING', NULL, NULL, '| Factor | Score | | ------------------ | ----: | | Family | 94 | | Honeymoon | 95 | | Luxury | 88 | | Budget | 90 | | Adventure | 86 | | Culture | 91 | | Food | 94 | | Shopping | 84 | | Nightlife | 91 | | Relaxation | 96 | | Nature | 94 | | Accessibility | 84 | | Safety | 89 | | First-time visitor | 96 | | Photography | 98 |', 701),
  ('batumi', 35, 'final-travel-agent-verdict', 'FINAL TRAVEL AGENT VERDICT', NULL, NULL, 'Best traveler profiles: 1. Beach / leisure traveler 2. Honeymoon / romantic traveler 3. Family traveler 4. Photography traveler 5. Nature / outdoor traveler 6. Food / gastronomy traveler 7. First-time international traveler 8. Culture / heritage traveler 9. Luxury traveler 10. Budget traveler Best duration: 3–4 nights Best season: May–October May–June for pleasant temperatures, beach time, sightseeing, outdoor activities, and comfortable coastal exploration July–August for beach holidays, nightlife, outdoor activities, and travelers comfortable with hotter, more humid weather and higher seasonal demand September–October for milder temperatures, fewer crowds, scenic experiences, food, culture, and comfortable sightseeing Best hotel strategy: Choose a clean, well-reviewed hotel, boutique property, seaside resort, or luxury hotel based on proximity to Batumi Boulevard, Old Batumi, Europe Square, the waterfront, restaurants, public transport, and the main purpose of the trip. Best transportation: Walking, city buses, taxis, private cars, guided tours, and local transport depending on distance, budget, comfort, and itinerary. Private transport for: Must-do for first-time visitor: Don''t-do: Biggest advantage: Exceptional combination of Black Sea beaches, Batumi Boulevard, subtropical nature, distinctive architecture, Georgian and Adjara cuisine, nightlife, family attractions, scenic sunsets, cultural experiences, and convenient access to the wider Adjara region. Biggest disadvantage: High summer humidity and rainfall, increased seasonal demand, occasional traffic congestion, uneven surfaces in some historic areas, and longer travel times for mountain, nature, and regional excursions outside central Batumi. Overall destination score: 94/100', 702),
  ('batumi', 36, 'data-quality', 'DATA QUALITY', NULL, NULL, 'information_completeness: 93/100 last_updated: 2026-08-18 last_verified: PARTIALLY_WEB_VERIFIED verified_by: OFFICIAL ADJARA TOURISM DEPARTMENT / VISIT BATUMI AND GEORGIA TRAVEL SOURCES sources: IMPORTANT: Prices, opening hours, ticket prices, cable-car schedules, museum timings, attraction operating conditions, accessibility, transport schedules, road conditions, weather conditions and other operational details must NOT be treated as permanently valid from this document. Batumi Boulevard, Argo Cable Car, Batumi Botanical Garden, museums, Dolphinarium, entertainment facilities and other visitor attractions should be checked against the latest official information before travel. Visit Batumi provides current tourism information, attraction information and visitor resources. Attraction opening hours, ticket prices, public transport availability, cable-car schedules and accessibility should be sourced from structured, refreshable data. Batumi municipal buses operate as a major public-transport option and include vehicles adapted for disabled passengers, but accessibility should still be verified for the specific route and journey. Batumi International Airport, railway connections, road transport and regional transfers may be affected by seasonal schedules, traffic, weather and operational changes. Current airport and transport information should therefore be verified before travel. Batumi and wider Adjara contain a combination of coastal, urban, forest, mountain and protected-area environments. Mountain excursions, hiking routes, waterfalls, canyoning, rafting and other outdoor activities can be affected by rainfall, visibility, road conditions, river conditions and seasonal restrictions. Mtirala National Park, Batumi Botanical Garden and other nature destinations may contain uneven terrain, slopes, stairs, natural paths and changing outdoor conditions, so practical accessibility should be verified before travel. Accessibility must be verified separately for each hotel, attraction, transport service and activity because Batumi''s historic areas, beaches, parks, natural attractions and surrounding mountain destinations can have significantly different accessibility conditions. Central Batumi has comparatively useful accessibility infrastructure, including accessible municipal buses, but travelers requiring step-free access should verify the exact route, vehicle, accommodation and attraction before relying on it. Taxis or private vehicles can provide greater flexibility for travelers with mobility requirements, especially when visiting attractions outside central Batumi or destinations in mountainous Adjara. Weather information should be treated as a planning guide rather than a guarantee. Batumi''s coastal climate can bring substantial rainfall, while mountain areas can experience different conditions from the city. Regional destinations such as Mtirala, Gonio, waterfalls, mountain villages, protected areas and other Adjara excursions should not be assumed to have the same accessibility, transport availability or operating conditions as central Batumi. Batumi''s tourism infrastructure, public transport, attraction operations, visitor facilities and event schedules may change seasonally or through local administrative decisions. Tourist Information Centres in Batumi and across Adjara provide visitor information, maps, attraction information, transport information and regional tour assistance, making them useful sources for current local conditions. The official Visit Batumi portal also provides current destination information covering nature, culture, gastronomy, accommodation, entertainment, transport and seasonal tourism activities. This dataset should be refreshed regularly before production use.', 703),
  ('gori', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Spring', NULL, 'months: March April May weather: Mild to warm and increasingly comfortable for sightseeing, with spring greenery and generally favorable conditions for exploring Gori, Gori Fortress, museums, historic sites, and the surrounding Shida Kartli countryside. Rainfall can occur, particularly during spring transition periods. crowd_level: LOW → MEDIUM price_level: LOW → MEDIUM overall_score: 91-94 recommended: true reason: One of the best periods for Gori, particularly for history, culture, archaeology, photography, walking, and regional excursions. Spring offers comfortable conditions for Gori Fortress and nearby Uplistsikhe, while the countryside becomes greener. Georgia Travel identifies spring as an ideal period for cultural and historical travel, with generally warm conditions but occasional rain.', 704),
  ('gori', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Summer', NULL, 'months: June July August weather: Warm to hot and generally suitable for sightseeing and outdoor excursions. Shida Kartli can experience substantial summer heat, with temperatures potentially reaching around 40°C in the hottest conditions. Rain and thunderstorms can still occur. crowd_level: MEDIUM price_level: MEDIUM overall_score: 84-89 recommended: true reason: Good for travelers combining Gori''s historical attractions with countryside exploration and longer regional excursions. Early mornings and late afternoons are preferable for walking and fortress visits during hotter periods. Summer is less comfortable than spring or autumn for intensive outdoor sightseeing because Shida Kartli can become very hot.', 705),
  ('gori', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Autumn', NULL, 'months: September October November weather: Warm and generally comfortable in September and October, gradually becoming cooler toward November. The countryside develops autumn colors, while conditions remain favorable for historical sightseeing, photography, food, wine, and regional excursions. crowd_level: LOW → MEDIUM price_level: LOW → MEDIUM overall_score: 94-96 recommended: true reason: One of the strongest periods for Gori, especially for cultural and historical sightseeing, photography, countryside exploration, food and wine experiences, and visits to nearby heritage sites. Georgia Travel identifies autumn as one of the preferred periods for cultural and historical tours because temperatures are generally warm and comfortable, with occasional wind and rain.', 706),
  ('gori', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Winter', NULL, 'months: December January February weather: Cool to cold, with average winter temperatures in Shida Kartli around 1°C and occasional frost or snow possible. Daylight hours are shorter and outdoor sightseeing can feel less comfortable during cold or wet periods. crowd_level: LOW price_level: LOW → MEDIUM overall_score: 78-84 recommended: true reason: Suitable for travelers primarily interested in Gori''s museums, historical attractions, local food, and a quieter city experience. Winter is less ideal for extended outdoor sightseeing, countryside walks, and archaeological sites when conditions are cold, wet, icy, or snowy. Shida Kartli has a relatively dry continental-influenced climate compared with Georgia''s wetter western regions, but winter conditions should still be checked before travel.', 707),
  ('gori', 10, 'budget-strategy', 'BUDGET STRATEGY', NULL, NULL, 'Where money can be saved: Where saving money is usually NOT recommended: Travel-agent rule: A slightly more expensive but clean, well-reviewed and reasonably central hotel or guesthouse in Gori usually provides better total value than a cheaper property outside the town once local transport costs, travel time, sightseeing convenience, and access to restaurants, museums, and historical attractions are considered. Gori is compact enough that a well-located stay can significantly reduce the need for taxis and make a short cultural or historical visit more efficient.', 708),
  ('gori', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Family', 'family', 'Pre-booked private car / MPV or reliable airport taxi from Tbilisi International Airport; door-to-door service, sufficient luggage space, and convenient for children. Gori does not have a commercial passenger airport of its own. Tbilisi International Airport is the nearest major airport, approximately 100 km from Gori by road, with an average driving time of around 1 hour 20 minutes according to Gori Municipality. A private transfer is generally the most convenient family option, particularly when arriving with children and luggage, because it avoids multiple changes between airport, Tbilisi, and Gori.', 709),
  ('gori', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Honeymoon', 'honeymoon', 'Pre-booked private car with direct hotel drop-off from Tbilisi International Airport; comfortable and convenient for couples arriving in Georgia and proceeding directly to Gori. A private transfer is especially suitable for couples carrying luggage and wanting a relaxed, uninterrupted journey. reason: Gori does not have its own commercial international airport. Tbilisi International Airport is the nearest major airport and is approximately 100 km from Gori by road. Direct private road transfer is therefore the simplest arrival option for travelers prioritizing comfort and convenience.', 710),
  ('gori', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Luxury', 'luxury', 'Chauffeured premium SUV / MPV or private luxury car from Tbilisi International Airport; personalized pickup, luggage assistance, comfortable direct transfer, and hotel drop-off suitable for boutique hotels, premium properties, and private cultural itineraries in Gori and surrounding Shida Kartli. A private chauffeur is particularly appropriate because the airport journey is a substantial intercity transfer rather than a short urban airport connection.', 711),
  ('gori', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Budget', 'budget', 'Public transport combination from Tbilisi International Airport via Tbilisi; budget travelers can use the municipal #337 airport bus to reach Tbilisi and then continue toward Gori by train or minibus. There is no direct airport-to-Gori municipal bus connection. The airport''s #337 municipal bus is a low-cost option between Tbilisi International Airport and the city. From Tbilisi, travelers can continue toward Gori using Georgian Railway services or a minibus from the Didube area. The combined journey requires additional transfers and generally takes longer than a direct car. A taxi or pre-booked private transfer is another practical option for travelers prioritizing convenience. The road distance from Gori to Tbilisi Airport is approximately 98–100 km, with driving time commonly around 1 hour 15 minutes to 1 hour 20 minutes, depending on traffic and road conditions.', 712),
  ('gori', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Senior', 'senior', 'Pre-booked private car or reliable airport taxi with minimal transfers and direct hotel drop-off from Tbilisi International Airport; prioritize comfortable seating, luggage assistance, and avoiding unnecessary changes between airport bus, Tbilisi transport, train, or minibus. A direct road transfer is generally preferable for seniors because Gori is approximately 100 km from Tbilisi International Airport and public-transport alternatives require one or more transfers.', 713),
  ('gori', 18, 'family-travel', 'FAMILY TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'child_friendly_score: 86 best_ages: Rules: For young children: Prefer: Avoid:', 714),
  ('gori', 19, 'honeymoon-travel', 'HONEYMOON TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'honeymoon_score: 72 romance_score: 74 privacy_score: 70 luxury_score: 58 Recommended: Honeymoon itinerary should NOT contain more than: 2–3 major activities/day. Prefer: One memorable historical, scenic, cultural, culinary, or countryside experience + free time over: Three or four attractions. Recommended hotel areas: Gori works better as a short cultural and historical couple experience than as a traditional luxury honeymoon destination. The city combines Gori Fortress, historical museums, Soviet-era history, nearby Uplistsikhe, churches, countryside landscapes, and local Georgian dining. Gori Fortress provides elevated views over the city, while Uplistsikhe offers a distinctive ancient rock-cut landscape approximately 10 km from Gori. For couples interested in history, archaeology, photography, and authentic Georgian experiences, Gori can provide a memorable stop within a wider Georgia honeymoon itinerary. The city is particularly suitable when combined with other destinations rather than used as the sole honeymoon base. A visit to the Stalin Museum can be included for travelers interested in 20th-century history, but it should be treated as a historical and politically complex experience rather than a romantic attraction. The official Georgia Travel source notes that the museum includes extensive material about Stalin''s life and Soviet-era history, including a section concerning repression. Private transport is recommended for couples who want greater flexibility, particularly when combining Gori with Uplistsikhe, Ateni Sioni, Gorisjvari, Tsedisi Fortress, or wider Shida Kartli sightseeing. Uplistsikhe is close to Gori, while nearby heritage sites can require additional road travel. Gori is particularly well suited to couples seeking a romantic combination of Georgian history, archaeology, scenic viewpoints, countryside, photography, local food, and a quieter cultural atmosphere. It is less suited to couples seeking beaches, extensive luxury resorts, major nightlife, spa-focused holidays, or a highly secluded luxury honeymoon.', 715),
  ('gori', 20, 'luxury-travel', 'LUXURY TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'luxury_score: 58 Recommended: Gori luxury travel should focus on: Luxury travelers should not simply be given more activities. Luxury in Gori should primarily increase: Gori has a more limited luxury-tourism ecosystem than Batumi or Tbilisi, so luxury positioning should emphasize personalized service, private transportation, high-quality accommodation, private guiding, Georgian cuisine, wine, and curated cultural experiences rather than large luxury-resort facilities. The strongest premium experiences are generally created by combining Gori''s historical attractions with private excursions into the surrounding Shida Kartli countryside. Uplistsikhe, Ateni Valley, Ateni Sioni Church, Gori Fortress, and other regional heritage sites can be incorporated into a customized private itinerary. For travelers seeking a high-end Georgia journey, Gori works particularly well as a premium cultural stop within a broader itinerary connecting Tbilisi, Mtskheta, Gori, Uplistsikhe, and other Georgian destinations rather than as a standalone luxury-resort destination.', 716),
  ('gori', 21, 'adventure', 'ADVENTURE', NULL, NULL, 'adventure_score: 78 Gori is primarily a historical, cultural, and heritage destination, but its location in Shida Kartli provides access to a strong range of outdoor and moderate adventure experiences in the surrounding valleys, hills, forests, waterfalls, lakes, and archaeological landscapes. The strongest adventure opportunities are generally found outside central Gori, particularly in the Ateni Valley and wider Shida Kartli region. Adventure experiences should be interpreted as: Travel-agent interpretation:', 717),
  ('gori', 22, 'senior-travel', 'SENIOR TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'senior_suitability: 82 walking_intensity: LOW–MEDIUM within central Gori MEDIUM for selected heritage sites and excursions Rules:', 718),
  ('gori', 23, 'accessibility', 'ACCESSIBILITY', NULL, NULL, 'wheelchair_accessibility: PARTIAL → GOOD IN SELECTED AREAS; varies by hotel, museum, historic site, terrain and transport public_transport_accessibility: LIMITED → VARIABLE; accessibility should be confirmed for the specific vehicle, route, stop and transfer hotel_accessibility: MUST_BE_VERIFIED_PER_HOTEL attraction_accessibility: MUST_BE_VERIFIED_PER_ATTRACTION Rule: Never infer accessibility from Gori''s overall accessibility. Each hotel and attraction must carry its own accessibility data. Additional notes:', 719),
  ('gori', 24, 'food', 'FOOD', NULL, NULL, 'Gori is particularly strong for: Gori''s food identity is strongly connected with Shida Kartli''s agricultural traditions and central-Georgian cuisine, combining hearty meat dishes, vegetarian recipes, soups, bread, cheese, seasonal fruits and vegetables, and traditional Georgian wine. The region is particularly known for its diverse vegetarian cuisine and distinctive shechamandi soups, while Goruli katleti is one of the city''s notable local specialties. Shida Kartli is also an important wine-producing region, particularly associated with Chinuri, Goruli Mtsvane and Shavkapito. Food experiences: Family: Prioritize clean, family-friendly Georgian and Shida Kartli restaurants with vegetarian options, familiar dishes, mild food choices, khachapuri, khinkali, soups, grilled dishes, bread, cheese and flexible menus. Gori has a good range of traditional Georgian restaurants and casual cafés suitable for relaxed family dining. Honeymoon: A cozy traditional Georgian restaurant, wine-focused dinner, family-style Georgian meal, or relaxed café experience can be included. Gori is better suited to an intimate cultural dining experience than a luxury romantic dining scene, so combine dinner with an evening walk around central Gori or the historic area. Luxury: Premium Georgian restaurants, curated Georgian wine tastings, private culinary experiences, boutique dining, chef-led meals and high-quality traditional Georgian cuisine can be included. However, Gori''s dining scene is comparatively modest rather than a major fine-dining destination, so luxury travellers may find a stronger premium culinary selection in Tbilisi. Budget: Mix local Georgian restaurants, traditional family eateries, bakeries, cafés, market-area food and casual khinkali or khachapuri restaurants for affordable meals. Khinkali, khachapuri, lobio, soups, mchadi, bread, seasonal vegetables and other traditional Georgian dishes can provide good-value dining while experiencing Gori and Shida Kartli''s regional cuisine.', 720),
  ('gori', 25, 'shopping', 'SHOPPING', NULL, NULL, 'Strong categories: Gori is better suited to local food shopping, regional wine, traditional crafts and everyday Georgian market experiences than to large-scale luxury or international-brand shopping. Shida Kartli''s agricultural character makes local produce, churchkhela, dried fruits, nuts, cheese, spices and homemade products particularly relevant purchases. Gori also has a genuine local ceramics tradition, with handmade pottery produced through longstanding family techniques. Luxury shopping: Prefer established wine cellars, wineries, specialist wine shops, artisan workshops and curated Georgian craft outlets for premium Shida Kartli wines, handmade ceramics, traditional crafts, jewellery and high-quality regional food products. Wine cellars around Gori and the wider municipality can offer tastings and direct purchases, including Chinuri and Shavkapito. Budget: Prefer: Gori''s markets are particularly useful for everyday Georgian products, fresh produce, cheese, nuts, dried fruits, churchkhela, spices, clothing and household goods. The 21st Century Shopping Centre is a more traditional local bazaar experience, while central Gori provides smaller shops and souvenir outlets. Gori is particularly known as a place to experience Shida Kartli''s agricultural and wine-producing character rather than as a major shopping destination. Regional wines such as Chinuri, Goruli Mtsvane and Shavkapito are among the most distinctive purchases, while churchkhela, dried fruits, nuts, cheese, spices, honey and handmade ceramics make practical regional souvenirs. Travel-agent rule: Prioritize authentic Georgian and Shida Kartli products over generic tourist merchandise. For wine, cheese, honey, spices, churchkhela, dried fruits, ceramics, jewellery and other regional products, compare quality and provenance before purchasing and prefer established wineries, wine cellars, specialist shops, artisan workshops or reputable local markets where authenticity and quality are easier to verify.', 721),
  ('gori', 26, 'nightlife', 'NIGHTLIFE', NULL, NULL, 'nightlife_level: 35 Suitable for: Best areas: Not a primary requirement for: Evening activities are better suited to: Gori has a relatively modest nightlife scene compared with Tbilisi or Batumi. Bars and restaurants often overlap, with Georgian wine, beer, food and casual socializing forming the main evening experience rather than large clubs or dedicated nightlife districts. Current listings show a selection of pubs, bars, cafés and restaurants in the city centre, but Gori should primarily be positioned as a cultural and historical destination with relaxed evening options. Honeymoon travelers should generally prefer: Romantic Georgian dinner + wine experience over: Late-night club itinerary unless nightlife is explicitly requested. For couples seeking a more atmospheric evening, prioritize a traditional Georgian dinner, local wine tasting, cozy café, evening walk through central Gori, Stalin Park, or a relaxed wine-cellar experience rather than building the itinerary around bars or late-night entertainment. Travel-agent rule: Position Gori as a **quiet-to-moderate evening destination with authentic local dining and wine experiences**, not as a major nightlife destination. Its evening appeal comes primarily from traditional Georgian restaurants, cafés, wine cellars, local bars, central streets, Stalin Park and relaxed social experiences. Travelers seeking extensive clubs, rooftop nightlife, casinos or late-night entertainment should generally be directed toward Tbilisi or Batumi instead.', 722),
  ('gori', 28, 'sample-itinerary-patterns', 'SAMPLE ITINERARY PATTERNS', '3 NIGHTS', NULL, '### Day 1 Arrival in Gori → Transfer from Tbilisi to Gori → Hotel check-in → Gori Fortress → Gori Old Town / central Gori → Gori Cathedral → Stalin Park → Evening Georgian dinner → Hotel ### Day 2 Morning: Stalin Museum → Stalin''s Birthplace → Stalin''s Railway Carriage → Gori Historical & Ethnographic Museum Afternoon: Uplistsikhe Cave Town → Ancient rock-hewn settlement → Rock-cut halls and tunnels → Mtkvari River viewpoints → Return to Gori Evening: Central Gori → Local café / Georgian restaurant → Relaxed evening → Hotel ### Day 3 Morning: Ateni Valley → Ateni Sioni Church → Medieval frescoes and inscriptions → Ateni vineyards → Scenic Tana Valley Afternoon: Local wine tasting / regional food experience → Rural Shida Kartli scenery → Return to Gori Evening: Gori Fortress / central Gori viewpoint → Georgian dinner → Hotel ### Day 4 Breakfast → Hotel checkout → Transfer to Tbilisi → Continue onward journey / departure', 723),
  ('gori', 29, 'four-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'FOUR-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 1', NULL, 'Arrival at Tbilisi International Airport → Private transfer to Tbilisi → Romantic hotel check-in → Relax and enjoy the hotel → Evening walk through Old Tbilisi → Romantic Georgian dinner → Overnight at Tbilisi', 724),
  ('gori', 29, 'four-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'FOUR-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 2', NULL, 'Morning: Private Tbilisi sightseeing → Freedom Square → Rustaveli Avenue → Old Tbilisi → Meidan Square → Abanotubani Afternoon: Private lunch → Sioni Cathedral → Metekhi Church → Rike Park → Bridge of Peace Evening: Cable car to Narikala Fortress → Panoramic Tbilisi views → Romantic dinner', 725),
  ('gori', 29, 'four-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'FOUR-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 3', NULL, 'Breakfast → Private excursion from Tbilisi to Mtskheta → Jvari Monastery → Scenic views over the Aragvi and Mtkvari rivers → Svetitskhoveli Cathedral → Explore historic Mtskheta Afternoon: Private Georgian lunch → Return to Tbilisi → Hotel relaxation Evening: Mtatsminda Funicular → Panoramic sunset views → Special honeymoon dinner', 726),
  ('gori', 29, 'four-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'FOUR-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 4', NULL, 'Breakfast → Private excursion from Tbilisi towards Ananuri → Ananuri Fortress → Zhinvali Reservoir viewpoint → Scenic Georgian Military Road → Gudauri Afternoon: Private lunch → Mountain scenery and couple photography → Relaxed return journey to Tbilisi Evening: Free time → Romantic café / wine experience → Special Georgian dinner → Overnight at Tbilisi', 727),
  ('gori', 29, 'four-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'FOUR-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 5', NULL, 'Breakfast → Leisure morning → Hotel checkout → Private transfer to Tbilisi International Airport → Departure', 728),
  ('gori', 30, 'four-nights-family-pattern', 'FOUR-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 1', NULL, 'Arrival at Tbilisi International Airport → Private family transfer to Tbilisi → Hotel check-in → Rest and refresh Evening: → Easy walk around Freedom Square → Bridge of Peace → Rike Park → Family-friendly dinner → Overnight at Tbilisi', 729),
  ('gori', 30, 'four-nights-family-pattern', 'FOUR-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 2', NULL, 'Morning: Private Tbilisi sightseeing → Old Tbilisi → Meidan Square → Sioni Cathedral → Abanotubani Afternoon: Family lunch → Tbilisi Cable Car → Narikala Fortress → Mother of Georgia viewpoint Evening: → Relaxed café / dessert experience → Dinner → Overnight at Tbilisi', 730),
  ('gori', 30, 'four-nights-family-pattern', 'FOUR-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 3', NULL, 'Breakfast → Private day trip to Mtskheta → Jvari Monastery → Scenic viewpoints → Svetitskhoveli Cathedral → Explore historic Mtskheta Afternoon: → Family lunch → Return to Tbilisi → Hotel rest Evening: → Mtatsminda Funicular → Mtatsminda Park → Family leisure time → Dinner → Overnight at Tbilisi', 731),
  ('gori', 30, 'four-nights-family-pattern', 'FOUR-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 4', NULL, 'Breakfast → Private excursion towards Ananuri → Ananuri Fortress → Zhinvali Reservoir → Scenic Georgian Military Road → Gudauri Afternoon: → Family lunch → Mountain scenery and photography → Return to Tbilisi Evening: → Free time → Family dinner → Overnight at Tbilisi', 732),
  ('gori', 30, 'four-nights-family-pattern', 'FOUR-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 5', NULL, 'Breakfast → Hotel checkout → Free time depending on flight schedule → Private transfer to Tbilisi International Airport → Departure', 733),
  ('gori', 31, 'four-nights-luxury-pattern', 'FOUR-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 1', NULL, 'Arrival at Tbilisi International Airport → Premium private airport transfer → Luxury hotel check-in → Welcome drink and leisure time → Relax at the hotel Evening: → Private Old Tbilisi walk → Bridge of Peace → Rike Park → Premium Georgian dinner → Overnight at Tbilisi', 734),
  ('gori', 31, 'four-nights-luxury-pattern', 'FOUR-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 2', NULL, 'Morning: Private chauffeur-driven Tbilisi sightseeing → Freedom Square → Rustaveli Avenue → Old Tbilisi → Sioni Cathedral → Abanotubani Afternoon: → Premium Georgian lunch → Private cable-car ride to Narikala Fortress → Mother of Georgia → Tbilisi Botanical Garden Evening: → Mtatsminda Funicular → Panoramic sunset views over Tbilisi → Fine-dining experience → Overnight at Tbilisi', 735),
  ('gori', 31, 'four-nights-luxury-pattern', 'FOUR-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 3', NULL, 'Breakfast → Private chauffeur-driven excursion to Mtskheta → Jvari Monastery → Panoramic views → Svetitskhoveli Cathedral → Private guided heritage experience Afternoon: → Premium Georgian lunch → Continue towards Ananuri Fortress → Zhinvali Reservoir → Scenic Georgian Military Road Evening: → Return to Tbilisi → Luxury hotel relaxation → Private dinner → Overnight at Tbilisi', 736),
  ('gori', 31, 'four-nights-luxury-pattern', 'FOUR-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 4', NULL, 'Breakfast → Private excursion to Kakheti → Scenic vineyard landscapes → Premium winery experience → Private wine tasting → Traditional Georgian cultural experience Afternoon: → Gourmet Georgian lunch at a selected winery → Leisurely countryside experience → Return to Tbilisi Evening: → Spa / wellness experience → Premium dinner → Relaxed evening at the hotel → Overnight at Tbilisi', 737),
  ('gori', 31, 'four-nights-luxury-pattern', 'FOUR-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 5', NULL, 'Breakfast → Luxury hotel checkout → Private airport transfer → Tbilisi International Airport → Departure', 738),
  ('gori', 32, 'travel-agent-insights', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS', 'What inexperienced planners often do wrong', NULL, '', 739),
  ('gori', 32, 'travel-agent-insights', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS', 'What an experienced planner does differently', NULL, '', 740),
  ('gori', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', NULL, NULL, 'IF: trip_length <= 2 nights THEN: prefer_GORI_CITY_CORE + ONE_MAJOR_EXCURSION AND: do not recommend UPLISTSIKHE + ATENI_VALLEY + WATERFALLS + MULTIPLE_RURAL_EXCURSIONS as default additions. Reason: Gori''s central attractions can be covered efficiently, but adding several surrounding excursions can make a short stay unnecessarily rushed. Uplistsikhe alone is around a 25-minute drive from central Gori, while Ateni Valley begins around 10 km from the city. IF: trip_type == HONEYMOON THEN: increase_romance_weight by 15% increase_privacy_weight by 15% increase_free_time_weight by 20% decrease_activity_density by 20% Reason: The objective is a relaxed cultural and countryside experience with scenic drives, Georgian dining, wine experiences, quiet rural landscapes, sunset viewpoints, and quality couple time rather than maximum sightseeing. IF: traveler_type == FAMILY AND: children_age <= 6 THEN: reduce_travel_intensity_target by 20% increase_downtime by 20% prefer_SHORT_CITY_SIGHTSEEING + PARKS + EASY_VIEWPOINTS + FAMILY_FRIENDLY_EXPERIENCES Reason: Young children can find long archaeological walks, uneven rocky terrain, extended road journeys, and excessive sightseeing tiring. Uplistsikhe in particular is an open-air archaeological site with rock-cut structures and uneven terrain. IF: hotel_is_far_from_CENTRAL_GORI AND: hotel_saving < additional_transport_cost + value_of_lost_time THEN: prefer_hotel_near_CENTRAL_GORI Reason: Gori''s main attractions are concentrated around the city centre, including Gori Fortress and the Stalin Museum. Staying centrally can reduce unnecessary daily transport and make short sightseeing periods more efficient. Gori Fortress is located in the heart of the city. IF: trip_length <= 4 nights THEN: prefer_one_hotel Reason: Hotel changes consume valuable short-trip time and reduce time available for Gori sightseeing, archaeological excursions, dining, wine experiences, and relaxation. IF: trip_length >= 3 nights AND: traveler_interest == NATURE_AND_SCENIC_EXPLORATION THEN: consider_GORI + ATENI_VALLEY + REGIONAL_NATURE_EXPERIENCES Reason: A longer stay makes it practical to combine Gori''s historic core with the Ateni Valley, where travelers can experience the Tana River, mountain scenery, Biisi Waterfall, hiking trails, and historic monuments. IF: traveler_type == LUXURY THEN: prefer_private_transfer AND: prefer_high_service_hotel_or_BOUTIQUE_STAY AND: prefer_private_or_personALIZED_EXPERIENCES Reason: Luxury value around Gori is better created through private transfers, boutique accommodation, curated wine experiences, private countryside excursions, Georgian culinary experiences, and personalized sightseeing rather than a large luxury-shopping or nightlife scene. Ateni wineries can offer wine tasting, Georgian cuisine, lunch/dinner and culinary experiences. IF: traveler_type == BUDGET THEN: prefer_CENTRAL_HOTEL_LOCATION AND: use_WALKING + LOCAL_TRANSPORT_WHERE_PRACTICAL AND: mix_FREE_AND_PAID_ATTRACTIONS Reason: Gori''s central attractions can be combined efficiently on foot, while paid transport can be reserved for Uplistsikhe, Ateni Valley and more distant rural sites. IF: traveler_interest == CULTURE_AND_RELAXATION THEN: prefer_CENTRAL_GORI AND: group_GORI_FORTRESS + OLD_GORI + STALIN_MUSEUM + CENTRAL_CAFES + GEORGIAN_DINING Reason: Central Gori provides convenient access to the fortress, museums, historic streets, restaurants and relaxed city experiences. Gori Fortress is centrally located on a rocky hill and also provides views over the city and surrounding mountains. IF: traveler_interest == SCENIC_AND_PHOTOGRAPHY THEN: prefer_GORI_FORTRESS + ATENI_VALLEY AND: group_CITY_VIEWS + MOUNTAIN_LANDSCAPES + VINEYARDS + HISTORIC_ARCHITECTURE Reason: Gori Fortress provides elevated views over Gori and the surrounding Caucasus Mountains, while Ateni Valley combines mountain scenery, terraced vineyards, waterways and historic monuments. IF: traveler_interest == ADVENTURE_AND_OUTDOORS THEN: prefer_ATENI_VALLEY AND: group_HIKING + WATERFALLS + FOREST + MOUNTAIN_VIEWS + RURAL_EXPERIENCES Reason: Ateni Valley is the strongest nearby option for outdoor experiences, with the Tana River, mountain scenery and the Biisi Waterfall accessible by a 2.5 km hiking trail. IF: traveler_interest == HISTORY_AND_CULTURE THEN: prefer_GORI_CITY_CORE + UPLISTSIKHE AND: group_GORI_FORTRESS + STALIN_MUSEUM + ETHNOGRAPHIC_EXPERIENCES + ANCIENT_SITES Reason: Gori combines medieval and regional history with Soviet-era heritage, while nearby Uplistsikhe adds an ancient rock-hewn settlement dating back to the 6th–5th century BC. IF: traveler_interest == HISTORY + DAY_TRIPS THEN: consider_UPLISTSIKHE + ATENI_SIONI + ATENI_FORTRESS AND: group_ANCIENT_SITES + MEDIEVAL_ARCHITECTURE + FORTRESS + RELIGIOUS_HERITAGE + REGIONAL_LANDSCAPES Reason: The area around Gori contains major archaeological and historical sites. Uplistsikhe is an ancient rock-hewn settlement, while Ateni Valley contains Ateni Sioni, Ateni Fortress and other historic monuments. IF: trip_length >= 3 nights AND: traveler_interest == MOUNTAINS + SCENIC_EXPLORATION THEN: consider_split_itinerary BETWEEN: CENTRAL_GORI + ATENI_VALLEY_OR_OTHER_REGIONAL_EXCURSIONS Reason: Separating central Gori sightseeing from rural and mountain excursions reduces unnecessary backtracking and keeps the itinerary comfortable. IF: traveler_interest == FOOD_AND_GASTRONOMY THEN: consider_SHIDA_KARTLI_CUISINE_AND_WINE AND: group_GEORGIAN_FOOD + LOCAL_PRODUCE + WINE_TASTING + FAMILY_WINE_CELLARS Reason: Gori and the surrounding Shida Kartli region provide access to local wine cellars, Georgian cuisine and agricultural products. Ateni is a notable wine area, and local wineries offer tastings and culinary experiences. IF: traveler_interest == WINE_AND_RURAL_EXPERIENCE THEN: prefer_ATENI_VALLEY AND: consider_WINE_CELLAR + VINEYARDS + GEORGIAN_MEAL Reason: Ateni is a distinctive winemaking area with historic vineyard terraces and local wine cellars offering tastings, food and cultural experiences. IF: weather == HEAVY_RAIN OR: visibility == LOW THEN: reduce_UPLISTSIKHE + WATERFALL + HIKING + REMOTE_OUTDOOR_ACTIVITIES AND: prefer_CENTRAL_GORI AND: increase_FLEXIBLE_INDOOR_OR_HOTEL_TIME Reason: Rain, poor visibility and slippery outdoor terrain can reduce the comfort and value of archaeological, hiking and mountain excursions. Uplistsikhe and the Ateni Valley contain substantial outdoor walking components. IF: traveler_interest == ROMANTIC_RELAXATION THEN: prefer_ATENI_VALLEY + WINE_EXPERIENCE + SCENIC_GORI AND: decrease_activity_density_by_20_percent Reason: Couples generally benefit more from scenic countryside, vineyard experiences, Georgian dining, wine tasting and relaxed time together than from packing multiple archaeological and historical sites into one day. Ateni wineries can combine wine, food, cultural experiences and countryside settings. IF: trip_length <= 2 nights AND: traveler_interest == HISTORY THEN: prioritize_GORI_FORTRESS + STALIN_MUSEUM + UPLISTSIKHE Reason: These provide the strongest combination of Gori''s central historical identity and its most important nearby archaeological attraction. Uplistsikhe is approximately a 25-minute drive from central Gori. IF: trip_length >= 3 nights AND: traveler_interest == CULTURE + NATURE THEN: prioritize_GORI_CITY_CORE + UPLISTSIKHE + ATENI_VALLEY Reason: This combination provides a balanced experience of Gori''s urban history, ancient archaeology, religious heritage, vineyards, mountains, rivers and outdoor landscapes without requiring excessively long regional travel. IF: traveler_type == SENIOR OR: traveler_mobility == LIMITED THEN: reduce_UPLISTSIKHE_HIKING_INTENSITY AND: prefer_CENTRAL_GORI + EASY_ACCESS_ATTRACTIONS AND: verify_SITE_ACCESS_BEFORE_BOOKING Reason: Gori Fortress involves an elevated hilltop setting, while Uplistsikhe and some Ateni Valley experiences involve uneven outdoor terrain. Site-specific accessibility should therefore be checked before confirming the itinerary. IF: traveler_interest == SHORT_TRANSIT_STOP THEN: prefer_GORI_FORTRESS + CENTRAL_GORI OR: prefer_STALIN_MUSEUM AND: avoid_multiple_OUTSKIRT_EXCURSIONS Reason: Gori is strategically positioned between Tbilisi and western Georgia, making it useful as a short cultural stop. The city is approximately 1 hour 10 minutes by road from Tbilisi. IF: traveler_interest == AUTHENTIC_LOCAL_EXPERIENCE THEN: prefer_ATENI_WINE_CELLARS + LOCAL_GEORGIAN_DINING + RURAL_SHIDA_KARTLI AND: decrease_GENERIC_TOURIST_ACTIVITY_WEIGHT Reason: The wider Gori area offers family-run wine cellars, local cuisine, vineyards and rural experiences that can provide a more regionally focused experience beyond the city''s major museums. IF: traveler_needs_CURRENT_LOCAL_INFORMATION THEN: consult_GORI_TOURIST_INFORMATION_CENTER Reason: The official Gori Tourist Information Center provides destination and attraction information and is listed by the Georgian National Tourism Administration.', 741),
  ('gori', 34, 'destination-scoring', 'DESTINATION SCORING', NULL, NULL, '| Factor | Score | | ------------------ | ----: | | Family | 88 | | Honeymoon | 76 | | Luxury | 68 | | Budget | 94 | | Adventure | 82 | | Culture | 97 | | Food | 91 | | Shopping | 72 | | Nightlife | 38 | | Relaxation | 82 | | Nature | 84 | | Accessibility | 70 | | Safety | 87 | | First-time visitor | 93 | | Photography | 94 |', 742),
  ('gori', 35, 'final-travel-agent-verdict', 'FINAL TRAVEL AGENT VERDICT', NULL, NULL, 'Best traveler profiles: 1. Culture / heritage traveler 2. History / archaeology traveler 3. Photography traveler 4. Food / gastronomy traveler 5. Budget traveler 6. First-time Georgia traveler 7. Nature / outdoor traveler 8. Family traveler 9. Wine / rural-experience traveler 10. Honeymoon / romantic traveler Best duration: 2–3 nights 3–4 nights for travelers who want to combine Gori with Uplistsikhe, Ateni Valley, wine experiences, rural landscapes, and additional Shida Kartli excursions. Best season: April–October April–May for green landscapes, comfortable sightseeing temperatures, spring countryside, waterfalls, and outdoor excursions. June for warm but generally comfortable sightseeing, hiking, rural exploration, and photography. July–August for travelers comfortable with hotter summer conditions; outdoor archaeological sites and hiking should be planned around the cooler parts of the day. September–October for pleasant sightseeing, harvest-season atmosphere, wine experiences, food, photography, and autumn landscapes. Winter can still work well for travelers primarily interested in museums, Gori Fortress, history, food, and short cultural visits, although outdoor and rural activities become less suitable in cold or wet conditions. Best hotel strategy: Choose a clean, well-reviewed central hotel, guesthouse, boutique property, or family-run accommodation based on proximity to Gori Fortress, Stalin Museum, central restaurants, cafés, transport connections, and the main purpose of the trip. For short stays, prioritize central Gori so the main city attractions can be reached easily on foot and transport can be reserved for Uplistsikhe and surrounding excursions. Best transportation: Walking, local taxis, marshrutkas, private cars, guided tours, and regional transport depending on distance, budget, comfort, and itinerary. Private transport for: Must-do for first-time visitor: Uplistsikhe is particularly important for a first-time visitor because it provides a completely different experience from central Gori, with ancient rock-cut architecture, archaeological remains, wine cellars, temples and views toward the Mtkvari River. Don''t-do: Biggest advantage: Exceptional concentration of Georgian history, archaeology, medieval heritage, Soviet-era history, traditional food, Shida Kartli wine, rural landscapes, and photography opportunities within and around a relatively compact destination. Gori also provides convenient access to major attractions such as Uplistsikhe and the Ateni Valley, making it an effective base for exploring central Georgia. Biggest disadvantage: Limited nightlife, relatively small luxury and high-end shopping infrastructure, fewer resort-style leisure options than Batumi or Tbilisi, and uneven terrain at some archaeological and outdoor attractions. Travelers focused mainly on beaches, major nightlife, luxury shopping, or resort relaxation may find Gori less suitable. Overall destination score: 86/100', 743),
  ('gori', 36, 'data-quality', 'DATA QUALITY', NULL, NULL, 'information_completeness: 94/100 last_updated: 2026-08-19 last_verified: PARTIALLY_WEB_VERIFIED verified_by: GEORGIAN NATIONAL TOURISM ADMINISTRATION / GEORGIA TRAVEL / AGENCY OF PROTECTED AREAS OF GEORGIA / OFFICIAL GORI TOURIST INFORMATION SOURCES sources: IMPORTANT: Prices, opening hours, ticket prices, museum timings, archaeological-site operating conditions, accessibility, transport schedules, road conditions, weather conditions, hiking conditions, winery availability and other operational details must NOT be treated as permanently valid from this document. Gori Fortress, Stalin Museum, Gori Museum of History and Ethnography, Uplistsikhe, Ateni Sioni, wineries, churches, archaeological sites and other visitor attractions should be checked against the latest official information before travel. Attraction opening hours, ticket prices, museum availability, archaeological-site access, local transport availability, winery schedules and accessibility should be sourced from structured, refreshable data. Gori is approximately 80 km west of Tbilisi and around 1 hour 10 minutes by road under normal conditions. Road travel time can vary according to traffic, weather, roadworks and other operational conditions, so current transfer conditions should be verified before travel. Gori''s central attractions are relatively concentrated, including Gori Fortress, Stalin Museum, Gori Museum of History and Ethnography, central parks and other cultural attractions. However, Uplistsikhe, Ateni Valley, Ateni Sioni, Gorisjvari, waterfalls and rural wine destinations require additional local transport and should be planned separately. Uplistsikhe is an open-air archaeological and heritage site several kilometres from Gori and contains rock-cut streets, chambers, temples, wine-related structures and other archaeological remains. Outdoor terrain can be uneven, so practical accessibility should be verified for travelers with mobility requirements before travel. Ateni Sioni, Ateni Valley and surrounding rural areas combine historical monuments, vineyards, mountain landscapes and outdoor activities. Weather, road conditions, trail conditions and seasonal factors can affect the practicality of hiking and countryside excursions. The Tana and Tedzami Protected Landscape was established in 2023 in Gori Municipality and covers 21,864 hectares. It contains important biodiversity as well as historical and cultural heritage, including churches, fortresses, towers and abandoned settlements. Outdoor conditions and access should therefore be checked before planning nature-based excursions. Shida Kartli contains diverse natural environments including forests, mountain ranges, valleys, waterfalls and lakes, alongside major historical and cultural monuments. Outdoor activities can therefore be affected by rainfall, visibility, temperature, trail conditions and seasonal changes. Accessibility must be verified separately for each hotel, attraction, transport service, archaeological site, religious site, hiking route and outdoor activity because central Gori, Gori Fortress, Uplistsikhe, rural valleys and mountain destinations can have significantly different accessibility conditions. Travelers requiring step-free access, limited walking, accessible vehicles or other mobility arrangements should verify the exact accommodation, route, vehicle and attraction before relying on general destination-level accessibility information. Taxis, private vehicles and organized tours can provide greater flexibility for travelers with mobility requirements or travelers visiting attractions outside central Gori, particularly Uplistsikhe, Ateni Valley, waterfalls, rural villages and wine destinations. Weather information should be treated as a planning guide rather than a guarantee. Gori and Shida Kartli can experience significant seasonal variation, while higher-elevation valleys and mountain areas may have different conditions from central Gori. Uplistsikhe, Ateni Valley, waterfalls, hiking areas, rural villages, protected landscapes and other regional excursions should not be assumed to have the same accessibility, transport availability or operating conditions as central Gori. Wine-cellar and culinary experiences should be checked directly before travel because some establishments operate by advance reservation. For example, Chateau Ateni lists wine tasting, meals, culinary experiences and accommodation with advance booking requirements. Gori Tourist Information Centers provide visitor information and are listed through the Georgian National Tourism Administration''s official tourism platform. Current contact details and operating information should be checked before relying on the center for same-day assistance. The official Georgia Travel portal provides destination information covering Gori, Shida Kartli, historical attractions, archaeological sites, nature, food, wine and regional travel experiences. This should be treated as the primary destination-level reference, while attraction-specific operational details should be refreshed separately. Gori''s tourism infrastructure, museum operations, attraction facilities, local transport, winery services, visitor facilities and event schedules may change seasonally or through local administrative decisions. Current road and transport conditions should be verified before regional excursions, especially when visiting rural valleys, waterfalls, mountain areas and sites outside the central Gori urban area. This dataset should be refreshed regularly before production use.', 744),
  ('uplistsikhe', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Spring', NULL, 'months: March April May weather: Mild to warm, with increasingly pleasant conditions for outdoor archaeological exploration. Rain and changeable weather are possible. crowd_level: LOW → MEDIUM price_level: LOW → MEDIUM overall_score: 70-80 recommended: true reason: One of the best periods for Uplistsikhe. Comfortable temperatures, greener landscapes and good conditions for walking, archaeology and photography.', 745),
  ('uplistsikhe', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Summer', NULL, 'months: June July August weather: Warm to hot, with strong sun and exposed conditions around the rocky archaeological site. Midday sightseeing can be uncomfortable during hotter periods. crowd_level: MEDIUM → HIGH price_level: MEDIUM overall_score: 60-70 recommended: true reason: Good for sightseeing, but early morning or later afternoon visits are preferable because Uplistsikhe is primarily an exposed outdoor site with substantial walking.', 746),
  ('uplistsikhe', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Autumn', NULL, 'months: September October November weather: Generally mild and comfortable during early to mid-autumn, becoming cooler toward November. crowd_level: LOW → MEDIUM price_level: LOW → MEDIUM overall_score: 80-90 recommended: true reason: One of the strongest seasons for Uplistsikhe, offering comfortable walking conditions, good visibility, scenic landscapes and excellent photography opportunities.', 747),
  ('uplistsikhe', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Winter', NULL, 'months: December January February weather: Cold, with possible frost, snow, rain and slippery conditions on exposed rock surfaces. crowd_level: LOW price_level: LOW overall_score: 70-80 recommended: CONDITIONAL reason: Possible for history-focused visitors, but less suitable for exploring the exposed cave complex because cold, wind, ice or wet rock can make walking less comfortable.', 748),
  ('uplistsikhe', 10, 'budget-strategy', 'BUDGET STRATEGY', NULL, NULL, 'Where money can be saved: Where saving money is usually NOT recommended: Travel-agent rule: Uplistsikhe is generally a low-cost attraction, so transportation and guiding usually influence the total trip cost more than the entrance fee itself. For budget travelers, public or shared transport plus independent exploration offers strong value. For families, couples, and premium travelers, paying more for a private vehicle or organized excursion can provide better overall value through easier transfers, flexible timing, and the ability to combine Uplistsikhe with Gori and other nearby attractions.', 749),
  ('uplistsikhe', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Family', 'family', 'Pre-booked private car / MPV from Tbilisi International Airport or from the family''s accommodation in Tbilisi; direct transfer is the most convenient option when traveling with children, luggage, or family equipment. For families already staying in Gori, a private taxi / MPV for the approximately 10 km journey to Uplistsikhe is generally the simplest option. A private transfer is recommended because Uplistsikhe is an archaeological attraction rather than a major transport hub, and direct transport avoids unnecessary changes with children.', 750),
  ('uplistsikhe', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Honeymoon', 'honeymoon', 'Pre-booked private car from Tbilisi or Gori to Uplistsikhe; comfortable, flexible, and suitable for couples combining the cave city with Gori and other Shida Kartli attractions. reason: Uplistsikhe is approximately 10 km from Gori and is normally visited as a day excursion. A private transfer provides flexible sightseeing time and allows couples to combine Uplistsikhe with Gori in a relaxed itinerary.', 751),
  ('uplistsikhe', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Luxury', 'luxury', 'Chauffeured premium SUV / MPV or luxury private car from Tbilisi; personalized pickup, comfortable direct transportation, flexible waiting time, and private return transfer. For a premium itinerary, combine Uplistsikhe with Gori, private guiding, premium dining, and other Shida Kartli attractions. A private chauffeur is the strongest luxury option because premium travel value at Uplistsikhe comes primarily from transportation, guiding, flexibility, and personalized touring rather than luxury facilities at the archaeological site.', 752),
  ('uplistsikhe', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Budget', 'budget', 'Use public transport from Tbilisi to Gori, followed by local minibus / taxi transportation toward Uplistsikhe. Travelers arriving at Tbilisi International Airport can first travel into Tbilisi and then continue toward Gori by train or minibus before taking local transportation to Uplistsikhe. This is considerably cheaper than a private airport transfer but requires additional connections and more travel time. Budget travelers already staying in Gori can use local minibus services where practical or share a taxi to reduce the per-person cost.', 753),
  ('uplistsikhe', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Senior', 'senior', 'Pre-booked private car or reliable taxi from Tbilisi or Gori with minimal transfers, comfortable seating, luggage assistance where required, and direct arrival close to the visitor entrance. A private road transfer is generally preferable for seniors because public-transport combinations require additional transfers, while the Uplistsikhe archaeological complex itself already involves walking over uneven and rocky terrain. Travelers with mobility limitations should prioritize transportation comfort and allow sufficient time for a slower visit.', 754),
  ('uplistsikhe', 18, 'family-travel', 'FAMILY TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'child_friendly_score: 72 best_ages: Rules: For young children: Prefer: Avoid:', 755),
  ('uplistsikhe', 19, 'honeymoon-travel', 'HONEYMOON TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'honeymoon_score: 68 romance_score: 70 privacy_score: 72 luxury_score: 42 Recommended: Honeymoon itinerary should NOT contain more than: 1–2 major Uplistsikhe experiences + complementary regional experiences. Prefer: Private archaeological exploration + scenic photography + quality dining over: A rushed sequence of multiple historical attractions. Recommended hotel areas: Uplistsikhe should generally be treated as a honeymoon excursion rather than a honeymoon accommodation base. Uplistsikhe works particularly well for couples interested in history, archaeology, photography, unusual landscapes, and quieter cultural experiences. The ancient rock-cut city provides distinctive scenery overlooking the Mtkvari River valley and offers a very different atmosphere from conventional urban sightseeing. For honeymoon travelers, private transport provides better flexibility and allows the visit to be combined with Gori, Mtskheta, Georgian dining, countryside scenery, or other romantic experiences. Uplistsikhe is less suitable for couples seeking luxury resorts, spas, nightlife, beaches, extensive shopping, or a traditional secluded honeymoon stay.', 756),
  ('uplistsikhe', 20, 'luxury-travel', 'LUXURY TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'luxury_score: 42 Recommended: Uplistsikhe luxury travel should focus on: Luxury travelers should not simply be given more activities. Luxury at Uplistsikhe should primarily increase: Uplistsikhe has very limited standalone luxury-tourism infrastructure. Premium positioning should therefore come from the quality of transportation, guiding, scheduling, dining, and the wider itinerary rather than facilities inside the archaeological site. For high-end travelers, Uplistsikhe works best as a privately guided cultural experience incorporated into a broader premium Georgia itinerary. A strong luxury itinerary can combine Tbilisi, Mtskheta, Gori, Uplistsikhe, premium Georgian dining, and other carefully selected cultural experiences.', 757),
  ('uplistsikhe', 21, 'adventure', 'ADVENTURE', NULL, NULL, 'adventure_score: 64 Uplistsikhe offers light-to-moderate active exploration rather than conventional high-intensity adventure tourism. Its appeal comes from walking through an extensive rock-cut archaeological landscape containing ancient footways, caves, chambers, streets, tunnels, religious structures, and elevated rocky terrain. Adventure experiences should be interpreted as: Travel-agent interpretation:', 758),
  ('uplistsikhe', 22, 'senior-travel', 'SENIOR TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'senior_suitability: 62 walking_intensity: MEDIUM → HIGH within the archaeological complex Rules:', 759),
  ('uplistsikhe', 23, 'accessibility', 'ACCESSIBILITY', NULL, NULL, 'wheelchair_accessibility: LIMITED; UPLISTSIKHE MUSEUM HAS A RAMP, BUT THE WIDER ARCHAEOLOGICAL COMPLEX IS NOT FULLY STEP-FREE public_transport_accessibility: LIMITED → VARIABLE; VERIFY SPECIFIC SERVICE AND VEHICLE hotel_accessibility: NOT APPLICABLE TO THE ARCHAEOLOGICAL SITE; VERIFY ACCOMMODATION IN GORI / TBILISI SEPARATELY attraction_accessibility: LIMITED → PARTIAL; MUST BE ASSESSED BY SPECIFIC SECTION Rule: Never interpret accessibility of the Uplistsikhe Museum as accessibility of the entire Uplistsikhe archaeological complex. Each visitor facility, route, archaeological section, and transport service should be assessed separately. Additional notes:', 760),
  ('uplistsikhe', 24, 'food', 'FOOD', NULL, NULL, 'Uplistsikhe is particularly suitable for combining with: Uplistsikhe itself should not be positioned as a major culinary destination. Food is best treated as a complementary experience before or after visiting the archaeological complex. There are Georgian restaurants and cafés close to the Uplistsikhe approach road, while Gori provides a substantially wider selection of restaurants, cafés, bakeries, and other dining options. The wider Shida Kartli region adds an important food-and-wine dimension to an Uplistsikhe excursion, allowing archaeological sightseeing to be combined with traditional Georgian cuisine and regional wines. Food experiences: Family: Plan a relaxed Georgian lunch before or after the archaeological visit. Prioritize clean, family-friendly restaurants with familiar Georgian dishes, mild options, bread, cheese, khachapuri, grilled meats, soups, and vegetarian choices. Avoid scheduling a long archaeological visit without sufficient water and food breaks. Honeymoon: Combine Uplistsikhe with a relaxed Georgian lunch, countryside restaurant, regional wine experience, or special dinner in Gori or Tbilisi. Archaeology + scenic countryside + Georgian food and wine creates a stronger honeymoon experience than treating Uplistsikhe as a standalone romantic destination. Luxury: Use private transportation to combine a privately guided Uplistsikhe visit with a premium Georgian lunch, curated wine tasting, countryside dining, or high-quality restaurant experience. For genuine fine dining and a broader premium restaurant selection, Tbilisi is the stronger base. Budget: Carry water and combine the archaeological visit with an affordable Georgian café or restaurant near Uplistsikhe or in Gori. Khinkali, khachapuri, lobio, bread, salads, soups, and other Georgian dishes can provide good-value meals. Budget travelers can also eat in Gori before or after visiting the site.', 761),
  ('uplistsikhe', 25, 'shopping', 'SHOPPING', NULL, NULL, 'Strong categories: Uplistsikhe is better suited to small souvenir purchases and regional Georgian products than extensive shopping. Shopping should be treated as a secondary activity attached to the archaeological visit rather than a major reason to visit. The most relevant purchases are Uplistsikhe-themed souvenirs, Georgian handicrafts, small heritage gifts, regional food products, and Georgian wine. Visitors seeking a wider selection should continue shopping in Gori or Tbilisi. Luxury shopping: Uplistsikhe has very limited luxury-shopping opportunities. For premium purchases, prefer established wineries, specialist wine shops, artisan producers, and curated Georgian craft stores in the wider Shida Kartli region, Gori, or Tbilisi. Premium regional wine is the strongest luxury-oriented purchase associated with the wider Uplistsikhe / Shida Kartli experience. Budget: Prefer: Budget travelers should keep shopping simple at Uplistsikhe and use Gori for a broader selection of food, wine, everyday products, and souvenirs. Uplistsikhe''s shopping value comes primarily from small keepsakes connected with the archaeological site and products representing Georgian culture. The wider Shida Kartli region strengthens the shopping experience through wine and agricultural products. Wine-related purchases can be particularly relevant for travelers combining Uplistsikhe with wineries or other regional experiences. Travel-agent rule: Treat shopping as a secondary Uplistsikhe experience. Prioritize a small authentic souvenir from the archaeological visit and use Gori, regional wineries, or Tbilisi for substantial shopping. For wine, food products, ceramics, and handicrafts, prefer established producers and reputable sellers where quality and provenance can be verified.', 762),
  ('uplistsikhe', 26, 'nightlife', 'NIGHTLIFE', NULL, NULL, 'nightlife_level: 5 Suitable for: Best areas: Not a primary requirement for: Evening activities are better suited to: Uplistsikhe itself has essentially no conventional nightlife scene. It is primarily a daytime archaeological and cultural attraction rather than a destination for bars, clubs, entertainment districts, or late-night activities. The strongest evening strategy is to visit Uplistsikhe during operating hours and continue to Gori for Georgian restaurants, cafés, wine, and relaxed evening experiences, or return to Tbilisi for a substantially broader nightlife scene. Honeymoon travelers should generally prefer: Late-afternoon Uplistsikhe visit + scenic photography + Georgian dinner / wine experience over: Late-night entertainment around Uplistsikhe. For couples, the area''s appeal comes from history, unusual landscapes, countryside atmosphere, photography, Georgian cuisine, and regional wine rather than nightlife. Travel-agent rule: Position Uplistsikhe as a **daytime archaeological destination with virtually no dedicated nightlife**. Do not market it for bars, clubs, casinos, rooftop nightlife, or late-night entertainment. Use nearby Gori for relaxed dining and wine experiences, and Tbilisi for travelers seeking substantial nightlife or late-night entertainment.', 763),
  ('uplistsikhe', 28, 'sample-itinerary-patterns', 'SAMPLE ITINERARY PATTERNS', '3 NIGHTS', NULL, '### Day 1 Arrival in Gori → Transfer from Tbilisi to Gori → Hotel check-in → Relax and refresh → Gori Fortress → Central Gori → Georgian dinner → Hotel ### Day 2 Morning: Breakfast → Transfer from Gori to Uplistsikhe → Uplistsikhe Cave Town → Visitor / archaeological museum → Ancient rock-cut streets and squares → Queen Tamar Hall → Uplistsikhe Theatre → Pillared Hall → Pagan temple remains → Rock-cut residential chambers Afternoon: Three-nave Basilica → Uplistsuli Church / Eklesia → Ancient wine presses and cellars → Secret Tunnel → Mtkvari River valley viewpoints → Panoramic archaeological landscape → Return to Gori Evening: Relaxed Georgian dinner → Local wine experience → Hotel ### Day 3 Morning: Breakfast → Gori sightseeing → Stalin Museum → Stalin''s Birthplace → Stalin''s Railway Carriage → Gori Historical & Ethnographic Museum Afternoon: Ateni Valley → Ateni Sioni Church → Scenic Tana Valley → Shida Kartli countryside → Regional wine / food experience Evening: Return to Gori → Georgian dinner → Relaxed evening → Hotel ### Day 4 Breakfast → Leisure morning → Hotel checkout → Transfer to Tbilisi → Continue onward journey / departure', 764),
  ('uplistsikhe', 29, 'four-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'FOUR-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 1', NULL, 'Arrival at Tbilisi International Airport → Private transfer to Tbilisi → Romantic hotel check-in → Relax and enjoy the hotel → Romantic Georgian dinner → Overnight at Tbilisi', 765),
  ('uplistsikhe', 29, 'four-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'FOUR-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 2', NULL, 'Breakfast at the hotel → Private excursion from Tbilisi to Gori → Explore Gori, the birthplace and hometown of Joseph Stalin → Visit the Stalin Museum → See the historic museum collection and Stalin''s personal railway carriage Afternoon: Private lunch → Continue to Uplistsikhe Cave City → Explore the ancient rock-carved settlement → Walk through the cave streets, temples, halls and dwellings → Discover the historic remains of this ancient cultural and religious centre Evening: Return to Tbilisi → Relax at the hotel → Romantic Georgian dinner → Overnight at Tbilisi', 766),
  ('uplistsikhe', 29, 'four-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'FOUR-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 3', NULL, 'Breakfast at the hotel → Private excursion from Tbilisi along the Georgian Military Road → Visit Ananuri Fortress → Explore the historic medieval castle and church complex → Enjoy scenic views of the Zhinvali Reservoir Afternoon: Private lunch → Continue towards Gudauri → Pass through the scenic Georgian Military Road → Visit Gudauri Ski Resort → Enjoy breathtaking mountain scenery and couple photography Evening: Return to Tbilisi → Relax at the hotel → Romantic dinner → Overnight at Tbilisi', 767),
  ('uplistsikhe', 29, 'four-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'FOUR-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 4', NULL, 'Breakfast at the hotel → Leisure morning in Tbilisi → Romantic time together → Relax and enjoy the hotel Afternoon: Shopping experience in Tbilisi → Visit Tbilisi Mall / Galleria Tbilisi → Couple shopping and leisure time → Private lunch Evening: Return to the hotel → Free time for relaxation → Special Georgian dinner → Overnight at Tbilisi', 768),
  ('uplistsikhe', 29, 'four-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'FOUR-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 5', NULL, 'Breakfast → Leisure morning → Romantic time together → Hotel checkout → Private transfer to Tbilisi International Airport → Departure', 769),
  ('uplistsikhe', 30, 'four-nights-family-pattern', 'FOUR-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 1', NULL, 'Arrival at Tbilisi International Airport → Private transfer to Tbilisi → Family-friendly hotel check-in → Relax and enjoy the hotel → Family dinner → Overnight at Tbilisi', 770),
  ('uplistsikhe', 30, 'four-nights-family-pattern', 'FOUR-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 2', NULL, 'Breakfast at the hotel → Private excursion from Tbilisi to Gori → Explore Gori, the historic city associated with Joseph Stalin → Visit the Stalin Museum → See the museum collection and Stalin''s personal railway carriage Afternoon: Family lunch → Continue to Uplistsikhe Cave City → Explore the ancient rock-carved settlement → Walk through the historic cave streets, temples, halls and dwellings → Discover the fascinating history of this ancient cultural centre Evening: Return to Tbilisi → Family leisure time → Dinner → Overnight at Tbilisi', 771),
  ('uplistsikhe', 30, 'four-nights-family-pattern', 'FOUR-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 3', NULL, 'Breakfast at the hotel → Private excursion from Tbilisi along the Georgian Military Road → Visit Ananuri Fortress → Explore the historic medieval castle and church complex → Enjoy scenic views of the Zhinvali Reservoir Afternoon: Family lunch → Continue towards Gudauri → Scenic drive through the Georgian Military Road → Visit Gudauri Ski Resort → Enjoy mountain views and family photography Evening: Return to Tbilisi → Relax at the hotel → Family dinner → Overnight at Tbilisi', 772),
  ('uplistsikhe', 30, 'four-nights-family-pattern', 'FOUR-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 4', NULL, 'Breakfast at the hotel → Family shopping tour in Tbilisi → Visit Tbilisi Mall / Galleria Tbilisi → Family shopping and leisure time → Private lunch Afternoon: → Continue exploring Tbilisi at leisure → Enjoy family time together → Return to the hotel Evening: → Free time for relaxation → Family dinner → Overnight at Tbilisi', 773),
  ('uplistsikhe', 30, 'four-nights-family-pattern', 'FOUR-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 5', NULL, 'Breakfast → Leisure morning → Enjoy family time at the hotel → Hotel checkout → Private transfer to Tbilisi International Airport → Departure', 774),
