  ('dambulla', 23, 'accessibility', 'ACCESSIBILITY', NULL, NULL, 'wheelchair_accessibility: LIMITED public_transport_accessibility: FAIR hotel_accessibility: FAIR_TO_GOOD; MUST_BE_VERIFIED_PER_HOTEL attraction_accessibility: LIMITED_TO_FAIR; MUST_BE_VERIFIED_PER_ATTRACTION Rule: Most sites involve stairs, uneven paths, or heat. Verify accessible room, ground*floor access, and attraction facilities before booking. A private driver is strongly recommended to minimise walking. Details:', 1304),
  ('dambulla', 24, 'food', 'FOOD', NULL, NULL, 'Dambulla is particularly strong for: Food experiences: Family: Prioritise hotel restaurants, clean local eateries, buffet options. Avoid very spicy food for kids. Early dinners 6-7pm. Bottled water only. Honeymoon: Include one memorable dinner at a boutique resort with Sigiriya view, private villa dining, or village cooking experience for two. Luxury: Chef-led tasting menus at heritage resorts, private dining by pool, wine with meals, spa wellness cuisine, private chef at villa. Budget: Use local rice & curry shops, kade shops, street fruit. $5*8/day is easy. Reserve one nicer resort meal for experience.', 1305),
  ('dambulla', 25, 'shopping', 'SHOPPING', NULL, NULL, 'Strong categories: Luxury shopping: Limited in Dambulla itself. Best at: Budget: Prefer: Note: Bargain politely. Prices are already low.', 1306),
  ('dambulla', 26, 'nightlife', 'NIGHTLIFE', NULL, NULL, 'nightlife_level: 25 Suitable for: Not a primary requirement for: Honeymoon travellers should generally prefer: Romantic dinner with rock view, poolside drinks, spa evening, or early night to wake for Pidurangala sunrise over: bars or clubs _ Dambulla has almost none. Closest nightlife is in Colombo or Negombo. Note: Most restaurants close 9*10pm. Plan for quiet nights. This is a nature + culture destination, not a party.', 1307),
  ('dambulla', 32, 'travel-agent-insights', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS', 'What inexperienced planners often do wrong', NULL, '', 1308),
  ('dambulla', 32, 'travel-agent-insights', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS', 'What an experienced planner does differently', NULL, '', 1309),
  ('dambulla', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', NULL, NULL, 'IF: `trip_length <= 2 nights` THEN: prioritise Dambulla Cave Temple + Golden Temple, and one Sigiriya sunrise. Reason: A very short stay should focus on Cultural Triangle icons, not driving to multiple parks. IF: `trip_length == 3 nights` THEN: include only one major full-day zone: Sigiriya/Pidurangala OR Safari Day. Reason: Both require early starts and energy. Combining both makes the trip exhausting in heat. IF: `trip_length >= 4 nights` THEN: Add either Sigiriya day, Safari Day, or Village + Polonnaruwa day trip. Reason: Four nights allow core Dambulla + 1 interest-led experience without rushing. IF: `trip_length >= 5 nights` THEN: include two themed days from Sigiriya, Safari, Village, Waterfall, or Polonnaruwa/Anuradhapura. Reason: Five nights gives time for culture, wildlife, nature, and recovery time between climbs. IF: `trip_length >= 7 nights` THEN: Consider a slower Dambulla programme + add Kandy, Ella, or South Coast beach. Reason: Most first*time Dambulla highlights can be covered in 3-4 nights. Extra days work best as part of Sri Lanka circuit. IF: `traveler_type == FAMILY` AND: `children_age <= 6` THEN: Schedule a maximum of one major activity per day and include afternoon pool + hotel downtime. Reason: Heat, climbing, and long jeep rides reduce practical capacity for young children. IF: `traveler_type == HONEYMOON` THEN: limit itinerary to 2 major activities per day and increase free*time allocation. Reason: Dambulla honeymoon value comes from sunrise views, boutique resorts, spa, and slow village experiences — not max attraction count. IF: `traveler_type == BUDGET` THEN: Use local buses + shared tuk-tuks, select Dambulla town guesthouse, and mix paid safaris with free temples. Reason: Dambulla is budget*friendly. Local food, guesthouses, and public transport keep costs low without losing experience. IF: `traveler_type == LUXURY` THEN: Prioritise Sigiriya area boutique resorts. Reason: These offer rock views, pools, spa, and privacy. Use private driver + guide for seamless experience.', 1310),
  ('dambulla', 34, 'destination-scoring', 'DESTINATION SCORING', NULL, NULL, '| Factor | Score | | ------------------ | ----: | | Family | 82 | | Honeymoon | 75 | | Luxury | 70 | | Budget | 92 | | Adventure | 80 | | Culture | 95 | | Food | 80 | | Shopping | 60 | | Nightlife | 25 | | Relaxation | 75 | | Nature | 90 | | Accessibility | 65 | | Safety | 88 | | First-time visitor | 90 | | Photography | 94 |', 1311),
  ('dambulla', 35, 'final-travel-agent-verdict', 'FINAL TRAVEL AGENT VERDICT', NULL, NULL, 'Best traveller profiles: 1. First-time Sri Lanka travellers 2. Culture + History enthusiasts 3. Wildlife + Nature lovers 4. Budget travellers 5. Photography + Adventure travellers 6. Families with kids 8+ Best duration: 4-5 nights Best season: February-April July-August _ for Minneriya elephants Best hotel strategy: Base in Dambulla town for convenience and budget. Choose Sigiriya area for views and romance. Choose Habarana/Minneriya for safari-focused stays. Best transportation: Hire a private driver for 3*4 days. Use tuk-tuks for short town trips. Shared jeeps for safaris. Private transfer for: Must-do for first-time visitor: Don''t-do: Biggest advantage: Dambulla offers incredible density: UNESCO caves, Sigiriya, elephants, and village life all within 30km. Authentic, affordable, and photogenic. Biggest disadvantage: Heat and humidity Mar-Aug. Limited nightlife, luxury brands, and wheelchair access. Requires early starts. Overall destination score: 87/100 — a must-visit cultural + wildlife hub for Sri Lanka. Best for first-timers, culture lovers, and budget-conscious travellers who don’t mind early mornings.', 1312),
  ('dambulla', 36, 'data-quality', 'DATA QUALITY', NULL, NULL, 'information_completeness: 85/100 last_updated: 2026-08-17 last_verified: PARTIALLY_LIVE_VERIFIED verified_by: SRI_LANKA_DESTINATION_KNOWLEDGE_DATASET sources: IMPORTANT: This Dambulla destination file is suitable for itinerary design, traveller profiling, hotel-area strategy, and initial package planning. Prices, hotel inventory, driver rates, safari park opening hours, elephant migration, temple dress codes, road conditions, and weather alerts must be live*verified before quotation or booking. Do not rely on generic "Cultural Triangle package" inclusions without confirming exact sites, driver type, safari park, and entry fees. Verify if Sigiriya is open on Poya days and check park closures before finalising.', 1313),
  ('kandy', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Spring Mar-May', NULL, 'weather: Warm, 24-28°C. Occasional rain. crowd_level: MEDIUM price_level: MEDIUM overall_score: 85 recommended: true reason: Good weather. Esala Perahera prep starts.', 1314),
  ('kandy', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Summer Jun-Aug', NULL, 'weather: Pleasant, 22-26°C. Monsoon showers. crowd_level: HIGH price_level: HIGH overall_score: 92 recommended: true reason: Peak season + Esala Perahera Festival in July/Aug. Book 6 months ahead.', 1315),
  ('kandy', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Autumn Sep-Nov', NULL, 'weather: Cooler, 20*24°C. More rain. crowd_level: LOW → MEDIUM price_level: LOW → MEDIUM overall_score: 82 recommended: true reason: Best value. Green landscapes. Fewer crowds.', 1316),
  ('kandy', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Winter Dec-Feb', NULL, 'weather: Cool and dry, 18*24°C. Perfect. crowd_level: HIGH price_level: HIGH overall_score: 90 recommended: true reason: Best weather. Peak tourist season.', 1317),
  ('kandy', 10, 'budget-strategy', 'BUDGET STRATEGY', NULL, NULL, 'Where money can be saved: Where saving money is usually NOT recommended: Travel-agent rule: A lake-view 3★ hotel beats a cheaper hilltop homestay. You’ll walk less and enjoy evenings more.', 1318),
