  ('punakha', 23, 'accessibility', 'ACCESSIBILITY', NULL, NULL, 'wheelchair_accessibility: LOW_TO_MODERATE public_transport_accessibility: LOW hotel_accessibility: GOOD; 4★-5★ HOTELS HAVE ELEVATORS + GROUND FLOOR attraction_accessibility: MODERATE; MUST_BE_VERIFIED_PER_ATTRACTION Rule: Verify accessible room + riverside lodge + private car.', 1603),
  ('punakha', 24, 'food', 'FOOD', NULL, NULL, 'Punakha is particularly strong for: Food experiences: 1. EMA_DATSHI_LOCAL - Chili cheese. BTN 250-400 2. LODGE_RIVERSIDE_DINING - COMO Uma farm-to-table. BTN 1500-2500 3. RED_RICE_PUNAKHA - Organic red rice + veg. BTN 400-600 4. RIVERSIDE_PICNIC - Guide sets picnic by Mo Chhu. Included 5. DZONG_CAFE - Small cafe near dzong + river Family: Prioritise lodge buffet + momo + fried rice + mild ema datshi. Honeymoon: Include one private riverside picnic + lodge fine dining with dzong view. Budget: Food included in package. Extra cafe BTN 300-600.', 1604),
  ('punakha', 25, 'shopping', 'SHOPPING', NULL, NULL, 'Strong categories: Luxury shopping: Lodge boutique - Textiles, incense Budget: Chimi village shops - Small + funny souvenirs.', 1605),
  ('punakha', 26, 'nightlife', 'NIGHTLIFE', NULL, NULL, 'nightlife_level: 40 Suitable for: Not a primary requirement for: Honeymoon travellers should generally prefer: Riverside lodge fireplace, private balcony with dzong lights, hot stone bath, stargazing, river sound over: late-night bars or clubs Note: Punakha has almost no nightlife. Town closes 7-8 PM. All evening at lodge - Bar + dinner + river sound + fireplace. Very quiet + romantic. For nightlife not Bhutan.', 1606),
  ('punakha', 28, 'sample-itinerary-patterns', 'SAMPLE ITINERARY PATTERNS', '1 NIGHT PUNAKHA ESSENTIALS', NULL, 'Day 1 Drive Thimphu → Punakha 2hr via Dochula Pass tea + 108 chortens. Check-in. Afternoon Punakha Dzong + Suspension Bridge + River walk. Day 2 Morning Chimi Lhakhang rice field walk + blessing. Afternoon river rafting Mo Chhu + drive to Paro/Thimphu. Package Includes: 1 night stay, guide, car, SDF, meals, rafting. Excludes: Luxury upgrade, tips, shopping, insurance.', 1607),
  ('punakha', 29, 'three-night-valley-culture-pattern-ideal-2n', 'THREE-NIGHT VALLEY + CULTURE PATTERN (IDEAL 2N)', NULL, NULL, 'Day 1 Arrive from Thimphu 2hr via Dochula Pass. Check into riverside luxury lodge COMO Uma. Afternoon Punakha Dzong interior + river confluence + suspension bridge walk. Evening riverside dinner. Overnight: Punakha Riverside Lodge Meals: Full Board Day 2 After breakfast, Chimi Lhakhang rice field walk + fertility blessing + Sobsokha village. Afternoon Khamsum Yulley Chorten hike 45min + valley view + Sangchhen Nunnery + Talo village drive. Evening hot stone bath. Overnight: Punakha Riverside Lodge Meals: Full Board Day 3 After breakfast, river rafting Mo Chhu 1.5hr gentle + riverside picnic + bike ride through rice fields + Limbukha village + evening at lodge with fireplace. Overnight: Punakha Riverside Lodge Meals: Full Board Day 4 Breakfast, check out and drive to Paro 4.5hr or Phobjikha 3hr with sweet valley memories. Meals: Breakfast', 1608),
  ('punakha', 30, 'three-night-family-pattern', 'THREE-NIGHT FAMILY PATTERN', NULL, NULL, 'Day 1 Drive Thimphu→Punakha with Dochula stop. Check-in riverside lodge. Afternoon Punakha Dzong + Suspension Bridge (hold kids) + river. Overnight: Punakha Family Lodge Meals: Full Board Day 2 Breakfast. Morning Chimi Lhakhang easy flat walk + village + blessing. Afternoon rafting gentle + rice field walk. Overnight: Punakha Family Lodge Meals: Full Board Day 3 Breakfast. Sangchhen Nunnery viewpoint + Khamsum Yulley lower part + Talo village + local school visit (if allowed). Evening lodge pool. Overnight: Punakha Family Lodge Meals: Full Board Day 4 Breakfast, check-out. Drive to Paro. Meals: Breakfast', 1609),
  ('punakha', 31, 'three-night-luxury-honeymoon-pattern', 'THREE-NIGHT LUXURY HONEYMOON PATTERN', NULL, NULL, 'Day 1 Arrive from Thimphu via Dochula with private tea. Check into COMO Uma Punakha private villa with river + rice view + fireplace + hot stone bath. Afternoon private Punakha Dzong tour + monk blessing + suspension bridge private + sunset riverside champagne. Overnight: COMO Uma Punakha Meals: Full Board Day 2 Breakfast. Morning private Chimi rice field walk at golden hour + blessing for couple + Sobsokha village. Afternoon private rafting with riverside BBQ lunch + private bike ride + Khamsum Yulley sunrise next day plan. Evening private dining at lodge with dzong view + spa. Overnight: COMO Uma Punakha Meals: Full Board Day 3 Breakfast. Private hike to Khamsum Yulley with breakfast on top + valley panorama. Afternoon: Sangchhen Nunnery private tour + Talo village + hot stone bath ritual + farewell private dinner with Bhutanese performance + fireplace. Alternative: Replace hike with private picnic + meditation with monk at Chimi. Overnight: COMO Uma Punakha Meals: Full Board Day 4 Breakfast. Check-out and drive to Paro with sweet luxury memories. Meals: Breakfast', 1610),
  ('punakha', 32, 'travel-agent-insights', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS', 'What inexperienced planners often do wrong', NULL, '', 1611),
  ('punakha', 32, 'travel-agent-insights', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS', 'What an experienced planner does differently', NULL, '1. Starts with purpose 2. Groups by geography: Dochula enroute, Punakha Dzong + Bridge + Rafting together, Chimi + Khamsum + Sangchhen together. 3. Uses hotel location strategically: RIVERSIDE for luxury/honeymoon/views, TOWN for budget/close to dzong. 4. Places Chimi morning or after 3:30 PM. Avoid midday heat + strong sun at 1200m. 5. Treats Punakha as a warm, relaxing valley, not a checklist. Max 2 major activities/day. 6. Always checks dzong opening + festival dates - Punakha Tshechu + Dromche Feb/Mar highlight - Book 6 months early.', 1612),
  ('punakha', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', NULL, NULL, 'IF: `trip_length == 1 night` THEN: Dochula + Punakha Dzong + Chimi Lhakhang + Suspension Bridge. Reason: Core best of Punakha. IF: `trip_length == 2 nights` THEN: Add Khamsum Yulley hike + Rafting + Sangchhen Nunnery. Reason: Complete valley experience. IF: `trip_length >= 3 nights` THEN: Add Talo village + bike ride + slow rice walks + Phobjikha day trip option. Reason: Slow luxury valley retreat. IF: `traveler_type == FAMILY` THEN: Chimi flat walk + Bridge + Dzong + Gentle rafting. Reason: Easy + warm + flat. IF: `traveler_type == HONEYMOON` THEN: Riverside luxury lodge + Private dzong sunset + Private rice field walk + Private raft picnic. Reason: Most romantic valley in Bhutan. IF: `travel_month == Apr` THEN: Must include Punakha Dzong jacaranda bloom + evening light. Reason: Purple trees + dzong = Best Bhutan photo.', 1613),
  ('punakha', 34, 'destination-scoring', 'DESTINATION SCORING', NULL, NULL, '| Factor | Score | | ------------------ | ----: | Family | 88 Honeymoon | 92 Luxury | 92 Budget | 55 Adventure | 75 Culture | 94 Food | 82 Shopping | 65 Nightlife | 40 Relaxation | 92 Nature | 92 Accessibility | 70 Safety | 94 First-time visitor | 94 Photography | 94', 1614),
  ('punakha', 35, 'final-travel-agent-verdict', 'FINAL TRAVEL AGENT VERDICT', NULL, NULL, 'Best traveller profiles: 1. Honeymoon + Romance - Riverside lodges + rice fields + dzong sunset 2. Culture + Heritage lovers - Punakha Dzong most beautiful dzong 3. Families - Warm valley + easy walks + rafting gentle + low altitude 4. Luxury travelers - COMO Uma / Dhensa / Amankora best in Bhutan 5. Photographers - Dzong reflection + jacaranda April + rice terraces + Dochula 108 Best duration: 1-2 nights Best season: Mar-May for jacaranda, Sep-Nov for golden rice + clear views Best hotel strategy: Best transportation: Private car + guide - Mandatory. 2hr from Thimphu via Dochula. Must-do: Don''t-do: Biggest advantage: Warmest, most fertile, most photogenic valley in Bhutan with Bhutan’s most beautiful dzong + luxury riverside lodges + low altitude. Biggest disadvantage: SDF $100/day + guide mandatory expensive, limited shopping/nightlife, hot in summer, activities limited to 1-2 days. Overall destination score: 93/100 - Most beautiful dzong + most romantic valley in Bhutan. Must 1-2 nights in any Bhutan circuit.', 1615),
  ('punakha', 36, 'data-quality', 'DATA QUALITY', NULL, NULL, 'information_completeness: 94/100 last_updated: 2026-08-17 last_verified: PARTIALLY_LIVE_VERIFIED verified_by: BHUTAN_DESTINATION_KNOWLEDGE_DATASET sources: IMPORTANT: This Punakha file is suitable for itinerary design, traveller profiling, hotel-area strategy, and initial package planning. Bhutan SDF $100/person/day + guide + private car mandatory. Punakha Dzong entry 9-11 AM and 1-5 PM. Closed during govt events. Dochula views weather dependent. Jacaranda bloom only mid-April. Prices, hotel inventory, festival dates Punakha Dromche/Tshechu Feb-Mar, rafting water levels, and SDF rules must be live-verified before quotation. Do not rely on generic Bhutan package inclusions without confirming exact attraction name, transfer type, ticket category, pickup timing, and whether the dzong is open on the client''s date.', 1616),
  ('paro', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Spring Mar-May', NULL, 'weather: 8-20°C, clear, rhododendron, Tiger Nest best. crowd_level: VERY HIGH price_level: VERY HIGH overall_score: 94 recommended: true reason: Paro Tshechu Mar/Apr - Biggest festival. Best hike weather.', 1617),
  ('paro', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Summer Jun-Aug', NULL, 'weather: 15-25°C, monsoon, green rice, clouds over Tiger Nest afternoons. crowd_level: LOW price_level: MEDIUM overall_score: 70 recommended: true (with rain) reason: Green valley, fewer tourists, Tiger Nest slippery + leeches.', 1618),
  ('paro', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Autumn Sep-Nov', NULL, 'weather: 6-18°C, post-monsoon crystal clear, best Tiger Nest views. crowd_level: VERY HIGH price_level: VERY HIGH overall_score: 95 recommended: true reason: Best season overall. Clear skies + golden rice + festivals.', 1619),
  ('paro', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Winter Dec-Feb', NULL, 'weather: -2 to 14°C, cold mornings, sunny days, snow at Chele La. crowd_level: LOW price_level: MEDIUM overall_score: 84 recommended: true reason: Cold but Tiger Nest clear + less crowd. Snow at higher passes.', 1620),
  ('paro', 10, 'budget-strategy', 'BUDGET STRATEGY', NULL, NULL, 'Where money can be saved: Where saving money is usually NOT recommended: Travel-agent rule: Paro is most expensive valley due to luxury lodges. But Tiger Nest is reason client pays Bhutan SDF. Budget $300-$500/day pp for luxury. Keep last night in Paro for early flight next day - Airport 15min from lodges.', 1621),
  ('paro', 12, 'airport-transfer-logic', 'AIRPORT TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Family', 'family', 'Guide + private SUV/van waiting outside Paro PBH with khadar + name board. 15min to Paro town hotel. Stop at Paro Dzong view + river. Child seat on request. Tiger hike next day early.', 1622),
  ('paro', 12, 'airport-transfer-logic', 'AIRPORT TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Honeymoon', 'honeymoon', 'Luxury SUV + COMO Uma/Amankora welcome + flower + hot towel. Private villa with rice field + Tiger Nest far view. Private blessing arrangement at Tiger Nest.', 1623),
  ('paro', 12, 'airport-transfer-logic', 'AIRPORT TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Luxury', 'luxury', 'Luxury SUV + Amankora/COMO Uma/Six Senses welcome + butler + hot stone bath ready. Amankora private transfer + fireplace. Private airport lounge.', 1624),
  ('paro', 12, 'airport-transfer-logic', 'AIRPORT TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Budget', 'budget', 'Still private car + guide mandatory. 3★ hotels pick up 15min from airport. Same welcome.', 1625),
  ('paro', 12, 'airport-transfer-logic', 'AIRPORT TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Senior', 'senior', 'Private car door-to-door + guide helps with luggage + oxygen check. Altitude 2280m + Tiger hike moderate tough. Pony arranged to cafeteria + slow pace + tea stops.', 1626),
  ('paro', 18, 'family-travel', 'FAMILY TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'child_friendly_score: 86 best_ages: Rules: For young children: Prefer: Avoid:', 1627),
  ('paro', 19, 'honeymoon-travel', 'HONEYMOON TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'honeymoon_score: 92 romance_score: 90 privacy_score: 92 luxury_score: 94 Recommended: Honeymoon itinerary should NOT contain more than: 2 major activities/day. Prefer: Tiger Nest + slow valley over many temples. Recommended hotel areas:', 1628),
  ('paro', 20, 'luxury-travel', 'LUXURY TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'luxury_score: 94 Recommended: Luxury should primarily increase:', 1629),
