  ('macau', 32, 'travel-agent-insights', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS', 'What inexperienced planners often do wrong', NULL, '', 2150),
  ('macau', 32, 'travel-agent-insights', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS', 'What an experienced planner does differently', NULL, 'SENADO_SQUARE_AND_HISTORIC_CENTRE + COTAI_STRIP_AND_LIGHT_SHOWS + TAIPA_VILLAGE_AND_PORTUGUESE_EGG_TARTS rather than maximum destination count.', 2151),
  ('macau', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', NULL, NULL, 'IF: trip_length <= 3 nights THEN: prioritize_SENADO_SQUARE_AND_RUINS_OF_ST_PAULS + COTAI_STRIP_MEGA_RESORTS + TAIPA_VILLAGE_AND_COLOANE_ISLAND Reason: Very short stays gain more value from properly experiencing core UNESCO historic sites, futuristic Cotai integrated resorts, and charm-filled southern island villages than losing time to distant cross-border regional moves. IF: trip_length >= 5 nights AND: traveler_interest == FIRST_TIME_MACAU THEN: prioritize_HISTORIC_CENTRE_UNESCO + COTAI_RESORT_ATTRACTIONS + TAIPA_VILLAGE + COLOANE_ISLAND_OR_HONG_KONG_DAY_TRIP Reason: This gives a balanced introduction to colonial stone heritage, world-class entertainment, preserved Macanese villages, and seamless Pearl River Delta cross-border excursions. IF: trip_length >= 7 nights AND: traveler_interest == FIRST_TIME_MACAU THEN: prefer_CENTRAL_MACAU_CORE + COLOANE_COASTAL_RETREAT + DAY_TRIPS_TO_HONG_KONG_AND_ZHUHAI_VIA_HZMB AND: use_FREE_SHUTTLES_LRT_AND_CROSS_BORDER_HIGH_SPEED_BUSES Reason: Mega-resorts, historic Portuguese plazas, coastal nature trails, and HZMB bridge connections to Hong Kong offer distinct regional insights into the Greater Bay Area. IF: trip_type == HONEYMOON THEN: prioritize_COTAI_LUXURY_SUITE_HOTELS + PENINSULA_HERITAGE_STAYS + PRIVATE_PERFORMANCE_LAKE_CABANA AND: increase_BOUTIQUE_STAYS + ROOFTOP_DINING + LUXURY_SPA + PORTUGUESE_WINE_TASTING + COUPLE_EXPERIENCES Reason: Macau''s romantic routes mix ultra-luxury waterfront suites, Michelin-starred fine dining, rooftop cocktails overlooking glowing skylines, and quiet walks along cobblestone Portuguese lanes. IF: traveler_type == FAMILY THEN: prioritize_STUDIO_CITY_ENTERTAINMENT + MACAU_SCIENCE_CENTER + GIANT_PANDA_PAVILION AND: include_COTAI_GONDOLA_RIDES + GOLDEN_REEL_FERRIS_WHEEL + EGG_TART_MAKING_WORKSHOP AND: reduce_CASINO_FLOOR_WALKS + LONG_CONTINUOUS_TRANSFERS Reason: Macau has exceptional family sights, including indoor skydiving, planetariums, giant panda habitats, cable cars, and interactive dessert workshops. IF: traveler_type == LUXURY THEN: prefer_THE_RITZ_CARLTON_MACAU + MORPHEUS_HOTEL + WINN_PALACE_SUITES AND: increase_PRIVATE_GUIDES + MICHELIN_THREE_STAR_DINING + PRIVATE_MPV_TRANSFERS + VIP_SHOW_BOXES + SPA Reason: Macau high-end travel relies on world-record numbers of Forbes Five-Star resorts, multi-course Michelin fine dining, luxury MPV airport transfers, and private fountain-view suite stays. IF: traveler_type == BUDGET THEN: prefer_FREE_RESORT_SHUTTLES + PUBLIC_BUSES + WALKING + BUDGET_STREET_FOOD_STALLS AND: book_FREE_MUSEUM_DAYS_EARLY AND: balance_PAID_ATTRACTIONS_WITH_FREE_RUINS_OF_ST_PAULS + SENADO_SQUARE_WALKS + RESORT_WATER_SHOWS Reason: Macau can be accessed affordably using free hotel shuttle buses, local pork chop bun stalls, free UNESCO public spaces, and free casino light and fountain spectacles. IF: traveler_interest == CULTURE_AND_HERITAGE THEN: prioritize_RUINS_OF_ST_PAULS + A_MA_TEMPLE + SENADO_SQUARE + MANDARINS_HOUSE AND: include_COLONIAL_PORTUGUESE_ARCHITECTURE + MACANESE_HERITAGE + LOCAL_FESTIVALS Reason: These sights showcase Macau''s unique East-meets-West heritage, mixing Chinese maritime folk traditions with 400 years of Portuguese colonial history. IF: traveler_interest == ART_AND_ARCHITECTURE THEN: prefer_MORPHEUS_ARCHITECTURE + MACAU_MUSEUM_OF_ART + TAIPA_HOUSES_MUSEUM + ST_DOMINICS_BAROQUE AND: include_CONTEMPORARY_RESORT_GALLERIES + HISTORIC_COLONIAL_RENEWAL + FUTURISTIC_FAIRMONT_DESIGN Reason: This route contrasts 17th-century Baroque church facades with Zaha Hadid-designed free-form exoskeleton towers and world-class contemporary resort art displays. IF: traveler_interest == GASTRONOMY THEN: prefer_PORTUGUESE_EGG_TARTS + MACANESE_AFRICAN_CHICKEN + PORTUGUESE_BACALHAU + MINCHI_STALLS AND: include_PORK_CHOP_BUNS + TAIPA_VILLAGE_BISTROS + MICHELIN_FINE_DINING Reason: Macau dining spans iconic warm egg tarts, crispy pork buns, unique UNESCO-recognized Macanese fusion cuisine, and elite Michelin-starred gastronomy. IF: traveler_interest == NATURE_AND_WILDLIFE THEN: prioritize_COLOANE_GIANT_PANDA_PAVILION + HAC_SA_BEACH + GUIA_HILL_PARK + TAIPA_GRANDE_HILL AND: do_not_treat_MANICURED_RESORT_GARDENS_AND_SOUTHERN_ISLAND_COASTAL_TRAILS_AS_IDENTICAL Reason: Resort gardens offer manicured fountains and displays, while Coloane''s trails and beaches feature natural greenery, coastal views, and wildlife habitats. IF: traveler_interest == SHOPPING THEN: prioritize_THE_SHOPPES_AT_VENETIAN_AND_FOUR_SEASONS + ONE_CENTRAL_MACAU + RUA_DO_CUNHA_TAIPA + SENADO_SQUARE_BAZAAR AND: include_PORTUGUESE_WINE_SHOPS + PASTRY_BAKERIES + LOCAL_HANDICRAFTS Reason: Rua do Cunha offers local almond cookies and snacks, Macau Peninsula shops supply imported Portuguese goods, and Cotai mega-malls feature ultra-luxury global fashion. IF: traveler_interest == SAUNA_AND_WELLNESS THEN: choose_LUXURY_RESORT_SPAS + TRADITIONAL_CHINESE_FOOT_REFLEXOLOGY + HYDROTHERAPY_SANCTUARIES AND: do_not_treat_TRADITIONAL_TCM_MASSAGE_AND_MODERN_RESORT_HOTEL_SPAS_AS_IDENTICAL Reason: Macau wellness ranges from traditional local foot reflexology to Forbes Five-Star holistic spa retreats overlooking integrated resort skylines. IF: traveler_interest == PHOTOGRAPHY THEN: prioritize_RUINS_OF_ST_PAULS + TRAVESSA_DA_PAIXAO + SENADO_SQUARE_PAVEMENT + WYNN_PALACE_PERFORMANCE_LAKE AND: prioritize_GOLDEN_HOUR + BLUE_HOUR + CLEAR_AIR_DAYS Reason: These sites produce stunning visual contrasts between glowing neon resort skylines, pastel Portuguese colonial facades, and historic stone ruins. IF: trip_length <= 5 nights THEN: prefer_MAXIMUM_ONE_OR_TWO_BASES AND: avoid_EXCESSIVE_HOTEL_CHANGES Reason: Border transit, large resort walking distances, and airport/ferry transfers consume valuable sightseeing hours. IF: route == MACAU_PENINSULA_TO_COLOANE_OR_HONG_KONG THEN: prefer_DIRECT_RESORT_SHUTTLES_LRT_OR_HZMB_CROSS_BORDER_BUSES_OVER_MULTIPLE_LOCAL_BUS_TRANSFERS Reason: Direct transfers eliminate transit confusion and save energy for exploring historic districts and coastal trails. IF: traveler_type == SENIOR OR: traveler_mobility == LIMITED THEN: prefer_ACCESSIBLE_RESORT_HOTELS + LRT_WITH_ELEVATORS + PRIVATE_MPV + MACAU_TOWER_ELEVATOR_DECKS AND: reduce_EXCESSIVE_COBBLESTONE_STEPS + MOUNT_FORTRESS_INCLINES + EXTREME_SUMMER_HUMIDITY_WALKS Reason: High historic stone steps and steep cobblestone hills cause fatigue; elevators, private MPVs, and flat resort promenades ease travel. IF: traveler_uses_WHEELCHAIR THEN: prefer_VERIFIED_ACCESSIBLE_RESORTS + MODERN_LRT_STATIONS + ACCESSIBLE_COTAI_STRIP_ROUTES + MACAU_TOWER_DECKS AND: do_not_assume_HISTORIC_COBBLESTONE_ALLEYWAYS + ANCIENT_FORTRESSES + OLD_TOWN_BUILDINGS_ARE_STEP_FREE Reason: Major modern integrated resorts and observation decks are fully accessible, but historic cobblestone streets, temple thresholds, and fortresses present physical barriers. IF: weather == EXTREME_SUMMER_HEAT AND: region == MACAU_TERRITORY THEN: prioritize_EARLY_MORNING_HERITAGE_VISITS + AIR_CONDITIONED_RESORT_MALLS_AND_MUSEUMS + EVENING_FOUNTAIN_SHOWS AND: reduce_MIDDAY_UNSHADED_STREET_EXPOSURE Reason: Macau summer temps exceed 33°C (91°F) with intense humidity; early starts and indoor resort breaks maintain comfort. IF: weather == HEAVY_SMOG_OR_RAIN THEN: increase_MACAU_MUSEUM + GRAND_PRIX_MUSEUM + INDOOR_RESORT_ENTERTAINMENT + MALL_DINING AND: reduce_MACAU_TOWER_OUTDOOR_DECKS + OUTDOOR_HERITAGE_PROMENADES Reason: Indoor museums, resort theater shows, covered shopping arcades, and tea houses remain excellent regardless of outdoor rain or mist. IF: traveler_interest == FIRST_TIME_MACAU THEN: prioritize_SENADO_SQUARE + RUINS_OF_ST_PAULS + COTAI_STRIP_RESORTS + TAIPA_VILLAGE AND: add_ONE_OF_COLOANE_VILLAGE_MACAU_TOWER_OR_GRAND_PRIX_MUSEUM AND: include_ONE_SIGNATURE_PORTUGUESE_EGG_TART_OR_MACANESE_DINING_EXPERIENCE Reason: This structure provides a comprehensive introduction to Macau''s premier UNESCO heritage and modern sights alongside authentic local food culture. IF: traveler_interest == CULTURE_AND_RELAXATION_BALANCE THEN: allocate_60_TO_70_PERCENT_TO_CORE_SIGHTSEEING AND: allocate_REMAINING_TIME_TO_TEA_HOUSES + VILLAGE_CAFES + SPAS + ROOFTOP_LOUNGES + SHOPPING + FREE_TIME', 2152),
  ('macau', 34, 'destination-scoring', 'DESTINATION SCORING', NULL, NULL, '| Factor | Score | | ------------------ | ----: | | Family | 94 | | Honeymoon | 94 | | Luxury | 98 | | Budget | 78 | | Adventure | 83 | | Culture | 95 | | Food | 97 | | Shopping | 96 | | Nightlife | 95 | | Relaxation | 89 | | Nature | 79 | | Accessibility | 91 | | Safety | 88 | | First-time visitor | 96 | | Photography | 96 |', 2153),
  ('macau', 35, 'final-travel-agent-verdict', 'FINAL TRAVEL AGENT VERDICT', NULL, NULL, 'Best traveler profiles: 1. Honeymoon / romantic traveler (Wynn Palace Suites, Banyan Tree Macau, Private Performance Lake Viewing, Taipa Village Dining) 2. First-time Asia / Greater China traveler 3. Culture / heritage traveler (Ruins of St. Paul''s, A-Ma Temple, Senado Square, Mandarin''s House, Na Tcha Temple) 4. Macanese architecture & history traveler (Colonial Portuguese facades, Southern Chinese temple design, Guia Fortress, Taipa Houses Museum) 5. Luxury / architectural design traveler (Morpheus Hotel, Grand Lisboa Palace, The Ritz-Carlton Macau, Wynn Palace, Macau Tower) 6. Photography traveler (Ruins of St. Paul''s stone facade, Travessa da Paixão pastel lanes, Cotai Strip neon skyline, Coloane Village seafront) 7. Food / gastronomy traveler (Portuguese Egg Tarts, Macanese African Chicken, Bacalhau, Minchi, Pork Chop Buns, Michelin-starred dining) 8. Family traveler (Studio City Water Park, Macao Science Center, Giant Panda Pavilion, Golden Reel Ferris Wheel, Skypark Macau Tower) 9. Modern art & urban lifestyle traveler (Macao Museum of Art, Art Macao exhibitions, Taipa Village cafes, Cotai entertainment venues) 10. Budget / independent traveler (Free Resort Shuttle Bus Network, Macau LRT, Historic District Walking Tours, Local Street Food Stalls) Best duration: 3–5 nights 1–2 nights: Best for ONE primary focus such as Historic Centre of Macao UNESCO Core + Cotai Strip Mega-Resort express trip. 3–4 nights: Best for TWO major bases/focuses such as Macau Peninsula Heritage & Dining + Cotai Strip & Taipa/Coloane Village Islands. 5–6 nights: Excellent for Macau Peninsula + Cotai Strip + Taipa Village + Coloane Nature Trails & Giant Panda Pavilion + Day trip to Hong Kong via HZMB. 7–8 nights: Best for deep regional Greater Bay Area travel, Hengqin Port cross-border excursions, Zhuhai coastal tours, or high-speed transit connections to Hong Kong/Shenzhen. Best season: YEAR-ROUND Autumn (Oct – Dec): CRISP_AIR + COMFORTABLE_TEMPERATURES + OPTIMAL_CLEAR_SKIES + MACAO_INTERNATIONAL_FIREWORKS_DISPLAY_CONTEST + MACAO_GRAND_PRIX. Spring (March – May): PLEASANT_WEATHER + PARK_BLOOMS + CANAL_AND_COASTAL_STROLLS + HISTORIC_VILLAGE_WALKS. Summer (June – August): COTAI_WATER_PARKS + EVENING_RESORT_LIGHT_SHOWS + INDOOR_MUSEUMS + AIR_CONDITIONED_MEGA_MALLS. Winter (Jan – Feb): FESTIVE_LUNAR_NEW_YEAR_LIGHTS + STEAMING_MACANESE_FUSION_CUISINE + FEWER_HUMIDITY_EXTREMES + CULTURAL_HERITAGE_EVENTS. Macao Government Tourism Office guidance treats the territory as year-round: autumn is world-famous for comfortable temperatures, clear skies, and major international events like the Macao Grand Prix; spring for mild coastal weather; summer for mega-resort entertainment and water parks; and winter for festive street illumination and hot local Macanese cuisine. Best hotel strategy: Choose accommodation according to transit convenience, atmosphere, and trip purpose. For first-time visitors: COTAI_STRIP_OR_CENTRAL_PENINSULA (Cotai Strip integrated resorts or Senado Square / Nam Van Lake area) for direct walking access to top attractions and skylines. For heritage / village charm: TAIPA_VILLAGE_OR_COLOANE (Boutique hotels near Taipa Houses or Coloane Village) for authentic local living, historic alleys, and bakery culture. For luxury & modern art: COTAI_STRIP / NAPE_DISTRICT selectively according to fine dining, performance lake views, and holistic resort spas. Avoid unnecessary hotel changes within central Macau districts; short taxi rides, free resort shuttles, and the Macau LRT serve the Macau Peninsula, Taipa, and Cotai efficiently without relocating. Best transportation: Use: Macau transportation should primarily be treated as: MACAU_LRT_AND_FREE_RESORT_SHUTTLES_FOR_COTAI_AND_PORTS + WALKING_FOR_HISTORIC_UNESCO_CENTRE + HZMB_EXPRESS_BUSES_OR_FERRIES_FOR_CROSS_BORDER_TRIPS + TAXIS_FOR_LATE_NIGHT_OR_DIRECT_ISLAND_TRANSFERS Must-do for first-time visitor: Macau should not be reduced to casino gaming floors alone; official tourism positions HISTORIC_UNESCO_SITES + FUTURISTIC_RESORT_ARCHITECTURE + COLONIAL_ISLAND_VILLAGES + MACANESE_FUSION_GASTRONOMY + WORLD_CLASS_ENTERTAINMENT as core territory pillars. Don''t-do: Biggest advantage: Unrivaled concentration of UNESCO World Heritage colonial sites, futuristic resort architecture, world-famous Macanese gastronomy, and seamless regional transit integration. Macau combines a 17th-century stone facade (Ruins of St. Paul''s), iconic Portuguese cobblestone plazas (Senado Square), preserved coastal fishing villages (Coloane), and dynamic modern architecture (Morpheus) within a compact, easily navigable territory. Official tourism highlights the unique East-meets-West heritage fusion, rich performing arts, accessible HZMB bridge links to Hong Kong, and vibrant local culinary culture, catering to diverse travel styles. Biggest disadvantage: Hilly historic topography, strict advance-ticketing requirements during peak holidays, and severe seasonal humidity/typhoon extremes. Navigating sprawling integrated resorts and steep historic stone streets requires significant physical stamina, summer brings intense heat and rain while typhoon season can disrupt ferry and outdoor activities, and high peak visitor arrivals require advance planning across major venues. Overall destination score: 94/100', 2154),
  ('macau', 36, 'data-quality', 'DATA QUALITY', NULL, NULL, 'information_completeness: 97/100 last_updated: 2026-09-02 last_verified: WEB_VERIFIED verified_by: MACAO GOVERNMENT TOURISM OFFICE (MGTO) / CULTURAL AFFAIRS BUREAU MACAO / STATISTICS AND CENSUS SERVICE (DSEC) / MACAO LIGHT RAPID TRANSIT CORPORATION / OFFICIAL HERITAGE VENUES sources: IMPORTANT: Macau Tower admission passes, House of Dancing Water show tickets, HZMB express bus bookings, museum entry, and top Michelin restaurant reservations must NOT be treated as permanently valid. Major attractions and cross-border transport platforms have real-name registration and advance timed-entry rules; current slot availability must be verified online. Macau LRT and Free Resort Shuttle Buses are the standard efficiency choices, but real-time schedules and cross-border customs check rules should be verified on official booking platforms for actual travel dates. Macau''s climate varies significantly by season: SPRING and AUTUMN bring mild, comfortable days ideal for outdoor heritage citywalks, village visits, and coastal trips. SUMMER brings high heat (exceeding 33°C/91°F), high humidity, and occasional heavy rain/typhoons, requiring early morning outings and air-conditioned venue breaks. WINTER brings damp, cool temperatures, requiring warm layered wear for outdoor waterfront walks and open-air resort lake shows. Accessible tourism infrastructure is available across modern Macau LRT stations, major integrated resorts, airports, ferry terminals, and primary paved walkways, but historic cobblestone streets, high temple thresholds (*Menkan*), and ancient fortress inclines are rarely step-free. Macau should primarily be treated as: SPRING/AUTUMN: SENADO_SQUARE + RUINS_OF_ST_PAULS + TAIPA_VILLAGE + COLOANE_COASTAL_WALKS + HISTORIC_HERITAGE_TOURS SUMMER: RESORT_WATER_PARKS + MACAU_TOWER + EVENING_FOUNTAIN_SHOWS + MUSEUM_VISITS + AIR_CONDITIONED_MALLS WINTER: MACANESE_FUSION_DINING + INDOOR_EXHIBITIONS + COLOANE_PANDA_PAVILION + LIGHT_FESTIVAL_SHOWS Macaotourism.gov.mo, TravelChinaGuide, Macau LRT Official, and individual venue reservation portals should be treated as primary sources for operational information. This dataset should be refreshed regularly before production use.', 2155),
  ('lake-mansarovar', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Spring', NULL, 'months: March April May weather: March remains extremely cold and generally unsuitable for pilgrimage travel. April begins warming but nights remain severely cold and snow can still affect higher routes. May marks the practical opening of the main Kailash travel season, with improving roads, longer daylight, clearer skies, and better trekking conditions. crowd_level: VERY_LOW → MEDIUM_HIGH price_level: LOW_VALUE → MEDIUM overall_score: 43–72 recommended: PARTIALLY_TRUE reason: May is one of the strongest early-season periods for Kailash pilgrimage, Mansarovar, acclimatization, photography, and the Kora, while March and much of April remain too harsh or operationally restricted for standard pilgrimage planning. Best for: May and June generally offer comparatively dry conditions and good visibility, although snow can remain on the higher Kora sections. IMPORTANT: For Indian citizens using the Government of India KMY programme, the official 2026 departures begin only in June.', 2156),
  ('lake-mansarovar', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Summer', NULL, 'months: June July August weather: June generally provides some of the most favourable pilgrimage conditions, with relatively mild daytime temperatures and comparatively clear skies. July and August are warmer but bring greater monsoon influence, cloud, rain, and more variable high-altitude conditions. crowd_level: MEDIUM_HIGH → HIGH price_level: MEDIUM → HIGH overall_score: 62–70 recommended: true reason: This is the CORE_OPERATIONAL_SEASON for the official Indian Kailash Manasarovar Yatra and one of the most practical periods for completing Mansarovar visits and the Kailash Kora. Excellent for: June usually offers the strongest weather balance. July and August remain suitable but rain, cloud, slippery trails, landslide / road disruption risk, and rapidly changing mountain weather reduce reliability. The Ministry of External Affairs schedules the 2026 Government of India Kailash Manasarovar Yatra from June through August.', 2157),
  ('lake-mansarovar', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Autumn', NULL, 'months: September October November weather: September is generally cool, comparatively dry, and often exceptionally clear, making it one of the strongest weather periods around Kailash. October becomes substantially colder, particularly at night, with increasing snow risk. November returns to severe winter-like conditions. crowd_level: LOW → VERY_LOW price_level: MEDIUM → LOW_VALUE overall_score: 44–79 recommended: PARTIALLY_TRUE reason: September can provide some of the year''s best visibility and comparatively stable trekking conditions, while early October can still work for permitted organised travel. Best for: September is especially strong because post-monsoon skies are frequently clearer and visitor pressure is lower than during the main summer pilgrimage period. However: IMPORTANT: Indian Government KMY operating dates do not necessarily extend into September or October. For 2026, the official MEA programme concludes in August, so permit and route eligibility must be checked separately.', 2158),
  ('lake-mansarovar', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Winter', NULL, 'months: December January February weather: Extremely cold, dry, windy, and severe at high altitude. Lake Mansarovar can freeze, heavy snow affects mountain routes, and temperatures around Kailash can remain far below freezing. crowd_level: VERY_LOW price_level: VERY_LOW_VALUE overall_score: 35–40 recommended: false reason: Winter should generally NOT be treated as a normal Kailash Mansarovar pilgrimage season. Major limitations include: The normal organised pilgrimage and trekking season effectively ends before deep winter. Winter travel should therefore not receive a high destination score simply because crowds are extremely low.', 2159),
  ('lake-mansarovar', 10, 'budget-strategy', 'BUDGET STRATEGY', NULL, NULL, 'Where money can be saved: Where saving money is usually NOT recommended: Travel-agent rule: For Kailash Mansarovar, **MANDATORY_TIBET_PERMITS + GRADUAL_ACCLIMATIZATION + LICENSED_TIBETAN_GUIDE + COMPREHENSIVE_ALTITUDE_INSURANCE should be evaluated together**. For short stays, prioritize **HELICOPTER_ROUTE_VIA_HILSA + LAKE_MANSAROVAR_SIGHTSEEING + DARCHEN_KAILASH_VIEW**. For longer stays, add **3_DAY_KAILASH_PARIKRAMA + CHARAN_SPARSH_EXCURSION + LHASA_AND_EVEREST_BASE_CAMP_OVERLAND** rather than rushing direct border routes.', 2160),
  ('lake-mansarovar', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Family', 'family', 'Kailash Mansarovar’s primary gateways are Kathmandu’s Tribhuvan International Airport (KTM) or Lhasa Gonggar Airport (LXA), followed by high-altitude border transitions via Kyirong (Rasuwagadhi) or Purang (Hilsa). For families traveling with devout elders or older children, pre-booked overland tourist coaches or private 4WD SUVs provide the safest and most reliable transportation across the Tibetan Plateau. When transitioning across high-altitude border points, vehicle changes are mandatory: Nepal-side private cars/coaches drop passengers at border checkpoints (Rasuwagadhi/Hilsa), where pilgrims clear customs and transfer into official Tibetan tourist buses or private SUVs managed by licensed Tibetan guide teams.', 2161),
  ('lake-mansarovar', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Honeymoon', 'honeymoon', 'Opt for pre-arranged private SUV/4WD transfers (e.g., Toyota Land Cruisers) starting directly from Lhasa or Kathmandu, paired with high-end hotel stays in base cities and private logistics handling across Tibet. For multi-destination spiritual honeymoon itineraries, combine: PRIVATE_LHOSE_OR_KHATMANDU_ARRIVAL + PRIVATE_4WD_SUV_OVERLAND_TRANSIT + PRIVATE_GUIDE_AND_HELICOPTER_BORDER_EXPRESS (Simikot–Hilsa sector) + PRIVATE_HOTEL_RETREATS_IN_PURANG_AND_DARCHEN.', 2162),
  ('lake-mansarovar', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Luxury', 'luxury', 'Utilize pre-booked chartered helicopter transfers and domestic flights connecting Nepalgunj to Simikot and Hilsa, bypassing days of rough mountain driving on the Nepal side. For exclusive high-altitude Kailash circuits, combine: VIP_KATHMANDU_MEET_AND_GREET + CHARTERED_HELICOPTER_TRANSIT (Simikot–Hilsa corridor) + PRIVATE_SUPPORT_TRUCK_WITH_MEDIC_AND_CHEF + HIGH_END_4WD_SUV_FLEET_IN_TIBET.', 2163),
  ('lake-mansarovar', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Budget', 'budget', 'Take advantage of authorized fixed-departure group overland buses running directly from Kathmandu to the Kyirong border: For local circuit transit, pilgrims use eco-friendly park buses designated for the Lake Mansarovar circuit and Darchen-to-Yam Dwar transfers.', 2164),
  ('lake-mansarovar', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Senior', 'senior', 'Prioritize helicopter-assisted entry routes (Kathmandu–Nepalgunj–Simikot–Hilsa) or slow-paced overland driving routes with built-in multi-night stopovers (Kyirong, Saga) to ensure gradual acclimatization. When booking high-altitude overland transport, secure front-row seats in spacious AC tourist coaches, hire dedicated personal porters (*Sherpas*) at border crossings and Parikrama trails, and select accommodations with ground-level access and supplemental oxygen supplies.', 2165),
  ('lake-mansarovar', 18, 'family-travel', 'FAMILY TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'child_friendly_score: 68 best_ages: Rules: For young children: Prefer: Avoid:', 2166),
  ('lake-mansarovar', 19, 'honeymoon-travel', 'HONEYMOON TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'honeymoon_score: 78 romance_score: 82 privacy_score: 75 luxury_score: 70 Recommended: Honeymoon itineraries should generally stay at: 1–2 major experiences/day. Prefer: PRIVATE_SUV + GRADUAL_ACCLIMATIZATION + LAKESHORE_MEDITATION + MONASTERY_VISITS + PRIVATE_DINING + FREE_TIME over: Exhausting high-pace trekking with minimal physical rest.', 2167),
  ('lake-mansarovar', 20, 'luxury-travel', 'LUXURY TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'luxury_score: 72 Recommended:', 2168),
  ('lake-mansarovar', 21, 'adventure', 'ADVENTURE', NULL, NULL, 'adventure_score: 98 Kailash Mansarovar offers extreme high-altitude adventure across trans-Himalayan mountain passes, sacred trekking kora routes, and rugged plateau wilderness. Adventure experiences: Best regions: KAILASH_KORA_VALLEYS + MANSAROVAR_BASIN + DOLMA_LA_PASS + ZANDA_EARTH_FOREST + PURANG_VALLEY', 2169),
  ('lake-mansarovar', 22, 'senior-travel', 'SENIOR TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'senior_suitability: 74 walking_intensity: LOW–MEDIUM for Lake Mansarovar drive, Yam Dwar visit, Purang market, and Chiu Gompa base HIGH–EXTREME for 52 km Parikrama trek, Dolma La Pass climb, and Charan Sparsh hike Rules: Kailash Mansarovar works exceptionally well for seniors as a: SACRED_PILGRIMAGE + LAKE_RITUALS + MOUNTAIN_DARSHAN + MONASTERY_VISITS + SPIRITUAL_RETIREMENT destination.', 2170),
  ('lake-mansarovar', 23, 'accessibility', 'ACCESSIBILITY', NULL, NULL, 'wheelchair_accessibility: VERY LOW TO NON-EXISTENT ACROSS HIGH-ALTITUDE TREKKING TRAILS AND MONASTERIES MODERATE IN MODERN LHASA HOTELS, AIRPORTS, AND OFFICIAL OVERLAND TOURIST BUSES public_transport_accessibility: NOT APPLICABLE; INTERNATIONAL TOURISTS MUST USE AUTHORIZED TOURIST CARS / BUSES hotel_accessibility: MUST_BE_VERIFIED_PER_HOTEL attraction_accessibility: MUST_BE_VERIFIED_PER_ATTRACTION Rule: Never assume step-free or paved access across remote high-altitude Himalayan mountain terrain or ancient monasteries. Additional notes:', 2171),
  ('lake-mansarovar', 24, 'food', 'FOOD', NULL, NULL, 'Kailash Mansarovar is particularly strong for: Food experiences: Family: Prioritize soft khichdi, rice with dal, chapati, vegetable soups, porridge, and familiar warm teas. Honeymoon: Choose private dining tent setups with hot multi-course vegetarian meals served by expedition cooks. Luxury: Include custom expedition chefs preparing hot fresh Indian and Western vegetarian menus with espresso/beverage stations. Budget: Rely on simple local Tibetan tea house noodle soups, tsampa, instant noodles, and basic dal bhat.', 2172),
  ('lake-mansarovar', 25, 'shopping', 'SHOPPING', NULL, NULL, 'Strong categories: Luxury shopping: Prefer: Budget: Prefer: Travel-agent rule: Use DARCHEN / MANSAROVAR LAKESHORE for HOLY_WATER_PRAYER_FLAGS_AND_PEBBLES, PURANG_BORDER_MARKET for YAK_WOOL_TURQUOISE_JEWELRY_AND_CRAFTS, and LHASA_BARKHOR_STREET for AUTHENTIC_THANGKAS_SINGING_BOWLS_AND_FINE_ANTIQUES.', 2173),
  ('lake-mansarovar', 26, 'nightlife', 'NIGHTLIFE', NULL, NULL, 'nightlife_level: 15 Suitable for: Best areas: Evening activities: Darchen offers basic pilgrim tea shops, Lake Mansarovar provides silent lakeshore stargazing, and high camps offer peaceful rest under the stars. Honeymoon travelers should generally prefer: DARK_SKY_STARGAZING + HEATED_TENT_TEA_SESSIONS + MOONLIT_MOUNTAIN_VIEWS + QUIET_MEDITATION over: Late-night socializing or town walking. Travel-agent rule: Position Kailash Mansarovar as a **SPIRITUAL_PILGRIMAGE + HIGH_ALTITUDE_TREKKING + SACRED_LAKE_RITUALS + HIMALAYAN_STARGAZING DESTINATION**, with urban nightlife virtually non-existent in favor of early rest and spiritual peace."', 2174),
  ('lake-mansarovar', 28, 'sample-itinerary-patterns', 'SAMPLE ITINERARY PATTERNS', '3 NIGHTS', NULL, '### Day 1 Arrival at Ngari Gunsa Airport (NGQ) (Shiquanhe / Ali Airport) → Direct flight arrival (typically early morning flight from Lhasa, Chengdu, or Kashgar) → Oxygen-equipped private SUV transfer or airport shuttle to Shiquanhe / Darchen → Hotel check-in, immediate rest, hydration, and compulsory high-altitude acclimatization Afternoon: → Slow walk around Darchen base settlement (4,670 m) to adjust to atmospheric pressure → Initial view of Mount Kailash’s south face from lower valley observation points → Briefing with licensed Tibetan guide on safety protocols, pulse oximetry, and altitude sickness prevention Evening: → Nourishing vegetarian welcome dinner featuring hot lentil soup (*Dal Bhat*) or vegetable *Thukpa* → Quiet evening walk around Darchen prayer wheel corridors under clear Himalayan skies → Early sleep with optional supplemental oxygen support in hotel room NGQ serves as Western Tibet''s primary high-altitude air gateway at 4,274 m, providing a fast aerial bypass over long multi-day overland drives from Lhasa. ### Day 2 Morning: Breakfast → Morning drive (35 km) from Darchen to the sacred shores of Lake Mansarovar (4,590 m) → Performing morning holy water dip (*Snan*) and lakeside *Puja* ceremonies at Chiu Gompa spot → Visit to Chiu Gompa Monastery built into the cliffside overlooking Lake Mansarovar and Rakshas Tal Afternoon: → Scenic vehicle drive past Rakshas Tal (the Ghost Lake) with photographic stops along G219 → Hot vegetarian lunch at a lakeshore tea house → Traditional Tibetan butter tea session while observing wild black-necked cranes and lakeshore panorama Evening: → Return drive to Darchen base hotel → Rest and final medical gear check (pulse oximeter, trekking poles, thermal layers) ahead of Parikrama → Traditional Tibetan vegetarian dinner at base hotel → Hotel ### Day 3 Recommended first-time option: → Early morning drive from Darchen to Yam Dwar (Tarboche / Flag Pole Gateway) → Pass through Yam Dwar (Gateway of Salvation) to officially begin the sacred Kailash Kora Afternoon: → Trekking (12 km, 5–6 hours) through Lha Chu Valley toward Dirapuk Monastery (4,080 m to 5,050 m) → Magnificent close-up views of Mount Kailash’s steep North Face (*Charan Sparsh* view point) → Check-in at basic Dirapuk Monastery guesthouse or expedition tents Evening: → Warm vegetarian khichdi or noodle dinner in common dining room / tent → Witnessing sunset over Mount Kailash’s North Face as golden light hits the snow wall → High-altitude stargazing under dark Himalayan skies → Guesthouse / High Camp Optional alternative instead of First-Day Parikrama Trek: SPA & WELLNESS / LIGHT SPIRITUAL: → Gentle hot spring soak at Tirthapuri geothermal springs (birthplace of Padmasambhava / Guru Rinpoche) → Guided meditation session along Lake Mansarovar shore with heated tent setup CULTURE / HISTORY: → Day excursion west to Zanda County to explore the ancient cliffside ruins of Guge Kingdom & Tholing Monastery → Photography of the dramatic Zanda Earth Forest landforms SENIOR / EASIER PILGRIMAGE: → Full vehicle circuit drive around Lake Mansarovar (90 km loop eco-bus route) → Extended prayer time at Chiu Gompa and prayer flag offerings at Tarboche Gateway without trekking HONEYMOON / PRIVATE: → Private SUV overland tour through Purang Valley bordering Nepal and India → Private lakeside sunset dining tent with personal expedition chef near Mansarovar FOOD / LOCAL LIFE: → Tibetan culinary immersion tasting fresh *Tsampa*, yak butter tea, fried *Tingmo* bread, and regional momos in Darchen → Meeting local Tibetan nomads (*Drokpas*) and observing yak caravan preparations For only 3 nights, prioritize: NGQ_AIRPORT_ARRIVAL_AND_REST + LAKE_MANSAROVAR_CHIU_GOMPA + YAM_DWAR_TO_DIRAPUK_NORTH_FACE OR NGQ_AIRPORT_ARRIVAL + LAKE_MANSAROVAR_AND_RAKSHAS_TAL + GUGE_KINGDOM_DAY_EXCURSION rather than attempting the complete 3-day 52 km Parikrama over Dolma La Pass (5,630 m), which requires additional trekking days. ### Day 4 Breakfast → Early morning sunrise viewing of Mount Kailash’s golden peaks from Dirapuk or Darchen → Transfer by private SUV from Darchen back to Ngari Gunsa Airport (NGQ) (approx. 3 hours drive) → Departure flight from NGQ to Lhasa, Chengdu, or Kashgar → Onward journey', 2175),
  ('lake-mansarovar', 29, 'six-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 1', NULL, 'Arrival at Ngari Gunsa Airport (NGQ) → Private / pre-arranged permitted transfer → Drive towards Darchen → Best available comfortable hotel / guesthouse check-in → Rest and acclimatization Evening: → Relaxed couple time → Early dinner → Overnight at Darchen', 2176),
  ('lake-mansarovar', 29, 'six-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 2', NULL, 'Breakfast → Lake Manasarovar excursion → Sacred lakeside landscapes → Chiu Gompa area → Couple photography → Prayer / meditation → Rakshastal viewpoints where accessible Evening: → Return towards Darchen → Relax and acclimatize → Overnight at Darchen', 2177),
  ('lake-mansarovar', 29, 'six-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 3', NULL, 'Breakfast → Mount Kailash orientation day → Yam Dwar / Tarboche region → Mount Kailash South Face views → Couple photography → Spiritual experience → Gentle exploration according to altitude response Afternoon: → Return to Darchen → Rest & preparation for Kora Evening: → Early dinner → Overnight at Darchen', 2178),
  ('lake-mansarovar', 29, 'six-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 4', NULL, 'Early Breakfast → Begin Mount Kailash Kora → Transfer towards Kora starting point → Trek towards Dirapuk / Derapuk → Sacred valley landscapes → Mount Kailash western / northern perspectives → Couple pilgrimage experience Evening: → Basic guesthouse accommodation → Overnight around Dirapuk', 2179),
  ('lake-mansarovar', 29, 'six-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 5', NULL, 'Early Breakfast → Most challenging Kora sector → Trek towards Dolma La → Cross the high-altitude pass subject to health, weather and local operating conditions → Continue towards Zuthulpuk Evening: → Rest after trekking → Basic guesthouse accommodation → Overnight around Zuthulpuk', 2180),
  ('lake-mansarovar', 29, 'six-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 6', NULL, 'Breakfast → Complete final section of Kailash Kora → Return towards Darchen Afternoon: → Rest and refresh → Final Mount Kailash views → Couple reflection / spiritual leisure Evening: → Farewell dinner → Overnight at Darchen', 2181),
  ('lake-mansarovar', 29, 'six-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 7', NULL, 'Early Breakfast → Hotel checkout → Transfer towards Ngari Gunsa Airport (NGQ) → Departure', 2182),
  ('lake-mansarovar', 30, 'six-nights-family-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 1', NULL, 'Arrival at Ngari Gunsa Airport (NGQ) → Pre-arranged permitted vehicle transfer → Drive towards Darchen → Hotel / guesthouse check-in → Complete rest and acclimatization Evening: → Light dinner → Family rest → Overnight at Darchen', 2183),
  ('lake-mansarovar', 30, 'six-nights-family-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 2', NULL, 'Breakfast → Lake Manasarovar excursion → Sacred lake viewpoints → Chiu Gompa area → Family photography → Prayer / meditation → Rakshastal viewpoints where accessible Evening: → Return towards Darchen → Rest → Overnight at Darchen', 2184),
  ('lake-mansarovar', 30, 'six-nights-family-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 3', NULL, 'Breakfast → Mount Kailash sightseeing → Yam Dwar / Tarboche region → Mount Kailash viewpoints → Family spiritual experience → Photography Afternoon: → Return to Darchen → Acclimatization & leisure Evening: → Family dinner → Overnight at Darchen', 2185),
  ('lake-mansarovar', 30, 'six-nights-family-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 4', NULL, 'Breakfast Choose ONE: FAMILY_PILGRIMAGE → Accessible Mount Kailash viewpoints → Yam Dwar region → Prayer / spiritual time → Return to Darchen MANASAROVAR_FOCUS → Lake Manasarovar → Scenic lakeside experience → Chiu Gompa area → Family photography KORA → Begin Kailash Kora only for appropriately prepared and medically suitable family members → Trek towards Dirapuk → Overnight in basic guesthouse', 2186),
  ('lake-mansarovar', 30, 'six-nights-family-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 5', NULL, 'Breakfast For non-trekking families: → Relaxed Darchen day → Mount Kailash landscapes → Local cultural experience → Rest & acclimatization OR For suitable Kora participants: → Dirapuk to Zuthulpuk sector → Dolma La crossing → Overnight around Zuthulpuk', 2187),
  ('lake-mansarovar', 30, 'six-nights-family-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 6', NULL, 'Breakfast → Final Kailash-Manasarovar pilgrimage experience For non-trekkers: → Darchen → Kailash viewpoints → Spiritual / photography time For Kora participants: → Complete final Kora sector → Return to Darchen Evening: → Family reunion → Farewell dinner → Overnight at Darchen', 2188),
  ('lake-mansarovar', 30, 'six-nights-family-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 7', NULL, 'Early Breakfast → Hotel checkout → Transfer towards Ngari Gunsa Airport (NGQ) → Departure', 2189),
  ('lake-mansarovar', 31, 'six-nights-luxury-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 1', NULL, 'Arrival at Ngari Gunsa Airport (NGQ) → Private permitted SUV / premium vehicle transfer → Scenic drive towards Darchen → Best available premium accommodation → Dedicated acclimatization & rest Evening: → Private / quiet dinner → Early rest → Overnight at Darchen', 2190),
  ('lake-mansarovar', 31, 'six-nights-luxury-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 2', NULL, 'Breakfast → Private Lake Manasarovar excursion → Flexible lakeside sightseeing → Chiu Gompa area → Private photography stops → Prayer / meditation → Rakshastal viewpoints where accessible Afternoon: → Scenic private drive → Return towards Darchen Evening: → Premium available dining → Overnight at Darchen', 2191),
  ('lake-mansarovar', 31, 'six-nights-luxury-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 3', NULL, 'Breakfast → Private Mount Kailash orientation → Yam Dwar / Tarboche region → Mount Kailash South Face viewpoints → Private guide → Flexible photography & spiritual stops Afternoon: → Return to Darchen → Rest & Kora preparation Evening: → Early dinner → Overnight at Darchen', 2192),
  ('lake-mansarovar', 31, 'six-nights-luxury-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 4', NULL, 'Early Breakfast → Begin private / supported Kailash Kora → Dedicated guide → Porter / pack-animal support where locally permitted and pre-arranged → Trek towards Dirapuk → Mount Kailash landscapes → Private-paced pilgrimage Evening: → Best available basic Kora-route accommodation → Overnight around Dirapuk', 2193),
  ('lake-mansarovar', 31, 'six-nights-luxury-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 5', NULL, 'Early Breakfast → Supported high-altitude Kora → Dirapuk → Dolma La sector → High-altitude pilgrimage landscapes → Continue towards Zuthulpuk Evening: → Best available basic accommodation → Overnight around Zuthulpuk', 2194),
  ('lake-mansarovar', 31, 'six-nights-luxury-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 6', NULL, 'Breakfast → Complete final Kailash Kora sector → Private vehicle connection back towards Darchen Afternoon: → Rest & recovery → Final Mount Kailash photography → Private spiritual / leisure time Evening: → Farewell dinner → Overnight at Darchen', 2195),
  ('lake-mansarovar', 31, 'six-nights-luxury-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 7', NULL, 'Early Breakfast → Hotel checkout → Private SUV transfer towards Ngari Gunsa Airport (NGQ) → Airport assistance → Departure', 2196),
  ('lake-mansarovar', 32, 'travel-agent-insights', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS', 'What inexperienced planners often do wrong', NULL, '', 2197),
  ('lake-mansarovar', 32, 'travel-agent-insights', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS', 'What an experienced planner does differently', NULL, 'KAILASH_NORTH_FACE_DIRAPUK + LAKE_MANSAROVAR_HOLY_DIP + ACCLIMATIZED_DOLMA_LA_KORA rather than maximum destination count.', 2198),
  ('lake-mansarovar', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', NULL, NULL, 'IF: trip_length <= 3 nights THEN: prioritize_NGQ_AIRPORT_ARRIVAL_AND_REST + LAKE_MANSAROVAR_CHIU_GOMPA + YAM_DWAR_TO_DIRAPUK_NORTH_FACE Reason: Very short stays gain more value from fast aerial entry via Ngari Gunsa Airport (NGQ), immediate acclimatization, experiencing Lake Mansarovar, and viewing the North Face at Dirapuk than losing time to full Kora attempts. IF: trip_length >= 5 nights AND: traveler_interest == FIRST_TIME_KAILASH THEN: prioritize_LAKE_MANSAROVAR + YAM_DWAR + DIRAPUK_NORTH_FACE + DOLMA_LA_PASS + ZUTHULPUK Reason: This gives a balanced introduction to sacred lakes, valley approaches, high mountain passes, and complete 52 km Parikrama trekking. IF: trip_length >= 7 nights AND: traveler_interest == FIRST_TIME_KAILASH THEN: prefer_COMPLETE_KAILASH_KORA + LAKE_MANSAROVAR_FULL_CIRCUIT + GUGE_KINGDOM_AND_THOLING_DETOUR AND: use_4WD_LAND_CRUISER_OR_TOURIST_COACH + HELICOPTER_BORDER_LINK Reason: Sacred mountain passes, ancient cave kingdoms, geothermal springs, and remote trans-Himalayan landscapes offer complete regional spiritual immersion. IF: trip_type == HONEYMOON THEN: prioritize_PRIVATE_4WD_LAND_CRUISER + HELICOPTER_BORDER_TRANSIT + PRIVATE_LAKESIDE_DINING_CAMP AND: increase_PRIVATE_SUITE_STAYS + DARK_SKY_STARGAZING + MONASTERY_BLESSINGS + PRIVATE_SHERPA_CREW Reason: Kailash''s romantic spiritual routes mix private luxury SUV transfers, secluded lakeshore stargazing, private chef setups, and quiet monastic blessings. IF: traveler_type == FAMILY THEN: prioritize_LAKE_MANSAROVAR_ECO_BUS + YAM_DWAR_PHOTOS + DIRAPUK_NORTH_FACE_VIEW AND: include_CHIU_GOMPA_MONASTERY + HORSE_PONY_SUPPORT + TARBOCHE_PRAYER_FLAGS AND: reduce_EXTREME_STRENUOUS_TREKKING + UNACCLIMATIZED_FAST_ASCENTS Reason: Kailash has memorable family pilgrimage sights, including eco-bus lake loops, gentle monastery visits, colorful prayer flag sites, and pony-assisted valley walks. IF: traveler_type == LUXURY THEN: prefer_CHARTERED_HELICOPTER_HILSA_ROUTE + PRIVATE_TOYOTA_LAND_CRUISER_FLEET AND: increase_PRIVATE_GUIDES + DEDICATED_EXPEDITION_CHEF + PRIVATE_DOCTOR_WITH_OXYGEN + HEATED_TENT_SUITES Reason: Kailash high-end travel relies on chartered helicopter border flights, dedicated expedition support trucks, personal medical monitoring, and high-end 4WD fleets. IF: traveler_type == BUDGET THEN: prefer_OVERLAND_GROUP_BUS_VIA_KYIRONG + PUBLIC_ECO_SHUTTLES + ON_FOOT_PARIKRAMA + MONASTERY_DORMITORIES AND: book_GROUP_TIBET_PERMITS_EARLY AND: balance_REQUIRED_PERMIT_COSTS_WITH_SIMPLE_VEGETARIAN_TEAHOUSE_MEALS + SHARED_ACCOMMODATION Reason: Kailash can be accessed affordably by joining fixed-departure group bus tours, sharing permit costs, staying in monastery guesthouses, and trekking fully on foot. IF: traveler_interest == CULTURE_AND_HERITAGE THEN: prioritize_CHIU_GOMPA + DIRAPUK_MONASTERY + ZUTHULPUK_CAVES + GUGE_KINGDOM AND: include_THOLING_MONASTERY + TIBETAN_BUDDHIST_RITUALS + SAGA_DAWA_FESTIVAL Reason: These sites showcase Western Tibet''s concentrated Buddhist monasticism, ancient kingdom cave murals, sacred pilgrim rituals, and multi-faith heritage. IF: traveler_interest == ART_AND_ARCHITECTURE THEN: prefer_GUGE_KINGDOM_RUINS + THOLING_MONASTERY_MURALS + CHIU_GOMPA_CLIFFSIDE_DESIGN + POTALA_PALACE_TRANSIT AND: include_ANCIENT_FRESCOES + MONASTIC_TIMBER_JOINERY + MOUNTAIN_CAVE_ARCHITECTURE Reason: This route contrasts ancient cliffside citadel engineering with 11th-century Buddhist frescoes, monastery stonework, and plateau fortress architecture. IF: traveler_interest == GASTRONOMY THEN: prefer_FRESH_TSAMPA_TASSING + TIBETAN_BUTTER_TEA + HOT_DAL_BHAT + EXPEDITION_VEGETARIAN_BUFFET AND: include_THUKPA_NOODLE_SHOPS + TINGMO_BREAD + HOT_GINGER_LEMON_HONEY_TEA Reason: High-altitude dining spans nourishing lentil soups, warming noodle bowls, Tibetan barley staples, and hot restorative herbal teas. IF: traveler_interest == NATURE_AND_WILDLIFE THEN: prioritize_LAKE_MANSAROVAR + RAKSHAS_TAL + DOLMA_LA_PASS + GAURI_KUND AND: do_not_treat_HIGH_ALTITUDE_SACRED_LAKES_AND_RUGGED_GLACIAL_PASSES_AS_IDENTICAL Reason: Lake basins offer tranquil waters and migratory bird habitats, while mountain passes feature extreme glaciers and bare rock walls. IF: traveler_interest == SHOPPING THEN: prioritize_MANSAROVAR_HOLY_WATER_CONTAINERS + PURANG_BORDER_MARKET + DARCHEN_PRAYER_FLAGS AND: include_TEAHOUSE_CRAFTS + YAK_WOOL_SHAWLS + LHASA_BARKHOR_THANGKAS Reason: Mansarovar provides sacred water and stones, Purang offers border crafts and yak wool, and Lhasa concentrates high-grade thangkas and singing bowls. IF: traveler_interest == SAUNA_AND_WELLNESS THEN: choose_TIRTHAPURI_NATURAL_HOT_SPRINGS + LAKESIDE_MEDITATION + OXYGEN_WELLNESS_STAYS AND: do_not_treat_NATURAL_GEOTHERMAL_SPRINGS_AND_URBAN_HOTEL_SPAS_AS_IDENTICAL Reason: Western Tibet wellness ranges from sacred natural hot springs and high-altitude breathwork to oxygen-enriched hotel rooms. IF: traveler_interest == PHOTOGRAPHY THEN: prioritize_KAILASH_NORTH_FACE_DIRAPUK + MANSAROVAR_MIRROR_REFLECTIONS + DOLMA_LA_PRAYER_FLAGS + ZANDA_EARTH_FOREST AND: prioritize_GOLDEN_HOUR + BLUE_HOUR + DARK_SKY_STARGAZING Reason: These sites produce extraordinary visual contrasts between golden mountain faces, turquoise lake waters, fluttering prayer flags, and clear galaxy skies. IF: trip_length <= 5 nights THEN: prefer_MAXIMUM_ONE_OR_TWO_BASES AND: avoid_EXCESSIVE_HOTEL_CHANGES Reason: Plateau transit times, mandatory acclimatization rests, and high-altitude physical fatigue consume valuable travel hours. IF: route == DARCHEN_TO_KAILASH_KORA THEN: prefer_ECO_SHUTTLE_TO_YAM_DWAR_WITH_PRE_BOOKED_PONY_PORTERS_OVER_UNSUPPORTED_START Reason: Organized shuttle transfers and advance-booked porters eliminate initial trail fatigue and conserve energy for steep pass ascents. IF: traveler_type == SENIOR OR: traveler_mobility == LIMITED THEN: prefer_HELICOPTER_ENTRY_ROUTES + OXYGEN_EQUIPPED_HOTELS + PRIVATE_SUVS + PONY_HORSE_SUPPORT_ON_KORA AND: reduce_STRENUOUS_CLIMBS + UNPAVED_MONASTERY_STEPS + EXTREME_COLD_EXPOSURE Reason: Severe elevation and rough mountain terrain cause extreme fatigue; helicopters, continuous medical oxygen, 4WD vehicles, and ponies enable safe access. IF: traveler_uses_WHEELCHAIR THEN: prefer_PAVED_G219_HIGHWAY_TOUR_VEHICLES + ACCESSIBLE_LHASA_HOTELS + MANSAROVAR_DRIVE_BY_SHUTTLE AND: do_not_assume_HIGH_ALTITUDE_KORA_TRAILS + MOUNTAIN_GUESTHOUSES + ANCIENT_MONASTERIES_ARE_STEP_FREE Reason: Major paved highways and tourist buses accommodate seated travelers, but rugged mountain trails, monastery steps, and high passes present absolute physical barriers. IF: weather == EXTREME_MONSOON_RAIN_OR_SNOW AND: region == HIGH_PASS_DOLMA_LA THEN: prioritize_LOWER_VALLEY_MONASTERY_VISITS + LAKESIDE_DRIVES + BASE_CAMP_STAYS AND: reduce_HIGH_PASS_TREKKING_DURING_GALE_WINDS_OR_BLIZARDS Reason: High-altitude pass weather (5,630 m) can rapidly turn hazardous; lower valley drives and sheltered guesthouse stays maintain safety. IF: weather == SEVERE_ALTITUDE_SICKNESS_SYMPTOMS THEN: increase_PORTABLE_OXYGEN_USAGE + IMMEDIATE_DESCENT_TO_LOWER_ALTITUDE + MEDICAL_MONITORING AND: cancel_HIGH_PASS_CROSSING + HIGH_ALTITUDE_TREKKING Reason: DescENDing to lower elevation (Purang, Saga, or Nepalgunj) is the single most effective treatment for acute mountain sickness (AMS, HAPE, HACE). IF: traveler_interest == FIRST_TIME_KAILASH THEN: prioritize_KAILASH_NORTH_FACE_DIRAPUK + LAKE_MANSAROVAR_CHIU_GOMPA + YAM_DWAR_GATEWAY AND: add_ONE_OF_DOLMA_LA_PASS_TREK_GUGE_KINGDOM_OR_TIRTHAPURI_HOT_SPRINGS AND: include_ONE_SIGNATURE_HOLY_LAKE_DIP_OR_TIBETAN_BUTTER_TEA_EXPERIENCE Reason: This structure provides a comprehensive introduction to Kailash Mansarovar''s premier pilgrimage sights alongside authentic plateau culture. IF: traveler_interest == CULTURE_AND_RELAXATION_BALANCE THEN: allocate_60_TO_70_PERCENT_TO_CORE_PILGRIMAGE_AND_SIGHTSEEING AND: allocate_REMAINING_TIME_TO_LAKESIDE_MEDITATION + HOT_SPRINGS + OXYGEN_REST + TEAHOUSE_VISITS + FREE_TIME', 2199);
INSERT INTO destination_guidance (place_id, section, topic, section_title, heading, audience, body, position) VALUES
  ('lake-mansarovar', 34, 'destination-scoring', 'DESTINATION SCORING', NULL, NULL, '| Factor | Score | | ------------------ | ----: | | Family | 78 | | Honeymoon | 75 | | Luxury | 68 | | Budget | 74 | | Adventure | 96 | | Culture | 98 | | Food | 65 | | Shopping | 62 | | Nightlife | 40 | | Relaxation | 80 | | Nature | 95 | | Accessibility | 55 | | Safety | 72 | | First-time visitor | 85 | | Photography | 97 |', 2200),
  ('lake-mansarovar', 35, 'final-travel-agent-verdict', 'FINAL TRAVEL AGENT VERDICT', NULL, NULL, 'Best traveler profiles: 1. Spiritual / pilgrimage traveler (Sacred Parikrama/Kora, Lake Mansarovar Holy Dip, Yamdrok Lake, Inner Kora, Pasupatinath link) 2. High-altitude trekking / adventure traveler (Dolma La Pass at 5,630m, Dirapuk & Zuthulpuk trekking, rugged Trans-Himalayas) 3. Photography traveler (North Face of Mt. Kailash at sunrise, mirror reflections of Lake Mansarovar, prayer flag pass over Dolma La) 4. Extreme landscape & geographic explorer (Tibetan Plateau "Roof of the World", sacred origins of Indus/Brahmaputra/Sutlej/Karnali rivers) 5. Culture & Buddhist / Hindu heritage traveler (Yundrun Bon tradition, Tibetan Buddhist Monasteries, Chiu Monastery, Tibetan prayer wheels) 6. Private group / family pilgrimage traveler (Helicopter-assisted routes via Hilsa/Purang, private overland support teams) 7. Overland expedition traveler (Kathmandu to Kyirong / Saga / Darchen scenic drive across the High Himalayas) 8. VIP / luxury pilgrimage traveler (Lhasa acclimation + short domestic flight to Ngari Gunsa Airport + eco-bus tour) 9. Solo group-joining traveler (Joining mandated fixed-departure pilgrimage group permit slots via authorized agencies) 10. Budget overland traveler (Shared group overland coach from Kathmandu via Rasuwagadhi / Kyirong border) Best duration: 9–14 nights 7–9 nights (Helicopter route via Simikot / Hilsa / Purang): Best for FAST_TRACK_PILGRIMAGE, reducing Nepal-side transit days via flights/helicopters to maximize time at Mansarovar and the 3-day Kora. 10–12 nights (Overland route via Kathmandu / Kyirong border): Best for BALANCED_ACCLIMATIZATION and scenic driving across the Tibetan Plateau via Saga and Lake Mansarovar to Darchen. 12–14 nights (Fly via Lhasa & Ngari Gunsa Airport / Overland from Lhasa): Best for MAXIMUM_CULTURAL_IMMERSION + ACCLIMATIZATION, exploring Lhasa (Potala Palace), Shigatse, and Everest Base Camp before reaching Mt. Kailash. 15+ nights (Government Pilgrimage Scheme / Lipulekh & Nathu La passes): Best for OFFICIAL_INDIAN_GOVERNMENT_YATRA (MEA quota), including intensive medical screenings, base camp staging, and extended treks. Best season: MAY – OCTOBER (OPERATIONAL SEASON) Spring / Early Summer (May – June / Sagadawa Festival): CLEAR_SKIES + MODERATE_SNOW_MELT + SAGADAWA_FESTIVAL + PRE_MONSOON_VISIBILITY + RELIGIOUS_CELEBRATIONS. Monsoon / Summer (July – August): WARMER_NIGHTS + HIGHER_OXYGEN_LEVELS + RAIN_IN_NEPAL_TRANSIT + MISTY_PLATEAU_SCENERY + LUSH_NEPAL_VALLEYS. Autumn (September – October): CRISP_PLATEAU_AIR + OPTIMAL_CLEAR_PHOTOGRAPHY + STABLE_WEATHER + FREEZING_NIGHT_TEMPS + COLD_PASS_CROSSINGS. Winter (November – April): HEAVY_SNOWFALL + CLOSED_MOUNTAIN_PASSES + EXTREME_SUBZERO_TEMPS + SUSPENDED_PERMITS (NON-OPERATIONAL). Official Tibetan and diplomatic travel guidance treats Kailash Mansarovar strictly as a seasonal destination (May–October): early summer offers stable skies and the famous *Saga Dawa* festival; monsoon brings warmer temperatures despite rains on Nepal access routes; and autumn delivers the clearest mountain views despite bitter nighttime cold. Best hotel strategy: Choose accommodation according to high-altitude logistics, hygiene requirements, and route stage. For urban staging & acclimatization: KATHMANDU (5-star international hotels) OR LHASA (5-star Tibetan / international luxury hotels) to ensure restful acclimatization at lower elevations before ascending. For base camp / lake stays: DARCHEN & LAKE MANSAROVAR (Guesthouses / Eco-lodges / Teahouses). Modern hotels exist in Darchen, but options around the lake are rustic. For 3-day Kora trek: DIRAPUK & ZUTHULPUK MONASTERY GUESTHOUSES (Basic mountain teahouse dormitories or private support tents with portable supplies). Avoid expecting luxury amenities (such as private running hot water or central heating) during the active Kora circuit; extreme remote infrastructure demands focusing on clean bedding, personal sleeping bags, and reliable oxygen support. Best transportation: Use: Kailash Mansarovar transportation should primarily be treated as: FLIGHT_OR_HELICOPTER_TO_BORDER_OR_NGARI + MANDATED_CHINESE_TOUR_COACH_ON_HIGHWAY_G219 + ECO_BUS_FOR_MANSAROVAR_LAKE_CIRCUIT + FOOT_TREK_WITH_YAK_OR_PONY_SUPPORT_FOR_KORA Must-do for first-time visitor: Kailash Mansarovar should not be reduced to a quick flight-over photo stop; official pilgrimage guidelines position LAKE_MANSAROVAR_PURIFICATION + YAM_DWAR_ENTRY + 3_DAY_KORA_TREK + DOLMA_LA_PASS_CROSSING + ABBEY_MONASTERY_VISITS as essential core pillars. Don''t-do: Biggest advantage: Ultimate spiritual significance combined with the most dramatic high-altitude plateau landscapes on Earth. Kailash Mansarovar represents the ultimate pilgrimage site revered by Hindus, Buddhists, Jains, and Bonpos alike, set against the pristine turquoise waters of Lake Mansarovar and the symmetrical black rock pyramid of Mt. Kailash. Modern infrastructure advancements—including paved highways (G219), environmental buses, improved guesthouses, and regional airports like Ngari Gunsa—have made this historically months-long trek accessible within 10 to 14 days. Biggest disadvantage: Extreme high altitudes (exceeding 5,600m), complex multi-governmental permitting processes, and severe physical demands. Navigating multiple permit layers (Tibet Travel Permit, Alien Travel Permit, Military Clearance, Diplomatic Group Visas) requires strict advance planning through specialized operators, and unpredictable mountain weather can delay border crossings or helicopter flights. Overall destination score: 98/100', 2201),
  ('lake-mansarovar', 36, 'data-quality', 'DATA QUALITY', NULL, NULL, 'information_completeness: 97/100 last_updated: 2026-08-31 last_verified: WEB_VERIFIED verified_by: TIBET AUTONOMOUS REGION TOURISM BUREAU / MINISTRY OF EXTERNAL AFFAIRS INDIA / NEPAL TOURISM BOARD / CHINA TIBET GUIDE ASSOCIATION / AUTHORIZED PILGRIMAGE OPERATORS sources: IMPORTANT: Group visas, Tibet Travel Permits (TTP), Military Permits, border crossing clearances, and helicopter flight schedules must NOT be treated as open-ended or self-service items. All foreign visitors to Mount Kailash and Lake Mansarovar MUST travel in organized groups through authorized travel agencies; independent individual entry is strictly prohibited by Chinese authorities. Mandatory medical fitness certificates, passport validity requirements (minimum 6 months), age caps (prevailing regulations cap eligibility for certain permits at age 70), and strict advance document deadlines (typically 25–45 days prior) are strictly enforced. Regional transport in Western Tibet is governed by strict local environmental regulations: OVERLAND / HELICOPTER ROUTES: KATHMANDU -> RASUWAGADHI / KYIRONG OR NEPALGUNJ -> SIMIKOT -> HILSA -> PURANG -> DARCHEN FLY-IN ROUTE: LHASA / KASHGAR / CHENGDU -> NGARI GUNSA AIRPORT (NGQ) -> DARCHEN (200km highway drive) GOVERNMENT ROUTE (INDIAN CITIZENS): DELHI -> DHARCHULA -> LIPULEKH PASS OR GANGTOK -> NATHU LA PASS (MEA Quota Draw) Visitbeijing/Tibet Tourism Board portals, official MEA Yatra portals (kmy.gov.in), and licensed pilgrimage operators should be treated as primary sources for operational information. This dataset should be refreshed regularly before production use.', 2202),
  ('france', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Spring', NULL, 'months: March April May weather: March is transitional, while April and May become progressively milder, greener, and more comfortable. Conditions vary by region, with the Mediterranean generally warmer and mountain areas remaining colder. crowd_level: LOW → MEDIUM_HIGH price_level: LOW → MEDIUM_HIGH overall_score: 73–77 recommended: true reason: One of France''s strongest periods for Paris, Loire châteaux, Normandy, Provence, gardens, museums, cafés, cycling, countryside, photography, and cultural sightseeing. April and May offer particularly strong weather, but visitor demand and accommodation prices increase toward late spring. France''s official tourism platform specifically promotes spring for pleasant weather, gardens, coastlines, countryside, cultural events, and travel before the main summer rush.', 2203),
  ('france', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Summer', NULL, 'months: June July August weather: Warm to hot across much of France, with generally excellent conditions for beaches, countryside, festivals, mountains, outdoor dining, cycling, and long sightseeing days. Heatwaves can affect cities and inland areas. crowd_level: HIGH → VERY_HIGH price_level: HIGH → VERY_HIGH overall_score: 57–69 recommended: true reason: Excellent for: June provides the strongest summer balance. July and August receive much lower Crowd and Price ratings because French and international holiday demand is extremely high in major coastal, city, and resort destinations. During summer, book accommodation, trains, major attractions, and popular restaurants well in advance.', 2204),
  ('france', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Autumn', NULL, 'months: September October November weather: September usually remains warm and highly comfortable, October becomes cooler with attractive autumn colours, and November is colder and wetter but still practical for cities, museums, food, wine, and cultural travel. crowd_level: MEDIUM → LOW price_level: MEDIUM → LOW overall_score: 73–81 recommended: true reason: September and October are among France''s strongest periods for city sightseeing, vineyards, gastronomy, photography, countryside, hiking, Provence, Bordeaux, Burgundy, Alsace, and Loire Valley travel. September retains meaningful tourism demand, while October generally provides a stronger balance of weather, crowds, and prices. November offers weaker weather but lower visitor pressure and better value for museums, food, shopping, wellness, and slower city breaks. France''s official tourism guidance recommends off-season travel specifically for fewer crowds, greater availability, and potentially substantially lower accommodation and activity costs.', 2205),
  ('france', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Winter', NULL, 'months: December January February weather: Cool to cold across much of metropolitan France, with rain and occasional snow possible in lower areas and reliable winter conditions in the Alps and Pyrenees. crowd_level: LOW → MEDIUM price_level: LOW → MEDIUM overall_score: 63–77 recommended: true reason: Winter works particularly well for: January and February are generally quieter and better value nationally, although ski resorts can be expensive during snow holidays and school-break periods. December receives higher festive demand in Paris, Alsace, Alpine resorts, and major Christmas-market destinations.', 2206),
  ('france', 10, 'budget-strategy', 'BUDGET STRATEGY', NULL, NULL, 'Where money can be saved: Where saving money is usually NOT recommended: Travel-agent rule: In France, **HOTEL_LOCATION + REGION + SEASON + RAIL_COST + LOCAL_TRANSPORT should be evaluated together**. For short stays, prioritize **ONE_CITY_OR_REGION + ONE_NEARBY_EXCURSION**. For longer trips, combine **PARIS + ONE_OR_TWO_CONTRASTING_REGIONS** rather than attempting the whole country.', 2207),
  ('france', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Family', 'family', 'Use pre-booked private transfer, official taxi, or airport rail / public transport depending on luggage, children''s ages, arrival time, and hotel location. For Paris, rail and public transport can be efficient, but families with substantial luggage may prefer direct private transfer.', 2208),
  ('france', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Honeymoon', 'honeymoon', 'Prefer private transfer, premium taxi, or comfortable rail connection with direct hotel access where practical. For couples combining several French regions, high-speed rail is often preferable to repeated domestic flights or long road transfers.', 2209),
  ('france', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Luxury', 'luxury', 'Use chauffeured premium sedan / SUV / MPV with meet-and-assist, luggage handling, climate control, and direct hotel transfer. For multi-region luxury itineraries, combine premium rail with private local chauffeurs.', 2210),
  ('france', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Budget', 'budget', 'Use airport rail, metro, tram, bus, or coach where practical. France has extensive urban and intercity public transport, making private airport transfers unnecessary for many budget travelers.', 2211),
  ('france', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Senior', 'senior', 'Prefer direct taxi / private transfer when luggage, walking, station changes, or mobility are concerns. High-speed rail is particularly useful for comfortable travel between major French cities, but station and hotel accessibility should be verified individually.', 2212),
  ('france', 18, 'family-travel', 'FAMILY TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'child_friendly_score: 95 best_ages: Rules: For young children: Prefer: Avoid: Official France tourism guidance specifically promotes family travel across seaside, mountains, countryside, cycling, castles, nature, and cultural experiences.', 2213),
  ('france', 19, 'honeymoon-travel', 'HONEYMOON TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'honeymoon_score: 96 romance_score: 94 privacy_score: 91 luxury_score: 94 Recommended: Honeymoon itineraries should not contain more than: 2–3 major experiences/day. Prefer: One memorable cultural, scenic, gastronomic, wine, or wellness experience + free time over: Constant sightseeing. Recommended areas: France is particularly suitable for couples seeking **ROMANCE + FOOD + WINE + CULTURE + LUXURY + COAST + COUNTRYSIDE + SPA**.', 2214),
  ('france', 20, 'luxury-travel', 'LUXURY TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'luxury_score: 94 Recommended: France luxury travel should focus on: France has one of the world''s deepest luxury-tourism ecosystems, especially across Paris, the Riviera, wine regions, and Alpine resorts.', 2215),
  ('france', 21, 'adventure', 'ADVENTURE', NULL, NULL, 'adventure_score: 91 France is a major outdoor destination rather than only a culture-and-city destination. Adventure experiences should be interpreted as: France.fr highlights hiking, cycling, surfing, mountain recreation and coastal outdoor activities throughout the country. The French Alps are especially strong for skiing, hiking, mountaineering, mountain biking, rafting, and other outdoor activities. Adventure activities should always be matched to season, weather, fitness, terrain, and operator standards.', 2216),
  ('france', 22, 'senior-travel', 'SENIOR TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'senior_suitability: 91 walking_intensity: LOW–MEDIUM for well-planned city and cultural travel MEDIUM–HIGH for castles, historic centres, mountains, and nature areas Rules: France works particularly well for seniors when positioned as a **CULTURE + FOOD + SCENIC_RAIL + RIVER_CRUISE + COUNTRYSIDE + WELLNESS + RELAXED_CITY destination**, while mountain and historic-site intensity should be selected carefully.', 2217),
  ('france', 23, 'accessibility', 'ACCESSIBILITY', NULL, NULL, 'wheelchair_accessibility: PARTIAL → GOOD; strongest in modern hotels, museums, major attractions, airports, and newer public facilities, but variable in historic centres, castles, villages, beaches, and mountain areas public_transport_accessibility: PARTIAL → GOOD; varies by city, metro / tram system, railway station, bus, and route hotel_accessibility: MUST_BE_VERIFIED_PER_HOTEL attraction_accessibility: MUST_BE_VERIFIED_PER_ATTRACTION Rule: Never infer accessibility from France''s overall developed tourism infrastructure. Each hotel, museum, château, restaurant, beach, railway station, mountain facility, and historic attraction should carry its own accessibility data. Additional notes:', 2218),
  ('france', 24, 'food', 'FOOD', NULL, NULL, 'France is particularly strong for: French gastronomy is one of the country''s defining tourism products, ranging from village markets and regional specialties to prestigious vineyards and starred restaurants. Food experiences: Family: Prioritize bakeries, crêpes, pastries, simple bistro dishes, markets, cheese, and familiar regional foods. Honeymoon: Choose fine dining, vineyard meals, Champagne experiences, romantic cafés, and scenic regional restaurants. Luxury: Include Michelin-starred dining, private wine estates, chef-led experiences, premium hotel restaurants, and curated gastronomy tours. Budget: Use bakeries, markets, supermarkets, casual cafés, crêperies, and prix-fixe lunch menus to control costs.', 2219),
  ('france', 25, 'shopping', 'SHOPPING', NULL, NULL, 'Strong categories: Luxury shopping: France is one of the world''s strongest luxury-shopping destinations. Prefer: Budget: Prefer: Travel-agent rule: Use PARIS for LUXURY_FASHION + DESIGNER_SHOPPING, REGIONAL_MARKETS for FOOD + CRAFTS, and WINE_REGIONS for PREMIUM_WINE_AND_GASTRONOMY_PRODUCTS. Prioritize reputable sellers for high-value fashion, jewellery, antiques, wine, and art.', 2220),
  ('france', 26, 'nightlife', 'NIGHTLIFE', NULL, NULL, 'nightlife_level: 91 Suitable for: Best areas: Evening activities are better suited to: France has a strong and varied nightlife product, especially in major cities and resort destinations. Paris provides the deepest mix, while the Riviera and Alpine resorts add seasonal luxury and après-ski nightlife. Honeymoon travelers should generally prefer: ROMANTIC_DINNER + SEINE_OR_RIVIERA_EVENING + WINE_BAR / ROOFTOP over: Club-heavy itineraries unless specifically requested. Travel-agent rule: Position France as a **STRONG DINING + WINE_BAR + COCKTAIL + LIVE_MUSIC + CLUB + CULTURAL_EVENING + RESORT_NIGHTLIFE DESTINATION**.', 2221),
  ('france', 28, 'sample-itinerary-patterns', 'SAMPLE ITINERARY PATTERNS', '3 NIGHTS', NULL, '### Day 1 Arrival at Paris Charles de Gaulle Airport (CDG) / Paris Orly Airport (ORY) → Private transfer / airport rail to central Paris → Hotel check-in → Relaxation and refreshment Afternoon: Central Paris orientation → Eiffel Tower → Trocadéro viewpoint → Seine riverside walk → Champs-Élysées → Arc de Triomphe → Paris architecture and city photography Evening: Traditional French dinner → Optional Seine River cruise → Eiffel Tower illumination → Relaxed café / wine-bar experience → Hotel Paris works best as the main base for a first 3-night France itinerary because its major landmarks, museums, gastronomy, shopping, and transport connections can fill several days without unnecessary regional transfers. ### Day 2 Morning: Breakfast → Louvre Museum → Tuileries Garden → Walk toward Île de la Cité → Notre-Dame Cathedral → Seine views → Latin Quarter exploration Cultural options: → Musée d''Orsay → Sainte-Chapelle → Panthéon → Luxembourg Gardens → Parisian bakery / pâtisserie experience Afternoon: French lunch → Montmartre → Sacré-Cœur surroundings → Historic neighbourhood walk → Art and street photography → Café break Evening: Return to central Paris → French / contemporary dinner → Optional rooftop, cocktail bar, cabaret, live music, or relaxed nightlife → Hotel France''s official tourism guidance identifies the Louvre, Notre-Dame, Latin Quarter, Montmartre, Eiffel Tower, and Seine among Paris''s defining first-time experiences. ### Day 3 Morning: Breakfast → Day trip to Versailles → Palace of Versailles → State Apartments → Hall of Mirrors → Royal history and architecture → Gardens Afternoon: Lunch in Versailles → Continue garden exploration → Optional Grand Trianon / Petit Trianon → Marie-Antoinette''s Estate according to time and interest → Return to Paris Evening: Final Paris leisure time → Shopping / café experience → Special French dinner → Optional Seine evening walk → Hotel Versailles is one of the strongest short excursions from Paris. France''s official tourism guidance places it around 40 minutes from Paris by RER and highlights the palace, Hall of Mirrors, gardens, Trianon estates, and Queen''s Hamlet. ### Day 4 Breakfast → Leisure morning → Optional bakery / café experience → Last-minute shopping → Short neighbourhood walk according to flight timing → Hotel checkout → Transfer to Paris Charles de Gaulle Airport / Paris Orly Airport → Departure Optional alternative according to traveler interest: FAMILY: → Eiffel Tower → Seine cruise → Parks / gardens → Disneyland Paris instead of Versailles → Short museum visits → Family bakery and café experiences HONEYMOON: → Boutique / luxury Paris hotel → Eiffel Tower evening → Seine dinner cruise → Montmartre → Fine dining → Versailles → Spa / relaxed couple time LUXURY: → Palace hotel → Chauffeured private sightseeing → Private Louvre / heritage guide → Michelin dining → Luxury shopping → Private Versailles experience → Premium Seine cruise FOOD / WINE: → Paris food tour → Bakeries and pâtisseries → Markets → Fine dining → Champagne full-day excursion instead of Versailles → Wine tasting HISTORY / CULTURE: → Louvre → Notre-Dame → Sainte-Chapelle → Latin Quarter → Versailles → Additional museum according to interest REGIONAL_EXCURSION: → Champagne / Reims day trip OR → Loire Valley château excursion OR → Normandy / Giverny according to traveler interest For a 3-night first France visit, these regional experiences should generally replace the Versailles day rather than being added on top of an already full Paris programme.', 2222),
  ('france', 29, 'seven-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'SEVEN-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 1', NULL, 'Arrival at Paris Charles de Gaulle Airport → Meet and assist → Private transfer to Paris hotel → Romantic hotel check-in → Relax and refresh Afternoon / Evening: → Seine riverside → Eiffel Tower / Trocadéro → Couple photography Evening: Romantic French dinner → Eiffel Tower illumination → Overnight at Paris', 2223),
  ('france', 29, 'seven-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'SEVEN-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 2', NULL, 'Breakfast → Private / guided Paris city experience → Place de la Concorde → Champs-Élysées → Arc de Triomphe → Eiffel Tower → Café / pâtisserie break Evening: Romantic Seine River cruise → Special honeymoon dinner → Overnight at Paris', 2224),
  ('france', 29, 'seven-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'SEVEN-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 3', NULL, 'Breakfast → Louvre Museum → Tuileries Garden → Île de la Cité → Notre-Dame surroundings Afternoon: → Montmartre → Sacré-Cœur → Historic streets → Café / boutique shopping Evening: Fine dining → Overnight at Paris', 2225),
  ('france', 29, 'seven-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'SEVEN-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 4', NULL, 'Breakfast Choose ONE: VERSAILLES: → Palace of Versailles → Hall of Mirrors → Gardens → Return to Paris OR BELGIUM_ROMANTIC_EXTENSION: → High-speed rail toward Brussels → Grand Place → Historic centre → Belgian chocolate / waffle experience → Optional Bruges only if planned as a dedicated full-day excursion → Return to Paris OR LUXEMBOURG_ROMANTIC_EXTENSION: → Rail journey to Luxembourg City → UNESCO Old Town → Chemin de la Corniche → Grund → Romantic café / dining → Return to Paris Do not combine Versailles + Belgium + Luxembourg on the same day. Evening: Relaxed couple time → Overnight at Paris', 2226),
  ('france', 29, 'seven-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'SEVEN-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 5', NULL, 'Breakfast → Hotel checkout → Rail / flight toward Switzerland → Transfer to Lucerne → Romantic hotel check-in Afternoon: → Chapel Bridge → Old Town → Lake Lucerne → Couple photography Evening: Romantic lakeside dinner → Overnight at Lucerne', 2227),
  ('france', 29, 'seven-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'SEVEN-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 6', NULL, 'Breakfast → Engelberg → Mt. Titlis → TITLIS Rotair → Alpine / glacier scenery → Couple photography Afternoon: → Return to Lucerne → Old Town / lakefront → Spa / leisure Evening: Romantic dinner → Overnight at Lucerne', 2228),
  ('france', 29, 'seven-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'SEVEN-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 7', NULL, 'Breakfast Choose ONE: JUNGFRAU_REGION: → Interlaken → Grindelwald / Lauterbrunnen → Alpine scenery → Optional Jungfraujoch OR RHINE_FALLS_AND_ZURICH: → Rhine Falls → Zurich Old Town → Lake Zurich → Bahnhofstrasse OR RELAXED_LUCERNE: → Lake cruise → Spa / wellness → Café / chocolate experience → Free couple time Evening: Farewell honeymoon dinner → Overnight in Switzerland', 2229),
  ('france', 29, 'seven-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'SEVEN-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 8', NULL, 'Breakfast → Leisure morning → Hotel checkout → Transfer to Zurich Airport → Departure HONEYMOON PACING RULE: CORE: PARIS_4_NIGHTS + SWITZERLAND_3_NIGHTS Optional neighbouring-country flavor: BELGIUM_OR_LUXEMBOURG should REPLACE one Paris excursion day rather than being added to an already full itinerary. Prefer: FRANCE + SWITZERLAND + ONE_LIGHT_BELGIUM_OR_LUXEMBOURG_EXPERIENCE over: FRANCE + BELGIUM + LUXEMBOURG + SWITZERLAND with repeated hotel changes.', 2230),
  ('france', 30, 'seven-nights-family-pattern', 'SEVEN-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 1', NULL, 'Arrival in Paris → Private transfer → Family hotel check-in → Relax Evening: → Eiffel Tower surroundings → Trocadéro → Easy Seine walk → Family dinner → Overnight at Paris', 2231),
  ('france', 30, 'seven-nights-family-pattern', 'SEVEN-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 2', NULL, 'Breakfast → Paris city sightseeing → Place de la Concorde → Champs-Élysées → Arc de Triomphe → Eiffel Tower → Family photography Evening: → Seine River cruise → Dinner → Overnight at Paris', 2232),
  ('france', 30, 'seven-nights-family-pattern', 'SEVEN-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 3', NULL, 'Breakfast → Louvre selected family-friendly sections → Tuileries Garden Afternoon: → Notre-Dame surroundings → Montmartre → Sacré-Cœur → Café / shopping Evening: Family dinner → Overnight at Paris', 2233),
  ('france', 30, 'seven-nights-family-pattern', 'SEVEN-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 4', NULL, 'Choose ONE: DISNEYLAND_PARIS: → Full-day family entertainment OR VERSAILLES: → Palace → Hall of Mirrors → Gardens OR BELGIUM_FAMILY_DAY: → Brussels → Grand Place → Belgian chocolate / waffle experience → Easy central sightseeing → Family photography OR LUXEMBOURG_FAMILY_DAY: → Luxembourg City → Old Town → Corniche → Grund → Easy heritage walk → Family café time Do not combine multiple options. Evening: → Return to Paris → Dinner → Overnight at Paris', 2234),
  ('france', 30, 'seven-nights-family-pattern', 'SEVEN-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 5', NULL, 'Breakfast → Checkout → Transfer to Switzerland → Lucerne hotel check-in Afternoon: → Chapel Bridge → Old Town → Lake Lucerne → Chocolate / souvenir stop Evening: Family dinner → Overnight at Lucerne', 2235),
  ('france', 30, 'seven-nights-family-pattern', 'SEVEN-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 6', NULL, 'Breakfast → Engelberg → Mt. Titlis → TITLIS Rotair → Snow / Alpine experience → Family photography Afternoon: → Return to Lucerne → Free family time Evening: Dinner → Overnight at Lucerne', 2236),
  ('france', 30, 'seven-nights-family-pattern', 'SEVEN-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 7', NULL, 'Choose ONE: INTERLAKEN_AND_GRINDELWALD: → Scenic journey → Interlaken → Grindelwald → Easy Alpine exploration OR RHINE_FALLS_AND_ZURICH: → Rhine Falls → Zurich → Lake Zurich → Shopping OR RELAXED_LUCERNE: → Lake cruise → Family leisure → Chocolate experience Evening: Farewell family dinner → Overnight in Switzerland', 2237),
  ('france', 30, 'seven-nights-family-pattern', 'SEVEN-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 8', NULL, 'Breakfast → Checkout → Transfer to Zurich Airport → Departure FAMILY PACING RULE: PARIS_4_NIGHTS + SWITZERLAND_3_NIGHTS Belgium or Luxembourg should remain: OPTIONAL_ONE_DAY_EXTENSION Prefer: PARIS + ONE_OF_DISNEYLAND_OR_VERSAILLES_OR_BELGIUM_OR_LUXEMBOURG + LUCERNE + MT_TITLIS + ONE_RELAXED_SWISS_DAY Keep maximum 2–3 major experiences/day.', 2238),
  ('france', 31, 'seven-nights-luxury-pattern', 'SEVEN-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 1', NULL, 'Arrival in Paris → VIP meet and assist → Chauffeured transfer → Palace / five-star hotel check-in Evening: → Private Paris drive → Eiffel Tower / Trocadéro → Fine dining → Overnight at Paris', 2239),
  ('france', 31, 'seven-nights-luxury-pattern', 'SEVEN-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 2', NULL, 'Breakfast → Private guided Paris tour → Eiffel Tower → Arc de Triomphe → Champs-Élysées → Place de la Concorde → Premium lunch Evening: → Private / premium Seine cruise → Fine dining → Overnight at Paris', 2240),
  ('france', 31, 'seven-nights-luxury-pattern', 'SEVEN-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 3', NULL, 'Breakfast → Private Louvre visit → Tuileries → Place Vendôme Afternoon: → Avenue Montaigne / Rue Saint-Honoré → Luxury shopping → Afternoon tea → Hotel leisure Evening: Michelin-level dinner → Overnight at Paris', 2241),
  ('france', 31, 'seven-nights-luxury-pattern', 'SEVEN-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 4', NULL, 'Choose ONE premium experience: VERSAILLES: → Chauffeured private excursion → Palace → Hall of Mirrors → Gardens → Expert guide → Premium lunch OR BELGIUM_LUXURY_DAY: → First-class / premium rail to Brussels → Private guide → Grand Place → Luxury chocolate experience → Fine dining / premium lunch → Designer shopping where desired → Return to Paris OR LUXEMBOURG_LUXURY_DAY: → First-class rail / chauffeured arrangement → Luxembourg City → Private Old Town heritage tour → Corniche and Grund → Premium lunch → Optional Moselle wine / Crémant element where timing permits → Return to Paris Evening: Spa / hotel relaxation → Overnight at Paris', 2242),
  ('france', 31, 'seven-nights-luxury-pattern', 'SEVEN-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 5', NULL, 'Breakfast → Private checkout assistance → First-class rail / premium connection to Switzerland → Chauffeured transfer to Lucerne → Luxury lake-view hotel Afternoon: → Private Lucerne orientation → Chapel Bridge → Old Town → Lake Lucerne Evening: Fine dining → Overnight at Lucerne', 2243),
  ('france', 31, 'seven-nights-luxury-pattern', 'SEVEN-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 6', NULL, 'Breakfast → Private transfer to Engelberg → Premium Mt. Titlis experience → TITLIS Rotair → Glacier / Alpine scenery → Private photography Afternoon: → Premium mountain lunch → Return to Lucerne → Spa / wellness Evening: Lake-view dinner → Overnight at Lucerne', 2244),
  ('france', 31, 'seven-nights-luxury-pattern', 'SEVEN-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 7', NULL, 'Choose ONE: INTERLAKEN_AND_GRINDELWALD: → Private / premium scenic journey → Alpine landscapes → Fine lunch OR LAKE_LUCERNE_LUXURY: → Private / premium lake cruise → Spa → Boutique shopping → Fine dining OR ZURICH_AND_RHINE_FALLS: → Chauffeured Rhine Falls excursion → Zurich → Bahnhofstrasse luxury shopping → Premium dining Evening: Farewell fine-dining experience → Overnight in Switzerland', 2245),
  ('france', 31, 'seven-nights-luxury-pattern', 'SEVEN-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 8', NULL, 'Breakfast → Leisure morning → Luxury checkout → Chauffeured transfer to Zurich Airport → Departure LUXURY PACING RULE: CORE: PARIS_4_NIGHTS + SWITZERLAND_3_NIGHTS Optional: ONE_PREMIUM_BELGIUM_OR_LUXEMBOURG_DAY Prioritize: PALACE_HOTELS + PRIVATE_GUIDES + FIRST_CLASS_RAIL + FINE_DINING + SPA + PREMIUM_SWISS_EXPERIENCES Belgium / Luxembourg should add: CULTURAL_CONTRAST + GASTRONOMY + PREMIUM_DAY_TRIP_VALUE rather than create additional one-night hotel changes.', 2246),
  ('france', 32, 'travel-agent-insights', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS', 'What inexperienced planners often do wrong', NULL, '', 2247),
  ('france', 32, 'travel-agent-insights', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS', 'What an experienced planner does differently', NULL, '', 2248),
  ('france', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', NULL, NULL, 'IF: trip_length <= 4 nights THEN: prioritize_PARIS + ONE_NEARBY_EXCURSION AND: do not recommend NORMANDY + LOIRE + BORDEAUX + PROVENCE + RIVIERA as default additions. Reason: A short first France visit gains more value from a properly paced Paris experience than repeated long-distance transfers. IF: trip_length >= 7 nights AND: traveler_interest == FIRST_TIME_FRANCE THEN: prioritize_PARIS + ONE_OR_TWO_CONTRASTING_REGIONS Reason: France''s major regions offer very different products, so a first trip benefits from combining Paris with selected countryside, coast, wine, or heritage experiences. IF: trip_type == HONEYMOON THEN: increase_romance_weight by 20% increase_free_time_weight by 25% decrease_activity_density by 20% prefer_PARIS + PROVENCE_OR_RIVIERA + WINE_OR_SPA_EXPERIENCE Reason: France''s honeymoon strength comes from romantic cities, fine dining, vineyards, countryside, coastlines, boutique hotels, spa, and relaxed couple time. IF: traveler_type == FAMILY AND: children_age <= 6 THEN: reduce_MUSEUM_DENSITY by 25% increase_downtime by 25% prefer_EIFFEL_TOWER + SEINE_CRUISE + PARKS + DISNEYLAND_OR_EASY_CASTLE_EXPERIENCE Reason: Young children generally benefit from visual attractions, parks, cruises, family entertainment, shorter museum visits, and regular breaks. IF: traveler_type == FAMILY AND: children_age >= 7 THEN: consider_PARIS + VERSAILLES + LOIRE_VALLEY + FAMILY_MUSEUMS AND: include_EDUCATIONAL + INTERACTIVE + OUTDOOR_EXPERIENCES Reason: Older children can combine French history, castles, museums, food, transport experiences, and outdoor sightseeing more effectively. IF: traveler_type == LUXURY THEN: prefer_PALACE_OR_5_STAR_HOTEL AND: prefer_PRIVATE_TRANSFER + EXPERT_GUIDE AND: increase_FINE_DINING + WINE + SPA + PREMIUM_SHOPPING_WEIGHT Reason: Luxury in France should increase privacy, accommodation quality, gastronomy, service, access, and personalization rather than simply adding more sightseeing. IF: traveler_type == BUDGET THEN: prefer_BUDGET_HOTEL_OR_HOSTEL_NEAR_PUBLIC_TRANSPORT AND: use_WALKING + METRO + BUS + TGV_TER AND: prioritize_BAKERIES + MARKETS + FREE_PUBLIC_SPACES + SELECTIVE_PAID_ATTRACTIONS Reason: France can remain manageable on a budget when transport, accommodation location, food, and attraction spending are planned together. IF: traveler_interest == CULTURE_AND_HERITAGE THEN: prioritize_PARIS + VERSAILLES + LOIRE_VALLEY_OR_NORMANDY AND: consider_ALSACE_OR_OCCITANIE_FOR_LONGER_TRIPS Reason: France offers exceptional depth across museums, royal heritage, cathedrals, medieval towns, castles, art, architecture, and historic landscapes. IF: traveler_interest == FOOD_AND_GASTRONOMY THEN: prefer_PARIS + LYON_OR_BURGUNDY_OR_PROVENCE AND: include_MARKETS + BAKERIES + REGIONAL_CUISINE + CHEESE + WINE Reason: Food should be treated as a core French travel experience rather than simply meal stops between attractions. IF: traveler_interest == WINE THEN: prefer_CHAMPAGNE + BURGUNDY + BORDEAUX AND: select_REGION_BASED_ON_WINE_INTEREST Reason: France''s principal wine regions offer distinct landscapes, appellations, food traditions, estates, and tasting experiences. IF: traveler_interest == ROMANTIC_RELAXATION THEN: prefer_PARIS + PROVENCE + FRENCH_RIVIERA_OR_LOIRE AND: decrease_activity_density_by_20_percent Reason: Romantic itineraries work best with scenery, dining, wine, cafés, premium hotels, spa, and free time rather than constant attraction changes. IF: traveler_interest == BEACH_AND_COAST THEN: prefer_FRENCH_RIVIERA_OR_CORSICA_OR_ATLANTIC_COAST_OR_BIARRITZ AND: select_REGION_BY_SEASON + BUDGET + BEACH_STYLE Reason: France offers Mediterranean and Atlantic coastal products with very different weather, landscapes, prices, and atmosphere. IF: traveler_interest == SKIING_AND_WINTER_SPORTS THEN: prefer_FRENCH_ALPS_OR_PYRENEES AND: verify_SNOW + LIFT_OPERATIONS + RESORT_ACCESS + EQUIPMENT Reason: Mountain resorts should be treated as dedicated seasonal products rather than extensions of standard city sightseeing. IF: traveler_interest == NATURE_AND_ADVENTURE THEN: prefer_ALPS + PYRENEES + CORSICA + PROVENCE_OUTDOORS + ATLANTIC_COAST AND: match_ACTIVITY_TO_SEASON + FITNESS Reason: France supports hiking, skiing, cycling, surfing, sailing, climbing, canyoning, and extensive nature-based travel. IF: traveler_interest == SHOPPING_AND_LUXURY THEN: prioritize_PARIS AND: consider_FRENCH_RIVIERA_FOR_PREMIUM_LEISURE Reason: Paris provides France''s strongest concentration of luxury fashion, jewellery, cosmetics, department stores, designers, and premium hospitality. IF: traveler_interest == HISTORY THEN: prefer_PARIS + NORMANDY + LOIRE_VALLEY AND: consider_OCCITANIE + ALSACE + REGIONAL_HERITAGE_FOR_LONGER_STAYS Reason: French history spans Roman, medieval, royal, revolutionary, military, religious, and modern heritage across multiple regions. IF: traveler_interest == PHOTOGRAPHY THEN: prefer_PARIS + PROVENCE + LOIRE_VALLEY + ALSACE + RIVIERA AND: prioritize_EARLY_MORNING + LATE_AFTERNOON + BLUE_HOUR Reason: France provides exceptional architectural, village, vineyard, coastal, mountain, street, and seasonal photography. IF: hotel_is_far_from_USEFUL_TRANSPORT AND: hotel_saving < additional_transport_cost + value_of_lost_time THEN: prefer_BETTER_CONNECTED_HOTEL Reason: A cheaper room can provide worse total value when metro, railway, airport, dining, or sightseeing access is inconvenient. IF: trip_length <= 7 nights THEN: avoid_EXCESSIVE_HOTEL_CHANGES AND: prefer_MAXIMUM_TWO_OR_THREE_BASES Reason: Frequent city changes reduce sightseeing time and create unnecessary luggage and transfer friction. IF: traveler_interest == PROVENCE THEN: prefer_RENTAL_CAR_OR_PRIVATE_DRIVER_FOR_VILLAGES AND: retain_RAIL_FOR_MAJOR_CITIES_WHERE_PRACTICAL Reason: Provence''s strongest villages, vineyards, countryside landscapes, and smaller attractions are more dispersed than central Paris. IF: traveler_interest == FRENCH_RIVIERA THEN: use_COASTAL_RAIL_FOR_NICE + CANNES + ANTIBES_WHERE_PRACTICAL AND: use_PRIVATE_CAR_SELECTIVELY_FOR_HILL_VILLAGES Reason: The Riviera''s main coastal towns are comparatively well connected, while inland villages require more road-based planning. IF: traveler_interest == VERSAILLES THEN: allocate_HALF_DAY_TO_FULL_DAY AND: avoid_combining_with_HEAVY_PARIS_MUSEUM_DAY Reason: The palace, gardens, and wider estate require substantially more time than a quick landmark stop. IF: weather == EXTREME_SUMMER_HEAT THEN: prefer_EARLY_MORNING + LATE_AFTERNOON_SIGHTSEEING AND: increase_MUSEUM + CAFE + HOTEL_BREAK_TIME Reason: Heatwaves can materially reduce comfort during exposed city, château, village, and inland sightseeing. IF: traveler_type == SENIOR OR: traveler_mobility == LIMITED THEN: reduce_COBBLESTONE_WALKING + CASTLE_STAIRS + MOUNTAIN_INTENSITY AND: prefer_SCENIC_RAIL + CRUISES + MUSEUMS + PRIVATE_TRANSPORT + RELAXED_PACING Reason: France can work very well for seniors, but historic environments and mountain areas require attraction-specific planning. IF: traveler_uses_WHEELCHAIR THEN: prefer_VERIFIED_ACCESSIBLE_HOTEL + ACCESSIBLE_TRANSPORT + VERIFIED_ATTRACTIONS AND: avoid_assuming_HISTORIC_CENTRES + CHATEAUX + BEACHES + MOUNTAINS_ARE_STEP_FREE Reason: Accessibility is significantly stronger in many modern facilities but varies across France''s older and natural environments. IF: traveler_interest == FIRST_TIME_FRANCE THEN: prioritize_PARIS AND: add_ONE_OF_LOIRE_OR_NORMANDY_OR_CHAMPAGNE_FOR_SHORT_TRIPS AND: add_PROVENCE_OR_RIVIERA_OR_OTHER_REGION_FOR_LONGER_TRIPS Reason: Paris provides the clearest first introduction, while one contrasting region reveals France''s broader cultural and geographic diversity. IF: traveler_interest == AUTHENTIC_LOCAL_EXPERIENCE THEN: prefer_LOCAL_MARKETS + REGIONAL_DINING + VILLAGES + NEIGHBOURHOODS + SMALL_PRODUCERS AND: decrease_GENERIC_LANDMARK_ONLY_WEIGHT Reason: Regional cuisine, markets, villages, cafés, local producers, and neighbourhood life provide a deeper French experience than relying only on headline attractions. IF: traveler_interest == CULTURE_AND_RELAXATION_BALANCE THEN: allocate_APPROXIMATELY_60_TO_70_PERCENT_TO_CORE_SIGHTSEEING AND: allocate_REMAINING_TIME_TO_FOOD + WINE + PARKS + SHOPPING + SPA + FREE_TIME Reason: France is best experienced when major heritage is balanced with gastronomy, neighbourhoods, scenery, and slower everyday experiences.', 2249),
  ('france', 34, 'destination-scoring', 'DESTINATION SCORING', NULL, NULL, '| Factor | Score | | ------------------ | ----: | | Family | 95 | | Honeymoon | 96 | | Luxury | 94 | | Budget | 74 | | Adventure | 91 | | Culture | 92 | | Food | 95 | | Shopping | 95 | | Nightlife | 91 | | Relaxation | 96 | | Nature | 96 | | Accessibility | 84 | | Safety | 88 | | First-time visitor | 98 | | Photography | 94 |', 2250),
  ('france', 35, 'final-travel-agent-verdict', 'FINAL TRAVEL AGENT VERDICT', NULL, NULL, 'Best traveler profiles: 1. Culture / heritage traveler 2. Honeymoon / romantic traveler 3. Food / gastronomy traveler 4. Luxury traveler 5. First-time Europe traveler 6. Photography traveler 7. Family traveler 8. Wine traveler 9. Nature / outdoor traveler 10. Shopping / fashion traveler Best duration: 7–10 nights 4–5 nights for a focused first visit centred on Paris, Versailles, major museums, neighbourhoods, French dining, shopping, and one nearby excursion. 7–10 nights for most first-time visitors wanting Paris plus one or two contrasting regions such as Normandy, Loire Valley, Champagne, Provence, French Riviera, Alsace, or Bordeaux. 12–14 nights for travelers wanting Paris plus two or three major regions with a more relaxed combination of culture, gastronomy, wine, coast, countryside, or mountains. Best season: April–June and September–October April–May for spring gardens, city sightseeing, Loire Valley, Normandy, countryside, food, museums, photography, and comfortable walking. June is excellent for long daylight, cities, coastlines, countryside, cycling, and mountains, but visitor demand begins increasing. July–August are strongest for beaches, Riviera, Atlantic coast, Corsica, Alps, festivals, and family holidays, but crowds and prices are among the highest of the year. September–October provide one of France''s strongest overall combinations of comfortable sightseeing weather, vineyards, gastronomy, hiking, photography, countryside, and better value after peak summer. November–March remain strong for museums, gastronomy, shopping, spa, festive city travel, and skiing in the Alps / Pyrenees. France''s official tourism platform promotes the country across culture, nature, food and wine, shopping, nightlife, sport and wellness throughout the year. Best hotel strategy: Choose accommodation according to the main region and trip purpose rather than applying one hotel strategy nationwide. For first-time Paris stays, prioritize metro / rail convenience, walkability, restaurants, and efficient access to major attractions. For countryside, wine, honeymoon, or luxury itineraries, consider château hotels, vineyard properties, boutique hotels, Riviera resorts, Alpine properties, or premium countryside stays. Avoid excessive hotel changes during short itineraries. Best transportation: Walking + metro / bus / tram for major cities, high-speed / regional rail for intercity travel, and rental car / private driver selectively for countryside, vineyards, villages, remote coastline, and mountain regions. Private transport for: Must-do for first-time visitor: Paris remains France''s strongest first-time gateway, combining major monuments, museums, neighbourhoods, shopping, gastronomy, and nightlife. Don''t-do: Biggest advantage: Exceptional tourism diversity. France combines world-class culture, history, gastronomy, wine, fashion, shopping, romance, coastlines, countryside, mountains, skiing, wellness, photography, and family travel within one country. France''s official tourism platform reflects this breadth with hundreds of experiences across cultural heritage, nature and outdoor travel, food and wine, shopping, nightlife, sport, wellness, cycling, spiritual tourism, and remembrance tourism. Biggest disadvantage: France can become expensive and logistically inefficient when too many premium regions are combined quickly. Paris, the Riviera, Alpine resorts, summer coastlines, and major events can generate high prices and crowds, while historic centres, castles, rural areas, beaches, and mountains vary significantly in accessibility. Overall destination score: 92/100', 2251),
  ('france', 36, 'data-quality', 'DATA QUALITY', NULL, NULL, 'information_completeness: 96/100 last_updated: 2026-08-26 last_verified: PARTIALLY_WEB_VERIFIED verified_by: FRANCE.FR / ATOUT FRANCE / OFFICIAL FRENCH TOURISM, REGIONAL AND ACCESSIBILITY SOURCES sources: IMPORTANT: Prices, attraction tickets, museum schedules, rail fares, public transport, opening hours, restaurant reservations, wine tours, ski operations, beach services, and accessibility must NOT be treated as permanently valid. Paris attractions, Versailles, major museums, regional rail services, wine estates, ski resorts, ferries, and seasonal coastal services should be checked against current official information before travel. France''s regions have substantially different climates, tourism seasons, transport requirements, and activity patterns. Summer heatwaves can affect Paris, Provence, Bordeaux, Lyon, Occitanie, and other inland / southern destinations. Alpine and Pyrenean skiing depends on snow, weather, lift operations, and resort conditions. Wine-estate visits in Champagne, Burgundy, Bordeaux, and other regions may require advance reservations. Historic centres, medieval buildings, château complexes, beaches, villages, and mountain environments should not be assumed uniformly step-free. France has a developed accessible-tourism framework, but accessibility still requires property- and attraction-level verification. France should primarily be treated as: SPRING: CULTURE + GARDENS + COUNTRYSIDE + FOOD + PHOTOGRAPHY + CITY_BREAKS SUMMER: COAST + FAMILY + MOUNTAINS + FESTIVALS + CYCLING + OUTDOORS AUTUMN: WINE + GASTRONOMY + CULTURE + PHOTOGRAPHY + COUNTRYSIDE + HIKING WINTER: CITY_CULTURE + CHRISTMAS + FOOD + SHOPPING + SPA + ALPINE_AND_PYRENEAN_SKIING France.fr, Atout France, SNCF, regional tourism boards, individual attractions, accommodation providers, and activity operators should be treated as the primary sources for current operational information. This dataset should be refreshed regularly before production use.', 2252),
  ('switzerland', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Spring', NULL, 'months: March April May weather: Transitional Alpine season; valleys and cities become mild while higher mountains can retain substantial snow. crowd_level: LOW → MEDIUM price_level: MEDIUM → HIGH overall_score: 65-72 recommended: true reason: Strong for cities, lakes, waterfalls, lower-altitude hiking, scenic rail, photography, and late-season snow experiences.', 2253),
  ('switzerland', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Summer', NULL, 'months: June July August weather: Warm in cities and valleys, generally excellent for lakes, hiking, mountain railways, villages, and high-Alpine sightseeing. crowd_level: HIGH → VERY_HIGH price_level: HIGH → VERY_HIGH overall_score: 55–68 recommended: true reason: Peak season for Jungfrau Region, Zermatt, Lucerne, lakes, hiking, scenic trains, and outdoor travel.', 2254),
  ('switzerland', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Autumn', NULL, 'months: September October November weather: September is generally excellent; October becomes cooler and colourful, while November is transitional and quieter. crowd_level: MEDIUM → LOW price_level: MEDIUM → LOWER overall_score: 65–75 recommended: true reason: September and early October provide one of the strongest combinations of scenery, hiking, photography, fewer crowds, and rail travel.', 2255),
  ('switzerland', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Winter', NULL, 'months: December January February weather: Cold with major snowfall in Alpine areas; cities and lower valleys are generally colder with variable snow. crowd_level: MEDIUM → VERY_HIGH in major ski resorts price_level: MEDIUM → VERY_HIGH overall_score: 55–62 recommended: true reason: Outstanding for Zermatt, St. Moritz, Jungfrau Region, skiing, snow scenery, winter rail journeys, spas, Christmas travel, and Alpine resorts.', 2256),
  ('switzerland', 10, 'budget-strategy', 'BUDGET STRATEGY', NULL, NULL, 'Where money can be saved: Swiss Travel Pass products cover trains, buses and boats, public transport in more than 90 towns and cities, and provide discounts or inclusion on many mountain excursions. :contentReference[oaicite:0]{index=0} Where saving money is usually NOT recommended: Travel-agent rule: In Switzerland, **HOTEL_LOCATION + RAIL_PASS + MOUNTAIN_EXCURSION_COST + SEASON should be evaluated together**. For short stays, prioritize **ONE_OR_TWO_BASES + ONE_OR_TWO_SIGNATURE_MOUNTAIN_EXPERIENCES**. For longer stays, combine **LUCERNE + JUNGFRAU_REGION + ZERMATT / ONE_CONTRASTING_REGION** rather than repeatedly changing hotels.', 2257),
  ('switzerland', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Family', 'family', 'Use direct airport train where hotel location and luggage make it practical; otherwise use a pre-booked private transfer / taxi. For families continuing immediately to Lucerne, Interlaken, Bern, Lausanne, or another rail-connected destination, continuing by train directly from the airport can avoid unnecessary city transfers.', 2258),
  ('switzerland', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Honeymoon', 'honeymoon', 'Prefer first-class rail or private transfer according to hotel location and luggage. For multi-destination honeymoon itineraries, scenic and regular rail generally provides a more relaxed experience than repeated driving.', 2259),
  ('switzerland', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Luxury', 'luxury', 'Use chauffeured premium sedan / SUV or first-class rail with luggage assistance and private local transfers. For luxury multi-region itineraries, combine FIRST_CLASS_RAIL + PRIVATE_CHAUFFEUR + PREMIUM_MOUNTAIN_TRANSFERS.', 2260),
  ('switzerland', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Budget', 'budget', 'Use airport trains and regular public transport. Zurich and Geneva airports both have exceptionally convenient rail integration, so private airport transfers are usually unnecessary for budget travelers.', 2261),
  ('switzerland', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Senior', 'senior', 'Use direct airport rail where station access and luggage are manageable; otherwise prefer private transfer. Minimize unnecessary changes and choose hotels close to railway stations or easy local transport.', 2262),
  ('switzerland', 18, 'family-travel', 'FAMILY TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'child_friendly_score: 96 best_ages: Rules: For young children: Prefer: Avoid: Switzerland Tourism specifically promotes family resorts, child-friendly hikes, lakes, cable cars, themed trails, snow parks, and family accommodation across the country.', 2263),
  ('switzerland', 19, 'honeymoon-travel', 'HONEYMOON TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'honeymoon_score: 97 romance_score: 96 privacy_score: 94 luxury_score: 96 Recommended: Honeymoon itineraries should not contain more than: 2–3 major experiences/day. Prefer: One memorable mountain, lake, scenic-rail, dining, or wellness experience + free time over: Constant sightseeing and hotel changes. Recommended areas: Switzerland is especially suitable for couples seeking **MOUNTAINS + LAKES + SCENIC_RAIL + LUXURY + PRIVACY + SPA + PHOTOGRAPHY + SLOW_TRAVEL**.', 2264),
  ('switzerland', 20, 'luxury-travel', 'LUXURY TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'luxury_score: 96 Recommended: Switzerland luxury travel should focus on: Zermatt, St. Moritz, Lake Geneva, Zurich, Lucerne, and selected Alpine resorts provide Switzerland''s strongest premium-travel ecosystem.', 2265),
  ('switzerland', 21, 'adventure', 'ADVENTURE', NULL, NULL, 'adventure_score: 97 Switzerland is one of Europe''s strongest mountain and outdoor destinations. Adventure experiences should be interpreted as: Switzerland Tourism identifies more than 65,000 km of waymarked hiking trails and promotes mountain biking, rafting, canyoning, kayaking, sailing, trail running and other Alpine activities. Adventure activities should always be matched to altitude, season, weather, avalanche conditions, traveler fitness, and professional guidance requirements.', 2266),
  ('switzerland', 22, 'senior-travel', 'SENIOR TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'senior_suitability: 94 walking_intensity: LOW–MEDIUM with rail / cable-car focused planning MEDIUM–HIGH for mountain trails and winter conditions Rules: Switzerland works exceptionally well for seniors when positioned as a **SCENIC_RAIL + LAKES + MOUNTAIN_RAILWAYS + HISTORIC_CITIES + WELLNESS + RELAXED_TRAVEL destination**. Train, boat and bus travel is specifically promoted by Switzerland Tourism as a comfortable way to explore the country.', 2267),
  ('switzerland', 23, 'accessibility', 'ACCESSIBILITY', NULL, NULL, 'wheelchair_accessibility: GOOD IN MANY MODERN TRANSPORT / URBAN ENVIRONMENTS → VARIABLE IN HISTORIC AND MOUNTAIN AREAS public_transport_accessibility: GOOD → VERY_GOOD overall; verify specific station, vehicle, mountain railway, cable car, and route hotel_accessibility: MUST_BE_VERIFIED_PER_HOTEL attraction_accessibility: MUST_BE_VERIFIED_PER_ATTRACTION Rule: Never infer accessibility from Switzerland''s excellent overall infrastructure. Each hotel, railway station, boat, cable car, mountain railway, restaurant, historic site, trail, and ski facility should carry its own accessibility data. Additional notes:', 2268),
  ('switzerland', 24, 'food', 'FOOD', NULL, NULL, 'Switzerland is particularly strong for: Swiss cuisine reflects German-, French-, Italian-, and Alpine regional influences. Food experiences: Family: Prioritize chocolate, rösti, pasta, breads, cheese, pastries, and simple Alpine meals. Honeymoon: Choose mountain-view dining, lakefront restaurants, chocolate experiences, wine, and fine dining. Luxury: Include Michelin-level dining, premium hotel restaurants, private culinary experiences, wine, and high-end Alpine dining. Budget: Use supermarkets, bakeries, casual cafés, takeaway meals, and picnic lunches to control Switzerland''s high food costs.', 2269),
  ('switzerland', 25, 'shopping', 'SHOPPING', NULL, NULL, 'Strong categories: Luxury shopping: Switzerland is particularly strong for watches, jewellery, premium chocolate, and luxury goods. Prefer: Budget: Prefer: Travel-agent rule: Use ZURICH + GENEVA + LUCERNE for WATCHES_AND_LUXURY, LOCAL_SHOPS for REGIONAL_CRAFTS, and SUPERMARKETS / CHOCOLATE_STORES for FOOD_GIFTS. Prioritize authorized dealers for high-value watches and jewellery.', 2270),
  ('switzerland', 26, 'nightlife', 'NIGHTLIFE', NULL, NULL, 'nightlife_level: 78 Suitable for: Best areas: Evening activities are better suited to: Switzerland has good nightlife in major cities and Alpine resorts, but nightlife is secondary to its mountain, lake, nature, and scenic-travel strengths. Honeymoon travelers should generally prefer: LAKE_OR_MOUNTAIN_DINNER + SPA + HOTEL_LOUNGE / SCENIC_EVENING over: Club-heavy itineraries unless specifically requested. Travel-agent rule: Position Switzerland as a **STRONG DINING + LOUNGE + APRÈS_SKI + PREMIUM_CITY_NIGHTLIFE destination**, but not primarily as a party-focused country.', 2271),
  ('switzerland', 28, 'sample-itinerary-patterns', 'SAMPLE ITINERARY PATTERNS', '3 NIGHTS', NULL, '### Day 1 Arrival at Zurich Airport (ZRH) → Direct train / private transfer toward Lucerne → Hotel check-in → Relaxation and refreshment Afternoon: Lucerne orientation → Chapel Bridge → Old Town → Lion Monument → Lake Lucerne waterfront → Historic streets and photography Evening: Traditional Swiss dinner → Optional Lake Lucerne cruise according to season and schedule → Relaxed lakeside walk → Hotel Lucerne works extremely well as the first base because it combines a historic city, lake scenery, mountain access, and excellent onward rail connections. Switzerland Tourism also positions Lucerne as one of the key stops on the Zurich–Lucerne–Interlaken scenic corridor. ### Day 2 Morning: Breakfast → Choose ONE signature Lucerne mountain excursion Option 1: → Mount Titlis → Engelberg → Cable-car / gondola experience → Alpine and glacier scenery → Snow experience according to season Option 2: → Mount Pilatus → Mountain railway / cable-car experience → Panoramic Central Switzerland views Option 3: → Mount Rigi → Cogwheel railway → Lake and Alpine panoramas → Relaxed mountain walking Afternoon: Mountain lunch → Continue scenic exploration → Return to Lucerne Evening: Hotel relaxation → Swiss fondue / raclette experience → Optional spa / lakefront leisure → Hotel For a short stay, one major mountain excursion provides better value than trying to combine Titlis + Pilatus + Rigi in the same day. ### Day 3 Morning: Breakfast → Luzern–Interlaken Express → Scenic railway through lakes and mountain landscapes → Arrival in Interlaken → Continue toward Jungfrau Region The Luzern–Interlaken Express takes roughly 1 hour 50 minutes and passes five mountain lakes; Switzerland Tourism treats it as part of the scenic GoldenPass route. Choose ONE primary experience: JUNGFRAUJOCH: → Interlaken → Grindelwald / Lauterbrunnen connection → Jungfraujoch – Top of Europe → High-Alpine scenery → Snow / glacier experience → Photography OR GRINDELWALD_AND_LAUTERBRUNNEN: → Grindelwald → Alpine village scenery → Lauterbrunnen Valley → Waterfalls → Easy scenic walking → Mountain photography OR INTERLAKEN_RELAXED: → Interlaken → Höhematte area → Lake / mountain views → Harder Kulm according to operation → Relaxed town and café experience Afternoon: Continue selected Jungfrau Region experience → Return toward Lucerne or overnight in Interlaken according to hotel strategy Evening: Swiss dinner → Relaxed final evening → Hotel The Jungfrau Region is one of the principal highlights on Switzerland Tourism''s official Grand Train Tour itineraries, alongside Lucerne, Interlaken and Zermatt. ### Day 4 Breakfast → Leisure morning according to departure schedule → Optional short Lucerne / Interlaken walk → Chocolate / souvenir shopping → Hotel checkout → Rail transfer to Zurich Airport → Departure Optional alternative according to traveler interest: FAMILY: → Lucerne → Lake cruise → Mount Rigi / Titlis → Interlaken → Grindelwald → Easy snow or mountain experience HONEYMOON: → Lake-view hotel → Lucerne evening → Scenic train → Lauterbrunnen → Grindelwald → Mountain dining → Spa / free couple time LUXURY: → Five-star lake or mountain hotel → First-class rail → Private guide → Chauffeured local transfers → Premium mountain excursion → Fine dining → Spa / wellness ADVENTURE: → Grindelwald First → Hiking → Paragliding according to conditions → Jungfrau Region outdoor activities → Mountain photography NATURE / PHOTOGRAPHY: → Lake Lucerne → Scenic rail → Lauterbrunnen Valley → Grindelwald → Jungfrau viewpoints → Alpine sunrise / sunset photography REGIONAL_EXCURSION: → Zermatt / Matterhorn instead of the Jungfrau day OR → Montreux + Chillon + Lavaux instead of the Jungfrau day For a 3-night first Switzerland visit, do not try to combine LUCERNE + JUNGFRAU + ZERMATT + MONTREUX + ST_MORITZ. Switzerland Tourism''s own Top Attractions itinerary requires a minimum of 5 days / 4 nights to combine Zurich, Lucerne, Interlaken, Montreux and Zermatt, while its Classic Grand Train Tour requires 7 days / 6 nights. Travel-agent rule: For 3 nights, prioritize: LUCERNE + ONE_SIGNATURE_MOUNTAIN_EXCURSION + INTERLAKEN / JUNGFRAU_REGION rather than maximum destination count.', 2272),
  ('switzerland', 29, 'five-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'FIVE-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 1', NULL, 'Arrival at Zurich Airport → Meet and assist → Scenic train journey to Lucerne using Swiss Travel Pass / valid rail ticket → Romantic hotel check-in → Relax and refresh Afternoon / Evening: Easy Lucerne orientation → Chapel Bridge → Old Town → Lake Lucerne waterfront → Couple photography → Optional short lake cruise according to schedule Evening: Romantic Swiss dinner → Lakeside walk → Relaxed couple time → Overnight at Lucerne', 2273),
  ('switzerland', 29, 'five-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'FIVE-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 2', NULL, 'Breakfast at the hotel → Train from Lucerne to Engelberg → Continue toward Mt. Titlis Morning / Afternoon: → Cable-car journey → TITLIS Rotair → Snow and glacier scenery → Ice Flyer where operating → Titlis Cliff Walk subject to weather → Couple photography Later Afternoon: → Return to Lucerne → Optional Lake Lucerne cruise → Lion Monument → Short Old Town leisure Evening: Romantic dinner → Optional spa / wellness → Overnight at Lucerne', 2274),
  ('switzerland', 29, 'five-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'FIVE-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 3', NULL, 'Breakfast at the hotel → Hotel checkout → Scenic Lucerne–Interlaken rail journey → Arrival in Interlaken → Romantic hotel check-in Afternoon: → Höhematte area → Interlaken town walk → Lake and mountain scenery → Café / chocolate stop → Couple photography Optional: → Harder Kulm according to seasonal operation Evening: Mountain-view dinner → Relaxed Interlaken evening → Overnight at Interlaken', 2275),
  ('switzerland', 29, 'five-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'FIVE-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 4', NULL, 'Breakfast at the hotel Choose ONE primary experience: JUNGFRAUJOCH: → Grindelwald / Lauterbrunnen connection → Jungfraujoch – Top of Europe → Snow and glacier experience → Alpine viewpoints → Couple photography OR ROMANTIC_JUNGFRAU_REGION: → Lauterbrunnen Valley → Waterfalls → Wengen / Grindelwald → Scenic village walks → Mountain cafés → Relaxed couple time OR BERN_CITY: → Train to Bern → UNESCO Old Town → Zytglogge → Aare River views → Historic streets → Café / shopping time Do not combine Jungfraujoch and Bern into the same full sightseeing day. Evening: Return to Interlaken → Special honeymoon dinner → Overnight at Interlaken', 2276),
  ('switzerland', 29, 'five-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'FIVE-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 5', NULL, 'Breakfast at the hotel → Hotel checkout → Scenic train toward Zurich → Zurich hotel check-in / luggage drop Afternoon: Private or rail-based excursion to Rhine Falls → Waterfall viewpoints → Couple photography → Optional boat experience where operating → Return to Zurich Late Afternoon / Evening: → Zurich Old Town → Bahnhofstrasse → Lake Zurich waterfront → Café / luxury shopping → Relaxed city walk Evening: Farewell honeymoon dinner → Optional cocktail lounge / hotel bar → Overnight at Zurich', 2277),
  ('switzerland', 29, 'five-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'FIVE-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 6', NULL, 'Breakfast at the hotel → Leisure morning according to flight / onward-travel schedule → Optional short Lake Zurich walk → Swiss chocolate / souvenir shopping → Hotel checkout → Transfer to Zurich Airport for departure OR, for a longer European honeymoon: → Continue by air / rail toward Luxembourg or Belgium → Add Luxembourg City for Old Town, Grund, Corniche, castles and romantic dining OR: → Add Brussels / Bruges for Grand Place, canals, Belgian chocolate, historic streets and romantic city atmosphere HONEYMOON PACING RULE: LUCERNE_2_NIGHTS + INTERLAKEN_2_NIGHTS + ZURICH_1_NIGHT Prioritize: LUCERNE + MT_TITLIS + SCENIC_RAIL + INTERLAKEN + ONE_JUNGFRAU_REGION_EXPERIENCE + RHINE_FALLS + ZURICH Keep: 2–3 major experiences/day maximum. Prefer: SCENERY + ROMANTIC_HOTELS + MOUNTAIN_VIEWS + LAKE_TIME + SCENIC_RAIL + DINING + FREE_COUPLE_TIME For extended multi-country honeymoons: SWITZERLAND + ONE_OF_LUXEMBOURG_OR_BELGIUM works better than adding several additional countries rapidly. Luxembourg adds CASTLES + OLD_TOWN + WINE + QUIET_ROMANCE, while Belgium adds BRUGES + BRUSSELS + CHOCOLATE + HISTORIC_CITY_ROMANCE. Avoid trying to add Luxembourg + Belgium + Zermatt + Montreux + St. Moritz within the same 5-night programme.', 2278),
  ('switzerland', 30, 'five-nights-family-pattern', 'FIVE-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 1', NULL, 'Arrival at Zurich Airport → Train / private transfer to Lucerne → Family hotel check-in → Relax and refresh Afternoon / Evening: Easy Lucerne orientation → Chapel Bridge → Old Town → Lake Lucerne waterfront → Family photography → Optional short lake cruise Evening: Family-friendly Swiss / international dinner → Relaxed lakeside walk → Overnight at Lucerne', 2279),
  ('switzerland', 30, 'five-nights-family-pattern', 'FIVE-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 2', NULL, 'Breakfast at the hotel → Train to Engelberg → Continue toward Mt. Titlis Morning / Afternoon: → Cable-car journey → TITLIS Rotair → Snow and glacier scenery → Ice Flyer where operating → Titlis Cliff Walk subject to weather and children''s comfort → Family snow time → Photography Later Afternoon: → Return to Lucerne → Lion Monument → Optional Lake Lucerne cruise → Free family time Evening: Dinner → Hotel relaxation → Overnight at Lucerne', 2280),
  ('switzerland', 30, 'five-nights-family-pattern', 'FIVE-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 3', NULL, 'Breakfast at the hotel → Hotel checkout → Scenic Lucerne–Interlaken train journey → Arrival in Interlaken → Family hotel check-in Afternoon: → Höhematte → Interlaken town walk → Mountain views → Swiss chocolate / café stop → Family leisure time Optional: → Harder Kulm according to season, weather, and operation Evening: Family dinner → Relaxed evening → Overnight at Interlaken', 2281),
  ('switzerland', 30, 'five-nights-family-pattern', 'FIVE-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 4', NULL, 'Breakfast at the hotel Choose ONE primary family experience: JUNGFRAUJOCH: → Grindelwald connection → Jungfraujoch – Top of Europe → Snow and glacier scenery → Family photography → Indoor and outdoor viewpoints OR EASY_FAMILY_ALPINE_DAY: → Lauterbrunnen → Waterfalls → Wengen / Grindelwald → Easy village exploration → Scenic train journeys → Family lunch → Relaxed mountain time For families with younger children, the lower-altitude Lauterbrunnen / Grindelwald option can provide an easier day than Jungfraujoch. Evening: → Return to Interlaken → Family dinner → Overnight at Interlaken', 2282),
  ('switzerland', 30, 'five-nights-family-pattern', 'FIVE-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 5', NULL, 'Breakfast at the hotel → Hotel checkout → Train to Zurich → Hotel check-in / luggage drop Afternoon: → Rhine Falls excursion → Waterfall viewpoints → Family photography → Optional boat experience where operating Later: → Return to Zurich → Old Town → Bahnhofstrasse → Lake Zurich waterfront → Chocolate / souvenir shopping Evening: Farewell family dinner → Overnight at Zurich', 2283),
  ('switzerland', 30, 'five-nights-family-pattern', 'FIVE-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 6', NULL, 'Breakfast → Leisure morning according to flight / onward schedule → Hotel checkout → Transfer to Zurich Airport → Departure OR, for a longer family Europe itinerary: → Continue toward Luxembourg or Belgium LUXEMBOURG_FAMILY_EXTENSION: → Luxembourg City → Vianden Castle → Parc Merveilleux → Easy Mullerthal / Echternach experience BELGIUM_FAMILY_EXTENSION: → Brussels → Grand Place → Belgian chocolate / waffle experience → Bruges where itinerary time allows FAMILY PACING RULE: LUCERNE_2_NIGHTS + INTERLAKEN_2_NIGHTS + ZURICH_1_NIGHT Prioritize: LUCERNE + MT_TITLIS + SCENIC_TRAIN + INTERLAKEN + JUNGFRAU_REGION + RHINE_FALLS + ZURICH Keep: 2–3 major experiences/day maximum. For younger children, prioritize: LAKE_CRUISES + SCENIC_TRAINS + EASY_VILLAGE_WALKS + SNOW_PLAY + SHORT_CITY_WALKS over: LONG_HIKES + MULTIPLE_MOUNTAIN_EXCURSIONS + OVERPACKED_TRANSFER_DAYS For longer Europe family trips: SWITZERLAND + LUXEMBOURG works well for MOUNTAINS + CASTLES + FAMILY_ATTRACTIONS, while: SWITZERLAND + BELGIUM works well for MOUNTAINS + HISTORIC_CITIES + CHOCOLATE + FAMILY_CITY_EXPERIENCES. Do not attempt Switzerland + Luxembourg + Belgium within the same 5 nights.', 2284),
  ('switzerland', 31, 'five-nights-luxury-pattern', 'FIVE-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 1', NULL, 'Arrival at Zurich Airport → VIP meet and assist → Private chauffeured transfer to Lucerne → Premium lake-view hotel check-in → Welcome amenities → Relax and refresh Afternoon / Evening: Private Lucerne orientation → Chapel Bridge → Old Town → Lake Lucerne waterfront → Private / premium photography opportunity Evening: Fine-dining experience → Optional private lake cruise → Hotel spa / lounge → Overnight at Lucerne', 2285),
  ('switzerland', 31, 'five-nights-luxury-pattern', 'FIVE-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 2', NULL, 'Breakfast at the hotel → Private transfer / first-class rail to Engelberg → Premium Mt. Titlis excursion Morning / Afternoon: → Cable-car journey → TITLIS Rotair → Glacier and Alpine scenery → Ice Flyer where operating → Titlis Cliff Walk subject to conditions → Private guide where preferred → Mountain lunch Afternoon: → Return to Lucerne → Hotel relaxation → Spa / wellness → Optional private Lake Lucerne cruise Evening: Premium Swiss / international dinner → Overnight at Lucerne', 2286),
  ('switzerland', 31, 'five-nights-luxury-pattern', 'FIVE-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 3', NULL, 'Breakfast → Hotel checkout → First-class scenic rail journey to Interlaken → Private station transfer → Premium hotel / suite check-in Afternoon: → Relaxed Interlaken orientation → Höhematte → Luxury shopping / Swiss chocolate → Optional Harder Kulm → Hotel spa and leisure Evening: Fine dining / private dinner → Overnight at Interlaken', 2287),
  ('switzerland', 31, 'five-nights-luxury-pattern', 'FIVE-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 4', NULL, 'Breakfast at the hotel Choose ONE premium experience: JUNGFRAUJOCH: → Private guide → Premium rail arrangements → Jungfraujoch – Top of Europe → Glacier scenery → Alpine viewpoints → Private photography → Premium lunch OR LUXURY_ALPINE_DAY: → Lauterbrunnen → Wengen → Grindelwald → Chauffeured / premium rail connections → Scenic village exploration → Mountain dining → Flexible photography stops Afternoon: → Return to Interlaken → Spa / wellness → Free leisure time Evening: Special fine-dining experience → Overnight at Interlaken', 2288),
  ('switzerland', 31, 'five-nights-luxury-pattern', 'FIVE-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 5', NULL, 'Breakfast → Hotel checkout → First-class rail / private chauffeur to Zurich → Luxury hotel check-in Afternoon: Private Rhine Falls excursion → Chauffeured transfer → Premium viewpoint experience → Optional boat experience where operating → Flexible photography time Return to Zurich → Bahnhofstrasse → Luxury boutiques → Old Town → Lake Zurich waterfront Evening: Farewell fine-dining experience → Optional luxury bar / lounge → Overnight at Zurich', 2289),
  ('switzerland', 31, 'five-nights-luxury-pattern', 'FIVE-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 6', NULL, 'Breakfast → Leisure morning → Optional spa / premium shopping → Luxury hotel checkout → Chauffeured private transfer to Zurich Airport → Departure OR, for an extended luxury Europe itinerary: LUXEMBOURG_EXTENSION: → Premium Luxembourg City hotel → Chauffeured Old Town / castle touring → Fine dining → Moselle wine / Crémant experience → Boutique countryside stay where desired OR BELGIUM_EXTENSION: → Luxury Brussels / Bruges stay → Private heritage guide → Grand Place → Premium Belgian chocolate experience → Fine dining → Designer / luxury shopping → Private Bruges excursion LUXURY PACING RULE: LUCERNE_2_NIGHTS + INTERLAKEN_2_NIGHTS + ZURICH_1_NIGHT Prioritize: 5_STAR_HOTELS + PRIVATE_TRANSFERS + FIRST_CLASS_RAIL + PRIVATE_GUIDES + PREMIUM_MOUNTAIN_EXPERIENCES + FINE_DINING + SPA_AND_WELLNESS + FLEXIBLE_FREE_TIME Luxury Switzerland should emphasize: PRIVACY + COMFORT + SCENIC_TRAVEL + PERSONALIZED_SERVICE + PREMIUM_HOTELS + ALPINE_EXPERIENCES For an extended premium itinerary: SWITZERLAND + LUXEMBOURG provides: ALPINE_LUXURY + CASTLES + WINE + QUIET_PREMIUM_TRAVEL while: SWITZERLAND + BELGIUM provides: ALPINE_LUXURY + HISTORIC_CITIES + GASTRONOMY + CHOCOLATE + PREMIUM_SHOPPING. Luxembourg or Belgium should be added as a proper extension after Switzerland, rather than reducing Lucerne / Interlaken into rushed one-night stays.', 2290),
  ('switzerland', 32, 'travel-agent-insights', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS', 'What inexperienced planners often do wrong', NULL, '', 2291),
  ('switzerland', 32, 'travel-agent-insights', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS', 'What an experienced planner does differently', NULL, '', 2292),
  ('switzerland', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', NULL, NULL, 'IF: trip_length <= 4 nights THEN: prioritize_LUCERNE + ONE_SIGNATURE_MOUNTAIN_EXCURSION + INTERLAKEN_OR_JUNGFRAU AND: do not recommend ZERMATT + MONTREUX + ST_MORITZ + TICINO as default additions. Reason: A short Switzerland trip gains more value from two well-connected bases and one or two major mountain experiences than from repeated hotel and rail changes. IF: trip_length >= 7 nights AND: traveler_interest == FIRST_TIME_SWITZERLAND THEN: prioritize_LUCERNE + JUNGFRAU_REGION + ZERMATT AND: consider_ZURICH_OR_MONTREUX_OR_ONE_PANORAMIC_RAIL_ROUTE Reason: This combination introduces Switzerland''s strongest first-time products: lakes, historic cities, Alpine villages, mountain railways, Matterhorn scenery, and scenic train travel. Switzerland Tourism''s Classic Grand Train Tour requires at least 7 days / 6 nights, confirming that broader multi-region touring needs substantially more time. IF: trip_type == HONEYMOON THEN: increase_romance_weight by 20% increase_free_time_weight by 25% decrease_activity_density by 20% prefer_LUCERNE + JUNGFRAU_REGION + ZERMATT_OR_MONTREUX Reason: Switzerland''s honeymoon strength comes from lakes, mountain-view hotels, panoramic trains, Alpine villages, spa, fine dining, scenery, and relaxed couple time. IF: traveler_type == FAMILY AND: children_age <= 6 THEN: reduce_HIGH_ALTITUDE_ACTIVITY_DENSITY by 25% increase_downtime by 25% prefer_LAKE_CRUISES + EASY_MOUNTAIN_RAILWAYS + SNOW_PLAY + FAMILY_RESORTS + SHORT_VILLAGE_WALKS Reason: Young children generally benefit more from cable cars, lakes, themed trails, easy hikes, snow play, and family resorts than repeated high-altitude summit days. Switzerland Tourism specifically promotes child-friendly hikes, swimming lakes, cable cars, themed trails, and family resorts. IF: traveler_type == FAMILY AND: children_age >= 7 THEN: consider_LUCERNE + TITLIS_OR_RIGI + INTERLAKEN + GRINDELWALD + LAUTERBRUNNEN AND: include_EDUCATIONAL + SCENIC_RAIL + OUTDOOR_EXPERIENCES Reason: Older children can combine mountain railways, waterfalls, snow experiences, hiking, trains, lakes, and interactive outdoor activities more effectively. IF: traveler_type == LUXURY THEN: prefer_5_STAR_ALPINE_OR_LAKE_HOTEL AND: prefer_FIRST_CLASS_RAIL + PRIVATE_DRIVER + EXPERT_GUIDE AND: increase_SPA + FINE_DINING + PREMIUM_MOUNTAIN + LUXURY_SHOPPING_WEIGHT Reason: Luxury in Switzerland should improve privacy, service, hotel quality, rail comfort, mountain access, gastronomy, wellness, and itinerary flexibility rather than simply adding more destinations. IF: traveler_type == BUDGET THEN: prefer_HOSTEL_OR_GUESTHOUSE_NEAR_RAILWAY_STATION AND: compare_SWISS_TRAVEL_PASS + HALF_FARE_CARD + POINT_TO_POINT_TICKETS AND: prioritize_HIKING + LAKEFRONTS + HISTORIC_CENTRES + SELECTIVE_SUMMIT_EXCURSIONS Reason: Switzerland remains expensive, so accommodation location, rail products, food costs, and mountain-ticket spending must be optimized together. IF: traveler_interest == SCENIC_RAIL THEN: prefer_ONE_OF_GLACIER_EXPRESS_OR_BERNINA_EXPRESS_OR_GOLDENPASS_EXPRESS AND: allocate_FULL_TRAVEL_DAY_WHERE_REQUIRED Reason: Panoramic trains are destination experiences in their own right. Switzerland Tourism''s Grand Train Tour spans 1,280 km, eight sections, eleven major lakes and several flagship scenic routes. IF: traveler_interest == CULTURE_AND_HERITAGE THEN: prefer_BERN + LUCERNE + ZURICH_OR_BASEL AND: consider_CHILLON + BELLINZONA + APPENZELL_FOR_LONGER_STAYS Reason: Switzerland''s cultural layer is strongest through medieval old towns, museums, castles, regional architecture, multilingual traditions, and historic transport heritage. IF: traveler_interest == FOOD_AND_GASTRONOMY THEN: prefer_LUCERNE + ZURICH + TICINO + GRUYERES_REGION AND: include_FONDUE + RACLETTE + CHOCOLATE + CHEESE + REGIONAL_SWISS_CUISINE Reason: Swiss gastronomy varies regionally and should be treated as more than a simple fondue experience. IF: traveler_interest == ROMANTIC_RELAXATION THEN: prefer_LUCERNE + ZERMATT + MONTREUX AND: decrease_activity_density_by_20_percent Reason: Lakefront hotels, Matterhorn views, panoramic trains, spa, mountain dining, and quiet scenic environments create Switzerland''s strongest romantic product. IF: traveler_interest == SKIING_AND_WINTER_SPORTS THEN: prefer_ZERMATT + ST_MORITZ + DAVOS_KLOSTERS_OR_JUNGFRAU_REGION AND: verify_SNOW + LIFT_OPERATIONS + PISTE_STATUS + EQUIPMENT Reason: Switzerland''s ski product is destination-specific and depends on altitude, snow, resort operations, traveler ability, and seasonal conditions. IF: traveler_interest == SUMMER_HIKING THEN: prefer_JUNGFRAU_REGION + ZERMATT + APPENZELL + ENGADIN AND: verify_TRAIL_STATUS + WEATHER + ALTITUDE + FITNESS Reason: Summer provides extensive Alpine hiking, but routes differ greatly in difficulty, exposure, altitude, and seasonal opening. IF: traveler_interest == NATURE_AND_ADVENTURE THEN: prefer_JUNGFRAU_REGION + ZERMATT + ENGADIN + APPENZELL AND: match_ACTIVITY_TO_SEASON + FITNESS + WEATHER Reason: Switzerland supports hiking, mountaineering, paragliding, skiing, mountain biking, canyoning, rafting, and other Alpine activities. IF: traveler_interest == LAKES_AND_RELAXATION THEN: prefer_LUCERNE + MONTREUX_LAKE_GENEVA + TICINO AND: include_BOAT_CRUISES + WATERFRONT_WALKS + SPA + SLOW_TRAVEL Reason: Lake travel provides a lower-intensity alternative to repeated mountain excursions and works especially well for couples, families, and seniors. IF: traveler_interest == SHOPPING_AND_LUXURY THEN: prioritize_ZURICH + GENEVA + LUCERNE AND: consider_ST_MORITZ_FOR_PREMIUM_RESORT_SHOPPING Reason: Zurich and Geneva provide the strongest concentrations of watches, jewellery, designer retail, luxury hotels, and premium shopping. IF: traveler_interest == PHOTOGRAPHY THEN: prefer_JUNGFRAU_REGION + ZERMATT + LUCERNE + MONTREUX + APPENZELL AND: prioritize_EARLY_MORNING + LATE_AFTERNOON + CLEAR_WEATHER_WINDOWS Reason: Swiss photography depends heavily on visibility, light, mountain weather, reflections, snow conditions, and seasonal landscapes. IF: traveler_interest == MATTERHORN THEN: allocate_MINIMUM_TWO_NIGHTS_ZERMATT AND: keep_ONE_WEATHER_FLEXIBLE_PERIOD Reason: The Matterhorn can disappear behind cloud even during otherwise good weather, so a one-night visit increases the risk of missing the signature view. IF: traveler_interest == JUNGFRAUJOCH THEN: use_INTERLAKEN_OR_JUNGFRAU_REGION_AS_BASE AND: verify_WEATHER + VISIBILITY + HIGH_ALTITUDE_SUITABILITY Reason: Jungfraujoch is a major high-altitude excursion and should be treated as a dedicated mountain day rather than combined with heavy city sightseeing. IF: traveler_interest == LUCERNE_MOUNTAINS THEN: choose_ONE_OF_TITLIS_OR_PILATUS_OR_RIGI_PER_MAJOR_DAY Reason: Trying to cover multiple signature peaks in one day reduces scenic value and adds unnecessary transport and queue time. IF: traveler_interest == GOLDENPASS_ROUTE THEN: prefer_INTERLAKEN_TO_MONTREUX_DIRECTION_OR_REVERSE AND: treat_ROUTE_AS_MAJOR_SCENIC_EXPERIENCE Reason: Switzerland Tourism identifies Interlaken–Montreux as one of the core panoramic stages connecting the Bernese Oberland with Lake Geneva. IF: traveler_interest == GLACIER_EXPRESS THEN: prefer_ZERMATT + ST_MORITZ_OR_CHUR_ITINERARY AND: avoid_adding_HEAVY_SIGHTSEEING_ON_THE_SAME_DAY Reason: The Glacier Express is a long panoramic journey and should be treated as a full scenic travel day rather than simply transportation between hotels. IF: trip_length <= 7 nights THEN: avoid_EXCESSIVE_HOTEL_CHANGES AND: prefer_MAXIMUM_TWO_OR_THREE_BASES Reason: Even Switzerland''s efficient railway network cannot eliminate the time lost to packing, luggage handling, hotel check-in, and repeated station transfers. IF: hotel_is_far_from_RAILWAY_STATION_OR_REQUIRED_MOUNTAIN_CONNECTION AND: hotel_saving < additional_transport_cost + value_of_lost_time THEN: prefer_BETTER_CONNECTED_HOTEL Reason: Railway-station proximity can materially improve total value in a country where trains form the backbone of most itineraries. IF: traveler_interest == PANORAMIC_MULTI_REGION_ITINERARY AND: trip_length >= 6 nights THEN: consider_GRAND_TRAIN_TOUR_LOGIC Reason: Switzerland Tourism''s Lakes & Peaks itinerary requires at least 6 days / 5 nights and combines Zurich, Lucerne, Interlaken, Montreux, Zermatt, Lugano and St. Moritz through multiple panoramic routes. IF: weather == POOR_MOUNTAIN_VISIBILITY THEN: reduce_HIGH_ALPINE_VIEWPOINTS AND: prefer_LUCERNE_OR_BERN_OR_ZURICH_CITY + MUSEUMS + LAKEFRONT + SPA Reason: Cloud, fog, strong wind, or precipitation can substantially reduce the value or operation of high-mountain excursions. IF: weather == HEAVY_SNOW OR: avalanche_risk == ELEVATED THEN: verify_MOUNTAIN_RAILWAYS + SKI_LIFTS + TRAILS + ROAD_ACCESS AND: avoid_UNVERIFIED_HIGH_ALPINE_ACTIVITY Reason: Good snowfall can improve ski conditions while simultaneously restricting hiking, road travel, cable cars, and other mountain activities. IF: traveler_type == SENIOR OR: traveler_mobility == LIMITED THEN: reduce_STEEP_HIKING + MULTIPLE_HIGH_ALTITUDE_DAYS AND: prefer_SCENIC_RAIL + LAKE_CRUISES + MOUNTAIN_RAILWAYS + HISTORIC_CITIES + SPA Reason: Switzerland is exceptionally suitable for lower-intensity scenic touring when railways, boats, funiculars, and cable cars are used strategically. IF: traveler_uses_WHEELCHAIR THEN: prefer_VERIFIED_ACCESSIBLE_HOTEL + VERIFIED_RAIL_CONNECTION + VERIFIED_MOUNTAIN_TRANSPORT AND: avoid_assuming_ALPINE_TRAILS + HISTORIC_STREETS + SNOW_AREAS_ARE_STEP_FREE Reason: Switzerland has strong transport infrastructure, but accessibility still varies substantially between stations, mountain facilities, historic environments, and natural attractions. IF: traveler_interest == FIRST_TIME_SWITZERLAND THEN: prioritize_LUCERNE + INTERLAKEN_JUNGFRAU AND: add_ZERMATT_FOR_7_PLUS_NIGHTS AND: add_ONE_OF_ZURICH_OR_MONTREUX_OR_PANORAMIC_RAIL_FOR_LONGER_TRIPS Reason: This sequence provides the clearest introduction to Switzerland''s lakes, mountains, villages, railways, historic centres, and iconic Alpine scenery. IF: traveler_interest == AUTHENTIC_LOCAL_EXPERIENCE THEN: prefer_APPENZELL + SMALL_ALPINE_VILLAGES + REGIONAL_DINING + LOCAL_CHEESE_AND_CHOCOLATE AND: decrease_SIGNATURE_SUMMIT_ONLY_WEIGHT Reason: Traditional villages, regional food, local railways, farms, architecture, and everyday Alpine culture provide deeper Swiss context than visiting only famous summit attractions. IF: traveler_interest == RELAXATION_AND_SCENERY_BALANCE THEN: allocate_APPROXIMATELY_60_TO_70_PERCENT_TO_MOUNTAIN + LAKE + SCENIC_RAIL_EXPERIENCES AND: allocate_REMAINING_TIME_TO_SPA + DINING + VILLAGE_WALKS + SHOPPING + FREE_TIME Reason: Switzerland is best experienced when major scenic attractions are balanced with slower rail travel, lakes, villages, wellness, and unstructured time.', 2293),
  ('switzerland', 34, 'destination-scoring', 'DESTINATION SCORING', NULL, NULL, '| Factor | Score | | ------------------ | ----: | | Family | 96 | | Honeymoon | 97 | | Luxury | 96 | | Budget | 58 | | Adventure | 97 | | Culture | 88 | | Food | 88 | | Shopping | 89 | | Nightlife | 78 | | Relaxation | 97 | | Nature | 99 | | Accessibility | 88 | | Safety | 95 | | First-time visitor | 97 | | Photography | 99 |', 2294),
  ('switzerland', 35, 'final-travel-agent-verdict', 'FINAL TRAVEL AGENT VERDICT', NULL, NULL, 'Best traveler profiles: 1. Nature / mountain traveler 2. Honeymoon / romantic traveler 3. Photography traveler 4. Adventure / hiking traveler 5. Family traveler 6. Luxury traveler 7. Ski / winter-sports traveler 8. Scenic-rail traveler 9. Relaxation / wellness traveler 10. First-time Europe traveler Best duration: 7–10 nights 4–5 nights for a focused first visit covering Lucerne, one signature mountain excursion, Interlaken / Jungfrau Region, and limited city sightseeing. 7–10 nights for most first-time visitors wanting Lucerne + Jungfrau Region + Zermatt with Zurich, Montreux, Bern, or one panoramic railway added according to interests. 12–14 nights for travelers wanting a broader rail-focused itinerary including Zermatt, St. Moritz, Ticino, Lake Geneva, Bern, or several sections of the Grand Train Tour. Switzerland Tourism''s official Top Attractions Tour requires at least 5 days / 4 nights, while its Classic Grand Train Tour begins at 7 days / 6 nights. Best season: YEAR-ROUND May–June for green landscapes, waterfalls, lakes, lower- and mid-altitude hiking, scenic trains, photography, and generally better balance before peak summer. July–August for the strongest overall hiking, mountain-railway, lake, village, cycling, and family-holiday conditions, but also some of the year''s highest crowds and prices. September–early October provide one of Switzerland''s strongest combinations of Alpine scenery, hiking, lakes, scenic rail, photography, and improving crowd levels. December–March are strongest for skiing, snowboarding, winter hiking, snow scenery, Alpine resorts, spa, and romantic winter travel. April and November are more transitional and can provide better value, but some mountain railways, hiking routes, cable cars, and seasonal facilities may have reduced operations. Best hotel strategy: Choose accommodation according to railway access and the main purpose of each stay. For first-time visitors, prioritize hotels close to stations in Lucerne, Interlaken / Jungfrau Region, Zermatt, Zurich, or Montreux to reduce luggage and transfer friction. For honeymoon and luxury travelers, consider lake-view hotels, Alpine resorts, premium mountain properties, spa hotels, or car-free Zermatt accommodation with strong scenic value. Avoid unnecessary one-night hotel changes. Best transportation: Train + regional rail + bus + boat for most national travel, trams / buses + walking within cities, and mountain railways / cable cars / funiculars for Alpine access. Switzerland''s Grand Train Tour alone covers 1,280 km across eight sections and eleven major lakes, demonstrating how strongly the country''s tourism product is structured around public transport and panoramic rail. Private transport for: Do not treat rental cars as essential for standard first-time Switzerland itineraries. Must-do for first-time visitor: Switzerland Tourism''s official Top Attractions Tour similarly centres on Lucerne, Interlaken, Montreux and Zermatt, with Chapel Bridge, Jungfrau Region, Lavaux, Chillon Castle and Matterhorn among its key highlights.} Don''t-do: Biggest advantage: Exceptional concentration of world-class Alpine scenery within an unusually efficient transport system. Switzerland combines mountains, glaciers, lakes, waterfalls, scenic railways, historic cities, mountain villages, skiing, hiking, luxury resorts, wellness, family travel, and some of Europe''s strongest landscape photography. Its official Grand Train Tour connects landscapes ranging from glaciers and major Alpine peaks to lakes, cities and palm-lined Ticino, while spanning four national languages and five UNESCO World Heritage Sites. Biggest disadvantage: Switzerland is expensive. Accommodation, restaurants, mountain railways, summit excursions, skiing, and premium scenic trains can raise costs quickly. Mountain weather also introduces uncertainty: cloud, wind, snowfall, seasonal closures, or poor visibility can reduce the value of expensive high-altitude excursions. Frequent hotel changes can additionally make even an efficient rail itinerary unnecessarily tiring. Overall destination score: 91/100', 2295),
  ('switzerland', 36, 'data-quality', 'DATA QUALITY', NULL, NULL, 'information_completeness: 96/100 last_updated: 2026-08-26 last_verified: PARTIALLY_WEB_VERIFIED verified_by: SWITZERLAND TOURISM / SBB / OFFICIAL SWISS DESTINATION, TRANSPORT, FAMILY AND ACCESSIBILITY SOURCES sources: IMPORTANT: Prices, hotel rates, rail fares, seat reservations, mountain-railway tickets, ski passes, cable-car schedules, lake-cruise timetables, attraction opening hours, and accessibility must NOT be treated as permanently valid. Lucerne mountain excursions, Jungfraujoch, Grindelwald First, Schilthorn, Gornergrat, Matterhorn Glacier Paradise, Glacier Express, Bernina Express, GoldenPass Express, and other major mountain / rail experiences should be checked against current official information before travel. Panoramic trains may require advance seat reservations even when the underlying rail journey is covered by a travel pass. Switzerland Tourism specifically identifies reservation requirements for selected panoramic services. Mountain weather, cloud, wind, snowfall, avalanche conditions, and visibility can materially affect high-altitude sightseeing, hiking, skiing, cable cars, and photography. Zermatt is car-free, so rail-based arrival and local transport arrangements should be planned accordingly. Accessibility is strong in many transport environments but must still be verified connection by connection. SBB provides accessible-connection information and assistance for passengers with reduced mobility. Historic streets, Alpine trails, snow surfaces, mountain viewpoints, cable-car stations, and older properties should not be assumed uniformly step-free. Switzerland should primarily be treated as: SPRING: LAKES + WATERFALLS + SCENIC_RAIL + CITIES + LOWER_ALTITUDE_HIKING + PHOTOGRAPHY SUMMER: MOUNTAINS + HIKING + LAKES + FAMILY + ADVENTURE + SCENIC_RAIL + VILLAGES AUTUMN: ALPINE_SCENERY + HIKING + PHOTOGRAPHY + SCENIC_RAIL + RELAXATION WINTER: SKIING + SNOWBOARDING + ALPINE_RESORTS + SNOW_SCENERY + SPA + WINTER_RAIL Switzerland Tourism, SBB, regional destination boards, mountain-railway operators, ski resorts, hotels, and individual attractions should be treated as the primary sources for current operational information. This dataset should be refreshed regularly before production use.', 2296),
  ('luxembourg', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Spring', NULL, 'months: March April May weather: March is cool and transitional, while April and May become progressively milder, greener, and better for city walks, castles, vineyards, cycling, and hiking. crowd_level: LOW → MEDIUM price_level: MEDIUM overall_score: 76–82 recommended: true reason: One of Luxembourg''s strongest periods for Luxembourg City, Vianden, Mullerthal, Echternach, castles, gardens, hiking, cycling, and photography. May offers particularly strong conditions before peak summer demand.', 2297),
  ('luxembourg', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Summer', NULL, 'months: June July August weather: Generally warm and suitable for sightseeing, hiking, cycling, forests, lakes, vineyards, outdoor dining, and countryside exploration. Hot spells and thunderstorms remain possible. crowd_level: MEDIUM → HIGH price_level: MEDIUM → HIGH overall_score: 68–77 recommended: true reason: Excellent for Mullerthal, Éislek, Upper Sûre, Luxembourg City, castles, cycling, festivals, outdoor activities, and family travel. July and August receive lower Crowd and Price scores because European summer holidays increase visitor demand.', 2298),
  ('luxembourg', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Autumn', NULL, 'months: September October November weather: September is usually comfortable for outdoor travel, October becomes cooler with strong autumn colours, while November is colder, wetter, and more transitional. crowd_level: MEDIUM → LOW price_level: MEDIUM → LOW overall_score: 76–82 recommended: true reason: September and October are among Luxembourg''s strongest months for hiking, castles, vineyards, Moselle wine experiences, photography, Luxembourg City, and countryside touring. November offers fewer crowds and better value but weaker outdoor conditions.', 2299),
  ('luxembourg', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Winter', NULL, 'months: December January February weather: Cold, cloudy, and often damp, with frost and occasional snow possible. Outdoor daylight is limited, but city, museum, castle, gastronomy, and festive travel remain practical. crowd_level: LOW → MEDIUM price_level: LOW → MEDIUM overall_score: 65–78 recommended: true reason: Best for Luxembourg City, museums, gastronomy, castles, winter walks, Christmas markets, wellness, and quieter cultural travel. December gains strong festive appeal through Luxembourg City''s Winterlights and Christmas markets, while January and February provide quieter conditions and generally stronger value.', 2300),
  ('luxembourg', 10, 'budget-strategy', 'BUDGET STRATEGY', NULL, NULL, 'Where money can be saved: Where saving money is usually NOT recommended: Travel-agent rule: In Luxembourg, **HOTEL_LOCATION + FREE_PUBLIC_TRANSPORT + ATTRACTION_ACCESS + SEASON should be evaluated together**. For short stays, prioritize **LUXEMBOURG_CITY + ONE_OR_TWO_REGIONAL_DAY_TRIPS**. For longer stays, combine **LUXEMBOURG_CITY + VIANDEN + MULLERTHAL + ONE_OF_MOSELLE_OR_EISLEK_OR_MINETT** without excessive hotel changes.', 2301),
  ('luxembourg', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Family', 'family', 'Use the free airport bus / public transport where luggage and children''s ages make it practical; otherwise use a pre-booked taxi or private transfer. Because Luxembourg Airport is close to the capital, families can reach central Luxembourg City relatively easily without a long transfer.', 2302),
  ('luxembourg', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Honeymoon', 'honeymoon', 'Prefer private transfer for maximum comfort or use free public transport when staying near a convenient central stop. For short honeymoon stays, avoid renting a car unless several rural experiences are planned.', 2303),
  ('luxembourg', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Luxury', 'luxury', 'Use chauffeured premium sedan / SUV with meet-and-assist, luggage handling, and direct hotel transfer. For luxury regional touring, combine PRIVATE_DRIVER + PREMIUM_HOTEL + SELECTIVE_CASTLE / WINE / COUNTRYSIDE_EXCURSIONS.', 2304),
  ('luxembourg', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Budget', 'budget', 'Use the free bus / tram / train system. Luxembourg is particularly budget-friendly for transportation because second-class national trains, buses, and trams are free.', 2305),
  ('luxembourg', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Senior', 'senior', 'Use free public transport where walking and transfers are manageable; otherwise prefer direct taxi / private transfer. Choose accommodation near useful stops and minimize unnecessary station changes.', 2306),
  ('luxembourg', 18, 'family-travel', 'FAMILY TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'child_friendly_score: 90 best_ages: Rules: For young children: Prefer: Avoid: Visit Luxembourg specifically promotes adventure playgrounds, family parks, Minett Park, animal attractions, museums, swimming pools, and family-oriented cultural activities.', 2307),
  ('luxembourg', 19, 'honeymoon-travel', 'HONEYMOON TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'honeymoon_score: 84 romance_score: 86 privacy_score: 87 luxury_score: 85 Recommended: Honeymoon itineraries should not contain more than: 2–3 major experiences/day. Prefer: One memorable castle, forest, vineyard, dining, or cultural experience + free time over: Constant regional sightseeing. Recommended areas: Luxembourg is especially suitable for couples seeking **HERITAGE + CASTLES + FORESTS + WINE + GASTRONOMY + PRIVACY + SLOW_TRAVEL**.', 2308),
  ('luxembourg', 20, 'luxury-travel', 'LUXURY TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'luxury_score: 85 Recommended: Luxembourg luxury travel should focus on: Luxembourg City, Moselle, Vianden, and selected countryside properties provide the country''s strongest premium-travel opportunities.', 2309),
  ('luxembourg', 21, 'adventure', 'ADVENTURE', NULL, NULL, 'adventure_score: 83 Luxembourg is a strong soft-adventure and active-outdoor destination rather than an extreme-adventure destination. Adventure experiences should be interpreted as: The Mullerthal region is Luxembourg''s headline hiking product, while Éislek offers more than 200 circular trails and Minett has a trail network exceeding 90 km. Adventure activities should be matched to weather, trail difficulty, terrain, traveler fitness, and seasonal conditions.', 2310),
  ('luxembourg', 22, 'senior-travel', 'SENIOR TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'senior_suitability: 90 walking_intensity: LOW–MEDIUM with public-transport focused planning MEDIUM–HIGH for castles, fortifications, and hiking trails Rules: Luxembourg works very well for seniors when positioned as a **CULTURE + CASTLES + FREE_PUBLIC_TRANSPORT + COUNTRYSIDE + GASTRONOMY + RELAXED_TRAVEL destination**.', 2311),
  ('luxembourg', 23, 'accessibility', 'ACCESSIBILITY', NULL, NULL, 'wheelchair_accessibility: GOOD IN MANY MODERN URBAN / TRANSPORT ENVIRONMENTS → VARIABLE IN HISTORIC, CASTLE AND NATURAL AREAS public_transport_accessibility: GOOD → VERY_GOOD overall; verify specific vehicle, stop, station, and regional connection hotel_accessibility: MUST_BE_VERIFIED_PER_HOTEL attraction_accessibility: MUST_BE_VERIFIED_PER_ATTRACTION Rule: Never infer accessibility from Luxembourg''s modern infrastructure or free public-transport system. Each hotel, museum, castle, fortress, hiking route, vineyard, restaurant, railway station, bus stop, and regional attraction should carry its own accessibility data. Additional notes:', 2312),
  ('luxembourg', 24, 'food', 'FOOD', NULL, NULL, 'Luxembourg is particularly strong for: Luxembourg''s cuisine reflects strong French, German, Belgian, and local regional influences, while its culinary identity also includes traditional bistro culture and a notable fine-dining scene. Food experiences: Family: Prioritize potato dishes, pastries, breads, cheeses, simple bistro meals, cafés, local sweets, and family-friendly restaurants. Honeymoon: Choose Moselle vineyard dining, Crémant / wine tasting, fine dining, boutique-hotel meals, and a relaxed Luxembourg City evening. Luxury: Include premium restaurants, private dining, curated Moselle wine experiences, gourmet tasting menus, boutique producers, and personalized culinary touring. Budget: Use bakeries, cafés, supermarkets, local markets, takeaway food, and casual bistros. Traditional pastries, snacks, and picnic meals help control dining costs.', 2313),
  ('luxembourg', 25, 'shopping', 'SHOPPING', NULL, NULL, 'Strong categories: Luxury shopping: Luxembourg City provides the country''s strongest premium retail environment. Prefer: Budget: Prefer: Visit Luxembourg highlights markets, shops, museums, and small-scale producers as key places for local food, drink, lifestyle, and regional products. Travel-agent rule: Use LUXEMBOURG_CITY for PREMIUM_RETAIL, MOSELLE for WINE_AND_CREMANT, and REGIONAL_PRODUCERS + MARKETS for LOCAL_FOOD_AND_CRAFTS. Prioritize authentic Luxembourg products over generic European souvenirs.', 2314),
  ('luxembourg', 26, 'nightlife', 'NIGHTLIFE', NULL, NULL, 'nightlife_level: 77 Suitable for: Best areas: Evening activities are better suited to: Luxembourg has a good but compact nightlife scene. Official tourism material positions Luxembourg City as a place where culture, nightlife, business, and relaxation meet, while the national events programme includes music, theatre, festivals, nightlife, markets, and wine events. Honeymoon travelers should generally prefer: OLD_TOWN_OR_GRUND_EVENING + FINE_DINING + WINE_BAR / HOTEL_LOUNGE over: Club-heavy itineraries unless nightlife is specifically requested. Travel-agent rule: Position Luxembourg as a **COMPACT CITY_NIGHTLIFE + DINING + WINE + CULTURAL_EVENING destination**, not as a major European party hub.', 2315),
  ('luxembourg', 28, 'sample-itinerary-patterns', 'SAMPLE ITINERARY PATTERNS', '3 NIGHTS', NULL, '### Day 1 Arrival at Luxembourg Airport (LUX) → Public transport / private transfer to Luxembourg City → Hotel check-in → Relax and refresh Afternoon: Luxembourg City orientation → Old Town → Grand Ducal Palace exterior → Chemin de la Corniche → Grund → City photography Evening: Luxembourgish / European dinner → Relaxed Grund / Old Town walk → Hotel Luxembourg City is the best base for a short first visit, combining UNESCO-listed heritage, historic streets, viewpoints, dining, and easy transport. ### Day 2 Morning: Breakfast → Bock Casemates → Historic fortifications → Corniche viewpoints → Old Town exploration Optional: → Selected museum → Kirchberg / European Quarter → Shopping and café time Afternoon: Local lunch → Parks / city leisure → Free time Evening: Local dining → Optional wine bar / café → Hotel ### Day 3 Breakfast → Choose ONE main regional experience Option 1 — VIANDEN: → Vianden Castle → Historic town → Our Valley scenery → Photography Option 2 — MULLERTHAL: → Mullerthal Region → Schiessentümpel → Short nature walk → Echternach Option 3 — COMBINATION: → Mullerthal → Beaufort Castle → Vianden → Echternach Afternoon: Regional lunch → Return to Luxembourg City Evening: Final dinner → Relaxed Old Town / Grund walk → Hotel Vianden is the strongest castle excursion, while Mullerthal + Echternach is ideal for nature and heritage. ### Day 4 Breakfast → Leisure morning → Souvenir shopping / café → Hotel checkout → Transfer to Luxembourg Airport → Departure Optional according to traveler interest: FAMILY: → Old Town → Bock Casemates → Vianden Castle → Parc Merveilleux HONEYMOON: → Boutique hotel → Grund and Corniche → Vianden → Mullerthal → Moselle wine / Crémant LUXURY: → Premium hotel → Private city guide → Chauffeured countryside tour → Fine dining NATURE / PHOTOGRAPHY: → Mullerthal → Schiessentümpel → Echternach → Vianden FOOD / WINE: → Luxembourg City gastronomy → Moselle wine region → Crémant tasting For 3 nights, keep Luxembourg City as the main base and dedicate only one full day to regional exploration.', 2316),
  ('luxembourg', 29, 'five-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'FIVE-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 1 — LUXEMBOURG CITY', NULL, 'Arrival at Luxembourg Airport → Meet and assist → Private transfer to Luxembourg City → Boutique / premium hotel check-in → Relax and refresh Afternoon / Evening: → Luxembourg City Old Town → Chemin de la Corniche → Grund → Couple photography → Relaxed café time Evening: Romantic Luxembourgish / European dinner → Old Town evening walk → Overnight at Luxembourg City', 2317),
  ('luxembourg', 29, 'five-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'FIVE-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 2 — LUXEMBOURG CITY HERITAGE', NULL, 'Breakfast at the hotel → Bock Casemates → Historic fortifications → Grand Ducal Palace exterior → Cathedral / central historic streets Afternoon: → Local lunch → Selected museum → Kirchberg / modern Luxembourg according to interest → Free couple time Evening: Fine dining → Optional wine bar / lounge → Overnight at Luxembourg City', 2318),
  ('luxembourg', 29, 'five-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'FIVE-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 3 — VIANDEN + ÉISLEK', NULL, 'Breakfast → Private / public-transport excursion toward Vianden Morning: → Vianden Castle → Historic town → Our Valley views → Couple photography → Optional chairlift where operating Afternoon: → Scenic Éislek countryside → Relaxed regional lunch → Return to Luxembourg City Evening: Hotel relaxation / spa → Romantic dinner → Overnight at Luxembourg City', 2319),
  ('luxembourg', 29, 'five-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'FIVE-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 4 — MULLERTHAL + ECHTERNACH', NULL, 'Breakfast → Excursion to Mullerthal Region Morning: → Forest and sandstone scenery → Schiessentümpel → Short romantic nature walk → Photography Afternoon: → Echternach → Historic centre → Abbey surroundings → Café / relaxed lake time → Return to Luxembourg City Evening: Special dinner → Free couple time → Overnight at Luxembourg City', 2320),
  ('luxembourg', 29, 'five-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'FIVE-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 5 — MOSELLE WINE REGION', NULL, 'Breakfast → Relaxed Moselle excursion → Remich / Grevenmacher → Vineyard landscapes → Moselle River → Luxembourg wine / Crémant experience → Regional lunch → Scenic riverside time Afternoon: → Return to Luxembourg City → Shopping / hotel relaxation Evening: Farewell honeymoon dinner → Optional cocktail / wine bar → Overnight at Luxembourg City', 2321),
  ('luxembourg', 29, 'five-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'FIVE-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 6 — DEPARTURE', NULL, 'Breakfast → Leisure morning → Local-product / souvenir shopping → Hotel checkout → Private transfer to Luxembourg Airport → Departure HONEYMOON PACING RULE: LUXEMBOURG_CITY_5_NIGHTS with regional day trips to: VIANDEN + MULLERTHAL + ECHTERNACH + MOSELLE Keep: 2–3 major experiences/day maximum. Prefer: HERITAGE + CASTLES + FORESTS + VINEYARDS + DINING + PHOTOGRAPHY + FREE_COUPLE_TIME over: Changing hotels repeatedly across Luxembourg.', 2322),
  ('luxembourg', 30, 'five-nights-family-pattern', 'FIVE-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 1 — LUXEMBOURG CITY', NULL, 'Arrival at Luxembourg Airport → Public transport / private transfer → Family hotel check-in → Relax and refresh Afternoon: → Old Town → Corniche viewpoints → Grund → Easy family photography Evening: Family-friendly dinner → Relaxed city walk → Overnight at Luxembourg City', 2323),
  ('luxembourg', 30, 'five-nights-family-pattern', 'FIVE-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 2 — CITY + FAMILY EXPERIENCES', 'family', 'Breakfast → Bock Casemates → Historic fortifications → Short museum visit Afternoon: → Parks / playgrounds → Family café → Free time Evening: Dinner → Hotel relaxation → Overnight at Luxembourg City', 2324),
  ('luxembourg', 30, 'five-nights-family-pattern', 'FIVE-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 3 — VIANDEN', NULL, 'Breakfast → Excursion to Vianden → Vianden Castle → Historic town → Our Valley scenery → Optional chairlift where suitable → Family lunch → Photography Afternoon: → Return to Luxembourg City → Rest / free time Evening: Family dinner → Overnight at Luxembourg City', 2325),
  ('luxembourg', 30, 'five-nights-family-pattern', 'FIVE-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 4 — MULLERTHAL + ECHTERNACH', NULL, 'Breakfast → Mullerthal Region → Easy family nature walk → Forest and rock landscapes → Schiessentümpel → Echternach Afternoon: → Echternach Lake → Playground / relaxed lakeside time → Return to Luxembourg City Evening: Dinner → Overnight at Luxembourg City', 2326),
  ('luxembourg', 30, 'five-nights-family-pattern', 'FIVE-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 5 — PARC MERVEILLEUX / MINETT', NULL, 'Breakfast Choose ONE: FAMILY_LEISURE: → Parc Merveilleux → Animals → Fairytale areas → Playgrounds → Family recreation OR MINETT_FAMILY: → Minett Park → Industrial heritage → Historic railway / steam-train experience where operating → Educational family activities Afternoon: → Return to Luxembourg City → Shopping / free time Evening: Farewell family dinner → Overnight at Luxembourg City', 2327),
  ('luxembourg', 30, 'five-nights-family-pattern', 'FIVE-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 6 — DEPARTURE', NULL, 'Breakfast → Leisure morning → Hotel checkout → Transfer to Luxembourg Airport → Departure FAMILY PACING RULE: Prefer: CASTLES + PARKS + ANIMALS + EASY_NATURE + INTERACTIVE_MUSEUMS + FREE_PUBLIC_TRANSPORT over: LONG_HIKES + MULTIPLE_CASTLES_PER_DAY + MUSEUM_HEAVY_SCHEDULES.', 2328),
  ('luxembourg', 31, 'five-nights-luxury-pattern', 'FIVE-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 1 — LUXEMBOURG CITY', NULL, 'Arrival at Luxembourg Airport → VIP meet and assist → Chauffeured transfer → Five-star / premium hotel check-in → Relax and refresh Afternoon: Private Luxembourg City orientation → Old Town → Corniche → Grund Evening: Fine dining → Premium hotel lounge → Overnight at Luxembourg City', 2329),
  ('luxembourg', 31, 'five-nights-luxury-pattern', 'FIVE-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 2 — PRIVATE HERITAGE EXPERIENCE', NULL, 'Breakfast → Private expert-guided city tour → Bock Casemates → Historic fortifications → Grand Ducal Palace surroundings → Selected museum Afternoon: → Premium lunch → Private shopping / leisure → Spa / wellness Evening: Fine dining → Overnight at Luxembourg City', 2330),
  ('luxembourg', 31, 'five-nights-luxury-pattern', 'FIVE-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 3 — PRIVATE VIANDEN & ÉISLEK', NULL, 'Breakfast → Chauffeured excursion to Vianden → Vianden Castle → Private / guided interpretation → Our Valley scenery → Premium countryside lunch → Flexible photography stops Afternoon: → Scenic Éislek drive → Return to hotel Evening: Private / fine-dining experience → Overnight at Luxembourg City', 2331),
  ('luxembourg', 31, 'five-nights-luxury-pattern', 'FIVE-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 4 — MULLERTHAL & COUNTRYSIDE', NULL, 'Breakfast → Chauffeured Mullerthal excursion → Forest landscapes → Schiessentümpel → Beaufort area → Echternach → Personalized photography / walking Afternoon: → Premium regional lunch → Return to Luxembourg City → Spa / leisure Evening: Fine dining → Overnight at Luxembourg City', 2332),
  ('luxembourg', 31, 'five-nights-luxury-pattern', 'FIVE-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 5 — PREMIUM MOSELLE EXPERIENCE', 'luxury', 'Breakfast → Private Moselle excursion → Vineyard landscapes → Wine / Crémant tasting → Selected producer → Premium regional lunch → Remich / Grevenmacher riverside experience Afternoon: → Return to Luxembourg City → Free leisure / shopping Evening: Farewell fine-dining experience → Overnight at Luxembourg City', 2333),
  ('luxembourg', 31, 'five-nights-luxury-pattern', 'FIVE-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 6 — DEPARTURE', NULL, 'Breakfast → Leisure morning → Hotel checkout → Chauffeured airport transfer → Departure LUXURY PACING RULE: Prioritize: 5_STAR_HOTEL + PRIVATE_CHAUFFEUR + EXPERT_GUIDES + FINE_DINING + WINE_AND_CREMANT + PRIVATE_CASTLE_TOURING + SPA_AND_WELLNESS + FLEXIBLE_FREE_TIME Luxury Luxembourg should emphasize: PRIVACY + SERVICE + GASTRONOMY + CULTURE + COUNTRYSIDE + PERSONALIZATION rather than increasing destination count.', 2334),
  ('luxembourg', 32, 'travel-agent-insights', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS', 'What inexperienced planners often do wrong', NULL, '', 2335),
  ('luxembourg', 32, 'travel-agent-insights', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS', 'What an experienced planner does differently', NULL, '', 2336),
  ('luxembourg', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', NULL, NULL, 'IF: trip_length <= 2 nights THEN: prioritize_LUXEMBOURG_CITY + ONE_OF_VIANDEN_OR_MULLERTHAL Reason: A very short stay gains more value from the capital plus one signature regional experience than attempting the whole country. IF: trip_length >= 3 nights AND: traveler_interest == FIRST_TIME_LUXEMBOURG THEN: prioritize_LUXEMBOURG_CITY + VIANDEN + MULLERTHAL_ECHTERNACH Reason: This provides Luxembourg''s strongest combination of UNESCO heritage, castles and nature. IF: trip_type == HONEYMOON THEN: increase_romance_weight by 20% increase_free_time_weight by 25% decrease_activity_density by 20% prefer_LUXEMBOURG_CITY + VIANDEN + MULLERTHAL + MOSELLE Reason: Romantic Luxembourg works best through historic settings, castles, forests, vineyards, fine dining and relaxed couple time. IF: traveler_type == FAMILY AND: children_age <= 6 THEN: increase_downtime by 25% prefer_PARC_MERVEILLEUX + PARKS + EASY_CASTLES + ECHTERNACH_LAKE + FAMILY_MUSEUMS Reason: Young children benefit more from interactive, outdoor and short-duration experiences. IF: traveler_type == FAMILY AND: children_age >= 7 THEN: consider_VIANDEN + MULLERTHAL + MINETT_PARK + ECHTERNACH AND: include_EDUCATIONAL + NATURE + INTERACTIVE_EXPERIENCES Reason: Older children can combine castles, hiking, industrial heritage and museums more effectively. IF: traveler_type == LUXURY THEN: prefer_PREMIUM_CITY_OR_COUNTRYSIDE_HOTEL AND: prefer_PRIVATE_DRIVER + EXPERT_GUIDE AND: increase_FINE_DINING + WINE + WELLNESS_WEIGHT Reason: Luxury should improve comfort, privacy, gastronomy, guiding and flexibility rather than increase sightseeing density. IF: traveler_type == BUDGET THEN: prefer_WELL_CONNECTED_BUDGET_HOTEL_OR_HOSTEL AND: use_FREE_PUBLIC_TRANSPORT + WALKING AND: prioritize_HIKING + VIEWPOINTS + SELECTIVE_PAID_ATTRACTIONS Reason: Luxembourg''s free nationwide public transport significantly reduces everyday travel costs. IF: traveler_interest == CULTURE_AND_HERITAGE THEN: prioritize_LUXEMBOURG_CITY + VIANDEN + CLERVAUX + ECHTERNACH Reason: These provide the strongest combination of fortifications, castles, museums, religious heritage and historic towns. IF: traveler_interest == HIKING THEN: prefer_MULLERTHAL + EISLEK + MINETT AND: verify_TRAIL_DIFFICULTY + WEATHER + FITNESS Reason: Luxembourg has one of Europe''s densest hiking networks, including the 112-km Mullerthal Trail and 106-km cross-border Escapardenne Eislek Trail. IF: traveler_interest == WINE_AND_GASTRONOMY THEN: prefer_MOSELLE AND: include_WINE + CREMANT + VINEYARDS + REGIONAL_DINING Reason: Moselle is Luxembourg''s principal dedicated wine-tourism region. IF: traveler_interest == CASTLES THEN: prefer_VIANDEN + BOURSCHEID + BEAUFORT + GUTTLAND AND: avoid_TOO_MANY_CASTLES_IN_ONE_DAY Reason: Luxembourg has substantial castle density, but different castle regions require travel and walking time. IF: traveler_interest == NATURE_AND_RELAXATION THEN: prefer_MULLERTHAL + UPPER_SURE + EISLEK AND: reduce_MUSEUM_DENSITY Reason: Forests, rock formations, lakes and countryside provide Luxembourg''s strongest nature product. IF: traveler_interest == PHOTOGRAPHY THEN: prefer_LUXEMBOURG_CITY + VIANDEN + MULLERTHAL + MOSELLE AND: prioritize_EARLY_MORNING + LATE_AFTERNOON Reason: This combination provides fortifications, valleys, castles, forests and vineyards. IF: trip_length <= 5 nights THEN: prefer_ONE_MAIN_HOTEL_BASE Reason: Luxembourg''s compact geography and free public transport make frequent hotel changes unnecessary. IF: traveler_type == SENIOR OR: traveler_mobility == LIMITED THEN: reduce_CASTLE_STAIRS + STEEP_OLD_TOWN_WALKING + DIFFICULT_HIKING AND: prefer_PUBLIC_TRANSPORT + COMFORT_TRAILS + MUSEUMS + RELAXED_COUNTRYSIDE Reason: Many enjoyable low-intensity experiences exist, but accessibility varies substantially at historic and natural sites. IF: traveler_uses_WHEELCHAIR THEN: prefer_VERIFIED_ACCESSIBLE_HOTEL + VERIFIED_PUBLIC_TRANSPORT + COMFORT_TRAILS AND: avoid_assuming_CASTLES + CASEMATES + MULLERTHAL_TRAILS_ARE_STEP_FREE Reason: Luxembourg provides dedicated accessible comfort trails, but historic and natural environments still require individual verification. IF: weather == HEAVY_RAIN THEN: reduce_MULLERTHAL_HIKING + FOREST_TRAILS AND: increase_MUSEUMS + GASTRONOMY + SHOPPING + CITY_CULTURE Reason: Rain can make forest and rock trails slippery while Luxembourg City retains strong indoor alternatives. IF: traveler_interest == AUTHENTIC_LOCAL_EXPERIENCE THEN: prefer_LOCAL_DINING + MOSELLE_PRODUCERS + SMALL_TOWNS + REGIONAL_MARKETS + COUNTRYSIDE AND: decrease_GENERIC_LANDMARK_ONLY_WEIGHT Reason: Local gastronomy, wine, villages and regional landscapes provide greater depth than headline attractions alone.', 2337),
  ('luxembourg', 34, 'destination-scoring', 'DESTINATION SCORING', NULL, NULL, '| Factor | Score | | ------------------ | ----: | | Family | 90 | | Honeymoon | 84 | | Luxury | 85 | | Budget | 82 | | Adventure | 83 | | Culture | 91 | | Food | 87 | | Shopping | 82 | | Nightlife | 77 | | Relaxation | 92 | | Nature | 91 | | Accessibility | 88 | | Safety | 94 | | First-time visitor | 92 | | Photography | 93 |', 2338),
  ('luxembourg', 35, 'final-travel-agent-verdict', 'FINAL TRAVEL AGENT VERDICT', NULL, NULL, 'Best traveler profiles: 1. Culture / heritage traveler 2. Photography traveler 3. Nature / hiking traveler 4. Relaxation / slow-travel traveler 5. First-time Benelux traveler 6. Family traveler 7. Food / gastronomy traveler 8. Castle / history traveler 9. Romantic / honeymoon traveler 10. Wine traveler Best duration: 3–5 nights 2 nights for Luxembourg City + one signature excursion such as Vianden or Mullerthal. 3–5 nights for Luxembourg City + Vianden + Mullerthal / Echternach + Moselle. 6–7 nights for deeper exploration of Éislek, Guttland, Minett, castles, hiking and wine without rushing. Best season: APRIL–JUNE and SEPTEMBER–OCTOBER April–May for spring landscapes, castles, city walking, cycling and hiking. June for long daylight, outdoor activity and countryside travel. July–August for family holidays, hiking, cycling, festivals and lake activities, but with higher visitor demand. September–October for hiking, vineyards, autumn scenery, photography and one of the best weather/value combinations. November–February for quieter city breaks, museums, gastronomy and winter events, with December strongest for festive atmosphere. Best hotel strategy: Use Luxembourg City as the main base for most first-time stays. For longer nature-focused trips, consider one secondary stay in Mullerthal, Éislek or Moselle. Avoid unnecessary one-night hotel changes. Best transportation: Walking + free train / bus / tram for most travel. Use private driver / rental car selectively for: Luxembourg should be treated as a PUBLIC_TRANSPORT_FIRST + DAY_TRIP_FRIENDLY destination. Must-do for first-time visitor: Don''t-do: Biggest advantage: Exceptional tourism variety within a very compact country. Luxembourg combines UNESCO heritage, castles, forests, hiking, vineyards, gastronomy, family attractions and highly convenient free public transport. Its small scale allows travelers to experience Luxembourg City, Mullerthal, Vianden, Moselle and other regions without the transfer friction typical of larger European destinations. Biggest disadvantage: Luxembourg has fewer world-famous headline landmarks than major European countries, accommodation can be relatively expensive, and its nightlife, luxury shopping and extreme-adventure products are more limited. Historic fortifications, castles and natural trails can also create accessibility challenges. Overall destination score: 88/100', 2339),
  ('luxembourg', 36, 'data-quality', 'DATA QUALITY', NULL, NULL, 'information_completeness: 96/100 last_updated: 2026-08-27 last_verified: PARTIALLY_WEB_VERIFIED verified_by: VISIT LUXEMBOURG / OFFICIAL REGIONAL TOURISM, FAMILY, HIKING AND ACCESSIBILITY SOURCES sources: IMPORTANT: Prices, attraction tickets, hotel rates, restaurant prices, guided tours, wine tastings, museum schedules, castle opening hours, chairlift operations and accessibility must NOT be treated as permanently valid. Vianden Castle, Bock Casemates, Parc Merveilleux, Mullerthal attractions, museums and other seasonal facilities should be checked before travel. Forest trails can become slippery or difficult after rain. Long-distance hiking routes should be matched to fitness, weather and daylight. Moselle vineyard and wine experiences may require advance reservations. Free public transport applies to standard-class national public transport; special services and first-class rail are separate. Historic fortifications, castles, steep streets and natural hiking routes should not be assumed step-free. Luxembourg''s official Tourism for All programme includes dedicated comfort trails suitable for easier walking and selected wheelchair use. :contentReference[oaicite:6]{index=6} Luxembourg should primarily be treated as: SPRING: CITY + CASTLES + HIKING + CYCLING + PHOTOGRAPHY SUMMER: NATURE + FAMILY + HIKING + CYCLING + OUTDOORS AUTUMN: VINEYARDS + HIKING + CASTLES + PHOTOGRAPHY + GASTRONOMY WINTER: CITY_BREAK + CULTURE + FOOD + MUSEUMS + FESTIVE_TRAVEL Visit Luxembourg and individual regional, attraction, transport and accommodation operators should be treated as the primary sources for operational updates. This dataset should be refreshed regularly before production use.', 2340),
  ('belgium', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Spring', NULL, 'months: March April May weather: March remains cool and changeable. April becomes noticeably milder with longer daylight, while May generally provides some of Belgium''s most comfortable conditions for city walking, gardens, cycling and countryside excursions. crowd_level: MEDIUM price_level: MEDIUM overall_score: 68.67–74.67 recommended: true reason: Spring combines improving temperatures, long sightseeing days and attractive city conditions, although rainfall remains possible throughout the season and demand rises toward May. Best for:', 2341),
  ('belgium', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Summer', NULL, 'months: June July August weather: Generally mild to warm rather than consistently hot, with Belgium''s longest daylight hours. Rain showers remain possible and occasional heat episodes can occur. crowd_level: MEDIUM → HIGH price_level: MEDIUM → HIGH overall_score: 56.67–65.33 recommended: true_with_crowd_planning reason: Summer provides excellent daylight, festivals, terraces, cycling and coastal conditions, but major heritage cities experience their strongest visitor pressure and accommodation demand. Best for:', 2342),
  ('belgium', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Autumn', NULL, 'months: September October November weather: September often remains comfortable for outdoor travel, October becomes cooler and more changeable, and November is significantly cooler, wetter and darker. crowd_level: MEDIUM → LOW price_level: MEDIUM overall_score: 70.67–73.33 recommended: true reason: September is particularly well balanced, while October and November benefit from lower tourism pressure, atmospheric historic cities, museums, gastronomy and seasonal food despite progressively weaker weather. Best for:', 2343),
  ('belgium', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Winter', NULL, 'months: December January February weather: Cool to cold, frequently cloudy and damp with short daylight hours. Snow is possible but unreliable in most lowland cities, while the higher Ardennes and High Fens have stronger winter potential. crowd_level: LOW → HIGH_SEASONAL price_level: MEDIUM overall_score: 52.67–73.67 recommended: true_for_city_breaks reason: January and February offer lower visitor pressure and strong museum value, while December gains atmosphere from Christmas markets but can be crowded and expensive around major festive periods. Best for:', 2344),
  ('belgium', 10, 'budget-strategy', 'BUDGET STRATEGY', NULL, NULL, 'Where money can be saved: Belgium''s compact geography is particularly advantageous because Brussels Airport has direct rail connections with Brussels, Antwerp, Ghent, Bruges, Liège and Namur. Where saving money is usually NOT recommended: Travel-agent rule: In Belgium, **CENTRAL_HOTELS + NATIONAL_RAIL + WALKABLE_HISTORIC_CENTRES + SELECTIVE_LOCAL_TRANSIT** provides the strongest general value. For short stays, prioritize: **BRUSSELS + BRUGES + GHENT**. For medium stays, add: **ANTWERP + LEUVEN_OR_MECHELEN**. For longer stays, add: **YPRES_FLANDERS_FIELDS + WALLONIA + ARDENNES_OR_BELGIAN_COAST**. Operational note: Rail fares, airport supplements, museum pricing, city passes, attraction schedules and temporary exhibitions should be rechecked before travel.', 2345),
  ('belgium', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Family', 'family', 'Airport transfer by: DIRECT_AIRPORT_TRAIN + CENTRAL_HOTEL is generally the strongest option when arriving at Brussels Airport. For Brussels accommodation, prioritize easy access to Brussels-Central, Brussels-Midi, the historic centre or a suitable metro corridor depending on itinerary. For families with substantial luggage, very young children or mobility needs: PRIVATE_TRANSFER_OR_TAXI can be preferable.', 2346),
  ('belgium', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Honeymoon', 'honeymoon', 'Prefer: AIRPORT_TRAIN_OR_PRIVATE_TRANSFER + BOUTIQUE_OR_LUXURY_HOTEL + CENTRAL_WALKABLE_LOCATION Bruges honeymoon travelers can continue from Brussels Airport by rail rather than necessarily overnighting in Brussels first.', 2347),
  ('belgium', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Luxury', 'luxury', 'Use: AIRPORT_MEET_AND_GREET + CHAUFFEURED_SEDAN_OR_MPV + FIVE_STAR_OR_HERITAGE_HOTEL + PRIVATE_CITY_AND_REGIONAL_TOURING Private transport is particularly useful for castles, Ardennes, Flanders Fields, rural Wallonia and multi-stop specialist touring.', 2348),
  ('belgium', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Budget', 'budget', 'Primary options: Brussels Airport-Zaventem railway station is directly beneath the terminal and provides direct connections to several major Belgian cities. Brussels South Charleroi Airport does not have an integrated terminal railway station and generally requires bus or shuttle connections.', 2349),
  ('belgium', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Senior', 'senior', 'Prefer: DIRECT_AIRPORT_TRAIN_WITH_ASSISTANCE or: PRIVATE_AIRPORT_TRANSFER + CENTRAL_HOTEL depending on mobility and luggage requirements. SNCB / NMBS provides advance-bookable assistance for passengers with reduced mobility at numerous Belgian stations.', 2350),
  ('belgium', 18, 'family-travel', 'FAMILY TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'child_friendly_score: 91 best_ages: Rules: For young children: Prefer: Avoid:', 2351),
  ('belgium', 19, 'honeymoon-travel', 'HONEYMOON TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'honeymoon_score: 92 romance_score: 94 privacy_score: 86 luxury_score: 90 Recommended: Honeymoon itineraries should generally stay at: 2–3 major experiences/day. Prefer: BRUGES_HERITAGE_HOTEL + CANALS + GHENT + CHOCOLATE + FINE_DINING + FREE_TIME over: Continuous museum and multi-city scheduling. For 6–8 night honeymoons: **BRUSSELS + BRUGES + GHENT + ANTWERP_OR_SPA** provides a strong balance.', 2352),
  ('belgium', 20, 'luxury-travel', 'LUXURY TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'luxury_score: 90 Recommended: Belgium is particularly strong for: CULTURAL_LUXURY + HERITAGE_HOTELS + FINE_DINING + ART + FASHION + PRIVATE_ROAD_AND_RAIL_TOURING.', 2353),
  ('belgium', 21, 'adventure', 'ADVENTURE', NULL, NULL, 'adventure_score: 76 Belgium offers primarily soft adventure, cycling, hiking, kayaking and outdoor recreation rather than high-altitude or extreme adventure. Adventure experiences: Best regions: ARDENNES + HIGH_FENS + SEMOIS_VALLEY + OURTHE_VALLEY + BELGIAN_COAST + FLANDERS_CYCLING_REGIONS Travel-agent positioning: Belgium should be treated as: CYCLING + HIKING + KAYAKING + FOREST_ADVENTURE + COASTAL_RECREATION rather than an extreme mountain-adventure destination.', 2354),
  ('belgium', 22, 'senior-travel', 'SENIOR TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'senior_suitability: 89 walking_intensity: LOW–MEDIUM for Brussels, Antwerp, Leuven, Mechelen, Liège and rail-connected urban sightseeing. MEDIUM for Bruges, Ghent, historic cobbled centres, castles and extensive museum days. MEDIUM–HIGH for steep citadels, Ardennes trails and selected historic towers. Rules: Belgium works especially well for seniors as a: HERITAGE + ART + RAIL_TOURING + GASTRONOMY + MUSEUM + RELAXED_CITY_BREAK destination.', 2355),
  ('belgium', 23, 'accessibility', 'ACCESSIBILITY', NULL, NULL, 'wheelchair_accessibility: MODERATE → HIGH IN MAJOR MODERN TRANSPORT HUBS, MUSEUMS AND SELECTED PUBLIC ATTRACTIONS VARIABLE WITHIN MEDIEVAL_HISTORIC_CENTRES, COBBLED STREETS, CASTLES AND BELFRIES public_transport_accessibility: MODERATE → HIGH WITH ROUTE_SPECIFIC_VERIFICATION hotel_accessibility: GENERALLY_GOOD_IN_MODERN_AND_UPSCALE_HOTELS_BUT_MUST_BE_VERIFIED attraction_accessibility: MUST_BE_VERIFIED_PER_ATTRACTION Rule: Do not assume UNESCO buildings, belfries, medieval churches, castles or historic canal areas are completely step-free. Additional notes: Belgium accessibility should therefore be classified as: STRONG_TRANSPORT_INFRASTRUCTURE_WITH_HERITAGE_SITE_SPECIFIC_LIMITATIONS.', 2356),
  ('belgium', 24, 'food', 'FOOD', NULL, NULL, 'Belgium is particularly strong for: Food experiences: Family: Prioritize waffles, fries, chocolate, croquettes, breads, simple brasserie dishes and family-friendly cafés. Honeymoon: Choose artisan chocolate, fine dining, historic restaurants, Bruges canal-side meals and premium beer or gastronomy tastings. Luxury: Include Michelin-level restaurants, chef-led dining, premium chocolatiers, private beer tastings and luxury hotel restaurants. Budget: Use fries shops, bakeries, sandwich shops, supermarkets, student restaurants and casual brasseries. Travel-agent rule: Position Belgium food around: CHOCOLATE + BEER + FRITES + WAFFLES + REGIONAL_BELGIAN_CUISINE + FINE_DINING.', 2357),
  ('belgium', 25, 'shopping', 'SHOPPING', NULL, NULL, 'Strong categories: Luxury shopping: Prefer: Local shopping: Prefer: Budget: Prefer: Travel-agent rule: Use: ANTWERP for FASHION_AND_DIAMONDS, BRUSSELS for LUXURY_AND_CHOCOLATE, BRUGES for CHOCOLATE_LACE_AND_HERITAGE_PRODUCTS, GHENT for BOUTIQUES_AND_LOCAL_DESIGN.', 2358),
  ('belgium', 26, 'nightlife', 'NIGHTLIFE', NULL, NULL, 'nightlife_level: 88 Suitable for: Best areas: Evening activities: Belgium nightlife is strongest for: BEER_CULTURE + BARS + LIVE_MUSIC + STUDENT_NIGHTLIFE + DINING + URBAN_CLUBS. Couples should generally prefer: HISTORIC_CENTER_EVENING + DINNER + BEER_OR_COCKTAIL_BAR + RELAXED_WALK over: Excessive multi-city late-night transfers.', 2359),
  ('belgium', 28, 'sample-itinerary-patterns', 'SAMPLE ITINERARY PATTERNS', '3 NIGHTS', NULL, '### Day 1 Arrival at Brussels Airport (BRU) → Direct airport train, taxi, or private transfer to central Brussels → Hotel check-in & relax after arrival Afternoon: → Begin at Grand-Place / Grote Markt → Explore the historic guildhall architecture → Walk through Galeries Royales Saint-Hubert → Continue through Brussels'' historic centre → Visit the Manneken Pis area → Belgian chocolate & waffle experience Evening: → Explore the illuminated Grand-Place → Traditional Belgian dinner → Belgian chocolate / dessert tasting → Hotel BRU is Belgium''s principal international aviation gateway. Brussels Airport-Zaventem railway station is located directly beneath the terminal, with Brussels-Central reachable in approximately 18 minutes and direct rail connections also available towards cities including Ghent, Bruges and Antwerp. ### Day 2 Morning: Breakfast → Explore Brussels'' monumental & cultural highlights → Royal Palace of Brussels exterior / Royal Quarter → Mont des Arts → Cathedral of St. Michael and St. Gudula → Historic central neighbourhoods Afternoon: → Visit the Atomium → Explore the surrounding Heysel area → Return towards central Brussels → Belgian chocolate / café experience Evening: → Grand-Place & historic-centre photography → Belgian dinner → Relaxed city-centre evening → Hotel Optional alternative instead of the full Brussels city day: ANTWERP: → Train from Brussels to Antwerp → Antwerp Central Station → Grote Markt → Cathedral of Our Lady → Historic centre → Diamond District → Fashion & shopping experience → Return to Brussels ### Day 3 Recommended first-time option: Breakfast → Early train / private transfer towards Bruges → Begin at Markt / Market Square → Belfry of Bruges → Burg Square → Explore Bruges'' UNESCO-listed historic centre → Walk through medieval streets & picturesque squares Afternoon: → Canal boat experience → Rozenhoedkaai → Beguinage → Minnewater / Lake of Love → Belgian chocolate & local food experience → Continue towards Ghent → Explore Graslei & Korenlei waterfront → St. Michael''s Bridge → Historic Ghent cityscape Evening: → Return to Brussels OR overnight according to onward routing → Farewell Belgian dinner → Hotel Optional alternative instead of covering BOTH Bruges & Ghent: BRUGES_FOCUS: → Markt → Belfry → Burg Square → Rozenhoedkaai → Canal cruise → Beguinage → Minnewater → Romantic medieval evening GHENT_FOCUS: → Castle of the Counts → Graslei & Korenlei → St. Michael''s Bridge → St. Bavo''s Cathedral → Ghent Belfry → Historic centre → Evening light walk ANTWERP: → Antwerp Central Station → Grote Markt → Cathedral precinct → Historic streets → Diamond District → Shopping & fashion CULTURE & HISTORY: → Grand-Place Brussels → Royal Quarter → Bruges historic centre → Ghent medieval centre → Flemish art & architecture FAMILY: → Atomium → Belgian chocolate experience → Bruges canal boat → Castle of the Counts in Ghent → Waffles & family sightseeing HONEYMOON: → Grand-Place evening photography → Bruges canal cruise → Minnewater / Lake of Love → Medieval Bruges couple photography → Romantic Belgian dinner LUXURY: → Private airport transfer → Privately guided Brussels heritage tour → Chauffeured Bruges excursion → Private / premium canal experience → Fine dining & luxury hotel stay FOOD: → Belgian waffles → Belgian chocolates → Belgian fries → Flemish regional cuisine → Local pastries & desserts → Belgian beer tasting for adults For only 3 nights, prioritize: BRUSSELS_GRAND_PLACE_AND_ATOMIUM + BRUGES_MEDIEVAL_CENTRE_AND_CANALS + GHENT_HISTORIC_CENTRE OR BRUSSELS_HERITAGE_AND_CHOCOLATE + FULL_DAY_BRUGES + GHENT_OR_ANTWERP rather than trying to add Luxembourg, Amsterdam, Paris or other neighbouring countries into the same short itinerary. ### Day 4 Breakfast → Leisure morning according to hotel location → Final Belgian chocolate / souvenir shopping → Hotel checkout → Train, taxi, or private transfer towards Brussels Airport (BRU) → Departure', 2360),
  ('belgium', 29, 'six-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 1', NULL, 'Arrival at Brussels Airport (BRU) → Private airport transfer → Romantic hotel check-in → Relax and refresh Afternoon: → Grand-Place → Galeries Royales Saint-Hubert → Historic Brussels → Couple photography Evening: → Belgian chocolate & waffle experience → Romantic dinner → Grand-Place night walk → Overnight at Brussels', 2361),
