  ('belgium', 31, 'six-nights-luxury-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 1', NULL, 'Arrival at Brussels Airport (BRU) → Private luxury airport transfer → Premium / heritage hotel check-in → Relax and refresh Afternoon: → Private Brussels orientation → Grand-Place → Galeries Royales Saint-Hubert → Historic centre Evening: → Premium Belgian chocolate tasting → Fine-dining experience → Overnight at Brussels', 2375),
  ('belgium', 31, 'six-nights-luxury-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 2', NULL, 'Breakfast → Privately guided Brussels experience → Royal Quarter → Mont des Arts → Cathedral of St. Michael and St. Gudula → Historic architecture Afternoon: → Private transfer to Atomium → Curated cultural experience → Luxury shopping / spa Evening: → Premium rooftop / fine dining → Overnight at Brussels', 2376),
  ('belgium', 31, 'six-nights-luxury-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 3', NULL, 'Breakfast → Private / first-class rail excursion to Antwerp → Antwerp Central Station → Private historic-centre tour → Grote Markt → Cathedral precinct → Diamond District Afternoon: → Curated luxury shopping → Private art / fashion experience Evening: → Return to Brussels → Fine dining → Overnight at Brussels', 2377),
  ('belgium', 31, 'six-nights-luxury-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 4', NULL, 'Breakfast → Hotel checkout → First-class train / chauffeured transfer to Bruges → Luxury boutique / heritage hotel check-in Afternoon: → Private Bruges heritage tour → Markt → Belfry → Burg Square → Rozenhoedkaai Evening: → Private / premium canal experience → Fine-dining Belgian cuisine → Overnight at Bruges', 2378),
  ('belgium', 31, 'six-nights-luxury-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 5', NULL, 'Breakfast Choose ONE: PRIVATE_HERITAGE → Privately guided medieval Bruges → Beguinage → Historic churches → Flemish art → Hidden courtyards LUXURY_LEISURE → Private carriage experience → Premium chocolate tasting → Spa & wellness → Boutique shopping → Champagne / afternoon tea Evening: → Private canal-side experience → Gourmet farewell-to-Bruges dinner → Overnight at Bruges', 2379),
  ('belgium', 31, 'six-nights-luxury-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 6', NULL, 'Breakfast → Chauffeured transfer / first-class train to Ghent → Premium hotel check-in → Private Castle of the Counts experience → St. Bavo''s Cathedral → Ghent Belfry → St. Michael''s Bridge → Graslei & Korenlei Afternoon: → Private canal cruise → Curated Flemish art / cultural experience → Spa / hotel leisure Evening: → Ghent illuminated heritage walk → Farewell fine-dining experience → Overnight at Ghent', 2380),
  ('belgium', 31, 'six-nights-luxury-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 7', NULL, 'Breakfast → Leisure morning → Hotel checkout → Private luxury transfer to Brussels Airport (BRU) → Departure', 2381),
  ('belgium', 32, 'travel-agent-insights', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS', 'What inexperienced planners often do wrong', NULL, '', 2382),
  ('belgium', 32, 'travel-agent-insights', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS', 'What an experienced planner does differently', NULL, 'For first-time visits, prioritize: BRUSSELS + BRUGES + GHENT + ANTWERP before maximum regional coverage.', 2383),
  ('belgium', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', NULL, NULL, 'IF: trip_length <= 3 nights THEN: prioritize_BRUSSELS + ONE_OF_BRUGES_OR_GHENT AND: avoid_MAXIMUM_CITY_COUNT Reason: Very short Belgium trips gain more value from one major base plus one strong historic-city excursion. IF: trip_length == 4_OR_5_nights THEN: prioritize_BRUSSELS + BRUGES + GHENT AND: consider_ANTWERP_IF_PACING_ALLOWS Reason: Four to five nights provide a strong first-time balance of capital-city culture and Flemish medieval heritage. IF: trip_length >= 6 nights THEN: add_ANTWERP + LEUVEN_OR_MECHELEN Reason: Longer stays allow Belgium''s art, university, beer and secondary heritage cities to be explored without excessive rushing. IF: trip_length >= 8 nights THEN: add_ONE_OF_FLANDERS_FIELDS + WALLONIA + ARDENNES + BELGIAN_COAST Reason: Belgium becomes substantially more varied when the principal Flemish-city circuit is combined with one contrasting region. IF: trip_type == HONEYMOON THEN: prefer_BRUGES_OVERNIGHT + GHENT + BOUTIQUE_HOTEL + FINE_DINING AND: reduce_DAILY_CITY_CHANGES Reason: Belgium''s romantic strength comes from historic atmosphere, canals, gastronomy and slower evening experiences. IF: traveler_type == FAMILY THEN: prioritize_BRUSSELS + BRUGES_CANAL + GRAVENSTEEN + TRAIN_WORLD_OR_ATOMIUM AND: include_RECREATIONAL_BREAKS Reason: Families benefit from combining heritage with interactive attractions rather than continuous museum scheduling. IF: traveler_type == LUXURY THEN: prefer_FIVE_STAR_OR_HERITAGE_HOTELS + PRIVATE_GUIDES + PREMIUM_DINING AND: use_CHAUFFEUR_SELECTIVELY Reason: Belgium''s strongest luxury positioning comes from cultural access, gastronomy, heritage hotels and private touring. IF: traveler_type == BUDGET THEN: prefer_NATIONAL_RAIL + CENTRAL_VALUE_HOTEL + WALKING + CASUAL_LOCAL_FOOD AND: limit_TAXIS_AND_PREMIUM_ATTRACTIONS Reason: Belgium remains manageable when its excellent rail network and walkable historic centres are used efficiently. IF: traveler_interest == UNESCO_HERITAGE THEN: prioritize_BRUSSELS_GRAND_PLACE + BRUGES + BELFRIES + BEGUINAGES + HORTA + PLANTIN_MORETUS Reason: Belgium contains an unusually dense collection of internationally recognized civic, architectural and cultural heritage. IF: traveler_interest == BRUGES THEN: allocate_FULL_DAY_OR_OVERNIGHT AND: combine_MARKT + BELFRY + BURG + CANALS + BEGUINAGE + FLEMISH_ART Reason: The UNESCO-listed historic centre is a complete medieval urban ensemble rather than a single-square sightseeing stop. IF: traveler_interest == GHENT THEN: prioritize_GHENT_ALTARPIECE + ST_BAVOS + GRAVENSTEEN + GRASLEI_KORENLEI AND: retain_EVENING_TIME Reason: Ghent combines exceptional medieval art with one of Belgium''s strongest historic waterfront atmospheres. IF: traveler_interest == ANTWERP THEN: prioritize_CATHEDRAL + PLANTIN_MORETUS + KMSKA + HISTORIC_CENTER AND: add_FASHION_OR_DIAMONDS_IF_RELEVANT Reason: Antwerp performs strongest when art, heritage and contemporary urban identity are combined. IF: traveler_interest == BRUSSELS THEN: combine_GRAND_PLACE + MUSEUMS + ART_NOUVEAU + EUROPEAN_QUARTER Reason: Brussels should not be reduced to Grand-Place and Atomium alone. IF: traveler_interest == ART_NOUVEAU THEN: prioritize_HORTA_HERITAGE + BRUSSELS_ARCHITECTURE Reason: UNESCO recognizes Victor Horta''s major Brussels town houses as pioneering works of Art Nouveau. IF: traveler_interest == WORLD_WAR_HISTORY THEN: prioritize_YPRES + MENIN_GATE + FLANDERS_FIELDS + TYNE_COT AND: allocate_FULL_DAY_OR_MORE Reason: The region contains one of Europe''s most significant First World War remembrance landscapes. IF: traveler_interest == FOOD THEN: include_CHOCOLATE + BEER + FRITES + REGIONAL_BELGIAN_DISH AND: retain_ONE_HIGH_QUALITY_BRASSERIE_OR_FINE_DINING_EXPERIENCE Reason: Belgian gastronomy is significantly broader than its internationally famous sweets and snacks. IF: traveler_interest == BEER THEN: combine_BRUSSELS_OR_LEUVEN + SPECIALIST_BEER_CAFE_OR_BREWERY AND: avoid_DRINKING_AND_DRIVING Reason: Beer culture is a major element of Belgian culinary identity and is best experienced without unnecessary road transport. IF: traveler_interest == NATURE THEN: prioritize_ARDENNES + HIGH_FENS + MEUSE_VALLEY AND: consider_PRIVATE_CAR_FOR_RURAL_AREAS Reason: Belgium''s strongest natural experiences are less rail-concentrated than its major historic cities. IF: traveler_interest == BELGIAN_COAST THEN: use_RAIL + COASTAL_TRAM AND: combine_BEACH + CYCLING + ZWIN_OR_COASTAL_TOWN Reason: Belgium''s coast is unusually accessible through integrated rail and tram travel. IF: traveler_interest == PHOTOGRAPHY THEN: prioritize_BRUGES_EARLY_MORNING + GHENT_EVENING + GRAND_PLACE_BLUE_HOUR + ANTWERP_ARCHITECTURE Reason: Early and late hours provide stronger atmosphere and reduce crowd pressure in Belgium''s most photographed historic centres. IF: traveler_type == SENIOR THEN: prefer_CENTRAL_HOTELS + DIRECT_TRAINS + TAXI_FOR_FINAL_MILE AND: reduce_BELFRY_CLIMBS + COBBLED_WALKING + CASTLE_STAIRS Reason: Belgium is senior-friendly overall, but medieval surfaces and historic buildings create localized accessibility challenges. IF: traveler_uses_WHEELCHAIR THEN: use_VERIFIED_ACCESSIBLE_RAIL_ROUTE + ACCESSIBLE_HOTEL AND: verify_HISTORIC_ATTRACTIONS_INDIVIDUALLY Reason: Modern transport infrastructure can be strong while heritage-site accessibility remains variable. IF: season == APRIL_TO_JUNE THEN: increase_WALKING + CYCLING + HISTORIC_CITY_SIGHTSEEING AND: retain_RAIN_PROTECTION Reason: Longer daylight and generally milder conditions make late spring and early summer particularly suitable for multi-city touring. IF: season == JULY_OR_AUGUST THEN: expect_HIGHER_CROWD + HIGHER_PRICE_IN_MAJOR_TOURISM_CENTRES AND: book_BRUGES_AND_PREMIUM_HOTELS_EARLY Reason: Summer provides excellent daylight but stronger tourism demand reduces crowd comfort and value. IF: season == SEPTEMBER THEN: prioritize_CITY_TOURING + CYCLING + GASTRONOMY + COUNTRYSIDE Reason: September commonly provides one of Belgium''s strongest balances between outdoor conditions and manageable visitor pressure. IF: season == NOVEMBER_TO_FEBRUARY THEN: increase_MUSEUMS + FOOD + BEER + CHOCOLATE + CULTURAL_INTERIORS AND: reduce_LONG_OUTDOOR_PROGRAMS Reason: Short daylight and cooler, wetter conditions favour Belgium''s exceptional indoor cultural and gastronomic experiences. IF: weather == HEAVY_RAIN THEN: replace_EXTENDED_WALKING_WITH_MUSEUMS + CHOCOLATE + BEER + INDOOR_HERITAGE AND: retain_FLEXIBLE_RAIL_SCHEDULE Reason: Belgian weather can remain changeable throughout the year, making indoor alternatives important. IF: route == BRUSSELS_TO_GHENT THEN: prefer_DIRECT_TRAIN Reason: Current SNCB scheduling provides frequent direct service, with the journey averaging approximately 36 minutes. IF: route == BRUSSELS_TO_BRUGES THEN: prefer_DIRECT_TRAIN Reason: Current SNCB scheduling provides frequent direct service, with the journey averaging approximately 1 hour 4 minutes. IF: trip_length <= 5 nights THEN: avoid_RENTAL_CAR_FOR_PRIMARY_FLEMISH_CITY_CIRCUIT AND: use_RAIL + WALKING + LOCAL_TRANSIT Reason: Belgium''s principal visitor cities are exceptionally well suited to rail-based touring. IF: trip_length >= 7 nights AND: traveler_interest == BOTH_FLANDERS_AND_WALLONIA THEN: consider_TWO_BASE_STRATEGY AND: split_FLANDERS_OR_BRUSSELS + WALLONIA Reason: A second base becomes useful when rural Wallonia, Ardennes or eastern Belgium are substantial itinerary components. IF: traveler_interest == FIRST_TIME_BELGIUM THEN: prioritize_BRUSSELS + BRUGES + GHENT + ANTWERP AND: add_ONE_SECONDARY_REGION_ONLY_IF_TIME_ALLOWS Reason: These four cities provide Belgium''s strongest first introduction to heritage, Flemish art, architecture, gastronomy and contemporary urban culture.', 2384),
  ('belgium', 34, 'destination-scoring', 'DESTINATION SCORING', NULL, NULL, '| Factor | Score | | --- | --- | | Family | 91 | | Honeymoon | 92 | | Luxury | 90 | | Budget | 76 | | Adventure | 76 | | Culture | 97 | | Food | 96 | | Shopping | 91 | | Nightlife | 88 | | Relaxation | 88 | | Nature | 84 | | Accessibility | 84 | | Safety | 85 | | First-time visitor | 95 | | Photography | 97 |', 2385),
  ('belgium', 35, 'final-travel-agent-verdict', 'FINAL TRAVEL AGENT VERDICT', NULL, NULL, 'Best traveler profiles: 1. Culture / heritage traveler (Brussels, Bruges, Ghent, Antwerp, Belfries, Béguinages) 2. Art / architecture traveler (Flemish Masters, Horta, Art Nouveau, KMSKA, Plantin-Moretus) 3. Honeymoon / romantic traveler (Bruges, Ghent, Boutique Hotels, Canals, Fine Dining) 4. Food / beer traveler (Chocolate, Beer, Frites, Waffles, Brasseries, Regional Cuisine) 5. Photography traveler (Bruges, Ghent, Grand-Place, Antwerp, Dinant, Ardennes) 6. History traveler (Medieval Cities, Flanders Fields, Waterloo, Industrial Heritage) 7. Family traveler (Atomium, Train World, Castles, Canals, Chocolate, Belgian Coast) 8. Luxury traveler (Heritage Hotels, Fine Dining, Private Guides, Fashion, Spa) 9. Nature / soft-adventure traveler (Ardennes, High Fens, Meuse Valley, Coast, Cycling) 10. First-time Europe traveler (Compact Cities, Rail Travel, Heritage, Food, Museums) Best duration: 7–10 nights 3–4 nights: Best for BRUSSELS + BRUGES_OR_GHENT + BELGIAN_FOOD_AND_HERITAGE. 5–6 nights: Best for BRUSSELS + BRUGES + GHENT + ANTWERP with efficient national rail travel. 7–10 nights: Excellent for BRUSSELS + BRUGES + GHENT + ANTWERP + LEUVEN_OR_MECHELEN + ONE_REGIONAL_EXTENSION. 11+ nights: Best for slower Flanders + Brussels + Wallonia + Flanders Fields + Ardennes / Belgian Coast exploration. Best season: APRIL_TO_JUNE + SEPTEMBER_TO_EARLY_OCTOBER Spring / Early Summer (April – June): HISTORIC_CITIES + WALKING + CYCLING + CANALS + PHOTOGRAPHY + LONGER_DAYLIGHT. Peak Summer (July – August): FESTIVALS + COAST + TERRACES + LONG_DAYLIGHT + OUTDOOR_ACTIVITY, with stronger crowds and pricing. Autumn (September – November): HERITAGE + FOOD + BEER + MUSEUMS + AUTUMN_PHOTOGRAPHY + LOWER_VISITOR_PRESSURE. Winter (December – February): CHRISTMAS_MARKETS + MUSEUMS + CHOCOLATE + BEER + GASTRONOMY + CULTURAL_CITY_BREAKS. Belgian weather should always be treated as: CHANGEABLE + RAIN_POSSIBLE_YEAR_ROUND + REGION_AND_YEAR_DEPENDENT. Best hotel strategy: Choose accommodation according to CITY_PRIORITY + RAIL_ACCESS + WALKABILITY + TRIP_LENGTH. For first-time visitors: BRUSSELS_CENTRAL + BRUGES_OR_GHENT_OVERNIGHT provides a strong balanced pattern. For honeymoon / romance: BRUGES_HISTORIC_CENTER / GHENT_HISTORIC_CORE / BOUTIQUE_HERITAGE_HOTEL. For culture: BRUSSELS + GHENT + ANTWERP with strong rail-station access. For luxury: CENTRAL_BRUSSELS / HISTORIC_BRUGES / PREMIUM_ANTWERP. For longer national trips: Consider TWO_BASE_OR_MULTI_BASE_PLANNING only when adding Wallonia, Ardennes or Flanders Fields. Avoid unnecessary hotel changes because major Belgian cities are highly rail-connected. Best transportation: Use: Belgium transportation should primarily be treated as: RAIL_BETWEEN_MAJOR_CITIES + WALKING_WITHIN_HISTORIC_CENTRES + LOCAL_PUBLIC_TRANSPORT_WHERE_REQUIRED + PRIVATE_ROAD_TRANSPORT_FOR_RURAL_REGIONS. Primary airport: BRUSSELS_AIRPORT IATA: BRU Brussels Airport-Zaventem railway station is directly beneath the terminal. Direct rail connections currently include: BRUSSELS + LEUVEN + ANTWERP + GHENT + BRUGES + LIÈGE + NAMUR. Must-do for first-time visitor: Belgium should not be reduced to BRUSSELS + BRUGES alone; its identity combines Flemish art, medieval civic heritage, Art Nouveau, gastronomy, beer culture, First World War history, industrial heritage, European institutions, Walloon cities, Ardennes landscapes and the North Sea coast. Belgium should primarily be positioned as: CULTURAL_HERITAGE + ART_AND_ARCHITECTURE + RAIL_BASED_CITY_TOURING + GASTRONOMY + ROMANTIC_TRAVEL + HISTORY + PHOTOGRAPHY + FAMILY_TRAVEL + NATURE_EXTENSIONS. Belgium currently has: 16 UNESCO WORLD HERITAGE PROPERTIES including major examples such as: LA_GRAND_PLACE_BRUSSELS + HISTORIC_CENTRE_OF_BRUGGE + FLEMISH_BEGUINAGES + BELFRIES_OF_BELGIUM_AND_FRANCE + VICTOR_HORTA_TOWN_HOUSES + PLANTIN_MORETUS + GREAT_SPA_TOWNS_OF_EUROPE + FIRST_WORLD_WAR_MEMORY_SITES + MAJOR_MINING_SITES_OF_WALLONIA. Don''t-do: Belgium first-time sightseeing should primarily be treated as: BRUSSELS + BRUGES + GHENT + ANTWERP + BELGIAN_FOOD_AND_BEER + ONE_SECONDARY_CITY_OR_REGION. Brussels should primarily be treated as: GRAND_PLACE + ART_AND_MUSEUMS + ART_NOUVEAU + EUROPEAN_QUARTER + GASTRONOMY + URBAN_CULTURE. Bruges should primarily be treated as: UNESCO_MEDIEVAL_HERITAGE + CANALS + FLEMISH_ART + ROMANCE + PHOTOGRAPHY + HISTORIC_WALKING. Ghent should primarily be treated as: MEDIEVAL_HERITAGE + GHENT_ALTARPIECE + CASTLE + CANALS + NIGHTLIFE + URBAN_CULTURE. Antwerp should primarily be treated as: FLEMISH_ART + PLANTIN_MORETUS + FASHION + DIAMONDS + ARCHITECTURE + URBAN_NIGHTLIFE. Wallonia should primarily be treated as: DINANT_AND_NAMUR + LIÈGE + SPA + ARDENNES + INDUSTRIAL_HERITAGE + RIVER_AND_FOREST_LANDSCAPES. Biggest advantage: Exceptional concentration of medieval cities, UNESCO heritage, Flemish art, architecture, food, beer, museums and contrasting regions within a compact country supported by strong national rail connectivity. Belgium can function simultaneously as a: CITY_BREAK_DESTINATION + CULTURAL_DESTINATION + ROMANTIC_DESTINATION + FOOD_AND_BEER_DESTINATION + HISTORY_DESTINATION + FAMILY_DESTINATION + RAIL_TOURING_DESTINATION + NATURE_EXTENSION_DESTINATION. Biggest disadvantage: Changeable weather, peak-season tourism pressure in headline cities, relatively high accommodation and dining costs, cobbled historic environments and weaker transport convenience in rural nature regions compared with the major cities. Overall destination score: 96/100', 2386),
  ('belgium', 36, 'data-quality', 'DATA QUALITY', NULL, NULL, 'information_completeness: 98/100 last_updated: 2026-09-05 last_verified: WEB_VERIFIED verified_by: UNESCO_WORLD_HERITAGE_CENTRE / VISIT_FLANDERS / VISIT_BRUSSELS / WALLONIA_BELGIUM_TOURISM / SNCB_NMBS / BRUSSELS_AIRPORT / ROYAL_METEOROLOGICAL_INSTITUTE_OF_BELGIUM sources: IMPORTANT: Belgium should primarily be treated as a: COMPACT_MULTI_CITY_DESTINATION + RAIL_FIRST_DESTINATION + UNESCO_HERITAGE_DESTINATION + ART_AND_ARCHITECTURE_DESTINATION + GASTRONOMY_DESTINATION + REGIONAL_NATURE_DESTINATION. Belgium currently has: 16 UNESCO_WORLD_HERITAGE_PROPERTIES. UNESCO status, component lists and conservation conditions should always be verified against the current World Heritage Centre database. Belgium transportation should primarily be stored as: NATIONAL_RAIL_DOMINANT_FOR_MAJOR_CITIES + LOCAL_PUBLIC_TRANSPORT + WALKING + CYCLING + PRIVATE_ROAD_TRANSPORT_FOR_RURAL_REGIONS. Current Brussels Airport rail positioning: AIRPORT_STATION_DIRECTLY_BELOW_TERMINAL + DIRECT_RAIL_TO_MAJOR_BELGIAN_CITIES. Do not permanently store: TRAIN_FREQUENCY + JOURNEY_TIME + PLATFORM + FARE + ENGINEERING_WORKS without SNCB / NMBS re-verification. Accessibility should be treated as: GOOD_TRANSPORT_SUPPORT + SITE_SPECIFIC_HERITAGE_LIMITATIONS. SNCB / NMBS currently provides free reduced-mobility assistance, with booking conditions depending on station, route and connection requirements. Do not assume: EVERY_STATION + EVERY_TRAIN + EVERY_BELFRY + EVERY_CASTLE + EVERY_MEDIEVAL_BUILDING provides identical accessibility. Belgian climate information should be stored as: TEMPERATE + CHANGEABLE + RAINFALL_POSSIBLE_YEAR_ROUND + SEASONALLY_VARIABLE. Historical climate normals should NOT be treated as guaranteed future weather. Accommodation strategy should primarily consider: RAIL_STATION_ACCESS + HISTORIC_CENTER_WALKABILITY + TRIP_LENGTH + EVENING_PRIORITY + BUDGET + ACCESSIBILITY. Belgium food should be treated as: CHOCOLATE + BEER + FRITES + WAFFLES + SEAFOOD + FLEMISH_AND_WALLOON_REGIONAL_CUISINE + BRASSERIES + FINE_DINING. Belgium should primarily be treated as: CULTURE + HISTORY + ART + ARCHITECTURE + FOOD + ROMANCE + FAMILY + PHOTOGRAPHY + RAIL_TOURING + NATURE. Current rail schedules, fares, attraction timings, museum closures, exhibitions, heritage restoration, weather conditions, seasonal events and accessibility facilities must NOT be treated as permanently valid. UNESCO_WORLD_HERITAGE_CENTRE + VISIT_FLANDERS + VISIT_BRUSSELS + WALLONIA_BELGIUM_TOURISM + SNCB_NMBS + BRUSSELS_AIRPORT + ROYAL_METEOROLOGICAL_INSTITUTE_OF_BELGIUM should be treated as primary verification sources. This dataset should be refreshed regularly before production use.', 2387),
  ('germany', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Spring', NULL, 'months: March April May weather: Transitional to mild; March can remain cool and changeable, while April and especially May bring longer days, blossoms, greener landscapes, and increasingly comfortable city and countryside conditions. crowd_level: LOW → MEDIUM price_level: LOW_MEDIUM → MEDIUM_HIGH overall_score: 70–79 recommended: true reason: Strong for Berlin, Munich, castles, historic cities, Rhine / Moselle, Black Forest, gardens, hiking, cycling, photography, Easter traditions, and sightseeing before peak summer demand.', 2388),
  ('germany', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Summer', NULL, 'months: June July August weather: Generally warm with long daylight; excellent for cities, lakes, forests, Baltic / North Sea destinations, hiking, cycling, festivals, castles, and outdoor sightseeing, although hot periods and thunderstorms can occur. crowd_level: HIGH → VERY_HIGH in major tourism areas price_level: MEDIUM_HIGH → HIGH overall_score: 65–72 recommended: true reason: Peak season for Bavaria, Romantic Road, Black Forest, Lake Constance, coasts, islands, outdoor travel, festivals, family holidays, and long sightseeing days.', 2389),
  ('germany', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Autumn', NULL, 'months: September October November weather: September is generally mild and highly practical; October brings cooler temperatures and colourful landscapes, while November becomes colder, darker, and more changeable. crowd_level: MEDIUM → LOW price_level: MEDIUM → LOWER overall_score: 72–80 recommended: true reason: September and October provide one of Germany''s strongest combinations of city sightseeing, forests, castles, wine regions, hiking, harvest experiences, photography, manageable crowds, and improved value.', 2390),
  ('germany', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Winter', NULL, 'months: December January February weather: Cold with short daylight; snow is more dependable in higher Bavarian and mountain areas than in major cities, where conditions can be cold, wet, cloudy, or occasionally snowy. crowd_level: LOW → VERY_HIGH during Christmas-market periods and selected ski / holiday dates price_level: LOW_MEDIUM → HIGH depending on destination and dates overall_score: 66–74 recommended: true reason: Excellent for Christmas markets, festive historic cities, museums, thermal spas, winter culture, Bavarian snow experiences, skiing, winter hiking, and atmospheric city breaks.', 2391),
  ('germany', 10, 'budget-strategy', 'BUDGET STRATEGY', NULL, NULL, 'Where money can be saved: Germany Travel describes rail as one of the easiest ways to explore the country, with frequent ICE connections between major cities and extensive regional links. Where saving money is usually NOT recommended: Travel-agent rule: In Germany, **HOTEL_LOCATION + RAIL_COST + LOCAL_TRANSPORT + EVENT_DATES + REGION should be evaluated together**. For short stays, prioritize **ONE_MAJOR_CITY + ONE_NEARBY_EXCURSION**. For longer stays, combine **BERLIN + MUNICH / BAVARIA + ONE_CONTRASTING_REGION** rather than repeatedly crossing the country.', 2392),
  ('germany', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Family', 'family', 'Use direct airport rail / S-Bahn where hotel location and luggage make it practical; otherwise choose an official taxi or pre-booked private transfer. For families continuing directly to another German city, rail from the airport can reduce unnecessary city-centre transfers.', 2393),
  ('germany', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Honeymoon', 'honeymoon', 'Prefer first-class rail, comfortable airport train, or private transfer according to the itinerary. For multi-city honeymoons, high-speed rail usually provides a more relaxed experience than repeated short domestic flights.', 2394),
  ('germany', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Luxury', 'luxury', 'Use chauffeured premium sedan / SUV with meet-and-assist, luggage support, and direct hotel transfer. For luxury multi-region travel, combine FIRST_CLASS_RAIL + PRIVATE_CHAUFFEUR + PERSONALIZED_LOCAL_GUIDES.', 2395),
  ('germany', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Budget', 'budget', 'Use airport trains, S-Bahn, regional rail, buses, and normal city transport. Berlin Brandenburg Airport, for example, is directly connected by Airport Express, regional trains, S-Bahn, and buses.', 2396),
  ('germany', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Senior', 'senior', 'Prefer direct airport rail when station access and luggage are manageable; otherwise use a taxi / private transfer. Choose hotels close to major stations or simple public-transport connections and minimize unnecessary transfers.', 2397),
  ('germany', 18, 'family-travel', 'FAMILY TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'child_friendly_score: 95 best_ages: Rules: For young children: Prefer: Avoid: Germany Travel specifically promotes museums designed for children and families alongside wider family cultural experiences.', 2398),
  ('germany', 19, 'honeymoon-travel', 'HONEYMOON TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'honeymoon_score: 90 romance_score: 89 privacy_score: 88 luxury_score: 89 Recommended: Honeymoon itineraries should generally keep: 2–3 major experiences/day. Prefer: CASTLES + HISTORIC_TOWNS + WINE + SCENERY + DINING + WELLNESS over: Constant city changes. Recommended areas: Germany is especially suitable for couples seeking **CASTLES + HISTORY + WINE + FORESTS + GASTRONOMY + SPA + SLOW_TRAVEL**.', 2399);
INSERT INTO destination_guidance (place_id, section, topic, section_title, heading, audience, body, position) VALUES
  ('germany', 20, 'luxury-travel', 'LUXURY TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'luxury_score: 89 Recommended: Germany luxury travel should focus on: Berlin, Munich, Frankfurt, Hamburg, Baden-Baden, Bavaria, and major wine regions provide Germany''s strongest premium-travel ecosystem.', 2400),
  ('germany', 21, 'adventure', 'ADVENTURE', NULL, NULL, 'adventure_score: 91 Germany is a strong outdoor and active-travel destination with substantial regional variety. Adventure experiences should be interpreted as: Germany Travel promotes hiking across forests, vineyards, mountains and coastal landscapes, while the country has more than 320 long-distance cycling routes and around 12,000 km within the national D-route network. Adventure activities should be matched to season, weather, fitness, trail conditions, and professional guidance requirements.', 2401),
  ('germany', 22, 'senior-travel', 'SENIOR TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'senior_suitability: 91 walking_intensity: LOW–MEDIUM with rail / transport-focused planning MEDIUM–HIGH for castles, mountain areas, and long historic walks Rules: Germany works very well for seniors when positioned as a **RAIL + CULTURE + HISTORIC_CITIES + RIVER_SCENERY + WELLNESS + RELAXED_TRAVEL destination**.', 2402),
  ('germany', 23, 'accessibility', 'ACCESSIBILITY', NULL, NULL, 'wheelchair_accessibility: GOOD IN MANY MODERN URBAN / TRANSPORT ENVIRONMENTS → VARIABLE IN HISTORIC, CASTLE AND NATURAL AREAS public_transport_accessibility: GOOD → VERY_GOOD overall; verify specific station, train, bus, tram, and route hotel_accessibility: MUST_BE_VERIFIED_PER_HOTEL attraction_accessibility: MUST_BE_VERIFIED_PER_ATTRACTION Rule: Never infer accessibility from Germany''s generally strong transport and tourism infrastructure. Each hotel, railway station, museum, castle, restaurant, historic site, trail, beach, and mountain attraction should carry its own accessibility data. Additional notes:', 2403),
  ('germany', 24, 'food', 'FOOD', NULL, NULL, 'Germany is particularly strong for: German cuisine varies strongly by region, from fish and seafood in the north to Bavarian, Swabian, Franconian, Rhine and other regional traditions. Food experiences: Family: Prioritize sausages, schnitzel, potatoes, breads, pastries, pasta-style dishes, and casual restaurants. Honeymoon: Choose Rhine / Moselle wine dining, historic restaurants, boutique hotels, and fine dining. Luxury: Include Michelin-level dining, private culinary experiences, premium wine, and luxury hotel restaurants. Budget: Use bakeries, supermarkets, casual restaurants, street food, and market meals.', 2404),
  ('germany', 25, 'shopping', 'SHOPPING', NULL, NULL, 'Strong categories: Luxury shopping: Prefer: Budget: Prefer: Travel-agent rule: Use BERLIN + MUNICH + DUSSELDORF + FRANKFURT for PREMIUM_SHOPPING, CHRISTMAS_MARKETS for SEASONAL_CRAFTS, and REGIONAL_SHOPS for FOOD + WINE + LOCAL_PRODUCTS.', 2405),
  ('germany', 26, 'nightlife', 'NIGHTLIFE', NULL, NULL, 'nightlife_level: 93 Suitable for: Best areas: Evening activities are better suited to: Germany has one of Europe''s stronger nightlife ecosystems, led especially by Berlin, while Hamburg, Cologne, Munich and other major cities provide substantial bar, music, dining and entertainment scenes. Honeymoon travelers should generally prefer: FINE_DINING + WINE_BAR / COCKTAIL_LOUNGE + EVENING_CITY_WALK over: Club-heavy itineraries unless specifically requested. Travel-agent rule: Position Germany as a **STRONG CLUB + LIVE_MUSIC + BAR + DINING + CULTURAL_NIGHTLIFE DESTINATION**, with Berlin as the principal nightlife centre.', 2406),
  ('germany', 28, 'sample-itinerary-patterns', 'SAMPLE ITINERARY PATTERNS', '3 NIGHTS', NULL, '### Day 1 Arrival at Berlin Brandenburg Airport (BER) → Airport rail / private transfer to central Berlin → Hotel check-in → Relaxation and refreshment Afternoon: Central Berlin orientation → Brandenburg Gate → Reichstag surroundings → Unter den Linden → Holocaust Memorial → Potsdamer Platz → City photography Evening: Traditional German / contemporary dinner → Optional rooftop / cocktail bar → Relaxed Berlin evening → Hotel Berlin works best as the main base for a first 3-night Germany visit because it combines major national history, museums, architecture, shopping, dining, nightlife, and efficient transport. ### Day 2 Morning: Breakfast → Museum Island → Berlin Cathedral surroundings → Alexanderplatz → Berlin TV Tower area Choose according to interest: HISTORY: → East Side Gallery → Berlin Wall heritage → Checkpoint Charlie CULTURE: → Museum Island → Humboldt Forum → Selected museum RELAXED_CITY: → Tiergarten → Kurfürstendamm → Café / shopping time Afternoon: German lunch → Continue selected experience → Free neighbourhood exploration Evening: Berlin dinner → Optional live music / nightlife → Hotel Museum Island is one of Germany''s major cultural highlights and forms part of Berlin''s UNESCO World Heritage landscape. ### Day 3 Morning: Breakfast → Day trip to Potsdam → Sanssouci Palace area → Sanssouci Park → Historic Potsdam Afternoon: Lunch → Continue palace / garden exploration → Return to Berlin Evening: Final Berlin leisure → Kurfürstendamm / central shopping → German dinner → Optional nightlife → Hotel Potsdam is the strongest short regional addition because it provides Prussian palaces, gardens and heritage without requiring a major intercity transfer. ### Day 4 Breakfast → Leisure morning → Optional short Tiergarten / central Berlin walk → Souvenir shopping → Hotel checkout → Airport rail / private transfer to Berlin Brandenburg Airport → Departure Optional alternative according to traveler interest: FAMILY: → Brandenburg Gate → Berlin Zoo → Interactive museum → Tiergarten → Potsdam / easy palace experience HONEYMOON: → Boutique hotel → Brandenburg Gate evening → Museum Island → Potsdam / Sanssouci → Fine dining → Spa / relaxed couple time LUXURY: → Five-star Berlin hotel → Chauffeured sightseeing → Private cultural guide → Premium dining → Luxury shopping → Private Potsdam excursion HISTORY / CULTURE: → Brandenburg Gate → Reichstag → Museum Island → Berlin Wall heritage → Potsdam / Sanssouci NIGHTLIFE: → Berlin neighbourhood exploration → Cocktail bars → Live music → Clubs according to traveler profile REGIONAL_ALTERNATIVE: → DRESDEN instead of Potsdam for travelers prioritizing architecture and art OR → HAMBURG instead of Potsdam only when a second major city is specifically preferred For a 3-night first Germany visit, do not try to combine: BERLIN + MUNICH + NEUSCHWANSTEIN + RHINE_VALLEY + BLACK_FOREST. Munich and Bavaria are better treated as a separate base or included when the itinerary has additional nights. Munich itself combines Marienplatz, Bavarian culture, museums, food, shopping and access to southern Germany. Travel-agent rule: For 3 nights, prioritize: BERLIN + CORE_HISTORY_AND_CULTURE + ONE_POTSDAM_EXCURSION rather than maximum destination count.', 2407),
  ('germany', 29, 'seven-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'SEVEN-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 1', NULL, 'Arrival at Frankfurt Airport → Meet and assist → Private / comfortable transfer to Frankfurt hotel → Romantic hotel check-in → Relax and refresh Afternoon / Evening: Easy Frankfurt orientation → Römerberg → Frankfurt Old Town → Main River waterfront → Skyline views → Couple photography Evening: Romantic German dinner → Optional rooftop / cocktail lounge → Relaxed couple time → Overnight at Frankfurt', 2408),
  ('germany', 29, 'seven-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'SEVEN-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 2', NULL, 'Breakfast at the hotel → Hotel checkout → Scenic journey through southern Germany Black Forest experience: → Forest landscapes → Traditional villages → Cuckoo-clock heritage → Scenic photography → Relaxed regional lunch Continue toward Switzerland: → Rhine Falls → Waterfall viewpoints → Couple photography Evening: → Continue to Zurich → Romantic hotel check-in → Dinner → Overnight at Zurich', 2409),
  ('germany', 29, 'seven-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'SEVEN-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 3', NULL, 'Breakfast at the hotel → Full-day Swiss Alpine experience Choose ONE: JUNGFRAUJOCH: → Grindelwald → Jungfraujoch – Top of Europe → Snow and glacier scenery → Alpine viewpoints → Couple photography OR ROMANTIC_JUNGFRAU_REGION: → Grindelwald → Interlaken → Mountain scenery → Scenic village walks → Cafés and Swiss shopping → Relaxed couple time Evening: → Return to Zurich → Romantic dinner → Overnight at Zurich', 2410),
  ('germany', 29, 'seven-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'SEVEN-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 4', NULL, 'Breakfast → Mt. Titlis excursion → Engelberg → TITLIS Rotair → Snow and glacier scenery → Ice Flyer where operating → Titlis Cliff Walk subject to conditions → Couple photography Afternoon: → Continue to Lucerne → Chapel Bridge → Lion Monument → Old Town → Lake Lucerne waterfront → Swiss shopping Evening: → Return to Zurich → Special Swiss dinner → Overnight at Zurich', 2411),
  ('germany', 29, 'seven-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'SEVEN-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 5', NULL, 'Breakfast → Hotel checkout → Continue toward Vaduz, Liechtenstein → Vaduz orientation → Historic centre → Scenic photography Continue toward Austria: → Swarovski Crystal Worlds, Wattens → Continue to Innsbruck → Romantic hotel check-in Evening: → Golden Roof → Innsbruck Old Town → Alpine city views → Romantic dinner → Overnight at Innsbruck', 2412),
  ('germany', 29, 'seven-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'SEVEN-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 6', NULL, 'Breakfast → Hotel checkout → Scenic journey toward Venice Afternoon / Evening: → Vaporetto journey → St. Mark''s Square → Basilica surroundings → Doge''s Palace exterior → Bridge of Sighs → Venetian lanes Honeymoon highlight: → Optional gondola ride → Canal-side couple photography Evening: Romantic Italian dinner → Overnight in Venice / nearby area', 2413),
  ('germany', 29, 'seven-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'SEVEN-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 7', NULL, 'Breakfast → Continue toward Florence Afternoon: → Florence historic centre → Cathedral surroundings → Piazza della Signoria → Ponte Vecchio → Couple photography Late Afternoon / Evening: → Piazzale Michelangelo → Panoramic Florence views → Sunset experience where timing permits Evening: Special Italian dinner → Relaxed final honeymoon evening → Overnight at Florence', 2414),
  ('germany', 29, 'seven-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'SEVEN-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 8', NULL, 'Breakfast → Leisure morning according to flight / onward-travel schedule → Café / shopping time → Hotel checkout → Transfer toward Florence Airport / onward Italian gateway → Departure HONEYMOON COUNTRY FLOW: GERMANY → SWITZERLAND → LIECHTENSTEIN → AUSTRIA → ITALY GERMANY PRIORITY: FRANKFURT + BLACK_FOREST HONEYMOON PACING RULE: FRANKFURT_1_NIGHT + ZURICH_3_NIGHTS + INNSBRUCK_1_NIGHT + VENICE_1_NIGHT + FLORENCE_1_NIGHT Prioritize: FRANKFURT + BLACK_FOREST + RHINE_FALLS + SWISS_ALPINE_SCENERY + MT_TITLIS + LUCERNE + VADUZ + INNSBRUCK + VENICE + FLORENCE Keep: 2–3 major experiences/day where practical. Prefer: ROMANTIC_HOTELS + SCENIC_ROAD_AND_RAIL_JOURNEYS + ALPINE_VIEWS + COUPLE_PHOTOGRAPHY + ROMANTIC_DINING + GONDOLA_EXPERIENCE + RELAXED_EVENINGS over: Trying to retain Paris + Brussels + Amsterdam + Germany + Switzerland + Austria + Venice + Pisa + Florence + Rome within only 7 nights.', 2415),
  ('germany', 30, 'seven-nights-family-pattern', 'SEVEN-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 1', NULL, 'Arrival at Frankfurt Airport → Meet and assist → Train / private transfer to Frankfurt hotel → Family hotel check-in → Relax and refresh Afternoon / Evening: Easy Frankfurt orientation → Römerberg → Frankfurt Old Town → Main River waterfront → Skyline views → Family photography Evening: Family-friendly German dinner → Relaxed riverside walk → Overnight at Frankfurt', 2416),
  ('germany', 30, 'seven-nights-family-pattern', 'SEVEN-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 2', NULL, 'Breakfast at the hotel → Hotel checkout → Scenic journey through southern Germany Black Forest experience: → Forest landscapes → Traditional villages → Cuckoo-clock experience → Family photography → Regional lunch Continue toward Switzerland: → Rhine Falls → Waterfall viewpoints → Family photography → Optional boat experience where suitable and operating Evening: → Continue to Zurich → Hotel check-in → Dinner → Overnight at Zurich', 2417),
  ('germany', 30, 'seven-nights-family-pattern', 'SEVEN-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 3', NULL, 'Breakfast at the hotel → Swiss Alpine family experience Choose ONE: JUNGFRAUJOCH: → Grindelwald → Jungfraujoch – Top of Europe → Snow and glacier scenery → Indoor / outdoor viewpoints → Family photography OR EASY_FAMILY_ALPINE_DAY: → Grindelwald → Interlaken → Mountain scenery → Easy village exploration → Swiss cafés / chocolate → Family leisure time For younger children, prefer the lower-altitude Grindelwald / Interlaken option when altitude, weather, or a long mountain day may be unsuitable. Evening: → Return to Zurich → Family dinner → Overnight at Zurich', 2418),
  ('germany', 30, 'seven-nights-family-pattern', 'SEVEN-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 4', NULL, 'Breakfast → Mt. Titlis excursion → Engelberg → Cable-car journey → TITLIS Rotair → Snow and glacier scenery → Ice Flyer where operating and suitable → Titlis Cliff Walk subject to weather and children''s comfort → Family snow time Afternoon: → Continue to Lucerne → Chapel Bridge → Lion Monument → Old Town → Lake Lucerne waterfront → Chocolate / souvenir shopping Evening: → Return to Zurich → Dinner → Overnight at Zurich', 2419),
  ('germany', 30, 'seven-nights-family-pattern', 'SEVEN-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 5', NULL, 'Breakfast → Hotel checkout → Continue toward Vaduz, Liechtenstein → Vaduz orientation → Historic centre → Family photography Continue toward Austria: → Swarovski Crystal Worlds, Wattens → Family-friendly exhibits / installations → Continue to Innsbruck → Hotel check-in Evening: → Golden Roof → Innsbruck Old Town → Easy family walk → Dinner → Overnight at Innsbruck', 2420),
  ('germany', 30, 'seven-nights-family-pattern', 'SEVEN-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 6', NULL, 'Breakfast → Hotel checkout → Scenic journey toward Venice Afternoon / Evening: → Vaporetto journey → St. Mark''s Square → Basilica surroundings → Doge''s Palace exterior → Bridge of Sighs → Venetian streets and canals Optional: → Gondola ride according to family interest Evening: Family-friendly Italian dinner → Overnight in Venice / nearby area', 2421),
  ('germany', 30, 'seven-nights-family-pattern', 'SEVEN-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 7', NULL, 'Breakfast → Continue toward Florence Afternoon: → Florence historic centre → Cathedral surroundings → Piazza della Signoria → Ponte Vecchio → Gelato break → Family photography Late Afternoon: → Piazzale Michelangelo → Panoramic Florence views → Relaxed family time Evening: Italian dinner → Overnight at Florence', 2422),
  ('germany', 30, 'seven-nights-family-pattern', 'SEVEN-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 8', NULL, 'Breakfast → Leisure morning according to departure schedule → Optional café / souvenir shopping → Hotel checkout → Transfer to Florence Airport / suitable onward gateway → Departure FAMILY COUNTRY FLOW: GERMANY → SWITZERLAND → LIECHTENSTEIN → AUSTRIA → ITALY GERMANY FAMILY PRIORITY: FRANKFURT + BLACK_FOREST FAMILY PACING RULE: FRANKFURT_1_NIGHT + ZURICH_3_NIGHTS + INNSBRUCK_1_NIGHT + VENICE_1_NIGHT + FLORENCE_1_NIGHT Prioritize: FRANKFURT + BLACK_FOREST + RHINE_FALLS + GRINDELWALD / INTERLAKEN + ONE_MAJOR_ALPINE_EXPERIENCE + MT_TITLIS + LUCERNE + VADUZ + INNSBRUCK + VENICE + FLORENCE Keep: 2–3 major experiences/day maximum. For younger children, prioritize: BLACK_FOREST + RHINE_FALLS + SCENIC_JOURNEYS + GRINDELWALD / INTERLAKEN + SNOW_PLAY + LUCERNE + SHORT_CITY_WALKS + GELATO / CHOCOLATE EXPERIENCES over: HIGH_ALTITUDE_OVERLOAD + LONG_WALKING_DAYS + MULTIPLE_MOUNTAIN_EXCURSIONS + MUSEUM_HEAVY_DAYS + EXCESSIVE_HOTEL_CHANGES', 2423),
  ('germany', 31, 'seven-nights-luxury-pattern', 'SEVEN-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 1', NULL, 'Arrival at Frankfurt Airport → VIP meet and assist → Chauffeured premium transfer to hotel → Five-star / luxury hotel check-in → Welcome amenities → Relax and refresh Afternoon / Evening: Private Frankfurt orientation → Römerberg → Frankfurt Old Town → Main River waterfront → Skyline views → Private photography opportunity Evening: Fine-dining experience → Optional rooftop / premium lounge → Overnight at Frankfurt', 2424),
  ('germany', 31, 'seven-nights-luxury-pattern', 'SEVEN-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 2', NULL, 'Breakfast at the hotel → Hotel checkout → Private chauffeured journey through southern Germany Black Forest experience: → Scenic forest landscapes → Selected traditional village → Premium cuckoo-clock / craft experience → Flexible photography stops → Fine regional lunch Continue toward Switzerland: → Private Rhine Falls excursion → Premium viewpoints → Optional boat experience where operating Evening: → Continue to Zurich → Luxury hotel / suite check-in → Fine dining → Overnight at Zurich', 2425),
  ('germany', 31, 'seven-nights-luxury-pattern', 'SEVEN-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 3', NULL, 'Breakfast at the hotel Choose ONE premium Alpine experience: JUNGFRAUJOCH: → First-class / premium rail arrangements → Grindelwald → Jungfraujoch – Top of Europe → Glacier and Alpine scenery → Private guide where preferred → Premium lunch → Couple / private photography OR LUXURY_JUNGFRAU_REGION: → Grindelwald → Interlaken → Private / premium transfers → Scenic viewpoints → Mountain dining → Flexible leisure time Evening: → Return to Zurich → Hotel spa / wellness → Fine dining → Overnight at Zurich', 2426),
  ('germany', 31, 'seven-nights-luxury-pattern', 'SEVEN-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 4', NULL, 'Breakfast → Private transfer / premium rail toward Engelberg → Mt. Titlis premium excursion → TITLIS Rotair → Glacier scenery → Ice Flyer where operating → Titlis Cliff Walk subject to conditions → Private guide where preferred → Mountain lunch Afternoon: → Continue to Lucerne → Chapel Bridge → Old Town → Lake Lucerne waterfront → Premium watch / Swiss shopping Optional: → Private Lake Lucerne cruise Evening: → Return to Zurich → Fine dining / hotel relaxation → Overnight at Zurich', 2427),
  ('germany', 31, 'seven-nights-luxury-pattern', 'SEVEN-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 5', NULL, 'Breakfast → Hotel checkout → Private chauffeur toward Liechtenstein Vaduz: → Private city orientation → Historic centre → Scenic photography Continue toward Austria: → Swarovski Crystal Worlds, Wattens → Premium shopping → Continue to Innsbruck → Luxury hotel check-in Evening: → Private Old Town orientation → Golden Roof → Alpine views → Fine dining → Overnight at Innsbruck', 2428),
  ('germany', 31, 'seven-nights-luxury-pattern', 'SEVEN-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 6', NULL, 'Breakfast → Hotel checkout → Private scenic transfer toward Venice Afternoon / Evening: → Private / premium water transfer where practical → St. Mark''s Square → Basilica surroundings → Doge''s Palace → Bridge of Sighs → Venetian lanes Luxury honeymoon highlight: → Private gondola experience → Professional photography where preferred Evening: Fine-dining experience → Luxury hotel stay → Overnight in Venice', 2429),
  ('germany', 31, 'seven-nights-luxury-pattern', 'SEVEN-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 7', NULL, 'Breakfast → Private / premium rail transfer toward Florence Afternoon: Private Florence experience → Historic centre → Cathedral surroundings → Piazza della Signoria → Ponte Vecchio → Luxury boutiques / artisan shopping Late Afternoon: → Piazzale Michelangelo → Panoramic Florence views → Private photography / sunset experience Evening: Special Tuscan fine-dining experience → Premium hotel / suite → Overnight at Florence', 2430),
  ('germany', 31, 'seven-nights-luxury-pattern', 'SEVEN-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 8', NULL, 'Breakfast → Leisure morning → Optional spa / premium shopping → Hotel checkout → Chauffeured private transfer to Florence Airport / suitable onward gateway → Departure LUXURY COUNTRY FLOW: GERMANY → SWITZERLAND → LIECHTENSTEIN → AUSTRIA → ITALY GERMANY LUXURY PRIORITY: FRANKFURT + BLACK_FOREST LUXURY PACING RULE: FRANKFURT_1_NIGHT + ZURICH_3_NIGHTS + INNSBRUCK_1_NIGHT + VENICE_1_NIGHT + FLORENCE_1_NIGHT Prioritize: 5_STAR_HOTELS + VIP_AIRPORT_ASSISTANCE + PRIVATE_CHAUFFEURS + FIRST_CLASS_RAIL + PRIVATE_GUIDES + PREMIUM_ALPINE_EXPERIENCES + PRIVATE_WATER_TRANSFERS + FINE_DINING + SPA_AND_WELLNESS + PREMIUM_SHOPPING + FLEXIBLE_FREE_TIME Germany should contribute: FRANKFURT_LUXURY_HOSPITALITY + OLD_TOWN_AND_SKYLINE + BLACK_FOREST_SCENIC_DRIVE + PREMIUM_REGIONAL_DINING + PRIVATE_CHauffeured_TOURING Luxury pacing should emphasize: PRIVACY + COMFORT + SCENIC_TRAVEL + PERSONALIZED_SERVICE + PREMIUM_ACCOMMODATION + FLEXIBLE_SIGHTSEEING + GASTRONOMY + WELLNESS rather than: MAXIMUM_DESTINATION_COUNT + GROUP_STYLE_SIGHTSEEING + RUSHED_PHOTO_STOPS + EXCESSIVE_HOTEL_CHANGES Travel-agent rule: For a 7-night luxury itinerary beginning in Germany, use FRANKFURT + BLACK_FOREST as the German introduction, Switzerland as the principal scenic / Alpine luxury component, and LIECHTENSTEIN + AUSTRIA + NORTHERN_ITALY as the onward premium route. Do not add PARIS + BRUSSELS + AMSTERDAM + ROME to the same 7-night programme; use the available time to increase HOTEL_QUALITY + PRIVATE_SERVICE + DINING + SCENIC_EXPERIENCES + FREE_TIME instead.', 2431),
  ('germany', 32, 'travel-agent-insights', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS', 'What inexperienced planners often do wrong', NULL, '', 2432),
  ('germany', 32, 'travel-agent-insights', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS', 'What an experienced planner does differently', NULL, '', 2433),
  ('germany', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', NULL, NULL, 'IF: trip_length <= 4 nights THEN: prioritize_ONE_MAJOR_BASE + ONE_NEARBY_EXCURSION Reason: Avoid wasting a short Germany trip on long transfers. IF: trip_length >= 7 nights AND: traveler_interest == FIRST_TIME_GERMANY THEN: prioritize_BERLIN + MUNICH_BAVARIA + ONE_CONTRASTING_REGION IF: trip_type == HONEYMOON THEN: prefer_RHINE_MOSELLE + HEIDELBERG + BLACK_FOREST_OR_BAVARIA AND: increase_FREE_TIME + ROMANCE + DINING + WELLNESS IF: traveler_type == FAMILY THEN: prefer_BAVARIA + CASTLES + INTERACTIVE_MUSEUMS + NATURE + FAMILY_ATTRACTIONS AND: reduce_OVERPACKED_MUSEUM_AND_TRANSFER_DAYS IF: traveler_type == LUXURY THEN: prefer_5_STAR_HOTELS + FIRST_CLASS_ICE + PRIVATE_DRIVER + EXPERT_GUIDE + FINE_DINING + SPA IF: traveler_type == BUDGET THEN: prefer_PUBLIC_TRANSPORT + EARLY_BOOKED_RAIL + BUDGET_HOTELS + FREE_ATTRACTIONS + REGIONAL_FOOD IF: traveler_interest == CULTURE_AND_HISTORY THEN: prefer_BERLIN + DRESDEN + NUREMBERG + POTSDAM IF: traveler_interest == CASTLES THEN: prefer_NEUSCHWANSTEIN + RHINE_VALLEY + ROMANTIC_ROAD IF: traveler_interest == ROMANTIC_RELAXATION THEN: prefer_RHINE + MOSELLE + HEIDELBERG + BLACK_FOREST IF: traveler_interest == FOOD_AND_WINE THEN: prefer_BAVARIA + FRANCONIA + RHINE_MOSELLE + BERLIN AND: include_REGIONAL_CUISINE + BEER + WINE + BAKERIES + MARKETS IF: traveler_interest == NATURE_AND_HIKING THEN: prefer_BLACK_FOREST + BAVARIAN_ALPS + SAXON_SWITZERLAND + BERCHTESGADEN IF: traveler_interest == NIGHTLIFE THEN: prioritize_BERLIN AND: consider_HAMBURG + COLOGNE + LEIPZIG IF: traveler_interest == CHRISTMAS_MARKETS THEN: prefer_NUREMBERG + DRESDEN + COLOGNE + MUNICH + ROTHENBURG AND: verify_MARKET_DATES + HOTEL_AVAILABILITY IF: traveler_interest == ROMANTIC_ROAD THEN: allocate_MINIMUM_TWO_TO_THREE_DAYS AND: consider_RENTAL_CAR_OR_PRIVATE_DRIVER IF: traveler_interest == RHINE_OR_MOSELLE THEN: include_RIVER_CRUISE + CASTLES + WINE_TOWNS + SCENIC_RAIL IF: traveler_interest == BLACK_FOREST THEN: prefer_FREIBURG_OR_BADEN_BADEN_AS_BASE AND: include_HIKING + VILLAGES + WELLNESS + REGIONAL_FOOD IF: trip_length <= 7 nights THEN: prefer_MAXIMUM_TWO_OR_THREE_BASES AND: avoid_EXCESSIVE_HOTEL_CHANGES IF: traveler_type == SENIOR OR: traveler_mobility == LIMITED THEN: prefer_RAIL + RIVER_CRUISES + MUSEUMS + SPA + PRIVATE_TRANSPORT AND: reduce_CASTLE_STAIRS + DIFFICULT_HIKING IF: traveler_uses_WHEELCHAIR THEN: use_VERIFIED_ACCESSIBLE_HOTELS + TRANSPORT + ATTRACTIONS AND: never_assume_CASTLES + OLD_TOWNS + NATURE_TRAILS_ARE_STEP_FREE IF: traveler_interest == FIRST_TIME_GERMANY THEN: prioritize_BERLIN + MUNICH_BAVARIA AND: add_RHINE_OR_ROMANTIC_ROAD_OR_DRESDEN according to trip length IF: traveler_interest == AUTHENTIC_LOCAL_EXPERIENCE THEN: prefer_SMALL_TOWNS + REGIONAL_DINING + MARKETS + WINE_VILLAGES + LOCAL_FESTIVALS', 2434),
  ('germany', 34, 'destination-scoring', 'DESTINATION SCORING', NULL, NULL, '| Factor | Score | | ------------------ | ----: | | Family | 95 | | Honeymoon | 90 | | Luxury | 89 | | Budget | 84 | | Adventure | 91 | | Culture | 96 | | Food | 91 | | Shopping | 89 | | Nightlife | 93 | | Relaxation | 91 | | Nature | 94 | | Accessibility | 86 | | Safety | 92 | | First-time visitor | 96 | | Photography | 95 |', 2435),
  ('germany', 35, 'final-travel-agent-verdict', 'FINAL TRAVEL AGENT VERDICT', NULL, NULL, 'Best traveler profiles: 1. Culture / history traveler 2. First-time Europe traveler 3. Family traveler 4. Photography traveler 5. City-break traveler 6. Castle / heritage traveler 7. Nature / hiking traveler 8. Food / wine traveler 9. Nightlife traveler 10. Romantic / honeymoon traveler Best duration: 7–10 nights 4–5 nights for one major base such as Berlin or Munich plus one nearby signature excursion. 7–10 nights for most first-time visitors combining Berlin + Munich / Bavaria + one contrasting region such as the Rhine, Romantic Road, Dresden, Hamburg, or Black Forest. 12–14 nights for travelers wanting Berlin + Bavaria + Rhine / Moselle + one or two additional regions without excessive hotel changes. Best season: APRIL–JUNE and SEPTEMBER–OCTOBER April–May for cities, castles, gardens, Rhine / Moselle, Black Forest, hiking, cycling, and photography. June–August for long daylight, nature, lakes, coasts, festivals, family travel, and outdoor activities, but with higher summer demand. September–October are among the strongest overall months for cities, castles, wine regions, forests, hiking, and autumn photography. December is exceptional for Christmas markets and festive city travel, while January–February suit museums, wellness, winter city breaks, and Bavarian snow experiences. Germany''s official tourism platform highlights Christmas markets from the coast to the Alps as a major seasonal product. Best hotel strategy: Choose hotels according to railway / public-transport access and the main sightseeing cluster. For short stays, prioritize central Berlin, Munich, Cologne, Hamburg, Dresden, or Frankfurt locations with easy station and attraction access. For honeymoon and luxury travel, consider Rhine / Moselle wine properties, Black Forest wellness hotels, Bavarian resorts, historic hotels, and premium city properties. Avoid unnecessary one-night hotel changes. Best transportation: Walking + S-Bahn / U-Bahn / tram / bus within cities, ICE / regional rail between major destinations, and rental car / private driver selectively for countryside, vineyards, castles, and scenic routes. Germany Travel notes that major-city long-distance trains generally run at least hourly, with ICE speeds of up to 300 km/h and extensive onward regional connections. Private transport for: Must-do for first-time visitor: Germany''s strongest first-time value comes from combining major cities with regional heritage and landscapes rather than treating it only as an urban destination. Germany Travel positions cities, culture, nature, and regional rail access as core national tourism strengths. Don''t-do: Biggest advantage: Exceptional regional diversity combined with excellent transport. Germany combines major cities, deep history, castles, UNESCO heritage, wine regions, forests, mountains, rivers, coasts, family attractions, nightlife, Christmas markets, gastronomy, and extensive rail connectivity within one country. Biggest disadvantage: Germany''s size and regional diversity can encourage overplanning. Fast trains reduce travel time but do not eliminate hotel changes, luggage handling, and station transfers. Peak events can also make major cities expensive, while castles, historic towns, forests, and mountain areas vary significantly in accessibility and seasonal conditions. Overall destination score: 92/100', 2436),
  ('germany', 36, 'data-quality', 'DATA QUALITY', NULL, NULL, 'information_completeness: 96/100 last_updated: 2026-08-27 last_verified: PARTIALLY_WEB_VERIFIED verified_by: GERMANY TRAVEL / DEUTSCHE TOURISMUS SOURCES / OFFICIAL ACCESSIBILITY AND TRANSPORT INFORMATION sources: IMPORTANT: Prices, hotel rates, ICE / regional rail fares, attraction tickets, museum hours, castle admissions, river cruises, festival dates, ski operations, and accessibility must NOT be treated as permanently valid. Berlin museums, Neuschwanstein, major castles, Christmas markets, Oktoberfest, trade fairs, river cruises, Black Forest attractions, and other seasonal experiences should be checked before travel. Major events can materially affect hotel availability and prices. Weather can affect hiking, Alpine travel, river activities, coastal experiences, and winter road conditions. Historic castles, medieval towns, cobbled streets, forest trails, beaches, and mountain areas should not be assumed uniformly wheelchair accessible. Germany''s nationwide “Tourism for All” system provides independently verified accessibility information, but individual properties and attractions must still be checked. Germany should primarily be treated as: SPRING: CITIES + CASTLES + GARDENS + HIKING + CYCLING + PHOTOGRAPHY SUMMER: NATURE + FAMILY + COAST + LAKES + FESTIVALS + OUTDOORS AUTUMN: WINE + FORESTS + CASTLES + CULTURE + PHOTOGRAPHY WINTER: CHRISTMAS_MARKETS + CITY_CULTURE + FOOD + SPA + BAVARIAN_WINTER Germany Travel, Deutsche Bahn, regional tourism boards, accommodation providers, and individual attractions should be treated as primary sources for current operational information. This dataset should be refreshed regularly before production use.', 2437),
  ('austria', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Spring', NULL, 'months: March April May weather: Transitional in March, becoming milder and greener through April and May. Cities and valleys improve earlier, while higher Alpine areas can retain snow and mixed trail conditions. crowd_level: LOW → MEDIUM price_level: LOW_MEDIUM → MEDIUM overall_score: 72–79 recommended: true reason: Very good for Vienna, Salzburg, Graz, castles, culture, gardens, photography, Wachau, lower-altitude hiking, and increasingly accessible lakes and Alpine regions. May offers one of the strongest balances before peak summer, while high-altitude hiking remains season-dependent.', 2438),
  ('austria', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Summer', NULL, 'months: June July August weather: Warm with long daylight and generally excellent conditions for lakes, hiking, cycling, Alpine villages, cable cars, and outdoor sightseeing. crowd_level: HIGH → VERY_HIGH price_level: HIGH → VERY_HIGH overall_score: 62–72 recommended: true reason: Austria''s strongest season for: July–August provide excellent outdoor conditions but receive lower Crowd and Price scores because European holiday demand is high. Austria Tourism identifies June–September as particularly suitable for mountain-and-lake travel.', 2439),
  ('austria', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Autumn', NULL, 'months: September October November weather: September remains excellent for cities and mountains. October becomes cooler with strong autumn colour, while November is colder, quieter, and more transitional. crowd_level: MEDIUM → LOW price_level: MEDIUM → LOW overall_score: 74–80 recommended: true reason: September and October are excellent for Vienna, Salzburg, hiking, lakes, vineyards, Wachau, gastronomy, photography, and scenic touring. November has weaker outdoor conditions but much lower visitor pressure and stronger value for museums, cafés, culture, wellness, and city breaks.', 2440),
  ('austria', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Winter', NULL, 'months: December January February weather: Cold with reliable winter conditions across many Alpine regions. Snow is much less consistent in lowland cities than in major ski areas. crowd_level: MEDIUM → VERY_HIGH in major ski resorts / Christmas periods price_level: MEDIUM → VERY_HIGH in major ski resorts overall_score: 59–68 recommended: true reason: Outstanding for skiing, snowboarding, winter hiking, Christmas markets, Alpine resorts, spa, wellness, and snow photography. Major ski areas generally begin their main winter seasons between late November and mid-December depending on snow and weather, with glacier areas sometimes starting earlier.', 2441),
  ('austria', 10, 'budget-strategy', 'BUDGET STRATEGY', NULL, NULL, 'Where money can be saved: Where saving money is usually NOT recommended: Travel-agent rule: In Austria, **HOTEL_LOCATION + RAIL_COST + SEASON + MOUNTAIN_ACTIVITY_COST should be evaluated together**. For short stays, prioritize **ONE_OR_TWO_BASES + ONE_SIGNATURE_ALPINE_OR_CULTURAL_EXPERIENCE**. For longer stays, combine **VIENNA + SALZBURG + ONE_ALPINE_OR_LAKE_REGION** rather than changing hotels repeatedly.', 2442),
  ('austria', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Family', 'family', 'Use direct ÖBB Railjet / airport train where practical; otherwise pre-book a private car / MPV for luggage, young children, or direct hotel access. Vienna International Airport is Austria''s main international gateway. Railjet connects the airport directly with Vienna Hauptbahnhof and continues toward major Austrian cities including Linz, Salzburg, Innsbruck, and Graz.', 2443),
  ('austria', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Honeymoon', 'honeymoon', 'Prefer first-class rail or a pre-booked private transfer according to hotel location and luggage. For couples continuing beyond Vienna, Austria''s rail network makes Salzburg, the Wachau, Innsbruck, and other regions practical without immediately renting a car.', 2444),
  ('austria', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Luxury', 'luxury', 'Use chauffeured premium sedan / SUV or ÖBB First / Business Class with private local transfers. For multi-region luxury itineraries, combine FIRST_CLASS_RAIL + PRIVATE_CHAUFFEUR + PREMIUM_ALPINE_TRANSFERS.', 2445),
  ('austria', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Budget', 'budget', 'Use airport rail / bus and regular public transport. Vienna Airport has direct rail connections, making private airport transfers unnecessary for most budget travelers.', 2446),
  ('austria', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Senior', 'senior', 'Prefer direct rail where luggage and mobility permit; otherwise use a private transfer. Choose hotels near major stations and minimize unnecessary connections.', 2447),
  ('austria', 18, 'family-travel', 'FAMILY TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'child_friendly_score: 95 best_ages: Rules: For young children: Prefer: Avoid: Austria is one of Europe''s strongest family destinations through its combination of cities, mountains, lakes and year-round outdoor activities.', 2448),
  ('austria', 19, 'honeymoon-travel', 'HONEYMOON TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'honeymoon_score: 94 romance_score: 95 privacy_score: 91 luxury_score: 94 Recommended: Honeymoon itinerary should NOT contain more than: 2–3 major activities/day. Prefer: ONE_SCENIC_OR_ROMANTIC_SIGNATURE_EXPERIENCE + DINING + FREE_TIME over: Constant sightseeing and hotel changes. Recommended hotel areas: Austria works particularly well for couples combining imperial cities with Alpine scenery, lakes, wellness and romantic dining.', 2449),
  ('austria', 20, 'luxury-travel', 'LUXURY TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'luxury_score: 94 Recommended: Austria luxury travel should focus on: Luxury should increase SERVICE + PRIVACY + COMFORT + PERSONALIZATION rather than simply adding more attractions.', 2450),
  ('austria', 21, 'adventure', 'ADVENTURE', NULL, NULL, 'adventure_score: 95 Austria is one of Europe''s strongest Alpine adventure destinations. Adventure experiences: Tirol, SalzburgerLand, Vorarlberg and other Alpine regions provide the strongest concentration of mountain activities. Match all mountain activities to season, weather, snow conditions, fitness and traveler experience.', 2451),
  ('austria', 22, 'senior-travel', 'SENIOR TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'senior_suitability: 91 walking_intensity: LOW–MEDIUM for city and scenic touring MEDIUM–HIGH for Alpine trails and snow activities Rules: Austria works particularly well for seniors as a: CULTURE + SCENIC_RAIL + LAKES + ALPINE_VIEWS + DINING + WELLNESS destination.', 2452),
  ('austria', 23, 'accessibility', 'ACCESSIBILITY', NULL, NULL, 'wheelchair_accessibility: GOOD IN MANY URBAN / MODERN TOURISM ENVIRONMENTS → VARIABLE IN HISTORIC AND ALPINE AREAS public_transport_accessibility: GOOD → VERY_GOOD overall; verify specific train, station, tram, bus, cable car, and route hotel_accessibility: MUST_BE_VERIFIED_PER_HOTEL attraction_accessibility: MUST_BE_VERIFIED_PER_ATTRACTION Rule: Never assume universal accessibility from Austria''s strong overall tourism infrastructure. Additional notes:', 2453),
  ('austria', 24, 'food', 'FOOD', NULL, NULL, 'Austria is particularly strong for: Austria''s gastronomy combines Viennese cuisine, Alpine regional food, wine regions, traditional inns, coffeehouses, mountain huts, and modern fine dining. Austria''s 2026 Michelin selection includes 101 starred restaurants, reinforcing its premium culinary strength. Food experiences: Family: Prioritize schnitzel, dumplings, pasta-style dishes, breads, pastries, soups, and simple Alpine meals. Honeymoon: Choose lakefront or mountain-view dining, wine tasting, historic restaurants, coffeehouses, and fine dining. Luxury: Include Michelin-level dining, premium hotel restaurants, private wine experiences, and chef-led regional cuisine. Budget: Use bakeries, supermarkets, markets, casual Gasthäuser, Würstelstands, cafés, and lunch menus. Vienna''s Naschmarkt alone contains around 120 stalls and eateries.', 2454),
  ('austria', 25, 'shopping', 'SHOPPING', NULL, NULL, 'Strong categories: Luxury shopping: Prefer: Budget: Prefer: Travel-agent rule: Use VIENNA for PREMIUM_FASHION + JEWELLERY + LUXURY, SALZBURG / INNSBRUCK for REGIONAL_CRAFTS + TRADITIONAL_PRODUCTS, CHRISTMAS_MARKETS for SEASONAL_GIFTS, and WINE_REGIONS + LOCAL_SHOPS for FOOD_AND_WINE_PRODUCTS. Prioritize reputable sellers for jewellery, crystal, premium crafts, and higher-value purchases.', 2455),
  ('austria', 26, 'nightlife', 'NIGHTLIFE', NULL, NULL, 'nightlife_level: 84 Suitable for: Best areas: Evening activities are better suited to: Vienna has a genuine club and bar scene ranging from polished cocktail bars to electronic and underground venues, while Austria''s Alpine resorts add après-ski and mountain-evening experiences. Honeymoon travelers should generally prefer: CLASSICAL_CONCERT + FINE_DINING + WINE_OR_COCKTAIL_BAR + EVENING_WALK or: ALPINE_DINNER + SPA + RELAXED_RESORT_EVENING over: Club-heavy itineraries unless nightlife is specifically requested. Travel-agent rule: Position Austria as a **STRONG CULTURAL_EVENING + DINING + WINE + BAR + APRÈS_SKI DESTINATION**, with Vienna providing the strongest conventional nightlife.', 2456),
  ('austria', 28, 'sample-itinerary-patterns', 'SAMPLE ITINERARY PATTERNS', '3 NIGHTS', NULL, '### Day 1 Arrival at Vienna International Airport (Schwechat) → Airport express train (CAT) or private transfer to central Vienna → Hotel check-in → Relaxation and refreshment Afternoon: Historic Inner City (Innere Stadt) heritage orientation → St. Stephen''s Cathedral (Stephansdom) → Graben and Kohlmarkt historic pedestrian avenues → Imperial Hofburg Palace exterior and Heldenplatz → Historic Habsburg architecture → Continue toward Naschmarkt → Open-air market exploration → Viennese delicacies, regional cheeses, wine, international spices, and local products → Optional Karlskirche (St. Charles'' Church) exterior / nearby Baroque heritage walk Evening: Traditional Viennese dinner (Wiener Schnitzel, Tafelspitz) → Historic Ringstraße evening drive / tram loop or relaxed stroll → Classic Viennese coffeehouse experience (Café Central, Café Sacher, or Demel) → Hotel St. Stephen''s Cathedral and the Hofburg form Vienna''s principal historic and royal cluster, while Naschmarkt remains one of the city''s defining culinary-and-market experiences. ### Day 2 Morning: Breakfast → Regional Rail (ÖBB / WESTbahn) or private transfer toward the Wachau Danube Valley or Alpine foothills → Innsbruck / Tyrol Alpine corridor or Wachau Valley (Melk & Dürnstein) → Nordkette Cable Car (Innsbruck) or Wachau panoramic experience according to season and location → Alpine / Danube Valley panoramas → Mountain and valley photography → Relaxed alpine resort exploration Winter options: → Skiing and snowboarding (Tyrol / Arlberg or Semmering alpine access) → Beginner ski/snowboard lesson → Alpine tobogganing (Rodelbahn) → Winter wonderland trail walking → Snow photography → Mountain hut (Skihütte) refreshment Spring / Summer / Autumn options: → Panoramic Nordkette or Kitzsteinhorn cable car experience → Alpine walking and panoramic trail hiking according to ability → Family mountain recreation → Danube riverboat cruise (Spitz to Krems) → Alpine / vineyard outdoor cafés → Landscape photography Afternoon: Alpine / Danube riverside lunch → Continue toward Salzkammergut Lake District or Zell am See according to interest and conditions → Scenic alpine lake viewpoints (Lake Hallstatt, Lake Wolfgang, or Lake Zell) → Alpine lake panoramas → Relaxed lakeside / promenade experience → Photography Summer options: → Boat / electric solar yacht cruise on Lake Wolfgang or Lake Zell → Alpine lakeside lido / swimming → Selected water sports and paddleboarding → Lakeside resort relaxation Evening: Return to Vienna (or alpine base) → Hotel relaxation → Austrian modern / traditional alpine dinner → Optional spa / hotel thermal lounge → Hotel The Wachau Valley, Salzkammergut, and Tyrolean Alps form the strongest scenic and leisure day extensions from Vienna or regional capitals. Current Austrian National Tourist Office information highlights the Alpine lakes and mountain cable cars for year-round escapes, supported by ÖBB''s high-speed Railjet network connecting the capital directly to the mountains. ### Day 3 Morning: Breakfast → Schönbrunn Palace and Imperial Gardens (former Habsburg summer residence) → Gloriette viewpoint and maze gardens according to operating hours → Belvedere Palace (Klimt collection and Baroque gardens) → Ringstraße boulevard monumental architecture → Viennese Ringstraße Tram / walk → Explore selected imperial and Art Nouveau highlights (Secession, Otto Wagner architecture) Afternoon: Lunch → Danube Tower (Donauturm) according to current visitor access → Panoramic city and Danube river views → Prater Park and the historic Giant Ferris Wheel (Riesenrad) → Modern and leisure Vienna sightseeing → Optional MuseumsQuartier (MQ) / city culture courtyard → Relaxed art and urban photography Evening: Return toward central Vienna → Shopping time along Kärntner Straße or Goldenes Quartier → Special Viennese classical concert experience (Kursalon, Musikverein, or Opera) → Traditional Heuriger (Viennese wine tavern) dinner in Grinzing or Neustift am Walde → Evening city walk along illuminated imperial monuments → Hotel Official Austrian tourism itineraries regularly combine Schönbrunn Palace, St. Stephen''s Cathedral, Belvedere Palace, the Ringstraße, and classical music venues as core first-time Austrian experiences. Optional alternative according to traveler interest: FAMILY: → Schönbrunn Zoo (Tiergarten Schönbrunn - world''s oldest zoo) → Prater Amusement Park and Giant Ferris Wheel → Zoom Children''s Museum at MuseumsQuartier → Haus des Meeres (Aqua Terra Zoo) → Easy Naschmarkt / Prater park stroll HONEYMOON: → Schönbrunn Grand Carriage & Gardens stroll → Salzkammergut / Hallstatt scenic lake day → Private vineyard wine tasting in Wachau or Vienna Heurigen → Luxury hotel spa / thermal bath retreat → Vienna State Opera or Musikverein classical evening → Candlelight dinner with city views (Das Loft or Danube Tower) ADVENTURE: → Tyrolean Alps hiking or via ferrata → Salzkammergut mountain biking or caving → Arlberg / Innsbruck winter sports → Danube Canal water sports / kayaking CULTURE / HISTORY: → Imperial Hofburg Palace (Sisi Museum, Imperial Apartments) → Kunsthistorisches Museum (Art History Museum) → Belvedere Palace (Gustav Klimt''s "The Kiss") → St. Stephen''s Catacombs & Tower climb → Mozarthaus or House of Music (Haus der Musik) FOOD: → Naschmarkt and Brunnenmarkt tasting tours → Traditional Viennese Schnitzel and Tafelspitz dining → Historic Coffeehouse crawling (Demel, Sacher, Central) → Vienna Heuriger wine tavern experience → New Austrian Michelin-starred dining (Steirereck, Amador) MOUNTAIN / NATURE: → Full-day Semmering / Rax / Wachau Valley circuit from Vienna → Tyrol / Innsbruck Nordkette alpine excursion → Salzkammergut lakes & Hallstatt photography → Seasonal alpine outdoor recreation Official Austrian National Tourist Office material positions Austria''s mountain and lake regions as major year-round extensions to the imperial capital, with high-speed Railjet trains supporting seamless access for both active alpine adventures and cultural city breaks. ### Day 4 Breakfast → Leisure morning → Optional Naschmarkt or Old Town revisit → Local Austrian products / Mozartkugeln, Manner wafers, and wine shopping → Optional Viennese coffeehouse or Museum quarter café time → Hotel checkout → Airport express train / private transfer to Vienna International Airport → Departure', 2457),
  ('austria', 29, 'six-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 1', NULL, 'Arrival at Vienna Airport → Private transfer to hotel → Romantic hotel check-in → Relax and refresh Evening: → Vienna historic centre → Elegant city streets → Romantic Austrian dinner → Optional café / evening walk → Overnight at Vienna', 2458),
  ('austria', 29, 'six-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 2', NULL, 'Breakfast at the hotel Morning: → Guided Vienna sightseeing → Ringstrasse → Hofburg area → Historic centre → St. Stephen''s Cathedral Afternoon: → Schönbrunn Palace → Palace gardens → Couple photography → Free café / shopping time Evening: → Rathaus / central Vienna → Romantic dinner → Optional classical concert → Overnight at Vienna', 2459),
  ('austria', 29, 'six-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 3', NULL, 'Breakfast → Hotel checkout → Scenic journey toward Slovenia Stop at Maribor: → Historic centre → Cathedral area → Riverside / Old Town walk Continue to Zagreb → Romantic hotel check-in Evening: → Zagreb Upper Town → Historic streets → Relaxed couple walk → Dinner → Overnight at Zagreb', 2460),
  ('austria', 29, 'six-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 4', NULL, 'Breakfast → Scenic journey into Bosnia and Herzegovina En route: → Jajce historic town → Fortress area → Jajce Waterfall → Couple photography Continue to Sarajevo Evening: → Baščaršija → Ottoman Old Town atmosphere → Traditional dinner → Overnight at Sarajevo', 2461),
  ('austria', 29, 'six-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 5', NULL, 'Breakfast → Sarajevo sightseeing → Baščaršija → Historic religious and Ottoman heritage Continue to Mostar: → UNESCO Old Bridge area → Historic Old Town → Riverside views → Couple photography → Leisure lunch Continue to Dubrovnik → Hotel check-in → Romantic dinner → Overnight at Dubrovnik', 2462),
  ('austria', 29, 'six-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 6', NULL, 'Breakfast Morning: → Dubrovnik Old Town → Historic city walls area → Stradun → Cathedral → Franciscan Monastery Afternoon: → Boat excursion to Lokrum where seasonally operating → Adriatic views → Relaxed couple time Evening: → Dubrovnik sunset → Romantic farewell dinner → Optional waterfront walk → Overnight at Dubrovnik', 2463),
  ('austria', 29, 'six-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 7', NULL, 'Breakfast → Leisure morning according to flight / onward schedule → Hotel checkout → Airport transfer → Departure', 2464),
  ('austria', 30, 'six-nights-family-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 1', NULL, 'Arrival at Vienna Airport → Transfer to hotel → Family hotel check-in → Relax and refresh Evening: → Easy Vienna city-centre walk → Historic streets → Family-friendly Austrian / international dinner → Overnight at Vienna', 2465),
  ('austria', 30, 'six-nights-family-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 2', NULL, 'Breakfast at the hotel Morning: → Vienna sightseeing → Ringstrasse → Hofburg area → St. Stephen''s Cathedral → Historic centre Afternoon: → Schönbrunn Palace → Palace gardens → Family photography → Optional Schönbrunn Zoo according to family interest Evening: → Rathaus / central Vienna → Dinner → Overnight at Vienna', 2466),
  ('austria', 30, 'six-nights-family-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 3', NULL, 'Breakfast → Hotel checkout → Scenic journey toward Slovenia Stop at Maribor: → Historic centre → Cathedral area → Short family walk Continue to Zagreb → Hotel check-in Evening: → Zagreb Upper Town → Historic streets → Relaxed family exploration → Dinner → Overnight at Zagreb', 2467),
  ('austria', 30, 'six-nights-family-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 4', NULL, 'Breakfast → Journey into Bosnia and Herzegovina En route: → Jajce → Historic centre → Fortress views → Jajce Waterfall → Family photography Continue to Sarajevo Evening: → Baščaršija → Old Town walk → Traditional dinner → Overnight at Sarajevo', 2468),
  ('austria', 30, 'six-nights-family-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 5', NULL, 'Breakfast → Sarajevo orientation → Baščaršija → Historic and cultural landmarks Continue to Mostar: → Old Bridge → Historic Old Town → Riverside scenery → Family lunch / leisure Continue to Dubrovnik → Hotel check-in → Dinner → Overnight at Dubrovnik', 2469),
  ('austria', 30, 'six-nights-family-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 6', NULL, 'Breakfast Morning: → Dubrovnik Old Town → Stradun → Cathedral → Franciscan Monastery → Historic city-wall surroundings Afternoon: → Optional Lokrum boat excursion where seasonally operating → Family leisure → Adriatic scenery Evening: → Relaxed waterfront walk → Farewell family dinner → Overnight at Dubrovnik', 2470),
  ('austria', 30, 'six-nights-family-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 7', NULL, 'Breakfast → Leisure morning according to departure schedule → Hotel checkout → Airport transfer → Departure', 2471),
  ('austria', 31, 'six-nights-luxury-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 1', NULL, 'Arrival at Vienna Airport → VIP meet and assist → Chauffeured private transfer → Luxury hotel / suite check-in → Welcome amenities → Relax and refresh Evening: → Private Vienna orientation → Historic centre → Premium Austrian dinner → Optional hotel lounge / cocktail bar → Overnight at Vienna', 2472),
  ('austria', 31, 'six-nights-luxury-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 2', NULL, 'Breakfast at the hotel Morning: → Private guided Vienna sightseeing → Ringstrasse → Hofburg area → St. Stephen''s Cathedral → Historic centre Afternoon: → Premium Schönbrunn Palace experience → Palace gardens → Private photography → Luxury café / shopping time Evening: → Fine dining → Optional classical concert / opera → Overnight at Vienna', 2473),
  ('austria', 31, 'six-nights-luxury-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 3', NULL, 'Breakfast → Hotel checkout → Private chauffeured journey toward Slovenia Stop at Maribor: → Historic centre → Cathedral area → Relaxed private walk / lunch Continue to Zagreb → Luxury hotel check-in Evening: → Private Upper Town orientation → Premium Croatian dinner → Overnight at Zagreb', 2474),
  ('austria', 31, 'six-nights-luxury-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 4', NULL, 'Breakfast → Chauffeured journey into Bosnia and Herzegovina En route: → Jajce historic centre → Jajce Waterfall → Flexible photography stops Continue to Sarajevo → Premium hotel check-in Evening: → Private Baščaršija experience → Curated Bosnian dinner → Hotel lounge / relaxation → Overnight at Sarajevo', 2475),
  ('austria', 31, 'six-nights-luxury-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 5', NULL, 'Breakfast → Private Sarajevo heritage tour → Baščaršija → Selected cultural landmarks Continue to Mostar: → Private Old Town walk → Old Bridge → Riverside views → Premium lunch Continue to Dubrovnik → Luxury Adriatic hotel check-in Evening: → Fine dining → Sea-view relaxation → Overnight at Dubrovnik', 2476),
  ('austria', 31, 'six-nights-luxury-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 6', NULL, 'Breakfast Morning: → Private guided Dubrovnik Old Town experience → Stradun → Historic walls area → Cathedral → Franciscan Monastery Afternoon: → Private / premium boat experience according to season → Lokrum or Adriatic coastal cruising → Free spa / resort time Evening: → Sunset experience → Farewell fine-dining dinner → Optional premium lounge → Overnight at Dubrovnik', 2477),
  ('austria', 31, 'six-nights-luxury-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 7', NULL, 'Breakfast → Leisure morning → Optional spa / private shopping → Hotel checkout → Chauffeured airport transfer → Departure', 2478),
  ('austria', 32, 'travel-agent-insights', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS', 'What inexperienced planners often do wrong', NULL, '', 2479),
  ('austria', 32, 'travel-agent-insights', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS', 'What an experienced planner does differently', NULL, 'VIENNA + SALZBURG + SALZKAMMERGUT / HALLSTATT + INNSBRUCK / ONE_ALPINE_REGION rather than maximum destination count.', 2480),
  ('austria', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', NULL, NULL, 'IF: trip_length <= 4 nights THEN: prioritize_VIENNA + SALZBURG_OR_ONE_NEARBY_EXCURSION Reason: Short stays work better with one or two strong bases than multiple Alpine transfers. IF: trip_length >= 7 nights AND: traveler_interest == FIRST_TIME_AUSTRIA THEN: prioritize_VIENNA + SALZBURG + ONE_ALPINE_OR_LAKE_REGION Reason: This provides Austria''s strongest balance of imperial culture, historic cities, lakes, and mountains. IF: trip_type == HONEYMOON THEN: prefer_VIENNA + SALZBURG + HALLSTATT_SALZKAMMERGUT_OR_ALPINE_RESORT AND: increase_FREE_TIME + SPA + SCENIC_DINING Reason: Austria''s romantic strength comes from historic cities, lakes, Alpine scenery, wellness, and relaxed dining. IF: traveler_type == FAMILY THEN: prefer_SCHONBRUNN + PRATER + SALZBURG + LAKES + EASY_CABLE_CARS + FAMILY_SKI_AREAS AND: reduce_LONG_MUSEUM_AND_HIKING_DAYS Reason: Austria has extensive family-oriented skiing, mountain, lake, and cultural experiences. IF: traveler_type == LUXURY THEN: prefer_5_STAR_HOTEL + FIRST_CLASS_RAIL + PRIVATE_DRIVER + FINE_DINING + SPA + PRIVATE_GUIDE Reason: Luxury should improve comfort, privacy, dining, wellness, and flexibility rather than increase attraction count. IF: traveler_type == BUDGET THEN: prefer_PUBLIC_TRANSPORT + REGIONAL_RAIL + WELL_CONNECTED_HOTEL + FREE_CITY_AND_NATURE_EXPERIENCES Reason: Transport planning and hotel location are the main ways to control Austrian travel costs. IF: traveler_interest == CULTURE_AND_HERITAGE THEN: prioritize_VIENNA + SALZBURG + WACHAU + GRAZ AND: include_PALACES + MUSEUMS + CLASSICAL_MUSIC + HISTORIC_CENTRES IF: traveler_interest == MOUNTAINS_AND_NATURE THEN: prefer_INNSBRUCK_TIROL + SALZKAMMERGUT + ZELL_AM_SEE_KAPRUN + HOHE_TAUERN AND: verify_WEATHER + LIFT_OPERATIONS + TRAIL_CONDITIONS IF: traveler_interest == SKIING_AND_WINTER_SPORTS THEN: prefer_TIROL + KITZBUHEL + ARLBERG + ZELL_AM_SEE_KAPRUN_OR_GASTEIN AND: verify_SNOW + LIFTS + EQUIPMENT + SKI_LEVEL Reason: Austria''s ski regions include strong beginner, family, and advanced products. IF: traveler_interest == WELLNESS_AND_RELAXATION THEN: prefer_GASTEIN + OTZTAL + ZELL_AM_SEE_KAPRUN + THERMAL_SPA_REGIONS AND: reduce_ACTIVITY_DENSITY Reason: Austria strongly combines Alpine holidays with thermal spas and wellness. IF: traveler_interest == FOOD_AND_GASTRONOMY THEN: prefer_VIENNA + SALZBURG + STYRIA + WACHAU AND: include_COFFEEHOUSES + REGIONAL_CUISINE + WINE + ALPINE_DINING IF: traveler_interest == PHOTOGRAPHY THEN: prefer_HALLSTATT + SALZKAMMERGUT + INNSBRUCK + HOHE_TAUERN + VIENNA AND: prioritize_EARLY_MORNING + SUNSET IF: trip_length <= 7 nights THEN: prefer_MAXIMUM_TWO_OR_THREE_BASES AND: avoid_EXCESSIVE_HOTEL_CHANGES IF: traveler_type == SENIOR OR: traveler_mobility == LIMITED THEN: prefer_RAIL + CITY_CULTURE + LAKES + EASY_CABLE_CARS + SPA AND: reduce_STEEP_HIKING + SNOW_INTENSITY IF: traveler_uses_WHEELCHAIR THEN: prefer_VERIFIED_ACCESSIBLE_HOTELS + TRANSPORT + ATTRACTIONS AND: do_not_assume_HISTORIC_BUILDINGS + ALPINE_TRAILS + SKI_AREAS_ARE_STEP_FREE Reason: Austria offers many accessible tourism experiences, but conditions vary by attraction and mountain environment IF: weather == POOR_MOUNTAIN_VISIBILITY THEN: reduce_HIGH_ALPINE_EXCURSIONS AND: increase_MUSEUMS + PALACES + FOOD + SPA + CITY_TIME IF: traveler_interest == FIRST_TIME_AUSTRIA THEN: prioritize_VIENNA + SALZBURG AND: add_ONE_OF_HALLSTATT_SALZKAMMERGUT_OR_INNSBRUCK_TIROL according to trip length IF: traveler_interest == CULTURE_AND_RELAXATION_BALANCE THEN: allocate_60_TO_70_PERCENT_TO_CORE_SIGHTSEEING AND: allocate_REMAINING_TIME_TO_FOOD + SPA + LAKES + CAFÉS + FREE_TIME', 2481),
  ('austria', 34, 'destination-scoring', 'DESTINATION SCORING', NULL, NULL, '| Factor | Score | | ------------------ | ----: | | Family | 94 | | Honeymoon | 93 | | Luxury | 92 | | Budget | 72 | | Adventure | 94 | | Culture | 96 | | Food | 91 | | Shopping | 87 | | Nightlife | 84 | | Relaxation | 95 | | Nature | 96 | | Accessibility | 88 | | Safety | 93 | | First-time visitor | 95 | | Photography | 96 |', 2482),
  ('austria', 35, 'final-travel-agent-verdict', 'FINAL TRAVEL AGENT VERDICT', NULL, NULL, 'Best traveler profiles: 1. Culture / heritage traveler 2. Nature / mountain traveler 3. Honeymoon / romantic traveler 4. Family traveler 5. Photography traveler 6. Ski / winter-sports traveler 7. Adventure / hiking traveler 8. Wellness / relaxation traveler 9. First-time Europe traveler 10. Luxury / gastronomy traveler Best duration: 7–10 nights 4–5 nights: Vienna + Salzburg or one focused city-and-region combination. 7–10 nights: Best for Vienna + Salzburg + Salzkammergut / Hallstatt + Innsbruck / one Alpine region. 11–14 nights: Excellent for adding Wachau, Graz / Styria, Zell am See-Kaprun, Hohe Tauern, Carinthia, or deeper Tirol exploration. Best season: YEAR-ROUND Spring: Cities + culture + gardens + food + lower-altitude nature. Summer: HIKING + LAKES + CYCLING + ALPS + FAMILY + OUTDOORS. Autumn: PHOTOGRAPHY + WINE + FOOD + HIKING + CULTURE + BETTER_VALUE. Winter: SKIING + SNOW + CHRISTMAS_MARKETS + SPA + ALPINE_RESORTS. Austria Tourism specifically positions summer for lakes and hiking, winter for skiing, and spring / autumn for culture and culinary travel. Best hotel strategy: Choose hotels according to rail access and trip purpose. For first-time visitors: VIENNA + SALZBURG + ONE_ALPINE_OR_LAKE_BASE. For honeymoon / luxury: Prefer lake-view, Alpine, spa, historic, or premium city hotels. Avoid unnecessary one-night hotel changes. Best transportation: Use: Austria does not require a rental car for a standard first-time itinerary; Vienna–Salzburg services run frequently and Vienna–Innsbruck has direct Railjet connections. Must-do for first-time visitor: Don''t-do: Biggest advantage: Austria combines exceptional imperial culture with Alpine scenery in a compact, highly connected country. Vienna, Salzburg, Innsbruck, lakes, ski regions, national parks, wine regions, spas, and excellent rail connections allow very different travel styles within one itinerary. Austria has six national parks and 47 nature parks, while roughly 63% of the country is high-Alpine terrain. Biggest disadvantage: Popular destinations and Alpine resorts can become expensive and crowded during summer, Christmas, and ski periods. Mountain weather, seasonal lift operations, snow conditions, and the distance between some Alpine regions can also complicate overpacked itineraries. Overall destination score: 93/100', 2483),
  ('austria', 36, 'data-quality', 'DATA QUALITY', NULL, NULL, 'information_completeness: 96/100 last_updated: 2026-08-27 last_verified: PARTIALLY_WEB_VERIFIED verified_by: AUSTRIA TOURISM / ÖBB / OFFICIAL AUSTRIAN REGIONAL, TRANSPORT, CULTURAL AND ACCESSIBILITY SOURCES sources: IMPORTANT: Prices, rail fares, attraction tickets, hotel rates, cable-car schedules, ski passes, lift operations, hiking access, lake services, and accessibility must NOT be treated as permanently valid. Mountain weather, snowfall, visibility, maintenance, and seasonal operations should be checked shortly before travel. Rail accessibility is strong overall, but station and train details should be verified connection by connection; ÖBB provides dedicated mobility assistance and wheelchair-capable long-distance services. Historic centres, castles, Alpine trails, snow surfaces, and older properties should not be assumed fully step-free. Austria should primarily be treated as: SPRING: CULTURE + CITIES + GARDENS + FOOD + SCENIC_TRAVEL SUMMER: ALPS + LAKES + HIKING + CYCLING + FAMILY + NATURE AUTUMN: PHOTOGRAPHY + FOOD + WINE + CULTURE + HIKING WINTER: SKIING + SNOW + CHRISTMAS + SPA + ALPINE_RESORTS Austria Tourism, ÖBB, regional tourism boards, mountain-lift operators, ski resorts, hotels, and individual attractions should be treated as primary sources for current operational information. This dataset should be refreshed regularly before production use.', 2484),
  ('netherlands', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Spring', NULL, 'months: March April May weather: Cool and changeable in March, becoming milder through April and May. Rain and wind remain possible, but daylight increases and the countryside becomes especially colourful. crowd_level: MEDIUM → HIGH price_level: MEDIUM → HIGH overall_score: 66–74 recommended: true reason: Spring is one of the Netherlands'' signature travel seasons for tulips, Keukenhof, cycling, canals, historic cities, parks, photography, and King''s Day. Flower season broadly runs from March to May, with tulips usually strongest around mid-April.', 2485),
  ('netherlands', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Summer', NULL, 'months: June July August weather: Generally mild to warm with long daylight, but rain and cooler periods remain possible because of the temperate maritime climate. crowd_level: HIGH → VERY_HIGH price_level: HIGH → VERY_HIGH overall_score: 61–68 recommended: true reason: Best for: July and August have excellent outdoor conditions but weaker Crowd and Price scores because they overlap with the main European holiday season.', 2486),
  ('netherlands', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Autumn', NULL, 'months: September October November weather: September is generally mild, while October and November become cooler, wetter, windier, and progressively darker. crowd_level: MEDIUM → LOW price_level: MEDIUM → LOW overall_score: 73–80 recommended: true reason: September and October are excellent for cities, museums, cycling, forests, dunes, historic towns, photography, and quieter travel. November has weaker weather but very low visitor pressure and better value for museums, cafés, architecture, shopping, and city breaks.', 2487),
  ('netherlands', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Winter', NULL, 'months: December January February weather: Cool, damp, windy, and often cloudy. Snow and prolonged freezing conditions are possible but not reliable. crowd_level: LOW → MEDIUM price_level: LOW → MEDIUM overall_score: 66–79 recommended: true reason: Strong for museums, historic cities, cafés, light festivals, winter photography, shopping, and relaxed cultural travel. December receives stronger festive demand, while January and February are generally quieter. Natural canal skating should never be assumed because sufficiently cold conditions are not guaranteed.', 2488),
  ('netherlands', 10, 'budget-strategy', 'BUDGET STRATEGY', NULL, NULL, 'Where money can be saved: Where saving money is usually NOT recommended: Travel-agent rule: In the Netherlands, **HOTEL_LOCATION + PUBLIC_TRANSPORT + ATTRACTION_COST + SEASON should be evaluated together**. For short stays, prioritize **AMSTERDAM + ONE_OR_TWO_NEARBY_EXPERIENCES**. For longer stays, combine **AMSTERDAM + ROTTERDAM / THE_HAGUE / UTRECHT + ONE_COAST_OR_COUNTRYSIDE_REGION** rather than changing hotels excessively.', 2489),
  ('netherlands', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Family', 'family', 'Use the direct train from Amsterdam Airport Schiphol where practical; otherwise use a pre-booked taxi / private transfer for young children, heavy luggage, or direct hotel access. Schiphol has a railway station directly beneath the terminal with direct connections to Amsterdam, Utrecht, The Hague, Rotterdam, Leiden, Delft, and other cities.', 2490),
  ('netherlands', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Honeymoon', 'honeymoon', 'Prefer first-class rail or a comfortable private transfer according to luggage and hotel location. For couples continuing beyond Amsterdam, direct rail makes Utrecht, Rotterdam, The Hague, Delft, and other cities easy to combine without immediately renting a car.', 2491),
  ('netherlands', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Luxury', 'luxury', 'Use chauffeured premium sedan / MPV or first-class rail with private local transfers. For multi-city luxury itineraries, combine FIRST_CLASS_RAIL + PRIVATE_TRANSFER + PREMIUM_CITY_EXPERIENCES.', 2492),
  ('netherlands', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Budget', 'budget', 'Use airport rail and regular public transport. Schiphol–Amsterdam Centraal is approximately 17 minutes by train, with frequent services.', 2493),
  ('netherlands', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Senior', 'senior', 'Prefer direct rail where luggage and mobility permit; otherwise use a private transfer. Choose hotels near major stations or tram / metro corridors and minimize unnecessary connections.', 2494),
  ('netherlands', 18, 'family-travel', 'FAMILY TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'child_friendly_score: 94 best_ages: Rules: For young children: Prefer: Avoid: The Netherlands'' compact geography, public transport, beaches, national parks and family attractions make it especially easy to plan for children.', 2495),
  ('netherlands', 19, 'honeymoon-travel', 'HONEYMOON TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'honeymoon_score: 88 romance_score: 90 privacy_score: 85 luxury_score: 88 Recommended: Honeymoon itineraries should generally stay at: 2–3 major experiences/day. Prefer: CANALS + HISTORIC_TOWNS + COUNTRYSIDE + DINING + FREE_TIME over: Constant museum visits and city changes. Recommended areas:', 2496),
  ('netherlands', 20, 'luxury-travel', 'LUXURY TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'luxury_score: 88 Recommended: Netherlands luxury travel should focus on: Luxury value is strongest in Amsterdam and selected heritage / coastal destinations rather than resort-style luxury.', 2497),
  ('netherlands', 21, 'adventure', 'ADVENTURE', NULL, NULL, 'adventure_score: 79 The Netherlands is a strong active-travel destination, but not a mountain-adventure destination. Adventure experiences: The country has more than 32,000 km of cycling paths, while its lakes, rivers and North Sea coast support sailing, windsurfing, canoeing and kitesurfing. Match water and coastal activities to weather, wind, tides, ability and operator guidance.', 2498),
  ('netherlands', 22, 'senior-travel', 'SENIOR TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'senior_suitability: 92 walking_intensity: LOW–MEDIUM with public-transport and cruise-focused planning MEDIUM for cycling, dunes and longer historic-city walks Rules: Dutch public transport is progressively adapted for travelers with disabilities, and many museums, trains, buses and other visitor facilities provide accessible options, though historic centres remain variable. The Netherlands works particularly well for seniors as a: CULTURE + CANALS + MUSEUMS + RAIL + COAST + RELAXED_CITY_TRAVEL destination.', 2499),
  ('netherlands', 23, 'accessibility', 'ACCESSIBILITY', NULL, NULL, 'wheelchair_accessibility: GOOD IN MANY URBAN / MODERN TOURISM ENVIRONMENTS → VARIABLE IN HISTORIC, BEACH AND NATURE AREAS public_transport_accessibility: GOOD → VERY_GOOD overall; verify specific train, station, tram, bus, metro, ferry, and route hotel_accessibility: MUST_BE_VERIFIED_PER_HOTEL attraction_accessibility: MUST_BE_VERIFIED_PER_ATTRACTION Rule: Never assume universal accessibility from the Netherlands'' strong transport infrastructure. Additional notes:', 2500),
  ('netherlands', 24, 'food', 'FOOD', NULL, NULL, 'The Netherlands is particularly strong for: Dutch gastronomy combines traditional comfort food, North Sea seafood, cheese, colonial and international influences, markets, cafés, and increasingly creative modern cuisine. Food experiences: Family: Prioritize pancakes, fries, poffertjes, cheese, bakery items, and family-friendly cafés. Honeymoon: Choose canal-side dining, waterfront restaurants, fine dining, cocktails, and relaxed café experiences. Luxury: Include premium restaurants, private dining, chef-led experiences, and high-end hotel dining. Budget: Use bakeries, supermarkets, markets, snack bars, food halls, and casual cafés. Albert Cuyp Market is particularly useful for traditional snacks such as herring.', 2501),
  ('netherlands', 25, 'shopping', 'SHOPPING', NULL, NULL, 'Strong categories: Luxury shopping: Prefer: Amsterdam''s P.C. Hooftstraat and Oud-Zuid contain the country''s strongest concentration of international luxury fashion and jewellery. Budget: Prefer: The Nine Streets are especially strong for boutiques, vintage, jewellery, speciality shops, cafés, and local design. Travel-agent rule: Use AMSTERDAM_OUD_ZUID for LUXURY, NINE_STREETS for BOUTIQUES + DUTCH_DESIGN, MARKETS for VINTAGE + LOCAL_PRODUCTS, and DELFT / REGIONAL_SHOPS for CERAMICS + TRADITIONAL_GIFTS.', 2502),
  ('netherlands', 26, 'nightlife', 'NIGHTLIFE', NULL, NULL, 'nightlife_level: 90 Suitable for: Best areas: Evening activities are better suited to: Amsterdam has one of Europe''s strongest nightlife ecosystems, ranging from techno and electronic clubs to live music, jazz, cabaret, rooftop venues, and relaxed bars. Honeymoon travelers should generally prefer: CANAL_CRUISE + FINE_DINING + COCKTAIL_BAR + EVENING_WALK over: Club-heavy itineraries unless nightlife is specifically requested. Travel-agent rule: Position the Netherlands as a **STRONG CITY_NIGHTLIFE + ELECTRONIC_MUSIC + LIVE_MUSIC + BAR + DINING DESTINATION**, with Amsterdam providing the strongest nightlife concentration.', 2503),
  ('netherlands', 28, 'sample-itinerary-patterns', 'SAMPLE ITINERARY PATTERNS', '3 NIGHTS', NULL, '### Day 1 Arrival at Amsterdam Airport Schiphol → Direct train / private transfer to central Amsterdam → Hotel check-in → Relaxation and refreshment Afternoon: Amsterdam canal-ring orientation → Rijksmuseum exterior / Museumplein → Van Gogh Museum area → Historic canal houses and bridges → Continue toward Dam Square → Royal Palace exterior → Nieuwe Kerk area → Optional Anne Frank House exterior / Jordaan neighbourhood walk Evening: Traditional Dutch / contemporary dinner → Central Amsterdam evening canal walk → Optional brown café or relaxed city experience → Hotel The Museumplein and Rijksmuseum form one of Amsterdam''s principal cultural clusters, while the canal ring remains one of the city''s defining UNESCO heritage experiences. ### Day 2 Morning: Breakfast → Train toward Amsterdam Region countryside / heritage area → Zaanse Schans / Zaan Region → Historic windmill cluster → Traditional Dutch crafts and houses → Water-management heritage → Relaxed village exploration Winter options: → Indoor museum visits → Windmill photography in low-season light → Short countryside walks → Traditional craft demonstrations → Winter village atmosphere → Café culture Spring / Summer / Autumn options: → Windmill visits where open → Cycling through polder landscapes → Cheese / clog / craft experiences → Family recreation → Outdoor activities → Canal boat experience → Landscape and heritage photography Afternoon: Village lunch → Continue toward Haarlem / Amsterdam countryside according to interest and conditions → Scenic polder and waterway viewpoints → Continue toward North Sea coast / IJmuiden / Zandvoort → Coastal panoramas → Relaxed beach / dune / viewpoint experience → Photography Summer options: → Beach walk / dune exploration → Selected water recreation → Beach cafés → Resort relaxation Evening: Return to Amsterdam → Hotel relaxation → Dutch / contemporary dinner → Optional canal cruise / lounge → Hotel Zaanse Schans, Haarlem, Zandvoort, and the Dutch coast form the strongest countryside-and-leisure extension from Amsterdam. Current Netherlands tourism material highlights Zaanse Schans and the coast for classic Dutch heritage and summer beach escapes, while efficient rail connects the Amsterdam metropolitan region through Haarlem, Zandvoort, and the Zaan area. ### Day 3 Morning: Breakfast → Dam Square area → Royal Palace exterior according to visiting hours → New Church (Nieuwe Kerk) area → Central Amsterdam architecture → Amsterdam Metro / tram experience → Explore selected city corridors and canals Afternoon: Lunch → A''DAM Lookout / panoramic city views according to current visitor access → Optional canal cruise → Modern Amsterdam sightseeing → Optional Oosterpark / city leisure area → Relaxed photography Evening: Return toward central Amsterdam → Shopping / café time → Special Dutch / international dinner → Optional nightlife / lounge / evening canal walk → Hotel Official tourism itineraries regularly combine Dam Square, Museumplein, the canal ring, A''DAM Lookout, and a canal cruise as core first-time Amsterdam experiences. Optional alternative according to traveler interest: FAMILY: → Zaanse Schans family recreation → NEMO Science Museum / family attractions → Amsterdam City Park / family leisure → Optional Vondelpark / playgrounds → Easy canal cruise experience HONEYMOON: → Private canal cruise → Boutique canal-side hotel → Private countryside lunch → Spa / wellness → A''DAM Lookout evening panorama → Premium Dutch / international dinner ADVENTURE: → Dutch coast cycling → Dune and beach exploration → Sailing / water sports according to season → Seasonal outdoor activities according to weather and ability CULTURE / HISTORY: → Rijksmuseum deeper exploration → Van Gogh Museum → Anne Frank heritage → Historic canal ring → Selected museums and Dutch heritage FOOD: → Albert Cuyp Market food exploration → Traditional Dutch snacks / cheese / herring → Indonesian rijsttafel experience → Dutch pancakes / stroopwafels / bitterballen tasting → Modern Dutch dining MOUNTAIN / NATURE: → Full-day Zaanse Schans + Haarlem / Zandvoort + Dutch coast circuit → Polder and coastal photography → Waterway and dune views → Seasonal outdoor recreation Official Netherlands tourism material currently positions the Amsterdam Region''s countryside and coast as major year-round extensions to the capital, with Zaanse Schans supporting family and heritage recreation and the Dutch coast offering substantial summer beach and water-based leisure. ### Day 4 Breakfast → Leisure morning → Optional canal cruise revisit / Nine Streets shopping → Local products / souvenir shopping → Optional tram / metro or café experience → Hotel checkout → Train / private transfer to Amsterdam Airport Schiphol → Departure', 2504),
  ('netherlands', 29, 'seven-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'SEVEN-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 1', NULL, 'Arrival at Amsterdam / transfer from Brussels → Romantic hotel check-in → Relax and refresh Evening: → Amsterdam Canal Ring → Dam Square → Jordaan → Romantic canal-side dinner → Overnight at Amsterdam Amsterdam''s UNESCO canal landscape, historic streets and waterfront atmosphere make it the principal Netherlands honeymoon base.', 2505),
  ('netherlands', 29, 'seven-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'SEVEN-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 2', NULL, 'Breakfast at the hotel Morning: → Amsterdam city sightseeing → Rijksmuseum / Museum Quarter → Dam Square → Historic canal streets Seasonal option: → Keukenhof during spring opening season OR → Zaanse Schans → Windmills → Cheese / traditional Dutch experience Evening: → Romantic canal cruise → Couple photography → Special dinner → Overnight at Amsterdam Canal cruises are one of Amsterdam''s signature experiences. Keukenhof is seasonal; its confirmed 2027 opening is 18 March–9 May.', 2506),
  ('netherlands', 29, 'seven-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'SEVEN-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 3', NULL, 'Breakfast → Hotel checkout → Journey toward Germany Cologne: → Cologne Cathedral → Old Town / Rhine waterfront → Couple photography Continue to Frankfurt → Hotel check-in → Relaxed dinner → Overnight at Frankfurt', 2507),
  ('netherlands', 29, 'seven-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'SEVEN-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 4', NULL, 'Breakfast → Hotel checkout → Scenic Black Forest journey → Traditional villages / cuckoo-clock experience → Countryside photography Continue toward Switzerland → Rhine Falls → Waterfall viewpoints → Optional boat experience according to operation Evening: → Continue to Zurich → Romantic hotel check-in → Overnight at Zurich', 2508),
  ('netherlands', 29, 'seven-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'SEVEN-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 5', NULL, 'Breakfast → Excursion toward Grindelwald & Interlaken Choose ONE: JUNGFRAUJOCH: → Mountain railway → Snow / glacier scenery → Couple photography OR ROMANTIC_JUNGFRAU_REGION: → Grindelwald → Interlaken → Alpine cafés → Scenic walks → Relaxed couple time Evening: → Return to Zurich → Romantic dinner → Overnight at Zurich', 2509),
  ('netherlands', 29, 'seven-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'SEVEN-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 6', NULL, 'Breakfast → Mt. Titlis excursion → TITLIS Rotair → Snow / glacier experience → Cliff Walk / Ice Flyer where operating Later: → Lucerne → Chapel Bridge → Old Town → Lakefront walk → Couple photography Evening: → Return to Zurich → Overnight at Zurich', 2510),
  ('netherlands', 29, 'seven-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'SEVEN-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 7', NULL, 'Breakfast → Hotel checkout → Scenic journey via Vaduz Continue toward Austria: → Swarovski Crystal Worlds, Wattens → Innsbruck Old Town → Golden Roof → Alpine city views Evening: → Romantic Austrian dinner → Overnight at Innsbruck', 2511),
  ('netherlands', 29, 'seven-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'SEVEN-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 8', NULL, 'Breakfast → Leisure morning → Optional Innsbruck Old Town walk → Souvenir / couple shopping → Hotel checkout → Airport / onward transfer → Departure Travel-agent honeymoon rule: For this 7-night route, prioritize: AMSTERDAM_CANALS + ONE_DUTCH_SIGNATURE_EXPERIENCE + GERMANY_COLOGNE + BLACK_FOREST + SWISS_ALPINE_EXPERIENCES + INNSBRUCK Keep AMSTERDAM as the principal Netherlands experience and avoid adding too many Dutch cities, as the itinerary already covers multiple countries.', 2512),
  ('netherlands', 30, 'seven-nights-family-pattern', 'SEVEN-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 1', NULL, 'Arrival at Amsterdam / transfer from Brussels → Hotel check-in → Relax and refresh Evening: → Dam Square → Amsterdam Canal Ring → Easy family walk → Family dinner → Overnight at Amsterdam', 2513),
  ('netherlands', 30, 'seven-nights-family-pattern', 'SEVEN-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 2', NULL, 'Breakfast at the hotel Morning: → Amsterdam city sightseeing → Canal areas → Museum Quarter / selected family attraction Choose ONE: SPRING: → Keukenhof → Tulip gardens → Family photography OR YEAR-ROUND: → Zaanse Schans → Windmills → Cheese experience → Traditional Dutch atmosphere Evening: → Family canal cruise → Relaxed dinner → Overnight at Amsterdam', 2514),
  ('netherlands', 30, 'seven-nights-family-pattern', 'SEVEN-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 3', NULL, 'Breakfast → Hotel checkout → Continue toward Germany Cologne: → Cologne Cathedral → Old Town → Rhine waterfront → Family sightseeing Continue to Frankfurt → Hotel check-in → Dinner → Overnight at Frankfurt', 2515),
  ('netherlands', 30, 'seven-nights-family-pattern', 'SEVEN-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 4', NULL, 'Breakfast → Black Forest scenic journey → Forest landscapes → Traditional villages → Cuckoo-clock experience Continue toward Switzerland: → Rhine Falls → Waterfall viewpoints → Optional boat ride where operating Evening: → Continue to Zurich → Hotel check-in → Overnight at Zurich', 2516),
  ('netherlands', 30, 'seven-nights-family-pattern', 'SEVEN-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 5', NULL, 'Breakfast → Grindelwald & Interlaken excursion Choose ONE: JUNGFRAUJOCH: → Mountain railway → Snow and glacier experience → Family photography OR RELAXED_FAMILY_OPTION: → Grindelwald → Interlaken → Easy village walks → Cafés → Alpine scenery Evening: → Return to Zurich → Family dinner → Overnight at Zurich', 2517),
  ('netherlands', 30, 'seven-nights-family-pattern', 'SEVEN-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 6', NULL, 'Breakfast → Mt. Titlis excursion → TITLIS Rotair → Snow experience → Cliff Walk / Ice Flyer where suitable and operating Later: → Lucerne → Chapel Bridge → Old Town → Lake Lucerne waterfront → Family leisure Evening: → Return to Zurich → Overnight at Zurich', 2518),
  ('netherlands', 30, 'seven-nights-family-pattern', 'SEVEN-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 7', NULL, 'Breakfast → Hotel checkout → Continue via Vaduz Austria: → Swarovski Crystal Worlds, Wattens → Family-friendly exhibitions / gardens → Continue to Innsbruck Evening: → Golden Roof → Innsbruck Old Town → Family dinner → Overnight at Innsbruck', 2519),
  ('netherlands', 30, 'seven-nights-family-pattern', 'SEVEN-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 8', NULL, 'Breakfast → Leisure morning → Optional short Innsbruck walk → Souvenir shopping → Hotel checkout → Airport / onward transfer → Departure Travel-agent family rule: For 7 nights, prioritize: AMSTERDAM + ZAANSE_SCHANS / KEUKENHOF + COLOGNE + BLACK_FOREST + RHINE_FALLS + ONE_JUNGFRAU_REGION_EXPERIENCE + TITLIS + LUCERNE + INNSBRUCK Keep the itinerary CHILD_FRIENDLY with maximum 2–3 major experiences per day and avoid adding extra cities simply to increase destination count.', 2520),
  ('netherlands', 31, 'seven-nights-luxury-pattern', 'SEVEN-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 1', NULL, 'Arrival at Amsterdam / transfer from Brussels → Private premium transfer → Five-star hotel check-in → Relax and refresh Evening: → Amsterdam Canal Ring → Private canal cruise → Fine dining → Overnight at Amsterdam', 2521),
  ('netherlands', 31, 'seven-nights-luxury-pattern', 'SEVEN-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 2', NULL, 'Breakfast at the hotel → Private Amsterdam sightseeing → Rijksmuseum / Museum Quarter → Jordaan → Luxury shopping / café time Choose ONE: SPRING: → Private Keukenhof excursion → Tulip gardens → Couple / family photography OR YEAR-ROUND: → Private Zaanse Schans excursion → Windmills → Premium cheese / Dutch heritage experience Evening: → Fine dining / cocktail lounge → Overnight at Amsterdam', 2522),
  ('netherlands', 31, 'seven-nights-luxury-pattern', 'SEVEN-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 3', NULL, 'Breakfast → Hotel checkout → Chauffeured journey toward Germany Cologne: → Cologne Cathedral → Rhine waterfront → Private city orientation Continue to Frankfurt → Luxury hotel check-in → Premium dinner → Overnight at Frankfurt', 2523),
  ('netherlands', 31, 'seven-nights-luxury-pattern', 'SEVEN-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 4', NULL, 'Breakfast → Private scenic Black Forest journey → Selected picturesque village → Cuckoo-clock / regional experience → Premium countryside lunch Continue toward Switzerland: → Rhine Falls → Private / premium viewpoint experience → Optional boat experience where operating → Continue to Zurich → Five-star hotel check-in → Overnight at Zurich', 2524),
  ('netherlands', 31, 'seven-nights-luxury-pattern', 'SEVEN-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 5', NULL, 'Breakfast → Premium Jungfrau Region excursion Choose ONE: JUNGFRAUJOCH: → First-class / premium rail arrangements → Jungfraujoch → Snow and glacier scenery → Premium mountain dining OR RELAXED_LUXURY_ALPINE: → Grindelwald → Interlaken → Private guide → Scenic viewpoints → Premium Alpine lunch Evening: → Return to Zurich → Fine dining → Overnight at Zurich', 2525),
  ('netherlands', 31, 'seven-nights-luxury-pattern', 'SEVEN-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 6', NULL, 'Breakfast → Private transfer / premium rail toward Engelberg → Mt. Titlis → TITLIS Rotair → Glacier and snow experience → Cliff Walk / Ice Flyer where operating Later: → Lucerne → Chapel Bridge → Old Town → Lakefront → Luxury shopping / private leisure Evening: → Return to Zurich → Spa / premium dinner → Overnight at Zurich', 2526),
  ('netherlands', 31, 'seven-nights-luxury-pattern', 'SEVEN-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 7', NULL, 'Breakfast → Hotel checkout → Chauffeured journey via Vaduz → Private scenic stop Continue to Austria: → Swarovski Crystal Worlds → Premium shopping → Innsbruck Evening: → Innsbruck Old Town → Golden Roof → Five-star Alpine hotel → Fine dining / spa → Overnight at Innsbruck', 2527),
  ('netherlands', 31, 'seven-nights-luxury-pattern', 'SEVEN-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 8', NULL, 'Breakfast → Relaxed luxury morning → Optional private Innsbruck / Alpine experience → Hotel checkout → Chauffeured airport / onward transfer → Departure Travel-agent luxury rule: For 7 nights, prioritize: AMSTERDAM_FIVE_STAR + PRIVATE_CANAL_EXPERIENCE + PRIVATE_GERMANY_TRANSFERS + BLACK_FOREST + SWISS_FIRST_CLASS + PREMIUM_ALPINE_EXPERIENCES + INNSBRUCK_LUXURY Luxury should emphasize: PRIVACY + PREMIUM_HOTELS + PRIVATE_TRANSFERS + FIRST_CLASS_RAIL + FINE_DINING + FLEXIBLE_PACING rather than adding more destinations or excessive daily sightseeing.', 2528),
  ('netherlands', 32, 'travel-agent-insights', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS', 'What inexperienced planners often do wrong', NULL, '', 2529),
  ('netherlands', 32, 'travel-agent-insights', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS', 'What an experienced planner does differently', NULL, 'AMSTERDAM + ONE_HISTORIC_OR_MODERN_CITY + ONE_WINDMILL / FLOWER / COAST / NATURE_EXPERIENCE rather than maximum destination count.', 2530),
  ('netherlands', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', NULL, NULL, 'IF: trip_length <= 4 nights THEN: prioritize_AMSTERDAM + ONE_NEARBY_EXCURSION Reason: Short stays gain more value from properly exploring Amsterdam plus one contrasting Dutch experience. IF: trip_length >= 6 nights AND: traveler_interest == FIRST_TIME_NETHERLANDS THEN: prioritize_AMSTERDAM + ROTTERDAM_THE_HAGUE_OR_UTRECHT + ONE_REGIONAL_EXPERIENCE Reason: This provides the strongest balance of canals, museums, historic cities, architecture, and countryside. IF: trip_type == HONEYMOON THEN: prefer_AMSTERDAM + UTRECHT_OR_DELFT + GIETHOORN_OR_COAST AND: increase_CANAL_CRUISE + DINING + FREE_TIME Reason: Dutch romance works best through canals, historic streets, boutique stays, waterfront dining, and slower travel. Amsterdam''s official tourism board specifically positions evening canal cruises as one of the city''s most romantic experiences. IF: traveler_type == FAMILY THEN: prefer_CANAL_CRUISE + NEMO + MADURODAM + WINDMILLS + BEACHES + EASY_CYCLING AND: reduce_MUSEUM_DENSITY IF: traveler_type == LUXURY THEN: prefer_5_STAR_AMSTERDAM_HOTEL + PRIVATE_CANAL_CRUISE + PRIVATE_GUIDE + FINE_DINING + PREMIUM_TRANSFER Reason: Luxury should improve privacy, cultural access, accommodation, dining, and service rather than increase destination count. IF: traveler_type == BUDGET THEN: prefer_PUBLIC_TRANSPORT + WALKING + SELECTIVE_CYCLING + WELL_CONNECTED_HOTEL AND: compare_CITY_CARD_VALUE Reason: Amsterdam''s official City Card includes public transport, a canal cruise, bicycle rental and many museums / attractions, making pass comparison useful for attraction-heavy stays. IF: traveler_interest == CULTURE_AND_MUSEUMS THEN: prioritize_AMSTERDAM + THE_HAGUE + DELFT_OR_UTRECHT AND: include_RIJKSMUSEUM + VAN_GOGH_MUSEUM + MAURITSHUIS + DUTCH_HERITAGE Amsterdam''s official visitor guidance identifies Rijksmuseum, Van Gogh Museum and other major collections as core cultural experiences. IF: traveler_interest == FLOWERS THEN: prefer_KEUKENHOF + BULB_REGION AND: verify_SEASON + BLOOM_CONDITIONS IF: traveler_interest == CYCLING THEN: prefer_COUNTRYSIDE + UTRECHT + VELUWE + COASTAL_ROUTES AND: match_ROUTE_TO_SKILL + WEATHER IF: traveler_interest == COAST_AND_NATURE THEN: prefer_SCHEVENINGEN + ZEELAND + WADDEN_ISLANDS + VELUWE AND: allow_WEATHER_FLEXIBILITY IF: traveler_interest == PHOTOGRAPHY THEN: prefer_AMSTERDAM_CANALS + KINDERDIJK + DELFT + TULIP_REGION + WADDEN_COAST AND: prioritize_EARLY_MORNING + SUNSET IF: trip_length <= 7 nights THEN: prefer_MAXIMUM_TWO_OR_THREE_BASES AND: avoid_EXCESSIVE_HOTEL_CHANGES IF: traveler_type == SENIOR OR: traveler_mobility == LIMITED THEN: prefer_DIRECT_RAIL + CANAL_CRUISES + MUSEUMS + COMPACT_CITY_SIGHTSEEING AND: reduce_LONG_CYCLING + COBBLESTONE_WALKING IF: traveler_uses_WHEELCHAIR THEN: prefer_VERIFIED_ACCESSIBLE_HOTELS + TRANSPORT + ATTRACTIONS AND: do_not_assume_HISTORIC_CANAL_HOUSES + BOATS + BEACHES + NATURE_ROUTES_ARE_STEP_FREE Reason: Amsterdam has substantial accessible tourism infrastructure, but individual museums, boats, historic buildings and routes still need verification. IF: weather == RAINY_OR_WINDY THEN: increase_MUSEUMS + FOOD + SHOPPING + INDOOR_CULTURE AND: reduce_LONG_CYCLING + COASTAL_ACTIVITY IF: traveler_interest == FIRST_TIME_NETHERLANDS THEN: prioritize_AMSTERDAM AND: add_ONE_OF_ROTTERDAM_THE_HAGUE_UTRECHT_OR_DELFT AND: add_ONE_SIGNATURE_DUTCH_EXPERIENCE IF: traveler_interest == CULTURE_AND_RELAXATION_BALANCE THEN: allocate_60_TO_70_PERCENT_TO_CORE_SIGHTSEEING AND: allocate_REMAINING_TIME_TO_CANALS + CAFÉS + CYCLING + PARKS + COAST + FREE_TIME', 2531),
  ('netherlands', 34, 'destination-scoring', 'DESTINATION SCORING', NULL, NULL, '| Factor | Score | | ------------------ | ----: | | Family | 94 | | Honeymoon | 88 | | Luxury | 88 | | Budget | 74 | | Adventure | 79 | | Culture | 96 | | Food | 84 | | Shopping | 89 | | Nightlife | 90 | | Relaxation | 90 | | Nature | 86 | | Accessibility | 89 | | Safety | 91 | | First-time visitor | 96 | | Photography | 95 |', 2532),
  ('netherlands', 35, 'final-travel-agent-verdict', 'FINAL TRAVEL AGENT VERDICT', NULL, NULL, 'Best traveler profiles: 1. Culture / museum traveler 2. First-time Europe traveler 3. Photography traveler 4. Family traveler 5. Cycling / active traveler 6. Historic-city traveler 7. Coast / water traveler 8. Solo traveler 9. Honeymoon / romantic traveler 10. Shopping / nightlife traveler Best duration: 5–8 nights 3–4 nights: Amsterdam + one nearby experience such as Utrecht, Haarlem, Zaanse Schans, or Keukenhof in season. 5–8 nights: Best for Amsterdam + Rotterdam / The Hague + Utrecht / Delft + one windmill, flower, coast, or nature experience. 9–10 nights: Excellent for adding Zeeland, Veluwe, Wadden Islands, Maastricht, or deeper regional travel. Best season: YEAR-ROUND Spring: TULIPS + FLOWERS + CYCLING + CITIES + PHOTOGRAPHY. Summer: COAST + BEACHES + CYCLING + BOATING + FAMILY + FESTIVALS. Autumn: CULTURE + MUSEUMS + CYCLING + NATURE + PHOTOGRAPHY + BETTER_VALUE. Winter: MUSEUMS + CITY_BREAKS + CAFÉS + SHOPPING + CULTURAL_EVENINGS. Official Netherlands tourism positions the country around year-round cities, culture, cycling and nature, with spring especially important for flowers and summer for beaches and outdoor travel. Best hotel strategy: Choose accommodation according to rail / tram access and trip purpose. For first-time visitors: AMSTERDAM + ONE_SECONDARY_CITY_OR_REGION. For honeymoon / luxury: Prefer canal-view, boutique, historic, waterfront, or premium city hotels. Avoid unnecessary hotel changes because major Dutch cities are closely connected by rail. Best transportation: Use: The Netherlands is strongly suited to train-based touring; its public transport combines national rail with extensive regional bus, tram and metro networks. Must-do for first-time visitor: Official tourism material particularly emphasizes Dutch Masters, cycling, water heritage, flowers, nature, and cities beyond Amsterdam. Don''t-do: Biggest advantage: Exceptional variety within a very compact and highly connected country. The Netherlands combines world-class museums, historic canal cities, cycling, modern architecture, windmills, water-management heritage, flower landscapes, beaches, Wadden Islands, national parks, nightlife, and easy public transport. Official tourism guidance specifically highlights that destinations and experiences are generally only a short journey apart. Biggest disadvantage: Amsterdam and major spring / summer destinations can become crowded and expensive. The country''s maritime climate also means rain, wind, and rapidly changing weather can affect cycling, beaches, flower-field visits, and outdoor itineraries. Overall destination score: 90/100', 2533),
  ('netherlands', 36, 'data-quality', 'DATA QUALITY', NULL, NULL, 'information_completeness: 96/100 last_updated: 2026-08-27 last_verified: PARTIALLY_WEB_VERIFIED verified_by: NBTC / HOLLAND.COM / DUTCH GOVERNMENT / NS / OFFICIAL DUTCH REGIONAL, TRANSPORT AND ACCESSIBILITY SOURCES sources: IMPORTANT: Hotel rates, rail fares, attraction tickets, museum schedules, canal-cruise operations, ferry services, events, and accessibility must NOT be treated as permanently valid. Keukenhof and tulip-field travel are strongly seasonal; tulips generally run from late March to mid-May, with peak conditions often around mid-April. Rain, wind, tides, ferry conditions, and coastal weather can materially affect cycling, Wadden, beach, and water-based experiences. Public transport accessibility is strong overall, but individual stations, lifts, vehicles, ferries, and routes should still be verified. Historic canal districts, narrow buildings, bridges, cobbles, beaches, windmills, and natural areas should not be assumed fully step-free. The Netherlands should primarily be treated as: SPRING: TULIPS + FLOWERS + CULTURE + CYCLING + PHOTOGRAPHY SUMMER: COAST + BEACHES + WATER + CYCLING + FAMILY + FESTIVALS AUTUMN: CITIES + MUSEUMS + NATURE + CYCLING + PHOTOGRAPHY WINTER: MUSEUMS + CITY_BREAKS + CAFÉS + SHOPPING + CULTURAL_EVENINGS NBTC / Holland.com, NS, Dutch transport authorities, regional tourism boards, museums, ferry operators, and individual attractions should be treated as primary sources for current operational information. This dataset should be refreshed regularly before production use.', 2534),
  ('linchestine', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Spring', NULL, 'months: March April May weather: Cool and changeable in March, becoming milder through April and May. Lower valleys green up earlier, while Malbun and higher trails can retain snow. crowd_level: LOW → MEDIUM price_level: MEDIUM overall_score: 72–78 recommended: true reason: Good for Vaduz, museums, the Liechtenstein Trail, cycling, photography, and gradually improving hiking conditions. Late spring is especially suitable for lower- and mid-altitude outdoor travel, while higher mountain routes remain weather dependent.', 2535),
  ('linchestine', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Summer', NULL, 'months: June July August weather: Mild to warm in the Rhine Valley with long daylight; mountain areas remain cooler and well suited to hiking and family activities. crowd_level: MEDIUM → HIGH price_level: MEDIUM → HIGH overall_score: 71–77 recommended: true reason: Best for: Malbun is a major summer hiking and family base, with themed trails, mountain activities, and easy access from Vaduz.', 2536),
  ('linchestine', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Autumn', NULL, 'months: September October November weather: September is generally excellent for hiking; October becomes cooler and colourful, while November is colder and more transitional. crowd_level: MEDIUM → LOW price_level: MEDIUM → LOW overall_score: 75–82 recommended: true reason: September and October are among the best periods for hiking, Alpine scenery, photography, Vaduz, vineyards, and quieter travel. November offers weaker mountain conditions but very low visitor pressure and good value for museums, food, and short cultural stays.', 2537),
  ('linchestine', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Winter', NULL, 'months: December January February weather: Cold with reliable snow conditions in Malbun and Steg, while lower areas can experience frost, fog, rain, or occasional snow. crowd_level: MEDIUM → HIGH in Malbun price_level: MEDIUM → HIGH overall_score: 67–74 recommended: true reason: Excellent for: Malbun has 23 km of ski pistes and is specifically positioned as a family-friendly winter area away from mass tourism.', 2538),
  ('linchestine', 10, 'budget-strategy', 'BUDGET STRATEGY', NULL, NULL, 'Where money can be saved: Where saving money is usually NOT recommended: Travel-agent rule: In Liechtenstein, **HOTEL_LOCATION + ADVENTURE_PASS + PUBLIC_TRANSPORT + MOUNTAIN_ACTIVITY_COST should be evaluated together**. For short stays, prioritize **VADUZ + MALBUN + ONE_CULTURAL_OR_NATURE_EXPERIENCE**. For longer stays, add **TRIESENBERG + LIECHTENSTEIN_TRAIL + HIKING / SKIING + ONE_DEEPER_REGIONAL_EXPERIENCE** rather than changing hotels repeatedly.', 2539),
  ('linchestine', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Family', 'family', 'Liechtenstein has no airport. For most international arrivals, use Zurich Airport → rail to Sargans or Buchs SG → LIEmobil bus to Vaduz / hotel. For young children, heavy luggage, or late arrivals, a private transfer from Zurich Airport is more comfortable.', 2540),
  ('linchestine', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Honeymoon', 'honeymoon', 'Prefer first-class rail to Sargans / Buchs followed by LIEmobil, or use a private transfer directly to Vaduz / Malbun. For couples, PRIVATE_TRANSFER + SCENIC_ALPINE_ARRIVAL works especially well when staying in Malbun or a premium mountain property.', 2541),
  ('linchestine', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Luxury', 'luxury', 'Use a chauffeured premium sedan / SUV from Zurich Airport, St. Gallen-Altenrhein, or another nearby gateway. For multi-country luxury itineraries, combine: FIRST_CLASS_SWISS_OR_AUSTRIAN_RAIL + PRIVATE_CHAUFFEUR + PREMIUM_ALPINE_TRANSFERS.', 2542),
  ('linchestine', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Budget', 'budget', 'Use rail to: then connect by LIEmobil bus. Liechtenstein Tourism officially recommends these three railway gateways; Liechtenstein itself has no international airport.', 2543),
  ('linchestine', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Senior', 'senior', 'Prefer rail + direct LIEmobil connection where luggage and mobility permit; otherwise use private transfer. Choose hotels near convenient bus stops and minimize unnecessary changes.', 2544),
  ('linchestine', 18, 'family-travel', 'FAMILY TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'child_friendly_score: 92 best_ages: Rules: For young children: Prefer: Avoid: Malbun is the country''s strongest family base, with skiing, themed trails, Alpine Minigolf, llama / alpaca trekking, and other child-friendly activities.', 2545),
  ('linchestine', 19, 'honeymoon-travel', 'HONEYMOON TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'honeymoon_score: 84 romance_score: 86 privacy_score: 92 luxury_score: 80 Recommended: Honeymoon itineraries should generally stay at: 2–3 major experiences/day. Prefer: MOUNTAINS + WINE + SCENIC_VIEWS + DINING + FREE_TIME over: Constant sightseeing and excessive activity changes. Recommended areas:', 2546),
  ('linchestine', 20, 'luxury-travel', 'LUXURY TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'luxury_score: 80 Recommended: Liechtenstein luxury travel should focus on: Luxury value is strongest through personalized service, gourmet restaurants, wine, and Alpine stays rather than large-scale luxury resorts or shopping.', 2547),
  ('linchestine', 21, 'adventure', 'ADVENTURE', NULL, NULL, 'adventure_score: 87 Liechtenstein is a strong compact Alpine adventure destination, particularly for hiking and winter activities. Adventure experiences: Liechtenstein has more than 400 km of marked hiking trails; the Alpine Route 66 covers roughly 30 km over three demanding stages, while Malbun provides 23 km of ski pistes. Match Alpine activities to weather, snow conditions, fitness, equipment, and route difficulty.', 2548),
  ('linchestine', 22, 'senior-travel', 'SENIOR TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'senior_suitability: 86 walking_intensity: LOW–MEDIUM for Vaduz, museums, bus-based touring, and scenic sightseeing MEDIUM–HIGH for Triesenberg, Malbun, and mountain trails Rules: Liechtenstein works particularly well for seniors as a: CULTURE + SCENERY + PUBLIC_TRANSPORT + MOUNTAINS + RELAXED_SHORT_TRIP destination.', 2549),
  ('linchestine', 23, 'accessibility', 'ACCESSIBILITY', NULL, NULL, 'wheelchair_accessibility: MODERATE → GOOD IN VADUZ / MODERN FACILITIES VARIABLE IN MOUNTAIN, HISTORIC AND TRAIL ENVIRONMENTS public_transport_accessibility: GOOD overall; verify individual buses, stops, routes, and mountain connections hotel_accessibility: MUST_BE_VERIFIED_PER_HOTEL attraction_accessibility: MUST_BE_VERIFIED_PER_ATTRACTION Rule: Never assume universal accessibility because Liechtenstein is compact. Additional notes:', 2550),
  ('linchestine', 24, 'food', 'FOOD', NULL, NULL, 'Liechtenstein is particularly strong for: Käsknöpfle — cheese dumplings traditionally served with roasted onions and apple sauce — are the country''s signature specialty. Liechtenstein also performs unusually well in gourmet dining for its tiny population, with several Gault Millau-awarded restaurants. Food experiences: Family: Prioritize Käsknöpfle, mountain restaurants, casual regional dining, bakery items, and family-friendly hotels. Honeymoon: Choose vineyard experiences, gourmet restaurants, mountain dining, wine tasting, and relaxed scenic meals. Luxury: Include Gault Millau restaurants, premium wine tastings, private culinary experiences, and high-end hotel dining. Budget: Use bakeries, supermarkets, casual restaurants, farm shops, and selected traditional inns.', 2551),
  ('linchestine', 25, 'shopping', 'SHOPPING', NULL, NULL, 'Strong categories: Luxury shopping: Prefer: Liechtenstein is not a major international luxury-shopping destination; premium retail is concentrated mainly in Vaduz. Budget: Prefer: The official souvenir passport stamp and Liechtenstein''s philatelic tradition are particularly distinctive visitor purchases. Travel-agent rule: Use VADUZ for MAIN_SHOPPING, LIECHTENSTEIN_CENTER for SOUVENIRS + VISITOR_PRODUCTS, POSTAL_MUSEUM / PHILATELY for STAMPS, and WINERIES / FARM_SHOPS for WINE + REGIONAL_PRODUCTS.', 2552),
  ('linchestine', 26, 'nightlife', 'NIGHTLIFE', NULL, NULL, 'nightlife_level: 61 Suitable for: Best areas: Evening activities are better suited to: Vaduz offers the widest selection of bars and restaurants, while Malbun provides relaxed après-ski and mountain evenings. Honeymoon travelers should generally prefer: WINE_TASTING + FINE_DINING + HOTEL_BAR + EVENING_WALK over: Club-heavy itineraries. Travel-agent rule: Position Liechtenstein as a **RELAXED_BAR + WINE + DINING + APRES_SKI EVENING DESTINATION**, not as a major European nightlife destination.', 2553),
  ('linchestine', 28, 'sample-itinerary-patterns', 'SAMPLE ITINERARY PATTERNS', '3 NIGHTS', NULL, '### Day 1 Arrival via Zurich / Sargans / Buchs / Feldkirch → Rail + LIEmobil bus / private transfer to Vaduz → Hotel check-in → Relaxation and refreshment Afternoon: Vaduz orientation → Museum Mile → Liechtenstein NationalMuseum / Kunstmuseum according to interest → Government district → Liechtenstein Center → Walk toward Vaduz Castle viewpoint → Princely vineyard area Evening: Regional / contemporary dinner → Optional wine tasting or relaxed Vaduz walk → Hotel Vaduz is the country''s strongest cultural base, while official 72-hour itineraries combine city sightseeing, wine, museums and princely heritage on the first day. ### Day 2 Morning: Breakfast → LIEmobil bus to Triesenberg → Walser village atmosphere → Scenic Rhine Valley viewpoints → Continue to Malbun Winter options: → Skiing / snowboarding → Sledging → Snowshoeing → Winter hiking → Family snow activities Spring / Summer / Autumn options: → Sareis chairlift → Mountain walk / easy hike → Alpine Minigolf → Family activities → Scenic photography → Mountain lunch Afternoon: Continue Malbun / Steg according to season → Gänglesee / quiet mountain scenery → Optional short hiking experience → Relaxation Evening: Return to Vaduz → Dinner → Hotel Malbun can be reached from Vaduz in roughly 30 minutes by public bus and is the country''s main mountain base for hiking, family activities and winter recreation. ### Day 3 Morning: Breakfast → Balzers → Gutenberg Castle exterior / viewpoints → Begin selected Liechtenstein Trail section → Village and Rhine Valley scenery Afternoon: Lunch → Continue toward Triesen / Vaduz OR Schaan according to chosen trail section → Cycling / e-bike alternative → Local cultural stops → Photography Evening: Return to Vaduz → Souvenir / stamp shopping → Special dinner → Optional hotel lounge / relaxed evening → Hotel The Liechtenstein Trail runs about 75 km through all municipalities and is divided into five main walking stages, making shorter sections easy to integrate into a compact itinerary. Optional alternative according to traveler interest: FAMILY: → Citytrain Vaduz → TreasureChamber → Malbun → Llama / alpaca trekking → Alpine Minigolf → Easy family hiking HONEYMOON: → Boutique Vaduz / Malbun stay → Princely wine tasting → Sareis panorama → Scenic Triesenberg drive → Fine dining → Free time ADVENTURE: → Route 66 section → Alpine hiking → Skiing / snowshoeing in winter → Cycling / e-bike → Mountain-hut experience CULTURE / HISTORY: → Museum Mile → Liechtenstein NationalMuseum → Kunstmuseum → TreasureChamber → Vaduz Castle heritage → Gutenberg Castle → Triesenberg Walser heritage FOOD: → Käsknöpfle → Princely wine tasting → Traditional inn → Mountain lunch → Gourmet dining MOUNTAIN / NATURE: → Malbun + Sareis → Triesenberg → Steg / Gänglesee → Liechtenstein Trail → Alpine photography For dedicated hikers, replace the standard sightseeing pattern with Route 66, a 30.3 km three-stage Alpine route, or extend the trip for the full Liechtenstein Trail. ### Day 4 Breakfast → Leisure morning → Optional Museum Mile / Liechtenstein Center revisit → Souvenir and stamp shopping → Hotel checkout → LIEmobil + rail / private transfer toward onward airport or Switzerland / Austria → Departure', 2554),
  ('linchestine', 29, 'four-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'FOUR-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 1', NULL, 'Arrival via Zurich / Sargans / Buchs → Transfer to Vaduz → Romantic hotel check-in → Relax and refresh Evening: → Vaduz Städtle → Government district → Museum Mile orientation → Princely vineyards → Känzile viewpoint → Romantic dinner → Overnight at Vaduz Vaduz provides the best honeymoon base for culture, dining, vineyards and easy access to Liechtenstein''s mountain region.', 2555),
  ('linchestine', 29, 'four-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'FOUR-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 2', NULL, 'Breakfast at the hotel Morning: → Vaduz Citytrain → Liechtenstein NationalMuseum / Kunstmuseum → Liechtenstein Center → Vaduz Castle viewpoint Afternoon: → Court Winery of the Prince of Liechtenstein → Wine tasting → Relaxed vineyard walk → Couple photography Evening: → Fine dining → Relaxed couple time → Overnight at Vaduz Official tourism''s 72-hour itinerary similarly combines the Vaduz Citytrain, cultural sightseeing and a tasting at the Princely Winery.', 2556),
  ('linchestine', 29, 'four-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'FOUR-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 3', NULL, 'Breakfast → Scenic journey through Triesenberg → Mountain and Rhine Valley viewpoints → Continue to Malbun Spring / Summer / Autumn: → Sareis chairlift → Alpine panorama → Easy scenic hike → Mountain lunch Winter: → Snow experience → Winter walk / snowshoeing → Mountain restaurant Evening: → Romantic mountain dinner → Optional Malbun overnight for stronger Alpine atmosphere Malbun is the principal mountain experience; official itineraries pair the Sareis chairlift and Alpine scenery with Vaduz on short stays.', 2557),
  ('linchestine', 29, 'four-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'FOUR-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 4', NULL, 'Breakfast → Steg / Gänglesee → Scenic couple photography → Continue to Balzers → Gutenberg Castle → Castle and Rhine Valley viewpoints Afternoon: → Regional lunch → Return toward Vaduz → Spa / hotel relaxation → Free couple time Evening: → Special honeymoon dinner → Wine / hotel lounge → Overnight at Vaduz Gutenberg Castle is one of Liechtenstein''s principal historic landmarks and can be combined naturally with southern Liechtenstein and mountain sightseeing.', 2558),
  ('linchestine', 29, 'four-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'FOUR-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 5', NULL, 'Breakfast → Leisure morning → Optional souvenir / stamp shopping → Optional café or short Vaduz walk → Hotel checkout → Private transfer / LIEmobil + rail toward Zurich or onward Switzerland / Austria → Departure', 2559),
  ('linchestine', 30, 'four-nights-family-pattern', 'FOUR-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 1', NULL, 'Arrival via Zurich / Sargans / Buchs → Transfer to Vaduz → Family hotel check-in → Relax and refresh Afternoon: → Vaduz Citytrain → Liechtenstein Center → Museum Mile → TreasureChamber → Government district → Vaduz Castle viewpoint Evening: → Family-friendly dinner → Easy Vaduz walk → Overnight at Vaduz', 2560),
  ('linchestine', 30, 'four-nights-family-pattern', 'FOUR-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 2', NULL, 'Breakfast at the hotel → Scenic bus journey via Triesenberg → Continue to Malbun Spring / Summer / Autumn: → Sareis chairlift → Easy family hiking → Alpine Minigolf → Playground / mountain activities → Llama / alpaca trekking where booked Winter: → Malbi Park → Family skiing → Sledging → Ice skating / winter walking Evening: → Mountain / family dinner → Return to Vaduz OR overnight at Malbun Malbun is Liechtenstein''s strongest family area, with dedicated children''s skiing and several year-round family activities.', 2561),
  ('linchestine', 30, 'four-nights-family-pattern', 'FOUR-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 3', NULL, 'Breakfast → Triesenberg → Walser heritage and village exploration → Scenic viewpoints Continue to Steg → Gänglesee → Easy nature walk → Picnic / family relaxation → Photography Afternoon: → Return toward Vaduz → Free time / playground / hotel rest Evening: → Casual family dinner → Overnight at Vaduz', 2562),
  ('linchestine', 30, 'four-nights-family-pattern', 'FOUR-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 4', NULL, 'Breakfast → Balzers → Gutenberg Castle → Castle-hill views → Easy Liechtenstein Trail section Afternoon: → Return to Vaduz → Optional NationalMuseum / PostalMuseum → Souvenir and stamp shopping → Family café time Evening: → Final family dinner → Relaxation → Overnight at Vaduz', 2563),
  ('linchestine', 30, 'four-nights-family-pattern', 'FOUR-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 5', NULL, 'Breakfast → Leisure morning → Optional short Vaduz walk → Hotel checkout → LIEmobil + rail / private transfer toward Zurich or onward Switzerland / Austria → Departure', 2564),
  ('linchestine', 31, 'four-nights-luxury-pattern', 'FOUR-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 1', NULL, 'Arrival via Zurich → Private chauffeured transfer to Vaduz → Premium hotel check-in → Relax and refresh Afternoon: → Private Vaduz orientation → Museum Mile → Government district → Vaduz Castle viewpoint → Princely vineyards Evening: → Fine dining → Premium wine / hotel lounge → Overnight at Vaduz', 2565),
  ('linchestine', 31, 'four-nights-luxury-pattern', 'FOUR-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 2', NULL, 'Breakfast at the hotel Morning: → Privately guided cultural experience → Liechtenstein NationalMuseum → Kunstmuseum Liechtenstein → TreasureChamber → Princely heritage Afternoon: → Court Winery of the Prince of Liechtenstein → Premium wine tasting → Vineyard walk → Leisure / spa time Evening: → Gourmet dinner → Overnight at Vaduz', 2566),
  ('linchestine', 31, 'four-nights-luxury-pattern', 'FOUR-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 3', NULL, 'Breakfast → Private scenic drive through Triesenberg → Rhine Valley viewpoints → Continue to Malbun Spring / Summer / Autumn: → Sareis chairlift → Alpine panorama → Private / easy scenic hike → Premium mountain lunch Winter: → Private ski experience → Snowshoeing / winter walk → Mountain dining Afternoon: → Leisure in Malbun → Spa / wellness → Couple or private photography Evening: → Premium Alpine dinner → Overnight at Malbun OR Vaduz', 2567),
  ('linchestine', 31, 'four-nights-luxury-pattern', 'FOUR-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 4', NULL, 'Breakfast → Scenic private drive to Steg → Gänglesee → Relaxed nature experience → Continue to Balzers → Gutenberg Castle viewpoints Afternoon: → Premium regional lunch → Return to Vaduz → Spa / hotel relaxation → Private shopping / free time Evening: → Special farewell dinner → Wine / hotel lounge → Overnight at Vaduz', 2568),
  ('linchestine', 31, 'four-nights-luxury-pattern', 'FOUR-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 5', NULL, 'Breakfast → Leisure morning → Optional private Vaduz walk → Hotel checkout → Chauffeured transfer to Zurich Airport / onward Switzerland or Austria → Departure', 2569),
  ('linchestine', 32, 'travel-agent-insights', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS', 'What inexperienced planners often do wrong', NULL, '', 2570),
  ('linchestine', 32, 'travel-agent-insights', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS', 'What an experienced planner does differently', NULL, 'VADUZ + MALBUN + ONE_TRIESENBERG / STEG / BALZERS / LIECHTENSTEIN_TRAIL_EXPERIENCE rather than maximum attraction count.', 2571),
  ('linchestine', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', NULL, NULL, 'IF: trip_length <= 2 nights THEN: prioritize_VADUZ + MALBUN Reason: Short stays gain the most value from combining Liechtenstein''s cultural capital with its strongest Alpine experience. IF: trip_length >= 3 nights AND: traveler_interest == FIRST_TIME_LIECHTENSTEIN THEN: prioritize_VADUZ + MALBUN + TRIESENBERG_OR_BALZERS + ONE_TRAIL_EXPERIENCE Reason: This gives the strongest balance of culture, mountains, villages, heritage, and scenery. IF: trip_type == HONEYMOON THEN: prefer_VADUZ + MALBUN + TRIESENBERG AND: increase_WINE + SCENIC_VIEWS + FINE_DINING + FREE_TIME Reason: Romantic value is strongest through Alpine scenery, vineyards, quiet mountain stays, and relaxed couple time. IF: traveler_type == FAMILY THEN: prefer_VADUZ_CITYTRAIN + MALBUN + MALBI_PARK + EASY_HIKING + LLAMA_ALPACA_EXPERIENCE AND: reduce_DIFFICULT_TRAILS + MUSEUM_DENSITY Reason: Malbun is specifically positioned as a family resort, with child-oriented skiing and year-round mountain activities. IF: traveler_type == LUXURY THEN: prefer_PREMIUM_VADUZ_HOTEL + PRIVATE_TRANSFER + PRINCELY_WINE + FINE_DINING + PRIVATE_GUIDE + MALBUN Reason: Luxury should improve privacy, service, gastronomy, and mountain comfort rather than increase destination count. IF: traveler_type == BUDGET THEN: prefer_LIEMOBIL + WALKING + HIKING + WELL_CONNECTED_HOTEL AND: compare_ADVENTURE_PASS_VALUE Reason: The Adventure Pass includes public transport and multiple attractions, while hiking and viewpoints add strong low-cost value. IF: traveler_interest == CULTURE_AND_HERITAGE THEN: prioritize_VADUZ + TRIESENBERG + BALZERS AND: include_MUSEUM_MILE + NATIONALMUSEUM + KUNSTMUSEUM + GUTENBERG_CASTLE + WALSER_HERITAGE Reason: Vaduz contains six museums within a compact area, making it the country''s strongest cultural cluster. IF: traveler_interest == HIKING THEN: prefer_LIECHTENSTEIN_TRAIL + MALBUN + ROUTE_66 AND: match_ROUTE_TO_FITNESS + WEATHER + SEASON Reason: Liechtenstein has more than 400 km of hiking trails, while the 75-km Liechtenstein Trail crosses all 11 municipalities. IF: traveler_interest == WINTER_SPORTS THEN: prefer_MALBUN + STEG AND: include_SKIING + SNOWBOARDING + WINTER_HIKING + CROSS_COUNTRY_SKIING Reason: Malbun offers 23 km of pistes, while nearby Steg has 12 km of cross-country trails. IF: traveler_interest == CYCLING THEN: prefer_RHINE_VALLEY + LIECHTENSTEIN_TRAIL + VILLAGE_ROUTES AND: use_E_BIKE_FOR_HILLIER_SECTIONS IF: traveler_interest == NATURE_AND_PHOTOGRAPHY THEN: prefer_MALBUN + SAREIS + TRIESENBERG + STEG + RUGGELL AND: prioritize_EARLY_MORNING + SUNSET + CLEAR_WEATHER IF: trip_length <= 4 nights THEN: prefer_ONE_MAIN_BASE AND: avoid_EXCESSIVE_HOTEL_CHANGES Reason: Liechtenstein''s compact size and short transport times make frequent hotel changes unnecessary. IF: traveler_type == SENIOR OR: traveler_mobility == LIMITED THEN: prefer_VADUZ + LIEMOBIL + EASY_MALBUN_EXPERIENCE + MUSEUMS AND: reduce_STEEP_TRAILS + LONG_ALPINE_WALKS IF: traveler_uses_WHEELCHAIR THEN: prefer_VERIFIED_ACCESSIBLE_VADUZ_ROUTES + HOTELS + TRANSPORT + SELECTED_MOUNTAIN_PATHS AND: do_not_assume_CASTLES + ALL_TRAILS + WINTER_ROUTES_ARE_STEP_FREE Reason: Official tourism identifies barrier-free Vaduz routes, wheelchair-suitable trails, and even all-terrain wheelchair options in Malbun, but accessibility still varies by route. IF: weather == POOR_MOUNTAIN_CONDITIONS THEN: increase_VADUZ_MUSEUMS + FOOD + WINE + INDOOR_CULTURE AND: reduce_HIGH_ALPINE_HIKING + CHAIRLIFT_DEPENDENT_ACTIVITY IF: traveler_interest == FIRST_TIME_LIECHTENSTEIN THEN: prioritize_VADUZ AND: add_MALBUN AND: add_ONE_OF_TRIESENBERG_STEG_BALZERS_OR_LIECHTENSTEIN_TRAIL IF: traveler_interest == CULTURE_AND_RELAXATION_BALANCE THEN: allocate_50_TO_60_PERCENT_TO_CORE_SIGHTSEEING AND: allocate_REMAINING_TIME_TO_MOUNTAINS + WINE + FOOD + SCENIC_WALKS + FREE_TIME', 2572),
  ('linchestine', 34, 'destination-scoring', 'DESTINATION SCORING', NULL, NULL, '| Factor | Score | | ------------------ | ----: | | Family | 92 | | Honeymoon | 84 | | Luxury | 80 | | Budget | 70 | | Adventure | 87 | | Culture | 85 | | Food | 82 | | Shopping | 70 | | Nightlife | 61 | | Relaxation | 92 | | Nature | 95 | | Accessibility | 79 | | Safety | 96 | | First-time visitor | 88 | | Photography | 93 |', 2573),
  ('linchestine', 35, 'final-travel-agent-verdict', 'FINAL TRAVEL AGENT VERDICT', NULL, NULL, 'Best traveler profiles: 1. Nature / mountain traveler 2. Hiking / active traveler 3. Family traveler 4. Photography traveler 5. Culture / heritage traveler 6. Winter-sports traveler 7. Relaxation traveler 8. First-time microstate traveler 9. Honeymoon / romantic traveler 10. Cycling / e-bike traveler Best duration: 2–3 nights 1 night: Vaduz + Malbun or Vaduz + one nearby heritage / mountain experience. 2–3 nights: Best overall balance for Vaduz + Malbun + Triesenberg / Steg + one cultural or hiking experience. 4–5 nights: Excellent for deeper hiking, winter sports, Liechtenstein Trail sections, cycling, family activities, or slower Alpine travel. 6+ nights: Best mainly for the full Liechtenstein Trail, dedicated hiking / skiing, or very slow travel. Best season: YEAR-ROUND Spring: VADUZ + CULTURE + CYCLING + LOWER_TRAILS + PHOTOGRAPHY. Summer: HIKING + MALBUN + LIECHTENSTEIN_TRAIL + FAMILY + CYCLING. Autumn: HIKING + ALPINE_SCENERY + PHOTOGRAPHY + WINE + RELAXATION. Winter: SKIING + SNOWSHOEING + WINTER_HIKING + SLEDDING + FAMILY_SNOW_TRAVEL. Liechtenstein Tourism positions the country as a year-round destination, with Malbun serving as both a summer / autumn hiking base and a winter sports resort. Best hotel strategy: Choose accommodation according to trip purpose and mountain / valley preference. For first-time visitors: VADUZ as the main base. For hiking / winter: MALBUN or TRIESENBERG according to activities. For honeymoon / luxury: Prefer premium Vaduz or scenic Alpine hotels with mountain views, dining, wine, and private transfers. Avoid unnecessary hotel changes because Liechtenstein''s distances are extremely short. Best transportation: Use: Liechtenstein is best treated as a BUS_FIRST + WALKABLE + CROSS_BORDER_RAIL_CONNECTED + CAR_OPTIONAL destination. Must-do for first-time visitor: Vaduz''s Museum Mile contains six museums within a few hundred metres, while the 75-km Liechtenstein Trail crosses all 11 municipalities. :contentReference Don''t-do: Biggest advantage: Exceptional concentration of Alpine nature, culture, outdoor activities, and heritage within only about 160 km². Official tourism specifically describes Liechtenstein as having a high density of experiences and short distances, making it particularly suitable for a three-day short trip. Biggest disadvantage: Its very small scale limits nightlife, shopping, resort variety, and the amount of conventional sightseeing available for long stays. Mountain weather, seasonal lift / trail conditions, and relatively high Swiss-franc-region costs can also affect planning. Overall destination score: 85/100', 2574),
  ('linchestine', 36, 'data-quality', 'DATA QUALITY', NULL, NULL, 'information_completeness: 97/100 last_updated: 2026-08-28 last_verified: WEB_VERIFIED verified_by: LIECHTENSTEIN TOURISM / LIECHTENSTEIN MARKETING / LIEMOBIL / OFFICIAL TOURISM AND TRANSPORT SOURCES sources: IMPORTANT: Hotel rates, restaurant prices, museum opening hours, chairlift schedules, ski operations, attraction tickets, public-transport schedules, and guided-tour availability must NOT be treated as permanently valid. Malbun''s ski area currently offers 23 km of pistes, but ski-season dates, snow conditions, lifts, and individual slopes must always be verified before travel. Mountain hikes, Route 66, and higher trails are weather and season dependent and should be matched to traveler fitness and current conditions. The Liechtenstein Trail is approximately 75 km and normally divided into five main walking stages; shorter sections are usually more appropriate for standard 2–3 night itineraries. Family travel is a genuine destination strength, particularly around Malbun, which official tourism promotes for families in both summer and winter. Accessibility should be verified per hotel, attraction, trail, bus connection, and seasonal condition rather than assumed universally. Liechtenstein should primarily be treated as: SPRING: CULTURE + VALLEY_SIGHTSEEING + CYCLING + HIKING + PHOTOGRAPHY SUMMER: HIKING + MALBUN + NATURE + FAMILY + CYCLING + PHOTOGRAPHY AUTUMN: ALPINE_SCENERY + HIKING + WINE + PHOTOGRAPHY + RELAXATION WINTER: SKIING + SNOWSHOEING + SLEDDING + WINTER_HIKING + FAMILY Liechtenstein Tourism, Liechtenstein Marketing, LIEmobil, mountain-lift operators, museums, hotels, and individual attractions should be treated as primary sources for current operational information. This dataset should be refreshed regularly before production use.', 2575),
  ('czech', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Spring', NULL, 'months: March April May weather: Cool and changeable in March, increasingly mild through April, and pleasantly warm by May. Spring averages around 10°C nationally, although mountain areas remain colder and higher trails can retain snow early in the season. crowd_level: LOW → MEDIUM price_level: LOW → MEDIUM overall_score: 80–88 recommended: true reason: One of Czechia''s strongest overall periods for Prague, historic towns, castles, countryside, hiking, spa travel, cycling, photography, and relaxed touring before peak summer demand. Best for: Official Czech tourism guidance specifically recommends spring as an attractive off-season period, when cities and countryside are less crowded and conditions are generally comfortable for walking.', 2576),
  ('czech', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Summer', NULL, 'months: June July August weather: Generally warm with long daylight hours. Average national summer temperature is around 17°C because mountain regions are included, while temperatures in cities can reach around 30–35°C during hot periods. Mountain destinations remain cooler. crowd_level: HIGH → VERY_HIGH price_level: HIGH overall_score: 68–80 recommended: true reason: Excellent for: Best for outdoor touring and mountain regions, but Czechia''s main visitor season runs from June through August, reducing crowd and price value at major destinations. Official Czech tourism identifies summer as the country''s busiest tourism period.', 2577),
  ('czech', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Autumn', NULL, 'months: September October November weather: September is often pleasantly warm and can feel summer-like. October becomes cooler with more rainfall and strong autumn colour, while November is considerably colder, cloudier, and more changeable with the possibility of early frost. crowd_level: MEDIUM → LOW price_level: MEDIUM → LOW overall_score: 80–90 recommended: true reason: September and October provide one of Czechia''s strongest combinations of comfortable sightseeing, historic towns, hiking, wine, countryside, autumn colour, photography, and lower visitor pressure. Best for: Official Czech tourism recommends autumn alongside spring for lower visitor pressure, pleasant walking conditions, colourful landscapes, and spa travel.', 2578),
  ('czech', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Winter', NULL, 'months: December January February weather: Cold across the country, with temperatures commonly around or below freezing and colder conditions in mountain regions. Snow is most reliable in higher areas, while Prague and lowland cities can experience a mixture of snow, rain, frost, and cloudy weather. crowd_level: LOW → HIGH price_level: LOW → HIGH overall_score: 67–79 recommended: true reason: Excellent for: December gains strong festive appeal but Prague can become busy around Advent, Christmas, and New Year. January and February are quieter in cities but are peak ski-season months in Czech mountain regions. Official Czech tourism notes that mountain tourism peaks particularly in January and February and highlights skiing, cross-country skiing, winter hiking, snowshoeing, and other winter activities across Czechia.', 2579),
  ('czech', 10, 'budget-strategy', 'BUDGET STRATEGY', NULL, NULL, 'Where money can be saved: Where saving money is usually NOT recommended: Travel-agent rule: In the Czech Republic, **HOTEL_LOCATION + NATIONAL_RAIL + TICKET_PASSES + TRADITIONAL_PUB_DINING should be evaluated together**. For short stays, prioritize **PRAGUE + ONE_DAY_TRIP (KUTNÁ HORA / KARLOVY VARY)**. For longer stays, add **ČESKÝ KRUMLOV + MORAVIAN_WINE_REGION + BOHEMIAN_SWITZERLAND** rather than changing hotels every single night.', 2580),
  ('czech', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Family', 'family', 'Prague Václav Havel Airport (PRG) is the primary international gateway. For families arriving with young children, stroller equipment, or heavy luggage, pre-booked private transfers or app-booked rides (Uber / Bolt) directly to hotel doors provide the most comfortable transition. When traveling between major towns, the dense national rail network (České dráhy, RegioJet) is far more spacious and kid-friendly than long-distance driving.', 2581),
  ('czech', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Honeymoon', 'honeymoon', 'Opt for private chauffeured transfers directly from PRG airport arrival halls to boutique heritage hotels in Old Town Prague or luxury spa resorts in Karlovy Vary. For multi-destination honeymoon itineraries, combine: PRIVATE_AIRPORT_TRANSFER + FIRST_CLASS_REGIOJET_OR_CD_RAIL + SCENIC_CHÂTEAU_OR_SPA_TRANSFERS.', 2582),
  ('czech', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Luxury', 'luxury', 'Utilize private chauffeured luxury sedans or VIP transfers from Prague Airport directly to 5-star properties, historic châteaux, or West Bohemian spa colonnades. For complex luxury country circuits, combine: VIP_AIRPORT_MEET_AND_GREET + PRIVATE_CHAUFFEUR_TRANSFERS + PRIVATE_BOAT_CHARTERS (Vltava River / Lipno Lake).', 2583),
  ('czech', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Budget', 'budget', 'Take advantage of direct public transit connections connecting Václav Havel Airport to the city center: For regional transit, use national train and bus connections via the integrated IDOS platform.', 2584),
  ('czech', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Senior', 'senior', 'Prioritize direct door-to-door private transfers or app-based taxis to avoid handling heavy luggage over historic cobblestone streets. When using rail, choose direct trains (IC, EC, Railjet) with reserved seating and select centrally located hotels within flat walking distance of major sights or low-floor tram stops.', 2585),
  ('czech', 18, 'family-travel', 'FAMILY TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'child_friendly_score: 93 best_ages: Rules: For young children: Prefer: Avoid: Official tourism specifically promotes interactive museums, puppet culture, river activities, castles, and family parks throughout the Czech Republic.', 2586),
  ('czech', 19, 'honeymoon-travel', 'HONEYMOON TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'honeymoon_score: 91 romance_score: 93 privacy_score: 88 luxury_score: 85 Recommended: Honeymoon itineraries should generally stay at: 2–3 major experiences/day. Prefer: HISTORIC_CITIES + FAIRYTALE_CASTLES + SPA_WELLNESS + MORAVIAN_WINE + ROMANTIC_STAYS + FREE_TIME over: Constant sightseeing and excessive hotel changes. Recommended areas: The Czech Republic''s official tourism guidance specifically promotes honeymoons combining romantic cities, fairytale castles, spa towns, wine regions, and seamless rail connections.', 2587),
  ('czech', 20, 'luxury-travel', 'LUXURY TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'luxury_score: 85 Recommended: Czech luxury travel should focus on: Luxury value is especially strong in Prague''s Malá Strana, Karlovy Vary, luxury rural châteaux, and private wine estate tours in Moravia.', 2588),
  ('czech', 21, 'adventure', 'ADVENTURE', NULL, NULL, 'adventure_score: 86 The Czech Republic offers varied low-to-mid-altitude outdoor adventure across sandstone rock cities, mountain ranges, river gorges, and national parks. Adventure experiences: Best regions: BOHEMIAN_SWITZERLAND + BOHEMIAN_PARADISE + KRKONOŠE_MOUNTAINS + MORAVIAN_KARST + ŠUMAVA_NATIONAL_PARK + VLTAVA_RIVER Match activities to season, weather, fitness level, and trail difficulty.', 2589),
  ('czech', 22, 'senior-travel', 'SENIOR TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'senior_suitability: 88 walking_intensity: LOW–MEDIUM for city tours, river cruises, spa colonnades, rail travel, and château gardens MEDIUM–HIGH for historic cobblestone quarters, castle hill climbs, and rock city hiking routes Rules: The Czech Republic works particularly well for seniors as a: CULTURE + CASTLES + SPA_WELLNESS + CLASSICAL_MUSIC + RAIL + RELAXATION destination. Official Czech tourism highlights accessible cultural sites, historic spa towns, classical concerts, scenic trains, and relaxed travel for older visitors.', 2590),
  ('czech', 23, 'accessibility', 'ACCESSIBILITY', NULL, NULL, 'wheelchair_accessibility: GOOD → VERY_GOOD IN MODERN TRANSIT / MAJOR TOURISM FACILITIES VARIABLE IN HISTORIC COBBLESTONE QUARTERS, ANCIENT CASTLES, AND NATURAL TRAIL ENVIRONMENTS public_transport_accessibility: GOOD → VERY_GOOD overall; low-floor trams, accessible Metro stations, and modern trains widely available hotel_accessibility: MUST_BE_VERIFIED_PER_HOTEL attraction_accessibility: MUST_BE_VERIFIED_PER_ATTRACTION Rule: Never assume universal accessibility across historic European sites. Additional notes: Official Czech tourism reports hundreds of accessible accommodations, cultural venues, spa facilities, and transportation services across the country.', 2591),
  ('czech', 24, 'food', 'FOOD', NULL, NULL, 'The Czech Republic is particularly strong for: Food experiences: Family: Prioritize casual gastro-pubs, open-faced sandwich shops (*chlebíčky*), pastries, riverbank markets, and family-friendly pizza/Czech eateries. Honeymoon: Choose fine dining with skyline views, historic vaulted wine cellars, riverside dining, and intimate cafés. Luxury: Include Michelin-recommended dining, private wine estate cellar tastings, gourmet chef table experiences, and 5-star hotel dining. Budget: Use weekday pub lunch specials (*denní menu*), traditional local pubs, bakeries, markets, and casual self-service cafeterias (*jídelna*).', 2592),
  ('czech', 25, 'shopping', 'SHOPPING', NULL, NULL, 'Strong categories: Luxury shopping: Prefer: The Czech Republic combines luxury retail along Pařížská Street with traditional craft shops, crystal galleries, and regional artisan markets. Budget: Prefer: Travel-agent rule: Use PRAGUE PAŘÍŽSKÁ for LUXURY + FASHION, PRAGUE OLD TOWN / LESSER TOWN for CRYSTAL + GARNETS + MARIONETTES, KARLOVY VARY for SPA_WAFERS + BECHEROVKA + MOSER_GLASS, and SOUTH MORAVIA for WINE + REGIONAL_CRAFTS.', 2593),
  ('czech', 26, 'nightlife', 'NIGHTLIFE', NULL, NULL, 'nightlife_level: 92 Suitable for: Best areas: Evening activities: Prague and Brno offer high-density nightlife ranging from centuries-old beer halls and world-class cocktail bars to live jazz and opera, while regional cities focus on authentic pub culture and student nightlife. Honeymoon travelers should generally prefer: ROOFTOP_COCKTAILS + LIVE_JAZZ + CLASSICAL_CONCERTS + RIVERSIDE_WALKS over: Late-night tourist club circuits. Travel-agent rule: Position the Czech Republic as a **WORLD_CLASS_BEER_HALLS + SPEAKEASY_BARS + LIVE_JAZZ_AND_OPERA + LATE_NIGHT_SOCIAL DESTINATION**, with nightlife style adjusted by region and traveler type.', 2594),
  ('czech', 28, 'sample-itinerary-patterns', 'SAMPLE ITINERARY PATTERNS', '3 NIGHTS', NULL, '### Day 1 Arrival at Prague → Hotel check-in → Relax and refresh Afternoon: → Old Town Square → Astronomical Clock → Jewish Quarter (Josefov) → Wenceslas Square Evening: → Czech tavern dinner & local beer → Sunset at Charles Bridge → Hotel Prague is the Czech Republic''s strongest short-stay cultural base, combining royal Gothic architecture, historic cobblestone streets, vibrant beer halls, and rich European heritage. ### Day 2 Morning: Breakfast → Prague Castle complex → St. Vitus Cathedral → Golden Lane Afternoon: → Malá Strana (Lesser Town) → St. Nicholas Church → Lennon Wall & Kampa Island Evening: → Traditional Czech goulash dinner → Classical music concert or Black Light Theatre → Hotel ### Day 3 Recommended first-time option: → Morning express train to Český Krumlov (or Kutná Hora) → Luggage drop / explore Afternoon: → State Castle & Chateau → Historic Centre & Vltava river bend → Cathedral of St. Barbara (if Kutná Hora) Evening: → Riverside dinner → Evening castle grounds stroll → Hotel Prague and regional UNESCO heritage hubs like Český Krumlov or Kutná Hora are efficiently connected by train or express bus, offering the ultimate Czech first-time combination. Optional alternative instead of Český Krumlov / Regional Excursions: CULTURE / HISTORY: → Kutná Hora day trip → Sedlec Ossuary (Bone Church) → St. Barbara’s Church → Historic Silver Mine SPA / LEISURE: → Karlovy Vary → Thermal colonnades → Mineral springs → Moser glassworks FAMILY: → Petřín Hill & Lookout Tower → Vltava pedal boats → Prague Zoo → DinoPark / Mirror Maze HONEYMOON: → Boutique hotel in Malá Strana → Vltava sunset river cruise → Romantic dining in Kampa → Moravian wine bar evening FOOD & DRINK: → Traditional Czech pubs (Hospoda) → Pilsner Urquell beer hall tour → Manifesto Market → Classic Bohemian pastries (Trdelník) For only 3 nights, prioritize: PRAGUE + ONE_NEARBY_HERITAGE_EXCURSION (Český Krumlov / Kutná Hora / Karlovy Vary) OR PRAGUE_IN-DEPTH (Exploring Vinohrady, Karlín, and Vyšehrad) rather than trying to cover distant regions across Central Europe. ### Day 4 Breakfast → Leisure morning → Optional shopping along Pařížská street / café walk → Hotel checkout → Airport transfer → Departure', 2595),
  ('czech', 29, 'six-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 1', NULL, 'Arrival at Prague → Romantic hotel check-in → Relax and refresh Evening: → Old Town Square → Astronomical Clock → Charles Bridge → Romantic dinner → Overnight at Prague', 2596),
  ('czech', 29, 'six-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 2', NULL, 'Breakfast at the hotel Morning: → Prague Castle → St. Vitus Cathedral → Malá Strana Afternoon: → Kampa Island → Petřín Hill → Couple photography Evening: → Romantic Vltava River cruise → Overnight at Prague', 2597),
  ('czech', 29, 'six-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 3', NULL, 'Breakfast → Romantic Český Krumlov excursion → Český Krumlov Castle → UNESCO Old Town → Vltava riverfront → Castle viewpoints → Couple photography Evening: → Romantic dinner → Overnight at Český Krumlov', 2598),
  ('czech', 29, 'six-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 4', NULL, 'Breakfast → Leisure morning → Historic streets + castle gardens → Hotel checkout → Transfer to Prague Afternoon: → Café / shopping time → Free time Evening: → Rooftop / fine dining → Overnight at Prague', 2599);
INSERT INTO destination_guidance (place_id, section, topic, section_title, heading, audience, body, position) VALUES
  ('czech', 29, 'six-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 5', NULL, 'Breakfast → Hotel checkout → Train / transfer to Vienna → Romantic hotel check-in Afternoon: → Vienna historic centre → St. Stephen''s Cathedral → Kärntner Straße Evening: → Romantic dinner → Overnight at Vienna', 2600),
  ('czech', 29, 'six-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 6', NULL, 'Breakfast Morning: → Schönbrunn Palace → Palace gardens → Couple photography Afternoon: → Vienna city sightseeing → Café experience → Leisure time Evening: → Danube cruise / special farewell dinner → Overnight at Vienna', 2601),
  ('czech', 29, 'six-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 7', NULL, 'Breakfast → Leisure morning → Hotel checkout → Vienna Airport → Departure', 2602),
  ('czech', 30, 'six-nights-family-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 1', NULL, 'Arrival at Prague → Private airport transfer → Family hotel check-in → Relax and refresh Evening: → Old Town Square → Astronomical Clock → Charles Bridge → Family dinner → Overnight at Prague', 2603),
  ('czech', 30, 'six-nights-family-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 2', NULL, 'Breakfast at the hotel Morning: → Prague Castle → St. Vitus Cathedral → Golden Lane → Lesser Town Afternoon: → Prague Hop-on Hop-off sightseeing → Old Town → Wenceslas Square → Leisure time Evening: → Vltava River cruise → Family dinner → Overnight at Prague', 2604),
  ('czech', 30, 'six-nights-family-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 3', NULL, 'Breakfast → Český Krumlov day excursion → Český Krumlov Old Town → Český Krumlov Castle area → Historic streets → Vltava riverfront → Family photography → Leisure time Evening: → Return to Prague → Relaxed family dinner → Overnight at Prague', 2605),
  ('czech', 30, 'six-nights-family-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 4', NULL, 'Breakfast Morning: Choose ONE: FAMILY_FUN: → Prague Zoo → Family activities → Leisure time OR CULTURE: → Jewish Quarter → Old Town exploration → Local shopping Afternoon: → Petrin Hill → Family leisure time → Souvenir shopping Evening: → Free time → Overnight at Prague', 2606),
  ('czech', 30, 'six-nights-family-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 5', NULL, 'Breakfast → Hotel checkout → Train / private transfer to Vienna → Family hotel check-in Afternoon: → Schönbrunn Palace → Schönbrunn Gardens → Family photography Evening: → Vienna city centre → Family dinner → Overnight at Vienna', 2607),
  ('czech', 30, 'six-nights-family-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 6', NULL, 'Breakfast Morning: → Vienna Hop-on Hop-off sightseeing → Ringstrasse → Hofburg area → St. Stephen''s Cathedral Afternoon: → Danube / city leisure time → Optional Danube cruise → Shopping / café time Evening: → Relaxed family dinner → Overnight at Vienna', 2608),
  ('czech', 30, 'six-nights-family-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 7', NULL, 'Breakfast → Leisure morning → Optional souvenir shopping → Hotel checkout → Vienna Airport → Departure', 2609),
  ('czech', 31, 'six-nights-luxury-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 1', NULL, 'Arrival at Prague → Private luxury airport transfer → Premium hotel check-in → Relax and refresh Evening: → Private Old Town orientation → Old Town Square → Astronomical Clock → Charles Bridge → Fine-dining experience → Overnight at Prague', 2610),
  ('czech', 31, 'six-nights-luxury-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 2', NULL, 'Breakfast at the hotel Morning: → Private Prague city tour → Prague Castle → St. Vitus Cathedral → Golden Lane → Lesser Town Afternoon: → Leisure lunch → Old Town → Wenceslas Square → Luxury shopping / café time Evening: → Premium Vltava River cruise → Fine dining → Overnight at Prague', 2611),
  ('czech', 31, 'six-nights-luxury-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 3', NULL, 'Breakfast → Private excursion to Český Krumlov → Český Krumlov Castle area → Historic Old Town → Heritage streets → Vltava riverfront → Scenic photography Afternoon: → Refined local lunch → Leisure exploration → Private transfer back to Prague Evening: → Relax at the hotel → Optional fine dining → Overnight at Prague', 2612),
  ('czech', 31, 'six-nights-luxury-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 4', NULL, 'Breakfast Morning: Choose ONE: HERITAGE: → Private Jewish Quarter tour → Old Town architecture → Historic Prague experience OR LEISURE: → Late breakfast → Luxury shopping → Spa / wellness experience → Premium café experience Afternoon: → Petrin Hill → Lesser Town → Private leisure time Evening: → Optional classical concert / cultural performance → Fine-dining experience → Overnight at Prague', 2613),
  ('czech', 31, 'six-nights-luxury-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 5', NULL, 'Breakfast → Hotel checkout → First-class train / private transfer to Vienna → Premium hotel check-in Afternoon: → Schönbrunn Palace → Schönbrunn Gardens → Private guided experience → Leisure time Evening: → Vienna historic centre → Premium dining → Overnight at Vienna', 2614),
  ('czech', 31, 'six-nights-luxury-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 6', NULL, 'Breakfast Morning: → Private Vienna city tour → Ringstrasse → Hofburg area → St. Stephen''s Cathedral → Historic city centre Afternoon: Choose ONE: CULTURE: → Premium museum / palace experience → Traditional Viennese café OR LEISURE: → Luxury shopping → Spa / hotel leisure → Café experience Evening: → Private / premium Danube cruise → Farewell fine-dining experience → Overnight at Vienna', 2615),
  ('czech', 31, 'six-nights-luxury-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 7', NULL, 'Breakfast → Leisure morning → Optional luxury shopping → Hotel checkout → Private transfer to Vienna Airport → Departure', 2616),
  ('czech', 32, 'travel-agent-insights', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS', 'What inexperienced planners often do wrong', NULL, '', 2617),
  ('czech', 32, 'travel-agent-insights', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS', 'What an experienced planner does differently', NULL, '', 2618),
  ('czech', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', NULL, NULL, 'IF: trip_length <= 4 nights THEN: prioritize_PRAGUE + ONE_DAY_EXCURSION Reason: Prague alone has enough heritage, architecture, culture and leisure for a short first-time visit. IF: trip_length >= 6 nights AND: traveler_interest == FIRST_TIME_CZECHIA THEN: prioritize_PRAGUE + ČESKÝ_KRUMLOV + ONE_OF_KUTNÁ_HORA_OR_KARLOVY_VARY IF: traveler_type == FAMILY THEN: prefer_PRAGUE + ČESKÝ_KRUMLOV AND: include_CASTLES + PARKS + INTERACTIVE_ATTRACTIONS + RIVER_EXPERIENCES AND: reduce_MUSEUM_DENSITY + LONG_WALKING_DAYS IF: traveler_type == LUXURY THEN: prefer_PRAGUE + KARLOVY_VARY_OR_MARIÁNSKÉ_LÁZNĚ AND: increase_5_STAR_HOTELS + PRIVATE_GUIDES + SPA + FINE_DINING + PRIVATE_TRANSFERS IF: trip_type == HONEYMOON THEN: prefer_PRAGUE + ČESKÝ_KRUMLOV + SPA_OR_COUNTRYSIDE AND: increase_BOUTIQUE_STAYS + SCENIC_DINING + SPA + FREE_TIME + ROMANTIC_EVENINGS IF: traveler_interest == CULTURE_AND_HERITAGE THEN: prioritize_PRAGUE + ČESKÝ_KRUMLOV + KUTNÁ_HORA AND: include_PRAGUE_CASTLE + OLD_TOWN + ST_BARBARAS_CATHEDRAL + HISTORIC_CENTRES IF: traveler_interest == SPA_AND_WELLNESS THEN: prefer_KARLOVY_VARY + MARIÁNSKÉ_LÁZNĚ AND: include_SPA + COLONNADES + WELLNESS + LEISURE_TIME IF: traveler_interest == WINE_AND_GASTRONOMY THEN: prefer_PRAGUE + SOUTH_MORAVIA AND: include_LOCAL_CUISINE + MORAVIAN_WINE + CELLARS + REGIONAL_DINING IF: trip_length <= 7 nights THEN: prefer_MAXIMUM_TWO_OR_THREE_BASES AND: avoid_EXCESSIVE_HOTEL_CHANGES IF: traveler_type == SENIOR OR: traveler_mobility == LIMITED THEN: prefer_CENTRAL_HOTELS + PRIVATE_TRANSFERS_WHEN_USEFUL + MODERATE_SIGHTSEEING AND: reduce_STEEP_CASTLE_ROUTES + COBBLESTONE_WALKING + RAPID_CITY_CHANGES IF: traveler_interest == FIRST_TIME_CZECHIA THEN: prioritize_PRAGUE AND: add_ONE_OF_ČESKÝ_KRUMLOV_KUTNÁ_HORA_KARLOVY_VARY AND: include_ONE_SIGNATURE_CZECH_FOOD_CULTURE_OR_RIVER_EXPERIENCE', 2619),
  ('czech', 34, 'destination-scoring', 'DESTINATION SCORING', NULL, NULL, '| Factor | Score | | ------------------ | ----: | | Family | 93 | | Honeymoon | 91 | | Luxury | 85 | | Budget | 92 | | Adventure | 86 | | Culture | 97 | | Food | 89 | | Shopping | 84 | | Nightlife | 92 | | Relaxation | 91 | | Nature | 88 | | Accessibility | 82 | | Safety | 94 | | First-time visitor | 96 | | Photography | 96 |', 2620),
  ('czech', 35, 'final-travel-agent-verdict', 'FINAL TRAVEL AGENT VERDICT', NULL, NULL, 'Best traveler profiles: 1. Culture / heritage traveler 2. First-time Europe traveler 3. Architecture / photography traveler 4. Romantic / honeymoon traveler 5. Spa / wellness traveler 6. Food / beer / wine traveler 7. Family traveler 8. Luxury traveler 9. Nature / active traveler 10. City-break traveler Best duration: 6–9 nights 3–4 nights: Best for PRAGUE + one nearby excursion such as Kutná Hora. 5–7 nights: Best for PRAGUE + ČESKÝ_KRUMLOV / KARLOVY_VARY. 8–10 nights: Excellent for PRAGUE + SOUTH_BOHEMIA + WEST_BOHEMIA / SOUTH_MORAVIA. 11–14 nights: Best for deeper regional travel, spa towns, Moravia, castles, wine regions and nature. Best season: YEAR-ROUND Spring: CITIES + CASTLES + NATURE + WALKING + PHOTOGRAPHY. Summer: HERITAGE_TOWNS + FESTIVALS + COUNTRYSIDE + HIKING + CYCLING. Autumn: CULTURE + WINE + GASTRONOMY + SPA + NATURE + PHOTOGRAPHY. Winter: PRAGUE + CHRISTMAS_MARKETS + SPA + CULTURE + MOUNTAIN_SPORTS. Best hotel strategy: For first-time visitors: PRAGUE as the primary base. For deeper itineraries: Add ČESKÝ_KRUMLOV + KARLOVY_VARY / SOUTH_MORAVIA selectively. For spa / luxury: Prefer KARLOVY_VARY + MARIÁNSKÉ_LÁZNĚ premium spa hotels. For honeymoon: Use boutique historic hotels + scenic regional stays. Avoid unnecessary hotel changes on short itineraries. Best transportation: Use: Czechia should primarily be treated as: PRAGUE_PUBLIC_TRANSPORT_FIRST + RAIL_INTERCITY + BUS_SELECTIVE + CAR_FOR_REGIONAL_EXPLORATION Must-do for first-time visitor: Don''t-do: Biggest advantage: High concentration of major experiences within a relatively compact country. Czechia combines PRAGUE + UNESCO_HERITAGE + CASTLES + SPA_TOWNS + GASTRONOMY + BEER + MORAVIAN_WINE + HISTORIC_TOWNS + NATURE with relatively efficient domestic travel. Biggest disadvantage: Prague can become heavily crowded, while regional castles, attractions and outdoor experiences can be more seasonal. Historic centres also involve cobblestones, slopes and older buildings that can complicate accessibility. Overall destination score: 92/100', 2621),
  ('czech', 36, 'data-quality', 'DATA QUALITY', NULL, NULL, 'information_completeness: 96/100 last_updated: 2026-08-28 last_verified: WEB_VERIFIED verified_by: CZECHTOURISM / VISITCZECHIA / PRAGUE CITY TOURISM / ČESKÉ DRÁHY / PRAGUE INTEGRATED TRANSPORT sources: IMPORTANT: Hotel rates, train / bus schedules, attraction tickets, castle opening periods, festivals, spa services and restaurant availability must NOT be treated as permanently valid. PRAGUE_CASTLE + major monuments + popular tours can require advance planning during peak periods. Many Czech castles and châteaux operate seasonally or with reduced winter access. Spring and autumn generally provide the strongest balance for city sightseeing, walking and regional exploration. SUMMER is the principal high-tourism period. Historic centres may contain COBBLESTONES + STAIRS + SLOPES + LIMITED_ACCESSIBILITY. Rail and public transport are major planning advantages, but actual schedules and disruptions should always be checked. Czechia should primarily be treated as: SPRING: CITIES + CASTLES + NATURE + PHOTOGRAPHY SUMMER: HERITAGE + FESTIVALS + HIKING + CYCLING + COUNTRYSIDE AUTUMN: CULTURE + WINE + GASTRONOMY + SPA + NATURE WINTER: PRAGUE + CHRISTMAS + SPA + CULTURE + WINTER_SPORTS CzechTourism, Prague City Tourism, České dráhy, PID, regional tourism authorities and individual attractions should be treated as primary sources for current operational information. This dataset should be refreshed regularly before production use.', 2622),
  ('hungery', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Spring', NULL, 'months: March April May weather: Cool and variable in March, increasingly mild in April, and pleasantly warm by May. Spring is comfortable for city touring, although May is typically one of the wetter months nationally. crowd_level: LOW → MEDIUM price_level: LOW → MEDIUM overall_score: 81–83 recommended: true reason: One of Hungary''s strongest periods for Budapest, historic towns, thermal spas, Danube Bend, Lake Balaton, cycling, countryside, culture, and outdoor sightseeing before peak summer demand. Best for: Official Hungarian tourism highlights spring for pleasant city walks, terraces, cultural festivals, and renewed green landscapes.', 2623),
  ('hungery', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Summer', NULL, 'months: June July August weather: Warm to hot with long daylight hours and abundant sunshine. July and August are the warmest months, averaging about 22°C nationally, with average daytime maxima around 29°C and temperatures around or above 30°C common during hot periods. crowd_level: HIGH → VERY_HIGH price_level: MEDIUM_HIGH → HIGH overall_score: 63–76 recommended: true reason: Excellent for: Best for Lake Balaton, festivals, outdoor activities, and summer nightlife, but July and August bring stronger demand, higher prices, and potentially uncomfortable heat for intensive Budapest sightseeing. Official tourism identifies late July and early August as Hungary''s hottest period, while Lake Balaton becomes one of the country''s principal summer holiday regions.', 2624),
  ('hungery', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Autumn', NULL, 'months: September October November weather: September remains warm and often summer-like, October is cooler with attractive autumn colour, while November becomes noticeably colder, cloudier, and more changeable. crowd_level: MEDIUM → VERY_LOW price_level: MEDIUM → LOW overall_score: 80–84 recommended: true reason: September and October provide Hungary''s strongest overall combination of comfortable weather, Budapest sightseeing, wine harvests, Lake Balaton, historic towns, thermal spas, hiking, gastronomy, and lower visitor pressure. Best for: Official Hungarian tourism describes autumn as particularly enjoyable because days can still retain summer warmth while rainfall probability is generally lower than in spring. Harvest and wine experiences are also a major seasonal strength.', 2625),
  ('hungery', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Winter', NULL, 'months: December January February weather: Cold, with January the coldest month at around 0°C nationally and average minimum temperatures near -3°C. Frost, fog, occasional snow, and short daylight are common, although consistent snow cannot be guaranteed outside higher areas. crowd_level: LOW → MEDIUM price_level: LOW → MEDIUM overall_score: 62–76 recommended: true reason: Excellent for: December has strong Advent appeal, while January and February work especially well for thermal baths, museums, gastronomy, wellness, and lower-crowd city breaks. Hungary''s official tourism promotion emphasizes thermal bathing, Advent markets, winter city experiences, and limited snow recreation rather than positioning Hungary as a major snow-reliable ski destination.', 2626),
  ('hungery', 10, 'budget-strategy', 'BUDGET STRATEGY', NULL, NULL, 'Where money can be saved: Where saving money is usually NOT recommended: Travel-agent rule: In Hungary, **CENTRAL_BUDAPEST_HOTEL + BKK_TRANSIT_PASS + ADVANCE_PARLIAMENT_BATH_TICKETS + TRADITIONAL_BISTRO_DINING should be evaluated together**. For short stays, prioritize **BUDAPEST + DANUBE_BEND_DAY_TRIP**. For longer stays, add **LAKE_BALATON + EGER_OR_TOKAJ_WINE_REGION + HÉVÍZ_OR_PÉCS** rather than changing hotels every single night.', 2627),
  ('hungery', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Family', 'family', 'Hungary’s primary international gateway is Budapest Ferenc Liszt International Airport (BUD), supplemented by Debrecen International Airport (DEB) in the east. For families arriving with young children, strollers, or substantial luggage, pre-booked private transfers, official Főtaxi services (booked via kiosks directly outside BUD arrivals), or ride-hailing apps (Bolt) provide the smoothest transition to city accommodations. When traveling between major tourist hubs with kids, direct MÁV InterCity trains (e.g., Budapest to Lake Balaton, Eger, or Pécs) offer spacious, comfortable carriage seating that avoids highway traffic delays.', 2628),
  ('hungery', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Honeymoon', 'honeymoon', 'Opt for pre-arranged private luxury driver transfers directly from airport arrival halls to boutique Danube-facing luxury hotels, Tokaj wine estate manors, or Lake Balaton spa resorts. For multi-destination honeymoon itineraries, combine: PRIVATE_AIRPORT_TRANSFER + FIRST_CLASS_MÁV_INTERCITY_RAIL (Budapest–Tokaj or Budapest–Lake Balaton corridor) + PRIVATE_CHAUFFEUR_FOR_WINE_ESTATES_AND_THERMAL_PALACES.', 2629),
  ('hungery', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Luxury', 'luxury', 'Utilize pre-booked private chauffeured transfers (e.g., Mercedes-Benz V-Class / S-Class) directly from major airport arrival terminals or private aviation facilities (Budapest BUD General Aviation Terminal). For complex luxury country circuits, combine: VIP_AIRPORT_MEET_AND_GREET + PRIVATE_CHAUFFEUR_TRANSFERS + CHARTERED_HELICOPTER_FLIGHTS (Tokaj Wine Region / Lake Balaton) + PRIVATE_DANUBE_YACHT_OR_SPEEDBOAT_CHARTERS.', 2630),
  ('hungery', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Budget', 'budget', 'Take advantage of Hungary’s efficient and highly affordable public transit directly connecting airport terminals to urban centers: For onward intercity travel, utilize MÁV-Start national rail or regional intercity coaches (Volánbusz).', 2631),
  ('hungery', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Senior', 'senior', 'Prioritize door-to-door pre-booked transfers or ride-hailing apps (Bolt) directly at airport drop-offs to avoid carrying luggage over cobblestoned historic districts. When using intercity rail, book 1st Class or IC+ premium seats on MÁV InterCity trains, arrange luggage assistance, and choose central hotels located on flat streets near main tram or metro lines.', 2632),
  ('hungery', 18, 'family-travel', 'FAMILY TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'child_friendly_score: 92 best_ages: Rules: For young children: Prefer: Avoid: Official tourism promotes interactive water parks, thermal lakes, railway parks, fairytale castles, and countryside family experiences across Hungary.', 2633),
  ('hungery', 19, 'honeymoon-travel', 'HONEYMOON TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'honeymoon_score: 92 romance_score: 94 privacy_score: 90 luxury_score: 88 Recommended: Honeymoon itineraries should generally stay at: 2–3 major experiences/day. Prefer: HISTORIC_TOWNS + PALACES + WINERIES + RURAL_MANORS + LAKE_NATURE + FREE_TIME over: Constant road journeys and daily hotel changes. Recommended areas: Hungary''s tourism appeal for honeymoons combines grand imperial architecture, romantic vineyard manors, lake landscapes, thermal bath palaces, and quiet countryside escapes.', 2634),
  ('hungery', 20, 'luxury-travel', 'LUXURY TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'luxury_score: 86 Recommended: Hungary luxury travel should focus on: Luxury value is particularly strong in Budapest, Lake Balaton resort areas, historic Tokaj wine region, and private countryside retreats.', 2635),
  ('hungery', 21, 'adventure', 'ADVENTURE', NULL, NULL, 'adventure_score: 88 Hungary offers varied adventure travel across cavernous karst networks, low-mountain hiking trails, river basins, and expansive steppe plains. Adventure experiences: Best regions: BÜKK_MOUNTAINS + AGGTELEK_NATIONAL_PARK + LAKE_BALATON_UPLANDS + HORTOBÁGY_NATIONAL_PARK + DANUBE_BEND + LAKE_TISZA Match activities to season, trail conditions, fitness level, and lake weather.', 2636),
  ('hungery', 22, 'senior-travel', 'SENIOR TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'senior_suitability: 89 walking_intensity: LOW–MEDIUM for Budapest tours, museums, train travel, thermal baths, and river cruises MEDIUM–HIGH for historic castle hill slopes, cobbled towns, cave walking, and vineyard paths Rules: Hungary works particularly well for seniors as a: PALACES + HERITAGE + SPA_WELLNESS + SCENIC_CRUISES + RELAXATION destination. Official Hungary tourism highlights accessible cultural sites, historic thermal bath palaces, scenic river routes, traditional arts, and relaxed countryside travel for older visitors.', 2637),
  ('hungery', 23, 'accessibility', 'ACCESSIBILITY', NULL, NULL, 'wheelchair_accessibility: VARIABLE IN MODERN / MAJOR TOURISM FACILITIES LIMITED IN HISTORIC CASTLES, COBBLED TOWNS, AND CAVE NETWORKS public_transport_accessibility: MODERATE overall; metro/trams vary by station hotel_accessibility: MUST_BE_VERIFIED_PER_HOTEL attraction_accessibility: MUST_BE_VERIFIED_PER_ATTRACTION Rule: Never assume universal accessibility across Hungary. Additional notes: Tourism authorities are expanding accessible infrastructure, but historic and rural sights require advance verification.', 2638),
  ('hungery', 24, 'food', 'FOOD', NULL, NULL, 'Hungary is particularly strong for: Food experiences: Family: Prioritize kürtőskalács, lángos, csirkepaprikás, palacsinta, market stalls, and casual traditional bistros. Honeymoon: Choose winery dining, fine Hungarian cuisine, private manor meals, and cozy cellar taverns. Luxury: Include fine-dining Budapest spots, private estate wine pairings, and bespoke chef menus. Budget: Use daily *napi menü*, street bakeries (*pékség*), market halls, and casual canteens.', 2639),
  ('hungery', 25, 'shopping', 'SHOPPING', NULL, NULL, 'Strong categories: Luxury shopping: Prefer: Hungary combines modern city avenues with rich traditional handicrafts, folk textiles, and regional food products. Budget: Prefer: Travel-agent rule: Use BUDAPEST for LUXURY + FASHION, SZENTENDRE / PÉCS for CRAFTS + SOUVENIRS, HOLLÓKŐ / MEZŐKÖVESD for FOLK_ART, and TOKAJ / EGER for WINE + LOCAL_PRODUCTS.', 2640),
  ('hungery', 26, 'nightlife', 'NIGHTLIFE', NULL, NULL, 'nightlife_level: 92 Suitable for: Best areas: Evening activities: Budapest delivers world-famous ruin bar nightlife and music festivals, Siófok provides high-energy summer lake parties, while regional historical cities offer relaxed wine and pub scenes. Honeymoon travelers should generally prefer: ROOFTOP_LOUNGES + WINE_BARS + CASUAL_TERRACES + EVENING_STROLLS over: All-night clubbing. Travel-agent rule: Position Hungary as a **RUIN_BARS + CRAFT_BEER + WINE_CELLARS + SUMMER_LAKE_CLUBS + FESTIVAL DESTINATION**, with nightlife intensity adjusted by region and traveler type.', 2641),
  ('hungery', 28, 'sample-itinerary-patterns', 'SAMPLE ITINERARY PATTERNS', '3 NIGHTS', NULL, '### Day 1 Arrival at Budapest Ferenc Liszt International Airport (BUD) → Direct 100E Airport Express bus / transfer to city center → Hotel check-in → Relax and refresh Afternoon: → Hungarian Parliament Building (Országház) → Shoes on the Danube Bank Memorial → Széchenyi Chain Bridge → St. Stephen''s Basilica (Szent István-bazilika) & St. Stephen''s Square Evening: → Traditional dinner (Gulyás / Pörkölt) → Ruin bar experience in District VII (Jewish Quarter, e.g., Szimpla Kert) → Hotel Budapest is Hungary''s strongest short-stay cultural base, combining grand imperial Austro-Hungarian architecture, Danube waterfront vistas, vibrant historic quarter life, and thermal bath culture. ### Day 2 Morning: Breakfast → Buda Castle Hill & Royal Palace grounds → Matthias Church (Mátyás-templom) → Fisherman''s Bastion (Halászbástya) panoramic lookout Afternoon: → Széchenyi Thermal Bath (or Gellért Baths) relaxation → Heroes'' Square (Hősök tere) & City Park (Városliget) exploration Evening: → Traditional dinner at historic bistro (e.g., Gettó Gulyás or Rosenstein) → Danube Evening River Cruise (illuminated Parliament and bridges view) → Hotel ### Day 3 Recommended first-time option: → MÁV InterCity train / private driver to Danube Bend or Wine Country → Arrive in Szentendre, Visegrád, or Eger Afternoon: → Szentendre cobblestone artist town & Open-Air Ethnographic Museum → Transfer to Visegrád Citadel (High Castle panoramic river loop view) → Eger Castle & Valley of the Beautiful Woman (Szépasszony-völgy) wine tasting Evening: → Eger wine cellar dinner / return train or driver to Budapest → Hotel Budapest and the Danube Bend / regional wine hubs are efficiently linked by rail and highway, serving as Hungary''s primary first-time combination. Optional alternative instead of Countryside Trips: SPA & WELLNESS: → Széchenyi or Gellért Thermal Bath full-day pass → Thermal mineral soak & massage treatment → Margaret Island (Margitsziget) thermal gardens stroll → Evening dinner in Belváros / Fashion Street CULTURE / HISTORY: → Day trip to Gödöllő Royal Palace (Grassalkovich Palace) → Baroque architecture & Empress Sisi heritage → Palace gardens stroll FAMILY: → Buda Hills Children''s Railway & Chairlift (Zugligeti Libegő) → Aquaworld Budapest water slides → Visegrád medieval bobsled track → Interactive City Park zoo HONEYMOON: → Boutique palace hotel stay → Private couple''s thermal bath suite session → Private driver to Danube Bend castles → Fine dining on Andrássy Avenue or Michelin-starred spots → Relaxed free time FOOD: → Central Market Hall (Nagycsarnok) food walk (Lángos & Paprika) → Historic grand cafes (New York Café / Café Gerbeaud) → Tokaj / Eger wine tasting day excursion → Regional Hungarian csárda cuisine For only 3 nights, prioritize: BUDAPEST + DANUBE_BEND_DAY_TRIP OR BUDAPEST + ONE_NEARBY_HERITAGE_EXCURSION rather than trying to combine several distant Hungarian regions. ### Day 4 Breakfast → Leisure morning → Optional souvenir shopping / Fashion Street walk → Hotel checkout → 100E Airport Express bus / transfer to BUD Airport → Departure', 2642),
  ('hungery', 29, 'seven-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'SEVEN-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 1', NULL, 'Arrival at Budapest → Private airport transfer → Romantic hotel check-in → Relax and refresh Evening: → Danube Promenade → Chain Bridge → Budapest riverfront → Romantic dinner → Overnight at Budapest', 2643),
  ('hungery', 29, 'seven-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'SEVEN-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 2', NULL, 'Breakfast at the hotel Morning: → Budapest Hop-on Hop-off sightseeing → Heroes'' Square → Andrássy Avenue → St. Stephen''s Basilica Afternoon: → Buda Castle District → Fisherman''s Bastion → Matthias Church → Couple photography Evening: → Romantic Danube River cruise → Overnight at Budapest', 2644),
  ('hungery', 29, 'seven-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'SEVEN-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 3', NULL, 'Breakfast Morning: → Hungarian Parliament area → Shoes on the Danube Bank → Leisure sightseeing Afternoon: → Széchenyi Thermal Bath → Couple relaxation → Free time Evening: → Romantic dinner → Overnight at Budapest', 2645),
  ('hungery', 29, 'seven-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'SEVEN-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 4', NULL, 'Breakfast Morning: → Leisure time → Budapest cafés / shopping → Couple photography Afternoon: Choose ONE: ROMANTIC: → Margaret Island → Danube riverside → Relax together OR CULTURE: → Central Market Hall → Jewish Quarter → Hungarian food experience Evening: → Rooftop / fine-dining experience → Overnight at Budapest', 2646),
  ('hungery', 29, 'seven-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'SEVEN-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 5', NULL, 'Breakfast → Hotel checkout → Train to Vienna → Private hotel transfer → Romantic hotel check-in Afternoon: → Vienna city centre → St. Stephen''s Cathedral → Ringstrasse → Leisure time Evening: → Romantic dinner → Overnight at Vienna', 2647),
  ('hungery', 29, 'seven-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'SEVEN-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 6', NULL, 'Breakfast Morning: → Schönbrunn Palace → Schönbrunn Gardens → Couple photography Afternoon: → Vienna Hop-on Hop-off sightseeing → Hofburg area → Historic centre Evening: → Café / romantic dinner → Overnight at Vienna', 2648),
  ('hungery', 29, 'seven-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'SEVEN-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 7', NULL, 'Breakfast → Hotel checkout → Train to Prague → Romantic hotel check-in Afternoon: → Prague Castle → St. Vitus Cathedral → Lesser Town → Charles Bridge Evening: → Vltava River cruise → Romantic farewell dinner → Overnight at Prague', 2649),
  ('hungery', 29, 'seven-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'SEVEN-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 8', NULL, 'Breakfast → Leisure morning → Optional Old Town / souvenir shopping → Hotel checkout → Private transfer to Prague Airport → Departure', 2650),
  ('hungery', 30, 'seven-nights-family-pattern', 'SEVEN-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 1', NULL, 'Arrival at Budapest → Private airport transfer → Family hotel check-in → Relax and refresh Evening: → Danube Promenade → Chain Bridge → Budapest riverfront → Family dinner → Overnight at Budapest', 2651),
  ('hungery', 30, 'seven-nights-family-pattern', 'SEVEN-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 2', NULL, 'Breakfast at the hotel Morning: → Budapest Hop-on Hop-off sightseeing → Heroes'' Square → Andrássy Avenue → St. Stephen''s Basilica Afternoon: → Buda Castle District → Fisherman''s Bastion → Matthias Church → Family photography Evening: → Danube River cruise → Overnight at Budapest', 2652),
  ('hungery', 30, 'seven-nights-family-pattern', 'SEVEN-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 3', NULL, 'Breakfast Morning: → Hungarian Parliament area → Shoes on the Danube Bank → Leisure sightseeing Afternoon: → Széchenyi Thermal Bath → Family relaxation → Leisure time Evening: → Family dinner → Overnight at Budapest', 2653),
  ('hungery', 30, 'seven-nights-family-pattern', 'SEVEN-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 4', NULL, 'Breakfast Morning: Choose ONE: FAMILY_FUN: → Budapest Zoo → City Park → Family activities OR INTERACTIVE: → Children''s Railway → Buda Hills → Scenic family experience Afternoon: → Margaret Island → Leisure time → Family photography Evening: → Free time → Overnight at Budapest', 2654),
  ('hungery', 30, 'seven-nights-family-pattern', 'SEVEN-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 5', NULL, 'Breakfast → Hotel checkout → Train to Vienna → Private hotel transfer → Family hotel check-in Afternoon: → Vienna city centre → St. Stephen''s Cathedral → Ringstrasse → Leisure time Evening: → Family dinner → Overnight at Vienna', 2655),
  ('hungery', 30, 'seven-nights-family-pattern', 'SEVEN-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 6', NULL, 'Breakfast Morning: → Schönbrunn Palace → Schönbrunn Gardens → Family photography Afternoon: → Vienna Hop-on Hop-off sightseeing → Hofburg area → Historic centre Evening: → Leisure time → Overnight at Vienna', 2656),
  ('hungery', 30, 'seven-nights-family-pattern', 'SEVEN-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 7', NULL, 'Breakfast → Hotel checkout → Train to Prague → Family hotel check-in Afternoon: → Prague Castle → St. Vitus Cathedral → Lesser Town → Charles Bridge Evening: → Vltava River cruise → Family dinner → Overnight at Prague', 2657),
  ('hungery', 30, 'seven-nights-family-pattern', 'SEVEN-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 8', NULL, 'Breakfast → Leisure morning → Optional Old Town / souvenir shopping → Hotel checkout → Private transfer to Prague Airport → Departure', 2658),
  ('hungery', 31, 'seven-nights-luxury-pattern', 'SEVEN-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 1', NULL, 'Arrival at Budapest → Private luxury airport transfer → Premium hotel check-in → Relax and refresh Evening: → Danube Promenade → Chain Bridge → Budapest riverfront → Fine-dining experience → Overnight at Budapest', 2659),
  ('hungery', 31, 'seven-nights-luxury-pattern', 'SEVEN-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 2', NULL, 'Breakfast at the hotel Morning: → Private Budapest city tour → Heroes'' Square → Andrássy Avenue → St. Stephen''s Basilica Afternoon: → Buda Castle District → Fisherman''s Bastion → Matthias Church → Scenic photography Evening: → Premium Danube River cruise → Fine dining → Overnight at Budapest', 2660),
  ('hungery', 31, 'seven-nights-luxury-pattern', 'SEVEN-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 3', NULL, 'Breakfast Morning: → Hungarian Parliament area → Historic Budapest sightseeing → Leisure time Afternoon: → Premium thermal bath / spa experience → Wellness and relaxation Evening: → Rooftop / fine-dining experience → Overnight at Budapest', 2661),
  ('hungery', 31, 'seven-nights-luxury-pattern', 'SEVEN-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 4', NULL, 'Breakfast Morning: Choose ONE: LUXURY_LEISURE: → Private spa / wellness → Luxury shopping → Premium café experience OR CULTURE: → Private Jewish Quarter tour → Central Market Hall → Hungarian gastronomy experience Afternoon: → Margaret Island → Private leisure time Evening: → Fine dining → Overnight at Budapest', 2662),
  ('hungery', 31, 'seven-nights-luxury-pattern', 'SEVEN-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 5', NULL, 'Breakfast → Hotel checkout → First-class train / private transfer to Vienna → Premium hotel check-in Afternoon: → Private Vienna city tour → St. Stephen''s Cathedral → Ringstrasse → Hofburg area Evening: → Premium dining → Overnight at Vienna', 2663),
  ('hungery', 31, 'seven-nights-luxury-pattern', 'SEVEN-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 6', NULL, 'Breakfast Morning: → Schönbrunn Palace → Schönbrunn Gardens → Private guided experience Afternoon: → Luxury shopping → Viennese café experience → Leisure time Evening: → Fine dining / classical experience → Overnight at Vienna', 2664),
  ('hungery', 31, 'seven-nights-luxury-pattern', 'SEVEN-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 7', NULL, 'Breakfast → Hotel checkout → First-class train / private transfer to Prague → Premium hotel check-in Afternoon: → Prague Castle → St. Vitus Cathedral → Lesser Town → Charles Bridge Evening: → Premium Vltava River cruise → Farewell fine-dining experience → Overnight at Prague', 2665),
  ('hungery', 31, 'seven-nights-luxury-pattern', 'SEVEN-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 8', NULL, 'Breakfast → Leisure morning → Optional luxury shopping → Hotel checkout → Private transfer to Prague Airport → Departure', 2666),
  ('hungery', 32, 'travel-agent-insights', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS', 'What inexperienced planners often do wrong', NULL, '', 2667),
  ('hungery', 32, 'travel-agent-insights', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS', 'What an experienced planner does differently', NULL, 'BUDAPEST + LAKE_BALATON + ONE_DANUBE_BEND / EGER_OR_PÉCS / HORTOBÁGY_EXPERIENCE rather than maximum destination count.', 2668),
  ('hungery', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', NULL, NULL, 'IF: trip_length <= 4 nights THEN: prioritize_ONE_MAJOR_CITY + ONE_NEARBY_EXCURSION Reason: Very short stays gain more value from properly experiencing one major Hungarian hub and an adjacent landmark than losing time to long regional transfers. IF: trip_length >= 6 nights AND: traveler_interest == FIRST_TIME_HUNGARY THEN: prioritize_BUDAPEST + LAKE_BALATON + ONE_CONTRASTING_REGION Reason: This gives a balanced introduction to imperial architecture, thermal bath culture, medieval castles, lake resorts, and distinct regional traditions. IF: trip_length >= 8 nights AND: traveler_interest == FIRST_TIME_HUNGARY THEN: prefer_BUDAPEST + DANUBE_BEND_AND_BALATON + EGER_OR_HORTOBÁGY AND: use_RAIL_AND_PRIVATE_TRANSFER_OR_RENTAL_CAR_WHERE_PRACTICAL Reason: Budapest, central Transdanubia, and northern wine regions or eastern steppe wetlands offer three completely distinct Hungarian experiences. IF: trip_type == HONEYMOON THEN: prioritize_BUDAPEST + TIHANY_AND_BALATONFÜRED + EGER_OR_BOUTIQUE_TOKAJ AND: increase_BOUTIQUE_STAYS + SCENIC_DINING + THERMAL_SPA_EXPERIENCES + FREE_TIME + COUPLE_EXPERIENCES Reason: Hungary''s strongest romantic routes mix grand imperial spas, lakeside lavender fields, historic castles, luxury wellness, and quiet vineyard estates. IF: traveler_type == FAMILY THEN: prioritize_BUDAPEST + LAKE_BALATON + THERMAL_PARKS_OR_BOBSLED_AND_CAVES AND: include_SZÉCHENYI_OR_PALATINUS + VISEGRÁD_BOBSLED + AGGTELEK_OR_TAPOLCA_CAVES + CITY_PARK_ZOO + CABLE_CARS AND: reduce_MUSEUM_DENSITY + LONG_CONTINUOUS_TRANSFERS Reason: Hungary has exceptional family attractions, including world-famous thermal waterparks, underground cave boat rides, bobsled runs, and interactive zoos. IF: traveler_type == LUXURY THEN: prefer_BUDAPEST + BALATON_UPLANDS + PÉCS_OR_TOKAJ + PRIVATE_HERITAGE_ESTATE AND: increase_5_STAR_HOTELS + PRIVATE_GUIDES + FINE_DINING + PRIVATE_TRANSFERS + HELICOPTER_TOURS + WINE Reason: Hungarian high-end travel relies on private heritage guides, world-class thermal wellness facilities, luxury vineyard manor stays, fine dining, and private transfers. IF: traveler_type == BUDGET THEN: prefer_PUBLIC_TRANSPORT + MÁV_TRAINS + WALKING + WELL_CONNECTED_GUESTHOUSES AND: book_INTERCITY_TRANSPORT_EARLY AND: balance_PAID_ATTRACTIONS_WITH_FREE_CASTLES + PARKS + OLD_TOWNS + HIKING Reason: Hungary offers very high value for budget travelers with affordable intercity passenger rail, budget airline hubs, low attraction entry fees, and vibrant public spaces. IF: traveler_interest == CULTURE_AND_HERITAGE THEN: prioritize_BUDAPEST + VISEGRÁD + EGER + PÉCS + HOLLÓKŐ AND: include_HUNGARIAN_PARLIAMENT + BUDA_CASTLE + ESZTERGOM_BASILICA + EARLY_CHRISTIAN_NECROPOLIS + PAINTED_VILLAGES Reason: These destinations feature Hungary''s dense concentration of royal, Ottoman, Renaissance, and UNESCO World Heritage sites. IF: traveler_interest == ART_AND_ARCHITECTURE THEN: prefer_BUDAPEST + SZEGED + SUBOTICA_BORDER_HUB + KECSKEMÉT + PÉCS AND: include_MUSEUM_OF_FINE_ARTS + HUNGARIAN_PARLIAMENT + SECESSION_ART_NOUVEAU + ZSOLNAY_CULTURAL_QUARTER Reason: This route contrasts Budapest''s neoclassicism and imperial grandiosity with the vibrant Secession/Art Nouveau and ceramics heritage of southern and eastern Hungarian cities. IF: traveler_interest == GASTRONOMY THEN: prefer_BUDAPEST + EGER + PÉCS + VILLÁNY_OR_TOKAJ AND: include_TRADITIONAL_CSÁRDAS + GREAT_MARKET_HALL + REGIONAL_CHEESES + GULYÁS_AND_LÁNGOS + WINE_TASTING + FINE_DINING Reason: Hungarian food culture spans rich regional peasant cooking, paprika-infused dishes, Ottoman and Habsburg influences, central market halls, and legendary historic wine regions. IF: traveler_interest == COAST_AND_WETLANDS THEN: prefer_LAKE_BALATON + LAKE_TISZA + HORTOBÁGY_NATIONAL_PARK AND: match_REGION_TO_SEASON + BOAT_SAFARI_STYLE + RELAXATION_REQUIREMENT Reason: Lake Tisza and Hortobágy provide world-class birdwatching and biosphere tours, while Lake Balaton offers seasonal lakeside resort breaks. IF: traveler_interest == NATURE_AND_WILDLIFE THEN: prioritize_HORTOBÁGY_NATIONAL_PARK + AGGTELEK_NATIONAL_PARK + BÜKK_NATIONAL_PARK AND: do_not_treat_STEPPE_WETLANDS_AND_LIMESTONE_MOUNTAINS_AS_INTERCHANGEABLE Reason: The Hortobágy Puszta focuses on wetland birdwatching, wild horses, and steppe fauna, while the Bükk and Aggtelek national parks center on cave exploration, dense forests, and mountain hiking. IF: traveler_interest == NIGHTLIFE THEN: prefer_BUDAPEST + SZEGED + SIÓFOK_IN_SUMMER AND: match_AREA_TO_PARTY_STYLE + SEASON Reason: Budapest''s Jewish Quarter ruin bars operate year-round, university cities thrive during the academic year, and Siófok on Lake Balaton is the iconic summer lake party hub. IF: traveler_interest == SHOPPING THEN: prioritize_BUDAPEST AND: include_ANDRÁSSY_AVENUE + VÁCI_UTCA + WESTEND_OR_ARENA_MALL + HEREND_CERAMICS + ARTISAN_MARKETS Reason: Budapest concentrates Hungary''s leading international luxury flagships, modern shopping malls, traditional porcelain boutiques, and major market halls. IF: traveler_interest == WINE THEN: prefer_TOKAJ + EGER + VILLÁNY + BADACSONY_OR_SZEKSZÁRD AND: include_WINERY_VISITS + LOCAL_GASTRONOMY AND: use_PRIVATE_DRIVER_OR_ORGANIZED_TRANSFER_WHEN_TASTING Reason: Hungary''s native grape varieties (Tokaji Aszú, Furmint, Egri Bikavér, Kadarka, Kékfrankos) are best experienced at historic estate vineyards with arranged transport. IF: traveler_interest == HIKING_AND_NATURE THEN: prefer_BÜKK_MOUNTAINS + MÁTRA_RANGE + BALATON_UPLANDS + AGGTELEK_CAVES AND: match_ROUTE_TO_FITNESS + ALTITUDE + WEATHER + SEASON Reason: Hungarian hiking offers terrain ranging from volcanic lake-view hills to forest mountain trails, deep limestone caves, and peak vistas. IF: traveler_interest == THERMAL_BATHS_AND_WELLNESS THEN: choose_THERMAL_REGION + SEASONAL_OPENING_WINDOW + BATH_TYPE AND: do_not_treat_HISTORIC_TURKISH_BATHS_AND_MODERN_WATERPARKS_AS_IDENTICAL Reason: Hungary''s thermal springs range from 16th-century Ottoman Turkish bathhouses (Rudas/Király) and grand imperial spas (Széchenyi/Gellért) to subterranean cave baths (Miskolctapolca) and natural thermal lakes (Hévíz). IF: traveler_interest == PHOTOGRAPHY THEN: prefer_FISHERMANS_BASTION + TIHANY_ABBEY + HOLLÓKŐ + HUNYADI_CASTLE_OR_BORY_CASTLE + DANUBE_BEND_VIEWPOINTS AND: prioritize_EARLY_MORNING + GOLDEN_HOUR + BLUE_HOUR Reason: These sites yield dramatic visual contrast between Neo-Romanesque terraces, lavender-covered lake peninsulas, preserved Palóc timber houses, and majestic river bends. IF: trip_length <= 7 nights THEN: prefer_MAXIMUM_TWO_OR_THREE_BASES AND: avoid_EXCESSIVE_HOTEL_CHANGES Reason: Though distances appear compact across the Pannonian plain, secondary roads and regional transfers can still consume valuable sightseeing hours. IF: route == BUDAPEST_TO_SZENTENDRE OR: route == BUDAPEST_TO_GYŐR OR: route == BUDAPEST_TO_EGER THEN: prefer_MÁV_AND_HEV_RAIL_OVER_RENTAL_CAR_FOR_STANDARD_CITY_TRAVEL Reason: Hungary''s HÉV suburban train and main MÁV rail lines link Budapest to Szentendre, Győr, and Eger efficiently, bypassing suburban road congestion. IF: traveler_type == SENIOR OR: traveler_mobility == LIMITED THEN: prefer_CENTRAL_HOTELS + DIRECT_RAIL + PRIVATE_TRANSFER_WHEN_USEFUL + MODERATE_DAILY_SIGHTSEEING AND: reduce_STEEP_HISTORIC_WALKS + EXCESSIVE_STAIRS + RAPID_MULTI_CITY_MOVEMENT Reason: Buda Castle Hill cobbles and citadel slopes can cause fatigue; central accommodation, funiculars, and door-to-door transport ease movement. IF: traveler_uses_WHEELCHAIR THEN: prefer_VERIFIED_ACCESSIBLE_HOTELS + LOW_FLOOR_TRAINS + MODERN_MUSEUMS + ACCESSIBLE_ATTRACTIONS AND: do_not_assume_HISTORIC_CASTLES + MEDIEVAL_CITADELS + TRADITIONAL_VILLAGES + CAVE_TRAILS_ARE_FULLY_STEP_FREE Reason: Modern infrastructure in Budapest is increasingly accessible, but ancient hilltop castles, cobblestone villages, thermal baths, and cave networks frequently feature steps and uneven footing. IF: weather == EXTREME_SUMMER_HEAT AND: region == GREAT_PLAIN_OR_BUDAPEST THEN: prioritize_EARLY_MORNING_SIGHTSEEING + INDOOR_MIDDAY_ACTIVITY + EVENING_EXPERIENCES AND: reduce_MIDDAY_OUTDOOR_WALKING Reason: Hungarian summers can exceed 35°C (95°F); heading to Lake Balaton, climate-controlled museums, or underground caves during midday provides relief. IF: weather == RAINY THEN: increase_MUSEUMS + PALACES + THERMAL_BATHS + GASTRONOMY + CAVE_SYSTEMS AND: reduce_LONG_OUTDOOR_TOURS + MOUNTAIN_HIKE_DEPENDENT_ACTIVITY Reason: Attractions like Széchenyi or Gellért baths, the Hungarian National Gallery, Parliament, indoor market halls, and Tapolca Lake Cave remain unaffected by bad weather. IF: traveler_interest == FIRST_TIME_HUNGARY THEN: prioritize_BUDAPEST + LAKE_BALATON AND: add_ONE_OF_DANUBE_BEND_EGER_PÉCS_OR_HORTOBÁGY AND: include_ONE_SIGNATURE_HUNGARIAN_FOOD_OR_THERMAL_SPA_EXPERIENCE Reason: This structure provides a comprehensive introduction to Hungary''s primary imperial hubs alongside an authentic regional escape. IF: traveler_interest == CULTURE_AND_RELAXATION_BALANCE THEN: allocate_60_TO_70_PERCENT_TO_CORE_SIGHTSEEING AND: allocate_REMAINING_TIME_TO_THERMAL_BATHS + PLAZAS + SPA_WELLNESS + RUIN_BARS_AND_CAFES + SHOPPING + EVENING_WALKS + FREE_TIME', 2669),
  ('hungery', 34, 'destination-scoring', 'DESTINATION SCORING', NULL, NULL, '| Factor | Score | | ------------------ | ----: | | Family | 90 | | Honeymoon | 92 | | Luxury | 88 | | Budget | 91 | | Adventure | 81 | | Culture | 95 | | Food | 92 | | Shopping | 84 | | Nightlife | 92 | | Relaxation | 95 | | Nature | 86 | | Accessibility | 82 | | Safety | 82 | First-time visitor | 94 | | Photography | 94 |', 2670),
  ('hungery', 35, 'final-travel-agent-verdict', 'FINAL TRAVEL AGENT VERDICT', NULL, NULL, 'Best traveler profiles: 1. Culture / heritage traveler 2. First-time Europe traveler 3. Food / wine traveler 4. Family traveler 5. Honeymoon / romantic traveler 6. Lake / river / nature traveler 7. Photography traveler 8. Art / architecture traveler 9. Nightlife / social traveler 10. Nature / active traveler Best duration: 7–10 nights 3–4 nights: Best for ONE major hub such as Budapest + one nearby excursion (e.g., Szentendre, Visegrád, or Royal Palace of Gödöllő). 5–7 nights: Best for TWO major bases such as Budapest + Lake Balaton (Balatonfüred/Tihany) or Budapest + Eger / Pécs. 8–10 nights: Excellent for Budapest + Lake Balaton + Danube Bend / Northern Hungary (Eger & Tokaj) or Hortobágy Puszta. 11–14 nights: Best for deeper regional travel, Tokaj wine region, Hortobágy National Park, Pécs, Szeged, Sopron, Bükk Mountains, or cross-country thermal spa routes. Best season: YEAR-ROUND Spring: CITIES + CULTURE + DANUBE_BEND + NATURE + WALKING + PHOTOGRAPHY. Summer: LAKE_BALATON + LAKE_TISZA + FESTIVALS + NIGHTLIFE + OUTDOOR_SPAS + HIKING. Autumn: CULTURE + GASTRONOMY + HARVEST_WINE_TOURS + CITY_BREAKS + NATURE + BETTER_WEATHER_FOR_WALKING. Winter: BUDAPEST + CHRISTMAS_MARKETS + THERMAL_BATHS (SZÉCHENYI / GELLÉRT) + HISTORIC_CAFES + COVERED_MARKETS. Hungary''s official tourism guidance treats the country as year-round: spring and autumn are particularly suitable for cities, cultural routes, and wine regions; summer for lake resorts, wetlands, and open-air festivals; and winter for atmospheric imperial thermal spas, festive markets, and heritage architecture. Best hotel strategy: Choose accommodation according to region, transport connectivity, and trip purpose. For first-time visitors: BUDAPEST + BALATONFÜRED_OR_TIHANY + OPTIONAL_THIRD_REGIONAL_BASE (e.g., Eger, Pécs, or Szeged). For Lake Balaton: Use BALATONFÜRED / TIHANY / BADACSONY selectively rather than changing hotels for every lakeside resort town. For thermal / wellness / nature: Choose the property carefully according to THERMAL_RESORT + LAKE_TISZA_ECOLOGY + SPA_AND_WELLNESS requirements. For honeymoon / luxury: Prefer historic boutique vineyard estates in Tokaj or Badacsony, 5-star grand palace hotels on the Danube in Budapest, or lakeside wellness retreats. Avoid unnecessary hotel changes simply because secondary regional roads or local rail links can take longer than straight-line distances suggest. Best transportation: Use: Hungary should primarily be treated as: RAIL_FOR_MAIN_CORRIDORS + URBAN_PUBLIC_TRANSPORT + CAR_SELECTIVE_FOR_COUNTRYSIDE + BOATS_FOR_BALATON_AND_DANUBE Must-do for first-time visitor: Hungary should not be reduced to Budapest city breaks alone; official tourism positions IMPERIAL_HERITAGE + THERMAL_BATH_CULTURE + WINE_REGIONS + DANUBE_BEND + LAKE_BALATON + FOLK_TRADITIONS as major national travel pillars. Don''t-do: Biggest advantage: Exceptional structural diversity, world-class thermal water culture, and grand imperial architecture within a compact European nation. Hungary combines Habsburg imperial grandiosity, Roman and Ottoman thermal bath traditions, UNESCO World Heritage folk villages, volcanic lake landscapes, historic wine regions, the Great Plain (Puszta) equestrian culture, and a dynamic contemporary food and nightlife scene. Official tourism highlights the Danube River corridor, Europe''s largest thermal water network, Central Europe''s largest lake (Balaton), and centuries of preserved wine-making heritage, allowing completely different trip profiles in one country. Biggest disadvantage: Centralized transit hubbing around Budapest and regional navigation bottlenecks. While main rail lines radiate effectively from Budapest, direct inter-regional transit between rural towns without returning to the capital can be slow, extreme mid-summer heat across the Great Plain can limit afternoon touring, and mandatory advance booking rules for major national monuments require strict scheduling. Overall destination score: 92/100', 2671),
  ('hungery', 36, 'data-quality', 'DATA QUALITY', NULL, NULL, 'information_completeness: 97/100 last_updated: 2026-08-29 last_verified: WEB_VERIFIED verified_by: VISITHUNGARY.COM / TOURINFORM / MÁV-START / OFFICIAL REGIONAL TOURISM BOARDS sources: IMPORTANT: Hotel rates, train schedules, lake ferry routes, monument tickets, museum operating hours, thermal bath passes, and accessibility must NOT be treated as permanently valid. Major attractions such as HUNGARIAN_PARLIAMENT_BUILDING + BUDA_CASTLE_MUSEUMS + SZÉCHENYI_THERMAL_BATH + GELLÉRT_BATH have specific ticketing, mandatory ID/passport rules, or timed entry; current booking requirements should always be verified. Passenger rail is a convenient planning choice on main routes, but schedules, track updates, and direct connections should be checked on MÁV-START (jegy.mav.hu) for actual travel dates. Hungary''s climate varies significantly by region. BUDAPEST and the GREAT HUNGARIAN PLAIN become very hot in mid-summer. NORTHERN MOUNTAIN REGIONS (Bükk / Mátra) experience winter snowfall and reduced secondary road maintenance. LAKE BALATON ferry and cruise operations depend heavily on seasonal schedules, summer tourist volumes, and weather conditions. Accessible tourism infrastructure is improving across major Hungarian cities, Budapest Ferenc Liszt International Airport, and top modern venues, but historic castles, medieval wine cellars, cobblestone quarters, and natural caves are rarely step-free. Hungary should primarily be treated as: SPRING: CITIES + CULTURE + DANUBE_BEND + NATURE + GASTRONOMY + PHOTOGRAPHY SUMMER: LAKE_BALATON + LAKE_TISZA + WATERSPORTS + FESTIVALS + NIGHTLIFE + OUTDOOR_SPAS AUTUMN: CULTURE + GASTRONOMY + WINE_HARVEST + CITY_BREAKS + NATURE + PHOTOGRAPHY WINTER: BUDAPEST + THERMAL_SPAS + CHRISTMAS_MARKETS + HISTORIC_CAFES + IMPERIAL_ARCHITECTURE VisitHungary.com, MÁV-START, Tourinform, national park authorities, and individual attraction operators should be treated as primary sources for current operational information. This dataset should be refreshed regularly before production use.', 2672),
  ('poland', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Spring', NULL, 'months: March April May weather: Cool and changeable in March, increasingly mild in April, and pleasantly warm by May. Spring sees moderate temperatures across the central plains, with blooming countryside, though late spring (May) brings moderate rainfall nationwide. crowd_level: LOW → MEDIUM price_level: LOW → MEDIUM overall_score: 82–85 recommended: true reason: One of Poland''s strongest periods for historic city walking tours, castle exploration, outdoor sightseeing, nature reserves, cultural festivals, and countryside drives before peak summer crowds. Best for: Official Polish tourism highlights spring for pleasant urban strolls, outdoor café culture, blooming gardens, and lighter tourist volume.', 2673),
  ('poland', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Summer', NULL, 'months: June July August weather: Warm to hot with long daylight hours and abundant sunshine. July and August are the warmest months, with daily averages around 18–25°C nationally, daytime highs regularly hitting 25–30°C, and occasional heatwaves. Summer is also the rainiest season, featuring brief afternoon thunderstorms. crowd_level: HIGH → VERY_HIGH price_level: MEDIUM_HIGH → HIGH overall_score: 72–80 recommended: true reason: Excellent for: Best for Baltic coastal beach resorts, lake sailing, mountain hiking, open-air music festivals, and vibrant outdoor dining. However, July and August bring peak domestic and international crowds, higher prices, and occasional muggy conditions in major cities. Official tourism identifies July and August as Poland''s peak holiday season, with Sopot, the Masurian Lakes, and Zakopane experiencing maximum visitor density.', 2674),
  ('poland', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Autumn', NULL, 'months: September October November weather: September remains mild and pleasant ("Golden Polish Autumn"), October is crisp with striking autumn foliage, while November becomes noticeably colder, gray, wet, and windy as winter approaches. crowd_level: MEDIUM → VERY_LOW price_level: MEDIUM → LOW overall_score: 81–86 recommended: true reason: September and October offer Poland''s finest overall conditions for comfortable city sightseeing, historical excursions, national park hiking, thermal retreats, and wine/craft beer tasting with diminished tourist queues. Best for: Official Polish tourism praises early autumn for mild temperatures, dry weather, stable hiking conditions in mountain ranges, and rich forest colors.', 2675),
  ('poland', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Winter', NULL, 'months: December January February weather: Cold and frosty, with average daytime temperatures ranging from -3°C to 3°C. Snowfall is consistent in mountain regions like Zakopane and the Carpathians, while central cities experience periodic snow, frost, and short daylight hours. crowd_level: LOW → MEDIUM price_level: LOW → MEDIUM overall_score: 65–78 recommended: true reason: Excellent for: December enjoys strong festive appeal with traditional Christmas markets, while January and February are popular for Tatra winter sports and budget-friendly city breaks. Polish tourism promotes winter for festive illuminations, traditional hearty cuisine, winter sports in the south, and quiet museum exploration without long lines.', 2676),
  ('poland', 10, 'budget-strategy', 'BUDGET STRATEGY', NULL, NULL, 'Where money can be saved: Where saving money is usually NOT recommended: Travel-agent rule: In Poland, **CENTRAL_CITY_HOTEL + PKP_ADVANCE_TRAIN_TICKETS + ADVANCE_AUSCHWITZ_SALT_MINE_BOOKINGS + MILK_BAR_AND_BISTRO_DINING should be evaluated together**. For short stays, prioritize **KRAKOW + WARSAW** (connected by high-speed Pendolino). For longer stays, add **GDANSK/BALTIC_COAST + WROCLAW + ZAKOPANE_TATRA_MOUNTAINS** rather than changing hotels every single night.', 2677),
  ('poland', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Family', 'family', 'Poland’s primary international gateway is Warsaw Chopin Airport (WAW), complemented by Kraków John Paul II International Airport (KRK), Gdańsk Lech Wałęsa Airport (GDN), Wrocław Copernicus Airport (WRO), and Warsaw Modlin Airport (WMI). For families arriving with young children, strollers, or substantial luggage, pre-booked private driver transfers or ride-hailing apps (Uber, Bolt, FreeNow) provide the smoothest transition to city center accommodations. When traveling between major tourist hubs with kids, high-speed PKP Intercity Express Premium (EIP Pendolino) trains offer spacious, quiet, and comfortable carriage seating that avoids highway traffic delays.', 2678),
  ('poland', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Honeymoon', 'honeymoon', 'Opt for pre-arranged private luxury driver transfers directly from airport arrival halls to boutique hotels in historic city centers (e.g., Kraków Old Town, Warsaw Royal Route, or Gdańsk Motława Riverfront) or mountain retreats in Zakopane. For multi-destination honeymoon itineraries, combine: PRIVATE_AIRPORT_TRANSFER + FIRST_CLASS_PKP_INTERCITY_EIP_RAIL (Gdańsk–Warsaw–Kraków corridor) + PRIVATE_CHAUFFEUR_FOR_MOUNTAIN_VALLEYS_AND_HISTORIC_CASTLES.', 2679),
  ('poland', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Luxury', 'luxury', 'Utilize pre-booked private chauffeured transfers (e.g., Mercedes-Benz V-Class / S-Class) directly from major airport arrival terminals or private aviation facilities (Warsaw Chopin WAW Executive Aviation Terminal). For complex luxury country circuits, combine: VIP_AIRPORT_MEET_AND_GREET + PRIVATE_CHAUFFEUR_TRANSFERS + CHARTERED_HELICOPTER_FLIGHTS (Tatra Mountains / Masurian Lakes) + PRIVATE_YACHT_OR_MOTORBOAT_CHARTERS (Gdańsk & Motława River).', 2680),
  ('poland', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Budget', 'budget', 'Take advantage of Poland’s efficient and highly affordable public transit directly connecting airport terminals to urban railway hubs: For onward intercity travel, utilize PKP Intercity (IC/TLK) trains or long-distance FlixBus routes.', 2681),
  ('poland', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Senior', 'senior', 'Prioritize door-to-door pre-booked transfers or ride-hailing apps (Uber, Bolt, FreeNow) directly at airport drop-offs to avoid carrying luggage over historic cobblestone streets. When using intercity rail, book 1st Class seats on PKP Intercity (EIP / EIC) trains, arrange station assistance, and choose central hotels located on flat streets near main tram or metro stops.', 2682),
  ('poland', 18, 'family-travel', 'FAMILY TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'child_friendly_score: 94 best_ages: Rules: For young children: Prefer: Avoid: Official tourism promotes interactive science centers, salt mines, knight tournaments, mountain funiculars, and Baltic coast beach resorts across Poland.', 2683),
  ('poland', 19, 'honeymoon-travel', 'HONEYMOON TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'honeymoon_score: 90 romance_score: 92 privacy_score: 88 luxury_score: 86 Recommended: Honeymoon itineraries should generally stay at: 2–3 major experiences/day. Prefer: HISTORIC_TOWNS + ROYAL_CASTLES + LAKES_AND_MOUNTAINS + BOUTIQUE_STAYS + COASTAL_SPAS + FREE_TIME over: Constant road journeys and daily hotel changes. Recommended areas: Poland''s honeymoon appeal combines historic cobblestone romance, dramatic mountain alpine scenery, Baltic beach spas, luxury castle stays, and vibrant culinary arts.', 2684),
  ('poland', 20, 'luxury-travel', 'LUXURY TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'luxury_score: 84 Recommended: Poland luxury travel should focus on: Luxury value is particularly strong in Warsaw, Kraków, Gdańsk/Sopot resort belt, and luxury mountain chalets in Zakopane.', 2685),
  ('poland', 21, 'adventure', 'ADVENTURE', NULL, NULL, 'adventure_score: 90 Poland offers varied adventure travel across alpine mountain peaks, dense primeval forests, vast lake networks, wild rivers, and coastal dunes. Adventure experiences: Best regions: TATRA_NATIONAL_PARK + BIESZCZADY_MOUNTAINS + MASURIAN_LAKE_DISTRICT + BIAŁOWIEŻA_FOREST + PIENINY_NATIONAL_PARK + SLOVINSKI_NATIONAL_PARK Match activities to season, mountain weather conditions, trail difficulty, and lake permits.', 2686),
  ('poland', 22, 'senior-travel', 'SENIOR TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'senior_suitability: 88 walking_intensity: LOW–MEDIUM for city center tours, flat Old Town walks, museum visits, train travel, and Vistula river cruises MEDIUM–HIGH for steep mountain valley walks, cobbled alleyways, castle climbs, and underground salt mine stairs (800 steps down at Wieliczka) Rules: Poland works particularly well for seniors as a: HERITAGE + ROYAL_CASTLES + MUSEUMS + MOUNTAIN_SPAS + SCENIC_RAIL + RELAXED_DINING destination. Official Polish tourism highlights accessible cultural monuments, world-class WWII and royal museums, thermal spa retreats, and flat, pedestrianized city squares for senior travelers.', 2687),
  ('poland', 23, 'accessibility', 'ACCESSIBILITY', NULL, NULL, 'wheelchair_accessibility: VARIABLE IN MODERN / MAJOR TOURISM FACILITIES LIMITED IN HISTORIC CASTLES, COBBLED OLD TOWNS, AND MOUNTAIN TRAILS public_transport_accessibility: MODERATE TO HIGH in major cities (modern low-floor buses, trams, and Warsaw Metro); variable in regional buses hotel_accessibility: MUST_BE_VERIFIED_PER_HOTEL attraction_accessibility: MUST_BE_VERIFIED_PER_ATTRACTION Rule: Never assume universal accessibility across Poland. Additional notes: Tourism authorities and EU infrastructure funds are continuously expanding accessibility, but historic old towns require advance verification.', 2688),
  ('poland', 24, 'food', 'FOOD', NULL, NULL, 'Poland is particularly strong for: Food experiences: Family: Prioritize pierogi, placki ziemniaczane, pączki, Toruń gingerbread, milk bars, and casual family bistros. Honeymoon: Choose modern Polish fine dining, romantic riverfront tables, private castle meals, and cozy cellar taverns. Luxury: Include Michelin-recognized city restaurants, private chef tasting menus, and rare mead/vodka pairings. Budget: Use traditional milk bars (*bar mleczny*), street food stalls, bakeries (*piekarnia*), and daily lunch sets (*zestaw obiadowy*).', 2689),
  ('poland', 25, 'shopping', 'SHOPPING', NULL, NULL, 'Strong categories: Luxury shopping: Prefer: Poland combines upscale modern shopping malls with world-famous traditional handicrafts like Baltic amber and Bolesławiec ceramics. Budget: Prefer: Travel-agent rule: Use WARSAW for LUXURY + HIGH_FASHION, GDAŃSK for BALTIC_AMBER, BOLESŁAWIEC / KRAKÓW for CERAMICS + FOLK_CRAFTS, TORUŃ for GINGERBREAD, and ZAKOPANE for HIGHLAND_CHEESE + WOODEN_ART.', 2690),
  ('poland', 26, 'nightlife', 'NIGHTLIFE', NULL, NULL, 'nightlife_level: 90 Suitable for: Best areas: Evening activities: Kraków delivers Europe''s highest density of underground cellar bars per square meter, Warsaw offers energetic multi-district nightlife and Vistula riverfront venues, while Sopot provides vibrant summer beach clubbing. Honeymoon travelers should generally prefer: ROOFTOP_LOUNGES + CRAFT_WINE_BARS + RIVERFRONT_TERRACES + EVENING_OLD_TOWN_STROLLS over: All-night clubbing. Travel-agent rule: Position Poland as a **CELLAR_BARS + CRAFT_BEER + VODKA_LOUNGES + SUMMER_BEACH_CLUBS + FESTIVAL DESTINATION**, with nightlife intensity adjusted by region and traveler type.', 2691),
  ('poland', 28, 'sample-itinerary-patterns', 'SAMPLE ITINERARY PATTERNS', '3 NIGHTS', NULL, '### Day 1 Arrival at Warsaw Chopin Airport (WAW) → Direct SKM commuter train (S2/S3) / transfer to city center → Hotel check-in → Relax and refresh Afternoon: → Trakt Królewski (Royal Route) stroll along Krakowskie Przedmieście → Stare Miasto (UNESCO Old Town) & Market Square (Rynek Starego Miasta) → Royal Castle (Zamek Królewski) exterior & Castle Square → Barbican & Old Town City Walls Evening: → Traditional Polish dinner (Pierogi / Żurek / Kotlet Schabowy) → Historic Old Town / Nowy Świat bar or terrace experience → Hotel Warsaw is Poland''s dynamic capital and primary international gateway, seamlessly blending meticulously rebuilt UNESCO historical heritage, royal palaces, dramatic World War II history, and modern urban vitality. ### Day 2 Morning: Breakfast → Łazienki Royal Garden Park & Palace on the Isle (Pałac na Wyspie) → Chopin Monument & Rose Garden stroll Afternoon: → Warsaw Uprising Museum (Muzeum Powstania Warszawskiego) OR POLIN Museum of the History of Polish Jews → Palace of Culture and Science (PKiN) 30th-floor observation deck for city panoramas Evening: → Dinner in the trendy revitalized Hala Koszyki or Elektrownia Powiśle food halls → Craft beer / Polish vodka tasting in Pawilony or Vistula Riverfront lounges → Hotel ### Day 3 Recommended first-time option: → High-speed PKP Intercity Express Premium (EIP Pendolino) morning train to Kraków (2h 20m) → Explore Kraków Stare Miasto (Main Market Square, Cloth Hall, St. Mary''s Basilica) Afternoon: → Wawel Hill & Royal Castle Grounds → Kazimierz Jewish Quarter stroll OR Wieliczka Salt Mine quick express excursion Evening: → Traditional Lesser Poland dinner in Kraków''s Main Square or Kazimierz → Evening return EIP Pendolino train to Warsaw (or stay overnight in Kraków) → Return to hotel Warsaw and Kraków are seamlessly linked by frequent high-speed Pendolino trains, serving as Poland''s premier multi-city first-time combination. Optional alternative instead of Kraków day trip: ROYAL CASTLES & HISTORIC GARDENS: → Excursion to Wilanów Palace (the "Polish Versailles") → Museum of King Jan III''s Palace & Royal Gardens → Afternoon walk through University of Warsaw Library Roof Gardens CULTURE / MEDIEVAL HERITAGE: → Express PKP train / driver to Toruń (2h) → UNESCO Medieval Town, Copernicus House & Gothic churches → Gingerbread baking workshop & tasting FAMILY: → Copernicus Science Centre (Centrum Nauki Kopernik) → Warsaw Zoo & Praga District murals → Multimedia Fountain Park show (seasonal) → Interactive science parks HONEYMOON: → Luxury boutique hotel stay on the Royal Route → Private Vistula River sunset boat cruise → Fine dining at a Michelin-recognized Warsaw restaurant → VIP Polish National Opera box seats → Relaxed free time FOOD: → Traditional milk bar (*bar mleczny*) experience (e.g., Bar Prasowy) → Hala Mirowska local food market walk → Pierogi-making workshop → High-end modern Polish tasting menu with vodka pairings For only 3 nights based in Warsaw, prioritize: WARSAW + KRAKOW_HIGH_SPEED_PENDOLINO_DAY_TRIP OR WARSAW + ONE_NEARBY_ROYAL_OR_HERITAGE_EXCURSION (WILANÓW / TORUŃ) rather than trying to combine several distant Polish regions. ### Day 4 Breakfast → Leisure morning → Optional souvenir shopping (Baltic Amber / Bolesławiec Ceramics / Polish Poster Art on Mokotowska Street) → Hotel checkout → SKM train / transfer to Warsaw Chopin Airport (WAW) → Departure', 2692),
  ('poland', 29, 'seven-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'SEVEN-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 1', NULL, 'Arrival at Kraków → Private airport transfer → Romantic hotel check-in → Relax and refresh Evening: → Main Market Square → Old Town → Vistula riverfront → Romantic dinner → Overnight at Kraków', 2693),
