  ('poland', 32, 'travel-agent-insights', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS', 'What inexperienced planners often do wrong', NULL, '', 2717),
  ('poland', 32, 'travel-agent-insights', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS', 'What an experienced planner does differently', NULL, 'KRAKOW + WARSAW + ONE_GDANSK / WROCLAW / ZAKOPANE_OR_MASURIA_EXPERIENCE rather than maximum destination count.', 2718),
  ('poland', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', NULL, NULL, 'IF: trip_length <= 4 nights THEN: prioritize_ONE_MAJOR_CITY + ONE_NEARBY_EXCURSION Reason: Very short stays gain significantly more value from properly experiencing one major Polish hub (like Kraków or Warsaw) and an adjacent landmark than losing precious hours to long regional transfers. IF: trip_length >= 6 nights AND: traveler_interest == FIRST_TIME_POLAND THEN: prioritize_KRAKOW + WARSAW + GDANSK_OR_WROCLAW Reason: This gives a perfectly balanced introduction to royal medieval history, World War II heritage, meticulously rebuilt capitals, Hanseatic coastal art, and modern Polish culture. IF: trip_length >= 8 nights AND: traveler_interest == FIRST_TIME_POLAND THEN: prefer_GOLDEN_TRIANGLE_KRAKOW_WARSAW_GDANSK + ZAKOPANE_OR_WROCLAW AND: use_HIGH_SPEED_PENDOLINO_RAIL_FOR_CITIES_AND_REGIONAL_TRANSFERS_WHERE_PRACTICAL Reason: Kraków, Warsaw, Gdańsk, and the Tatra Mountains or Lower Silesia offer four completely distinct, world-class Polish travel experiences connected seamlessly by rail. IF: trip_type == HONEYMOON THEN: prefer_KRAKOW + WARSAW + ZAKOPANE_LUXURY_CHALET_OR_SOPOT_COASTAL_SPA AND: increase_BOUTIQUE_STAYS + SCENIC_DINING + THERMAL_SPA_EXPERIENCES + FREE_TIME + COUPLE_EXPERIENCES Reason: Poland''s strongest romantic routes mix cobblestone Old Town charm, high-end Baltic beach spas, timber mountain retreats, fine dining, and private river boat cruises. IF: traveler_type == FAMILY THEN: prefer_WARSAW + WROCLAW + KRAKOW_AND_ENERGYLANDIA_OR_WIELICZKA AND: include_ENERGYLANDIA_THEME_PARK + COPERNICUS_SCIENCE_CENTRE + WROCŁAW_DWARF_HUNT + WIELICZKA_SALT_MINE + GOBAŁÓWKA_FUNICULAR AND: reduce_HEAVY_WAR_MUSEUM_DENSITY + LONG_CONTINUOUS_TRANSFERS Reason: Poland features exceptional family attractions, including Europe''s largest amusement park (Energylandia), subterranean salt mine trails, interactive science centers, and citywide gnome hunting. IF: traveler_type == LUXURY THEN: prefer_WARSAW + KRAKOW + GDANSK_OR_ZAKOPANE_LUXURY_LODGE AND: increase_5_STAR_FLAGSHIP_HOTELS + PRIVATE_GUIDES + FINE_DINING + PRIVATE_TRANSFERS + HELICOPTER_TOURS + PRIVATE_YACHT_CHARTERS Reason: Polish high-end travel relies on top-tier luxury hotels (Raffles Europejski, Hotel Copernicus), private historical guides, high-speed 1st Class Pendolino travel, Michelin-starred dining, and bespoke Baltic charters. IF: traveler_type == BUDGET THEN: prefer_PUBLIC_TRANSPORT + PKP_INTERCITY_EARLY_PROMO_TRAINS + WALKING + MILK_BARS AND: book_INTERCITY_TRANSPORT_30_DAYS_IN_ADVANCE AND: balance_PAID_ATTRACTIONS_WITH_FREE_MUSEUM_DAYS + PARKS + OLD_TOWNS + MOUNTAIN_HIKING Reason: Poland offers outstanding value for budget travelers with affordable passenger rail, milk bars (*bar mleczny*), low museum entry fees, and vibrant pedestrianized public squares. IF: traveler_interest == CULTURE_AND_HERITAGE THEN: prioritize_KRAKOW + WARSAW + GDANSK + TORUN + MALBORK_CASTLE AND: include_WAWEL_CASTLE + AUSCHWITZ_MEMORIAL + WARSAW_UPRISING_MUSEUM + POLIN_MUSEUM + TEUTONIC_CASTLES Reason: These destinations feature Poland''s dense concentration of UNESCO World Heritage sites, royal residences, Teutonic red-brick fortresses, and World War II monuments. IF: traveler_interest == ART_AND_ARCHITECTURE THEN: prefer_WROCLAW + WARSAW + KRAKOW + TORUN + POZNAN AND: include_CENTENNIAL_HALL + REBUILT_OLD_TOWNS + BRICK_GOTHIC + ART_NOUVEAU_AND_MODERNISM Reason: This route contrasts medieval Gothic market squares with Prussian, Austro-Hungarian Secessionist, modernist UNESCO monuments, and post-war reconstruction masterworks. IF: traveler_interest == GASTRONOMY THEN: prefer_KRAKOW + WARSAW + WROCLAW + POZNAN AND: include_MILK_BARS + PIEROGI_WORKSHOPS + REGIONAL_SOUPS + CRAFT_BEER_PUBS + TORUŃ_GINGERBREAD + FINE_DINING Reason: Polish food culture spans historic working-class canteens (*bar mleczny*), hearty highland specialties, artisan bakeries, world-class craft breweries, and innovative modern gastronomy. IF: traveler_interest == COAST_AND_LAKES THEN: prefer_GDANSK_SOPOT_HEL + MASURIAN_LAKES_DISTRICT AND: match_REGION_TO_SEASON + WATERSPORT_STYLE + RELAXATION_REQUIREMENT Reason: The Baltic Coast (Trójmiasto & Hel Peninsula) offers sandy beaches, pier walks, and health spas, while the Masurian Lake District provides world-class sailing and lake nature. IF: traveler_interest == NATURE_AND_WILDLIFE THEN: prioritize_BIAŁOWIEŻA_PRIMEVAL_FOREST + BIEBRZA_MARSHES + BIESZCZADY_NATIONAL_PARK AND: do_not_treat_PRIMEVAL_FORESTS_AND_MOUNTAIN_PARKS_AS_INTERCHANGEABLE Reason: Białowieża focuses on ancient primeval woodland and wild European bison tracking, Biebrza offers wetland birdwatching, and Bieszczady centers on wild Carpathian mountain ridges. IF: traveler_interest == NIGHTLIFE THEN: prefer_KRAKOW + WARSAW + SOPOT_IN_SUMMER + WROCLAW AND: match_AREA_TO_PARTY_STYLE + SEASON Reason: Kraków''s Kazimierz and Old Town cellar bars operate year-round, Warsaw offers multi-district nightlife and Vistula river barges, Wrocław features lively student venues, and Sopot is the summer beach club capital. IF: traveler_interest == SHOPPING THEN: prioritize_WARSAW + GDANSK + KRAKOW + BOLESLAWIEC AND: include_BALTIC_AMBER + BOLESŁAWIEC_CERAMICS + HIGH_FASHION_BOUTIQUES + CLOTH_HALL_CRAFTS Reason: Poland concentrates international luxury shopping in Warsaw, world-renowned Baltic amber galleries in Gdańsk, hand-painted ceramics in Bolesławiec, and artisan crafts in Kraków. IF: traveler_interest == CRAFT_BEER_AND_SPIRITS THEN: prefer_WROCLAW + WARSAW + KRAKOW + POZNAN AND: include_BREWPUB_TOURS + POLISH_VODKA_MUSEUM + ARTISAN_MEAD_TASTING AND: use_PUBLIC_TRANSIT_OR_RIDE_HAILING_WHEN_TASTING Reason: Poland is one of Europe''s top craft beer pioneers, complemented by historic vodka distillation heritage and traditional mead brewing. IF: traveler_interest == HIKING_AND_NATURE THEN: prefer_TATRA_NATIONAL_PARK + PIENINY_MOUNTAINS + BIESZCZADY_RANGES + KARKONOSZE_SUDETES AND: match_ROUTE_TO_FITNESS + ALTITUDE + WEATHER + SEASON Reason: Polish alpine hiking ranges from gentle valley walks and Dunajec River gorge rafting to technical high-peak ascents in the Tatras (e.g., Rysy or Orla Perć). IF: traveler_interest == CASTLES_AND_PALACES THEN: prefer_MALBORK_CASTLE + LOWER_SILESIA_KSIAŻ_AND_CZOCHA + WAWEL_ROYAL_CASTLE + WILANÓW_PALACE AND: choose_HIGH_DENSITY_CASTLE_REGIONS + RENTAL_CAR_FOR_RURAL_TRAILS Reason: Malbork represents the world''s largest brick Gothic castle, Lower Silesia features dozens of aristocratic châteaux, and Warsaw/Kraków host grand royal palaces. IF: traveler_interest == PHOTOGRAPHY THEN: prefer_KRAKOW_OLD_TOWN + WROCLAW_OSTRÓW_TUMSKI + GDANSK_MOTŁAWA_RIVERFRONT + MORSKIE_OKO_TATRAS + MALBORK_CASTLE AND: prioritize_EARLY_MORNING + GOLDEN_HOUR + BLUE_HOUR Reason: These sites yield dramatic visual contrast between medieval gas-lit cobblestone streets, colorful merchant townhouses, alpine mountain tarns, and massive brick fortresses. IF: trip_length <= 7 nights THEN: prefer_MAXIMUM_TWO_OR_THREE_BASES AND: avoid_EXCESSIVE_HOTEL_CHANGES Reason: Though train transit is fast between major cities, frequent hotel check-ins and unpacks diminish sightseeing time in primary hubs. IF: route == GDANSK_TO_WARSAW OR: route == WARSAW_TO_KRAKOW OR: route == WARSAW_TO_WROCLAW THEN: prefer_PKP_INTERCITY_EIP_PENDOLINO_RAIL_OVER_RENTAL_CAR_FOR_STANDARD_CITY_TRAVEL Reason: Poland''s high-speed rail network connects major metropolitan hubs in 2 to 3 hours, bypassing highway traffic and urban parking restrictions. IF: traveler_type == SENIOR OR: traveler_mobility == LIMITED THEN: prioritize_CENTRAL_HOTELS + HIGH_SPEED_RAIL_1ST_CLASS + RIDE_HAILING_BOLT_UBER + MODERATE_DAILY_SIGHTSEEING AND: reduce_STEEP_UNPAVED_MOUNTAIN_WALKS + EXCESSIVE_STAIRS + RAPID_MULTI_CITY_MOVEMENT Reason: Historic cobblestone Old Towns and salt mine stairwells can cause fatigue; central accommodation, city trams, and door-to-door transport ease movement. IF: traveler_uses_WHEELCHAIR THEN: prefer_VERIFIED_ACCESSIBLE_HOTELS + PKP_48H_ADVANCE_STATION_ASSISTANCE + MODERN_MUSEUMS + ACCESSIBLE_SALT_MINE_ROUTE AND: do_not_assume_HISTORIC_CASTLES + MEDIEVAL_TOWERS + UNPAVED_MOUNTAIN_TRAILS_ARE_FULLY_STEP_FREE Reason: Modern infrastructure and flagship museums in major Polish cities are accessible, but medieval castles, cobblestone squares, and mountain paths frequently have steep stairs and uneven terrain. IF: weather == EXTREME_SUMMER_HEAT AND: region == CENTRAL_PLAINS_OR_WARSAW THEN: prioritize_EARLY_MORNING_OUTDOOR_SIGHTSEEING + AIR_CONDITIONED_MUSEUMS_MIDDAY + EVENING_VISTULA_RIVER_LOUNGES AND: reduce_MIDDAY_OUTDOOR_WALKING_ON_OPEN_SQUARES Reason: Central Polish midsummer temperatures can exceed 32°C (90°F); visiting climate-controlled museums (POLIN, Schindler''s Factory) or riverside terraces provides comfort. IF: weather == RAINY THEN: increase_MUSEUMS + ROYAL_CASTLES + SALT_MINES + GASTRONOMY + THERMAL_BATHS AND: reduce_LONG_OUTDOOR_WALKING_TOURS + MOUNTAIN_HIKE_DEPENDENT_ACTIVITIES Reason: Attractions like Wieliczka Salt Mine, Warsaw Uprising Museum, Wawel Castle, and indoor thermal spas (Chochołowskie) remain completely unaffected by rain. IF: traveler_interest == FIRST_TIME_POLAND THEN: prioritize_KRAKOW + WARSAW AND: add_ONE_OF_GDANSK_WROCLAW_ZAKOPANE_OR_MASURIA AND: include_ONE_SIGNATURE_POLISH_FOOD_OR_HISTORICAL_EXPERIENCE Reason: This structure provides a comprehensive, highly rewarding introduction to Poland''s essential heritage hubs alongside a distinct regional contrast. IF: traveler_interest == CULTURE_AND_RELAXATION_BALANCE THEN: allocate_60_TO_70_PERCENT_TO_CORE_SIGHTSEEING AND: allocate_REMAINING_TIME_TO_MILK_BARS_AND_CAFES + PARKS + THERMAL_SPAS + CRAFT_BEER_GARDENS + EVENING_STROLLS + FREE_TIME', 2719),
  ('poland', 34, 'destination-scoring', 'DESTINATION SCORING', NULL, NULL, '| Factor | Score | | --- | --- | | Family | 91 | | Honeymoon | 90 | | Luxury | 86 | | Budget | 94 | | Adventure | 87 | | Culture | 96 | | Food | 89 | | Shopping | 85 | | Nightlife | 91 | | Relaxation | 90 | | Nature | 89 | | Accessibility | 84 | | Safety | 93 | | First-time visitor | 95 | | Photography | 95 |', 2720),
  ('poland', 35, 'final-travel-agent-verdict', 'FINAL TRAVEL AGENT VERDICT', NULL, NULL, 'Best traveler profiles: 1. Culture / heritage traveler 2. First-time Europe traveler 3. Food / craft beer & vodka traveler 4. Family traveler 5. Honeymoon / romantic traveler 6. Baltic coast / lakes / nature traveler 7. Photography traveler 8. Art / architecture traveler 9. Nightlife / social traveler 10. Nature / alpine active traveler Best duration: 7–10 nights 3–4 nights: Best for ONE major hub such as Kraków or Warsaw + one nearby excursion (e.g., Auschwitz-Birkenau / Wieliczka Salt Mine / Wilanów Palace). 5–7 nights: Best for TWO major bases such as Kraków + Warsaw or Warsaw + Gdańsk / Wrocław. 8–10 nights: Excellent for Kraków + Warsaw + Gdańsk / Tatra Mountains (Zakopane) / one contrasting region. 11–14 nights: Best for deeper regional travel, Lower Silesia castles, Masurian Lakes, Białowieża Primeval Forest, Podlasie, Baltic Riviera, or multiple Teutonic brick Gothic fortresses. Best season: YEAR-ROUND Spring: CITIES + CULTURE + OLD_TOWNS + NATURE + WALKING + PHOTOGRAPHY. Summer: TATRA_HIKING + BALTIC_SEA_COAST + MASURIAN_LAKES + FESTIVALS + NIGHTLIFE + ENERGYLANDIA. Autumn: CULTURE + GASTRONOMY + CRAFT_BEER_AND_MEAD + CITY_BREAKS + GOLDEN_POLISH_AUTUMN_PARKS + BETTER_WEATHER_FOR_WALKING. Winter: WARSAW + KRAKOW + CHRISTMAS_MARKETS + TATRA_WINTER_SPORTS_IN_ZAKOPANE + INDOOR_THERMAL_BATHS. Poland''s official tourism guidance treats the country as year-round: spring and "Golden Polish Autumn" are particularly suitable for cities, historical routes, and nature parks; summer for high alpine mountain trails, Baltic beaches, lake sailing, and open-air festivals; and winter for atmospheric snow-dusted Old Towns, festive Christmas markets, and Tatra ski resorts. Best hotel strategy: Choose accommodation according to region, transport connectivity, and trip purpose. For first-time visitors: KRAKÓW + WARSAW + OPTIONAL_THIRD_REGIONAL_BASE (e.g., Gdańsk, Wrocław, or Zakopane). For Lesser Poland & Tatras: Use KRAKÓW + ZAKOPANE selectively rather than changing hotels for every mountain valley or salt mine town. For coastal / lakes / wellness: Choose the property carefully according to BALTIC_RESORT + MASURIAN_LAKE_LODGE + SOPOT_SPA requirements. For honeymoon / luxury: Prefer boutique historic residences in Kraków Old Town or Kazimierz, 5-star flagship urban hotels in Warsaw (e.g., Raffles Europejski), luxury Tatra timber chalets, or Baltic beach spa resorts. Avoid unnecessary daily hotel changes simply because checking in and out diminishes sightseeing time in primary regional hubs. Best transportation: Use: Poland should primarily be treated as: HIGH_SPEED_PENDOLINO_RAIL_FOR_MAIN_CORRIDORS + URBAN_PUBLIC_TRANSIT + CAR_SELECTIVE_FOR_COUNTRYSIDE + BOATS_FOR_LAKES_AND_BALTIC Must-do for first-time visitor: Poland should not be reduced to World War II tragedy alone; official tourism positions MEDIEVAL_HERITAGE + ROYAL_CASTLES + TATRA_AND_CARPATHIAN_NATURE + BALTIC_COAST + REBUILT_URBAN_RESILIENCE + FOOD_AND_CRAFT_BEER + THERMAL_SPAS as major national travel pillars. Don''t-do: Biggest advantage: Exceptional structural diversity, rich cultural history, and world-class high-speed rail infrastructure within one country. Poland combines Gothic brick castles, meticulously rebuilt UNESCO medieval capitals, UNESCO royal salt mines, vibrant Jewish heritage, high alpine Tatra peaks, primeval bison forests, sandy Baltic shores, and a pioneering modern craft beer and culinary scene. Official tourism highlights the country''s over 1,000 years of preserved heritage, diverse natural parks from lakes to mountains, and high-value travel experience, allowing completely different trip profiles in one nation. Biggest disadvantage: High peak-season crowds at top UNESCO sites and advance booking strictness. Strict reservation requirements for major historical memorials, summer traffic bottlenecks in mountain valleys (Zakopane access), midsummer heat on unshaded city squares, harsh sub-zero winter snowfall in mountain passes, and urban parking zones can reduce itinerary efficiency if under-planned. Overall destination score: 93/100', 2721),
  ('poland', 36, 'data-quality', 'DATA QUALITY', NULL, NULL, 'information_completeness: 97/100 last_updated: 2026-08-29 last_verified: WEB_VERIFIED verified_by: POLAND.TRAVEL (POLISH TOURISM ORGANISATION) / PKP INTERCITY / OFFICIAL REGIONAL TOURISM BOARDS sources: IMPORTANT: Hotel rates, train schedules, flight routes, monument tickets, museum operating hours, boat transfers, salt mine access, festival dates, and accessibility must NOT be treated as permanently valid. Major attractions such as AUSCHWITZ-BIRKENAU + WIELICZKA_SALT_MINE + SCHINDLER''S_FACTORY + WAWEL_ROYAL_CHAMBERS have specific ticketing, mandatory ID/passport rules, or timed entry; current booking requirements should always be verified. Passenger rail is a premier planning choice on main routes, but schedules, mandatory seat reservations (e.g., EIP Pendolino), and direct connections should be checked on PKP Intercity for actual travel dates. Poland''s climate varies significantly by region. WARSAW and the CENTRAL PLAINS can become hot in mid-summer. TATRA MOUNTAIN TRAILS and high passes require proper alpine gear and weather verification; sudden summer storms or heavy winter snowfall occur regularly. BALTIC SEA (Trójmiasto / Sopot) resorts and MASURIAN LAKES operate on strong seasonal windows, with peak water sports in mid-summer. Accessible tourism infrastructure is exceptionally modern across major Polish cities, low-floor trams, high-speed PKP Intercity trains, airports, and top indoor museums, but historic castles, medieval cobblestone squares, wooden churches, and high mountain paths are rarely step-free. Poland should primarily be treated as: SPRING: CITIES + CULTURE + OLD_TOWNS + NATURE + GASTRONOMY + PHOTOGRAPHY SUMMER: TATRA_HIKING + BALTIC_COAST + MASURIAN_LAKES + FESTIVALS + NIGHTLIFE + ENERGYLANDIA AUTUMN: CULTURE + GASTRONOMY + CRAFT_BEER + CITY_BREAKS + GOLDEN_AUTUMN_PARKS + PHOTOGRAPHY WINTER: WARSAW + KRAKOW + TATRA_SKI_RESORTS + CHRISTMAS_MARKETS + THERMAL_SPAS Poland.travel, PKP Intercity, regional tourism authorities, national park bodies, and individual attraction operators should be treated as primary sources for current operational information. This dataset should be refreshed regularly before production use.', 2722),
  ('spain', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Spring', NULL, 'months: March April May weather: Generally mild and increasingly sunny. March can remain cool and changeable, April brings occasional rain, while May is warmer and highly suitable for outdoor sightseeing. crowd_level: MEDIUM price_level: MEDIUM overall_score: 84–91 recommended: true reason: One of Spain''s best overall periods for cities, culture, Andalusia, road trips, hiking, food, photography, and outdoor sightseeing before peak summer heat. Best for: Official Spanish tourism guidance identifies spring as one of the best periods because temperatures are generally mild and daylight increases.', 2723),
  ('spain', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Summer', NULL, 'months: June July August weather: Hot, dry, and very sunny across much of Spain. July and August are the hottest months, with temperatures frequently above 30°C and considerably hotter conditions possible inland and in southern Spain. Northern Spain is generally milder. crowd_level: HIGH → VERY_HIGH price_level: HIGH → VERY_HIGH overall_score: 72–82 recommended: true reason: Excellent for: Best for coast and island holidays, but heat, crowds, and peak-season prices reduce overall value for intensive city sightseeing.', 2724),
  ('spain', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Autumn', NULL, 'months: September October November weather: September remains warm and often summer-like, while October becomes milder and November cooler and more changeable. Southern and Mediterranean regions often retain pleasant conditions well into autumn. crowd_level: MEDIUM → LOW price_level: MEDIUM → LOW overall_score: 83–92 recommended: true reason: September and October offer one of Spain''s strongest combinations of good weather, culture, food, wine, hiking, coast, and lower visitor pressure. Best for: Official tourism guidance specifically identifies spring and autumn as excellent periods for cultural routes, villages, nature, and comfortable outdoor travel.', 2725),
  ('spain', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Winter', NULL, 'months: December January February weather: Cool to cold across inland and northern Spain, with more rain especially in the north and snow in mountain regions. Southern Spain is generally milder, while the Canary Islands remain especially warm. crowd_level: LOW → MEDIUM price_level: LOW → MEDIUM overall_score: 74–84 recommended: true reason: Excellent for: The Canary Islands provide strong winter-sun potential, while the Pyrenees and Sierra Nevada support major winter-sports travel.', 2726),
  ('spain', 10, 'budget-strategy', 'BUDGET STRATEGY', NULL, NULL, 'Where money can be saved: Where saving money is usually NOT recommended: Travel-agent rule: In Spain, **HOTEL_LOCATION + HIGH_SPEED_RAIL + ADVANCE_SIGHT_TICKETS + TAPAS_DINING should be evaluated together**. For short stays, prioritize **MADRID + BARCELONA** or **BARCELONA + ONE_DAY_TRIP**. For longer stays, add **SEVILLE + GRANADA + CÓRDOBA + ONE_COASTAL_OR_WINE_REGION** rather than changing hotels every single night.', 2727),
  ('spain', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Family', 'family', 'Spain has extensive international airport hubs across the country (Madrid-Barajas, Barcelona-El Prat, Málaga-Costa del Sol, Palma de Mallorca). For families arriving with young children, stroller equipment, or substantial luggage, pre-booked private transfers or official flat-rate airport taxis (e.g., €33 fixed fare from Madrid Airport T1/T2/T3/T4 to the city center inside the M-30 ring) provide the smoothest transition to accommodations. When traveling between major cities with kids, high-speed rail (AVE / Iryo / Ouigo) is far more comfortable and spacious than domestic flights.', 2728),
  ('spain', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Honeymoon', 'honeymoon', 'Opt for private luxury chauffeured transfers directly from airport arrival halls to heritage hotels, coastal resorts, or historic *Paradores*. For multi-destination honeymoon itineraries, combine: PRIVATE_AIRPORT_TRANSFER + FIRST_CLASS_HIGH_SPEED_RAIL (Preferente / Premium class on AVE / Iryo) + SCENIC_COASTAL_OR_WINE_ESTATE_TRANSFERS.', 2729),
  ('spain', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Luxury', 'luxury', 'Utilize private chauffeured Mercedes S-Class / V-Class transfers from major airport jet terminals or private aviation hubs (Madrid, Barcelona, Ibiza, Marbella). For complex luxury country circuits, combine: VIP_AIRPORT_MEET_AND_GREET + PRIVATE_CHAUFFEUR_TRANSFERS + CHARTERED_HELICOPTER_OR_YACHT_TRANSFERS (Balearics / Costa del Sol).', 2730),
  ('spain', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Budget', 'budget', 'Take advantage of Spain''s comprehensive public transit networks directly connecting airport terminals to city centers: For onward intercity travel, utilize low-cost high-speed operators (Avlo, Ouigo, Iryo) or long-distance buses (ALSA).', 2731),
  ('spain', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Senior', 'senior', 'Prioritize direct door-to-door private transfers or official airport taxi ranks to avoid navigating large multi-level transit hubs with luggage. When using high-speed rail, utilize Renfe Atendo (free mobility and luggage assistance service at major train stations) and select centrally located hotels within walking distance of flat town squares or taxi stands.', 2732),
  ('spain', 18, 'family-travel', 'FAMILY TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'child_friendly_score: 94 best_ages: Rules: For young children: Prefer: Avoid: Official tourism specifically promotes interactive museums, theme parks, aquariums, wildlife attractions, and family activities throughout Spain.', 2733),
  ('spain', 19, 'honeymoon-travel', 'HONEYMOON TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'honeymoon_score: 93 romance_score: 94 privacy_score: 88 luxury_score: 92 Recommended: Honeymoon itineraries should generally stay at: 2–3 major experiences/day. Prefer: HISTORIC_CITIES + COAST + DINING + WINE + ROMANTIC_STAYS + FREE_TIME over: Constant sightseeing and excessive hotel changes. Recommended areas: Spain''s official tourism guidance specifically promotes honeymoons combining cities, historic towns, landscapes, mountains, valleys, and excellent transport connections.', 2734),
  ('spain', 20, 'luxury-travel', 'LUXURY TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'luxury_score: 92 Recommended: Spain luxury travel should focus on: Luxury value is especially strong in Madrid, Barcelona, Mallorca, Marbella / Costa del Sol, Basque Country, wine regions, and premium historic properties.', 2735),
  ('spain', 21, 'adventure', 'ADVENTURE', NULL, NULL, 'adventure_score: 92 Spain offers exceptionally varied adventure travel across mountains, islands, coast, and national parks. Adventure experiences: Best regions: PYRENEES + CANARY_ISLANDS + NORTHERN_SPAIN + ANDALUSIA + BALEARICS + SIERRA_NEVADA Match activities to season, weather, fitness, sea conditions, and route difficulty.', 2736),
  ('spain', 22, 'senior-travel', 'SENIOR TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'senior_suitability: 90 walking_intensity: LOW–MEDIUM for city tours, museums, rail travel, resorts, and scenic touring MEDIUM–HIGH for historic hills, old quarters, mountain areas, and long walking days Rules: Spain works particularly well for seniors as a: CULTURE + GASTRONOMY + RAIL + COAST + RELAXATION destination. Official Spain tourism highlights accessible cultural attractions, Paradores, gastronomy, luxury trains, nature, and relaxed travel for older visitors.', 2737),
  ('spain', 23, 'accessibility', 'ACCESSIBILITY', NULL, NULL, 'wheelchair_accessibility: GOOD → VERY_GOOD IN MANY MODERN / MAJOR TOURISM FACILITIES VARIABLE IN HISTORIC, BEACH, MOUNTAIN AND RURAL ENVIRONMENTS public_transport_accessibility: GOOD → VERY_GOOD overall; verify individual services hotel_accessibility: MUST_BE_VERIFIED_PER_HOTEL attraction_accessibility: MUST_BE_VERIFIED_PER_ATTRACTION Rule: Never assume universal accessibility across Spain. Additional notes: Official tourism reports hundreds of accessible accommodations, restaurants, cultural spaces, nature areas, beaches, and leisure facilities across Spain.', 2738),
  ('spain', 24, 'food', 'FOOD', NULL, NULL, 'Spain is particularly strong for: Food experiences: Family: Prioritize tapas, paella, markets, churros, casual restaurants, and flexible dining. Honeymoon: Choose rooftop dining, wine regions, seafood, fine dining, and intimate tapas experiences. Luxury: Include Michelin-level restaurants, private winery visits, premium tasting menus, and luxury hotel dining. Budget: Use markets, bakeries, menú del día, tapas bars, and casual local restaurants.', 2739),
  ('spain', 25, 'shopping', 'SHOPPING', NULL, NULL, 'Strong categories: Luxury shopping: Prefer: Spain combines luxury retail with traditional markets, local crafts, contemporary fashion, and regional food products. Budget: Prefer: Travel-agent rule: Use MADRID for LUXURY + FASHION, BARCELONA for DESIGN + PREMIUM_RETAIL, SEVILLE / ANDALUSIA for CRAFTS, and REGIONAL_MARKETS for FOOD + LOCAL_PRODUCTS.', 2740),
  ('spain', 26, 'nightlife', 'NIGHTLIFE', NULL, NULL, 'nightlife_level: 92 Suitable for: Best areas: Evening activities: Madrid and Barcelona offer broad city nightlife, Seville adds tapas and flamenco, while Ibiza and Mediterranean resort areas provide Spain''s strongest club and beach-party experiences. Honeymoon travelers should generally prefer: ROOFTOP_DINING + WINE + FLAMENCO + COCKTAILS + EVENING_WALKS over: Club-heavy itineraries. Travel-agent rule: Position Spain as a **FOOD + BARS + LIVE_CULTURE + CLUBS + LATE_NIGHT_SOCIAL DESTINATION**, with nightlife intensity adjusted by region and traveler type.', 2741),
  ('spain', 28, 'sample-itinerary-patterns', 'SAMPLE ITINERARY PATTERNS', '3 NIGHTS', NULL, '### Day 1 Arrival at Madrid → Hotel check-in → Relax and refresh Afternoon: → Royal Palace → Plaza Mayor → Puerta del Sol → Gran Vía Evening: → Tapas / local dinner → Optional rooftop experience → Hotel Madrid is Spain''s strongest short-stay cultural base, combining royal heritage, historic neighbourhoods, major museums, shopping and nightlife. :contentReference[oaicite:0]{index=0} ### Day 2 Morning: Breakfast → Prado Museum → Retiro Park → Paseo del Arte Afternoon: → Optional Bernabéu OR Salamanca shopping → Local neighbourhood exploration Evening: → Tapas → Flamenco / cultural show → Hotel ### Day 3 Recommended first-time option: → High-speed train to Barcelona → Hotel / luggage drop Afternoon: → Sagrada Família → Passeig de Gràcia → Casa Batlló / La Pedrera Evening: → Gothic Quarter → Mediterranean waterfront → Dinner → Hotel Madrid and Barcelona are efficiently linked by AVE high-speed rail, with official tourism itineraries using the two cities as Spain''s primary first-time combination. :contentReference[oaicite:1]{index=1} Optional alternative instead of Barcelona: ANDALUSIA: → Seville → Real Alcázar → Cathedral + Giralda → Plaza de España → Tapas + flamenco CULTURE / HISTORY: → Toledo day trip → Historic Centre → Cathedral → Alcázar FAMILY: → Retiro Park → Bernabéu → Barcelona attractions → Beach / aquarium / interactive experiences HONEYMOON: → Boutique hotel → Sunset rooftop → Seville OR Barcelona → Fine dining → Relaxed free time FOOD: → Madrid tapas → San Miguel Market → Barcelona food markets → Regional Spanish cuisine For only 3 nights, prioritize: MADRID + BARCELONA OR MADRID + ONE_NEARBY_HERITAGE_EXCURSION rather than trying to combine several distant Spanish regions. ### Day 4 Breakfast → Leisure morning → Optional shopping / neighbourhood walk → Hotel checkout → Airport transfer → Departure', 2742),
  ('spain', 29, 'six-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 1', NULL, 'Arrival at Barcelona → Romantic hotel check-in → Relax and refresh Evening: → Gothic Quarter → Las Ramblas → Barcelona waterfront → Romantic dinner → Overnight at Barcelona', 2743),
  ('spain', 29, 'six-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 2', NULL, 'Breakfast at the hotel Morning: → Sagrada Família → Passeig de Gràcia → Casa Batlló / Gaudí architecture Afternoon: → Park Güell → Couple photography → Free time Evening: → Rooftop / romantic dinner → Overnight at Barcelona', 2744),
  ('spain', 29, 'six-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 3', NULL, 'Breakfast → Hotel checkout → Flight / train to Seville → Romantic hotel check-in Afternoon: → Plaza de España → María Luisa Park → Santa Cruz Quarter → Couple photography Evening: → Tapas dinner → Flamenco show → Overnight at Seville', 2745),
  ('spain', 29, 'six-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 4', NULL, 'Breakfast Morning: → Real Alcázar → Seville Cathedral → Giralda Afternoon: → Triana → Guadalquivir riverfront → Optional romantic river cruise → Leisure time Evening: → Rooftop / riverside dinner → Overnight at Seville', 2746),
  ('spain', 29, 'six-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 5', NULL, 'Breakfast → Hotel checkout → Transfer toward Portugal → Arrive Lisbon → Romantic hotel check-in Afternoon: → Belém → Jerónimos Monastery → Belém Tower → Historic Lisbon viewpoints Evening: → Alfama → Romantic dinner with Fado → Overnight at Lisbon', 2747),
  ('spain', 29, 'six-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 6', NULL, 'Breakfast → Romantic Sintra excursion → Pena Palace → Historic Centre of Sintra → Quinta da Regaleira → Cabo da Roca → Atlantic viewpoints → Couple photography Evening: → Return to Lisbon → Farewell dinner → Overnight at Lisbon', 2748),
  ('spain', 29, 'six-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 7', NULL, 'Breakfast → Leisure morning → Optional Lisbon café / shopping → Hotel checkout → Lisbon Airport → Departure', 2749),
  ('spain', 30, 'six-nights-family-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 1', NULL, 'Arrival at Barcelona → Family hotel check-in → Relax and refresh Evening: → Gothic Quarter → Las Ramblas → Barcelona waterfront → Family dinner → Overnight at Barcelona', 2750),
  ('spain', 30, 'six-nights-family-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 2', NULL, 'Breakfast at the hotel Morning: → Sagrada Família → Park Güell → Gaudí architecture Afternoon: Choose ONE: FAMILY_FUN: → Barcelona Aquarium → Waterfront → Leisure time OR INTERACTIVE: → CosmoCaixa → Family activities Evening: → Free time → Overnight at Barcelona', 2751),
  ('spain', 30, 'six-nights-family-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 3', NULL, 'Breakfast → Hotel checkout → Flight / train to Seville → Hotel check-in Afternoon: → Plaza de España → María Luisa Park → Santa Cruz Quarter → Family photography Evening: → Tapas / family dinner → Optional early Flamenco show → Overnight at Seville', 2752),
  ('spain', 30, 'six-nights-family-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 4', NULL, 'Breakfast Morning: → Real Alcázar → Seville Cathedral → Giralda Afternoon: → Triana → Guadalquivir riverfront → Optional river cruise → Ice cream / leisure time Evening: → Relaxed family dinner → Overnight at Seville', 2753),
  ('spain', 30, 'six-nights-family-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 5', NULL, 'Breakfast → Hotel checkout → Transfer toward Portugal → Arrive Lisbon → Family hotel check-in Afternoon: → Belém → Jerónimos Monastery → Belém Tower → Pastéis de Belém experience Evening: → Lisbon viewpoints → Family dinner → Overnight at Lisbon', 2754),
  ('spain', 30, 'six-nights-family-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 6', NULL, 'Breakfast → Sintra excursion → Pena Palace → Historic Centre of Sintra → Quinta da Regaleira → Cabo da Roca → Scenic family photography Evening: → Return to Lisbon → Leisure time → Overnight at Lisbon', 2755),
  ('spain', 30, 'six-nights-family-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 7', NULL, 'Breakfast → Leisure morning → Optional souvenir shopping → Hotel checkout → Lisbon Airport → Departure', 2756),
  ('spain', 31, 'six-nights-luxury-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 1', NULL, 'Arrival at Barcelona → Private airport transfer → 5-star / luxury hotel check-in → Relax and refresh Evening: → Private Barcelona orientation → Passeig de Gràcia → Gothic Quarter → Waterfront → Fine dining → Overnight at Barcelona', 2757),
  ('spain', 31, 'six-nights-luxury-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 2', NULL, 'Breakfast at the hotel Morning: → Private guided Sagrada Família → Casa Batlló / Gaudí architecture → Park Güell Afternoon: → Premium lunch → Luxury shopping at Passeig de Gràcia → Spa / hotel leisure Evening: → Rooftop sunset experience → Fine dining → Overnight at Barcelona', 2758),
  ('spain', 31, 'six-nights-luxury-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 3', NULL, 'Breakfast → Hotel checkout → Premium transfer / flight to Seville → Luxury hotel check-in Afternoon: → Private Real Alcázar visit → Seville Cathedral → Giralda → Santa Cruz Quarter Evening: → Premium tapas experience → Flamenco performance → Overnight at Seville', 2759),
  ('spain', 31, 'six-nights-luxury-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 4', NULL, 'Breakfast Morning: → Private Seville sightseeing → Plaza de España → María Luisa Park → Triana Afternoon: → Private / premium Guadalquivir cruise → Spa / pool / leisure time Evening: → Rooftop cocktails → Gourmet dinner → Overnight at Seville', 2760),
  ('spain', 31, 'six-nights-luxury-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 5', NULL, 'Breakfast → Hotel checkout → Private transfer / flight toward Lisbon → Luxury hotel check-in Afternoon: → Private Lisbon sightseeing → Belém → Jerónimos Monastery → Belém Tower → Historic viewpoints Evening: → Premium Fado + fine dining → Overnight at Lisbon', 2761),
  ('spain', 31, 'six-nights-luxury-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 6', NULL, 'Breakfast → Private chauffeured Sintra excursion → Pena Palace → Quinta da Regaleira → Historic Sintra → Cabo da Roca → Atlantic viewpoints Afternoon: → Premium lunch → Scenic return to Lisbon → Spa / leisure time Evening: → Special farewell dinner → Overnight at Lisbon', 2762),
  ('spain', 31, 'six-nights-luxury-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 7', NULL, 'Breakfast → Leisure morning → Optional luxury shopping / private experience → Hotel checkout → Private transfer to Lisbon Airport → Departure', 2763),
  ('spain', 32, 'travel-agent-insights', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS', 'What inexperienced planners often do wrong', NULL, '', 2764),
  ('spain', 32, 'travel-agent-insights', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS', 'What an experienced planner does differently', NULL, 'MADRID + BARCELONA + ONE_ANDALUSIA / MEDITERRANEAN / NORTHERN_SPAIN_EXPERIENCE rather than maximum destination count.', 2765),
  ('spain', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', NULL, NULL, 'IF: trip_length <= 4 nights THEN: prioritize_ONE_MAJOR_CITY + ONE_NEARBY_EXCURSION Reason: Very short stays gain more value from properly experiencing one major Spanish city than from losing time to repeated transfers. IF: trip_length >= 6 nights AND: traveler_interest == FIRST_TIME_SPAIN THEN: prioritize_MADRID + BARCELONA + ONE_CONTRASTING_REGION Reason: This gives a strong first-time balance of royal heritage, world-class museums, Gaudí architecture, gastronomy, city life, and regional contrast. IF: trip_length >= 8 nights AND: traveler_interest == FIRST_TIME_SPAIN THEN: prefer_MADRID + BARCELONA + SEVILLE_OR_GRANADA AND: use_HIGH_SPEED_RAIL_WHERE_PRACTICAL Reason: Madrid, Barcelona, and Andalusia provide three distinctly different Spanish experiences without requiring excessive destination count. IF: trip_type == HONEYMOON THEN: prefer_BARCELONA + SEVILLE_OR_GRANADA + ONE_COAST_OR_ISLAND_EXPERIENCE AND: increase_BOUTIQUE_STAYS + SCENIC_DINING + ROOFTOPS + FREE_TIME + COUPLE_EXPERIENCES Reason: Spain''s strongest honeymoon combinations mix historic cities, Mediterranean atmosphere, gastronomy, architecture, scenic evenings, and slower travel. IF: traveler_type == FAMILY THEN: prefer_BARCELONA + MADRID + VALENCIA_OR_COAST AND: include_INTERACTIVE_MUSEUMS + PARKS + AQUARIUMS + BEACHES + FAMILY_ATTRACTIONS AND: reduce_MUSEUM_DENSITY + LATE_NIGHT_ACTIVITY Reason: Spain offers strong family infrastructure through interactive museums, beaches, science attractions, theme parks, parks, and child-friendly urban experiences. IF: traveler_type == LUXURY THEN: prefer_MADRID + BARCELONA + MARBELLA_OR_MALLORCA + PREMIUM_REGIONAL_EXPERIENCE AND: increase_5_STAR_HOTELS + PRIVATE_GUIDES + FINE_DINING + PRIVATE_TRANSFERS + PREMIUM_SHOPPING + WINE Reason: Spanish luxury is strongest through high-end accommodation, internationally recognised gastronomy, premium shopping, wine regions, private cultural access, and Mediterranean resorts. IF: traveler_type == BUDGET THEN: prefer_PUBLIC_TRANSPORT + HIGH_SPEED_OR_STANDARD_RAIL + WALKING + WELL_CONNECTED_HOTELS AND: book_INTERCITY_TRANSPORT_EARLY AND: balance_PAID_ATTRACTIONS_WITH_FREE_NEIGHBOURHOODS + PARKS + BEACHES Reason: Spain can be travelled efficiently without a rental car on major city routes, while early transport planning and selective paid sightseeing improve value. IF: traveler_interest == CULTURE_AND_HERITAGE THEN: prioritize_MADRID + SEVILLE + GRANADA + CÓRDOBA + TOLEDO AND: include_PRADO + ROYAL_PALACE + REAL_ALCAZAR + ALHAMBRA + MEZQUITA_CATEDRAL Reason: These destinations provide one of Spain''s strongest combinations of royal, Islamic, Christian, artistic, and historic-city heritage. IF: traveler_interest == ART_AND_ARCHITECTURE THEN: prefer_MADRID + BARCELONA + BILBAO AND: include_PRADO + REINA_SOFIA + GAUDI + GUGGENHEIM IF: traveler_interest == GASTRONOMY THEN: prefer_SAN_SEBASTIAN + MADRID + BARCELONA + SEVILLE + BASQUE_COUNTRY_OR_RIOJA AND: include_TAPAS + PINTXOS + MARKETS + REGIONAL_DISHES + WINE + FINE_DINING Reason: Spain''s culinary strength extends from traditional regional cuisine and Mediterranean food to wine tourism and internationally recognised haute cuisine. IF: traveler_interest == BEACH_AND_MEDITERRANEAN THEN: prefer_BALEARES + COSTA_BRAVA + COSTA_DEL_SOL + VALENCIA_OR_ALICANTE AND: match_REGION_TO_SEASON + BEACH_STYLE + NIGHTLIFE_REQUIREMENT IF: traveler_interest == ISLAND_HOLIDAY THEN: choose_BALEARES_OR_CANARY_ISLANDS AND: do_not_treat_THEM_AS_INTERCHANGEABLE Reason: The Balearic Islands are particularly strong for Mediterranean summer travel, while the Canary Islands have different landscapes and a milder year-round climate profile. IF: traveler_interest == NIGHTLIFE THEN: prefer_MADRID + BARCELONA + IBIZA AND: match_AREA_TO_PARTY_STYLE + SEASON IF: traveler_interest == SHOPPING THEN: prefer_MADRID + BARCELONA AND: include_SERRANO_GOLDEN_MILE + PASSEIG_DE_GRACIA + MARKETS + LOCAL_DESIGN Reason: Madrid and Barcelona provide Spain''s strongest concentration of international luxury brands, Spanish fashion, boutiques, and premium shopping. IF: traveler_interest == WINE THEN: prefer_RIOJA + RIBERA_DEL_DUERO + JEREZ_OR_CATALONIA AND: include_WINERY_VISITS + LOCAL_GASTRONOMY AND: use_PRIVATE_DRIVER_OR_ORGANIZED_TRANSFER_WHEN_TASTING IF: traveler_interest == HIKING_AND_NATURE THEN: prefer_PYRENEES + PICOS_DE_EUROPA + CAMINO_DE_SANTIAGO + CANARY_ISLANDS + NATIONAL_PARKS AND: match_ROUTE_TO_FITNESS + ALTITUDE + WEATHER + SEASON IF: traveler_interest == CAMINO_DE_SANTIAGO THEN: choose_ROUTE + DAILY_DISTANCE + NUMBER_OF_STAGES AND: do_not_treat_CAMINO_AS_STANDARD_CITY_SIGHTSEEING Reason: The Camino is a multi-route walking or cycling experience whose itinerary should be designed around fitness, available days, luggage strategy, and preferred landscapes. IF: traveler_interest == PHOTOGRAPHY THEN: prefer_BARCELONA_GAUDI + SEVILLE + GRANADA + TOLEDO + ANDALUSIAN_WHITE_VILLAGES + COAST AND: prioritize_EARLY_MORNING + GOLDEN_HOUR + BLUE_HOUR IF: trip_length <= 7 nights THEN: prefer_MAXIMUM_TWO_OR_THREE_BASES AND: avoid_EXCESSIVE_HOTEL_CHANGES Reason: Spain''s excellent transport can encourage over-planning, but repeated transfers still reduce meaningful sightseeing and leisure time. IF: route == MADRID_TO_BARCELONA OR: route == MADRID_TO_SEVILLE OR: route == MADRID_TO_VALENCIA THEN: prefer_HIGH_SPEED_RAIL_OVER_RENTAL_CAR_FOR_STANDARD_CITY_TRAVEL Reason: Spain''s high-speed rail network links Madrid with Barcelona, Seville, Valencia, Málaga, and many other major destinations efficiently. IF: traveler_type == SENIOR OR: traveler_mobility == LIMITED THEN: prefer_CENTRAL_HOTELS + DIRECT_RAIL + PRIVATE_TRANSFER_WHEN_USEFUL + MODERATE_DAILY_SIGHTSEEING AND: reduce_STEEP_HISTORIC_WALKS + EXCESSIVE_STAIRS + RAPID_MULTI_CITY_MOVEMENT IF: traveler_uses_WHEELCHAIR THEN: prefer_VERIFIED_ACCESSIBLE_HOTELS + TRAINS + MUSEUMS + ATTRACTIONS + BEACHES AND: do_not_assume_HISTORIC_CENTRES + CASTLES + OLD_BUILDINGS + NATURE_ROUTES_ARE_FULLY_STEP_FREE Reason: Spain has substantial accessible tourism infrastructure across transport, museums, heritage cities, beaches, and nature areas, but individual facilities and routes still require verification. IF: weather == EXTREME_SUMMER_HEAT AND: region == CENTRAL_OR_SOUTHERN_SPAIN THEN: prioritize_EARLY_MORNING_SIGHTSEEING + INDOOR_MIDDAY_ACTIVITY + EVENING_EXPERIENCES AND: reduce_MIDDAY_OUTDOOR_WALKING IF: weather == RAINY THEN: increase_MUSEUMS + PALACES + MARKETS + GASTRONOMY + SHOPPING AND: reduce_LONG_OUTDOOR_TOURS + BEACH_DEPENDENT_ACTIVITY IF: traveler_interest == FIRST_TIME_SPAIN THEN: prioritize_MADRID + BARCELONA AND: add_ONE_OF_SEVILLE_GRANADA_VALENCIA_OR_NORTHERN_SPAIN AND: include_ONE_SIGNATURE_SPANISH_FOOD_OR_CULTURAL_EXPERIENCE IF: traveler_interest == CULTURE_AND_RELAXATION_BALANCE THEN: allocate_60_TO_70_PERCENT_TO_CORE_SIGHTSEEING AND: allocate_REMAINING_TIME_TO_TAPAS + PLAZAS + BEACHES + CAFES + SHOPPING + EVENING_WALKS + FREE_TIME', 2766),
  ('spain', 34, 'destination-scoring', 'DESTINATION SCORING', NULL, NULL, '| Factor | Score | | ------------------ | ----: | | Family | 94 | | Honeymoon | 92 | | Luxury | 90 | | Budget | 86 | | Adventure | 89 | | Culture | 97 | | Food | 98 | | Shopping | 88 | | Nightlife | 95 | | Relaxation | 90 | | Nature | 91 | | Accessibility | 85 | | Safety | 80 | | First-time visitor | 95 | | Photography | 96 |', 2767),
  ('spain', 35, 'final-travel-agent-verdict', 'FINAL TRAVEL AGENT VERDICT', NULL, NULL, 'Best traveler profiles: 1. Culture / heritage traveler 2. First-time Europe traveler 3. Food / wine traveler 4. Family traveler 5. Honeymoon / romantic traveler 6. Beach / island traveler 7. Photography traveler 8. Art / architecture traveler 9. Nightlife / social traveler 10. Nature / active traveler Best duration: 7–10 nights 3–4 nights: Best for ONE major city such as Madrid, Barcelona, or Seville + one nearby excursion. 5–7 nights: Best for TWO major bases such as Madrid + Barcelona or Barcelona + Seville. 8–10 nights: Excellent for Madrid + Barcelona + Andalusia / Valencia / one contrasting region. 11–14 nights: Best for deeper regional travel, northern Spain, islands, coast, wine regions, or multiple Andalusian cities. Best season: YEAR-ROUND Spring: CITIES + CULTURE + ANDALUSIA + NATURE + WALKING + PHOTOGRAPHY. Summer: BEACHES + ISLANDS + COAST + FESTIVALS + NIGHTLIFE + NORTHERN_SPAIN. Autumn: CULTURE + GASTRONOMY + WINE + CITY_BREAKS + NATURE + BETTER_WEATHER_FOR_WALKING. Winter: MADRID + BARCELONA + ANDALUSIA + CANARY_ISLANDS + CULTURE + WINTER_SPORTS. Spain''s official tourism guidance specifically treats the country as year-round: spring and autumn are particularly suitable for cities, cultural routes and nature; summer for beaches, outdoor activities and festivals; and winter for cities, the Canary Islands and snow sports. Best hotel strategy: Choose accommodation according to region, transport connectivity, and trip purpose. For first-time visitors: MADRID + BARCELONA + OPTIONAL_THIRD_REGIONAL_BASE. For Andalusia: Use SEVILLE + GRANADA selectively rather than changing hotels for every historic city. For beach / island: Choose the resort area carefully according to BEACH_STYLE + NIGHTLIFE + FAMILY + LUXURY requirements. For honeymoon / luxury: Prefer boutique historic hotels, premium urban hotels, beachfront resorts, vineyard stays, or scenic island properties. Avoid unnecessary hotel changes simply because high-speed rail makes many destinations appear close. Best transportation: Use: Spain should primarily be treated as: HIGH_SPEED_RAIL_FIRST + URBAN_PUBLIC_TRANSPORT + CAR_SELECTIVE + FLIGHT_FOR_ISLANDS_OR_LONG_DISTANCES Must-do for first-time visitor: Spain should not be reduced to monuments alone; official tourism positions ART_AND_CULTURE + COASTS_AND_BEACHES + URBAN_TOURISM + NATURE + FOOD_AND_WINE + SPORT_AND_ADVENTURE + SHOPPING + ROUTES as major national travel pillars. Don''t-do: Biggest advantage: Exceptional diversity within one country. Spain combines world-class art, UNESCO heritage, historic cities, Gaudí architecture, Mediterranean and Atlantic coasts, islands, beaches, gastronomy, wine, nightlife, mountains, pilgrimage routes, festivals, and strong transport infrastructure. Official tourism highlights more than 8,000 km of coastline and presents destinations ranging from Madrid, Barcelona and Seville to the Balearic and Canary Islands, allowing very different trip types within the same country. Biggest disadvantage: Spain''s size and regional variety make over-planning easy. Long distances between some regions, high summer temperatures in central and southern Spain, peak-season beach demand, major-event crowds, and advance-ticket requirements can reduce itinerary efficiency if planning is too aggressive. Overall destination score: 93/100', 2768),
  ('spain', 36, 'data-quality', 'DATA QUALITY', NULL, NULL, 'information_completeness: 97/100 last_updated: 2026-08-28 last_verified: WEB_VERIFIED verified_by: TURESPAÑA / SPAIN.INFO / RENFE / OFFICIAL REGIONAL TOURISM AND ACCESSIBILITY SOURCES sources: IMPORTANT: Hotel rates, rail fares, flight schedules, monument tickets, museum hours, ferry operations, attraction capacity, beach services, restaurant availability, festivals, and accessibility must NOT be treated as permanently valid. Major attractions such as SAGRADA_FAMILIA + ALHAMBRA + REAL_ALCAZAR + major museums can have timed-entry systems and strong demand; current ticket availability should always be verified. High-speed rail is a major planning advantage, but schedules, travel times, fares, operators, and direct services should be checked for the actual travel date. Spain''s climate varies significantly by region. CENTRAL_SPAIN and much of ANDALUSIA can become very hot in summer. NORTHERN_SPAIN generally has a cooler and wetter Atlantic influence. MEDITERRANEAN regions have different seasonal conditions from inland Spain. CANARY_ISLANDS offer a much milder winter climate than most mainland destinations. Beach conditions, sea temperature, seasonal services, storms, wind, and ferry operations should always be checked according to destination and month. Spain has substantial accessible tourism infrastructure. Official tourism currently highlights hundreds of accessible accommodation, dining, cultural, nature, beach, and leisure facilities, but accessibility varies considerably between individual sites and should still be verified. Historic quarters, medieval monuments, cobbled streets, castles, mountain routes, older hotels, and natural beaches should not automatically be considered step-free. Spain should primarily be treated as: SPRING: CITIES + CULTURE + ANDALUSIA + NATURE + FOOD + PHOTOGRAPHY SUMMER: BEACHES + ISLANDS + COAST + FESTIVALS + NIGHTLIFE + NORTHERN_SPAIN AUTUMN: CULTURE + GASTRONOMY + WINE + CITY_BREAKS + NATURE + PHOTOGRAPHY WINTER: CITIES + ANDALUSIA + CANARY_ISLANDS + GASTRONOMY + CULTURE + WINTER_SPORTS Turespaña / Spain.info, RENFE, official regional tourism boards, museums, monument authorities, ferry companies, national parks, airports, hotels, and individual attractions should be treated as primary sources for current operational information. This dataset should be refreshed regularly before production use.', 2769),
  ('portugal', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Spring', NULL, 'months: March April May weather: Mild and pleasant across Lisbon, Porto, and the Algarve, with warming temperatures and blooming landscapes. Higher inland areas like Serra da Estrela thaw out, while rainfall gradually decreases heading into May. crowd_level: LOW → MEDIUM price_level: MEDIUM overall_score: 76–80 recommended: true reason: Good for Lisbon, Porto, Sintra, wine tasting in the Douro Valley, coastal walking trails, photography, and spring sightseeing. Late spring is particularly ideal for outdoor adventures and historic city exploring before peak summer heat and tourist volumes arrive.', 2770),
  ('portugal', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Summer', NULL, 'months: June July August weather: Hot and sunny throughout the country, especially in the Algarve and Alentejo. Long daylight hours and near-zero rainfall along the coast. crowd_level: MEDIUM → HIGH price_level: HIGH → VERY HIGH overall_score: 70–76 recommended: true reason: Best for: July and August see peak European holiday traffic, high accommodation prices, and crowded beaches, though June benefits from vibrant cultural street festivals like Santos Populares.', 2771),
  ('portugal', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Autumn', NULL, 'months: September October November weather: September and October stay warm and dry with warm sea temperatures. November becomes cooler, windier, and significantly wetter across northern and central Portugal. crowd_level: HIGH → LOW price_level: MEDIUM → LOW overall_score: 76–83 recommended: true reason: September and October are widely considered the best time to visit Portugal for ideal weather, wine harvests (Douro Valley), warm water, and diminishing crowds. November sees increased rainfall, but offers exceptionally low prices and quiet city sightseeing in Lisbon, Porto, and local museums.', 2772),
  ('portugal', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Winter', NULL, 'months: December January February weather: Mild along the Algarve coast, cool and frequently rainy in Porto and the North, with occasional snowfall in the Serra da Estrela mountains. crowd_level: LOW → MEDIUM in Lisbon/Algarve during holidays price_level: LOW → MEDIUM overall_score: 69–75 recommended: true reason: Excellent for: Offers low accommodation rates and short queues at major sights like Sintra and Jerónimos Monastery, alongside big wave surfing season in Nazaré.', 2773),
  ('portugal', 10, 'budget-strategy', 'BUDGET STRATEGY', NULL, NULL, 'Where money can be saved: Where saving money is usually NOT recommended: Travel-agent rule: In Portugal, **ACCOMMODATION_BASE + REGIONAL_TRAIN + CITY_PASS + COASTAL_ACTIVITIES should be evaluated together**. For short stays, prioritize **LISBON + SINTRA_DAY_TRIP + CASCAIS** or **PORTO + DOURO_VALLEY_DAY_TRIP**. For longer stays, add **ALGARVE_COAST + COIMBRA / ÉVORA + DEEPER_REGIONAL_EXPLORATION** rather than changing hotels every night.', 2774),
  ('portugal', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Family', 'family', 'Portugal''s main international entry points are Lisbon (LIS), Porto (OPO), and Faro (FAO). For families arriving in Lisbon or Porto, direct Metro connections or family-friendly rideshares (Uber/Bolt) provide effortless city-center transfers. For young children, heavy luggage, or coastal stays in the Algarve or Douro Valley, pre-booked private transfers or airport rental car pickups are most comfortable.', 2775),
  ('portugal', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Honeymoon', 'honeymoon', 'Opt for private transfers directly from the airport to boutique city stays, Sintra palaces, or Douro Valley wine estates. For couples, PRIVATE_TRANSFER + SCENIC_COASTAL_OR_RIVER_ARRIVAL works exceptionally well when staying in luxury resorts or historic *pousadas*.', 2776),
  ('portugal', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Luxury', 'luxury', 'Use chauffeured premium sedans / SUVs from Lisbon (LIS), Porto (OPO), or Faro (FAO) airports. For multi-region luxury itineraries, combine: FIRST_CLASS_ALFA_PENDULAR_RAIL + PRIVATE_CHAUFFEUR + PRIVATE_YACHT_OR_HELICOPTER_TRANSFERS.', 2777),
  ('portugal', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Budget', 'budget', 'Use city Metro lines directly from Lisbon (Red Line) or Porto (Line E) terminals, or regional buses from Faro Airport. Main intercity gateways connect smoothly via: then continue via CP intercity trains or long-distance coaches (Rede Expressos / FlixBus).', 2778),
  ('portugal', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Senior', 'senior', 'Prefer direct express train connections (Alfa Pendular / Intercidades) or private door-to-door airport transfers to minimize luggage handling. Select centrally located hotels near elevator-accessible transit stations in hilly Lisbon and Porto.', 2779),
  ('portugal', 18, 'family-travel', 'FAMILY TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'child_friendly_score: 92 best_ages: Rules: For young children: Prefer: Avoid: Portugal''s warm climate, beaches, historic castles, and welcoming culture make it ideal for family travel.', 2780),
  ('portugal', 19, 'honeymoon-travel', 'HONEYMOON TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'honeymoon_score: 93 romance_score: 95 privacy_score: 88 luxury_score: 89 Recommended: Honeymoon itineraries should generally stay at: 2 major experiences/day. Prefer: SCENIC_VIEWS + HISTORIC_CHARM + LUXURY_STAYS + COAST / VINEYARDS + FINE_DINING over: Exhaustive sightseeing schedules and frequent hotel changes. Recommended areas:', 2781),
  ('portugal', 20, 'luxury-travel', 'LUXURY TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'luxury_score: 87 Recommended: Portugal luxury travel should focus on: Luxury value shines brightest in converted historic *pousadas*, Douro wine estates, and luxury Algarve coastal resorts.', 2782),
  ('portugal', 21, 'adventure', 'ADVENTURE', NULL, NULL, 'adventure_score: 85 Portugal is a top-tier European active-travel destination, particularly for water and coastal sports. Adventure experiences: With over 800 km of Atlantic coastline, famous surf breaks (Nazaré, Peniche, Ericeira), and rugged national parks, Portugal excels in marine and outdoor adventures. Match ocean activities to seasonal wave swells, tides, and certified local guide instructions.', 2783),
  ('portugal', 22, 'senior-travel', 'SENIOR TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'senior_suitability: 88 walking_intensity: LOW–MEDIUM when using taxis, trams, and flat promenades HIGH for self-guided walking on steep cobblestone hills and historic sights Rules: Portugal is highly welcoming to senior travelers, offering excellent healthcare, mild weather, rich history, and world-class rail connections. Portugal works particularly well for seniors as a: CULTURE + GASTRONOMY + SCENIC_RAIL + HISTORIC_TOWNS + RELAXED_COAST destination.', 2784),
  ('portugal', 23, 'accessibility', 'ACCESSIBILITY', NULL, NULL, 'wheelchair_accessibility: VARIABLE IN HISTORIC CITIES → GOOD IN MODERN INFRASTRUCTURE & RESORTS public_transport_accessibility: MODERATE → VERY_GOOD; modern Metros, Alfa Pendular trains, and buses are accessible, while historic trams are not hotel_accessibility: MUST_BE_VERIFIED_PER_HOTEL attraction_accessibility: MUST_BE_VERIFIED_PER_ATTRACTION Rule: Never assume step-free access in historic districts due to calcada cobblestones and steep slopes. Additional notes:', 2785),
  ('portugal', 24, 'food', 'FOOD', NULL, NULL, 'Portugal is particularly strong for: Portuguese cuisine centers on fresh ocean catches, rich regional meats, olive oil, local wines, and centuries-old conventual pastry traditions. Food experiences: Family: Prioritize Pastéis de Nata, grilled chicken (*Piri-Piri*), Bifanas, fresh fish, and casual beachside cafés. Honeymoon: Choose romantic cliffside seafood dining, Douro vineyard lunches, fine dining, and private wine pairings. Luxury: Include Michelin-starred restaurants, private chef dinners, exclusive cellar reserves, and high-end hotel dining. Budget: Utilize local *tascas* for the daily lunch special (*prato do dia*), neighborhood bakeries, and central food markets.', 2786),
  ('portugal', 25, 'shopping', 'SHOPPING', NULL, NULL, 'Strong categories: Luxury shopping: Prefer: Lisbon''s Avenida da Liberdade is Portugal''s flagship avenue for international luxury fashion and fine jewelry. Budget: Prefer: Travel-agent rule: Use LISBON_AVENIDA_LIBERDADE for LUXURY, CHIADO_AND_BAIXA for BOUTIQUES + CORK_PRODUCTS, LOCAL_MARKETS for FOOD_GIFTS + VINTAGE, and PORTO_AND_DOURO for PORT_WINE + TRADITIONAL_CERAMICS.', 2787),
  ('portugal', 26, 'nightlife', 'NIGHTLIFE', NULL, NULL, 'nightlife_level: 92 Suitable for: Best areas: Evening activities are better suited to: Portugal offers vibrant, late-night entertainment starting with dinner, moving to scenic rooftop bars, and continuing into lively street parties and dance clubs. Honeymoon travelers should generally prefer: ROOFTOP_BAR + FADO_DINNER + SUNSET_CRUISE + SCENIC_WALK over: Late-night clubbing unless specifically requested. Travel-agent rule: Position Portugal as a **VIBRANT LATE_NIGHT + ROOFTOP_BARS + FADO_CULTURE + WINE_BAR DESTINATION**, with Lisbon and Porto offering the highest nightlife concentration.', 2788),
  ('portugal', 28, 'sample-itinerary-patterns', 'SAMPLE ITINERARY PATTERNS', '3 NIGHTS', NULL, '### Day 1 Arrival at Lisbon Humberto Delgado Airport (LIS) → Metro / rideshare / private transfer to central Lisbon → Hotel check-in → Relaxation and refreshment Afternoon: Lisbon historic core orientation → Baixa and Rossio Square → Santa Justa Lift exterior → Chiado historic streets and cafés → Continue toward Commerce Square (Praça do Comércio) → Tagus Riverfront views → Tram 28 route corridor / Alfama neighborhood walk Evening: Traditional Portuguese dinner (Seafood / Bacalhau) → Scenic evening walk to a *Miradouro* (Viewpoint) → Optional traditional Fado music house experience → Hotel Baixa, Chiado, and Alfama form Lisbon''s primary historic cluster, offering an ideal introduction to the capital''s heritage, tiled architecture, and river views. ### Day 2 Morning: Breakfast → Train from Rossio Station to Sintra (40 mins) → UNESCO World Heritage landscape of Sintra → Pena National Palace and park → Panoramic views of the Sintra Mountains and coast → Historic center exploration Winter options: → Palácio Nacional de Sintra indoor touring → Sintra town center exploration → Traditional pastry tasting (*Travesseiros* & *Queijadas*) → Cosy café culture → Low-season palace photography Spring / Summer / Autumn options: → Park and Gardens of Pena walking trails → Quinta da Regaleira estate and initiation well → Castle of the Moors mountain walk → Cabo da Roca coastal viewpoint (Continental Europe''s westernmost point) → Outdoor photography and nature exploration Afternoon: Local Sintra lunch → Continue toward Cascais coastal town → Boca do Inferno cliffside viewpoint → Cascais historic center and promenade → Relaxed beach and seaside atmosphere → Atlantic coast panoramas Summer options: → Praia da Rainha beach relaxation → Coastal cycling or boardwalk walk → Oceanfront cafés → Seaside resort downtime Evening: Return to Lisbon (Scenic Cascais coastal train line to Cais do Sodré) → Hotel relaxation → Fresh seafood / contemporary dinner → Optional Time Out Market (Mercado da Ribeira) visit → Hotel Sintra, Cabo da Roca, Cascais, and the Estoril coast form the premier day-trip cluster from Lisbon, effortlessly combining royal heritage with Atlantic coastal landscapes. ### Day 3 Morning: Breakfast → Tram / bus to Belém maritime district → Jerónimos Monastery (UNESCO site) → Original Pastéis de Belém bakery visit → Belém Tower exterior and Tagus riverfront → Monument to the Discoveries (*Padrão dos Descobrimentos*) Afternoon: Waterfront lunch → Tagus River sunset sailboat cruise or MAAT Museum visit → Return to central Lisbon → Explore LX Factory creative district or Eduardo VII Park → Relaxed photography and shopping Evening: Return to central Lisbon → Sunset drinks at a hilltop *Miradouro* (e.g., Senhora do Monte) → Portuguese fine dining / gourmet *tasca* dinner → Optional Cais do Sodré / Bairro Alto nightlife → Hotel Belém''s Manueline monuments showcase Portugal''s Age of Discovery, making it a mandatory cultural pillar alongside Lisbon''s hilltop viewpoints and river cruises. Optional alternative according to traveler interest: FAMILY: → Lisbon Oceanarium (Oceanário de Lisboa) visit → Telecabine Lisboa cable car ride → Interactive Pavilhão do Conhecimento science museum → Cascais beach day and gentle coastal walks → Easy river cruise experience HONEYMOON: → Sunset private sailboat cruise on the Tagus → Romantic Sintra boutique hotel or palace day → Fine dining with Douro/Alentejo wine pairings → Luxury spa treatment → Sunset cocktails at a hilltop lounge → Intimate Fado dinner performance ADVENTURE: → Atlantic coast surf lesson (Carcavelos or Guincho) → Sintra mountain hiking / mountain biking → Sea kayaking along the Arrábida / Cascais cliffs → Coastal cliff trekking near Cabo da Roca CULTURE / HISTORY: → Deeper exploration of Jerónimos Monastery and Calouste Gulbenkian Museum → National Azulejo (Tile) Museum → São Jorge Castle and Roman Theatre ruins → Historic churches and conventual art tours FOOD: → Pastéis de Nata baking workshop → Time Out Market gourmet food tour → Traditional *tasca* lunch with *Prato do Dia* → Petiscos (Portuguese tapas) & Vinho Verde tasting → Modern Michelin-starred dining experience MOUNTAIN / NATURE: → Full-day Sintra Mountains + Cabo da Roca + Arrábida Natural Park circuit → Coastal cliff photography → Pristine Atlantic beaches and pine forest views → Nature reserve hiking trails Portugal tourism material consistently highlights Belém, Sintra, Cascais, and Lisbon''s historic quarters as essential year-round itineraries, supported by efficient rail links and a mild Atlantic climate. ### Day 4 Breakfast → Leisure morning in Lisbon → Shopping along Avenida da Liberdade or Chiado → Gourmet food souvenirs (Canned seafood, Port wine, Cork goods) → Café time at A Brasileira → Hotel checkout → Metro / rideshare / private transfer to Lisbon Airport (LIS) → Departure', 2789),
  ('portugal', 29, 'six-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 1', NULL, 'Arrival at Lisbon → Private transfer to Sintra → Romantic hotel check-in → Relax and refresh Evening: → Sintra Historic Centre → Romantic village walk → Portuguese dinner → Overnight at Sintra', 2790),
  ('portugal', 29, 'six-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 2', NULL, 'Breakfast Morning: → Pena Palace → Moorish Castle → Quinta da Regaleira → Romantic gardens and viewpoints Afternoon: → Cabo da Roca → Guincho / Atlantic coast → Cascais → Sunset couple photography Evening: → Romantic dinner → Overnight at Sintra', 2791),
  ('portugal', 29, 'six-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 3', NULL, 'Breakfast → Transfer to Lisbon Airport → Flight to Madeira → Hotel check-in Afternoon: → Câmara de Lobos → Cabo Girão viewpoint → Scenic coastal drive Evening: → Ocean-view dinner → Relaxed couple time → Overnight at Madeira', 2792),
  ('portugal', 29, 'six-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 4', NULL, 'Breakfast Morning: → Madeira scenic west tour → Ribeira Brava → Paul da Serra → Porto Moniz natural pools → Seixal Afternoon: → São Vicente → Mountain and coastal viewpoints → Couple photography Evening: → Spa / leisure → Romantic dinner → Overnight at Madeira', 2793),
