ational park (included). The horse and carriage tour will take us to Ross Castle which offers wonderful views by the lake. We include a short cruise to enjoy the beautiful views. Continuing, a brief stop in ADARE, a small village that preserves its picturesque traditional thatched-roof cottages and the ruins of the old abbey. Mid-afternoon we will arrive in LIMERICK. Time to stroll around its centre where you will have the opportunity to visit its castle, walk along the river, its cathedral or discover its shopping centre. Dinner included. Day 5 LIMERICK - MOHERS CLIFFS - GALWAY Today we will visit FOLK PARK in BUNRATTY (ticket included), a wonderful park where we can learn about how life was in Ireland in the past with its typical cottages and old markets. Its castle stands, accurately reproducing how life was in the Middle Ages. We will continue to CAHERCONNELL where the Poulnabrone dolmen is found. We may get the chance to see an exhibition of how dogs shepherd sheep. Afterwards, we will visit the impressive Cliffs of Moher which overlook the ocean, those who wish can walk to O’Brien’s Tower (entrance included). Our route continues through Burren National Park which displays amazing landscapes. Finally arriving in GALWAY. Day 6 GALWAY - CLONMACNOISE - DUBLIN We will depart for CONG, a small picturesque village located in a magnificent lake area. We will visit the ruins of the Royal Abbey and walk around Ashford Castle, a gorgeous medieval castle that has been turned into a hotel. We will travel to CLONMACNOISE, where after lunch, we will visit its monastic ruins (ticket and visit included). We will resume our journey back to DUBLIN, where we will arrive in the evening. Day 7 DUBLIN - CAERNARFON - LIVERPOOL We will board a ferry in the early morning. After a journey of three hours, we will arrive in Wales. We will visit CAERNARFON, a World Heritage site by the sea overlooked by an impressive castle. There will be time for lunch and a stroll. We continue to LIVERPOOL, where we will take a short bus ride through the city, a World Heritage Site and the second port of the United Kingdom. Afterwards, enjoy family-friendly free time along the historic Royal Albert Dock, take a turn on the Wheel of Liverpool for sweeping views of the River Mersey, or visit the interactive exhibits at the World Museum! Day 8 LIVERPOOL - STRATFORD - OXFORD - LONDON Today we explore central England. We will visit STRATFORD UPON AVON, Shakespeare’s hometown. Free time to have lunch and a stroll. Afterwards, we will travel to OXFORD, a town that is synonymous with study and culture. Kings, statesmen, philosophers and scientists have studied here! We will continue to LONDON, arriving in the evening. Day 9 LONDON After breakfast, end of our services.', 3290),
  ('liverpool', 31, '9-days-8-nights-luxury-itinerary', '9 Days 8 Nights Luxury Itinerary', NULL, NULL, 'Day 1 DUBLIN Welcome to international group departures! Upon arriving at Dublin Airport (DUB), your private luxury chauffeur will be waiting in the arrivals terminal to transfer you directly to your 5-star hotel in the city center (such as The Shelbourne or The Westbury). Check the information boards in the hotel reception area for details of the welcome meeting with your guide and fellow travelers. Enjoy a refined evening at leisure to settle into Ireland’s vibrant capital. Day 2 DUBLIN We start the day with an exclusive, expert-led sightseeing tour of DUBLIN, Ireland’s peaceful capital city. We will enjoy a stroll along the picturesque banks of the River Liffey, visiting its elegant Georgian parks, old university quadrangle, and lively downtown streets. We will stroll around Trinity College to view its historic architecture (depending on the duration of sunlight, this visit may take place the afternoon before, upon arrival in Dublin). Enjoy a free afternoon for high-end boutique shopping along Grafton Street or a private whiskey tasting. Day 3 DUBLIN - POWERSCOURT - KILKENNY - CASHEL - CORK In the morning we will depart from Dublin, heading south to the majestic POWERSCOURT estate. We will visit its magnificent gardens, designed in the 18th century and internationally considered among the most beautiful gardens in Ireland (entrance included). Admire its grand fountains, tranquility of the Japanese Gardens, and its unique historic pet cemetery. Afterwards, we will travel to KILKENNY, where we will have time for a gourmet lunch and to stroll around this lively medieval city. Further south, we will stop to visit the impressive Rock of CASHEL (entrance included), a breathtaking medieval fortress towering over the Golden Vale that symbolizes the historic fight of the Irish people against England. We will arrive in CORK in the evening. Time for a relaxed stroll through the center of Ireland’s second-largest city before an included fine-dining dinner. Day 4 CORK - KINSALE - KILLARNEY - LIMERICK We will depart for the gourmet coastal haven of KINSALE. Making a stop by Charles Fort, we will admire sweeping ocean views right beside the 17th-century star-shaped fortress. Time in the historic center of KINSALE, a colorful seaside town considered by many to be one of the most beautiful coastal destinations in Ireland. Afterwards, we will travel to KILLARNEY, a famed tourist town nestled in the heart of the countryside. Time for lunch and a stroll before enjoying a romantic horse-and-carriage (Jaunting Car) tour through Killarney National Park (included). The carriage tour takes us to the shores of Ross Castle, offering wonderful views across the lower lake, followed by a brief scenic lake cruise to take in the mountain scenery. Continuing onward, we make a brief stop in ADARE, a charming village preserved for its picturesque traditional thatched-roof cottages and old abbey ruins. Mid-afternoon we will arrive in LIMERICK. Time to stroll around its vibrant center, where you will have the opportunity to visit King John’s Castle, walk along the River Shannon, admire the cathedral, or explore its premier shopping venues. Dinner included. Day 5 LIMERICK - MOHERS CLIFFS - GALWAY Today we visit the iconic FOLK PARK in BUNRATTY (ticket included), an immersive heritage park where we learn how life was lived in Ireland’s past, complete with traditional thatched cottages and historic village shops. Its medieval castle stands proudly at the center, accurately reproducing life in the Middle Ages. We will continue through CAHERCONNELL, near the ancient Poulnabrone dolmen, where we may get the chance to see a sheepdog herding demonstration. Afterwards, we will visit the magnificent Cliffs of Moher soaring over the Atlantic Ocean; those who wish can walk up to O’Brien’s Tower for panoramic coastal vistas (entrance included). Our route continues through the limestone karst landscape of Burren National Park before finally arriving in vibrant GALWAY. Day 6 GALWAY - CLONMACNOISE - DUBLIN We depart for CONG, a picturesque village nestled in a serene lake district. We will visit the ruins of the Royal Abbey and stroll around the grounds of Ashford Castle, a magnificent 800-year-old medieval castle transformed into a world-renowned luxury hotel. We then travel to CLONMACNOISE, where after lunch, we will visit its ancient monastic ruins along the River Shannon (ticket and visit included). We will resume our journey back to DUBLIN, arriving in the evening for your final night in Ireland. Day 7 DUBLIN - CAERNARFON - LIVERPOOL We will board a premier morning ferry crossing the Irish Sea to North Wales. After a scenic three-hour journey across the water, we arrive on the Welsh coast and travel to historic CAERNARFON, a UNESCO World Heritage site by the sea overlooked by its massive 13th-century fortress. There will be time for lunch and a stroll through the walled town center. We continue into England to reach LIVERPOOL, where we will take a short bus ride through the city center, a maritime UNESCO World Heritage area and the historic second port of the United Kingdom. In the afternoon, embark on an exclusive VIP Beatles experience, exploring the city’s musical legacy with an option to visit The Beatles Story Museum at the Royal Albert Dock or take a private black cab tour of iconic Fab Four landmarks. Conclude the evening with fine dining and luxury accommodations at top heritage properties like The Municipal Hotel & Spa Liverpool - MGallery. Day 8 LIVERPOOL - STRATFORD - OXFORD - LONDON Today we explore the heart of central England. Leaving Liverpool, we travel to STRATFORD-UPON-AVON, the historic birthplace of William Shakespeare. Enjoy free time to stroll past half-timbered Tudor buildings, visit Shakespeare''s birthplace, and enjoy a riverside lunch along the River Avon. Afterwards, we travel to OXFORD, the world-famous city of spire architecture, deep intellect, and historic prestige. Walk in the footsteps of kings, statesmen, philosophers, and scientists who have studied in its centuries-old university colleges! We continue southeast to LONDON, arriving in the evening to check into your luxury capital accommodations. Day 9 LONDON After a full breakfast at your luxury hotel, our formal services come to an end. Depart at your leisure or extend your stay to enjoy private shopping, West End theatre, and fine dining in the UK capital.', 3291),
