  ('edinburg', 30, 'eight-nights-family-pattern', 'EIGHT-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 2', NULL, 'Breakfast Morning: → Edinburgh Castle → Royal Mile → St Giles'' Cathedral → Historic Old Town Afternoon: → National Museum of Scotland → Princes Street Gardens → Family photography Evening: → Relaxed Scottish dinner → Overnight at Edinburgh', 3329),
  ('edinburg', 30, 'eight-nights-family-pattern', 'EIGHT-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 3', NULL, 'Breakfast Choose ONE: FAMILY_FUN → Dynamic Earth → Holyrood Park → Camera Obscura / interactive city attraction → Family leisure ROYAL_EDINBURGH → Royal Yacht Britannia → Leith → Waterfront exploration Afternoon: → Dean Village / New Town → Shopping & cafés Evening: → Family dinner → Overnight at Edinburgh', 3330),
  ('edinburg', 30, 'eight-nights-family-pattern', 'EIGHT-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 4', NULL, 'Breakfast → Hotel checkout → Travel towards Dundee → Dundee waterfront → V&A Dundee → Discovery Point / RRS Discovery → Family-friendly waterfront exploration Afternoon: → Continue to Inverness → Family hotel check-in Evening: → River Ness → Inverness city centre → Family dinner → Overnight at Inverness', 3331),
  ('edinburg', 30, 'eight-nights-family-pattern', 'EIGHT-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 5', NULL, 'Breakfast → Loch Ness family excursion → Loch Ness viewpoints → Urquhart Castle → Optional Loch Ness cruise → Highland scenery Afternoon: → Culloden Battlefield OR Clava Cairns → Return to Inverness Evening: → Family leisure → Overnight at Inverness', 3332),
  ('edinburg', 30, 'eight-nights-family-pattern', 'EIGHT-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 6', NULL, 'Breakfast → Hotel checkout → Travel to Aberdeen → Family hotel check-in Afternoon: → Old Aberdeen → King''s College precinct → Aberdeen Beach → Harbour / Footdee area Evening: → Family dinner → Overnight at Aberdeen', 3333),
  ('edinburg', 30, 'eight-nights-family-pattern', 'EIGHT-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 7', NULL, 'Breakfast → Hotel checkout → Travel towards Stirling → Stirling Castle → Old Town → National Wallace Monument according to available time Afternoon: → Continue to Glasgow → Family hotel check-in Evening: → George Square → Buchanan Street → Family dinner → Overnight at Glasgow', 3334),
  ('edinburg', 30, 'eight-nights-family-pattern', 'EIGHT-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 8', NULL, 'Breakfast Morning: → Kelvingrove Art Gallery & Museum → Glasgow West End → University of Glasgow precinct Afternoon: Choose ONE: FAMILY_FUN → Glasgow Science Centre → Riverside Museum → River Clyde CITY_LEISURE → Glasgow Cathedral → Merchant City → Shopping → Cafés Evening: → Farewell family dinner → Overnight at Glasgow', 3335),
  ('edinburg', 30, 'eight-nights-family-pattern', 'EIGHT-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 9', NULL, 'Breakfast → Hotel checkout → Airport transfer → Departure', 3336),
  ('edinburg', 31, 'eight-nights-luxury-pattern', 'EIGHT-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 1', NULL, 'Arrival at Edinburgh Airport (EDI) → Private luxury airport transfer → Premium Edinburgh hotel check-in → Relax and refresh Evening: → Chauffeured Edinburgh orientation → Royal Mile → Calton Hill → Fine-dining Scottish experience → Overnight at Edinburgh', 3337),
  ('edinburg', 31, 'eight-nights-luxury-pattern', 'EIGHT-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 2', NULL, 'Breakfast → Privately guided Edinburgh heritage experience Morning: → Edinburgh Castle → Royal Mile → St Giles'' Cathedral → Historic closes & Old Town Afternoon: → Palace of Holyroodhouse → Holyrood Park → Private photography / curated city experience Evening: → Premium whisky tasting → Fine dining → Overnight at Edinburgh', 3338),
  ('edinburg', 31, 'eight-nights-luxury-pattern', 'EIGHT-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 3', NULL, 'Breakfast Choose ONE: PRIVATE_ROYAL_EDINBURGH → Royal Yacht Britannia → Chauffeured Leith waterfront exploration → Premium afternoon tea → Private New Town architecture tour LUXURY_LEISURE → Spa & wellness → George Street luxury shopping → Private afternoon tea → Chauffeured city leisure Evening: → Premium farewell Edinburgh dinner → Overnight at Edinburgh', 3339),
  ('edinburg', 31, 'eight-nights-luxury-pattern', 'EIGHT-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 4', NULL, 'Breakfast → Hotel checkout → Private chauffeured journey towards Dundee Morning / Afternoon: → Private Dundee waterfront experience → V&A Dundee → Discovery Point → Premium lunch overlooking the Tay → Continue through scenic Scotland towards Inverness → Luxury Highland hotel check-in Evening: → Premium Highland dining → Overnight at Inverness', 3340),
  ('edinburg', 31, 'eight-nights-luxury-pattern', 'EIGHT-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 5', NULL, 'Breakfast → Private chauffeured Highland experience → Loch Ness → Private / premium loch cruise → Urquhart Castle → Highland viewpoints Afternoon: Choose ONE: HIGHLAND_HERITAGE → Culloden Battlefield → Clava Cairns → Private historical interpretation LUXURY_LEISURE → Highland spa → Premium afternoon tea → Scenic estate experience Evening: → Fine dining → Overnight at Inverness', 3341),
  ('edinburg', 31, 'eight-nights-luxury-pattern', 'EIGHT-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 6', NULL, 'Breakfast → Hotel checkout → Private scenic transfer to Aberdeen → Luxury hotel check-in Afternoon: → Private Granite City tour → Old Aberdeen → King''s College → Footdee → Aberdeen coastline Evening: → Premium seafood / fine-dining experience → Overnight at Aberdeen', 3342),
  ('edinburg', 31, 'eight-nights-luxury-pattern', 'EIGHT-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 7', NULL, 'Breakfast → Hotel checkout → Private chauffeured transfer towards Stirling Afternoon: → Privately guided Stirling Castle → Stirling Old Town → National Wallace Monument viewpoints → Premium countryside lunch → Continue to Glasgow → Luxury hotel check-in Evening: → Chauffeured city orientation → Merchant City → Fine dining → Overnight at Glasgow', 3343),
  ('edinburg', 31, 'eight-nights-luxury-pattern', 'EIGHT-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 8', NULL, 'Breakfast → Private Glasgow city experience Morning: → Glasgow Cathedral → Kelvingrove Art Gallery & Museum → University of Glasgow / West End Afternoon: Choose ONE: LUXURY_LEISURE → Premium spa → Designer shopping → Afternoon tea → Chauffeured city exploration PRIVATE_CULTURE → Private architecture & art experience → Merchant City → Riverside / Clyde waterfront → Curated whisky experience Evening: → Farewell fine-dining Scottish experience → Overnight at Glasgow', 3344),
  ('edinburg', 31, 'eight-nights-luxury-pattern', 'EIGHT-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 9', NULL, 'Breakfast → Leisure morning → Hotel checkout → Private luxury airport transfer → Departure', 3345),
  ('edinburg', 32, 'travel-agent-insights', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS', 'What inexperienced planners often do wrong', NULL, '', 3346),
  ('edinburg', 32, 'travel-agent-insights', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS', 'What an experienced planner does differently', NULL, 'For first-time visits, prioritize: EDINBURGH_CASTLE + ROYAL_MILE + NATIONAL_MUSEUM_OR_HOLYROOD + GEORGIAN_NEW_TOWN before maximum attraction coverage.', 3347),
  ('edinburg', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', NULL, NULL, 'IF: trip_length <= 2 nights THEN: prioritize_EDINBURGH_CASTLE + ROYAL_MILE + NEW_TOWN_OR_CALTON_HILL AND: choose_ONE_OF_NATIONAL_MUSEUM_OR_HOLYROODHOUSE Reason: Very short Edinburgh trips gain more value from a concentrated Old Town + New Town itinerary than from attempting multiple outer neighborhoods. IF: trip_length == 3_OR_4_nights THEN: prioritize_EDINBURGH_CASTLE + ROYAL_MILE + NATIONAL_MUSEUM + HOLYROOD + NEW_TOWN AND: retain_ONE_BLOCK_FOR_CALTON_HILL_OR_ARTHURS_SEAT Reason: Three to four nights provide Edinburgh''s strongest first-time balance of medieval history, royal heritage, museums, Georgian architecture, landscapes and evening culture. IF: trip_length >= 5 nights THEN: add_DEAN_VILLAGE + STOCKBRIDGE_BOTANICS + LEITH_BRITANNIA Reason: Longer stays allow Edinburgh''s residential neighborhoods, waterfront, gardens and wider cultural experiences to be explored without excessive rushing. IF: trip_length >= 6 nights THEN: consider_ONE_OF_ROSSLYN_CHAPEL + SOUTH_QUEENSFERRY + EAST_LOTHIAN + STIRLING Reason: Edinburgh becomes a stronger extended base when central-city sightseeing is combined with one or more contrasting heritage, coastal or countryside excursions. IF: trip_type == HONEYMOON THEN: prefer_BOUTIQUE_OR_LUXURY_HOTEL + DEAN_VILLAGE + CALTON_HILL + FINE_DINING + RELAXED_NEW_TOWN_EVENING AND: reduce_DAILY_MUSEUM_COUNT Reason: Edinburgh''s romantic strength comes from historic architecture, scenic viewpoints, atmospheric neighborhoods, premium hotels and dining rather than nonstop attraction scheduling. IF: traveler_type == FAMILY THEN: prioritize_NATIONAL_MUSEUM + CAMERA_OBSCURA + DYNAMIC_EARTH + ZOO_OR_BRITANNIA AND: include_GARDEN_OR_PARK_BREAKS Reason: Families benefit from combining interactive museums and heritage with outdoor recreation rather than continuous history-heavy sightseeing. IF: traveler_type == LUXURY THEN: prefer_FIVE_STAR_OR_HERITAGE_HOTEL + PRIVATE_GUIDE + PREMIUM_DINING + CHAUFFEUR_SELECTIVELY AND: add_PRIVATE_COUNTRYSIDE_OR_STIRLING_EXCURSION_IF_RELEVANT Reason: Edinburgh''s strongest luxury positioning combines prestigious accommodation, private heritage interpretation, Scottish gastronomy and premium regional touring. IF: traveler_type == BUDGET THEN: prefer_CENTRAL_VALUE_HOTEL_OR_HOSTEL + WALKING + BUS_OR_TRAM + FREE_MUSEUMS_AND_GALLERIES AND: limit_TAXIS + FESTIVAL_PEAK_DATES + EXCESSIVE_PAID_ATTRACTIONS Reason: Edinburgh accommodation can be expensive, but extensive walking, public transport, free museums, galleries, parks and viewpoints significantly improve value. IF: traveler_interest == SCOTTISH_HISTORY THEN: prioritize_EDINBURGH_CASTLE + ROYAL_MILE + NATIONAL_MUSEUM + HOLYROODHOUSE + SCOTTISH_PARLIAMENT Reason: Edinburgh concentrates royal, military, religious, political and national history within a comparatively compact urban area. IF: traveler_interest == LITERATURE THEN: prioritize_OLD_TOWN + WRITERS_MUSEUM + SCOTTISH_LITERARY_HERITAGE + BOOKSHOPS + STORYTELLING_OR_LITERARY_WALK Reason: Edinburgh has an internationally significant literary identity associated with historic and contemporary Scottish writing and was the world''s first UNESCO City of Literature. IF: traveler_interest == EDINBURGH_CASTLE THEN: prioritize_CASTLE_INTERIORS + CROWN_AND_ROYAL_HISTORY + MILITARY_HERITAGE + CASTLE_VIEWPOINTS AND: reserve_TIMED_ENTRY_IN_ADVANCE Reason: Edinburgh Castle is the city''s defining paid heritage attraction and high-demand entry periods can sell out, particularly in summer and during festivals. IF: traveler_interest == ROYAL_MILE THEN: combine_CASTLE_ESPLANADE + ST_GILES + HISTORIC_CLOSES + VICTORIA_STREET_OR_GRASSMARKET Reason: The Royal Mile is most valuable when treated as a complete medieval urban landscape rather than simply a walking route between Edinburgh Castle and Holyrood. IF: traveler_interest == PALACE_OF_HOLYROODHOUSE THEN: verify_CURRENT_PUBLIC_OPENING_STATUS AND: combine_WITH_SCOTTISH_PARLIAMENT + HOLYROOD_PARK_IF_RELEVANT Reason: As a working royal residence, visitor access can be affected by royal use, ceremonial activity and seasonal operating arrangements. IF: traveler_interest == ROYAL_HISTORY THEN: prioritize_EDINBURGH_CASTLE + PALACE_OF_HOLYROODHOUSE + ROYAL_MILE + ROYAL_YACHT_BRITANNIA_IF_TIME_ALLOWS Reason: Edinburgh provides an unusually strong sequence of medieval, early-modern and modern royal heritage across the Castle, Holyrood and Britannia. IF: traveler_interest == ARTHURS_SEAT THEN: check_WEATHER + WIND + VISIBILITY + FOOTWEAR + MOBILITY AND: allocate_APPROXIMATELY_2_TO_3_HOURS_BASED_ON_ROUTE Reason: Arthur''s Seat is a volcanic hill rather than a conventional paved viewpoint and requires appropriate conditions and physical capability. IF: traveler_interest == ARTHURS_SEAT AND: weather == STRONG_WIND_OR_HEAVY_RAIN THEN: replace_WITH_CALTON_HILL_OR_INDOOR_CULTURAL_SIGHTSEEING Reason: Exposed slopes and uneven terrain make Arthur''s Seat considerably less suitable during poor weather. IF: traveler_interest == EASY_PANORAMIC_VIEW THEN: prioritize_CALTON_HILL OVER: ARTHURS_SEAT Reason: Calton Hill provides one of Edinburgh''s strongest city panoramas with substantially lower walking intensity than the ascent of Arthur''s Seat. IF: traveler_interest == GEORGIAN_ARCHITECTURE THEN: prioritize_NEW_TOWN + CHARLOTTE_SQUARE + GEORGE_STREET + ST_ANDREW_SQUARE + PRINCES_STREET_GARDENS Reason: Edinburgh''s planned Georgian New Town forms a defining part of the UNESCO World Heritage property and provides a major architectural contrast with the medieval Old Town. IF: traveler_interest == MUSEUMS THEN: prioritize_NATIONAL_MUSEUM_OF_SCOTLAND + NATIONAL_GALLERY + MODERN_ART_BASED_ON_INTEREST Reason: Edinburgh combines major national collections covering Scottish history, natural sciences, world cultures, fine art and modern art, with several institutions offering free general admission. IF: traveler_interest == FAMILY_INTERACTIVE_MUSEUMS THEN: prioritize_CAMERA_OBSCURA + DYNAMIC_EARTH + NATIONAL_MUSEUM AND: combine_WITH_PRINCES_STREET_GARDENS_OR_ZOO Reason: Interactive interpretation works particularly well for families when balanced with parks, wildlife or shorter outdoor experiences. IF: traveler_interest == EDINBURGH_ZOO THEN: allocate_HALF_DAY_OR_LONGER AND: prepare_FOR_HILLY_WALKING Reason: Edinburgh Zoo is a substantial attraction on sloping terrain and works best as a dedicated family or wildlife experience rather than a short city-centre add-on. IF: traveler_interest == ROYAL_YACHT_BRITANNIA THEN: prioritize_LEITH + BRITANNIA AND: combine_WITH_THE_SHORE_OR_WATERFRONT_DINING Reason: Britannia becomes a stronger half-day experience when combined with Leith''s historic waterfront and dining scene. IF: traveler_interest == LEITH THEN: use_TRAM_OR_BUS_WHERE_SUITABLE AND: combine_BRITANNIA + THE_SHORE + FOOD_OR_DRINK Reason: Leith is well connected to central Edinburgh and provides a strong contrast between royal maritime history and contemporary waterfront culture. IF: traveler_interest == FOOD THEN: include_MODERN_SCOTTISH_CUISINE + SEAFOOD + PUB_FOOD + LOCAL_SCOTTISH_PRODUCT AND: retain_ONE_HIGH_QUALITY_RESTAURANT_EXPERIENCE Reason: Edinburgh''s food scene extends well beyond traditional haggis through Scottish seafood, beef, game, bakeries, international cuisine and contemporary fine dining. IF: traveler_interest == WHISKY THEN: combine_ONE_QUALITY_TASTING_OR_WHISKY_EXPERIENCE + SCOTTISH_DINING AND: avoid_DRINKING_AND_DRIVING Reason: Whisky is an important element of Edinburgh''s visitor experience but is best incorporated selectively alongside wider Scottish gastronomy and culture. IF: traveler_interest == NIGHTLIFE THEN: combine_HISTORIC_PUB + LIVE_MUSIC_OR_THEATRE + ONE_NON_ROYAL_MILE_AREA AND: consider_GRASSMARKET + COWGATE + NEW_TOWN + LEITH_BASED_ON_STYLE Reason: Edinburgh nightlife extends beyond Royal Mile tourist pubs through live music, whisky bars, cocktail venues, theatres, comedy and neighborhood nightlife. IF: traveler_interest == FESTIVALS THEN: prioritize_EVENT_SCHEDULE + ADVANCE_TICKETS + CENTRAL_TRANSPORTABLE_HOTEL AND: reduce_NORMAL_DAILY_SIGHTSEEING_COUNT Reason: Major Edinburgh festivals can substantially change street conditions, attraction demand, restaurant availability and realistic sightseeing pace. IF: travel_month == AUGUST THEN: expect_EXTREME_VISITOR_PRESSURE + VERY_HIGH_ACCOMMODATION_DEMAND + FESTIVAL_CONGESTION AND: book_HOTEL + MAJOR_ATTRACTIONS + FESTIVAL_TICKETS + IMPORTANT_RESTAURANTS_EARLY Reason: The Edinburgh Festival Fringe, Edinburgh International Festival, Royal Edinburgh Military Tattoo and other major cultural events overlap during August, creating the city''s strongest annual demand period. IF: traveler_interest == MILITARY_TATTOO THEN: reserve_TICKET_WELL_IN_ADVANCE AND: allow_EXTRA_ACCESS_TIME_AROUND_CASTLE_ESPLANADE Reason: The Royal Edinburgh Military Tattoo is one of Edinburgh''s highest-demand seasonal events and operates directly in the Castle precinct during the busy August festival period. IF: traveler_interest == DEAN_VILLAGE THEN: combine_DEAN_VILLAGE + WATER_OF_LEITH + WEST_END_OR_STOCKBRIDGE Reason: Dean Village provides greater itinerary value when integrated into the surrounding riverside walking network instead of being treated as a brief isolated photography stop. IF: traveler_interest == STOCKBRIDGE THEN: combine_STOCKBRIDGE + ROYAL_BOTANIC_GARDEN + INVERLEITH_OR_WATER_OF_LEITH Reason: Stockbridge works particularly well as a relaxed half-day neighborhood experience combining cafés, independent shopping, gardens and local atmosphere. IF: traveler_interest == BOTANIC_GARDEN THEN: prioritize_ROYAL_BOTANIC_GARDEN + STOCKBRIDGE AND: check_INDIVIDUAL_GLASSHOUSE_OR_SPECIAL_EXHIBITION_STATUS_SEPARATELY Reason: The Royal Botanic Garden provides one of Edinburgh''s strongest free green-space experiences, while individual facilities or exhibitions can operate under separate access arrangements. IF: traveler_interest == PORTOBELLO THEN: combine_BEACH + PROMENADE + CAFE_OR_LOCAL_DINING AND: use_BUS_OR_OTHER_SUITABLE_PUBLIC_TRANSPORT Reason: Portobello provides Edinburgh''s strongest urban seaside contrast but works best as a relaxed neighborhood excursion rather than a rapid sightseeing stop. IF: traveler_interest == NATURE THEN: prioritize_ARTHURS_SEAT_OR_HOLYROOD_PARK + BOTANIC_GARDEN + WATER_OF_LEITH AND: consider_PORTOBELLO_IF_TIME_ALLOWS Reason: Edinburgh combines volcanic hills, major gardens, riverside corridors and coastline within the wider urban destination. IF: traveler_interest == PHOTOGRAPHY THEN: prioritize_CASTLE_AREA_EARLY + VICTORIA_STREET_EARLY + CALTON_HILL_GOLDEN_HOUR + DEAN_VILLAGE + ARTHURS_SEAT_WHEN_SUITABLE Reason: Early and late hours improve atmosphere and reduce crowd pressure at Edinburgh''s most photographed historic streets and viewpoints. IF: traveler_type == SENIOR THEN: prefer_CENTRAL_ACCESSIBLE_HOTEL + SHORT_WALKING_CLUSTERS + BUS_TRAM_OR_TAXI_FOR_LONGER_TRANSFERS AND: reduce_STEEP_OLD_TOWN_CLIMBS + ARTHURS_SEAT + LONG_COBBLED_WALKING Reason: Edinburgh is highly rewarding for seniors but its gradients, cobbles, castle terrain and elevation changes require considerably more mobility planning than flatter European city destinations. IF: traveler_uses_WHEELCHAIR THEN: use_VERIFIED_ACCESSIBLE_BUS_AND_TRAM_SERVICES + ACCESSIBLE_HOTEL AND: verify_CASTLE + HISTORIC_OLD_TOWN + INDIVIDUAL_HERITAGE_ATTRACTIONS_SEPARATELY Reason: Edinburgh''s modern public transport provides substantial accessible infrastructure while medieval terrain, cobbles, slopes and historic buildings remain variable. IF: traveler_uses_WHEELCHAIR AND: plan_includes_EDINBURGH_CASTLE THEN: verify_CURRENT_CASTLE_ACCESSIBILITY_SUPPORT + MOBILITY_ASSISTANCE + ROUTE_RESTRICTIONS Reason: Edinburgh Castle contains steep gradients, cobbled surfaces and historic buildings, so accessible routing requires attraction-specific planning rather than assumptions based on general city accessibility. IF: season == MARCH_TO_MAY THEN: increase_WALKING + BOTANIC_GARDEN + DEAN_VILLAGE + ARTHURS_SEAT_WHEN_WEATHER_ALLOWS AND: retain_RAIN_AND_WIND_PROTECTION Reason: Increasing daylight and improving temperatures make spring one of Edinburgh''s strongest periods for mixed heritage, gardens and outdoor sightseeing. IF: season == JUNE_TO_JULY THEN: expect_LONG_DAYLIGHT + STRONG_OUTDOOR_SIGHTSEEING + HIGHER_VISITOR_PRESSURE AND: book_MAJOR_ATTRACTIONS_AND_HOTELS_EARLY Reason: Early and mid-summer provide Edinburgh''s longest daylight and generally strongest outdoor conditions, but tourism demand and accommodation pressure rise substantially. IF: season == AUGUST THEN: prioritize_FESTIVALS + PREBOOKED_CASTLE + EVENING_EVENTS + FLEXIBLE_WALKING_BLOCKS AND: reduce_NORMAL_ATTRACTION_DENSITY Reason: August should be treated as a festival destination period rather than a normal sightseeing month because city-centre congestion and event schedules materially affect itinerary pace. IF: season == SEPTEMBER THEN: prioritize_WALKING + ARTHURS_SEAT + DEAN_VILLAGE + STOCKBRIDGE + CULTURE + FOOD Reason: September commonly provides a strong post-festival balance between relatively mild conditions, cultural activity and more manageable visitor pressure. IF: season == OCTOBER_TO_NOVEMBER THEN: increase_MUSEUMS + GALLERIES + FOOD + WHISKY + HISTORIC_INTERIORS AND: retain_SHORTER_OUTDOOR_BLOCKS Reason: Cooling temperatures, increasing rainfall and shorter daylight progressively increase the value of Edinburgh''s strong indoor cultural and gastronomic inventory. IF: season == DECEMBER THEN: prioritize_CHRISTMAS_ATMOSPHERE + MUSEUMS + FOOD + PUBS + NEW_TOWN_EVENINGS AND: expect_SHORT_DAYLIGHT + SEASONAL_DEMAND Reason: December combines strong festive atmosphere with limited daylight, cold weather and periods of increased accommodation and entertainment demand. IF: season == JANUARY_TO_FEBRUARY THEN: prioritize_MUSEUMS + GALLERIES + CASTLE + FOOD + WHISKY + THEATRE AND: reduce_LONG_OUTDOOR_PROGRAMS_DURING_POOR_WEATHER Reason: Winter''s short daylight, cold temperatures and changeable weather favor Edinburgh''s substantial indoor cultural inventory while often providing lower visitor pressure outside special events. IF: weather == HEAVY_RAIN THEN: replace_EXTENDED_WALKING_WITH_NATIONAL_MUSEUM + NATIONAL_GALLERY + CAMERA_OBSCURA + DYNAMIC_EARTH_OR_OTHER_INDOOR_ATTRACTION AND: retain_FLEXIBLE_BUS_TRAM_OR_TAXI_PLAN Reason: Edinburgh weather remains changeable throughout the year, making its extensive museum, gallery and indoor attraction inventory essential for resilient itinerary design. IF: weather == STRONG_WIND_OR_HEAVY_RAIN AND: plan_includes_ARTHURS_SEAT THEN: reduce_OR_REPLACE_HILL_WALK AND: use_CALTON_HILL_IF_SAFE_OR_INDOOR_CULTURAL_ALTERNATIVE Reason: Arthur''s Seat and Salisbury Crags are exposed landscapes where wind, rain and poor visibility can materially reduce comfort and suitability. IF: weather == SNOW_OR_ICE THEN: reduce_ARTHURS_SEAT + STEEP_CLOSES + UNEVEN_HISTORIC_WALKING AND: increase_MUSEUMS + GALLERIES + PUBLIC_TRANSPORT_USAGE Reason: Ice and snow can significantly increase difficulty on Edinburgh''s slopes, steps, cobbled streets and natural hill routes. IF: route == EDINBURGH_AIRPORT_TO_CITY_CENTRE THEN: prefer_TRAM_OR_AIRPORT_BUS_FOR_STANDARD_TRAVEL AND: use_TAXI_OR_PRIVATE_TRANSFER_FOR_HEAVY_LUGGAGE + MOBILITY_LIMITATIONS + PREMIUM_TRAVEL Reason: Edinburgh Airport has direct public-transport connections to the city centre, making a rental car unnecessary for most arriving city-break travelers. IF: route == CENTRAL_EDINBURGH_TO_LEITH THEN: prefer_TRAM_OR_BUS_WHERE_SUITABLE Reason: Leith and the Royal Yacht Britannia area are directly connected with central Edinburgh by frequent urban public transport. IF: route == CENTRAL_EDINBURGH_TO_EDINBURGH_ZOO THEN: prefer_BUS_OR_TAXI_BASED_ON_TRAVELER_NEEDS Reason: Edinburgh Zoo lies west of the principal historic centre and is more efficiently reached by road-based public transport than by incorporating it into a central walking itinerary. IF: route == CENTRAL_EDINBURGH_TO_PORTOBELLO THEN: prefer_BUS_OR_OTHER_SUITABLE_PUBLIC_TRANSPORT Reason: Portobello is easily incorporated as a separate coastal excursion without requiring a private vehicle or hotel change. IF: movement == CENTRAL_EDINBURGH_SIGHTSEEING THEN: prefer_WALKING AND: use_LOTHIAN_BUSES + EDINBURGH_TRAMS + SELECTIVE_TAXI_AS_REQUIRED Reason: Edinburgh''s principal visitor districts are geographically compact, while public transport is most valuable for longer movements and reducing repeated elevation changes. IF: movement == OLD_TOWN_TO_NEW_TOWN AND: traveler_has_MOBILITY_LIMITATION THEN: consider_BUS_OR_TAXI_FOR_DIFFICULT_ELEVATION_CHANGES Reason: Map distance alone understates the physical difficulty created by Edinburgh''s steep gradients, bridges, closes and elevation differences. IF: trip_length <= 4 nights THEN: avoid_RENTAL_CAR_FOR_PRIMARY_EDINBURGH_CITY_ITINERARY AND: use_WALKING + PUBLIC_TRANSPORT + SELECTIVE_TAXIS Reason: A car is generally unnecessary for Edinburgh''s principal visitor areas and can add parking, restricted-access and traffic friction to an otherwise walkable and transit-connected itinerary. IF: trip_length >= 5 nights AND: traveler_interest == BOTH_CITY_AND_COAST THEN: retain_ONE_EDINBURGH_HOTEL_BASE AND: use_PUBLIC_TRANSPORT_FOR_PORTOBELLO_OR_LOCAL_COASTAL_MOVEMENTS Reason: Edinburgh''s coastal districts can generally be explored without unnecessary hotel changes. IF: trip_length >= 5 nights AND: traveler_interest == SCOTTISH_HISTORY THEN: consider_STIRLING_AS_DAY_TRIP_OR_SECONDARY_STOP Reason: Stirling provides a strong extension of Edinburgh''s royal and national-history narrative through its castle, Old Town and central role in Scottish history. IF: trip_length >= 6 nights AND: traveler_interest == WIDER_SCOTLAND THEN: consider_EDINBURGH_BASE + ONE_SECONDARY_SCOTTISH_REGION AND: avoid_USING_EDINBURGH_AS_BASE_FOR_EVERY_DISTANT_HIGHLAND_EXCURSION Reason: Edinburgh is an excellent Scottish gateway, but Highlands, Inverness, Aberdeen, Glasgow and other distant regions become more enjoyable when unnecessary repeated long-distance day travel is reduced. IF: traveler_interest == FIRST_TIME_EDINBURGH THEN: prioritize_EDINBURGH_CASTLE + ROYAL_MILE + NATIONAL_MUSEUM_OR_HOLYROOD + GEORGIAN_NEW_TOWN AND: add_ARTHURS_SEAT + DEAN_VILLAGE + LEITH_ONLY_IF_TIME_ALLOWS Reason: These experiences provide Edinburgh''s strongest first introduction to Scottish history, medieval heritage, royal culture, architecture, museums and the city''s dramatic urban landscape.', 3348),
  ('edinburg', 34, 'destination-scoring', 'DESTINATION SCORING', NULL, NULL, '| Factor | Score | | --- | --- | | Family | 92 | | Honeymoon | 90 | | Luxury | 90 | | Budget | 69 | | Adventure | 74 | | Culture | 97 | | Food | 91 | | Shopping | 89 | | Nightlife | 92 | | Relaxation | 86 | | Nature | 88 | | Accessibility | 79 | | Safety | 86 | | First-time visitor | 97 | | Photography | 97 |', 3349),
  ('edinburg', 35, 'final-travel-agent-verdict', 'FINAL TRAVEL AGENT VERDICT', NULL, NULL, 'Best traveler profiles: 1. First-time heritage / history traveler (Edinburgh Castle, Royal Mile, St Giles'' Cathedral, Palace of Holyroodhouse, Old Town closes) 2. Culture / festival traveler (Edinburgh Festival Fringe, Edinburgh International Festival, Royal Edinburgh Military Tattoo, International Book Festival, museums and galleries) 3. Photography traveler (Edinburgh Castle skyline, Victoria Street, Calton Hill, Arthur''s Seat, Dean Village, Georgian New Town) 4. Architecture / urban-design traveler (UNESCO Old Town, Georgian New Town, Charlotte Square, Moray Estate, neoclassical monuments) 5. Romantic / honeymoon traveler (Dean Village, Stockbridge, Calton Hill sunset, historic hotels, fine dining, atmospheric Old Town evenings) 6. Family traveler (Edinburgh Castle, National Museum of Scotland, Camera Obscura, Dynamic Earth, Edinburgh Zoo, Royal Yacht Britannia) 7. Food / whisky traveler (traditional Scottish cuisine, whisky tastings, Leith dining, Stockbridge cafés, historic pubs, modern Scottish restaurants) 8. Luxury traveler (five-star heritage hotels, chauffeur transfers, private guides, premium dining, whisky experiences, private Scotland excursions) 9. Solo / independent traveler (compact historic centre, museums, walking routes, reliable bus and tram network, extensive cultural programming) 10. Nature / soft-adventure traveler (Arthur''s Seat, Salisbury Crags, Holyrood Park, Water of Leith, Royal Botanic Garden, Portobello coast) Best duration: 3–5 nights 2 nights: Best for EDINBURGH_CASTLE + ROYAL_MILE + NATIONAL_MUSEUM + NEW_TOWN + CALTON_HILL as a concentrated first-time heritage city break. 3–4 nights: Best for BALANCED_FIRST_VISIT, adding Palace of Holyroodhouse, Arthur''s Seat or Holyrood Park, Dean Village, Stockbridge and relaxed evening dining. 5–6 nights: Best for DEEPER_EDINBURGH including Royal Botanic Garden, Leith, Royal Yacht Britannia, modern-art galleries, Water of Leith, Portobello and neighborhood food experiences. 7+ nights: Best when Edinburgh is used as a SCOTLAND_GATEWAY, combining the capital with Rosslyn Chapel, South Queensferry, Stirling, East Lothian, whisky-country touring, golf or selected Highlands excursions. Best season: YEAR-ROUND Spring / Prime Sightseeing Season (March – May): LONGER_DAYLIGHT + BLOOMING_GARDENS + OLD_TOWN_WALKING + ARTHURS_SEAT + LOWER_PEAK_PRESSURE + PHOTOGRAPHY. Summer / Festival Season (June – August): LONG_DAYLIGHT + MILDER_WEATHER + OUTDOOR_SIGHTSEEING + FESTIVALS + MILITARY_TATTOO + EVENING_ACTIVITY, but August requires substantial advance planning because of exceptional visitor demand. Autumn / Cultural Season (September – November): POST_FESTIVAL_CALM + AUTUMN_PHOTOGRAPHY + MUSEUMS + WHISKY + FOOD + HISTORIC_WALKS + LOWER_VISITOR_PRESSURE. Winter / Festive City-Break Season (December – February): CHRISTMAS_AND_HOGMANAY + MUSEUMS + HISTORIC_PUBS + WHISKY + ATMOSPHERIC_OLD_TOWN + LOWER_OFF_PEAK_CROWDS, with cold weather and short daylight requiring flexible planning. Edinburgh should therefore be treated as a genuine YEAR_ROUND_CITY_DESTINATION, with spring and early autumn offering the strongest general sightseeing balance, summer providing maximum cultural activity, and August operating as a distinct high-demand festival season. Best hotel strategy: Choose accommodation according to walking tolerance, atmosphere, sightseeing priorities, festival dates and transport access. For first-time visitors: OLD_TOWN / NEW_TOWN / WEST_END for efficient access to Edinburgh Castle, Royal Mile, museums, restaurants, Waverley Station and major central attractions. For heritage atmosphere: OLD_TOWN / ROYAL_MILE / GRASSMARKET for medieval streets, historic buildings, nightlife and immediate sightseeing access. For luxury: NEW_TOWN / GEORGE_STREET / ST_ANDREW_SQUARE / WEST_END for five-star hotels, Georgian architecture, luxury shopping, premium restaurants and easier vehicle access. For honeymoon / romantic travel: NEW_TOWN / DEAN_VILLAGE_APPROACH / STOCKBRIDGE / BOUTIQUE_OLD_TOWN for atmospheric architecture, quieter evenings, dining and scenic walking. For food / local atmosphere: LEITH / STOCKBRIDGE for independent restaurants, cafés, bars, neighborhood life and stronger repeat-visitor appeal. For August festival travel: BOOK_CENTRAL_ACCOMMODATION_WELL_IN_ADVANCE and prioritize walking access to festival venues over minor room-rate savings. Avoid changing hotels unnecessarily; Edinburgh''s compact centre, bus network, tram system and rail connections make one well-positioned base the most efficient strategy. Best transportation: Use: Edinburgh transportation should primarily be treated as: WALKING_FOR_HISTORIC_CORE + BUS_FOR_CITYWIDE_NETWORK + TRAM_FOR_AIRPORT_AND_LEITH_CORRIDOR + TAXI_SELECTIVELY_FOR_MOBILITY_AND_LUGGAGE + RAIL_OR_PRIVATE_CAR_FOR_REGIONAL_EXCURSIONS Edinburgh Airport transportation baseline: EDINBURGH_AIRPORT + DIRECT_TRAM + CITY_CENTRE_IN_APPROXIMATELY_30_MINUTES + CONTINUING_SERVICE_TO_NEWHAVEN. Accessibility baseline: EDINBURGH_TRAMS: 100% LOW_FLOOR_WHEELCHAIR_ACCESSIBLE + DEDICATED_WHEELCHAIR_OR_BUGGY_SPACES + STEP_FREE_PLATFORM_ACCESS_VIA_RAMPS_OR_LIFTS. Historic central Edinburgh remains significantly less uniform because steep gradients, cobbles, closes and stairs are integral parts of the Old Town. Must-do for first-time visitor: Edinburgh should not be reduced to Edinburgh Castle and the Royal Mile alone; its essential tourism identity is: MEDIEVAL_OLD_TOWN + GEORGIAN_NEW_TOWN + SCOTTISH_ROYAL_HISTORY + MUSEUMS_AND_GALLERIES + VOLCANIC_LANDSCAPE + FESTIVAL_CULTURE + NEIGHBORHOOD_EXPLORATION. Don''t-do: Current Edinburgh Castle operational baseline: Edinburgh Castle accessibility baseline: Edinburgh festival baseline for 2026: August should therefore be treated as: EXCEPTIONAL_CULTURAL_VALUE + VERY_HIGH_VISITOR_PRESSURE + ADVANCE_ACCOMMODATION_BOOKING + ADVANCE_EVENT_TICKETING + ADDITIONAL_WALKING_AND_TRAFFIC_PLANNING. Biggest advantage: Extraordinary concentration of globally important architecture, Scottish history, museums, dramatic topography and cultural activity within a relatively compact capital-city core. UNESCO identifies Edinburgh''s defining urban quality as the remarkable juxtaposition between the organically developed medieval Old Town and the planned Georgian New Town, whose architecture and urban planning significantly influenced European development. Unlike many heritage cities, Edinburgh also integrates major natural landscapes directly into the visitor experience through Castle Rock, Arthur''s Seat, Salisbury Crags, Holyrood Park and panoramic hilltop viewpoints. Its festival ecosystem further transforms the destination from a conventional heritage capital into one of the world''s most important performing-arts and cultural-event cities. Biggest disadvantage: High peak-season accommodation costs, exceptional August crowd pressure, unpredictable weather and physically demanding historic terrain. The compact central map can be misleading because steep elevation changes, cobbled streets, closes and stairways can substantially increase walking fatigue. August festival travel requires particularly early accommodation and event planning, while Edinburgh Castle, premium restaurants, popular experiences and selected festival performances may sell out. Overall destination score: 95/100', 3350),
  ('edinburg', 36, 'data-quality', 'DATA QUALITY', NULL, NULL, 'information_completeness: 98/100 last_updated: 2026-09-05 last_verified: WEB_VERIFIED verified_by: FOREVER EDINBURGH / CITY OF EDINBURGH TOURISM SOURCES / HISTORIC ENVIRONMENT SCOTLAND / UNESCO WORLD HERITAGE CENTRE / EDINBURGH FESTIVAL CITY / EDINBURGH AIRPORT / EDINBURGH TRAMS / LOTHIAN BUSES / ROYAL COLLECTION TRUST / NATIONAL MUSEUMS SCOTLAND / ROYAL BOTANIC GARDEN EDINBURGH sources: IMPORTANT: Edinburgh Castle admission, Palace of Holyroodhouse access, festival performances, Royal Edinburgh Military Tattoo tickets, temporary exhibitions, guided tours and special events must NOT be treated as permanently available without verification. Edinburgh Castle currently warns that tickets can sell out far in advance, especially in summer. Online advance booking should therefore be treated as the default strategy for high-demand dates. Current Edinburgh Castle general opening baseline: APRIL_1_TO_SEPTEMBER_30: 09:30–18:00 + LAST_ENTRY_17:00 OCTOBER_1_TO_DECEMBER_23: 09:30–17:00 + LAST_ENTRY_16:00 DECEMBER_24: 09:30–16:00 + LAST_ENTRY_15:00 DECEMBER_25_AND_26: CLOSED DECEMBER_27_TO_31: 09:30–17:00 JANUARY_1: 11:00–17:00 JANUARY_2_TO_MARCH_31: 09:30–17:00. These hours remain subject to weather, events, conservation work and operational changes and must be reverified before production use. Edinburgh Castle accessibility should be interpreted carefully: CASTLE_ESPLANADE_UPHILL_APPROACH + COBBLED_INTERIOR_ROUTES + STEEP_SECTIONS + SELECTIVE_RAMPED_ACCESS + MOBILITY_VEHICLE_SUPPORT_TO_CROWN_SQUARE_ON_REQUEST + SOME_HISTORIC_SECTIONS_REQUIRING_STAIRS. Do not classify Edinburgh Castle itself as universally step-free. Edinburgh public-transport accessibility baseline: EDINBURGH_TRAMS: 100% WHEELCHAIR_ACCESSIBLE_LOW_FLOOR_TRAMS + TWO_DEDICATED_WHEELCHAIR_OR_BUGGY_SPACES_PER_TRAM + PRIORITY_SEATING + RAMP_OR_LIFT_PLATFORM_ACCESS. Historic-centre accessibility: OLD_TOWN: STEEP_GRADIENTS + COBBLES + STAIRS + NARROW_CLOSES + VARIABLE_BUILDING_ACCESS. NEW_TOWN: GENERALLY_MORE_REGULAR_STREET_LAYOUT + BETTER_ROAD_ACCESS + STILL_REQUIRES_GRADIENT_AND_BUILDING_SPECIFIC_VERIFICATION. Airport transfer baseline: EDINBURGH_AIRPORT + TRAM_TO_CITY_CENTRE_APPROXIMATELY_30_MINUTES + CONTINUING_SERVICE_TO_NEWHAVEN. Service frequencies, first/last departures, fares and engineering changes must be checked before travel. 2026 August festival baseline: EDINBURGH_FESTIVAL_FRINGE: 07_AUGUST_2026 – 31_AUGUST_2026 EDINBURGH_INTERNATIONAL_FESTIVAL: 07_AUGUST_2026 – 30_AUGUST_2026 ROYAL_EDINBURGH_MILITARY_TATTOO: 07_AUGUST_2026 – 29_AUGUST_2026 EDINBURGH_INTERNATIONAL_FILM_FESTIVAL: 13_AUGUST_2026 – 19_AUGUST_2026 EDINBURGH_ART_FESTIVAL: 14_AUGUST_2026 – 30_AUGUST_2026 EDINBURGH_INTERNATIONAL_BOOK_FESTIVAL: 15_AUGUST_2026 – 30_AUGUST_2026. Festival authorities explicitly characterize August as Edinburgh''s busiest festival period, with six major festivals operating during the month. Accommodation availability, restaurant reservations, central road access, public transport crowding, festival tickets and attraction capacity should therefore be treated as HIGHLY_DATE_SENSITIVE throughout August. Edinburgh climate and seasonality should be handled as: SPRING / PRIME GENERAL SIGHTSEEING: OLD_TOWN_WALKING + NEW_TOWN_ARCHITECTURE + BOTANIC_GARDEN + ARTHURS_SEAT + PHOTOGRAPHY + LONGER_DAYLIGHT. SUMMER / FESTIVAL_AND_LONG_DAYLIGHT_SEASON: CASTLE + OUTDOOR_WALKING + FESTIVALS + MILITARY_TATTOO + ARTHURS_SEAT + EVENING_ACTIVITY + VERY_HIGH_AUGUST_DEMAND. AUTUMN / CULTURAL_AND_PHOTOGRAPHY_SEASON: OLD_TOWN + MUSEUMS + WHISKY + FOOD + AUTUMN_COLOUR + DEAN_VILLAGE + LOWER_POST_FESTIVAL_PRESSURE. WINTER / CULTURAL_AND_FESTIVE_SEASON: MUSEUMS + CASTLE + PUBS + WHISKY + CHRISTMAS + HOGMANAY + ATMOSPHERIC_PHOTOGRAPHY + SHORT_DAYLIGHT + COLD_WIND + WEATHER_CONTINGENCY. Weather should never be treated as reliably dry in any season. Waterproof outerwear, layered clothing and footwear suitable for cobbles and gradients are advisable throughout much of the year. Edinburgh should primarily be treated as: SPRING: EDINBURGH_CASTLE + ROYAL_MILE + NEW_TOWN + ARTHURS_SEAT + BOTANIC_GARDEN + DEAN_VILLAGE SUMMER: EDINBURGH_CASTLE + FESTIVALS + MILITARY_TATTOO + HOLYROOD_PARK + LONG_EVENING_WALKS + OUTDOOR_EVENTS AUTUMN: OLD_TOWN + NEW_TOWN + NATIONAL_MUSEUM + STOCKBRIDGE + WATER_OF_LEITH + FOOD_AND_WHISKY WINTER: MUSEUMS + CASTLE + HISTORIC_PUBS + CHRISTMAS_AND_HOGMANAY + NEW_TOWN + WEATHER_PROTECTED_CULTURAL_SIGHTSEEING. UNESCO, Historic Environment Scotland, Forever Edinburgh, Edinburgh Festival City, Royal Collection Trust, Edinburgh Airport, Edinburgh Trams, Lothian Buses, National Museums Scotland and individual attraction portals should be treated as primary sources for current operational information. This dataset should be refreshed regularly before production use.', 3351),
  ('dublin', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Spring', NULL, 'months: March April May weather: Cool and changeable in March, increasingly mild through April and May. Longer daylight improves walking, parks, coastal excursions and photography, although rain remains possible throughout the season. crowd_level: MEDIUM price_level: MEDIUM → HIGH overall_score: 66.67–72.33 recommended: true reason: Spring offers increasingly comfortable temperatures, longer daylight and strong city-and-coast sightseeing before the heaviest summer visitor pressure. Best for:', 3352),
  ('dublin', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Summer', NULL, 'months: June July August weather: Dublin''s mildest and brightest period with long daylight hours and average daytime temperatures remaining moderate by European standards. Rain and cloudy periods still occur. crowd_level: HIGH price_level: HIGH overall_score: 56.67–60.33 recommended: true_with_advance_booking reason: Excellent daylight and outdoor conditions are offset by the year''s strongest international tourism demand, higher accommodation pressure and crowded flagship attractions. Best for:', 3353),
  ('dublin', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Autumn', NULL, 'months: September October November weather: September remains relatively mild before cooler, wetter and shorter days develop through October and November. crowd_level: MEDIUM price_level: MEDIUM overall_score: 62.33–72.33 recommended: true reason: September offers a strong balance between weather and post-summer demand, while October and November work increasingly well for museums, literature, food and indoor cultural experiences. Best for:', 3354),
  ('dublin', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Winter', NULL, 'months: December January February weather: Cool, damp and frequently cloudy with short daylight hours, but severe cold is relatively uncommon. Rain, wind and occasional frost can affect outdoor plans. crowd_level: LOW → MEDIUM price_level: MEDIUM overall_score: 62.00–73.67 recommended: true_for_cultural_city_breaks reason: Winter works particularly well for museums, literature, historic pubs, food and indoor attractions, with February offering comparatively strong value and manageable tourism pressure. Best for:', 3355),
  ('dublin', 10, 'budget-strategy', 'BUDGET STRATEGY', NULL, NULL, 'Where money can be saved: Current TFI Zone 1 Leap pricing provides a €2 adult 90-minute fare across eligible Dublin Bus, Luas, DART and commuter rail journeys, with adult daily and weekly caps of €6 and €24 respectively. Where saving money is usually NOT recommended: Travel-agent rule: In Dublin, **CENTRAL_OR_TRANSIT_CONNECTED_HOTEL + WALKING + LEAP_CARD + FREE_MUSEUMS + SELECTIVE_PREMIUM_ATTRACTIONS** provides the strongest value. For short stays, prioritize: **TRINITY_COLLEGE + MEDIEVAL_DUBLIN + TEMPLE_BAR + GUINNESS_STOREHOUSE + GEORGIAN_DUBLIN**. For longer stays, add: **KILMAINHAM_GAOL + PHOENIX_PARK + EPIC + LITERARY_DUBLIN + HOWTH + DUBLIN_BAY**. Operational note: Hotel prices, attraction tickets, public-transport fares, festival schedules and opening hours should be rechecked before travel.', 3356),
  ('dublin', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Family', 'family', 'Airport transfer by: AIRPORT_BUS_OR_PRIVATE_CAB + DIRECT_HOTEL_TRANSFER is generally the simplest option. Choose accommodation around Dublin 1, Dublin 2, St Stephen''s Green, Merrion Square or another central area with straightforward transport access.', 3357),
  ('dublin', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Honeymoon', 'honeymoon', 'Prefer: PRIVATE_TRANSFER + CENTRAL_BOUTIQUE_OR_LUXURY_HOTEL + WALKABLE_DINING_AND_GEORGIAN_DUBLIN_ACCESS for the strongest short romantic stay.', 3358),
  ('dublin', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Luxury', 'luxury', 'Use: AIRPORT_MEET_AND_GREET + CHAUFFEURED_SEDAN_OR_SUV + FIVE_STAR_CITY_HOTEL + PRIVATE_SIGHTSEEING_VEHICLE Private vehicles are particularly useful when Dublin is combined with Wicklow, Powerscourt, Kildare or longer-distance Ireland touring.', 3359),
  ('dublin', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Budget', 'budget', 'Primary options: Dublin Airport currently has no direct rail connection, so road-based airport transfers remain the standard arrival strategy.', 3360),
  ('dublin', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Senior', 'senior', 'Prefer: DIRECT_AIRPORT_CAB + CENTRAL_HOTEL + SELECTIVE_DOOR_TO_DOOR_TRANSPORT Central accommodation reduces long transfers and allows major sightseeing to be combined with short walks.', 3361),
  ('dublin', 18, 'family-travel', 'FAMILY TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'child_friendly_score: 90 best_ages: Rules: For young children: Prefer: Avoid:', 3362),
  ('dublin', 19, 'honeymoon-travel', 'HONEYMOON TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'honeymoon_score: 85 romance_score: 88 privacy_score: 80 luxury_score: 90 Recommended: Honeymoon itineraries should generally stay at: 2–3 major experiences/day. Prefer: LUXURY_OR_BOUTIQUE_HOTEL + GEORGIAN_DUBLIN + COASTAL_EXPERIENCE + DINING + LIVE_MUSIC + FREE_TIME over: Continuous museum and historical scheduling.', 3363),
  ('dublin', 20, 'luxury-travel', 'LUXURY TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'luxury_score: 90 Recommended: Dublin is particularly strong for: HERITAGE_LUXURY + PRIVATE_GUIDING + FINE_DINING + WHISKEY + BOUTIQUE_HOTELS + IRELAND_GATEWAY_TRAVEL.', 3364),
  ('dublin', 21, 'adventure', 'ADVENTURE', NULL, NULL, 'adventure_score: 69 Dublin offers primarily soft urban, coastal and outdoor adventure. Adventure experiences: Best regions: HOWTH + DUBLIN_BAY + PHOENIX_PARK + DUN_LAOGHAIRE + DUBLIN_MOUNTAINS + WICKLOW Travel-agent positioning: Dublin should be treated as: SOFT_COASTAL_ADVENTURE + WALKING + CYCLING + SEA_ACTIVITY + MOUNTAIN_GATEWAY rather than a high-adrenaline destination.', 3365),
  ('dublin', 22, 'senior-travel', 'SENIOR TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'senior_suitability: 87 walking_intensity: LOW_MEDIUM for Trinity, Georgian Dublin, national museums, Docklands and city-centre sightseeing. MEDIUM for extended Temple Bar, medieval Dublin, Phoenix Park, Kilmainham and coastal walking. Rules: Dublin works especially well for seniors as a: HISTORY + MUSEUMS + LITERATURE + GEORGIAN_ARCHITECTURE + GASTRONOMY + RELAXED_CITY_BREAK destination.', 3366),
  ('dublin', 23, 'accessibility', 'ACCESSIBILITY', NULL, NULL, 'wheelchair_accessibility: MODERATE → HIGH ACROSS MODERN PUBLIC TRANSPORT, MAJOR MUSEUMS AND MANY CENTRAL PUBLIC SPACES VARIABLE WITHIN HISTORIC BUILDINGS, COBBLED STREETS AND COASTAL ROUTES public_transport_accessibility: HIGH_OVERALL_WITH_SERVICE_SPECIFIC_VERIFICATION hotel_accessibility: GENERALLY_GOOD_IN_MODERN_AND_MAJOR_CHAIN_HOTELS_BUT_MUST_BE_VERIFIED attraction_accessibility: MUST_BE_VERIFIED_PER_ATTRACTION Rule: Do not assume every medieval church, Georgian building, historic pub, castle area or coastal route is completely step-free. Additional notes: Dublin accessibility should therefore be classified as: STRONG_PUBLIC_TRANSPORT_ACCESSIBILITY + VARIABLE_HERITAGE_ACCESS + ATTRACTION_SPECIFIC_VERIFICATION.', 3367),
  ('dublin', 24, 'food', 'FOOD', NULL, NULL, 'Dublin is particularly strong for: Food experiences: Family: Prioritize fish and chips, Irish breakfast, breads, soups, burgers, casual pubs, bakeries and familiar café options. Honeymoon: Choose modern Irish fine dining, atmospheric restaurants, seafood and premium cocktail or whiskey bars. Luxury: Include Michelin-level dining, chef-led modern Irish cuisine, private whiskey experiences and premium hotel restaurants. Budget: Use bakeries, casual pubs, cafés, takeaway shops, markets and lunch specials. Travel-agent rule: Position Dublin food around: MODERN_IRISH_CUISINE + PUB_FOOD + SEAFOOD + GUINNESS + WHISKEY + CONTEMPORARY_DINING.', 3368),
  ('dublin', 25, 'shopping', 'SHOPPING', NULL, NULL, 'Strong categories: Luxury shopping: Prefer: Local shopping: Prefer: Budget: Prefer: Travel-agent rule: Use: GRAFTON_STREET for PREMIUM_AND_CENTRAL_SHOPPING, HENRY_STREET for HIGH_STREET_VALUE, CREATIVE_QUARTER for INDEPENDENT_DESIGN, IRISH_DESIGN_STORES for LOCAL_PRODUCTS.', 3369),
  ('dublin', 26, 'nightlife', 'NIGHTLIFE', NULL, NULL, 'nightlife_level: 95 Suitable for: Best areas: Evening activities: Dublin nightlife is strongest for: PUBS + TRADITIONAL_MUSIC + LIVE_MUSIC + BARS + THEATRE + SOCIAL_EVENINGS rather than: LARGE_SCALE_RESORT_CLUBBING. Couples should generally prefer: DINNER + TRADITIONAL_PUB + LIVE_MUSIC + RELAXED_CITY_WALK over: Remaining exclusively inside the busiest Temple Bar venues all evening.', 3370),
  ('dublin', 28, 'sample-itinerary-patterns', 'SAMPLE ITINERARY PATTERNS', '3 NIGHTS', NULL, '### Day 1 Arrival at Dublin Airport (DUB) → Dublin Express / Aircoach / taxi / private transfer to central Dublin hotel → Hotel check-in & relax after arrival Afternoon: → Begin at Trinity College Dublin → Explore the historic university precinct → Visit the Book of Kells Experience according to pre-booked timing → Walk through Grafton Street → Continue towards St Stephen''s Green → Explore the Georgian streets around central Dublin Evening: → Walk through the Temple Bar district → Experience Dublin''s traditional pub & live-music atmosphere → Irish welcome dinner → Optional evening walk along the River Liffey → Hotel DUB is Ireland''s principal international aviation gateway and lies north of Dublin city centre. Central Dublin can be reached by airport coach, bus, taxi or private transfer. Dublin also serves as an excellent base for exploring Ireland''s east coast, including the Wicklow Mountains, Glendalough, Howth and coastal County Dublin. ### Day 2 Morning: Breakfast → Begin Dublin''s historic-city exploration → Visit Dublin Castle → Explore the surrounding historic quarter → Continue towards Christ Church Cathedral → Walk towards St Patrick''s Cathedral → Explore the Liberties district Afternoon: → Traditional Irish lunch → Visit the Guinness Storehouse → Explore its exhibitions on the history and brewing heritage of Guinness → Finish with panoramic Dublin views from the Gravity Bar experience → Continue towards the River Liffey → Ha''penny Bridge → O''Connell Street / central Dublin according to available time Evening: → Traditional Irish pub experience → Live Irish music → Dinner in central Dublin → Hotel Optional alternative instead of central Dublin sightseeing: HOWTH_AND_COAST: → Travel to Howth → Harbour exploration → Coastal scenery → Howth village → Seafood lunch → Cliff / coastal walk according to weather and fitness → Return to Dublin MALAHIDE: → Malahide Castle & Gardens → Historic village → Coastal leisure → Relaxed lunch → Return to Dublin DUBLIN_CULTURE: → National Museum of Ireland → National Gallery of Ireland → Georgian Dublin → Merrion Square → St Stephen''s Green ### Day 3 Recommended first-time option: → Breakfast → Full-day excursion into County Wicklow → Travel through the Wicklow Mountains landscapes → Scenic countryside viewpoints → Continue towards Glendalough → Explore the historic monastic settlement → Round Tower & ancient ecclesiastical remains → Walk around the surrounding valley and lakes according to available time Afternoon: → Continue through the Wicklow countryside → Scenic villages / viewpoints according to selected tour → Traditional Irish countryside lunch → Nature photography Evening: → Return to Dublin → Final Grafton Street / Temple Bar exploration → Farewell Irish dinner → Hotel Optional alternative instead of Wicklow & Glendalough: HOWTH_AND_DUBLIN_BAY: → Howth Harbour → Coastal walk → Dublin Bay scenery → Seafood experience → Return to Dublin for evening leisure MALAHIDE_AND_NORTH_COAST: → Malahide Castle & Gardens → Malahide village → Coastal scenery → Relaxed countryside experience CULTURE & HISTORY: → Trinity College → Dublin Castle → Christ Church Cathedral → St Patrick''s Cathedral → National Museum / National Gallery FAMILY: → Dublin Zoo → Phoenix Park → EPIC The Irish Emigration Museum → Dublin Castle → Howth coastal experience HONEYMOON: → Georgian Dublin couple photography → St Stephen''s Green → Howth coastal sunset experience → Couple spa treatment → Romantic Irish dinner LUXURY: → Private chauffeured Dublin sightseeing → Private Wicklow & Glendalough excursion → Luxury afternoon tea → Premium whiskey / culinary experience → Fine dining FOOD: → Traditional Irish breakfast → Irish stew / seafood → Dublin pub-food experience → Howth seafood → Irish whiskey experience For only 3 nights, prioritize: TRINITY_COLLEGE_AND_CENTRAL_DUBLIN + DUBLIN_CASTLE_AND_GUINNESS_STOREHOUSE + WICKLOW_AND_GLENDALOUGH OR DUBLIN_HISTORIC_CORE + GUINNESS_AND_IRISH_CULTURE + HOWTH_AND_DUBLIN_BAY rather than trying to include Galway, Cork, Belfast, Killarney and the Cliffs of Moher within the same short stay. ### Day 4 Breakfast → Leisurely morning around Grafton Street / St Stephen''s Green → Final Irish souvenir shopping → Hotel checkout → Dublin Express / Aircoach / taxi / private transfer towards Dublin Airport (DUB) → Departure', 3371),
  ('dublin', 29, 'six-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 1', NULL, 'Arrival at Dublin Airport (DUB) → Private airport transfer → Romantic central Dublin hotel check-in → Relax and refresh Afternoon: → Trinity College precinct → Grafton Street → St Stephen''s Green → Georgian Dublin → Couple photography Evening: → Temple Bar & River Liffey → Romantic Irish dinner → Overnight at Dublin', 3372),
  ('dublin', 29, 'six-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 2', NULL, 'Breakfast Morning: → Trinity College Dublin → Book of Kells Experience → Dublin Castle → Christ Church Cathedral Afternoon: → St Patrick''s Cathedral → Georgian Dublin → Merrion Square → Relaxed café experience Evening: → Traditional Irish music → Romantic dinner → Overnight at Dublin', 3373),
  ('dublin', 29, 'six-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 3', NULL, 'Breakfast → Dublin cultural & culinary experience Morning: → Guinness Storehouse → Historic Liberties district → River Liffey → Ha''penny Bridge Afternoon: → Grafton Street → Chilled shopping / café time → Couple spa / hotel leisure Evening: → Premium Irish dining → Overnight at Dublin', 3374),
  ('dublin', 29, 'six-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 4', NULL, 'Breakfast → Full-day romantic countryside excursion → Wicklow Mountains → Scenic countryside → Glendalough → Historic monastic settlement → Glendalough valley & lakes → Couple photography Evening: → Return to Dublin → Relaxed dinner → Overnight at Dublin', 3375),
  ('dublin', 29, 'six-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 5', NULL, 'Breakfast → Coastal Dublin excursion → Howth Harbour → Howth village → Dublin Bay scenery → Coastal walk according to weather → Seafood lunch Afternoon: → Coastal leisure → Couple photography Evening: → Return to Dublin → Romantic evening → Overnight at Dublin', 3376),
  ('dublin', 29, 'six-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 6', NULL, 'Breakfast Choose ONE: ROMANTIC_LEISURE → Couple spa → Luxury afternoon tea → St Stephen''s Green → Boutique shopping → Relaxed café experience CULTURE_AND_CITY → National Gallery of Ireland → Merrion Square → Georgian Dublin → Phoenix Park COASTAL_ESCAPE → Malahide → Malahide Castle & Gardens → Coastal village exploration → Romantic lunch Evening: → Farewell romantic dinner → Live Irish music → Overnight at Dublin', 3377),
  ('dublin', 29, 'six-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 7', NULL, 'Breakfast → Leisure morning → Hotel checkout → Private transfer to Dublin Airport (DUB) → Departure', 3378),
  ('dublin', 30, 'six-nights-family-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 1', NULL, 'Arrival at Dublin Airport (DUB) → Airport transfer → Family hotel check-in → Relax and refresh Afternoon: → Trinity College precinct → Grafton Street → St Stephen''s Green → Family photography Evening: → River Liffey → Temple Bar district walk → Family dinner → Overnight at Dublin', 3379),
  ('dublin', 30, 'six-nights-family-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 2', NULL, 'Breakfast Morning: → Trinity College Dublin → Book of Kells Experience → Dublin Castle → Christ Church Cathedral Afternoon: → St Patrick''s Cathedral → Georgian Dublin → Merrion Square Evening: → Central Dublin leisure → Family dinner → Overnight at Dublin', 3380),
  ('dublin', 30, 'six-nights-family-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 3', NULL, 'Breakfast → Family-oriented Dublin experience Morning: → Phoenix Park → Dublin Zoo Afternoon: → EPIC The Irish Emigration Museum → River Liffey → Ha''penny Bridge → City-centre exploration Evening: → Family-friendly Irish dining → Overnight at Dublin', 3381),
  ('dublin', 30, 'six-nights-family-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 4', NULL, 'Breakfast → Full-day Wicklow excursion → Wicklow Mountains → Scenic countryside → Glendalough → Historic monastic settlement → Valley & lakes → Family nature photography Evening: → Return to Dublin → Overnight at Dublin', 3382),
  ('dublin', 30, 'six-nights-family-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 5', NULL, 'Breakfast → Howth coastal excursion → Howth Harbour → Village exploration → Dublin Bay scenery → Short family-friendly coastal walk → Seafood / café lunch Afternoon: → Harbour leisure → Family photography Evening: → Return to Dublin → Overnight at Dublin', 3383),
  ('dublin', 30, 'six-nights-family-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 6', NULL, 'Breakfast Choose ONE: FAMILY_FUN → Dublin Zoo / Phoenix Park additional leisure → Family activities → Shopping → Irish food experience CASTLE_AND_COAST → Malahide Castle & Gardens → Malahide village → Coastal leisure → Family lunch CULTURE → National Museum of Ireland → National Gallery of Ireland → Georgian Dublin → St Stephen''s Green Evening: → Grafton Street → Souvenir shopping → Farewell family dinner → Overnight at Dublin', 3384),
  ('dublin', 30, 'six-nights-family-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 7', NULL, 'Breakfast → Hotel checkout → Transfer to Dublin Airport (DUB) → Departure', 3385),
  ('dublin', 31, 'six-nights-luxury-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 1', NULL, 'Arrival at Dublin Airport (DUB) → Private chauffeured luxury airport transfer → Premium 5-star Dublin hotel check-in → Relax and refresh Afternoon: → Private Dublin orientation → Georgian Dublin → St Stephen''s Green → Grafton Street Evening: → Premium cocktails / luxury hotel lounge → Fine-dining Irish experience → Overnight at Dublin', 3386),
  ('dublin', 31, 'six-nights-luxury-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 2', NULL, 'Breakfast → Privately guided historic Dublin experience Morning: → Trinity College Dublin → Book of Kells Experience → Dublin Castle → Christ Church Cathedral Afternoon: → St Patrick''s Cathedral → Merrion Square → Georgian architecture → Private cultural exploration Evening: → Luxury afternoon tea / premium leisure → Fine dining → Overnight at Dublin', 3387),
  ('dublin', 31, 'six-nights-luxury-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 3', NULL, 'Breakfast → Private Dublin culinary & heritage experience Morning: → Guinness Storehouse premium experience → The Liberties → Historic Dublin Afternoon: → Curated Irish whiskey / culinary experience → Luxury shopping → Spa & wellness Evening: → Chef-led / fine-dining experience → Overnight at Dublin', 3388),
  ('dublin', 31, 'six-nights-luxury-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 4', NULL, 'Breakfast → Private chauffeured Wicklow excursion → Wicklow Mountains → Scenic countryside viewpoints → Glendalough → Historic monastic settlement → Lakes & valley landscapes Afternoon: → Premium countryside lunch → Private scenic touring → Photography stops Evening: → Chauffeured return to Dublin → Hotel leisure → Overnight at Dublin', 3389),
  ('dublin', 31, 'six-nights-luxury-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 5', NULL, 'Breakfast → Private Dublin Bay coastal experience → Chauffeured transfer to Howth → Howth Harbour → Coastal viewpoints → Private / guided coastal exploration Afternoon: → Premium seafood lunch → Malahide Castle & Gardens OR additional Howth leisure → Private return to Dublin Evening: → Spa / premium cocktails → Overnight at Dublin', 3390),
  ('dublin', 31, 'six-nights-luxury-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 6', NULL, 'Breakfast Choose ONE: LUXURY_LEISURE → Premium spa & wellness → Luxury afternoon tea → Personal shopping → Chauffeured city leisure PRIVATE_HERITAGE → Private museum / gallery experience → Georgian Dublin → Merrion Square → Historic architecture → Curated cultural touring COUNTRYSIDE_AND_ESTATE → Private excursion beyond central Dublin → Historic estate / castle experience → Premium countryside lunch → Chauffeured scenic drive Evening: → Farewell fine-dining experience → Premium Irish whiskey / cocktail experience → Overnight at Dublin', 3391),
  ('dublin', 31, 'six-nights-luxury-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 7', NULL, 'Breakfast → Leisure morning → Hotel checkout → Private chauffeured luxury transfer to Dublin Airport (DUB) → Departure', 3392),
  ('dublin', 32, 'travel-agent-insights', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS', 'What inexperienced planners often do wrong', NULL, '', 3393),
  ('dublin', 32, 'travel-agent-insights', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS', 'What an experienced planner does differently', NULL, 'For first-time visits, prioritize: TRINITY_COLLEGE + MEDIEVAL_DUBLIN + GEORGIAN_DUBLIN + GUINNESS_OR_KILMAINHAM before maximum attraction coverage.', 3394),
  ('dublin', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', NULL, NULL, 'IF: trip_length <= 2 nights THEN: prioritize_TRINITY_COLLEGE + MEDIEVAL_DUBLIN + GEORGIAN_OR_TEMPLE_BAR AND: choose_ONE_OF_GUINNESS_OR_KILMAINHAM Reason: Very short Dublin trips gain more value from a concentrated historic-core itinerary than from attempting both city and coastal sightseeing. IF: trip_length == 3_OR_4_nights THEN: prioritize_TRINITY + MEDIEVAL_DUBLIN + GEORGIAN_DUBLIN + GUINNESS + KILMAINHAM AND: retain_ONE_EVENING_FOR_PUB_OR_LIVE_MUSIC Reason: Three to four nights provide Dublin''s strongest first-time balance of literature, history, architecture, gastronomy and nightlife. IF: trip_length >= 5 nights THEN: add_PHOENIX_PARK + DOCKLANDS_EPIC + HOWTH_OR_DUBLIN_BAY Reason: Longer stays allow Dublin''s coastal, family, emigrant-history and urban-nature experiences to be explored without excessive rushing. IF: trip_length >= 6 nights THEN: consider_ONE_OF_MALAHIDE + DUN_LAOGHAIRE + WICKLOW + BRU_NA_BOINNE Reason: Dublin becomes a stronger extended base when the central-city itinerary is combined with one or more contrasting coastal, archaeological or countryside excursions. IF: trip_type == HONEYMOON THEN: prefer_GEORGIAN_OR_LUXURY_HOTEL + HOWTH_OR_DUBLIN_BAY + FINE_DINING + LIVE_MUSIC AND: reduce_DAILY_MUSEUM_COUNT Reason: Dublin''s romantic strength comes from atmospheric streets, coastline, restaurants, historic pubs and relaxed evening experiences rather than nonstop sightseeing. IF: traveler_type == FAMILY THEN: prioritize_DUBLINIA + EPIC + PHOENIX_PARK_OR_DUBLIN_ZOO + TRINITY AND: include_PARK_OR_COASTAL_BREAKS Reason: Families benefit from combining interactive history with outdoor experiences rather than continuous cathedral and museum scheduling. IF: traveler_type == LUXURY THEN: prefer_FIVE_STAR_OR_BOUTIQUE_HOTEL + PRIVATE_GUIDE + PREMIUM_DINING + CHAUFFEUR_SELECTIVELY AND: add_PRIVATE_WICKLOW_OR_COASTAL_EXCURSION_IF_RELEVANT Reason: Dublin''s strongest luxury positioning combines heritage accommodation, private cultural interpretation, modern Irish gastronomy and premium regional touring. IF: traveler_type == BUDGET THEN: prefer_CENTRAL_VALUE_HOTEL_OR_HOSTEL + WALKING + TFI_LEAP_CARD + FREE_MUSEUMS AND: limit_TAXIS + PREMIUM_NIGHTLIFE + EXCESSIVE_PAID_ATTRACTIONS Reason: Dublin accommodation can be expensive, but walking, integrated public transport, parks and free national cultural institutions significantly improve value. IF: traveler_interest == IRISH_HISTORY THEN: prioritize_MEDIEVAL_DUBLIN + KILMAINHAM_GAOL + GPO_AREA + NATIONAL_MUSEUM + DUBLIN_CASTLE_WHEN_OPEN Reason: Dublin contains Viking, medieval, British-administration, revolutionary and independence-era heritage within a comparatively compact urban area. IF: traveler_interest == LITERATURE THEN: prioritize_TRINITY_COLLEGE + MOLI + NATIONAL_LIBRARY + JAMES_JOYCE_HERITAGE + LITERARY_WALK_OR_PUB Reason: Dublin is internationally recognized as a UNESCO City of Literature and has an unusually dense literary heritage associated with globally influential writers. IF: traveler_interest == TRINITY_COLLEGE THEN: prioritize_BOOK_OF_KELLS + OLD_LIBRARY + COLLEGE_GROUNDS AND: reserve_TIMED_ENTRY_IN_ADVANCE Reason: Trinity College is one of Dublin''s defining cultural landmarks and should be treated as a complete university-and-literature experience rather than only a manuscript viewing stop. IF: traveler_interest == MEDIEVAL_DUBLIN THEN: combine_CHRIST_CHURCH + DUBLINIA + ST_PATRICKS + MARSHS_LIBRARY_IF_RELEVANT Reason: This compact district provides the capital''s strongest concentration of medieval, Viking and ecclesiastical heritage. IF: traveler_interest == DUBLIN_CASTLE AND: travel_date >= 2026_05_05 AND: travel_date <= 2026_12_31 THEN: do_NOT_PLAN_NORMAL_PUBLIC_CASTLE_VISIT AND: substitute_CHESTER_BEATTY + MEDIEVAL_DUBLIN + GEORGIAN_OR_NATIONAL_MUSEUM_SIGHTSEEING Reason: Heritage Ireland confirms Dublin Castle is closed to the public from 5 May through 31 December 2026 to accommodate Ireland''s EU Presidency. IF: traveler_interest == REVOLUTIONARY_HISTORY THEN: prioritize_KILMAINHAM_GAOL + GPO_AREA + NATIONAL_MUSEUM + CITY_CENTER_HISTORY AND: book_KILMAINHAM_IN_ADVANCE Reason: Kilmainham Gaol and the central revolutionary-history sites are essential for understanding the Easter Rising, independence struggle and formation of modern Ireland. IF: traveler_interest == GUINNESS THEN: prioritize_GUINNESS_STOREHOUSE + LIBERTIES AND: combine_WITH_LOCAL_HISTORY_OR_FOOD Reason: The Guinness experience works best when placed within the wider industrial and neighborhood history of the Liberties rather than treated as an isolated drink stop. IF: traveler_interest == WHISKEY THEN: combine_ONE_DISTILLERY_OR_GUIDED_TASTING + QUALITY_IRISH_DINING AND: avoid_DRINKING_AND_DRIVING Reason: Dublin''s whiskey heritage is best experienced through dedicated tasting or distillery experiences without unnecessary road transport. IF: traveler_interest == FOOD THEN: include_MODERN_IRISH_CUISINE + SEAFOOD + PUB_FOOD + LOCAL_ARTISAN_PRODUCT AND: retain_ONE_HIGH_QUALITY_RESTAURANT_EXPERIENCE Reason: Official Dublin tourism positioning reflects a food scene extending from traditional pubs and seafood to markets, contemporary restaurants and Michelin-level dining. IF: traveler_interest == NIGHTLIFE THEN: combine_TRADITIONAL_PUB + LIVE_MUSIC + ONE_NON_TEMPLE_BAR_AREA AND: avoid_TEMPLE_BAR_ONLY_PLANNING Reason: Dublin''s nightlife extends well beyond Temple Bar through traditional music pubs, live venues, cocktail bars, theatres and multiple evening districts. IF: traveler_interest == TRADITIONAL_MUSIC THEN: prioritize_AUTHENTIC_TRAD_SESSION_OR_MUSIC_VENUE AND: consider_MERRION_ROW + SMITHFIELD_OR_OTHER_SPECIALIST_PUBS Reason: Traditional music remains a living part of Dublin''s cultural identity and can be experienced throughout the city rather than only in tourist-focused Temple Bar venues. IF: traveler_interest == GEORGIAN_ARCHITECTURE THEN: prioritize_MERRION_SQUARE + FITZWILLIAM_SQUARE_AREA + GEORGIAN_STREETS + NATIONAL_CULTURAL_INSTITUTIONS Reason: Georgian Dublin provides one of the city''s defining architectural landscapes and combines naturally with literature, parks, museums and photography. IF: traveler_interest == MUSEUMS THEN: prioritize_NATIONAL_MUSEUM + NATIONAL_GALLERY + EPIC + CHESTER_BEATTY_BASED_ON_INTEREST Reason: Dublin combines major free national collections with specialist museums covering art, archaeology, manuscripts, emigration and Irish social history. IF: traveler_interest == FAMILY_INTERACTIVE_MUSEUMS THEN: prioritize_DUBLINIA + EPIC AND: combine_WITH_PHOENIX_PARK_OR_DUBLIN_ZOO Reason: Interactive interpretation works particularly well for families when balanced with outdoor recreation. IF: traveler_interest == NATURE THEN: prioritize_PHOENIX_PARK + HOWTH + DUBLIN_BAY AND: consider_WICKLOW_IF_FULL_DAY_AVAILABLE Reason: Dublin combines major urban parkland with unusually convenient access to coastline and nearby mountain landscapes. IF: traveler_interest == PHOENIX_PARK THEN: allocate_HALF_DAY_IF_COMBINING_ZOO + WALKING_OR_CYCLING Reason: Phoenix Park covers approximately 1,750 acres and includes Dublin Zoo, cycling and walking routes, historic monuments, gardens and wild fallow deer. IF: traveler_interest == HOWTH THEN: use_DART_WHERE_SUITABLE AND: combine_HARBOUR + SEAFOOD + COASTAL_WALK_OR_VIEWPOINT Reason: Howth provides one of Dublin''s strongest city-to-coast contrasts and is particularly effective as a half-day or relaxed full-day excursion. IF: traveler_interest == DUBLIN_BAY THEN: consider_HOWTH + DUN_LAOGHAIRE_OR_OTHER_DART_CONNECTED_COASTAL_STOPS AND: avoid_OVERLOADING_MULTIPLE_COASTAL_TOWNS_IN_ONE_SHORT_DAY Reason: Dublin''s rail-connected coastline is best appreciated through one or two focused coastal districts rather than rapid station-hopping. IF: traveler_interest == PHOTOGRAPHY THEN: prioritize_TRINITY_EARLY + TEMPLE_BAR_EARLY_MORNING + GEORGIAN_DUBLIN + LIFFEY_BLUE_HOUR + HOWTH Reason: Early and late hours improve light and atmosphere while reducing crowd pressure at Dublin''s most photographed central locations. IF: traveler_type == SENIOR THEN: prefer_CENTRAL_HOTEL + SHORT_WALKING_CLUSTERS + BUS_OR_TAXI_FOR_LONGER_TRANSFERS AND: reduce_COBBLED_WALKING + LONG_COASTAL_TRAILS + MULTIPLE_STANDING_TOURS Reason: Dublin is relatively manageable for seniors, but historic surfaces, long walking days and older buildings create localized mobility challenges. IF: traveler_uses_WHEELCHAIR THEN: use_VERIFIED_ACCESSIBLE_TFI_SERVICES + ACCESSIBLE_HOTEL AND: verify_HISTORIC_ATTRACTIONS_INDIVIDUALLY Reason: Dublin''s modern public-transport network provides substantial accessible infrastructure while older heritage buildings and uneven streets remain variable. IF: season == MARCH_TO_MAY THEN: increase_WALKING + PARKS + GEORGIAN_DUBLIN + COASTAL_SIGHTSEEING AND: retain_RAIN_PROTECTION Reason: Increasing daylight and generally improving temperatures make spring one of Dublin''s strongest periods for mixed indoor and outdoor touring. IF: season == JUNE_TO_AUGUST THEN: expect_LONG_DAYLIGHT + HIGHER_VISITOR_PRESSURE + HIGHER_ACCOMMODATION_COST AND: book_MAJOR_ATTRACTIONS_AND_HOTELS_EARLY Reason: Summer provides Dublin''s longest daylight and strongest outdoor conditions, but tourism demand and accommodation pressure reduce value and crowd comfort. IF: season == SEPTEMBER THEN: prioritize_WALKING + HOWTH + PHOENIX_PARK + CULTURE + FOOD Reason: September commonly provides a strong balance between relatively mild conditions and reduced pressure compared with the busiest summer period. IF: season == OCTOBER_TO_NOVEMBER THEN: increase_MUSEUMS + LITERATURE + FOOD + PUB_CULTURE AND: retain_SHORTER_OUTDOOR_BLOCKS Reason: Cooling weather and shorter daylight progressively increase the value of Dublin''s strong indoor cultural and gastronomic inventory. IF: season == DECEMBER_TO_FEBRUARY THEN: prioritize_MUSEUMS + PUBS + LIVE_MUSIC + LITERATURE + FOOD AND: reduce_LONG_COASTAL_OR_PARK_PROGRAMS Reason: Short daylight and cool, damp conditions favour Dublin''s museums, historic interiors, food scene and evening culture. IF: weather == HEAVY_RAIN THEN: replace_EXTENDED_WALKING_WITH_NATIONAL_MUSEUM + NATIONAL_GALLERY + EPIC + CHESTER_BEATTY_OR_OTHER_INDOOR_ATTRACTION AND: retain_FLEXIBLE_PUBLIC_TRANSPORT_PLAN Reason: Irish weather remains changeable throughout the year, making Dublin''s extensive indoor cultural inventory particularly valuable. IF: weather == STRONG_WIND_OR_HEAVY_RAIN AND: plan_includes_HOWTH_CLIFF_WALK THEN: reduce_OR_REPLACE_COASTAL_WALK AND: retain_HOWTH_HARBOUR + SEAFOOD_OR_CITY_MUSEUM_ALTERNATIVE Reason: Exposed coastal routes can become considerably less comfortable or appropriate during poor weather. IF: route == CENTRAL_DUBLIN_TO_HOWTH THEN: prefer_DART_WHERE_SUITABLE Reason: Rail provides a straightforward connection between central Dublin and one of the capital''s strongest coastal sightseeing areas. IF: route == CENTRAL_DUBLIN_TO_DUN_LAOGHAIRE THEN: prefer_DART_WHERE_SUITABLE Reason: The coastal rail corridor makes Dún Laoghaire a practical public-transport excursion from the city centre. IF: movement == CENTRAL_DUBLIN_SIGHTSEEING THEN: prefer_WALKING + TFI_LEAP_CARD AND: use_DUBLIN_BUS + LUAS + DART_AS_REQUIRED Reason: Dublin''s central visitor districts are highly walkable, while the TFI network allows integrated travel across bus, Luas, DART and eligible commuter rail services. IF: traveler_uses_TFI_LEAP_CARD AND: travel_within_ELIGIBLE_DUBLIN_ZONE_1_SERVICES THEN: use_TFI_90_MINUTE_FARE_FOR_MULTIMODAL_TRAVEL Reason: Current Transport for Ireland pricing provides a €2 adult 90-minute fare across eligible Dublin Bus, Go-Ahead Ireland city bus, Luas, DART and commuter rail services in Zone 1. IF: trip_length <= 4 nights THEN: avoid_RENTAL_CAR_FOR_PRIMARY_DUBLIN_CITY_ITINERARY AND: use_WALKING + PUBLIC_TRANSPORT + SELECTIVE_TAXIS Reason: A car is generally unnecessary for Dublin''s principal visitor areas and can add parking and traffic friction to an otherwise walkable and transit-connected itinerary. IF: trip_length >= 5 nights AND: traveler_interest == BOTH_CITY_AND_COAST THEN: retain_ONE_DUBLIN_HOTEL_BASE AND: use_DART_FOR_COASTAL_DAY_TRIPS Reason: Howth, Dún Laoghaire and other Dublin Bay locations can generally be explored without unnecessary hotel changes. IF: trip_length >= 6 nights AND: traveler_interest == WIDER_IRELAND THEN: consider_DUBLIN_BASE + ONE_SECONDARY_REGION AND: avoid_USING_DUBLIN_AS_BASE_FOR_EVERY_DISTANT_IRELAND_EXCURSION Reason: Dublin is an excellent national gateway, but longer-distance regions become more enjoyable when overnight bases reduce repeated travel. IF: traveler_interest == FIRST_TIME_DUBLIN THEN: prioritize_TRINITY_COLLEGE + MEDIEVAL_DUBLIN + GEORGIAN_DUBLIN + GUINNESS_OR_KILMAINHAM AND: add_PHOENIX_PARK_OR_HOWTH_ONLY_IF_TIME_ALLOWS Reason: These experiences provide Dublin''s strongest first introduction to literature, Irish history, architecture, gastronomy and contemporary city culture.', 3395),
  ('dublin', 34, 'destination-scoring', 'DESTINATION SCORING', NULL, NULL, '| Factor | Score | | --- | --- | | Family | 90 | | Honeymoon | 85 | | Luxury | 90 | | Budget | 68 | | Adventure | 69 | | Culture | 97 | | Food | 93 | | Shopping | 88 | | Nightlife | 95 | | Relaxation | 84 | | Nature | 83 | | Accessibility | 84 | | Safety | 85 | | First-time visitor | 96 | | Photography | 94 |', 3396),
  ('dublin', 35, 'final-travel-agent-verdict', 'FINAL TRAVEL AGENT VERDICT', NULL, NULL, 'Best traveler profiles: 1. Culture / heritage traveler (Trinity College, Medieval Dublin, Georgian Dublin, Kilmainham, National Museums) 2. Literature traveler (Book of Kells, MoLI, James Joyce, Oscar Wilde, National Library, Literary Pubs) 3. History traveler (Dublin Castle, Kilmainham Gaol, GPO, Medieval Dublin, Revolutionary Heritage) 4. Food / pub traveler (Modern Irish Cuisine, Seafood, Guinness, Whiskey, Traditional Pubs) 5. Photography traveler (Trinity College, Georgian Dublin, Temple Bar, River Liffey, Howth, Dublin Bay) 6. Honeymoon / romantic traveler (Georgian Dublin, Howth, Boutique Hotels, Fine Dining, Live Music) 7. Family traveler (Dublinia, EPIC, Phoenix Park, Dublin Zoo, Trinity College, Coastal Excursions) 8. Luxury traveler (Five-Star Hotels, Private Guides, Fine Dining, Whiskey Experiences, Chauffeur Touring) 9. Nightlife / music traveler (Traditional Pubs, Live Music, Temple Bar, Camden Street, Theatre, Whiskey Bars) 10. First-time Europe traveler (Walkable Core, Heritage, Museums, Pub Culture, Public Transport, Coastal Day Trips) Best duration: 3–5 nights 2 nights: Best for TRINITY_COLLEGE + MEDIEVAL_DUBLIN + GEORGIAN_DUBLIN + ONE_OF_GUINNESS_OR_KILMAINHAM. 3–4 nights: Best for TRINITY + MEDIEVAL_DUBLIN + GEORGIAN_DUBLIN + GUINNESS + KILMAINHAM + PUB_AND_FOOD_EXPERIENCE. 5 nights: Excellent for CENTRAL_DUBLIN + PHOENIX_PARK + DOCKLANDS_EPIC + HOWTH_OR_DUBLIN_BAY with relaxed pacing. 6+ nights: Best when adding MALAHIDE + DUN_LAOGHAIRE + WICKLOW + BRU_NA_BOINNE_OR_WIDER_IRELAND rather than repeatedly covering only the central city. Best season: APRIL_TO_JUNE + SEPTEMBER Spring / Early Summer (April – June): HISTORIC_WALKING + GEORGIAN_DUBLIN + PHOENIX_PARK + HOWTH + PHOTOGRAPHY + LONGER_DAYLIGHT. Peak Summer (July – August): FESTIVALS + COAST + PARKS + LONG_DAYLIGHT + OUTDOOR_ACTIVITY, with stronger visitor pressure and accommodation pricing. Autumn (September – November): HERITAGE + LITERATURE + FOOD + PUB_CULTURE + MUSEUMS + AUTUMN_PHOTOGRAPHY. Winter (December – February): MUSEUMS + LITERATURE + TRADITIONAL_PUBS + LIVE_MUSIC + FOOD + CULTURAL_CITY_BREAKS. Dublin weather should always be treated as: MILD + CHANGEABLE + RAIN_POSSIBLE_YEAR_ROUND + WIND_AND_CLOUD_DEPENDENT. Best hotel strategy: Choose accommodation according to WALKABILITY + PUBLIC_TRANSPORT + EVENING_PRIORITY + BUDGET + TRIP_LENGTH. For first-time visitors: DUBLIN_2 / ST_STEPHENS_GREEN / TRINITY_OR_GEORGIAN_CORE provides the strongest walking convenience for major central attractions. For honeymoon / romance: GEORGIAN_DUBLIN / ST_STEPHENS_GREEN / PREMIUM_BOUTIQUE_HOTEL with easy restaurant and evening access. For culture: TRINITY_GEORGIAN_CORE / SOUTH_CITY / CENTRAL_DUBLIN with strong walking and public-transport access. For nightlife: TEMPLE_BAR_EDGE / CAMDEN_STREET / SOUTH_CITY depending desired nightlife intensity and noise tolerance. For luxury: ST_STEPHENS_GREEN / MERRION_SQUARE / PREMIUM_DUBLIN_2. For budget: Choose a VALUE_HOTEL_OR_HOSTEL with reliable BUS_LUAS_DART access rather than paying automatically for the most expensive historic-core address. Avoid unnecessary hotel changes because Dublin''s principal city attractions and Dublin Bay excursions work efficiently from one central base. Best transportation: Use: Dublin transportation should primarily be treated as: WALKING_WITHIN_CENTRAL_CORE + TFI_PUBLIC_TRANSPORT_FOR_LONGER_MOVEMENTS + DART_FOR_COASTAL_EXCURSIONS + SELECTIVE_TAXI + PRIVATE_ROAD_TRANSPORT_FOR_REGIONAL_TOURING. Current TFI Zone 1 positioning: TFI_90_MINUTE_FARE + DUBLIN_CITY_BUS + LUAS + DART + ELIGIBLE_COMMUTER_RAIL. Current adult TFI 90-minute Leap fare: €2.00 Current adult Zone 1 Leap caps: €6.00_DAILY + €24.00_WEEKLY. Primary airport: DUBLIN_AIRPORT IATA: DUB Dublin Airport currently has: NO_DIRECT_RAIL_STATION. Primary airport-city transport should therefore be treated as: AIRPORT_BUS_OR_COACH + TAXI + PRIVATE_TRANSFER. Dublin Airport currently provides direct bus / coach connections to central Dublin and multiple destinations across Ireland. Must-do for first-time visitor: Dublin should not be reduced to TEMPLE_BAR + GUINNESS alone; its identity combines medieval heritage, Georgian architecture, revolutionary history, internationally influential literature, national museums, theatre, traditional music, modern Irish gastronomy, historic pubs, major urban parkland and Dublin Bay coastal landscapes. Dublin should primarily be positioned as: CULTURAL_HERITAGE + LITERATURE + IRISH_HISTORY + WALKABLE_CITY_BREAK + PUB_AND_MUSIC_CULTURE + GASTRONOMY + PHOTOGRAPHY + FAMILY_TRAVEL + COASTAL_EXTENSIONS. Dublin currently holds: UNESCO_CREATIVE_CITY_OF_LITERATURE_STATUS since: 2010. This should NOT be confused with: UNESCO_WORLD_HERITAGE_SITE_STATUS. Dublin''s UNESCO literary identity is associated with a globally influential writing tradition including: JAMES_JOYCE + SAMUEL_BECKETT + W_B_YEATS + GEORGE_BERNARD_SHAW + OSCAR_WILDE + BRAM_STOKER. Don''t-do: Dublin first-time sightseeing should primarily be treated as: TRINITY_COLLEGE + MEDIEVAL_DUBLIN + GEORGIAN_DUBLIN + GUINNESS_OR_KILMAINHAM + PUB_AND_LIVE_MUSIC + ONE_PARK_OR_COASTAL_EXPERIENCE. Trinity / literary Dublin should primarily be treated as: BOOK_OF_KELLS + OLD_LIBRARY + UNIVERSITY_HERITAGE + MOLI + NATIONAL_LIBRARY + JAMES_JOYCE_AND_WIDER_LITERARY_CULTURE. Medieval Dublin should primarily be treated as: CHRIST_CHURCH + ST_PATRICKS + DUBLINIA + VIKING_AND_MEDIEVAL_HISTORY + HISTORIC_WALKING. Georgian Dublin should primarily be treated as: MERRION_SQUARE + GEORGIAN_ARCHITECTURE + NATIONAL_GALLERY + NATIONAL_MUSEUM + NATIONAL_LIBRARY + LITERARY_HERITAGE. Kilmainham should primarily be treated as: REVOLUTIONARY_HISTORY + IRISH_NATIONALISM + GUIDED_INTERPRETATION + IMMA + ADVANCE_BOOKING. Temple Bar should primarily be treated as: PUB_CULTURE + LIVE_MUSIC + CULTURAL_VENUES + PHOTOGRAPHY + DINING + EVENING_ACTIVITY rather than: DUBLINS_ONLY_NIGHTLIFE_AREA. Phoenix Park should primarily be treated as: URBAN_NATURE + DUBLIN_ZOO + CYCLING + WALKING + HISTORIC_MONUMENTS + FALLOW_DEER + FAMILY_RECREATION. Howth / Dublin Bay should primarily be treated as: COASTAL_SCENERY + SEAFOOD + DART_ACCESS + WALKING + PHOTOGRAPHY + ROMANTIC_AND_NATURE_EXTENSION. Biggest advantage: Exceptional concentration of Irish history, literary heritage, museums, Georgian and medieval architecture, traditional pub culture, live music and modern gastronomy within a highly walkable capital that also provides unusually convenient access to major parks and Dublin Bay coastal landscapes. Dublin can function simultaneously as a: CITY_BREAK_DESTINATION + CULTURAL_DESTINATION + LITERARY_DESTINATION + HISTORY_DESTINATION + FOOD_AND_PUB_DESTINATION + NIGHTLIFE_DESTINATION + ROMANTIC_DESTINATION + FAMILY_DESTINATION + COASTAL_GATEWAY_DESTINATION. Biggest disadvantage: High accommodation costs, substantial peak-event demand, changeable weather, tourist pressure around headline central attractions, accumulated walking over historic surfaces and variable accessibility within older buildings. Dublin''s lack of a direct rail station at Dublin Airport also makes airport-city access more road-dependent than several major European capitals. Overall destination score: 94/100', 3397),
  ('dublin', 36, 'data-quality', 'DATA QUALITY', NULL, NULL, 'information_completeness: 98/100 last_updated: 2026-09-05 last_verified: WEB_VERIFIED verified_by: FAILTE_IRELAND / VISIT_DUBLIN / HERITAGE_IRELAND_OPW / TRANSPORT_FOR_IRELAND / DUBLIN_AIRPORT / MET_EIREANN / UNESCO_CREATIVE_CITIES_NETWORK / TRINITY_COLLEGE_DUBLIN sources: IMPORTANT: Dublin should primarily be treated as a: COMPACT_CITY_BREAK_DESTINATION + WALKABLE_HISTORIC_CORE + LITERARY_DESTINATION + IRISH_HISTORY_DESTINATION + PUB_AND_MUSIC_DESTINATION + COASTAL_GATEWAY_DESTINATION. Dublin UNESCO status should be stored as: UNESCO_CREATIVE_CITY_OF_LITERATURE + MEMBER_SINCE_2010. Do NOT automatically classify central Dublin itself as: UNESCO_WORLD_HERITAGE_SITE. The UNESCO Creative Cities Network and UNESCO World Heritage List are separate designations. Dublin transportation should primarily be stored as: WALKING_DOMINANT_IN_CENTRAL_CORE + DUBLIN_BUS + LUAS + DART + COMMUTER_RAIL + SELECTIVE_TAXI + PRIVATE_ROAD_TRANSPORT_FOR_REGIONAL_TRIPS. Current TFI Zone 1 fare baseline: ADULT_90_MINUTE_FARE = €2.00 ADULT_DAILY_CAP = €6.00 ADULT_WEEKLY_CAP = €24.00 The eligible multimodal network currently includes: DUBLIN_CITY_BUS_SERVICES + LUAS + DART + ELIGIBLE_COMMUTER_RAIL_WITHIN_ZONE_1. Do not permanently store: FARES + ROUTES + TIMETABLES + SERVICE_FREQUENCIES + ENGINEERING_WORKS + FARE_ZONE_BOUNDARIES without Transport for Ireland re-verification. Current Dublin Airport positioning: NO_RAIL_STATION + BUS_AND_COACH_CONNECTIONS + TAXI + PRIVATE_TRANSFER + CAR_HIRE. Dublin Airport''s official guidance currently confirms that the airport does not have a train station. Do not permanently store: AIRPORT_BUS_ROUTE_NUMBER + DEPARTURE_FREQUENCY + TRANSFER_TIME + FARE + STOP_LOCATION without operator and Dublin Airport re-verification. Current Dublin Castle operational exception: CLOSED_TO_PUBLIC FROM_5_MAY_2026 TO_31_DECEMBER_2026 for: IRELAND_EU_PRESIDENCY_REQUIREMENTS. This closure should NOT be treated as a permanent attraction status beyond the confirmed period. Kilmainham Gaol should currently be treated as: ADVANCE_ONLINE_BOOKING_ESSENTIAL + OFFICIAL_TICKET_SOURCE_ONLY + LIMITED_CAPACITY_GUIDED_VISIT. Heritage Ireland currently warns that: THIRD_PARTY_RESALE_TICKETS_ARE_NOT_VALID + FRAUDULENT_LOOKALIKE_WEBSITES_EXIST. Book of Kells Experience should currently be treated as: TIMED_ADMISSION + ADVANCE_BOOKING_RECOMMENDED + OLD_LIBRARY_ACCESS + WHEELCHAIR_ACCESSIBLE_WITH_SITE_SPECIFIC_PROCEDURES. Visit Trinity currently states: OLD_LIBRARY_FULLY_WHEELCHAIR_ACCESSIBLE + STAFF_ASSISTANCE_REQUIRED_FOR_ELEVATORS + PAVILION_FULLY_WHEELCHAIR_ACCESSIBLE. Accessibility should be treated as: STRONG_MODERN_TRANSPORT_SUPPORT + VARIABLE_HISTORIC_BUILDING_ACCESS + ATTRACTION_SPECIFIC_VERIFICATION. Current Transport for Ireland positioning includes: MOST_TFI_BUSES_LOW_FLOOR_AND_WHEELCHAIR_ACCESSIBLE + DUBLIN_BUS_WHEELCHAIR_ACCESS_WITHOUT_ADVANCE_BOOKING_WITHIN_VEHICLE_LIMITS. Do not assume: EVERY_HISTORIC_BUILDING + EVERY_PUB + EVERY_CHURCH + EVERY_COASTAL_ROUTE + EVERY_TRANSPORT_STOP provides identical accessibility. Phoenix Park should currently be stored as approximately: 1,750_ACRES and primarily treated as: MAJOR_URBAN_PARK + DUBLIN_ZOO + CYCLING + WALKING + HISTORIC_MONUMENTS + FALLOW_DEER + FAMILY_RECREATION. Do not treat wildlife sightings as guaranteed or approach wild deer closely. Dublin climate information should primarily use: MET_EIREANN_DUBLIN_AIRPORT_1991_2020_NORMALS. Current climate baseline indicates approximately: JANUARY_MEAN_MAX = 8.0°C JULY_MEAN_MAX = 19.5°C ANNUAL_MEAN_TEMPERATURE = 9.7°C. Dublin climate should therefore be stored as: TEMPERATE_MARITIME + MILD + CHANGEABLE + RAIN_POSSIBLE_YEAR_ROUND + LIMITED_TEMPERATURE_EXTREMES_RELATIVE_TO_CONTINENTAL_EUROPE. Historical climate normals should NOT be interpreted as guaranteed future weather. Accommodation strategy should primarily consider: CENTRAL_WALKABILITY + PUBLIC_TRANSPORT + EVENING_NOISE + TRIP_LENGTH + EVENT_DATES + BUDGET + ACCESSIBILITY. Dublin food should be treated as: MODERN_IRISH_CUISINE + SEAFOOD + PUB_FOOD + IRISH_BEEF + ARTISAN_PRODUCTS + GUINNESS + IRISH_WHISKEY + BAKERIES + FINE_DINING. Dublin should primarily be treated as: CULTURE + HISTORY + LITERATURE + FOOD + NIGHTLIFE + FAMILY + ROMANCE + PHOTOGRAPHY + URBAN_NATURE + COASTAL_TRAVEL. Current attraction timings, admission prices, timed-entry procedures, temporary closures, exhibition schedules, transport fares, transport routes, weather conditions, event calendars and accessibility facilities must NOT be treated as permanently valid. VISIT_DUBLIN + HERITAGE_IRELAND_OPW + TRANSPORT_FOR_IRELAND + DUBLIN_AIRPORT + MET_EIREANN + UNESCO_CREATIVE_CITIES_NETWORK + TRINITY_COLLEGE_DUBLIN should be treated as primary verification sources. This dataset should be refreshed regularly before production use.', 3398),
  ('dubai', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Winter - BEST', NULL, 'months: November, December, January, February, March weather: 14-30°C pleasant sunny best + cool evening + best weather + beach best + desert best + city best crowd_level: HIGH - Winter best + New Year + Christmas + shopping festival + best season price_level: HIGH - Winter best + New Year + Christmas + shopping festival high overall_score: 94 recommended: true reason: Best weather + pleasant sunny best 14-30°C + cool evening + best beach + best desert + best city + best shopping + New Year + Christmas + Dubai Shopping Festival Jan + best season + must + but crowded + expensive + book 2 months early.', 3399);
