  ('cappadocia', 36, 'data-quality', 'DATA QUALITY', NULL, NULL, 'information_completeness: 92/100 last_updated: 2026-08-30 last_verified: PARTIALLY_LIVE_VERIFIED verified_by: CAPPADOCIA_DESTINATION_KNOWLEDGE_DATASET sources: Hot Air Balloon #1 world + 200 balloons sunrise + Fairy Chimneys + Love Valley + Rose Valley + Pigeon Valley + Goreme Open Air Museum UNESCO + Uchisar Castle + Underground City Derinkuyu + Kaymakli + Ihlara Valley + Selime Monastery + Belisirma + Avanos pottery + Urgup + cave hotels + Museum Hotel + Argos + Sacred House + 5★ cave + boutique cave + horse riding + ATV + hiking + Cappadocia tourism + Turkey Tourism + NAV Airport + ASR Airport + dolmus + taxi + private car + hotel supplier data hostel $15-$30 3★ $40-$80 cave hotel $60-$150 4★ cave $80-$200 5★ cave $200-$600 luxury Museum Hotel $400-$800 + food shopping festival culture heritage photography data + balloon fairy chimneys valleys IMPORTANT: This Cappadocia file is suitable for itinerary design, traveller profiling, hotel-area strategy, and initial package planning. Prices, hotel inventory, Hot Air Balloon timings, Goreme Open Air Museum timings, Underground City timings, Uchisar Castle timings, valleys timings must be live-verified before quotation. Do not rely on generic Cappadocia package inclusions without confirming exact Hot Air Balloon Fairy Chimneys Goreme Open Air Museum Uchisar Castle Love Valley Rose Valley Pigeon Valley Underground City Ihlara Valley Avanos pottery cave hotels hotel area Goreme Uchisar / Avanos Urgup / cave hotels luxury, private car included or not, guide included or not, Hot Air Balloon included or not, Goreme Museum included or not, Underground City included or not.', 3504),
  ('amman', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Spring Peak Season', NULL, 'months: March–May weather: Mild to warm and mostly sunny, with temperatures rising from around 18°C in March to 27–29°C in May. Rainfall drops sharply through the season, making April–May especially comfortable for walking, archaeological sightseeing, and day trips. crowd_level: HIGH price_level: HIGH overall_score: 76–80 recommended: true reason: One of Amman''s best sightseeing periods. Pleasant temperatures and increasingly dry weather make outdoor exploration excellent, although spring is a major tourism period with higher accommodation demand and prices.', 3505),
  ('amman', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Summer Season', NULL, 'months: June–August weather: Hot, dry, and virtually rain-free, with daytime temperatures generally around 30–33°C and occasional hotter spells. Evenings are more comfortable because of Amman''s elevated setting. crowd_level: LOW price_level: LOW overall_score: 76–81 recommended: true reason: Daytime heat reduces sightseeing comfort, but very low rainfall, fewer traditional leisure-season visitors, and generally better-value accommodation make summer attractive for budget-conscious travelers.', 3506),
  ('amman', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Autumn Peak Season', NULL, 'months: September–November weather: Warm and increasingly comfortable, dropping from around 30°C in September to about 21°C in November. Rain remains limited in September–October before increasing toward November. crowd_level: MEDIUM to HIGH price_level: MEDIUM to HIGH overall_score: 72–79 recommended: true reason: September and October provide excellent conditions for outdoor sightseeing, while November becomes cooler and quieter. Autumn is one of Jordan''s established high-demand travel periods, particularly for sightseeing and regional excursions.', 3507),
  ('amman', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Winter Low Season', NULL, 'months: December–February weather: Cool and occasionally wet, with daytime temperatures generally around 12–16°C and colder nights. January and February receive the highest rainfall, while occasional cold spells can occur. crowd_level: LOW price_level: LOW overall_score: 79–83 recommended: true reason: Although outdoor weather is less reliable, very low crowd pressure and lower accommodation costs make winter particularly attractive for budget and culture-focused travelers. Indoor museums, cafés, historic neighborhoods, and food experiences remain enjoyable.', 3508),
  ('amman', 10, 'budget-strategy', 'BUDGET STRATEGY', NULL, NULL, '**Where saving money is usually not recommended:**', 3509),
  ('amman', 12, 'airport-transfer-logic', 'AIRPORT TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Family', 'family', 'Pre-booked **private minivan or SUV** from AMM directly to the hotel for easy luggage management and child seats.', 3510),
  ('amman', 12, 'airport-transfer-logic', 'AIRPORT TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Honeymoon', 'honeymoon', 'Private **luxury sedan/SUV** booked through hotel concierge or transfer services for a seamless airport arrival.', 3511),
  ('amman', 12, 'airport-transfer-logic', 'AIRPORT TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Luxury', 'luxury', 'Chauffeur-driven **premium luxury vehicle** with VIP airport meet-and-assist services.', 3512),
  ('amman', 12, 'airport-transfer-logic', 'AIRPORT TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Budget', 'budget', 'Take the **Sariyah Airport Express Bus** to the 7th Circle or North Bus Station (3.30 JOD), then catch a short Careem/taxi to your destination. reason: Amman''s airport is located ~33 km south of the city center. App-based rideshares (Careem/Uber) or official fixed-fare airport taxis (22.50–25 JOD) provide direct door-to-door convenience across the city''s hilly topography.', 3513),
  ('amman', 18, 'family-travel', 'FAMILY TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'child_friendly_score: **86** best_ages: Rules: Prefer: Avoid:', 3514),
  ('amman', 19, 'honeymoon-travel', 'HONEYMOON TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'honeymoon_score: **87** romance_score: **85** privacy_score: **88** luxury_score: **90** Recommended: **Honeymoon itinerary should NOT contain more than:** **2–3 major excursions per day.** Prefer: **Atmospheric sights + private transfers + relaxed rooftop dining** over: **rushed group tours and continuous transit.**', 3515),
  ('amman', 20, 'luxury-travel', 'LUXURY TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'luxury_score: **90** Recommended: Luxury here primarily means: rather than:', 3516),
  ('amman', 21, 'adventure', 'ADVENTURE', NULL, NULL, 'adventure_score: **75** Amman is primarily a **cultural, historical, and culinary capital**, serving as an urban base for adventure excursions across northern and central Jordan rather than a wilderness hub itself. Top experiences:', 3517),
  ('amman', 22, 'senior-travel', 'SENIOR TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'senior_suitability: **81** walking_intensity: **LOW → MEDIUM** Rules: Prefer: Avoid:', 3518),
  ('amman', 23, 'accessibility', 'ACCESSIBILITY', NULL, NULL, 'wheelchair_accessibility: LIMITED: public_transport_accessibility: **LOW → MODERATE** hotel_accessibility: VERIFY_PER_HOTEL: attraction_accessibility: VERIFY_PER_ATTRACTION: Rule: Modern hotels, shopping malls (Abdali), and modern museums (The Jordan Museum) are accessible, but **historic districts, ancient ruins, and public sidewalks feature high curbs, steep stairways, and uneven terrain**.', 3519),
  ('amman', 24, 'food', 'FOOD', NULL, NULL, 'Amman is an **internationally acclaimed Middle Eastern culinary capital**, offering everything from legendary street food stalls to multi-hatted fine-dining institutions. Strong categories: Food experiences: Budget: Street-side falafel, shawarma, and knafeh (1–4 JOD). Premium: High-end Levantine restaurants and luxury hotel dining (20–50+ JOD).', 3520),
  ('amman', 25, 'shopping', 'SHOPPING', NULL, NULL, 'shopping_score: **84** Strong categories: Prefer: Shopping strength: **MEDIUM → HIGH** Amman offers a delightful contrast between **vibrant historic outdoor markets and sleek modern luxury malls**.', 3521),
  ('amman', 26, 'nightlife', 'NIGHTLIFE', NULL, NULL, 'nightlife_level: **78** Amman offers a **sophisticated, atmospheric, and relaxed nightlife scene** centered around rooftop lounges, craft cocktail bars, shisha cafes, and cultural venues. Suitable for: Night experiences: Best for: **Rooftop social gatherings and atmospheric evening dining** rather than: **All-night commercial mega-clubs.**', 3522),
  ('amman', 28, 'sample-itinerary-patterns', 'SAMPLE ITINERARY PATTERNS', 'HALF-DAY – AMMAN CITADEL & ANCIENT DOWNTOWN', NULL, 'Morning / Afternoon Pickup from your hotel in Amman → Begin at the hilltop **Amman Citadel**, exploring the majestic Temple of Hercules, Umayyad Palace, and panoramic city lookouts → Drive down to the historic **Roman Theater**, a magnificently preserved 2nd-century 6,000-seat amphitheater → Stroll through the bustling **Downtown Al-Balad Souks** to experience traditional spice, textile, and gold markets → Stop at legendary local eateries for authentic **falafel at Hashem** and hot **knafeh at Habibah Sweets** → Return to your hotel or enjoy a traditional cardamom coffee on Rainbow Street', 3523),
  ('amman', 28, 'sample-itinerary-patterns', 'SAMPLE ITINERARY PATTERNS', '1 DAY – ANCIENT CITADEL, ROMAN HERITAGE & RAINBOW STREET', NULL, 'Morning Morning pickup from your hotel for Amman''s primary historic circuit → Explore the hilltop **Amman Citadel** and visit the Jordan Archaeological Museum → Descend into Downtown to tour the **Roman Theater** and adjacent Museum of Popular Traditions Afternoon Continue to **The Jordan Museum** in Ras Al-Ein to view the ancient ''Ain Ghazal statues and historic Dead Sea Scrolls exhibits → Walk up to historic **Rainbow Street in Jabal Amman** for lunch at a traditional Levantine restaurant Evening Explore the boutique shops, art galleries, and stone-architecture alleyways along Rainbow Street → Enjoy sunset views across the seven hills from a hilltop rooftop lounge → Finish with a traditional Jordanian dinner featuring **Mansaf, fresh mezze, and mint lemonade**', 3524),
  ('amman', 28, 'sample-itinerary-patterns', 'SAMPLE ITINERARY PATTERNS', '2 DAYS – AMMAN HIGHLIGHTS & GRECO-ROMAN JERASH CIRCUIT', NULL, 'Day 1 Full-day exploration of Amman''s top urban and historical attractions → Begin at **Amman Citadel**, then continue to the **Roman Theater** and **Downtown Al-Balad Souks** → Tour **The Jordan Museum** before heading to **Jabal Weibdeh** for arts, culture, and bohemian cafes → Spend the evening on **Rainbow Street** with dinner at a historic courtyard villa Day 2 Morning departure for **Jerash**, located 45 minutes north of Amman → Explore the vast Greco-Roman ancient city, including Hadrian''s Arch, the Oval Plaza, the Colonnaded Street, and the Temple of Artemis → Continue to **Ajloun Castle**, a 12th-century Ayyubid fortress offering hilltop views over the Jordan Valley → Return to Amman for dinner and evening leisure', 3525),
  ('amman', 29, '6-days-and-5-nights-honeymoon-itinerary', '6 DAYS & 5 NIGHTS HONEYMOON ITINERARY', 'DAY 1 – ROMANTIC ARRIVAL & HILLTOP SKYLINE VIEWS', 'honeymoon', 'Morning / Afternoon Arrive at **Queen Alia International Airport (AMM)** → Meet your private chauffeur and transfer to your romantic 5-star hotel in Amman → Complete check-in and unwind in your suite Lunch Enjoy a relaxed Levantine lunch in a quiet historic courtyard Evening Take a private evening drive through the historic neighborhood of **Jabal Amman** → Walk along **Rainbow Street** for couple''s photography against classic stone architecture → Enjoy a romantic welcome dinner on a panoramic rooftop terrace overlooking the lit-up Citadel', 3526),
  ('amman', 29, '6-days-and-5-nights-honeymoon-itinerary', '6 DAYS & 5 NIGHTS HONEYMOON ITINERARY', 'DAY 2 – CITADEL SUNSET & ARTS DISTRICT STROLL', NULL, 'Morning After breakfast, depart for a private guided visit to the **Amman Citadel** → Explore ancient Roman columns, the Umayyad Palace, and 360-degree views of the capital → Descend to tour the majestic 2nd-century **Roman Theater** Afternoon Enjoy lunch in the creative neighborhood of **Jabal Weibdeh** → Stroll through peaceful art galleries at **Darat Al Funun** and small craft boutiques → Return to the hotel for couple''s relaxation or a private spa treatment Evening Drive to a vantage point for sunset photos over Amman''s hills → Enjoy a fine-dining Levantine meal in a restored historic villa', 3527),
  ('amman', 29, '6-days-and-5-nights-honeymoon-itinerary', '6 DAYS & 5 NIGHTS HONEYMOON ITINERARY', 'DAY 3 – ANCIENT JERASH & AJLOUN FOREST ESCAPE', NULL, 'Morning Depart with your private chauffeur for the ancient city of **Jerash** → Walk hand-in-hand down the grand Colonnaded Street, Oval Plaza, and ancient theaters Lunch Enjoy a traditional Middle Eastern feast featuring fresh mezze and grilled delicacies Afternoon Drive through green pine forests to **Ajloun Castle** → Explore the historic hilltop fortress and enjoy sweeping vistas across the northern valleys → Return to Amman in the late afternoon Evening Enjoy a quiet evening at your hotel or a cozy shisha lounge', 3528),
  ('amman', 29, '6-days-and-5-nights-honeymoon-itinerary', '6 DAYS & 5 NIGHTS HONEYMOON ITINERARY', 'DAY 4 – SACRED MOSAICS, MOUNT NEBO & DEAD SEA FLOAT', NULL, 'Morning Checkout of Amman and drive south to **Madaba** → Visit St. George''s Church to admire the famous 6th-century Mosaic Map of the Holy Land → Continue to **Mount Nebo** for breathtaking views overlooking the Jordan Valley and Dead Sea Lunch Enjoy lunch at a hilltop restaurant en route Afternoon Arrive at your luxury **Dead Sea Resort** → Experience floating weightlessly in the mineral-rich Dead Sea waters → Indulge in a natural Dead Sea mud bath and couple''s spa session Evening Watch the sunset over the Dead Sea waters followed by a candlelit beachside dinner', 3529),
  ('amman', 29, '6-days-and-5-nights-honeymoon-itinerary', '6 DAYS & 5 NIGHTS HONEYMOON ITINERARY', 'DAY 5 – HOLY BAPTISM SITE & ROMANTIC RESORT RELAXATION', 'honeymoon', 'Morning Visit the **Baptism Site of Jesus Christ (Bethany Beyond the Jordan)** → Take a peaceful guided tour through this historic UNESCO World Heritage sanctuary along the Jordan River Lunch Return to your Dead Sea resort for a relaxing poolside lunch Afternoon Enjoy resort leisure, private beach access, infinity pool floating, and wellness treatments Evening Celebrate your final night with an exclusive private beachfront dinner under the stars', 3530),
  ('amman', 29, '6-days-and-5-nights-honeymoon-itinerary', '6 DAYS & 5 NIGHTS HONEYMOON ITINERARY', 'DAY 6 – LEISURE BREAKFAST & DEPARTURE', NULL, 'Morning Enjoy a slow breakfast overlooking the Dead Sea → Complete checkout and meet your private chauffeur Late Morning / Afternoon Transfer to **Queen Alia International Airport (AMM)** for your departure flight → Depart Jordan with unforgettable memories of ancient history and romantic landscapes', 3531),
  ('amman', 30, '6-days-and-5-nights-family-itinerary', '6 DAYS & 5 NIGHTS FAMILY ITINERARY', 'DAY 1 – FAMILY ARRIVAL & DOWNTOWN INTRODUCTION', 'family', 'Morning / Afternoon Arrive at **Queen Alia International Airport (AMM)** → Meet your private family vehicle and transfer to your Amman hotel → Complete check-in and take time to unpack and relax Evening Head Downtown to **Al-Balad** for an easy family stroll → Stop at Hashem Restaurant for child-friendly falafel, hummus, and fresh bread → Try famous warm knafeh at Habibah Sweets → Return to the hotel for early family rest', 3532),
  ('amman', 30, '6-days-and-5-nights-family-itinerary', '6 DAYS & 5 NIGHTS FAMILY ITINERARY', 'DAY 2 – CITADEL, ROMAN THEATER & CAR MUSEUM', NULL, 'Morning Visit the **Amman Citadel** after breakfast → Kids can explore the massive ancient stone hand of Hercules and open-air ruins → Continue down to the **Roman Theater** and let children test the acoustic echoes on stage Lunch Enjoy a family-friendly lunch in central Amman Afternoon Visit the **Royal Automobile Museum** in King Hussein Park → Explore King Hussein''s vast collection of vintage sports cars, royal vehicles, and motorcycles → Optional stop at the adjacent **Children''s Museum Jordan** for interactive exhibits Evening Return to the hotel for dinner and rest', 3533),
  ('amman', 30, '6-days-and-5-nights-family-itinerary', '6 DAYS & 5 NIGHTS FAMILY ITINERARY', 'DAY 3 – GRECO-ROMAN JERASH & AJLOUN CASTLE', NULL, 'Morning Take a day trip north to **Jerash** → Explore the massive ancient Roman plaza, arches, and temples with an engaging guide Lunch Enjoy lunch at an outdoor garden restaurant with fresh flatbreads and grilled meats Afternoon Drive to **Ajloun Castle** → Kids can explore stone towers, passageways, and drawbridges in this medieval Islamic fortress Evening Return to Amman for a relaxed family dinner', 3534),
  ('amman', 30, '6-days-and-5-nights-family-itinerary', '6 DAYS & 5 NIGHTS FAMILY ITINERARY', 'DAY 4 – JORDAN MUSEUM & ABDALI BOULEVARD', NULL, 'Morning Visit **The Jordan Museum** in Ras Al-Ein → Discover interactive archaeological displays, ancient statues, and historical exhibits Lunch Enjoy lunch at a modern cafe on **The Boulevard in Abdali** Afternoon Walk through the pedestrian-friendly **Abdali Boulevard** and Abdali Mall for family shopping and treats Evening Enjoy a relaxed family dinner at Abdali before returning to your hotel', 3535),
  ('amman', 30, '6-days-and-5-nights-family-itinerary', '6 DAYS & 5 NIGHTS FAMILY ITINERARY', 'DAY 5 – MADABA MOSAICS & DEAD SEA FAMILY FLOAT', 'family', 'Morning Depart Amman for **Madaba** to see the ancient mosaic map at St. George''s Church → Continue to **Mount Nebo** to take in panoramic views of the valley below Lunch Enjoy a family lunch near Mount Nebo Afternoon Drive down to a day-use **Dead Sea Beach Resort** → Experience floating in the Dead Sea and playing in child-friendly resort pools Evening Enjoy a sunset dinner by the Dead Sea before returning to Amman for your final night', 3536),
  ('amman', 30, '6-days-and-5-nights-family-itinerary', '6 DAYS & 5 NIGHTS FAMILY ITINERARY', 'DAY 6 – RELAXED MORNING & DEPARTURE', NULL, 'Morning Enjoy breakfast at the hotel and complete checkout → Optional last-minute shopping for spices, sweets, or souvenirs in Downtown Late Morning / Afternoon Transfer by private family vehicle to **Queen Alia International Airport (AMM)** → Depart Amman for your onward journey', 3537),
  ('amman', 31, '6-days-and-5-nights-luxury-itinerary', '6 DAYS & 5 NIGHTS LUXURY ITINERARY', 'DAY 1 – VIP ARRIVAL & 5-STAR AMMAN RETREAT', NULL, 'Morning / Afternoon Arrive at **Queen Alia International Airport (AMM)** → Greeted by VIP airport meet-and-assist service and private luxury chauffeur transfer → Check into your flagship 5-star hotel (e.g., The St. Regis Amman, Four Seasons Hotel Amman, or The Ritz-Carlton) → Unwind in your suite with welcome refreshments Lunch Curated multi-course Middle Eastern lunch at your hotel Evening Private evening transfer to **Rainbow Street** in Jabal Amman → Private guided walk past historic stone mansions and boutique shops → Enjoy an exclusive fine-dining dinner at a premier Levantine restaurant like Sufra or Fakhr El-Din', 3538),
  ('amman', 31, '6-days-and-5-nights-luxury-itinerary', '6 DAYS & 5 NIGHTS LUXURY ITINERARY', 'DAY 2 – PRIVATE CITADEL & VIP ARCHAEOLOGY EXPERIENCE', NULL, 'Early Morning Meet your expert private historian guide for an early visit to the **Amman Citadel** → Enjoy exclusive insights into the Temple of Hercules and Umayyad Palace with minimal crowds → Private viewings at **The Jordan Museum** in Ras Al-Ein Lunch Refined regional tasting menu in Jabal Weibdeh Afternoon Private gallery access in **Jabal Weibdeh** and **Darat Al Funun** → Optional private shopping consultation for luxury Dead Sea cosmetics and fine gold crafts Evening Return to your hotel for spa treatments and relaxation → Sunset cocktails and fine dining at a luxury rooftop lounge', 3539),
  ('amman', 31, '6-days-and-5-nights-luxury-itinerary', '6 DAYS & 5 NIGHTS LUXURY ITINERARY', 'DAY 3 – EXCLUSIVE JERASH TOUR & AJLOUN PRIVATE ESCAPE', NULL, 'Morning Chauffeur-driven transfer to the ancient city of **Jerash** → Private guided tour through the Roman ruins, Oval Plaza, and ancient temples Lunch Exclusive private lunch arrangement at a top regional estate Afternoon Private transfer to **Ajloun Castle** for sweeping views over the northern hills → Return to Amman in luxury comfort Evening Gourmet dinner at an iconic Amman fine-dining venue', 3540),
  ('amman', 31, '6-days-and-5-nights-luxury-itinerary', '6 DAYS & 5 NIGHTS LUXURY ITINERARY', 'DAY 4 – MOUNT NEBO, BAPTISM SITE & DEAD SEA RESORT', NULL, 'Morning Private driver transfer to **Madaba** and **Mount Nebo** for private historical viewings → Continue down to the sacred **Baptism Site (Bethany Beyond the Jordan)** with a private guide Lunch Gourmet lunch overlooking the Jordan River valley Afternoon Arrive at your exclusive luxury 5-star resort on the **Dead Sea** (e.g., Kempinski Hotel Ishtar) → Private beach floating experience, mud treatments, and custom spa therapies Evening Watch the sunset over the water followed by a chef-curated private dinner', 3541),
  ('amman', 31, '6-days-and-5-nights-luxury-itinerary', '6 DAYS & 5 NIGHTS LUXURY ITINERARY', 'DAY 5 – DEAD SEA WELLNESS & BAPTISM SANCTUARY RELAXATION', NULL, 'Morning Leisurely luxury breakfast overlooking the Dead Sea → Full morning reserved for private wellness, infinity pool relaxation, and spa therapies Lunch Private poolside dining Afternoon Relax at your resort or enjoy an optional private helicopter tour over the Dead Sea and surrounding wadis Evening Celebrate your final evening with an exclusive candlelit beachside dinner experience', 3542),
  ('amman', 31, '6-days-and-5-nights-luxury-itinerary', '6 DAYS & 5 NIGHTS LUXURY ITINERARY', 'DAY 6 – ROYAL BREAKFAST & VIP DEPARTURE', NULL, 'Morning Enjoy a leisurely final breakfast at your luxury resort → Complete checkout and meet your dedicated chauffeur Late Morning / Afternoon Transfer in a premium vehicle directly to **Queen Alia International Airport (AMM)** → Depart Jordan following an exceptional blend of ancient history, luxury hospitality, private transfers, and fine dining', 3543),
  ('amman', 32, 'travel-agent-insights', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS', 'What inexperienced planners often do wrong', NULL, '', 3544),
  ('amman', 32, 'travel-agent-insights', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS', 'What an experienced planner does differently', NULL, '', 3545),
