  ('amman', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', NULL, NULL, 'IF: `trip_length <= 1 day` THEN: Focus exclusively on the hilltop **Amman Citadel**, descend to the ancient **Roman Theater**, explore the bustling markets of **Downtown Al-Balad**, and finish with authentic local cuisine at **Hashem Restaurant** and **Habibah Sweets**. Reason: A single day requires concentrating on central historic landmarks and core street-food culture to maximize sight-seeing efficiency within Amman''s urban core. IF: `trip_length == 3 days` THEN: Dedicate Day 1 to the **Amman Citadel**, **Roman Theater**, and **Rainbow Street**; take a Day 2 trip north to the Greco-Roman ruins of **Jerash** and **Ajloun Castle**; and reserve Day 3 for **The Jordan Museum**, art galleries in **Jabal Weibdeh**, and modern shopping in **Abdali**. Reason: A 3-day window provides a balanced mix of Amman''s ancient heritage, a premier northern excursion, and contemporary local culture. IF: `trip_length >= 5 days` THEN: Cover all major Amman urban districts, launch full day trips north to **Jerash** and **Ajloun**, head south to the mosaic city of **Madaba** and **Mount Nebo**, and spend multi-day leisure time floating at the **Dead Sea** and visiting the **Baptism Site**. Reason: Extended stays allow travelers to use Amman as a complete regional hub, venturing to surrounding holy sites, ancient cities, and therapeutic natural wonders. IF: `trip_type == FIRST_TIME_VISITOR` THEN: Book a structured itinerary covering **Amman Citadel**, **Roman Theater**, a walking food tour in **Downtown Al-Balad**, sunset views from **Rainbow Street**, and a day excursion to **Jerash**. Reason: First-time visitors experience Jordan''s core historic narrative—spanning Roman, Umayyad, and modern Levantine eras—without logistical complexity. IF: `trip_type == HONEYMOON` THEN: Stay at a boutique hotel in **Jabal Amman**, reserve private rooftop dinners overlooking the lit-up city skyline, stroll through art galleries in **Jabal Weibdeh**, and combine city exploring with a luxury wellness stay on the **Dead Sea**. Reason: Combining hilltop boutique views, fine Levantine dining, and Dead Sea spa luxury delivers an intimate, scenic, and romantic itinerary. IF: `traveler_type == FAMILY` THEN: Plan a comfortable itinerary visiting the **Roman Theater**, the interactive **Children''s Museum Jordan**, the **Royal Automobile Museum**, pedestrian walks along **Abdali Boulevard**, and an easy day trip to **Jerash**. Reason: Wide pedestrian spaces, engaging vehicle exhibits, and accessible ancient ruins offer a safe and entertaining environment for travelers of all ages. IF: `traveler_type == LUXURY` THEN: Reserve 5-star accommodations in central Amman, utilize private chauffeured luxury transfers, hire expert private historians for **Amman Citadel** and **Jerash**, and arrange private VIP spa packages at the **Dead Sea**. Reason: Amman offers world-class 5-star hospitality, private VIP airport handling, and high-end fine dining that elevate classical archaeological touring. IF: `traveler_type == BUDGET` THEN: Stay in hostels or budget hotels in **Downtown Al-Balad**, utilize ride-hailing apps or local buses, leverage the **Jordan Pass** for free site entries, and dine on street food like falafel, shawarma, and fresh flatbreads. Reason: Bundled entrance passes, affordable public sights, and cheap local food make Amman one of the most accessible historic capitals for budget travelers. IF: `traveler_interest == NATURE` THEN: Combine urban hill walks with day trips into the pine forests of **Ajloun**, explore the **Dana Bioreserve** trails south of the city, and experience the unique marine geology of the **Dead Sea**. Reason: Amman sits within short driving distance of northern forest reserves and the lowest land elevation on Earth, making nature day trips effortless. IF: `traveler_interest == FOOD` THEN: Embark on street-food walks for **falafel** and **knafeh** in Downtown, take cooking classes at **Beit Sitti** in Jabal Weibdeh, sample festive dinners of **Mansaf**, and enjoy contemporary Levantine fusion dining on Rainbow Street. Reason: Amman is a culinary capital offering everything from centuries-old street stalls to high-end Levantine gastronomy. IF: `traveler_interest == ADVENTURE` THEN: Use Amman as a launchpad for hiking sections of the **Jordan Trail**, canyoneering in nearby wadis like **Wadi Mujib**, or taking offbeat desert castle circuits into the eastern badia. Reason: Rugged wadis and historic desert trails begin just outside the capital, perfect for thrill-seekers seeking physical challenges. IF: `traveler_type == SENIOR` THEN: Utilize private chauffeured door-to-door transport, focus on flat or elevator-accessible sites like **The Jordan Museum**, take golf-cart or gentle walking routes at **Jerash**, and avoid steep, unpaved stair climbs between hills. Reason: Navigating Amman''s steep geography via private transport avoids strenuous hill walking while ensuring full access to major archaeological highlights. IF: `traveler_type == TRANSIT` THEN: If stopping over for a 4 to 6-hour layover from Queen Alia Airport, hire a private airport taxi directly to the **Amman Citadel** for panoramic views, grab a quick lunch on **Rainbow Street**, and return for your flight. Reason: The Citadel is easily reachable from the airport highway, allowing transit travelers to capture sweeping capital views efficiently. IF: `traveler_interest == SPIRITUALITY` THEN: Visit the iconic **King Abdullah I Mosque**, explore early Christian heritage at **Madaba** and **Mount Nebo**, and make a sacred pilgrimage to the **Baptism Site of Jesus Christ (Bethany Beyond the Jordan)**. Reason: The region surrounding Amman hosts pivotal Holy Land sites spanning early Islamic architecture, Byzantine mosaic art, and sacred biblical rivers.', 3547),
  ('amman', 34, 'destination-scoring', 'DESTINATION SCORING', NULL, NULL, '| Factor | Score | | --- | --- | | Family | 86 | | Honeymoon | 88 | | Luxury | 90 | | Budget | 92 | | Adventure | 78 | | Culture | 96 | | Food | 95 | | Shopping | 84 | | Nightlife | 76 | | Relaxation | 83 | | Nature | 75 | | Accessibility | 70 | | Safety | 91 | | First-time visitor | 91 | | Photography | 94 |', 3548),
  ('amman', 35, 'final-travel-agent-verdict', 'FINAL TRAVEL AGENT VERDICT', NULL, NULL, 'Best for: History enthusiasts, cultural explorers, food lovers, urban adventurers, couples, and families looking to experience ancient Roman ruins, vibrant street markets, rich Levantine gastronomy, and world-class museums in Jordan''s historic capital built across seven iconic hills. Best duration: 2 to 3 days for a complete Amman city tour covering the Amman Citadel, Roman Theater, The Jordan Museum, Rainbow Street, Jabal Weibdeh, and Downtown Al-Balad souks; extendable to 5 to 6 days when using Amman as a hub for northern and central day trips toward Jerash, Ajloun Castle, Madaba, Mount Nebo, the Baptism Site, and the Dead Sea. Best season: March to May (spring) and September to November (autumn). Spring delivers pleasant warm days, cool evenings, and blooming green hillsides; autumn brings mild temperatures and crisp clear skies ideal for urban hill walks. December to February is cool to cold with occasional rain or snowfall, while June to August sees hot summer temperatures best managed with early morning sightseeing. Best stay: Flagship 5-star international hotels and luxury high-rises in **West Amman** (such as Jabal Amman, Abdoun, or the Abdali district) for panoramic skyline views and modern amenities; paired with historic boutique guesthouses and converted Ottoman-era villas in **Jabal Amman** or **Jabal Weibdeh** for travelers seeking traditional architecture and bohemian charm. Best transport: Dedicated private chauffeured vehicles or organized tour transfers for seamless airport arrival and outer day trips (Jerash, Ajloun, Dead Sea); combined with app-based ride-hailing services (such as Uber or Careem) or registered yellow cabs for navigating the city''s steep hills, valleys, and narrow district roads. Must-do: Avoid: Biggest advantage: An extraordinary blend of thousands of years of ancient history with a vibrant modern Levantine food and arts scene, serving as a safe, highly accessible, and central base for exploring the northern and central highlights of Jordan. Biggest disadvantage: Challenging urban geography featuring steep hills, heavy traffic congestion during peak hours, and limited public walking infrastructure between distinct neighborhood districts. Overall destination score: **88/100**', 3549),
  ('amman', 36, 'data-quality', 'DATA QUALITY', NULL, NULL, 'information_completeness: 93/100 last_updated: 2026-09-05 last_verified: NOT_LIVE_VERIFIED verified_by: TRAVEL_ENGINE_INITIAL_DATASET sources: IMPORTANT: Prices, opening hours, schedules, visa requirements, availability, accessibility and operational conditions must NOT be treated as permanently valid from this document. These must be sourced from structured, refreshable data.', 3550),
  ('petra', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Spring Peak Season', NULL, 'months: March–May weather: Mild, pleasant, and highly favorable for hiking, with daytime temperatures rising from 19°C in March to 28°C in May. Skies are predominantly clear and sunny, providing ideal conditions for outdoor valley exploration and steep stone staircase climbs. crowd_level: HIGH price_level: HIGH overall_score: 72–76 recommended: true reason: The absolute best weather period for hiking through the Siq and climbing to Ad Deir (The Monastery). High demand leads to heavy tour group crowds and premium hotel pricing in Wadi Musa, but the comfortable outdoor conditions make it the premier visiting window.', 3551),
  ('petra', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Summer Season', NULL, 'months: June–August weather: Hot, dry, and intense, with daytime temperatures routinely exceeding 33–36°C in the exposed desert canyon. Zero rainfall and high UV exposure require early morning or late afternoon exploration to avoid peak heat. crowd_level: LOW price_level: LOW overall_score: 72–77 recommended: true reason: Intense midday desert heat reduces physical hiking comfort, but minimal crowd levels and significantly lower accommodation rates in Wadi Musa offer excellent value for budget travelers who plan early morning site entries.', 3552),
  ('petra', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Autumn Peak Season', NULL, 'months: September–November weather: Warm and dry, with temperatures dropping from 31°C in September to a comfortable 20°C in November. The air is clear and rain remains minimal until late November, creating prime conditions for desert photography and trekking. crowd_level: MEDIUM to HIGH price_level: MEDIUM to HIGH overall_score: 73–78 recommended: true reason: October and November feature near-perfect hiking temperatures with clear desert views. High tour demand brings larger crowds and elevated rates, but overall conditions are among the finest of the year.', 3553),
  ('petra', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Winter Low Season', NULL, 'months: December–February weather: Cool to cold, with daytime temperatures ranging from 12°C to 15°C and night temperatures dropping near freezing (2–4°C). Occasional rain or winter flash floods can occur, sometimes temporarily closing the Siq for safety. crowd_level: LOW price_level: LOW overall_score: 78–82 recommended: true reason: Although weather can be chilly and flash flood warnings must be monitored, very low crowd levels mean you can experience iconic monuments like Al-Khazneh without heavy tour groups, accompanied by discounted hotel rates.', 3554),
  ('petra', 10, 'budget-strategy', 'BUDGET STRATEGY', NULL, NULL, '**Where saving money is usually not recommended:**', 3555),
  ('petra', 12, 'airport-transfer-logic', 'AIRPORT TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Family', 'family', 'Pre-booked **private minivan or SUV transfer** from AMM (3 hours) or AQJ (2 hours) directly to your Wadi Musa hotel for comfort and luggage ease.', 3556),
  ('petra', 12, 'airport-transfer-logic', 'AIRPORT TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Honeymoon', 'honeymoon', 'Private **chauffeur-driven sedan or luxury SUV** transfer arranged via your resort or private tour company.', 3557),
  ('petra', 12, 'airport-transfer-logic', 'AIRPORT TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Luxury', 'luxury', 'VIP chauffeured **premium vehicle transfer** with meet-and-assist service directly from Queen Alia International Airport or Aqaba.', 3558),
  ('petra', 12, 'airport-transfer-logic', 'AIRPORT TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Budget', 'budget', 'Take the **JETT Bus** from Amman (Abdali/7th Circle) or Aqaba directly to the Petra Visitor Center bus terminal, or catch a local morning minibus from Amman''s South Bus Station. reason: Petra is located in Wadi Musa in southern Jordan, ~230 km from Amman (~3 hours drive) and ~125 km from Aqaba (~2 hours drive). Direct highway roads (Desert Highway or Kings'' Highway) connect the gateways, making private vehicles, rental cars, or JETT tourist buses the primary modes of arrival.', 3559),
  ('petra', 18, 'family-travel', 'FAMILY TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'child_friendly_score: **84** best_ages: Rules: Prefer: Avoid:', 3560),
  ('petra', 19, 'honeymoon-travel', 'HONEYMOON TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'honeymoon_score: **91** romance_score: **89** privacy_score: **88** luxury_score: **88** Recommended: **Honeymoon itinerary should NOT contain more than:** **2 major trail climbs per day.** Prefer: **Scenic cliffside viewpoints + private guide + relaxed resort recovery** over: **rushed multi-trail marathons under hot midday sun.**', 3561),
  ('petra', 20, 'luxury-travel', 'LUXURY TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'luxury_score: **88** Recommended: Luxury here primarily means: rather than:', 3562),
  ('petra', 21, 'adventure', 'ADVENTURE', NULL, NULL, 'adventure_score: **96** Petra is one of the world''s premier **archaeological and desert wilderness trekking destinations**, offering miles of carved stone trails, canyon gorges, and mountain summit paths. Top experiences:', 3563),
  ('petra', 22, 'senior-travel', 'SENIOR TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'senior_suitability: **79** walking_intensity: **MEDIUM → HIGH** Rules: Prefer: Avoid:', 3564),
  ('petra', 23, 'accessibility', 'ACCESSIBILITY', NULL, NULL, 'wheelchair_accessibility: LIMITED: public_transport_accessibility: **LOW → MODERATE** hotel_accessibility: VERIFY_PER_HOTEL: attraction_accessibility: VERIFY_PER_ATTRACTION: Rule: The Petra Visitor Center, Petra Museum, and paved paths through the Siq support electric golf carts and wheelchair accessibility, but **ancient ruins, backcountry trails, loose sand, and steep mountain stone staircases present severe physical barriers**.', 3565),
  ('petra', 24, 'food', 'FOOD', NULL, NULL, 'Wadi Musa and Petra offer authentic **Jordanian and Bedouin culinary experiences**, ranging from roadside falafel stands to lavish desert zarb feasts cooked in underground earth ovens. Strong categories: Food experiences: Budget: Local falafel sandwiches, shawarma, and bakery flatbreads (1–4 JOD). Premium: Resort buffet dinners and traditional Bedouin zarb banquets (15–30+ JOD).', 3566),
  ('petra', 25, 'shopping', 'SHOPPING', NULL, NULL, 'shopping_score: **78** Strong categories: Prefer: Shopping strength: MEDIUM: Petra excels in **traditional Bedouin artisan crafts, stone carvings, and authentic Jordanian keepsakes** rather than modern commercial retail malls.', 3567),
  ('petra', 26, 'nightlife', 'NIGHTLIFE', NULL, NULL, 'nightlife_level: **65** Petra features a **quiet, atmospheric evening environment** centered around cultural night tours, hotel cave bars, and traditional Bedouin tea circles under the stars. Suitable for: Night experiences: Best for: **Candlelit cultural walks, stargazing, and atmospheric cave bar drinks** rather than: **Late-night dance clubs or party street strips.**', 3568),
  ('petra', 28, 'sample-itinerary-patterns', 'SAMPLE ITINERARY PATTERNS', 'HALF-DAY – AMMAN CITADEL & ANCIENT DOWNTOWN', NULL, 'Morning / Afternoon Pickup from your hotel in Amman → Begin at the hilltop **Amman Citadel**, exploring the majestic Temple of Hercules, Umayyad Palace, and panoramic city lookouts → Drive down to the historic **Roman Theater**, a magnificently preserved 2nd-century 6,000-seat amphitheater → Stroll through the bustling **Downtown Al-Balad Souks** to experience traditional spice, textile, and gold markets → Stop at legendary local eateries for authentic **falafel at Hashem** and hot **knafeh at Habibah Sweets** → Return to your hotel or enjoy a traditional cardamom coffee on Rainbow Street', 3569),
  ('petra', 28, 'sample-itinerary-patterns', 'SAMPLE ITINERARY PATTERNS', '1 DAY – ANCIENT CITADEL, ROMAN HERITAGE & RAINBOW STREET', NULL, 'Morning Morning pickup from your hotel for Amman''s primary historic circuit → Explore the hilltop **Amman Citadel** and visit the Jordan Archaeological Museum → Descend into Downtown to tour the **Roman Theater** and adjacent Museum of Popular Traditions Afternoon Continue to **The Jordan Museum** in Ras Al-Ein to view the ancient ''Ain Ghazal statues and historic Dead Sea Scrolls exhibits → Walk up to historic **Rainbow Street in Jabal Amman** for lunch at a traditional Levantine restaurant Evening Explore the boutique shops, art galleries, and stone-architecture alleyways along Rainbow Street → Enjoy sunset views across the seven hills from a hilltop rooftop lounge → Finish with a traditional Jordanian dinner featuring **Mansaf, fresh mezze, and mint lemonade**', 3570),
  ('petra', 28, 'sample-itinerary-patterns', 'SAMPLE ITINERARY PATTERNS', '2 DAYS – AMMAN HIGHLIGHTS & GRECO-ROMAN JERASH CIRCUIT', NULL, 'Day 1 Full-day exploration of Amman''s top urban and historical attractions → Begin at **Amman Citadel**, then continue to the **Roman Theater** and **Downtown Al-Balad Souks** → Tour **The Jordan Museum** before heading to **Jabal Weibdeh** for arts, culture, and bohemian cafes → Spend the evening on **Rainbow Street** with dinner at a historic courtyard villa Day 2 Morning departure for **Jerash**, located 45 minutes north of Amman → Explore the vast Greco-Roman ancient city, including Hadrian''s Arch, the Oval Plaza, the Colonnaded Street, and the Temple of Artemis → Continue to **Ajloun Castle**, a 12th-century Ayyubid fortress offering hilltop views over the Jordan Valley → Return to Amman for dinner and evening leisure', 3571),
  ('petra', 29, '6-days-and-5-nights-honeymoon-itinerary', '6 DAYS & 5 NIGHTS HONEYMOON ITINERARY', 'DAY 1 – ROMANTIC ARRIVAL & HILLTOP SKYLINE VIEWS', 'honeymoon', 'Morning / Afternoon Arrive at **Queen Alia International Airport (AMM)** → Meet your private chauffeur and transfer to your romantic 5-star hotel in Amman → Complete check-in and unwind in your suite Lunch Enjoy a relaxed Levantine lunch in a quiet historic courtyard Evening Take a private evening drive through the historic neighborhood of **Jabal Amman** → Walk along **Rainbow Street** for couple''s photography against classic stone architecture → Enjoy a romantic welcome dinner on a panoramic rooftop terrace overlooking the lit-up Citadel', 3572),
  ('petra', 29, '6-days-and-5-nights-honeymoon-itinerary', '6 DAYS & 5 NIGHTS HONEYMOON ITINERARY', 'DAY 2 – CITADEL SUNSET & ARTS DISTRICT STROLL', NULL, 'Morning After breakfast, depart for a private guided visit to the **Amman Citadel** → Explore ancient Roman columns, the Umayyad Palace, and 360-degree views of the capital → Descend to tour the majestic 2nd-century **Roman Theater** Afternoon Enjoy lunch in the creative neighborhood of **Jabal Weibdeh** → Stroll through peaceful art galleries at **Darat Al Funun** and small craft boutiques → Return to the hotel for couple''s relaxation or a private spa treatment Evening Drive to a vantage point for sunset photos over Amman''s hills → Enjoy a fine-dining Levantine meal in a restored historic villa', 3573),
  ('petra', 29, '6-days-and-5-nights-honeymoon-itinerary', '6 DAYS & 5 NIGHTS HONEYMOON ITINERARY', 'DAY 3 – ANCIENT JERASH & AJLOUN FOREST ESCAPE', NULL, 'Morning Depart with your private chauffeur for the ancient city of **Jerash** → Walk hand-in-hand down the grand Colonnaded Street, Oval Plaza, and ancient theaters Lunch Enjoy a traditional Middle Eastern feast featuring fresh mezze and grilled delicacies Afternoon Drive through green pine forests to **Ajloun Castle** → Explore the historic hilltop fortress and enjoy sweeping vistas across the northern valleys → Return to Amman in the late afternoon Evening Enjoy a quiet evening at your hotel or a cozy shisha lounge', 3574),
  ('petra', 29, '6-days-and-5-nights-honeymoon-itinerary', '6 DAYS & 5 NIGHTS HONEYMOON ITINERARY', 'DAY 4 – SACRED MOSAICS, MOUNT NEBO & DEAD SEA FLOAT', NULL, 'Morning Checkout of Amman and drive south to **Madaba** → Visit St. George''s Church to admire the famous 6th-century Mosaic Map of the Holy Land → Continue to **Mount Nebo** for breathtaking views overlooking the Jordan Valley and Dead Sea Lunch Enjoy lunch at a hilltop restaurant en route Afternoon Arrive at your luxury **Dead Sea Resort** → Experience floating weightlessly in the mineral-rich Dead Sea waters → Indulge in a natural Dead Sea mud bath and couple''s spa session Evening Watch the sunset over the Dead Sea waters followed by a candlelit beachside dinner', 3575),
  ('petra', 29, '6-days-and-5-nights-honeymoon-itinerary', '6 DAYS & 5 NIGHTS HONEYMOON ITINERARY', 'DAY 5 – HOLY BAPTISM SITE & ROMANTIC RESORT RELAXATION', 'honeymoon', 'Morning Visit the **Baptism Site of Jesus Christ (Bethany Beyond the Jordan)** → Take a peaceful guided tour through this historic UNESCO World Heritage sanctuary along the Jordan River Lunch Return to your Dead Sea resort for a relaxing poolside lunch Afternoon Enjoy resort leisure, private beach access, infinity pool floating, and wellness treatments Evening Celebrate your final night with an exclusive private beachfront dinner under the stars', 3576),
  ('petra', 29, '6-days-and-5-nights-honeymoon-itinerary', '6 DAYS & 5 NIGHTS HONEYMOON ITINERARY', 'DAY 6 – LEISURE BREAKFAST & DEPARTURE', NULL, 'Morning Enjoy a slow breakfast overlooking the Dead Sea → Complete checkout and meet your private chauffeur Late Morning / Afternoon Transfer to **Queen Alia International Airport (AMM)** for your departure flight → Depart Jordan with unforgettable memories of ancient history and romantic landscapes', 3577),
  ('petra', 30, '6-days-and-5-nights-family-itinerary', '6 DAYS & 5 NIGHTS FAMILY ITINERARY', 'DAY 1 – FAMILY ARRIVAL & DOWNTOWN INTRODUCTION', 'family', 'Morning / Afternoon Arrive at **Queen Alia International Airport (AMM)** → Meet your private family vehicle and transfer to your Amman hotel → Complete check-in and take time to unpack and relax Evening Head Downtown to **Al-Balad** for an easy family stroll → Stop at Hashem Restaurant for child-friendly falafel, hummus, and fresh bread → Try famous warm knafeh at Habibah Sweets → Return to the hotel for early family rest', 3578),
  ('petra', 30, '6-days-and-5-nights-family-itinerary', '6 DAYS & 5 NIGHTS FAMILY ITINERARY', 'DAY 2 – CITADEL, ROMAN THEATER & CAR MUSEUM', NULL, 'Morning Visit the **Amman Citadel** after breakfast → Kids can explore the massive ancient stone hand of Hercules and open-air ruins → Continue down to the **Roman Theater** and let children test the acoustic echoes on stage Lunch Enjoy a family-friendly lunch in central Amman Afternoon Visit the **Royal Automobile Museum** in King Hussein Park → Explore King Hussein''s vast collection of vintage sports cars, royal vehicles, and motorcycles → Optional stop at the adjacent **Children''s Museum Jordan** for interactive exhibits Evening Return to the hotel for dinner and rest', 3579),
  ('petra', 30, '6-days-and-5-nights-family-itinerary', '6 DAYS & 5 NIGHTS FAMILY ITINERARY', 'DAY 3 – GRECO-ROMAN JERASH & AJLOUN CASTLE', NULL, 'Morning Take a day trip north to **Jerash** → Explore the massive ancient Roman plaza, arches, and temples with an engaging guide Lunch Enjoy lunch at an outdoor garden restaurant with fresh flatbreads and grilled meats Afternoon Drive to **Ajloun Castle** → Kids can explore stone towers, passageways, and drawbridges in this medieval Islamic fortress Evening Return to Amman for a relaxed family dinner', 3580),
  ('petra', 30, '6-days-and-5-nights-family-itinerary', '6 DAYS & 5 NIGHTS FAMILY ITINERARY', 'DAY 4 – JORDAN MUSEUM & ABDALI BOULEVARD', NULL, 'Morning Visit **The Jordan Museum** in Ras Al-Ein → Discover interactive archaeological displays, ancient statues, and historical exhibits Lunch Enjoy lunch at a modern cafe on **The Boulevard in Abdali** Afternoon Walk through the pedestrian-friendly **Abdali Boulevard** and Abdali Mall for family shopping and treats Evening Enjoy a relaxed family dinner at Abdali before returning to your hotel', 3581),
  ('petra', 30, '6-days-and-5-nights-family-itinerary', '6 DAYS & 5 NIGHTS FAMILY ITINERARY', 'DAY 5 – MADABA MOSAICS & DEAD SEA FAMILY FLOAT', 'family', 'Morning Depart Amman for **Madaba** to see the ancient mosaic map at St. George''s Church → Continue to **Mount Nebo** to take in panoramic views of the valley below Lunch Enjoy a family lunch near Mount Nebo Afternoon Drive down to a day-use **Dead Sea Beach Resort** → Experience floating in the Dead Sea and playing in child-friendly resort pools Evening Enjoy a sunset dinner by the Dead Sea before returning to Amman for your final night', 3582),
  ('petra', 30, '6-days-and-5-nights-family-itinerary', '6 DAYS & 5 NIGHTS FAMILY ITINERARY', 'DAY 6 – RELAXED MORNING & DEPARTURE', NULL, 'Morning Enjoy breakfast at the hotel and complete checkout → Optional last-minute shopping for spices, sweets, or souvenirs in Downtown Late Morning / Afternoon Transfer by private family vehicle to **Queen Alia International Airport (AMM)** → Depart Amman for your onward journey', 3583),
  ('petra', 31, '6-days-and-5-nights-luxury-itinerary', '6 DAYS & 5 NIGHTS LUXURY ITINERARY', 'DAY 1 – VIP ARRIVAL & 5-STAR AMMAN RETREAT', NULL, 'Morning / Afternoon Arrive at **Queen Alia International Airport (AMM)** → Greeted by VIP airport meet-and-assist service and private luxury chauffeur transfer → Check into your flagship 5-star hotel (e.g., The St. Regis Amman, Four Seasons Hotel Amman, or The Ritz-Carlton) → Unwind in your suite with welcome refreshments Lunch Curated multi-course Middle Eastern lunch at your hotel Evening Private evening transfer to **Rainbow Street** in Jabal Amman → Private guided walk past historic stone mansions and boutique shops → Enjoy an exclusive fine-dining dinner at a premier Levantine restaurant like Sufra or Fakhr El-Din', 3584),
  ('petra', 31, '6-days-and-5-nights-luxury-itinerary', '6 DAYS & 5 NIGHTS LUXURY ITINERARY', 'DAY 2 – PRIVATE CITADEL & VIP ARCHAEOLOGY EXPERIENCE', NULL, 'Early Morning Meet your expert private historian guide for an early visit to the **Amman Citadel** → Enjoy exclusive insights into the Temple of Hercules and Umayyad Palace with minimal crowds → Private viewings at **The Jordan Museum** in Ras Al-Ein Lunch Refined regional tasting menu in Jabal Weibdeh Afternoon Private gallery access in **Jabal Weibdeh** and **Darat Al Funun** → Optional private shopping consultation for luxury Dead Sea cosmetics and fine gold crafts Evening Return to your hotel for spa treatments and relaxation → Sunset cocktails and fine dining at a luxury rooftop lounge', 3585),
  ('petra', 31, '6-days-and-5-nights-luxury-itinerary', '6 DAYS & 5 NIGHTS LUXURY ITINERARY', 'DAY 3 – EXCLUSIVE JERASH TOUR & AJLOUN PRIVATE ESCAPE', NULL, 'Morning Chauffeur-driven transfer to the ancient city of **Jerash** → Private guided tour through the Roman ruins, Oval Plaza, and ancient temples Lunch Exclusive private lunch arrangement at a top regional estate Afternoon Private transfer to **Ajloun Castle** for sweeping views over the northern hills → Return to Amman in luxury comfort Evening Gourmet dinner at an iconic Amman fine-dining venue', 3586),
  ('petra', 31, '6-days-and-5-nights-luxury-itinerary', '6 DAYS & 5 NIGHTS LUXURY ITINERARY', 'DAY 4 – MOUNT NEBO, BAPTISM SITE & DEAD SEA RESORT', NULL, 'Morning Private driver transfer to **Madaba** and **Mount Nebo** for private historical viewings → Continue down to the sacred **Baptism Site (Bethany Beyond the Jordan)** with a private guide Lunch Gourmet lunch overlooking the Jordan River valley Afternoon Arrive at your exclusive luxury 5-star resort on the **Dead Sea** (e.g., Kempinski Hotel Ishtar) → Private beach floating experience, mud treatments, and custom spa therapies Evening Watch the sunset over the water followed by a chef-curated private dinner', 3587),
  ('petra', 31, '6-days-and-5-nights-luxury-itinerary', '6 DAYS & 5 NIGHTS LUXURY ITINERARY', 'DAY 5 – DEAD SEA WELLNESS & BAPTISM SANCTUARY RELAXATION', NULL, 'Morning Leisurely luxury breakfast overlooking the Dead Sea → Full morning reserved for private wellness, infinity pool relaxation, and spa therapies Lunch Private poolside dining Afternoon Relax at your resort or enjoy an optional private helicopter tour over the Dead Sea and surrounding wadis Evening Celebrate your final evening with an exclusive candlelit beachside dinner experience', 3588),
  ('petra', 31, '6-days-and-5-nights-luxury-itinerary', '6 DAYS & 5 NIGHTS LUXURY ITINERARY', 'DAY 6 – ROYAL BREAKFAST & VIP DEPARTURE', NULL, 'Morning Enjoy a leisurely final breakfast at your luxury resort → Complete checkout and meet your dedicated chauffeur Late Morning / Afternoon Transfer in a premium vehicle directly to **Queen Alia International Airport (AMM)** → Depart Jordan following an exceptional blend of ancient history, luxury hospitality, private transfers, and fine dining', 3589),
  ('petra', 32, 'travel-agent-insights', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS', 'What inexperienced planners often do wrong', NULL, '', 3590),
  ('petra', 32, 'travel-agent-insights', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS', 'What an experienced planner does differently', NULL, '', 3591),
  ('petra', 32, 'travel-agent-insights', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS', 'Best planning rule', NULL, '', 3592),
  ('petra', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', NULL, NULL, 'IF: `trip_length <= 1 day` THEN: Walk through the shaded canyon of **The Siq**, emerge at **Al-Khazneh (The Treasury)**, explore the monumental **Royal Tombs**, walk the ancient **Colonnaded Street**, and visit the air-conditioned **Petra Museum**. Reason: A single day requires focusing strictly on Petra''s core archaeological axis and iconic rock-cut monuments without undertaking exhausting multi-hour mountain stair climbs. IF: `trip_length == 3 days` THEN: Dedicate Day 1 to the Main Trail featuring **The Siq**, **Al-Khazneh**, **Royal Tombs**, and **Colonnaded Street**; reserve Day 2 for ascending the 800 steps to **Ad Deir (The Monastery)** and exploring **Little Petra (Siq al-Barid)**; and spend Day 3 hiking to the **High Place of Sacrifice** or the **Al-Khubtha Treasury Viewpoint** before experiencing **Petra by Night**. Reason: A 3-day window allows travelers to thoroughly explore both the main valley floor and the dramatic high-elevation mountain viewpoints without physical burnout. IF: `trip_length >= 5 days` THEN: Cover the entire main Petra park and backcountry trails, undertake the full **Jordan Trail Backdoor Route** from **Little Petra to the Monastery**, trek remote summit peaks like **Umm al-Biyara**, and take regional day trips to the desert wilderness of **Wadi Rum** and the coastal waters of **Aqaba**. Reason: Extended stays enable a comprehensive southern Jordan exploration, combining deep archaeological discovery with desert wilderness trekking and Red Sea relaxation. IF: `trip_type == FIRST_TIME_VISITOR` THEN: Purchase a **Jordan Pass** prior to arrival, enter the site gate at 6:00 AM opening to walk through **The Siq** before crowds arrive, admire **Al-Khazneh**, explore the **Royal Tombs**, ascend to **Ad Deir (The Monastery)**, and visit the **Petra Museum**. Reason: First-time visitors experience Petra''s quintessential bucket-list monuments, world-famous sandstone views, and core historical narrative efficiently. IF: `trip_type == HONEYMOON` THEN: Stay at a luxury resort or desert bubble glamping dome, experience a candlelit evening walk during **Petra by Night**, take a private guided Backdoor Trail trek from **Little Petra to Ad Deir**, and enjoy a sunset Bedouin zarb dinner under the stars. Reason: Combining dramatic desert canyon landscapes, luxury glamping amenities, candlelit walks, and intimate sunset vistas creates an unforgettable romantic escape. IF: `traveler_type == FAMILY` THEN: Take a relaxed walk through **The Siq**, utilize authorized electric golf carts for younger children or grandparents, engage with interactive exhibits at the **Petra Museum**, enjoy short camel encounters along the **Colonnaded Street**, and relax with Bedouin storytelling in Wadi Musa. Reason: Utilizing mobility support through the canyon and balancing outdoor ruin walks with interactive, climate-controlled museum visits keeps the experience safe and manageable for all ages. IF: `traveler_type == LUXURY` THEN: Reserve 5-star accommodations adjacent to the main park gate, utilize private VIP transfers, hire a dedicated licensed expert archaeologist guide, arrange golf cart transport through **The Siq**, and enjoy private luxury Bedouin dining in a secluded desert canyon. Reason: Top-tier resort stays right at the gate eliminate travel hassle, while private guides and VIP transport ensure exclusive, comfortable access to ancient history. IF: `traveler_type == BUDGET` THEN: Purchase a multi-day **Jordan Pass** online to waive visa fees and cover entry, stay in budget guesthouses in upper **Wadi Musa Town Center**, pack water and snacks, eat local falafel and shawarma, and trek all main trails and Ad Deir steps on foot. Reason: Pre-bundled digital passes, affordable local town dining, and self-guided trail networks make Petra exceptionally accessible for budget travelers. IF: `traveler_interest == NATURE` THEN: Hike through the soaring sandstone walls of **The Siq**, explore the desert canyons of **Little Petra (Siq al-Barid)**, trek the high cliff paths of the **Al-Khubtha Trail**, and take scenic backcountry mountain routes overlooking the vast **Wadi Araba** basin. Reason: Petra is set within spectacular rose-red sandstone geology, providing a world-class sanctuary of desert canyons, mountain summits, and wild valley vistas. IF: `traveler_interest == FOOD` THEN: Feast on traditional underground Bedouin **Zarb** barbecue, taste Jordan''s national lamb dish **Mansaf**, take a local cooking class at **Petra Kitchen** in Wadi Musa, and enjoy sweet **Knafeh** and cardamom-infused tea at mountain tea stalls inside the site. Reason: Petra and Wadi Musa offer deep culinary traditions, highlighting ancient Bedouin earth-oven cooking methods and classic Levantine flavors. IF: `traveler_interest == ADVENTURE` THEN: Scramble up the ancient stone staircases to the **High Place of Sacrifice**, complete the backcountry **Jordan Trail trek** from Little Petra to the Monastery, climb the **Al-Khubtha cliff trail** to the high Treasury lookout, and tackle the remote summit trek of **Umm al-Biyara**. Reason: Petra boasts miles of challenging rock stairways, steep cliff paths, and wild backcountry desert routes perfect for high-stamina adventurers. IF: `traveler_type == SENIOR` THEN: Ride an authorized electric golf cart through **The Siq** to **Al-Khazneh**, stroll along flat sections of the **Colonnaded Street**, rest frequently at shaded canyon cafes, explore the accessible **Petra Museum**, and avoid unrailed mountain climbs. Reason: Leveraging golf cart assistance through the long canyon and sticking to flat central valley paths allows senior travelers to appreciate iconic monuments without physical strain. IF: `traveler_type == TRANSIT` THEN: If taking a dedicated 12 to 14-hour express trip from Queen Alia International Airport or Aqaba, hire a direct private driver to **Wadi Musa**, walk through **The Siq** to view **Al-Khazneh (The Treasury)**, have lunch along Tourism Street, and return immediately to your departure gateway. Reason: Petra''s distance from major airports requires dedicated high-speed highway transfers, allowing express travelers to see the iconic Treasury facade before departing. IF: `traveler_interest == SPIRITUALITY` THEN: Visit the sacred peak of the **High Place of Sacrifice**, explore early Christian heritage and intricate 5th-century floor mosaics at the **Byzantine Church**, and take a day excursion to nearby **Jabal Haroun (Aaron''s Mountain)**, the sacred burial site of the Prophet Aaron. Reason: Petra holds rich spiritual history spanning ancient Nabataean sacrificial altars, early Christian mosaic sanctuaries, and revered Islamic-Judeo mountain pilgrimage sites.', 3593),
  ('petra', 34, 'destination-scoring', 'DESTINATION SCORING', NULL, NULL, '| Factor | Score | | --- | --- | | Family | 84 | | Honeymoon | 91 | | Luxury | 88 | | Budget | 83 | | Adventure | 96 | | Culture | 97 | | Food | 82 | | Shopping | 78 | | Nightlife | 65 | | Relaxation | 76 | | Nature | 94 | | Accessibility | 68 | | Safety | 92 | | First-time visitor | 96 | | Photography | 97 |', 3594),
  ('petra', 35, 'final-travel-agent-verdict', 'FINAL TRAVEL AGENT VERDICT', NULL, NULL, 'Best for: Archaeology enthusiasts, history buffs, trekkers, adventure seekers, couples, photographers, and bucket-list travelers eager to explore one of the New 7 Wonders of the World—an ancient Nabataean city hand-carved into dramatic rose-red sandstone canyons and mountain cliffs. Best duration: 2 to 3 days for a thorough experience covering the main canyon axis, Al-Khazneh (The Treasury), the Royal Tombs, Ad Deir (The Monastery), and scenic high-altitude trails like the High Place of Sacrifice or Al-Khubtha viewpoint; extendable to 4 to 5 days when combining Petra with the desert wilderness of Wadi Rum and the Red Sea at Aqaba. Best season: March to May (spring) and September to November (autumn). Spring brings pleasant daytime temperatures and desert wildflowers; autumn offers clear skies and comfortable hiking weather. December to February brings cold desert temperatures, chilly winds, and occasional flash floods, while June to August sees intense mid-day heat exceeding 35°C (95°F) best tackled with dawn site entries. Best stay: Luxury resorts, boutique hotels, and comfortable 3- to 4-star properties located along **Tourism Street in lower Wadi Musa** for immediate walking access to the main Visitor Center gate; paired with desert bubble glamping domes or authentic Bedouin camps in nearby **Little Petra (Siq al-Barid)** for an atmospheric stargazing experience. Best transport: Pre-booked private chauffeured transfers, rental cars, or JETT tourist express buses from Amman or Aqaba to Wadi Musa; combined with self-guided or guided walking, hiking, and authorized electric golf cart transport for mobiity-assisted transit through the Siq. Must-do: Avoid: Biggest advantage: A world-class, awe-inspiring archaeological wonder that combines ancient engineering brilliance, rich Bedouin heritage, and vast mountain desert scenery into an unforgettable open-air trekking environment. Biggest disadvantage: High physical demand requiring extensive walking and climbing across steep rock terrain, compounded by exposed desert heat and persistent local vendors along the main trails. Overall destination score: **96/100**', 3595),
  ('petra', 36, 'data-quality', 'DATA QUALITY', NULL, NULL, 'information_completeness: 93/100 last_updated: 2026-09-05 last_verified: NOT_LIVE_VERIFIED verified_by: TRAVEL_ENGINE_INITIAL_DATASET sources: IMPORTANT: Prices, opening hours, schedules, visa requirements, availability, accessibility and operational conditions must NOT be treated as permanently valid from this document. These must be sourced from structured, refreshable data.', 3596),
  ('auckland', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Spring', NULL, 'months: September October November weather: Changeable but progressively warmer, with longer daylight and improving conditions for island trips, gardens, coastal walking and outdoor sightseeing. Rain and wind remain possible. crowd_level: LOW → MEDIUM price_level: MEDIUM overall_score: 80.00–89.00 recommended: true reason: Spring combines manageable visitor pressure with increasing daylight, flowering landscapes and improving outdoor conditions before the peak summer travel period. Best for:', 3597),
  ('auckland', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Summer', NULL, 'months: December January February weather: Warmest and generally most suitable period for beaches, islands, harbour cruises and outdoor recreation, although Auckland remains changeable and rainfall can occur at any time. crowd_level: HIGH price_level: HIGH overall_score: 73.33–79.33 recommended: true reason: Summer offers Auckland''s strongest beach, island and outdoor conditions, but peak holiday demand and accommodation pricing reduce overall value. Best for:', 3598),
  ('auckland', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Autumn', NULL, 'months: March April May weather: March often retains warm summer-like conditions, while April and May become cooler and progressively wetter. Early autumn is particularly strong for outdoor sightseeing and vineyards. crowd_level: MEDIUM → LOW price_level: MEDIUM overall_score: 78.67–89.00 recommended: true reason: Autumn provides an excellent balance of comfortable temperatures, lower visitor pressure and strong conditions for city sightseeing, islands, vineyards and walking. Best for:', 3599);
INSERT INTO destination_guidance (place_id, section, topic, section_title, heading, audience, body, position) VALUES
  ('auckland', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Winter', NULL, 'months: June July August weather: Cool, wetter and changeable, with shorter daylight and greater risk of rain and wind affecting island and coastal activities. Auckland winters remain relatively mild compared with colder inland New Zealand regions. crowd_level: LOW price_level: LOW → MEDIUM overall_score: 72.00–75.67 recommended: true_with_flexible_planning reason: Lower visitor pressure and generally better accommodation value help winter travel, while museums, dining and urban sightseeing remain strong despite reduced outdoor reliability. Best for:', 3600),
  ('auckland', 10, 'budget-strategy', 'BUDGET STRATEGY', NULL, NULL, 'Where money can be saved: Where saving money is usually NOT recommended: Travel-agent rule: In Auckland, **CENTRAL_OR_TRANSIT_CONNECTED_HOTEL + PUBLIC_TRANSPORT + WALKABLE_CBD + SELECTIVE_FERRY_EXCURSIONS + LIMITED_CAR_HIRE** generally provides the strongest value. For short stays, prioritize: **CBD_WATERFRONT + AUCKLAND_MUSEUM + MAUNGAWHAU + ONE_ISLAND_EXPERIENCE**. For longer stays, add: **WAIHEKE + RANGITOTO_OR_DEVONPORT + WEST_COAST + MISSION_BAY + MOTAT_ZOO + MAUNGAKIEKIE**. Operational note: Ferry fares, attraction tickets, tours, parking rates and accommodation pricing should be rechecked before travel.', 3601),
  ('auckland', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Family', 'family', 'Airport transfer by: PRE_BOOKED_PRIVATE_TRANSFER_OR_RIDESHARE + DIRECT_HOTEL_TRANSFER is generally simplest with children and substantial luggage. Public transport option: AIRPORTLINK_BUS + PUHINUI_STATION + TRAIN_OR_CONNECTING_TRANSIT for families comfortable with luggage transfers. Choose accommodation around Auckland CBD, Britomart, Viaduct Harbour, Wynyard Quarter or another well-connected neighbourhood according to itinerary and budget.', 3602),
  ('auckland', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Honeymoon', 'honeymoon', 'Prefer: PRIVATE_AIRPORT_TRANSFER + PREMIUM_WATERFRONT_OR_CITY_HOTEL + HARBOUR_AND_WAIHEKE_ACCESS for a more seamless arrival.', 3603),
  ('auckland', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Luxury', 'luxury', 'Use: AIRPORT_MEET_AND_GREET + CHAUFFEURED_PREMIUM_SEDAN_OR_SUV + FIVE_STAR_CITY_OR_WATERFRONT_HOTEL + PRIVATE_TOURING Optional premium extensions: PRIVATE_HELICOPTER + YACHT_CHARTER + WAIHEKE_LUXURY_EXPERIENCE.', 3604),
  ('auckland', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Budget', 'budget', 'Primary options: AirportLink connects Auckland Airport with Puhinui Station, where passengers can transfer to Auckland''s Southern and Eastern rail lines.', 3605),
  ('auckland', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Senior', 'senior', 'Prefer: DIRECT_AIRPORT_TRANSFER + CENTRAL_HOTEL + DOOR_TO_DOOR_VEHICLE_SUPPORT especially when luggage, limited mobility or early / late flights are involved.', 3606),
  ('auckland', 18, 'family-travel', 'FAMILY TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'child_friendly_score: 92 best_ages: Rules: For young children: Prefer: Avoid:', 3607),
  ('auckland', 19, 'honeymoon-travel', 'HONEYMOON TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'honeymoon_score: 91 romance_score: 92 privacy_score: 88 luxury_score: 92 Recommended: Honeymoon itineraries should generally stay at: 2–3 major experiences/day. Prefer: LUXURY_CITY_HOTEL + WAIHEKE + HARBOUR + PRIVATE_EXPERIENCE + DINING + FREE_TIME over: Continuous urban sightseeing and museum scheduling.', 3608),
  ('auckland', 20, 'luxury-travel', 'LUXURY TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'luxury_score: 92 Recommended: Auckland is particularly strong for: WATERFRONT_LUXURY + PRIVATE_ISLAND_EXPERIENCES + FINE_DINING + YACHTING + SCENIC_AVIATION + WAIHEKE_WINE_TRAVEL.', 3609),
  ('auckland', 21, 'adventure', 'ADVENTURE', NULL, NULL, 'adventure_score: 88 Auckland offers particularly strong soft-adventure variety because the city combines volcanic landscapes, islands, ocean environments and regional parks. Adventure experiences: Best regions: RANGITOTO + WAIHEKE + WAITAKERE + WEST_COAST + HAURAKI_GULF + AUCKLAND_VOLCANIC_FIELD Travel-agent positioning: Auckland should be treated as: VOLCANIC_HIKING + ISLAND_ADVENTURE + SAILING + COASTAL_ACTIVITY + SOFT_OUTDOOR_ADVENTURE rather than a dedicated alpine or extreme-sports destination.', 3610),
  ('auckland', 22, 'senior-travel', 'SENIOR TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'senior_suitability: 87 walking_intensity: LOW for waterfront areas, museums, central-city sightseeing, Cornwall Park and vehicle-supported itineraries. MEDIUM for Maungawhau, Devonport viewpoints, Waiheke excursions and some volcanic landscapes. MEDIUM–HIGH for Rangitoto summit walking and rugged west-coast trails. Rules: Auckland works well for seniors as a: HARBOUR + CULTURE + FOOD + MUSEUM + SCENIC_DRIVING + RELAXED_ISLAND destination when walking intensity is controlled.', 3611),
  ('auckland', 23, 'accessibility', 'ACCESSIBILITY', NULL, NULL, 'wheelchair_accessibility: HIGH IN MANY MODERN CENTRAL_CITY_AREAS, MAJOR_MUSEUMS, TRANSPORT_INTERCHANGES AND SELECTED_WATERFRONT_AREAS VARIABLE ACROSS VOLCANIC, ISLAND, BEACH AND NATURAL_TERRAIN public_transport_accessibility: MODERATE → HIGH hotel_accessibility: GENERALLY_HIGH_IN_MODERN_HOTELS_BUT_MUST_BE_VERIFIED attraction_accessibility: MUST_BE_VERIFIED_PER_ATTRACTION Rule: Do not assume every volcanic trail, island ferry, beach, historic building or regional-park route is fully step-free. Additional notes: Auckland accessibility should therefore be classified as: STRONG_URBAN_ACCESSIBILITY_WITH_NATURAL_TERRAIN_LIMITATIONS.', 3612),
  ('auckland', 24, 'food', 'FOOD', NULL, NULL, 'Auckland is particularly strong for: Food experiences: Family: Prioritize cafés, fish and chips, burgers, bakeries, Asian food, casual waterfront restaurants and flexible food-hall options. Honeymoon: Choose Waiheke vineyard dining, harbour-view restaurants, chef-led tasting menus and premium wine experiences. Luxury: Include private vineyard experiences, chef-led dining, premium seafood, luxury hotel restaurants and curated wine pairing. Budget: Use food courts, bakeries, ethnic restaurants, markets, takeaway shops and casual neighbourhood dining. Travel-agent rule: Position Auckland food around: NEW_ZEALAND_PRODUCE + MAORI_AND_PACIFIC_INFLUENCE + ASIAN_DIVERSITY + SEAFOOD + WAIHEKE_WINE + CONTEMPORARY_DINING.', 3613),
  ('auckland', 25, 'shopping', 'SHOPPING', NULL, NULL, 'Strong categories: Luxury shopping: Prefer: Local shopping: Prefer: Budget: Prefer: Travel-agent rule: Use: COMMERCIAL_BAY_AND_QUEEN_STREET for CENTRAL_CITY_RETAIL, NEWMARKET for PREMIUM_AND_DESIGNER_SHOPPING, PONSONBY for BOUTIQUES_AND_LOCAL_DESIGN, WAIHEKE_AND_MARKETS for ARTISAN_PRODUCTS.', 3614),
  ('auckland', 26, 'nightlife', 'NIGHTLIFE', NULL, NULL, 'nightlife_level: 89 Suitable for: Best areas: Evening activities: Auckland nightlife is strongest for: DINING + BARS + LIVE_MUSIC + WATERFRONT_EVENINGS + COCKTAILS + URBAN_SOCIAL_LIFE rather than: MEGA_CLUB_DESTINATION_TRAVEL. Couples should generally prefer: HARBOUR_SUNSET + DINNER + COCKTAIL_OR_WINE_BAR + RELAXED_WATERFRONT_WALK over: Overloaded late-night venue hopping.', 3615),
  ('auckland', 28, 'sample-itinerary-patterns', 'SAMPLE ITINERARY PATTERNS', '3 NIGHTS', NULL, '### Day 1 Arrival at Auckland Airport (AKL) → Airport bus / taxi / rideshare / private transfer to central Auckland hotel → Hotel check-in & relax after arrival Afternoon: → Begin at Auckland Waterfront → Explore Viaduct Harbour → Walk around Wynyard Quarter → Continue towards the central waterfront & harbour precinct → Explore Queen Street / Commercial Bay according to available time Evening: → Visit Sky Tower for panoramic Auckland views → Waterfront sunset experience → Welcome dinner around Viaduct Harbour → Hotel AKL is New Zealand''s principal international aviation gateway and provides convenient domestic flight connections throughout the country, including Christchurch. Auckland also serves as a practical starting point for road excursions towards Rotorua and the geothermal landscapes of the central North Island. ### Day 2 Morning: Breakfast → Explore Auckland''s city highlights → Visit Mount Eden / Maungawhau for panoramic city views → Continue towards Auckland Domain → Explore the surrounding parklands → Visit Auckland War Memorial Museum according to interest Afternoon: → Travel towards Mission Bay → Relax along the waterfront → Enjoy views across the Waitematā Harbour → Return towards central Auckland Evening: → Explore Britomart & Viaduct Harbour → Harbourfront dinner → Optional Auckland Harbour sailing / sunset cruise → Hotel Optional alternative instead of Auckland city sightseeing: WAIHEKE_ISLAND: → Ferry from downtown Auckland → Island landscapes → Beaches & coastal viewpoints → Vineyard / culinary experience → Return by ferry to Auckland WAITOMO: → Day excursion south of Auckland → Waitomo Glowworm Caves → Underground cave landscapes → Countryside sightseeing → Return to Auckland ### Day 3 Recommended first-time option: Early Breakfast → Depart Auckland for Rotorua → Travel through the Waikato countryside → Arrive in Rotorua → Explore a major geothermal reserve → See geothermal pools, steaming landscapes & geyser activity Afternoon: → Māori cultural experience → Learn about traditional Māori arts, culture & heritage → Explore Rotorua lakefront → Optional Redwoods / Whakarewarewa Forest experience Evening: → Māori cultural performance & traditional dining experience according to selected programme → Return to Auckland OR overnight Rotorua according to departure arrangements Optional alternative instead of Rotorua: CHRISTCHURCH: → Early domestic flight Auckland (AKL) to Christchurch (CHC) → Christchurch Botanic Gardens → Avon River precinct → Riverside Market → Central Christchurch → Transitional / contemporary city architecture → Overnight Christchurch with onward departure from CHC HOBBITON_AND_ROTORUA: → Travel from Auckland towards Matamata → Hobbiton Movie Set experience → Continue to Rotorua → Geothermal landscapes → Māori cultural experience → Return / overnight according to routing NATURE: → Waiheke Island → Auckland volcanic viewpoints → Waitākere landscapes according to access → Rotorua geothermal attractions → Redwoods / Whakarewarewa Forest FAMILY: → Auckland Museum → Sky Tower → Rotorua geothermal experience → Māori cultural activities → Redwoods forest experience HONEYMOON: → Waiheke Island vineyard experience → Auckland Harbour sunset → Rotorua spa / geothermal wellness → Couple photography → Romantic waterfront dinner LUXURY: → Private Auckland sightseeing → Premium Waiheke Island experience → Private chauffeured Rotorua excursion → Luxury geothermal spa experience → Fine dining FOOD: → Auckland waterfront dining → New Zealand seafood → Waiheke vineyard cuisine → Māori-inspired dining experience → Rotorua regional dining For only 3 nights, prioritize: AUCKLAND_WATERFRONT_AND_CITY + AUCKLAND_VOLCANIC_AND_HARBOUR_HIGHLIGHTS + ROTORUA_GEOTHERMAL_AND_MAORI_CULTURE OR AUCKLAND_CITY_AND_WAIHEKE + ROTORUA_OR_HOBBITON + CHRISTCHURCH_AS_AN_ONWARD_EXTENSION rather than trying to fully cover Auckland, Rotorua and Christchurch within the same short stay. ### Day 4 Breakfast → Leisurely morning around Auckland waterfront / local cafés → Final shopping around Queen Street / Commercial Bay → Hotel checkout → Taxi, rideshare, airport bus, or private transfer to Auckland Airport (AKL) → Departure', 3616),
  ('auckland', 29, 'six-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 1', NULL, 'Arrival at Auckland Airport (AKL) → Private airport transfer → Romantic Auckland hotel check-in → Relax and refresh Afternoon: → Viaduct Harbour → Wynyard Quarter → Auckland Waterfront → Couple photography Evening: → Sky Tower → Waterfront sunset → Romantic harbourfront dinner → Overnight at Auckland', 3617),
  ('auckland', 29, 'six-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 2', NULL, 'Breakfast → Auckland city & coastal experience Morning: → Mount Eden / Maungawhau → Auckland Domain → Mission Bay → Scenic harbour viewpoints Afternoon: → Britomart → Commercial Bay → Leisure / shopping Evening: → Sunset harbour cruise / sailing experience → Romantic dinner → Overnight at Auckland', 3618),
  ('auckland', 29, 'six-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 3', NULL, 'Breakfast → Ferry excursion to Waiheke Island → Scenic island landscapes → Vineyard experience → Wine tasting → Coastal viewpoints → Beach leisure → Couple photography Evening: → Return by ferry to Auckland → Romantic waterfront evening → Overnight at Auckland', 3619),
  ('auckland', 29, 'six-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 4', NULL, 'Breakfast → Hotel checkout → Private transfer / scenic drive to Rotorua Optional en route: → Hobbiton Movie Set Afternoon: → Rotorua hotel / resort check-in → Geothermal landscapes → Rotorua lakefront Evening: → Māori cultural experience → Traditional dining / cultural performance → Overnight at Rotorua', 3620),
  ('auckland', 29, 'six-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 5', NULL, 'Breakfast → Rotorua nature & wellness experience Morning: → Geothermal reserve → Geysers & thermal pools → Māori arts & heritage Afternoon: → Redwoods / Whakarewarewa Forest → Couple photography → Geothermal spa / wellness experience Evening: → Romantic dinner → Overnight at Rotorua', 3621),
  ('auckland', 29, 'six-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 6', NULL, 'Breakfast → Transfer to Rotorua Airport / Auckland Airport according to flight routing → Domestic flight to Christchurch → Romantic Christchurch hotel check-in Afternoon: → Christchurch Botanic Gardens → Avon River precinct → Central Christchurch → Riverside Market Evening: → Relaxed city walk → Farewell romantic dinner → Overnight at Christchurch', 3622),
  ('auckland', 29, 'six-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 7', NULL, 'Breakfast → Leisure morning → Hotel checkout → Private transfer to Christchurch Airport (CHC) → Departure / onward journey', 3623),
  ('auckland', 30, 'six-nights-family-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 1', NULL, 'Arrival at Auckland Airport (AKL) → Airport transfer → Family hotel check-in → Relax and refresh Afternoon: → Auckland Waterfront → Viaduct Harbour → Wynyard Quarter → Family photography Evening: → Sky Tower → Waterfront exploration → Family dinner → Overnight at Auckland', 3624),
  ('auckland', 30, 'six-nights-family-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 2', NULL, 'Breakfast → Auckland family sightseeing Morning: → Mount Eden / Maungawhau → Auckland Domain → Auckland Museum Afternoon: → Mission Bay → Beachfront leisure → Family recreation Evening: → Britomart / waterfront → Family dinner → Overnight at Auckland', 3625),
  ('auckland', 30, 'six-nights-family-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 3', NULL, 'Breakfast Choose ONE: WAIHEKE_ISLAND → Ferry experience → Beaches → Scenic island exploration → Family-friendly activities FAMILY_FUN → Auckland Zoo → MOTAT → Parks & recreational activities → Waterfront leisure NATURE → Auckland volcanic landscapes → Coastal viewpoints → Nature walks → Harbour experience Evening: → Return to central Auckland → Overnight at Auckland', 3626),
  ('auckland', 30, 'six-nights-family-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 4', NULL, 'Breakfast → Hotel checkout → Road transfer towards Rotorua Optional en route: → Hobbiton Movie Set Afternoon: → Rotorua hotel check-in → Geothermal attraction → Geysers & thermal landscapes Evening: → Māori cultural experience → Family cultural dinner → Overnight at Rotorua', 3627),
  ('auckland', 30, 'six-nights-family-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 5', NULL, 'Breakfast → Rotorua family exploration Morning: → Geothermal reserve → Māori cultural heritage → Interactive nature experiences Afternoon: → Redwoods / Whakarewarewa Forest → Rotorua lakefront → Family leisure Evening: → Relaxed family dinner → Overnight at Rotorua', 3628),
  ('auckland', 30, 'six-nights-family-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 6', NULL, 'Breakfast → Hotel checkout → Transfer for domestic flight to Christchurch → Christchurch family hotel check-in Afternoon: → Christchurch Botanic Gardens → Avon River → Central city → Riverside Market Evening: → Family city exploration → Farewell dinner → Overnight at Christchurch', 3629),
  ('auckland', 30, 'six-nights-family-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 7', NULL, 'Breakfast → Leisure morning → Hotel checkout → Transfer to Christchurch Airport (CHC) → Departure / onward journey', 3630),
  ('auckland', 31, 'six-nights-luxury-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 1', NULL, 'Arrival at Auckland Airport (AKL) → Private luxury airport transfer → Premium waterfront hotel check-in → Relax and refresh Afternoon: → Chauffeured Auckland orientation → Viaduct Harbour → Wynyard Quarter → Premium waterfront experience Evening: → Sky Tower / panoramic city experience → Fine-dining waterfront dinner → Overnight at Auckland', 3631),
  ('auckland', 31, 'six-nights-luxury-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 2', NULL, 'Breakfast → Private Auckland sightseeing Morning: → Mount Eden / Maungawhau → Auckland Domain → Premium city & harbour viewpoints Afternoon: → Mission Bay → Private shopping / leisure → Luxury hotel spa Evening: → Private harbour sailing experience → Fine dining → Overnight at Auckland', 3632),
  ('auckland', 31, 'six-nights-luxury-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 3', NULL, 'Breakfast → Premium Waiheke Island excursion → Private / premium ferry or boat transfer → Curated vineyard experience → Premium wine tasting → Gourmet vineyard lunch → Scenic coastal exploration Afternoon: → Beach / estate leisure → Private island photography Evening: → Return to Auckland → Premium waterfront dining → Overnight at Auckland', 3633),
  ('auckland', 31, 'six-nights-luxury-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 4', NULL, 'Breakfast → Hotel checkout → Private chauffeured transfer towards Rotorua Optional en route: → Private / premium Hobbiton Movie Set experience Afternoon: → Luxury Rotorua resort check-in → Private geothermal exploration → Lakefront scenery Evening: → Premium Māori cultural experience → Curated regional dinner → Overnight at Rotorua', 3634),
  ('auckland', 31, 'six-nights-luxury-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 5', NULL, 'Breakfast → Private Rotorua nature & cultural experience Morning: → Premium geothermal reserve tour → Geysers & thermal landscapes → Māori arts & heritage Afternoon: → Private Redwoods experience → Luxury geothermal spa → Wellness treatment Evening: → Fine dining / private resort dinner → Overnight at Rotorua', 3635),
  ('auckland', 31, 'six-nights-luxury-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 6', NULL, 'Breakfast → Private transfer for domestic flight to Christchurch → Premium airport transfer → Luxury Christchurch hotel check-in Afternoon: → Private Christchurch city experience → Christchurch Botanic Gardens → Avon River → Central city architecture → Premium shopping / leisure Evening: → Private scenic / premium city experience → Farewell New Zealand fine-dining dinner → Overnight at Christchurch', 3636),
  ('auckland', 31, 'six-nights-luxury-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 7', NULL, 'Breakfast → Luxury hotel leisure → Hotel checkout → Private transfer to Christchurch Airport (CHC) → Departure / onward journey', 3637),
  ('auckland', 32, 'travel-agent-insights', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS', 'What inexperienced planners often do wrong', NULL, '', 3638),
  ('auckland', 32, 'travel-agent-insights', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS', 'What an experienced planner does differently', NULL, 'For first-time visits, prioritize: AUCKLAND_WATERFRONT_CBD + AUCKLAND_MUSEUM + MAUNGAWHAU_MOUNT_EDEN + WAIHEKE_OR_RANGITOTO before maximum attraction coverage.', 3639),
  ('auckland', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', NULL, NULL, 'IF: trip_length <= 1 night THEN: prioritize_CBD_WATERFRONT + SKY_TOWER_OR_CITY_VIEW AND: choose_ONE_OF_AUCKLAND_MUSEUM_OR_MAUNGAWHAU Reason: A very short Auckland stay gains more value from concentrated city, harbour, cultural and volcanic sightseeing than from attempting a full offshore-island excursion. IF: trip_length == 2_OR_3_nights THEN: prioritize_CBD_WATERFRONT + AUCKLAND_MUSEUM + MAUNGAWHAU AND: retain_ONE_DAY_OR_HALF_DAY_FOR_WAIHEKE_OR_RANGITOTO_OR_DEVONPORT Reason: Two to three nights provide Auckland''s essential first-time combination of harbour city, Māori and Pacific culture, volcanic heritage and one major Gulf experience. IF: trip_length == 4_OR_5_nights THEN: add_WAIHEKE + RANGITOTO_OR_DEVONPORT + NEIGHBORHOOD_OR_BEACH_TIME Reason: Four to five nights provide the strongest balanced introduction to Auckland without forcing city, island and volcanic experiences into rushed combinations. IF: trip_length >= 6 nights THEN: add_WAITAKERE_WEST_COAST + MAUNGAKIEKIE + MISSION_BAY + PONSONBY_OR_K_ROAD Reason: Longer stays allow Auckland''s regional nature, neighbourhood culture, beaches and additional volcanic landscapes to complement the core city and island program. IF: trip_length >= 7 nights AND: traveler_interest == WIDER_NEW_ZEALAND THEN: consider_AUCKLAND_BASE + ONE_SECONDARY_NORTH_ISLAND_REGION AND: avoid_REPEATED_EXTREME_DISTANCE_DAY_TRIPS_FROM_AUCKLAND Reason: Auckland is an excellent national gateway, but repeatedly returning to the city after long-distance North Island excursions creates unnecessary road fatigue. IF: trip_type == HONEYMOON THEN: prefer_PREMIUM_WATERFRONT_HOTEL + WAIHEKE + HARBOUR_EXPERIENCE + FINE_DINING + FREE_TIME AND: add_PRIVATE_YACHT_OR_SCENIC_FLIGHT_IF_BUDGET_ALLOWS Reason: Auckland''s strongest honeymoon positioning combines harbour scenery, Waiheke''s vineyards and beaches, premium dining and private experiences rather than continuous urban sightseeing. IF: traveler_type == FAMILY THEN: prioritize_AUCKLAND_MUSEUM + ZOO_MOTAT + WATERFRONT + BEACH_OR_SHORT_FERRY AND: include_PARK_AND_FOOD_BREAKS Reason: Families benefit most from balancing interactive education, wildlife, transport experiences, parks and manageable outdoor sightseeing. IF: traveler_type == FAMILY_WITH_YOUNG_CHILDREN THEN: reduce_RANGITOTO_LONG_WALKS + MULTIPLE_VOLCANIC_SUMMITS + LONG_WAITAKERE_HIKES AND: increase_ZOO + MOTAT + WESTERN_SPRINGS + MISSION_BAY + DEVONPORT Reason: Rough lava, steep slopes, ferry timing and long regional walks can reduce comfort for younger children despite Auckland''s overall family friendliness. IF: traveler_type == LUXURY THEN: prefer_FIVE_STAR_WATERFRONT_HOTEL + CHAUFFEURED_TRANSFER + PRIVATE_WAIHEKE + PREMIUM_DINING AND: consider_YACHT_CHARTER + HELICOPTER + PRIVATE_WEST_COAST_TOUR Reason: Auckland''s luxury strength lies in waterfront accommodation, private island touring, scenic aviation, yachting, gastronomy and wine. IF: traveler_type == BUDGET THEN: prefer_TRANSIT_CONNECTED_VALUE_HOTEL + WALKING + BUS_TRAIN + FREE_VOLCANIC_SITES AND: limit_PRIVATE_TRANSFERS + PREMIUM_WAIHEKE_TOURS + EXCESSIVE_CAR_HIRE Reason: Free parks, maunga, public spaces and urban walking can reduce costs significantly, while ferry excursions and accommodation require selective budgeting. IF: traveler_interest == MAORI_CULTURE THEN: prioritize_AUCKLAND_MUSEUM + MAUNGAWHAU + MAUNGAKIEKIE + APPROPRIATE_CULTURAL_INTERPRETATION AND: use_TAMAKI_MAKAURAU_CONTEXT_NOT_GENERIC_NEW_ZEALAND_ONLY Reason: Auckland''s Māori identity is embedded in its ancestral maunga, settlement history, place names, museum collections and contemporary cultural life. IF: traveler_interest == AUCKLAND_MUSEUM THEN: allocate_APPROXIMATELY_2_TO_4_HOURS_BASED_ON_INTEREST AND: combine_WITH_AUCKLAND_DOMAIN + PARNELL Reason: Auckland Museum contains major Māori and Pacific collections as well as natural-history, military and social-history material, making it one of the city''s highest-value cultural attractions. IF: traveler_interest == AUCKLAND_MUSEUM THEN: verify_CURRENT_OPENING_HOURS + EXHIBITIONS + CULTURAL_PROGRAM_TIMES + ADMISSION Reason: Museum programming, paid experiences, temporary exhibitions and operating hours can change and should be reconfirmed before travel. IF: traveler_interest == MAUNGAWHAU THEN: allocate_APPROXIMATELY_1_5_TO_3_HOURS AND: include_VOLCANIC_INTERPRETATION + MAORI_HERITAGE + SUMMIT_VIEW Reason: Maungawhau is both a major volcanic viewpoint and a highly significant ancestral Māori pā landscape rather than merely a scenic hill. IF: traveler_interest == MAUNGAWHAU THEN: respect_DESIGNATED_PATHS + WAHI_TAPU + CURRENT_MAUNGA_RULES Reason: Tūpuna maunga are culturally significant ancestral landscapes and should be visited according to current protection and access requirements. IF: traveler_interest == MAUNGAKIEKIE THEN: combine_MAUNGAKIEKIE + CORNWALL_PARK AND: allow_TIME_FOR_WALKING + HERITAGE + VOLCANIC_VIEWS Reason: Maungakiekie / One Tree Hill and Cornwall Park combine an important Māori settlement landscape with major urban parkland and panoramic viewpoints. IF: traveler_interest == WAIHEKE THEN: allocate_FULL_DAY_FOR_STANDARD_FIRST_VISIT AND: combine_ONE_OR_MORE_OF_VINEYARDS + ONEROA + BEACH + FOOD + ART Reason: Waiheke lies approximately 40 minutes from downtown Auckland by passenger ferry but its principal attractions are spread across the island, making a full-day structure substantially stronger than a rushed turnaround. IF: traveler_interest == WAIHEKE THEN: plan_ISLAND_TRANSPORT_BEFORE_ARRIVAL AND: choose_BUS + TAXI + TOUR + PRIVATE_DRIVER_BASED_ON_ITINERARY Reason: Matiatia Wharf is the principal arrival point but vineyards, Onetangi, beaches and other attractions are distributed across the island. IF: traveler_interest == WAIHEKE_WINE THEN: prebook_VINEYARDS_AND_TRANSPORT_DURING_BUSY_PERIODS AND: avoid_SELF_DRIVING_AFTER_MULTIPLE_TASTINGS Reason: Waiheke''s wine experiences can experience high demand and responsible transport planning is essential when alcohol tasting forms part of the itinerary. IF: traveler_interest == WAIHEKE AND: season == SUMMER_OR_PUBLIC_HOLIDAY_PERIOD THEN: book_FERRY_AND_KEY_EXPERIENCES_EARLY_WHERE_AVAILABLE AND: allow_EXTRA_CAPACITY_AND_QUEUE_BUFFER Reason: Auckland Transport specifically notes limited Waiheke ferry capacity and recommends advance planning during busy periods. IF: traveler_interest == RANGITOTO THEN: allocate_HALF_DAY_TO_FULL_DAY AND: prioritize_SUMMIT_TRACK + VOLCANIC_LANDSCAPE + OPTIONAL_LAVA_CAVES Reason: Rangitoto is Auckland''s iconic volcanic island and the Summit Track alone requires meaningful walking time before optional extensions are added. IF: traveler_interest == RANGITOTO THEN: carry_FOOD + 1_TO_2_LITRES_WATER_PER_PERSON + SUN_PROTECTION + WATERPROOF_LAYER + STURDY_SHOES Reason: DOC advises visitors that food and drinking water are unavailable on Rangitoto and that rugged lava surfaces, exposed conditions and changeable weather require appropriate preparation. IF: traveler_interest == RANGITOTO_LAVA_CAVES THEN: carry_TORCH AND: use_STURDY_FOOTWEAR Reason: The lava-cave extension involves dark volcanic terrain and official visitor advice recommends carrying appropriate lighting and footwear. IF: traveler_interest == RANGITOTO THEN: verify_FERRY_TIMES_BEFORE_DEPARTURE AND: build_RETURN_FERRY_BUFFER_INTO_WALKING_PLAN Reason: The island depends primarily on scheduled ferry access for ordinary visitors, so missing the intended return sailing can materially disrupt the itinerary. IF: traveler_interest == RANGITOTO THEN: follow_PEST_FREE_ISLAND_BIOSECURITY_RULES AND: check_clean_seal_FOOTWEAR_AND_GEAR Reason: Rangitoto and Motutapu require strict biosecurity care to reduce the risk of introducing pests, soil, seeds and other threats to protected island ecosystems. IF: traveler_type == SENIOR AND: plan_includes_RANGITOTO THEN: assess_WALKING_ABILITY + LAVA_SURFACES + FERRY_ACCESS + WEATHER AND: consider_DEVONPORT_OR_WAIHEKE_SCENIC_PROGRAM_IF_UNSUITABLE Reason: Rangitoto''s rough volcanic surfaces and sustained walking make it substantially more physically demanding than Auckland''s lower-intensity ferry excursions. IF: traveler_uses_WHEELCHAIR AND: plan_includes_RANGITOTO_SUMMIT THEN: replace_WITH_ACCESSIBLE_HARBOUR_OR_CITY_EXPERIENCE_UNLESS_SPECIALIST_ACCESS_HAS_BEEN_CONFIRMED Reason: DOC identifies rugged terrain and no accessible toilets on the Summit Track, so ordinary Rangitoto hiking should not be assumed wheelchair suitable. IF: traveler_interest == DEVONPORT THEN: combine_DEVONPORT_VILLAGE + MAUNGAUIKA_NORTH_HEAD + TAKARUNGA_MOUNT_VICTORIA_BASED_ON_MOBILITY Reason: Devonport offers a compact mix of ferry travel, coastal heritage, Māori pā landscapes, military history and skyline viewpoints. IF: traveler_interest == EASY_FERRY_EXCURSION THEN: prioritize_DEVONPORT OVER: RANGITOTO_SUMMIT Reason: Devonport provides ferry scenery, shops, cafés and flexible walking without requiring the same level of outdoor preparation as Rangitoto. IF: traveler_interest == BEACHES THEN: choose_MISSION_BAY_OR_EASTERN_BAYS_FOR_EASY_URBAN_BEACH AND: choose_PIHA_OR_WEST_COAST_FOR_DRAMATIC_SURF_COAST Reason: Auckland''s east-coast urban beaches and rugged Tasman west coast deliver substantially different beach experiences and should not be positioned interchangeably. IF: traveler_interest == PIHA THEN: allocate_HALF_DAY_OR_FULL_DAY_WITH_WAITAKERE_CONTEXT AND: prefer_PRIVATE_CAR + RENTAL_CAR + GUIDED_TOUR_BASED_ON_TRAVELER_STYLE Reason: Piha lies roughly an hour from central Auckland and works best as part of a dedicated west-coast excursion rather than a quick urban stop. IF: traveler_interest == PIHA_SWIMMING THEN: check_CURRENT_SURF + PATROL + BEACH_SAFETY_CONDITIONS AND: swim_ONLY_WHERE_CURRENT_LOCAL_GUIDANCE_INDICATES_SAFE Reason: Piha is a powerful surf beach where conditions differ significantly from Auckland''s more sheltered urban beaches. IF: traveler_interest == LION_ROCK_SUMMIT THEN: do_NOT_SCHEDULE_SUMMIT_ACCESS AND: use_PIHA_BEACH + OPEN_VIEWPOINTS + CURRENTLY_OPEN_TRACKS Reason: As of the latest 2026 Auckland Council regional-parks update, the Lion Rock summit track remains closed because of instability and major storm damage. IF: traveler_interest == WAITAKERE_RANGES THEN: verify_CURRENT_TRACK_STATUS_BEFORE_DEPARTURE AND: use_ONLY_OPEN_AUTHORISED_TRACKS Reason: Although many tracks have reopened, Auckland Council continues to maintain closures and rehabilitation work across parts of the western regional-park network. IF: traveler_interest == WAITAKERE_RANGES THEN: clean_FOOTWEAR_AND_EQUIPMENT + USE_CLEANING_STATIONS + STAY_ON_TRACK Reason: Kauri dieback remains an important environmental threat, and official guidance requires visitors to minimise the movement of contaminated soil and respect protected-track systems. IF: traveler_interest == WAITAKERE_RANGES AND: weather == HEAVY_RAIN_OR_SEVERE_WEATHER THEN: recheck_TRACKS + ROAD_ACCESS + LANDSLIP_RISK AND: replace_WITH_CITY_CULTURE_IF_NEEDED Reason: Auckland''s western regional parks contain steep forest and coastal terrain that can be affected by slips, erosion and storm damage. IF: traveler_interest == NATURE THEN: prioritize_ONE_OF_RANGITOTO + WAITAKERE_WEST_COAST + MAUNGAKIEKIE + MAUNGAWHAU AND: choose_BASED_ON_PHYSICAL_INTENSITY + WEATHER + AVAILABLE_TIME Reason: Auckland offers multiple levels of nature experience ranging from accessible urban maunga and parks to volcanic-island hiking and rugged west-coast forest. IF: traveler_interest == EASY_NATURE THEN: prioritize_CORNWALL_PARK + MISSION_BAY + AUCKLAND_DOMAIN + WATERFRONT OVER: RANGITOTO_LONG_WALKS + RUGGED_WAITAKERE_TRACKS Reason: These city-based options provide landscape and recreation with substantially lower transport and physical demands. IF: traveler_interest == ADVENTURE THEN: consider_RANGITOTO_HIKING + WAIHEKE_ZIPLINING + KAYAKING + SAILING + WEST_COAST_SURFING + SKY_ACTIVITIES Reason: Auckland''s adventure strength comes from combining a major city with volcanoes, islands, harbour activities and surf-oriented coastal environments. IF: traveler_interest == PHOTOGRAPHY THEN: prioritize_MAUNGAWHAU_GOLDEN_HOUR + WATERFRONT_BLUE_HOUR + DEVONPORT_SKYLINE + WAIHEKE + WEST_COAST Reason: Auckland''s photographic strength comes from combining skyline, harbour, volcanoes, vineyards, islands and dramatic coastal landscapes. IF: traveler_interest == CITY_PHOTOGRAPHY THEN: combine_SKY_TOWER + VIADUCT_WYNYARD + BRITOMART + DEVONPORT_VIEWPOINT Reason: These locations provide contrasting elevated, waterfront, architectural and across-harbour perspectives of central Auckland. IF: traveler_interest == FOOD THEN: include_CONTEMPORARY_NEW_ZEALAND + MAORI_INFLUENCE + PACIFIC_CUISINE + ASIAN_DINING + SEAFOOD AND: retain_ONE_QUALITY_WAIHEKE_OR_CITY_RESTAURANT_EXPERIENCE Reason: Auckland''s multicultural population and access to New Zealand produce give it one of the country''s broadest restaurant and culinary inventories. IF: traveler_interest == WINE THEN: prioritize_WAIHEKE AND: consider_KUMEU_OR_MATAKANA_ONLY_WITH_ADDITIONAL_TIME_AND_REGIONAL_TRANSPORT Reason: Waiheke offers the most convenient major wine experience directly associated with a standard central-Auckland itinerary. IF: traveler_interest == SHOPPING THEN: combine_COMMERCIAL_BAY_QUEEN_STREET + NEWMARKET + PONSONBY_BASED_ON_STYLE Reason: Auckland''s shopping inventory ranges from central-city retail and luxury brands to independent boutiques and local design districts. IF: traveler_interest == LOCAL_LIFESTYLE THEN: prioritize_PONSONBY + K_ROAD + DEVONPORT + LOCAL_CAFES + NEIGHBORHOOD_DINING Reason: Auckland becomes substantially more interesting for repeat visitors when the itinerary moves beyond landmark sightseeing into neighbourhood culture and everyday urban life. IF: traveler_interest == NIGHTLIFE THEN: combine_VIADUCT_OR_BRITOMART_DINNER + PONSONBY_OR_K_ROAD_BARS + SAFE_LATE_TRANSPORT Reason: Auckland''s nightlife is strongest through restaurants, cocktail bars, live venues and urban social districts rather than a single concentrated resort-style entertainment zone. IF: traveler_interest == WATERFRONT THEN: prioritize_VIADUCT + WYNYARD + BRITOMART_QUAY_STREET AND: consider_HARBOUR_CRUISE_OR_DEVONPORT_FERRY Reason: Auckland''s identity is fundamentally linked to its harbours, marinas, ferry network and sailing culture. IF: traveler_interest == HARBOUR_CRUISE THEN: verify_CURRENT_DEPARTURE_TIME + WEATHER + OPERATOR_STATUS AND: do_NOT_GUARANTEE_WILDLIFE_SIGHTINGS_UNLESS_PRODUCT_SPECIFIC_TERMS_SUPPORT_IT Reason: Marine and wildlife experiences remain dependent on weather, operating conditions and natural animal movement. IF: traveler_interest == FAMILY_EDUCATION THEN: prioritize_AUCKLAND_MUSEUM + MOTAT + AUCKLAND_ZOO AND: combine_WITH_WESTERN_SPRINGS_OR_WATERFRONT_BREAKS Reason: These attractions provide Auckland''s strongest combination of culture, technology, aviation, wildlife and interactive family learning. IF: traveler_interest == MOTAT THEN: allocate_HALF_DAY_OR_COMBINE_WITH_AUCKLAND_ZOO_BASED_ON_ENERGY AND: verify_CURRENT_EXHIBITION_AND_SITE_ACCESS Reason: MOTAT occupies a significant family sightseeing block and should not be treated as a quick stop between distant Auckland attractions. IF: traveler_interest == FESTIVALS THEN: verify_CURRENT_EVENT_DATES + VENUE + TRANSPORT_CHANGES + HOTEL_DEMAND AND: reduce_NORMAL_SIGHTSEEING_DENSITY Reason: Major Auckland cultural and sporting events can significantly alter accommodation availability, road conditions and central-city visitor pressure. IF: travel_dates_overlap_MATARIKI THEN: check_CURRENT_MATARIKI_PROGRAM AND: include_APPROPRIATE_MAORI_CULTURAL_EVENT_IF_AVAILABLE Reason: Matariki is an important period of Māori cultural reflection and celebration, with event dates and programs varying by year. IF: travel_dates_overlap_PASIFIKA_OR_LANTERN_FESTIVAL THEN: verify_CURRENT_DATE_AND_VENUE AND: allow_EXTRA_CROWD_AND_TRANSPORT_TIME Reason: Auckland''s large cultural festivals can materially affect realistic travel times while adding high-value cultural experiences. IF: traveler_type == SENIOR THEN: prefer_CENTRAL_HOTEL + SHORT_CLUSTER_WALKS + TAXI_OR_RIDESHARE_SUPPORT AND: reduce_RANGITOTO_SUMMIT + MULTIPLE_MAUNGA_CLIMBS + RUGGED_WAITAKERE_TRAILS Reason: Auckland is senior-friendly at city level, but its volcanic and natural attractions can significantly increase physical intensity. IF: traveler_uses_WHEELCHAIR THEN: prefer_VERIFIED_ACCESSIBLE_HOTEL + ACCESSIBLE_AT_SERVICES + TAXI_OR_PRIVATE_TRANSPORT_WHEN_REQUIRED AND: verify_EACH_ISLAND + MAUNGA + VINEYARD + NATURAL_ATTRACTION_SEPARATELY Reason: Central Auckland and major institutions offer comparatively strong accessibility, while natural terrain and individual island facilities vary substantially. IF: traveler_uses_WHEELCHAIR AND: plan_includes_AUCKLAND_MUSEUM THEN: use_ACCESSIBLE_ENTRANCE_AND_MOBILITY_SERVICES Reason: Auckland Museum provides ramps at its principal entrances, disabled parking and complimentary wheelchairs for visitors requiring mobility support. IF: season == DECEMBER_TO_FEBRUARY THEN: increase_BEACHES + WAIHEKE + SAILING + RANGITOTO + OUTDOOR_DINING AND: book_PEAK_DEMAND_PRODUCTS_EARLIER Reason: Auckland summer provides the strongest warm-weather island and beach conditions, but Christmas, New Year and school-holiday periods increase demand. IF: season == MARCH_TO_MAY THEN: increase_WAIHEKE + WALKING + FOOD_AND_WINE + VOLCANIC_SIGHTSEEING AND: retain_LIGHT_RAIN_LAYER Reason: Autumn generally combines mild conditions with excellent food, vineyard and outdoor sightseeing opportunities. IF: season == JUNE_TO_AUGUST THEN: increase_AUCKLAND_MUSEUM + ART_GALLERY + MOTAT + FOOD + CULTURAL_EVENTS AND: retain_CLEAR_WEATHER_BLOCKS_FOR_MAUNGA_AND_WATERFRONT Reason: Winter is cooler, wetter and sometimes windy, but Auckland remains a strong cultural and gastronomy destination year-round. IF: season == SEPTEMBER_TO_NOVEMBER THEN: increase_ISLAND_TRIPS + COASTAL_WALKS + GARDENS + CYCLING + VOLCANIC_SIGHTSEEING AND: retain_WEATHER_FLEXIBILITY Reason: Spring brings longer daylight and increasingly mild conditions while remaining changeable enough to justify adaptable scheduling. IF: weather == NORMAL_SHOWERS THEN: retain_FLEXIBLE_AUCKLAND_PROGRAM AND: move_BETWEEN_INDOOR_AND_OUTDOOR_ATTRACTIONS_AS_CONDITIONS_CHANGE Reason: Auckland''s maritime climate can produce sunshine, cloud and showers within the same day, so ordinary rainfall does not automatically require cancelling sightseeing. IF: weather == HEAVY_CONTINUOUS_RAIN THEN: replace_LONG_VOLCANIC_WALKS + WAITAKERE_HIKING_WITH_AUCKLAND_MUSEUM + ART_GALLERY + MOTAT + SHOPPING + FOOD AND: use_ROAD_TRANSPORT_MORE_SELECTIVELY Reason: Auckland has sufficient museum, cultural, retail and culinary inventory to build a strong poor-weather itinerary. IF: weather == STRONG_WIND THEN: recheck_FERRY_OPERATIONS + HARBOUR_CRUISES + SKY_TOWER + EXPOSED_VIEWPOINTS Reason: Wind can materially affect marine services, exposed volcanic sites and elevated attractions even when rainfall is limited. IF: weather == SEVERE_WEATHER_WARNING THEN: suspend_NONESSENTIAL_ISLAND_TRIPS + EXPOSED_COASTAL_HIKES + REMOTE_REGIONAL_PARK_PROGRAMS AND: follow_METservice + AUCKLAND_EMERGENCY_AND_OPERATOR_GUIDANCE Reason: Severe rain and wind can affect ferries, roads, flooding, slips and coastal safety, so official emergency guidance should override normal tourism scheduling. IF: route == AUCKLAND_AIRPORT_TO_CBD AND: traveler_type == BUDGET_OR_INDEPENDENT THEN: consider_AIRPORTLINK_TO_PUHINUI + TRAIN_TO_CENTRAL_AUCKLAND Reason: AirportLink connects both airport terminals with Puhinui Station, providing an integrated public-transport route into Auckland''s wider rail network. IF: route == AUCKLAND_AIRPORT_TO_CBD AND: traveler_type == FAMILY_OR_LUXURY_OR_SENIOR THEN: prefer_DIRECT_COACH + TAXI + RIDESHARE + PREBOOKED_TRANSFER_BASED_ON_COMFORT Reason: Direct road transport avoids luggage transfers and can provide substantially simpler arrival logistics for families, premium travelers and mobility-limited visitors. IF: route == AUCKLAND_AIRPORT_TO_CBD THEN: allow_TRAFFIC_BUFFER AND: avoid_FIXED_MAJOR_ATTRACTION_IMMEDIATELY_AFTER_INTERNATIONAL_ARRIVAL Reason: Central Auckland is approximately 30_TO_35_MINUTES from the airport under favorable road conditions, but traffic and international-arrival processing can materially extend the total journey. IF: movement == CENTRAL_AUCKLAND THEN: prefer_WALKING + BUS + TRAIN AND: use_TAXI_OR_RIDESHARE_FOR_STEEP_OR_INCONVENIENT_CONNECTIONS Reason: Central Auckland''s waterfront and CBD are highly walkable in clusters, while public transport reduces unnecessary parking and traffic friction. IF: movement == DEVONPORT THEN: prefer_FERRY_FROM_DOWNTOWN Reason: The ferry provides both practical transport and one of Auckland''s simplest scenic harbour experiences. IF: movement == WAIHEKE THEN: verify_FERRY_OPERATOR + DEPARTURE_TIME + TICKET_TYPE + PAYMENT_METHOD Reason: Multiple Waiheke services operate and ticketing / contactless rules differ between operators. IF: movement == FULLERS360_WAIHEKE THEN: do_NOT_ASSUME_STANDARD_CONTACTLESS_BANK_CARD_TAGGING AND: use_VALID_FULLERS_TICKET_OR_SUPPORTED_AT_HOP_ARRANGEMENT Reason: Auckland Transport explicitly excludes Fullers360 Waiheke services from its general contactless-payment system. IF: movement == ISLAND_DIRECT_WAIHEKE THEN: AT_HOP_OR_SUPPORTED_CONTACTLESS_PAYMENT_CAN_BE_USED AND: consider_ADVANCE_BOOKING_DURING_BUSY_PERIODS Reason: Island Direct participates in supported AT HOP and contactless payment arrangements, but capacity remains limited. IF: movement == RANGITOTO_FERRY THEN: purchase_OPERATOR_APPROPRIATE_TICKET AND: do_NOT_ASSUME_AT_HOP_VALIDITY Reason: AT HOP is not valid on the standard Rangitoto tourist ferry service, which requires operator-specific ticketing. IF: movement == AUCKLAND_BUS THEN: use_AT_HOP_OR_SUPPORTED_CONTACTLESS_PAYMENT AND: tag_ON_AND_OFF_CORRECTLY Reason: Cash is not accepted for ordinary Auckland bus boarding and travelers should use one of the supported electronic payment methods. IF: movement == CONTACTLESS_PUBLIC_TRANSPORT THEN: use_ONE_PAYMENT_METHOD_PER_TRAVELER AND: use_THE_SAME_CARD_OR_DEVICE_FOR_TAG_ON_AND_TAG_OFF Reason: Auckland Transport requires correct individual tagging to calculate fares and does not allow one contactless bank card to function as a shared payment method for multiple passengers. IF: trip_length <= 3 nights THEN: avoid_RENTAL_CAR_FOR_CBD + DEVONPORT + STANDARD_FERRY_ITINERARY AND: use_WALKING + PUBLIC_TRANSPORT + SELECTIVE_RIDESHARE Reason: Parking, traffic and vehicle logistics generally provide limited value when a short Auckland itinerary is concentrated around central and ferry-accessible attractions. IF: trip_length >= 4 nights AND: traveler_interest == WAITAKERE_OR_MULTIPLE_REGIONAL_EXCURSIONS THEN: consider_RENTAL_CAR_OR_PRIVATE_TOUR_FOR_SELECTED_DAYS AND: avoid_PAYING_FOR_UNUSED_CITY_CAR_DAYS_IF_NOT_REQUIRED Reason: A vehicle becomes more useful when the itinerary moves into dispersed west-coast and regional destinations rather than central Auckland. IF: traveler_self_drives THEN: account_FOR_LEFT_SIDE_DRIVING + PARKING + TRAFFIC + WEATHER + CAR_SECURITY AND: avoid_LEAVING_VISIBLE_VALUABLES_IN_VEHICLE Reason: Self-driving expands Auckland''s regional flexibility but creates additional navigation, parking and normal vehicle-security responsibilities. IF: traveler_interest == FIRST_TIME_NEW_ZEALAND THEN: use_AUCKLAND_FOR_MAORI_CULTURE + HARBOUR + VOLCANIC_LANDSCAPE + FOOD + ISLAND_EXPERIENCE AND: continue_TO_OTHER_NEW_ZEALAND_REGIONS_IF_ALPINE_OR_GEOTHERMAL_OR_EXTENDED_WILDERNESS_TRAVEL_IS_REQUIRED Reason: Auckland provides an unusually broad introduction to contemporary New Zealand, but it should not be treated as a substitute for every landscape and experience elsewhere in the country. IF: traveler_interest == FIRST_TIME_AUCKLAND THEN: prioritize_AUCKLAND_WATERFRONT + AUCKLAND_MUSEUM + MAUNGAWHAU AND: add_WAIHEKE_OR_RANGITOTO_BASED_ON_TRAVEL_STYLE Reason: These experiences provide Auckland''s strongest first introduction to harbour identity, Māori and Pacific culture, volcanic heritage and the Hauraki Gulf.', 3640),
  ('auckland', 34, 'destination-scoring', 'DESTINATION SCORING', NULL, NULL, '| Factor | Score | | --- | --- | | Family | 92 | | Honeymoon | 91 | | Luxury | 92 | | Budget | 70 | | Adventure | 88 | | Culture | 93 | | Food | 95 | | Shopping | 91 | | Nightlife | 89 | | Relaxation | 91 | | Nature | 96 | | Accessibility | 86 | | Safety | 88 | | First-time visitor | 95 | | Photography | 97 |', 3641),
  ('auckland', 35, 'final-travel-agent-verdict', 'FINAL TRAVEL AGENT VERDICT', NULL, NULL, 'Best traveler profiles: 1. First-time New Zealand traveler (Auckland waterfront, Auckland Museum, Maungawhau / Mount Eden, Waiheke Island, Devonport, Māori and Pacific cultural context) 2. Nature / volcanic-landscape traveler (Rangitoto Island, Maungawhau, Maungakiekie / One Tree Hill, Waitākere Ranges, Piha, Hauraki Gulf) 3. Honeymoon / romantic traveler (Waiheke vineyards, waterfront hotels, harbour cruises, fine dining, Mission Bay, sunset viewpoints) 4. Culture / Māori heritage traveler (Auckland Museum, tūpuna maunga, Māori cultural interpretation, Auckland Art Gallery, Parnell, Matariki programming) 5. Food / wine traveler (Waiheke vineyards, contemporary New Zealand dining, Māori and Pacific influences, seafood, Asian cuisine, Ponsonby, Karangahape Road) 6. Family traveler (Auckland Museum, Auckland Zoo, MOTAT, Western Springs, Mission Bay, Devonport, waterfront recreation) 7. Adventure traveler (Rangitoto hiking, sailing, kayaking, west-coast surfing, Waiheke activities, volcanic walks, Sky Tower adventure experiences) 8. Photography traveler (Auckland skyline, Waitematā Harbour, Maungawhau, Rangitoto, Devonport, Waiheke, Piha and west-coast landscapes) 9. Luxury traveler (five-star waterfront hotels, private Waiheke touring, yacht charters, scenic aviation, chauffeur transfers, premium dining) 10. Independent / repeat traveler (Ponsonby, Karangahape Road, Maungakiekie, Devonport, Waitākere Ranges, regional parks, neighbourhood food and additional Gulf islands) Best duration: 4–5 nights 1–2 nights: Best for CBD_WATERFRONT + AUCKLAND_MUSEUM + MAUNGAWHAU with either DEVONPORT or one concentrated harbour experience. 3–4 nights: Best for BALANCED_FIRST_VISIT, adding Waiheke Island or Rangitoto, Auckland Museum, waterfront dining, volcanic heritage and one neighbourhood experience. 5–6 nights: Best for DEEPER_AUCKLAND including WAIHEKE + RANGITOTO_OR_DEVONPORT + MAUNGAKIEKIE + MISSION_BAY + FOOD_AND_NIGHTLIFE + additional cultural sightseeing. 7+ nights: Best when Auckland is treated as a WIDER_REGIONAL_BASE, combining the central city with Waitākere / Piha, multiple Hauraki Gulf experiences, west Auckland, vineyards, regional parks or onward North Island touring. Best season: YEAR-ROUND_WITH_SEASONAL_ACTIVITY_PLANNING Summer / Peak Outdoor Season (December – February): BEACHES + WAIHEKE + RANGITOTO + SAILING + HARBOUR_CRUISES + SWIMMING + OUTDOOR_DINING + LONG_DAYLIGHT, with higher holiday demand and stronger accommodation / ferry pressure. Autumn / Prime Mixed Season (March – May): MILD_WEATHER + WAIHEKE_WINE + WALKING + VOLCANIC_SIGHTSEEING + FOOD + COASTAL_ACTIVITY + LOWER_POST_SUMMER_PRESSURE. Winter / Cultural Season (June – August): AUCKLAND_MUSEUM + ART_GALLERY + MATARIKI + FOOD + WINERY_LUNCHES + SHOPPING + NIGHTLIFE + SELECTIVE_CLEAR_WEATHER_OUTDOOR_BLOCKS, with cooler, wetter and occasionally windy conditions. Spring / Outdoor Shoulder Season (September – November): LONGER_DAYLIGHT + ISLAND_TRIPS + VOLCANIC_WALKS + GARDENS + CYCLING + WILDLIFE + COASTAL_ACTIVITY + MANAGEABLE_PRE_SUMMER_DEMAND. March, April, October and November generally provide some of the strongest overall balances for city, island and outdoor sightseeing. December through February provide Auckland''s strongest beach and island conditions but generally require earlier booking around Christmas, New Year, school holidays and peak summer weekends. June through August remain highly viable for culture, gastronomy, Matariki, wineries and flexible city breaks but require stronger weather contingency for exposed coastlines, Rangitoto and long outdoor programs. Auckland should therefore be treated as a genuine YEAR_ROUND_HARBOUR_CITY_AND_REGIONAL_DESTINATION rather than a destination dependent on one specific season. Best hotel strategy: Choose accommodation according to waterfront access, public transport, ferry convenience, nightlife, family requirements, mobility and whether regional self-driving is included. For first-time visitors: AUCKLAND_CBD / BRITOMART / VIADUCT_HARBOUR / WYNYARD_QUARTER for efficient access to ferries, waterfront sightseeing, Sky Tower, restaurants, shopping and urban public transport. For culture / museum travel: CBD / PARNELL / NEWMARKET_APPROACH for Auckland Museum, Auckland Domain, Auckland Art Gallery, historic neighbourhoods and easy inner-city transport. For luxury: VIADUCT_HARBOUR / WYNYARD_QUARTER / BRITOMART / PREMIUM_CBD_PROPERTIES for harbour-view accommodation, premium restaurants, private transfers, yacht access and high-end city experiences. For honeymoon / romantic travel: VIADUCT_WATERFRONT / PREMIUM_CBD / WAIHEKE_ISLAND for harbour atmosphere, fine dining, vineyard experiences, beaches and relaxed couple-oriented itineraries. For food / nightlife: BRITOMART / VIADUCT / PONSONBY / KARANGAHAPE_ROAD_APPROACH for restaurants, bars, cafés, contemporary dining and evening access. For families: CBD_OR_WESTERN_INNER_CITY_TRANSIT_CONNECTED_HOTEL for convenient access to Auckland Museum, MOTAT, Auckland Zoo, waterfront recreation and public transport. For road-trip travelers: Do not automatically choose central Auckland solely for parking convenience; consider whether the first urban days should remain CAR_FREE before collecting a rental vehicle for Waitākere or onward regional travel. Avoid changing hotels unnecessarily; one well-connected Auckland base can efficiently support CBD + Museum + Maungawhau + Devonport + ferry departures, while Waiheke overnight stays should be added only when island relaxation, vineyards or romance justify the hotel change. Best transportation: Use: Auckland transportation should primarily be treated as: WALKING_FOR_CENTRAL_WATERFRONT + BUS_AND_TRAIN_FOR_URBAN_NETWORK + FERRY_FOR_ISLANDS_AND_HARBOUR + RIDESHARE_FOR_CONVENIENCE + PRIVATE_OR_RENTAL_CAR_FOR_OUTER_REGION. Auckland Airport transportation baseline: AUCKLAND_AIRPORT + AIRPORTLINK_TO_PUHINUI_STATION + SOUTHERN_OR_EASTERN_LINE_CONNECTIONS + DIRECT_SKYDRIVE_TO_SKYCITY + TAXI + RIDESHARE + SHUTTLE + PRIVATE_TRANSFER. Current AirportLink baseline: OPERATES_APPROXIMATELY_EVERY_10_MINUTES + APPROXIMATELY_04:30_TO_00:40 + 7_DAYS_PER_WEEK + CONNECTS_AIRPORT_TERMINALS_WITH_PUHINUI_STATION_AND_MANUKAU. Current Auckland Airport direct coach baseline: SKYDRIVE + AUCKLAND_AIRPORT_TO_SKYCITY + APPROXIMATELY_30_MINUTE_FREQUENCY_DURING_STANDARD_OPERATING_PERIODS. Airport road journeys must retain traffic contingency because Auckland congestion, roadworks and peak-hour conditions can materially alter transfer time. Public-transport payment baseline: AT_HOP OR SUPPORTED_CONTACTLESS_DEBIT_CREDIT_CARD OR SUPPORTED_DIGITAL_WALLET for AT scheduled buses, trains and most ferries. BUS_CASH_PAYMENT: NOT_ACCEPTED. CONTACTLESS_TRAVEL: TAG_ON + TAG_OFF + ONE_PAYMENT_METHOD_PER_TRAVELER. Important ferry exception: FULLERS360_WAIHEKE_AND_TOURIST_FERRY_SERVICES + NOT_INCLUDED_IN_STANDARD_AT_CONTACTLESS_PAYMENT_SYSTEM. Operator-specific ticketing must therefore be checked before Waiheke, Rangitoto or other tourist ferry travel. Accessibility baseline: CENTRAL_AUCKLAND: MODERATE_HIGH_TO_HIGH_ACCESSIBILITY + MODERN_TRANSPORT + ACCESSIBLE_MAJOR_MUSEUMS + WATERFRONT_ROUTES + VARIABLE_HILLS_AND_GRADIENTS. AUCKLAND_MUSEUM: RAMP_ACCESS + DISABLED_PARKING + COMPLIMENTARY_WHEELCHAIRS + ACCESS_SUPPORT. RANGITOTO: ROUGH_VOLCANIC_TERRAIN + 250_METRE_HEIGHT_GAIN + UNEVEN_LAVA + LOOSE_GRAVEL + NO_ACCESSIBLE_TOILETS_ON_STANDARD_SUMMIT_TRACK + NOT_SUITABLE_FOR_UNIFORM_STEP_FREE_CLASSIFICATION. WAITAKERE_AND_WEST_COAST: NATURAL_FOREST_TERRAIN + STEPS_AND_GRADIENTS + TRACK_CLOSURES + WEATHER_DEPENDENCE + VARIABLE_ACCESSIBILITY. WAIHEKE: ACCESSIBILITY_DEPENDS_ON_FERRY + LOCAL_TRANSFER + INDIVIDUAL_VINEYARD + ACCOMMODATION. Accessible rooms, ferry boarding conditions, vineyard vehicles, natural trails and individual attractions should be verified before confirmation. Must-do for first-time visitor: Auckland should not be reduced to Sky Tower and Queen Street alone; its essential tourism identity is: WAITEMATA_HARBOUR + MAORI_AND_PACIFIC_CULTURE + VOLCANIC_LANDSCAPE + HAURAKI_GULF_ISLANDS + FOOD_AND_WINE + BEACHES_AND_COAST + MULTICULTURAL_CITY_LIFE + WEST_COAST_NATURE. Don''t-do: Current Auckland Museum operational baseline: Rangitoto operational and planning baseline: Rangitoto conservation baseline: YOUNGEST_AND_LARGEST_VOLCANO_IN_AUCKLAND_VOLCANIC_FIELD + ERUPTED_APPROXIMATELY_600_YEARS_AGO + WORLD_LARGEST_POHUTUKAWA_FOREST + NATIVE_BIRD_HABITAT + PEST_FREE_ISLAND_PROTECTION + HAURAKI_GULF_MARINE_PARK_CONTEXT. Waiheke operational and planning baseline: Maungawhau / Mount Eden baseline: TUPUNA_MAUNGA + MAORI_CULTURAL_AND_ARCHAEOLOGICAL_SIGNIFICANCE + VOLCANIC_CRATER + CITY_PANORAMA + PEDESTRIAN_SUMMIT_EXPERIENCE. Current principal entrance gate baseline: SUMMER: 07:00–20:30 WINTER: 07:00–19:00. Times currently align with daylight-saving arrangements and remain subject to change. Maungakiekie / One Tree Hill baseline: TUPUNA_MAUNGA + MAORI_SETTLEMENT_AND_ARCHAEOLOGICAL_SIGNIFICANCE + CORNWALL_PARK_ADJACENCY + SUMMIT_OBELISK + CITY_VIEWS. PRIVATE_MOTOR_VEHICLES_TO_SUMMIT: PROHIBITED. The summit road and tihi have been permanently closed to ordinary private motor vehicles since 2018. Current automatic-gate baseline: SUMMER: 07:00–20:30 WINTER: 07:00–19:00. Waitākere / Piha 2026 planning baseline: 2026 Auckland event baseline: MATARIKI_FESTIVAL_2026: 04_JULY_2026 – 19_JULY_2026 + MULTIPLE_AUCKLAND_LOCATIONS + MAORI_NEW_YEAR + KAI + KORERO + CEREMONY + PERFORMANCE + COMMUNITY_PROGRAMMING. PASIFIKA_FESTIVAL_2026: 14_MARCH_2026 – 15_MARCH_2026 + WESTERN_SPRINGS_PARK + PACIFIC_CULTURES + TRADITIONAL_AND_CONTEMPORARY_PERFORMANCE + FOOD + MULTIPLE_PACIFIC_VILLAGES. AUCKLAND_HERITAGE_FESTIVAL_2026: 26_SEPTEMBER_2026 – 11_OCTOBER_2026 + MULTIPLE_AUCKLAND_LOCATIONS + HERITAGE + MIGRATION + FOOD + COMMUNITY_HISTORY. AUCKLAND_DIWALI_FESTIVAL_2026: 31_OCTOBER_2026 – 01_NOVEMBER_2026 + AOTEA_SQUARE + MUSIC + DANCE + INDIAN_CULTURE + FOOD + FIREWORKS + FREE_ENTRY. Event dates, operating times, road controls, weather contingencies and specific programming must still be verified for the actual itinerary. Biggest advantage: Exceptional destination diversity within one metropolitan region: Auckland combines a major international gateway, Māori and Pacific culture, volcanic landscapes, harbour scenery, offshore islands, wine regions, beaches, nightlife, world-class food and substantial nature access. Unlike a conventional urban stopover, Auckland can shift from a central-city museum and waterfront morning to a volcanic viewpoint, harbour ferry, vineyard lunch or rugged Tasman Sea coastline within the same wider destination region. Its Māori identity is particularly important because ancestral maunga such as Maungawhau and Maungakiekie form culturally significant landscapes rather than simply scenic recreational viewpoints. The Hauraki Gulf provides another major advantage: Waiheke delivers developed wine, beach and luxury tourism while Rangitoto provides a dramatically different protected volcanic-island hiking experience only a short ferry journey from downtown. Biggest disadvantage: Auckland''s attractions are geographically dispersed, accommodation and premium experiences can be expensive, road congestion can materially affect travel time, and island / outdoor programs depend on weather, ferry schedules and realistic transport planning. The destination can therefore feel inefficient when planners attempt CBD attractions, distant suburbs, multiple islands and west-coast nature without geographical clustering. Accessibility also varies sharply between highly accessible modern urban infrastructure and rough volcanic, island and regional-park environments. Overall destination score: 95/100', 3642),
  ('auckland', 36, 'data-quality', 'DATA QUALITY', NULL, NULL, 'information_completeness: 99/100 last_updated: 2026-09-06 last_verified: WEB_VERIFIED verified_by: DISCOVER_AUCKLAND / TATAKI_AUCKLAND_UNLIMITED / AUCKLAND_TRANSPORT / AUCKLAND_AIRPORT / AUCKLAND_WAR_MEMORIAL_MUSEUM / TUPUNA_MAUNGA_AUTHORITY / DEPARTMENT_OF_CONSERVATION / AUCKLAND_COUNCIL / NEW_ZEALAND_POLICE / CURRENT_OFFICIAL_EVENT_AND_TRANSPORT_SOURCES sources: IMPORTANT: Ferry timetables, Waiheke capacity, Rangitoto sailings, Auckland Museum exhibitions, Sky Tower operations, vineyard reservations, regional-park tracks, west-coast roads, public-transport disruptions, event programs, scenic aviation, wildlife cruises and private tours must NOT be treated as permanently available without verification. Current Auckland Museum general operating baseline: DAILY: 10:00–17:00 CHRISTMAS_DAY: CLOSED. Building works can alter normal visitor circulation and internal access routes. Museum exhibitions, Māori cultural programming, admission charges, guided experiences and operating conditions must be reverified before production use. Current Auckland Museum accessibility baseline: NORTH_AND_SOUTH_ENTRANCE_RAMP_ACCESS + DISABLED_PARKING + COMPLIMENTARY_WHEELCHAIRS + ADAPTABLE_VISITOR_SUPPORT. Accessibility requirements should still be communicated in advance when specialist assistance is needed. Rangitoto Summit Track baseline: 7_KM_RETURN + APPROXIMATELY_2_HOURS + 250_METRES_HEIGHT_GAIN + ROUGH_VOLCANIC_ROCK + LOOSE_GRAVEL + LIMITED_SHADE + PANORAMIC_SUMMIT_VIEW + OPTIONAL_CRATER_RIM_AND_LAVA_CAVE_EXTENSIONS. Rangitoto visitor-support baseline: FOOD_AVAILABLE: NO DRINKING_WATER_AVAILABLE: NO RECOMMENDED_WATER: 1_TO_2_LITRES_PER_PERSON STURDY_FOOTWEAR: REQUIRED SUN_PROTECTION: REQUIRED WATERPROOF_AND_WARM_LAYER: RECOMMENDED TORCH_FOR_LAVA_CAVES: RECOMMENDED ACCESSIBLE_TOILETS_ON_SUMMIT_TRACK: NO MOBILE_COVERAGE: VARIABLE. Rangitoto ferry baseline: DOWNTOWN_AUCKLAND_TO_RANGITOTO: APPROXIMATELY_25_MINUTES DEVONPORT_TO_RANGITOTO: APPROXIMATELY_20_MINUTES. Travelers must check actual sailing dates, operator schedules, ticket requirements and return times. Rangitoto biosecurity baseline: PEST_FREE_ISLAND + CHECK_GEAR + CLEAN_GEAR + SEAL_FOOD_AND_BAGS + REMOVE_SOIL_AND_SEEDS + TAKE_RUBBISH_AWAY. Biosecurity requirements are integral to island travel and should not be treated as optional visitor advice. Waiheke baseline: APPROXIMATELY_40_MINUTES_FROM_CENTRAL_AUCKLAND_BY_STANDARD_PASSENGER_FERRY_POSITIONING + 50_PLUS_WINERIES_AND_VINEYARD_PROPERTIES_PROMOTED + APPROXIMATELY_100_KM_COASTLINE + APPROXIMATELY_25_BEACHES + FOOD + ART + WINE + BEACHES + LUXURY + OUTDOOR_ACTIVITY. Waiheke ferry, vineyard, restaurant and transfer availability should be reverified during weekends, summer, public holidays and major event periods. Auckland public-transport baseline: AT_SCHEDULED_BUSES + TRAINS + MOST_FERRIES PAYMENT: AT_HOP OR SUPPORTED_CONTACTLESS_BANK_CARD OR SUPPORTED_DIGITAL_WALLET. CONTACTLESS_CONCESSIONS: NOT_GENERALLY_AVAILABLE REGISTERED_AT_HOP_REQUIRED_FOR_ELIGIBLE_CONCESSIONS. BUS_CASH_PAYMENT: NOT_ACCEPTED. Contactless exclusions currently include: FULLERS360_WAIHEKE + TOURIST_FERRY_SERVICES. Operator-specific rules must therefore be checked for individual Gulf-island journeys. Airport public-transport baseline: AIRPORTLINK: AUCKLAND_AIRPORT + PUHINUI_STATION + MANUKAU FREQUENCY: APPROXIMATELY_EVERY_10_MINUTES OPERATING_WINDOW: APPROXIMATELY_04:30_TO_00:40 DAYS: 7_DAYS_PER_WEEK. ROUTE_38: AUCKLAND_AIRPORT + MANGERE_TOWN_CENTRE + ONEHUNGA APPROXIMATE_FREQUENCY: 15_TO_20_MINUTES_DURING_STANDARD_DAYTIME_OPERATION. SKYDRIVE: AUCKLAND_AIRPORT + SKYCITY_CENTRAL_AUCKLAND APPROXIMATE_STANDARD_FREQUENCY: 30_MINUTES. Airport times and frequencies remain operational information and must be reverified. Airport taxi / shuttle baseline: LICENSED_TAXIS + SUPERSHUTTLE + RIDESHARE + PREBOOKED_PRIVATE_TRANSFER. Current airport-published taxi fares to Auckland CBD vary materially by provider and should NOT be embedded as permanent fixed pricing in production itineraries. Maungawhau baseline: SUMMER_MAIN_GATE: 07:00–20:30 WINTER_MAIN_GATE: 07:00–19:00 + TUPUNA_MAUNGA + VOLCANIC_CRATER + MAORI_ARCHAEOLOGICAL_SIGNIFICANCE + PANORAMIC_VIEWS. Gate times align with daylight-saving periods and remain subject to events, safety work or operational changes. Maungakiekie baseline: PRIVATE_VEHICLE_SUMMIT_ACCESS: NOT_PERMITTED + TUPUNA_MAUNGA + MAORI_CULTURAL_SIGNIFICANCE + CORNWALL_PARK_ADJACENCY + OBELISK + PEDESTRIAN_SUMMIT_ACCESS. Current gate baseline: SUMMER: 07:00–20:30 WINTER: 07:00–19:00. Gate arrangements can change for events or operational requirements. Waitākere 2026 baseline: MULTIPLE_TRACKS_REOPENED + CONTINUING_TRACK_REHABILITATION + KAURI_DIEBACK_PROTECTION + CURRENT_TRACK_STATUS_REQUIRED. Current confirmed closure baseline from the May 2026 Auckland Council update: LION_ROCK_SUMMIT_TRACK: CLOSED LAIRD_THOMSON_TRACK: CLOSED TASMAN_LOOKOUT_TRACK: CLOSED. Track status can change after publication and Auckland Council''s current regional-park information should be rechecked immediately before travel. Kauri-protection baseline: USE_OPEN_TRACKS_ONLY + CLEAN_FOOTWEAR + CLEAN_EQUIPMENT + USE_PROVIDED_CLEANING_STATIONS + AVOID_TRANSPORTING_SOIL + FOLLOW_CURRENT_BIOSECURITY_SIGNAGE. Auckland climate and seasonality should be handled as: SUMMER / DECEMBER_TO_FEBRUARY: BEACHES + SWIMMING + WAIHEKE + RANGITOTO + SAILING + OUTDOOR_DINING + WARM_HUMID_CONDITIONS + LONG_DAYLIGHT + PASSING_SHOWERS_POSSIBLE + HIGHER_HOLIDAY_DEMAND. AUTUMN / MARCH_TO_MAY: MILD_DAYS + VINEYARDS + WALKING + FOOD + COASTAL_ACTIVITY + COOLER_MORNINGS_AND_EVENINGS + GOOD_SHOULDER_SEASON_BALANCE. WINTER / JUNE_TO_AUGUST: MUSEUMS + MATARIKI + FOOD + WINERIES + CULTURE + SHOPPING + COOLER_WEATHER + MORE_RAIN + OCCASIONAL_STRONG_WIND + SHORTER_DAYLIGHT. SPRING / SEPTEMBER_TO_NOVEMBER: ISLAND_TRIPS + WALKING + CYCLING + GARDENS + WILDLIFE + OUTDOOR_EVENTS + INCREASINGLY_MILD_WEATHER + LONGER_EVENINGS + CHANGEABLE_SHOWERS_AND_WIND. Auckland has a temperate maritime climate and should never be treated as having guaranteed stable weather during any season. Severe-weather baseline: HEAVY_RAIN + STRONG_WIND + FLOODING + LANDSLIPS + COASTAL_CONDITIONS can affect: WAITAKERE + PIHA + FERRIES + RANGITOTO + HARBOUR_CRUISES + ROADS + REGIONAL_PARKS. Official MetService, Auckland emergency-management, Auckland Transport, ferry-operator and Auckland Council advice should override fixed tourism itineraries during severe-weather conditions. 2026 Matariki Festival baseline: MATARIKI_FESTIVAL: 04_JULY_2026 – 19_JULY_2026 LOCATION: MULTIPLE_TAMAKI_MAKAURAU_LOCATIONS POSITIONING: MAORI_NEW_YEAR + REFLECTION + KAI + KORERO + CEREMONY + ART + PERFORMANCE + COMMUNITY. The nationally observed Matariki public holiday occurred on 10_JULY_2026. 2026 Pasifika Festival baseline: PASIFIKA_FESTIVAL: 14_MARCH_2026 – 15_MARCH_2026 LOCATION: WESTERN_SPRINGS_PARK POSITIONING: PACIFIC_CULTURES + MULTIPLE_PACIFIC_VILLAGES + MUSIC + DANCE + FOOD + TRADITIONAL_AND_CONTEMPORARY_PERFORMANCE. 2026 Auckland Heritage Festival baseline: AUCKLAND_HERITAGE_FESTIVAL: 26_SEPTEMBER_2026 – 11_OCTOBER_2026 LOCATION: MULTIPLE_AUCKLAND_LOCATIONS POSITIONING: HERITAGE + MIGRATION + MANAakitanga + FOOD + COMMUNITY_HISTORY + TOURS + EXHIBITIONS. 2026 Auckland Diwali Festival baseline: AUCKLAND_DIWALI_FESTIVAL: 31_OCTOBER_2026 – 01_NOVEMBER_2026 LOCATION: AOTEA_SQUARE_AND_CENTRAL_CITY_PRECINCT POSITIONING: INDIAN_CULTURE + MUSIC + DANCE + FOOD + CRAFTS + FIREWORKS + FREE_PUBLIC_EVENT. Festival dates, crowd controls, road closures, public-transport changes and event programming must be verified for actual travel dates. Current general safety baseline: NEW_ZEALAND: RELATIVELY_SAFE_TRAVEL_DESTINATION BUT: NOT_CRIME_FREE + NORMAL_PERSONAL_SECURITY_PRECAUTIONS_REQUIRED. NEW_ZEALAND_POLICE_VISITOR_GUIDANCE: AVOID_UNLIT_AREAS_LATE_AT_NIGHT + SECURE_VALUABLES + DO_NOT_LEAVE_LUGGAGE_OR_CAMERAS_VISIBLE_IN_PARKED_CARS + TAKE_EXTRA_CARE_AT_SCENIC_SPOTS_AND_TRAILHEADS + CHECK_WEATHER_AND_OUTDOOR_CONDITIONS + TELL_SOMEONE_ABOUT_SIGNIFICANT_OUTDOOR_PLANS. EMERGENCY_NUMBER: 111 for police, ambulance and fire emergencies. Auckland should primarily be treated as: SUMMER: WAIHEKE + RANGITOTO + BEACHES + HARBOUR + VOLCANIC_VIEWPOINTS + OUTDOOR_DINING AUTUMN: WAIHEKE_WINE + CITY_WALKING + MAUNGA + FOOD + COASTAL_EXPLORATION + LOWER_POST_SUMMER_PRESSURE WINTER: AUCKLAND_MUSEUM + ART_GALLERY + MATARIKI + FOOD + SHOPPING + WINERY_LUNCHES + WEATHER_DEPENDENT_OUTDOOR_BLOCKS SPRING: ISLANDS + MAUNGA + COASTAL_WALKS + GARDENS + CYCLING + WILDLIFE + OUTDOOR_EVENTS FIRST_TIME_TRAVEL: CBD_WATERFRONT + AUCKLAND_MUSEUM + MAUNGAWHAU + WAIHEKE_OR_RANGITOTO + DEVONPORT_IF_TIME_ALLOWS REPEAT_TRAVEL: WAITAKERE_PIHA + MAUNGAKIEKIE + PONSONBY_K_ROAD + REGIONAL_PARKS + ADDITIONAL_GULF_ISLANDS + DEEPER_FOOD_AND_CULTURE. Discover Auckland / Tātaki Auckland Unlimited, Auckland Transport, Auckland Airport, Auckland Museum, Tūpuna Maunga Authority, Department of Conservation, Auckland Council, New Zealand Police and current individual ferry / attraction / event portals should be treated as primary sources for operational information. This dataset should be refreshed regularly before production use.', 3643),
  ('queenstown', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Spring', NULL, 'months: September October November weather: September retains winter-like alpine conditions and late-season skiing, while October and November progressively become warmer with longer daylight, spring growth and increasingly strong hiking, cycling and sightseeing conditions. crowd_level: LOW → MEDIUM price_level: MEDIUM overall_score: 67.33–75.33 recommended: true reason: Spring provides strong versatility, combining snow-capped scenery and possible early-season skiing overlap with progressively improving hiking, cycling, golf, wine and general sightseeing conditions. Best for:', 3644),
  ('queenstown', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Summer', NULL, 'months: December January February weather: Summer delivers Queenstown''s warmest temperatures and longest daylight hours, creating excellent conditions for hiking, biking, lake activities, jet boating, road trips and outdoor dining. crowd_level: HIGH price_level: HIGH overall_score: 58.00–66.00 recommended: true reason: Weather and activity conditions are exceptional, but Christmas-New Year and peak summer demand can substantially increase accommodation prices, activity demand and visitor pressure. Best for:', 3645),
  ('queenstown', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Autumn', NULL, 'months: March April May weather: March remains relatively warm, April brings cooler temperatures and strong autumn colour, while May becomes colder and quieter as Queenstown transitions toward winter. crowd_level: LOW → MEDIUM price_level: MEDIUM → LOW overall_score: 75.33–80.67 recommended: true reason: Autumn provides one of Queenstown''s strongest combinations of scenic beauty, photography, comfortable outdoor conditions, wine experiences and generally better value than peak summer or ski season. Best for:', 3646),
  ('queenstown', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Winter', NULL, 'months: June July August weather: Cold alpine conditions dominate, with regular snow on surrounding mountains and temperatures suitable for Queenstown''s internationally important ski and snowboard season. crowd_level: MEDIUM → HIGH price_level: MEDIUM_HIGH → HIGH overall_score: 51.67–62.67 recommended: true_for_winter_travel reason: Winter is Queenstown''s defining snow-sports season and offers spectacular alpine scenery and après-ski atmosphere, although peak ski demand significantly raises prices and visitor pressure. Best for:', 3647),
  ('queenstown', 10, 'budget-strategy', 'BUDGET STRATEGY', NULL, NULL, 'Where money can be saved: Current Queenstown public-bus pricing provides comparatively strong transport value, with Bee Card fares substantially lower than cash fares. Where saving money is usually NOT recommended: Travel-agent rule: In Queenstown, **CENTRAL_OR_WELL_CONNECTED_HOTEL + PUBLIC_TRANSPORT + FREE_SCENIC_WALKS + SELECTIVE_PREMIUM_ADVENTURES** provides the strongest value. For short stays, prioritize: **QUEENSTOWN_BAY + SKYLINE + LAKE_WHAKATIPU + ONE_MAJOR_ADVENTURE + ARROWTOWN_OR_GIBBSTON**. For longer stays, add: **GLENORCHY + CORONET_PEAK_OR_REMARKABLES + QUEENSTOWN_TRAIL + WALTER_PEAK + MOKE_LAKE + ADDITIONAL_ADVENTURE**. Operational note: Adventure prices, ski passes, gondola pricing, rental-car costs, lake cruises and seasonal transport should always be rechecked before travel.', 3648),
  ('queenstown', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Family', 'family', 'Airport transfer by: PUBLIC_BUS_OR_PRE_BOOKED_SHUTTLE + DIRECT_HOTEL_TRANSFER is generally the simplest approach depending on luggage and group size. Choose accommodation around Queenstown Town Centre, Lake Esplanade, Frankton Road or Frankton depending on itinerary, budget and transport preference.', 3649),
  ('queenstown', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Honeymoon', 'honeymoon', 'Prefer: PRIVATE_TRANSFER + LAKE_VIEW_OR_ALPINE_HOTEL + CENTRAL_OR_SCENIC_LOCATION for a relaxed premium arrival.', 3650),
  ('queenstown', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Luxury', 'luxury', 'Use: AIRPORT_MEET_AND_GREET + CHAUFFEURED_PREMIUM_VEHICLE + LUXURY_HOTEL_OR_LODGE + PRIVATE_SIGHTSEEING with helicopter transfers or scenic-flight combinations selectively for high-end itineraries.', 3651),
  ('queenstown', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Budget', 'budget', 'Primary options: Queenstown Airport is well connected to Frankton and Queenstown''s town centre, so a private transfer is not compulsory for budget travelers.', 3652),
  ('queenstown', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Senior', 'senior', 'Prefer: DIRECT_AIRPORT_TRANSFER + ACCESSIBLE_OR_CENTRAL_HOTEL + DOOR_TO_DOOR_EXCURSIONS particularly when traveling with substantial luggage or during winter.', 3653),
  ('queenstown', 18, 'family-travel', 'FAMILY TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'child_friendly_score: 96 best_ages: Rules: For young children: Prefer: Avoid:', 3654),
  ('queenstown', 19, 'honeymoon-travel', 'HONEYMOON TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'honeymoon_score: 97 romance_score: 97 privacy_score: 94 luxury_score: 96 Recommended: Honeymoon itineraries should generally stay at: 2–3 major experiences/day. Prefer: LUXURY_LAKE_OR_ALPINE_STAY + SCENIC_EXPERIENCE + WINE_OR_DINING + PRIVATE_ADVENTURE + SPA + FREE_TIME over: Continuous high-adrenaline scheduling from morning until night.', 3655),
  ('queenstown', 20, 'luxury-travel', 'LUXURY TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'luxury_score: 96 Recommended: Queenstown is particularly strong for: ALPINE_LUXURY + PRIVATE_AVIATION + ADVENTURE + LUXURY_LODGES + FOOD_AND_WINE + SCENIC_WILDERNESS.', 3656),
  ('queenstown', 21, 'adventure', 'ADVENTURE', NULL, NULL, 'adventure_score: 97 Queenstown is one of the world''s strongest concentrated adventure-tourism destinations. Adventure experiences: Best regions: QUEENSTOWN + SHOTOVER_CANYON + KAWARAU_GORGE + CORONET_PEAK + THE_REMARKABLES + GLENORCHY Travel-agent positioning: Queenstown should be treated as: WORLD_CLASS_ADVENTURE + SKIING + WATER_ADVENTURE + AERIAL_ADVENTURE + HIKING + MOUNTAIN_BIKING rather than a soft-adventure-only destination.', 3657),
  ('queenstown', 22, 'senior-travel', 'SENIOR TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'senior_suitability: 82 walking_intensity: LOW for Queenstown Bay, scenic cruises, accessible Queenstown Gardens sections, winery visits and road-based sightseeing. MEDIUM–HIGH for hill walks, alpine terrain, snow environments and adventure-focused experiences. Rules: Queenstown works especially well for seniors as a: SCENIC_CRUISE + GONDOLA + ALPINE_ROAD_TRIP + WINE + DINING + LUXURY + RELAXED_NATURE destination.', 3658),
  ('queenstown', 23, 'accessibility', 'ACCESSIBILITY', NULL, NULL, 'wheelchair_accessibility: MODERATE → HIGH FOR MANY CENTRAL HOTELS, LAKEFRONT AREAS, SELECTED TRAILS AND MAJOR COMMERCIAL ATTRACTIONS VARIABLE FOR ALPINE, TRAIL AND ADVENTURE EXPERIENCES public_transport_accessibility: MODERATE → HIGH ON SUITABLE SERVICES hotel_accessibility: GENERALLY_GOOD_IN_MODERN_HOTELS_BUT_MUST_BE_VERIFIED attraction_accessibility: MUST_BE_VERIFIED_PER_ACTIVITY Rule: Do not assume hiking trails, ski areas, boats, adventure activities or alpine viewpoints are universally step-free. Additional notes: Queenstown accessibility should therefore be classified as: STRONG_INCLUSIVE_TOURISM_INFRASTRUCTURE_WITH_ACTIVITY_SPECIFIC_VERIFICATION.', 3659),
  ('queenstown', 24, 'food', 'FOOD', NULL, NULL, 'Queenstown is particularly strong for: Food experiences: Family: Prioritize burgers, pizza, cafés, casual New Zealand restaurants, bakery products and family-friendly lakefront dining. Honeymoon: Choose fine dining, vineyard restaurants, intimate lake-view restaurants and premium Central Otago wine experiences. Luxury: Include private wine touring, degustation dining, lodge cuisine, premium New Zealand produce and chef-led experiences. Budget: Use bakeries, takeaway food, supermarkets, food courts, casual cafés and self-catering accommodation. Travel-agent rule: Position Queenstown food around: NEW_ZEALAND_PRODUCE + CENTRAL_OTAGO_WINE + ALPINE_DINING + WINERY_RESTAURANTS + COSMOPOLITAN_CAFES.', 3660),
  ('queenstown', 25, 'shopping', 'SHOPPING', NULL, NULL, 'Strong categories: Luxury shopping: Prefer: Local shopping: Prefer: Budget: Prefer: Travel-agent rule: Use: QUEENSTOWN_CBD for PREMIUM_AND_TOURIST_SHOPPING, ARROWTOWN for BOUTIQUE_AND_HERITAGE_SHOPPING, FRANKTON for PRACTICAL_AND_LARGE_FORMAT_RETAIL, LOCAL_MARKETS for ARTISAN_AND_NEW_ZEALAND_PRODUCTS.', 3661),
  ('queenstown', 26, 'nightlife', 'NIGHTLIFE', NULL, NULL, 'nightlife_level: 94 Suitable for: Best areas: Evening activities: Queenstown nightlife is strongest for: APRES_SKI + BARS + PUBS + CLUBS + WINE + DINING and is significantly stronger than most similarly sized resort destinations. Couples should generally prefer: SUNSET_VIEW + DINNER + WINE_OR_COCKTAIL_BAR + RELAXED_LAKEFRONT_WALK while groups and younger travelers can easily build: ADVENTURE + APRES + BAR_HOPPING + LATE_NIGHT_CLUBBING.', 3662),
  ('queenstown', 28, 'sample-itinerary-patterns', 'SAMPLE ITINERARY PATTERNS', '3 NIGHTS', NULL, '### Day 1 Arrival at Queenstown Airport (ZQN) → Airport shuttle, taxi, rideshare, or private transfer to Queenstown hotel → Hotel check-in & relax after arrival Afternoon: → Begin exploring Queenstown town centre → Walk along the Queenstown Bay waterfront → Explore the cafés, shops & pedestrian streets around the town centre → Continue towards the Lake Wakatipu waterfront → Enjoy panoramic views of The Remarkables and surrounding Southern Alps Evening: → Skyline Queenstown Gondola → Bob''s Peak panoramic viewpoint → Sunset overlooking Queenstown, Lake Wakatipu & surrounding mountains → Welcome dinner / relaxed lakefront evening → Hotel ZQN is Queenstown''s principal aviation gateway and provides convenient access to New Zealand''s Southern Lakes region. Queenstown is one of the country''s major adventure and alpine resort destinations and can be combined with Christchurch in the South Island and Rotorua in the North Island through domestic air connections. ### Day 2 Morning: Breakfast → Full-day Milford Sound / Piopiotahi excursion → Travel through the spectacular landscapes of Fiordland → Te Anau → Eglinton Valley → Mirror Lakes according to tour routing → Homer Tunnel → Arrive at Milford Sound Afternoon: → Milford Sound scenic cruise → Cruise beneath dramatic fiord landscapes → See waterfalls, rainforest-covered cliffs & Mitre Peak scenery → Wildlife viewing according to conditions → Return towards Queenstown Evening: → Relaxed Queenstown waterfront walk → Dinner overlooking Lake Wakatipu → Hotel Optional alternative instead of Milford Sound: ADVENTURE: Choose ONE: → Shotover Jet OR → Kawarau Bungy OR → Queenstown zipline / adventure experience → Skyline Gondola & Luge GLENORCHY: → Scenic drive along Lake Wakatipu → Bennett''s Bluff viewpoints → Glenorchy township → Paradise / surrounding landscapes according to tour → Photography & nature experience WINE_AND_FOOD: → Gibbston Valley → Central Otago wine region → Boutique vineyard visits → Wine tasting → Premium local lunch FAMILY: → Skyline Gondola → Luge → Kiwi Park → Lake Wakatipu cruise → Family-friendly adventure activities HONEYMOON: → Glenorchy scenic experience → Couple photography around Lake Wakatipu → Boutique wine tasting → Couple spa → Romantic lakefront dinner LUXURY: → Private Milford Sound scenic flight / helicopter experience → Premium cruise → Private Central Otago wine tour → Luxury spa → Fine dining ### Day 3 Morning: Breakfast → Hotel checkout → Transfer to Queenstown Airport (ZQN) → Domestic flight to Christchurch → Christchurch city orientation according to flight timing → Explore Cathedral Square → Avon River precinct → Riverside Market / central-city area Afternoon: → Continue Christchurch sightseeing → Botanic Gardens → Hagley Park → Optional Avon River punting experience → Transfer to Christchurch Airport → Domestic flight towards Rotorua via an available connecting service if required → Rotorua hotel check-in Evening: → Explore the Rotorua lakefront → Māori cultural experience & traditional hāngī-style dinner where scheduled → Optional geothermal evening / spa experience → Hotel Optional alternative instead of covering BOTH Christchurch & Rotorua: CHRISTCHURCH_FOCUS: → Fly Queenstown to Christchurch → Cathedral Square → Christchurch Botanic Gardens → Avon River → Riverside Market → Tram / central-city exploration → Overnight Christchurch ROTORUA_FOCUS: → Fly from Queenstown towards Rotorua via an appropriate domestic connection → Rotorua lakefront → Te Puia / geothermal experience → Māori culture → Geothermal landscapes → Traditional cultural dinner QUEENSTOWN_FOCUS: → Remain in Queenstown for the entire third day → Arrowtown → Gibbston Valley → Central Otago wine experience → Lake Wakatipu → Skyline Queenstown sunset SPA & WELLNESS: → Premium Queenstown spa → Hot-pool / wellness experience → Couple treatments → Mountain-view relaxation → Fine dining NATURE & ADVENTURE: → Milford Sound → Glenorchy → Lake Wakatipu → Shotover River → Skyline Queenstown FAMILY: → Skyline Gondola & Luge → Kiwi Park → Lake cruise → Arrowtown → Family adventure experience HONEYMOON: → Milford Sound scenic experience → Glenorchy couple photography → Private hot-pool / spa experience → Central Otago wine tasting → Romantic lakefront dinner LUXURY: → Private helicopter / scenic flight → Premium Milford Sound experience → Chauffeured Glenorchy excursion → Luxury lodge / resort spa → Fine dining For only 3 nights, prioritize: QUEENSTOWN_LAKE_WAKATIPU_AND_SKYLINE + MILFORD_SOUND + CHRISTCHURCH_OR_ROTORUA_EXTENSION OR QUEENSTOWN_ALPINE_EXPERIENCES + GLENORCHY_AND_CENTRAL_OTAGO + ONE_CHRISTCHURCH_OR_ROTORUA_EXTENSION rather than trying to properly sightsee Queenstown, Christchurch and Rotorua within the same very short itinerary. ### Day 4 Breakfast → Leisurely Rotorua lakefront / hotel morning → Optional souvenir shopping → Hotel checkout → Transfer to Rotorua Airport (ROT) → Departure / onward domestic connection', 3663),
  ('queenstown', 29, 'six-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 1', NULL, 'Arrival at Queenstown Airport (ZQN) → Private airport transfer → Romantic lake / mountain-view hotel check-in → Relax and refresh Afternoon: → Queenstown Bay → Lake Wakatipu waterfront → Town-centre exploration → Couple photography Evening: → Skyline Gondola → Bob''s Peak sunset → Romantic dinner → Overnight at Queenstown', 3664),
  ('queenstown', 29, 'six-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 2', NULL, 'Breakfast → Full-day Milford Sound experience → Scenic journey through Fiordland → Te Anau → Mirror Lakes / scenic stops → Milford Sound cruise → Mitre Peak & waterfall landscapes Evening: → Return to Queenstown → Lakefront dinner → Overnight at Queenstown', 3665),
  ('queenstown', 29, 'six-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 3', NULL, 'Breakfast → Glenorchy scenic excursion → Lake Wakatipu scenic road → Mountain viewpoints → Glenorchy → Couple photography → Nature & alpine landscapes Afternoon: → Return towards Queenstown → Couple spa / hot-pool experience Evening: → Romantic dinner → Overnight at Queenstown', 3666),
  ('queenstown', 29, 'six-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 4', NULL, 'Breakfast Morning: → Arrowtown → Historic village exploration → Boutique cafés Afternoon: → Gibbston Valley / Central Otago wine region → Vineyard experience → Wine tasting → Scenic countryside Evening: → Return to Queenstown → Farewell Queenstown dinner → Overnight at Queenstown', 3667),
  ('queenstown', 29, 'six-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 5', NULL, 'Breakfast → Hotel checkout → Transfer to ZQN → Domestic flight to Christchurch → Romantic hotel check-in Afternoon: → Christchurch Botanic Gardens → Avon River → Central Christchurch → Riverside precinct Evening: → Romantic Avon / city-centre experience → Dinner → Overnight at Christchurch', 3668),
  ('queenstown', 29, 'six-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 6', NULL, 'Breakfast → Hotel checkout → Domestic flight towards Rotorua → Romantic hotel / resort check-in Afternoon: → Rotorua geothermal experience → Māori cultural heritage → Geothermal landscapes → Rotorua lakefront Evening: → Māori cultural performance / hāngī experience → Couple spa / geothermal wellness → Farewell romantic dinner → Overnight at Rotorua', 3669),
  ('queenstown', 29, 'six-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 7', NULL, 'Breakfast → Leisure morning → Hotel checkout → Transfer to Rotorua Airport (ROT) → Departure / onward connection', 3670),
  ('queenstown', 30, 'six-nights-family-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 1', NULL, 'Arrival at Queenstown Airport (ZQN) → Airport transfer → Family hotel check-in → Relax and refresh Afternoon: → Queenstown Bay → Lake Wakatipu → Town-centre exploration → Family photography Evening: → Skyline Gondola → Family dinner → Overnight at Queenstown', 3671),
  ('queenstown', 30, 'six-nights-family-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 2', NULL, 'Breakfast → Full-day Milford Sound excursion → Fiordland scenic journey → Te Anau → Scenic viewpoints → Milford Sound cruise → Waterfalls & mountain landscapes Evening: → Return to Queenstown → Family dinner → Overnight at Queenstown', 3672),
  ('queenstown', 30, 'six-nights-family-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 3', NULL, 'Breakfast → Queenstown family adventure day Choose ONE: FAMILY_ADVENTURE → Skyline Gondola → Luge → Kiwi Park → Family-friendly adventure activities GLENORCHY → Scenic Lake Wakatipu drive → Glenorchy → Nature walks → Family photography Afternoon: → Lake Wakatipu cruise / town leisure Evening: → Family dinner → Overnight at Queenstown', 3673),
  ('queenstown', 30, 'six-nights-family-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 4', NULL, 'Breakfast Morning: → Arrowtown → Historic streets → Family exploration Afternoon: → Gibbston Valley → Countryside experience → Family-friendly food / farm experience → Leisure Evening: → Return to Queenstown → Overnight at Queenstown', 3674),
  ('queenstown', 30, 'six-nights-family-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 5', NULL, 'Breakfast → Hotel checkout → Transfer to ZQN → Domestic flight to Christchurch → Family hotel check-in Afternoon: → Christchurch Botanic Gardens → Hagley Park → Avon River → Riverside Market Evening: → Family city exploration → Dinner → Overnight at Christchurch', 3675),
  ('queenstown', 30, 'six-nights-family-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 6', NULL, 'Breakfast → Hotel checkout → Domestic flight towards Rotorua → Family hotel check-in Afternoon: → Geothermal attraction → Geysers & geothermal landscapes → Māori cultural experience → Rotorua lakefront Evening: → Cultural performance / traditional dinner → Family leisure → Overnight at Rotorua', 3676),
  ('queenstown', 30, 'six-nights-family-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 7', NULL, 'Breakfast → Hotel checkout → Transfer to Rotorua Airport (ROT) → Departure / onward connection', 3677),
  ('queenstown', 31, 'six-nights-luxury-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 1', NULL, 'Arrival at Queenstown Airport (ZQN) → Private luxury airport transfer → Premium lakefront / alpine resort check-in → Relax and refresh Afternoon: → Chauffeured Queenstown orientation → Lake Wakatipu → Premium couple / travel photography Evening: → Skyline Queenstown → Sunset aperitif → Fine dining → Overnight at Queenstown', 3678),
  ('queenstown', 31, 'six-nights-luxury-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 2', NULL, 'Breakfast → Premium Milford Sound experience Choose ONE: PRIVATE_AIR_AND_CRUISE → Scenic flight / helicopter from Queenstown → Milford Sound aerial landscapes → Premium fiord cruise → Scenic return flight PRIVATE_ROAD_EXPERIENCE → Chauffeured Fiordland journey → Te Anau → Private scenic stops → Premium Milford Sound cruise Evening: → Return to Queenstown → Spa & wellness → Fine dining → Overnight at Queenstown', 3679),
  ('queenstown', 31, 'six-nights-luxury-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 3', NULL, 'Breakfast → Private Glenorchy experience → Chauffeured Lake Wakatipu scenic drive → Glenorchy → Premium photography stops → Alpine landscapes → Private nature experience Afternoon: → Luxury spa / private hot-pool experience → Resort leisure Evening: → Premium lakefront dining → Overnight at Queenstown', 3680),
  ('queenstown', 31, 'six-nights-luxury-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 4', NULL, 'Breakfast → Private Arrowtown & Central Otago experience → Historic Arrowtown → Gibbston Valley → Premium vineyard → Private wine tasting → Gourmet lunch Afternoon: → Scenic countryside → Luxury lodge / spa leisure Evening: → Farewell Queenstown fine dining → Overnight at Queenstown', 3681),
  ('queenstown', 31, 'six-nights-luxury-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 5', NULL, 'Breakfast → Hotel checkout → Private transfer to ZQN → Premium domestic flight arrangement to Christchurch → Private airport transfer → Luxury hotel check-in Afternoon: → Privately guided Christchurch experience → Botanic Gardens → Avon River → Central-city architecture → Premium punting / curated city experience Evening: → Fine dining → Overnight at Christchurch', 3682),
  ('queenstown', 31, 'six-nights-luxury-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 6', NULL, 'Breakfast → Private airport transfer → Domestic flight towards Rotorua → Chauffeured transfer → Premium geothermal resort / luxury lodge check-in Afternoon: → Private geothermal experience → Māori cultural heritage → Geysers & geothermal landscapes → Curated Rotorua sightseeing Evening: → Premium Māori cultural / dining experience → Geothermal spa & wellness → Farewell fine dining → Overnight at Rotorua', 3683),
  ('queenstown', 31, 'six-nights-luxury-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 7', NULL, 'Breakfast → Leisure / spa morning → Hotel checkout → Private luxury transfer to Rotorua Airport (ROT) → Departure / onward connection', 3684),
  ('queenstown', 32, 'travel-agent-insights', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS', 'What inexperienced planners often do wrong', NULL, '', 3685),
  ('queenstown', 32, 'travel-agent-insights', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS', 'What an experienced planner does differently', NULL, 'For first-time visits, prioritize: QUEENSTOWN_BAY_LAKE_WHAKATIPU + SKYLINE_BOBS_PEAK + ONE_SIGNATURE_ADVENTURE + ARROWTOWN_OR_GIBBSTON_OR_GLENORCHY before maximum attraction coverage.', 3686),
  ('queenstown', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', NULL, NULL, 'IF: trip_length <= 1 night THEN: prioritize_QUEENSTOWN_BAY + SKYLINE_BOBS_PEAK AND: choose_ONE_OF_SHOTOVER_JET_OR_CENTRAL_LAKE_CRUISE Reason: A very short Queenstown stay gains more value from concentrated lake, alpine-view and one signature experience than from attempting distant regional excursions. IF: trip_length == 2_OR_3_nights THEN: prioritize_QUEENSTOWN_BAY + SKYLINE + ONE_SIGNATURE_ADVENTURE AND: retain_ONE_HALF_DAY_OR_DAY_FOR_ARROWTOWN_OR_GIBBSTON_OR_GLENORCHY Reason: Two to three nights provide Queenstown''s essential combination of alpine scenery, Lake Whakatipu and one regional or adventure experience without excessive road time. IF: trip_length == 4_OR_5_nights THEN: add_ARROWTOWN + GIBBSTON_OR_WALTER_PEAK + GLENORCHY AND: retain_ONE_BLOCK_FOR_HIKING_OR_CYCLING_OR_SECOND_ADVENTURE Reason: Four to five nights create a strong balanced introduction combining the resort core with wine, heritage, wilderness and outdoor activity. IF: trip_length >= 6 nights THEN: add_MOKE_LAKE + DEEPER_GLENORCHY + QUEENSTOWN_TRAIL + MULTIPLE_ACTIVITY_OPTIONS AND: consider_SECOND_SKI_DAY_OR_LONGER_HIKE_BASED_ON_SEASON Reason: Longer stays allow Queenstown''s surrounding valleys, trails, mountain environments and quieter scenic experiences to complement headline attractions. IF: trip_length >= 7 nights AND: traveler_interest == WIDER_SOUTH_ISLAND THEN: consider_QUEENSTOWN_BASE + ONE_SECONDARY_SOUTH_ISLAND_BASE AND: avoid_REPEATED_EXTREME_DISTANCE_DAY_TRIPS_FROM_QUEENSTOWN Reason: Queenstown is an excellent Southern Lakes gateway, but repeatedly returning after very long regional road journeys can create unnecessary travel fatigue. IF: trip_type == HONEYMOON THEN: prefer_PREMIUM_LAKE_VIEW_HOTEL + GIBBSTON_WINE + SCENIC_EXPERIENCE + FINE_DINING + FREE_TIME AND: add_PRIVATE_HELICOPTER_OR_HOT_POOL_OR_PRIVATE_CRUISE_IF_BUDGET_ALLOWS Reason: Queenstown''s strongest honeymoon positioning combines alpine scenery, lake views, wine, privacy and premium experiential travel rather than continuous adrenaline activities. IF: traveler_type == FAMILY THEN: prioritize_SKYLINE + QUEENSTOWN_GARDENS + ARROWTOWN + WALTER_PEAK_OR_LAKE_CRUISE AND: include_ONE_OR_TWO_AGE_APPROPRIATE_ADVENTURE_ACTIVITIES Reason: Families benefit most from balancing scenery, interactive activities, heritage, lake experiences and manageable adventure rather than overloading extreme products. IF: traveler_type == FAMILY_WITH_YOUNG_CHILDREN THEN: reduce_BEN_LOMOND + MULTIPLE_EXTREME_ADVENTURES + LONG_REGIONAL_DRIVES AND: increase_SKYLINE + SNOWPLAY_IF_SEASONAL + QUEENSTOWN_GARDENS + ARROWTOWN + WALTER_PEAK Reason: Long hikes, high-adrenaline products and repeated road journeys can reduce comfort for younger children despite Queenstown''s strong family appeal. IF: traveler_type == LUXURY THEN: prefer_PREMIUM_LAKEFRONT_OR_LODGE + CHAUFFEURED_TRANSFER + PRIVATE_GLENORCHY_OR_WINE_TOUR + PREMIUM_DINING AND: consider_HELICOPTER + PRIVATE_BOAT + BESPOKE_SKI_OR_ALPINE_EXPERIENCE Reason: Queenstown''s luxury strength lies in dramatic scenery, remote lodges, scenic aviation, wine, private transport and personalized alpine experiences. IF: traveler_type == BUDGET THEN: prefer_BUS_CONNECTED_VALUE_HOTEL + WALKING + ORBUS + FREE_LAKEFRONT_AND_TRAILS AND: limit_PRIVATE_TRANSFERS + MULTIPLE_PREMIUM_ADVENTURES + UNUSED_RENTAL_CAR_DAYS Reason: Queenstown can be expensive, but walking, public buses, free scenery and carefully selecting one or two signature paid experiences can control costs. IF: traveler_interest == ADVENTURE THEN: prioritize_ONE_OR_MORE_OF_SHOTOVER_JET + KAWARAU_BUNGY + NEVIS + SKYDIVING + RAFTING + PARAGLIDING AND: select_BASED_ON_RISK_TOLERANCE + AGE + WEIGHT + HEALTH + WEATHER Reason: Queenstown offers an unusually broad adventure inventory, but each activity has different participant and operating requirements. IF: traveler_interest == BUNGY THEN: choose_KAWARAU_FOR_HISTORIC_FIRST_COMMERCIAL_BUNGY_CONTEXT OR: choose_NEVIS_FOR_MORE_EXTREME_REMOTE_VALLEY_EXPERIENCE Reason: Kawarau and Nevis deliver substantially different settings, heights, logistics and psychological intensity. IF: traveler_interest == KAWARAU_BUNGY THEN: verify_CURRENT_OPENING_HOURS + WEIGHT_RULES + MEDICAL_REQUIREMENTS + CHECK_IN AND: consider_COMBINING_WITH_GIBBSTON Reason: Kawarau lies within the Gibbston / Kawarau corridor, making bungy and wine-region sightseeing geographically compatible when alcohol and driving are managed responsibly. IF: traveler_interest == NEVIS THEN: use_OPERATOR_TRANSPORT_TO_REMOTE_ACTIVITY_SITE AND: do_NOT_INSTRUCT_STANDARD_VISITORS_TO_SELF_DRIVE_DIRECTLY_TO_PLATFORM Reason: The Nevis operation uses controlled access and dedicated transport into its remote valley environment. IF: traveler_interest == SHOTOVER_JET THEN: allocate_APPROXIMATELY_1_TO_2_HOURS_TOTAL_BASED_ON_TRANSPORT AND: verify_WEATHER + RIVER_CONDITIONS + CURRENT_DEPARTURE_TIME Reason: The boat ride itself is approximately 25 minutes, but check-in, briefing, transport and operational conditions require a larger itinerary block. IF: traveler_interest == SHOTOVER_JET THEN: check_IN_APPROXIMATELY_30_MINUTES_BEFORE_BOOKED_TRIP AND: use_OPERATOR_SHUTTLE_OR_DIRECT_TRANSPORT_AS_APPROPRIATE Reason: Shotover Jet operates from Arthurs Point rather than directly from Queenstown Bay and requires pre-ride preparation. IF: weather == HEAVY_RAIN_OR_UNSAFE_RIVER_CONDITIONS AND: plan_includes_SHOTOVER_JET THEN: reconfirm_OPERATOR_STATUS AND: replace_WITH_INDOOR_OR_LOW_WEATHER_DEPENDENCE_ACTIVITY_IF_CANCELLED Reason: Shotover Jet operates subject to weather and river conditions and can be suspended when conditions are unsafe. IF: traveler_interest == SKYLINE THEN: allocate_APPROXIMATELY_2_TO_4_HOURS_BASED_ON_LUGE_DINING_AND_VIEWING AND: verify_SEPARATE_GONDOLA + LUGE + DINING + MTB_TIMES Reason: Skyline Queenstown combines multiple products with different operating windows rather than one universal attraction schedule. IF: traveler_interest == SKYLINE_MOUNTAIN_BIKING THEN: verify_CURRENT_UPLIFT_SEASON + TRAIL_STATUS + BIKE_PARK_OPERATION Reason: Mountain-bike uplift is seasonal and should not be assumed to operate continuously throughout winter. IF: traveler_interest == BEN_LOMOND THEN: allocate_FULL_DAY_FOR_SUMMIT_FROM_QUEENSTOWN AND: allow_APPROXIMATELY_6_TO_8_HOURS + 14_KM_RETURN + 1438_M_ELEVATION_GAIN Reason: DOC classifies the Ben Lomond summit route as a demanding climb requiring high fitness and substantial elevation gain. IF: traveler_interest == BEN_LOMOND THEN: check_WEATHER + SNOW_ICE + DAYLIGHT + FITNESS AND: carry_FOOD + WATER + WARM_LAYER + WATERPROOF_LAYER + APPROPRIATE_FOOTWEAR Reason: Ben Lomond is an exposed alpine environment where conditions can change rapidly and snow or ice can occur outside mid-winter. IF: traveler_type == SENIOR AND: plan_includes_BEN_LOMOND_SUMMIT THEN: assess_CARDIO_FITNESS + JOINT_MOBILITY + WEATHER + ELEVATION_GAIN AND: replace_WITH_QUEENSTOWN_HILL_OR_SKYLINE_OR_LAKEFRONT_IF_UNSUITABLE Reason: Ben Lomond is materially more physically demanding than Queenstown''s easier scenic walking options. IF: traveler_uses_WHEELCHAIR AND: plan_includes_BEN_LOMOND THEN: replace_WITH_VERIFIED_ACCESSIBLE_LAKEFRONT_OR_GONDOLA_OR_TRAIL_EXPERIENCE Reason: Ben Lomond''s steep alpine terrain is not appropriate for standard step-free itinerary classification. IF: traveler_interest == EASY_NATURE THEN: prioritize_QUEENSTOWN_GARDENS + LAKEFRONT + SELECTED_QUEENSTOWN_TRAIL_SECTIONS OVER: BEN_LOMOND_SUMMIT + REMOTE_BACKCOUNTRY_TRACKS Reason: These central options provide strong lake and mountain scenery with substantially lower physical and transport demands. IF: traveler_interest == MOKE_LAKE THEN: allocate_HALF_DAY_OR_RELAXED_SCENIC_BLOCK AND: use_APPROPRIATE_VEHICLE + ALLOW_FOR_UNSEALED_ROAD + WEATHER Reason: Moke Lake provides excellent mountain scenery close to Queenstown but its final road approach is unsealed and should not be treated as urban-road access. IF: traveler_interest == MOKE_LAKE_MOUNTAIN_BIKING THEN: follow_CURRENT_DOC_SIGNAGE AND: avoid_PENINSULA_AND_RESTRICTED_EROSION_AFFECTED_SECTIONS Reason: DOC currently restricts mountain biking on parts of the Moke Lake Loop because of erosion. IF: traveler_interest == GLENORCHY THEN: allocate_MINIMUM_HALF_DAY AND: prefer_FULL_DAY_IF_ADDING_PARADISE + DART_RIVER + HIKING + FILM_LOCATIONS Reason: Glenorchy is approximately 45 km from Queenstown and its scenery, road viewpoints and wilderness activities justify substantially more time than pure driving duration suggests. IF: traveler_interest == GLENORCHY THEN: allow_PHOTOGRAPHY_AND_VIEWPOINT_BUFFER_ON_QUEENSTOWN_GLENORCHY_ROAD AND: stop_ONLY_IN_SAFE_DESIGNATED_LOCATIONS Reason: The road is a major scenic attraction in its own right, but narrow sections make unsafe roadside stopping inappropriate. IF: route == QUEENSTOWN_TO_GLENORCHY AND: weather == SNOW_ICE_HEAVY_RAIN_OR_SEVERE_WEATHER THEN: recheck_ROAD_CONDITIONS + OPERATOR_STATUS AND: allow_DELAY_OR_REPLACEMENT_PROGRAM Reason: Alpine weather, slips, ice and road conditions can materially affect regional road travel. IF: traveler_interest == ARROWTOWN THEN: allocate_APPROXIMATELY_2_TO_4_HOURS AND: include_BUCKINGHAM_STREET + CHINESE_SETTLEMENT + ARROW_RIVER + HERITAGE_CONTEXT Reason: Arrowtown offers meaningful gold-rush and Chinese-settlement heritage in addition to scenic streets, cafés and shopping. IF: traveler_interest == ARROWTOWN AND: season == AUTUMN THEN: increase_PHOTOGRAPHY_TIME + WALKING_TIME AND: allow_FOR_HIGHER_VISITOR_DEMAND_AROUND_AUTUMN_FESTIVAL Reason: Arrowtown''s autumn colours are among the region''s signature seasonal experiences and festival periods can increase demand. IF: traveler_interest == ARROWTOWN_AND_WINE THEN: combine_ARROWTOWN + GIBBSTON Reason: Arrowtown and Gibbston form a geographically efficient heritage-and-wine regional itinerary from Queenstown. IF: traveler_interest == WINE THEN: prioritize_GIBBSTON AND: include_PINOT_NOIR + CELLAR_DOORS + WINERY_LUNCH_OR_CYCLING_BASED_ON_STYLE Reason: Gibbston is Queenstown''s nearest major wine sub-region and a principal gateway to Central Otago Pinot Noir. IF: traveler_interest == GIBBSTON_WINE THEN: prebook_HIGH_DEMAND_CELLAR_DOORS_AND_RESTAURANTS AND: arrange_TOUR + TAXI + PRIVATE_DRIVER_OR_DESIGNATED_NON_DRINKING_DRIVER Reason: Wine tastings and winery meals require both reservation and responsible transport planning during busy periods. IF: traveler_interest == WINE AND: traveler_self_drives THEN: limit_ALCOHOL_TASTING_OR_USE_DESIGNATED_DRIVER Reason: Driving after multiple tastings creates unnecessary road-safety risk and should not form part of responsible itinerary planning. IF: traveler_interest == CYCLING THEN: select_QUEENSTOWN_TRAIL_SECTION_BASED_ON_DISTANCE + ELEVATION + SURFACE + FITNESS AND: consider_E_BIKE_FOR_LONGER_REGIONAL_ROUTES Reason: Queenstown''s trail network connects major regional destinations but different sections create materially different physical demands. IF: traveler_interest == EASY_ACCESSIBLE_CYCLING_OR_TRAIL THEN: consider_SELECTED_QUEENSTOWN_TRAIL + GIBBSTON_RIVER_WINE_TRAIL + QUEENSTOWN_GARDENS_SECTIONS AND: verify_CURRENT_SURFACE_AND_ASSISTANCE_REQUIREMENTS Reason: Official Queenstown accessibility guidance identifies several relatively accessible trail environments, although individual sections still require verification. IF: traveler_interest == TSS_EARNSLAW THEN: verify_CURRENT_VESSEL_OPERATION + DEPARTURE_TIME + ANNUAL_MAINTENANCE AND: do_NOT_GUARANTEE_VINTAGE_STEAMSHIP_DURING_MAINTENANCE_PERIOD Reason: TSS Earnslaw normally operates extensively through the year but undergoes annual survey and maintenance. IF: travel_dates_overlap_18_MAY_2026_TO_26_JUNE_2026 AND: plan_includes_TSS_EARNSLAW THEN: replace_EXPECTED_STEAMSHIP_WITH_CURRENT_REALNZ_SUBSTITUTE_VESSEL_IF_APPLICABLE AND: verify_SPIRIT_OF_QUEENSTOWN_OPERATION Reason: RealNZ scheduled TSS Earnslaw''s 2026 annual maintenance from 18 May through 26 June, with Walter Peak services transferred to the Spirit of Queenstown. IF: traveler_interest == WALTER_PEAK THEN: allocate_APPROXIMATELY_HALF_DAY_BASED_ON_SELECTED_PRODUCT AND: combine_LAKE_CRUISE + FARM_OR_DINING_EXPERIENCE Reason: Walter Peak experiences combine lake transport with dining, farm or heritage components and require more time than a simple boat crossing. IF: traveler_uses_WHEELCHAIR AND: plan_includes_TSS_EARNSLAW_OR_WALTER_PEAK THEN: verify_VESSEL_BOARDING + TOILET_REQUIREMENTS + SELECTED_WALTER_PEAK_PRODUCT Reason: Selected elements are accessible, but the historic TSS Earnslaw does not provide the same accessible facilities as a modern vessel and individual products differ. IF: season == JUNE_TO_AUGUST THEN: increase_SKIING + SNOWBOARDING + SNOWPLAY + APRES_SKI + HOT_POOLS + WINTER_SCENERY AND: book_ACCOMMODATION + SKI_PRODUCTS + TRANSPORT_EARLIER Reason: Winter is one of Queenstown''s major peak seasons and snow-sport demand materially increases accommodation and mountain-service pressure. IF: season == WINTER AND: traveler_interest == SKIING THEN: compare_CORONET_PEAK + THE_REMARKABLES_BASED_ON_SKILL + ROAD + TERRAIN + DATES AND: check_DAILY_SNOW_REPORT + LIFT_STATUS + SKIBUS + ROAD_CONDITIONS Reason: Queenstown''s principal ski fields have different terrain, access and operating dates, and daily mountain conditions matter more than fixed itinerary assumptions. IF: travel_dates == 29_MAY_2026_TO_12_JUNE_2026 AND: traveler_interest == CORONET_PEAK THEN: treat_AS_EARLY_WINTER_LIMITED_OPERATION AND: prioritize_BEGINNER_TERRAIN + SNOWPLAY + PEAK_GONDOLA_SIGHTSEEING Reason: Coronet Peak''s special 2026 early-winter period operates from approximately 10:00–15:00 with focused beginner and snowplay terrain before full-mountain opening. IF: travel_date >= 13_JUNE_2026 AND: travel_date <= 04_OCTOBER_2026 AND: traveler_interest == CORONET_PEAK THEN: use_FULL_SEASON_OPERATION_BASELINE AND: verify_DAILY_OPEN_TERRAIN + WEATHER + LIFTS Reason: Coronet Peak''s published 2026 full season runs from 13 June to 4 October with standard operations approximately 09:00–16:00 subject to conditions. IF: travel_date < 27_JUNE_2026 AND: traveler_interest == THE_REMARKABLES THEN: do_NOT_ASSUME_2026_SKI_OPERATION AND: consider_CORONET_PEAK_EARLY_SEASON_IF_APPROPRIATE Reason: The Remarkables'' published 2026 season begins on 27 June, later than Coronet Peak''s 2026 early and full-season opening. IF: travel_date >= 27_JUNE_2026 AND: travel_date <= 11_OCTOBER_2026 AND: traveler_interest == THE_REMARKABLES THEN: use_2026_SEASON_BASELINE AND: verify_DAILY_TERRAIN + ROAD + LIFT_STATUS Reason: The Remarkables'' official 2026 season is scheduled from 27 June through 11 October, with daily operations approximately 09:00–16:00 subject to conditions. IF: traveler_interest == NIGHT_SKI THEN: check_CORONET_PEAK_CURRENT_NIGHT_SKI_CALENDAR AND: do_NOT_ASSUME_NIGHT_SKI_DAILY Reason: Night skiing operates only on selected dates rather than throughout every winter evening. IF: traveler_self_drives_TO_SKIFIELD THEN: check_ROAD_REPORT + SNOW + ICE + CHAINS + PARKING AND: carry_AND_KNOW_HOW_TO_USE_CHAINS_WHEN_REQUIRED Reason: Queenstown ski-field access roads can require winter-driving preparation and conditions may change quickly. IF: traveler_is_UNCOMFORTABLE_WITH_WINTER_DRIVING THEN: prefer_SKIBUS_OR_OPERATOR_TRANSFER OVER: SELF_DRIVE_TO_SKIFIELD Reason: Dedicated ski transport reduces chain, parking and mountain-road stress for travelers without winter-driving experience. IF: traveler_type == NON_SKIER AND: season == WINTER THEN: prioritize_SNOWPLAY + GONDOLA_SIGHTSEEING + SPA + ARROWTOWN + WINE + LAKE_CRUISE + DINING Reason: Queenstown remains a strong winter destination for non-skiers because alpine sightseeing, snowplay, food, wine and wellness continue alongside skiing. IF: season == DECEMBER_TO_FEBRUARY THEN: increase_HIKING + CYCLING + LAKE_ACTIVITIES + GLENORCHY + JET_BOATING + OUTDOOR_DINING AND: book_PEAK_SUMMER_PRODUCTS_EARLIER Reason: Queenstown summer offers long daylight and strong outdoor conditions, but Christmas, New Year and summer holidays create higher accommodation and activity demand. IF: season == MARCH_TO_MAY THEN: increase_ARROWTOWN + PHOTOGRAPHY + WINE + HIKING + CYCLING AND: retain_WARM_LAYERS_FOR_COOLER_MORNINGS_AND_EVENINGS Reason: Autumn combines distinctive colour, generally strong outdoor sightseeing and wine experiences with cooler temperatures and comparatively balanced visitor pressure. IF: season == SEPTEMBER_TO_NOVEMBER THEN: combine_LATE_SKIIING_IF_OPEN + HIKING + CYCLING + WINE + GOLF + SCENIC_TOURING AND: retain_HIGH_WEATHER_FLEXIBILITY Reason: Queenstown spring can offer snow-covered peaks alongside increasingly green valleys and multiple seasonal activities, but weather remains changeable. IF: weather == NORMAL_SHOWERS THEN: retain_FLEXIBLE_QUEENSTOWN_PROGRAM AND: move_BETWEEN_OUTDOOR + WINE + FOOD + SPA + INDOOR_ACTIVITIES_AS_CONDITIONS_CHANGE Reason: Ordinary alpine weather changes do not automatically require cancelling an entire Queenstown sightseeing day. IF: weather == HEAVY_CONTINUOUS_RAIN THEN: recheck_RIVER_ACTIVITIES + HIKING + GLENORCHY_ROADS + SCENIC_AVIATION AND: replace_WITH_WINE + SPA + DINING + SHOPPING + INDOOR_ADVENTURE_WHERE_NEEDED Reason: Heavy rain can affect river levels, trail surfaces, road conditions and aviation while Queenstown still retains strong indoor and culinary alternatives. IF: weather == STRONG_WIND THEN: recheck_SKYLINE + SCENIC_FLIGHTS + HELICOPTERS + PARAGLIDING + LAKE_CRUISES + SKI_LIFTS Reason: Wind can materially affect elevated, airborne, marine and mountain experiences even when rainfall is limited. IF: weather == LOW_CLOUD_OR_POOR_VISIBILITY THEN: recheck_HELICOPTER + FIXED_WING + ALPINE_SIGHTSEEING_PRODUCTS AND: do_NOT_GUARANTEE_SCENIC_FLIGHT_OPERATION Reason: Scenic aviation requires suitable visibility and safe flying conditions and can be delayed or cancelled by weather. IF: weather == HEAVY_SNOW_OR_ICE THEN: recheck_AIRPORT_TRANSFER + SKI_ROADS + GLENORCHY_ROAD + REGIONAL_DRIVING AND: allow_ADDITIONAL_TRANSPORT_BUFFER Reason: Snow and ice can affect mountain roads, regional routes, airport journeys and activity transfers. IF: weather == SEVERE_WEATHER_WARNING THEN: suspend_NONESSENTIAL_ALPINE_HIKES + REMOTE_DRIVES + SCENIC_AVIATION + UNSAFE_WATER_ACTIVITIES AND: follow_METservice + DOC + NZSKI + ROAD_AND_OPERATOR_GUIDANCE Reason: Official weather and operator safety information should override fixed tourism schedules during severe alpine conditions. IF: route == QUEENSTOWN_AIRPORT_TO_CBD AND: traveler_type == BUDGET_OR_INDEPENDENT THEN: consider_ORBUS_PUBLIC_BUS AND: use_BEE_CARD_FOR_LOWEST_STANDARD_CURRENT_FARE_WHEN_PRACTICAL Reason: Queenstown Airport is served by the local Orbus network, providing the lowest-cost standard transfer option for suitable travelers. IF: route == QUEENSTOWN_AIRPORT_TO_CBD AND: traveler_type == FAMILY_OR_LUXURY_OR_SENIOR THEN: prefer_TAXI + UBER + SHUTTLE + PREBOOKED_PRIVATE_TRANSFER_BASED_ON_COMFORT Reason: Door-to-door transport reduces luggage handling and provides simpler arrival logistics for families, premium travelers and mobility-limited visitors. IF: route == QUEENSTOWN_AIRPORT_TO_CBD THEN: allow_FRANKTON_TRAFFIC_BUFFER AND: avoid_FIXED_MAJOR_ACTIVITY_IMMEDIATELY_AFTER_INTERNATIONAL_ARRIVAL Reason: The airport is close to Queenstown, but traffic, immigration, baggage, weather and peak visitor periods can materially extend total arrival time. IF: movement == CENTRAL_QUEENSTOWN THEN: prefer_WALKING AND: use_ORBUS_OR_TAXI_OR_RIDESHARE_FOR_STEEP_OR_LONGER_CONNECTIONS Reason: Queenstown Bay, The Mall, Steamer Wharf, restaurants, Gardens and Skyline base form a compact central sightseeing cluster. IF: movement == QUEENSTOWN_BUS THEN: use_BEE_CARD_OR_CASH AND: do_NOT_ASSUME_STANDARD_BANK_CARD_PAYMENT_ON_BUS Reason: Current Orbus guidance states that Queenstown buses accept Bee Card or cash and not standard bank or credit-card payment onboard. IF: movement == QUEENSTOWN_AIRPORT_BUS THEN: prefer_BEE_CARD_FOR_REPEATED_OR_VALUE_FOCUSED_TRAVEL Reason: The current adult Bee Card airport fare is substantially lower than the adult airport cash fare. IF: movement == QUEENSTOWN_FERRY THEN: verify_CURRENT_FERRY_ROUTE + TIMETABLE + FARE + PAYMENT_METHOD Reason: Queenstown ferry services have different fare and payment arrangements from standard buses and should be checked independently. IF: trip_length <= 3 nights THEN: avoid_FULL_STAY_RENTAL_CAR_IF_ITINERARY_IS_CENTRAL + SKYLINE + SHOTOVER + CRUISE AND: use_WALKING + ORBUS + OPERATOR_SHUTTLES + SELECTIVE_TAXI Reason: Parking and rental costs often provide limited additional value when a short itinerary is concentrated around central Queenstown and transport-supported activities. IF: trip_length >= 4 nights AND: traveler_interest == GLENORCHY_OR_MOKE_LAKE_OR_MULTIPLE_REGIONAL_EXCURSIONS THEN: consider_RENTAL_CAR_OR_PRIVATE_TOUR_FOR_SELECTED_DAYS AND: avoid_PAYING_FOR_UNUSED_CENTRAL_CAR_DAYS_IF_NOT_REQUIRED Reason: A private vehicle becomes more valuable when the itinerary expands to dispersed regional scenery rather than central sightseeing. IF: traveler_self_drives THEN: account_FOR_LEFT_SIDE_DRIVING + ALPINE_ROADS + PARKING + WEATHER + WINTER_CHAINS + CAR_SECURITY AND: avoid_LEAVING_VISIBLE_VALUABLES_IN_VEHICLE Reason: Self-driving increases regional flexibility but creates additional road, parking, weather and vehicle-security responsibilities. IF: traveler_self_drives AND: season == WINTER THEN: increase_ROAD_CONDITION_CHECKS + CHAIN_PREPARATION + EXTRA_TRAVEL_TIME Reason: Queenstown''s winter environment can introduce snow, ice and mountain-road restrictions not encountered during ordinary urban driving. IF: traveler_interest == PHOTOGRAPHY THEN: prioritize_BOBS_PEAK + GLENORCHY_ROAD + MOKE_LAKE + ARROWTOWN + LAKE_WHAKATIPU AND: schedule_BASED_ON_LIGHT + SEASON + WEATHER Reason: Queenstown''s photographic strength comes from combining alpine peaks, reflective lakes, autumn colours, snow, historic streets and dramatic road landscapes. IF: traveler_interest == AUTUMN_PHOTOGRAPHY THEN: prioritize_ARROWTOWN + LAKE_HAYES + QUEENSTOWN_GARDENS + GIBBSTON Reason: Autumn transforms parts of the Whakatipu Basin into strong red, orange and gold landscapes particularly suited to photography. IF: traveler_interest == FOOD THEN: include_MODERN_NEW_ZEALAND + CENTRAL_OTAGO_WINE + LOCAL_PRODUCE + CASUAL_LOCAL_FAVOURITES AND: retain_ONE_PREMIUM_RESTAURANT_EXPERIENCE_IF_BUDGET_ALLOWS Reason: Queenstown combines a major resort restaurant scene with Central Otago wine and diverse dining beyond stereotypical pub food. IF: traveler_interest == NIGHTLIFE THEN: combine_CENTRAL_DINNER + BARS_OR_APRES + SAFE_LATE_TRANSPORT AND: reduce_LATE_NIGHT_ALCOHOL_IF_EARLY_SKI_HIKE_OR_DRIVE_NEXT_DAY Reason: Queenstown has strong resort nightlife, but fatigue and alcohol can materially affect the safety and enjoyment of early outdoor programs. IF: traveler_interest == SHOPPING THEN: combine_QUEENSTOWN_CBD + ARROWTOWN_BOUTIQUES AND: use_FRANKTON_FOR_PRACTICAL_LARGER_RETAIL_REQUIREMENTS Reason: Queenstown offers visitor-oriented boutiques and outdoor retail in town while Frankton provides broader practical shopping. IF: traveler_interest == HERITAGE THEN: prioritize_ARROWTOWN + CHINESE_SETTLEMENT + LAKES_DISTRICT_MUSEUM + TSS_EARNSLAW Reason: Queenstown''s strongest heritage experiences combine gold-rush settlement history, Chinese mining heritage and Lake Whakatipu transport history. IF: traveler_interest == RELAXATION THEN: prioritize_LAKEFRONT + SPA_OR_HOT_POOL + WINE + SCENIC_CRUISE + EASY_WALKS AND: reduce_MULTIPLE_ADRENALINE_PRODUCTS Reason: Queenstown can function as a highly effective scenic relaxation destination despite its adventure-capital reputation. IF: traveler_interest == FIRST_TIME_QUEENSTOWN THEN: prioritize_QUEENSTOWN_BAY + SKYLINE_BOBS_PEAK + ONE_SIGNATURE_ADVENTURE AND: add_ARROWTOWN_OR_GIBBSTON_OR_GLENORCHY_BASED_ON_TRAVEL_STYLE Reason: These experiences provide Queenstown''s strongest first introduction to lake scenery, alpine geography, adventure identity and surrounding regional diversity. IF: traveler_interest == FIRST_TIME_NEW_ZEALAND THEN: use_QUEENSTOWN_FOR_ALPINE_SCENERY + ADVENTURE + CENTRAL_OTAGO_WINE + SOUTH_ISLAND_OUTDOOR_EXPERIENCE AND: continue_TO_OTHER_NEW_ZEALAND_REGIONS_IF_GEOTHERMAL + MAJOR_MAORI_CULTURAL + TROPICAL_COASTAL_OR_LARGE_CITY_EXPERIENCE_IS_REQUIRED Reason: Queenstown provides an exceptional introduction to New Zealand''s alpine South Island identity but should not be treated as a substitute for every landscape and cultural experience elsewhere in the country. IF: traveler_type == SENIOR THEN: prefer_CENTRAL_OR_ACCESSIBLE_HOTEL + SHORT_SCENIC_WALKS + CRUISE + ARROWTOWN + PRIVATE_OR_TAXI_SUPPORT AND: reduce_BEN_LOMOND + MULTIPLE_EXTREME_ADVENTURES + LONG_UNBROKEN_ROAD_DAYS Reason: Queenstown is highly rewarding for seniors at resort and scenic level, but mountain terrain and adventure activities can rapidly increase physical intensity. IF: traveler_uses_WHEELCHAIR THEN: prefer_VERIFIED_ACCESSIBLE_HOTEL + ACCESSIBLE_TRANSPORT + QUEENSTOWN_GARDENS_OR_LAKEFRONT + VERIFIED_ATTRACTIONS AND: verify_EACH_BOAT + SKI + TRAIL + WINERY + ADVENTURE_ACTIVITY_SEPARATELY Reason: Queenstown offers a growing range of inclusive experiences, but accessibility varies sharply between central infrastructure and natural alpine terrain. IF: traveler_uses_WHEELCHAIR AND: plan_includes_SKYLINE THEN: verify_CURRENT_GONDOLA_ACCESS + STAFF_ASSISTANCE + SELECTED_PRODUCT_ACCESSIBILITY Reason: Skyline provides accessible visitor infrastructure, but Gondola, Luge, dining and other activities should still be evaluated individually. IF: traveler_uses_WHEELCHAIR AND: plan_includes_GIBBSTON_TRAIL THEN: consider_GIBBSTON_RIVER_WINE_TRAIL_WITH_CURRENT_ACCESS_CHECK Reason: Official Queenstown accessibility information identifies the Gibbston River Wine Trail as one of the region''s more accessible trail options. IF: traveler_interest == FESTIVALS THEN: verify_CURRENT_EVENT_DATES + VENUE + TRANSPORT + HOTEL_DEMAND + ROAD_CONTROLS AND: reduce_NORMAL_SIGHTSEEING_DENSITY_WHERE_REQUIRED Reason: Queenstown''s major winter, sporting and seasonal events can materially change accommodation demand, nightlife and transport conditions. IF: travel_dates_overlap_ARROWTOWN_AUTUMN_FESTIVAL THEN: increase_ARROWTOWN_TIME AND: allow_EXTRA_TRAFFIC + PARKING + CROWD_BUFFER Reason: The Arrowtown Autumn Festival is a major seasonal draw and can substantially increase local visitor pressure. IF: travel_dates_overlap_SNOW_MACHINE_OR_MAJOR_WINTER_EVENT THEN: book_ACCOMMODATION_AND_NIGHTLIFE_EARLY AND: allow_EXTRA_CENTRAL_AND_SKIFIELD_DEMAND Reason: Large winter festivals combine ski activity with nightlife and can significantly increase Queenstown''s peak-period visitor pressure. IF: travel_dates_overlap_QUEENSTOWN_MARATHON THEN: verify_ROAD_CLOSURES + TRAIL_IMPACTS + TRANSPORT_CHANGES AND: avoid_TIGHT_FIXED_TRANSFER_ASSUMPTIONS Reason: Major running events can affect roads, trails and normal local transport patterns. IF: traveler_has_FLIGHT_DEPARTURE AND: same_day_plan_includes_GLENORCHY_OR_SKIFIELD_OR_REMOTE_ACTIVITY THEN: build_SUBSTANTIAL_RETURN_BUFFER AND: prefer_CENTRAL_OR_NEAR_AIRPORT_ACTIVITY_LATER_IN_DAY Reason: Regional roads, snow, activity delays and traffic can compromise fixed airport timing when remote sightseeing is scheduled too late. IF: traveler_has_INTERNATIONAL_DEPARTURE THEN: follow_AIRLINE_AND_QUEENSTOWN_AIRPORT_CHECK_IN_GUIDANCE AND: do_NOT_USE_MINIMUM_DRIVING_TIME_AS_TOTAL_AIRPORT_BUFFER Reason: Airport journeys must include road conditions, luggage, check-in, security and international-processing requirements rather than only vehicle travel time. IF: traveler_interest == REPEAT_QUEENSTOWN THEN: prioritize_MOKE_LAKE + BEN_LOMOND_OR_ADVANCED_HIKE + DEEPER_GLENORCHY + QUEENSTOWN_TRAIL + SPECIALIST_WINE_OR_ADVENTURE AND: reduce_REPEAT_ONLY_SKYLINE_AND_STANDARD_CBD_SIGHTSEEING Reason: Queenstown becomes substantially richer for repeat visitors when itineraries move beyond the headline resort attractions into trails, valleys and specialist regional experiences.', 3687),
  ('queenstown', 34, 'destination-scoring', 'DESTINATION SCORING', NULL, NULL, '| Factor | Score | | --- | --- | | Family | 96 | | Honeymoon | 97 | | Luxury | 96 | | Budget | 64 | | Adventure | 97 | | Culture | 78 | | Food | 93 | | Shopping | 82 | | Nightlife | 94 | | Relaxation | 95 | | Nature | 97 | | Accessibility | 80 | | Safety | 88 | | First-time visitor | 96 | | Photography | 97 |', 3688),
  ('queenstown', 35, 'final-travel-agent-verdict', 'FINAL TRAVEL AGENT VERDICT', NULL, NULL, 'Best traveler profiles: 1. First-time New Zealand / South Island traveler (Lake Whakatipu, Queenstown Bay, Skyline Queenstown, Shotover Jet, Arrowtown, Gibbston, Southern Alps scenery) 2. Adventure traveler (Kawarau Bungy, Nevis Bungy, Shotover Jet, skydiving, rafting, paragliding, canyoning, mountain biking, hiking) 3. Honeymoon / romantic traveler (lake-view hotels, alpine lodges, private hot pools, scenic helicopters, Gibbston vineyards, Glenorchy drives, fine dining) 4. Ski / snowboard traveler (Coronet Peak, The Remarkables, ski buses, snow schools, après-ski, alpine dining, winter events) 5. Nature / alpine-landscape traveler (Lake Whakatipu, Glenorchy, Paradise, Moke Lake, Ben Lomond, Queenstown Hill, Southern Alps, nearby national-park gateways) 6. Food / wine traveler (Gibbston vineyards, Central Otago Pinot Noir, winery restaurants, Queenstown fine dining, Arrowtown cafés, craft beer) 7. Family traveler (Skyline Gondola, Luge, Kiwi Park, TSS Earnslaw, Walter Peak, Queenstown Gardens, Arrowtown, age-appropriate adventure activities) 8. Photography traveler (Lake Whakatipu, Bob''s Peak, The Remarkables, Glenorchy, Moke Lake, Arrowtown autumn colour, Kawarau Gorge, alpine snow scenery) 9. Luxury traveler (five-star lakefront hotels, alpine lodges, helicopter touring, private boats, bespoke ski experiences, premium wine tours, chauffeured transfers) 10. Independent / repeat traveler (Glenorchy, Paradise, Moke Lake, Lake Hayes, Gibbston, Arrowtown, advanced hiking, cycling, mountain biking, deeper Southern Lakes exploration) Best duration: 4–6 nights 1–2 nights: Best for QUEENSTOWN_BAY + SKYLINE_BOBS_PEAK + ONE_MAJOR_ADVENTURE with either ARROWTOWN or one concentrated Lake Whakatipu experience. 3–4 nights: Best for BALANCED_FIRST_VISIT, adding SHOTOVER_OR_BUNGY + ARROWTOWN + GIBBSTON_OR_WALTER_PEAK + central Queenstown dining and one scenic alpine experience. 5–6 nights: Best for DEEPER_QUEENSTOWN including GLENORCHY + ARROWTOWN + GIBBSTON + SKYLINE + LAKE_WHAKATIPU + ADVENTURE + HIKING_OR_CYCLING + optional skiing according to season. 7+ nights: Best when Queenstown is treated as a SOUTHERN_LAKES_ADVENTURE_BASE, combining the town with Glenorchy, Paradise, multiple ski days, deeper wine touring, Moke Lake, regional hiking, mountain biking, Milford Sound / Fiordland excursions or wider South Island travel. Best season: YEAR_ROUND_WITH_STRONG_SEASONAL_ACTIVITY_DIFFERENTIATION Summer / Peak Outdoor Season (December – February): HIKING + CYCLING + LAKE_ACTIVITIES + JET_BOATING + BUNGY + GLENORCHY + SCENIC_FLIGHTS + WINE_TOURING + LONG_DAYLIGHT, with stronger Christmas / New Year and summer-holiday accommodation pressure. Autumn / Prime Scenic Shoulder Season (March – May): AUTUMN_COLOUR + ARROWTOWN + WINE + HIKING + CYCLING + PHOTOGRAPHY + ROAD_TRIPS + LOWER_POST_SUMMER_PRESSURE + INCREASINGLY_COOL_EVENINGS. Winter / Peak Ski Season (June – August): SKIING + SNOWBOARDING + CORONET_PEAK + THE_REMARKABLES + ALPINE_SCENERY + APRES_SKI + HOT_POOLS + WINTER_EVENTS, with high ski-season accommodation demand and weather-dependent mountain access. Spring / Mixed Adventure Season (September – November): LATE_SEASON_SKIING + HIKING + CYCLING + GOLF + WINE + WATER_ADVENTURE + SNOW_CAPPED_PHOTOGRAPHY + LONGER_DAYLIGHT + VARIABLE_ALPINE_WEATHER. March, April, May, October and November generally provide some of Queenstown''s strongest balances for sightseeing, adventure, photography and value outside peak summer and peak ski demand. December through February provide Queenstown''s strongest long-day hiking, cycling, lake and outdoor-adventure conditions but generally require earlier booking around Christmas, New Year and summer holiday periods. June through August are critical for Queenstown''s ski identity and remain exceptionally strong for alpine travel, but accommodation, ski products and mountain transport require much earlier planning. September can provide a distinctive crossover where skiing may continue while lower-elevation cycling, golf, wine and spring sightseeing become increasingly viable. Queenstown should therefore be treated as a genuine FOUR_SEASON_ALPINE_RESORT_AND_ADVENTURE_DESTINATION rather than a destination dependent only on winter skiing or summer hiking. Best hotel strategy: Choose accommodation according to lake views, walking convenience, nightlife, parking, ski transport, family requirements, mobility, airport access and whether multiple regional road trips are included. For first-time visitors: QUEENSTOWN_CBD / QUEENSTOWN_BAY / LAKE_ESPLANADE / CENTRAL_FRANKTON_ROAD_APPROACH for efficient access to restaurants, nightlife, lake cruises, Skyline, activity pick-ups and central sightseeing. For adventure travel: CBD / SHOTOVER_STREET / BRECON_STREET_APPROACH for easy operator check-ins, activity buses, Skyline access, nightlife and flexible daily departures. For luxury: CENTRAL_LAKEFRONT / KELVIN_HEIGHTS / PREMIUM_FRANKTON_ROAD / SECLUDED_ALPINE_LODGES for lake views, privacy, helicopter access, chauffeurs, spa experiences and premium dining. For honeymoon / romantic travel: LAKEFRONT_QUEENSTOWN / KELVIN_HEIGHTS / ARROWTOWN / LUXURY_LODGE_PROPERTIES for mountain views, privacy, fine dining, wine, hot pools and scenic-drive access. For ski travel: CBD_OR_FRANKTON_BASE with practical ski-bus access, equipment storage, drying facilities and efficient road access toward CORONET_PEAK_OR_THE_REMARKABLES. For food / nightlife: QUEENSTOWN_CBD / BEACH_STREET / THE_MALL / SHOTOVER_STREET_APPROACH for restaurants, bars, après-ski, late-night venues and walkable evenings. For families: CENTRAL_QUEENSTOWN / FRANKTON / KELVIN_HEIGHTS depending whether walking convenience, apartment space, parking, lake recreation or airport proximity is more important. For road-trip travelers: Do not automatically keep a rental car throughout a purely central stay; QUEENSTOWN_CBD + SKYLINE + LAKE_CRUISE + SHOTOVER_OPERATOR_TRANSFERS can often be completed without daily self-driving. Avoid changing hotels unnecessarily; one well-located Queenstown base can efficiently support Queenstown Bay + Skyline + Shotover + Arrowtown + Gibbston + Glenorchy, while a second lodge or Glenorchy-area overnight should be added only when wilderness immersion, privacy, hiking or luxury positioning justifies the hotel change. Best transportation: Use: Queenstown transportation should primarily be treated as: WALKING_FOR_CENTRAL_QUEENSTOWN + ORBUS_FOR_LOCAL_NETWORK + SHUTTLES_FOR_ACTIVITY_AND_SKI_ACCESS + RIDESHARE_FOR_CONVENIENCE + PRIVATE_OR_RENTAL_CAR_FOR_OUTER_REGION. Queenstown Airport transportation baseline: QUEENSTOWN_AIRPORT_ZQN + ORBUS_PUBLIC_BUS + TAXI + RIDESHARE + SHUTTLE + VIP_PRIVATE_TRANSFER + RENTAL_CAR. Queenstown Airport positioning: APPROXIMATELY_20_MINUTES_TO_DOWNTOWN_QUEENSTOWN under favourable standard road conditions + APPROXIMATELY_30_MINUTES_TO_NEAREST_MAJOR_SKIFIELD_POSITIONING + FRANKTON_LOCATION + DIRECT_ACCESS_TO_LOCAL_BUS_NETWORK. Actual transfer time must retain traffic contingency because Frankton, State Highway 6, winter traffic, roadworks and peak visitor periods can materially alter journey time. Current Queenstown Airport public-bus baseline: ORBUS + AIRPORT_TERMINAL_BUS_STOPS + DIRECT_AND_CONNECTING_SERVICES + FRANKTON_BUS_INTERCHANGE + QUEENSTOWN_CBD + APPROXIMATELY_15_MINUTE_AIRPORT_SERVICE_POSITIONING. Current Orbus Queenstown bus-fare baseline: ADULT_BEE_CARD: NZD_2.50 ADULT_CASH: NZD_4.00 AIRPORT_ADULT_BEE_CARD: NZD_2.50 AIRPORT_ADULT_CASH: NZD_10.00. Current child, youth, Community Connect and SuperGold concessions remain operator-specific and must be reverified. Queenstown bus payment baseline: BEE_CARD OR CASH. BANK_CARD_OR_CREDIT_CARD_PAYMENT_ON_STANDARD_ORBUS_BUSES: NOT_ACCEPTED. Bee Card provides the lower standard fare and should be considered for travelers making multiple local bus journeys. Queenstown ferry baseline: BEE_CARD OR SUPPORTED_BANK_CARD may be used according to current Orbus ferry arrangements, with fares different from standard bus travel. Bus, ferry, Bee Card, concession and route arrangements remain operational information and must be rechecked before production use. Accessibility baseline: CENTRAL_QUEENSTOWN: MODERATE_HIGH_ACCESSIBILITY + MODERN_HOTELS + ACCESSIBLE_RESTAURANTS + LAKEFRONT_AREAS + VARIABLE_HILLS_AND_GRADIENTS. QUEENSTOWN_AIRPORT: ACCESSIBLE_TERMINAL + PUBLIC_TRANSPORT_OPTIONS + TAXI_AND_PRIVATE_TRANSFER + SPECIAL_ASSISTANCE_COORDINATION. QUEENSTOWN_GARDENS_AND_SELECTED_LAKEFRONT_TRAILS: RELATIVELY_ACCESSIBLE_SECTIONS + LOW_GRADIENT_RECREATION + SURFACE_CONDITIONS_REQUIRE_ROUTE_SELECTION. SKYLINE_QUEENSTOWN: ACCESSIBLE_GONDOLA_FACILITIES + STAFF_SUPPORT + ACTIVITY_SPECIFIC_LIMITATIONS. TSS_EARNSLAW_AND_WALTER_PEAK: SELECTED_WHEELCHAIR_ACCESS + BOARDING_SUPPORT + NO_ACCESSIBLE_TOILET_ON_TSS_EARNSLAW + WALTER_PEAK_GOURMET_BBQ_ACCESSIBLE. BEN_LOMOND: STEEP + HIGH_FITNESS_REQUIRED + SIGNIFICANT_ELEVATION_GAIN + NOT_SUITABLE_FOR_UNIFORM_STEP_FREE_CLASSIFICATION. MOKE_LAKE: NATURAL_UNEVEN_TERRAIN + GRAVEL_ROAD_ACCESS + WEATHER_EXPOSURE + LIMITED_FORMAL_ACCESSIBILITY. SKI_AREAS: ACCESSIBILITY_VARIES_BY_TRANSPORT + SNOW_CONDITIONS + EQUIPMENT + INDIVIDUAL_ACTIVITY, although adaptive-snow opportunities exist within Queenstown''s wider inclusive-tourism offering. Accessible rooms, ski transport, boats, hiking routes, vineyards, adventure products and individual activity requirements should be verified before confirmation. Must-do for first-time visitor: Queenstown should not be reduced to bungy jumping and skiing alone; its essential tourism identity is: LAKE_WHAKATIPU + SOUTHERN_ALPS + WORLD_CLASS_ADVENTURE + SKI_AND_SNOW + CENTRAL_OTAGO_WINE + HIKING_AND_CYCLING + ALPINE_LUXURY + GLENORCHY_WILDERNESS + ARROWTOWN_HERITAGE + FOOD_AND_NIGHTLIFE. Don''t-do: Current Queenstown Airport operational baseline: SINGLE_TERMINAL + DOMESTIC_AND_INTERNATIONAL_OPERATIONS + PUBLIC_BUS + TAXI + RIDESHARE + SHUTTLE + RENTAL_CAR + CAMPERVAN_HIRE. Current terminal baseline: OPEN_DAILY_APPROXIMATELY: 04:00–22:30. OVERNIGHT_TERMINAL_STAY: NOT_PERMITTED. Airport Information Desk baseline: APPROXIMATELY_09:00–17:00_DAILY. Flight schedules, terminal operating arrangements, border-processing requirements, airline check-in times and ground transport must be reverified before travel. Current Orbus Queenstown fare baseline: ADULT_LOCAL_BUS_BEE_CARD: NZD_2.50 ADULT_LOCAL_BUS_CASH: NZD_4.00 ADULT_AIRPORT_BUS_BEE_CARD: NZD_2.50 ADULT_AIRPORT_BUS_CASH: NZD_10.00 CHILD_5_TO_12_BEE_CARD: NZD_1.50 YOUTH_13_TO_18_BEE_CARD: NZD_1.50. Current fares remain subject to review and should not be treated as permanently fixed. Queenstown ferry fare baseline: ADULT_BEE_CARD_SINGLE_TRIP: NZD_10.00 ADULT_BANK_CARD_SINGLE_TRIP: NZD_14.00. Current ferry network, service frequency and fare policy should be rechecked before itinerary production. Coronet Peak 2026 operational baseline: 2026_SEASON: 29_MAY_2026 – 04_OCTOBER_2026 EARLY_WINTER_OPERATION_POSITIONING: 29_MAY – 12_JUNE_2026 STANDARD_NZSKI_LIFT_OPERATION_BASELINE: APPROXIMATELY_09:00–16:00 on operational days. NIGHT_SKI_BASELINE: SELECTED_WEDNESDAYS_AND_FRIDAYS + LATE_JUNE_TO_EARLY_SEPTEMBER_POSITIONING + SELECTED_SCHOOL_HOLIDAY_DATES + APPROXIMATELY_16:00–21:00 where scheduled. The 2026 Coronet Peak season introduced / promoted: NEW_SNOW_FACTORY + EXPANDED_KIDSZONE + UPGRADED_RENTAL_EQUIPMENT + ADDITIONAL_SKIBUS_CAPACITY + UPDATED_TRAIL_MAPPING. Ski-field opening, lifts, terrain, night skiing, snowmaking, roads, lessons and events remain weather and operationally dependent. The Remarkables planning baseline: MAJOR_QUEENSTOWN_SKIFIELD + SKIING + SNOWBOARDING + BEGINNER_TERRAIN + ALPINE_SCENERY + NZSKI_OPERATIONS + QUEENSTOWN_SKIBUS_ACCESS. Standard NZSki winter lift-operating baseline is approximately: 09:00–16:00 on operational days, but actual season dates, lift status, road access, snow cover and weather closures must be checked directly before confirmation. Current NZSki Queenstown ski-transport baseline: QUEENSTOWN_SKIBUS + CORONET_PEAK + THE_REMARKABLES + ADVANCE_BOOKING_RECOMMENDED + CAPACITY_DEPENDENT. Private vehicles heading to ski fields must retain: WINTER_ROAD_CONDITION_CHECK + CHAIN_REQUIREMENT_CHECK + WEATHER_CHECK + PARKING_AVAILABILITY_CHECK. Skyline Queenstown operational baseline: GONDOLA + BOBS_PEAK + LUGE + DINING + VIEWPOINTS + SEASONAL_MOUNTAIN_BIKING + SELECTED_ADDITIONAL_ACTIVITIES. Opening hours vary by attraction and date and should therefore NOT be stored as one permanent daily operating schedule. Current September 2026 operational information confirms: MOUNTAIN_BIKE_UPLIFT: WINTER_CLOSURE + REOPENING_POSITIONED_FROM_19_SEPTEMBER_2026. Gondola, Luge, restaurant, café and mountain-bike schedules require date-specific verification. Shotover Jet operational baseline: LOCATION: ARTHURS_POINT OPERATION: 7_DAYS_PER_WEEK + WEATHER_AND_RIVER_CONDITIONS_PERMITTING. STANDARD_TRIP_WINDOW: APPROXIMATELY_09:30_OR_10:00_TO_16:00 depending current timetable. JET_BOAT_RIDE: APPROXIMATELY_25_MINUTES. TOTAL_EXPERIENCE_ALLOWANCE: APPROXIMATELY_1_HOUR_OR_MORE. CHECK_IN: APPROXIMATELY_30_MINUTES_PRIOR_AT_RIVER_BASE. SELECTED_COMPLIMENTARY_SHUTTLES_FROM_CENTRAL_QUEENSTOWN: AVAILABLE_ON_SELECTED_DEPARTURES. CHRISTMAS_DAY: CLOSED under current published operating baseline. Heavy rainfall, flooding and unsafe river conditions can postpone or cancel operations. Kawarau Bungy operational baseline: WORLD_HOME_OF_BUNGY + FIRST_COMMERCIAL_BUNGY_SITE_1988 + KAWARAU_GORGE_SUSPENSION_BRIDGE + 43_METRE_BUNGY + KAWARAU_SWING + KAWARAU_ZIPRIDE + VIEWING_DECK. Current seasonal operating baseline: SUMMER / OCTOBER_TO_APRIL: APPROXIMATELY_08:30–17:00 WINTER / MAY_TO_SEPTEMBER: APPROXIMATELY_09:00–16:30. Last activity is generally scheduled before closing and current check-in times apply. Kawarau Bungy participant baseline includes: MINIMUM_AND_MAXIMUM_WEIGHT_REQUIREMENTS + TANDEM_WEIGHT_RULES + MEDICAL_CONDITION_DISCLOSURE + PHOTO_ID + OPERATOR_SAFETY_APPROVAL. These conditions must be checked for the individual traveler before booking. Nevis adventure baseline: NEVIS_BUNGY + NEVIS_SWING + NEVIS_CATAPULT + REMOTE_NEVis_VALLEY_LOCATION + OPERATOR_4WD_TRANSPORT_REQUIRED_FOR_STANDARD_GUEST_ACCESS. NEVIS_BUNGY_HEIGHT: 134_METRES. Independent self-driving directly to the operational Nevis activity site should not be assumed; current operator transport rules must be followed. TSS Earnslaw / Walter Peak baseline: TSS_EARNSLAW + 1912_VINTAGE_STEAMSHIP + LAKE_WHAKATIPU + WALTER_PEAK_HIGH_COUNTRY_FARM + SCENIC_CRUISING + HERITAGE + FARM_EXPERIENCES + DINING. QUEENSTOWN_TO_WALTER_PEAK_CRUISE: APPROXIMATELY_45_MINUTES_EACH_DIRECTION_POSITIONING. TSS Earnslaw is generally scheduled to operate throughout the year except during annual survey / maintenance periods. 2026 scheduled maintenance baseline: 18_MAY_2026 – 26_JUNE_2026. During this maintenance period, Walter Peak experiences were scheduled to use the SPIRIT_OF_QUEENSTOWN catamaran rather than TSS Earnslaw. This maintenance window must NOT be copied into future years without re-verification. TSS Earnslaw accessibility baseline: WHEELCHAIR_ACCESSIBLE_BOARDING_SUPPORT_AVAILABLE + NO_ACCESSIBLE_TOILET_ON_VINTAGE_STEAMSHIP + ASSISTANCE_REQUIREMENTS_SHOULD_BE_COMMUNICATED_AT_BOOKING. Walter Peak Gourmet BBQ Dining baseline: WHEELCHAIR_ACCESSIBLE. Specific farm, horse, dining and cruise products require individual accessibility confirmation. Ben Lomond operational and hiking baseline: TIKI_TRAIL_TO_BEN_LOMOND_SUMMIT: APPROXIMATELY_14_KM_RETURN + APPROXIMATELY_6_TO_8_HOURS + APPROXIMATELY_1,438_METRES_ELEVATION_GAIN_FROM_QUEENSTOWN + HIGH_FITNESS_REQUIRED + STEEP_GRADIENT. The route can be accessed from central Queenstown / Tiki Trail or via Skyline-assisted positioning. Ben Lomond conditions should be treated as: ALPINE + WEATHER_DEPENDENT + SEASONALLY_SNOW_OR_ICE_AFFECTED + DAYLIGHT_DEPENDENT + FITNESS_SENSITIVE. Walkers should carry sufficient food, water, clothing, navigation / communication equipment and a headtorch according to conditions. Moke Lake operational baseline: MOKE_LAKE_LOOP + MOUNTAIN_LAKE + GRASSLAND + WETLAND + WALKING + PHOTOGRAPHY + CAMPING_CONTEXT. Road access baseline: QUEENSTOWN_GLENORCHY_ROAD + MOKE_LAKE_ROAD + STEEP_AND_WINDING_SECTION + UNSEALED_GRAVEL_FINAL_APPROACH. Mountain-biking baseline: NOT_ALL_LOOP_SECTIONS_OPEN_TO_BIKES + PENINSULA_RESTRICTIONS_DUE_TO_EROSION + CURRENT_SIGNAGE_REQUIRED. Moke Lake should therefore not be marketed as a fully sealed, universally accessible roadside lake attraction. Arrowtown baseline: APPROXIMATELY_19_KM_FROM_QUEENSTOWN + APPROXIMATELY_20_MINUTES_STANDARD_DRIVING_POSITIONING + HISTORIC_GOLD_MINING_TOWN + BUCKINGHAM_STREET + LAKES_DISTRICT_MUSEUM + ARROWTOWN_CHINESE_SETTLEMENT + ARROW_RIVER + AUTUMN_COLOUR + CAFES_AND_BOUTIQUES. Arrowtown''s destination value should combine: HERITAGE + FOOD + WALKING + PHOTOGRAPHY + SHOPPING + CYCLING rather than treating it only as a scenic photo stop. Gibbston baseline: APPROXIMATELY_25_MINUTES_FROM_QUEENSTOWN + CLOSEST_MAJOR_WINE_SUB_REGION + CENTRAL_OTAGO + PINOT_NOIR + CELLAR_DOORS + WINERY_RESTAURANTS + QUEENSTOWN_TRAIL + KAWARAU_BUNGY. Queenstown-region wine baseline: 75_PLUS_WINERIES_ACROSS_WIDER_CENTRAL_OTAGO_POSITIONING + MOST_WITHIN_APPROXIMATELY_ONE_HOUR_OF_QUEENSTOWN_POSITIONING + GIBBSTON_AS_CLOSEST_MAJOR_SUB_REGION. Guided transport is strongly recommended when multiple wine tastings are scheduled. Glenorchy operational and planning baseline: QUEENSTOWN_TO_GLENORCHY: APPROXIMATELY_45_KM + APPROXIMATELY_45_MINUTES_STANDARD_DRIVING_POSITIONING. Core positioning: LAKE_WHAKATIPU_SCENIC_DRIVE + GLENORCHY_WATERFRONT + DART_AND_REES_VALLEYS + PARADISE + FILM_LOCATIONS + HIKING_GATEWAY + TE_WAHIPOUNAMU_CONTEXT + WILDERNESS_TOURISM. Actual journey time should be longer for travelers stopping at scenic viewpoints. Weather, roadworks, ice, high traffic, photography stops and regional events can materially alter travel time. 2026 Queenstown event baseline: ARROWTOWN_AUTUMN_FESTIVAL_2026: 15_APRIL_2026 – 19_APRIL_2026 + ARROWTOWN + AUTUMN_COLOUR + HERITAGE + PARADE + MARKET + FOOD + COMMUNITY_PROGRAMMING. NZ_MOUNTAIN_FILM_AND_BOOK_FESTIVAL_QUEENSTOWN_2026: 25_JUNE_2026 – 26_JUNE_2026 + ADVENTURE_FILM + MOUNTAIN_CULTURE + AUTHORS + OUTDOOR_COMMUNITY. REMARKABLES_ICE_AND_MIXED_FESTIVAL_2026: 06_AUGUST_2026 – 08_AUGUST_2026 + WINTER_CLIMBING + ALPINE_COMMUNITY. WINTER_PRIDE_2026: 28_AUGUST_2026 – 09_SEPTEMBER_2026 + QUEENSTOWN + SKIING + APRES_SKI + NIGHTLIFE + PRIDE_PROGRAMMING. PEAK_TO_PEAK_2026: 29_AUGUST_2026 + THE_REMARKABLES + CORONET_PEAK + MULTISPORT. JOSSI_WELLS_INVITATIONAL_2026: 06_SEPTEMBER_2026 – 12_SEPTEMBER_2026 + SNOW_SPORTS + FREESTYLE + ALPINE_EVENT. SNOW_MACHINE_FESTIVAL_2026: 08_SEPTEMBER_2026 – 13_SEPTEMBER_2026 + QUEENSTOWN + MUSIC + SKIING + APRES_SKI + WINTER_NIGHTLIFE. QUEENSTOWN_MARATHON_2026: 14_NOVEMBER_2026 + 42.2_KM + HALF_MARATHON + 10_KM + KIDS_EVENT + QUEENSTOWN_LAKES_SCENERY. Festival dates, ski-field venues, road controls, accommodation demand, activity capacity, snow conditions and event programs must be verified for actual travel dates. Biggest advantage: Exceptional concentration of world-class scenery and experiences within one compact alpine resort region: Queenstown combines Lake Whakatipu, the Southern Alps, skiing, bungy jumping, jet boating, hiking, cycling, wine, luxury lodges, fine dining, nightlife and access to Glenorchy wilderness. Unlike a conventional mountain resort focused only on winter, Queenstown operates as a genuine four-season destination where a traveler can combine lake cruising, adventure, wine, heritage, luxury dining and alpine scenery within the same short itinerary. Its adventure identity is unusually authentic because the Kawarau Bridge became the site of the world''s first commercial bungy operation in 1988, while modern Queenstown now supports an exceptionally broad portfolio ranging from jet boating and skydiving to skiing, rafting, mountain biking and paragliding. Its regional geography adds another major advantage: Arrowtown provides heritage, Gibbston provides Central Otago wine, Glenorchy provides dramatic wilderness, Coronet Peak and The Remarkables provide winter sport, and Queenstown itself provides the principal dining, accommodation and nightlife hub. Biggest disadvantage: Queenstown can be expensive, peak summer and winter periods create significant accommodation and activity pressure, many signature experiences are weather dependent, and regional sightseeing becomes transport intensive when Glenorchy, wineries, ski fields and distant day trips are combined without realistic clustering. The destination can therefore become inefficient or excessively expensive when planners schedule too many premium adventure products, repeatedly use taxis instead of suitable shuttles or buses, or attempt Queenstown, Glenorchy, Milford Sound, Wānaka and Central Otago within an unrealistically short stay. Accessibility also varies sharply between relatively inclusive central infrastructure and demanding alpine, snow, gravel-road, hiking and adventure environments. Overall destination score: 97/100', 3689),
  ('queenstown', 36, 'data-quality', 'DATA QUALITY', NULL, NULL, 'information_completeness: 99/100 last_updated: 2026-09-06 last_verified: WEB_VERIFIED verified_by: DESTINATION_QUEENSTOWN / QUEENSTOWN_AIRPORT / OTAGO_REGIONAL_COUNCIL_ORBUS / NZSKI / SKYLINE_QUEENSTOWN / REALNZ / SHOTOVER_JET / AJ_HACKETT_BUNGY_NEW_ZEALAND / DEPARTMENT_OF_CONSERVATION / NEW_ZEALAND_POLICE / CURRENT_OFFICIAL_EVENT_AND_ACTIVITY_SOURCES sources: IMPORTANT: Ski-field openings, lift status, snow depth, road access, ski buses, Skyline schedules, Shotover Jet departures, bungy products, scenic aviation, rafting, paragliding, TSS Earnslaw operation, Walter Peak access, winery reservations, Glenorchy excursions, Queenstown Trail sections and weather-sensitive outdoor products must NOT be treated as permanently available without verification. Current Queenstown Airport general operating baseline: TERMINAL_OPEN: APPROXIMATELY_04:00–22:30_DAILY OVERNIGHT_TERMINAL_STAY: NOT_PERMITTED. AIRPORT_INFORMATION_DESK: APPROXIMATELY_09:00–17:00. Queenstown Airport currently operates domestic and international services through one terminal building. Airport operating hours, airline schedules, border processing, bag-drop procedures, check-in windows and ground-transport arrangements must be reverified before production use. Current Queenstown Airport ground-transport baseline: ORBUS_PUBLIC_BUS + TAXI + UBER_OR_SUPPORTED_RIDESHARE + SHARED_SHUTTLE + VIP_PRIVATE_TRANSFER + RENTAL_CAR + CAMPERVAN_HIRE. Airport public buses connect Queenstown Airport with central Queenstown, Frankton and onward Orbus routes through the wider local network. Current airport bus-stop service positioning: APPROXIMATELY_EVERY_15_MINUTES. Actual timetable should be checked for travel date and arrival time. Current Orbus bus-fare baseline: ADULT_19_PLUS: BEE_CARD_NZD_2.50 CASH_NZD_4.00 CHILD_5_TO_12: BEE_CARD_NZD_1.50 CASH_NZD_4.00 YOUTH_13_TO_18: BEE_CARD_NZD_1.50 CASH_NZD_4.00 UNDER_5: FREE. Queenstown Airport adult fare baseline: BEE_CARD_NZD_2.50 CASH_NZD_10.00. Queenstown Airport child / youth cash fare baseline: NZD_8.00. Current Queenstown Orbus payment baseline: BEE_CARD OR CASH. BANK_AND_CREDIT_CARD_PAYMENT_ON_BUS: NOT_ACCEPTED. Bee Card purchasing, minimum top-up requirements, concessions and current fare policy must be reverified before production use. Current Queenstown ferry fare baseline: ADULT_BEE_CARD_SINGLE: NZD_10.00 ADULT_BANK_CARD_SINGLE: NZD_14.00. Current ferry services carry no standard bus-style concessions under the present published fare baseline. Ferry routes, schedules, fares and payment methods remain operational information and should be checked before travel. Queenstown accessibility baseline: DESTINATION_POSITIONING: INCLUSIVE_ADVENTURE_DESTINATION + ACCESSIBLE_HOTELS + ACCESSIBLE_RESTAURANTS + SELECTED_ACCESSIBLE_ATTRACTIONS + ADAPTIVE_ACTIVITY_SUPPORT + ATTRACTION_SPECIFIC_VERIFICATION_REQUIRED. Central Queenstown contains numerous accessible dining, accommodation and commercial options, but steep streets and gradients remain relevant. Wheelchairs, adaptive sporting requirements, accessible vehicle needs, companion requirements and individual adventure restrictions should be communicated before booking. Queenstown should never be classified as uniformly wheelchair accessible because alpine terrain, hiking tracks, snow, natural surfaces, boats and adventure products vary materially. Coronet Peak 2026 baseline: SEASON: 29_MAY_2026 – 04_OCTOBER_2026 EARLY_SEASON_POSITIONING: 29_MAY_2026 – 12_JUNE_2026 STANDARD_OPERATING_HOURS_POSITIONING: 09:00–16:00 NIGHT_SKI: SELECTED_WEDNESDAYS_AND_FRIDAYS + LATE_JUNE_TO_EARLY_SEPTEMBER + SELECTED_SCHOOL_HOLIDAY_DATES. Current season dates remain weather and operations dependent. Mountain-road conditions, parking, chain requirements, lift openings, snowmaking, terrain and lesson capacity must be verified each day during winter itineraries. The Remarkables baseline: THE_REMARKABLES + MAJOR_QUEENSTOWN_SKIFIELD + NZSKI + SKIING + SNOWBOARDING + BEGINNER_FACILITIES + ALPINE_TERRAIN + QUEENSTOWN_SKIBUS. STANDARD_LIFT_OPERATION_POSITIONING: APPROXIMATELY_09:00–16:00 during scheduled operational days. Actual 2026 / future season dates, road status, ski buses, snow conditions and lift availability must be checked through current NZSki operational information. Queenstown ski-road baseline: WINTER_WEATHER + SNOW + ICE + CHAIN_REQUIREMENTS + PARKING_LIMITATIONS + MOUNTAIN_TRAFFIC can affect: CORONET_PEAK_ROAD + REMARKABLES_SKI_FIELD_ACCESS_ROAD + ACTIVITY_TRANSFERS + RENTAL_CAR_PLANNING. Official ski-field and road-condition information should override fixed itinerary timing. Skyline Queenstown baseline: SKYLINE_GONDOLA + BOBS_PEAK + LUGE + PANORAMIC_VIEWPOINTS + DINING + SEASONAL_MOUNTAIN_BIKING. Individual products operate on different schedules and should not be assigned one universal permanent opening time. Current September 2026 mountain-bike uplift baseline: WINTER_CLOSED + REOPENING_FROM_19_SEPTEMBER_2026_POSITIONING. Gondola, Luge, restaurant and cycling operations should be checked against the actual date of travel. Shotover Jet baseline: OPEN: 7_DAYS_PER_WEEK WEATHER_AND_RIVER_CONDITIONS: OPERATION_DEPENDENT. STANDARD_TRIP_DEPARTURE_WINDOW: APPROXIMATELY_09:30_OR_10:00_TO_16:00 RIDE_DURATION: APPROXIMATELY_25_MINUTES CHECK_IN: APPROXIMATELY_30_MINUTES_PRIOR_AT_BASE. CENTRAL_QUEENSTOWN_SHUTTLE: AVAILABLE_FOR_SELECTED_DEPARTURES. CHRISTMAS_DAY: CLOSED under current published baseline. Heavy rain and flooding may suspend operations. Shotover Jet accessibility / visitor-facility baseline includes: DISABLED_PARKING + ACCESS_TO_RIVER_BASE + TOILETS + SEATING + SPECTATOR_ACCESS. The jet-boat ride itself still requires individual mobility and safety verification. Kawarau Bungy Centre baseline: WORLD_HOME_OF_BUNGY + FIRST_COMMERCIAL_BUNGY_OPERATION_1988 + 43_METRE_KAWARAU_BRIDGE_BUNGY + KAWARAU_SWING + ZIPRIDE + VIEWING_DECK + CAFE + SHUTTLE_OPTIONS. Current opening baseline: OCTOBER_TO_APRIL: APPROXIMATELY_08:30–17:00 MAY_TO_SEPTEMBER: APPROXIMATELY_09:00–16:30. Current participant rules include activity-specific: MINIMUM_WEIGHT + MAXIMUM_WEIGHT + TANDEM_WEIGHT_DIFFERENCE + MEDICAL_REQUIREMENTS + SAFETY_APPROVAL. These requirements should never be generalized across all adventure products. Nevis baseline: NEVIS_BUNGY + 134_METRES + NEVIS_SWING + NEVIS_CATAPULT + REMOTE_VALLEY + OPERATOR_4WD_TRANSPORT. Guests should not be instructed to self-drive directly to the Nevis operational platform. Transport schedules and participant criteria must be verified for the booked activity. TSS Earnslaw baseline: 1912_STEAMSHIP + LAKE_WHAKATIPU + STEAMER_WHARF + WALTER_PEAK + HERITAGE + SCENIC_CRUISE. QUEENSTOWN_TO_WALTER_PEAK: APPROXIMATELY_45_MINUTES. Current operation is generally year-round except annual survey / maintenance periods. 2026 maintenance baseline: 18_MAY_2026 – 26_JUNE_2026. During this period the Spirit of Queenstown was scheduled to service Walter Peak experiences instead. Future maintenance dates must be independently reverified. TSS Earnslaw / Walter Peak accessibility baseline: SELECTED_WHEELCHAIR_ACCESS + NO_ACCESSIBLE_TOILET_ON_TSS_EARNSLAW + WALTER_PEAK_GOURMET_BBQ_ACCESSIBLE + ADVANCE_NOTICE_RECOMMENDED. Actual vessel, boarding tide / lake conditions, excursion type and staff assistance should be checked for each booking. Ben Lomond baseline: TIKI_TRAIL_TO_SUMMIT: 14_KM_RETURN TIME: 6_TO_8_HOURS_RETURN ELEVATION_GAIN_FROM_QUEENSTOWN: APPROXIMATELY_1,438_METRES FITNESS: HIGH GRADIENT: STEEP. Ben Lomond should be treated as a demanding alpine day hike rather than conventional city sightseeing. Conditions can include: STRONG_SUN + WIND + LOW_TEMPERATURE + SNOW + ICE + RAPID_WEATHER_CHANGE. Current Department of Conservation advice and current forecast should override fixed itinerary assumptions. Moke Lake baseline: MOKE_LAKE_LOOP + UNDULATING_WALK + MOUNTAIN_SCENERY + WETLAND_BOARDWALK + PHOTOGRAPHY + CAMPING. Access includes: SEALED_MAIN_ROAD + STEEP_AND_WINDING_MOKE_LAKE_ROAD + APPROXIMATELY_8_KM_UNSEALED_GRAVEL_APPROACH_POSITIONING. Current mountain-bike restrictions: NO_MOUNTAIN_BIKING_ON_PENINSULA_AND_AFFECTED_ADJACENT_SECTIONS + FOLLOW_CURRENT_SIGNAGE. Road, erosion and track conditions must be rechecked. Glenorchy baseline: QUEENSTOWN_TO_GLENORCHY + 45_KM + APPROXIMATELY_45_MINUTES_STANDARD_DRIVING + LAKE_WHAKATIPU + SCENIC_ROAD + WILDERNESS + FILM_LOCATIONS + HIKING_GATEWAYS. Actual sightseeing transfer time is commonly longer because photographic stops materially affect journey duration. Glenorchy should not be scheduled as a rushed add-on immediately before a fixed airport departure. Arrowtown baseline: APPROXIMATELY_20_MINUTES_FROM_QUEENSTOWN + GOLD_RUSH_HERITAGE + LAKES_DISTRICT_MUSEUM + CHINESE_SETTLEMENT + ARROW_RIVER + AUTUMN_COLOUR + CAFES + BOUTIQUES. Arrowtown Autumn Festival 2026: 15_APRIL_2026 – 19_APRIL_2026. The festival''s dates and programming must be checked independently for future years. Gibbston baseline: APPROXIMATELY_25_MINUTES_FROM_QUEENSTOWN + VALLEY_OF_VINES + CENTRAL_OTAGO_PINOT_NOIR + WINERY_RESTAURANTS + CELLAR_DOORS + QUEENSTOWN_TRAIL + KAWARAU_BUNGY. Queenstown wine-region positioning: 75_PLUS_WINERIES_IN_WIDER_CENTRAL_OTAGO_CONTEXT + GIBBSTON_AS_CLOSEST_MAJOR_WINE_SUB_REGION. Cellar-door hours, restaurant openings, tastings and transportation must always be reverified. Queenstown climate and seasonality should be handled as: SUMMER / DECEMBER_TO_FEBRUARY: HIKING + CYCLING + LAKE_WHAKATIPU + JET_BOATING + BUNGY + GLENORCHY + WINE + OUTDOOR_DINING + WARMER_CONDITIONS + LONG_DAYLIGHT + HIGHER_PEAK_HOLIDAY_DEMAND + ALPINE_WEATHER_VARIABILITY. AUTUMN / MARCH_TO_MAY: ARROWTOWN_AUTUMN_COLOUR + PHOTOGRAPHY + WINE + HIKING + CYCLING + ROAD_TRIPS + COOLER_EVENINGS + STRONG_SHOULDER_SEASON_VALUE + INCREASING_FROST_RISK_LATER_IN_SEASON. WINTER / JUNE_TO_AUGUST: CORONET_PEAK + THE_REMARKABLES + SKIING + SNOWBOARDING + APRES_SKI + HOT_POOLS + ALPINE_SCENERY + COLD_CONDITIONS + SNOW_AND_ICE + SHORTER_DAYLIGHT + HIGH_SKIER_DEMAND. SPRING / SEPTEMBER_TO_NOVEMBER: LATE_SKIING + HIKING + CYCLING + GOLF + WINE + ADVENTURE + BLOSSOM_AND_NEW_GROWTH + LONGER_DAYLIGHT + MIXED_SNOW_AND_GREEN_LANDSCAPES + RAPIDLY_CHANGEABLE_WEATHER. Queenstown has a strongly seasonal alpine / inland climate and should never be treated as having guaranteed stable mountain weather in any month. Severe-weather baseline: HEAVY_RAIN + HIGH_WINDS + SNOW + ICE + LOW_CLOUD + FLOODING + AVALANCHE_OR_ALPINE_HAZARD_CONTEXT can affect: SKI_FIELDS + BEN_LOMOND + GLENORCHY_ROAD + MOKE_LAKE + SCENIC_FLIGHTS + HELICOPTERS + JET_BOATS + RAFTING + CYCLING + BACKCOUNTRY_HIKING. Official MetService, NZSki, Department of Conservation, road authorities, activity operators and local emergency advice should override fixed tourism itineraries during severe-weather conditions. 2026 Arrowtown Autumn Festival baseline: ARROWTOWN_AUTUMN_FESTIVAL: 15_APRIL_2026 – 19_APRIL_2026 LOCATION: ARROWTOWN POSITIONING: AUTUMN_COLOUR + GOLD_RUSH_HERITAGE + PARADE + MARKET + FOOD + ART + COMMUNITY_EVENTS. 2026 NZ Mountain Film & Book Festival Queenstown baseline: 25_JUNE_2026 – 26_JUNE_2026 POSITIONING: MOUNTAINEERING + ADVENTURE + FILM + BOOKS + OUTDOOR_CULTURE. 2026 Winter Pride baseline: 28_AUGUST_2026 – 09_SEPTEMBER_2026 POSITIONING: PRIDE + SKIING + ALPINE_EVENTS + APRES_SKI + NIGHTLIFE + ENTERTAINMENT. 2026 Snow Machine baseline: 08_SEPTEMBER_2026 – 13_SEPTEMBER_2026 POSITIONING: MUSIC + SNOW_SPORTS + APRES_SKI + QUEENSTOWN_NIGHTLIFE. 2026 Queenstown Marathon baseline: 14_NOVEMBER_2026 POSITIONING: MARATHON + HALF_MARATHON + 10_KM + KIDS_EVENT + QUEENSTOWN_TRAILS + LAKE_AND_MOUNTAIN_SCENERY. Festival dates, accommodation demand, road closures, parking restrictions, public transport, ski-field programs and weather contingencies must be verified for actual travel dates. Current general safety baseline: NEW_ZEALAND: RELATIVELY_SAFE_TRAVEL_DESTINATION BUT: NOT_CRIME_FREE + NORMAL_PERSONAL_SECURITY_PRECAUTIONS_REQUIRED + ALPINE_AND_OUTDOOR_RISK_MANAGEMENT_IMPORTANT. NEW_ZEALAND_POLICE_VISITOR_GUIDANCE: AVOID_UNLIT_AREAS_LATE_AT_NIGHT + SECURE_ACCOMMODATION_AND_VEHICLES + DO_NOT_LEAVE_LUGGAGE_CAMERAS_OR_VALUABLES_VISIBLE_IN_PARKED_CARS + TAKE_EXTRA_CARE_AT_SCENIC_SPOTS_AND_TRAILHEADS + CHECK_WEATHER_AND_OUTDOOR_CONDITIONS + TELL_SOMEONE_ABOUT_SIGNIFICANT_OUTDOOR_PLANS + NEVER_DRIVE_UNDER_THE_INFLUENCE_OF_ALCOHOL_OR_DRUGS. Seat belts are compulsory, child-restraint requirements apply and winter road driving requires additional preparation. EMERGENCY_NUMBER: 111 for police, ambulance and fire emergencies. Queenstown should primarily be treated as: SUMMER: LAKE_WHAKATIPU + HIKING + CYCLING + GLENORCHY + JET_BOATING + BUNGY + WINE + LONG_DAYLIGHT AUTUMN: ARROWTOWN_COLOURS + WINE + PHOTOGRAPHY + HIKING + CYCLING + ROAD_TRIPS + LOWER_POST_SUMMER_PRESSURE WINTER: CORONET_PEAK + THE_REMARKABLES + SKIING + SNOWBOARDING + APRES_SKI + HOT_POOLS + WINTER_EVENTS SPRING: LATE_SKIING + HIKING + CYCLING + GOLF + WINE + GLENORCHY + ADVENTURE + SNOW_CAPPED_SCENERY FIRST_TIME_TRAVEL: QUEENSTOWN_BAY + SKYLINE_BOBS_PEAK + SHOTOVER_OR_BUNGY + ARROWTOWN + GIBBSTON_OR_WALTER_PEAK + GLENORCHY_IF_TIME_ALLOWS REPEAT_TRAVEL: MOKE_LAKE + BEN_LOMOND + DEEPER_GLENORCHY + PARADISE + EXTENDED_WINE_REGION + MOUNTAIN_BIKING + MULTIPLE_SKI_DAYS + SPECIALIST_ADVENTURE. Destination Queenstown, Queenstown Airport, Otago Regional Council / Orbus, NZSki, Skyline Queenstown, RealNZ, Shotover Jet, AJ Hackett Bungy New Zealand, Department of Conservation, New Zealand Police and current individual activity / event portals should be treated as primary sources for operational information. This dataset should be refreshed regularly before production use.', 3690),
  ('melbourne', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Spring', NULL, 'months: September October November weather: Cool to pleasantly mild but highly changeable. September remains crisp, October becomes wetter and variable, while November is generally warmer and increasingly suitable for outdoor sightseeing. crowd_level: MEDIUM price_level: MEDIUM overall_score: 79–86 recommended: true reason: One of Melbourne''s strongest periods for city exploration, gardens, food, culture, sporting events, day trips, and photography, although rapidly changing weather remains a planning factor. Best for: Official tourism describes spring as Melbourne''s most variable season, with conditions capable of changing quickly from sunny to cold and windy; October is typically the wettest month.', 3691),
  ('melbourne', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Summer', NULL, 'months: December January February weather: Warm to hot and generally relatively dry. Average daytime maximums are around 25–27°C, but January and February can experience periods above 30°C and occasional much hotter conditions. crowd_level: HIGH → VERY_HIGH price_level: HIGH → VERY_HIGH overall_score: 73–82 recommended: true reason: Excellent for: Summer offers long daylight, beaches, events, outdoor dining, and excellent regional touring, but holiday demand, major sporting events, and heat spikes reduce overall value.', 3692),
  ('melbourne', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Autumn', NULL, 'months: March April May weather: Mild and increasingly cool. March remains comfortably warm, April is moderate, and May becomes noticeably cooler. Fine sunny periods and autumn colour make outdoor touring particularly attractive. crowd_level: MEDIUM → LOW price_level: MEDIUM overall_score: 83–91 recommended: true reason: Arguably Melbourne''s strongest all-round season for comfortable city sightseeing, food, wine, Great Ocean Road travel, gardens, neighbourhood exploration, and photography. Best for: Tourism Australia describes autumn as generally mild, with cooler temperatures and many fine, sunny days.', 3693),
  ('melbourne', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Winter', NULL, 'months: June July August weather: Cool, frequently cloudy, and occasionally wet, with average daytime temperatures around 14–16°C and colder nights. Snow is generally a regional Victorian High Country experience rather than a Melbourne-city feature. crowd_level: LOW price_level: LOW → MEDIUM overall_score: 72–82 recommended: true reason: Excellent for: Winter provides strong city-break value with lower general visitor pressure and excellent indoor culture, dining, shopping, sport, and entertainment.', 3694),
  ('melbourne', 10, 'budget-strategy', 'BUDGET STRATEGY', NULL, NULL, 'Where money can be saved: Where saving money is usually NOT recommended: Travel-agent rule: In Melbourne, **FREE_CITY_TRAMS_OR_MYKI_CARD + LANEWAY_CAFES_AND_MARKET_EATS + CBD_OR_INNER_SUBURB_STAY + FREE_PUBLIC_GALLERIES should be evaluated together**. For short stays, prioritize **CBD_LANEWAYS_BASE + FREE_TRAM_EXPLORATION + NGV_AND_BOTANIC_GARDENS_VISIT + SOUTHBANK_DINING**. For longer stays, add **GREAT_OCEAN_ROAD_DAY_TRIP + YARRA_VALLEY_WINE_TOUR + PHILLIP_ISLAND_PENGUINS + NEIGHBORHOOD_EXPLORATION_FITZROY_ST_KILDA** rather than switching accommodations between different inner suburbs frequently.', 3695),
  ('melbourne', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Family', 'family', 'Melbourne’s primary international and domestic gateway is Melbourne Airport (Tullamarine / MEL), alongside Avalon Airport (AVV) for select domestic routes, and regional rail arrivals via Southern Cross Station. For families arriving with young children and multi-piece luggage at Tullamarine Airport, pre-booked private minivans, rideshares (Uber/DiDi at designated pickup zones), or chauffeured airport transfers provide a direct, stress-free link to accommodations in the CBD, Southbank, or Docklands. For families traveling light or budget-conscious households, the **SkyBus Melbourne City Express** operates high-frequency express trips directly between airport terminals and Southern Cross Station. From Southern Cross, families can easily transition onto the low-floor Free Tram Zone or hail short rideshare transfers directly to their hotel doorstep.', 3696),
  ('melbourne', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Honeymoon', 'honeymoon', 'Opt for pre-arranged private luxury transfers (chauffeured luxury sedans or premium SUVs) departing directly from Melbourne Airport’s kerbside arrivals or private aviation terminals directly to high-end skyline stays such as The Ritz-Carlton, Crown Towers, or Park Hyatt. For multi-destination Victorian honeymoon itineraries, combine: PRIVATE_AIRPORT_LUXURY_CAR_TRANSFER + CBD_SKYLINE_SUITE_STAY + HELICOPTER_TRANSFER_TO_YARRA_VALLEY_WINERIES + CHAUFFEURED_GREAT_OCEAN_ROAD_COASTAL_TOUR.', 3697),
  ('melbourne', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Luxury', 'luxury', 'Utilize pre-booked luxury private chauffeured transfers directly from Tullamarine Airport''s arrivals terminals, private jet fixed-base operators (FBOs), or regional helipads. For complex luxury Victorian itineraries, combine: VIP_AIRPORT_MEET_AND_GREET + PRIVATE_LUXURY_SEDAN_TRANSFERS + HELICOPTER_WINERY_TRANSFERS + DEDICATED_PRIVATE_DRIVER_AND_ART_CURATOR_GUIDE_SERVICES.', 3698),
  ('melbourne', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Budget', 'budget', 'Take advantage of Melbourne’s world-class public transport network and efficient airport express infrastructure: For regional coastal or alpine journeys, regional V/Line train and coach services depart directly from Southern Cross Station.', 3699),
  ('melbourne', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Senior', 'senior', 'Prioritize door-to-door pre-booked taxi or rideshare transfers directly at airport terminal drop-offs to bypass heavy luggage handling and long walks through public transport interchange halls. When navigating inner-city locations, utilize step-free, low-floor city trams, leverage accessible underground stations across the Metro Tunnel network (e.g., Town Hall and State Library), or choose central accommodations situated directly adjacent to flat, paved promenades along Southbank or Collins Street.', 3700),
  ('melbourne', 18, 'family-travel', 'FAMILY TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'child_friendly_score: 92 best_ages: Rules: For young children: Prefer: Avoid:', 3701),
  ('melbourne', 19, 'honeymoon-travel', 'HONEYMOON TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'honeymoon_score: 91 romance_score: 93 privacy_score: 88 luxury_score: 94 Recommended: Honeymoon itineraries should generally stay at: 2–3 major experiences/day. Prefer: LUXURY_CBD_SUITES + PRIVATE_YARRA_VALLEY_WINE_TOUR + HOTEL_SPA_RELAXATION + FINE_DINING_LANEWAY_BISTRO + SUNSET_ROOFTOP_DRINKS + FREE_TIME over: Constant inner-suburb hotel switching and rushed multi-region daily driving.', 3702),
  ('melbourne', 20, 'luxury-travel', 'LUXURY TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'luxury_score: 94 Recommended:', 3703),
  ('melbourne', 21, 'adventure', 'ADVENTURE', NULL, NULL, 'adventure_score: 75 Melbourne offers vibrant urban exploration, coastal watersports, scenic trail cycling, and mountain day trips rather than high-altitude extreme mountaineering. Adventure experiences: Best regions: GREAT_OCEAN_ROAD_COAST + DANDENONG_RANGES_FORESTS + MORNINGTON_PENINSULA + YARRA_VALLEY_VALES', 3704),
  ('melbourne', 22, 'senior-travel', 'SENIOR TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'senior_suitability: 90 walking_intensity: LOW–MEDIUM for CBD Free Tram Zone, Southbank Promenade, Royal Botanic Gardens, and NGV galleries MEDIUM–HIGH for full laneway network cobbles, Fitzroy shopping streets, and coastal cliff walks Rules: Melbourne works exceptionally well for seniors as a: WORLD_CLASS_ARTS_AND_CULTURE + SPECIALTY_COFFEE_AND_DINING + ACCESSIBLE_PUBLIC_TRANSIT + SCENIC_GARDEN_STROLLS + SEATED_DAY_TRIPS destination.', 3705),
  ('melbourne', 23, 'accessibility', 'ACCESSIBILITY', NULL, NULL, 'wheelchair_accessibility: HIGH IN MODERN LUXURY HOTELS, CBD PUBLIC INFRASTRUCTURE, NGV GALLERIES, AND LOW-FLOOR TRAM STOPS VARIABLE TO LIMITED IN HISTORIC NARROW LANEWAYS, OLD SUBTERRANEAN BARS, AND VINTAGE STEAM TRAINS public_transport_accessibility: HIGH across low-floor inner-city trams, accessible Metro train stations, and SkyBus airport shuttles hotel_accessibility: MUST_BE_VERIFIED_PER_HOTEL attraction_accessibility: MUST_BE_VERIFIED_PER_ATTRACTION Rule: Never assume universal step-free access inside historic heritage basements, older venue staircases, or cobbled alleyways. Additional notes:', 3706),
  ('melbourne', 24, 'food', 'FOOD', NULL, NULL, 'Melbourne is particularly strong for: Food experiences: Family: Prioritize market food courts, casual Italian pasta spots, woodfired pizza, bakery treats, and seaside fish and chips. Honeymoon: Choose romantic laneway bistros, skyline rooftop dining, intimate wine bars, and Yarra Valley vineyard lunches. Luxury: Include multi-course degustation menus with sommelier wine pairings, private chef tables, and exclusive VIP lounge dining. Budget: Utilize market stalls at Queen Victoria Market, Chinatown dumpling houses, Swanston Street food courts, and suburban cheap eats.', 3707),
  ('melbourne', 25, 'shopping', 'SHOPPING', NULL, NULL, 'Strong categories: Luxury shopping: Prefer: Budget: Prefer: Travel-agent rule: Use COLLINS_STREET_AND_CHADSTONE for HIGH_END_LUXURY_DESIGNER_SHOPPING, FITZROY_AND_BRUNSWICK_STREET for INDEPENDENT_VINTAGE_AND_LOCAL_DESIGNERS, and QUEEN_VICTORIA_AND_SOUTH_MELBOURNE_MARKETS for ARTISANAL_FOODS_COFFEE_AND_SOUVENIRS.', 3708),
  ('melbourne', 26, 'nightlife', 'NIGHTLIFE', NULL, NULL, 'nightlife_level: 92 Suitable for: Best areas: Evening activities: Melbourne offers a world-renowned, multi-faceted nightlife scene ranging from intimate laneway cocktail dens and rooftop bars to vibrant live music venues and late-night underground clubs. Honeymoon travelers should generally prefer: ROOFTOP_SKYLINE_BARS + HIDDEN_LANEWAY_SPEAKEASIES + FINE_DINING_SUPPERS + THEATER_SHOWS over: High-volume late-night student clubs. Travel-agent rule: Position Melbourne as a **LANEWAY_SPEAKEASIES + ROOFTOP_COCKTAIL_BARS + LIVE_MUSIC_AND_THEATER + MULTICULTURAL_LATE_NIGHT_DINING DESTINATION**, with sophisticated after-dark culture serving as primary highlight pillars.', 3709),
  ('melbourne', 28, 'sample-itinerary-patterns', 'SAMPLE ITINERARY PATTERNS', '3 NIGHTS', NULL, '### Day 1 Arrival at Melbourne Airport (MEL) → SkyBus Melbourne City Express to Southern Cross Station or private airport transfer to central Melbourne hotel → Hotel check-in & Myki / contactless transport preparation Afternoon: → Begin at the iconic Flinders Street Station & Federation Square precinct → Explore Melbourne''s famous laneways including Hosier Lane, Degraves Street & Centre Place → Walk along the Yarra River through Birrarung Marr and Southbank Promenade → Continue towards the Royal Botanic Gardens Melbourne for landscaped gardens & relaxed city views Evening: → Welcome dinner showcasing Melbourne''s multicultural food scene → Explore Southbank riverfront and the illuminated Melbourne skyline → Optional Melbourne Skydeck experience for panoramic evening views → Rooftop drinks / relaxed laneway bar experience → Hotel MEL serves as Melbourne''s principal international and domestic aviation gateway. The SkyBus Melbourne City Express operates between Melbourne Airport and Southern Cross Station, while Melbourne''s tram, train and bus network provides convenient access throughout the inner city. ### Day 2 Morning: Breakfast Recommended first-time option: → Early departure for a full-day Great Ocean Road scenic excursion → Drive along Victoria''s dramatic southern coastline → Stop around the Surf Coast / coastal viewpoints → Continue through Great Otway landscapes towards Port Campbell National Park Afternoon: → Visit the iconic Twelve Apostles limestone formations → Explore additional coastal viewpoints around Loch Ard Gorge / Port Campbell coastline where time permits → Scenic photography overlooking the Southern Ocean → Relaxed regional lunch during the touring route Evening: → Return to Melbourne → Dinner in Chinatown, Southbank, Carlton, or one of Melbourne''s renowned dining precincts → Hotel Optional alternative instead of Great Ocean Road: PHILLIP_ISLAND: → Scenic drive from Melbourne towards Phillip Island → Wildlife & coastal viewpoints → Explore the island''s rugged southern coastline → Evening Penguin Parade experience MELBOURNE_CITY_AND_CULTURE: → Queen Victoria Market → Melbourne Museum & Carlton Gardens → National Gallery of Victoria → Royal Botanic Gardens → Melbourne Cricket Ground precinct → Fitzroy / Carlton neighbourhood exploration YARRA_VALLEY: → Yarra Valley vineyard landscapes → Premium winery lunch → Local produce & gourmet tasting → Healesville Sanctuary for Australian wildlife ### Day 3 Morning: Breakfast → Hotel checkout → Transfer to Melbourne Airport (MEL) → Morning domestic flight to Gold Coast Airport (OOL) → Private transfer / airport connection towards Surfers Paradise or Broadbeach → Gold Coast hotel check-in / luggage drop Afternoon: → Explore Surfers Paradise Beach and its famous high-rise beachfront skyline → Walk along the beachfront promenade → Continue to Broadbeach or Burleigh Heads for a more relaxed coastal atmosphere → Beachside lunch featuring fresh Australian seafood Evening: → Golden-hour beach walk along the Gold Coast → SkyPoint Observation Deck / Surfers Paradise skyline experience → Farewell dinner at a beachfront or high-rise restaurant → Hotel Optional alternative for the Gold Coast afternoon: WILDLIFE: → Currumbin Wildlife Sanctuary → Australian native wildlife encounters → Kangaroos, koalas, lorikeets & conservation experiences → Continue towards Currumbin Beach THEME_PARK: Choose ONE: → Warner Bros. Movie World OR → Dreamworld OR → Sea World BEACH_AND_NATURE: → Burleigh Heads → Burleigh Head National Park coastal walk → Tallebudgera Creek → Surfers Paradise sunset FAMILY: → Full-day Gold Coast theme park experience → Currumbin Wildlife Sanctuary → Surfers Paradise beachfront → Family-friendly evening entertainment HONEYMOON: → Burleigh Heads scenic coastline → Couple sunset photography at Surfers Paradise → Premium beachfront dining → Luxury ocean-view hotel stay LUXURY: → Private helicopter / scenic coastal experience → Premium Broadbeach or Main Beach resort → Spa & wellness treatment → Fine-dining beachfront dinner For only 3 nights, prioritize: MELBOURNE_CITY_AND_LANES + GREAT_OCEAN_ROAD_AND_12_APOSTLES + GOLD_COAST_SURFERS_PARADISE OR MELBOURNE_CULTURE + PHILLIP_ISLAND + GOLD_COAST_BEACH_AND_WILDLIFE rather than attempting to combine Melbourne, Sydney, Brisbane and the Gold Coast within the same short itinerary. ### Day 4 Breakfast → Leisurely sunrise beach walk at Surfers Paradise / Broadbeach → Souvenir shopping or relaxed beachfront breakfast → Hotel checkout → Private transfer, taxi, rideshare or public transport connection to Gold Coast Airport (OOL) → Departure', 3710),
  ('melbourne', 29, 'six-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 1', NULL, 'Arrival at Melbourne Airport (MEL) → Private airport transfer → Romantic hotel check-in → Relax and refresh Evening: → SEA LIFE Melbourne Aquarium → Southbank waterfront → Romantic dinner → Overnight at Melbourne', 3711),
