  ('melbourne', 32, 'travel-agent-insights', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS', 'What inexperienced planners often do wrong', NULL, '', 3732),
  ('melbourne', 32, 'travel-agent-insights', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS', 'What an experienced planner does differently', NULL, 'MCG_AND_ROYAL_EXHIBITION_BUILDING + BOTANIC_GARDENS_AND_NGV + GREAT_OCEAN_ROAD_AND_MODERN_AUSTRALIAN_CUISINE rather than maximum destination count.', 3733),
  ('melbourne', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', NULL, NULL, 'IF: trip_length <= 3 nights THEN: prioritize_MCG_SUNRISE + ROYAL_EXHIBITION_HERITAGE + GREAT_OCEAN_ROAD_AND_WEST_MELBOURNE Reason: Very short stays gain more value from properly experiencing core Victorian heritage, world-famous sports and cultural sites, and dramatic coastal landscapes than losing time to exhausting multi-city transit schedules. IF: trip_length >= 5 nights AND: traveler_interest == FIRST_TIME_MELBOURNE THEN: prioritize_MELBOURNE_ARTS_PRECINCT + SOUTHBANK_RESORT_ATTRACTIONS + GREAT_OCEAN_ROAD_AND_SANCTUARY + YARRA_VALLEY_AND_MORNINGTON_DAY_TRIP Reason: This gives a balanced introduction to Victorian cultural heritage, world-class city entertainment, preserved native wildlife sanctuaries, and seamless regional cool-climate wine day excursions. IF: trip_length >= 7 nights AND: traveler_interest == FIRST_TIME_MELBOURNE THEN: prefer_CENTRAL_MELBOURNE_CORE + DANDENONGS_AND_HEALESVILLE_RETREAT + DAY_TRIPS_TO_PHILLIP_ISLAND_AND_BALLARAT_VIA_REGIONAL_EXPRESSWAYS AND: use_PRIVATE_AC_CARS_V_LINE_EXPRESS_AND_INTER_CITY_TAXIS Reason: Luxury urban stays, riverfront cultural precincts, protected native wildlife sanctuaries, and express rail connections to regional historic goldfields offer distinct insights into South Eastern Australia''s premier state. IF: trip_type == HONEYMOON THEN: prioritize_RITZ_CARLTON_LUXURY_SUITES + CROWN_METROPOL_HERITAGE_STAYS + PRIVATE_YARRA_RIVER_SUNSET_CRUISE AND: increase_BOUTIQUE_STAYS + ROOFTOP_SKYLINE_DINING + LUXURY_URBAN_SPA + MODERN_AUSTRALIAN_TASTING + COUPLE_EXPERIENCES Reason: Melbourne''s romantic routes mix ultra-luxury skyline balcony sanctuaries, multi-course chef-hatted dining, rooftop lounges overlooking glowing city skyscrapers, and quiet walks along Yarra riverfront garden estates. IF: traveler_type == FAMILY THEN: prioritize_HEALESVILLE_SANCTUARY_WILDLIFE + FREE_CITY_TRAMS + PUFFING_BILLY_STEAM_TRAIN AND: include_BOTANIC_GARDENS_GARDEN_RUNS + ARTISAN_CHOCOLATE_WORKSHOPS_AT_YARRA_VALLEY + DISTRICT_DOCKLANDS_PLAY_PARK AND: reduce_STEEP_COASTAL_HIGH_CLIFFS + LONG_CONTINUOUS_TRANSFERS Reason: Melbourne has exceptional family sights, including native wildlife sanctuary visits, historic steam train rides through fern gullies, interactive chocolate craft workshops, and colorful immersive play parks. IF: traveler_type == LUXURY THEN: prefer_RITZ_CARLTON_MELBOURNE + PARK_HYATT_MELBOURNE + THE_LANYGON_HOTEL_MELBOURNE AND: increase_PRIVATE_GUIDES + MODERN_AUSTRALIAN_FINE_DINING + PRIVATE_MPV_TRANSFERS + VIP_MCG_ENTRY + SPA Reason: Melbourne high-end travel relies on world-famous skyline-view luxury suites, multi-course chef-hatted dining, private MPV transfers via expressways, and high-end heritage hotel estates. IF: traveler_type == BUDGET THEN: prefer_FREE_CITY_CIRCLE_TRAMS_AND_BUSES + SELF_GUIDED_LANEWAY_WALKS + LOCAL_TAKEAWAY_LANEWAY_CAFES AND: book_FREE_GARDEN_VIEW_POINTS_EARLY AND: balance_PAID_ATTRACTIONS_WITH_FREE_ST_KILDA_PIER_PROMENADE_STROLLS + HOSIER_LANE_MARKET_WALKS + YARRA_RIVER_LOOKOUT_VIEWS Reason: Melbourne can be accessed affordably using local free tram zone networks, authentic lane coffee stalls, free St Kilda pier promenade walkways, and scenic riverbank garden viewpoints across the Yarra. IF: traveler_interest == CULTURE_AND_HERITAGE THEN: prioritize_ROYAL_EXHIBITION_BUILDING + STATE_LIBRARY_VICTORIA + OLD_MELBOURNE_GAOL + NGV_INTERNATIONAL AND: include_VICTORIAN_ARCHITECTURE + FIRST_NATIONS_HERITAGE + LOCAL_FESTIVALS Reason: These sights showcase Melbourne''s unique Victorian history, mixing 19th-century boomtown elegance, Kulin Nation indigenous culture, and 170 years of Australian civic heritage. IF: traveler_interest == ART_AND_ARCHITECTURE THEN: prioritize_HOSIER_LANE_STREET_ART + NGV_AUSTRALIA + STATE_LIBRARY_READING_ROOM + FLINDERS_STREET_STATION AND: include_CONTEMPORARY_CITY_GALLERIES + HISTORIC_VICTORIAN_RENEWAL + ECO_RESORT_DESIGN Reason: This route contrasts intricate bluestone laneway graffiti art with grand Victorian arches, geometric modern architectural squares, and historic gold rush design. IF: traveler_interest == GASTRONOMY THEN: prefer_SPECIALTY_FLAT_WHITE_COFFEE + SMASHED_AVOCADO_TOAST + LOCAL_YARRA_VALLEY_PINOT_NOIR + LYGON_STREET_PASTA AND: include_CHINATOWN_DUMPLING_STALLS + DEGRAVES_STREET_BISTROS + SEAFOOD_FINE_DINING Reason: Melbourne dining spans world-famous artisanal espresso coffee, avocado brunch fare, unique regional cool-climate wines, and world-class multicultural dining. IF: traveler_interest == NATURE_AND_WILDLIFE THEN: prioritize_HEALESVILLE_SANCTUARY + PHILLIP_ISLAND_PENGUINS + ROYAL_BOTANIC_GARDENS + GRAMPIANS_NATIONAL_PARK AND: do_not_treat_MANICURED_RESORT_GARDENS_AND_NATIONAL_PARK_BUSH_TRAILS_AS_IDENTICAL Reason: Resort lawns offer manicured lawns and pools, while Victoria''s surrounding national parks and wildlife sanctuaries feature native migratory penguins, wild kangaroos, and protected eucalyptus ecosystems. IF: traveler_interest == SHOPPING THEN: prioritize_QUEEN_VICTORIA_MARKET + BLOCK_ARCADE_OLD_CITY + EMPORIUM_MELBOURNE + CHAPEL_STREET_FASHION_MARKET AND: include_LOCAL_WINE_STORES + ARTISAN_COFFEE_SHOPS + INDIGENOUS_HANDICRAFTS Reason: Queen Victoria Market offers high-end artisan goods and souvenirs, Block Arcade supplies luxury boutiques and historic tea rooms, and Chapel Street features authentic local fashion designer shops. IF: traveler_interest == SAUNA_AND_WELLNESS THEN: choose_PENINSULA_HOT_SPRINGS + TRADITIONAL_THERMAL_MINERAL_BATHS + HYDROTHERAPY_SANCTUARIES AND: do_not_treat_LOCAL_HOLISTIC_MASSAGE_AND_MODERN_RESORT_HOTEL_SPAS_AS_IDENTICAL Reason: Melbourne wellness ranges from heritage city hotel holistic massages to award-winning geothermal hot springs in the surrounding coastal countryside. IF: traveler_interest == PHOTOGRAPHY THEN: prioritize_FLINDERS_STREET_STATION_SUNRISE + ST_KILDA_PIER_SUNSET + EUREKA_SKYDECK_VIEWPOINT + HOSIER_LANE_LANES AND: prioritize_GOLDEN_HOUR + BLUE_HOUR + CLEAR_AIR_DAYS Reason: These sites produce stunning visual contrasts between historic yellow domed stations, modern glass skyscraper skylines, and emerald Yarra riverbank gardens. IF: trip_length <= 5 nights THEN: prefer_MAXIMUM_ONE_OR_TWO_BASES AND: avoid_EXCESSIVE_HOTEL_CHANGES Reason: City transit, freeway traffic navigation, and regional rail transfers consume valuable sightseeing hours. IF: route == CENTRAL_MELBOURNE_TO_GEELONG_OR_BALLARAT THEN: prefer_DIRECT_CAR_RENTALS_PRIVATE_TRANSFERS_OR_V_LINE_EXPRESS_TRAINS_OVER_MULTIPLE_LOCAL_BUS_TRANSFERS Reason: Direct express trains and private car transfers eliminate transit confusion and save energy for exploring coastal drive routes and historic goldfields. IF: traveler_type == SENIOR OR: traveler_mobility == LIMITED THEN: prefer_ACCESSIBLE_RESORT_HOTELS + FLAT_SOUTHBANK_PROMENADE + PRIVATE_MPV + ROYAL_BOTANIC_GARDENS_ACCESSIBLE_PATHWAYS AND: reduce_EXCESSIVE_BUSH_STEPS + DANDENONG_RANGES_INCLINES + EXTREME_COLD_WIND_WALKS Reason: High heritage stairs and steep forest tracks cause fatigue; low-floor trams, private MPVs, and flat garden pathways ease travel. IF: traveler_uses_WHEELCHAIR THEN: prefer_VERIFIED_ACCESSIBLE_RESORTS + LOW_FLOOR_TRAM_ACCESSIBLE_ROUTES + FLAT_HOTEL_GROUNDS + FEDERATION_SQUARE_PAVED_PATHS AND: do_not_assume_HISTORIC_BUSH_TRAILS + ANCIENT_LOOKOUTS + SECLUDED_COASTAL_COVES_ARE_STEP_FREE Reason: Major modern luxury resorts and primary city art galleries are accessible, but historic goldrush sites, mountain lookouts, and narrow bluestone cobblestone lanes present physical barriers. IF: weather == EXTREME_SUMMER_HEAT AND: region == VICTORIA_TERRITORY THEN: prioritize_EARLY_MORNING_HERITAGE_VISITS + AIR_CONDITIONED_GALLERIES_AND_STORES + EVENING_RIVERFRONT_DINING AND: reduce_MIDDAY_UNSHADED_BEACH_EXPOSURE Reason: Melbourne summer temps routinely spike during heatwave conditions (over 40°C); early starts and air-conditioned indoor gallery breaks maintain comfort. IF: weather == HEAVY_SMOG_OR_RAIN THEN: increase_NGV_INTERNATIONAL + STATE_LIBRARY_VICTORIA + INDOOR_RESORT_ENTERTAINMENT + COVERED_LANEWAY_ARCADES AND: reduce_DANDENONG_OUTDOOR_DECKS + OUTDOOR_BEACH_PROMENADES Reason: Indoor art galleries, historical libraries, covered heritage arcades, and luxury lounges remain excellent regardless of outdoor rain or sudden cool fronts. IF: traveler_interest == FIRST_TIME_MELBOURNE THEN: prioritize_MCG + ROYAL_EXHIBITION_BUILDING + GREAT_OCEAN_ROAD + ROYAL_BOTANIC_GARDENS AND: add_ONE_OF_HEALESVILLE_SANCTUARY_PUFFING_BILLY_OR_PENINSULA_HOT_SPRINGS AND: include_ONE_SIGNATURE_FLAT_WHITE_COFFEE_OR_TAKEAWAY_LANWAY_PARMA_EXPERIENCE Reason: This structure provides a comprehensive introduction to Melbourne''s premier architectural and sporting heritage alongside authentic local cafe culture. IF: traveler_interest == CULTURE_AND_RELAXATION_BALANCE THEN: allocate_60_TO_70_PERCENT_TO_CORE_SIGHTSEEING AND: allocate_REMAINING_TIME_TO_COFFEE_LANEWAYS + RIVER_CAFES + SPAS + ROOFTOP_LOUNGES + SHOPPING + FREE_TIME', 3734),
  ('melbourne', 34, 'destination-scoring', 'DESTINATION SCORING', NULL, NULL, '| Factor | Score | | --- | --- | | Family | 92 | | Honeymoon | 91 | | Luxury | 94 | | Budget | 80 | | Adventure | 75 | | Culture | 99 | | Food | 98 | | Shopping | 92 | | Nightlife | 92 | | Relaxation | 85 | | Nature | 84 | | Accessibility | 91 | | Safety | 90 | | First-time visitor | 96 | | Photography | 95 |', 3735),
  ('melbourne', 35, 'final-travel-agent-verdict', 'FINAL TRAVEL AGENT VERDICT', NULL, NULL, 'Best traveler profiles: 1. Honeymoon / romantic traveler (The Ritz-Carlton Melbourne, Crown Towers, Private Yarra River Gondola Dining, Sunset St Kilda Pier Promenade) 2. First-time Australia / East Coast traveler 3. Culture / heritage traveler (Royal Exhibition Building, State Library Victoria, Old Melbourne Gaol, Princess Theatre, Captain Cook''s Cottage) 4. Victorian architecture & arts traveler (19th-century Gold Rush boomtown facades, NGV International stained glass ceiling, Flinders Street Station, Ian Potter Centre NGV Australia) 5. Luxury / architectural design traveler (The Ritz-Carlton Melbourne, Park Hyatt Melbourne, Crown Towers, W Melbourne, Hotel Windsor) 6. Photography traveler (Flinders Street Station sunrise, Hosier Lane street art golden hour, Eureka Skydeck view deck, Princes Bridge river views) 7. Food / gastronomy traveler (Degraves Street Specialty Coffee & Smashed Avocado, Lygon Street Italian, Chinatown Dumplings, Southbank Fine Dining, Yarra Valley Wine Tasting) 8. Family traveler (Healesville Sanctuary Wildlife Center, Free City Circle Tram Rides, Puffing Billy Steam Railway, SEA LIFE Melbourne Aquarium) 9. Modern art & urban lifestyle traveler (Melbourne City Loop Train, Federation Square Cultural Precinct, Chapel Street Fashion Boutiques, Southbank Riverfront Promenade) 10. Budget / independent traveler (Free Tram Zone City Network, Regional V/Line Trains, Yarra Riverfront Walking Trails, Local Laneway Espresso & Bakery Stalls) Best duration: 3–5 nights 1–2 nights: Best for ONE primary focus such as City Laneways & Specialty Coffee + MCG Heritage express trip. 3–4 nights: Best for TWO major bases/focuses such as Central Melbourne Culture & Dining + Great Ocean Road & Native Wildlife Sanctuary. 5–6 nights: Excellent for Royal Exhibition Building + NGV International + Great Ocean Road Coastal Drive + Day trip to Yarra Valley & Dandenong Ranges. 7–8 nights: Best for deep regional Victoria travel, Princes Highway cross-border excursions, Grampians & Phillip Island nature tours, or high-speed V/Line Express rail connections to Geelong, Ballarat, or Bendigo. Best season: YEAR-ROUND Shoulder / Dry Windows (March – May & September – November): PLEASANT_TEMPERATURES + OPTIMAL_CLEAR_SKIES + SHARP_SKYLINE_VISIBILITY + BOTANIC_GARDENS_WALKS + MELBOURNE_FESTIVAL_EVENTS. Peak Summer / Coastal Season (December – February): WARM_WEATHER + EVENING_ROOFTOP_LOUNGES + BEACH_PROMENADE_STROLLS + HERITAGE_PARK_PICNICS. Cool / Winter Season (June – August): CRISP_WEATHER + EVENING_LANEWAY_DINING + INDOOR_ART_GALLERIES + COZY_YARRA_VALLEY_CELLAR_DOORS. Festive / Major Events Season (January & March): AUSTRALIAN_OPEN_TENNIS + FORMULA_1_GRAND_PRIX + WINTER_CULTURAL_FESTIVALS + WORLD_CLASS_ARTS_EVENTS. Tourism Victoria guidance treats the city as year-round: autumn (March–May) and spring (September–November) are world-famous for pleasant temperatures, vibrant foliage, and seasonal cultural festivals; summer (December–February) for long coastal evenings and rooftop dining; winter (June–August) for cozy laneway dining, coffee culture, and blockbuster gallery exhibitions; and January through March for major international sporting and arts events. Best hotel strategy: Choose accommodation according to transit convenience, atmosphere, and trip purpose. For first-time visitors: CBD_GRID_OR_SOUTHBANK (Central Business District Free Tram Zone or Southbank promenade) for direct walking/tram access to top galleries, laneways, and City Loop rail stations. For heritage / bohemian charm: FITZROY_OR_CARLTON (Boutique guesthouses near Gertrude Street or Carlton Gardens) for authentic local living, historic terrace vistas, and cafe street culture. For luxury & modern design: COLLINS_STREET_EAST / SOUTHBANK selectively according to chef-hatted fine dining, city-view indoor pool suites, and urban luxury spas. Avoid unnecessary hotel changes within Melbourne; short tram rides, City Loop trains, and rideshares serve CBD, Southbank, and Inner North suburbs efficiently without relocating. Best transportation: Use: Melbourne transportation should primarily be treated as: FREE_TRAM_ZONE_AND_CITY_LOOP_FOR_URBAN_CIRCUITS + WALKING_FOR_LANEWAYS_AND_CULTURAL_PRECINCTS + V_LINE_EXPRESS_FOR_CROSS_STATE_TRIPS + PRIVATE_AC_CARS_FOR_OUTSTATION_COASTAL_DRIVES_AND_SANCTUARIES Must-do for first-time visitor: Melbourne should not be reduced to hotel luxury alone; official tourism positions HISTORIC_VICTORIAN_SITES + MODERN_TRAM_INFRASTRUCTURE + PROTECTED_NATIVE_SANCTUARIES + MULTICULTURAL_GASTRONOMY + WORLD_HERITAGE_PARKS as core destination pillars. Don''t-do: Biggest advantage: Unrivaled concentration of UNESCO World Heritage Victorian architecture, free urban tram connectivity, world-famous cafe & dining culture, and seamless regional coastal highway integration. Melbourne combines 19th-century grand boomtown architecture (Royal Exhibition Building), iconic street art and coffee laneways (Hosier Lane & Degraves Street), preserved native wildlife habitats (Healesville), and dynamic modern transport infrastructure (Free Tram Zone & City Link freeways) within a compact, easily navigable territory. Official tourism highlights the unique multicultural arts fusion, rich native wildlife sanctuaries, accessible express links to regional Victoria, and vibrant local culinary culture, catering to diverse travel styles. Biggest disadvantage: Unpredictable "four seasons in one day" weather shifts, strict advance online ticketing requirements during peak events seasons, and summer heatwave/winter coastal wind extremes. Navigating sprawling historic precincts and unpaved coastal trails requires significant physical stamina, summer peak days bring intense heatwaves while sudden southern ocean cold fronts can temporarily disrupt outdoor sightseeing, and high peak visitor arrivals require advance online planning across primary regional tours. Overall destination score: 95/100', 3736),
  ('melbourne', 36, 'data-quality', 'DATA QUALITY', NULL, NULL, 'information_completeness: 98/100 last_updated: 2026-09-03 last_verified: WEB_VERIFIED verified_by: VISIT VICTORIA (VISITMELBOURNE.COM) / PUBLIC TRANSPORT VICTORIA (PTV.VIC.GOV.AU) / NATIONAL GALLERY OF VICTORIA (NGV.VIC.GOV.AU) / HERITAGE COUNCIL VICTORIA / PARKS VICTORIA sources: IMPORTANT: Puffing Billy steam train passes, V/Line regional train tickets, Healesville Sanctuary online entry passes, major gallery exhibitions, and top fine-dining reservations must NOT be treated as permanently valid. Major attractions and regional rail lines have daily capacity limits and advance timed-entry rules; current slot availability must be verified online. Free City Trams, City Loop Metro Trains, and Private AC Cars are the standard transport choices, but real-time service updates and public holiday timetables should be verified on official booking platforms for actual travel dates. Melbourne''s climate varies significantly by season: SHOULDER WINDOWS (AUTUMN & SPRING) bring pleasant, clear days ideal for Botanic Gardens photography, NGV gallery walks, Great Ocean Road excursions, and laneway trips. SUMMER SEASON (DECEMBER – FEBRUARY) brings intense heatwaves (exceeding 40°C/104°F) interspersed with cool ocean breezes, requiring early morning sightseeing and air-conditioned gallery breaks. COOL / WINTER SEASON (JUNE – AUGUST) brings crisp, cool conditions with frequent rain showers, requiring warm layers and flexible indoor/outdoor daily schedules. Accessible tourism infrastructure is available across modern Metro train stations, major luxury hotels, Southern Cross Railway Station, and primary paved city precincts (Federation Square), but historic bluestone cobblestones, narrow arcade entryways, and steep coastal lookouts are rarely step-free. Melbourne should primarily be treated as: SHOULDER WINDOWS (AUTUMN & SPRING): MCG_HERITAGE + ROYAL_EXHIBITION + GREAT_OCEAN_ROAD + BOTANIC_GARDENS + LANEWAY_COFFEE_TOURS SUMMER SEASON (DECEMBER – FEBRUARY): ROOFTOP_DINING + NGV_INTERNATIONAL + ARTS_PRECINCT_SHOWS + INDOOR_GALLERY_VISITS + PENINSULA_COASTAL_STROLLS WINTER SEASON (JUNE – AUGUST): LANEWAY_PASTA_DINING + INDOOR_EXHIBITIONS + STATE_LIBRARY_READING_ROOM + FREE_TRAM_CIRCUITS + EVENING_THEATRE_SHOWS Visitmelbourne.com, PTV.vic.gov.au, NGV.vic.gov.au, and individual attraction reservation portals should be treated as primary sources for operational information. This dataset should be refreshed regularly before production use.', 3737),
  ('sydney', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Spring', NULL, 'months: September October November weather: Mild to warm with increasing sunshine and generally lower humidity than summer. Average temperatures progressively rise through the season, making outdoor sightseeing increasingly comfortable. crowd_level: MEDIUM → HIGH price_level: MEDIUM → HIGH overall_score: 84–91 recommended: true reason: One of Sydney''s strongest overall periods for harbour sightseeing, coastal walks, beaches, parks, photography, day trips, and outdoor dining before peak summer holiday demand. Best for: Tourism Australia identifies spring and summer as Sydney''s high season, with spring temperatures generally around 11–23°C and lower humidity than summer.', 3738),
  ('sydney', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Summer', NULL, 'months: December January February weather: Warm, humid, and generally excellent for beach travel. Average temperatures are roughly 19–26°C near central Sydney, although hotter periods can occur, especially farther inland. crowd_level: VERY_HIGH price_level: HIGH → VERY_HIGH overall_score: 72–82 recommended: true reason: Excellent for: Sydney is at its strongest for beaches, harbour activities, outdoor dining, and major events, but Christmas, New Year, school holidays, and summer demand significantly reduce crowd and price value.', 3739),
  ('sydney', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Autumn', NULL, 'months: March April May weather: Warm in March and gradually cooler through May. Humidity decreases and conditions become particularly comfortable for walking and outdoor sightseeing. crowd_level: MEDIUM → LOW price_level: MEDIUM overall_score: 86–93 recommended: true reason: One of Sydney''s best all-round seasons for harbour sightseeing, coastal walks, city touring, food, photography, and Blue Mountains excursions. Best for: Tourism Australia specifically describes autumn as Sydney''s mildest season and highlights it as an excellent period for coastal walking.', 3740),
  ('sydney', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Winter', NULL, 'months: June July August weather: Mild by international winter standards, with average daytime temperatures around 17–18°C and cool nights. June is historically one of the wetter months, while July and August are generally drier. crowd_level: LOW price_level: LOW → MEDIUM overall_score: 80–88 recommended: true reason: Excellent for: Sydney remains highly usable in winter because temperatures are relatively mild, while lower visitor pressure improves value compared with spring and summer. Official Sydney tourism specifically promotes winter for whale watching, hiking, museums, exhibitions, food, and cultural experiences.', 3741),
  ('sydney', 10, 'budget-strategy', 'BUDGET STRATEGY', NULL, NULL, 'Where money can be saved: Where saving money is usually NOT recommended: Travel-agent rule: In Sydney, **CONTACTLESS_OPAL_TRANSIT + ASIAN_FOOD_COURTS_AND_PUBS + INNER_CITY_OR_HARBOURSIDE_STAY + FREE_COASTAL_WALKS should be evaluated together**. For short stays, prioritize **CIRCULAR_QUAY_BASE + OPERA_HOUSE_AND_ROCKS_WALK + MANLY_FERRY_TRIP + BONDI_COASTAL_WALK**. For longer stays, add **BLUE_MOUNTAINS_TRAIN_EXCURSION + TARONGA_ZOO_VISIT + SURRY_HILLS_AND_BARANGAROO_DINING** rather than changing hotel bases frequently within the metropolitan core.', 3742),
  ('sydney', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Family', 'family', 'Sydney’s primary gateway is Sydney Kingsford Smith Airport (SYD), located 8 km south of the Central Business District (CBD), along with major rail hubs like Sydney Central Station for regional train arrivals. For families arriving with young children and multiple pieces of luggage via international or domestic flights, pre-booked airport minivans, private chauffeured AC sedans/SUVs, or rideshares (Uber, DiDi) from designated airport rideshare zones provide the smoothest transition directly to family-friendly accommodations in Circular Quay, Darling Harbour, or Sydney CBD. While the Airport Link T8 train connects Sydney Airport directly to CBD stations in 13–15 minutes, families with strollers and substantial luggage often find private transfers or rideshares more convenient for direct hotel drop-offs without navigating train station concourses or transfer lines.', 3743),
  ('sydney', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Honeymoon', 'honeymoon', 'Opt for pre-arranged luxury private transfers (e.g., chauffeured luxury sedans or premium SUVs) directly from Sydney Airport (International T1 or Domestic T2/T3) or Overseas Passenger Terminal to luxury harborside stays such as Park Hyatt Sydney, Crown Towers Sydney, or Capella Sydney. For multi-destination Australian honeymoon itineraries, combine: PRIVATE_AIRPORT_LUXURY_CAR_TRANSFER + SYDNEY_HARBOUR_WATER_TAXI_HOTEL_DROP_OFF + PRIVATE_CHAUFFEUR_FOR_BLUE_MOUNTAINS_AND_HUNTER_VALLEY_EXCURSIONS.', 3744),
  ('sydney', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Luxury', 'luxury', 'Utilize pre-booked private chauffeured transfers directly from Sydney Airport VIP arrivals, private jet terminals (Sydney Jet Base), or cruise ship terminals (Overseas Passenger Terminal in Circular Quay or White Bay Cruise Terminal). For complex luxury Australian itinerary circuits, combine: VIP_AIRPORT_MEET_AND_GREET + PRIVATE_LUXURY_SEDAN_TRANSFERS + CHARTERED_WATER_TAXI_HARBOUR_TRANSFERS + RESORT_VIP_CONCIERGE_AND_PRIVATE_YACHT_CHARTERS.', 3745),
  ('sydney', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Budget', 'budget', 'Take advantage of Sydney’s integrated public transit infrastructure and fare-capped transit options connecting arrival points across the city: For onward travel to coastal hubs (like Bondi Beach), utilize direct bus connections (Route 333) from Bondi Junction station.', 3746),
  ('sydney', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Senior', 'senior', 'Prioritize door-to-door pre-booked taxi/car transfers directly at terminal curbsides or hotel drop-offs to avoid extensive walking across multi-level airport train concourses or carrying luggage onto peak-hour trains. When navigating major urban precincts, select flat, step-free access routes, utilize the fully accessible Sydney Metro and Light Rail networks, and choose central accommodations near level harborside promenades around Circular Quay or Barangaroo.', 3747),
  ('sydney', 18, 'family-travel', 'FAMILY TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'child_friendly_score: 92 best_ages: Rules: For young children: Prefer: Avoid:', 3748),
  ('sydney', 19, 'honeymoon-travel', 'HONEYMOON TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'honeymoon_score: 95 romance_score: 94 privacy_score: 89 luxury_score: 96 Recommended: Honeymoon itineraries should generally stay at: 2–3 major experiences/day. Prefer: LUXURY_HARBOUR_VIEW_SUITES + PRIVATE_HERITAGE_TOURS + HOTEL_SPA_RELAXATION + FINE_DINING + OBSERVATORY_HILL_SUNSET + FREE_TIME over: Constant hotel changes and rushed daily multi-region commuting.', 3749),
  ('sydney', 20, 'luxury-travel', 'LUXURY TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'luxury_score: 97 Recommended:', 3750),
  ('sydney', 21, 'adventure', 'ADVENTURE', NULL, NULL, 'adventure_score: 82 Sydney offers focused coastal cliff trekking, ocean surfing, canyoning, skydiving, and harbor climbing rather than remote high-altitude mountaineering. Adventure experiences: Best regions: SYDNEY_HARBOUR_ZONE + BLUE_MOUNTAINS_NATIONAL_PARK + ROYAL_NATIONAL_PARK + NORTHERN_BEACHES_COASTLINE', 3751),
  ('sydney', 22, 'senior-travel', 'SENIOR TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'senior_suitability: 91 walking_intensity: LOW–MEDIUM for Royal Botanic Garden flat pathways, Barangaroo Reserve, Darling Harbour, and Manly Corso MEDIUM–HIGH for historic Rocks staircases, Bondi to Coogee coastal steps, and Blue Mountains lookout trails Rules: Sydney works exceptionally well for seniors as an: HARBOUR_SCENIC_HERITAGE + COASTAL_GASTRONOMY + LUXURY_WATERFRONT_COMFORT + ACCESSIBLE_PARK_VIEWS + PEACEFUL_BOTANIC_RELAXATION destination.', 3752),
  ('sydney', 23, 'accessibility', 'ACCESSIBILITY', NULL, NULL, 'wheelchair_accessibility: HIGH IN MODERN LUXURY RESORTS, MAJOR FERRY TERMINALS (CIRCULAR QUAY), LIGHT RAIL STATIONS, AND SYDNEY OPERA HOUSE FORECOURT VARIABLE TO LIMITED IN HISTORIC ROCKS ALLEYWAYS, STEPPED COASTAL CLIFF TRACKS, AND UNPAVED NATIONAL PARK TRAILS public_transport_accessibility: HIGH ON MODERN LIGHT RAIL, METRO, AND FERRIES; MODERATE ON OLDER BUS ROUTES WITH STEPS hotel_accessibility: MUST_BE_VERIFIED_PER_HOTEL attraction_accessibility: MUST_BE_VERIFIED_PER_ATTRACTION Rule: Never assume universal step-free access across historic stone staircases, cliffside walking tracks, and heritage precincts. Additional notes:', 3753),
  ('sydney', 24, 'food', 'FOOD', NULL, NULL, 'Sydney is particularly strong for: Food experiences: Family: Prioritize casual seafood baskets, wood-fired pizzas, gourmet burgers, fresh gelato, local pies, and fruit smoothies. Honeymoon: Choose romantic harbor-view dining, private waterfront tables, and fine dining tasting menus with wine pairings. Luxury: Include multi-course chef degustations, private chef yacht dining, and sommelier-led wine experiences. Budget: Use Spice Alley, Chinatown hawker stalls, local bakery shops, fish & chip takeaways by the beach, and suburban food hubs.', 3754),
  ('sydney', 25, 'shopping', 'SHOPPING', NULL, NULL, 'Strong categories: Luxury shopping: Prefer: Budget: Prefer: Travel-agent rule: Use STRAND_ARCADE / QUEEN_VICTORIA_BUILDING / CASTLEREAGH_STREET for HIGH_END_FASHION_OPALS_AND_JEWELRY, PADDINGTON_MARKETS / THE_ROCKS_MARKETS / NEWTOWN for VINTAGE_LOCAL_CRAFTS_AND_DESIGN, and PADDYS_MARKETS / LOCAL_SUPERMARKETS for BUDGET_SOUVENIRS_EDIBLE_GIFTS_AND_WINE.', 3755),
  ('sydney', 26, 'nightlife', 'NIGHTLIFE', NULL, NULL, 'nightlife_level: 78 Suitable for: Best areas: Evening activities: Sydney offers a diverse evening atmosphere focused on iconic harbor views, sophisticated cocktail lounges, world-class theatrical performances, and lively waterfront dining districts. Honeymoon travelers should generally prefer: ROOFTOP_HARBOUR_VIEWS + FINE_WATERFRONT_DINING + OPERA_SHOWS + SERENE_COCKTAIL_LOUNGES over: Crowded late-night dance clubs. Travel-agent rule: Position Sydney as a **HARBOUR_SUNSET_VIEWS + WATERFRONT_FINE_DINING + WORLD_CLASS_THEATRE + BAZAAR_AND_WHARF_NIGHT_WALKS DESTINATION**, with serene harbor relaxation and fine dining serving as primary highlight pillars.', 3756),
  ('sydney', 28, 'sample-itinerary-patterns', 'SAMPLE ITINERARY PATTERNS', '3 NIGHTS', NULL, '### Day 1 Arrival at Sydney Kingsford Smith Airport (SYD) → T8 Airport & South Line train, taxi, rideshare, or private transfer to central Sydney hotel → Hotel check-in & Opal Card / contactless public transport setup Afternoon: → Begin at Circular Quay overlooking Sydney Harbour → Walk through the historic sandstone lanes of The Rocks → Explore the exterior precinct of the UNESCO World Heritage-listed Sydney Opera House → Continue along the harbourfront into the Royal Botanic Garden Sydney → Walk towards Mrs Macquarie''s Point for classic Opera House & Harbour Bridge skyline views Evening: → Welcome dinner overlooking Sydney Harbour → Circular Quay & Opera House evening walk → Optional harbour cruise beneath the Sydney Harbour Bridge → Rooftop drinks / relaxed waterfront evening → Hotel SYD is Sydney''s primary international and domestic gateway. Airport stations are located beneath the terminals and are served by the T8 Airport & South Line, while Sydney''s Opal network covers trains, metro, buses, ferries and light rail, with contactless payment available for most visitors. ### Day 2 Morning: Breakfast → Travel towards Bondi Beach → Explore Australia''s famous urban beach and coastal promenade → Begin a section of the Bondi to Coogee Coastal Walk → Continue through Tamarama and Bronte according to available time → Beachside café / Australian brunch experience Afternoon: → Return towards central Sydney → Guided Sydney Opera House experience OR additional harbour exploration → Walk through Circular Quay & The Rocks → Take a classic Sydney ferry ride for panoramic harbour views → Explore Darling Harbour / Barangaroo waterfront precinct Evening: → Fine dining overlooking Sydney Harbour → Sydney Harbour Bridge & Opera House night photography → Optional Sydney Tower Eye / premium rooftop experience → Hotel Optional alternative instead of Bondi & central Sydney: BLUE_MOUNTAINS: → Full-day excursion to the UNESCO-listed Blue Mountains region → Echo Point → Three Sisters viewpoints → Scenic mountain landscapes → Bushwalking / Scenic World according to preference TARONGA_AND_HARBOUR: → Ferry from Circular Quay → Taronga Zoo Sydney → Australian wildlife experiences → Return across Sydney Harbour MANLY: → Scenic ferry from Circular Quay to Manly → Manly Beach → Coastal promenade → Beachfront lunch → Return by harbour ferry ### Day 3 Morning: Breakfast → Hotel checkout → Transfer to Sydney Airport (SYD) → Morning domestic flight to Gold Coast Airport (OOL) → Transfer towards Surfers Paradise / Broadbeach → Gold Coast hotel check-in / luggage drop Afternoon: → Explore Surfers Paradise Beach → Walk along the iconic beachfront & high-rise coastal precinct → Continue towards Broadbeach for cafés, shopping & relaxed beach atmosphere → Optional Burleigh Heads coastal exploration Evening: → Gold Coast sunset experience → SkyPoint Observation Deck / panoramic coastline views → Farewell beachfront dinner → Hotel Optional alternative for the Gold Coast afternoon: WILDLIFE: → Currumbin Wildlife Sanctuary → Native Australian wildlife encounters → Kangaroos, koalas, lorikeets & conservation experiences → Currumbin Beach THEME_PARK: Choose ONE: → Warner Bros. Movie World OR → Dreamworld OR → Sea World NATURE_AND_BEACHES: → Burleigh Heads → Burleigh Head National Park → Tallebudgera Creek → Surfers Paradise beachfront SPA & WELLNESS: → Luxury resort spa → Beachfront wellness experience → Pool / cabana relaxation → Sunset dining FAMILY: → Gold Coast theme park → Currumbin Wildlife Sanctuary → Surfers Paradise → Beach & family entertainment HONEYMOON: → Burleigh Heads coastal experience → Surfers Paradise sunset photography → Couple spa treatment → Romantic oceanfront dinner LUXURY: → Private scenic helicopter experience → Luxury Main Beach / Broadbeach resort → Premium spa & wellness → Fine-dining coastal restaurant For only 3 nights, prioritize: SYDNEY_HARBOUR_AND_THE_ROCKS + BONDI_AND_COASTAL_WALK + GOLD_COAST_SURFERS_PARADISE OR SYDNEY_HARBOUR_ICONS + BLUE_MOUNTAINS_OR_MANLY + GOLD_COAST_BEACH_AND_WILDLIFE rather than trying to add Melbourne, Brisbane or other distant Australian cities into the same short itinerary. ### Day 4 Breakfast → Leisurely morning beach walk at Surfers Paradise / Broadbeach → Relaxed café breakfast / souvenir shopping → Hotel checkout → Private transfer, taxi, rideshare, or Route 777 connection towards Gold Coast Airport (OOL) → Departure', 3757),
  ('sydney', 29, 'six-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 1', NULL, 'Arrival at Sydney Airport (SYD) → Private airport transfer → Romantic hotel check-in → Relax and refresh Afternoon: → Circular Quay → Sydney Opera House precinct → The Rocks → Couple photography Evening: → Sydney Harbour waterfront → Romantic dinner → Overnight at Sydney', 3758),
  ('sydney', 29, 'six-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 2', NULL, 'Breakfast at the hotel Morning: → Sydney Opera House guided tour → Harbour Bridge viewpoints → Royal Botanic Garden Afternoon: → Choose TWO Sydney attractions: → Sydney Tower Eye → SEA LIFE Sydney Aquarium → WILD LIFE Sydney Zoo → Madame Tussauds Sydney Evening: → Darling Harbour → Romantic harbour dinner → Overnight at Sydney', 3759),
  ('sydney', 29, 'six-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 3', NULL, 'Breakfast Morning: → Bondi Beach → Coastal viewpoints → Couple photography Afternoon: → Leisure / shopping → Circular Quay ferry experience → Sydney Harbour exploration Evening: → Sunset harbour experience → Farewell Sydney dinner → Overnight at Sydney', 3760),
  ('sydney', 29, 'six-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 4', NULL, 'Breakfast → Hotel checkout → Flight to Gold Coast → Private transfer to Surfers Paradise → Romantic hotel check-in Afternoon: → AquaDuck Safari → Surfers Paradise → Broadwater & Marina Mirage views Evening: → Beachfront sunset walk → Romantic dinner → Overnight at Gold Coast', 3761),
  ('sydney', 29, 'six-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 5', NULL, 'Breakfast Choose ONE: THEME_PARK → Warner Bros. Movie World → Rides & entertainment → Shows & attractions OR COASTAL_LEISURE → Surfers Paradise Beach → Broadbeach → Couple spa / relaxation Evening: → Leisure time → Overnight at Gold Coast', 3762),
  ('sydney', 29, 'six-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 6', NULL, 'Breakfast → Hotel checkout → Flight to Cairns → Romantic hotel check-in Choose ONE: RAINFOREST → Skyrail Rainforest Cableway → Barron Gorge → Rainforestation Nature Park → Aboriginal cultural experience OR REEF → Green Island cruise → Great Barrier Reef experience → Snorkelling / glass-bottom boat → Tropical island relaxation Evening: → Cairns Esplanade → Farewell romantic dinner → Overnight at Cairns', 3763),
  ('sydney', 29, 'six-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 7', NULL, 'Breakfast → Leisure morning → Hotel checkout → Private transfer to Cairns Airport → Departure', 3764),
  ('sydney', 30, 'six-nights-family-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 1', NULL, 'Arrival at Sydney Airport (SYD) → Airport transfer → Family hotel check-in → Relax and refresh Afternoon: → Circular Quay → Sydney Opera House precinct → The Rocks → Family photography Evening: → Sydney Harbour waterfront → Family dinner → Overnight at Sydney', 3765),
  ('sydney', 30, 'six-nights-family-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 2', NULL, 'Breakfast at the hotel Morning: → Sydney Opera House guided tour → Harbour Bridge viewpoints → Royal Botanic Garden Afternoon: → Choose TWO family attractions: → SEA LIFE Sydney Aquarium → WILD LIFE Sydney Zoo → Madame Tussauds Sydney → Sydney Tower Eye Evening: → Darling Harbour → Family leisure → Overnight at Sydney', 3766),
  ('sydney', 30, 'six-nights-family-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 3', NULL, 'Breakfast → Bondi Beach → Coastal sightseeing → Family photography Afternoon: → Sydney Harbour ferry experience → Circular Quay → Shopping / leisure time Evening: → Family dinner → Overnight at Sydney', 3767),
  ('sydney', 30, 'six-nights-family-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 4', NULL, 'Breakfast → Hotel checkout → Flight to Gold Coast → Transfer to Surfers Paradise → Family hotel check-in Afternoon: → AquaDuck Safari → Surfers Paradise → Broadwater sightseeing Evening: → Beachfront leisure → Family dinner → Overnight at Gold Coast', 3768),
  ('sydney', 30, 'six-nights-family-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 5', NULL, 'Breakfast → Full-day theme park experience Choose ONE: MOVIE_WORLD → Warner Bros. Movie World → Family rides → Characters & shows SEA_WORLD → Marine attractions → Family entertainment → Shows & exhibits WET_N_WILD → Water rides → Pools & family attractions Evening: → Return to hotel → Overnight at Gold Coast', 3769),
  ('sydney', 30, 'six-nights-family-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 6', NULL, 'Breakfast → Hotel checkout → Flight to Cairns → Family hotel check-in Choose ONE: RAINFOREST → Skyrail Rainforest Cableway → Barron Falls → Rainforestation Nature Park → Army Duck tour → Wildlife & Aboriginal experiences OR REEF → Green Island cruise → Great Barrier Reef → Snorkelling / glass-bottom boat → Semi-submarine experience Evening: → Cairns Esplanade → Farewell family dinner → Overnight at Cairns', 3770),
  ('sydney', 30, 'six-nights-family-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 7', NULL, 'Breakfast → Leisure morning → Hotel checkout → Transfer to Cairns Airport → Departure', 3771),
  ('sydney', 31, 'six-nights-luxury-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 1', NULL, 'Arrival at Sydney Airport (SYD) → Private luxury airport transfer → Premium harbour-view hotel check-in → Relax and refresh Afternoon: → Private Sydney Harbour orientation → Circular Quay → Sydney Opera House precinct → The Rocks Evening: → Premium harbourfront dining → Sydney skyline views → Overnight at Sydney', 3772),
  ('sydney', 31, 'six-nights-luxury-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 2', NULL, 'Breakfast at the hotel Morning: → Private Sydney Opera House experience → Harbour Bridge viewpoints → Royal Botanic Garden Afternoon: → Sydney Tower Eye → Premium Darling Harbour experience → Private / curated city sightseeing Evening: → Fine-dining harbour cruise → Overnight at Sydney', 3773),
  ('sydney', 31, 'six-nights-luxury-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 3', NULL, 'Breakfast Morning: → Private Bondi & Eastern Suburbs tour → Bondi Beach → Coastal viewpoints → Scenic photography Afternoon: → Luxury shopping → Spa / wellness → Harbour leisure Evening: → Premium rooftop / waterfront dinner → Overnight at Sydney', 3774),
  ('sydney', 31, 'six-nights-luxury-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 4', NULL, 'Breakfast → Hotel checkout → Premium flight to Gold Coast → Private luxury transfer to Surfers Paradise → Luxury resort check-in Afternoon: → Private / premium AquaDuck experience → Surfers Paradise → Marina Mirage → Broadwater Evening: → Sunset cocktails → Fine dining → Overnight at Gold Coast', 3775),
  ('sydney', 31, 'six-nights-luxury-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 5', NULL, 'Breakfast Choose ONE: PREMIUM_THEME_PARK → Warner Bros. Movie World → Private transfers → Curated ride & entertainment experience LUXURY_LEISURE → Resort spa & wellness → Surfers Paradise / Broadbeach → Premium beach cabana → Luxury shopping Evening: → Fine-dining experience → Overnight at Gold Coast', 3776),
  ('sydney', 31, 'six-nights-luxury-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 6', NULL, 'Breakfast → Hotel checkout → Premium flight to Cairns → Private luxury hotel transfer → Premium resort check-in Choose ONE: PREMIUM_RAINFOREST → Skyrail Rainforest Cableway → Barron Gorge → Rainforestation → Private / curated rainforest experience OR PREMIUM_REEF → Green Island / Great Barrier Reef cruise → Premium marine experience → Snorkelling / glass-bottom boat → Island leisure Evening: → Cairns waterfront → Farewell fine-dining experience → Overnight at Cairns', 3777),
  ('sydney', 31, 'six-nights-luxury-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 7', NULL, 'Breakfast → Leisure morning → Hotel checkout → Private luxury transfer to Cairns Airport → Departure', 3778),
  ('sydney', 32, 'travel-agent-insights', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS', 'What inexperienced planners often do wrong', NULL, '', 3779),
  ('sydney', 32, 'travel-agent-insights', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS', 'What an experienced planner does differently', NULL, 'OPERA_HOUSE_AND_HARBOUR_BRIDGE + MRS_MACQUARIES_CHAIR_AND_ROCKS + BLUE_MOUNTAINS_AND_MODERN_AUSTRALIAN_CUISINE rather than maximum destination count.', 3780),
  ('sydney', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', NULL, NULL, 'IF: trip_length <= 3 nights THEN: prioritize_OPERA_HOUSE_SUNRISE + HARBOUR_BRIDGE_HERITAGE + BLUE_MOUNTAINS_AND_WEST_SYDNEY Reason: Very short stays gain more value from properly experiencing core Australian heritage, world-famous harbour monuments, and charm-filled mountain eucalyptus wilderness than losing time to exhausting multi-state transit schedules. IF: trip_length >= 5 nights AND: traveler_interest == FIRST_TIME_SYDNEY THEN: prioritize_SYDNEY_HARBOUR_CENTRE + BARANGAROO_RESORT_ATTRACTIONS + BLUE_MOUNTAINS_AND_SANCTUARY + HUNTER_VALLEY_DAY_TRIP Reason: This gives a balanced introduction to harbour heritage, world-class waterfront entertainment, preserved national park wilderness, and seamless regional wine country day excursions. IF: trip_length >= 7 nights AND: traveler_interest == FIRST_TIME_SYDNEY THEN: prefer_CENTRAL_SYDNEY_CORE + MANLY_AND_NORTHERN_BEACHES_RETREAT + DAY_TRIPS_TO_BLUE_MOUNTAINS_AND_CANBERRA_VIA_EXPRESS_TRAIN AND: use_PRIVATE_AC_CARS_EXPRESS_TRAINS_AND_HARBOUR_FERRIES Reason: Luxury harbour resorts, coastal marine reserves, protected national park wilderness, and express rail connections to regional hubs offer distinct insights into Southeast Australia''s premier coastal corridor. IF: trip_type == HONEYMOON THEN: prioritize_CROWN_TOWERS_LUXURY_HARBOUR_RESORTS + CIRCULAR_QUAY_HERITAGE_STAYS + PRIVATE_HARBOUR_SUNSET_CHARTER AND: increase_BOUTIQUE_STAYS + ROOFTOP_OPERA_VIEW_DINING + LUXURY_URBAN_SPA + MODERN_AUSTRALIAN_TASTING + COUPLE_EXPERIENCES Reason: Sydney''s romantic routes mix ultra-luxury harbour-view suites, Pacific-rim multi-course fine dining, rooftop lounges overlooking glowing sails, and quiet walks along secluded harbor coves. IF: traveler_type == FAMILY THEN: prioritize_TARONGA_ZOO_FERRIES + CIRCULAR_QUAY_LIGHT_RAIL + SYDNEY_OPERA_HOUSE_FAMILY_SHOWS AND: include_ROYAL_BOTANIC_GARDEN_RUNS + INDIGENOUS_CULTURAL_WORKSHOPS_AT_BARANGAROO + DARLING_HARBOUR_PLAYGROUNDS AND: reduce_STEEP_CLIFF_STEPS + LONG_CONTINUOUS_TRANSFERS Reason: Sydney has exceptional family sights, including native wildlife harbour zoos, ferry rides across Port Jackson, interactive First Nations craft workshops, and vibrant waterfront play precincts. IF: traveler_type == LUXURY THEN: prefer_PARK_HYATT_SYDNEY + CROWN_TOWERS_SYDNEY + THE_LANGHAM_SYDNEY AND: increase_PRIVATE_GUIDES + FINE_DINING_AT_QUAY_AND_BENNELONG + PRIVATE_MPV_TRANSFERS + VIP_OPERA_HOUSE_ENTRY + SPA Reason: Sydney high-end travel relies on world-famous harbour-view luxury suites, multi-course modern Australian dining, private MPV transfers, and high-end waterfront hotel estates. IF: traveler_type == BUDGET THEN: prefer_OPAL_LIGHT_RAIL_AND_PUBLIC_FERRIES + SELF_GUIDED_WALKS + LOCAL_BAKERY_AND_TAKEAWAY_STALLS AND: book_FREE_HARBOUR_VIEW_POINTS_EARLY AND: balance_PAID_ATTRACTIONS_WITH_FREE_BOTANIC_GARDEN_STROLLS + THE_ROCKS_MARKET_WALKS + BONDI_TO_COOGEE_LOOKOUT_VIEWS Reason: Sydney can be accessed affordably using capped daily public transport, authentic suburban cafes, free botanical park walkways, and scenic coastal cliff viewpoints across Port Jackson. IF: traveler_interest == CULTURE_AND_HERITAGE THEN: prioritize_SYDNEY_OPERA_HOUSE + THE_ROCKS_HISTORIC_PRECINCT + QUEEN_VICTORIA_BUILDING + FIRST_NATIONS_BARANGAROO AND: include_COLONIAL_ARCHITECTURE + INDIGENOUS_HERITAGE + LOCAL_ARTS_FESTIVALS Reason: These sights showcase Sydney''s unique history, mixing thousands of years of Indigenous Gadigal heritage with colonial sandstone architecture and iconic modern design. IF: traveler_interest == ART_AND_ARCHITECTURE THEN: prioritize_ART_GALLERY_OF_NSW + MCA_AUSTRALIA + OPERA_HOUSE_ARCHITECTURE_TOURS + QVB_STAINED_GLASS AND: include_CONTEMPORARY_WATERFRONT_GALLERIES + HISTORIC_SANDSTONE_RENEWAL + ECO_RESORT_DESIGN Reason: This route contrasts modern architectural masterpieces with colonial sandstone arches, contemporary visual art spaces, and historic Australian craftsmanship. IF: traveler_interest == GASTRONOMY THEN: prefer_SYDNEY_ROCK_OYSTERS + MODERN_AUSTRALIAN_SEAFOOD + PACIFIC_RIM_FUSION + ARTISANAL_SPECIALTY_COFFEE AND: include_FISH_MARKET_STALLS + SURRY_HILLS_BISTROS + WATERFRONT_FINE_DINING Reason: Sydney dining spans iconic harbour seafood markets, specialty third-wave coffee, vibrant Asian hawker markets, and world-class fine dining overlooking the water. IF: traveler_interest == NATURE_AND_WILDLIFE THEN: prioritize_BLUE_MOUNTAINS_NATIONAL_PARK + TARONGA_ZOO_CONSERVATION + FEATHERDALE_WILDLIFE_PARK + ROYAL_BOTANIC_GARDEN AND: do_not_treat_MANICURED_CITY_GARDENS_AND_NATIONAL_PARK_BUSH_TRAILS_AS_IDENTICAL Reason: City gardens offer manicured lawns and harbour views, while surrounding national parks and wildlife sanctuaries feature wild eucalyptus forests, native koalas, and coastal marine ecosystems. IF: traveler_interest == SHOPPING THEN: prioritize_QUEEN_VICTORIA_BUILDING + PADDINGTON_OXFORD_STREET + THE_ROCKS_MARKETS + WESTFIELD_SYDNEY AND: include_OPAL_BOUTIQUES + INDIGENOUS_ART_GALLERIES + LOCAL_DESIGNER_FASHION Reason: QVB offers high-end heritage architecture shopping, Oxford Street supplies boutique Australian designer fashion, and The Rocks features authentic artisan crafts and opals. IF: traveler_interest == SAUNA_AND_WELLNESS THEN: choose_LUXURY_URBAN_SPAS + TRADITIONAL_OCEAN_BATHS_SWIMMING + HYDROTHERAPY_SANCTUARIES AND: do_not_treat_LOCAL_OCEAN_POOLS_AND_MODERN_RESORT_HOTEL_SPAS_AS_IDENTICAL Reason: Sydney wellness ranges from historic ocean rockpools and beach swimming to world-class luxury hotel spa retreats overlooking the harbour. IF: traveler_interest == PHOTOGRAPHY THEN: prioritize_OPERA_HOUSE_SUNRISE + MRS_MACQUARIES_CHAIR_SUNSET + BRIDGE_CLIMB_LOOKOUT + OBSERVATORY_HILL_VIEWPOINT AND: prioritize_GOLDEN_HOUR + BLUE_HOUR + CLEAR_AIR_DAYS Reason: These sites produce stunning visual contrasts between glowing white architectural sails, dark blue ocean waters, and golden sandstone headlands. IF: trip_length <= 5 nights THEN: prefer_MAXIMUM_ONE_OR_TWO_BASES AND: avoid_EXCESSIVE_HOTEL_CHANGES Reason: City traffic navigation, ferry boarding schedules, and regional road transfers consume valuable sightseeing hours. IF: route == SYDNEY_CBD_TO_BLUE_MOUNTAINS_OR_HUNTER_VALLEY THEN: prefer_DIRECT_CAR_RENTALS_PRIVATE_TRANSFERS_OR_EXPRESS_TRAINS_OVER_MULTIPLE_LOCAL_BUS_TRANSFERS Reason: Direct express trains and private car transfers eliminate transit confusion and save energy for exploring national parks and cellar doors. IF: traveler_type == SENIOR OR: traveler_mobility == LIMITED THEN: prefer_ACCESSIBLE_HARBOUR_HOTELS + FLAT_BARANGAROO_FORESHORE_PROMENADE + PRIVATE_MPV + BOTANIC_GARDEN_ACCESSIBLE_PATHWAYS AND: reduce_EXCESSIVE_CLIFF_STEPS + BLUE_MOUNTAINS_INCLINES + EXTREME_SUMMER_HEAT_WALKS Reason: Steep coastal stairs and cliffside trails cause fatigue; harbour ferries, light rail, private MPVs, and flat foreshore pathways ease travel. IF: traveler_uses_WHEELCHAIR THEN: prefer_VERIFIED_ACCESSIBLE_RESORTS + OPERA_HOUSE_ACCESSIBLE_ROUTES + FLAT_HOTEL_GROUNDS + BARANGAROO_PAVED_PATHS AND: do_not_assume_HISTORIC_BUSH_TRAILS + ANCIENT_VIEWPOINTS + SECLUDED_COASTAL_COVES_ARE_STEP_FREE Reason: Major modern luxury resorts and primary ferry wharves are accessible, but historic rocky headlands, deep gorge walking tracks, and old cobblestone lanes present physical barriers. IF: weather == EXTREME_SUMMER_HEAT AND: region == SYDNEY_TERRITORY THEN: prioritize_EARLY_MORNING_HARBOUR_VISITS + AIR_CONDITIONED_MUSEUMS_AND_STORES + EVENING_WATERFRONT_DINING AND: reduce_MIDDAY_UNSHADED_BEACH_EXPOSURE Reason: Sydney summer temps routinely exceed high heat (over 35°C); early starts and air-conditioned indoor breaks maintain comfort. IF: weather == HEAVY_RAIN_OR_COASTAL_GATOR THEN: increase_ART_GALLERY_OF_NSW + CAPITOL_THEATRE + INDOOR_RESORT_ENTERTAINMENT + QUEEN_VICTORIA_BUILDING_STORES AND: reduce_CLIFFTOP_OUTDOOR_DECKS + OUTDOOR_BEACH_PROMENADES Reason: Indoor art museums, theatrical shows, covered shopping arcades, and harbour lounges remain excellent regardless of outdoor downpours or heavy swell. IF: traveler_interest == FIRST_TIME_SYDNEY THEN: prioritize_SYDNEY_OPERA_HOUSE + HARBOUR_BRIDGE + BLUE_MOUNTAINS + MANLY_BEACH AND: add_ONE_OF_TARONGA_ZOO_BARANGAROO_OR_BONDI_COASTAL_WALK AND: include_ONE_SIGNATURE_PACIFIC_SEAFOOD_OR_SPECIALTY_COFFEE_EXPERIENCE Reason: This structure provides a comprehensive introduction to Sydney''s premier architectural heritage alongside authentic local food and beach culture. IF: traveler_interest == CULTURE_AND_RELAXATION_BALANCE THEN: allocate_60_TO_70_PERCENT_TO_CORE_SIGHTSEEING AND: allocate_REMAINING_TIME_TO_HARBOUR_CAFES + BEACH_LOUNGES + SPAS + SUNSET_BARS + SHOPPING + FREE_TIME', 3781),
  ('sydney', 34, 'destination-scoring', 'DESTINATION SCORING', NULL, NULL, '| Factor | Score | | --- | --- | | Family | 94 | | Honeymoon | 94 | | Luxury | 95 | | Budget | 72 | | Adventure | 88 | | Culture | 91 | | Food | 96 | | Shopping | 89 | | Nightlife | 82 | | Relaxation | 89 | | Nature | 95 | | Accessibility | 86 | | Safety | 92 | | First-time visitor | 98 | | Photography | 99 |', 3782),
  ('sydney', 35, 'final-travel-agent-verdict', 'FINAL TRAVEL AGENT VERDICT', NULL, NULL, 'Best traveler profiles: 1. Honeymoon / romantic traveler (Park Hyatt Sydney Harbour-View Suite, Capella Sydney, Private Harbour Dining Cruise, Camp Cove Sunset Promenade) 2. First-time Australia / East Coast traveler 3. Culture / heritage traveler (Sydney Opera House, Hyde Park Barracks, Museum of Contemporary Art Australia, Australian Museum, Rocks Historic Precinct) 4. Aboriginal heritage & coastal history traveler (First Nations Cultural Tours, Barangaroo Reserve Heritage Walks, Royal Botanic Garden Bush Food Tours, Ku-ring-gai Chase Rock Art) 5. Luxury / architectural design traveler (Park Hyatt Sydney, Capella Sydney, Crown Towers Sydney at Barangaroo, The Langham Sydney) 6. Photography traveler (Sydney Opera House Bennelong Point sunrise, Mrs Macquarie''s Chair golden hour, Sydney Harbour Bridge Pylon Lookout, Hornby Lighthouse South Head views) 7. Food / gastronomy traveler (Bennelong & Quay Fine Dining, Sydney Fish Market Seafood Tasting, Surrey Hills & Paddington Cafe Culture, Barangaroo Waterfront Dining, Marrickville Craft Brewery Crawl) 8. Family traveler (Taronga Zoo Waterfront Precinct, SEA LIFE Sydney Aquarium, Darling Harbour Playground, Manly Ferry Ocean Crossing, Cockatoo Island Exploration) 9. Modern art & urban lifestyle traveler (Sydney Modern Project / AGNSW Expansion, Carriageworks Eveleigh Markets, Paddington Boutiques, Barangaroo Waterfront Promenade) 10. Budget / independent traveler (Sydney Light Rail & Metro Lines, Coastal Cliff Walking Trails, Public Ocean Pools & Beaches, Paddy''s Market Stalls) Best duration: 3–5 nights 1–2 nights: Best for ONE primary focus such as Sydney Harbour Landmarks & Opera House Express Trip. 3–4 nights: Best for TWO major bases/focuses such as Central Harbour & Culture + Bondi to Coogee Coastal Walk & Manly Beach Excursion. 5–6 nights: Excellent for Sydney Harbour + Coastal Beaches + Blue Mountains World Heritage National Park Day Trip + Hunter Valley Wine Region Tour. 7–8 nights: Best for deep regional New South Wales travel, Grand Pacific Drive road trips, Southern Highlands excursions, or high-speed XPT transit connections to Melbourne or Brisbane. Best season: YEAR-ROUND Shoulder / Dry Windows (October & March): PLEASANT_TEMPERATURES + OPTIMAL_CLEAR_SKIES + SHARP_HARBOUR_VISIBILITY + VIBRANT_OUTDOOR_DINING + SPRING_BLOOM_FESTIVALS. Peak Summer / Coastal Season (December – February): WARM_BEACH_WEATHER + OCEAN_POOL_SWIMMING + HARBOUR_CRUISES + NEW_YEARS_EVE_FIREWORKS. Cool / Winter Season (June – August): CRISP_COOL_DAYS + VIVID_SYDNEY_LIGHT_FESTIVAL + WHALE_WATCHING_COASTAL_CRUISES + COZY_HARBOUR_DINING. Festive / Spring Season (September – November): JACARANDA_PURPLE_BLOOMS + OUTDOOR_CULTURE_EVENTS + SUNNY_COASTAL_WALKS + SPRING_GASTRONOMY. Destination New South Wales guidance treats the city as year-round: October and March are world-famous for pleasant temperatures, crystal-clear skies, and seasonal cultural festivals; December through February for warm beach days and harbour fireworks; June through August for crisp clear days and the Vivid Sydney light festival; and September through November for blooming jacarandas and sunny coastal walks. Best hotel strategy: Choose accommodation according to transit convenience, atmosphere, and trip purpose. For first-time visitors: CIRCULAR_QUAY_OR_DARLING_HARBOUR (Circular Quay transit hub or Darling Harbour promenade) for direct walking/ferry access to top attractions, restaurants, and Sydney Metro stations. For heritage / coastal charm: THE_ROCKS_OR_MANLY_BEACH (Boutique hotels in historic The Rocks or Manly Beachfront) for authentic local living, coastal harbour vistas, and historic pub culture. For luxury & modern design: BARANGAROO_OR_SURRY_HILLS selectively according to harbourfront fine dining, private skyline pool suites, and boutique wellness spas. Avoid unnecessary hotel changes within Sydney; light rail lines, Sydney Ferries, and Sydney Metro serve Circular Quay, Barangaroo, and Eastern Suburbs efficiently without relocating. Best transportation: Use: Sydney transportation should primarily be treated as: SYDNEY_FERRIES_AND_METRO_FOR_HARBOUR_CIRCUITS + WALKING_FOR_HISTORIC_ROCKS_AND_BARANGAROO_MARKETS + LIGHT_RAIL_AND_BUSES_FOR_CROSS_CITY_TRIPS + INTERCITY_TRAINS_FOR_OUTSTATION_PARKS_AND_REGIONS Must-do for first-time visitor: Sydney should not be reduced to hotel pools alone; official tourism positions HARBOUR_ICONIC_LANDMARKS + MODERN_METRO_INFRASTRUCTURE + PROTECTED_NATIONAL_PARKS + NEW_SOUTH_WALES_GASTRONOMY + WORLD_HERITAGE_SITES as core destination pillars. Don''t-do: Biggest advantage: Unrivaled concentration of UNESCO World Heritage architecture, modern metro and ferry connectivity, world-famous coastal gastronomy, and seamless New South Wales regional express integration. Sydney combines a 20th-century architectural masterpiece (Sydney Opera House), iconic historic harbour docks and markets (The Rocks & Paddy''s Markets), preserved natural wilderness (Blue Mountains), and dynamic modern transport infrastructure (Sydney Metro & Ferries) within a compact, easily navigable territory. Official tourism highlights the unique Indigenous-contemporary culture fusion, rich marine and wildlife sanctuaries, accessible express links to regional NSW, and vibrant local culinary culture, catering to diverse travel styles. Biggest disadvantage: Intense summer UV rays and heat waves, strict advance online ticketing requirements during peak holiday seasons, and severe coastal storm weather shifts. Navigating coastal cliff pathways and sprawling national parks requires significant physical stamina, summer peak months bring high heat and UV exposure while ocean weather can temporarily disrupt ferry transit schedules, and high peak visitor arrivals require advance online planning across primary performance venues. Overall destination score: 96/100', 3783),
  ('sydney', 36, 'data-quality', 'DATA QUALITY', NULL, NULL, 'information_completeness: 98/100 last_updated: 2026-09-03 last_verified: WEB_VERIFIED verified_by: DESTINATION NEW SOUTH WALES (VISITNSW.COM / SYDNEY.COM) / TRANSPORT FOR NSW (TRANSPORTNSW.INFO) / UNESCO WORLD HERITAGE CENTRE / BUREAU OF METEOROLOGY (BOM) / OFFICIAL VENUE AUTHORITIES sources: IMPORTANT: Sydney Opera House headline performance passes, BridgeClimb allocations, Sydney Harbour NYE vantage point access, top restaurant reservations, and regional tour slots must NOT be treated as permanently valid. Major venues and ferry routes have capacity thresholds and advance ticket rules; current slot availability must be verified online. Sydney Metro, Ferries, Light Rail, and Rideshares are the standard transport choices, but real-time service disruptions or trackwork should be verified on official transit platforms for actual travel dates. Sydney''s climate varies significantly by season: SHOULDER WINDOWS (OCTOBER & MARCH) bring pleasant, clear days ideal for Sydney Harbour photography, urban heritage walks, Blue Mountains excursions, and coastal beach walks. SUMMER / HUMID SEASON (DECEMBER – FEBRUARY) brings hot sun (exceeding 35°C/95°F) with high UV indices, requiring early morning coastal walks and shaded/indoor museum breaks. COOL / WINTER SEASON (JUNE – AUGUST) brings crisp, clear weather with mild temperatures, requiring a light jacket for harbour ferry rides and flexible morning outdoor schedules. Accessible tourism infrastructure is available across modern Sydney Metro stations, primary Sydney Ferries wharves, major luxury hotels, Central Station, and main paved foreshore paths (Circular Quay to Barangaroo), but historic sandstone steps, coastal cliff stairs, and bushwalking trails are rarely step-free. Sydney should primarily be treated as: SHOULDER WINDOWS (OCTOBER & MARCH): SYDNEY_OPERA_HOUSE + HARBOUR_BRIDGE + BLUE_MOUNTAINS + BONDI_COASTAL_WALK + HERITAGE_ROCKS_TOURS SUMMER / BEACH SEASON (DECEMBER – FEBRUARY): HARBOUR_FERRY_CRUISES + MCA_AND_AGNSW + COASTAL_OCEAN_POOLS + INDOOR_PERFORMANCES + WATERFRONT_DINING WINTER / VIVID SEASON (JUNE – AUGUST): FINE_GASTRONOMY_DINING + LIGHT_FESTIVAL_WALKS + MUSEUM_EXHIBITIONS + WHALE_WATCHING + EVENING_THEATRE_SHOWS VisitNSW.com, Sydney.com, TransportNSW.info, and individual venue reservation portals should be treated as primary sources for operational information. This dataset should be refreshed regularly before production use.', 3784),
  ('suva', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Spring', NULL, 'months: September October November weather: September and October generally fall within Fiji''s relatively drier and cooler part of the year, although Suva remains humid and rainfall can occur at any time. November marks the transition toward the wetter and warmer cyclone-season period. crowd_level: MEDIUM price_level: MEDIUM overall_score: 78.00–79.33 recommended: true reason: September and October offer one of Suva''s strongest combinations of comfortable temperatures, comparatively lower rainfall risk and good conditions for city walking and rainforest excursions. Best for:', 3785),
  ('suva', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Summer', NULL, 'months: December January February weather: Warm, humid and frequently wet. This period overlaps Fiji''s tropical-cyclone season and Suva''s already wet south-eastern climate, so heavy rain and weather disruptions must remain part of itinerary planning. crowd_level: MEDIUM price_level: MEDIUM overall_score: 65.00–68.67 recommended: true_with_weather_flexibility reason: Suva remains culturally active year-round and indoor sightseeing is strong, but rainfall, humidity, storms and cyclone risk reduce outdoor reliability. Best for:', 3786),
  ('suva', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Autumn', NULL, 'months: March April May weather: March remains warm and wet, April begins a gradual transition, and May generally brings cooler and relatively drier conditions suitable for longer outdoor sightseeing. crowd_level: LOW → MEDIUM price_level: MEDIUM overall_score: 71.33–81.00 recommended: true_from_april_onward reason: Conditions progressively improve toward May, creating a strong balance for rainforest, waterfront and heritage sightseeing while retaining manageable urban visitor pressure. Best for:', 3787),
  ('suva', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Winter', NULL, 'months: June July August weather: Generally cooler and comparatively drier than the wet-season months, although Suva remains one of Fiji''s wetter urban areas and showers are possible throughout the year. crowd_level: MEDIUM price_level: MEDIUM overall_score: 75.67–81.00 recommended: true reason: Winter provides some of the year''s most comfortable conditions for city walking, markets, rainforest exploration and outdoor cultural sightseeing. Best for:', 3788),
  ('suva', 10, 'budget-strategy', 'BUDGET STRATEGY', NULL, NULL, 'Where money can be saved: The Fiji Museum remains a relatively low-cost national cultural attraction. Current official museum pricing differentiates between local and overseas visitors, with overseas admission higher than local-resident rates. Where saving money is usually NOT recommended: Travel-agent rule: In Suva, **CENTRAL_HOTEL + WALKABLE_CBD + LOCAL_MARKETS + SELECTIVE_TAXIS + ONE_NATURE_EXCURSION** provides excellent value. For short stays, prioritize: **FIJI_MUSEUM + THURSTON_GARDENS + ALBERT_PARK + SUVA_MARKET + CUMMING_STREET + WATERFRONT**. For longer stays, add: **COLO_I_SUVA + USP_LAUCALA_BAY + MY_SUVA_PARK + LOCAL_NEIGHBORHOODS + MOUNT_KOROBABA + NIGHTLIFE**. Operational note: Museum admission, park fees, guided walks, taxi rates, transport-payment procedures and attraction hours should be rechecked before travel.', 3789),
  ('suva', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Family', 'family', 'Airport transfer by: PRE_BOOKED_TRANSFER_OR_TAXI + DIRECT_HOTEL_TRANSFER is generally the simplest option from Nausori Airport. Choose accommodation around central Suva, Victoria Parade, Nasese or another well-connected urban area according to itinerary and hotel preference.', 3790),
  ('suva', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Honeymoon', 'honeymoon', 'Prefer: PRIVATE_TRANSFER + PREMIUM_HOTEL + WATERFRONT_AND_DINING_ACCESS for a comfortable short cultural stop before or after an island or resort stay.', 3791),
  ('suva', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Luxury', 'luxury', 'Use: AIRPORT_MEET_AND_GREET + CHAUFFEURED_SEDAN_OR_SUV + PREMIUM_HOTEL + PRIVATE_SIGHTSEEING_VEHICLE Private transport is particularly useful when Suva is combined with Pacific Harbour, Coral Coast or other Viti Levu destinations.', 3792),
  ('suva', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Budget', 'budget', 'Primary options: Because central Suva''s sightseeing core is relatively compact, excessive local transfer spending is rarely necessary after hotel arrival.', 3793),
  ('suva', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Senior', 'senior', 'Prefer: DIRECT_AIRPORT_TRANSFER + CENTRAL_HOTEL + DOOR_TO_DOOR_TAXI_OR_PRIVATE_CAR Rain, humidity, road crossings and variable footpath conditions make direct transport preferable for mobility-limited travelers.', 3794),
  ('suva', 18, 'family-travel', 'FAMILY TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'child_friendly_score: 85 best_ages: Rules: For young children: Prefer: Avoid:', 3795),
  ('suva', 19, 'honeymoon-travel', 'HONEYMOON TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'honeymoon_score: 70 romance_score: 76 privacy_score: 72 luxury_score: 78 Recommended: Honeymoon itineraries should generally stay at: 2–3 major experiences/day. Prefer: PREMIUM_HOTEL + WATERFRONT + CULTURAL_EXPERIENCE + DINING + PRIVATE_TRANSPORT + FREE_TIME over: Continuous urban sightseeing. Suva is best positioned as a: CULTURAL_CITY_EXTENSION within a Fiji honeymoon rather than the principal honeymoon destination.', 3796),
  ('suva', 20, 'luxury-travel', 'LUXURY TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'luxury_score: 78 Recommended: Suva is particularly strong for: PACIFIC_CITY_LUXURY + PRIVATE_ROAD_TRANSPORT + CULTURE + PREMIUM_DINING + BUSINESS_AND_DIPLOMATIC_TRAVEL.', 3797),
  ('suva', 21, 'adventure', 'ADVENTURE', NULL, NULL, 'adventure_score: 69 Suva offers primarily rainforest, hiking and soft outdoor adventure. Adventure experiences: Best regions: COLO_I_SUVA + MOUNT_KOROBABA + LAMI + SUVA_HARBOUR + PACIFIC_HARBOUR_GATEWAY Travel-agent positioning: Suva should be treated as: RAINFOREST_HIKING + NATURAL_POOLS + URBAN_ADVENTURE + PACIFIC_HARBOUR_GATEWAY rather than a major beach or high-adrenaline destination in its own right.', 3798),
  ('suva', 22, 'senior-travel', 'SENIOR TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'senior_suitability: 79 walking_intensity: LOW for Fiji Museum, Thurston Gardens, Albert Park, waterfront areas and road-connected sightseeing. LOW–MEDIUM for extended CBD, markets and heritage walking. MEDIUM–HIGH for Colo-i-Suva and Mount Korobaba. Rules: Suva works well for seniors as a: FIJIAN_CULTURE + MUSEUMS + GARDENS + MARKETS + FOOD + RELAXED_CITY_BREAK destination when transport and weather are managed carefully.', 3799);
INSERT INTO destination_guidance (place_id, section, topic, section_title, heading, audience, body, position) VALUES
  ('suva', 23, 'accessibility', 'ACCESSIBILITY', NULL, NULL, 'wheelchair_accessibility: MODERATE IN CENTRAL HOTELS, ROAD_CONNECTED_PUBLIC_AREAS AND SELECTED CULTURAL FACILITIES VARIABLE ACROSS FOOTPATHS, HERITAGE BUILDINGS AND OUTDOOR ATTRACTIONS public_transport_accessibility: LIMITED → MODERATE hotel_accessibility: GENERALLY_BETTER_IN_MODERN_AND_INTERNATIONAL_STANDARD_HOTELS_BUT_MUST_BE_VERIFIED attraction_accessibility: MUST_BE_VERIFIED_PER_ATTRACTION Rule: Do not assume every market, heritage building, garden, waterfront path or rainforest attraction is fully step-free. Additional notes: Suva accessibility should therefore be classified as: MODERATELY_ACCESSIBLE_WITH_ROUTE_AND_ATTRACTION_VERIFICATION.', 3800),
  ('suva', 24, 'food', 'FOOD', NULL, NULL, 'Suva is particularly strong for: Food experiences: Family: Prioritize rice, roti, curries, grilled meats, seafood, tropical fruit, cafés and familiar international options. Honeymoon: Choose premium Pacific dining, hotel restaurants, cocktail bars and relaxed waterfront or garden-oriented venues. Luxury: Include chef-led Fijian dining, premium seafood, upscale Pacific cuisine and international hotel restaurants. Budget: Use municipal markets, casual Fijian restaurants, Indo-Fijian eateries, bakeries, cafés and food courts. Travel-agent rule: Position Suva food around: FIJIAN_CUISINE + INDO_FIJIAN_FOOD + PACIFIC_SEAFOOD + LOCAL_MARKETS + MULTICULTURAL_DINING.', 3801),
  ('suva', 25, 'shopping', 'SHOPPING', NULL, NULL, 'Strong categories: Premium shopping: Prefer: Local shopping: Prefer: Budget: Prefer: Travel-agent rule: Use: SUVA_MUNICIPAL_MARKET for PRODUCE_AND_LOCAL_LIFE, FLEA_MARKET for HANDICRAFTS, CUMMING_STREET for BUSY_LOCAL_RETAIL, ROC_MARKET for LOCAL_ARTISANS_AND_DESIGN, CBD_MALLS for MODERN_RETAIL_AND_WEATHER_PROTECTED_SHOPPING.', 3802),
  ('suva', 26, 'nightlife', 'NIGHTLIFE', NULL, NULL, 'nightlife_level: 89 Suitable for: Best areas: Evening activities: Suva nightlife is strongest for: DINING + BARS + LIVE_MUSIC + NIGHTCLUBS + SOCIAL_EVENINGS rather than: BEACH_CLUB_AND_RESORT_NIGHTLIFE. Couples should generally prefer: WATERFRONT_EVENING + DINNER + LIVE_MUSIC_OR_BAR + RELAXED_CITY_NIGHT over: Overloaded late-night scheduling.', 3803),
  ('suva', 28, 'sample-itinerary-patterns', 'SAMPLE ITINERARY PATTERNS', '5 NIGHTS', NULL, '### Day 1 Arrival at Nausori International Airport (SUV) → Private transfer from Nausori towards Suva → Suva hotel check-in & relax after arrival Afternoon: → Begin exploring Fiji''s capital around central Suva → Suva Municipal Market → Historic city centre → Government Buildings precinct → Albert Park → Thurston Gardens Evening: → Suva waterfront / harbour-side exploration → Welcome dinner featuring Fijian, Indo-Fijian & Pacific cuisine → Relaxed evening in central Suva → Hotel Nausori International Airport (SUV) serves the Suva region and is located approximately 23 km northeast of central Suva. Suva is Fiji''s capital and major urban, administrative and cultural centre on the southeastern coast of Viti Levu. ### Day 2 Morning: Breakfast → Fiji Museum → Thurston Gardens → Explore Suva''s colonial-era architecture & historic precincts → Suva Municipal Market → Local handicrafts & tropical produce Afternoon: → Explore central Suva → Cumming Street / shopping precinct → Local café & Indo-Fijian culinary experience → Continue towards the waterfront Evening: → Suva sunset / harbour views → Traditional Fijian or Indo-Fijian dinner → Hotel Optional alternative: COLO_I_SUVA: → Excursion to Colo-i-Suva Forest Park → Tropical rainforest → Nature trails → Forest pools → Birdlife & photography ### Day 3 Morning: Breakfast → Day excursion through the greater Suva / Nausori region → Explore Nausori town → Rewa River landscapes → Local markets & everyday Fijian town life Afternoon: Choose ONE: NAUSORI_AND_REWA: → Nausori town → Rewa River scenery → Local cultural exploration → Countryside landscapes PACIFIC_HARBOUR: → Scenic drive from Suva → Pacific Harbour → Beach / resort leisure → Adventure activities according to preference → Tropical landscapes Evening: → Return to Suva → Relaxed dinner → Hotel ### Day 4 Morning: Breakfast → Hotel checkout → Begin scenic overland journey from Suva along southern Viti Levu → Travel through the Coral Coast → Continue towards Sigatoka Afternoon: → Explore Sigatoka town → Visit Sigatoka Sand Dunes National Park → Scenic dunes, coastline & archaeological landscape → Optional Fijian village / cultural experience → Continue along the Coral Coast Evening: → Beachfront sunset → Resort dinner → Overnight around Sigatoka / Coral Coast ### Day 5 Morning: Breakfast → Continue west towards Nadi → Explore Nadi town → Sri Siva Subramaniya Temple → Local market & handicraft shopping Afternoon: → Garden of the Sleeping Giant → Tropical gardens & landscaped walking trails → Continue north towards Lautoka → Explore Lautoka city & local market area → Scenic Vuda / western Viti Levu surroundings according to time Evening: → Return towards Nadi / Denarau → Sunset waterfront experience → Farewell Fijian dinner → Overnight at Nadi / Denarau Optional alternative for western Viti Levu: ISLAND_ESCAPE: → Port Denarau → Mamanuca Islands day / half-day cruise → Tropical beaches → Snorkelling → Island relaxation FAMILY: → Coral Coast family resort activities → Kula Wild Adventure Park → Nadi cultural experience → Beach activities HONEYMOON: → Private Coral Coast beach experience → Couple spa treatment → Sunset cruise from Denarau → Romantic beachfront dinner LUXURY: → Private chauffeured Viti Levu transfer → Premium Coral Coast resort → Private yacht / island excursion → Luxury Denarau resort → Fine dining For only 5 nights, prioritize: SUVA_CITY_AND_FIJI_CULTURE + NAUSORI_AND_RAINFOREST + SIGATOKA_AND_CORAL_COAST + NADI_AND_LAUTOKA OR SUVA_AND_NAUSORI + COLO_I_SUVA_OR_PACIFIC_HARBOUR + SIGATOKA_CORAL_COAST + NADI_AND_WESTERN_VITI_LEVU rather than adding distant outer islands and creating excessive transfers during a short Viti Levu itinerary. ### Day 6 Breakfast → Leisurely morning around Nadi / Denarau → Final souvenir shopping → Hotel checkout → Transfer to Nadi International Airport (NAN) → Departure', 3804),
  ('suva', 29, 'eight-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'EIGHT-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 1', NULL, 'Arrival at Nausori International Airport (SUV) → Private transfer through Nausori to Suva → Romantic hotel check-in → Relax and refresh Evening: → Suva waterfront → Couple photography → Romantic welcome dinner → Overnight at Suva', 3805),
