  ('suva', 31, 'eight-nights-luxury-pattern', 'EIGHT-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 8', NULL, 'Breakfast → Private chauffeured excursion to Lautoka → Curated Lautoka city & market experience → Vuda Point / scenic western coastline Afternoon: Choose ONE: PRIVATE_ISLAND_ESCAPE → Private yacht / premium sailing experience → Mamanuca waters → Snorkelling → Tropical island leisure LUXURY_RESORT → Return to Denarau → Premium spa → Private cabana → Luxury shopping → Pool & resort leisure Evening: → Private sunset cruise → Farewell fine-dining experience → Overnight at Nadi / Denarau', 3830),
  ('suva', 31, 'eight-nights-luxury-pattern', 'EIGHT-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 9', NULL, 'Breakfast → Leisure morning → Hotel checkout → Private luxury transfer to Nadi International Airport (NAN) → Departure', 3831),
  ('suva', 32, 'travel-agent-insights', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS', 'What inexperienced planners often do wrong', NULL, '', 3832),
  ('suva', 32, 'travel-agent-insights', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS', 'What an experienced planner does differently', NULL, 'For first-time visits, prioritize: FIJI_MUSEUM + THURSTON_GARDENS_ALBERT_PARK + SUVA_MARKET_CUMMING_STREET + COLO_I_SUVA_OR_WATERFRONT before maximum attraction coverage.', 3833),
  ('suva', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', NULL, NULL, 'IF: trip_length <= 1 night THEN: prioritize_FIJI_MUSEUM + THURSTON_GARDENS + ALBERT_PARK AND: choose_ONE_OF_SUVA_MARKET_CUMMING_STREET_OR_WATERFRONT Reason: A very short Suva visit gains more value from concentrated culture, heritage and local-life sightseeing than from attempting distant outer-city attractions. IF: trip_length == 2_OR_3_nights THEN: prioritize_FIJI_MUSEUM + THURSTON_GARDENS + ALBERT_PARK + SUVA_MARKET_CUMMING_STREET AND: retain_ONE_HALF_DAY_FOR_COLO_I_SUVA_OR_DEEPER_CITY_EXPLORATION Reason: Two to three nights provide Suva''s strongest first-time balance of national history, multicultural urban life, markets, food, rainforest and evening culture. IF: trip_length >= 4 nights THEN: add_COLO_I_SUVA + WATERFRONT_NASESE + USP_LAUCALA_BAY + LOCAL_NEIGHBORHOODS Reason: Longer stays allow Suva''s rainforest, educational institutions, waterfront, restaurants and wider neighborhoods to be explored without excessive rushing. IF: trip_length >= 5 nights THEN: consider_ONE_OF_PACIFIC_HARBOUR + NAVUA + MOUNT_KOROBABA + NAUSORI_SURROUNDS Reason: Suva becomes a stronger extended base when city culture is combined with rainforest, river, adventure or surrounding Viti Levu experiences. IF: trip_length >= 6 nights AND: traveler_interest == WIDER_FIJI THEN: consider_SUVA_BASE + ONE_SECONDARY_FIJI_REGION AND: avoid_USING_SUVA_AS_BASE_FOR_REPEATED_LONG_WESTERN_VITI_LEVU_DAY_TRIPS Reason: Suva is an excellent eastern Viti Levu cultural base, but repeated long-distance road travel to Coral Coast, Nadi, Denarau or western regions can reduce itinerary quality. IF: trip_type == HONEYMOON THEN: prefer_PREMIUM_HOTEL + WATERFRONT_EVENING + FINE_DINING + SPA + ONE_CULTURAL_EXPERIENCE AND: combine_WITH_RESORT_OR_ISLAND_DESTINATION_IF_TIME_ALLOWS Reason: Suva''s romantic strength comes from culture, dining, greenery and city atmosphere, while Fiji''s strongest classic honeymoon experiences remain concentrated in resort and island regions. IF: traveler_type == FAMILY THEN: prioritize_FIJI_MUSEUM + THURSTON_GARDENS + MY_SUVA_PARK + SHORT_COLO_I_SUVA_VISIT_WHEN_SAFE AND: include_INDOOR_OR_CAFE_BREAKS Reason: Families benefit from balancing educational culture with gardens, recreation and manageable nature experiences rather than continuous city walking. IF: traveler_type == FAMILY_WITH_YOUNG_CHILDREN THEN: reduce_LONG_MARKET_WALKS + DIFFICULT_RAINFOREST_TRAILS + MOUNT_KOROBABA AND: increase_GARDENS + MUSEUM + WATERFRONT_PARK + SHORT_TRANSPORT_SEGMENTS Reason: Heat, humidity, rain, busy urban environments and slippery natural terrain can quickly reduce comfort for younger children. IF: traveler_type == LUXURY THEN: prefer_PREMIUM_HOTEL + PRIVATE_GUIDE + CHAUFFEURED_TRANSFER + PREMIUM_DINING AND: add_PRIVATE_COLO_I_SUVA_OR_PACIFIC_HARBOUR_EXCURSION_IF_RELEVANT Reason: Suva''s strongest luxury positioning combines premium city accommodation, private cultural interpretation, Pacific gastronomy and chauffeured regional touring rather than resort isolation. IF: traveler_type == BUDGET THEN: prefer_CENTRAL_VALUE_HOTEL + WALKING + LOCAL_BUS + MARKET_AND_LOCAL_RESTAURANT_FOOD AND: limit_PRIVATE_TRANSFERS + PREMIUM_HOTELS + EXCESSIVE_TAXI_USAGE Reason: Suva offers unusually strong value through local buses, markets, inexpensive restaurants, public parks and low-cost cultural experiences. IF: traveler_interest == FIJIAN_HISTORY THEN: prioritize_FIJI_MUSEUM + THURSTON_GARDENS + ALBERT_PARK + GOVERNMENT_PRECINCT + CITY_HERITAGE_WALK Reason: Suva concentrates archaeological interpretation, colonial history, national political development and multicultural heritage within a compact urban area. IF: traveler_interest == FIJI_MUSEUM THEN: allocate_APPROXIMATELY_2_TO_3_HOURS_BASED_ON_INTEREST AND: combine_WITH_THURSTON_GARDENS + ALBERT_PARK Reason: The Fiji Museum is the country''s principal national museum and preserves archaeological material dating back approximately 3,700 years alongside collections documenting Fiji''s Indigenous and later communities. IF: traveler_interest == FIJI_MUSEUM THEN: verify_CURRENT_OPENING_HOURS + ADMISSION + HOLIDAY_STATUS Reason: Museum hours, admission rates, guided-tour arrangements and holiday closures are operational information that should be reconfirmed before travel. IF: traveler_interest == COLONIAL_HISTORY THEN: prioritize_ALBERT_PARK + GOVERNMENT_BUILDINGS_PRECINCT + GRAND_PACIFIC_HOTEL_EXTERIOR + CENTRAL_HERITAGE_STREETS Reason: Suva''s rise as Fiji''s colonial administrative centre after the capital moved from Levuka in 1882 remains visible through its civic landscape and surviving historic architecture. IF: traveler_interest == INDIGENOUS_FIJIAN_CULTURE THEN: prioritize_FIJI_MUSEUM + CULTURAL_INTERPRETATION + MARKET + FIJIAN_FOOD + APPROPRIATE_COMMUNITY_EXPERIENCE Reason: Understanding Suva requires Indigenous iTaukei history and contemporary culture rather than treating the capital purely through colonial-era architecture. IF: traveler_interest == INDO_FIJIAN_CULTURE THEN: prioritize_MULTICULTURAL_FOOD + RELIGIOUS_HERITAGE + SAMABULA_OR_RELEVANT_NEIGHBORHOOD + MARKET_CONTEXT Reason: Indo-Fijian communities form a major part of Fiji''s cultural, religious, culinary and commercial history and are essential to understanding contemporary Suva. IF: traveler_interest == LOCAL_LIFE THEN: prioritize_SUVA_MUNICIPAL_MARKET + CUMMING_STREET + LOCAL_BUS_EXPERIENCE + LOCAL_RESTAURANTS + COMMUNITY_MARKET_IF_AVAILABLE Reason: Suva is one of Fiji''s strongest destinations for experiencing everyday urban culture outside the country''s resort-oriented tourism zones. IF: traveler_interest == SUVA_MARKET THEN: combine_MUNICIPAL_MARKET + CUMMING_STREET + LOCAL_FOOD + HANDICRAFT_OR_RETAIL_EXPLORATION Reason: Suva Market is most valuable when treated as part of a wider local-life and commercial district rather than only a produce-photo stop. IF: traveler_interest == ROC_MARKET THEN: verify_CURRENT_MARKET_DATE_AND_LOCATION AND: combine_WITH_LOCAL_FOOD + ARTISANS + CONTEMPORARY_SUVA Reason: RoC Market is a periodic community event rather than a permanently operating daily attraction. IF: traveler_interest == FOOD THEN: include_FIJIAN_CUISINE + INDO_FIJIAN_CUISINE + SEAFOOD + MARKET_FOOD + CONTEMPORARY_PACIFIC_DINING AND: retain_ONE_QUALITY_RESTAURANT_EXPERIENCE Reason: Suva''s food scene reflects Fiji''s multicultural population and extends well beyond simplified resort interpretations of traditional Fijian cuisine. IF: traveler_interest == KAVA THEN: include_MARKET_OR_CULTURALLY_INTERPRETED_KAVA_EXPERIENCE AND: avoid_TREATING_KAVA_AS_SIMPLE_ALCOHOL_STYLE_NIGHTLIFE Reason: Kava has important cultural and ceremonial meaning in Fiji and is best presented with appropriate context and etiquette. IF: traveler_interest == SHOPPING THEN: combine_SUVA_MARKET + HANDICRAFT_RETAIL + CUMMING_STREET + CBD_MALL_OR_DEPARTMENT_STORE Reason: Suva provides both traditional local shopping and modern retail, giving travelers greater variety than a single market or resort shop. IF: traveler_interest == HANDICRAFTS THEN: prioritize_LOCAL_MARKETS + REPUTABLE_HANDICRAFT_RETAILERS + ROC_MARKET_IF_OPERATING AND: check_HOME_COUNTRY_CUSTOMS_RULES_FOR_PLANT_OR_WOOD_PRODUCTS Reason: Fijian handicrafts include woven pandanus products, wood carvings, masi and other natural-material goods that may be subject to import controls at the traveler''s destination. IF: traveler_interest == NIGHTLIFE THEN: combine_DINNER + LIVE_MUSIC_OR_BAR + CENTRAL_SUVA_OR_TOORAK_VENUE AND: use_TAXI_FOR_LATE_NIGHT_MOVEMENT_WHERE_APPROPRIATE Reason: Suva has one of Fiji''s strongest urban nightlife scenes, centered on restaurants, bars, bands and a smaller number of nightclubs rather than beach-club nightlife. IF: traveler_interest == WATERFRONT THEN: prioritize_NASESE + QUEEN_ELIZABETH_DRIVE + MY_SUVA_PARK AND: position_AS_WALKING_AND_RECREATION_NOT_CLASSIC_BEACH_RESORT Reason: Suva''s waterfront is valuable for harbor views, local recreation and evening atmosphere but should not be confused with Fiji''s famous white-sand resort beaches. IF: traveler_interest == BEACHES THEN: do_NOT_POSITION_CENTRAL_SUVA_AS_PRIMARY_BEACH_DESTINATION AND: consider_PACIFIC_HARBOUR + CORAL_COAST + ISLAND_REGION_BASED_ON_TRIP Reason: Suva''s primary destination strengths are cultural and urban, while Fiji''s major classic beach experiences are stronger elsewhere. IF: traveler_interest == NATURE THEN: prioritize_COLO_I_SUVA + WATERFRONT_GREEN_SPACE AND: consider_MOUNT_KOROBABA_IF_FIT_AND_WEATHER_SUITABLE Reason: Suva provides unusually strong urban access to tropical rainforest, freshwater pools, birdlife and hiking despite being Fiji''s largest city. IF: traveler_interest == COLO_I_SUVA THEN: allocate_HALF_DAY AND: prepare_FOR_RAINFOREST_TRAILS + NATURAL_POOLS + BIRDWATCHING + WEATHER_VARIABILITY Reason: Tourism Fiji identifies Colo-i-Suva as a major rainforest attraction where the popular loop alone requires roughly 1.5_TO_2_HOURS and longer exploration can fill half a day. IF: traveler_interest == COLO_I_SUVA AND: weather == HEAVY_RAIN_OR_RECENT_SEVERE_RAIN THEN: verify_TRAIL_CONDITIONS_BEFORE_DEPARTURE AND: replace_WITH_CITY_CULTURE_IF_CONDITIONS_ARE_UNSUITABLE Reason: Tropical rainforest trails, roots and pool approaches can become considerably more slippery and difficult after substantial rainfall. IF: traveler_interest == BIRDWATCHING THEN: prioritize_COLO_I_SUVA AND: consider_LOCAL_GUIDE_OR_RANGER_INTERPRETATION Reason: Tourism Fiji identifies Colo-i-Suva as an important birdwatching location within Viti Levu''s rainforest environment. IF: traveler_interest == MOUNT_KOROBABA THEN: check_WEATHER + FITNESS + FOOTWEAR + TRAIL_CONDITIONS AND: allocate_APPROXIMATELY_HALF_DAY Reason: Mount Korobaba is a genuine hiking experience with steep natural terrain rather than a conventional road-accessible city viewpoint. IF: traveler_interest == MOUNT_KOROBABA AND: weather == HEAVY_RAIN_OR_STORM THEN: replace_WITH_COLO_I_SUVA_IF_SAFE_OR_INDOOR_CITY_SIGHTSEEING Reason: Steep tropical terrain becomes significantly less suitable when saturated or during severe weather. IF: traveler_interest == EASY_NATURE THEN: prioritize_THURSTON_GARDENS + MY_SUVA_PARK + SHORT_COLO_I_SUVA_PROGRAM_WHEN_SUITABLE OVER: MOUNT_KOROBABA Reason: These options deliver greenery and tropical landscape with substantially lower physical intensity than the Korobaba hike. IF: traveler_interest == PHOTOGRAPHY THEN: prioritize_SUVA_MARKET_EARLY + THURSTON_GARDENS + ALBERT_PARK + COLONIAL_STREETSCAPES + WATERFRONT_LATE AND: add_COLO_I_SUVA_FOR_NATURE_PHOTOGRAPHY Reason: Suva''s strongest photographic diversity comes from combining people, markets, civic architecture, tropical gardens, rainforest and harbor scenery. IF: traveler_interest == STREET_PHOTOGRAPHY THEN: prioritize_MARKET + CUMMING_STREET + CBD + COMMUNITY_AREAS AND: respect_PERSONAL_PRIVACY + REQUEST_PERMISSION_WHERE_APPROPRIATE Reason: Suva''s busy multicultural streets provide strong photographic material, but everyday residents and vendors should not be treated as anonymous tourism props. IF: traveler_interest == EDUCATIONAL_TRAVEL THEN: prioritize_FIJI_MUSEUM + USP_LAUCALA_BAY + CITY_HISTORY + MULTICULTURAL_CONTEXT Reason: Suva is one of the South Pacific''s major educational and institutional hubs and offers unusually strong opportunities for history, anthropology, politics and Pacific-studies travel. IF: traveler_interest == PACIFIC_REGIONAL_AFFAIRS THEN: prioritize_CIVIC_SUVA + USP + GOVERNMENT_DISTRICT + RELEVANT_PUBLIC_INSTITUTIONS Reason: Suva''s role as an economic, educational and diplomatic hub gives it unusual importance within the wider South Pacific. IF: traveler_interest == FESTIVALS THEN: verify_CURRENT_EVENT_DATES + VENUE + ROAD_RESTRICTIONS + ACCOMMODATION_DEMAND AND: reduce_NORMAL_SIGHTSEEING_DENSITY Reason: Large Suva events can significantly change traffic, park access, hotel demand and realistic city movement. IF: travel_dates_overlap_HIBISCUS_FESTIVAL THEN: prioritize_FESTIVAL_PROGRAM + ALBERT_PARK_AREA + EVENING_EVENTS AND: allow_EXTRA_TRAFFIC_AND_CROWD_TIME Reason: The Hibiscus Festival is one of Suva''s major cultural events and brings concentrated entertainment, cultural activity and visitor pressure to the capital. IF: traveler_type == SENIOR THEN: prefer_CENTRAL_HOTEL + DOOR_TO_DOOR_TAXI + SHORT_WALKING_CLUSTERS AND: reduce_LONG_MARKET_WALKS + SLIPPERY_RAINFOREST_TRAILS + MOUNT_KOROBABA Reason: Suva can work well for seniors, but tropical heat, humidity, rain, variable footpaths and natural terrain require pacing and transport support. IF: traveler_uses_WHEELCHAIR THEN: prefer_VERIFIED_ACCESSIBLE_HOTEL + PRIVATE_OR_TAXI_TRANSPORT AND: verify_FIJI_MUSEUM + MARKET + HERITAGE_BUILDINGS + WATERFRONT_ROUTES_SEPARATELY Reason: Accessibility varies significantly between modern hotels, older buildings, urban footpaths and outdoor attractions. IF: traveler_uses_WHEELCHAIR AND: plan_includes_COLO_I_SUVA THEN: verify_CURRENT_ACCESSIBLE_OPTIONS_DIRECTLY AND: do_NOT_ASSUME_FOREST_TRAILS_OR_POOL_ROUTES_ARE_WHEELCHAIR_ACCESSIBLE Reason: Colo-i-Suva is primarily a natural rainforest environment with trails, roots, slopes and swimming-hole access rather than uniform paved infrastructure. IF: season == MAY_TO_OCTOBER THEN: increase_CITY_WALKING + COLO_I_SUVA + WATERFRONT + PHOTOGRAPHY + OUTDOOR_PROGRAMS AND: retain_RAIN_PROTECTION Reason: Fiji''s May-to-October period is generally the cooler and drier season, but Suva''s location on wetter eastern Viti Levu means rainfall remains possible year-round. IF: season == NOVEMBER_TO_APRIL THEN: increase_FLEXIBLE_INDOOR_CULTURE + FOOD + SHOPPING AND: retain_SHORT_WEATHER_DEPENDENT_OUTDOOR_BLOCKS Reason: November through April is Fiji''s warmer and wetter season with higher humidity and more frequent rainfall. IF: season == NOVEMBER_TO_APRIL THEN: check_TROPICAL_CYCLONE_OUTLOOK + CURRENT_WEATHER_ALERTS AND: avoid_GUARANTEEING_WEATHER_SENSITIVE_EXCURSIONS Reason: Tropical cyclones in the southwest Pacific are most likely during Fiji''s warmer November-to-April season. IF: weather == NORMAL_TROPICAL_SHOWERS THEN: retain_FLEXIBLE_CITY_PROGRAM AND: move_BETWEEN_INDOOR_AND_OUTDOOR_ATTRACTIONS_AS_CONDITIONS_CHANGE Reason: Short tropical showers do not automatically require cancelling an entire Suva sightseeing day. IF: weather == HEAVY_CONTINUOUS_RAIN THEN: replace_EXTENDED_WALKING_AND_HIKING_WITH_FIJI_MUSEUM + SHOPPING + CAFES + FOOD + OTHER_INDOOR_EXPERIENCES AND: use_TAXIS_MORE_SELECTIVELY Reason: Suva''s cultural, shopping and dining inventory provides useful all-weather alternatives when prolonged rain reduces walking comfort. IF: weather == TROPICAL_CYCLONE_WARNING_OR_SEVERE_WEATHER_ALERT THEN: suspend_NONESSENTIAL_OUTDOOR_EXCURSIONS + FOREST_HIKES + LONG_ROAD_TRIPS AND: follow_OFFICIAL_LOCAL_EMERGENCY_AND_WEATHER_GUIDANCE Reason: Cyclones can bring destructive winds, flooding and severe rainfall, so normal tourism scheduling must become secondary to official safety instructions. IF: weather == VERY_HOT_AND_HUMID THEN: schedule_WALKING_EARLIER + INDOOR_MIDDAY + WATERFRONT_OR_DINING_LATER AND: increase_HYDRATION_AND_REST_BREAKS Reason: Suva''s tropical climate can create significant humidity even when absolute temperatures are not extreme by continental standards. IF: route == NAUSORI_AIRPORT_TO_SUVA_CITY THEN: prefer_PREBOOKED_TRANSFER_OR_TAXI_FOR_STANDARD_VISITOR_COMFORT AND: consider_PUBLIC_TRANSPORT_FOR_BUDGET_TRAVEL_WHEN_PRACTICAL Reason: Nausori International Airport is Suva''s principal air gateway and lies outside the central city, making a dedicated road transfer necessary after arrival. IF: route == NADI_AIRPORT_TO_SUVA THEN: compare_DOMESTIC_FLIGHT_TO_NAUSORI + INTERCITY_BUS + PRIVATE_ROAD_TRANSFER AND: choose_BASED_ON_TIME + BUDGET + LUGGAGE + ITINERARY Reason: Nadi remains Fiji''s principal international gateway while Suva is on the opposite side of Viti Levu, so the onward connection materially affects itinerary design. IF: route == NADI_TO_SUVA_BY_ROAD THEN: allocate_APPROXIMATELY_HALF_DAY_WITH_TRAFFIC_AND_STOPS AND: avoid_SCHEDULING_MAJOR_FIXED_TIME_SUVA_SIGHTSEEING_IMMEDIATELY_AFTER_ARRIVAL Reason: Tourism Fiji positions Suva roughly 3.5_TO_4_HOURS from Nadi by road under standard travel conditions, making the transfer a meaningful itinerary component. IF: route == CENTRAL_SUVA_TO_COLO_I_SUVA THEN: prefer_TAXI + PRIVATE_TRANSFER + LOCAL_BUS_WHERE_PRACTICAL Reason: Colo-i-Suva lies outside the compact central sightseeing core and is more efficiently treated as a dedicated road-accessed nature excursion. IF: route == CENTRAL_SUVA_TO_PACIFIC_HARBOUR THEN: prefer_PRIVATE_TRANSFER_OR_INTERCITY_BUS_BASED_ON_TRAVELER_STYLE Reason: Pacific Harbour is a separate adventure destination south-west of Suva and Tourism Fiji positions it at approximately a 45-minute drive from the capital under suitable conditions. IF: movement == CENTRAL_SUVA_SIGHTSEEING THEN: prefer_WALKING AND: use_LOCAL_BUS + SELECTIVE_TAXI_FOR_LONGER_MOVEMENTS Reason: Suva''s museum, civic, market and CBD areas can be combined efficiently on foot, while outer districts are better connected by road transport. IF: movement == OUTER_SUVA_SIGHTSEEING THEN: prefer_LOCAL_BUS_OR_TAXI AND: use_PRIVATE_VEHICLE_FOR_MULTI_STOP_PROGRAMS Reason: Laucala Bay, Colo-i-Suva, Samabula, Lami and other outer areas are too dispersed for efficient all-day walking. IF: movement == LOCAL_BUS THEN: verify_CURRENT_ELECTRONIC_TICKETING_REQUIREMENTS AND: carry_APPROPRIATE_PAYMENT_METHOD Reason: Fiji''s bus network uses electronic-ticketing arrangements that should be confirmed before relying on buses for timed sightseeing movements. IF: movement == TAXI THEN: carry_FIJI_DOLLARS AND: confirm_METER_OR_LONG_DISTANCE_FARE_BEFORE_TRAVEL Reason: Tourism Fiji advises travelers to carry cash for taxis and to confirm correct meter or fare use rather than assuming card-based rideshare-style operation. IF: traveler_requests_UBER_OR_LYFT THEN: replace_WITH_LICENSED_TAXI_OR_PRIVATE_TRANSFER Reason: Major international rideshare platforms such as Uber, Lyft and Ola are not currently standard operating options in Fiji. IF: trip_length <= 3 nights THEN: avoid_RENTAL_CAR_FOR_PRIMARY_CENTRAL_SUVA_ITINERARY AND: use_WALKING + BUS + TAXI + SELECTIVE_PRIVATE_TRANSFER Reason: A short Suva city break generally does not require the added parking, navigation and driving friction of a rental car. IF: trip_length >= 4 nights AND: traveler_interest == MULTIPLE_VITI_LEVU_EXCURSIONS THEN: consider_PRIVATE_CAR_OR_RENTAL_CAR AND: account_FOR_LEFT_SIDE_DRIVING + ROAD_CONDITIONS + PARKING + WEATHER Reason: A vehicle becomes more useful when Suva is combined with repeated outer-city or regional touring rather than central sightseeing alone. IF: traveler_interest == PACIFIC_HARBOUR_ADVENTURE THEN: consider_SEPARATE_HALF_DAY_OR_FULL_DAY_EXCURSION AND: do_NOT_LABEL_ACTIVITY_AS_CENTRAL_SUVA Reason: Pacific Harbour substantially expands the region''s rafting, diving and adventure inventory but is geographically distinct from Suva city. IF: traveler_interest == UNESCO_HERITAGE THEN: do_NOT_LABEL_SUVA_AS_UNESCO_WORLD_HERITAGE_SITE AND: consider_LEVUKA_HISTORICAL_PORT_TOWN_IF_TIME_AND_LOGISTICS_ALLOW Reason: Levuka Historical Port Town on Ovalau, rather than Suva, is Fiji''s UNESCO World Heritage property. IF: traveler_interest == LEVUKA THEN: treat_AS_SEPARATE_OVALAU_EXCURSION_OR_OVERNIGHT_COMPONENT AND: verify_CURRENT_AIR_OR_FERRY_LOGISTICS Reason: Levuka is Fiji''s former capital and a UNESCO World Heritage destination but should not be represented as part of central Suva sightseeing. IF: traveler_interest == FIRST_TIME_FIJI THEN: use_SUVA_FOR_CULTURE + HISTORY + FOOD + LOCAL_LIFE AND: combine_WITH_BEACH_OR_ISLAND_REGION_IF_CLASSIC_FIJI_EXPERIENCE_IS_REQUIRED Reason: Suva provides one of Fiji''s strongest introductions to contemporary national life, but it does not independently represent the country''s full beach, reef and island-resort tourism identity. IF: traveler_interest == FIRST_TIME_SUVA THEN: prioritize_FIJI_MUSEUM + THURSTON_GARDENS_ALBERT_PARK + SUVA_MARKET_CUMMING_STREET AND: add_COLO_I_SUVA_OR_WATERFRONT_IF_TIME_ALLOWS Reason: These experiences provide Suva''s strongest first introduction to Fijian history, multicultural culture, everyday urban life, tropical greenery and the capital''s distinctive South Pacific identity.', 3834),
  ('suva', 34, 'destination-scoring', 'DESTINATION SCORING', NULL, NULL, '| Factor | Score | | --- | --- | | Family | 85 | | Honeymoon | 70 | | Luxury | 78 | | Budget | 90 | | Adventure | 69 | | Culture | 95 | | Food | 94 | | Shopping | 88 | | Nightlife | 89 | | Relaxation | 80 | | Nature | 88 | | Accessibility | 72 | | Safety | 84 | | First-time visitor | 87 | | Photography | 90 |', 3835),
  ('suva', 35, 'final-travel-agent-verdict', 'FINAL TRAVEL AGENT VERDICT', NULL, NULL, 'Best traveler profiles: 1. Culture / local-life traveler (Fiji Museum, Thurston Gardens, Suva Municipal Market, Cumming Street, multicultural neighborhoods, local food) 2. History / heritage traveler (Fiji Museum, Albert Park, Government Buildings precinct, Sacred Heart Cathedral, colonial-era streetscapes, national-history interpretation) 3. Food traveler (iTaukei Fijian cuisine, Indo-Fijian curries, seafood, market produce, cafés, contemporary Pacific dining) 4. Photography traveler (Suva Market, Thurston Gardens, Albert Park, colonial streetscapes, Nasese waterfront, Colo-i-Suva rainforest) 5. Nature / soft-adventure traveler (Colo-i-Suva Forest Park, freshwater swimming holes, rainforest birdlife, Mount Korobaba, waterfront green spaces) 6. Family traveler (Fiji Museum, Thurston Gardens, My Suva Picnic Park, markets, short rainforest experiences, family dining) 7. Budget / independent traveler (local buses, markets, affordable restaurants, public parks, low-cost cultural sightseeing, central walking) 8. Nightlife / social traveler (restaurants, bars, live music, cafés, Toorak, central Suva, community events) 9. Educational / Pacific-studies traveler (Fiji Museum, University of the South Pacific, government district, multicultural society, regional institutions) 10. Luxury / business traveler (premium city hotels, chauffeur transfers, private guides, premium dining, business and diplomatic travel, private regional excursions) Best duration: 2–4 nights 1 night: Best for FIJI_MUSEUM + THURSTON_GARDENS + ALBERT_PARK + SUVA_MARKET_CUMMING_STREET as a concentrated introduction to Fiji''s capital. 2–3 nights: Best for BALANCED_FIRST_VISIT, adding Colo-i-Suva Forest Park, Nasese waterfront, local dining, nightlife and relaxed central-city exploration. 4–5 nights: Best for DEEPER_SUVA including USP / Laucala Bay, My Suva Picnic Park, local neighborhoods, community markets, Mount Korobaba based on fitness and weather, and additional food experiences. 6+ nights: Best when Suva is used as an EASTERN_VITI_LEVU_BASE, combining the capital with Pacific Harbour, Navua, Nausori surroundings, rainforest experiences or another contrasting Fiji region. Best season: YEAR-ROUND_WITH_SEASONAL_WEATHER_PLANNING Cooler / Drier Season (May – October): LOWER_HUMIDITY + COMFORTABLE_CITY_WALKING + COLO_I_SUVA + PHOTOGRAPHY + WATERFRONT + HIKING + STRONGER_OUTDOOR_RELIABILITY. Warmer / Wetter Season (November – April): FIJI_MUSEUM + MARKETS + FOOD + SHOPPING + NIGHTLIFE + FLEXIBLE_OUTDOOR_BLOCKS + TROPICAL_GREENERY, with heavier rainfall, greater humidity and tropical-cyclone-season considerations. May, June, September and October generally provide some of the strongest balances for mixed urban and outdoor sightseeing. July and August remain excellent for outdoor comfort but coincide with stronger overall Fiji tourism demand. November through April should retain significantly greater weather flexibility, especially for Colo-i-Suva, Mount Korobaba, long road excursions and outdoor-heavy programs. Suva should therefore be treated as a genuine YEAR_ROUND_CULTURAL_CITY_DESTINATION, but not as a uniformly dry tropical destination. Its location on eastern Viti Levu makes it wetter than Fiji''s western tourism regions. Best hotel strategy: Choose accommodation according to central sightseeing access, business requirements, dining, transport convenience, mobility and planned outer-city excursions. For first-time visitors: CENTRAL_SUVA / VICTORIA_PARADE / GOVERNMENT_PRECINCT_APPROACH for efficient access to Fiji Museum, Thurston Gardens, Albert Park, CBD shopping, restaurants and markets. For heritage / culture: CENTRAL_SUVA / THURSTON_GARDENS_APPROACH / NASESE for museum access, historic civic areas, waterfront atmosphere and walkable cultural sightseeing. For luxury: PREMIUM_CENTRAL_SUVA / NASESE / WATERFRONT_ORIENTED_PROPERTIES for stronger hotel facilities, premium dining, chauffeur access and business convenience. For honeymoon / romantic travel: NASESE / QUIETER_CENTRAL_PREMIUM_HOTEL for waterfront evenings, dining, spa access and less commercially intense surroundings. For food / nightlife: CENTRAL_SUVA / TOORAK / CBD_APPROACH for restaurants, bars, cafés, local dining and evening access. For business / diplomatic travel: CENTRAL_SUVA / GOVERNMENT_AND_COMMERCIAL_DISTRICT for efficient access to government, corporate and diplomatic institutions. Avoid changing hotels unnecessarily; central Suva provides the strongest base for CBD sightseeing while taxis, buses and private transfers can handle Colo-i-Suva, Laucala Bay, Nausori and regional excursions. Best transportation: Use: Suva transportation should primarily be treated as: WALKING_FOR_CENTRAL_CORE + BUS_FOR_VALUE_AND_LOCAL_MOVEMENT + TAXI_FOR_CROSS_CITY_CONVENIENCE + PRIVATE_TRANSFER_FOR_AIRPORT_AND_PREMIUM_TRAVEL + ROAD_OR_DOMESTIC_FLIGHT_FOR_REGIONAL_CONNECTIONS Suva airport transportation baseline: NAUSORI_INTERNATIONAL_AIRPORT + APPROXIMATELY_30_MINUTE_ROAD_TRANSFER_TO_SUVA_UNDER_NORMAL_CONDITIONS + TAXI_OR_PREBOOKED_TRANSFER_PREFERRED_FOR_MOST_FIRST_TIME_VISITORS. Nadi connection baseline: NADI + APPROXIMATELY_3.5_TO_4_HOURS_BY_ROAD_TO_SUVA OR DOMESTIC_FLIGHT_TO_NAUSORI_IN_APPROXIMATELY_25_TO_30_MINUTES + ONWARD_ROAD_TRANSFER_TO_SUVA. Accessibility baseline: CENTRAL_SUVA: MODERATE_ACCESSIBILITY + ROAD_CONNECTED_HOTELS_AND_ATTRACTIONS + SHORT_TAXI_TRANSFERS + VARIABLE_FOOTPATH_AND_BUILDING_ACCESS. COLO_I_SUVA_AND_MOUNT_KOROBABA: NATURAL_TERRAIN + ROOTS + MUD + SLOPES + WEATHER_DEPENDENT_TRAIL_CONDITIONS + NOT_SUITABLE_FOR_UNIFORM_STEP_FREE_CLASSIFICATION. Accessible rooms, lifts, bathrooms, museum routes, vehicle requirements and individual attraction access should be verified before confirmation. Must-do for first-time visitor: Suva should not be reduced to Fiji Museum and Suva Market alone; its essential tourism identity is: FIJIAN_AND_PACIFIC_CULTURE + MULTICULTURAL_LOCAL_LIFE + NATIONAL_HISTORY + MARKETS_AND_FOOD + RAINFOREST_ACCESS + WATERFRONT_CITY_LIFE + NIGHTLIFE_AND_REGIONAL_INSTITUTIONS. Don''t-do: Current Fiji Museum operational baseline: Colo-i-Suva operational and planning baseline: Mount Korobaba planning baseline: 2026 Suva event baseline: HIBISCUS_FESTIVAL_2026: 29_AUGUST_2026 – 05_SEPTEMBER_2026 + ALBERT_PARK + MUSIC + PERFORMANCES + CULTURAL_PROGRAMMING + MULTICULTURAL_FIJI_IDENTITY. The 2026 festival is promoted as the 70TH_HIBISCUS_FESTIVAL. RoC Market baseline: MONTHLY_COMMUNITY_MARKET + THIRD_SUNDAY_OF_EACH_MONTH + LOCAL_FOOD + ARTISANS + CULTURAL_PRODUCTS + HANDMADE_GOODS + ENTERTAINMENT. Market dates and location must still be verified for the actual travel date. Biggest advantage: Exceptional access to Fiji''s everyday national culture, history, markets, gastronomy, political life, education and rainforest environment within one relatively compact capital-city destination. Unlike Fiji''s resort regions, Suva provides direct exposure to contemporary urban Fijian life rather than a tourism environment primarily organized around beaches and resorts. The Fiji Museum provides exceptional cultural depth through archaeological material extending approximately 3,700 years, while the wider city reflects Indigenous iTaukei, Indo-Fijian, Rotuman, colonial and contemporary Pacific influences. Suva also offers an unusually strong nature contrast for a capital city because Colo-i-Suva Forest Park lies only a short drive from the CBD and combines rainforest trails, natural swimming holes and birdwatching. Biggest disadvantage: Frequent rainfall, high humidity, weaker conventional beach appeal and a tourism inventory that is less immediately spectacular than Fiji''s resort islands for travelers seeking a classic tropical holiday. Suva''s eastern Viti Levu location makes it significantly wetter than western Fiji, so outdoor itineraries require more flexibility even during the cooler season. Accessibility is also inconsistent across sidewalks, older buildings, markets and natural attractions, while normal urban safety precautions become more important at night and in isolated areas. Overall destination score: 88/100', 3836),
  ('suva', 36, 'data-quality', 'DATA QUALITY', NULL, NULL, 'information_completeness: 98/100 last_updated: 2026-09-05 last_verified: WEB_VERIFIED verified_by: TOURISM FIJI / FIJI MUSEUM / SUVA CITY COUNCIL / FIJI METEOROLOGICAL AND HYDROLOGICAL SERVICES / UNESCO WORLD HERITAGE CENTRE / FIJI TOURISM EVENT SOURCES / CURRENT GOVERNMENT TRAVEL ADVISORY SOURCES sources: IMPORTANT: Fiji Museum admission, guided tours, temporary exhibitions, Colo-i-Suva access, rainforest trail conditions, community markets, Hibiscus Festival programming, accommodation availability and private excursions must NOT be treated as permanently available without verification. Current Fiji Museum general operating baseline: MONDAY_TO_SUNDAY: 09:00–16:30 MOST_PUBLIC_HOLIDAYS: 09:00–16:30 CHRISTMAS_DAY: CLOSED NEW_YEARS_DAY: CLOSED EASTER_SUNDAY: CLOSED DIWALI: CLOSED. Current Fiji Museum normal admission baseline: LOCAL_ADULT: FJD_10 OVERSEAS_ADULT: FJD_20 LOCAL_CHILD: FJD_5 OVERSEAS_CHILD: FJD_10 ENTRY_AND_GUIDED_TOUR_LOCAL_ADULT: FJD_15 ENTRY_AND_GUIDED_TOUR_OVERSEAS_ADULT: FJD_30. These prices, hours and holiday arrangements remain subject to operational change and must be reverified before production use. Fiji Museum collection baseline: APPROXIMATELY_3700_YEARS_OF_ARCHAEOLOGICAL_MATERIAL + INDIGENOUS_FIJIAN_COLLECTIONS + ROTUMAN_AND_OTHER_COMMUNITY_HISTORY + MARITIME_HERITAGE + MASI + GIRMIT + ARCHAEOLOGICAL_AND_HISTORICAL_COLLECTIONS. Colo-i-Suva baseline: APPROXIMATELY_20_MINUTES_FROM_SUVA + 6.5_KM_OF_WALKING_TRAILS + NATURAL_SWIMMING_HOLES + RAINFOREST + BIRDWATCHING + POPULAR_LOOP_APPROXIMATELY_1.5_TO_2_HOURS + HALF_DAY_FOR_DEEPER_EXPLORATION. Colo-i-Suva should not be classified as uniformly accessible or weather-independent. Mount Korobaba baseline: APPROXIMATELY_441_METRES + CHALLENGING_HIKING + APPROXIMATELY_2.5_TO_3_HOUR_SUMMIT_TIMING_FOR_MANY_HIKERS + 360_DEGREE_VIEW_POTENTIAL + SUITABLE_FOOTWEAR_REQUIRED + AVOID_AFTER_SIGNIFICANT_RAIN. Tourism Fiji specifically warns that wet conditions can make the trail extremely muddy and tree roots slippery. Suva parks baseline: SUVA_CITY_COUNCIL_MANAGES_MORE_THAN_50_PARKS_AND_GARDENS + THURSTON_GARDENS + ALBERT_PARK + MY_SUVA_PICNIC_PARK + OTHER_MUNICIPAL_GREEN_SPACES. Albert Park has substantial national historical importance, including its association with Fiji''s independence-era flag raising and major civic events. Suva UNESCO classification: SUVA: NOT_CURRENTLY_INSCRIBED_AS_UNESCO_WORLD_HERITAGE_PROPERTY. FIJI_CURRENT_WORLD_HERITAGE_PROPERTY: LEVUKA_HISTORICAL_PORT_TOWN + OVALAU_ISLAND + INSCRIBED_2013. Do not transfer Levuka''s UNESCO status to Suva. Airport transfer baseline: NAUSORI_INTERNATIONAL_AIRPORT + PRIMARY_AIR_GATEWAY_FOR_SUVA + APPROXIMATELY_30_MINUTE_ROAD_TRANSFER_TO_SUVA_UNDER_NORMAL_CONDITIONS. NADI_TO_SUVA: APPROXIMATELY_3.5_TO_4_HOURS_BY_ROAD OR APPROXIMATELY_25_TO_30_MINUTE_DOMESTIC_FLIGHT_TO_NAUSORI + APPROXIMATELY_30_MINUTE_ONWARD_ROAD_TRANSFER_TO_SUVA. Traffic, roadworks, rainfall, flooding and individual transfer arrangements can materially change road journey times. 2026 Hibiscus Festival baseline: HIBISCUS_FESTIVAL: 29_AUGUST_2026 – 05_SEPTEMBER_2026 LOCATION: ALBERT_PARK_SUVA POSITIONING: 70TH_HIBISCUS_FESTIVAL + MUSIC + PERFORMANCE + CULTURAL_CELEBRATION + MULTICULTURAL_IDENTITY. Festival schedules, individual performances, road controls and venue access must be verified for actual travel dates. RoC Market baseline: THIRD_SUNDAY_OF_EACH_MONTH + COMMUNITY_MARKET + FOOD + ARTISANS + CULTURAL_PRODUCTS + HANDMADE_GOODS + ENTERTAINMENT. Do not classify RoC Market as a daily attraction. Suva climate and seasonality should be handled as: COOLER_DRIER_SEASON / MAY_TO_OCTOBER: CITY_WALKING + FIJI_MUSEUM + MARKETS + COLO_I_SUVA + WATERFRONT + PHOTOGRAPHY + HIKING + CONTINUED_RAIN_CONTINGENCY. WARMER_WETTER_SEASON / NOVEMBER_TO_APRIL: FIJI_MUSEUM + FOOD + MARKETS + SHOPPING + NIGHTLIFE + SHORT_FLEXIBLE_OUTDOOR_BLOCKS + HIGHER_HUMIDITY + HEAVIER_RAINFALL + TROPICAL_CYCLONE_AWARENESS. Eastern Viti Levu receives greater rainfall than western Viti Levu because of Fiji''s topography and prevailing southeast trade winds. Suva should therefore never be described as having the same comparatively dry climate profile as Nadi or western Viti Levu. Tropical-cyclone baseline: REGIONAL_TROPICAL_CYCLONE_SEASON: NOVEMBER_TO_APRIL PEAK_ACTIVITY: GENERALLY_JANUARY_TO_MARCH OUT_OF_SEASON_CYCLONES: POSSIBLE. Official Fiji Meteorological and Hydrological Services advisories should override fixed tourism itineraries during tropical disturbances, cyclones, flooding or other severe-weather events. Current general safety baseline: FIJI: EXERCISE_NORMAL_SAFETY_PRECAUTIONS. However: URBAN_AREAS_AND_NIGHT: INCREASED_ATTENTION_TO_PERSONAL_SECURITY SUVA_AND_NADI: NORMAL_URBAN_PRECAUTIONS_REQUIRED PARKS_AND_NATURE_TRAILS: KEEP_VALUABLES_SECURE + MAINTAIN_SITUATIONAL_AWARENESS. Safety classifications and government travel advisories can change and must be reverified before travel. Suva should primarily be treated as: MAY_TO_OCTOBER: FIJI_MUSEUM + THURSTON_GARDENS + SUVA_MARKET + ALBERT_PARK + COLO_I_SUVA + WATERFRONT + CITY_WALKING NOVEMBER_TO_APRIL: FIJI_MUSEUM + MARKETS + FOOD + SHOPPING + NIGHTLIFE + FLEXIBLE_CITY_SIGHTSEEING + WEATHER_DEPENDENT_NATURE FIRST_TIME_TRAVEL: FIJI_MUSEUM + THURSTON_GARDENS + ALBERT_PARK + SUVA_MARKET_CUMMING_STREET + COLO_I_SUVA_OR_WATERFRONT REPEAT_TRAVEL: USP_LAUCALA_BAY + LOCAL_NEIGHBORHOODS + COMMUNITY_MARKETS + MOUNT_KOROBABA + PACIFIC_HARBOUR_EXTENSION + DEEPER_FOOD_AND_CULTURE. Tourism Fiji, Fiji Museum, Suva City Council, Fiji Meteorological and Hydrological Services, UNESCO World Heritage Centre and current individual attraction / event portals should be treated as primary sources for operational information. This dataset should be refreshed regularly before production use.', 3837),
  ('ha-noi', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Spring', NULL, 'months: March April May weather: Warm and pleasant. 18–27°C. Low humidity, light drizzle in March = "Hanoi Drizzle Season" crowd_level: MEDIUM → HIGH price_level: MEDIUM → HIGH overall_score: 90-92 recommended: true reason: Best season in Hanoi. Clear skies, blooming flowers, perfect for walking the Old Quarter. Tet holidays in late Jan/Feb can spill into March, so book early. Ideal for first-time tourists and photography.', 3838),
  ('ha-noi', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Summer', NULL, 'months: June July August weather: Hot and humid. 30–38°C with occasional thunderstorms and heavy rain. Southwest Monsoon. crowd_level: MEDIUM price_level: MEDIUM → LOW overall_score: 78-82 recommended: true with caveats reason: Very hot but cheaper hotels + fewer crowds. Good for budget backpackers and food trips. Rain usually comes in short bursts in the evening. Not ideal for Ha Long Bay due to potential storms/cruise cancellations. Carry an umbrella + stay hydrated.', 3839),
  ('ha-noi', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Autumn', NULL, 'months: September October November weather: The best weather. 22–30°C. Cool, dry, sunny. "Hanoi Autumn" is famous. crowd_level: HIGH price_level: HIGH overall_score: 93-95 recommended: true reason: Peak season for Hanoi. Perfect weather for Ha Long Bay cruises, Ninh Binh, and city walking. Golden leaves, Mid-Autumn Festival in Sep. Most expensive + book 1 month ahead.', 3840),
  ('ha-noi', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Winter', NULL, 'months: December January February weather: Cool and dry. 15–22°C. Can feel chilly due to humidity—no heating in most hotels. Drizzle in Feb. crowd_level: MEDIUM → VERY HIGH in late Dec–early Jan price_level: MEDIUM → VERY HIGH in late Dec–early Jan overall_score: 85-88 recommended: true reason: Great weather for sightseeing without sweat. Christmas + New Year + Tet = peak prices and crowds. Jan-Feb is the sweet spot for Indian families: cool weather, lower crowds after Tet, perfect for Ha Long Bay. Pack a light jacket.', 3841),
  ('ha-noi', 10, 'budget-strategy', 'BUDGET STRATEGY', NULL, NULL, 'Where money can be saved: Where saving money is usually NOT recommended: Travel-agent rule: A slightly more expensive but centrally located, well-reviewed 3★ hotel in Old Quarter generally delivers better total value than a cheaper hotel 5km away. You save 2 hrs daily in traffic + $10 in Grab + you can walk back for afternoon rest. In Hanoi, location = time = money.', 3842),
  ('ha-noi', 12, 'airport-transfer-logic', 'AIRPORT TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Family', 'family', 'Pre-booked private MPV / 7-seater van; Door-to-door, space for 2-3 big pieces of luggage + stroller + car seats.', 3843),
  ('ha-noi', 12, 'airport-transfer-logic', 'AIRPORT TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Honeymoon', 'honeymoon', 'Pre-booked private car or sedan; meet-and-greet, board, cold water, direct drop to boutique hotel in Old Quarter. reason: The first impression of the trip matters, and private transfer provides comfort and privacy.', 3844),
  ('ha-noi', 12, 'airport-transfer-logic', 'AIRPORT TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Luxury', 'luxury', 'Chauffeured limo / Mercedes E-Class / Luxury MPV; priority pickup, VIP lounge assistance, 5* premium comfort, bottled water;', 3845),
  ('ha-noi', 12, 'airport-transfer-logic', 'AIRPORT TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Budget', 'budget', 'Airport Bus 86 + Grab Bike / Short walk; lowest cost, best for light luggage and solo travellers.', 3846),
  ('ha-noi', 12, 'airport-transfer-logic', 'AIRPORT TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Senior', 'senior', 'Pre-booked private taxi or car; Minimal walking, assistance with luggage, direct access to hotel lobby. Avoid bus stairs and crowded buses.', 3847),
  ('ha-noi', 18, 'family-travel', 'FAMILY TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'child_friendly_score: 75 best_ages: Rules: For young children: Prefer: Avoid:', 3848),
  ('ha-noi', 19, 'honeymoon-travel', 'HONEYMOON TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'honeymoon_score: 88 romance_score: 90 privacy_score: 75 luxury_score: 85 Recommended: Honeymoon itinerary should NOT contain more than: 2 major activities/day. Prefer: One memorable experience. over: Three or four attractions. Recommended hotel areas:', 3849),
  ('ha-noi', 20, 'luxury-travel', 'LUXURY TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'luxury_score: 87 Recommended: Luxury should primarily increase:', 3850),
