  ('ha-noi', 22, 'senior-travel', 'SENIOR TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'senior_suitability: 65 walking_intensity: MEDIUM-HIGH Rules:', 3852),
  ('ha-noi', 23, 'accessibility', 'ACCESSIBILITY', NULL, NULL, 'wheelchair accessibility: MODERATE public transport accessibility: LOW_TO_MODERATE hotel accessibility: GOOD_TO_EXCELLENT; MUST_BE_VERIFIED_PER_HOTEL attraction accessibility: MODERATE_TO_GOOD; MUST_BE_VERIFIED_PER_ATTRACTION Rule: Verify accessible room, step-free access, and attraction facilities before booking. Get written confirmation from hotel + tour operator. Send photos of bathroom if possible.', 3853),
  ('ha-noi', 24, 'food', 'FOOD', NULL, NULL, 'Hanoi is particularly strong for: Food experiences: Family: Prioritise clean restaurants with AC, familiar menu, early dining at 6 PM. Honeymoon: Include one rooftop dinner at French Quarter. Budget: Use street food + Bia hoi. Reserve 1 premium meal', 3854),
  ('ha-noi', 25, 'shopping', 'SHOPPING', NULL, NULL, 'Strong categories: Luxury shopping: Budget: Prefer:', 3855),
  ('ha-noi', 26, 'nightlife', 'NIGHTLIFE', NULL, NULL, 'nightlife_level: 75 Suitable for: Not a primary requirement for: Honeymoon travellers should generally prefer: Romantic rooftop dinner at Apricot/Press Club, West Lake sunset drinks, Hoan Kiem Lake evening walk, or 5★ hotel jazz over: late-night club itinerary', 3856),
  ('ha-noi', 28, 'sample-itinerary-patterns', 'SAMPLE ITINERARY PATTERNS', '3 NIGHTS', NULL, 'Day 1 Arrive at Noi Bai Airport and private transfer to hotel in OLD QUARTER. Check in, rest. Evening: Walk Hoan Kiem Lake + Old Quarter + Train Street + Water Puppet Show + Egg Coffee at Giang Cafe. Overnight: Hanoi Meals: Breakfast Day 2 Breakfast at the hotel. Full-day Ha Long Bay 2D1N Luxury Cruise. Kayaking, cave, sunset party, squid fishing on board. Overnight: On Cruise Meals: Breakfast, Lunch, Dinner Day 3 Breakfast on cruise. Morning Tai Chi + cave visit. Return to Hanoi by 4 PM. Free time for shopping at Dong Xuan Market + Old Quarter. Overnight: Hanoi Meals: Breakfast, Lunch Day 4 Breakfast, check out. Visit Temple of Literature + Ho Chi Minh Mausoleum. Private transfer to Noi Bai Airport for departure. Package Includes: 3 nights stay with breakfast, 2D1N Ha Long cruise, all tours, private transfers, e-visa support. Excludes: Flight fare, travel insurance, Ha Long cruise tips', 3857),
  ('ha-noi', 29, 'five-night-honeymoon-pattern', 'FIVE-NIGHT HONEYMOON PATTERN', NULL, NULL, 'Day 1 Arrive at Noi Bai Airport and private transfer to 5★ hotel in BA DINH. Check in, relax. Optional evening add-on: Romantic dinner at Sofitel Metropole + West Lake sunset. Overnight: Hanoi Meals: Breakfast Day 2 After breakfast, private half-day city tour: Hoan Kiem Lake + French Quarter + Temple of Literature. Evening: Rooftop bar at Apricot Hotel with Hoan Kiem Lake view. Overnight: Hanoi Meals: Breakfast Day 3 After breakfast, check out and transfer to Ha Long Bay 2D1N 5★ Cruise with private balcony. Couples spa, private dinner on deck, kayaking. Overnight: On Cruise Meals: Breakfast, Lunch, Dinner Day 4 Breakfast on cruise. Return to Hanoi. Check in to hotel. Evening free for couple photos, cafe hopping, shopping in Old Quarter. Overnight: Hanoi Meals: Breakfast, Lunch Day 5 After breakfast, day trip to Ninh Binh with private car. Tam Coc boat + Mua Cave + Trang An. Return to Hanoi. Farewell dinner at Gia Restaurant. Overnight: Hanoi Meals: Breakfast, Lunch Day 6 Breakfast, check-out and private transfer to Noi Bai Airport for departure with sweet honeymoon memories. Meals: Breakfast', 3858),
  ('ha-noi', 30, 'five-night-family-pattern', 'FIVE-NIGHT FAMILY PATTERN', NULL, NULL, 'Day 1 Arrive at Noi Bai Airport, private transfer to hotel in OLD QUARTER. Check-in and relax by the pool. Optional: Evening walk to Hoan Kiem Lake + Water Puppet. Overnight: Hanoi Meals: Breakfast Day 2 Breakfast at hotel. Halong Bay 2D1N Family Cruise with family cabin. Kids activities, cave, kayaking. Overnight: On Cruise Meals: Breakfast, Lunch, Dinner Day 3 Breakfast on cruise. Return to Hanoi. Afternoon free at Vincom Mall + West Lake. Overnight: Hanoi Meals: Breakfast, Lunch Day 4 Breakfast and check-out. Full-day Ninh Binh tour. Tam Coc boat ride + bike + Trang An. Kids love the boat. Return to Hanoi. Overnight: Hanoi Meals: Breakfast, Lunch Day 5 Breakfast at hotel. Visit Ethnology Museum + Temple of Literature. Afternoon shopping + ice cream. Overnight: Hanoi Meals: Breakfast Day 6 Breakfast, check-out and airport transfer for return flight. Meals: Breakfast. Family Rules Applied: Max 1 major activity/day, outdoor in morning, AC lunch breaks', 3859),
  ('ha-noi', 31, 'five-night-luxury-pattern', 'FIVE-NIGHT LUXURY PATTERN', NULL, NULL, 'Day 1 Arrive at Noi Bai Airport and receive VIP meet-and-greet. Private transfer to Sofitel Legend Metropole. Evening at leisure, followed by premium dinner at French Grill. Overnight: Hanoi Meals: Breakfast Day 2 Breakfast at hotel. Private half-day city tour with guide: Mausoleum, Temple of Literature, French Quarter. Afternoon: Spa ritual at hotel + luxury shopping at Trang Tien Plaza. Evening: Sunset at Skyline Bar JW Marriott. Overnight: Hanoi Meals: Breakfast Day 3 Breakfast at hotel. Private transfer to Halong Bay 5★ Cruise - Indochina Sails. Private butler, balcony suite, cooking class, spa. Overnight: On Cruise Meals: Breakfast, Lunch, Dinner Day 4 Breakfast on cruise. Return to Hanoi. Check in. Evening: Private cyclo + street food tour in Old Quarter with guide. Overnight: Hanoi Meals: Breakfast Day 5 Breakfast at hotel. Private excursion to Ninh Binh with Mercedes MPV. VIP boat + gourmet lunch. Return for farewell dinner at El Gaucho. Alternative: Replace with couple spa + personal shopping. Overnight: Hanoi Meals: Breakfast, Lunch Day 6 Breakfast at hotel. Check-out and private transfer to Noi Bai Airport for departure. Meals: Breakfast', 3860),
  ('ha-noi', 32, 'travel-agent-insights', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS', NULL, NULL, 'What inexperienced planners often do wrong What an experienced planner does differently', 3861),
  ('ha-noi', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', NULL, NULL, 'IF: trip length <= 2 nights THEN: Prioritise OLD QUARTER + HOAN KIEM + WATER PUPPET + 1 food experience. Reason: First impression is the city vibe. IF: trip length == 3 nights THEN: Include only one major day trip: Ha Long Bay OR Ninh Binh. Reason: Both need a full day + travel time. IF: trip length >= 4 nights THEN: Add Ha Long Bay 2D1N + Ninh Binh day trip. Reason: 4+ nights allows city + 2 nature experiences. IF: traveler_type == FAMILY THEN: Max 1 major attraction/day + afternoon pool/AC break. Reason: Heat and walking are heavy for kids. IF: traveler type == HONEYMOON THEN: Limit to 2 activities/day + 2D1N Ha Long cruise. Reason: Value comes from slow pace + romance.', 3862),
  ('ha-noi', 34, 'destination-scoring', 'DESTINATION SCORING', NULL, NULL, '| Factor | Score | | ------------------ | ----: | | Family | 75 | | Honeymoon | 88 | | Luxury | 87 | | Budget | 95 | | Adventure | 70 | | Culture | 92 | | Food | 98 | | Shopping | 70 | | Nightlife | 65 | | Relaxation | 70 | | Nature | 90 | | Accessibility | 60 | | Safety | 85 | | First-time visitor | 90 | | Photography | 95 |', 3863),
  ('ha-noi', 35, 'final-travel-agent-verdict', 'FINAL TRAVEL AGENT VERDICT', NULL, NULL, 'Best travellers profiles: 1. Budget travellers 2. Food travelers 3. Culture travellers 4. First-time Vietnam visitors 5. Honeymoon on budget Best duration: 3-4 nights Best season: March-April September-November Best hotel strategy: Stay in OLD QUARTER for first-timers. BA DINH for luxury. Best transportation: Walk + Grab Bike/Car. Private car for day trips. Must-do for first-time visitor: Don''t-do: Biggest advantage: City with world-class experiences. Food + culture is unmatched. Biggest disadvantage: Traffic, heat, pollution, walking intensity. Overall destination score: 88/100 - Amazing value, culture, and food destination. Best for 3-5 night trips.', 3864),
  ('ha-noi', 36, 'data-quality', 'DATA QUALITY', NULL, NULL, 'information_completeness: 88/100 last_updated: 2026-08-07 last_verified: PARTIALLY_LIVE_VERIFIED verified_by: HANOI_DESTINATION_KNOWLEDGE_DATASET sources: IMPORTANT: This Hanoi destination file is suitable for itinerary design, travellers profiling, hotel-area strategy, and initial package planning. Prices, hotel inventory, flight schedules, attraction operating hours, show timings, maintenance closures, ticket availability, visa and entry rules, public-transport notices, weather alerts, AQI/pollution levels, and supplier cancellation policies must be live-verified before quotation, payment collection, or ticket issuance. Do not rely on generic “Hanoi package” inclusions without confirming the exact: Correct outdated or inconsistent records before production use:', 3865),
  ('ha-long-bay', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Autumn Season', NULL, 'months: September–November weather: Warm, comfortable temperatures (20–28°C), low humidity, clear skies, and calm waters. crowd_level: HIGH price_level: HIGH overall_score: 92–98 recommended: true reason: Peak conditions for cruising with pleasant temperatures, crisp views of the limestone karsts, minimal rain, and ideal sea conditions for kayaking.', 3866),
  ('ha-long-bay', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Spring Season', NULL, 'months: March–May weather: Warm, pleasant days (22–30°C) with clear skies and occasional light mist; temperatures gradually increase toward May. crowd_level: HIGH price_level: HIGH overall_score: 90–95 recommended: true reason: Excellent weather for cruising and outdoor water sports before summer humidity and storms set in.', 3867),
  ('ha-long-bay', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Winter Season', NULL, 'months: December–February weather: Cool to cold (12–20°C), dry, with persistent fog, mist, and occasional overcast drizzle. crowd_level: MEDIUM → HIGH price_level: MEDIUM → HIGH overall_score: 75–82 recommended: true reason: Atmospheric and moody landscape photography with mist-shrouded karsts, though cooler temperatures mean swimming is less appealing.', 3868),
  ('ha-long-bay', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Summer Season', NULL, 'months: June–August weather: Hot and humid (28–35°C) with heavy tropical downpours and occasional monsoon storms or typhoons. crowd_level: MEDIUM price_level: LOW → MEDIUM overall_score: 65–72 recommended: false reason: High chance of sudden cruise cancellations or itinerary disruptions due to tropical storms, though prices drop and domestic travel discounts abound.', 3869),
  ('ha-long-bay', 10, 'budget-strategy', 'BUDGET STRATEGY', NULL, NULL, 'Where saving money is not recommended:', 3870),
  ('ha-long-bay', 18, 'family-travel', 'FAMILY TRAVEL', 'Family rating format', 'family', 'child_friendly_score: 90 best_ages: Rules:', 3871),
  ('ha-long-bay', 19, 'honeymoon-travel', 'HONEYMOON TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'Best areas: Lan Ha Bay: best for private luxury boutique cruises, uncrowded secluded lagoons, and private balcony suites. Bai Tu Long Bay: best for serene off-the-beaten-path sailing, peaceful starry nights, and untouched limestone nature. Central Ha Long Bay: best for iconic bucket-list scenery, luxury charter yachts, and classic cave excursions. Cat Ba Island (Boutique Resorts): best for combining ocean luxury with private eco-lodge stays and coastal cliff views. Tuan Chau Marina: best for seamless luxury seaplane arrivals and private boat embarkation. Honeymoon rules: Prefer one special experience (such as private sea kayaking or a seaplane flight) plus relaxed deck downtime. Overpacked day itineraries and frequent harbor transfers reduce the romantic feel. Private transfers and a high-end balcony cabin on a small-capacity cruise matter more than squeezing in extra tourist stops.', 3872),
  ('ha-long-bay', 20, 'luxury-travel', 'LUXURY TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'luxury_score: 95 Best-value luxury pattern Book an executive or presidential balcony suite on an exclusive 5-star boutique vessel (such as Stellar of the Seas, Paradise Peak, or Capella Cruise) in Lan Ha Bay or Bai Tu Long Bay. Use private scenic seaplane transfers (Hai Au Aviation) directly from Hanoi (Noi Bai Airport) to Tuan Chau Marina, combined with private chauffeured luxury limousine vans via the expressway for return land transfers. Charter a private luxury junk or yacht for customized sailing routes into secluded, uncrowded lagoons, featuring private sea kayaking and off-itinerary cave exploration. Enjoy multi-course gourmet seafood dining with a private onboard chef, wine pairings, evening deck lounge service, and bespoke spa wellness treatments while anchored in tranquil waters. Luxury rules: Keep the itinerary light and avoid overpacking the day with fast-paced group excursions. Prefer comfort, privacy, service, convenience, and exclusivity over cramming in every standard tourist cave. Avoid crowded 100+ passenger day-boats, standard shared shuttle buses, peak harbor embarkation lines, and frequent hotel changes. For Ha Long Bay, a dedicated 2-night / 3-day luxury cruise provides the ideal balance of scenic nature, secluded exploration, and world-class maritime hospitality.', 3873),
  ('ha-long-bay', 21, 'adventure', 'ADVENTURE', NULL, NULL, 'adventure_score: 90 Ha Long Bay and the surrounding Cat Ba Archipelago form a premier outdoor seascape adventure destination, renowned for deep-water soloing, limestone karst rock climbing, sea kayaking through submerged caves, and rugged jungle trekking rather than purely artificial attractions. It is best explored by combining an active small-vessel cruise with a land-based adventure stay on Cat Ba Island, as the region encompasses expansive marine national parks, secluded lagoons, and dramatic vertical karst cliffs. Top experiences: Recommended areas: Best for:', 3874),
  ('ha-long-bay', 22, 'senior-travel', 'SENIOR TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'senior_suitability: 82 walking_intensity: LOW → MEDIUM (mostly boat-based) Ha Long Bay is a very good fit for senior travelers when itineraries prioritize comfortable overnight cruise vessels, accessible cabin options, and relaxed deck-based sightseeing. The region''s iconic limestone karsts and emerald waters can be fully enjoyed from the comfort of an ocean-view balcony or sun deck without requiring rigorous physical exertion. Rules: Prefer: Avoid:', 3875),
  ('ha-long-bay', 23, 'accessibility', 'ACCESSIBILITY', NULL, NULL, 'wheelchair_accessibility: PARTIAL_TO_GOOD depending on attraction and transport public_transport_accessibility: VARIABLE hotel_accessibility: MUST_BE_VERIFIED_PER_HOTEL attraction_accessibility: MUST_BE_VERIFIED_PER_ATTRACTION Rule: Never infer accessibility from destination-level accessibility. Each hotel and attraction must carry its own accessibility data.', 3876),
  ('ha-long-bay', 24, 'food', 'FOOD', NULL, NULL, 'food_score: 85 Ha Long Bay and Quang Ninh province are celebrated across Vietnam for fresh ocean seafood, distinct regional specialties, and rich maritime flavors. Dining ranges from multi-course seafood banquets on overnight cruise vessels to casual local eateries and floating seafood rafts scattered across the bay. Food experiences: Best for: Recommended areas:', 3877),
  ('ha-long-bay', 25, 'shopping', 'SHOPPING', NULL, NULL, 'shopping_score: 65 Shopping in the Ha Long Bay area focuses on unique maritime crafts, local artisanal products, and regional culinary specialties rather than modern high-street fashion or mega shopping malls. Experiences center around colorful night markets, pearl farms floating on the water, and local mainland markets. Best buys: Prefer: Avoid: Best for:', 3878),
  ('ha-long-bay', 26, 'nightlife', 'NIGHTLIFE', NULL, NULL, 'nightlife_level: 45 Ha Long Bay nightlife is divided into two distinct experiences: peaceful, low-key onboard activities on overnight cruise ships, and a vibrant mainland tourist scene in Ha Long City. Nightlife on the water centers around calm ocean views, deck cocktail hours, and night squid fishing, while mainland areas like Bãi Cháy offer lively night markets, open-air beach bars, and late-night clubs. Best for: Prefer: Avoid: Best evening areas:', 3879),
  ('ha-long-bay', 28, 'sample-itinerary-patterns', 'SAMPLE ITINERARY PATTERNS', '2 NIGHTS – CLASSIC HA LONG BAY CRUISE', NULL, 'Day 1: Expressway limousine transfer from Hanoi (HAN Airport or Old Quarter) to Tuan Chau Marina / Sun Group Port (~2.5 hours) → Embarkation on 5-star overnight cruise vessel & welcome drink → Onboard lunch sailing past iconic limestone karsts → Afternoon excursion to Sung Sot (Surprise) Cave or Titov Island peak climb → Sunset cocktail hour & Vietnamese cooking demonstration on the open sun deck → Multi-course seafood dinner & evening squid fishing Day 2: Morning Tai Chi session on the sun deck at sunrise → Light breakfast with panoramic ocean views → Morning sea kayaking through Luon Cave lagoon or bamboo boat tour → Brunch onboard while cruising back toward mainland harbor → Disembarkation at harbor (~11:30 AM) → Transfer to Ha Long City hotel base for evening relaxation → Evening walk through Bãi Cháy Night Market & local seafood dinner (*Chả Mực*) Day 3: Morning visit to Sun World Ha Long Complex (Queen Cable Car) or local Hon Gai Market → Direct expressway transfer back to Hanoi or Cat Bi Airport (HPH)', 3880),
  ('ha-long-bay', 28, 'sample-itinerary-patterns', 'SAMPLE ITINERARY PATTERNS', '3 NIGHTS – LAN HA BAY & CAT BA ARCHIPELAGO', NULL, 'Day 1: Transfer from Hanoi to Tuan Chau Marina or Got Harbor → Board luxury boutique cruise bound for Lan Ha Bay → Lunch onboard surrounded by tranquil, uncrowded limestone islets → Afternoon sea kayaking through Dark & Bright Cave into hidden lagoons → Sunset watching & wine tasting on deck → Gourmet dinner onboard under the stars Day 2: Early morning Tai Chi & breakfast on deck → Day-boat tender excursion to Cat Ba Island → Cycling trip to remote Viet Hai eco-village inside Cat Ba National Park → Local lunch in Viet Hai village → Afternoon swimming & beach downtime at Ba Trai Dao (Three Peaches) secluded beaches → Return to main cruise vessel for evening dinner & deck relaxation Day 3: Breakfast onboard while sailing past floating fishing communities → Check-out of cruise & disembarkation to Cat Ba Island (Ben Beo Harbor) → Check-in to Cat Ba Island resort or eco-lodge → Afternoon hike to Ngu Lam Peak or exploration of historical Hospital Cave → Seaside dinner in Cat Ba Town Day 4: Breakfast at resort → Final morning swim at Cat Co 3 Beach → Speedboat/ferry transfer to Hai Phong / Hanoi for flight departure', 3881),
  ('ha-long-bay', 28, 'sample-itinerary-patterns', 'SAMPLE ITINERARY PATTERNS', '4 NIGHTS – ULTIMATE BAY & ISLAND EXPLORATION', NULL, 'Day 1: Arrival via Hanoi (HAN) or Cat Bi (HPH) Airport → Private transfer to Tuan Chau Marina → Board luxury cruise for Bai Tu Long Bay or Lan Ha Bay → Check-in to private oceanview balcony cabin → Afternoon kayaking & cave exploration in Thien Canh Son Cave → Dinner & evening relaxation onboard Day 2: Full-day luxury sailing in untouched outer bay zones → Morning bamboo boat tour through Vung Vieng floating fishing village → Visit local pearl cultivation farm → Afternoon swimming, stand-up paddleboarding, and secluded beach BBQ → Sunset deck lounge with live acoustic music → Gourmet chef dinner onboard Day 3: Morning sunrise Tai Chi & breakfast cruise back to port → Disembarkation & private transfer to Cat Ba Island → Check-in to island hotel base → Trekking expedition through Cat Ba National Park jungle trails → Sunset viewpoint visit at Cannon Fort overlooking Lan Ha Bay archipelago → Local seafood feast in Cat Ba harbor district Day 4: Morning rock climbing or deep-water soloing session around Lan Ha karsts → Afternoon leisure time at Cat Co beaches or resort spa → Evening stroll along Bãi Cháy walking street on the mainland → Farewell seafood dinner in Ha Long City Day 5: Breakfast at hotel → Optional 45-minute scenic seaplane flight (Hai Au Aviation) over the karst seascape → Direct private transfer to Hanoi airport for departure', 3882),
  ('ha-long-bay', 28, 'sample-itinerary-patterns', 'SAMPLE ITINERARY PATTERNS', '1 NIGHT – EXPRESS BAY HIGHLIGHTS', NULL, 'Day 1: Morning expressway departure from Hanoi to Tuan Chau Marina (~2.5 hours) → Embarkation on classic overnight cruise (~12:00 PM) → Buffet lunch while sailing into Central Ha Long Bay → Afternoon visit to Sung Sot Cave and swimming at Titov Beach → Sunset deck party, cooking class, and dinner onboard → Night squid fishing on the rear deck Day 2: Sunrise Tai Chi & coffee on the upper deck → Early morning kayaking through Luon Cave water arch → Brunch served while sailing back past Fighting Cocks Islet → Disembarkation at harbor (~11:00 AM) → Direct return transfer to Hanoi or airport connection by mid-afternoon', 3883),
  ('ha-long-bay', 29, '7-nights-8-days-honeymoon-grand-vietnam-ha-long-bay-and-beyond', '7 NIGHTS / 8 DAYS – HONEYMOON GRAND VIETNAM (HA LONG BAY & BEYOND)', NULL, NULL, '**Day 1: Hanoi Arrival & Leisure** Arrival at Hanoi Airport (Noi Bai) → Private transfer without guide to Hanoi city center hotel (Check-in after 2:00 PM) → Rest of day at leisure to unwind from flight → Quiet evening exploration of Hanoi Old Quarter **Day 2: Hanoi → Ha Long Bay Cruise (Overnight on Board)** Breakfast at hotel & check-out → 08:00–08:30: Hotel pick-up for scenic transfer to Ha Long Bay → 12:30: Embarkation on V’Spirit Classic Cruise & safety briefing → 13:30: Onboard lunch sailing past limestone karst formations → 15:00: Explore Sung Sot (Surprise) Cave stalactite chambers → 16:00: Visit Titov Island for beach swimming or climbing the peak for panoramic views → 17:30: Sunset party on the upper sundeck → 19:00: Multi-course dinner, followed by evening squid fishing, board games, or deck relaxation **Day 3: Ha Long Bay Kayaking → Hanoi** 06:30: Sunrise Tai Chi session on sundeck → 07:00: Breakfast onboard overlooking the bay → 08:30: Sea kayaking around Drum Cave and hidden lagoons → 09:45: Cabin check-out & cruise past Ba Hang Fishing Village and Dog Islet → 10:30: Fruit carving demonstration and Vietnamese cooking class onboard → 11:30: Disembarkation at harbor & transfer back to Hanoi (~17:00 arrival) → Evening at leisure in Hanoi **Day 4: Hanoi ✈ Da Nang** Breakfast at hotel → Morning free time for shopping or local cafes → Check-out by 12:00 PM & private airport transfer to Noi Bai Airport → Flight to Da Nang → Private arrival transfer to Da Nang hotel (Check-in 14:00 PM) → Evening free at your own leisure **Day 5: Ba Na Hills & Golden Bridge ✈ Ho Chi Minh City** Breakfast at hotel & check-out → 08:00: Transfer to Ba Na Hills & world-record cable car ride → Morning visit to Golden Bridge (Hands of God), Debay Wine Cellar, Le Jardin D’Amour Flower Garden, and Linh Ung Pagoda → 11:30: Buffet lunch at local restaurant → 12:30: Summit Chua Mountain (1,487m) & explore French Square / Fantasy Park → 14:00: Cable car down & private transfer to Da Nang Airport → Flight to Ho Chi Minh City (Departure 18:00 or later) → Private transfer from Tan Son Nhat Airport to hotel **Day 6: Ho Chi Minh City Highlights & Cu Chi Tunnels** Breakfast at hotel → 07:30: Guided city tour visiting Independence Palace, Notre Dame Cathedral, Central Post Office, and War Remnants Museum → Lunch at local restaurant → Afternoon drive to Cu Chi Tunnels for historical underground network exploration and guerilla tea/cassava tasting → Return to Saigon by late afternoon & free evening **Day 7: Full Day Mekong Delta Excursion** Breakfast at hotel → 07:30: Departure for My Tho in the Mekong Delta → Sampan cruise around Dragon, Unicorn, Phoenix, and Tortoise Islands → Tropical fruit tasting, local folk music performance, honey-bee farm visit, and coconut candy workshop → Hand-rowed sampan ride through Thoi Son canal & local restaurant lunch → Afternoon village cycling through Tan Thach or hammock relaxation → Return to Ho Chi Minh City **Day 8: Ho Chi Minh City Departure** Breakfast at hotel → Day at leisure for final souvenir shopping (Check-out by 12:00 PM) → Private transfer without guide to Tan Son Nhat Airport for onward departure flight', 3884),
