  ('ha-long-bay', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', NULL, NULL, 'IF: `trip_length <= 1 night` THEN: Choose an express 2D1N cruise departing from Tuan Chau Marina or stay in Ha Long City/Cat Ba Town with a 4-hour day-boat tour. Reason: Overnights under 24 hours require tight logistics; a structured 2D1N itinerary minimizes transit gaps and maximizes time on the water. IF: `trip_length == 2 nights` THEN: Book a 3D2N luxury cruise covering deep Lan Ha Bay or Bai Tu Long Bay, or pair a 2D1N cruise with 1 night in Hanoi/Cat Ba Island. Reason: Two full nights on the bay allow access to uncrowded outer lagoons, floating villages, and off-the-beaten-path sea caves without daily packing. IF: `trip_length >= 3 nights` THEN: Combine a 2D1N/3D2N luxury cruise with a 2-night land stay on Cat Ba Island or in Ha Long City/Bãi Cháy. Reason: Three or more nights allow you to combine marine karst navigation with inland jungle trekking, cave exploring, and mainland market dining. IF: `trip_type == FIRST_TIME_VISITOR` THEN: Prioritize Central Ha Long Bay highlights including Sung Sot (Surprise) Cave, Titov Island peak viewpoint, and Luon Cave. Reason: These classic UNESCO heritage landmarks provide the most iconic, quintessential postcard images of Ha Long Bay. IF: `trip_type == HONEYMOON` THEN: Book a private oceanfront balcony suite on a boutique vessel sailing Lan Ha Bay or Bai Tu Long Bay, paired with a private seaplane flight. Reason: Lan Ha and Bai Tu Long offer far quieter anchorages, secluded sea lagoons, and elevated privacy compared to the busier central routes. IF: `traveler_type == FAMILY` THEN: Select a large, high-safety 5-star cruise ship featuring family interconnecting suites, sun deck swimming pools, and guided bamboo boat transfers. Reason: Modern 5-star ships provide high deck safety railings, kid-friendly cooking masterclasses, and gentle water activities suitable for all ages. IF: `traveler_type == LUXURY` THEN: Fly via private Hai Au Aviation seaplane from Hanoi to Tuan Chau Marina, chartering a executive suite or private yacht with dedicated butler service. Reason: Seaplane arrival eliminates highway transit and provides dramatic aerial views, paired with bespoke fine dining and private tender excursions. IF: `traveler_type == BUDGET` THEN: Base in Cat Ba Town, book local day-boat tours from Ben Beo Harbor, and use public ferries or direct Hanoi tourist buses. Reason: Cat Ba Island offers abundant affordable hostels, cheap harbor-front seafood, and low-cost kayaking rentals without luxury cruise surcharges. IF: `traveler_interest == NATURE` THEN: Combine a Bai Tu Long Bay eco-cruise with multi-day trekking in Cat Ba National Park (Ngu Lam Peak & Viet Hai Village). Reason: The northern wilderness sector of Bai Tu Long and the terrestrial biosphere reserve of Cat Ba contain the region’s highest ecological diversity. IF: `traveler_interest == FOOD` THEN: Sample hand-pounded squid patties (*Chả Mực*) at Bãi Cháy Night Market and enjoy onboard seafood banquets and cooking masterclasses. Reason: Regional cuisine centers on world-class fresh catches, artisanal squid preparations, and interactive culinary demonstrations. IF: `traveler_interest == SHOPPING` THEN: Focus on certified floating pearl farms in Lan Ha Bay and Bãi Cháy/Hon Gai local markets. Reason: Ha Long shopping centers around cultured marine pearls, vacuum-sealed seafood specialties, and traditional wooden vessel handicrafts. IF: `traveler_type == SENIOR` THEN: Book high-end vessels with ground-level suite access, private expressway limousine transfers, and local bamboo rowboat cave excursions. Reason: Bamboo rowboats and stable luxury vessels eliminate strenuous cavern stairs and physical kayaking demands. IF: `traveler_type == TRANSIT` THEN: Stay in Tuan Chau Marina or Ha Long City near the expressway interchange for easy access to Cat Bi (HPH) or Hanoi (HAN) airports. Reason: Close proximity to major highway arteries ensures rapid harbor-to-airport transfers for tight flight schedules. IF: `trip_length >= 4 nights` THEN: Split your stay between Ha Long Bay/Lan Ha Bay marine cruising and land-based regional hubs like Cat Ba Island, Hanoi, or Ninh Binh.', 3904),
  ('ha-long-bay', 34, 'destination-scoring', 'DESTINATION SCORING', NULL, NULL, '| Factor | Score | | --- | --- | | Family | 90 | | Honeymoon | 87 | | Luxury | 90 | | Budget | 82 | | Adventure | 88 | | Culture | 80 | | Food | 84 | | Shopping | 52 | | Nightlife | 45 | | Relaxation | 88 | | Nature | 99 | | Accessibility | 60 | | Senior travelers | 86 | | First-time visitor | 90 | | Photography | 88 |', 3905),
  ('ha-long-bay', 35, 'final-travel-agent-verdict', 'FINAL TRAVEL AGENT VERDICT', NULL, NULL, 'Best for: Honeymooners, eco-tourists, landscape photographers, sea kayakers, luxury travelers, and families seeking iconic karst scenery and UNESCO World Heritage maritime beauty. Best duration: 2–3 days / 2 nights Best season: March–May; September–November Best stay: Lan Ha Bay overnight cruise, Bai Tu Long Bay luxury vessel, or Cat Ba Island eco-lodge Best transport: Private luxury limousine van via Hanoi Expressway, private seaplane transfers, or chauffeured harbor transfers Must-do: Avoid: Biggest advantage: World-renowned, bucket-list seascape geometry featuring thousands of towering limestone karsts rising out of emerald green waters. Biggest disadvantage: Harbor congestion and crowded tourist routes around core central bay caves, alongside seasonal weather cancellations during summer monsoon storms. Overall destination score: **95/100**', 3906),
  ('ha-long-bay', 36, 'data-quality', 'DATA QUALITY', NULL, NULL, 'information_completeness: 94/100 last_updated: 2026-08-25 last_verified: NOT_LIVE_VERIFIED verified_by: TRAVEL_ENGINE_INITIAL_DATASET sources: IMPORTANT: Prices, opening hours, schedules, visa requirements, availability, accessibility and operational conditions must NOT be treated as permanently valid from this document. These must be sourced from structured, refreshable data.', 3907),
  ('danang', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Spring', NULL, 'months: March April May weather: Warm and dry. 24-30°C. Low humidity, sunny skies, perfect sea temp 26°C crowd_level: MEDIUM → HIGH in late April price_level: MEDIUM → HIGH overall_score: 88-90 recommended: true reason: Best season for Danang. Perfect beach weather + clear views of Son Tra + Ba Na. Sea is calm for Cham Islands. Ideal for first-time tourists, families, and photography. Book early for April 30 - May 1 Vietnam Reunification holiday.', 3908),
  ('danang', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Summer', NULL, 'months: June July August weather: Hot. 30-35°C. Sunny with short afternoon thunderstorms. Sea temp 29°C crowd_level: HIGH price_level: HIGH overall_score: 85-87 recommended: true reason: Peak domestic travel + school holidays. Best time for beach swimming and water sports. Hotels/resorts are most expensive. Ba Na Hills is cooler 18-22°C - perfect escape. Rain comes in 1hr bursts, not all-day. Good for families on summer break.', 3909),
  ('danang', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Autumn', NULL, 'months: September October November weather: Warm to cool. 26-32°C Sep, 24-28°C Oct-Nov. Rainy season starts mid-Sep. Typhoon risk Oct-Nov crowd_level: MEDIUM → LOW price_level: MEDIUM → LOW overall_score: 75-82 recommended: true with caveats reason: Cheapest rates + fewer crowds. Great value for luxury resorts. BUT risk: typhoons can cancel Cham Islands, beach activities, and even flights. Sep still good for beach. Oct-Nov: plan indoor backup - museums, spa, Vincom. Not ideal for honeymoon beach-only trips.', 3910),
  ('danang', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Winter', NULL, 'months: December January February weather: Cool and dry. 20-25°C. Sea temp 23°C - too cool for long swims. Occasional drizzle crowd_level: LOW → VERY HIGH late Dec-early Jan + Tet price_level: LOW → VERY HIGH late Dec-early Jan + Tet overall_score: 80-84 recommended: true reason: Best season for sightseeing without sweat. Perfect for Marble Mountains, Hue, Hoi An walking. Beach is for sunbathing, not swimming. Christmas, New Year, Tet = peak prices 2x-3x. Jan-Feb post-Tet = sweet spot for Indian families: cool weather, low crowds, good deals. Pack light jacket.', 3911),
  ('danang', 10, 'budget-strategy', 'BUDGET STRATEGY', NULL, NULL, 'Where money can be saved: Where saving money is usually NOT recommended: Travel-agent rule: Stay within 500m of My Khe Beach. You save daily Grab + time.', 3912),
