  ('danang', 23, 'accessibility', 'ACCESSIBILITY', NULL, NULL, 'wheelchair accessibility: MODERATE public transport accessibility: LOW hotel accessibility: GOOD_TO_EXCELLENT; MUST_BE_VERIFIED_PER_HOTEL attraction accessibility: MODERATE_TO_GOOD; MUST_BE_VERIFIED_PER_ATTRACTION Rule: Verify accessible room, step-free access, and attraction facilities before booking. Get written confirmation from hotel + tour operator. Send photos of bathroom if possible.', 3923),
  ('danang', 24, 'food', 'FOOD', NULL, NULL, 'Danang is particularly strong for: Food experiences: 1. MY_KHE_BEACH_FOOD_WALK - Mi Quang, Banh Xeo, Bun Cha Ca, Nem Lui. 2. HOI_AN_FOOD_TOUR + COOKING_CLASS - Cao Lau, White Rose, market visit. 4hrs 3. SEAFOOD_AT_BIEN_DONG_OR_BE_MANH - Grilled fish, crab, clams by the beach 4. CAFE_AT_ROOFTOP - Cold brew, coconut coffee, city view 5. FINE-DINING - La Maison 1888, Madame Lan, Borgo Italian Family: Prioritise clean restaurants with AC, familiar menu, early dining at 6 PM. Go to: Vin-com Mall food court, Pho 24, Banh Xeo Ba Duong AC branch, Hotel buffet Honeymoon: Include one rooftop dinner at SKY36 or a beachfront dinner at Son Tra. Candlelight + ocean. Add: Private cooking class in Hoi An + riverside dinner Budget: Use street food + local beer. Reserve 1 premium meal. Go to: Han Market, Con Market, Bia corner Le Duan Street', 3924),
  ('danang', 25, 'shopping', 'SHOPPING', NULL, NULL, 'Strong categories: Luxury shopping: Budget: Prefer:', 3925),
  ('danang', 26, 'nightlife', 'NIGHTLIFE', NULL, NULL, 'nightlife_level: 75 Suitable for: Not a primary requirement for: Honeymoon travellers should generally prefer: Romantic rooftop dinner at Apricot/Press Club, West Lake sunset drinks, Hoan Kiem Lake evening walk, or 5★ hotel jazz over: late-night club itinerary', 3926),
  ('danang', 28, 'sample-itinerary-patterns', 'SAMPLE ITINERARY PATTERNS', '3 NIGHTS', NULL, 'Day 1 Arrive at Danang Airport. Private transfer to hotel in MY KHE BEACH. Check in, rest. Evening: Walk My Khe + Dragon Bridge + Han Market dinner. Overnight: Danang Meals: Breakfast Day 2 Breakfast. Full-day Ba Na Hills + Golden Bridge. Buffet lunch included. Return 5PM. Evening free at hotel pool. Overnight: Danang Meals: Breakfast, Lunch Day 3 Breakfast. Half-day Marble Mountains + Cham Museum. Afternoon: Free for shopping Vincom + Beach time. Overnight: Danang Meals: Breakfast, Lunch Day 4 Breakfast. Check out. Day trip to Hoi An Ancient Town. Lunch riverside. Evening transfer to Danang Airport for departure. Meals: Breakfast Package Includes: 3 nights stay with breakfast & Lunch, 2D1N Ha Long cruise, all tours, private transfers, e-visa support. Excludes: Flight fare, travel insurance, Ha Long cruise tips', 3927),
  ('danang', 29, 'five-night-honeymoon-pattern', 'FIVE-NIGHT HONEYMOON PATTERN', NULL, NULL, 'Day 1 Arrive Danang. VIP transfer to 5★ resort in SON TRA. Check in, beach relax. Evening: Romantic dinner at resort. Overnight: Son Trai Resort Meals: Breakfast Day 2 Breakfast. Private tour: Linh Ung Pagoda + My Khe + Dragon Bridge. Evening: Sky36 Rooftop bar sunset cocktails. Overnight: Son Trai Resort Meals: Breakfast Day 3 Check out. Transfer to Hoi An 1N boutique hotel. Afternoon: Tailoring + Ancient Town + Lantern boat ride. Romantic dinner by Thu Bon River. Overnight: Hoi An Meals: Breakfast, Dinner Day 4 Breakfast. Hoi An Cooking Class + Market. Return to Danang. Check in My Khe 5★. Spa for couple. Overnight: Danang Meals: Breakfast, Lunch Day 5 Breakfast. Full-day Ba Na Hills. Stay 1N at Mercure for sunrise photos - Or return to Danang for a beach day. Overnight: Danang Meals: Breakfast, Lunch Day 6 Breakfast. Check-out. Private transfer to Danang Airport. Meals: Breakfast', 3928),
  ('danang', 30, 'five-night-family-pattern', 'FIVE-NIGHT FAMILY PATTERN', NULL, NULL, 'Day 1 Arrive Danang. Transfer to My Khei 4★ with pool. Check-in, beach. Evening: Asia Park Sun Wheel + dinner. Overnight: Danang Meals: Breakfast Day 2 Breakfast. Ba Na Hills + Fantasy Park full day. 18°C for kids. Overnight: Danang Meals: Breakfast, Lunch Day 3 Breakfast. Cham Islands day trip - Boat + snorkelling + beach. Mar-Aug Rain backup: Helio Centre + Vincom Mall Overnight: Danang Meals: Breakfast, Lunch Day 4 Breakfast. Check-out. Hoi An day trip. Bike in rice fields + Ancient Town. Return to Danang hotel. Overnight: Danang Meals: Breakfast, Lunch Day 5 Breakfast. Marble Mountains elevator + Cham Museum AC. Afternoon: Pool + Vin-com shopping + ice cream. Overnight: Danang Meals: Breakfast Day 6 Breakfast. Check-out + Airport transfer. Meals: Breakfast Family Rules Applied: Max 1 major activity/day, outdoor in morning, AC lunch breaks', 3929),
  ('danang', 31, 'five-night-luxury-pattern', 'FIVE-NIGHT LUXURY PATTERN', NULL, NULL, 'Day 1 Arrive Danang. VIP meet-greet. Private transfer to InterContinental Son Tra. Evening: Premium dinner at La Maison 1888. Overnight: Inter-Con Meals: Breakfast Day 2 Breakfast. Private tour: Son Tra + Linh Ung + My Khe. Afternoon: TIA Spa ritual + beach. Evening: Sunset at resort bar. Overnight: Inter-Con Meals: Breakfast Day 3 Breakfast. Private Ba Na Hills with skip-line + golf cart. Return for dinner at resort. Overnight: Inter-Con Meals: Breakfast, Lunch Day 4 Breakfast. Private transfer to Hoi An. Luxury cyclo + private shopping. Return to Danang. Farewell dinner at Madame Lan. Overnight: Inter-Con Meals: Breakfast, Lunch Day 5 Breakfast. Private Hue day trip in Mercedes. VIP lunch. Return for spa. Overnight: Inter-Con Meals: Breakfast, Lunch Day 6 Breakfast. Check-out + private transfer to Danang Airport. Meals: Breakfast', 3930),
  ('danang', 32, 'travel-agent-insights', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS', NULL, NULL, 'What inexperienced planners often do wrong What an experienced planner does differently 1. Starts with purpose 2. Groups by geography: Day 1 Danang City + Beach, Day 2 Ba Na, Day 3 Hoi An, Day 4 Hue or Relax 3. Uses hotel location strategically: MY KHE for first timers/family, SON TRA for luxury/honeymoon, 1N HOI AN for romance 4. Places outdoor early morning 7-11 AM or after 4 PM - Avoid 12-3 PM sun on Marble Mountains + Beach 5. Treats Ba Na Hills as a full-day commitment, not half day - 7:30 AM pickup, 5:30 PM return 6. Chooses 2-3 high-value experiences over 8 checklist items - 1 sunset, 1 cable car, 1 lantern night > rushing 8 spots 7. Always builds 1 buffer day - For rain, typhoon, or just pool/beach time', 3931),
  ('danang', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', NULL, NULL, 'IF: trip length <= 2 nights THEN: Prioritise MY KHE BEACH + DRAGON BRIDGE + 1 DAY TRIP: Hoi An OR Ba Na Reason: First impression is beach + 1 iconic day trip. Don’t add Hue. IF: trip length == 3 nights THEN: Include Danang 1N + Hoi An 1N + Ba Na 1 Day Reason: This is the perfect "Central Vietnam Triangle". Skip Hue. IF: trip length >= 4 nights THEN: Add Danang 2N + Hoi An 1N + Hue 1 Day + Ba Na 1 Day Reason: 4+ nights allows city + beach + 3 UNESCO sites without rushing. IF: traveler type == FAMILY THEN: Max 1 major attraction/day + afternoon pool/beach break + Ba Na Fantasy Park Reason: Heat + transfers are heavy for kids. Resort time = happy kids. IF: traveler type == HONEYMOON THEN: Limit to 2 activities/day + 1N Hoi An boutique + 5★ beach resort + private car Reason: Value comes from a slow pace + romantic dinners + a spa, not a sightseeing checklist. IF: traveler type == SENIOR THEN: Skip Marble Mountains 500 steps + Mua Cave. Do Cham Museum + River Cruise + Car to Hoi An/Hue Reason: Flat, AC, minimal walking. Danang is excellent for seniors. IF: travel month == Sep-Nov THEN: Book refundable hotels + indoor activities backup and avoid Cham Islands Reason: Typhoon risk. Have Vincom Mall, Museum, Spa as Plan B.', 3932),
  ('danang', 34, 'destination-scoring', 'DESTINATION SCORING', NULL, NULL, '| Factor | Score | | ------------------ | ----: | | Family | 88 | | Honeymoon | 92 | | Luxury | 94 | | Budget | 90 | | Adventure | 75 | | Culture | 82 | | Food | 88 | | Shopping | 70 | | Nightlife | 72 | | Relaxation | 93 | | Nature | 88 | | Accessibility | 80 | | Safety | 88 | | First-time visitor | 98 | | Photography | 90 |', 3933),
  ('danang', 35, 'final-travel-agent-verdict', 'FINAL TRAVEL AGENT VERDICT', NULL, NULL, 'Best traveller profiles: 1. Family travellers - Safe beaches, easy logistics, Ba Na Hills + resorts 2. Honeymoon & Couples - Beachfront 5★, romantic Hoi An, spa + sunsets 3. Relaxation seekers - Beach + spa + slow pace. No traffic stress 4. First-time Vietnam visitors - Easy airport, clean, 1 base covers 3 UNESCO sites 5. Budget to Mid-range travelers - Great value resorts + cheap food + free beaches Best duration: 4-5 nights - 2N Danang + 1N Hoi An + 1N Ba Na/Hue day trip Best season: March - May June - August Best hotel strategy: Best transportation: Must-do for first-time visitor: Don''t-do: Biggest advantage: Most balanced + stress-free city in Vietnam. Beach + City + 3 UNESCO day trips all within 2 hours. Clean, safe, new infrastructure. Best value luxury resorts in Asia. Biggest disadvantage: Danang itself is light on history. Seasonal weather risk Sep-Nov. Lacks late nightlife after 1 AM. Overall destination score: 89/100 - Best "easy Vietnam" destination. Perfect for families, honeymoon, and first-timers who want beach + culture without chaos.', 3934),
  ('danang', 36, 'data-quality', 'DATA QUALITY', NULL, NULL, 'information_completeness: 90/100 last_updated: 2026-08-12 last_verified: PARTIALLY_LIVE_VERIFIED verified_by: DANANG_DESTINATION_KNOWLEDGE_DATASET + CENTRAL_VIETNAM_SUPPLIER_NETWORK sources: IMPORTANT: This Danang destination file is suitable for itinerary design, traveller profiling, hotel-area strategy, and initial package planning. Prices, hotel inventory, flight schedules, attraction operating hours, show timings, maintenance closures, ticket availability, visa and entry rules, public-transport notices, weather alerts, AQI/pollution levels, and supplier cancellation policies must be live-verified before quotation, payment collection, or ticket issuance. Do not rely on generic “Danang package” inclusions without confirming the exact: Correct outdated or inconsistent records before production use:', 3935),
  ('hochiminh', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Spring', NULL, 'months: March April May weather: Hot and getting hotter. 27-35°C. Still dry till mid-April. Very humid. crowd_level: MEDIUM → HIGH. High in April for local holidays + school break price_level: MEDIUM → HIGH overall_score: 86-89 recommended: true reason: Good weather but heat starts. Great for families before summer rush. 30 April - 1 May = Vietnamese National Holiday. Domestic tourists flood HCMC. Avoid.', 3936),
  ('hochiminh', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Summer', NULL, 'months: June July August weather: Hot + Humid + Afternoon rain 3-5 PM daily. crowd_level: MEDIUM → HIGH in June. MEDIUM in July-Aug price_level: HIGH in June. MEDIUM in July-Aug overall_score: 83-86 recommended: true reason: June: School holidays. Busy + expensive July-Aug: Smart value window. Rains are predictable 1hr downpour, then clear. Fewer crowds. Great for indoor: museums, malls, coffee shops.', 3937),
  ('hochiminh', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Autumn', NULL, 'months: September October November weather: Peak wet season. Heavy rain + possible flooding in low areas. crowd_level: LOW → MEDIUM price_level: LOW → MEDIUM overall_score: 78-82 recommended: true reason: Best value season. Hotels 30% cheaper. Mekong is greenest + fullest. But: Plan flexible. 1-2hrs rain daily. Some Mekong tours are cancelled if there is heavy flooding. Pro: Lightest queues at War Museum, Cu Chi. Rooftop views dramatic with clouds Avoid: Late Oct if typhoon warning in Central Vietnam', 3938),
  ('hochiminh', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Winter', NULL, 'months: December January February weather: Least hot. 24-32°C. Dry, sunny, low humidity. Best weather of the year. crowd_level: VERY HIGH in late Dec - early Jan. HIGH in Feb. price_level: VERY HIGH in late Dec - early Jan. HIGH in Feb. overall_score: 92-95 recommended: true reason: Peak season for everyone. Perfect weather for walking, rooftop, Cu Chi, Mekong. Dec-Jan: Tet + Christmas + NY. Hotels 2x-3x, book 60 days ahead Feb: Post-Tet sweet spot. Weather still great, prices drop 20%. Best for Indian families', 3939),
  ('hochiminh', 10, 'budget-strategy', 'BUDGET STRATEGY', NULL, NULL, 'Where money can be saved: Where saving money is usually NOT recommended: Travel-agent rule: A slightly more expensive but centrally located, well-reviewed hotel beside efficient public transport generally delivers better total value than a cheaper, peripheral property once you factor in extra transport costs and the value of lost time each day.', 3940),
  ('hochiminh', 12, 'airport-transfer-logic', 'AIRPORT TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Family', 'family', 'Airport taxi or pre-booked private MPV / van; Door-to-door, space for 3-4 luggage + stroller, child-friendly.', 3941),
  ('hochiminh', 12, 'airport-transfer-logic', 'AIRPORT TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Honeymoon', 'honeymoon', 'Pre-booked Private Car with Meet-and-Greet; First impression matters. Privacy + AC + cold towels. reason: The first impression of the trip matters, and private transfer provides comfort and privacy.', 3942),
  ('hochiminh', 12, 'airport-transfer-logic', 'AIRPORT TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Luxury', 'luxury', 'Chauffeured Luxury Sedan / MPV. Priority pickup; Premium comfort for 5★ stays like The Reverie, Park Hyatt.', 3943),
  ('hochiminh', 12, 'airport-transfer-logic', 'AIRPORT TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Budget', 'budget', 'Grab Car OR Airport Bus 109 + Short Grab; Lowest cost, good for light luggage + young travellers.', 3944),
