  ('nathrang', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'IF:', NULL, 'trip_length == 3 nights THEN: City 1 day + 1 Island + 1 Vin-Wonders Reason: Pick 2 major activities max. Don''t add Mud Bath.', 4082),
  ('nathrang', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'IF:', NULL, 'trip_length >= 4 nights THEN: Add VinWonders OR Mud Bath Reason: Time for 1 major + relaxation', 4083),
  ('nathrang', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'IF:', NULL, 'trip_length >= 5 nights THEN: Tran Phu 3N + North 2N OR Add Da Lat 2N Reason: Experience both city + luxury + nature', 4084),
  ('nathrang', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'IF:', NULL, 'traveler_type == FAMILY THEN: Tran Phu 4★. Central location Reason: Walk to food, beach, Grab. Easy for kids', 4085),
  ('nathrang', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'IF:', NULL, 'traveler_type == HONEYMOON THEN: North Beach 5★. Ocean view Reason: Romance + quiet + spa', 4086),
  ('nathrang', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'IF:', NULL, 'traveler_type == BUDGET THEN: Tran Phu 3★. Grab + Group tours Reason: Cheapest base, still beach + nightlife access', 4087),
  ('nathrang', 34, 'destination-scoring', 'DESTINATION SCORING', NULL, NULL, '| Factor | Score | | ------------------ | ----: | | Family | 88 | | Honeymoon | 87 | | Luxury | 88 | | Budget | 90 | | Adventure | 78 | | Culture | 75 | | Food | 86 | | Shopping | 78 | | Nightlife | 85 | | Relaxation | 82 | | Nature | 80 | | Accessibility | 78 | | Safety | 88 | | First-time visitor | 89 | | Photography | 85 |', 4088),
  ('nathrang', 35, 'final-travel-agent-verdict', 'FINAL TRAVEL AGENT VERDICT', 'Best traveller profiles:', NULL, '1. Families with kids 4+ 2. Budget travellers and Backpackers 3. Active couples and Adventure seekers 4. First-time Vietnam beach + city combo 5. Wellness travellers - Mud Bath + Spa Best duration: 4–5 nights Best season: Mar–April, August - Dry, calm sea, best for diving Avoid: Jun–Nov- rough sea, typhoon risk, island tours often cancelled Best hotel strategy: Tran Phu for first-time/family/budget/value, North Beach for honeymoon/luxury, Vinpearl Island for family + theme park Avoid: Inland hotels 3km+ from the beach. You’ll spend more on Grab than you save. Best transportation: Use Grab + Walking as default. City is compact and cheap. Private transfer for: Must-do for first-time visitor: 1. 4 Islands Tour - Snorkelling + Floating Bar. "Best day in NA Trang" 2. Vin-Wonders + Cable Car - Longest sea cable car 3. I-Resort Mud Bath - Unique wellness experience 4. Tran Phu Beach sunset + Night Market - City beach life 5. Po Nagar Cham Towers - Culture in 1 hour Don''t-do: Biggest advantage: City + Beach combo + Best value in Vietnam + Great nightlife + More activities Biggest disadvantage: Traffic + Less private than Phu Quoc + Monsoon Jun-Nov + Public beach can be busy. Overall destination score: 86/100 — Vietnam''s best value beach city. Perfect for families, budget travellers, adventurers, and first-timers. Best paired with Da Lat 2N or HCMC 2N.', 4089),
  ('nathrang', 36, 'data-quality', 'DATA QUALITY', NULL, NULL, 'information completeness: 78/100 last updated: 2026-08-07 last verified: PARTIALLY LIVE VERIFIED verified by: VIETNAM DESTINATION KNOWLEDGE DATASET sources: IMPORTANT: Sea conditions, cable car maintenance, Vin-Wonders show timings, island boat operations, mud bath timings, and hotel inventory MUST be live-verified before quotation or booking.', 4090),
  ('sapa', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', '## Dry Season / Peak - Spring & Autumn', NULL, 'months: March, April, September, October, November weather: Cool 15-22°C, dry, clear skies. Rice terraces at best. Low humidity. Perfect trekking weather. crowd_level: MEDIUM → VERY HIGH. Peak Mar-Apr + Sep-Oct. Chinese/Korean/Western tourists high. price_level: MEDIUM → HIGH overall_score: 92-96 recommended: true reason: Best weather of the year. Ideal for trekking, photography, homestays, mountain views. Mar-Apr: Rice planting season. Green terraces + waterfalls. Best for honeymoon + photographers. Sep-Oct: Rice harvest season. Golden terraces. Most famous view. Book 45 days ahead. Nov: Cool 12-18°C, misty, romantic. Prices drop 20%.', 4091),
  ('sapa', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', '## Shoulder / Cool Season', NULL, 'months: December, January, February weather: Cold 8-15°C. Possible frost. Occasional snow on Fansipan. Clear mountain views. Dry. crowd_level: LOW → MEDIUM price_level: LOW → MEDIUM overall_score: 82-86 recommended: true reason: Dec-Jan: Coldest months. Cozy resort + fireplace + hotpot. 30% cheaper hotels. Feb: Tet. Some shops closed but festive. Mountain views are clearest. Risk: Need warm clothes + heater. Some village roads muddy. Pro: No crowds, best prices, romantic misty vibe.', 4092),
  ('sapa', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', '## Wet Season / Low - Summer', NULL, 'months: May, June, July, August weather: Warm 18-25°C. Daily rain 3-5 PM. High humidity. Fog. Leeches on treks. Lush green. crowd_level: LOW → MEDIUM. July-Aug busy with domestic summer holidays. price_level: LOW → MEDIUM overall_score: 74-79 recommended: true with caveats reason: Best value season. Resorts 30% off. Cool escape from Hanoi heat 35°C. Rains are predictable: Morning sun, afternoon shower. Pros: Lush green terraces, empty trails, spa deals, waterfalls full. Cons: Trekking slippery. Views often blocked by fog. Leeches May-Jul. Tip: Stay Sapa Town 4★/5★. Focus on Cable Car, Town, Spa, Cooking class. Avoid late Jul if heavy rain warning.', 4093),
  ('sapa', 10, 'budget-strategy', 'BUDGET STRATEGY', NULL, NULL, 'Where money can be saved: Where saving money is usually NOT recommended: Travel-agent rule: A slightly more expensive Sapa Town 4★ with mountain view + heater generally delivers better total value than a cheaper homestay once you factor in taxi costs, cold nights, and "walk to dinner + market every night".', 4094),
  ('sapa', 12, 'airport-transfer-logic', 'AIRPORT TRANSFER LOGIC', '## Family', 'family', 'Pre-booked private Van from Hanoi. Door-to-door to Sapa Town hotel. Space for stroller + 3-4 luggage + warm clothes. Book sleeper bus with 2-bed cabin.', 4095),
  ('sapa', 12, 'airport-transfer-logic', 'AIRPORT TRANSFER LOGIC', '## Honeymoon', 'honeymoon', 'Pre-booked Private Car with Meet-and-Greet at Hanoi. Direct to Sapa Town 5★ resort. First impression = mountain view + fireplace + welcome tea. reason: Mountain arrival can be cold + foggy. Private transfer avoids bus hassle and starts romantic mood.', 4096),
  ('sapa', 12, 'airport-transfer-logic', 'AIRPORT TRANSFER LOGIC', '## Luxury', 'luxury', 'Chauffeured SUV/Van from Hanoi. Priority pickup. Direct to Topas Ecolodge / Victoria Sapa / Silk Path. Hot towel, water, direct check-in.', 4097),
  ('sapa', 12, 'airport-transfer-logic', 'AIRPORT TRANSFER LOGIC', '## Budget', 'budget', 'Overnight Sleeper Bus $12-$18 or Overnight Train $30-$45 to Lao Cai + Shuttle $4 to Sapa. Good for saving 1 hotel night.', 4098),
  ('sapa', 12, 'airport-transfer-logic', 'AIRPORT TRANSFER LOGIC', '## Senior', 'senior', 'Pre-booked Private Car from Hanoi with rest stops. Minimal walking. Hotel with elevator + heater essential. Avoid bus + long treks.', 4099),
  ('sapa', 18, 'family-travel', 'FAMILY TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'child_friendly_score: 88 best_ages: Rules: For young children: Prefer: Fansipan Cable Car, Cat Cat Village, Ham Rong, Herbal Bath. Avoid: Long 4-5hr treks, steep stairs, homestays without heater, Jun-Jul slippery trails, overnight trains without cabin.', 4100),
  ('sapa', 19, 'honeymoon-travel', 'HONEYMOON TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'honeymoon_score: 91 romance_score: 90 privacy_score: 85 luxury_score: 88 Recommended: Honeymoon itinerary should NOT contain more than: 2 major activities/day. Prefer: One memorable experience + free time in villa. Recommended hotel areas:', 4101),
  ('sapa', 20, 'luxury-travel', 'LUXURY TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'luxury_score: 88 Recommended: Luxury should primarily increase: Comfort, Privacy, Service, Convenience, Views, Exclusivity.', 4102),
  ('sapa', 21, 'adventure', 'ADVENTURE', NULL, NULL, 'adventure_score: 78 Adventure-like experiences should be interpreted as:', 4103),
  ('sapa', 22, 'senior-travel', 'SENIOR TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'senior_suitability: 70 walking_intensity: MEDIUM Rules: Note: Cold weather 8-15°C in winter. Bring warm clothes + meds.', 4104),
  ('sapa', 23, 'accessibility', 'ACCESSIBILITY', NULL, NULL, 'wheelchair_accessibility: POOR public_transport_accessibility: FAIR - Grab limited, taxis ok hotel_accessibility: FAIR in 4★/5★. MUST_BE_VERIFIED_PER_HOTEL attraction_accessibility: POOR-FAIR. Fansipan Cable Car = GOOD. Town = stairs. Villages = not accessible Rule: Verify accessible room, step-free access, elevator + heater before booking. Sapa Town 4★/5★ best for mobility. Villages + waterfalls require stairs. Cable Car is wheelchair accessible with assistance.', 4105),
  ('sapa', 24, 'food', 'FOOD', NULL, NULL, 'Paris is particularly strong for: Food experiences: Family: Hotel buffets, Sapa Town restaurants with heater, early 6:30 PM dinner. Avoid late night cold. Honeymoon: 1 mountain view dinner + 1 private hotpot in villa. Private setup + flowers available. Luxury: Victoria / Topas fine dining, private villa dinner, wine pairing, fireplace. Budget: Night market $3-$5, local quan $4-$6. Resort meals expensive so mix 1 resort + 2 local.', 4106),
  ('sapa', 25, 'shopping', 'SHOPPING', NULL, NULL, 'Strong categories: Luxury shopping: Sapa Square, Victoria Gift Shop, Topas Boutique, Silk Path Shop Budget: Prefer: Sapa Market, Love Market, Cat Cat village shops, Street stalls', 4107),
  ('sapa', 26, 'nightlife', 'NIGHTLIFE', NULL, NULL, 'nightlife_level: 85 Suitable for: Not a primary requirement for: Honeymoon travellers should generally prefer: Romantic mountain dinner, villa fireplace + wine, rooftop bar view over late-night clubs. Top Spots: Cloud Bar, Viet Emotion, Gecko Bar, Hmong Sisters, Mountain View Bar Vibe: Chill, acoustic music, hotpot + beer. Closes 11-12 PM. Cold nights.', 4108),
  ('sapa', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', NULL, NULL, 'IF: trip_length <= 2 nights THEN: Sapa Town + Fansipan only. Skip trekking Reason: Travel time eats day IF: trip_length == 3 nights THEN: Town 1N + Trek 1N + Fansipan 1N Reason: Minimum culture + nature IF: traveler_type == FAMILY THEN: Sapa Town 4★. Cable Car + Cat Cat Reason: Easy, safe, no long treks IF: traveler_type == HONEYMOON THEN: Muong Hoa Valley 5★. Private villa Reason: Romance + views + privacy IF: traveler_type == BUDGET THEN: Sapa Town 3★ + Group trek + Homestay 1N Reason: Cheapest mountain experience', 4109),
  ('sapa', 34, 'destination-scoring', 'DESTINATION SCORING', NULL, NULL, '| Factor | Score | | ------------------ | ----: | | Family | 80 | | Honeymoon | 91 | | Luxury | 88 | | Budget | 85 | | Adventure | 88 | | Culture | 92 | | Food | 80 | | Shopping | 75 | | Nightlife | 55 | | Relaxation | 86 | | Nature | 95 | | Accessibility | 60 | | Safety | 88 | | First-time visitor | 90 | | Photography | 96 |', 4110),
  ('sapa', 35, 'final-travel-agent-verdict', 'FINAL TRAVEL AGENT VERDICT', 'Best traveller profiles:', NULL, '1. Honeymooners and couples - Mountain views + privacy 2. Photographers and nature lovers - Terraces + clouds 3. Culture + Trekking travelers - Hmong, Dao villages 4. Families with kids 6+ - Cable car + easy walks 5. Summer escape from Hanoi heat - 15°C cooler Best duration: 3–4 nights Best season: Mar–April, Sep–October - Clear skies, dry, rice terraces best Avoid: Jun–Jul - Heavy rain, fog, leeches, slippery trails. Dec-Jan - Very cold 5-8°C Best hotel strategy: Sapa Town for first-time/family/budget, Muong Hoa Valley for honeymoon/luxury, Homestay for culture Avoid: Lao Cai city. 40min away with no view. Best transportation: Private car from Hanoi 5hr as default. Walking in town. Private transfer + guide for: Must-do for first-time visitor: 1. Fansipan Cable Car - "Roof of Indochina" + cloud sea 2. Muong Hoa Valley trek - Rice terraces + bamboo 3. 1 Homestay night - Ta Van / Lao Chai 4. Sapa Night Market - Food + culture 5. Dao Herbal Bath - Unique wellness Don''t-do: Biggest advantage: #1 Mountain + Culture destination in Vietnam + Cool climate + Affordable luxury resorts Biggest disadvantage: Weather dependent + 5hr transfer from Hanoi + Stairs and trekking required Overall destination score: 89/100 — Vietnam''s best mountain destination. Perfect honeymoon + nature + culture add-on to Hanoi.', 4111),
  ('sapa', 36, 'data-quality', 'DATA QUALITY', NULL, NULL, 'information completeness: 82/100 last updated: 2026-08-07 last verified: PARTIALLY LIVE VERIFIED verified by: VIETNAM DESTINATION KNOWLEDGE DATASET sources: IMPORTANT: Mountain weather, cable car maintenance, trekking trail conditions, road landslides, and hotel heating MUST be live-verified before quotation or booking.', 4112),
  ('bau-trang', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', '## Dry Season / Peak - Wind & Sunshine', NULL, 'months: November, December, January, February, March, April weather: Hot 28-33°C, dry, strong wind. Blue skies. Perfect for photos. No rain. crowd_level: MEDIUM → HIGH. Peak Dec-Jan + Tet. Russian/Western tourists high. price_level: MEDIUM → HIGH overall_score: 90-95 recommended: true reason: Best weather of the year. Perfect for jeep tours, sandboarding, photography. Nov-Feb: Cool evenings 22°C. Best for sunrise/sunset. Mar-Apr: Hottest but clearest skies. Lotus starts blooming at White Lake. Book jeep tours early for sunrise slot.', 4113),
  ('bau-trang', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', '## Shoulder / Hot Season', NULL, 'months: May, September, October weather: Very hot 30-34°C. Occasional rain. Wind drops. Humid. crowd_level: LOW → MEDIUM price_level: LOW → MEDIUM overall_score: 80-85 recommended: true reason: May: Still dry. Cheaper resorts. Sep-Oct: Start of rainy season. 1-2 short showers. Green lotus at White Lake. Pro: 30% cheaper hotels, empty dunes. Con: Midday 11am-3pm too hot. Must do morning/evening tours only.', 4114),
  ('bau-trang', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', '## Wet Season / Low', NULL, 'months: June, July, August weather: Hot 29-33°C. Rain 3-4 days/week. Muddy sand. Windy. Waves rough. crowd_level: LOW. Domestic summer holidays spike Jul. price_level: LOW overall_score: 70-75 recommended: true with caveats reason: Best value season. Resorts 40% off. Pros: Green lotus full bloom at Bau Trang, empty dunes, dramatic clouds for photos. Cons: Rain cancels jeep tours. Sand gets muddy. Red Dunes slippery. Tip: Stay Mui Ne 4★/5★ with pool. Focus on morning tour, spa, resort day. Avoid late Jul if typhoon warning.', 4115),
  ('bau-trang', 10, 'budget-strategy', 'BUDGET STRATEGY', NULL, NULL, 'Where money can be saved: Where saving money is usually NOT recommended: Travel-agent rule: A slightly more expensive Sapa Town 4★ with mountain view + heater generally delivers better total value than a cheaper homestay once you factor in taxi costs, cold nights, and "walk to dinner + market every night".', 4116),
  ('bau-trang', 12, 'airport-transfer-logic', 'AIRPORT TRANSFER LOGIC', '## Family', 'family', 'Pre-booked private Van from Hanoi. Door-to-door to Sapa Town hotel. Space for stroller + 3-4 luggage + warm clothes. Book sleeper bus with 2-bed cabin.', 4117),
  ('bau-trang', 12, 'airport-transfer-logic', 'AIRPORT TRANSFER LOGIC', '## Honeymoon', 'honeymoon', 'Pre-booked Private Car with Meet-and-Greet at Hanoi. Direct to Sapa Town 5★ resort. First impression = mountain view + fireplace + welcome tea. reason: Mountain arrival can be cold + foggy. Private transfer avoids bus hassle and starts romantic mood.', 4118),
  ('bau-trang', 12, 'airport-transfer-logic', 'AIRPORT TRANSFER LOGIC', '## Luxury', 'luxury', 'Chauffeured SUV/Van from Hanoi. Priority pickup. Direct to Topas Ecolodge / Victoria Sapa / Silk Path. Hot towel, water, direct check-in.', 4119),
  ('bau-trang', 12, 'airport-transfer-logic', 'AIRPORT TRANSFER LOGIC', '## Budget', 'budget', 'Overnight Sleeper Bus $12-$18 or Overnight Train $30-$45 to Lao Cai + Shuttle $4 to Sapa. Good for saving 1 hotel night.', 4120),
  ('bau-trang', 12, 'airport-transfer-logic', 'AIRPORT TRANSFER LOGIC', '## Senior', 'senior', 'Pre-booked Private Car from Hanoi with rest stops. Minimal walking. Hotel with elevator + heater essential. Avoid bus + long treks.', 4121),
  ('bau-trang', 34, 'destination-scoring', 'DESTINATION SCORING', NULL, NULL, '| Factor | Score | | ------------------ | ----: | | Family | 78 | | Honeymoon | 82 | | Luxury | 75 | | Budget | 92 | | Adventure | 88 | | Culture | 60 | | Food | 65 | | Shopping | 55 | | Nightlife | 60 | | Relaxation | 70 | | Nature | 90 | | Accessibility | 55 | | Safety | 85 | | First-time visitor | 88 | | Photography | 95 |', 4122),
  ('bau-trang', 35, 'final-travel-agent-verdict', 'FINAL TRAVEL AGENT VERDICT', 'Best traveller profiles:', NULL, '1. Photographers and couples - Desert dunes + lotus lake + golden hour 2. Adventure travelers - ATV, Jeep 4x4, Sandboarding 3. Budget travelers - $10 tours, cheap resorts, free dunes 4. Families with kids 6+ - Jeep rides + sand play + beach 5. Beach + Desert combo travelers - Mui Ne add-on Best duration: 2–3 nights in Mui Ne Best season: Nov–April - Dry, windy, clear skies, best light for photos Avoid: Jun–Aug - Rain, muddy sand, jeep tours cancelled. 11am–3pm - Too hot 35°C Best hotel strategy: Mui Ne Beachfront for all. 4★ $70-$110 best value. No hotels at Bau Trang itself. Avoid: Phan Thiet city center. 30min away with no beach view. Best transportation: Private car from HCMC 4.5hr as default. Jeep 4x4 for dunes. Private transfer + guide for: Must-do for first-time visitor: 1. White Sand Dunes Sunrise - "Mini Sahara" + Lotus Lake + ATV 2. Red Sand Dunes Sunset - Sandboarding + photos 3. Jeep 4x4 Tour - White + Red + Lotus in 1 tour 4. Fairy Stream - Red canyon barefoot walk 5. Mui Ne Seafood Dinner - Beachfront BBQ Don''t-do: Biggest advantage: #1 Desert destination in Vietnam + Unique photo spot + Very affordable + 20min from Mui Ne beach Biggest disadvantage: No accommodation at dunes + Weather dependent + 4.5hr from HCMC + Hot summer Overall destination score: 84/100 — Vietnam''s best desert experience. Perfect half-day adventure + photography add-on to Mui Ne.', 4123),
  ('bau-trang', 36, 'data-quality', 'DATA QUALITY', NULL, NULL, 'information completeness: 78/100 last updated: 2026-08-07 last verified: PARTIALLY LIVE VERIFIED verified by: VIETNAM DESTINATION KNOWLEDGE DATASET sources: IMPORTANT: Desert wind speed, rain, jeep tour operation, ATV safety, lotus bloom season, and hotel beach conditions MUST be live-verified before quotation or booking.', 4124),
  ('bangkok', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Cool Season (Peak Season)', NULL, 'months: November–February weather: Warm, pleasant days (22–32°C) with low humidity, clear skies, and comfortable evenings. crowd_level: HIGH price_level: HIGH overall_score: 92–98 recommended: true reason: The most comfortable time for urban exploration, temple visits, floating market tours, and walking through outdoor night markets with minimal rainfall and manageable heat.', 4125),
  ('bangkok', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Hot Season', NULL, 'months: March–May weather: Sweltering and intensely humid (28–38°C) with persistent heat, intense sun, and occasional pre-monsoon thunderstorms. crowd_level: MEDIUM → HIGH price_level: MEDIUM overall_score: 70–78 recommended: true reason: Temperatures reach peak annual high levels, making midday walking difficult; however, April hosts the iconic Songkran (Thai New Year) water festival, making it a unique cultural draw.', 4126),
  ('bangkok', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Rainy Season (Monsoon Season)', NULL, 'months: June–October weather: Hot and muggy (24–33°C) with frequent, heavy torrential downpours, occasional localized street flooding, and cloudy skies (peaking in September/October). crowd_level: LOW → MEDIUM price_level: LOW overall_score: 62–70 recommended: false reason: Sudden tropical downpours can disrupt outdoor sight-seeing, street food exploration, and river transit, though low-season hotel rates and indoor air-conditioned mega-malls offer great value for budget travelers.', 4127),
  ('bangkok', 10, 'budget-strategy', 'BUDGET STRATEGY', NULL, NULL, 'Where saving money is not recommended:', 4128),
  ('bangkok', 18, 'family-travel', 'FAMILY TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'child_friendly_score: 92 best_ages: Rules:', 4129),
  ('bangkok', 19, 'honeymoon-travel', 'HONEYMOON TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'Best areas: Chao Phraya Riverside: best for iconic luxury flagship resorts, romantic private dinner cruises, and private balcony suites overlooking illuminated temples. Silom & Sathorn: best for world-class high-altitude rooftop lounges, intimate fine dining, and sleek design hotels near Lumphini Park. Sukhumvit (Phrom Phong / Thonglor): best for stylish boutique hotels, trendy cocktail speakeasies, and vibrant international culinary experiences. Chinatown & Charoenkrung: best for atmospheric heritage boutique stays, art galleries, and late-night speakeasy bar hopping along historic alleyways. Rattanakosin Island (Old City): best for quiet riverside boutique hideaways, sunset views over Wat Arun, and traditional cultural charm. Honeymoon rules: Prefer one special experience (such as a sunset rooftop cocktail or a private dinner cruise on a teak barge) combined with relaxed, unhurried downtime. Overpacked daily sightseeing tours in intense midday heat reduce the romantic feel; schedule relaxation breaks or spa sessions during afternoon hours. Private luxury airport transfers and riverside 5-star hotel accommodations with private balconies or pool suites matter more than squeezing in excessive market stops.', 4130),
  ('bangkok', 20, 'luxury-travel', 'LUXURY TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'luxury_score: 96 Best-value luxury pattern Book a riverside suite or private villa at an iconic 5-star flagship property (such as The Mandarin Oriental, Capella Bangkok, or The Siam) along the Chao Phraya River. Use VIP Airport Fast-Track arrival services paired with private luxury chauffeurs (such as a Mercedes-Benz S-Class, Lexus LM, or VIP Toyota Alphard) for seamless airport transfers from Suvarnabhumi or Don Mueang. Charter a private luxury longtail boat or private yacht for customized river and canal tours, featuring champagne, private temple stops, and off-the-beaten-path urban exploration. Enjoy multi-course tasting menus at Michelin-starred restaurants (such as Sorn, Gaggan Anand, or Le Du), private rooftop lounge reservations, and bespoke multi-hour Thai massage and wellness rituals at top-tier hotel spas. Luxury rules: Keep the itinerary light and avoid overpacking the day with fast-paced group sightseeing in the intense midday heat. Prefer comfort, privacy, service, convenience, and exclusivity over cramming in every standard tourist market. Avoid unmetered street taxis, overcrowded public tour buses, long queues at major attractions, and frequent hotel changes. For Bangkok, a dedicated 3 to 4-night luxury stay provides the ideal balance of rich heritage, fine dining, world-class spas, and high-altitude rooftop views.', 4131),
  ('bangkok', 21, 'adventure', 'ADVENTURE', NULL, NULL, 'adventure_score: 82 While Bangkok is globally famed for its urban culture and temple heritage, it offers a surprisingly thrilling landscape for urban and outdoor adventure enthusiasts. Beyond the concrete jungle lies a dynamic network of high-altitude skywalks, vibrant urban cycling loops through jungle oases, adrenaline-fueled Muay Thai rings, fast-paced river waterways, and nearby coastal and jungle excursion spots. It is best explored by mixing high-energy urban challenges within the city with nearby outdoor day trips into surrounding wilderness zones. Top experiences: Recommended areas: Best for:', 4132),
  ('bangkok', 22, 'senior-travel', 'SENIOR TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'senior_suitability: 85 walking_intensity: MEDIUM (can be customized to LOW with private transit and golf carts) Bangkok is a very good fit for senior travelers when itineraries prioritize air-conditioned transit, well-paved accessible attractions, comfortable riverside accommodation, and a relaxed sightseeing pace. The city''s magnificent temples, rich cultural heritage, and legendary hospitality can be fully enjoyed with minimal physical strain by taking advantage of river express boats and private transport. Rules: Prefer: Avoid:', 4133),
  ('bangkok', 23, 'accessibility', 'ACCESSIBILITY', NULL, NULL, 'wheelchair_accessibility: PARTIAL_TO_GOOD depending on attraction and transport public_transport_accessibility: VARIABLE hotel_accessibility: MUST_BE_VERIFIED_PER_HOTEL attraction_accessibility: MUST_BE_VERIFIED_PER_ATTRACTION Rule: Never infer accessibility from destination-level accessibility. Each hotel and attraction must carry its own accessibility data.', 4134),
  ('bangkok', 24, 'food', 'FOOD', NULL, NULL, 'food_score: 98 Bangkok is widely considered one of the ultimate street food and culinary capitals of the world. Dining ranges from legendary street stalls along neon-lit alleyways to royal Thai cuisine and multi-course Michelin-starred fine dining. Food experiences: Best for: Recommended areas:', 4135),
  ('bangkok', 25, 'shopping', 'SHOPPING', NULL, NULL, 'shopping_score: 98 Bangkok is globally renowned as one of the ultimate shopping destinations in the world. The city seamlessly combines high-end luxury mega-malls, sprawling wholesale plazas, air-conditioned mega-complexes, night markets, and the world''s largest open-air weekend market into a premier retail hub. Best buys: Prefer: Avoid: Best for:', 4136),
  ('bangkok', 26, 'nightlife', 'NIGHTLIFE', NULL, NULL, 'nightlife_level: 95 Bangkok nightlife is one of the most vibrant, diverse, and high-energy after-dark scenes in the world. It spans everything from high-rise rooftop bars with sweeping skyline views and secret speakeasies in Chinatown to chaotic backpacker street parties, massive EDM megaclubs, and lively night markets serving world-class street food. Best for: Prefer: Avoid: Best evening areas:', 4137),
  ('bangkok', 28, 'sample-itinerary-patterns', 'SAMPLE ITINERARY PATTERNS', '2 NIGHTS – CLASSIC BANGKOK ESSENTIALS', NULL, 'Day 1: Arrival at Suvarnabhumi (BKK) or Don Mueang (DMK) Airport → Airport Rail Link or private hotel transfer to central Bangkok base → Afternoon walk around Siam mega-mall complex (Siam Paragon & CentralWorld) → Evening stroll to Erawan Shrine & Lumphini Park → Sunset craft cocktails at a high-altitude rooftop lounge (e.g., Vertigo or Octave) → Dinner at a trendy Sukhumvit restaurant or local night market Day 2: Early morning visit to the Grand Palace & Wat Phra Kaew (Temple of the Emerald Buddha) → Walk to nearby Wat Pho to see the giant Reclining Buddha → Cross the Chao Phraya River on a local ferry to explore Wat Arun (Temple of Dawn) → Afternoon Chao Phraya Express Boat ride down to ICONSIAM for shopping & river views → Evening street food crawl along neon-lit Yaowarat Road in Chinatown → Late-night drinks at a heritage speakeasy bar in Chinatown or Charoenkrung Day 3: Morning visit to the Jim Thompson House Museum & peaceful garden cafe → Last-minute souvenir shopping at CentralWorld or Pratunam Market → Direct train or private airport transfer for flight departure', 4138),
  ('bangkok', 28, 'sample-itinerary-patterns', 'SAMPLE ITINERARY PATTERNS', '3 NIGHTS – HERITAGE, FOOD & RIVER LUXURY', 'luxury', 'Day 1: Arrival via BKK or DMK Airport → VIP Fast-Track assistance & private chauffeur transfer to a Chao Phraya riverside hotel → Check-in to oceanview or riverfront balcony suite → Afternoon relaxation by the resort pool or private longtail boat canal (khlong) tour through Thonburi → Romantic sunset dinner cruise along the Chao Phraya River aboard a restored teak rice barge Day 2: Early morning guided cultural tour of Old City landmarks (Grand Palace, Wat Pho, and Wat Arun) → Lunch at a traditional riverside restaurant in Tha Tien → Afternoon Thai massage and spa ritual at a luxury hotel spa → Sunset photography along the Charoenkrung creative district → Multi-course tasting menu dinner at a Michelin-starred Thai fine-dining restaurant (e.g., Sorn or Le Du) Day 3: Morning trip to Chatuchak Weekend Market (if weekend) or the Jim Thompson House & Bangkok Art and Culture Centre (BACC) → Afternoon luxury high tea at a riverside flagship hotel lounge (e.g., Mandarin Oriental or Capella) → Evening visit to King Power Mahanakhon SkyWalk for 360-degree glass-tray city views → Farewell dinner and drinks at a high-altitude rooftop bar in Silom/Sathorn Day 4: Breakfast overlooking the Chao Phraya River → Leisurely morning stroll or paddleboarding session in Benjakitti Forest Park → Private chauffeur transfer back to the airport for flight departure', 4139),
  ('bangkok', 28, 'sample-itinerary-patterns', 'SAMPLE ITINERARY PATTERNS', '4 NIGHTS – ULTIMATE URBAN EXPLORER & DAY TRIPS', NULL, 'Day 1: Arrival in Bangkok & transfer to hotel base in Sukhumvit or Silom → Afternoon walk along the elevated skywalk connecting Siam malls → Evening visit to Jodd Fairs or Asiatique The Riverfront for street food and shopping → Casual drinks at an open-air beer garden or rooftop venue Day 2: Full-day historical & cultural immersion → Early morning entry to the Grand Palace, Wat Phra Kaew, and Wat Pho → Crossing over to Wat Arun for temple architecture photography → Afternoon exploration of the historic Talat Noi neighborhood and Chinatown alleyways → Evening Yaowarat street food night tour sampling crab fried rice, roast duck, and mango sticky rice Day 3: Day trip excursion to the UNESCO World Heritage site of Ayutthaya → Morning drive (~1.5 hours) to explore ancient temple ruins (Wat Mahathat, Wat Chaiwatthanaram, Wat Phra Si Sanphet) → Traditional riverfront lunch in Ayutthaya → Return to Bangkok by late afternoon → Relaxed evening in Sukhumvit (Thonglor district) for dinner and vinyl bar/speakeasy hopping Day 4: Morning jungle cycling loop through Bang Krachao (Bangkok’s "Green Lung") → Afternoon shopping at Chatuchak Weekend Market or wholesale fashion browsing at Platinum Mall → Late-afternoon Thai cooking class or authentic Muay Thai boxing match at Rajadamnern Stadium → Farewell rooftop dinner with views of the Bangkok skyline Day 5: Breakfast at hotel → Optional morning walk through Lumphini Park to spot Asian water monitor lizards → Direct private or express transit transfer to BKK/DMK Airport for departure', 4140),
  ('bangkok', 28, 'sample-itinerary-patterns', 'SAMPLE ITINERARY PATTERNS', '1 NIGHT – EXPRESS CITY HIGHLIGHTS', NULL, 'Day 1: Morning arrival at BKK or DMK Airport (~9:00 AM) → Express train or taxi transfer directly to hotel for luggage drop → Late-morning visit to Wat Pho (Reclining Buddha) and Wat Arun via river ferry → Afternoon shopping & air-conditioned lunch break at ICONSIAM or Siam Paragon → Sunset drinks at a skyline rooftop bar (e.g., Sky Bar at Lebua or Mahanakhon SkyWalk) → Late-night street food feast along Yaowarat Road in Chinatown Day 2: Early morning stroll through Lumphini Park or breakfast at a local cafe → Quick stop at the Jim Thompson House Museum or Erawan Shrine → Hotel check-out (~12:00 PM) → Direct train or private transfer back to the airport for afternoon/evening departure', 4141),
  ('bangkok', 29, '7-days-6-nights-thailand-honeymoon-itinerary', '7 Days / 6 Nights Thailand Honeymoon Itinerary', 'Day 1: Arrival & Transit to Phuket', NULL, '', 4142),
  ('bangkok', 29, '7-days-6-nights-thailand-honeymoon-itinerary', '7 Days / 6 Nights Thailand Honeymoon Itinerary', 'Day 2: Phi Phi Island Excursion', NULL, '', 4143),
  ('bangkok', 29, '7-days-6-nights-thailand-honeymoon-itinerary', '7 Days / 6 Nights Thailand Honeymoon Itinerary', 'Day 3: Phuket to Pattaya (via Bangkok)', NULL, '', 4144),
  ('bangkok', 29, '7-days-6-nights-thailand-honeymoon-itinerary', '7 Days / 6 Nights Thailand Honeymoon Itinerary', 'Day 4: Coral Island Tour & Alcazar Cabaret Show', NULL, '', 4145),
  ('bangkok', 29, '7-days-6-nights-thailand-honeymoon-itinerary', '7 Days / 6 Nights Thailand Honeymoon Itinerary', 'Day 5: Pattaya to Bangkok via Safari World & Marine Park', NULL, '', 4146),
  ('bangkok', 29, '7-days-6-nights-thailand-honeymoon-itinerary', '7 Days / 6 Nights Thailand Honeymoon Itinerary', 'Day 6: Bangkok City & Temple Tour + Shopping', NULL, '', 4147),
  ('bangkok', 29, '7-days-6-nights-thailand-honeymoon-itinerary', '7 Days / 6 Nights Thailand Honeymoon Itinerary', 'Day 7: Leisure & Departure', NULL, '', 4148),
  ('bangkok', 30, '7-days-6-nights-family-itinerary-bangkok-phuket-and-pattaya', '7 DAYS 6 NIGHTS FAMILY ITINERARY: BANGKOK, PHUKET & PATTAYA', NULL, NULL, 'Day 1: Arrive Phuket APT, Customs and baggage clearance process at the Airport. Transfer to Phuket Hotel. Checking Hotel and evening free at own. MEALS: NA Day 2: After American Breakfast proceed for fun filled half day excursion to Phi Phi Island in Phuket, followed by lunch, Dinner at local restaurant. MEALS: Breakfast & Lunch Day 3: After American Breakfast proceed to Phuket APT, flight to BKK, after arrival at BKK airport transfer to Pattaya Hotel, overnight stay at Pattaya hotel. MEALS: Breakfast Day 4: After American Breakfast proceed for fun filled half day excursion to Coral Island the picture postcard island of Pattaya, followed by lunch, Check-in at Pattaya hotel, At Evening proceed for Alcazar Show, Dinner at local restaurant. MEALS: Breakfast & Lunch Day 5: Early Break Fast Transfer to Bangkok enroute Safari World & Marine Park (Dolphin Show, Orang Utang Show, Sea Lion Show, Cowboy Show, take selfies at Safari Mini World with Friendly tiny Birds sitting on your head). Overnight at Bangkok hotel. MEALS: Breakfast & Lunch Day 6: American Break Fast at Hotel, set on Bangkok City and Temple Tour with Gems Gallery (Grand Palace, Wat Pho & Wat Arun), Lunch. Evening free for shopping at Siam Paragon / Pratunam, overnight at Bangkok hotel. MEALS: Breakfast & Lunch Day 7: After ABF checkout at 12:00 HRS, time free for last-minute shopping at CentralWorld / MBK Center, and transfer to BKK Airport at Night for boarding flight back home with sweet memories. MEALS: Breakfast', 4149),
  ('bangkok', 31, '7-days-6-nights-luxury-itinerary', '**7 DAYS 6 NIGHTS LUXURY ITINERARY**', NULL, NULL, '**Day 2: Luxury Phi Phi Island Speedboat Excursion** **Day 3: Flight back to Bangkok & Executive Transfer to Pattaya** **Day 4: Private Coral Island Yacht Tour & Alcazar VIP Show** **Day 5: Safari World & Marine Park en route to Bangkok** **Day 6: Bangkok City & Temple Tour with Gems Gallery** **Day 7: Farewell Shopping & Departure Transfer**', 4150),
  ('bangkok', 32, 'travel-agent-insights', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS', 'What inexperienced planners often do wrong', NULL, '', 4151),
  ('bangkok', 32, 'travel-agent-insights', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS', 'What an experienced planner does differently', NULL, '', 4152),
  ('bangkok', 32, 'travel-agent-insights', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS', 'Best planning rule', NULL, '', 4153),
  ('bangkok', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', NULL, NULL, 'IF: `trip_length <= 1 night` THEN: Choose an express 2D1N city stay staying near Siam or Rattanakosin, focusing on early morning major temples (Wat Pho, Wat Arun) and an evening street food crawl in Chinatown (Yaowarat). Reason: Overnights under 24 hours require tight logistics; staying along key mass transit corridors (BTS/MRT) or the river minimizes transit bottlenecks and maximizes sightseeing efficiency. IF: `trip_length == 2 nights` THEN: Book a 3D2N stay based along the Chao Phraya Riverside or Sukhumvit, pairing historic Old City sightseeing with a luxury rooftop lounge experience and ICONSIAM shopping. Reason: Two full nights allow you to balance historic temple heritage and canal tours with modern skyline dining and upscale shopping without rushing. IF: `trip_length >= 3 nights` THEN: Combine a 3-night urban stay in Bangkok with a full-day excursion to the UNESCO World Heritage ruins of Ayutthaya or a jungle cycling day trip to Bang Krachao. Reason: Three or more nights allow you to venture beyond the main commercial core into ancient regional capitals or mangrove oases while keeping your urban hotel base. IF: `trip_type == FIRST_TIME_VISITOR` THEN: Prioritize Rattanakosin Island (Old City) landmarks including the Grand Palace, Wat Phra Kaew, Wat Pho (Reclining Buddha), Wat Arun, and Yaowarat Road street food. Reason: These iconic royal and cultural landmarks form the essential spiritual and historical foundation of Bangkok. IF: `trip_type == HONEYMOON` THEN: Book a riverfront balcony suite at a flagship 5-star resort (Mandarin Oriental, Capella, or The Siam), paired with a private teak barge dinner cruise and high-altitude rooftop cocktails. Reason: Riverside sanctuaries offer world-class privacy, serene water views, and romantic fine dining away from dense urban noise. IF: `traveler_type == FAMILY` THEN: Select central luxury hotels in Siam or Sukhumvit with direct BTS skywalk access, swimming pools, and proximity to indoor attractions like SEA LIFE Bangkok Ocean World. Reason: Direct skywalk and transit connectivity avoids long street walks in intense heat and allows easy midday rest breaks. IF: `traveler_type == LUXURY` THEN: Arrange VIP Airport Fast-Track arrival clearance, chauffeured executive transfers (Mercedes S-Class or Toyota Alphard), private longtail boat canal charters, and Michelin-starred tasting menus (Sorn, Gaggan Anand). Reason: Fast-track services and private transfers eliminate airport queues, heavy traffic gridlock, and crowded public transport lines. IF: `traveler_type == BUDGET` THEN: Base around Khao San Road / Rambuttri Village or along the MRT Blue Line, using Chao Phraya Express Boats, public mass transit, and street food stalls under ฿100. Reason: These zones offer abundant low-cost hostels, cheap street dining, and direct access to affordable river transport without expensive taxi fares. IF: `traveler_interest == NATURE` THEN: Plan an active day trip to Bang Krachao ("Green Lung") for elevated path cycling, combined with morning strolls through Lumphini Park or Benjakitti Forest Park. Reason: These protected green reserves and urban forest parks feature wild Asian water monitor lizards, tropical flora, and car-free nature trails. IF: `traveler_interest == FOOD` THEN: Take night street food crawls through Yaowarat (Chinatown), Charoenkrung, and Ban Tad Thong Road, paired with Michelin bib gourmand noodle shops. Reason: Bangkok is a world culinary capital famous for fiery stir-fries, heritage roast duck, boat noodles, and night market culinary culture. IF: `traveler_interest == SHOPPING` THEN: Focus on Chatuchak Weekend Market for authentic handicrafts, alongside Siam Paragon, ICONSIAM, and Platinum Fashion Mall for wholesale fashion and luxury labels. Reason: Bangkok seamlessly combines the world''s largest open-air market with ultra-modern air-conditioned retail complexes. IF: `traveler_type == SENIOR` THEN: Book accessible riverside hotels, utilize chauffeured air-conditioned cars or express boats, schedule early morning temple visits, and reserve afternoon spa downtime. Reason: Guided private transport and early morning itineraries prevent heat exhaustion and eliminate long walks on uneven city sidewalks. IF: `traveler_type == TRANSIT` THEN: Choose a hotel along the Airport Rail Link (ARL) corridor (such as Phaya Thai or Makkasan) or near Suvarnabhumi (BKK) / Don Mueang (DMK) airports. Reason: Direct rail link connectivity ensures reliable, traffic-proof transfers to terminal departure gates. IF: `trip_length >= 4 nights` THEN: Multi-center your trip by combining 2 nights in central Bangkok (shopping/nightlife) with 2 nights in Pattaya/Phuket or a deep heritage extension in Ayutthaya.', 4154),
  ('bangkok', 34, 'destination-scoring', 'DESTINATION SCORING', NULL, NULL, '| Factor | Score | | --- | --- | | Family | 78 | | Honeymoon | 88 | | Luxury | 96 | | Budget | 95 | | Adventure | 72 | | Culture | 95 | | Food | 90 | | Shopping | 90 | | Nightlife | 96 | | Relaxation | 85 | | Nature | 65 | | Accessibility | 68 | | Senior travelers | 82 | | First-time visitor | 96 | | Photography | 94 |', 4155),
  ('bangkok', 35, 'final-travel-agent-verdict', 'FINAL TRAVEL AGENT VERDICT', NULL, NULL, 'Best for: Foodies, culture seekers, luxury travelers, nightlife enthusiasts, avid shoppers, and urban explorers looking for a world-class blend of historic heritage, dynamic street life, and modern sophistication. Best duration: 3–4 days / 3 nights Best season: November–February Best stay: Chao Phraya Riverfront flagship hotel, luxury boutique resort in Sathorn/Silom, or high-end hotel in Siam/Sukhumvit Best transport: BTS Skytrain / MRT Subway, Chao Phraya Express Boat, VIP airport fast-track service, or private chauffeured limousine Must-do: Avoid: Biggest advantage: An unparalleled culinary landscape combining world-renowned street food with Michelin-starred fine dining, paired with extraordinary cultural heritage and legendary Thai hospitality. Biggest disadvantage: Intense humidity, midday tropical heat, and heavy traffic gridlock across major city intersections during peak transit hours. Overall destination score: **96/100**', 4156),
  ('bangkok', 36, 'data-quality', 'DATA QUALITY', NULL, NULL, 'information_completeness: 94/100 last_updated: 2026-08-26 last_verified: NOT_LIVE_VERIFIED verified_by: TRAVEL_ENGINE_INITIAL_DATASET sources: IMPORTANT: Prices, opening hours, schedules, visa requirements, availability, accessibility and operational conditions must NOT be treated as permanently valid from this document. These must be sourced from structured, refreshable data.', 4157),
  ('pattaya', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Cool Season (Peak Season)', NULL, 'months: November–February weather: Warm, comfortable days (22–31°C) with low humidity, minimal rainfall, abundant sunshine, and pleasant sea breezes. crowd_level: HIGH price_level: HIGH overall_score: 90–96 recommended: true reason: Ideal conditions for beach relaxation, island trips to Koh Larn, outdoor watersports, and exploring nightlife and cultural landmarks without oppressive heat or rain.', 4158),
  ('pattaya', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Hot Season', NULL, 'months: March–May weather: Hot and humid (25–35°C) with intense sunshine and occasional brief afternoon heat showers as the monsoons approach. crowd_level: MEDIUM → HIGH price_level: MEDIUM overall_score: 72–80 recommended: true reason: Higher temperatures and humidity make mid-day walking tiring, but April features the world-famous Songkran (Thai New Year) water festival, drawing massive festival crowds.', 4159),
  ('pattaya', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Rainy Season (Monsoon Season)', NULL, 'months: June–October weather: Hot and humid (24–32°C) with frequent monsoon showers, torrential downpours, high cloud cover, and occasional short-term localized street flooding (peaking in September/October). crowd_level: LOW → MEDIUM price_level: LOW overall_score: 60–68 recommended: false reason: Strong sea waves can interrupt boat trips to nearby islands and unexpected downpours disrupt beach days, though discounted luxury hotels make it attractive for budget travelers and indoor activity seekers.', 4160),
  ('pattaya', 10, 'budget-strategy', 'BUDGET STRATEGY', NULL, NULL, 'Where saving money is not recommended:', 4161),
  ('pattaya', 18, 'family-travel', 'FAMILY TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'child_friendly_score: 88 best_ages: Rules:', 4162),
  ('pattaya', 19, 'honeymoon-travel', 'HONEYMOON TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'Best areas: Wong Amat (North Pattaya): best for luxury oceanfront flagship resorts, quiet private beaches, scenic sunset dining, and serene luxury spa retreats away from city noise. Na Jomtien: best for exclusive beach club lounges, high-end private pool villas, romantic oceanfront seafood halls, and private yacht departures from Ocean Marina. Pratamnak Hill (Khao Phra Tamnak): best for intimate boutique hillside hotels, scenic cliffside sunset cocktails, quiet beach coves, and panoramic views of Pattaya Bay. Jomtien Beach (Southern End): best for peaceful oceanfront walks, cozy beachside dining, and relaxed boutique resorts away from the central nightlife strip. Central Pattaya Riverside / Bayfront: best for luxury high-rise oceanfront suites with private balconies overlooking Pattaya Bay, rooftop infinity pools, and executive lounge access. Honeymoon rules: Prefer one signature romantic experience (such as a private luxury yacht charter to Koh Pai or a sunset oceanfront dinner at a cliffside beach club) paired with relaxed, unhurried downtime. Avoid crowded tourist hubs and noisy nightlife strips during peak evening hours; instead, reserve private beachfront cabanas or intimate spa sessions for two during afternoon hours. Investing in high-end private airport transfers from Bangkok and luxury 5-star beachfront resorts with private pool villas or ocean-view balconies matters far more than squeezing in crowded group day tours.', 4163),
  ('pattaya', 20, 'luxury-travel', 'LUXURY TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'luxury_score: 88 Best-value luxury pattern Book an ocean-view suite or private pool villa at an iconic 5-star oceanfront flagship property (such as Royal Wing Suites & Spa, InterContinental Pattaya Resort, or Centara Grand Mirage Beach Resort) in quiet enclaves like Wong Amat or Na Jomtien. Use VIP Airport Fast-Track arrival services at BKK or DMK paired with private luxury chauffeurs (such as a Mercedes-Benz S-Class, Lexus LM, or VIP Toyota Alphard) for a seamless 1.5 to 2-hour highway transfer down Motorway 7. Charter a private luxury yacht or catamaran from Ocean Marina Yacht Club for customized Gulf of Thailand island-hopping cruises to Koh Pai or Koh Rin, featuring private snorkeling, champagne, and sunset dining. Enjoy fine-dining seafood tasting menus at premier beachfront venues, VIP table reservations at executive rooftop lounges like Horizon, championship golf rounds at Siam Country Club, and multi-hour holistic spa rituals at top-tier hotel sanctuaries. Luxury rules: Keep the itinerary unhurried and avoid overpacking the day with fast-paced group tours in the intense midday heat. Prefer comfort, privacy, service, convenience, and exclusivity over cramming in crowded city night markets or noisy central entertainment strips. Avoid unmetered songthaews, overcrowded public ferry boats to Koh Larn, long queues at major water parks, and frequent hotel moves. For Pattaya, a dedicated 3 to 4-night luxury stay provides the ideal balance of island cruising, oceanfront fine dining, world-class spas, and panoramic sunset views.', 4164),
  ('pattaya', 21, 'adventure', 'ADVENTURE', NULL, NULL, 'adventure_score: 88 While Pattaya is globally famous for its vibrant nightlife and bustling beach resorts, it stands as Thailand’s premier capital for high-octane coastal, extreme sky, and off-road motorsport adventures. Beyond the shoreline lies a high-energy playground featuring world-class skydiving drop zones, adrenaline-charged flyboarding and water sports, tactical off-road dirt bike tracks, and towering bungy platforms. It is best explored by combining extreme aerial and marine challenges along the coast with rugged interior jungle excursions through mud trails and forest canopies. Top experiences: Recommended areas: Best for:', 4165),
  ('pattaya', 22, 'senior-travel', 'SENIOR TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'senior_suitability: 80 walking_intensity: MEDIUM (can be customized to LOW with private transit and golf carts) Pattaya is a very good fit for senior travelers when itineraries emphasize peaceful coastal districts, air-conditioned direct transit, accessible cultural sites, and a measured travel pace. The city''s scenic bay views, botanical gardens, unique wooden architecture, and warm seaside hospitality can be thoroughly enjoyed without excessive physical strain by utilizing private chauffeured transport and resort-based amenities. Rules: Prefer: Avoid:', 4166),
  ('pattaya', 23, 'accessibility', 'ACCESSIBILITY', NULL, NULL, 'wheelchair_accessibility: PARTIAL_TO_GOOD depending on attraction and transport public_transport_accessibility: VARIABLE hotel_accessibility: MUST_BE_VERIFIED_PER_HOTEL attraction_accessibility: MUST_BE_VERIFIED_PER_ATTRACTION Rule: Never infer accessibility from destination-level accessibility. Each hotel and attraction must carry its own accessibility data.', 4167),
  ('pattaya', 24, 'food', 'FOOD', NULL, NULL, 'food_score: 92 Pattaya is a vibrant coastal culinary hub renowned for fresh Gulf of Thailand seafood, classic Isan street food, and diverse international dining. Culinary experiences range from sizzling oceanfront night market stalls to upscale beachfront dining and authentic local seafood halls. Food experiences: Best for: Recommended areas:', 4168),
  ('pattaya', 25, 'shopping', 'SHOPPING', NULL, NULL, 'shopping_score: 85 Pattaya offers a surprisingly diverse shopping experience that balances modern oceanfront mega-malls, sprawling wholesale centers, vibrant night markets, and unique cultural floating markets. Whether hunting for budget beachwear, international designer brands, local handicrafts, or Thai snacks, the city provides convenient options right along the coast. Best buys: Prefer: Avoid: Best for:', 4169),
  ('pattaya', 26, 'nightlife', 'NIGHTLIFE', NULL, NULL, 'nightlife_level: 98 Pattaya is globally famous for its intense, legendary, and continuous after-dark entertainment scene. The city transforms at sundown, offering everything from world-renowned neon-lit pedestrian walking streets and massive multi-level megaclubs to oceanfront beach clubs, high-rise rooftop lounges, vibrant night markets, and live music venues. Best for: Prefer: Avoid: Best evening areas:', 4170),
  ('pattaya', 28, 'sample-itinerary-patterns', 'SAMPLE ITINERARY PATTERNS', '2 NIGHTS – CLASSIC PATTAYA ESSENTIALS', NULL, 'Day 1: Arrival at Suvarnabhumi (BKK) or Don Mueang (DMK) Airport → Pre-booked private transfer down Motorway 7 to central Pattaya base → Afternoon stroll along Pattaya Beach Road & shopping at Terminal 21 Pattaya → Sunset cocktails with panoramic bay views at Horizon Rooftop Bar → Evening exploration of neon-lit Walking Street or Jomtien Night Market → Dinner at a local seaside restaurant sampling fresh grilled seafood Day 2: Early morning boat trip from Bali Hai Pier to Koh Larn (Coral Island) → Morning swimming, water sports, and white-sand relaxation at Tawaen or Tien Beach → Return to mainland by mid-afternoon for hotel pool downtime → Late-afternoon visit to Wat Phra Yai (Big Buddha Temple) & Pattaya Viewpoint on Pratamnak Hill → Evening world-class Thai cultural cabaret performance at Tiffany’s Show or Alcazar Cabaret → Late-night street food crawl at Thepprasit Night Market Day 3: Morning guided tour of the handcrafted all-wood Sanctuary of Truth temple → Souvenir shopping and coconut water break at Pattaya Floating Market → Direct private transfer back to Bangkok or airport for flight departure', 4171),
  ('pattaya', 28, 'sample-itinerary-patterns', 'SAMPLE ITINERARY PATTERNS', '3 NIGHTS – COASTAL LUXURY, ISLANDS & RESORT RELAXATION', 'luxury', 'Day 1: Arrival via BKK or DMK Airport → VIP Fast-Track arrival & private luxury chauffeur transfer to a Wong Amat or Na Jomtien oceanfront resort → Check-in to a luxury ocean-view balcony suite or private pool villa → Afternoon relaxation by the infinity pool or private beachfront massage → Romantic oceanfront sunset dinner at a stylish beach venue (e.g., Cave Beach Club or Glass House Na Jomtien) Day 2: Early morning private guided architectural exploration of the Sanctuary of Truth → Lunch at a traditional seaside seafood hall in Naklua → Afternoon multi-hour luxury spa ritual at an elite resort spa (e.g., Oasis Spa) → Sunset drinks and squid fishing aboard Tapia Floating Cafe off the coast → Multi-course fine-dining seafood dinner in Na Jomtien Day 3: Full-day private luxury yacht or catamaran charter from Ocean Marina Yacht Club → Cruise out to pristine outer islands like Koh Pai or Koh Rin for snorkeling, swimming, and champagne on board → Return to marina by late afternoon → Sunset photo stop at Pattaya City Sign Viewpoint (Khao Phra Tamnak) → Farewell dinner and high-altitude rooftop drinks overlooking Pattaya Bay Day 4: Breakfast overlooking the Gulf of Thailand → Leisurely morning beach stroll along Wong Amat Beach → Private chauffeur transfer back to Bangkok or the airport for departure', 4172),
  ('pattaya', 28, 'sample-itinerary-patterns', 'SAMPLE ITINERARY PATTERNS', '4 NIGHTS – ULTIMATE ADVENTURE, CULTURE & THEME PARKS', 'adventure', 'Day 1: Arrival in Pattaya & transfer to hotel base in Jomtien or Central Pattaya → Afternoon walk along Jomtien Beach promenade → Evening visit to Terminal 21 Pattaya for food court dining and themed shopping → Casual beachfront drinks along Dongtan or Jomtien Beach Day 2: Full-day island adventure & high-energy water sports → Speedboat transfer from Bali Hai Pier to Koh Larn (Coral Island) → Morning parasailing, jet-skiing, or scuba diving offshore → Beachside seafood lunch on Tien Beach → Return to mainland for late-afternoon relaxation → Evening street food crawl through Thepprasit Night Market sampling *Pla Pao* (salt-baked fish) and mango sticky rice Day 3: Full-day cultural & natural hinterland exploration → Early morning visit to Khao Chi Chan (Buddha Mountain) to view the massive golden cliff carving → Morning walk through the tropical grounds and cultural shows at Nong Nooch Tropical Botanical Garden → Afternoon traditional wooden rowboat ride through Pattaya Floating Market → Evening cultural performance at Tiffany’s Show or live music bar hopping in South Pattaya Day 4: Morning trip to Ramayana Water Park or Columbia Pictures Aquaverse for high-adrenaline slides → Afternoon interactive photoshoots at Art in Paradise 3D trick-eye gallery → Sunset view of Pattaya Bay from Pattaya Viewpoint (Khao Phra Tamnak) → Farewell dinner at a cliffside restaurant on Pratamnak Hill Day 5: Breakfast at hotel → Optional morning tour of Monster Aquarium Pattaya or local souvenir shopping at Central Pattaya Mall → Direct private transfer back to BKK/DMK Airport for departure', 4173),
  ('pattaya', 28, 'sample-itinerary-patterns', 'SAMPLE ITINERARY PATTERNS', '1 NIGHT – EXPRESS COASTAL HIGHLIGHTS', NULL, 'Day 1: Morning arrival from Bangkok or airport (~9:00 AM) → Direct taxi or minivan transfer to Pattaya hotel for luggage drop → Late-morning visit to the all-wood Sanctuary of Truth architectural site → Afternoon air-conditioned shopping break & lunch at Terminal 21 Pattaya or Central Pattaya Mall → Sunset viewpoint photo stop at Wat Phra Yai (Big Buddha Temple) on Pratamnak Hill → Late-night seafood feast and stroll through Walking Street or Jomtien Night Market Day 2: Early morning beach walk along Central Pattaya Beach or Wong Amat Beach → Morning ฿30 public ferry run to Koh Larn for a quick 2-hour beach swim (or visit Pattaya Floating Market) → Hotel check-out (~12:00 PM) → Direct private transfer back to Bangkok or airport for afternoon/evening departure', 4174),
  ('pattaya', 29, '7-days-6-nights-thailand-honeymoon-itinerary', '7 Days / 6 Nights Thailand Honeymoon Itinerary', 'Day 1: Arrival & Transit to Phuket', NULL, '', 4175),
  ('pattaya', 29, '7-days-6-nights-thailand-honeymoon-itinerary', '7 Days / 6 Nights Thailand Honeymoon Itinerary', 'Day 2: Phi Phi Island Excursion', NULL, '', 4176),
  ('pattaya', 29, '7-days-6-nights-thailand-honeymoon-itinerary', '7 Days / 6 Nights Thailand Honeymoon Itinerary', 'Day 3: Phuket to Pattaya (via Bangkok)', NULL, '', 4177),
  ('pattaya', 29, '7-days-6-nights-thailand-honeymoon-itinerary', '7 Days / 6 Nights Thailand Honeymoon Itinerary', 'Day 4: Coral Island Tour & Alcazar Cabaret Show', NULL, '', 4178),
  ('pattaya', 29, '7-days-6-nights-thailand-honeymoon-itinerary', '7 Days / 6 Nights Thailand Honeymoon Itinerary', 'Day 5: Pattaya to Bangkok via Safari World & Marine Park', NULL, '', 4179),
  ('pattaya', 29, '7-days-6-nights-thailand-honeymoon-itinerary', '7 Days / 6 Nights Thailand Honeymoon Itinerary', 'Day 6: Bangkok City & Temple Tour + Shopping', NULL, '', 4180),
  ('pattaya', 29, '7-days-6-nights-thailand-honeymoon-itinerary', '7 Days / 6 Nights Thailand Honeymoon Itinerary', 'Day 7: Leisure & Departure', NULL, '', 4181),
  ('pattaya', 30, '7-days-6-nights-family-itinerary-bangkok-phuket-and-pattaya', '7 DAYS 6 NIGHTS FAMILY ITINERARY: BANGKOK, PHUKET & PATTAYA', NULL, NULL, 'Day 1: Arrive Phuket APT, Customs and baggage clearance process at the Airport. Transfer to Phuket Hotel. Checking Hotel and evening free at own. MEALS: NA Day 2: After American Breakfast proceed for fun filled half day excursion to Phi Phi Island in Phuket, followed by lunch, Dinner at local restaurant. MEALS: Breakfast & Lunch Day 3: After American Breakfast proceed to Phuket APT, flight to BKK, after arrival at BKK airport transfer to Pattaya Hotel, overnight stay at Pattaya hotel. MEALS: Breakfast Day 4: After American Breakfast proceed for fun filled half day excursion to Coral Island the picture postcard island of Pattaya, followed by lunch, Check-in at Pattaya hotel, At Evening proceed for Alcazar Show, Dinner at local restaurant. MEALS: Breakfast & Lunch Day 5: Early Break Fast Transfer to Bangkok enroute Safari World & Marine Park (Dolphin Show, Orang Utang Show, Sea Lion Show, Cowboy Show, take selfies at Safari Mini World with Friendly tiny Birds sitting on your head). Overnight at Bangkok hotel. MEALS: Breakfast & Lunch Day 6: American Break Fast at Hotel, set on Bangkok City and Temple Tour with Gems Gallery (Grand Palace, Wat Pho & Wat Arun), Lunch. Evening free for shopping at Siam Paragon / Pratunam, overnight at Bangkok hotel. MEALS: Breakfast & Lunch Day 7: After ABF checkout at 12:00 HRS, time free for last-minute shopping at CentralWorld / MBK Center, and transfer to BKK Airport at Night for boarding flight back home with sweet memories. MEALS: Breakfast', 4182),
  ('pattaya', 31, '7-days-6-nights-luxury-itinerary', '**7 DAYS 6 NIGHTS LUXURY ITINERARY**', NULL, NULL, '**Day 2: Luxury Phi Phi Island Speedboat Excursion** **Day 3: Flight back to Bangkok & Executive Transfer to Pattaya** **Day 4: Private Coral Island Yacht Tour & Alcazar VIP Show** **Day 5: Safari World & Marine Park en route to Bangkok** **Day 6: Bangkok City & Temple Tour with Gems Gallery** **Day 7: Farewell Shopping & Departure Transfer**', 4183),
  ('pattaya', 32, 'travel-agent-insights', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS', 'What inexperienced planners often do wrong', NULL, '', 4184),
  ('pattaya', 32, 'travel-agent-insights', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS', 'What an experienced planner does differently', NULL, '', 4185),
  ('pattaya', 32, 'travel-agent-insights', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS', 'Best planning rule', NULL, '', 4186),
  ('pattaya', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', NULL, NULL, 'IF: `trip_length <= 1 night` THEN: Choose an express 2D1N coastal stay in Central Pattaya or Wong Amat, prioritizing an early morning visit to the Sanctuary of Truth and an evening stroll through Walking Street or Jomtien Night Market. Reason: Short overnights require tight logistics; staying in central or northern coastal hubs keeps highway transit from Bangkok under 2 hours and maximizes beach and temple access. IF: `trip_length == 2 nights` THEN: Book a 3D2N stay in North Pattaya (Wong Amat) or Jomtien, combining iconic sightseeing (Sanctuary of Truth, Big Buddha Temple) with a day trip to Koh Larn (Coral Island) and sunset rooftop drinks at Horizon. Reason: Two full nights allow you to balance cultural heritage and island water sports with oceanfront dining without rushing your itinerary. IF: `trip_length >= 3 nights` THEN: Combine a 3-night coastal stay in Pattaya with a full-day hinterland excursion to Nong Nooch Tropical Botanical Garden, Khao Chi Chan (Buddha Mountain), and Ramayana Water Park or Columbia Pictures Aquaverse. Reason: Three or more nights allow you to explore beyond the central beach strip into expansive botanical gardens, water parks, and vineyard countryside while maintaining your resort base. IF: `trip_type == FIRST_TIME_VISITOR` THEN: Prioritize iconic landmarks including the Sanctuary of Truth, Koh Larn (Coral Island) speedboat trip, Wat Phra Yai (Big Buddha Temple), Pattaya Viewpoint, and an evening cabaret show (Tiffany’s or Alcazar). Reason: These signature coastal and cultural attractions represent the essential highlights and architectural wonders of Pattaya. IF: `trip_type == HONEYMOON` THEN: Book a luxury ocean-view suite or private pool villa in Wong Amat or Na Jomtien (e.g., InterContinental Pattaya or Royal Wing Suites), paired with a private luxury yacht charter from Ocean Marina and cliffside sunset dining. Reason: Quiet coastal enclaves offer romantic privacy, pristine ocean vistas, and exclusive dining away from noisy central nightlife strips. IF: `traveler_type == FAMILY` THEN: Select family-friendly resorts in Na Jomtien, Jomtien, or Wong Amat featuring expansive pools and kids'' clubs, paired with visits to Ramayana Water Park, Underwater World, and Nong Nooch Botanical Garden. Reason: Quiet beach zones avoid adult nightlife strips while providing immediate access to world-class water parks and interactive marine attractions. IF: `traveler_type == LUXURY` THEN: Arrange VIP Airport Fast-Track arrival clearance at BKK/DMK, chauffeured executive transfers (Mercedes S-Class or Toyota Alphard) down Motorway 7, private catamaran charters to outer islands (Koh Pai), and oceanfront fine dining. Reason: Private chauffeured transfers and custom marine charters eliminate airport queues, highway travel stress, and crowded public ferry lines. IF: `traveler_type == BUDGET` THEN: Base along Jomtien Beach or Soi Buakhao, using public ฿10–฿20 songthaews ("baht buses"), ฿30 public ferries to Koh Larn from Bali Hai Pier, and night market street food stalls under ฿100. Reason: These zones offer abundant low-cost guesthouses, cheap seafood night markets, and direct access to affordable shared transport. IF: `traveler_interest == NATURE` THEN: Plan a day trip to Nong Nooch Tropical Botanical Garden, combined with off-road hinterland trails near Mabprachan Reservoir or snorkeling in the pristine waters of Koh Rin and Koh Pai. Reason: Pattaya’s surrounding region features vast botanical collections, protected island reefs, and scenic countryside eco-trails. IF: `traveler_interest == FOOD` THEN: Take evening seafood crawls through the Naklua Lan Pho Seafood Market, Thepprasit Night Market, and Jomtien Night Market, paired with beachfront salt-baked fish (*Pla Pao*) and local Isan specialties. Reason: Pattaya is a major coastal culinary destination famous for ultra-fresh Gulf seafood, spicy papaya salads, charcoal-grilled squid, and night market snacks. IF: `traveler_interest == SHOPPING` THEN: Focus on Terminal 21 Pattaya and Central Pattaya for air-conditioned global retail, alongside Thepprasit Night Market and Pattaya Floating Market for local handicrafts and beachwear. Reason: Pattaya seamlessly combines modern themed oceanfront mega-malls with bustling open-air evening markets. IF: `traveler_type == SENIOR` THEN: Book step-free beachfront resorts in Wong Amat or Jomtien, utilize private air-conditioned cars via Bolt/Grab, schedule early morning visits to Wat Phra Yai, and reserve afternoon spa downtime. Reason: Private chauffeured transport and early morning itineraries prevent heat exhaustion and eliminate long walks on uneven street pavements. IF: `traveler_type == TRANSIT` THEN: Choose a resort near Motorway 7 entry points or North Pattaya, utilizing pre-booked private chauffeured transfers for direct airport access to Suvarnabhumi (BKK) or Don Mueang (DMK). Reason: Proximity to the main highway ensures reliable, traffic-controlled transfers to airport departure gates (~1.5 hours to BKK). IF: `trip_length >= 4 nights` THEN: Multi-center your trip by combining 2 nights in Central Pattaya (shopping/nightlife/Koh Larn) with 2 nights in a quiet Na Jomtien luxury resort or a city extension in Bangkok.', 4187),
  ('pattaya', 34, 'destination-scoring', 'DESTINATION SCORING', NULL, NULL, '| Factor | Score | | --- | --- | | Family | 88 | | Honeymoon | 82 | | Luxury | 88 | | Budget | 92 | | Adventure | 86 | | Culture | 78 | | Food | 90 | | Shopping | 84 | | Nightlife | 98 | | Relaxation | 84 | | Nature | 75 | | Accessibility | 70 | | Senior travelers | 80 | | First-time visitor | 90 | | Photography | 88 |', 4188),
  ('pattaya', 35, 'final-travel-agent-verdict', 'FINAL TRAVEL AGENT VERDICT', NULL, NULL, 'Best for: Beach lovers, luxury resort seekers, nightlife enthusiasts, water sports fans, shoppers, and travelers looking for a high-energy coastal getaway with easy highway access from Bangkok. Best duration: 3–4 days / 3 nights Best season: November–February Best stay: Oceanfront resort in Wong Amat Beach (North Pattaya) for luxury and quiet, central beachfront hotel for nightlife, or Na Jomtien pool villa for families and couples Best transport: Pre-booked private chauffeured car down Motorway 7, private speedboat charters for islands, and ride-hailing apps (Bolt or Grab) for local transit Must-do: Avoid: Biggest advantage: Incredible destination versatility combining world-class resort infrastructure, high-end yachting, vibrant nightlife, and major family attractions just 90 minutes from Suvarnabhumi Airport. Biggest disadvantage: High central beach crowds, variable water clarity along urban shores, and loud adult nightlife strips that require thoughtful zone-based itinerary planning. Overall destination score: **96/100**', 4189),
  ('pattaya', 36, 'data-quality', 'DATA QUALITY', NULL, NULL, 'information_completeness: 94/100 last_updated: 2026-08-26 last_verified: NOT_LIVE_VERIFIED verified_by: TRAVEL_ENGINE_INITIAL_DATASET sources: IMPORTANT: Prices, opening hours, schedules, visa requirements, availability, accessibility and operational conditions must NOT be treated as permanently valid from this document. These must be sourced from structured, refreshable data.', 4190),
  ('phuket', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Cool Season (Peak Season)', NULL, 'months: November–February weather: Warm, comfortable days (24–32°C) with low humidity, minimal rainfall, abundant sunshine, and calm, clear seas. crowd_level: HIGH price_level: HIGH overall_score: 92–98 recommended: true reason: Ideal weather for beach relaxation, diving, island-hopping to the Phi Phi and Similan Islands, and exploring cultural landmarks like Big Buddha without intense heat or monsoons.', 4191),
  ('phuket', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Hot Season', NULL, 'months: March–May weather: Very hot and humid (26–35°C) with intense sunshine and increasing pre-monsoon afternoon showers. crowd_level: MEDIUM → HIGH price_level: MEDIUM overall_score: 74–82 recommended: true reason: High heat and humidity make midday sightseeing tiring, but April brings the nationwide Songkran (Thai New Year) water festival, drawing energetic crowds and offering lower shoulder-season rates.', 4192),
  ('phuket', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Rainy Season (Monsoon Season)', NULL, 'months: June–October weather: Hot and humid (25–31°C) with frequent southwest monsoon downpours, high ocean swells, heavy cloud cover, and peak rainfall in September and October. crowd_level: LOW → MEDIUM price_level: LOW overall_score: 58–66 recommended: false reason: Strong ocean waves often cause red-flag beach warnings and interrupt boat tours to offshore islands, though budget travelers benefit from steep discounts on luxury resorts and optimal surfing conditions on west coast beaches.', 4193),
  ('phuket', 10, 'budget-strategy', 'BUDGET STRATEGY', NULL, NULL, 'Where saving money is not recommended:', 4194),
  ('phuket', 18, 'family-travel', 'FAMILY TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'child_friendly_score: 90 best_ages: Rules:', 4195),
  ('phuket', 19, 'honeymoon-travel', 'HONEYMOON TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'Best areas: Bang Tao & Laguna: best for sprawling 5-star oceanfront resorts, private pool villas, upscale beach club lounging at Catch Beach Club, and romantic sunset walks along a 6-kilometer stretch of white sand. Kamala ("Millionaire''s Mile"): best for ultra-luxury clifftop sanctuaries (such as Amanpuri and Paresa), total privacy, dramatic Andaman Sea views, and world-class fine dining. Nai Thon & Mai Khao (North Phuket): best for untouched, peaceful beach hideaways, secluded luxury resorts, pristine national park coastlines, and complete escape from island crowds. Kata Noi: best for an intimate, high-end beach cove experience anchored by luxury cliffside resorts, crystal-clear swimming waters, and quiet oceanfront dining. Old Phuket Town (Heritage Center): best for romantic boutique stays in restored Sino-Portuguese shop-houses, cozy café hopping, vibrant street art photography, and intimate candlelit dinners. Honeymoon rules: Prefer one signature romantic experience (such as a private luxury yacht charter through the dramatic limestone karsts of Phang Nga Bay or a private oceanfront dinner on a secluded beach cove) paired with relaxed, unhurried downtime. Avoid high-density tourist hubs like central Patong during peak evening hours; instead, reserve private beachfront cabanas, cliffside sunset cocktail spots, or couple''s spa packages during afternoon hours. Investing in seamless private airport transfers and luxury 5-star beachfront resorts with private infinity pool villas or ocean-view balconies matters far more than squeezing in crowded group day tours.', 4196),
  ('phuket', 20, 'luxury-travel', 'LUXURY TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'luxury_score: 94 Best-value luxury pattern Book a private oceanfront pool villa at an iconic 5-star resort enclave such as Amanpuri, Trisara, Banyan Tree Phuket, or Rosewood Phuket in exclusive zones like Bang Tao, Surin, or along "Millionaire''s Mile" in Kamala. Use VIP Airport Fast-Track arrival services at Phuket International Airport (HKT) paired with pre-booked private luxury chauffeurs (such as a VIP Toyota Alphard or luxury SUV) for a smooth direct transfer straight to your resort villa. Charter a private luxury yacht or motor catamaran from Royal Phuket Marina or Yacht Haven Marina for customized cruises through the dramatic karst formations of Phang Nga Bay or offshore to the Racha and Similan Islands, complete with private onboard dining and champagne. Enjoy fine dining at Michelin-starred venues like PRU , reserve private VIP daybeds at high-end beach clubs like Catch Beach Club, play championship golf rounds at RED MOUNTAIN GOLF CLUB, and experience multi-hour holistic wellness rituals at award-winning hotel spa sanctuaries. Luxury rules: Keep the itinerary unhurried and avoid overpacking your schedule with crowded group excursions during peak midday heat. Prefer privacy, personal concierge services, comfort, and exclusivity over visiting noisy tourist centers or crowded party strips. Avoid unmetered street tuk-tuks, crowded public ferry boats, unverified tour operators, and frequent resort changes. For Phuket, a dedicated 5 to 7-night luxury stay provides the ideal balance of island cruising, fine dining, world-class wellness, and pristine beach relaxation.', 4197),
  ('phuket', 21, 'adventure', 'ADVENTURE', NULL, NULL, 'adventure_score: 91 As Thailand’s largest island, Phuket is a high-octane tropical playground that seamlessly bridges extreme ocean thrills with interior island adventures. Framed by the Andaman Sea and dense rainforest-covered mountain peaks, the island offers everything from world-class deep-sea diving and seasonal swell surfing to high-velocity canopy ziplines and coastal air-sports. Adventure seekers can transition effortlessly from navigating sea-cave tunnels and offshore drop-offs to powering heavy-duty quad bikes up muddy jungle ridges to iconic peak viewpoints. Top experiences: Recommended areas: Best for:', 4198),
  ('phuket', 22, 'senior-travel', 'SENIOR TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'senior_suitability: 80 walking_intensity: MEDIUM (can be customized to LOW with private transit and golf carts) Phuket is a very good fit for senior travelers when itineraries emphasize peaceful resort enclaves, accessible beachfront promenades, direct private transfers, and a measured travel pace. The island''s tranquil Andaman views, world-class private healthcare infrastructure, gentle boat tours, and warm hospitality can be thoroughly enjoyed without physical strain by utilizing private chauffeured transport and accessible resort amenities. Rules: Prefer: Avoid:', 4199);
INSERT INTO destination_guidance (place_id, section, topic, section_title, heading, audience, body, position) VALUES
  ('phuket', 23, 'accessibility', 'ACCESSIBILITY', NULL, NULL, 'wheelchair_accessibility: PARTIAL_TO_GOOD depending on attraction and transport public_transport_accessibility: VARIABLE hotel_accessibility: MUST_BE_VERIFIED_PER_HOTEL attraction_accessibility: MUST_BE_VERIFIED_PER_ATTRACTION Rule: Never infer accessibility from destination-level accessibility. Each hotel and attraction must carry its own accessibility data.', 4200),
  ('phuket', 24, 'food', 'FOOD', NULL, NULL, 'food_score: 95 Phuket is a UNESCO-designated City of Gastronomy blending fiery Southern Thai spice with rich Peranakan Baba-Thai heritage and fresh Andaman seafood. Culinary experiences range from heritage shophouses serving century-old Chinese-Thai recipes to bustling beachside night markets and world-class Michelin-starred fine dining. Food experiences: Best for: Recommended areas:', 4201),
  ('phuket', 25, 'shopping', 'SHOPPING', NULL, NULL, 'shopping_score: 88 Phuket offers a dynamic shopping landscape that seamlessly blends air-conditioned mega-malls, upscale lifestyle avenues, vibrant weekend night markets, and charming historic heritage streets. Whether searching for high-end luxury brands, bespoke tailored suits, authentic Southern Thai spices, or unique handmade souvenirs, the island provides rich options from beachside strips to inland hubs. Best buys: Prefer: Avoid: Best for:', 4202),
  ('phuket', 26, 'nightlife', 'NIGHTLIFE', NULL, NULL, 'nightlife_level: 96 Phuket offers one of Asia’s most dynamic and diverse nightlife landscapes. When the sun goes down, the island shifts seamlessly from world-class sunset beach clubs and high-altitude rooftop lounges to neon-lit pedestrian party streets, mega-nightclubs, and chill night market bars. Whether seeking high-energy neon mayhem or sophisticated coastal lounge vibes, Phuket covers the full spectrum. Best for: Prefer: Avoid: Best evening areas:', 4203),
  ('phuket', 28, 'sample-itinerary-patterns', 'SAMPLE ITINERARY PATTERNS', '2 NIGHTS – CLASSIC PHUKET ESSENTIALS', NULL, 'Day 1: Arrival at Phuket International Airport (HKT) → Pre-booked private transfer to hotel base in Patong, Kata, or Karon → Afternoon stroll along the beach promenade and relaxation by the ocean → Sunset photo stop and panoramic views from Karon Viewpoint or Windmill Viewpoint → Evening exploration of Old Phuket Town or Bangla Road nightlife → Dinner at a local Southern Thai or fresh seafood eatery Day 2: Early morning full-day speedboat excursion to the Phi Phi Islands (Maya Bay, Pileh Lagoon, and Viking Cave) → Morning swimming, snorkeling, and pristine white-sand beach relaxation → Buffet lunch on Phi Phi Don Island → Return to main island by late afternoon for hotel pool downtime → Evening visit to Wat Chalong temple complex or Phuket Big Buddha on Nakkerd Hill → Late-night street food crawl at Chillva Market or Naka Weekend Market Day 3: Morning guided heritage walking tour of Old Phuket Town along Thalang Road and Soi Romanee → Souvenir shopping, cafe-hopping, and coconut ice cream break in historic shophouses → Direct private transfer back to Phuket International Airport (HKT) for flight departure', 4204),
  ('phuket', 28, 'sample-itinerary-patterns', 'SAMPLE ITINERARY PATTERNS', '3 NIGHTS – COASTAL LUXURY, ISLANDS & RESORT RELAXATION', 'luxury', 'Day 1: Arrival via Phuket International Airport (HKT) → VIP Fast-Track arrival & private luxury chauffeur transfer to a Bang Tao, Surin, or Kamala oceanfront resort → Check-in to a luxury ocean-view balcony suite or private pool villa → Afternoon relaxation by the infinity pool or private beachfront massage → Romantic oceanfront sunset dinner at a stylish beach club venue (e.g., Catch Beach Club or Café del Mar) Day 2: Early morning private guided tour of the Phuket Big Buddha and Wat Chalong → Lunch at a Michelin Bib Gourmand Southern Thai restaurant in Old Phuket Town → Afternoon multi-hour luxury spa ritual at an elite resort spa (e.g., Banyan Tree Spa or Oasis Spa) → Sunset drinks and tapas at an exclusive 360-degree viewpoint lounge (e.g., Baba Nest) → Multi-course fine-dining experience at PRU or an oceanfront cliffside venue Day 3: Full-day private luxury yacht or motor catamaran charter from Royal Phuket Marina → Cruise through the dramatic limestone karsts of Phang Nga Bay and James Bond Island with private sea kayaking and champagne on board → Return to marina by late afternoon → Sunset photo stop at Promthep Cape → Farewell dinner and evening drinks overlooking the Andaman coast Day 4: Breakfast overlooking the ocean → Leisurely morning beach walk along Bang Tao Beach → Private chauffeur transfer back to Phuket International Airport (HKT) for departure', 4205),
  ('phuket', 28, 'sample-itinerary-patterns', 'SAMPLE ITINERARY PATTERNS', '4 NIGHTS – ULTIMATE ADVENTURE, CULTURE & THEME PARKS', 'adventure', 'Day 1: Arrival in Phuket & transfer to hotel base in Kata, Karon, or Patong → Afternoon walk along Kata Beach promenade → Evening visit to Central Phuket (Festival & Floresta) for food court dining and shopping → Casual beachfront drinks along Patong or Kata Beach Day 2: Full-day island adventure & high-energy marine activities → Speedboat transfer to Racha and Coral Islands (Koh Racha & Koh Hey) → Morning parasailing, sea walking, or scuba diving offshore → Beachside seafood lunch on Coral Island → Return to main island for late-afternoon relaxation → Evening street food crawl through Sunday Walking Street Market (Lard Yai) or Malin Plaza sampling *Moo Hong* and mango sticky rice Day 3: Full-day cultural & natural hinterland exploration → Early morning ethical elephant feeding and interaction experience at Phuket Elephant Sanctuary → Morning rainforest canopy ziplining and skywalk at Hanuman World → Afternoon tour of the Thai Hua Museum and historic Sino-Portuguese shophouses in Old Phuket Town → Evening cultural performance and theatrical show at Phuket FantaSea or Carnival Magic Day 4: Morning trip to Andamanda Water Park or Splash Jungle Water Park for high-adrenaline slides → Afternoon interactive photoshoots at Museum of Natural Illusions (Trickeye Museum) → Sunset view over the Andaman Sea from Windmill Viewpoint or Promthep Cape → Farewell fresh seafood feast at Rawai Seafood Market Day 5: Breakfast at hotel → Optional morning tour of Phuket Aquarium or local souvenir shopping at Boat Avenue → Direct private transfer back to HKT Airport for departure', 4206),
  ('phuket', 28, 'sample-itinerary-patterns', 'SAMPLE ITINERARY PATTERNS', '1 NIGHT – EXPRESS COASTAL HIGHLIGHTS', NULL, 'Day 1: Morning arrival at Phuket International Airport (HKT) (~9:00 AM) → Direct taxi or minivan transfer to hotel for luggage drop → Late-morning heritage walk through Old Phuket Town for street art and Sino-Portuguese architecture → Afternoon air-conditioned shopping break & lunch at Central Phuket Mall → Sunset viewpoint photo stop at the Big Buddha atop Nakkerd Hill or Promthep Cape → Late-night seafood feast and stroll through Bangla Road or Chillva Night Market Day 2: Early morning beach walk along Patong Beach, Kata Beach, or Bang Tao Beach → Morning longtail boat run to Coral Island for a quick 2-hour beach swim (or visit Wat Chalong) → Hotel check-out (~12:00 PM) → Direct private transfer back to HKT Airport for afternoon/evening departure', 4207),
  ('phuket', 29, '7-days-6-nights-thailand-honeymoon-itinerary', '7 Days / 6 Nights Thailand Honeymoon Itinerary', 'Day 1: Arrival & Transit to Phuket', NULL, '', 4208),
  ('phuket', 29, '7-days-6-nights-thailand-honeymoon-itinerary', '7 Days / 6 Nights Thailand Honeymoon Itinerary', 'Day 2: Phi Phi Island Excursion', NULL, '', 4209),
  ('phuket', 29, '7-days-6-nights-thailand-honeymoon-itinerary', '7 Days / 6 Nights Thailand Honeymoon Itinerary', 'Day 3: Phuket to Pattaya (via Bangkok)', NULL, '', 4210),
  ('phuket', 29, '7-days-6-nights-thailand-honeymoon-itinerary', '7 Days / 6 Nights Thailand Honeymoon Itinerary', 'Day 4: Coral Island Tour & Alcazar Cabaret Show', NULL, '', 4211),
  ('phuket', 29, '7-days-6-nights-thailand-honeymoon-itinerary', '7 Days / 6 Nights Thailand Honeymoon Itinerary', 'Day 5: Pattaya to Bangkok via Safari World & Marine Park', NULL, '', 4212),
  ('phuket', 29, '7-days-6-nights-thailand-honeymoon-itinerary', '7 Days / 6 Nights Thailand Honeymoon Itinerary', 'Day 6: Bangkok City & Temple Tour + Shopping', NULL, '', 4213),
  ('phuket', 29, '7-days-6-nights-thailand-honeymoon-itinerary', '7 Days / 6 Nights Thailand Honeymoon Itinerary', 'Day 7: Leisure & Departure', NULL, '', 4214),
  ('phuket', 30, '7-days-6-nights-family-itinerary-bangkok-phuket-and-pattaya', '7 DAYS 6 NIGHTS FAMILY ITINERARY: BANGKOK, PHUKET & PATTAYA', NULL, NULL, 'Day 1: Arrive Phuket APT, Customs and baggage clearance process at the Airport. Transfer to Phuket Hotel. Checking Hotel and evening free at own. MEALS: NA Day 2: After American Breakfast proceed for fun filled half day excursion to Phi Phi Island in Phuket, followed by lunch, Dinner at local restaurant. MEALS: Breakfast & Lunch Day 3: After American Breakfast proceed to Phuket APT, flight to BKK, after arrival at BKK airport transfer to Pattaya Hotel, overnight stay at Pattaya hotel. MEALS: Breakfast Day 4: After American Breakfast proceed for fun filled half day excursion to Coral Island the picture postcard island of Pattaya, followed by lunch, Check-in at Pattaya hotel, At Evening proceed for Alcazar Show, Dinner at local restaurant. MEALS: Breakfast & Lunch Day 5: Early Break Fast Transfer to Bangkok enroute Safari World & Marine Park (Dolphin Show, Orang Utang Show, Sea Lion Show, Cowboy Show, take selfies at Safari Mini World with Friendly tiny Birds sitting on your head). Overnight at Bangkok hotel. MEALS: Breakfast & Lunch Day 6: American Break Fast at Hotel, set on Bangkok City and Temple Tour with Gems Gallery (Grand Palace, Wat Pho & Wat Arun), Lunch. Evening free for shopping at Siam Paragon / Pratunam, overnight at Bangkok hotel. MEALS: Breakfast & Lunch Day 7: After ABF checkout at 12:00 HRS, time free for last-minute shopping at CentralWorld / MBK Center, and transfer to BKK Airport at Night for boarding flight back home with sweet memories. MEALS: Breakfast', 4215),
  ('phuket', 31, '7-days-6-nights-luxury-itinerary', '**7 DAYS 6 NIGHTS LUXURY ITINERARY**', NULL, NULL, '**Day 2: Luxury Phi Phi Island Speedboat Excursion** **Day 3: Flight back to Bangkok & Executive Transfer to Pattaya** **Day 4: Private Coral Island Yacht Tour & Alcazar VIP Show** **Day 5: Safari World & Marine Park en route to Bangkok** **Day 6: Bangkok City & Temple Tour with Gems Gallery** **Day 7: Farewell Shopping & Departure Transfer**', 4216),
  ('phuket', 32, 'travel-agent-insights', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS', 'What inexperienced planners often do wrong', NULL, '', 4217),
  ('phuket', 32, 'travel-agent-insights', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS', 'What an experienced planner does differently', NULL, '', 4218),
  ('phuket', 32, 'travel-agent-insights', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS', 'Best planning rule', NULL, '', 4219),
  ('phuket', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', NULL, NULL, 'IF: `trip_length <= 1 night` THEN: Choose an express 2D1N coastal stay in Patong or Kata Beach, prioritizing an early morning heritage walk in Old Phuket Town and a sunset visit to Promthep Cape or the Big Buddha. Reason: Short overnights require tight logistics; staying in central west-coast hubs keeps airport transit efficient and maximizes access to top cultural landmarks and beach views. IF: `trip_length == 2 nights` THEN: Book a 3D2N stay in Patong, Kata, or Karon, combining iconic cultural heritage (Big Buddha, Wat Chalong) with a full-day speedboat excursion to the Phi Phi Islands or Coral Island. Reason: Two full nights allow you to balance historic island sights and offshore island hopping with oceanfront dining without rushing your itinerary. IF: `trip_length >= 3 nights` THEN: Combine a 3-night coastal stay in Phuket with a full-day hinterland excursion to the Phuket Elephant Sanctuary, Hanuman World ziplining, and a day trip to Phang Nga Bay or James Bond Island. Reason: Three or more nights allow you to explore beyond the main beach strip into lush rainforest hinterlands, ethical wildlife reserves, and dramatic limestone sea caves while keeping your resort base. IF: `trip_type == FIRST_TIME_VISITOR` THEN: Prioritize iconic landmarks including the Phuket Big Buddha, Wat Chalong, Old Phuket Town Sino-Portuguese architecture, a Phi Phi Islands speedboat tour, Promthep Cape sunset, and a cultural show (Phuket FantaSea or Carnival Magic). Reason: These signature coastal, cultural, and island highlights represent the essential attractions and historical identity of Phuket. IF: `trip_type == HONEYMOON` THEN: Book a luxury ocean-view suite or private pool villa in Bang Tao, Surin, or Kamala (e.g., Banyan Tree Phuket, Amanpuri, or Keemala), paired with a private motor yacht charter through Phang Nga Bay and cliffside sunset cocktails at Baba Nest. Reason: Quiet upscale enclaves offer high-end privacy, breathtaking Andaman sunsets, and world-class fine dining away from commercial party corridors. IF: `traveler_type == FAMILY` THEN: Select family-friendly resorts in Laguna/Bang Tao, Kata, or Karon featuring expansive pool complexes and kids'' clubs, paired with visits to Andamanda Water Park, Phuket Elephant Sanctuary, and Splash Jungle. Reason: Tranquil beach zones steer clear of adult nightlife strips while providing fast access to top-tier water parks, calm swimming waters, and educational nature reserves. IF: `traveler_type == LUXURY` THEN: Arrange VIP Airport Fast-Track arrival clearance at HKT, chauffeured luxury executive transfers (Toyota Alphard or Mercedes S-Class), private catamaran charters to outer islands (Racha or Similan), and fine-dining experiences at Michelin-recognized venues. Reason: Private chauffeured transit and custom yacht charters eliminate airport arrival queues, local taxi negotiation stress, and crowded public ferry terminals. IF: `traveler_type == BUDGET` THEN: Base along Kata, Karon, or Old Phuket Town, utilizing local Smart Buses or songthaews (฿40–฿100), longtail boat runs to Coral Island, and night market street food stalls under ฿100. Reason: These areas offer budget guesthouses, affordable local night markets, and cheap public coastal transport links across the island. IF: `traveler_interest == NATURE` THEN: Plan an ethical visit to the Phuket Elephant Sanctuary, combined with jungle trekking in Khao Phra Thaeo National Park, snorkeling in the Similan Islands, or kayaking through the mangroves of Phang Nga Bay. Reason: Phuket’s surrounding marine and mainland ecosystems feature dense virgin rainforests, protected coral reefs, and ethical wildlife conservation zones. IF: `traveler_interest == FOOD` THEN: Take evening street food crawls through the Sunday Walking Street Market (Lard Yai) and Naka Weekend Market, paired with authentic Southern Thai curry (*Gaeng Som*), slow-braised pork belly (*Moo Hong*), and fresh seafood at Rawai Seafood Market. Reason: Phuket is a UNESCO City of Gastronomy celebrated for its fiery Southern Thai cuisine, Hokkien Chinese culinary heritage, and ultra-fresh Andaman seafood. IF: `traveler_interest == SHOPPING` THEN: Focus on Central Phuket (Festival & Floresta) for air-conditioned high-end global retail, alongside Lard Yai Sunday Market and Chillva Market for handmade crafts, local art, and trendy beachwear. Reason: Phuket offers a versatile shopping environment blending luxury multi-concept mega-malls with vibrant night markets set against historic architecture. IF: `traveler_type == SENIOR` THEN: Book step-free beachfront resorts in Bang Tao, Kamala, or Karon, utilize private air-conditioned cars via Grab/Bolt or private drivers, schedule early morning visits to Wat Chalong, and reserve afternoon spa downtime. Reason: Dedicated chauffeured transport and early morning scheduling avoid peak midday heat, steep hill climbs, and long walks on crowded pavements. IF: `traveler_type == TRANSIT` THEN: Choose a resort near Nai Yang or Mai Khao Beach, utilizing pre-booked private chauffeured transfers for quick 10-to-15-minute access to Phuket International Airport (HKT). Reason: Proximity to the northern beach strip ensures zero risk of coastal traffic jams and easy access to airport departure terminals. IF: `trip_length >= 4 nights` THEN: Multi-center your stay by combining 2 nights in a vibrant beach hub like Kata or Patong (for island tours, dining, and shopping) with 2 nights in a quiet Bang Tao pool villa or a nature extension in Khao Sok National Park.', 4220),
  ('phuket', 34, 'destination-scoring', 'DESTINATION SCORING', NULL, NULL, '| Factor | Score | | --- | --- | | Family | 90 | | Honeymoon | 92 | | Luxury | 94 | | Budget | 88 | | Adventure | 90 | | Culture | 80 | | Food | 94 | | Shopping | 86 | | Nightlife | 96 | | Relaxation | 90 | | Nature | 92 | | Accessibility | 68 | | Senior travelers | 82 | | First-time visitor | 94 | | Photography | 94 |', 4221),
  ('phuket', 35, 'final-travel-agent-verdict', 'FINAL TRAVEL AGENT VERDICT', NULL, NULL, 'Best for: Island lovers, luxury resort seekers, beach enthusiasts, adventure travelers, culture seekers, and travelers looking for a premier tropical island destination with world-class marine access, fine dining, and vibrant culture. Best duration: 4–5 days / 4 nights Best season: November–April Best stay: Oceanfront pool villa in Bang Tao or Surin for luxury and tranquility, Kata or Karon beachfront resort for active families, or Central Patong for high-energy nightlife access Best transport: Pre-booked private chauffeured VIP airport transfer, private yacht/catamaran charters for island hopping, and ride-hailing apps (Grab or Bolt) for short intra-island trips Must-do: Avoid: Biggest advantage: Unmatched destination diversity combining international luxury resorts, pristine Andaman offshore islands, rich Sino-Portuguese cultural heritage, UNESCO-recognized gastronomy, and top-tier family infrastructure on a single island. Biggest disadvantage: Significant coastal traffic congestion during peak hours, higher local transit costs compared to mainland Thailand, and heavy tourist density in central beach hubs. Overall destination score: **97/100**', 4222),
  ('phuket', 36, 'data-quality', 'DATA QUALITY', NULL, NULL, 'information_completeness: 93/100 last_updated: 2026-08-26 last_verified: NOT_LIVE_VERIFIED verified_by: TRAVEL_ENGINE_INITIAL_DATASET sources: IMPORTANT: Prices, opening hours, schedules, visa requirements, availability, accessibility and operational conditions must NOT be treated as permanently valid from this document. These must be sourced from structured, refreshable data.', 4223),
  ('krabi', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Cool Season (Peak Season)', NULL, 'months: November–February weather: Warm, pleasant days (24–32°C) with low humidity, minimal rainfall, abundant sunshine, and calm, crystal-clear seas. crowd_level: HIGH price_level: HIGH overall_score: 92–98 recommended: true reason: Perfect conditions for island-hopping to the 4 Islands and Phi Phi, world-class rock climbing at Railay with excellent grip, and exploring Tiger Cave Temple without intense heat.', 4224),
  ('krabi', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Hot Season', NULL, 'months: March–May weather: Very hot and humid (26–36°C) with intense sun, rising mugginess, and afternoon pre-monsoon showers starting in late April. crowd_level: MEDIUM → HIGH price_level: MEDIUM overall_score: 72–80 recommended: true reason: Midday heat makes climbing and jungle hiking challenging, but April features vibrant Songkran (Thai New Year) water festival celebrations, along with solid resort discounts before the heavy monsoon arrives.', 4225),
  ('krabi', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Rainy Season (Monsoon Season)', NULL, 'months: June–October weather: Warm and humid (25–31°C) with frequent southwest monsoon downpours, high ocean swells, heavy cloud cover, and peak rainfall in September and October. crowd_level: LOW → MEDIUM price_level: LOW overall_score: 56–64 recommended: false reason: Choppy seas frequently lead to cancelled boat tours and red-flag beach warnings, though budget travelers benefit from steep resort discounts and lush, green jungle scenery around inland waterfalls and hot springs.', 4226),
  ('krabi', 10, 'budget-strategy', 'BUDGET STRATEGY', NULL, NULL, 'Where saving money is not recommended:', 4227),
  ('krabi', 18, 'family-travel', 'FAMILY TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'child_friendly_score: 90 best_ages: Rules:', 4228),
  ('krabi', 19, 'honeymoon-travel', 'HONEYMOON TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'Best areas: Tubkaak Beach: best for ultra-exclusive, secluded luxury sanctuaries (such as Phulay Bay, a Ritz-Carlton Reserve and The Tubkaak Resort), complete privacy, pristine mountain-meets-ocean views, and intimate sunset dining directly facing the Hong Islands. Railay Peninsula & Phra Nang: best for dramatic, fairytale-like limestone cliff scenery, romantic beachfront dining inside ancient limestone caves (The Grotto at Rayavadee), secluded luxury pavilions, and car-free, island-like tranquility. Klong Muang Beach: best for peaceful, high-end 5-star beachfront resort stays (such as Dusit Thani Krabi and Banyan Tree Krabi), uncrowded soft sand stretches, and private clifftop pool villas overlooking calm sea horizons. Hong Islands Archipelago (Offshore Sanctuary): best for private longtail or speedboat day escapes to hidden emerald lagoons, crystal-clear snorkeling, and intimate beach picnic setups far removed from tourist crowds. Pai Plong Bay: best for total romantic isolation at Centara Grand Beach Resort, set within a private, cliff-ringed bay accessible exclusively by boat or scenic cliffside wooden walking trail. Honeymoon rules: Prefer one signature romantic experience (such as a private longtail boat charter to the Hong Islands Lagoon or an intimate candlelight seafood dinner inside Phra Nang Cave) paired with relaxed, unhurried resort downtime. Avoid high-density tourist piers and central Ao Nang beachfront during peak mid-day hours (10:00 AM–3:00 PM); instead, enjoy private pool villa seclusion or schedule afternoon couple''s spa treatments. Investing in seamless private airport van-and-boat transfers and high-end 5-star beachfront resorts with private infinity pools or direct beach access matters far more than squeezing in crowded group island excursions.', 4229),
  ('krabi', 20, 'luxury-travel', 'LUXURY TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'luxury_score: 94 Best-value luxury pattern Book a private oceanfront pool villa or pavilion at an iconic 5-star sanctuary such as Phulay Bay (a Ritz-Carlton Reserve), Rayavadee, Banyan Tree Krabi, or The Tubkaak Boutique Resort in exclusive coastal enclaves like Tubkaak Beach, Klong Muang, or Railay Peninsula. Arrange resort-managed private VIP airport transfers from Krabi International Airport (KBV) featuring direct executive SUV chauffeurs combined with private longtail or luxury boat transfers to reach secluded beach sanctuaries. Charter a private luxury yacht, catamarans, or traditional wooden longtail boat for customized private island-hopping cruises to the Hong Islands archipelago, Phi Phi Islands, or Maya Bay, complete with private onboard catering, champagne, and secluded beach picnics. Savor exquisite fine dining at signature oceanfront venues like Lae Lay Pavilion or The Grotto inside Phra Nang Cave, experience multi-hour hydrotherapy and traditional Thai massage rituals at award-winning spa sanctuaries like Wareerak Hot Springs, and enjoy private helicopter tours over Krabi''s dramatic limestone karst coastlines. Luxury rules: Keep the itinerary unhurried and avoid overpacking your schedule with crowded group excursions during peak midday heat. Prefer privacy, personal concierge services, comfort, and exclusivity over visiting noisy tourist centers or crowded party strips. Avoid unmetered street tuk-tuks, crowded public ferry boats, unverified tour operators, and frequent resort changes. For Krabi, a dedicated 5 to 7-night luxury stay provides the ideal balance of island cruising, fine dining, world-class wellness, and pristine beach relaxation.', 4230),
  ('krabi', 21, 'adventure', 'ADVENTURE', NULL, NULL, 'adventure_score: 96 Krabi is Southeast Asia’s ultimate natural adventure playground, world-famous for its dramatic limestone karst topography, turquoise ocean basins, and dense jungle interior. Centered around the iconic vertical cliffs of Railay Peninsula and the marine sanctuaries of the Andaman Sea, the province offers an incredible mix of high-altitude rock climbing, coastal sea kayaking, deep-water diving, and intense jungle ridge trekking. Adventure seekers can seamlessly transition from scaling towering sheer cliff faces above the ocean to paddling through hidden mangrove canyons and climbing over a thousand steps to mountain peak shrines. Top experiences: Recommended areas: Best for:', 4231),
  ('krabi', 22, 'senior-travel', 'SENIOR TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'senior_suitability: 82 walking_intensity: MEDIUM (can be customized to LOW with private transit, flat resorts, and boat jetty departures) Krabi is a great fit for senior travelers when itineraries prioritize quiet resort enclaves, flat beachfront promenades, private chauffeured transfers, and an unhurried travel pace. While Krabi is famous for its dramatic vertical limestone karsts, mature travelers can easily enjoy stunning ocean views, gentle marine cruises, rich local cuisine, and soothing thermal hot springs without physical exertion by choosing accessible accommodations and structured transit options. Rules: Prefer: Avoid:', 4232),
  ('krabi', 23, 'accessibility', 'ACCESSIBILITY', NULL, NULL, 'wheelchair_accessibility: PARTIAL_TO_GOOD depending on attraction and transport public_transport_accessibility: VARIABLE hotel_accessibility: MUST_BE_VERIFIED_PER_HOTEL attraction_accessibility: MUST_BE_VERIFIED_PER_ATTRACTION Rule: Never infer accessibility from destination-level accessibility. Each hotel and attraction must carry its own accessibility data.', 4233),
  ('krabi', 24, 'food', 'FOOD', NULL, NULL, 'food_score: 93 Krabi offers a vibrant culinary blend of intense Southern Thai spices, ultra-fresh Andaman seafood, and rich Thai-Muslim heritage. Food options span roadside night markets and riverside seafood spots to cliffside sunset dining and luxury beachfront retreats set against dramatic limestone karsts. Food experiences: Best for: Recommended areas:', 4234),
  ('krabi', 25, 'shopping', 'SHOPPING', NULL, NULL, 'shopping_score: 78 Krabi offers a relaxed, laid-back shopping landscape focused primarily on vibrant weekend night markets, coastal walking streets, and local handicraft bazaars rather than mega luxury malls. While lacking the massive high-end retail options of Bangkok or Phuket, it excels in authentic Southern Thai textiles, handcrafted wooden items, beachwear, and affordable souvenirs scattered across Krabi Town and Ao Nang. Best buys: Prefer: Avoid: Best for:', 4235),
  ('krabi', 26, 'nightlife', 'NIGHTLIFE', NULL, NULL, 'nightlife_level: 80 Krabi’s nightlife delivers a distinctly laid-back, tropical, and bohemian vibe compared to neighboring party hubs. Instead of massive multi-level megaclubs, the evening scene centers on scenic cliffside sunset lounges, casual open-air beach bars with nightly fire shows, lively reggae spots, and bustling local night markets tucked beneath dramatic limestone karsts. Best for: Prefer: Avoid: Best evening areas:', 4236),
  ('krabi', 28, 'sample-itinerary-patterns', 'SAMPLE ITINERARY PATTERNS', '2 NIGHTS – CLASSIC KRABI ESSENTIALS', NULL, 'Day 1: Arrival at Krabi International Airport (KBV) → Pre-booked private transfer or shared shuttle to hotel base in Ao Nang Beach → Afternoon longtail boat run (~15 mins) from Ao Nang Pier to Railay West Beach → Chill on the sand and scenic walk along the limestone pathways to Phra Nang Cave Beach → Golden hour sunset photos against the iconic karst backdrop at Railay West → Return longtail boat to Ao Nang for evening street food and shopping at Ao Nang Landmark Night Market Day 2: Early morning 4 Islands Tour via speedboat or private longtail (Koh Poda, Chicken Island, Koh Tup & Thale Waek sandbar) → Swim, snorkel turquoise waters, and walk across the natural ocean sandbar connecting the islands → Beachside picnic or local buffet lunch on Koh Poda → Return to Ao Nang by mid-afternoon for hotel pool downtime or an authentic Thai massage → Golden hour drinks at a hilltop viewpoint lounge overlooking Ao Nang Bay → Seafood dinner along the Ao Nang oceanfront promenade and late-night fire show on the beach Day 3: Early morning taxi to Wat Tham Suea (Tiger Cave Temple) → Challenge the 1,260-step summit climb for panoramic 360-degree views over Krabi’s karst landscape → Return to hotel for check-out (~12:00 PM) → Souvenir stop at Krabi Town or quick coffee break along the Krabi River promenade by the Mudshell Crab Statue → Direct private transfer back to KBV Airport for flight departure', 4237),
  ('krabi', 28, 'sample-itinerary-patterns', 'SAMPLE ITINERARY PATTERNS', '3 NIGHTS – COASTAL LUXURY, KARST LAGOONS & WELLNESS', 'luxury', 'Day 1: Arrival via Krabi International Airport (KBV) → VIP private chauffeur transfer to an oceanfront luxury resort in Tubkaek Beach or Klong Muang → Check-in to a luxury beachfront pool villa or ocean-view suite → Afternoon relaxation by the infinity pool or private beach lounge with views of the Hong Islands → Romantic sunset cocktail hour and seafood dinner right on the sand at Tubkaek Beach Day 2: Full-day private luxury speed-catamaran charter to Hong Islands (Koh Hong, Hong Lagoon & Koh Lao Lading) → Cruise into the hidden interior emerald lagoon through a narrow limestone canyon entrance → Climb the 360-degree panoramic glass viewpoint peak on Koh Hong for panoramic island views → Gourmet catered beach picnic and private snorkeling off secluded coves → Return to resort by late afternoon for a multi-hour holistic spa treatment → Fine-dining Thai dinner at an elevated cliffside restaurant overlooking the Andaman Sea Day 3: Early morning guided nature trek up Dragon Crest Mountain (Khao Ngon Nak) for panoramic coastal views → Mid-day wellness immersion at Wareerak Hot Spring Retreat—mineral bath soaking, herbal scrubs, and hydrotherapy in natural jungle pools → Afternoon return to resort for downtime → Sunset lounge drinks, tapas, and live acoustic music at a chic beach club Day 4: Leisurely breakfast overlooking the ocean → Morning beach stroll or private paddleboarding session on calm Tubkaek waters → Private chauffeur transfer back to Krabi International Airport (KBV) for departure', 4238),
  ('krabi', 28, 'sample-itinerary-patterns', 'SAMPLE ITINERARY PATTERNS', '4 NIGHTS – ULTIMATE JUNGLE ADVENTURE, CAVES & ARCHIPELAGO HOPPING', 'adventure', 'Day 1: Arrival in Krabi & transfer to hotel base in Ao Nang or Railay → Check-in and afternoon walk through the Monkey Trail pathway from Ao Nang to Pai Plong Bay → Casual beachfront lunch and ocean swim → Evening stroll around Ao Nang Center Point for drinks and casual dining Day 2: Full-day Phi Phi Islands & Maya Bay marine expedition → Early morning speedboat departure to beat the main crowds at Maya Bay (from *The Beach*) → Swim and snorkel at Pileh Lagoon, view Viking Cave, and explore Bamboo Island → Buffet lunch on Phi Phi Don Island → Return to Krabi mainland by late afternoon → Night market street food crawl at Ao Nang Night Market sampling Southern Thai massaman curry and coconut pancakes Day 3: Full-day inland jungle, thermal spring & cultural explorer → Morning dip in the natural turquoise geothermal waters of the Emerald Pool (Sa Morakot) inside Khao Phra-Bang Khram Nature Reserve → Walk the rainforest boardwalk to the vibrant Blue Lagoon → Soak in the cascading natural thermal water jacuzzi basins at Krabi Hot Springs (Namtok Ron) → Late afternoon visit to Wat Tham Suea (Tiger Cave Temple) for sunset over the limestone peaks → Night market feast at Krabi Town Weekend Walking Street Market (if Fri–Sun) or Chao Fah Night Market Day 4: Morning guided kayaking expedition through the dramatic karst canyons and mangrove tunnels of Ao Thalane → Afternoon rock climbing session on the world-famous limestone cliffs of Railay East or Tonsai Beach → Sunset view and cave exploration at Phra Nang Beach → Farewell dinner at a cave restaurant or beachfront grill Day 5: Breakfast at hotel → Morning souvenir shopping for local cashew nuts and handcrafted goods in Krabi Town → Direct private transfer back to KBV Airport for departure', 4239),
  ('krabi', 28, 'sample-itinerary-patterns', 'SAMPLE ITINERARY PATTERNS', '1 NIGHT – EXPRESS KARST & COAST HIGHLIGHTS', NULL, 'Day 1: Morning arrival at Krabi International Airport (KBV) (~8:30 AM) → Direct taxi/minivan transfer to Ao Nang Pier (~30 mins) → Morning longtail boat hop over to Railay Beach (Phra Nang Cave Beach, rock climbing walls, and Railay West) → Beachside lunch at Railay Walking Street → Mid-afternoon longtail boat back to Ao Nang for check-in and luggage drop → Sunset photo stop and drinks along Ao Nang Beach → Evening dinner and fire show at an open-air beachfront lounge Day 2: Early morning taxi run to Wat Tham Suea (Tiger Cave Temple) for a morning summit climb before the heat → Quick hotel check-out (~11:30 AM) → Quick street food lunch in Krabi Town (Southern Thai rice noodles or roti) → Direct private transfer back to KBV Airport for afternoon/evening departure', 4240),
  ('krabi', 29, '7-days-6-nights-thailand-honeymoon-itinerary', '7 Days / 6 Nights Thailand Honeymoon Itinerary', 'Day 1: Arrival & Transit to Phuket', NULL, '', 4241),
  ('krabi', 29, '7-days-6-nights-thailand-honeymoon-itinerary', '7 Days / 6 Nights Thailand Honeymoon Itinerary', 'Day 2: Phi Phi Island Excursion', NULL, '', 4242),
  ('krabi', 29, '7-days-6-nights-thailand-honeymoon-itinerary', '7 Days / 6 Nights Thailand Honeymoon Itinerary', 'Day 3: Phuket to Pattaya (via Bangkok)', NULL, '', 4243),
  ('krabi', 29, '7-days-6-nights-thailand-honeymoon-itinerary', '7 Days / 6 Nights Thailand Honeymoon Itinerary', 'Day 4: Coral Island Tour & Alcazar Cabaret Show', NULL, '', 4244),
  ('krabi', 29, '7-days-6-nights-thailand-honeymoon-itinerary', '7 Days / 6 Nights Thailand Honeymoon Itinerary', 'Day 5: Pattaya to Bangkok via Safari World & Marine Park', NULL, '', 4245),
  ('krabi', 29, '7-days-6-nights-thailand-honeymoon-itinerary', '7 Days / 6 Nights Thailand Honeymoon Itinerary', 'Day 6: Bangkok City & Temple Tour + Shopping', NULL, '', 4246),
  ('krabi', 29, '7-days-6-nights-thailand-honeymoon-itinerary', '7 Days / 6 Nights Thailand Honeymoon Itinerary', 'Day 7: Leisure & Departure', NULL, '', 4247),
  ('krabi', 30, '7-days-6-nights-family-itinerary-bangkok-phuket-and-pattaya', '7 DAYS 6 NIGHTS FAMILY ITINERARY: BANGKOK, PHUKET & PATTAYA', NULL, NULL, 'Day 1: Arrive Phuket APT, Customs and baggage clearance process at the Airport. Transfer to Phuket Hotel. Checking Hotel and evening free at own. MEALS: NA Day 2: After American Breakfast proceed for fun filled half day excursion to Phi Phi Island in Phuket, followed by lunch, Dinner at local restaurant. MEALS: Breakfast & Lunch Day 3: After American Breakfast proceed to Phuket APT, flight to BKK, after arrival at BKK airport transfer to Pattaya Hotel, overnight stay at Pattaya hotel. MEALS: Breakfast Day 4: After American Breakfast proceed for fun filled half day excursion to Coral Island the picture postcard island of Pattaya, followed by lunch, Check-in at Pattaya hotel, At Evening proceed for Alcazar Show, Dinner at local restaurant. MEALS: Breakfast & Lunch Day 5: Early Break Fast Transfer to Bangkok enroute Safari World & Marine Park (Dolphin Show, Orang Utang Show, Sea Lion Show, Cowboy Show, take selfies at Safari Mini World with Friendly tiny Birds sitting on your head). Overnight at Bangkok hotel. MEALS: Breakfast & Lunch Day 6: American Break Fast at Hotel, set on Bangkok City and Temple Tour with Gems Gallery (Grand Palace, Wat Pho & Wat Arun), Lunch. Evening free for shopping at Siam Paragon / Pratunam, overnight at Bangkok hotel. MEALS: Breakfast & Lunch Day 7: After ABF checkout at 12:00 HRS, time free for last-minute shopping at CentralWorld / MBK Center, and transfer to BKK Airport at Night for boarding flight back home with sweet memories. MEALS: Breakfast', 4248),
  ('krabi', 31, '7-days-6-nights-luxury-itinerary', '**7 DAYS 6 NIGHTS LUXURY ITINERARY**', NULL, NULL, '**Day 2: Luxury Phi Phi Island Speedboat Excursion** **Day 3: Flight back to Bangkok & Executive Transfer to Pattaya** **Day 4: Private Coral Island Yacht Tour & Alcazar VIP Show** **Day 5: Safari World & Marine Park en route to Bangkok** **Day 6: Bangkok City & Temple Tour with Gems Gallery** **Day 7: Farewell Shopping & Departure Transfer**', 4249),
  ('krabi', 32, 'travel-agent-insights', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS', 'What inexperienced planners often do wrong', NULL, '', 4250),
  ('krabi', 32, 'travel-agent-insights', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS', 'What an experienced planner does differently', NULL, '', 4251),
  ('krabi', 32, 'travel-agent-insights', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS', 'Best planning rule', NULL, '', 4252),
  ('krabi', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', NULL, NULL, 'IF: `trip_length <= 1 night` THEN: Choose an express 2D1N coastal stay in Ao Nang Beach, prioritizing an early longtail boat hop to Railay Beach (Phra Nang Cave Beach) and a morning climb up Tiger Cave Temple (Wat Tham Suea). Reason: Short overnights require tight logistics; basing in Ao Nang keeps airport transit simple while giving instant longtail access to Railay''s iconic limestone scenery and top cultural lookouts. IF: `trip_length == 2 nights` THEN: Book a 3D2N stay in Ao Nang or Railay, combining iconic karst landscapes (Phra Nang Beach, Railay West) with a full-day 4 Islands or Hong Islands speedboat excursion and an evening night market tour. Reason: Two full nights let you balance dramatic mainland cliff walks, island hopping across turquoise lagoons, and fresh street food without rushing your transit schedule. IF: `trip_length >= 3 nights` THEN: Combine a coastal stay in Ao Nang or Railay with a full-day jungle inland excursion to the Emerald Pool (Sa Morakot), Krabi Hot Springs, and a mangrove kayaking tour through the canyons of Ao Thalane. Reason: Three or more nights allow you to venture past the coastline into thermal jungle springs, sacred high-altitude summits, and prehistoric mangrove sea caves while maintaining a seaside base. IF: `trip_type == FIRST_TIME_VISITOR` THEN: Prioritize signature highlights including Tiger Cave Temple, Railay West & Phra Nang Cave Beach, an early-morning 4 Islands or Hong Islands boat tour, Ao Nang Night Market, and sunset beachfront drinks. Reason: These quintessential limestone cliffs, sacred summits, emerald lagoons, and night markets showcase the definitive scenery and culture of Krabi. IF: `trip_type == HONEYMOON` THEN: Book a luxury oceanfront villa or suite in Tubkaek Beach or Klong Muang (e.g., Phulay Bay a Ritz-Carlton Reserve, Rayavadee, or Banyan Tree Krabi), paired with a private speed-catamaran charter to Hong Lagoon and sunset dining on the sand. Reason: Serene upscale enclaves offer high-end privacy, dramatic views of the Hong Archipelago, and romantic candlelit beachfront dining far from tourist crowds. IF: `traveler_type == FAMILY` THEN: Select family-friendly resorts along Noppharat Thara or Klong Muang featuring shallow pool complexes and direct beach access, paired with a private longtail boat to 4 Islands, easy kayak trips, and visits to Ao Nang Landmark Night Market. Reason: Calm, shallow beach zones keep kids safe while avoiding steep cliff stairs, keeping transit simple for island excursions and evening meals. IF: `traveler_type == LUXURY` THEN: Arrange VIP Airport Fast-Track arrival clearance at KBV, chauffeured private transfers, private luxury yacht charters to Hong Islands or Phi Phi, and multi-hour hydrotherapy spa treatments at Wareerak Hot Springs. Reason: Private watercraft and dedicated luxury vehicles eliminate waiting in longtail boat queues, crowded pier transfers, and standard group tour schedules. IF: `traveler_type == BUDGET` THEN: Base in Krabi Town or back-street Ao Nang, utilizing shared *songthaews* (฿50–฿100), public longtail boat runs to Railay (฿100–฿150), and street food meals under ฿100 at Chao Fah or Krabi Town Walking Street Market. Reason: Krabi Town offers affordable guesthouses, rich night market food culture, and cheap public transit connecting directly to coastal piers and inland attractions. IF: `traveler_interest == NATURE` THEN: Plan a trek up Dragon Crest Mountain (Khao Ngon Nak), paired with kayaking through Ao Thalane mangrove canyons, swimming in the Emerald Pool, and exploring the sea caves at Ban Bor Thor. Reason: Krabi boasts exceptional biodiversity across virgin rainforests, thermal mineral springs, mangrove ecosystems, and dramatic karst mountain trails. IF: `traveler_interest == FOOD` THEN: Take evening street food crawls through Krabi Town Weekend Walking Street and Ao Nang Landmark Night Market, sampling Southern Thai massaman curry, fresh grilled seafood, *Khao Yam* (rice salad), and crispy Thai rotis. Reason: Krabi is famous for its rich Southern Thai culinary traditions, characterized by aromatic curry pastes, fresh seafood, and lively street market culture. IF: `traveler_interest == ADVENTURE` THEN: Focus on world-class rock climbing on the limestone cliffs of Railay East and Tonsai Beach, deep-water soloing, jungle trekking, and high-intensity kayaking through mangrove canyons. Reason: Krabi''s towering vertical limestone karsts and jungle terrain make it one of the world''s premier destinations for rock climbing and active eco-adventures. IF: `traveler_type == SENIOR` THEN: Book step-free beachfront resorts in Klong Muang or Noppharat Thara, utilize private air-conditioned cars or longtail boats with low-tide boarding platforms, schedule early morning visits, and plan midday resort downtime. Reason: Accessible transport and careful timing avoid steep climbs like Tiger Cave Temple, long wading transfers through sea surf, and oppressive midday heat. IF: `traveler_type == TRANSIT` THEN: Choose a hotel base in Krabi Town, leveraging pre-booked private chauffeured transfers or taxis for swift 15-to-20-minute access to Krabi International Airport (KBV). Reason: Proximity to the central riverfront district avoids coastal beach traffic bottlenecks and ensures effortless, stress-free access to airport departure terminals. IF: `trip_length >= 4 nights` THEN: Multi-center your stay by combining 2 nights in an active beach hub like Ao Nang or Railay (for climbing and island hopping) with 2 nights in a peaceful sanctuary like Tubkaek Beach or an island jump to Koh Lanta or Koh Yao Noi.', 4253),
  ('krabi', 34, 'destination-scoring', 'DESTINATION SCORING', NULL, NULL, '| Factor | Score | | --- | --- | | Family | 88 | | Honeymoon | 94 | | Luxury | 88 | | Budget | 92 | | Adventure | 96 | | Culture | 78 | | Food | 88 | | Shopping | 72 | | Nightlife | 78 | | Relaxation | 94 | | Nature | 98 | | Accessibility | 58 | | Senior travelers | 76 | | First-time visitor | 92 | | Photography | 96 |', 4254),
  ('krabi', 35, 'final-travel-agent-verdict', 'FINAL TRAVEL AGENT VERDICT', NULL, NULL, 'Best for: Island lovers, rock climbers, honeymooners, nature enthusiasts, eco-adventurers, and travelers seeking dramatic limestone landscapes, world-class island hopping, thermal jungle springs, and a more laid-back tropical getaway compared to neighboring party hubs. Best duration: 4–5 days / 4 nights Best season: November–April Best stay: Oceanfront luxury pool villa in Tubkaek Beach or Klong Muang for tranquility and sunsets, beachfront resort in Railay West for rock climbing and scenery, or central Ao Nang Beach for convenient island-hopping access and night markets. Best transport: Pre-booked private chauffeured VIP airport transfer, private longtail boat or speedboat charters for early-morning island hopping, and ride-hailing apps (Grab or Bolt) for mainland road transit. Must-do: Avoid: Biggest advantage: Breathtaking natural topography where soaring limestone karsts meet crystal-clear turquoise waters, paired with a laid-back bohemian vibe, exceptional eco-adventures, and world-class offshore marine access. Biggest disadvantage: Boat-dependent logistics for key beaches, tide-sensitive beach access, and fewer high-end shopping or intense party options compared to Phuket or Bangkok. Overall destination score: **95/100**', 4255),
  ('krabi', 36, 'data-quality', 'DATA QUALITY', NULL, NULL, 'information_completeness: 90/100 last_updated: 2026-08-27 last_verified: NOT_LIVE_VERIFIED verified_by: TRAVEL_ENGINE_INITIAL_DATASET sources: IMPORTANT: Prices, opening hours, schedules, visa requirements, availability, accessibility and operational conditions must NOT be treated as permanently valid from this document. These must be sourced from structured, refreshable data.', 4256),
  ('sentosa-island', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Spring', NULL, 'months: March April May weather: Hot and Humid. crowd_level: MEDIUM → HIGH price_level: MEDIUM → HIGH overall_score: 88-90 recommended: true reason: Very good mix of reliable weather and full event calendar; ideal for families who want outdoor time, but expect higher prices and crowds around long weekends and school breaks.', 4257),
  ('sentosa-island', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Summer', NULL, 'months: June July August weather: Warm and humid with Southwest Monsoon. crowd_level: MEDIUM → HIGH price_level: HIGH in June; MEDIUM in July–August overall_score: 85-88 recommended: true reason: Great for family itineraries and theme parks; June is busy and expensive, while July–August can be a smart “good weather + slightly lower cost” window if you avoid haze alerts and peak holiday dates.', 4258),
  ('sentosa-island', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Autumn', NULL, 'months: September October November weather: Still warm (25–32°C) but rainfall increases. crowd_level: LOW → MEDIUM price_level: LOW → MEDIUM overall_score: 82-86 recommended: true reason: Best value season for cost-conscious travelers and repeat visitors; plan more indoor attractions and flexible schedules, but you gain lower prices and lighter queues.', 4259),
  ('sentosa-island', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Winter', NULL, 'months: December January February weather: Cool/cold; shorter daylight. crowd_level: VERY HIGH in late Dec–early price_level: VERY HIGH in late Dec–early overall_score: 80-90 recommended: true reason: Peak festive atmosphere and major sales, but also peak prices, crowds, and rain in Dec–Jan; February is often the sweet spot for Indian families wanting great weather with slightly fewer holiday spikes.', 4260),
  ('sentosa-island', 10, 'budget-strategy', 'BUDGET STRATEGY', NULL, NULL, 'Where money can be saved: Where saving money is usually NOT recommended: Travel-agent rule: A slightly more expensive but centrally located, well-reviewed hotel beside efficient public transport generally delivers better total value than a cheaper, peripheral property once you factor in extra transport costs and the value of lost time each day.', 4261),
  ('sentosa-island', 12, 'airport-transfer-logic', 'AIRPORT TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Family', 'family', 'Airport taxi or pre-booked private MPV / van; door-to-door, space for luggage, child-friendly.', 4262),
  ('sentosa-island', 12, 'airport-transfer-logic', 'AIRPORT TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Honeymoon', 'honeymoon', 'Pre-booked private car or limo; meet-and-greet, seamless hotel drop, good for late-night arrivals. reason: The first impression of the trip matters and private transfer provides comfort and privacy.', 4263),
  ('sentosa-island', 12, 'airport-transfer-logic', 'AIRPORT TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Luxury', 'luxury', 'Chauffeured limo or luxury sedan/MPV; priority pickup, premium comfort, ideal for 5★ Marina Bay / Sentosa stays.', 4264),
  ('sentosa-island', 12, 'airport-transfer-logic', 'AIRPORT TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Budget', 'budget', 'MRT from Changi plus short walk or local bus; lowest cost, best for light luggage and younger travelers.', 4265),
  ('sentosa-island', 12, 'airport-transfer-logic', 'AIRPORT TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Senior', 'senior', 'Taxi or private transfer with minimal walking; prioritize comfort, assistance and direct access to hotel lobby.', 4266),
  ('sentosa-island', 18, 'family-travel', 'FAMILY TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'child_friendly_score: 90 best_ages: Rules: For young children: Prefer: Avoid:', 4267),
  ('sentosa-island', 19, 'honeymoon-travel', 'HONEYMOON TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'honeymoon_score: 96 romance_score: 98 privacy_score: 90 luxury_score: 95 Recommended: Honeymoon itinerary should NOT contain more than: 2 major activities/day. Prefer: One memorable experience + free time over: Three or four attractions. Recommended hotel areas:', 4268),
  ('sentosa-island', 20, 'luxury-travel', 'LUXURY TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'luxury_score: 97 Recommended: Luxury should primarily increase:', 4269),
  ('sentosa-island', 21, 'adventure', 'ADVENTURE', NULL, NULL, 'adventure_score: 59 Adventure-like experiences should be interpreted as:', 4270),
  ('sentosa-island', 22, 'senior-travel', 'SENIOR TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'senior_suitability: 70 walking_intensity: MEDIUM unless carefully managed Rules:', 4271),
  ('sentosa-island', 23, 'accessibility', 'ACCESSIBILITY', NULL, NULL, 'wheelchair_accessibility: EXCELLENT public_transport_accessibility: EXCELLENT hotel_accessibility: GOOD_TO_EXCELLENT; MUST_BE_VERIFIED_PER_HOTEL attraction_accessibility: GOOD_TO_EXCELLENT; MUST_BE_VERIFIED_PER_ATTRACTION Rule: Verify accessible room, step-free access, and attraction facilities before booking.', 4272),
  ('sentosa-island', 24, 'food', 'FOOD', NULL, NULL, 'Paris is particularly strong for: Food experiences: Family: Prioritise clean, convenient restaurants, familiar menu options, hawker centres, food courts, and early dining times. Honeymoon: Include one memorable waterfront, rooftop, seafood, or fine-dining dinner. Luxury: Fine dining, chef-led menus, premium seafood, cocktail bars, and private dining can be key itinerary elements. Budget: Use hawker centres, food courts, casual local eateries, and breakfast spots; reserve one selected premium meal for the trip.', 4273),
  ('sentosa-island', 25, 'shopping', 'SHOPPING', NULL, NULL, 'Strong categories: Luxury shopping: Prefer Orchard Road, Marina Bay Sands, The Shoppes, ION Orchard, Paragon, and premium department stores. Budget: Prefer:', 4274),
  ('sentosa-island', 26, 'nightlife', 'NIGHTLIFE', NULL, NULL, 'nightlife_level: 82 Suitable for: Not a primary requirement for: Honeymoon travelers should generally prefer: Romantic rooftop dinner, riverfront drinks, Gardens by the Bay light show, sunset cruise, or Sentosa beach evening over: late-night club itinerary', 4275),
  ('sentosa-island', 28, 'sample-itinerary-patterns', 'SAMPLE ITINERARY PATTERNS', '3 NIGHTS', NULL, '### Day 1 Arrive in Singapore and transfer to hotel. Rest of the day free. ### Day 2 Half-day Singapore city tour, then Sentosa Island with cable car, 4D Adventure Land, and Sky Helix. ### Day 3 Breakfast at hotel, then full-day Universal Studios. ### Day 4 Breakfast, check out, and transfer to Changi Airport for departure. Package Includes: 3 nights stay with breakfast, visa, all mentioned tours, and private transfers. Excludes: Flight fare and travel insurance.', 4276),
  ('sentosa-island', 29, 'five-night-honeymoon-pattern', 'FIVE-NIGHT HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 1', NULL, 'Arrive at Singapore Changi Airport and transfer privately to the hotel. Check in, relax, and enjoy the evening at leisure. Optional evening add-on: Night Safari for wildlife-loving couples, or a romantic dinner at Marina Bay/Clarke Quay. Overnight: Singapore Meals: Breakfast', 4277),
  ('sentosa-island', 29, 'five-night-honeymoon-pattern', 'FIVE-NIGHT HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 2', NULL, 'After breakfast, proceed for a half-day Singapore city tour covering major photo stops. Later, continue to Sentosa Island with a one-way cable-car ride. Enjoy free time at Sentosa Beach or S.E.A. Aquarium, followed by the Wings of Time evening show. Return to the hotel. Overnight: Singapore Meals: Breakfast', 4278),
  ('sentosa-island', 29, 'five-night-honeymoon-pattern', 'FIVE-NIGHT HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 3', NULL, 'After breakfast, visit Gardens by the Bay, including Cloud Forest and Flower Dome. In the evening, enjoy Supertree Grove light show, Marina Bay waterfront views, and a Singapore River Cruise or Singapore Flyer experience. Universal Studios Singapore may be selected instead for couples who prefer a full day of rides and entertainment. Overnight: Singapore Meals: Breakfast', 4279),
  ('sentosa-island', 29, 'five-night-honeymoon-pattern', 'FIVE-NIGHT HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 4', NULL, 'After breakfast, check out and proceed to Kuala Lumpur by coach/private transfer or flight, as per final travel arrangement. Check in at the hotel and relax. In the evening, enjoy Kuala Lumpur night city tour with Petronas Twin Towers photo stop and KL Tower area. Overnight: Kuala Lumpur Meals: Breakfast', 4280),
  ('sentosa-island', 29, 'five-night-honeymoon-pattern', 'FIVE-NIGHT HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 5', NULL, 'After breakfast, proceed for a full-day Genting Highlands tour. Enjoy the two-way cable-car ride, scenic mountain views, and leisure time at the resort. Couples may choose indoor theme-park activities, casino visit, cafés, shopping, or a relaxed highland date before returning to Kuala Lumpur. Overnight: Kuala Lumpur Meals: Breakfast', 4281),
  ('sentosa-island', 29, 'five-night-honeymoon-pattern', 'FIVE-NIGHT HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 6', NULL, 'After breakfast, check out from the hotel and transfer to Kuala Lumpur Airport for the return flight to India with sweet honeymoon memories. Meals: Breakfast', 4282),
  ('sentosa-island', 30, 'five-night-family-pattern', 'FIVE-NIGHT FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 1', NULL, 'Arrive at Singapore Airport, private transfer to hotel, check-in and relax. Optional: Night Safari. Overnight: Singapore Meals: Breakfast', 4283),
  ('sentosa-island', 30, 'five-night-family-pattern', 'FIVE-NIGHT FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 2', NULL, 'Breakfast at hotel. Half-day Singapore city tour, followed by Sentosa Island tour with one-way cable car, 4D AdventureLand and Wings of Time show. Return to hotel. Overnight: Singapore Meals: Breakfast', 4284),
  ('sentosa-island', 30, 'five-night-family-pattern', 'FIVE-NIGHT FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 3', NULL, 'Breakfast at hotel. Full-day Universal Studios Singapore tour. Return to hotel. Overnight: Singapore Meals: Breakfast', 4285),
  ('sentosa-island', 30, 'five-night-family-pattern', 'FIVE-NIGHT FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 4', NULL, 'Breakfast and check-out. Proceed to Kuala Lumpur, check in at hotel. Evening Kuala Lumpur city tour with KL Tower area and Petronas Twin Towers photo stop. Overnight: Kuala Lumpur Meals: Breakfast', 4286),
  ('sentosa-island', 30, 'five-night-family-pattern', 'FIVE-NIGHT FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 5', NULL, 'Breakfast at hotel. Full-day Genting Highlands tour with two-way cable car and indoor theme-park visit. Return to hotel. Overnight: Kuala Lumpur Meals: Breakfast', 4287),
  ('sentosa-island', 30, 'five-night-family-pattern', 'FIVE-NIGHT FAMILY PATTERN', 'Day 6', NULL, 'Breakfast, check-out and airport transfer for return flight to India. Meals: Breakfast', 4288),
  ('sentosa-island', 31, 'five-night-luxury-pattern', 'FIVE-NIGHT LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 1', NULL, 'Arrive at Singapore Changi Airport and receive VIP meet-and-greet assistance. Private transfer to a 5-star hotel in Marina Bay or Sentosa. Evening at leisure, followed by a premium waterfront or rooftop dinner.', 4289),
  ('sentosa-island', 31, 'five-night-luxury-pattern', 'FIVE-NIGHT LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 2', NULL, 'Breakfast at hotel. Enjoy a private half-day Singapore city tour covering Marina Bay, Merlion Park, Civic District, and selected heritage areas. Continue to Sentosa for a cable-car ride, resort leisure, beach club/spa, or sunset yacht experience. Return to hotel for overnight stay.', 4290),
  ('sentosa-island', 31, 'five-night-luxury-pattern', 'FIVE-NIGHT LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 3', NULL, 'Breakfast at hotel. Visit Gardens by the Bay, including Cloud Forest and Flower Dome, followed by leisure for luxury shopping at Marina Bay Sands or Orchard Road. Evening visit to SkyPark/Singapore Flyer and a signature fine-dining dinner.', 4291),
  ('sentosa-island', 31, 'five-night-luxury-pattern', 'FIVE-NIGHT LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 4', NULL, 'Breakfast and check-out. Private transfer to airport and fly to Kuala Lumpur, preferably in business class where available. On arrival, private transfer to a luxury hotel. Evening private city orientation with Petronas Twin Towers photo stop and rooftop dinner.', 4292),
  ('sentosa-island', 31, 'five-night-luxury-pattern', 'FIVE-NIGHT LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 5', NULL, 'Breakfast at hotel. Private excursion to Genting Highlands with two-way cable car, scenic leisure, premium shopping, and mountain dining. Return to Kuala Lumpur for a relaxed evening and farewell fine-dining dinner. Alternative: Replace Genting with luxury shopping at Pavilion KL, a couple spa, a private cultural tour, or afternoon tea for a more relaxed premium experience.', 4293),
  ('sentosa-island', 31, 'five-night-luxury-pattern', 'FIVE-NIGHT LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 6', NULL, 'Breakfast at hotel. Check-out and private transfer to Kuala Lumpur International Airport for departure with sweet memories.', 4294),
  ('sentosa-island', 32, 'travel-agent-insights', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS', 'What inexperienced planners often do wrong', NULL, '', 4295),
  ('sentosa-island', 32, 'travel-agent-insights', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS', 'What an experienced planner does differently', NULL, '', 4296),
  ('sentosa-island', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', NULL, NULL, 'IF: trip_length <= 2 nights THEN: prioritise Marina Bay, Gardens by the Bay, and one signature evening experience. Reason: A very short stay should focus on Singapore’s strongest first-impression experiences, not on covering multiple distant zones. IF: trip_length == 3 nights THEN: include only one major full-day attraction zone: Sentosa or Mandai Wildlife Reserve. Reason: Both areas require substantial travel time and activity time; combining them with a compact city-break schedule creates an exhausting itinerary. IF: trip_length >= 4 nights THEN: add either a Sentosa full day, Mandai wildlife day, or a relaxed cultural-and-food day. Reason: Four or more nights allow core Marina Bay sightseeing plus one interest-led experience without rushing. IF: trip_length >= 5 nights THEN: include two themed days from Sentosa, Universal Studios, Mandai Wildlife Reserve, Orchard/Botanic Gardens, or East Coast. Reason: A five-night stay gives enough time to combine iconic sightseeing, attractions, leisure, and recovery time. IF: trip_length >= 7 nights THEN: consider a slower Singapore programme, regional add-ons, or a Singapore–Malaysia itinerary. Reason: Most first-time Singapore highlights can be covered comfortably in 4–5 nights; extra days work best with a slower pace or multi-destination routing. IF: traveler_type == FAMILY AND: children_age <= 6 THEN: schedule a maximum of one major attraction per day and include afternoon hotel, pool, or beach downtime. Reason: Heat, walking, queues, and long attraction days reduce practical capacity for young children. IF: traveler_type == HONEYMOON THEN: limit the itinerary to two major activities per day and increase free-time allocation. Reason: Singapore honeymoon value comes from atmosphere, privacy, dining, skyline views, gardens, and relaxed shared experiences—not maximum attraction count. IF: traveler_type == BUDGET THEN: use MRT and buses as the default transport, select a well-connected mid-range or budget hotel, and mix paid attractions with free experiences. Reason: Singapore can be expensive, but transport, hawker food, public spaces, waterfront walks, Jewel Changi, and selected free light shows help protect the budget without reducing trip quality. IF: traveler_type == LUXURY THEN: prioritise Marina Bay, Sentosa Island, or Orchard Road for hotel selection. Reason: These areas offer Singapore’s strongest concentration of five-star hotels, premium shopping, skyline views, resort facilities, fine dining, and high-touch service.', 4297),
  ('sentosa-island', 34, 'destination-scoring', 'DESTINATION SCORING', NULL, NULL, '| Factor | Score | | ------------------ | ----: | | Family | 90 | | Honeymoon | 94 | | Luxury | 95 | | Budget | 70 | | Adventure | 55 | | Culture | 88 | | Food | 94 | | Shopping | 90 | | Nightlife | 82 | | Relaxation | 80 | | Nature | 80 | | Accessibility | 94 | | Safety | 95 | | First-time visitor | 94 | | Photography | 90 |', 4298),
  ('sentosa-island', 35, 'final-travel-agent-verdict', 'FINAL TRAVEL AGENT VERDICT', NULL, NULL, 'Best traveler profiles: 1. First-time international travelers 2. Honeymooners and romantic couples 3. Families 4. Luxury travelers 5. Food, culture, shopping, and photography-focused travelers 6. Solo travelers and seniors seeking a safe, organised city break Best duration: 4–5 nights Best season: February–April September–October Best hotel strategy: Stay in an MRT-connected hotel. Choose Marina Bay for premium first-time and luxury stays, Chinatown/Bugis for culture and value, Orchard for shopping, or Sentosa for resort-style family and leisure holidays. Best transportation: Use MRT and public buses. Private transfer for: Must-do for first-time visitor: Don''t-do: Biggest advantage: Singapore offers an exceptionally smooth first Asia trip: safe, English-friendly, clean, highly connected, multicultural, visually impressive, and strong across food, luxury, family attractions, shopping, and urban nature. Biggest disadvantage: It is a relatively expensive destination for accommodation and paid attractions, while tropical heat, humidity, rain, queues, and excessive walking can make poorly planned itineraries tiring. Overall destination score: 94/100— a premium, highly reliable, first-time-friendly Southeast Asian city destination, especially strong for couples, families, luxury guests, food lovers, and short-to-medium city breaks.', 4299),
  ('sentosa-island', 36, 'data-quality', 'DATA QUALITY', NULL, NULL, 'information_completeness: 88/100 last_updated: 2026-08-07 last_verified: PARTIALLY_LIVE_VERIFIED verified_by: SINGAPORE_DESTINATION_KNOWLEDGE_DATASET sources: Singapore Changi Airport — airport facilities, transfers, passenger services, and operational updates Land Transport Authority Singapore / SMRT — MRT, bus, accessibility, fare, and service information Mandai Wildlife Reserve — Singapore Zoo, Night Safari, River Wonders, Bird Paradise, hours, tickets, and visitor rules Resorts World Sentosa / Sentosa Development Corporation — Universal Studios Singapore, Sentosa attractions, resort access, and operational information Gardens by the Bay, National Parks Board, National Museum of Singapore, and other official attraction websites Immigration & Checkpoints Authority and Ministry of Foreign Affairs Singapore — entry, visa, customs, and traveller requirements Hotel, airline, transfer, and attraction supplier data — live availability, final prices, inclusions, cancellation terms, and booking restrictions. IMPORTANT: This Singapore destination file is suitable for itinerary design, traveller profiling, hotel-area strategy, and initial package planning. Prices, hotel inventory, flight schedules, attraction operating hours, show timings, maintenance closures, ticket availability, visa and entry rules, public-transport notices, weather alerts, haze conditions, and supplier cancellation policies must be live-verified before quotation, payment collection, or ticket issuance. Do not rely on generic “Singapore package” inclusions without confirming the exact attraction name, transfer type, ticket category, pickup timing, age policy, and whether a listed attraction is operating on the client’s selected date. Correct outdated or inconsistent records before production use—for example, remove non-Singapore attraction IDs, replace legacy attraction names where required, and verify all scored recommendations against current official operational information.', 4300),
  ('kuala-lumpur', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Dry Season (Peak Season)', NULL, 'months: May–August weather: Hot and sunny (24–33°C) with the lowest rainfall of the year, bright skies, and high but manageable humidity. crowd_level: HIGH price_level: HIGH overall_score: 88–95 recommended: true reason: Best window for walking tours around Merdeka Square and Chinatown, exploring Batu Caves, and enjoying rooftop bar skylines with minimal rain disruption.', 4301),
  ('kuala-lumpur', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Festive & Shoulder Season', NULL, 'months: December–February weather: Warm and pleasant (23–32°C) with brief afternoon showers, sunny intervals, and vibrant holiday illuminations. crowd_level: HIGH price_level: HIGH overall_score: 82–90 recommended: true reason: Perfect for experiencing Chinese New Year, Christmas, and Thaipusam celebrations at Batu Caves, though hotel prices spike around holidays.', 4302),
  ('kuala-lumpur', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Inter-Monsoon / Heavy Wet Season', NULL, 'months: March–April & September–November weather: Hot and humid (24–33°C) with frequent afternoon downpours, strong thunderous rainstorms, and high mugginess. crowd_level: LOW → MEDIUM price_level: LOW overall_score: 60–70 reason: Heavy afternoon rain can disrupt outdoor walking and sightseeing, though KL''s massive indoor air-conditioned malls, covered walkways, and indoor attractions make it easy to wait out showers while enjoying off-season hotel discounts.', 4303),
  ('kuala-lumpur', 10, 'budget-strategy', 'BUDGET STRATEGY', NULL, NULL, 'Where saving money is not recommended:', 4304),
  ('kuala-lumpur', 18, 'family-travel', 'FAMILY TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'child_friendly_score: 92 best_ages: Rules:', 4305),
  ('kuala-lumpur', 19, 'honeymoon-travel', 'HONEYMOON TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'Best areas: KLCC (Kuala Lumpur City Centre): best for ultra-luxurious high-rise stays (such as Four Seasons Hotel Kuala Lumpur, Mandarin Oriental, and Grand Hyatt), direct views of the Petronas Twin Towers, fine-dining restaurants, and strolling through KLCC Park during the evening fountain light shows. Bukit Bintang & Impiana Corridor: best for vibrant urban luxury, world-class luxury shopping at Pavilion KL, chic rooftop cocktail lounges (like Vertigo at Banyan Tree), and stylish boutique hotels connected via air-conditioned skywalks. Bangsar & Damansara Heights: best for a quieter, romantic residential escape featuring trendy cafe culture, intimate speakeasy bars, artisanal bakeries, and upscale private condo rentals away from tourist crowds. Perdana Botanical Gardens & Lake Gardens Enclave: best for romantic daytime strolls through lush tropical greenery, orchids, and peaceful lake paths near historic heritage hotels like The Majestic Hotel Kuala Lumpur. Chinatown (Petaling Street Heritage District): best for couples seeking historic charm, staycations in restored boutique shophouse hotels (such as Else Kuala Lumpur or ChoCha Foodstore stays), and hidden speakeasy cocktail bars tucked behind unmarked doors. Honeymoon rules: Prefer high-floor executive suites or skyline pool villas with unobstructed views of the Petronas Twin Towers or Merdeka 118, paired with unhurried fine-dining experiences at rooftop venues. Avoid exploring outdoor street markets like Jalan Alor during peak humid afternoon hours (12:00 PM–3:00 PM); instead, relax in luxury hotel infinity pools or schedule couple''s spa sessions. Investing in private airport executive transfers and five-star luxury accommodation with dedicated concierge services elevates the city honeymoon experience far more than crowded group day-trip tours.', 4306),
  ('kuala-lumpur', 20, 'luxury-travel', 'LUXURY TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'luxury_score: 90 Best-value luxury pattern Book a high-floor executive skyline suite or penthouse at an iconic 5-star sanctuary such as The RuMa Hotel & Residences, Four Seasons Hotel Kuala Lumpur, Mandarin Oriental, Banyan Tree Kuala Lumpur, or The Majestic Hotel in premier enclaves like KLCC, Bukit Bintang, or the historic heritage precinct. Arrange resort-managed private VIP airport transfers from Kuala Lumpur International Airport (KLIA) featuring dedicated tarmac/arrivals escort services paired with private executive chauffeurs (such as a Mercedes-Benz S-Class or Toyota Vellfire) straight to your city property. Charter private chauffeured luxury transport or helicopter tours for seamless day trips to historic Malacca, Genting Highlands, or royal heritage sites, complete with private local guides, fast-track access, and curated high-end dining experiences. Savor exquisite fine dining at signature skyline venues like Horizon Grill, Nobu, or Troika Sky Dining, experience multi-hour hydrotherapy and traditional Malay massage rituals at award-winning wellness centers like The Spa at Mandarin Oriental, and indulge in exclusive personal shopper services at Pavilion KL and Suria KLCC. Luxury rules: Keep the itinerary unhurried and avoid overpacking your schedule with walking tours during peak midday humidity and heat. Prefer privacy, personal concierge services, comfort, and exclusivity over visiting noisy, low-end tourist markets or unmetered transit routes. Avoid unmetered street taxis, overcrowded public transport during rush hours, unverified tour operators, and frequent hotel changes. For Kuala Lumpur, a dedicated 3 to 5-night luxury stay provides the ideal balance of city exploration, fine dining, world-class shopping, skyline views, and premium wellness relaxation.', 4307),
  ('kuala-lumpur', 21, 'adventure', 'ADVENTURE', NULL, NULL, 'adventure_score: 88 Kuala Lumpur is a dynamic tropical metropolis framed by ancient limestone massifs, dense sub-montane rainforests, and fast-flowing river systems. Centered around the iconic jungle ridges of the Titiwangsa Range, the dramatic karst formations of Batu Caves, and the wild rivers of Hulu Selangor, the region delivers an intense mix of high-altitude peak hiking, natural rock face climbing, white-water kayaking, and canopy obstacle navigation. Adventure seekers can seamlessly transition from scaling natural multi-pitch limestone cliffs in the morning to navigating Class III+ river rapids and trekking through ancient rainforest trails by afternoon. Top experiences: Recommended areas: Best for:', 4308),
  ('kuala-lumpur', 22, 'senior-travel', 'SENIOR TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'senior_suitability: 80 walking_intensity: MEDIUM (can be customized to LOW with private door-to-door transit, climate-controlled skywalks, and flat garden pathways) Kuala Lumpur is a solid destination for senior travelers when itineraries emphasize air-conditioned skywalks, ground-level garden boardwalks, private chauffeured rides, and an unhurried, heat-conscious travel pace. While the city features dense urban traffic and occasional uneven street pavements, mature travelers can seamlessly enjoy world-class shopping, iconic skyline views, rich multicultural heritage, and lush green parks by choosing centrally connected accommodations and flat, indoor-linked transit routes. Rules: Prefer: Avoid:', 4309),
  ('kuala-lumpur', 23, 'accessibility', 'ACCESSIBILITY', NULL, NULL, 'wheelchair_accessibility: PARTIAL_TO_GOOD depending on attraction and transport public_transport_accessibility: VARIABLE hotel_accessibility: MUST_BE_VERIFIED_PER_HOTEL attraction_accessibility: MUST_BE_VERIFIED_PER_ATTRACTION Rule: Never infer accessibility from destination-level accessibility. Each hotel and attraction must carry its own accessibility data.', 4310),
  ('kuala-lumpur', 24, 'food', 'FOOD', NULL, NULL, 'food_score: 98 Kuala Lumpur is one of Asia’s premier culinary capitals, offering an extraordinary fusion of Malay, Chinese, and Indian flavors alongside indigenous ingredients and global influences. The city’s dining spectrum stretches from fiery street-side hawker stalls and historic late-night *mamak* joints to multi-generational *kopitiums*, hip contemporary cafes, and Michelin-recognized fine dining set against iconic skyline views. Food experiences: Best for: Recommended areas:', 4311),
  ('kuala-lumpur', 25, 'shopping', 'SHOPPING', NULL, NULL, 'shopping_score: 98 Kuala Lumpur is a global shopping paradise that caters to every budget and taste. The city''s retail landscape spans ultra-luxury mega-malls and high-end designer flagships to historic heritage bazaars, air-conditioned underground shopping corridors, and vibrant open-air night markets. Best buys: Prefer: Avoid: Best for:', 4312),
  ('kuala-lumpur', 26, 'nightlife', 'NIGHTLIFE', NULL, NULL, 'nightlife_level: 92 Kuala Lumpur delivers a vibrant, diverse, and sophisticated nightlife scene that caters to every mood and style. The city''s evening landscape ranges from glamorous high-altitude rooftop cocktail lounges and pulsating electronic music clubs to hidden speakeasies, lively craft beer bars, and bustling late-night street food markets framed by glowing skyscrapers. Best for: Prefer: Avoid: Best evening areas:', 4313),
  ('kuala-lumpur', 28, 'sample-itinerary-patterns', 'SAMPLE ITINERARY PATTERNS', '2 NIGHTS – CLASSIC KUALA LUMPUR ESSENTIALS', NULL, 'Day 1: Arrival at Kuala Lumpur International Airport (KLIA T1 or T2) → Express KLIA Ekspres train (28 mins) or GrabCar transfer to your hotel base in KLCC or Bukit Bintang → Afternoon stroll through Suria KLCC and a walk through the lush green paths of KLCC Park → Photo stop at the base of the iconic Petronas Twin Towers followed by the evening Lake Symphony light-and-water fountain show → Walk the elevated, air-conditioned skywalk over to Jalan Alor for an evening street food feast of grilled satay, chicken wings, and tropical fruits Day 2: Early morning Grab ride or KTM Komuter train to Batu Caves before midday heat and crowds arrive → Climb the 272 colorful rainbow steps to the main Temple Cave and admire the massive golden Lord Murugan Statue → Return to central city for an afternoon historic heritage walking tour around Merdeka Square, Sultan Abdul Samad Building, and the River of Life convergence point → Explore local arts, handicrafts, and souvenirs inside Central Market (Pasar Seni) → Sunset drinks at a high-altitude rooftop bar (such as Vertigo at Banyan Tree or Horizon Grill) with 360-degree views of the illuminated skyline → Evening dinner and stroll along the vibrant streets of Chinatown and Kwai Chai Hong Day 3: Leisurely morning visit to Thean Hou Temple to marvel at multi-tiered Chinese architecture overlooking the city → Hotel check-out (~12:00 PM) and quick lunch at a local *mamak* stall for authentic *Roti Canai* and *Teh Tarik* → Final souvenir shopping spree at Pavilion Kuala Lumpur → Direct KLIA Ekspres train ride from KL Sentral back to the airport for your evening flight departure', 4314),
  ('kuala-lumpur', 28, 'sample-itinerary-patterns', 'SAMPLE ITINERARY PATTERNS', '3 NIGHTS – URBAN LUXURY, CULTURAL HERITAGE & DAY TRIPS', 'luxury', 'Day 1: Arrival via Kuala Lumpur International Airport (KLIA T1/T2) → Private executive VIP transfer to a luxury hotel base in KLCC (such as The RuMa, Four Seasons, or Mandarin Oriental) → Check-in and afternoon relaxation by the high-rise infinity pool featuring view lines of Merdeka 118 or the Twin Towers → Pre-booked late afternoon Skybridge and Observation Deck tour at the Petronas Twin Towers → Sophisticated fine dining at Troika Sky Dining or Marini''s on 57 overlooking the glowing cityscape Day 2: Morning cultural deep-dive through Chinatown, visiting Petaling Street Market, Guan Di Temple, and historic coffee shops (kopitiums) for kaya toast → Air-conditioned museum tour through the world-class Islamic Arts Museum Malaysia → Afternoon stroll through the orchids and shaded paths of Perdana Botanical Garden (Lake Gardens) → Elegant English high tea in the historic Tea Lounge at The Majestic Hotel Kuala Lumpur → Hidden speakeasy hunting through Chinatown for craft cocktails tucked behind unmarked shophouse doors Day 3: Full-day private chauffeured excursion to historic UNESCO-listed Malacca (Melaka) (~2 hours south of KL) → Explore Dutch Square, Christ Church, A Famosa fortress ruins, and St. Paul''s Hill → Sample authentic Nyonya (Peranakan) lunch and fresh chicken rice balls along Jonker Street → Relaxing scenic boat cruise along the historic Malacca River before driving back to Kuala Lumpur → Farewell luxury dinner and rooftop cocktails at Horizon Grill or Nobu Kuala Lumpur Day 4: Leisurely gourmet breakfast at the hotel → Morning walk through KLCC Park or luxury shopping at Pavilion Kuala Lumpur featuring personal shopper options → Private chauffeur transfer back to KLIA for your departure', 4315),
  ('kuala-lumpur', 28, 'sample-itinerary-patterns', 'SAMPLE ITINERARY PATTERNS', '4 NIGHTS – ULTIMATE METROPOLITAN ADVENTURE, RAINFOREST & THEME PARKS', 'adventure', 'Day 1: Arrival in KL & airport coach or Grab ride to hotel base in Bukit Bintang or Chinatown → Check-in and afternoon forest canopy walk at KL Forest Eco Park—a real rainforest reserve set right beneath KL Tower → Ascend to the Sky Deck and Sky Box at KL Tower (Menara Kuala Lumpur) for open-air city panoramas → Evening street food exploration along Jalan Alor, sampling *Char Kway Teow*, grilled stingray, and coconut ice cream Day 2: Morning visit to Batu Caves followed by an outdoor limestone rock-climbing session or zip-lining at Gua Damai Extreme Park → Afternoon dip and marine walk inside Aquaria KLCC, exploring the 90-meter underwater ocean tunnel → Dinner in Kampung Baru, indulging in authentic *Nasi Lemak* and satay while looking out at the modern skyline → Nighttime stroll around the illuminated River of Life waterfront area near Merdeka Square Day 3: Full-day adventure trip to Genting Highlands (~1 hour drive north) → Ride the Awana SkyWay cable car over ancient rainforest canopies to the mountain peak → Spend the day enjoying high-altitude outdoor and indoor theme park rides at Genting SkyWorlds → Duty-free outlet shopping at Genting Highlands Premium Outlets before taking the cable car and Grab back to KL → Midnight supper at a 24-hour *mamak* stall in Bukit Bintang, eating hot *Roti Canai* and drinking *Teh Tarik* Day 4: Full-day water park and thrill ride trip to Sunway Lagoon Theme Park → Splash through massive wave pools, water slides, wildlife park encounters, and extreme ride zones → Return to central KL by late afternoon for hotel shower and downtime → Nightlife pub crawl and live music gig along the Changkat Bukit Bintang bar strip Day 5: Leisurely morningDim Sum breakfast in Chinatown or ICC Pudu market hall → Last-minute souvenir shopping for Malaysian batik and Royal Selangor pewter at Central Market → Direct airport transfer to KLIA for departure', 4316),
  ('kuala-lumpur', 28, 'sample-itinerary-patterns', 'SAMPLE ITINERARY PATTERNS', '1 NIGHT – EXPRESS CITY & LANDMARK HIGHLIGHTS', NULL, 'Day 1: Morning arrival at Kuala Lumpur International Airport (KLIA T1/T2) (~8:30 AM) → KLIA Ekspres train straight to KL Sentral (28 mins), drop bags at hotel or terminal luggage storage → Take LRT to KLCC station to view the iconic Petronas Twin Towers and stroll KLCC Park → Quick lunch at the Suria KLCC Signatures Food Court (trying *Nasi Lemak* or *Laksa*) → Take the elevated skywalk to Bukit Bintang for afternoon shopping at Pavilion Kuala Lumpur → Evening Grab ride to Batu Caves for late afternoon photos at the rainbow stairs before dusk → Return to city core for evening street food dinner on Jalan Alor and rooftop drinks overlooking the illuminated towers Day 2: Early morning walk around historic Merdeka Square and Sultan Abdul Samad Building → Quick coffee and traditional kaya toast breakfast at a heritage kopitium in Chinatown (Petaling Street Market → Express transit back to KL Sentral to retrieve bags → Board KLIA Ekspres train for smooth arrival at KLIA in time for afternoon/evening departure flight', 4317),
  ('kuala-lumpur', 29, '8-days-and-7-nights-honeymoon-itenarary', '8 DAYS & 7 NIGHTS – HONEYMOON Itenarary', NULL, NULL, 'Day 1: Arrival at Kuala Lumpur International Airport (KUL) (~7:15 AM) → Meet private driver for a scenic road journey up to the cool mist of Cameron Highlands → Enjoy a scenic local lunch en route as the air cools down → Photo stop at Port Lepak Viewpoint (Jerung) to take in sweeping views of the lush green mountain range → Stroll through the fairy-tale set of Hobbiton Village and explore nearby floral installations → Check-in to your highland resort and enjoy a cozy, relaxed evening together in the cool mountain climate Day 2: Morning breakfast at the hotel → Visit the iconic BOH Tea Centre; walk through emerald-green tea gardens and share tea & pastries at the glass café overlooking the valley → Wander hand-in-hand through Cameron Flora Park to view colorful flower arrangements, glasshouses, and romantic picnic pathways → Quick optional stops at the Strawberry Park (to pick fresh strawberries) or Cameron Lavender Garden if time permits → Scenic land transfer back down to Kuala Lumpur → Check-in to your Kuala Lumpur hotel base for a relaxing overnight stay Day 3: Breakfast at the hotel → Morning half-day Kuala Lumpur City Tour: view the grand Istana Negara (National Palace), drive past the National Mosque (Masjid Negara), and admire historic colonial architecture at Merdeka Square → Photo stop at the base of the world-famous Petronas Twin Towers and walk through Central Market (Pasar Seni) → Afternoon free for hotel pool downtime or romantic couples shopping at Pavilion Kuala Lumpur → Evening street food stroll along Jalan Alor or romantic rooftop drinks overlooking the illuminated city skyline Day 4: Breakfast at the hotel → Morning drive to the legendary Batu Caves—climb the iconic 272 vibrant rainbow steps up to the limestone temple cave guarded by the golden Lord Murugan Statue → Continue drive up to Genting Highlands hill resort → Board the Awana SkyWay cable car for a sweeping ride over ancient rainforest canopy to the mountain peak → Spend the afternoon exploring indoor amusement attractions, Skytropolis, and luxury shopping at Genting Highlands Premium Outlets → Transfer back to central Kuala Lumpur for your evening stay Day 5: Breakfast at the hotel & check-out → Direct transfer to Kuala Lumpur Airport (KUL) for your short domestic flight to Langkawi Island → Touch down at Langkawi International Airport (LGK); welcome transfer to your beach resort → Check-in and relax on the white sands of Pantai Cenang or your private resort beach → Late afternoon board an romantic Sunset Dinner Cruise: sail across calm turquoise ocean waters, enjoy an open-bar sea-jacuzzi net session, BBQ dinner, and golden hour views over the Andaman Sea → Overnight stay at your resort in Langkawi Day 6: Breakfast at the hotel → Board a shared (SIC) Langkawi Island Hopping boat excursion across the limestone archipelago → Visit Dayang Bunting (Lake of the Pregnant Maiden)—swim in the freshwater mountain lake surrounded by rainforest → Stop at Singa Besar Island for wild eagle feeding watching from the boat → Swim and relax on the soft sands of Beras Basah Island → Return to main island by mid-afternoon for spa downtime, couples massage, or beach lounge drinks Day 7: Breakfast at the hotel → Full-day Langkawi City & Island Highlights Tour: head to Oriental Village base station → Ride the famous Langkawi SkyCab (cable car) to the peak of Mount Machinchang → Included combo attractions: immersive 3D Art Museum, SkyDome, and dynamic 5D SkyRex simulator ride → Walk across the curved Sky Bridge suspended over high jungle cliffs (accessed via walking path or SkyGlide elevator) → Afternoon visit to Eagle Square (Dataran Lang) for photos by the landmark giant eagle statue → Special final honeymoon dinner at a cliffside or beachfront restaurant on the island Day 8: Breakfast at the hotel → Morning leisure time for last-minute duty-free shopping (chocolates, perfumes, and local crafts) or a quiet beach walk → Hotel check-out and private transfer to Langkawi Airport (LGK) for departure flight back home to Kolkata (CCU) via KUL connection', 4318),
  ('kuala-lumpur', 30, '8-days-7-nights-family-itinerary', '8 Days / 7 Nights Family Itinerary', NULL, NULL, 'Day 1: Arrival at Kuala Lumpur International Airport (KLIA T1/T2) (~7:15 AM) → Meet private driver for a scenic land transfer north to Cameron Highlands (~3.5 to 4 hours) → Stop for a traditional family lunch en route at a local restaurant → Scenic roadside drive with photo stops at Port Lepak Viewpoint, Hobbiton Village, and Cameron Santorini → Hotel check-in at Cameron Highlands base → Evening at leisure to stroll through local night markets and enjoy the cool mountain climate before overnight stay in Cameron Highlands Day 2: Breakfast at the hotel → Morning visit to the emerald tea rolling hills at BOH Tea Centre → Walk through vibrant floral displays and photo spots at Cameron Flora Park → Optional visit to Lavender Park and a strawberry picking experience at Strawberry Park (if time permits) → Afternoon land transfer back down to Kuala Lumpur (~3.5 hours) → Check-in and overnight stay in Kuala Lumpur Day 3: Breakfast at the hotel → Half-day guided Kuala Lumpur City Tour featuring photo stops at the iconic Petronas Twin Towers, King''s Palace (Istana Negara), Merdeka Square, and Central Market → Afternoon at leisure to explore the street food lanes of Jalan Alor or shop at Pavilion Kuala Lumpur → Overnight stay in Kuala Lumpur Day 4: Breakfast at the hotel → Morning excursion to Batu Caves to see the massive golden Lord Murugan Statue and climb the colorful 272 steps → Continue drive up to Genting Highlands mountain resort → Ride the scenic Awana SkyWay cable car to the peak for shopping, entertainment, and theme park fun → Late afternoon return transfer to Kuala Lumpur city center → Overnight stay in Kuala Lumpur Day 5: Breakfast at the hotel → Hotel check-out and private transfer to Kuala Lumpur Airport → Catch domestic flight to Langkawi Airport → Warm welcome upon arrival at Langkawi and hotel transfer for check-in → Late afternoon transfer to the harbor for a romantic Sunset Dinner Cruise along the Andaman Sea → Overnight stay in Langkawi Day 6: Breakfast at the hotel → Morning pickup for shared (SIC) Langkawi Island Hopping Tour → Speedboat run to Dayang Bunting (Pregnant Maiden Island) for lake swimming and sightseeing → Eagle feeding spectacle off Singa Besar Island and beach relax/snorkeling at Beras Basah Island → Afternoon return to hotel for pool downtime → Overnight stay in Langkawi Day 7: Breakfast at the hotel → Full-day Langkawi City Tour & Panorama Langkawi Complex → Cable Car Combo experience featuring SkyCab, SkyDome, SkyRex, and 3D Art Museum → Ride the SkyGlide down to walk across the famous curved Langkawi Sky Bridge suspended over the rainforest → Visit Eagle Square (Dataran Lang) for classic family photos with the giant eagle monument → Overnight stay in Langkawi Day 8: Breakfast at the hotel → Hotel check-out and luggage collection → Direct transfer to Langkawi International Airport (LGK) for homeward departure flight to Kolkata (CCU)', 4319),
  ('kuala-lumpur', 31, '8-nights-7-days-luxury-itenarary', '8 NIGHTS / 7 DAYS – LUXURY Itenarary', NULL, NULL, 'Day 1: Early morning arrival at Kuala Lumpur International Airport (KLIA T1/T2) (~7:15 AM) → VIP Private Luxury SUV Transfer pickup from KLIA direct to Cameron Highlands (~3.5 to 4-hour scenic drive) → En-route stop at **Port Lepak Viewpoint** (Simpang Pulai route) to take in misty mountain vistas and enjoy fresh highland air → Scenic mountain-view lunch stop enjoying local highland specialties → Visit **Hobbiton Village** (Hobbitoon / Flora Park Shire) for photo opportunities amidst whimsical fairy-tale gardens → Check-in to your luxury heritage resort (e.g., *The Cameron Highlands Resort* or *The Zenith Hotel*) → Afternoon English High Tea on the veranda overlooking lush green hills → Evening leisure and fine dining at the resort''s signature restaurant; overnight stay in Cameron Highlands Day 2: Breakfast at the resort → Private morning visit to the iconic **BOH Tea Center (Sungei Palas)**—walk the elevated glass viewing deck overlooking endless rolling emerald tea plantations → Explore **Flora Park**, wandering through vibrant flower tunnels and cloud gardens → *Optional stops (time permitting):* Fresh strawberry picking at **Strawberry Park** or colorful floral strolls at **Lavender Park** → Afternoon private transfer back down to Kuala Lumpur (~3.5 hours) → Check-in to a luxury high-rise hotel in KLCC (e.g., *Four Seasons Hotel Kuala Lumpur*, *The Ritz-Carlton*, or *Mandarin Oriental*) → Evening gourmet dinner with skyline views; overnight stay in Kuala Lumpur Day 3: Breakfast at the hotel → Premium **Half-Day Kuala Lumpur City Tour** via private air-conditioned vehicle → Photo stop at the world-famous Petronas Twin Towers & KLCC Park → Scenic pass by the King''s Palace (Istana Negara, National Monument, and National Mosque (Masjid Negara → Walk around historic Merdeka Square and the Sultan Abdul Samad Building overlooking the River of Life → Afternoon shopping spree at Suria KLCC or high-end boutiques at Pavilion Kuala Lumpur → Evening street food and night market stroll along Jalan Alor or luxury dining at Troika Sky Dining; overnight stay in Kuala Lumpur Day 4: Breakfast at the hotel → Private morning transfer to Batu Caves → Marvel at the massive golden Lord Murugan Statue and climb the colorful 272 steps to the cathedral limestone cave → Continue drive up to **Genting Highlands** (~1 hour from KL) → Board the **Awana SkyWay Glass-Floor Gondola / Cable Car** soaring over 130-million-year-old rainforest canopy → Afternoon exploration of Genting SkyWorlds Theme Park, duty-free shopping at Genting Highlands Premium Outlets, or entertainment at SkyAvenue → Evening return private transfer back to the city → Relaxing drinks at a high-altitude rooftop bar (e.g., Vertigo at Banyan Tree); overnight stay in Kuala Lumpur Day 5: Breakfast at the hotel and check-out → Private transfer to Kuala Lumpur International Airport (KLIA) for your domestic flight to Langkawi → Welcome to **Langkawi International Airport (LGK)** → Private chauffeur transfer to your beachfront luxury resort (e.g., *The St. Regis Langkawi*, *The Datai Langkawi*, or *Four Seasons Resort Langkawi*) → Check-in and afternoon relaxation on private white-sand beaches → Late afternoon transfer to the marina for your **Luxury Sunset Dinner Cruise** → Sail the Andaman Sea on a catamarans/yacht, enjoying an open bar, saltwater jacuzzi net, free-flow drinks, and a gourmet BBQ dinner against a tropical sunset → Return to resort; overnight stay in Langkawi Day 6: Breakfast at the resort → Pick-up for a **Langkawi Island Hopping Tour** (SIC basis or upgradeable to private speed yacht) → Cruise to **Dayang Bunting Island (Lake of the Pregnant Maiden)**—take a refreshing dip in the famous freshwater lake surrounded by natural limestone cliffs → Eagle watching at Singa Besar Island, observing wild sea eagles diving for food → Relax, swim, and soak up the sun on the powdery sands of Beras Basah Island → Afternoon return to hotel base for spa treatments or pool downtime → Evening dining at a oceanfront seafood restaurant; overnight stay in Langkawi Day 7: Breakfast at the resort → Private morning transfer to Oriental Village for the **Langkawi City & Heights Tour** → Board the world''s steepest cable car—**Langkawi SkyCab**—ascending Mount Machinchang → Access the **Langkawi Sky Bridge**, suspended 660 meters above sea level with glass-floor viewing platforms → Full access to SkyCab Combo inclusions: **SkyDome** 360-degree projection theatre, **SkyRex** 3D simulation ride, and **3D Art Museum** (Art in Paradise) → Experience the **SkyGlide** funicular ride connecting the top station to the Sky Bridge → Evening leisure stroll along Pantai Cenang beach promenade or dinner at an exclusive cliffside restaurant; overnight stay in Langkawi Day 8: Breakfast at the resort → Morning leisure time for last-minute beach walks, souvenir shopping, or duty-free chocolates → Hotel check-out and private transfer to Langkawi International Airport (LGK) → Board departure flight back to Kolkata (CCU) via connecting flight', 4320),
  ('kuala-lumpur', 32, 'travel-agent-insights', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS', 'What inexperienced planners often do wrong', NULL, '', 4321),
  ('kuala-lumpur', 32, 'travel-agent-insights', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS', 'What an experienced planner does differently', NULL, '', 4322),
  ('kuala-lumpur', 32, 'travel-agent-insights', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS', 'Best planning rule', NULL, '', 4323),
  ('kuala-lumpur', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', NULL, NULL, 'IF: `trip_length <= 1 night` THEN: Choose an express 2D1N central stay in KLCC or Bukit Bintang, prioritizing an early morning visit to Batu Caves, an afternoon walk around Suria KLCC and KLCC Park, photo ops at the Petronas Twin Towers, and evening street food on Jalan Alor. Reason: Short overnights require tight transit logistics; staying in the city core allows fast access via the KLIA Ekspres while putting the city''s most famous landmarks and dining hubs within walking distance. IF: `trip_length == 2 nights` THEN: Book a 3D2N stay in KLCC or Bukit Bintang, combining iconic skyline views (Petronas Twin Towers, rooftop lounges) with a morning trip to Batu Caves, historic heritage walks around Merdeka Square and Chinatown, and shopping at Pavilion Kuala Lumpur. Reason: Two nights allow a seamless blend of modern architectural marvels, sacred cultural monuments, high-end shopping, and vibrant street food lanes without feeling rushed. IF: `trip_length >= 3 nights` THEN: Base in Kuala Lumpur and add full-day excursions—such as a mountain retreat to Genting Highlands via the Awana SkyWay cable car, a day trip to the UNESCO-listed historic city of Malacca (Melaka), or an eco-adventure day at Sunway Lagoon Theme Park. Reason: Three or more nights enable exploring beyond the city center into cool mountain highlands, historic colonial river towns, or theme parks while maintaining a single luxury city base. IF: `trip_type == FIRST_TIME_VISITOR` THEN: Prioritize signature highlights including the Petronas Twin Towers, the 272 colorful steps of Batu Caves, Merdeka Square, Central Market (Pasar Seni), Chinatown (Petaling Street Market, and an evening food feast on Jalan Alor. Reason: These quintessential landmarks, historic bazaars, sacred temples, and street food lanes showcase the definitive skyline, multi-ethnic culture, and culinary richness of Kuala Lumpur. IF: `trip_type == HONEYMOON` THEN: Book a high-floor luxury suite in KLCC (e.g., Four Seasons Hotel Kuala Lumpur, Banyan Tree Kuala Lumpur, The RuMa Hotel & Residences, or Mandarin Oriental KL), paired with pre-booked sunset Skybridge tickets, private fine dining overlooking the glowing Twin Towers, and high-altitude rooftop cocktails. Reason: Sophisticated urban enclaves offer romantic high-rise skyline views, world-class luxury spas, elevated dining options, and glamorous nightlife away from street-level crowds. IF: `traveler_type == FAMILY` THEN: Select family-friendly hotels near KLCC Park featuring splash pools and playground access, paired with visits to Aquaria KLCC, Petrosains Discovery Centre, a full day at Sunway Lagoon Theme Park, and interactive cable car rides at Genting Highlands. Reason: Proximity to pedestrian parks, indoor science centers, aquariums, and world-class theme parks keeps children entertained safely while minimizing long transit times. IF: `traveler_type == LUXURY` THEN: Arrange VIP Airport Fast-Track clearance at KLIA, private chauffeured luxury sedan transfers, pre-booked private observation deck experiences, high tea at The Majestic Hotel, and fine dining at Troika Sky Dining or Marini''s on 57. Reason: Dedicated private vehicles and executive privileges eliminate long airport queues, traffic delays, and crowded public tourist tours. IF: `traveler_type == BUDGET` THEN: Base in Chinatown or Bukit Bintang backstreets, utilizing the free Go KL City Bus routes, LRT/MRT rail networks, and eating meals under RM 15 at local *mamak* stalls (*Roti Canai*), market halls (ICC Pudu), or street stalls along Petaling Street Market. Reason: Central Kuala Lumpur offers an abundance of affordable boutique guesthouses, clean public rail transit, and legendary cheap street food. IF: `traveler_interest == NATURE` THEN: Plan a visit to the KL Forest Eco Park (canopy walk inside a virgin rainforest), Perdana Botanical Garden (Lake Gardens), KL Bird Park (world''s largest free-flight walk-in aviary), and an excursion to Kanching Falls or the Cameron Highlands tea plantations. Reason: KL is uniquely situated around lush tropical rainforest reserves, botanical sanctuaries, mountain tea estates, and expansive aviary gardens. IF: `traveler_interest == FOOD` THEN: Take evening street food crawls through Jalan Alor and Chinatown, explore ICC Pudu for authentic morning breakfasts, sample Nasi Lemak in Kampung Baru, and enjoy banana leaf rice in Little India (Brickfields). Reason: Kuala Lumpur is one of Asia''s premier culinary capitals, celebrated for its unique blend of Malay, Chinese, and Indian flavors, vibrant hawker centers, and 24-hour *mamak* food culture. IF: `traveler_interest == ADVENTURE` THEN: Focus on outdoor rock climbing at Gua Damai Extreme Park near Batu Caves, canopy walks at KL Forest Eco Park, high-altitude coaster rides at Genting SkyWorlds Theme Park, or white-water rafting in nearby Kuala Kubu Bharu. Reason: Beyond modern shopping malls, the limestone karsts, mountain ridges, and rivers surrounding KL provide world-class outdoor thrills. IF: `traveler_type == SENIOR` THEN: Book step-free hotels in KLCC connected via covered, air-conditioned skywalks (KLCC-to-Bukit Bintang Walkway), utilize Grab rides or private drivers, schedule early morning visits to outdoor sites like Batu Caves, and plan air-conditioned museum or high tea breaks in the afternoon. Reason: Accessible indoor walkways and private door-to-door transit help avoid steep climbs, uneven pavements, and oppressive tropical midday heat. IF: `traveler_type == TRANSIT` THEN: Choose a hotel base near KL Sentral, leveraging direct access to the 28-minute nonstop **KLIA Ekspres** airport train for seamless transit to KLIA T1/T2. Reason: Basing at the primary transit hub completely bypasses unpredictable city highway traffic gridlock, ensuring fast, stress-free access to departure terminals. IF: `trip_length >= 4 nights` THEN: Multi-center your stay by combining 2 or 3 nights in modern, bustling Kuala Lumpur (for culture, shopping, and nightlife) with 2 nights in a mountain tea retreat in Cameron Highlands or an island beach escape to Langkawi or Penang. Reason: A multi-center approach balances the high-energy metropolitan skyline of KL with cool highland tea plantations or relaxing tropical island beaches.', 4324),
  ('kuala-lumpur', 34, 'destination-scoring', 'DESTINATION SCORING', NULL, NULL, '| Factor | Score | | --- | --- | | Family | 92 | | Honeymoon | 84 | | Luxury | 90 | | Budget | 94 | | Adventure | 62 | | Culture | 92 | | Food | 98 | | Shopping | 96 | | Nightlife | 88 | | Relaxation | 80 | | Nature | 72 | | Accessibility | 82 | | Senior travelers | 84 | | First-time visitor | 96 | | Photography | 90 |', 4325),
  ('kuala-lumpur', 35, 'final-travel-agent-verdict', 'FINAL TRAVEL AGENT VERDICT', NULL, NULL, 'Best for: Culture seekers, city skyline lovers, luxury travelers, street food enthusiasts, families, shoppers, and travelers seeking a dynamic mix of ultra-modern skyscrapers, lush urban rainforests, rich multi-ethnic heritage (Malay, Chinese, Indian), and accessible mountain/highland day trips. Best duration: 4–5 days / 4 nights Best season: May–September (drier season across West Malaysia) or November–February (for holiday festivities and lower humidity, despite occasional afternoon showers) Best stay: High-rise luxury hotels in KLCC (such as Four Seasons, Mandarin Oriental, or Banyan Tree) for Twin Tower views and pedestrian park access; heritage boutique stays in Chinatown/Pasar Seni for culture lovers; or upscale central hotels in Bukit Bintang for shopping and nightlife. Best transport: Pre-booked **KLIA Ekspres** train for quick 28-minute transfers between KLIA and KL Sentral (bypassing highway traffic), ride-hailing apps (Grab) for city transit, LRT/MRT rail systems for city center exploring, and private chauffeured vehicles for highland day trips (Cameron Highlands & Genting Highlands). Must-do: Avoid: Biggest advantage: Incredible value-for-money luxury, exceptional multi-cultural culinary diversity, world-class infrastructure, seamless public rail transit, and iconic modern/heritage architecture. Biggest disadvantage: Unpredictable tropical afternoon monsoons, heavy city traffic jams during rush hours, and hot, humid weather for outdoor walking during midday. Overall destination score: **94/100**', 4326),
  ('kuala-lumpur', 36, 'data-quality', 'DATA QUALITY', NULL, NULL, 'information_completeness: 90/100 last_updated: 2026-08-27 last_verified: NOT_LIVE_VERIFIED verified_by: TRAVEL_ENGINE_INITIAL_DATASET sources: IMPORTANT: Prices, opening hours, schedules, visa requirements, availability, accessibility and operational conditions must NOT be treated as permanently valid from this document. These must be sourced from structured, refreshable data.', 4327),
  ('cameron-highlands', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Relatively Dry & Peak Season', NULL, 'months: June–August & February weather: Pleasantly cool (14–24°C) with the lowest rainfall of the year, clearer skies, and comfortable crisp air. crowd_level: HIGH price_level: HIGH overall_score: 88–95 recommended: true reason: Ideal window for tea estate walks, clear valley photography, outdoor flower garden tours, and jungle trekking along dry trails without muddy paths.', 4328),
  ('cameron-highlands', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Cool Holiday & Festive Season', NULL, 'months: December–January weather: Coolest conditions of the year (13–22°C) with chilly nights, misty mornings, and brief afternoon showers. crowd_level: HIGH price_level: HIGH overall_score: 82–90 recommended: true reason: Popular for festive school holiday getaways and escaping lowland heat, offering quintessential cozy highland weather, though weekend traffic jams can be severe.', 4329),
  ('cameron-highlands', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Wet / Inter-Monsoon Season', NULL, 'months: March–May & September–November weather: Cool and humid (15–23°C) with frequent afternoon downpours, misty cloud cover, and heavy rainfall (peaking in October/November). crowd_level: LOW → MEDIUM price_level: LOW overall_score: 60–72 reason: Heavy afternoon rain can make forest trails slippery and cause occasional road delays, though morning visits to tea estates are exceptionally green, prices drop, and steamboat dining in the rain is cozy.', 4330),
  ('cameron-highlands', 10, 'budget-strategy', 'BUDGET STRATEGY', NULL, NULL, 'Where saving money is not recommended:', 4331),
  ('cameron-highlands', 18, 'family-travel', 'FAMILY TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'child_friendly_score: 90 best_ages: Rules:', 4332),
  ('cameron-highlands', 19, 'honeymoon-travel', 'HONEYMOON TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'Best areas: Ringlet & Lakehouse Enclave: best for ultra-romantic luxury escapes, features classic English Tudor-style architecture, secluded lakeside surroundings, private fireplace dining, and maximum privacy tucked away from central highland traffic. Tanah Rata (Resort & Heritage Precinct): best for refined colonial luxury, high-end spa retreats (such as Spa Village at Cameron Highlands Resort), sweeping golf course views, and convenient access to boutique cafes and private nature tours. Golden Hills & Strawberry Park Corridor: best for romantic mid-range to luxury stays in alpine-style chalets, tranquil valley views, peaceful walking paths, and close proximity to night markets and private strawberry picking experiences. Sungei Palas & Kea Heights: best for couples seeking dramatic high-altitude views, early morning sunrise access over BOH Tea Plantations, private boutique lodge stays, and scenic photo opportunities along misty cloud forest edges. Honeymoon rules: Book colonial-style heritage suites or private valley-view chalets with four-poster beds, fireplaces, and private balconies overlooking lush tea gardens or forest canopy. Avoid traveling along the main Brinchang-Kea Farm arterial road during peak weekend afternoon hours (12:00 PM–4:00 PM) to bypass heavy holiday traffic; focus instead on private in-resort high tea services or spa treatments. Pre-arrange private 4WD charters or chauffeured transfers for early-morning sunrise excursions to BOH Tea Centre and Mossy Forest, ensuring an intimate, crowd-free experience.', 4333),
  ('cameron-highlands', 20, 'luxury-travel', 'LUXURY TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'luxury_score: 78 Best-value luxury pattern Book a luxury suite or traditional heritage room at premier highland sanctuaries such as Cameron Highlands Resort or The Smokehouse Hotel, located in quiet, picturesque enclaves along the golf course and southern hill valleys. Arrange resort-managed private chauffeur transfers in a executive MPV or SUV directly from Kuala Lumpur International Airport (KLIA), Penang, or Ipoh, ensuring a smooth, air-conditioned journey up the mountain switchbacks straight to your property. Charter private 4WD vehicles paired with dedicated local naturalists for personalized, crowd-free morning excursions to the Mossy Forest, private off-road tea estate viewpoints, and exclusive organic farms. Savor multi-course colonial-style dining and signature steambot dinners, indulge in traditional tea-infused spa treatments at the award-winning Spa Village Cameron Highlands, and enjoy private English high tea served on lush garden lawns overlooking rolling tea plantations. Luxury rules: Keep the itinerary unhurried and avoid traveling along the main Brinchang-Kea Farm corridor during peak weekend midday traffic. Prefer private guided 4WD excursions, in-resort dining, custom concierge services, and tranquil heritage stays over crowded mass-tourist stops. Avoid unmetered local street taxis, self-driving down steep mountain switchbacks during foggy weather, and unverified group tour operators. For Cameron Highlands, a dedicated 2 to 3-night luxury stay provides the ideal balance of highland relaxation, private nature exploration, fine colonial dining, and premium wellness treatments.', 4334),
  ('cameron-highlands', 21, 'adventure', 'ADVENTURE', NULL, NULL, 'adventure_score: 74 Cameron Highlands is a serene highland sanctuary set within Peninsular Malaysia''s rugged Titiwangsa Mountains. Characterized by dense montane cloud forests, mist-laden peaks, steep tea estate valleys, and hidden waterfalls, the region offers a tranquil yet exhilarating blend of jungle trekking, ridge hiking, and off-road exploration. Outdoor enthusiasts can swap the lowland heat for crisp mountain air while tackling challenging multi-hour forest trails, navigating ancient moss-covered tree roots, and ascending high-altitude peaks with sweeping views over the surrounding highlands. Top experiences: Recommended areas: Best for:', 4335),
  ('cameron-highlands', 22, 'senior-travel', 'SENIOR TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'senior_suitability: 80 walking_intensity: MEDIUM (can be customized to LOW with private tour charters, resort-based high tea, and flat garden boardwalks) Cameron Highlands is a peaceful and highly appealing destination for senior travelers seeking crisp mountain air, scenic tea estate views, and a relaxed, cool-climate pace. While the region presents hilly terrain, uneven farm steps, and narrow highland roads, mature travelers can comfortably experience world-class plantation vistas, colonial heritage, and vibrant gardens by choosing accessible resort accommodations, private vehicle transport, and morning tours focused on flat, paved attractions. Rules: Prefer: Avoid:', 4336),
  ('cameron-highlands', 23, 'accessibility', 'ACCESSIBILITY', NULL, NULL, 'wheelchair_accessibility: PARTIAL_TO_GOOD depending on attraction and transport public_transport_accessibility: VARIABLE hotel_accessibility: MUST_BE_VERIFIED_PER_HOTEL attraction_accessibility: MUST_BE_VERIFIED_PER_ATTRACTION Rule: Never infer accessibility from destination-level accessibility. Each hotel and attraction must carry its own accessibility data.', 4337),
  ('cameron-highlands', 24, 'food', 'FOOD', NULL, NULL, 'food_score: 88 Cameron Highlands offers a distinct culinary landscape defined by its cool mountain climate, rich British colonial heritage, and vast agricultural bounty. Dining in the region revolves around warming communal meals, farm-to-table produce, iconic colonial tea rituals, and vibrant local night markets. Food experiences: Best for: Recommended areas:', 4338),
  ('cameron-highlands', 25, 'shopping', 'SHOPPING', NULL, NULL, 'shopping_score: 72 Cameron Highlands offers a delightful and relaxed shopping experience centered on mountain-fresh agricultural produce, artisanal tea, local floral goods, and unique highland souvenirs rather than high-end luxury malls or high-street retail chains. Best buys: Prefer: Avoid: Best for:', 4339),
  ('cameron-highlands', 26, 'nightlife', 'NIGHTLIFE', NULL, NULL, 'nightlife_level: 45 Cameron Highlands offers a quiet, relaxed, and laid-back evening environment centered around cool-climate comfort, cozy socializing, and late-night dining rather than high-energy party clubs, loud dance venues, or rowdy bar strips. Evening entertainment here revolves around gathering with friends or family for steaming hotpot dinners, unwinding at cozy pub lounges, visiting weekend night markets, and enjoying quiet drinks by open fireplaces. Best for: Prefer: Avoid: Best evening areas:', 4340),
  ('cameron-highlands', 28, 'sample-itinerary-patterns', 'SAMPLE ITINERARY PATTERNS', '2 NIGHTS – CLASSIC CAMERON HIGHLANDS ESSENTIALS', NULL, 'Day 1: Arrival in Tanah Rata or Brinchang via private vehicle or express coach from Kuala Lumpur / Penang → Check-in to your hotel or highland guesthouse base and unpack → Afternoon walk along Tanah Rata Main Street to browse local tour agencies, shops, and casual cafes → Scenic coffee and snack break at a local cafe sampling fresh highland strawberry tarts and tea → Evening communal Highland Steamboat (Hot Pot) dinner in Brinchang, dipping fresh local vegetables and sliced meats in boiling broths Day 2: Early morning 4WD tour departure to beat the crowds at the Sungei Palas BOH Tea Estate → Walk out onto the floating tea cafe viewing deck to enjoy freshly brewed black tea with sweeping 360-degree plantation views → Guided boardwalk stroll through the mist-shrouded Mossy Forest (Gunung Brinchang) to view rare pitcher plants, mosses, and orchids → Afternoon self-pick strawberry harvesting experience at Big Red Strawberry Farm or Raju’s Hill Strawberry Farm → Traditional English Afternoon High Tea at The Smokehouse Hotel or Cameron Highlands Resort, complete with warm scones, clotted cream, and strawberry jam → Weekend evening browsing and street-food snacking at the Golden Hills Night Market (Brinchang Night Market) Day 3: Leisurely morning visit to the MARDI Agro Technology Park in Tanah Rata to explore experimental fruit orchards and flower gardens → Souvenir and fresh produce shopping at Kea Farm Market to pick up highland sweet corn, strawberries, and tea gift tins → Hotel check-out (~12:00 PM) and a hearty Indian Banana Leaf lunch or mamak meal in Tanah Rata town center → Direct express bus departure from Tanah Rata Bus Terminal or private car transfer back down the mountain road', 4341),
  ('cameron-highlands', 28, 'sample-itinerary-patterns', 'SAMPLE ITINERARY PATTERNS', '3 NIGHTS – COLONIAL HERITAGE, SCENIC VALLEYS & NATURE', NULL, 'Day 1: Arrival via private executive MPV transfer from KLIA or Ipoh to a colonial heritage resort (such as Cameron Highlands Resort or The Lakehouse) → Welcome tea and check-in to your heritage suite overlooking manicured lawns or southern hill valleys → Relaxed afternoon walking around the hotel grounds and enjoying the cool mountain air → Evening fine-dining multi-course dinner at the resort dining room, followed by drinks by an open brick fireplace Day 2: Morning visit to the Cameron Valley Tea House (Bharat Tea Estate) for panoramic valley photography and a walk down through the hillside tea trails → Cultural history tour through the Time Tunnel Museum, browsing thousands of vintage Malaysian collectibles and historical photographs → Scenic lunch break featuring fresh farm-to-table salads and strawberry desserts → Afternoon luxury spa treatment (such as a signature tea-infused body scrub) at Spa Village Cameron Highlands → Romantic evening private steamboat or western candlelit dinner at your heritage lodge Day 3: Private morning guided 4WD excursion up to the Mossy Forest cloud forest boardwalk → VIP guided walkthrough of the Sungei Palas BOH Tea Factory to observe traditional tea processing methods from leaf to cup → Afternoon stroll through the vibrant terraced flower displays at Cameron Flora Park or the Lavender Garden → Relaxed high tea served on garden lawns amidst cool mountain breezes → Farewell dinner at a top-rated local dining spot in Tanah Rata Day 4: Leisurely breakfast on the outdoor terrace featuring freshly baked breads and local preserves → Short morning visit to Ee Feng Gu Bee Farm or Cactus Valley to pick up natural honey and mountain succulents → Private chauffeured transfer back down to Ipoh Airport or Kuala Lumpur International Airport', 4342),
  ('cameron-highlands', 28, 'sample-itinerary-patterns', 'SAMPLE ITINERARY PATTERNS', '4 NIGHTS – ULTIMATE HIGHLAND ADVENTURE, TREKKING & AGRO-TOURISM', 'adventure', 'Day 1: Arrival in Tanah Rata & check-in to an eco-lodge, hostel, or central hotel base → Afternoon warmup hike along Trail 9 or Trail 4 leading to Robinson Falls and Parit Falls → Relaxed evening dinner at a local mamak stall in Tanah Rata, enjoying hot *Roti Canai* and *Teh Tarik* Day 2: Full-day active jungle trek along Trail 10 to the summit of Gunung Batu Brinchang, continuing along mountain ridge paths surrounded by montane dipterocarp forest → Picnic lunch at a mountain lookout point overlooking surrounding valleys → Descend into Brinchang town for a well-earned afternoon rest and cold local drinks → Evening feast at a traditional charcoal steamboat restaurant in Brinchang Day 3: Early morning departures for a deep jungle guided Rafflesia Flower Trek (seasonal search for the world''s largest individual bloom) → Visit a nearby indigenous Orang Asli village to learn about traditional blowpipe crafting and rainforest survival skills → Late afternoon return to town for shower and recovery → Casual evening cafe hopping along Tanah Rata Main Street, trying local Western and Malay fusion dishes Day 4: Morning visit to The Sheep Sanctuary at Kea Farm for hands-on feeding and photo interactions with mountain sheep → Full afternoon exploring northern agricultural farms including Rose Centre, Cactus Valley, and local hydroponic vegetable greenhouses → Sunset views from high mountain roadside lookouts along the northern Blue Valley route → Evening visit to the weekend night market for grilled corn, satay, and sweet street snacks Day 5: Early morning breakfast and final walk through the Tanah Rata local market strip → Last-minute shopping for local fruit wines, strawberry jams, and loose-leaf teas → Mid-day bus departure from Tanah Rata Bus Terminal or private transfer to your next destination', 4343),
  ('cameron-highlands', 28, 'sample-itinerary-patterns', 'SAMPLE ITINERARY PATTERNS', '1 NIGHT – EXPRESS HIGHLAND HIGHLIGHTS', NULL, 'Day 1: Morning arrival in Cameron Highlands via early morning drive or coach from Ipoh / Kuala Lumpur (~10:30 AM) → Drive directly to Sungei Palas BOH Tea Estate for lunch at the floating tea cafe and photos over rolling green tea hills → Brief afternoon walk through the timber boardwalk section of the Mossy Forest → Check-in to your Tanah Rata or Brinchang hotel base (~3:00 PM) → Quick stop at a local strawberry farm (such as Big Red Strawberry Farm) for self-pick harvesting and strawberry ice cream → Piping-hot evening Highland Steamboat dinner in Brinchang town center to warm up in the cool night air Day 2: Early morning breakfast and traditional English scones at a local bakery or colonial cafe → Quick morning visit to Kea Farm Market to pick up fresh sweet corn, strawberries, and tea souvenirs → Photo stop at Cameron Valley Tea House (Bharat Tea Estate) along the main road heading south → Departure down the mountain pass toward Tapah or Simpang Pulai for your ongoing journey', 4344),
  ('cameron-highlands', 29, '8-days-and-7-nights-honeymoon-itenarary', '8 DAYS & 7 NIGHTS – HONEYMOON Itenarary', NULL, NULL, 'Day 1: Arrival at Kuala Lumpur International Airport (KUL) (~7:15 AM) → Meet private driver for a scenic road journey up to the cool mist of Cameron Highlands → Enjoy a scenic local lunch en route as the air cools down → Photo stop at Port Lepak Viewpoint (Jerung) to take in sweeping views of the lush green mountain range → Stroll through the fairy-tale set of Hobbiton Village and explore nearby floral installations → Check-in to your highland resort and enjoy a cozy, relaxed evening together in the cool mountain climate Day 2: Morning breakfast at the hotel → Visit the iconic BOH Tea Centre; walk through emerald-green tea gardens and share tea & pastries at the glass café overlooking the valley → Wander hand-in-hand through Cameron Flora Park to view colorful flower arrangements, glasshouses, and romantic picnic pathways → Quick optional stops at the Strawberry Park (to pick fresh strawberries) or Cameron Lavender Garden if time permits → Scenic land transfer back down to Kuala Lumpur → Check-in to your Kuala Lumpur hotel base for a relaxing overnight stay Day 3: Breakfast at the hotel → Morning half-day Kuala Lumpur City Tour: view the grand Istana Negara (National Palace), drive past the National Mosque (Masjid Negara), and admire historic colonial architecture at Merdeka Square → Photo stop at the base of the world-famous Petronas Twin Towers and walk through Central Market (Pasar Seni) → Afternoon free for hotel pool downtime or romantic couples shopping at Pavilion Kuala Lumpur → Evening street food stroll along Jalan Alor or romantic rooftop drinks overlooking the illuminated city skyline Day 4: Breakfast at the hotel → Morning drive to the legendary Batu Caves—climb the iconic 272 vibrant rainbow steps up to the limestone temple cave guarded by the golden Lord Murugan Statue → Continue drive up to Genting Highlands hill resort → Board the Awana SkyWay cable car for a sweeping ride over ancient rainforest canopy to the mountain peak → Spend the afternoon exploring indoor amusement attractions, Skytropolis, and luxury shopping at Genting Highlands Premium Outlets → Transfer back to central Kuala Lumpur for your evening stay Day 5: Breakfast at the hotel & check-out → Direct transfer to Kuala Lumpur Airport (KUL) for your short domestic flight to Langkawi Island → Touch down at Langkawi International Airport (LGK); welcome transfer to your beach resort → Check-in and relax on the white sands of Pantai Cenang or your private resort beach → Late afternoon board an romantic Sunset Dinner Cruise: sail across calm turquoise ocean waters, enjoy an open-bar sea-jacuzzi net session, BBQ dinner, and golden hour views over the Andaman Sea → Overnight stay at your resort in Langkawi Day 6: Breakfast at the hotel → Board a shared (SIC) Langkawi Island Hopping boat excursion across the limestone archipelago → Visit Dayang Bunting (Lake of the Pregnant Maiden)—swim in the freshwater mountain lake surrounded by rainforest → Stop at Singa Besar Island for wild eagle feeding watching from the boat → Swim and relax on the soft sands of Beras Basah Island → Return to main island by mid-afternoon for spa downtime, couples massage, or beach lounge drinks Day 7: Breakfast at the hotel → Full-day Langkawi City & Island Highlights Tour: head to Oriental Village base station → Ride the famous Langkawi SkyCab (cable car) to the peak of Mount Machinchang → Included combo attractions: immersive 3D Art Museum, SkyDome, and dynamic 5D SkyRex simulator ride → Walk across the curved Sky Bridge suspended over high jungle cliffs (accessed via walking path or SkyGlide elevator) → Afternoon visit to Eagle Square (Dataran Lang) for photos by the landmark giant eagle statue → Special final honeymoon dinner at a cliffside or beachfront restaurant on the island Day 8: Breakfast at the hotel → Morning leisure time for last-minute duty-free shopping (chocolates, perfumes, and local crafts) or a quiet beach walk → Hotel check-out and private transfer to Langkawi Airport (LGK) for departure flight back home to Kolkata (CCU) via KUL connection', 4345),
  ('cameron-highlands', 30, '8-days-7-nights-family-itinerary', '8 Days / 7 Nights Family Itinerary', NULL, NULL, 'Day 1: Arrival at Kuala Lumpur International Airport (KLIA T1/T2) (~7:15 AM) → Meet private driver for a scenic land transfer north to Cameron Highlands (~3.5 to 4 hours) → Stop for a traditional family lunch en route at a local restaurant → Scenic roadside drive with photo stops at Port Lepak Viewpoint, Hobbiton Village, and Cameron Santorini → Hotel check-in at Cameron Highlands base → Evening at leisure to stroll through local night markets and enjoy the cool mountain climate before overnight stay in Cameron Highlands Day 2: Breakfast at the hotel → Morning visit to the emerald tea rolling hills at BOH Tea Centre → Walk through vibrant floral displays and photo spots at Cameron Flora Park → Optional visit to Lavender Park and a strawberry picking experience at Strawberry Park (if time permits) → Afternoon land transfer back down to Kuala Lumpur (~3.5 hours) → Check-in and overnight stay in Kuala Lumpur Day 3: Breakfast at the hotel → Half-day guided Kuala Lumpur City Tour featuring photo stops at the iconic Petronas Twin Towers, King''s Palace (Istana Negara), Merdeka Square, and Central Market → Afternoon at leisure to explore the street food lanes of Jalan Alor or shop at Pavilion Kuala Lumpur → Overnight stay in Kuala Lumpur Day 4: Breakfast at the hotel → Morning excursion to Batu Caves to see the massive golden Lord Murugan Statue and climb the colorful 272 steps → Continue drive up to Genting Highlands mountain resort → Ride the scenic Awana SkyWay cable car to the peak for shopping, entertainment, and theme park fun → Late afternoon return transfer to Kuala Lumpur city center → Overnight stay in Kuala Lumpur Day 5: Breakfast at the hotel → Hotel check-out and private transfer to Kuala Lumpur Airport → Catch domestic flight to Langkawi Airport → Warm welcome upon arrival at Langkawi and hotel transfer for check-in → Late afternoon transfer to the harbor for a romantic Sunset Dinner Cruise along the Andaman Sea → Overnight stay in Langkawi Day 6: Breakfast at the hotel → Morning pickup for shared (SIC) Langkawi Island Hopping Tour → Speedboat run to Dayang Bunting (Pregnant Maiden Island) for lake swimming and sightseeing → Eagle feeding spectacle off Singa Besar Island and beach relax/snorkeling at Beras Basah Island → Afternoon return to hotel for pool downtime → Overnight stay in Langkawi Day 7: Breakfast at the hotel → Full-day Langkawi City Tour & Panorama Langkawi Complex → Cable Car Combo experience featuring SkyCab, SkyDome, SkyRex, and 3D Art Museum → Ride the SkyGlide down to walk across the famous curved Langkawi Sky Bridge suspended over the rainforest → Visit Eagle Square (Dataran Lang) for classic family photos with the giant eagle monument → Overnight stay in Langkawi Day 8: Breakfast at the hotel → Hotel check-out and luggage collection → Direct transfer to Langkawi International Airport (LGK) for homeward departure flight to Kolkata (CCU)', 4346),
  ('cameron-highlands', 31, '8-nights-7-days-luxury-itenarary', '8 NIGHTS / 7 DAYS – LUXURY Itenarary', NULL, NULL, 'Day 1: Early morning arrival at Kuala Lumpur International Airport (KLIA T1/T2) (~7:15 AM) → VIP Private Luxury SUV Transfer pickup from KLIA direct to Cameron Highlands (~3.5 to 4-hour scenic drive) → En-route stop at **Port Lepak Viewpoint** (Simpang Pulai route) to take in misty mountain vistas and enjoy fresh highland air → Scenic mountain-view lunch stop enjoying local highland specialties → Visit **Hobbiton Village** (Hobbitoon / Flora Park Shire) for photo opportunities amidst whimsical fairy-tale gardens → Check-in to your luxury heritage resort (e.g., *The Cameron Highlands Resort* or *The Zenith Hotel*) → Afternoon English High Tea on the veranda overlooking lush green hills → Evening leisure and fine dining at the resort''s signature restaurant; overnight stay in Cameron Highlands Day 2: Breakfast at the resort → Private morning visit to the iconic **BOH Tea Center (Sungei Palas)**—walk the elevated glass viewing deck overlooking endless rolling emerald tea plantations → Explore **Flora Park**, wandering through vibrant flower tunnels and cloud gardens → *Optional stops (time permitting):* Fresh strawberry picking at **Strawberry Park** or colorful floral strolls at **Lavender Park** → Afternoon private transfer back down to Kuala Lumpur (~3.5 hours) → Check-in to a luxury high-rise hotel in KLCC (e.g., *Four Seasons Hotel Kuala Lumpur*, *The Ritz-Carlton*, or *Mandarin Oriental*) → Evening gourmet dinner with skyline views; overnight stay in Kuala Lumpur Day 3: Breakfast at the hotel → Premium **Half-Day Kuala Lumpur City Tour** via private air-conditioned vehicle → Photo stop at the world-famous Petronas Twin Towers & KLCC Park → Scenic pass by the King''s Palace (Istana Negara, National Monument, and National Mosque (Masjid Negara → Walk around historic Merdeka Square and the Sultan Abdul Samad Building overlooking the River of Life → Afternoon shopping spree at Suria KLCC or high-end boutiques at Pavilion Kuala Lumpur → Evening street food and night market stroll along Jalan Alor or luxury dining at Troika Sky Dining; overnight stay in Kuala Lumpur Day 4: Breakfast at the hotel → Private morning transfer to Batu Caves → Marvel at the massive golden Lord Murugan Statue and climb the colorful 272 steps to the cathedral limestone cave → Continue drive up to **Genting Highlands** (~1 hour from KL) → Board the **Awana SkyWay Glass-Floor Gondola / Cable Car** soaring over 130-million-year-old rainforest canopy → Afternoon exploration of Genting SkyWorlds Theme Park, duty-free shopping at Genting Highlands Premium Outlets, or entertainment at SkyAvenue → Evening return private transfer back to the city → Relaxing drinks at a high-altitude rooftop bar (e.g., Vertigo at Banyan Tree); overnight stay in Kuala Lumpur Day 5: Breakfast at the hotel and check-out → Private transfer to Kuala Lumpur International Airport (KLIA) for your domestic flight to Langkawi → Welcome to **Langkawi International Airport (LGK)** → Private chauffeur transfer to your beachfront luxury resort (e.g., *The St. Regis Langkawi*, *The Datai Langkawi*, or *Four Seasons Resort Langkawi*) → Check-in and afternoon relaxation on private white-sand beaches → Late afternoon transfer to the marina for your **Luxury Sunset Dinner Cruise** → Sail the Andaman Sea on a catamarans/yacht, enjoying an open bar, saltwater jacuzzi net, free-flow drinks, and a gourmet BBQ dinner against a tropical sunset → Return to resort; overnight stay in Langkawi Day 6: Breakfast at the resort → Pick-up for a **Langkawi Island Hopping Tour** (SIC basis or upgradeable to private speed yacht) → Cruise to **Dayang Bunting Island (Lake of the Pregnant Maiden)**—take a refreshing dip in the famous freshwater lake surrounded by natural limestone cliffs → Eagle watching at Singa Besar Island, observing wild sea eagles diving for food → Relax, swim, and soak up the sun on the powdery sands of Beras Basah Island → Afternoon return to hotel base for spa treatments or pool downtime → Evening dining at a oceanfront seafood restaurant; overnight stay in Langkawi Day 7: Breakfast at the resort → Private morning transfer to Oriental Village for the **Langkawi City & Heights Tour** → Board the world''s steepest cable car—**Langkawi SkyCab**—ascending Mount Machinchang → Access the **Langkawi Sky Bridge**, suspended 660 meters above sea level with glass-floor viewing platforms → Full access to SkyCab Combo inclusions: **SkyDome** 360-degree projection theatre, **SkyRex** 3D simulation ride, and **3D Art Museum** (Art in Paradise) → Experience the **SkyGlide** funicular ride connecting the top station to the Sky Bridge → Evening leisure stroll along Pantai Cenang beach promenade or dinner at an exclusive cliffside restaurant; overnight stay in Langkawi Day 8: Breakfast at the resort → Morning leisure time for last-minute beach walks, souvenir shopping, or duty-free chocolates → Hotel check-out and private transfer to Langkawi International Airport (LGK) → Board departure flight back to Kolkata (CCU) via connecting flight', 4347),
