  ('boracay', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', NULL, NULL, 'IF: `trip_length <= 0.5 days` THEN: Choose a focused walking loop along **White Beach Station 2**, taking photos at **Willy''s Rock** in Station 1, grabbing a fresh mango shake along the beachfront path, browsing through **D''Mall Boracay**, and enjoying a seaside lunch before heading to the jetty port or Caticlan Airport. Reason: Half-day layovers require high transit efficiency; concentrating on central White Beach provides iconic island views, fresh tropical drinks, and easy souvenir shopping without risking missed boat or flight departures. IF: `trip_length == 1 day` THEN: Spend the morning on an outrigger boat tour snorkeling around **Crocodile Island** and visiting **Puka Shell Beach**, return to **White Beach Station 2** for lunch at **D''Mall**, spend the afternoon swimming in the calm Station 1 waters, and end the day with a *paraw* sailboat sunset ride and cocktails on the beach. Reason: A single day allows travelers to efficiently experience Boracay''s pristine outer reefs, iconic powdery white sands, and world-famous sailboat sunsets in one seamless flow. IF: `trip_length >= 2 days` THEN: Spend day one exploring **White Beach** (Stations 1 to 3), visiting **Willy''s Rock**, trying water activities like helmet diving or paddleboarding, and taking a sunset *paraw* sail; spend day two visiting northern beaches like **Puka Shell Beach** and **Diniwid Beach**, going up **Mount Luho Viewpoint**, and enjoying seafood dining at **D''Talipapa Market**. Reason: Multi-day stays allow travelers to balance White Beach''s central lifestyle and water sports with the island''s quieter northern coves, panoramic viewpoints, and local culinary markets. IF: `trip_type == FIRST_TIME_VISITOR` THEN: Focus on core island highlights—strolling the powdery sand of **White Beach Station 1**, taking photos at **Willy''s Rock**, shopping and dining in **D''Mall**, taking an island-hopping boat tour to **Puka Shell Beach** and **Magic Island**, watching the sunset via a local *paraw* sailboat, and dining along the Station 2 beach promenade. Reason: Combining the island''s signature white sand beaches, central retail arcades, offshore reef snorkeling, and iconic sailboat sunsets provides a comprehensive introduction to Boracay. IF: `trip_type == HONEYMOON` THEN: Book a private villa at an exclusive cliffside or northern luxury resort like *Shangri-La Boracay* or *Crimson Resort*, schedule private sunset *paraw* cruises, book couples'' hilot massage treatments at an oceanfront spa, and arrange private candlelit dinners on the quiet sands of **Puka Beach** or **Diniwid Beach**. Reason: Combining secluded luxury resorts, quiet northern coves, private sea excursions, and fine oceanfront dining creates an intimate and romantic island escape. IF: `traveler_type == FAMILY` THEN: Stay at beachfront resorts with direct access in **Station 1** or **Station 3**, enjoy gentle shallow swimming in front of Station 1, take a glass-bottom boat tour or banana boat ride, visit **Puka Shell Beach** for shell hunting, and dine at family-friendly restaurants around **D''Mall**. Reason: Step-free beach access, shallow swimmable waters, fun group water activities, and pedestrian-friendly dining zones keep children safe and entertained while minimizing travel stress. IF: `traveler_type == LUXURY` THEN: Book high-end ocean-view suites or private pool villas at 5-star resorts in **Station 1** or **Boracay Newcoast**, arrange private speedboat transfers directly from Caticlan Jetty Port, charter private yachts for sunset sailing, and indulge in beachfront fine dining and private spa treatments. Reason: Private water transit, exclusive cliffside accommodations, custom yacht charters, and personalized resort services eliminate travel friction while ensuring top-tier privacy and comfort. IF: `traveler_type == BUDGET` THEN: Stay in social hostels or budget guesthouses around **Station 3** or **Bulabog Beach**, join shared group island-hopping boat tours, walk along the beachfront promenade, swim at public access beaches, and eat at local *carinderias* or budget-friendly stalls near **D''Talipapa**. Reason: Boracay offers accessible shared boat tours, affordable guesthouses near Station 3, cheap street eats, and free public beach access, making the island enjoyable on a modest budget. IF: `traveler_interest == NATURE` THEN: Explore the marine life by snorkeling at **Crocodile Island** and **Coral Garden**, take a peaceful walk along the coarse, shell-filled shores of **Puka Shell Beach**, visit the tranquil mangroves at **Lugutan Mangrove Park**, and take in 360-degree island views from **Mount Luho**. Reason: Beyond White Beach''s commercial core, Boracay features marine sanctuaries, protected mangrove ecosystems, natural shell beaches, and elevated forest viewpoints. IF: `traveler_interest == FOOD` THEN: Map out a dynamic island food tour, sampling fresh grilled seafood at **D''Talipapa Market**, enjoying calamansi muffins at local bakery staples, trying beachfront mango soft-serve shakes, dining at international expat bistros in **D''Mall**, and enjoying seafood tapas with craft cocktails during sunset happy hours in **Station 1**. Reason: Boracay offers an impressive culinary mix, ranging from local Filipino seafood markets and beach snacks to upscale international restaurants and trendy sunset bars. IF: `traveler_interest == ADVENTURE` THEN: Go kitesurfing or windsurfing on the high-wind shores of **Bulabog Beach**, jump into the ocean at **Magic Island cliff jumping spot**, try scuba diving or helmet diving off Station 2, ride ATVs or mainland zorb courses, and try parasailing over the island''s turquoise waters. Reason: Boracay is a major center for water sports, offering world-class wind sports, high-flying parasailing, cliff jumping, and scuba diving opportunities. IF: `traveler_type == SENIOR` THEN: Stay at flat, accessible beachfront resorts in **Station 1**, utilize electric tricycles (e-trikes) for island transit, take gentle sunset *paraw* sailboat rides, enjoy flat walks along the paved paths of **D''Mall**, and relax at quiet beachfront cafes overlooking calm waters. Reason: Step-free beach access in Station 1, smooth e-trike transport, flat pedestrian walkways, and gentle boat options allow senior travelers to experience the island comfortably and safely. IF: `traveler_type == TRANSIT` THEN: Take a quick 10-minute boat ride from Caticlan Jetty Port to **Tambisaan Beach** or **Station 3**, spend 2 to 3 hours relaxing on the beach, grab a quick seafood lunch along the promenade, buy local souvenirs at **D''Mall**, and return directly to the port. Reason: Close proximity to Caticlan''s entry ports allows layover travelers to enjoy beach views, ocean swimming, and quick shopping within a tight schedule. IF: `trip_length >= 3 days` THEN: Divide your stay between 1 day of White Beach activities and sunset sailing, 1 day of offshore island hopping (**Crocodile Island**, **Puka Beach**, **Magic Island**), and 1 day exploring northern beaches (**Diniwid**, **Ilig-Iligan**), wind sports at **Bulabog Beach**, and mountain views from **Mount Luho**. Reason: A three-day itinerary balances Boracay''s world-famous main beach lifestyle with outer reef boat tours, quiet northern coves, high-wind sports, and panoramic inland viewpoints.', 4717),
  ('boracay', 34, 'destination-scoring', 'DESTINATION SCORING', NULL, NULL, '| Factor | Score | | --- | --- | | Family | 90 | | Honeymoon | 92 | | Luxury | 88 | | Budget | 84 | | Adventure | 86 | | Culture | 60 | | Food | 90 | | Shopping | 75 | | Nightlife | 94 | | Relaxation | 92 | | Nature | 90 | | Accessibility | 72 | | Senior travelers | 80 | | First-time visitor | 95 | | Photography | 94 |', 4718),
  ('boracay', 35, 'final-travel-agent-verdict', 'FINAL TRAVEL AGENT VERDICT', NULL, NULL, 'Best for: Beach lovers, sunset seekers, water sports enthusiasts, luxury resort goers, nightlife fans, and social travelers looking for ultra-fine powdery white sand, turquoise swimming waters, high-wind kiteboarding, and vibrant beachfront dining. Best duration: 3 to 4 days for a complete Boracay stay to cover White Beach stations, island-hopping tours, water sports, and sunset sailing; or 8 to 12 days when combining with other Visayan and Palawan destinations like Cebu, Bohol, or El Nido. Best season: November to May (Amihan dry season, offering calm seas along White Beach, clear sunny skies, and optimal conditions for swimming and paraw sailing); June to October (Habagat wet season) brings onshore winds, occasional rain, and shifts main water activity setups to Bulabog Beach. Best stay: Multi-station or resort-focused split—2 to 3 nights in Station 1 (e.g., Discovery Shores or Shangri-La Boracay) for quiet, wide stretches of powdery sand and luxury beachfront amenities; paired with 1 to 2 nights near Station 2 or Bulabog Beach for direct access to D’Mall dining, water sports, and social nightlife. Best transport: Direct commercial flights into Caticlan / Godofredo P. Ramos Airport (MPH) for minimal transfer times; short private van and 10-minute speedboats or outrigger ferries from Caticlan Jetty Port to the island; and eco-friendly electric tricycles (e-trikes) for effortless transfers between island stations. Must-do: Avoid: Biggest advantage: World-renowned beach infrastructure—White Beach features 4 kilometers of ultra-fine, non-heating white sand and calm, crystal-clear shallow waters, paired with a walkable, fully developed resort and dining promenade. Biggest disadvantage: High peak-season tourist density and strict environmental regulations that limit some traditional beachfront structures and spontaneous activities. Overall destination score: **91/100**', 4719),
  ('boracay', 36, 'data-quality', 'DATA QUALITY', NULL, NULL, 'information_completeness: 93/100 last_updated: 2026-08-31 last_verified: NOT_LIVE_VERIFIED verified_by: TRAVEL_ENGINE_INITIAL_DATASET sources: IMPORTANT: Prices, opening hours, schedules, visa requirements, availability, accessibility and operational conditions must NOT be treated as permanently valid from this document. These must be sourced from structured, refreshable data.', 4720),
  ('cebu', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Dry Peak Season & Cool Winds', NULL, 'months: December–February weather: Warm and pleasant (24–31°C) with calm blue waters, minimal rainfall, and comfortable breezes brought by the Northeast Monsoon (*Amihan*). crowd_level: HIGH price_level: HIGH overall_score: 90–96 recommended: true reason: Ideal conditions for island hopping, beach relaxing, and outdoor exploration throughout Mactan and Moalboal. January brings the massive Sinulog Festival, drawing hundreds of thousands of visitors to Cebu City, making advance accommodation and transport bookings essential.', 4721),
  ('cebu', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Hot Dry Season & Summer Peak', NULL, 'months: March–May weather: Hot and sunny (26–33°C) with low rainfall, clear skies, and calm sea conditions perfect for water sports. crowd_level: HIGH price_level: HIGH overall_score: 88–94 recommended: true reason: Excellent period for underwater visibility—ideal for scuba diving in Malapascua, swimming with whale sharks in Oslob, and canyoneering in Badian. Easter holidays (Holy Week) bring heavy domestic tourism rushes to Bantayan Island and coastal resorts.', 4722),
  ('cebu', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Southwest Monsoon Transition Season', NULL, 'months: June–August weather: Hot and humid (25–32°C) with short, heavy afternoon rain showers or scattered thunderstorms driven by the Southwest Monsoon (*Habagat*). crowd_level: MEDIUM price_level: MEDIUM overall_score: 72–80 recommended: true reason: Good option for budget-conscious travelers as resort rates drop and crowds diminish. While rain showers occur, sunny mornings are common, allowing scheduled morning activities like canyoneering and snorkeling to proceed smoothly.', 4723),
  ('cebu', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Rainy & Typhoon shoulder Season', NULL, 'months: September–November weather: Warm and humid (24–31°C) with frequent rainfall and an increased chance of tropical typhoons passing through the broader region. crowd_level: LOW price_level: LOW overall_score: 58–68 recommended: false reason: The wettest stretch of the year. Rough seas can lead to coast guard cancellations for boat transfers to offshore destinations like Bantayan or Camotes Islands, and heavy rains can render canyoneering trails at Kawasan Falls temporarily unsafe.', 4724),
  ('cebu', 10, 'budget-strategy', 'BUDGET STRATEGY', NULL, NULL, 'Where saving money is not recommended:', 4725),
  ('cebu', 18, 'family-travel', 'FAMILY TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'child_friendly_score: 86 best_ages: Rules:', 4726),
  ('cebu', 19, 'honeymoon-travel', 'HONEYMOON TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'Best areas: Mactan Island & Punta Engaño: best for high-end coastal luxury, world-class resort pampering, and effortless accessibility; stay in 5-star beachfront resorts offering oceanfront villas, private infinity pools, signature overwater dining, and holistic couples'' spa sanctuaries just minutes from the international airport. Sumilon Island & Oslob Coast: best for exclusive eco-luxury, crystal-clear marine sanctuaries, and intimate island escapes; stay at a private island resort featuring secluded villas with plunge pools, shifting white sandbars, and direct access to sunset snorkeling and private beach picnics. Bantayan Island & Santa Fe: best for laid-back barefoot romance, wide stretches of powdery sand, and quiet coastal charm; choose boutique beachfront villas to enjoy slow-paced days, private sunset walks along serene shores, and candlelit seafood dinners away from crowded commercial hubs. Malapascua Island & North Cebu: best for secluded tropical tranquility, vibrant diving, and unpretentious luxury; head north to boutique beach hideaways for intimate cliffside cocktails, tranquil stargazing, and private boat excursions to untouched white sandbars like Kalanggaman. Honeymoon rules: Charter a private outrigger boat or private yacht for day trips to Moalboal, Sumilon, or Island Hopping around Mactan to explore marine sanctuaries on your own schedule and avoid crowded tour groups. Arrange private, air-conditioned resort transfers and fast-craft ferry tickets in advance when traveling to offshore islands like Bantayan or Malapascua to ensure a seamless, stress-free journey between destinations. Reserve private beachfront sunset dinners, couples'' hydrotherapy spa treatments, and private sunset sailing cruises early—especially during peak dry season—to secure prime reservations and secluded setups.', 4727),
  ('cebu', 20, 'luxury-travel', 'LUXURY TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'luxury_score: 86 Best-value luxury pattern Book a high-end beachfront resort on Mactan Island or Punta Engaño—such as Shangri-La Mactan, Crimson Resort and Spa, or Plantation Bay—featuring private oceanfront villas, private plunge pools, and dedicated butler service. Arrange private VIP chauffeured transfers directly from Mactan-Cebu International Airport (CEB) or private chartered speedboats straight to your coastal sanctuary, bypassing public transport routes in complete comfort. Pair your stay with elite private additions, such as custom-chartered luxury speedboats or yachts for private island hopping around Mactan and Sumilon, secluded sandbar dining setups, and private guided dive expeditions. Indulge in exclusive culinary experiences, including private multi-course seafood tasting menus served under the stars on private beaches, sunset champagne cruises along the coastline, and custom wellness retreats at world-class beachfront spas. Luxury rules: Book private oceanfront villas or luxury suites along Mactan Island, Badian, or Sumilon Island to enjoy breathtaking sea views, private beaches, and top-tier hospitality. Utilize private yacht charters and private driver-guided SUVs to explore Cebu’s marine sanctuaries and waterfalls without adhering to rigid shared tour schedules or crowded joiner vans. Combine high-end marine adventures—such as private scuba diving or canyoneering excursions—with holistic hydrotherapy spa treatments and private beach barbecues for a balanced luxury escape. Reserve luxury resort villas, private boat charters, and executive vehicle transfers several months in advance to secure top availability during the peak dry season (December through April).', 4728),
  ('cebu', 21, 'adventure', 'ADVENTURE', NULL, NULL, 'adventure_score: 98 Cebu is the ultimate tropical adventure capital of the Philippines, offering a thrill-packed terrain that ranges from soaring jagged mountain peaks to deep river canyons and world-renowned marine ecosystems. Thrill-seekers can leap off massive waterfalls into turquoise pools, swim alongside thousands of shimmering ocean marine creatures, scale sharp limestone ridges for panoramic sea views, and dive through deep ocean walls to encounter pelagic thresher sharks. Whether navigating river rapids or trekking backcountry trails, Cebu provides an unparalleled spectrum of high-adrenaline outdoor excursions. Top experiences: Recommended areas: Best for:', 4729),
  ('cebu', 22, 'senior-travel', 'SENIOR TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'senior_suitability: 75 walking_intensity: MEDIUM (can be customized to LOW by utilizing private air-conditioned vehicle transfers, choosing beachfront resorts with elevators or ground-floor rooms, and utilizing golf carts or shuttles within larger resort properties) Cebu offers senior travelers a rich blend of historic charm, cultural landmarks, and world-class coastal beauty. While certain adventure hubs involve rugged terrain and stepped entries, mature visitors can easily explore the island at a comfortable, leisurely pace with thoughtful planning. By flying directly into Mactan-Cebu International Airport, arranging pre-booked private driver transfers, staying at self-contained 5-star beachfront resorts in Mactan, and opting for gentle private boat charters, senior travelers can experience Cebu''s marine and historical attractions safely, comfortably, and stress-free. Rules: Prefer: Avoid:', 4730),
  ('cebu', 23, 'accessibility', 'ACCESSIBILITY', NULL, NULL, 'wheelchair_accessibility: PARTIAL_TO_GOOD depending on attraction and transport public_transport_accessibility: VARIABLE hotel_accessibility: MUST_BE_VERIFIED_PER_HOTEL attraction_accessibility: MUST_BE_VERIFIED_PER_ATTRACTION Rule: Never infer accessibility from destination-level accessibility. Each hotel and attraction must carry its own accessibility data.', 4731),
  ('cebu', 24, 'food', 'FOOD', NULL, NULL, 'food_score: 95 Cebu is widely recognized as the undisputed culinary capital of the Central Visayas, world-renowned for its legendary roasted pork, rich Spanish-influenced heritage dishes, and vibrant coastal seafood culture. From bustling open-air night markets and century-old local eateries to upscale harborfront dining and inventive modern Filipino bistros, Cebu delivers an unforgettable, flavor-packed gastronomic journey. Food experiences: Best for: Recommended areas:', 4732),
  ('cebu', 25, 'shopping', 'SHOPPING', NULL, NULL, 'shopping_score: 88 Shopping in Cebu offers a dynamic blend of massive modern mega-malls, world-renowned local artisanal workshops, vibrant public street markets, and high-end retail districts. Unlike smaller island destinations, Cebu is a premier commercial hub in the Philippines, providing everything from international luxury brands and tech electronics to hand-crafted musical instruments and world-famous edible souvenirs. Best buys: Prefer: Avoid: Best for:', 4733),
  ('cebu', 26, 'nightlife', 'NIGHTLIFE', NULL, NULL, 'nightlife_level: 82 Nightlife in Cebu is energetic, diverse, and heavily anchored in vibrant city centers, high-energy mega-clubs, and elevated rooftop lounges. Rather than quiet beach bars, the region''s main evening scene takes place within Metro Cebu''s urban heartbeat—ranging from late-night dining and craft cocktail spots in IT Park to sprawling dance clubs, open-air bar clusters, and panoramic mountain-view lounges in Busay. Best for: Prefer: Avoid: Best evening areas:', 4734),
  ('cebu', 28, 'sample-itinerary-patterns', 'SAMPLE ITINERARY PATTERNS', 'HALF-DAY – EXPRESS HISTORIC CEBU CITY HIGHLIGHTS', NULL, 'Morning / Afternoon: Pickup from your central Cebu City hotel or meet at the historic district core → Walk through the historic Plaza Sugbo to view **Magellan''s Cross**, housed inside a stone chapel marking the introduction of Christianity to the Philippines in 1521 → Step inside the adjacent **Basilica Minore del Santo Niño**, the country''s oldest Roman Catholic church, to observe local devotees and the venerated Santo Niño statuette → Take a brief stroll to **Fort San Pedro**, exploring the 18th-century Spanish stone triangular bastion and its quiet inner courtyard gardens → Drive through the historic Parian district to tour the **Yap-Sandiego Ancestral House**, marveling at centuries-old coral stone walls and hardwood architecture → Conclude with a warm plate of authentic Cebuano *lechon* at a nearby local restaurant before returning to your hotel or airport drop-off', 4735),
  ('cebu', 28, 'sample-itinerary-patterns', 'SAMPLE ITINERARY PATTERNS', '1 DAY – MOALBOAL SARDINE RUN & KAWASAN FALLS CANYONEERING', NULL, 'Morning: Early morning pickup (approx. 5:00 AM) from Cebu City or Mactan in an air-conditioned private vehicle, driving southwest toward Moalboal → Arrive at Panagsama Beach, gear up with a mask and snorkel, and wade straight off the shore into the turquoise ocean → Swim alongside the world-famous **Moalboal Sardine Run**, watching millions of shimmering sardines form mesmerizing bait balls alongside resident sea turtles → Take a brief 30-minute transfer south to Badian for safety briefing, helmet fitting, and harness gearing for Kawasan Falls Afternoon: Begin your high-adrenaline **Kawasan Canyoneering** adventure, trekking, swimming, and sliding down natural rock formations into clear river pools → Test your courage with optional cliff jumps ranging from 3 to 12 meters into deep turquoise river basins framed by lush jungle canyons → Reach the final tier of Kawasan Falls to celebrate with a traditional Filipino buffet lunch of grilled meats, seafood, and fresh tropical fruits near the tumbling cascades Evening: Doff your gear, change into dry clothes, and relax on your private drive back across the central mountain range toward Metro Cebu → Arrive in Cebu City by late evening for a relaxed dinner at Sugbo Mercado in IT Park, sampling local street food and fresh smoothies', 4736),
  ('cebu', 28, 'sample-itinerary-patterns', 'SAMPLE ITINERARY PATTERNS', '2 DAYS – ULTIMATE CEBU ADVENTURE & BANTAYAN BEACH ESCAPE', 'adventure', 'Day 1: Early morning departure from Cebu City to Moalboal for morning snorkeling with the Sardine Run and sea turtles along the Panagsama reef wall → Transfer to Badian for full-afternoon river canyoneering through Kawasan Falls, ending with cliff jumps and a riverfront lunch → Drive to the central mountain peaks of Dalaguete to catch the late afternoon light over the dramatic jagged limestone peaks of **Osmeña Peak** → Head back toward Metro Cebu for an evening seafood dinner and overnight stay near Mactan or the city center Day 2: Early morning transfer north to Hagnaya Port (~3.5 hours) and board the express passenger ferry across the azure sea to **Bantayan Island** → Check into your beachfront resort in Santa Fe, rent a motor scooter, and head straight to the powdery white sands of **Kota Beach and Sandbar** → Spend the afternoon exploring the natural subterranean swimming hole at Ogtong Cave or walking through the Obo-ob Mangrove Garden boardwalks → Enjoy fresh grilled scallops, garlic butter shrimp, and ice-cold San Miguel beers at a casual beachside bistro in Santa Fe as the sun sets over the Visayan Sea', 4737),
  ('cebu', 28, 'sample-itinerary-patterns', 'SAMPLE ITINERARY PATTERNS', 'COMBINED DAY TRIP – UPLAND BUSAY ESCAPE & SUNSET SKYLINE VIEWS', NULL, 'Morning: Morning pickup in Cebu City and drive up the winding Transcentral Highway into the cool, breezy mountain district of Busay → Arrive at **Sirao Flower Garden** (the "Little Amsterdam of Cebu"), strolling through vibrant terraced gardens, giant hand sculptures, and colorful celosia blooms → Drive further uphill to the Roman-inspired **Temple of Leah**, exploring its massive stone columns, lion statues, and grand plaza built as a shrine of devotion → Stop for a rustic mountain lunch at a hillside café, savoring hot native chicken soup (*tinola*) and fresh mangoes paired with panoramic valley views Afternoon: Head to the **Taoist Temple** in Beverly Hills, climbing the 81 steps representing the 81 chapters of Taoist scriptures to admire Chinese architecture and city views → Drive down to the city for afternoon shopping or a quick coffee break in the modern lifestyle precinct of Cebu IT Park Evening: Ascend back toward the mountain ridgeline as twilight approaches to visit the newly renovated **Tops Lookout** → Take in a breathtaking 180-degree panoramic sunset view as the city lights of Metro Cebu, Mandaue, and Mactan Island begin to sparkle below → Conclude your day with a romantic dinner of Spanish-Filipino tapas and fine wine at *La Vie in the Sky* before returning down to the city core', 4738),
  ('cebu', 29, '12-day-13-night-el-nido-honeymoon-itinerary', '12-day, 13-night El Nido honeymoon itinerary', NULL, NULL, 'Day 01: Arrival PPS Arrival at Puerto Princesa Airport (PPS) and meet and greet. Transfer to hotel, check in, and relax. Evening free for leisure. Overnight stay in PPS. Day 02: Under Ground River Tour + El Nido Transfer Breakfast at hotel. Pick up for Underground River Tour with picnic lunch at Sabang Wharf. Enjoy the Underground River Cave Exploration experience (admiring stalagmites and stalactites formed over thousands of years) with picnic lunch included. Proceed to El Nido by road on a private basis (~6 hours drive). *NOTE: Arrival in El Nido may be late (around 10:00 PM – 11:00 PM) following the full day tour and transfer.* Check in at resort. Overnight in El Nido. Day 03: EL NIDO ISLAND HOPPING TOUR A Breakfast at hotel. Proceed for Island Hopping Tour A with local beach lunch included. Visit Big Lagoon, Small Lagoon, Secret Lagoon, Shimizu Island, and Seven Commandos Beach. Return to El Nido town. Overnight in El Nido. Day 04: EL NIDO ISLAND HOPPING TOUR (TOUR C) Breakfast at hotel. Proceed for Island Hopping Tour C with local lunch. Visit Secret Beach, Hidden Beach, Helicopter Island, Talisay Beach, and premier marine snorkeling areas. Return to hotel. Overnight in El Nido. Day 05: FLIGHT TO BORACAY Breakfast at the hotel. Check out and transfer to airport for your flight to Boracay (via Lio Airport or PPS). Arrive in Boracay, transfer to resort, and check in. Evening free for romantic strolls along White Beach. Overnight in Boracay. Day 06: BORACAY ISLAND HOPPING TOUR After breakfast, proceed for an Island Hopping Tour on SIC basis. Explore Puka Shell Beach for swimming, photo opportunities, and cricket market shopping. Depart Puka Beach to visit Crystal Cove Island. Return to boat station with buffet lunch included during the tour. Overnight stay in Boracay. Day 07: BORACAY SUNSET CRUISE Breakfast at the hotel. Morning at leisure for relaxing on the beach or resort spa treatments. Afternoon proceed for a classic Boracay Sunset Cruise around 3:00 PM. Return to hotel. Overnight in Boracay. Day 08: TRANSFER TO CEBU Breakfast at the hotel. Check out of hotel and transfer to airport for your flight to Cebu. Arrival in Cebu, transfer to hotel, and check in. Overnight stay in Cebu. Day 09: CEBU CITY TOUR Breakfast at the hotel. Proceed for a comprehensive Cebu City Tour covering top attractions: Temple of Leah, La Vie Parisienne, Heritage Park, Yap-San Diego Ancestral House, Fort San Pedro, Magellan''s Cross, Basilica Minore del Santo Niño, Tops Lookout (for night viewing of the metropolitan area), CCLEX Bridge, and 10,000 Roses Cafe. Return to hotel. Overnight in Cebu. Day 10: OSLOB WHALE SHARK WATCHING & KAWASAN WATERFALLS Early morning (around 3:00 AM) departure for Oslob Whale Shark watching and Kawasan Waterfalls canyoneering. Arrive in Oslob for the whale shark encounter (hotel provides packed breakfast). Proceed to Badian for Kawasan Falls (bamboo raft view and turquoise waters) and enjoy the thrilling Canyoneering activity. Return to hotel. Overnight in Cebu. Day 11: MACTAN ISLAND HOPPING TOUR Breakfast at the hotel. Pick-up around 7:00 AM for Mactan Island Hopping. Destinations include: Return to Cebu hotel. Overnight in Cebu. Day 12: BOHOL COUNTRYSIDE TOUR Breakfast at the hotel. Pick up from hotel for full-day Bohol Countryside Tour (via fast ferry). Destinations include: Return via ferry to Cebu hotel. Overnight in Cebu. Day 13: DEPARTURE CEBU Breakfast at the hotel. Check out of hotel and transfer to Mactan-Cebu International Airport (CEB) for your onwards international flight home.', 4739),
  ('cebu', 30, '13-day-12-night-family-itinerary', '13-Day / 12 -Night Family Itinerary', NULL, NULL, 'Day 01: Arrival PPS Day 02: Underground River Tour + El Nido Transfer Day 03: EL NIDO ISLAND HOPPING TOUR A Day 04: EL NIDO ISLAND HOPPING TOUR C Day 05: FLIGHT TO BORACAY Day 06: BORACAY ISLAND HOPPING TOUR Day 07: BORACAY SUNSET CRUISE Day 08: TRANSFER TO CEBU Day 09: CEBU CITY TOUR Day 10: OSLOB WHALE SHARK WATCHING & KAWASAN WATERFALLS Day 11: MACTAN ISLAND HOPPING TOUR Day 12: BOHOL COUNTRYSIDE DAY TOUR Day 13: DEPARTURE CEBU', 4740),
  ('cebu', 31, '13-days-12-nights-luxury-itinerary', '13 Days 12 Nights Luxury Itinerary', NULL, NULL, 'Day 01: ARRIVAL PUERTO PRINCESA Welcome to Palawan! Upon arriving at El Nido Airport (ENI), your private luxury chauffeur will greet you in the arrivals terminal and transfer you to your hotel (such as Best Western Plus The Ivywall Hotel or similar upgraded luxury suites). Check in to your Deluxe Room and take the evening to relax by the pool or indulge in fine local dining. Overnight stay in Puerto Princesa. Day 02: UNDERGROUND RIVER TOUR & SCENIC EL NIDO TRANSFER Begin your day with a gourmet breakfast at the hotel before departing for the world-renowned Puerto Princesa Subterranean River National Park, a UNESCO World Heritage Site. Board your private boat at Sabang Wharf for an immersive Underground River Cave Exploration, admiring the towering stalactites and stalagmites formed over thousands of years. A private picnic lunch is served by the shore. Following the tour, relax in your private vehicle during a scenic 6-hour overland transfer north to El Nido. Check in to your resort (such as El Nido Garden Resort, Pangulasian Island, or similar premier beach resort) for a well-deserved rest. Overnight in El Nido. Day 03: EL NIDO ISLAND HOPPING TOUR A After breakfast, embark on a private outrigger yacht charter for the iconic Island Hopping Tour A across Bacuit Bay. Strap on a life vest and paddle a kayak through the calm, emerald passageways of the Big Lagoon, step through the limestone opening into the secluded Secret Lagoon, and visit Shimizu Island and Seven Commandos Beach. A delicious beachside seafood and local barbecue lunch is freshly prepared and served on the island sands. Return to the resort by late afternoon to enjoy sunset drinks along the shore. Overnight in El Nido. Day 04: EL NIDO ISLAND HOPPING TOUR C Enjoy breakfast before setting sail on Island Hopping Tour C to explore Bacuit Bay''s outer island sanctuaries. Swim through a hidden underwater tunnel to reach the legendary Secret Beach, wade onto the pristine shore of Hidden Beach framed by towering jagged cliffs, take photos of Helicopter Island''s unique silhouette, and snorkel along vibrant coral reefs off Talisay Beach. A gourmet grilled lunch is served on the beach during the tour. Return to your resort for a relaxed evening. Overnight in El Nido. Day 05: FLIGHT TO BORACAY Savor breakfast at the hotel before transferring to Lio Airport (ENI) or Puerto Princesa for your domestic flight to Caticlan (Boracay). Upon arrival, enjoy a seamless private land and speedboat transfer to your luxury beachfront sanctuary (such as Boracay Mandarin Bay Resort and Spa or Crimson Resort & Spa). Check in to your Premier Suite and spend the evening at leisure, enjoying a barefoot stroll along White Beach or sampling beachfront mixology. Overnight in Boracay. Day 06: BORACAY ISLAND HOPPING TOUR Start the day with a lavish beachfront breakfast, then board your outrigger boat for a island hopping excursion around Boracay''s sparkling coastline. Stop at Puka Shell Beach for swimming, picturesque coastal photos, and local shell markets before continuing to the private shores of Crystal Cove Island. Enjoy a freshly prepared buffet lunch included during the tour before returning to Station 1 or 2. Spend your late afternoon swimming in the turquoise waters. Overnight in Boracay. Day 07: BORACAY SUNSET CRUISE Enjoy a lazy morning with breakfast at your own pace and a free day to relax by the infinity pool, visit a luxury spa, or enjoy watersports along White Beach. At 3:00 PM, transfer to the beachfront to board your private sunset cruise. Sail along Boracay''s world-famous coastline with drinks and light snacks while watching the golden sun dip behind the ocean horizon. Return to the resort for an evening at leisure. Overnight in Boracay. Day 08: TRANSFER TO CEBU Following breakfast, check out of your hotel and take a private speedboat and land transfer to Caticlan Airport for your domestic flight to Cebu. Arriving at Mactan-Cebu International Airport (CEB), your private chauffeur will take you to your hotel (such as BAI Hotel Cebu or NUSTAR Resort and Casino). Check in to your Deluxe Room and spend the evening relaxing or dining at one of the hotel''s premier restaurants. Overnight in Cebu. Day 09: CEBU CITY & HIGHLANDS HERITAGE TOUR After breakfast, depart on a comprehensive tour showcasing Cebu’s rich historic heart and picturesque mountain vantage points. Visit the majestic Greek-inspired Temple of Leah, stroll through the vibrant floral terraces of Sirao Garden or 10,000 Roses, and take in sweeping city skyline vistas from Tops Lookout. Return to the historic center to explore Fort San Pedro, Magellan''s Cross, the Basilica Minore del Santo Niño, the Heritage of Cebu Monument, and the Yap-Sandiego Ancestral House. Stop by La Vie Parisienne or cross the iconic CCLEX Bridge before returning to your hotel. Overnight in Cebu. Day 10: OSLOB WHALE SHARK ENCOUNTER & KAWASAN FALLS CANYONEERING An early 3:00 AM private departure takes you south to Oslob for an unforgettable early-morning marine encounter (a packed breakfast is provided by your hotel). Swim alongside the gentle giants during your Oslob Whale Shark Watching experience. Afterward, travel across to Badian for an adrenaline-filled Canyoneering adventure through lush jungle canyons, ending at the breathtaking turquoise pools of Kawasan Falls, where you can ride a bamboo raft under the cascading waters. Return to your hotel in the evening for rest. Overnight in Cebu. Day 11: MACTAN ISLAND HOPPING & MARINE SANCTUARY TOUR Enjoy a 7:00 AM pickup for a private island-hopping cruise across the clear waters of the Hilutungan Channel. Snorkel through vibrant coral gardens teeming with tropical fish at the Gilutongan Island Marine Sanctuary, visit the peaceful shores of Caohagan Island to sample local seaside treats, and walk along the iconic scenic wooden boardwalk of Nalusuan Island. A fresh seafood lunch is served island-style before returning to your Cebu hotel by mid-afternoon. Overnight in Cebu. Day 12: BOHOL COUNTRYSIDE DAY TOUR Following breakfast, take a fast ferry crossing or private charter to Bohol for a countryside heritage tour. Visit the Blood Compact Shrine and the historic stone structure of Baclayon Church before driving through the lush canopy of the Bilar Man-Made Mahogany Forest. View native wildlife at the exotic Python & Butterfly Sanctuary and observe the world''s smallest primates up close at the Tarsier Conservation Area. Conclude your tour gazing over the world-famous Chocolate Hills viewdeck. Return by ferry to your Cebu hotel in the evening. Overnight in Cebu. Day 13: DEPARTURE CEBU Enjoy a final breakfast at your hotel before checking out. Your private chauffeur will transfer you to Mactan-Cebu International Airport (CEB) in time to check in for your onward international flight home, completing an extraordinary 13-day luxury Philippine island getaway.', 4741),
  ('cebu', 32, 'travel-agent-insights', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS', 'What inexperienced planners often do wrong', NULL, '', 4742),
  ('cebu', 32, 'travel-agent-insights', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS', 'What an experienced planner does differently', NULL, '', 4743),
