  ('cebu', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', NULL, NULL, 'IF: `trip_length <= 0.5 days` THEN: Choose a focused historic walking loop in **Cebu City''s Parian and Plaza Sugbo district**, taking photos at **Magellan''s Cross**, stepping inside the ancient **Basilica Minore del Santo Niño**, taking a brief walk to **Fort San Pedro**, and enjoying a plate of authentic Cebuano *lechon* at a nearby restaurant before departing toward Mactan-Cebu International Airport. Reason: Half-day layovers require maximum transit efficiency near the city center; focusing on the compact historic core delivers centuries of Filipino heritage, iconic religious landmarks, and celebrated local cuisine without risking missed flight connections. IF: `trip_length == 1 day` THEN: Take an early-morning transfer southwest to **Moalboal** to snorkel alongside the world-famous **Sardine Run** and sea turtles off Panagsama Beach, head to **Badian** for a full afternoon of adrenaline-fueled river canyoneering through **Kawasan Falls**, and return to **Metro Cebu** in the evening for street food at **Sugbo Mercado** in IT Park. Reason: A single full day allows energetic travelers to experience Cebu''s most famous natural water adventures—massive sardine bait balls and turquoise river canyoneering—in one action-packed loop. IF: `trip_length >= 2 days` THEN: Spend day one exploring the natural marine wall at **Moalboal** (Sardine Run) and river canyoneering at **Kawasan Falls**, followed by a scenic evening drive; spend day two discovering Cebu''s urban highlights (**Magellan''s Cross**, **Basilica del Santo Niño**) before ascending into the cool **Busay Hills** for **Temple of Leah**, **Sirao Flower Garden**, and sunset skyline views at **Tops Lookout**. Reason: Multi-day stays allow travelers to balance Cebu''s world-class marine and river adventures in the south with its rich cultural heritage and scenic mountain highland views overlooking the city. IF: `trip_type == FIRST_TIME_VISITOR` THEN: Focus on the ultimate island highlights—swimming with the **Moalboal Sardine Run**, canyoneering down **Kawasan Falls**, touring historic landmarks (**Magellan''s Cross**, **Basilica Minore del Santo Niño**), exploring the mountain sights of **Busay** (**Temple of Leah**, **Sirao Garden**), and dining on authentic **Cebu lechon**. Reason: Combining Cebu''s iconic marine ecosystems, thrill-seeker river canyons, colonial Spanish heritage, and mountain panoramic viewpoints delivers a complete first-time overview of the province. IF: `trip_type == HONEYMOON` THEN: Book a private oceanfront villa at a luxury resort on **Mactan Island** or **Bantayan Island**, arrange private sunset yacht charters across the Mactan Channel, indulge in couples'' spa treatments in open-air garden pavilions, and enjoy romantic mountain-top dinners at *La Vie in the Sky* in **Busay**. Reason: Pairing coastal beach resort luxury with private island charters, elevated mountain skyline dining, and secluded tropical sandbars creates an unforgettable romantic getaway. IF: `traveler_type == FAMILY` THEN: Stay at family-friendly beach resorts along **Mactan Island** with private lagoons and kids'' clubs, take accessible day trips to **Sirao Flower Garden** and **Temple of Leah** in Busay, enjoy gentle boat rides and shallow snorkeling at **Hilutungan Marine Sanctuary**, and dine at family-friendly food halls like **Sugbo Mercado**. Reason: Gentle beach access, resort amenities, child-friendly mountain gardens, and easily accessible marine sanctuaries keep children safe and entertained without physical strain. IF: `traveler_type == LUXURY` THEN: Book 5-star oceanfront suites at top-tier Mactan resorts like *Shangri-La Mactan* or *Jpark Island Resort*, charter private speedboats or luxury yachts for island hopping around the Olango Reef Flat, arrange helicopter transfers to island resorts, and enjoy private chef dining overlooking the Visayan Sea. Reason: Exclusive resort amenities, private maritime transport, and dedicated concierge services eliminate travel friction while delivering high-end comfort across island and marine settings. IF: `traveler_type == BUDGET` THEN: Stay in central hostels or budget guesthouses around **Cebu IT Park** or **Moalboal (Panagsama Beach)**, take local Ceres buses or shared vans across the island, join shared group tours for **Kawasan Canyoneering**, visit swimmable public stretches like **Kota Beach** in Bantayan, and dine at local *carinderias* and night markets. Reason: Cebu offers an extensive network of affordable public buses, cheap street-food markets, budget guesthouses, and accessible shore-entry snorkeling spots suitable for modest budgets. IF: `traveler_interest == NATURE` THEN: Explore the marine biodiversity at **Moalboal Reef Wall** and **Hilutungan Marine Sanctuary**, hike the dramatic jagged limestone peaks of **Osmeña Peak** in Dalaguete, explore subterranean waters in **Ogtong Cave**, and stroll through the **Obo-ob Mangrove Eco-Park** on Bantayan Island. Reason: Cebu features diverse natural eco-systems ranging from high-altitude karst mountain peaks and underground caves to dense mangrove forests and thriving coral reef walls. IF: `traveler_interest == FOOD` THEN: Map out an iconic Cebuano culinary trail, sampling world-famous roasted **Cebu Lechon** (at *Rico''s* or *House of Lechon*), fresh seafood *Kinilaw*, sweet **Carcar chicharon**, herbal *Pochero* stew, and local street stalls at **Sugbo Mercado** in IT Park. Reason: Cebu is celebrated as the culinary capital of the Visayas, famous for producing the Philippines'' best roasted pig, fresh seafood ceviche, and a bustling 24/7 street food culture. IF: `traveler_interest == ADVENTURE` THEN: Combine high-intensity river canyoneering through the limestone canyons of **Kawasan Falls**, scuba diving with thresher sharks off **Malapascua Island**, freediving alongside the **Moalboal Sardine Run**, and trekking across the rugged ridgelines of **Osmeña Peak** and **Casino Peak**. Reason: Cebu is a premier adventure hub, offering world-class shark diving, extreme river jumping, freediving, and high-ridge mountain trekking. IF: `traveler_type == SENIOR` THEN: Stay at accessible, full-service beachfront resorts in **Mactan Island**, take private air-conditioned vehicle tours to historic city landmarks (**Magellan''s Cross**, **Basilica del Santo Niño**) and **Busay mountain viewdecks**, and enjoy flat seaside strolls along **Kota Beach** on Bantayan Island. Reason: Step-free heritage sights, private vehicle transit, accessible beachfront resorts, and gentle mountain gardens allow senior travelers to experience Cebu comfortably without strenuous hiking. IF: `traveler_type == TRANSIT` THEN: Take a 10-to-15 minute taxi from Mactan-Cebu International Airport (CEB) to **Mactan Marina Mall** or **Mactan Newtown**, enjoy a relaxed meal of fresh seafood or Cebuano lechon, grab a coffee at an open-air plaza, and return directly to the terminal. Reason: Proximity between Mactan-Cebu International Airport and adjacent Mactan commercial hubs allows layover travelers to sample local cuisine and tropical atmosphere efficiently without city traffic risks. IF: `trip_length >= 3 days` THEN: Divide your stay between 1 day of historic city sights and **Busay mountain escapes**, 1 day of south Cebu adventures (**Moalboal Sardine Run** and **Kawasan Falls Canyoneering**), and 1-2 days relaxing on the pristine white sandbars of **Bantayan Island** or **Malapascua Island** in the north. Reason: A multi-day itinerary smoothly bridges Cebu''s urban cultural heritage and mountain outlooks with its high-adrenaline southern river canyons and peaceful northern island beaches.', 4745),
  ('cebu', 34, 'destination-scoring', 'DESTINATION SCORING', NULL, NULL, '| Factor | Score | | --- | --- | | Family | 86 | | Honeymoon | 90 | | Luxury | 85 | | Budget | 92 | | Adventure | 98 | | Culture | 85 | | Food | 92 | | Shopping | 82 | | Nightlife | 84 | | Relaxation | 86 | | Nature | 95 | | Accessibility | 60 | | Senior travelers | 72 | | First-time visitor | 90 | | Photography | 96 |', 4746),
  ('cebu', 35, 'final-travel-agent-verdict', 'FINAL TRAVEL AGENT VERDICT', NULL, NULL, 'Best for: Thrill-seekers, marine wildlife enthusiasts, history buffs, scuba divers, canyoning adventurers, and foodies looking for a versatile mix of urban heritage, high-adrenaline outdoor sports, vibrant island hopping, and world-famous regional cuisine. Best duration: 4 to 6 days for a comprehensive Cebu exploration to experience historic landmarks, canyoneering, sardine runs, and island beaches; or 10 to 14 days when expanding into a broader Visayas itinerary incorporating nearby Bohol, Dumaguete, Siquijor, or Boracay. Best season: November to May (the dry season, featuring sunny skies, calm sea conditions, ideal underwater visibility, and optimal safety for canyoneering and trekking); June to October brings monsoon rains, higher river levels, and potential tour cancellations due to rough sea swells or tropical storms. Best stay: Split-stay strategy—2 nights in Cebu City or Busay (e.g., Radisson Blu or NUSTAR Resort) for historical touring, vibrant dining, and nightlife, paired with 2 to 3 nights in a luxury oceanfront resort in Mactan (e.g., Shangri-La Mactan or Plantation Bay) or a coastal hideaway in Moalboal or Bantayan Island for marine adventures and beach relaxation. Best transport: Direct international or domestic flights into Mactan-Cebu International Airport (CEB); private air-conditioned vans or car rentals for long-distance travel down to South Cebu (Badian/Moalboal); grab ride-hailing apps for urban transit in Metro Cebu; and private outrigger boats (*bangkas*) or express ferries for island transfers. Must-do: Avoid: Biggest advantage: Incredible diversity and connectivity—Cebu serves as the ultimate Visayas transit hub, seamlessly blending modern city luxuries and historical landmarks with world-class waterfalls, pelagic dive sites, and island-hopping within short traveling distances. Biggest disadvantage: Traffic congestion along Metro Cebu''s main corridors during peak hours, alongside long overland drive times required to reach major adventure hubs in the far north and south of the island. Overall destination score: **94/100**', 4747),
  ('cebu', 36, 'data-quality', 'DATA QUALITY', NULL, NULL, 'information_completeness: 94/100 last_updated: 2026-08-31 last_verified: NOT_LIVE_VERIFIED verified_by: TRAVEL_ENGINE_INITIAL_DATASET sources: IMPORTANT: Prices, opening hours, schedules, visa requirements, availability, accessibility and operational conditions must NOT be treated as permanently valid from this document. These must be sourced from structured, refreshable data.', 4748),
  ('bohol', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Dry Peak Season & Cool Winds', NULL, 'months: December–February weather: Comfortable and pleasant (24–30°C) with low humidity, calm sea conditions, and gentle breezes brought by the Northeast Monsoon (*Amihan*). crowd_level: HIGH price_level: HIGH overall_score: 92–96 recommended: true reason: Absolute prime weather for countryside tours, island hopping around Panglao and Balicasag, and wildlife spot tours. The dry heat causes the grass on the iconic Chocolate Hills to begin turning brown. Heavy holiday travel (Christmas to Chinese New Year) makes early hotel and resort bookings essential.', 4749),
  ('bohol', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Hot Dry Season & Summer Peak', NULL, 'months: March–May weather: Hot, dry, and sunny (26–34°C) with minimal rainfall, clear blue skies, and ultra-calm, clear waters ideal for underwater visibility. crowd_level: HIGH price_level: HIGH overall_score: 88–94 recommended: true reason: Peak time to see the Chocolate Hills in their famous signature "chocolate-brown" color. Outstanding underwater visibility makes this the best window for diving Balicasag Island marine sanctuaries and paddleboarding on the Loboc River. Holy Week brings massive domestic travel rushes to Panglao Island resorts.', 4750),
  ('bohol', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Southwest Monsoon Transition Season', NULL, 'months: June–August weather: Warm and humid (25–32°C) with scattered, short afternoon rain showers or localized downpours caused by the Southwest Monsoon (*Habagat*). crowd_level: MEDIUM price_level: MEDIUM overall_score: 72–80 recommended: true reason: Excellent period for value travelers as hotel rates soften and popular sites become less crowded. The Chocolate Hills transition into a vibrant lush green hue. Morning hours are typically bright and clear, allowing countryside excursions and Panglao beach outings to go ahead as planned.', 4751),
  ('bohol', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Rainy & Typhoon Shoulder Season', NULL, 'months: September–November weather: Warm and humid (24–31°C) with higher frequency of widespread rainfall, overcast skies, and an elevated risk of regional tropical storms or typhoons. crowd_level: LOW price_level: LOW overall_score: 58–68 recommended: false reason: The wettest period of the year in Bohol. Rougher ocean conditions often lead to Coast Guard suspensions for boat tours to offshore islands like Balicasag and Pamilacan, while heavy inland rains can make cave trails muddy and river cruises less picturesque.', 4752),
  ('bohol', 10, 'budget-strategy', 'BUDGET STRATEGY', NULL, NULL, 'Where saving money is not recommended:', 4753),
  ('bohol', 18, 'family-travel', 'FAMILY TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'child_friendly_score: 86 best_ages: Rules:', 4754),
  ('bohol', 19, 'honeymoon-travel', 'HONEYMOON TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'Best areas: Panglao Island & Alona Cliffside: best for high-end eco-luxury, oceanfront infinity pools, and direct access to tropical marine life; stay in private cliffside villas perched over the Bohol Sea offering personal plunge pools, private beach coves, and fine dining away from busy shorelines. Dauis & Northern Panglao Coast: best for secluded boutique pampering, lush mangrove views, and tranquil wellness retreats; book intimate resort suites set in quiet coastal enclaves featuring private island platforms, overwater dining, and holistic couples'' spa treatments. Anda Peninsula & Eastern Bohol: best for off-the-beaten-path romance, serene powder-white beaches, and untouched natural beauty; escape to private beach sanctuaries along quiet coves to enjoy uncrowded shores, crystal-clear cave pools, and peaceful starlit evenings. Loboc River & Inland Countryside: best for exotic rainforest romance, serene nature escapes, and unique jungle luxury; stay at intimate riverside resorts surrounded by tropical greenery, featuring romantic balcony views over emerald waters, private river cruises, and evening firefly watching. Honeymoon rules: Charter a private outrigger boat or private yacht for early-morning trips to Balicasag Island and Virgin Island to enjoy dolphin watching, snorkeling, and secluded sandbar walks on your own schedule. Book a private, candlelit dinner setup on the beach or a cliffside viewing deck in advance to enjoy fresh seafood and panoramic sunset views over the Bohol Sea in complete privacy. Arrange private, air-conditioned vehicle transfers directly through your resort for seamless airport pickups and hassle-free day trips across the Chocolate Hills and countryside.', 4755),
  ('bohol', 20, 'luxury-travel', 'LUXURY TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'luxury_score: 84 Best-value luxury pattern Book a high-end beachfront resort or private cliffside sanctuary on Panglao Island—such as Amorita Resort, Eskaya Beach Resort & Spa, The Bellevue Resort, or Donatela Resort & Sanctuary—featuring private pool villas, dedicated butler service, and exclusive beach access. Arrange private VIP chauffeured transfers directly from Bohol-Panglao International Airport (TAG) or Tagbilaran Sea Port in a premium SUV or executive van, ensuring a swift and seamless arrival to your resort in complete comfort. Pair your stay with elite private additions, such as custom-chartered luxury speedboats for private dolphin watching and snorkeling around Balicasag and Virgin Islands, scenic helicopter flights over the Chocolate Hills, and bespoke countryside tours. Indulge in exclusive culinary and wellness experiences, including private cliffside seafood tasting menus overlooking the Bohol Sea, sunset champagne cruises along the Panglao coastline, and signature holistic spa retreats in tropical garden cabanas. Luxury rules: Book private oceanfront villas or cliffside suites along Panglao Island to enjoy panoramic sea views, private plunge pools, and top-tier Filipino hospitality. Utilize private speedboat charters and driver-guided executive SUVs to explore Bohol’s marine sanctuaries and inland geological wonders without adhering to rigid shared tour schedules or crowded joiner vans. Combine high-end marine adventures—such as private scuba diving or island hopping—with private beach barbecues, holistic spa treatments, and exclusive eco-tours for a balanced luxury escape. Reserve luxury resort villas, private yacht charters, and executive vehicle transfers several months in advance to secure top availability during the peak dry season (December through April).', 4756),
  ('bohol', 21, 'adventure', 'ADVENTURE', NULL, NULL, 'adventure_score: 88 Bohol is a dynamic eco-adventure haven in the Visayas, offering a diverse array of outdoor thrills set against striking geological wonders, pristine marine sanctuaries, and lush jungle river systems. Adventurers can soar across deep river canyons on high-speed ziplines, plunge into freshwater limestone cave pools, navigate rugged all-terrain trails around iconic geological mounds, and dive down dramatic marine wall drop-offs teeming with sea turtles and vibrant coral reefs. From paddleboarding down emerald jungle rivers to scaling panoramic mountain ridges, Bohol delivers a thrilling spectrum of nature-centric excursions for all skill levels. Top experiences: Recommended areas: Best for:', 4757),
  ('bohol', 22, 'senior-travel', 'SENIOR TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'senior_suitability: 82 walking_intensity: LOW_TO_MEDIUM (can be easily kept to LOW by opting for private air-conditioned vehicle charters, choosing flat beachfront resorts or ground-floor rooms, and taking advantage of gentle, full-service river cruises) Bohol is an exceptional, senior-friendly destination in the Philippines, renowned for its calm environment, gentle eco-tours, and rich cultural heritage. While certain inland viewing decks involve stepped climbs, mature travelers can comfortably explore the island''s iconic sights at a relaxed pace with proper planning. By arriving via Bohol-Panglao International Airport, arranging private driver-guided transfers, staying at self-contained resorts along Panglao or Dumaluan Beach, and enjoying leisurely Loboc River buffet cruises, senior travelers can experience Bohol''s natural and historical wonders safely, smoothly, and without physical strain. Rules: Prefer: Avoid:', 4758),
  ('bohol', 23, 'accessibility', 'ACCESSIBILITY', NULL, NULL, 'wheelchair_accessibility: PARTIAL_TO_GOOD depending on attraction and transport public_transport_accessibility: VARIABLE hotel_accessibility: MUST_BE_VERIFIED_PER_HOTEL attraction_accessibility: MUST_BE_VERIFIED_PER_ATTRACTION Rule: Never infer accessibility from destination-level accessibility. Each hotel and attraction must carry its own accessibility data.', 4759),
  ('bohol', 24, 'food', 'FOOD', NULL, NULL, 'food_score: 88 Bohol offers a delightful, authentic Visayan culinary landscape rooted in sweet local delicacies, fresh ocean-to-table seafood, and comforting eco-resort gastronomy. While less urbanized than neighboring Cebu, Bohol charms visitors with its famous coconut-shell confections, floating river buffet feasts, and vibrant seaside dining hubs along Panglao Island. Food experiences: Best for: Recommended areas:', 4760),
  ('bohol', 25, 'shopping', 'SHOPPING', NULL, NULL, 'shopping_score: 72 Shopping in Bohol centers around charming local handicrafts, authentic sweet delicacies, artisan workshops, and vibrant public markets rather than massive commercial mega-malls. While it lacks sprawling retail complexes, Bohol offers travelers memorable, locally crafted keepsakes and world-famous edible souvenirs that celebrate the island’s rich heritage and natural produce. Best buys: Prefer: Avoid: Best for:', 4761),
  ('bohol', 26, 'nightlife', 'NIGHTLIFE', NULL, NULL, 'nightlife_level: 75 Nightlife in Bohol is vibrant yet laid-back, centered predominantly along the bustling beachfront strips of Panglao Island. Rather than massive multi-story urban mega-clubs, the island’s evening scene is defined by lively oceanfront bars, live acoustic acoustic bands, fire-dancing performances on the sand, cozy craft cocktail lounges, and relaxed late-night beach gatherings under the stars. Best for: Prefer: Avoid: Best evening areas:', 4762),
  ('bohol', 28, 'sample-itinerary-patterns', 'SAMPLE ITINERARY PATTERNS', 'HALF-DAY – EXPRESS HISTORIC TAGBILARAN & BACLAYON HIGHLIGHTS', NULL, 'Morning / Afternoon: Pickup from your Panglao resort or meet at Tagbilaran Sea Port upon arrival → Walk through the historical park to view the **Sandugo (Blood Compact Shrine)** monument, marking the 1565 peace treaty between Spanish explorer Miguel López de Legazpi and Datu Sikatuna → Drive along the scenic coastal road to the historic town of Baclayon to explore the **Baclayon Church & Museum**, one of the oldest coral-stone Catholic churches in the Philippines → Tour the interior museum housing centuries-old religious relics, vestments, and Latin hymnals hand-written on animal parchment → Visit a local artisan workshop to taste and purchase authentic **Calamay**, Bohol''s signature sweet sticky rice treat packed in coconut shells → Conclude with a delicious Visayan lunch overlooking Tagbilaran Bay before returning to your hotel or port drop-off', 4763),
  ('bohol', 28, 'sample-itinerary-patterns', 'SAMPLE ITINERARY PATTERNS', '1 DAY – CLASSIC BOHOL COUNTRYSIDE & CHOCOLATE HILLS TOUR', NULL, 'Morning: Early morning pickup (approx. 8:00 AM) from your Panglao resort or Tagbilaran hotel in an air-conditioned private vehicle, heading inland toward Corella → Arrive at the **Philippine Tarsier Sanctuary** in Corella, taking a quiet guided walking path through the protected forest to spot the world''s smallest primates in their natural habitat → Drive through the lush, emerald canopy of the **Bilar Man-Made Forest**, stopping brief moments for photos along the two-kilometer stretch of mahogany trees → Reach the main viewing deck in Carmen to behold panoramic 360-degree views of the iconic Chocolate Hills, viewing over 1,200 perfectly symmetrical cone-shaped mounds Afternoon: Head down toward Loboc town for a scenic afternoon **Loboc River Cruise**, boarding a covered floating restaurant barge → Enjoy a traditional Filipino buffet lunch of grilled meats, seafood, and fresh tropical fruits while cruising down the emerald river, accompanied by live local acoustic music and cultural dance performances → Stop by the historic **Baclayon Church** and the **Blood Compact Shrine** on your return journey toward the coast Evening: Return to Panglao Island by late afternoon to relax on the beach → Conclude your day with a relaxed beachfront seafood dinner and sunset cocktails along Alona Beach', 4764),
  ('bohol', 28, 'sample-itinerary-patterns', 'SAMPLE ITINERARY PATTERNS', '2 DAYS – ISLAND HOPPING, SEA TURTLES & COUNTRYSIDE ADVENTURE', 'adventure', 'Day 1: Early morning departure (approx. 6:00 AM) from Alona Beach aboard a private or shared outrigger boat to spot wild dolphins leaping in the open waters surrounding Panglao → Cruise toward **Balicasag Island Marine Sanctuary** to gear up with a mask and snorkel, swimming alongside sea turtles and giant schools of fish along the colorful coral drop-off → Stop at the shifting white sandbar of **Virgin Island** to stroll the clear shallow waters and sample fresh sea urchins from local boat vendors → Return to Panglao for lunch, spending the afternoon relaxing on the soft white sands of **Dumaluan Beach** → Enjoy a candlelit seaside dinner and live music along the Alona Beach strip in the evening Day 2: Morning pickup for an action-packed tour through Bohol''s interior countryside highlights → Ride ATVs (all-terrain vehicles) along rugged dirt trails around the base of the Chocolate Hills before heading up to the main observation deck → Visit the protected **Philippine Tarsier Sanctuary** in Corella and drive through the scenic Bilar Man-Made Forest → Enjoy a relaxing floating restaurant buffet lunch along the **Loboc River** → Optional late-afternoon stand-up paddleboarding or ziplining across deep jungle river gorges before driving back to Panglao for your final evening', 4765),
  ('bohol', 28, 'sample-itinerary-patterns', 'SAMPLE ITINERARY PATTERNS', 'COMBINED DAY TRIP – ANDA PENINSULA & EASTERN BOHOL ESCAPE', NULL, 'Morning: Morning pickup from Panglao or Tagbilaran and drive east along the scenic coastal highway toward the quiet Anda Peninsula (~2 hours) → Arrive at the breathtaking **Quinale Beach** in Anda, strolling along its 1.5-kilometer stretch of powdery, uncrowded white sand and turquoise waters → Drive to the famous **Cabagnow Cave Pool**, gearing up for a daring leap into the refreshing subterranean freshwater limestone sinkhole → Visit neighboring natural cave pools like *Tibaw Cave* or *Combento Cave* for a unique cooling dip in crystal-clear cavern basins Afternoon: Enjoy a fresh beachfront seafood lunch at a local coastal resort in Anda town, savoring grilled squid, garlic shrimp, and ice-cold young coconut water → Drive toward the scenic terraces and historic coastal landmarks of Eastern Bohol, taking in unhurried views of rural countryside life Evening: Begin your relaxing drive back toward central Bohol as twilight approaches → Stop along the Abatan or Loboc River for a magical evening **Firefly Watching Boat Tour**, observing thousands of glowing fireflies illuminating the mangrove trees against the night sky → Return to your resort for a peaceful late dinner under the starlit island sky', 4766),
  ('bohol', 29, '12-day-13-night-el-nido-honeymoon-itinerary', '12-day, 13-night El Nido honeymoon itinerary', NULL, NULL, 'Day 01: Arrival PPS Arrival at Puerto Princesa Airport (PPS) and meet and greet. Transfer to hotel, check in, and relax. Evening free for leisure. Overnight stay in PPS. Day 02: Under Ground River Tour + El Nido Transfer Breakfast at hotel. Pick up for Underground River Tour with picnic lunch at Sabang Wharf. Enjoy the Underground River Cave Exploration experience (admiring stalagmites and stalactites formed over thousands of years) with picnic lunch included. Proceed to El Nido by road on a private basis (~6 hours drive). *NOTE: Arrival in El Nido may be late (around 10:00 PM – 11:00 PM) following the full day tour and transfer.* Check in at resort. Overnight in El Nido. Day 03: EL NIDO ISLAND HOPPING TOUR A Breakfast at hotel. Proceed for Island Hopping Tour A with local beach lunch included. Visit Big Lagoon, Small Lagoon, Secret Lagoon, Shimizu Island, and Seven Commandos Beach. Return to El Nido town. Overnight in El Nido. Day 04: EL NIDO ISLAND HOPPING TOUR (TOUR C) Breakfast at hotel. Proceed for Island Hopping Tour C with local lunch. Visit Secret Beach, Hidden Beach, Helicopter Island, Talisay Beach, and premier marine snorkeling areas. Return to hotel. Overnight in El Nido. Day 05: FLIGHT TO BORACAY Breakfast at the hotel. Check out and transfer to airport for your flight to Boracay (via Lio Airport or PPS). Arrive in Boracay, transfer to resort, and check in. Evening free for romantic strolls along White Beach. Overnight in Boracay. Day 06: BORACAY ISLAND HOPPING TOUR After breakfast, proceed for an Island Hopping Tour on SIC basis. Explore Puka Shell Beach for swimming, photo opportunities, and cricket market shopping. Depart Puka Beach to visit Crystal Cove Island. Return to boat station with buffet lunch included during the tour. Overnight stay in Boracay. Day 07: BORACAY SUNSET CRUISE Breakfast at the hotel. Morning at leisure for relaxing on the beach or resort spa treatments. Afternoon proceed for a classic Boracay Sunset Cruise around 3:00 PM. Return to hotel. Overnight in Boracay. Day 08: TRANSFER TO CEBU Breakfast at the hotel. Check out of hotel and transfer to airport for your flight to Cebu. Arrival in Cebu, transfer to hotel, and check in. Overnight stay in Cebu. Day 09: CEBU CITY TOUR Breakfast at the hotel. Proceed for a comprehensive Cebu City Tour covering top attractions: Temple of Leah, La Vie Parisienne, Heritage Park, Yap-San Diego Ancestral House, Fort San Pedro, Magellan''s Cross, Basilica Minore del Santo Niño, Tops Lookout (for night viewing of the metropolitan area), CCLEX Bridge, and 10,000 Roses Cafe. Return to hotel. Overnight in Cebu. Day 10: OSLOB WHALE SHARK WATCHING & KAWASAN WATERFALLS Early morning (around 3:00 AM) departure for Oslob Whale Shark watching and Kawasan Waterfalls canyoneering. Arrive in Oslob for the whale shark encounter (hotel provides packed breakfast). Proceed to Badian for Kawasan Falls (bamboo raft view and turquoise waters) and enjoy the thrilling Canyoneering activity. Return to hotel. Overnight in Cebu. Day 11: MACTAN ISLAND HOPPING TOUR Breakfast at the hotel. Pick-up around 7:00 AM for Mactan Island Hopping. Destinations include: Return to Cebu hotel. Overnight in Cebu. Day 12: BOHOL COUNTRYSIDE TOUR Breakfast at the hotel. Pick up from hotel for full-day Bohol Countryside Tour (via fast ferry). Destinations include: Return via ferry to Cebu hotel. Overnight in Cebu. Day 13: DEPARTURE CEBU Breakfast at the hotel. Check out of hotel and transfer to Mactan-Cebu International Airport (CEB) for your onwards international flight home.', 4767),
  ('bohol', 30, '13-day-12-night-family-itinerary', '13-Day / 12 -Night Family Itinerary', NULL, NULL, 'Day 01: Arrival PPS Day 02: Underground River Tour + El Nido Transfer Day 03: EL NIDO ISLAND HOPPING TOUR A Day 04: EL NIDO ISLAND HOPPING TOUR C Day 05: FLIGHT TO BORACAY Day 06: BORACAY ISLAND HOPPING TOUR Day 07: BORACAY SUNSET CRUISE Day 08: TRANSFER TO CEBU Day 09: CEBU CITY TOUR Day 10: OSLOB WHALE SHARK WATCHING & KAWASAN WATERFALLS Day 11: MACTAN ISLAND HOPPING TOUR Day 12: BOHOL COUNTRYSIDE DAY TOUR Day 13: DEPARTURE CEBU', 4768),
  ('bohol', 31, '13-days-12-nights-luxury-itinerary', '13 Days 12 Nights Luxury Itinerary', NULL, NULL, 'Day 01: ARRIVAL PUERTO PRINCESA Welcome to Palawan! Upon arriving at El Nido Airport (ENI), your private luxury chauffeur will greet you in the arrivals terminal and transfer you to your hotel (such as Best Western Plus The Ivywall Hotel or similar upgraded luxury suites). Check in to your Deluxe Room and take the evening to relax by the pool or indulge in fine local dining. Overnight stay in Puerto Princesa. Day 02: UNDERGROUND RIVER TOUR & SCENIC EL NIDO TRANSFER Begin your day with a gourmet breakfast at the hotel before departing for the world-renowned Puerto Princesa Subterranean River National Park, a UNESCO World Heritage Site. Board your private boat at Sabang Wharf for an immersive Underground River Cave Exploration, admiring the towering stalactites and stalagmites formed over thousands of years. A private picnic lunch is served by the shore. Following the tour, relax in your private vehicle during a scenic 6-hour overland transfer north to El Nido. Check in to your resort (such as El Nido Garden Resort, Pangulasian Island, or similar premier beach resort) for a well-deserved rest. Overnight in El Nido. Day 03: EL NIDO ISLAND HOPPING TOUR A After breakfast, embark on a private outrigger yacht charter for the iconic Island Hopping Tour A across Bacuit Bay. Strap on a life vest and paddle a kayak through the calm, emerald passageways of the Big Lagoon, step through the limestone opening into the secluded Secret Lagoon, and visit Shimizu Island and Seven Commandos Beach. A delicious beachside seafood and local barbecue lunch is freshly prepared and served on the island sands. Return to the resort by late afternoon to enjoy sunset drinks along the shore. Overnight in El Nido. Day 04: EL NIDO ISLAND HOPPING TOUR C Enjoy breakfast before setting sail on Island Hopping Tour C to explore Bacuit Bay''s outer island sanctuaries. Swim through a hidden underwater tunnel to reach the legendary Secret Beach, wade onto the pristine shore of Hidden Beach framed by towering jagged cliffs, take photos of Helicopter Island''s unique silhouette, and snorkel along vibrant coral reefs off Talisay Beach. A gourmet grilled lunch is served on the beach during the tour. Return to your resort for a relaxed evening. Overnight in El Nido. Day 05: FLIGHT TO BORACAY Savor breakfast at the hotel before transferring to Lio Airport (ENI) or Puerto Princesa for your domestic flight to Caticlan (Boracay). Upon arrival, enjoy a seamless private land and speedboat transfer to your luxury beachfront sanctuary (such as Boracay Mandarin Bay Resort and Spa or Crimson Resort & Spa). Check in to your Premier Suite and spend the evening at leisure, enjoying a barefoot stroll along White Beach or sampling beachfront mixology. Overnight in Boracay. Day 06: BORACAY ISLAND HOPPING TOUR Start the day with a lavish beachfront breakfast, then board your outrigger boat for a island hopping excursion around Boracay''s sparkling coastline. Stop at Puka Shell Beach for swimming, picturesque coastal photos, and local shell markets before continuing to the private shores of Crystal Cove Island. Enjoy a freshly prepared buffet lunch included during the tour before returning to Station 1 or 2. Spend your late afternoon swimming in the turquoise waters. Overnight in Boracay. Day 07: BORACAY SUNSET CRUISE Enjoy a lazy morning with breakfast at your own pace and a free day to relax by the infinity pool, visit a luxury spa, or enjoy watersports along White Beach. At 3:00 PM, transfer to the beachfront to board your private sunset cruise. Sail along Boracay''s world-famous coastline with drinks and light snacks while watching the golden sun dip behind the ocean horizon. Return to the resort for an evening at leisure. Overnight in Boracay. Day 08: TRANSFER TO CEBU Following breakfast, check out of your hotel and take a private speedboat and land transfer to Caticlan Airport for your domestic flight to Cebu. Arriving at Mactan-Cebu International Airport (CEB), your private chauffeur will take you to your hotel (such as BAI Hotel Cebu or NUSTAR Resort and Casino). Check in to your Deluxe Room and spend the evening relaxing or dining at one of the hotel''s premier restaurants. Overnight in Cebu. Day 09: CEBU CITY & HIGHLANDS HERITAGE TOUR After breakfast, depart on a comprehensive tour showcasing Cebu’s rich historic heart and picturesque mountain vantage points. Visit the majestic Greek-inspired Temple of Leah, stroll through the vibrant floral terraces of Sirao Garden or 10,000 Roses, and take in sweeping city skyline vistas from Tops Lookout. Return to the historic center to explore Fort San Pedro, Magellan''s Cross, the Basilica Minore del Santo Niño, the Heritage of Cebu Monument, and the Yap-Sandiego Ancestral House. Stop by La Vie Parisienne or cross the iconic CCLEX Bridge before returning to your hotel. Overnight in Cebu. Day 10: OSLOB WHALE SHARK ENCOUNTER & KAWASAN FALLS CANYONEERING An early 3:00 AM private departure takes you south to Oslob for an unforgettable early-morning marine encounter (a packed breakfast is provided by your hotel). Swim alongside the gentle giants during your Oslob Whale Shark Watching experience. Afterward, travel across to Badian for an adrenaline-filled Canyoneering adventure through lush jungle canyons, ending at the breathtaking turquoise pools of Kawasan Falls, where you can ride a bamboo raft under the cascading waters. Return to your hotel in the evening for rest. Overnight in Cebu. Day 11: MACTAN ISLAND HOPPING & MARINE SANCTUARY TOUR Enjoy a 7:00 AM pickup for a private island-hopping cruise across the clear waters of the Hilutungan Channel. Snorkel through vibrant coral gardens teeming with tropical fish at the Gilutongan Island Marine Sanctuary, visit the peaceful shores of Caohagan Island to sample local seaside treats, and walk along the iconic scenic wooden boardwalk of Nalusuan Island. A fresh seafood lunch is served island-style before returning to your Cebu hotel by mid-afternoon. Overnight in Cebu. Day 12: BOHOL COUNTRYSIDE DAY TOUR Following breakfast, take a fast ferry crossing or private charter to Bohol for a countryside heritage tour. Visit the Blood Compact Shrine and the historic stone structure of Baclayon Church before driving through the lush canopy of the Bilar Man-Made Mahogany Forest. View native wildlife at the exotic Python & Butterfly Sanctuary and observe the world''s smallest primates up close at the Tarsier Conservation Area. Conclude your tour gazing over the world-famous Chocolate Hills viewdeck. Return by ferry to your Cebu hotel in the evening. Overnight in Cebu. Day 13: DEPARTURE CEBU Enjoy a final breakfast at your hotel before checking out. Your private chauffeur will transfer you to Mactan-Cebu International Airport (CEB) in time to check in for your onward international flight home, completing an extraordinary 13-day luxury Philippine island getaway.', 4769),
  ('bohol', 32, 'travel-agent-insights', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS', 'What inexperienced planners often do wrong', NULL, '', 4770),
  ('bohol', 32, 'travel-agent-insights', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS', 'What an experienced planner does differently', NULL, '', 4771),
  ('bohol', 32, 'travel-agent-insights', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS', 'Best planning rule', NULL, '', 4772),
  ('bohol', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', NULL, NULL, 'IF: `trip_length <= 0.5 days` THEN: Choose a focused transit loop from Tagbilaran Port or Bohol-Panglao International Airport (TAG) to **Panglao Island**, enjoying a relaxed seaside lunch at **Alona Beach**, taking photos along the powder-white shoreline, sipping fresh coconut water at an open-air beachfront lounge, and returning directly for your departure connection. Reason: Half-day layovers demand quick, frictionless transit; Panglao Island''s immediate proximity to the airport (~10 minutes) provides a stress-free taste of Bohol''s coastal charm without risking missed connections. IF: `trip_length == 1 day` THEN: Embark on an early-morning **Bohol Countryside Tour**, taking photos at the iconic **Chocolate Hills** in Carmen, walking through the lush canopy of the **Bilar Man-Made Forest**, viewing rescued primates at the **Corella Tarsier Sanctuary**, taking a scenic buffet lunch cruise down the **Loboc River**, and stopping at the historic **Baclayon Church** before heading back. Reason: A single full day allows travelers to efficiently cover Bohol''s core geographic highlights—geological wonders, endemic wildlife, river scenery, and Spanish colonial heritage—in one cohesive inland circuit. IF: `trip_length >= 2 days` THEN: Spend day one discovering the central countryside highlights (**Chocolate Hills**, **Tarsier Sanctuary**, and **Loboc River Cruise**); spend day two taking a early-morning outrigger boat trip to **Balicasag Island Marine Sanctuary** for dolphin watching and sea turtle snorkeling, followed by a walk across the shifting sandbar of **Virgin Island (Pungtud Reef)** and an afternoon relaxing on **Dumaluan Beach**. Reason: Multi-day stays allow visitors to seamlessly balance Bohol''s world-famous inland eco-wonders with its thriving marine ecosystems and white-sand beaches. IF: `trip_type == FIRST_TIME_VISITOR` THEN: Focus on the quintessential Bohol combination—touring the **Chocolate Hills**, spotting Philippine tarsiers at the **Corella Tarsier Sanctuary**, taking the **Loboc River Cruise**, snorkeling with sea turtles at **Balicasag Island**, strolling across **Virgin Island Sandbar**, and enjoying sunset drinks along **Alona Beach**. Reason: Combining the island''s iconic geological monuments, rare endemic wildlife, scenic riverways, and premier marine sanctuaries delivers the ultimate first-timer overview of Bohol. IF: `trip_type == HONEYMOON` THEN: Book a private oceanfront pool villa at an exclusive cliffside resort on Panglao (such as *Amorita Resort* or *South Palms*), arrange a private sunset sailboat charter across the Bohol Sea, indulge in couples'' spa treatments over the ocean, and book a romantic private dinner cruise down the tranquil **Loboc River**. Reason: Pairing secluded luxury resort accommodations with private maritime charters, serene riverways, and tranquil white-sand beaches creates an unhurried, intimate romantic retreat. IF: `traveler_type == FAMILY` THEN: Stay at family-friendly beachfront resorts along **Dumaluan Beach** with shallow swimming waters, visit the **Chocolate Hills Complex** via easy paved viewing decks, observe tarsiers at the **Corella Sanctuary**, take a gentle boat ride down the **Loboc River**, and go dolphin watching off **Balicasag Island**. Reason: Calm, shallow beach waters, accessible viewing platforms, educational wildlife encounters, and smooth river cruises keep children engaged and safe without physical exhaustion. IF: `traveler_type == LUXURY` THEN: Stay in top-tier suites or private villas at luxury boutique resorts on Panglao Island, charter private speedboats for island-hopping around **Balicasag Island** with private marine guides, arrange private helicopter tours over the **Chocolate Hills**, and enjoy fine dining at high-end venues like *MIST* or *Treetops*. Reason: High-end boutique accommodations, tailored private charters, and exclusive aerial viewpoints eliminate travel friction while providing personalized comfort across Bohol''s natural settings. IF: `traveler_type == BUDGET` THEN: Stay in budget hostels or guesthouses around **Tawala/Alona Beach** or **Tagbilaran City**, rent a motor scooter to explore the inland countryside independently, join shared group tours for the **Countryside Circuit** and **Balicasag Island**, and dine at local *carinderias* and casual night markets. Reason: Bohol offers affordable scooter rentals, cheap shared outrigger tours, budget hostel networks, and low-cost local eateries that make its major attractions accessible on a modest budget. IF: `traveler_interest == NATURE` THEN: Explore the limestone formations of the **Chocolate Hills**, walk through the quiet **Bilar Man-Made Mahogany Forest**, observe primates at the **Corella Tarsier Sanctuary**, snorkel the coral walls of **Balicasag Island Sanctuary**, paddleboard through the **Loboc-Anding River System**, and trek to hidden falls in **Anda**. Reason: Bohol features exceptionally diverse natural ecosystems ranging from ancient coral karst hills and tropical rainforests to riverine jungles and marine biodiversity hotspots. IF: `traveler_interest == FOOD` THEN: Sample local Boholano specialties including **Kalamay** (sweet sticky rice treat in coconut shells), fresh farm-to-table organic dishes at **Bohol Bee Farm**, fresh seafood grills along **Alona Beach**, traditional *peanut kisses*, and local riverfront buffets serving native Filipino dishes. Reason: Bohol offers a distinct regional culinary identity centered on traditional coconut-based sweets, farm-fresh organic produce, and vibrant oceanfront seafood dining. IF: `traveler_interest == ADVENTURE` THEN: Experience ziplining and sky-biking across river canyons at **Chocolate Hills Adventure Park (CHAP)**, stand-up paddleboarding or night firefly kayaking down the **Loboc River**, scuba diving along the deep drop-offs of **Balicasag Reef**, and cave-swimming at **Cabagnow Cave Pool** in Anda. Reason: Beyond quiet sightseeing, Bohol provides adrenaline-packed aerial ziplines, river paddle sports, deep-wall scuba diving, and subterranean cave exploration. IF: `traveler_type == SENIOR` THEN: Stay at accessible beachfront resorts on **Dumaluan Beach**, take private air-conditioned van tours to the **Chocolate Hills** (utilizing the accessible ramp areas) and **Baclayon Church**, enjoy a comfortable, seated lunch cruise on the **Loboc River**, and take gentle strolls through the **Corella Tarsier Sanctuary**. Reason: Smooth private vehicle transportation, step-conscious viewing areas, and relaxing seated river cruises allow senior travelers to experience Bohol''s highlights with ease and comfort. IF: `traveler_type == TRANSIT` THEN: Take a 10-minute taxi from Bohol-Panglao International Airport (TAG) to **Dumaluan Beach** or **Alona Beach**, enjoy a relaxed beachfront seafood meal, take a quiet stroll along the shore, and return smoothly to the departure terminal. Reason: The extreme proximity of Bohol''s international airport to Panglao''s primary beach strips allows layover passengers to enjoy authentic coastal hospitality without transit delays. IF: `trip_length >= 3 days` THEN: Divide your itinerary into 1 day for the inland **Countryside Circuit** (Chocolate Hills, Tarsier Sanctuary, Loboc River), 1 day for **Panglao & Balicasag Island Hopping** (dolphins, sea turtles, Virgin Island sandbar), and 1–2 days heading east to **Anda** for quiet white-sand beaches, cave pools, and tranquil eco-resort relaxation. Reason: A multi-day stay balances Bohol''s essential inland sights and Panglao island-hopping with the serene, uncrowded coastal landscapes of eastern Bohol.', 4773),
  ('bohol', 34, 'destination-scoring', 'DESTINATION SCORING', NULL, NULL, '| Factor | Score | | --- | --- | | Family | 92 | | Honeymoon | 90 | | Luxury | 84 | | Budget | 90 | | Adventure | 88 | | Culture | 82 | | Food | 80 | | Shopping | 68 | | Nightlife | 74 | | Relaxation | 92 | | Nature | 98 | | Accessibility | 62 | | Senior travelers | 78 | | First-time visitor | 92 | | Photography | 96 |', 4774),
  ('bohol', 35, 'final-travel-agent-verdict', 'FINAL TRAVEL AGENT VERDICT', NULL, NULL, 'Best for: Eco-adventurers, scuba divers, families, nature lovers, beach purists, and couples seeking a harmonious mix of iconic geological wonders, gentle river cruises, rare wildlife encounters, and relaxed beachfront luxury. Best duration: 3 to 5 days for a comprehensive Bohol experience covering the inland countryside highlights, island-hopping marine sanctuaries, and beach relaxation; or 8 to 12 days when combining Bohol with neighboring Visayan hubs like Cebu, Dumaguete, Siquijor, or Boracay. Best season: November to May (the dry season, offering clear sunny skies, calm sea swells for diving and dolphin watching, and optimal visibility); June to October brings afternoon monsoon showers and occasional tropical storms, though inland tours remain largely accessible. Best stay: Split-stay strategy—2 to 3 nights in a luxury beachfront resort along Panglao Island (e.g., Amorita Resort, Henann Resort, or South Palms) for marine activities, sunset dining, and nightlife, paired with 1 to 2 nights in an eco-lodge or riverfront resort in Loboc or Anda for serene rainforest views, firefly cruises, and quiet coastal escapes. Best transport: Direct domestic flights into Bohol-Panglao International Airport (TAG) or high-speed ocean ferries into Tagbilaran Sea Port from Cebu; private air-conditioned vans or car rentals for the inland Countryside Tour circuit; motor scooters for flexible local exploring in Panglao; and licensed private outrigger boats (*bangkas*) for island hopping. Must-do: Avoid: Biggest advantage: Compact, diverse geography—Bohol seamlessly combines world-renowned geological landmarks, dense tropical rainforests, and rare wildlife with pristine white-sand beaches and top-tier coral reef diving all within short, manageable travel distances. Biggest disadvantage: Public transit limitations across the main island, requiring travelers to rely on private van rentals, tours, or scooter hires to comfortably navigate between Panglao and inland countryside attractions. Overall destination score: **91/100**', 4775),
  ('bohol', 36, 'data-quality', 'DATA QUALITY', NULL, NULL, 'information_completeness: 94/100 last_updated: 2026-08-31 last_verified: NOT_LIVE_VERIFIED verified_by: TRAVEL_ENGINE_INITIAL_DATASET sources: IMPORTANT: Prices, opening hours, schedules, visa requirements, availability, accessibility and operational conditions must NOT be treated as permanently valid from this document. These must be sourced from structured, refreshable data.', 4776),
  ('manila', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Cool Dry Peak Season', NULL, 'months: December–February weather: Coolest and most comfortable time of the year (24–31°C) with low humidity, clear skies, and gentle breezes from the Northeast Monsoon (*Amihan*). crowd_level: HIGH price_level: HIGH overall_score: 90–96 recommended: true reason: Ideal conditions for walking tours through Intramuros, exploring Chinatown in Binondo, and attending outdoor events. Major holidays around Christmas and New Year bring massive festive crowds and surging hotel rates, making early reservations essential.', 4777),
  ('manila', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Hot Dry Summer Season', NULL, 'months: March–May weather: Very hot and humid (26–34°C) with low rainfall, bright sunshine, and heat index spikes in April and May. crowd_level: HIGH price_level: HIGH overall_score: 82–90 recommended: true reason: Great for urban sightseeing, indoor mall explorations, and taking day trips to higher-altitude destinations like Tagaytay. Easter Holy Week causes major citywide shutdowns while domestic tourists flood nearby beaches, resulting in heavy holiday traffic exits.', 4778),
  ('manila', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Southwest Monsoon Transition Season', NULL, 'months: June–August weather: Hot and muggy (25–32°C) with frequent afternoon thunderstorms and sudden downpours brought by the Southwest Monsoon (*Habagat*). crowd_level: MEDIUM price_level: MEDIUM overall_score: 68–78 recommended: true reason: A decent option for budget-conscious urban travelers as accommodation discounts become widely available. While bright morning hours allow for museum visits and historical tours, torrential afternoon rains can cause quick street flooding in low-lying metro areas.', 4779),
  ('manila', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Typhoon & Peak Wet Season', NULL, 'months: September–November weather: Warm and humid (24–31°C) with heavy monthly rainfall and the highest frequency of tropical typhoons passing through Luzon. crowd_level: LOW price_level: LOW overall_score: 52–64 recommended: false reason: The rainiest period of the year in Manila. Strong typhoons regularly cause flight delays, power interruptions, severe urban flooding, and transport gridlocks across Metro Manila, making outdoor travel unpredictable.', 4780),
  ('manila', 10, 'budget-strategy', 'BUDGET STRATEGY', NULL, NULL, 'Where saving money is not recommended:', 4781),
  ('manila', 18, 'family-travel', 'FAMILY TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'child_friendly_score: 82 best_ages: Rules:', 4782),
  ('manila', 19, 'honeymoon-travel', 'HONEYMOON TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'Best areas: Manila Bay & Entertainment City: best for world-class waterfront luxury, iconic golden-hour sunsets, and opulent urban indulgence; stay in 5-star integrated resorts like Okada Manila or Conrad Manila offering romantic Bay-view suites, private infinity pools, and couples'' spa sanctuaries overlooking the water. Makati Central Business District: best for sophisticated urban charm, fine dining, and cosmopolitan nightlife; choose luxury heritage hotels like The Peninsula Manila or sleek boutique suites surrounded by high-end shopping, lush green parks, and intimate cocktail lounges. Bonifacio Global City (BGC): best for contemporary elegance, walkable luxury, and trendy romantic spots; stay in upscale properties like Shangri-La The Fort to enjoy world-class dining, chic rooftop bars, and serene tree-lined streets perfect for evening strolls. Intramuros & Rizal Park: best for old-world colonial romance, historic charm, and quiet heritage walks; stay in boutique heritage hotels or luxury colonial-style properties to enjoy horse-drawn carriage rides, intimate courtyard dining, and sunset strolls along historic stone walls. Honeymoon rules: Book a private sunset dinner cruise along Manila Bay or charter a private yacht to experience the world-famous Manila Bay golden hour in complete privacy away from city crowds. Arrange private, executive hotel transfers in advance to navigate Metro Manila’s dense traffic seamlessly and ensure a stress-free transition from Ninoy Aquino International Airport to your luxury suite. Reserve fine dining tables at premier chef-led restaurants in BGC or Makati, as well as couples'' treatment suites at award-winning hotel spas, well in advance to secure prime times for intimate celebrations.', 4783),
  ('manila', 20, 'luxury-travel', 'LUXURY TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'luxury_score: 88 Best-value luxury pattern Book an opulent suite or private villa at iconic 5-star properties in Entertainment City or Makati—such as Okada Manila, Solaire Resort, The Peninsula Manila, or Shangri-La Fort—featuring dedicated butler service, private plunge pools or ocean-facing balconies, and access to exclusive executive lounges. Arrange private VIP chauffeured transfers in high-end SUVs or executive sedans directly from Ninoy Aquino International Airport (NAIA), bypassing city traffic in total comfort. Pair your urban stay with elite tailored additions, such as private helicopter charters to nearby luxury enclaves like Balesin Island or Mount Pinatubo, private yacht rentals along Manila Bay for sunset drinks, and custom curator-led tours of historic sites like Intramuros. Indulge in exclusive culinary and wellness experiences, including multi-course tasting menus by internationally acclaimed chefs, private wine pairings at high-end dining spots in Bonifacio Global City (BGC) or Makati, and holistic therapies at world-class luxury hotel spas. Luxury rules: Book presidential suites, skyline penthouses, or casino-integrated luxury villas along Entertainment City, Makati CBD, or BGC to enjoy panoramic city and bay views, private spa facilities, and unmatched personal hospitality. Utilize private chauffeured vehicles and luxury town car services to navigate Metro Manila''s sprawling districts without dealing with public transit or waiting for standard ride-hailing services. Combine high-end urban lifestyle experiences—such as private designer shopping trips in Greenbelt or Shangri-La Plaza—with world-class casino gaming, private theater boxes, and fine dining at top-tier integrated resorts. Reserve luxury suites, fine-dining tasting menus, and private executive transit well in advance—especially during peak festival and holiday seasons—to secure top availability and preferred scheduling.', 4784),
  ('manila', 21, 'adventure', 'ADVENTURE', NULL, NULL, 'adventure_score: 82 Metro Manila serves as an expansive gateway to high-octane thrill destinations across Luzon, where urban concrete quickly gives way to volcanic landscapes, rugged mountain ranges, rapid-filled rivers, and world-class dive spots. Thrill-seekers can navigate turbulent whitewaters, hike up active volcanic craters, tackle off-road ATV trails through mountain mud, scale sharp limestone ridges, and dive with vibrant marine life. Combining high-speed urban pursuits with rapid day-trip access to extreme wilderness, Manila provides a dynamic launchpad for action-packed expeditions. Top experiences: Recommended areas: Best for:', 4785),
  ('manila', 22, 'senior-travel', 'SENIOR TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'senior_suitability: 82 walking_intensity: MEDIUM (can be customized to LOW by utilizing private air-conditioned chauffeured vehicles, focusing on climate-controlled indoor venues, and selecting hotels with step-free access and modern elevators) Metro Manila offers senior travelers a rich tapestry of historical heritage, world-class dining, and vibrant cultural arts. While the metropolis is dense and prone to traffic, mature visitors can navigate the capital comfortably with well-structured itineraries. By staying in modern, walkable commercial districts like Bonifacio Global City (BGC) or Makati CBD, utilizing private chauffeured cars or ride-hailing services, and exploring historic sites like Intramuros during cooler morning hours, senior travelers can experience Manila''s deep history and contemporary charm at an unhurried, comfortable pace. Rules: Prefer: Avoid:', 4786),
  ('manila', 23, 'accessibility', 'ACCESSIBILITY', NULL, NULL, 'wheelchair_accessibility: PARTIAL_TO_GOOD depending on attraction and transport public_transport_accessibility: VARIABLE hotel_accessibility: MUST_BE_VERIFIED_PER_HOTEL attraction_accessibility: MUST_BE_VERIFIED_PER_ATTRACTION Rule: Never infer accessibility from destination-level accessibility. Each hotel and attraction must carry its own accessibility data.', 4787),
  ('manila', 24, 'food', 'FOOD', NULL, NULL, 'food_score: 92 Manila is a bustling culinary epicenter where rich Spanish-colonial traditions, indigenous Malay roots, Chinese heritage, and vibrant modern food trends intersect. From centuries-old eateries in the world''s oldest Chinatown to energetic street night markets and sophisticated culinary hubs in modern financial districts, Metro Manila offers an extraordinarily diverse and flavor-filled gastronomic journey. Food experiences: Best for: Recommended areas:', 4788),
  ('manila', 25, 'shopping', 'SHOPPING', NULL, NULL, 'shopping_score: 95 Metro Manila is widely regarded as the ultimate shopping capital of the Philippines and one of Southeast Asia''s premier retail destinations. The metropolis offers a vast spectrum of options ranging from massive, air-conditioned luxury mega-malls and high-end designer districts to bustling, bargain-filled street markets and curated artisanal craft centers. Best buys: Prefer: Avoid: Best for:', 4789),
  ('manila', 26, 'nightlife', 'NIGHTLIFE', NULL, NULL, 'nightlife_level: 88 Nightlife in Manila is electric, sprawling, and extremely varied, spanning upscale rooftop lounges, trendy craft cocktail bars, high-stakes casino complexes, and energetic live-music venues. Rather than a single bar district, Metro Manila’s nightlife scene is concentrated across distinct commercial hubs—ranging from the bohemian, bar-hopping streets of Poblacion in Makati to the sophisticated clubs of Bonifacio Global City (BGC) and the world-class entertainment resorts along Manila Bay. Best for: Prefer: Avoid: Best evening areas:', 4790),
  ('manila', 28, 'sample-itinerary-patterns', 'SAMPLE ITINERARY PATTERNS', 'HALF-DAY – EXPRESS HISTORIC INTRAMUROS & OLD MANILA', NULL, 'Morning / Afternoon: Pickup from your central hotel or meet at the historic gates of Intramuros → Begin at **Fort Santiago**, walking through the stone gate lodge to explore the 16th-century Spanish citadel, dungeon chambers, and the Jose Rizal Shrine museum → Stroll along cobblestone streets to the **Manila Cathedral**, admiring its neo-Romanesque facade, intricate stained glass, and grand pipe organ → Visit the UNESCO World Heritage-listed **San Agustin Church**, marveling at its trompe-l''œil ceiling frescoes and rich colonial monastery museum collection → Cross the street to **Casa Manila**, stepping inside a meticulously reconstructed 19th-century Spanish colonial mansion showcasing period furniture and courtyard architecture → Conclude with a traditional Filipino snack of *halo-halo* or *empanadas* at a local cafe inside the historic walls before returning to your hotel', 4791),
  ('manila', 28, 'sample-itinerary-patterns', 'SAMPLE ITINERARY PATTERNS', '1 DAY – HISTORIC CULTURAL CORE & BGC NIGHTLIFE', NULL, 'Morning: Morning pickup from your hotel for a full-day city tour starting in the historic heart of Metro Manila → Arrive in **Intramuros** for a guided walk or electric *kalesa* ride around Fort Santiago, San Agustin Church, and the historic city walls → Walk to adjacent **Rizal Park (Luneta)**, stopping at the Dr. Jose Rizal Monument guarded by ceremonial sentries → Head into the **National Museum of Fine Arts**, standing in awe before Juan Luna''s iconic masterwork, the *Spoliarium* Afternoon: Transfer to **Binondo**, the world''s oldest Chinatown, for an authentic culinary food crawl down Ongpin Street, sampling *hopia*, pan-fried pork buns, and handmade dumplings → Visit the historic **Binondo Church** (Minor Basilica of St. Lorenzo Ruiz) to admire its unique octagonal bell tower → Cross the Pasig River toward Makati for a mid-afternoon coffee or shopping break at the Greenbelt complex Evening: Drive to the sleek, pedestrianized district of **Bonifacio Global City (BGC)** as twilight sets in → Take an evening stroll along Bonifacio High Street to view public art installations, interactive fountains, and modern high-rise architecture → Enjoy a multi-course dinner at a top-tier modern Filipino restaurant followed by craft cocktails at a BGC rooftop lounge overlooking the skyline', 4792),
  ('manila', 28, 'sample-itinerary-patterns', 'SAMPLE ITINERARY PATTERNS', '2 DAYS – ULTIMATE MANILA HERITAGE & TAGAYTAY HIGHLAND ESCAPE', NULL, 'Day 1: Full-day urban immersion exploring Intramuros, the National Museum Complex, and a Binondo Chinatown street food crawl → Afternoon visit to the **Ayala Museum** in Makati to explore detailed historical dioramas and indigenous gold artifact collections → Spend the evening sampling craft beers and creative Filipino fusion small plates in the trendy, bohemian neighborhood of Poblacion, Makati Day 2: Early morning departure (approx. 6:30 AM) in a private vehicle heading south toward the cool ridge of **Tagaytay** (~2 hours) → Arrive at a ridge-side restaurant for breakfast, taking in breathtaking panoramic views over Taal Volcano and its surrounding crater lake → Visit the **Palace in the Sky** (People''s Park in the Sky) or **Picnic Grove** for elevated views over the Cavite countryside and Taal Lake → Drive down to the charming town of Silang to explore organic farm-to-table estates or the historic Pink Sisters Convent → Enjoy a steaming bowl of authentic *Bulalo* (beef shank soup) for lunch while taking in the fresh highland mountain breeze → Return to Metro Manila in the late afternoon, stopping at the **Okada Manila** complex in Entertainment City to watch the evening fountain light and music show', 4793),
  ('manila', 28, 'sample-itinerary-patterns', 'SAMPLE ITINERARY PATTERNS', 'COMBINED DAY TRIP – BAYFRONT CULTURE & SUNSET SKYLINE VIEWS', NULL, 'Morning: Morning pickup and transfer to the waterfront district of Metro Manila → Begin at the **Cultural Center of the Philippines (CCP) Complex**, admiring brutalist modernist architecture and open-air theater grounds → Head to **Manila Ocean Park**, exploring the underwater oceanarium tunnel, marine life exhibits, and stingray touch pools → Enjoy a fresh seafood lunch along the oceanfront concourse overlooking Manila Bay Afternoon: Transfer to the massive **SM Mall of Asia** complex, browsing regional crafts, international high-street brands, and local *pasalubong* centers → Take an afternoon ride on the **MOA Eye** ferris wheel for aerial views over the bay and metropolitan coastline → Walk along the **Manila Baywalk** promenade as late afternoon approaches, watching local street performers and seaside crowds gather Evening: Secure a prime seaside table or rooftop lounge spot along the bayfront to watch Manila''s world-famous golden-hour sunset → Head into Entertainment City for a lavish buffet dinner inside Solaire Resort or Okada Manila → Conclude your evening watching the choreographed multi-million dollar water fountain performance at Okada Manila before heading back to your hotel', 4794),
  ('manila', 29, '12-day-13-night-el-nido-honeymoon-itinerary', '12-day, 13-night El Nido honeymoon itinerary', NULL, NULL, 'Day 01: Arrival PPS Arrival at Puerto Princesa Airport (PPS) and meet and greet. Transfer to hotel, check in, and relax. Evening free for leisure. Overnight stay in PPS. Day 02: Under Ground River Tour + El Nido Transfer Breakfast at hotel. Pick up for Underground River Tour with picnic lunch at Sabang Wharf. Enjoy the Underground River Cave Exploration experience (admiring stalagmites and stalactites formed over thousands of years) with picnic lunch included. Proceed to El Nido by road on a private basis (~6 hours drive). *NOTE: Arrival in El Nido may be late (around 10:00 PM – 11:00 PM) following the full day tour and transfer.* Check in at resort. Overnight in El Nido. Day 03: EL NIDO ISLAND HOPPING TOUR A Breakfast at hotel. Proceed for Island Hopping Tour A with local beach lunch included. Visit Big Lagoon, Small Lagoon, Secret Lagoon, Shimizu Island, and Seven Commandos Beach. Return to El Nido town. Overnight in El Nido. Day 04: EL NIDO ISLAND HOPPING TOUR (TOUR C) Breakfast at hotel. Proceed for Island Hopping Tour C with local lunch. Visit Secret Beach, Hidden Beach, Helicopter Island, Talisay Beach, and premier marine snorkeling areas. Return to hotel. Overnight in El Nido. Day 05: FLIGHT TO BORACAY Breakfast at the hotel. Check out and transfer to airport for your flight to Boracay (via Lio Airport or PPS). Arrive in Boracay, transfer to resort, and check in. Evening free for romantic strolls along White Beach. Overnight in Boracay. Day 06: BORACAY ISLAND HOPPING TOUR After breakfast, proceed for an Island Hopping Tour on SIC basis. Explore Puka Shell Beach for swimming, photo opportunities, and cricket market shopping. Depart Puka Beach to visit Crystal Cove Island. Return to boat station with buffet lunch included during the tour. Overnight stay in Boracay. Day 07: BORACAY SUNSET CRUISE Breakfast at the hotel. Morning at leisure for relaxing on the beach or resort spa treatments. Afternoon proceed for a classic Boracay Sunset Cruise around 3:00 PM. Return to hotel. Overnight in Boracay. Day 08: TRANSFER TO CEBU Breakfast at the hotel. Check out of hotel and transfer to airport for your flight to Cebu. Arrival in Cebu, transfer to hotel, and check in. Overnight stay in Cebu. Day 09: CEBU CITY TOUR Breakfast at the hotel. Proceed for a comprehensive Cebu City Tour covering top attractions: Temple of Leah, La Vie Parisienne, Heritage Park, Yap-San Diego Ancestral House, Fort San Pedro, Magellan''s Cross, Basilica Minore del Santo Niño, Tops Lookout (for night viewing of the metropolitan area), CCLEX Bridge, and 10,000 Roses Cafe. Return to hotel. Overnight in Cebu. Day 10: OSLOB WHALE SHARK WATCHING & KAWASAN WATERFALLS Early morning (around 3:00 AM) departure for Oslob Whale Shark watching and Kawasan Waterfalls canyoneering. Arrive in Oslob for the whale shark encounter (hotel provides packed breakfast). Proceed to Badian for Kawasan Falls (bamboo raft view and turquoise waters) and enjoy the thrilling Canyoneering activity. Return to hotel. Overnight in Cebu. Day 11: MACTAN ISLAND HOPPING TOUR Breakfast at the hotel. Pick-up around 7:00 AM for Mactan Island Hopping. Destinations include: Return to Cebu hotel. Overnight in Cebu. Day 12: BOHOL COUNTRYSIDE TOUR Breakfast at the hotel. Pick up from hotel for full-day Bohol Countryside Tour (via fast ferry). Destinations include: Return via ferry to Cebu hotel. Overnight in Cebu. Day 13: DEPARTURE CEBU Breakfast at the hotel. Check out of hotel and transfer to Mactan-Cebu International Airport (CEB) for your onwards international flight home.', 4795),
  ('manila', 30, '13-day-12-night-family-itinerary', '13-Day / 12 -Night Family Itinerary', NULL, NULL, 'Day 01: Arrival PPS Day 02: Underground River Tour + El Nido Transfer Day 03: EL NIDO ISLAND HOPPING TOUR A Day 04: EL NIDO ISLAND HOPPING TOUR C Day 05: FLIGHT TO BORACAY Day 06: BORACAY ISLAND HOPPING TOUR Day 07: BORACAY SUNSET CRUISE Day 08: TRANSFER TO CEBU Day 09: CEBU CITY TOUR Day 10: OSLOB WHALE SHARK WATCHING & KAWASAN WATERFALLS Day 11: MACTAN ISLAND HOPPING TOUR Day 12: BOHOL COUNTRYSIDE DAY TOUR Day 13: DEPARTURE CEBU', 4796),
  ('manila', 31, '13-days-12-nights-luxury-itinerary', '13 Days 12 Nights Luxury Itinerary', NULL, NULL, 'Day 01: ARRIVAL PUERTO PRINCESA Welcome to Palawan! Upon arriving at El Nido Airport (ENI), your private luxury chauffeur will greet you in the arrivals terminal and transfer you to your hotel (such as Best Western Plus The Ivywall Hotel or similar upgraded luxury suites). Check in to your Deluxe Room and take the evening to relax by the pool or indulge in fine local dining. Overnight stay in Puerto Princesa. Day 02: UNDERGROUND RIVER TOUR & SCENIC EL NIDO TRANSFER Begin your day with a gourmet breakfast at the hotel before departing for the world-renowned Puerto Princesa Subterranean River National Park, a UNESCO World Heritage Site. Board your private boat at Sabang Wharf for an immersive Underground River Cave Exploration, admiring the towering stalactites and stalagmites formed over thousands of years. A private picnic lunch is served by the shore. Following the tour, relax in your private vehicle during a scenic 6-hour overland transfer north to El Nido. Check in to your resort (such as El Nido Garden Resort, Pangulasian Island, or similar premier beach resort) for a well-deserved rest. Overnight in El Nido. Day 03: EL NIDO ISLAND HOPPING TOUR A After breakfast, embark on a private outrigger yacht charter for the iconic Island Hopping Tour A across Bacuit Bay. Strap on a life vest and paddle a kayak through the calm, emerald passageways of the Big Lagoon, step through the limestone opening into the secluded Secret Lagoon, and visit Shimizu Island and Seven Commandos Beach. A delicious beachside seafood and local barbecue lunch is freshly prepared and served on the island sands. Return to the resort by late afternoon to enjoy sunset drinks along the shore. Overnight in El Nido. Day 04: EL NIDO ISLAND HOPPING TOUR C Enjoy breakfast before setting sail on Island Hopping Tour C to explore Bacuit Bay''s outer island sanctuaries. Swim through a hidden underwater tunnel to reach the legendary Secret Beach, wade onto the pristine shore of Hidden Beach framed by towering jagged cliffs, take photos of Helicopter Island''s unique silhouette, and snorkel along vibrant coral reefs off Talisay Beach. A gourmet grilled lunch is served on the beach during the tour. Return to your resort for a relaxed evening. Overnight in El Nido. Day 05: FLIGHT TO BORACAY Savor breakfast at the hotel before transferring to Lio Airport (ENI) or Puerto Princesa for your domestic flight to Caticlan (Boracay). Upon arrival, enjoy a seamless private land and speedboat transfer to your luxury beachfront sanctuary (such as Boracay Mandarin Bay Resort and Spa or Crimson Resort & Spa). Check in to your Premier Suite and spend the evening at leisure, enjoying a barefoot stroll along White Beach or sampling beachfront mixology. Overnight in Boracay. Day 06: BORACAY ISLAND HOPPING TOUR Start the day with a lavish beachfront breakfast, then board your outrigger boat for a island hopping excursion around Boracay''s sparkling coastline. Stop at Puka Shell Beach for swimming, picturesque coastal photos, and local shell markets before continuing to the private shores of Crystal Cove Island. Enjoy a freshly prepared buffet lunch included during the tour before returning to Station 1 or 2. Spend your late afternoon swimming in the turquoise waters. Overnight in Boracay. Day 07: BORACAY SUNSET CRUISE Enjoy a lazy morning with breakfast at your own pace and a free day to relax by the infinity pool, visit a luxury spa, or enjoy watersports along White Beach. At 3:00 PM, transfer to the beachfront to board your private sunset cruise. Sail along Boracay''s world-famous coastline with drinks and light snacks while watching the golden sun dip behind the ocean horizon. Return to the resort for an evening at leisure. Overnight in Boracay. Day 08: TRANSFER TO CEBU Following breakfast, check out of your hotel and take a private speedboat and land transfer to Caticlan Airport for your domestic flight to Cebu. Arriving at Mactan-Cebu International Airport (CEB), your private chauffeur will take you to your hotel (such as BAI Hotel Cebu or NUSTAR Resort and Casino). Check in to your Deluxe Room and spend the evening relaxing or dining at one of the hotel''s premier restaurants. Overnight in Cebu. Day 09: CEBU CITY & HIGHLANDS HERITAGE TOUR After breakfast, depart on a comprehensive tour showcasing Cebu’s rich historic heart and picturesque mountain vantage points. Visit the majestic Greek-inspired Temple of Leah, stroll through the vibrant floral terraces of Sirao Garden or 10,000 Roses, and take in sweeping city skyline vistas from Tops Lookout. Return to the historic center to explore Fort San Pedro, Magellan''s Cross, the Basilica Minore del Santo Niño, the Heritage of Cebu Monument, and the Yap-Sandiego Ancestral House. Stop by La Vie Parisienne or cross the iconic CCLEX Bridge before returning to your hotel. Overnight in Cebu. Day 10: OSLOB WHALE SHARK ENCOUNTER & KAWASAN FALLS CANYONEERING An early 3:00 AM private departure takes you south to Oslob for an unforgettable early-morning marine encounter (a packed breakfast is provided by your hotel). Swim alongside the gentle giants during your Oslob Whale Shark Watching experience. Afterward, travel across to Badian for an adrenaline-filled Canyoneering adventure through lush jungle canyons, ending at the breathtaking turquoise pools of Kawasan Falls, where you can ride a bamboo raft under the cascading waters. Return to your hotel in the evening for rest. Overnight in Cebu. Day 11: MACTAN ISLAND HOPPING & MARINE SANCTUARY TOUR Enjoy a 7:00 AM pickup for a private island-hopping cruise across the clear waters of the Hilutungan Channel. Snorkel through vibrant coral gardens teeming with tropical fish at the Gilutongan Island Marine Sanctuary, visit the peaceful shores of Caohagan Island to sample local seaside treats, and walk along the iconic scenic wooden boardwalk of Nalusuan Island. A fresh seafood lunch is served island-style before returning to your Cebu hotel by mid-afternoon. Overnight in Cebu. Day 12: BOHOL COUNTRYSIDE DAY TOUR Following breakfast, take a fast ferry crossing or private charter to Bohol for a countryside heritage tour. Visit the Blood Compact Shrine and the historic stone structure of Baclayon Church before driving through the lush canopy of the Bilar Man-Made Mahogany Forest. View native wildlife at the exotic Python & Butterfly Sanctuary and observe the world''s smallest primates up close at the Tarsier Conservation Area. Conclude your tour gazing over the world-famous Chocolate Hills viewdeck. Return by ferry to your Cebu hotel in the evening. Overnight in Cebu. Day 13: DEPARTURE CEBU Enjoy a final breakfast at your hotel before checking out. Your private chauffeur will transfer you to Mactan-Cebu International Airport (CEB) in time to check in for your onward international flight home, completing an extraordinary 13-day luxury Philippine island getaway.', 4797),
  ('manila', 32, 'travel-agent-insights', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS', 'What inexperienced planners often do wrong', NULL, '', 4798),
  ('manila', 32, 'travel-agent-insights', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS', 'What an experienced planner does differently', NULL, '', 4799);
INSERT INTO destination_guidance (place_id, section, topic, section_title, heading, audience, body, position) VALUES
  ('manila', 32, 'travel-agent-insights', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS', 'Best planning rule', NULL, '', 4800),
  ('manila', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', NULL, NULL, 'IF: `trip_length <= 0.5 days` THEN: Choose a focused historic walking loop inside **Intramuros**, exploring **Fort Santiago**, walking past **San Agustin Church** and **Manila Cathedral**, and enjoying a traditional meal or *halo-halo* at *Barbara''s* or *Bambike Ecotours* before departing back toward Ninoy Aquino International Airport (NAIA). Reason: Half-day layovers require maximum transit efficiency near the city center; focusing on the compact historic core delivers centuries of Spanish colonial heritage, iconic religious landmarks, and celebrated local cuisine without risking missed flight connections. IF: `trip_length == 1 day` THEN: Tour the historic sights of **Intramuros** and the **National Museum of Fine Arts** in the morning, embark on an authentic Chinatown food crawl down Ongpin Street in **Binondo** for lunch, and head to **Bonifacio Global City (BGC)** in the evening for high-street shopping, dinner, and craft cocktails. Reason: A single full day allows energetic travelers to experience Metro Manila''s contrast between its rich 16th-century colonial past, vibrant culinary trade history, and sleek, modern modern urban lifestyle. IF: `trip_length >= 2 days` THEN: Spend day one exploring historic **Intramuros**, **Rizal Park**, the **National Museum Complex**, and **Binondo Chinatown**; spend day two taking a scenic day trip south to **Tagaytay** to view **Taal Volcano and Lake** before returning to **Entertainment City** in Manila for dinner and the **Okada Manila** water fountain show. Reason: Multi-day stays allow travelers to balance Metro Manila''s rich urban heritage and culinary districts with scenic highland escapes overlooking active volcanic landscapes. IF: `trip_type == FIRST_TIME_VISITOR` THEN: Focus on the quintessential city highlights—exploring Spanish heritage in **Intramuros** (**Fort Santiago**, **San Agustin Church**), viewing Juan Luna''s *Spoliarium* at the **National Museum of Fine Arts**, eating street food in **Binondo**, catching the golden-hour sunset along **Manila Bay**, and dining in **BGC** or **Makati**. Reason: Combining Manila''s iconic colonial monuments, national art treasures, culinary trade roots, world-famous bay sunsets, and modern commercial centers delivers a complete first-time overview of the Philippine capital. IF: `trip_type == HONEYMOON` THEN: Book a luxury suite at top-tier heritage or bayfront properties like *The Manila Hotel*, *Okada Manila*, or *Raffles Makati*, indulge in private fine-dining dinners in **Poblacion** or **BGC**, arrange private sunset yacht charters across **Manila Bay**, and take a day trip to Tagaytay for romantic ridge-side dining. Reason: Pairing colonial elegance and modern bayfront luxury with private yacht charters, fine-dining gastronomy, and scenic mountain viewports creates a memorable romantic getaway. IF: `traveler_type == FAMILY` THEN: Visit **Manila Ocean Park** along the bayfront, explore hands-on interactive exhibits at **The Mind Museum** in BGC, ride the **MOA Eye** ferris wheel at SM Mall of Asia, take a child-friendly *Bambike* (bamboo bicycle) tour through **Intramuros**, and enjoy the musical fountain show at **Okada Manila**. Reason: Accessible marine exhibits, interactive science centers, safe pedestrianized plazas, and colorful entertainment shows keep children engaged and entertained without physical strain. IF: `traveler_type == LUXURY` THEN: Book 5-star suites at luxury integrated resorts like *Okada Manila*, *Solaire Resort*, or *Raffles Makati*, shop international designer boutiques at **Greenbelt** or **Shangri-La Plaza**, hire private chauffeur transfers, and enjoy multi-course tasting menus at fine-dining establishments in BGC and Makati. Reason: World-class integrated resort casinos, private luxury transport, designer shopping precincts, and acclaimed culinary venues provide high-end comfort and seamless service. IF: `traveler_type == BUDGET` THEN: Stay in central hostels or budget guesthouses around **Poblacion (Makati)** or **Ermita**, navigate the city using LRT/MRT lines, Grab, and jeepneys, take self-guided walking tours through **Intramuros** and **Rizal Park**, visit free-admission venues like the **National Museum Complex**, and feast on cheap street food in **Binondo**. Reason: Manila provides an extensive network of affordable street markets, free national museum galleries, budget hostels, and low-cost public transit suitable for price-conscious travelers. IF: `traveler_interest == NATURE` THEN: Take day trips out of the urban center to trek the crater lake of **Mount Pinatubo**, view active volcanic islands at **Taal Volcano Viewpoint (Tagaytay)**, shoot rapids at **Pagsanjan Falls**, or explore the open-air art installations and terraced gardens at **Pinto Art Museum** in Antipolo. Reason: While Metro Manila is an urban metropolis, its surrounding provinces offer rapid access to active volcanoes, roaring waterfalls, lush mountain ridges, and eco-art sanctuaries. IF: `traveler_interest == FOOD` THEN: Embark on an epic culinary journey—sampling street food and dim sum in **Binondo** (the world''s oldest Chinatown), tasting traditional Filipino staples like *Adobo*, *Sinigang*, and *Sizzling Sisig*, exploring modern Filipino fusion in **BGC**, and hopping between craft cocktail bars and hipster bistros in **Poblacion, Makati**. Reason: Manila is the ultimate melting pot of Philippine gastronomy, offering centuries-old Chinese-Filipino street eats alongside cutting-edge culinary fusion and world-class mixology. IF: `traveler_interest == ADVENTURE` THEN: Head on outdoor day trips outside the city perimeter—taking 4x4 off-road rides and trekking to the crater lake of **Mount Pinatubo**, river rafting and canoeing through **Pagsanjan Falls**, or mountain hiking in the nearby **Sierra Madre** range (like Mount Daraitan). Reason: Adrenaline seekers can easily use Manila as a launching pad for thrilling off-road volcano treks, white-water river navigation, and rugged mountain trail hikes. IF: `traveler_type == SENIOR` THEN: Stay at full-service luxury hotels in **Makati** or **BGC**, take private air-conditioned vehicle tours through **Intramuros** with horse-drawn *kalesa* rides, explore flat museum halls at the **Ayala Museum**, and enjoy scenic, low-effort ridge dining in **Tagaytay**. Reason: Accessible cultural museums, private vehicular transport, step-free shopping complexes, and gentle highland dining allow senior travelers to experience Manila comfortably. IF: `traveler_type == TRANSIT` THEN: Take a 10-to-15 minute taxi from Ninoy Aquino International Airport (NAIA) to **Resorts World Manila (Newport World Resorts)** or **SM Mall of Asia**, enjoy a relaxed meal of authentic Filipino cuisine, browse shop concourses, and return directly to the terminal. Reason: Immediate proximity between NAIA and adjacent Newport or bayfront commercial hubs allows layover passengers to sample local food and modern Filipino atmosphere safely without city traffic delays. IF: `trip_length >= 3 days` THEN: Divide your stay between 1 full day of historic heritage and museums (**Intramuros**, **National Museum**, **Binondo**), 1 full day exploring modern lifestyle and nightlife hubs (**BGC**, **Makati**, **Manila Bay**), and 1-2 days taking highland and natural day trips to **Tagaytay**, **Antipolo**, or **Pagsanjan Falls**. Reason: A comprehensive multi-day itinerary seamlessly bridges Manila''s urban historic roots and high-energy modern districts with scenic volcanic lakes and lush outdoor attractions nearby.', 4801),
  ('manila', 34, 'destination-scoring', 'DESTINATION SCORING', NULL, NULL, '| Factor | Score | | --- | --- | | Family | 84 | | Honeymoon | 78 | | Luxury | 92 | | Budget | 90 | | Adventure | 68 | | Culture | 95 | | Food | 96 | | Shopping | 98 | | Nightlife | 94 | | Relaxation | 70 | | Nature | 62 | | Accessibility | 70 | | Senior travelers | 78 | | First-time visitor | 92 | | Photography | 90 |', 4802),
  ('manila', 35, 'final-travel-agent-verdict', 'FINAL TRAVEL AGENT VERDICT', NULL, NULL, 'Best for: History enthusiasts, urban explorers, foodies, culture seekers, luxury shoppers, and night-owls looking for an intriguing mix of 16th-century Spanish colonial heritage, vibrant street-food history, world-famous bay sunsets, cutting-edge modern lifestyle districts, and dynamic nightlife. Best duration: 2 to 4 days for a comprehensive Metro Manila urban exploration (historic sites, museum complexes, Chinatown food crawls, and modern lifestyle hubs); or 7 to 10 days when using Manila as an international gateway and pairing it with regional day trips (Tagaytay, Mount Pinatubo, Pagsanjan) and domestic island flights. Best season: December to April (the dry season, featuring lower humidity, minimal rainfall, pleasant tropical temperatures, and ideal walking conditions for heritage tours); May to October brings heavy monsoon downpours, high humidity, and increased typhoon risks that can disrupt city walking tours and outdoor excursions. Best stay: Split-stay strategy—1 to 2 nights in a heritage or bayfront luxury hotel (e.g., The Manila Hotel or Okada Manila in Entertainment City) for easy access to Intramuros, National Museums, Binondo, and bayfront sunsets, paired with 1 to 2 nights in a sleek, high-end district like Bonifacio Global City or Makati (e.g., Shangri-La The Fort or Raffles Makati) for walkable high-street shopping, fine dining, and craft cocktail lounges. Best transport: International arrival via Ninoy Aquino International Airport (NAIA); Grab ride-hailing app for reliable point-to-point urban transit; private air-conditioned vehicle transfers for day trips outside the metro (Tagaytay or Laguna); and the LRT/MRT elevated rail system for navigating high-traffic corridors during peak hours. Must-do: Avoid: Biggest advantage: Unmatched cultural and connectivity hub—Manila serves as the primary international gateway and melting pot of the Philippines, offering centuries of rich Spanish and Chinese trade history, world-class culinary options, mega-malls, and vibrant urban entertainment all in one metropolis. Biggest disadvantage: Heavy urban traffic congestion along major transit corridors, heavy tropical humidity during summer months, and intense contrast between densely populated historical commercial quarters and modern lifestyle districts. Overall destination score: **89/100**', 4803),
  ('manila', 36, 'data-quality', 'DATA QUALITY', NULL, NULL, 'information_completeness: 92/100 last_updated: 2026-08-31 last_verified: NOT_LIVE_VERIFIED verified_by: TRAVEL_ENGINE_INITIAL_DATASET sources: IMPORTANT: Prices, opening hours, schedules, visa requirements, availability, accessibility and operational conditions must NOT be treated as permanently valid from this document. These must be sourced from structured, refreshable data.', 4804),
  ('cochin', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Spring', NULL, 'months: March-May weather: Hot and humid increasingly uncomfortable toward late May. crowd_level: MEDIUM → HIGH price_level: MEDIUM → HIGH overall_score: 82-86 recommended: true reason: Good for heritage sightseeing, food, and photography, but heat and humidity start building up, so outdoor pacing matters.', 4805),
  ('cochin', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Summer', NULL, 'months: June-August weather: Warm and humid with Southwest Monsoon; frequent rain and overcast skies. crowd_level: MEDIUM price_level: LOW → MEDIUM overall_score: 86-82 recommended: true reason: A strong value season for Kochi if you do not mind rain. The city feels greener, calmer, and often cheaper, with good options for backwaters, indoor culture, and food-focused trips.', 4806),
  ('cochin', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Autumn', NULL, 'months: September-November weather: Warm,with the monsoon easing and improving outdoor conditions. crowd_level: LOW → MEDIUM price_level: LOW → MEDIUM overall_score: 86-90 recommended: true reason: One of the best all-around periods for Kochi, balancing better weather, lower crowds, and stronger value than peak winter.', 4807),
  ('cochin', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Winter', NULL, 'months: December-February weather: Pleasant,drier,and more comfortable for walking and sightseeing. crowd_level: HIGH → VERY HIGH price_level: HIGH → VERY HIGH overall_score: 88-92 recommended: true reason: Best weather for first-time visitors, heritage walks, and outdoor experiences, but also the busiest and most expensive period. February is often the sweet spot.', 4808),
  ('cochin', 10, 'budget-strategy', 'BUDGET STRATEGY', NULL, NULL, 'Travel-agent rule: Kochi is best positioned as a good-value cultural city, not an ultra-cheap destination and not an expensive one. It offers strong experience quality for the money, especially when the trip is built around heritage, food, and relaxed exploration.', 4809),
  ('cochin', 12, 'airport-transfer-logic', 'AIRPORT TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Family', 'family', 'Airport taxi or pre-booked private MPV/van; door-to-door, luggage-friendly, and easiest after arrival.', 4810),
  ('cochin', 12, 'airport-transfer-logic', 'AIRPORT TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Honeymoon', 'honeymoon', 'Pre-booked private car or limo; best for privacy, comfort, and a smooth first impression. reason: The first impression of the trip matters and private transfer provides comfort and privacy.', 4811),
  ('cochin', 12, 'airport-transfer-logic', 'AIRPORT TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Luxury', 'luxury', 'Chauffeured sedan or luxury MPV; ideal for premium stays, added comfort, and seamless service.', 4812),
  ('cochin', 12, 'airport-transfer-logic', 'AIRPORT TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Budget', 'budget', 'Prepaid taxi or airport bus to the city, then local transport if needed; best value for cost-conscious travelers.', 4813),
  ('cochin', 18, 'family-travel', 'FAMILY TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'child_friendly_score: 84 best_ages: Rules: For young children: Prefer: Avoid:', 4814),
  ('cochin', 19, 'honeymoon-travel', 'HONEYMOON TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'honeymoon_score: 96 romance_score: 98 privacy_score: 90 luxury_score: 95 Recommended: Honeymoon itinerary should NOT contain more than: 2 major activities/day. Prefer: One memorable experience + free time over: Three or four attractions. Recommended hotel areas: Fort Kochi works best for romance and atmosphere, while Bolgatty / Willingdon Island is better for privacy and a more premium feel.', 4815),
  ('cochin', 20, 'luxury-travel', 'LUXURY TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'luxury_score: 97 Recommended: Luxury travelers should not be given an itinerary that simply contains more activities. Luxury should primarily increase: Recommended hotel areas: Fort Kochi works best for character and atmosphere, while Bolgatty / Willingdon Island is better for privacy and a more premium feel.', 4816),
  ('cochin', 21, 'adventure', 'ADVENTURE', NULL, NULL, 'adventure_score: 40 Kochi is not a primary high-adrenaline adventure destination. Adventure-like experiences should be interpreted as: Recommended adventure-style areas: Best for:', 4817),
  ('cochin', 22, 'senior-travel', 'SENIOR TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'senior_suitability: 78 walking_intensity: MEDIUM_HIGH unless carefully managed Rules: Recommended hotel areas:', 4818),
  ('cochin', 23, 'accessibility', 'ACCESSIBILITY', NULL, NULL, 'wheelchair_accessibility: PARTIAL_TO_GOOD depending on attraction and transport public_transport_accessibility: VARIABLE hotel_accessibility: MUST_BE_VERIFIED_PER_HOTEL attraction_accessibility: MUST_BE_VERIFIED_PER_ATTRACTION Rule: Never infer accessibility from destination-level accessibility. Each hotel and attraction must carry its own accessibility data.', 4819),
  ('cochin', 24, 'food', 'FOOD', NULL, NULL, 'Kochi is particularly strong for: Food experiences: Family: Prioritize clean, convenient restaurants with familiar and flexible menus. Honeymoon: At least one memorable dinner or waterfront meal is recommended. Luxury: Fine dining, premium seafood, and curated tasting experiences may be important. Budget: Mix local eateries, casual restaurants, and selected paid dining experiences.', 4820),
  ('cochin', 25, 'shopping', 'SHOPPING', NULL, NULL, 'Strong categories: Luxury shopping: Prefer premium malls, high-end jewellery stores, and curated handicraft boutiques. Prefer:', 4821),
  ('cochin', 26, 'nightlife', 'NIGHTLIFE', NULL, NULL, 'nightlife_level: 85 Suitable for: Not a primary requirement for: Honeymoon travelers should generally prefer: romantic evening over: late-night club itinerary unless nightlife is explicitly requested.', 4822),
  ('cochin', 28, 'sample-itinerary-patterns', 'SAMPLE ITINERARY PATTERNS', NULL, NULL, '3 NIGHTS Day 1 Arrival → Hotel → Fort Kochi light exploration → Dinner Day 2 Morning: Fort Kochi core Afternoon: Mattancherry / Jew Town Evening: Waterfront dinner or sunset Day 3 Morning: One major attraction Afternoon: One relaxed activity or café stop Evening: Free time / romantic dinner Day 4 Breakfast → Airport transfer → Departure', 4823),
  ('cochin', 29, 'five-night-honeymoon-pattern-for-kochi', 'FIVE-NIGHT HONEYMOON PATTERN FOR KOCHI', 'Day 1', NULL, 'Arrival → Private transfer → Hotel in Fort Kochi or Bolgatty → Relax → Romantic dinner', 4824),
  ('cochin', 29, 'five-night-honeymoon-pattern-for-kochi', 'FIVE-NIGHT HONEYMOON PATTERN FOR KOCHI', 'Day 2', NULL, 'Morning: Fort Kochi heritage walk → Chinese fishing nets → St. Francis Church / Santa Cruz Basilica Afternoon: Lunch → Relaxed café time → Slow exploration Evening: Sunset at Fort Kochi or Marine Drive → Waterfront dinner', 4825),
  ('cochin', 29, 'five-night-honeymoon-pattern-for-kochi', 'FIVE-NIGHT HONEYMOON PATTERN FOR KOCHI', 'Day 3', NULL, 'Morning: Mattancherry / Jew Town → Mattancherry Palace → Spice market stroll Afternoon: Free time → Hotel rest → Spa or café break Evening: Private backwater cruise or sunset cruise → Romantic dinner', 4826),
  ('cochin', 29, 'five-night-honeymoon-pattern-for-kochi', 'FIVE-NIGHT HONEYMOON PATTERN FOR KOCHI', 'Day 4', NULL, 'Morning: Cherai Beach → Leisure walk → Couple time Afternoon: Lunch by the beach → Return to hotel → Downtime Evening: Optional Kathakali performance or quiet dinner', 4827),
  ('cochin', 29, 'five-night-honeymoon-pattern-for-kochi', 'FIVE-NIGHT HONEYMOON PATTERN FOR KOCHI', 'Day 5', NULL, 'Morning: Flexible → Sleep in → Late breakfast Afternoon: Shopping for spices / handicrafts → Optional massage or spa → Free time Evening: Premium farewell dinner → Special romantic experience', 4828),
  ('cochin', 29, 'five-night-honeymoon-pattern-for-kochi', 'FIVE-NIGHT HONEYMOON PATTERN FOR KOCHI', 'Day 6', NULL, 'Breakfast → Checkout → Airport transfer', 4829),
  ('cochin', 30, 'five-night-family-pattern-for-kochi', 'FIVE-NIGHT FAMILY PATTERN FOR KOCHI', 'Day 1', NULL, 'Arrival → Private transfer → Hotel in Fort Kochi or Ernakulam → Dinner → Rest', 4830),
  ('cochin', 30, 'five-night-family-pattern-for-kochi', 'FIVE-NIGHT FAMILY PATTERN FOR KOCHI', 'Day 2', NULL, 'Fort Kochi heritage area → Chinese fishing nets → Lunch → Early dinner', 4831),
  ('cochin', 30, 'five-night-family-pattern-for-kochi', 'FIVE-NIGHT FAMILY PATTERN FOR KOCHI', 'Day 3', NULL, 'Mattancherry / Jew Town → Mattancherry Palace → Lunch → Spice market walk → Relax at hotel', 4832),
  ('cochin', 30, 'five-night-family-pattern-for-kochi', 'FIVE-NIGHT FAMILY PATTERN FOR KOCHI', 'Day 4', NULL, 'Marine Drive → One major family-friendly attraction → Lunch → Free time or café stop → Evening stroll', 4833),
  ('cochin', 30, 'five-night-family-pattern-for-kochi', 'FIVE-NIGHT FAMILY PATTERN FOR KOCHI', 'Day 5', NULL, 'Flexible: shopping / Cherai Beach / backwater cruise / optional attraction', 4834),
  ('cochin', 30, 'five-night-family-pattern-for-kochi', 'FIVE-NIGHT FAMILY PATTERN FOR KOCHI', 'Day 6', NULL, 'Breakfast → Checkout → Airport transfer', 4835),
  ('cochin', 31, 'five-night-luxury-pattern-for-kochi', 'FIVE-NIGHT LUXURY PATTERN FOR KOCHI', 'Day 1', NULL, 'Arrival → Private transfer → Luxury hotel in Fort Kochi or Bolgatty → Relax → Premium dinner', 4836),
  ('cochin', 31, 'five-night-luxury-pattern-for-kochi', 'FIVE-NIGHT LUXURY PATTERN FOR KOCHI', 'Day 2', NULL, 'Private guided Fort Kochi experience → Chinese fishing nets → Premium lunch → Free afternoon → Fine dining', 4837),
  ('cochin', 31, 'five-night-luxury-pattern-for-kochi', 'FIVE-NIGHT LUXURY PATTERN FOR KOCHI', 'Day 3', NULL, 'Mattancherry / Jew Town private cultural visit → Relaxed exploration → Spa → Romantic dinner', 4838),
  ('cochin', 31, 'five-night-luxury-pattern-for-kochi', 'FIVE-NIGHT LUXURY PATTERN FOR KOCHI', 'Day 4', NULL, 'Private shopping / heritage neighborhood experience → Free afternoon → Premium backwater or sunset cruise', 4839),
  ('cochin', 31, 'five-night-luxury-pattern-for-kochi', 'FIVE-NIGHT LUXURY PATTERN FOR KOCHI', 'Day 5', NULL, 'Flexible premium experience → Cherai Beach or waterfront leisure → Fine dining', 4840),
  ('cochin', 31, 'five-night-luxury-pattern-for-kochi', 'FIVE-NIGHT LUXURY PATTERN FOR KOCHI', 'Day 6', NULL, 'Private airport transfer → Departure', 4841),
  ('cochin', 32, 'travel-agent-insights', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS', 'What inexperienced planners often do wrong', NULL, '', 4842),
