  ('rameswaram', 31, 'six-nights-luxury-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 4', NULL, 'Private guided Kodaikanal experience → Bryant Park → Coaker''s Walk → Pillar Rock → Suicide Point → Premium lunch → Hotel relaxation → Kodai Lake → Premium dinner → Overnight at Kodaikanal', 5203),
  ('rameswaram', 31, 'six-nights-luxury-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 5', NULL, 'Breakfast → Private chauffeur transfer from Kodaikanal to Rameswaram → Premium hotel check-in → Relax → Evening private pilgrimage experience → Ramanathaswamy Temple → Premium dinner → Overnight at Rameswaram', 5204),
  ('rameswaram', 31, 'six-nights-luxury-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 6', NULL, 'Breakfast → Private chauffeur transfer from Rameswaram to Madurai → Premium lunch → Meenakshi Sundareshwara Temple → Temple Art Museum → Puthu Mandapam → Raya Gopuram → Premium hotel check-in → Relaxed evening → Premium Tamil dinner → Overnight at Madurai', 5205),
  ('rameswaram', 31, 'six-nights-luxury-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 7', NULL, 'Breakfast → Private transfer → Madurai Airport / Railway Station → Departure', 5206),
  ('rameswaram', 32, 'travel-agent-insights', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS', 'What inexperienced planners often do wrong', NULL, '', 5207),
  ('rameswaram', 32, 'travel-agent-insights', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS', 'What an experienced planner does differently', NULL, '', 5208),
  ('rameswaram', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', NULL, NULL, 'IF: trip_length <= 2 nights THEN: do not recommend Devipattinam or Thirupullani as default day trips. Reason: The additional road travel can make a short Rameshwaram stay unnecessarily rushed. IF: trip_type == HONEYMOON THEN: increase romance_weight by 20% increase privacy_weight by 15% increase free_time_weight by 25% decrease activity_density by 20% Reason: The objective is a peaceful and romantic coastal/spiritual experience rather than maximum sightseeing. IF: traveler_type == FAMILY AND: children_age <= 6 THEN: reduce travel_intensity_target by 20% increase downtime by 20% prefer short sightseeing + coastal activities Reason: Young children can find heat, temple queues and long road journeys tiring. IF: hotel_is_far_from_ramanathaswamy_temple AND: hotel_saving < additional_transport_cost + value_of_lost_time THEN: prefer_hotel_near_central_rameshwaram Reason: A cheaper hotel may not provide better total value once daily transport costs and travel time are considered. IF: trip_length <= 3 nights THEN: prefer_one_hotel Reason: Hotel changes consume valuable short-trip time. IF: trip_length >= 4 nights AND: traveler_interest == PILGRIMAGE_AND_CULTURE THEN: consider_rameshwaram + NEARBY_PILGRIMAGE_SITES Reason: A longer stay makes it practical to explore Rameshwaram''s core temples along with destinations such as Devipattinam and Thirupullani. IF: traveler_type == LUXURY THEN: prefer_private_transfer AND: prefer_high_service_hotel AND: prefer_private_or_personalized_experiences Reason: Luxury value in Rameshwaram is primarily created through comfort, convenience, privacy, service and personalized sightseeing. IF: traveler_type == BUDGET THEN: prefer_central_hotel_location AND: use_local_bus_or_auto_where_practical AND: mix_free_and_paid_attractions Reason: Maintain pilgrimage and sightseeing quality while reducing unnecessary transportation and accommodation costs. IF: traveler_interest == PILGRIMAGE_AND_SPIRITUALITY THEN: prefer_CENTRAL_RAMESHWARAM AND: group_ramanathaswamy_temple + agni_theertham + nearby_temples Reason: The central area provides convenient access to Rameshwaram''s principal pilgrimage attractions. IF: traveler_interest == COASTAL_AND_PHOTOGRAPHY THEN: prefer_DHANUSHKODI_AND_PAMBAN AND: group_coastal_views + bridge_views + sunrise_or_sunset Reason: Dhanushkodi and Pamban provide some of Rameshwaram''s strongest coastal and photographic experiences. IF: traveler_interest == HISTORY_AND_CULTURE THEN: prefer_CENTRAL_RAMESHWARAM AND: group_ramanathaswamy_temple + gandhamadana_parvatham + APJ_ABDUL_KALAM_MEMORIAL Reason: These attractions provide a strong combination of religious heritage, local history and cultural significance. IF: trip_length >= 4 nights AND: traveler_interest == PILGRIMAGE + COASTAL THEN: consider_split_itinerary BETWEEN: CENTRAL_RAMESHWARAM + DHANUSHKODI/PAMBAN Reason: Separating the temple-focused and coastal sightseeing days reduces unnecessary backtracking and keeps the itinerary comfortable.', 5209),
  ('rameswaram', 34, 'destination-scoring', 'DESTINATION SCORING', NULL, NULL, '| Factor | Score | | ------------------ | ----: | | Family | 88 | | Honeymoon | 72 | | Luxury | 58 | | Budget | 91 | | Adventure | 72 | | Culture | 98 | | Food | 82 | | Shopping | 68 | | Nightlife | 25 | | Relaxation | 80 | | Nature | 89 | | Accessibility | 60 | | Safety | 80 | | First-time visitor | 90 | | Photography | 94 |', 5210),
  ('rameswaram', 35, 'final-travel-agent-verdict', 'FINAL TRAVEL AGENT VERDICT', NULL, NULL, 'Best traveler profiles: 1. Pilgrimage traveler 2. Culture / heritage traveler 3. Family traveler 4. Spiritual traveler 5. Photography traveler 6. Budget traveler 7. Coastal / nature traveler 8. Senior traveler with appropriate pacing Best duration: 2–3 nights Best season: December–February September–March Best hotel strategy: Choose a clean, well-reviewed hotel based on proximity to Ramanathaswamy Temple, transport access, and the main purpose of the trip. Best transportation: Auto-rickshaws, taxis, local buses and private drivers depending on distance, budget and comfort. Private transfer for: Must-do for first-time visitor: Don''t-do: Biggest advantage: Exceptional combination of pilgrimage, spirituality, Tamil cultural heritage, historic sites, coastal scenery, Dhanushkodi, Pamban Bridge and affordable travel. Biggest disadvantage: Limited nightlife and luxury infrastructure, hot and humid weather for much of the year, variable accessibility, and longer transfers for some coastal and nearby pilgrimage attractions. Overall destination score: 84/100', 5211),
  ('rameswaram', 36, 'data-quality', 'DATA QUALITY', NULL, NULL, 'information_completeness: 88/100 last_updated: 2026-08-15 last_verified: PARTIALLY_WEB_VERIFIED verified_by: OFFICIAL_RAMANATHAPURAM_DISTRICT_AND_GOVERNMENT_OF_INDIA_TOURISM_SOURCES sources: IMPORTANT: Prices, opening hours, temple schedules, availability, accessibility, transport schedules, weather conditions and operational conditions must NOT be treated as permanently valid from this document. Temple timings, darshan procedures, special pooja schedules and religious-event conditions must be checked against the latest official temple or local authority information before travel. Attraction opening hours, ticket prices, transport schedules, road conditions and accessibility should be sourced from structured, refreshable data. Dhanushkodi and other coastal areas may be affected by weather, sea conditions, road restrictions and local administrative decisions. Rameswaram travel conditions can vary during major religious festivals, holidays and peak pilgrimage periods. This dataset should be refreshed regularly before production use.', 5212),
  ('kodaikanal', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Spring', NULL, 'months: March April May weather: Cool to mild in March, gradually becoming warmer through April and May, with pleasant mornings and evenings and occasional pre-monsoon showers. Kodaikanal remains considerably cooler than the plains, although May can become relatively warm during the daytime. crowd_level: HIGH price_level: MEDIUM → HIGH overall_score: 87-92 recommended: true reason: A good period for Kodaikanal sightseeing, particularly for travelers interested in pleasant hill-station weather, Kodaikanal Lake, gardens, viewpoints, waterfalls, forests, and outdoor activities. April and May are popular holiday months, so accommodation and transport demand can increase. Early booking is recommended during school holidays and long weekends.', 5213),
  ('kodaikanal', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Summer', NULL, 'months: June July August weather: Cool, cloudy, misty, and frequently rainy due to the southwest monsoon. Temperatures remain comfortable, but showers can interrupt sightseeing, trekking, viewpoints, and longer road journeys. crowd_level: MEDIUM → LOW price_level: MEDIUM → LOW overall_score: 78-85 recommended: true reason: A suitable period for travelers who enjoy misty mountain scenery, lush forests, waterfalls, cool temperatures, and a quieter hill-station atmosphere. Rain can reduce visibility at viewpoints and affect outdoor activities, so flexible sightseeing plans and weather checks are recommended.', 5214),
  ('kodaikanal', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Autumn', NULL, 'months: September October November weather: Cool to mild with increasing rainfall and cloud cover during the northeast monsoon, particularly in October and November. Misty conditions are common, while forests, waterfalls, valleys, and surrounding hills become lush and scenic. crowd_level: LOW → MEDIUM price_level: LOW → MEDIUM overall_score: 83-89 recommended: true reason: September is a strong shoulder-season option for sightseeing, photography, nature walks, waterfalls, and relaxed stays. October and November can receive more rainfall, but the landscape can be particularly green and atmospheric. Travelers should check local weather conditions before planning trekking, forest excursions, or longer journeys to remote attractions.', 5215),
  ('kodaikanal', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Winter', NULL, 'months: December January February weather: Cool to cold, generally comfortable during the daytime, with chilly mornings and evenings. Mist, low temperatures, and occasional cold conditions are common, particularly during December and January. crowd_level: MEDIUM → HIGH price_level: MEDIUM → HIGH overall_score: 91-95 recommended: true reason: One of the best overall periods to visit Kodaikanal for comfortable sightseeing, honeymoon trips, photography, scenic walks, lake experiences, waterfalls, and relaxed mountain holidays. December and January can see increased demand because of the festive holiday season, while February generally offers a good balance of cool weather and manageable visitor levels. Warm clothing is recommended for early mornings and evenings.', 5216),
  ('kodaikanal', 10, 'budget-strategy', 'BUDGET STRATEGY', NULL, NULL, 'Where money can be saved: Where saving money is usually NOT recommended: Travel-agent rule: A slightly more expensive but clean, well-reviewed and reasonably central hotel in Kodaikanal usually delivers better total value than a cheaper property far outside town once you factor in daily taxi costs, winding mountain roads, travel time, weather, and sightseeing convenience.', 5217),
  ('kodaikanal', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Family', 'family', 'Pre-booked private car / MPV or reliable taxi from Madurai International Airport; door-to-door service, sufficient luggage space, and convenient for children. Kodaikanal is approximately 120 km from Madurai Airport by road, so a direct private transfer is generally the most convenient family option.', 5218),
  ('kodaikanal', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Honeymoon', 'honeymoon', 'Pre-booked private car with direct hotel drop-off; comfortable and convenient for couples arriving at Madurai International Airport. A private transfer is especially suitable for couples carrying luggage and wanting a relaxed start to their hill-station stay. reason: Madurai is the nearest major airport for Kodaikanal, while Kodaikanal is connected to Madurai by road and regular bus services. The journey includes winding hill roads and can take several hours depending on traffic and weather, making a private transfer more comfortable and convenient for most travelers.', 5219),
  ('kodaikanal', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Luxury', 'luxury', 'Chauffeured premium SUV / MPV or private luxury car from Madurai International Airport; personalized pickup, comfortable hill-road transfer, luggage assistance, and direct hotel drop-off suitable for premium resorts and boutique properties.', 5220),
  ('kodaikanal', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Budget', 'budget', 'Public bus from Madurai where practical; shared/local taxi or standard private cab for travelers prioritizing convenience. Bus services connect Madurai with Kodaikanal, while travelers can also use bus connections through Batlagundu depending on the route and schedule. Public transport is generally the most economical option, although the journey takes longer and involves less flexibility than a private transfer.', 5221),
  ('kodaikanal', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Senior', 'senior', 'Pre-booked private car or airport taxi with minimal transfers and direct hotel drop-off; prioritize comfortable seating, luggage assistance, and avoiding unnecessary changes between airport, bus, and hill transport. A direct road transfer is generally preferable for seniors because Kodaikanal is a high-altitude hill destination and the journey includes winding mountain-road sections.', 5222),
  ('kodaikanal', 18, 'family-travel', 'FAMILY TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'child_friendly_score: 91 best_ages: Rules: For young children: Prefer: Avoid:', 5223),
  ('kodaikanal', 19, 'honeymoon-travel', 'HONEYMOON TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'honeymoon_score: 94 romance_score: 95 privacy_score: 84 luxury_score: 70 Recommended: Honeymoon itinerary should NOT contain more than: 2 major activities/day. Prefer: One memorable scenic, nature, lake, or forest experience + free time over: Three or four attractions. Recommended hotel areas: Kodaikanal works particularly well for a romantic honeymoon because of its cool mountain climate, misty hills, pine forests, scenic lake, viewpoints, waterfalls, gardens, and peaceful atmosphere. Kodaikanal Lake, Coaker''s Walk, Pillar Rocks, Pine Forest, Bryant Park, and scenic mountain roads can each provide memorable couple experiences, but they should be spread across the itinerary rather than packed into a single day. Private transport is recommended for couples who want flexibility and comfort, especially when visiting Berijam Lake, Mannavanur, Dolphin''s Nose, Silver Cascade, or other attractions outside central Kodaikanal. The winding hill roads and changing weather can make longer sightseeing routes tiring if too many distant attractions are combined. Kodaikanal is better suited to couples seeking a peaceful, scenic, nature-focused, and romantic hill-station honeymoon than couples looking for an ultra-luxury resort destination with extensive nightlife, private villas, or large-scale premium entertainment.', 5224),
  ('kodaikanal', 20, 'luxury-travel', 'LUXURY TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'luxury_score: 70 Recommended: Kodaikanal luxury travel should focus on: Luxury travelers should not simply be given more activities. Luxury in Kodaikanal should primarily increase:', 5225),
  ('kodaikanal', 21, 'adventure', 'ADVENTURE', NULL, NULL, 'adventure_score: 82 Kodaikanal is primarily a hill-station and nature destination, but it offers a strong range of outdoor and moderate-to-challenging adventure experiences across the Palani Hills. Trekking, hiking, cycling, boating, horse riding, nature walks, camping, and forest exploration are among its notable outdoor activities. Adventure experiences should be interpreted as:', 5226),
  ('kodaikanal', 22, 'senior-travel', 'SENIOR TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'senior_suitability: 84 walking_intensity: MEDIUM unless carefully managed Rules:', 5227),
  ('kodaikanal', 23, 'accessibility', 'ACCESSIBILITY', NULL, NULL, 'wheelchair_accessibility: PARTIAL; varies significantly by hotel, attraction, terrain and transport public_transport_accessibility: VARIABLE; private cars/taxis are often more practical for wheelchair users because of Kodaikanal''s hilly terrain and spread-out attractions hotel_accessibility: MUST_BE_VERIFIED_PER_HOTEL attraction_accessibility: MUST_BE_VERIFIED_PER_ATTRACTION Rule: Never infer accessibility from Kodaikanal''s overall accessibility. Each hotel and attraction must carry its own accessibility data. Additional notes:', 5228),
  ('kodaikanal', 24, 'food', 'FOOD', NULL, NULL, 'Kodaikanal is particularly strong for: Food experiences: Family: Prioritize clean, family-friendly restaurants with vegetarian options, familiar South Indian dishes, bakery items, mild food choices, and flexible menus. Honeymoon: A comfortable hill-view, lake-view, resort, or café dinner is recommended, with a relaxed evening after sightseeing. Luxury: Premium resorts, boutique hotels, curated multi-cuisine dining, private dining, scenic restaurant experiences, and high-quality local chocolate, coffee, and food experiences can be included, although Kodaikanal has a smaller fine-dining scene than major metropolitan or luxury resort destinations. Budget: Mix local South Indian restaurants, vegetarian eateries, bakeries, affordable cafés, tiffin outlets, small local restaurants, and casual hill-station dining experiences.', 5229),
  ('kodaikanal', 25, 'shopping', 'SHOPPING', NULL, NULL, 'Strong categories: Luxury shopping: Prefer established specialty stores, artisan outlets, gourmet shops, and curated local-product stores around PT Road, Bazaar Road, Anna Salai, and central Kodaikanal for premium chocolates, organic coffee, specialty spices, essential oils, handicrafts, artwork, cheese, and locally produced gourmet products. Kodaikanal''s shopping scene is more focused on local and artisanal products than high-end branded shopping. Budget: Prefer: Kodaikanal is particularly known for homemade chocolates, eucalyptus and other essential oils, spices, coffee, honey, jams, handicrafts, pottery, woollens, and locally produced food products. The municipal shopping directory also identifies Anna Salai Market, Potter''s Shed, Kodai Chocolate Factory, Spices Corner, and other local outlets as notable shopping options. Travel-agent rule: Prioritize authentic locally produced goods over generic tourist-shop merchandise. For chocolates, oils, coffee, honey, spices, and other consumables, compare quality and packaging before purchasing, and prefer established local producers or specialty stores where authenticity and product quality are easier to verify.', 5230),
  ('kodaikanal', 26, 'nightlife', 'NIGHTLIFE', NULL, NULL, 'nightlife_level: 35 Suitable for: Best areas: Not a primary requirement for: Evening activities are better suited to: Honeymoon travelers should generally prefer: Romantic mountain evening over: Late-night party or club itinerary unless nightlife is explicitly requested. For couples seeking a more atmospheric evening, prioritize a cozy café, premium hotel dinner, dessert or homemade-chocolate experience, resort-based evening, or safe stargazing/campfire experience rather than building the itinerary around nightlife. Travel-agent rule: Do not position Kodaikanal as a nightlife destination. Position its evening appeal around peaceful mountain atmosphere, cafés, dining, lake surroundings, romantic experiences, and resort-based relaxation.', 5231),
  ('kodaikanal', 28, 'sample-itinerary-patterns', 'SAMPLE ITINERARY PATTERNS', '3 NIGHTS', NULL, '### Day 1 Arrival at Madurai → Road transfer to Kodaikanal → Hotel check-in → Kodaikanal Lake / Boat Club → Bryant Park → Central Kodaikanal / Anna Salai → Dinner ### Day 2 Morning: Coaker''s Walk → Bryant Park / relaxed garden experience Afternoon: Pillar Rocks → Guna Caves → Pine Forest Evening: Kodaikanal Lake / café → Local market / shopping → Hotel ### Day 3 Morning: Poombarai Village → Poombarai scenic viewpoints → Kuzhanthai Velappar Temple Afternoon: Mannavanur Lake / scenic countryside → Return to Kodaikanal → Hotel / rest Evening: Sunset / relaxed mountain-view experience → Dinner ### Day 4 Breakfast → Hotel checkout → Road transfer to Madurai → Airport / railway station → Departure', 5232),
  ('kodaikanal', 29, 'six-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 1', NULL, 'Arrival at Coimbatore Airport / Railway Station → Private transfer to Ooty → Romantic hotel check-in → Relax and enjoy the hotel → Romantic dinner → Overnight at Ooty Intensity: LOW', 5233),
  ('kodaikanal', 29, 'six-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 2', NULL, 'Morning: Private Ooty sightseeing → Doddabetta Peak → Botanical Garden Afternoon: Private lunch → Ooty Lake → Optional boating / horse riding → Hotel relaxation Evening: Free time → Romantic dinner Intensity: MEDIUM', 5234),
  ('kodaikanal', 29, 'six-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 3', NULL, 'Breakfast → Private chauffeur transfer from Ooty to Kodaikanal → Romantic hotel check-in → Relax → Leisure evening → Special dinner Intensity: LOW–MEDIUM', 5235),
