  ('kodaikanal', 31, 'six-nights-luxury-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 2', NULL, 'Private guided Ooty sightseeing → Doddabetta Peak → Premium lunch → Botanical Garden → Ooty Lake → Optional private boating / leisure experience → Hotel relaxation → Premium dinner', 5248),
  ('kodaikanal', 31, 'six-nights-luxury-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 3', NULL, 'Breakfast → Private chauffeur transfer from Ooty to Kodaikanal → Premium hotel check-in → Relax and enjoy the hotel → Private / premium dinner → Overnight at Kodaikanal', 5249),
  ('kodaikanal', 31, 'six-nights-luxury-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 4', NULL, 'Private guided Kodaikanal experience → Bryant Park → Coaker''s Walk → Pillar Rock → Suicide Point → Premium lunch → Hotel relaxation → Kodai Lake → Premium dinner → Overnight at Kodaikanal', 5250),
  ('kodaikanal', 31, 'six-nights-luxury-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 5', NULL, 'Breakfast → Private chauffeur transfer from Kodaikanal to Rameswaram → Premium hotel check-in → Relax → Evening private pilgrimage experience → Ramanathaswamy Temple → Premium dinner → Overnight at Rameswaram', 5251),
  ('kodaikanal', 31, 'six-nights-luxury-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 6', NULL, 'Breakfast → Private chauffeur transfer from Rameswaram to Madurai → Premium lunch → Meenakshi Sundareshwara Temple → Temple Art Museum → Puthu Mandapam → Raya Gopuram → Premium hotel check-in → Relaxed evening → Premium Tamil dinner → Overnight at Madurai', 5252),
  ('kodaikanal', 31, 'six-nights-luxury-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 7', NULL, 'Breakfast → Private transfer → Madurai Airport / Railway Station → Departure', 5253),
  ('kodaikanal', 32, 'travel-agent-insights', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS', 'What inexperienced planners often do wrong', NULL, '', 5254),
  ('kodaikanal', 32, 'travel-agent-insights', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS', 'What an experienced planner does differently', NULL, '', 5255),
  ('kodaikanal', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', NULL, NULL, 'IF: trip_length <= 2 nights THEN: do not recommend Berijam Lake, Poombarai, Mannavanur or wider Palani Hills day trips as default additions. Reason: The additional mountain-road travel can make a short Kodaikanal stay unnecessarily rushed. IF: trip_type == HONEYMOON THEN: increase romance_weight by 20% increase privacy_weight by 15% increase free_time_weight by 25% decrease activity_density by 20% Reason: The objective is a peaceful and romantic mountain experience rather than maximum sightseeing. IF: traveler_type == FAMILY AND: children_age <= 6 THEN: reduce travel_intensity_target by 20% increase downtime by 20% prefer short sightseeing + gardens + lake + scenic experiences Reason: Young children can find winding mountain roads, long transfers, cold/rainy weather and excessive sightseeing tiring. IF: hotel_is_far_from_central_kodaikanal AND: hotel_saving < additional_transport_cost + value_of_lost_time THEN: prefer_hotel_near_central_kodaikanal Reason: A cheaper hotel may not provide better total value once daily taxi costs, mountain travel time and sightseeing convenience are considered. IF: trip_length <= 3 nights THEN: prefer_one_hotel Reason: Hotel changes consume valuable short-trip time and reduce time available for sightseeing and relaxation. IF: trip_length >= 4 nights AND: traveler_interest == NATURE_AND_SCENIC_EXPLORATION THEN: consider_kodaikanal + NEARBY_PALANI_HILLS_DESTINATIONS Reason: A longer stay makes it practical to explore Kodaikanal''s core attractions along with destinations such as Poombarai, Mannavanur, Berijam and other surrounding Palani Hills experiences. IF: traveler_type == LUXURY THEN: prefer_private_transfer AND: prefer_high_service_hotel AND: prefer_private_or_personalized_experiences Reason: Luxury value in Kodaikanal is primarily created through comfort, convenience, privacy, service, premium accommodation, scenic access and personalized sightseeing. IF: traveler_type == BUDGET THEN: prefer_central_hotel_location AND: use_local_bus_or_auto_where_practical AND: mix_free_and_paid_attractions Reason: Maintain sightseeing quality while reducing unnecessary transportation and accommodation costs. IF: traveler_interest == NATURE_AND_RELAXATION THEN: prefer_CENTRAL_KODAIKANAL AND: group_kodaikanal_lake + bryant_park + coakers_walk + nearby_scenic_experiences Reason: Central Kodaikanal provides convenient access to the lake, gardens, viewpoints, restaurants, cafés, shopping and other relaxed sightseeing experiences. IF: traveler_interest == SCENIC_AND_PHOTOGRAPHY THEN: prefer_PILLAR_ROCKS_AND_POOMBARAI AND: group_mountain_views + pine_forest + valley_views + scenic_villages Reason: Pillar Rocks, Poombarai, Mannavanur and the surrounding Palani Hills provide some of Kodaikanal''s strongest scenic and photographic experiences. IF: traveler_interest == ADVENTURE_AND_OUTDOORS THEN: prefer_VATTAKANAL_AND_PALANI_HILLS AND: group_trekking + nature_trails + viewpoints + waterfall_experiences Reason: Vattakanal and the surrounding Palani Hills offer opportunities for hiking, nature walks, viewpoints, waterfall exploration and other outdoor experiences. IF: traveler_interest == HISTORY_AND_CULTURE THEN: prefer_CENTRAL_KODAIKANAL AND: group_coakers_walk + kodaikanal_solar_observatory + shenbaganur_museum + local_temple_experiences Reason: These experiences provide a combination of Kodaikanal''s colonial-era character, scientific heritage, local culture, botanical heritage and religious traditions. IF: traveler_interest == NATURE + RURAL_EXPLORATION THEN: consider_POOMBARAI_AND_MANNAVANUR AND: group_village_views + terraced_hills + lake_views + rural_landscapes Reason: Poombarai and Mannavanur provide a quieter countryside experience beyond central Kodaikanal, with scenic valleys, agricultural landscapes, villages and mountain views. IF: trip_length >= 4 nights AND: traveler_interest == NATURE + SCENIC_EXPLORATION THEN: consider_split_itinerary BETWEEN: CENTRAL_KODAIKANAL + POOMBARAI/MANNAVANUR/BERIJAM Reason: Separating central Kodaikanal sightseeing from longer nature excursions reduces unnecessary backtracking and keeps the itinerary comfortable. IF: traveler_interest == FOREST_AND_WILDERNESS THEN: consider_BERIJAM_LAKE AND: verify_forest_access_and_PERMITS Reason: Berijam is located within a protected forest environment and access conditions can be regulated, so availability, permissions and local forest rules should be verified before including it in the itinerary. IF: weather == HEAVY_RAIN OR: visibility == LOW THEN: reduce_viewpoint_and_remote_outdoor_activities AND: prefer_CENTRAL_KODAIKANAL AND: increase_flexible_indoor_or_hotel_time Reason: Rain, fog and poor visibility can reduce the value and safety of viewpoints, forest excursions and longer mountain-road journeys. IF: traveler_interest == ROMANTIC_RELAXATION THEN: prefer_KODAIKANAL_LAKE + COAKERS_WALK + SCENIC_VIEWPOINTS AND: decrease_activity_density_by_20_percent Reason: Couples generally benefit more from scenic walks, boating, mountain views, cafés and free time than from packing multiple distant attractions into one day.', 5256),
  ('kodaikanal', 34, 'destination-scoring', 'DESTINATION SCORING', NULL, NULL, '| Factor | Score | | ------------------ | ----: | | Family | 92 | | Honeymoon | 94 | | Luxury | 70 | | Budget | 87 | | Adventure | 82 | | Culture | 82 | | Food | 84 | | Shopping | 80 | | Nightlife | 35 | | Relaxation | 97 | | Nature | 99 | | Accessibility | 65 | | Safety | 83 | | First-time visitor | 94 | | Photography | 99 |', 5257),
  ('kodaikanal', 35, 'final-travel-agent-verdict', 'FINAL TRAVEL AGENT VERDICT', NULL, NULL, 'Best traveler profiles: 1. Nature traveler 2. Honeymoon / romantic traveler 3. Family traveler 4. Relaxation / leisure traveler 5. Photography traveler 6. Adventure / outdoor traveler 7. Budget traveler 8. Culture / heritage traveler 9. Spiritual / temple traveler 10. Senior traveler with appropriate pacing Best duration: 3–4 nights Best season: October–June October–February for cool weather, misty landscapes, and comfortable sightseeing March–May for pleasant summer escapes and popular seasonal activities June–September for travelers comfortable with rain, greener landscapes, and fewer crowds Best hotel strategy: Choose a clean, well-reviewed hotel, resort, cottage, or heritage property based on proximity to central Kodaikanal, Kodaikanal Lake, transport access, mountain views, weather preferences, and the main purpose of the trip. Best transportation: Private cars, taxis, local buses, auto-rickshaws, walking, boating, cycling, and guided/local transport depending on distance, budget, comfort, and itinerary. Private transport for: Must-do for first-time visitor: Don''t-do: Biggest advantage: Exceptional combination of cool and misty mountain climate, Kodaikanal Lake, forests, waterfalls, viewpoints, pine landscapes, gardens, trekking opportunities, village experiences, photography, romantic atmosphere, and quieter nature experiences around the Palani Hills. Biggest disadvantage: Limited nightlife compared with major cities, seasonal traffic and crowding, winding mountain roads, variable weather, partial accessibility at some outdoor attractions, and longer transfers or additional permissions for certain remote forest and nature destinations. Overall destination score: 90/100', 5258),
  ('kodaikanal', 36, 'data-quality', 'DATA QUALITY', NULL, NULL, 'information_completeness: 91/100 last_updated: 2026-08-17 last_verified: PARTIALLY_WEB_VERIFIED verified_by: OFFICIAL_DINDIGUL_DISTRICT_ADMINISTRATION_AND_GOVERNMENT_OF_INDIA_TOURISM_SOURCES sources: IMPORTANT: Prices, opening hours, ticket prices, boating availability, attraction operating conditions, accessibility, transport schedules, road conditions, weather conditions and other operational details must NOT be treated as permanently valid from this document. Kodaikanal Observatory visitor timings and access conditions must be checked against the latest official information before travel. Attraction opening hours, ticket prices, boating schedules, local transport availability and accessibility should be sourced from structured, refreshable data. Berijam Lake, Kodaikanal Forest Division attractions, forest areas, trekking locations and other remote nature destinations may be affected by weather, rainfall, fog, road conditions, forest regulations, permits and local administrative decisions. Kodaikanal travel conditions can vary significantly during peak summer periods, weekends, holidays, festivals, flower-show periods, monsoon periods and major local events. Mountain-road travel times should be treated as variable because traffic, weather, road conditions, road restrictions and seasonal congestion can affect journey duration. Berijam Lake requires appropriate Forest Department permission/access arrangements, and access conditions should be verified before including it in an itinerary. Accessibility must be verified separately for each hotel, attraction, transport service and activity because Kodaikanal''s steep terrain, forest paths, viewpoints and outdoor environments can create significant differences in practical accessibility. Weather information should be treated as a planning guide rather than a guarantee. Remote attractions such as Berijam Lake, Poombarai, Kookal, Mannavanur and other surrounding nature areas should not be assumed to have the same accessibility, transport availability or operating conditions as central Kodaikanal. Kodaikanal''s tourism infrastructure and operating conditions may change seasonally or through local administrative decisions. This dataset should be refreshed regularly before production use.', 5259),
  ('madurai', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Spring', NULL, 'months: March April May weather: Hot and humid, with temperatures rising toward May and occasional pre-monsoon showers. crowd_level: MEDIUM price_level: MEDIUM overall_score: 82-87 recommended: true reason: A good period for Rameshwaram pilgrimage and sightseeing, especially in March and April. The Ramanathaswamy Temple and coastal attractions can be busy around major religious festivals. May can be quite hot, so sightseeing should be planned around cooler morning and evening hours.', 5260),
  ('madurai', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Summer', NULL, 'months: June July August weather: Hot, humid, and generally influenced by the southwest monsoon, although Rameshwaram receives less rainfall than many parts of Tamil Nadu. crowd_level: MEDIUM → LOW price_level: MEDIUM → LOW overall_score: 75-82 recommended: true reason: A workable period for travelers who can manage the heat and humidity. Tourist crowds are generally lower than during major pilgrimage and festival periods. Early-morning temple visits and shorter outdoor sightseeing sessions are recommended.', 5261),
  ('madurai', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Autumn', NULL, 'months: September October November weather: Warm and humid, with increasing rainfall risk during the northeast monsoon, particularly in October and November. crowd_level: MEDIUM price_level: MEDIUM overall_score: 78-85 recommended: true reason: September can be a comfortable shoulder-season option for sightseeing. October and November may bring more rain because of the northeast monsoon, but the weather can remain suitable for temple visits and cultural travel between showers. Check local weather conditions before planning coastal excursions.', 5262),
  ('madurai', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Winter', NULL, 'months: December January February weather: Warm to pleasantly warm, relatively dry, with lower humidity and comfortable conditions for sightseeing. crowd_level: HIGH during major festivals and pilgrimage periods, otherwise MEDIUM price_level: MEDIUM → HIGH overall_score: 88-93 recommended: true reason: One of the best overall periods to visit Rameshwaram because temperatures are more comfortable for temple visits, Dhanushkodi, Pamban Bridge, and other outdoor attractions. December and January can see increased pilgrimage activity and crowds around major religious occasions, while February generally offers a good balance of weather and visitor levels.', 5263),
  ('madurai', 10, 'budget-strategy', 'BUDGET STRATEGY', NULL, NULL, 'Where money can be saved: Where saving money is usually NOT recommended: Travel-agent rule: A slightly more expensive but clean, well-reviewed and centrally located hotel near the Meenakshi Amman Temple and major city attractions usually delivers better total value than a cheaper property farther away once you factor in daily transport costs, traffic, heat, and sightseeing convenience.', 5264),
  ('madurai', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Family', 'family', 'Pre-booked private car / MPV or reliable taxi from Madurai Airport; door-to-door service, sufficient luggage space, and convenient for children.', 5265),
  ('madurai', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Honeymoon', 'honeymoon', 'Pre-booked private car with direct hotel drop-off; comfortable, private, and convenient for couples arriving at Madurai Airport. reason: Madurai Airport is located approximately 12 km from central Madurai, so a private transfer provides a comfortable and hassle-free arrival experience, especially for travelers with luggage.', 5266),
  ('madurai', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Luxury', 'luxury', 'Chauffeured premium SUV / MPV or private car from Madurai Airport; personalized pickup, comfortable transfer, and suitable for premium hotels.', 5267),
  ('madurai', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Budget', 'budget', 'Public bus or local bus services from the airport where practical; app-based taxis, auto-rickshaws, or standard taxis for travelers prioritizing convenience. Public transport can be a cost-effective option for travelers with light luggage and flexible schedules.', 5268),
  ('madurai', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Senior', 'senior', 'Pre-booked private car or airport taxi with minimal walking and direct hotel drop-off; prioritize comfortable seating, luggage assistance, and avoiding unnecessary transfers.', 5269),
  ('madurai', 18, 'family-travel', 'FAMILY TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'child_friendly_score: 86 best_ages: Rules: For young children: Prefer: Avoid:', 5270),
  ('madurai', 19, 'honeymoon-travel', 'HONEYMOON TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'honeymoon_score: 74 romance_score: 78 privacy_score: 68 luxury_score: 60 Recommended: Honeymoon itinerary should NOT contain more than: 2 major activities/day. Prefer: One memorable cultural or heritage experience + free time over: Three or four attractions. Recommended hotel areas: Madurai can work well for couples seeking a cultural, heritage, spiritual, and food-focused getaway, particularly through experiences around Meenakshi Amman Temple, Thirumalai Nayak Palace, Mariamman Teppakulam, traditional markets, and local cuisine. Thirumalai Nayak Palace and Mariamman Teppakulam can provide atmospheric evening experiences for couples, while a private car can make it easier to explore attractions outside the central city. Madurai is better suited to couples seeking a cultural and heritage-oriented getaway than couples looking for a luxury-resort honeymoon with private beaches, extensive nightlife, private villas, or exclusive leisure experiences.', 5271),
  ('madurai', 20, 'luxury-travel', 'LUXURY TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'luxury_score: 68 Recommended: Madurai luxury travel should focus on: Luxury travelers should not simply be given more activities. Luxury in Madurai should primarily increase:', 5272),
  ('madurai', 21, 'adventure', 'ADVENTURE', NULL, NULL, 'adventure_score: 58 Madurai is primarily a cultural, pilgrimage, and heritage destination, but it also offers a moderate range of outdoor and family-oriented adventure experiences. Adventure experiences should be interpreted as:', 5273),
  ('madurai', 22, 'senior-travel', 'SENIOR TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'senior_suitability: 84 walking_intensity: MEDIUM unless carefully managed Rules:', 5274),
  ('madurai', 23, 'accessibility', 'ACCESSIBILITY', NULL, NULL, 'wheelchair_accessibility: PARTIAL_TO_GOOD depending on hotel, attraction, terrain and transport public_transport_accessibility: VARIABLE; private cars/taxis are often more practical for wheelchair users hotel_accessibility: MUST_BE_VERIFIED_PER_HOTEL attraction_accessibility: MUST_BE_VERIFIED_PER_ATTRACTION Rule: Never infer accessibility from Madurai''s overall accessibility. Each hotel and attraction must carry its own accessibility data. Additional notes:', 5275),
  ('madurai', 24, 'food', 'FOOD', NULL, NULL, 'Madurai is particularly strong for: Food experiences: Family: Prioritize clean, family-friendly restaurants with vegetarian options, familiar South Indian dishes, mild-spice choices, and flexible menus. Honeymoon: A comfortable hotel or quality local restaurant dinner is recommended, with a relaxed evening after temple and heritage sightseeing. Luxury: Premium hotel restaurants, curated Tamil cuisine, quality vegetarian and non-vegetarian dining, and private dining may be included, although Madurai is better known for authentic local food than an extensive luxury fine-dining scene. Budget: Mix local messes, vegetarian eateries, traditional tiffin shops, parotta and dosa restaurants, street-food spots, and affordable local dining experiences.', 5276),
  ('madurai', 25, 'shopping', 'SHOPPING', NULL, NULL, 'Strong categories: Luxury shopping: Prefer established textile and jewellery stores around Madurai Main, Chithirai Street, Masi Street, and major shopping areas for silk sarees, premium textiles, jewellery, traditional clothing, and higher-value purchases. Madurai is particularly well known for its Sungudi textiles and traditional textile trade. Budget: Prefer:', 5277),
  ('madurai', 26, 'nightlife', 'NIGHTLIFE', NULL, NULL, 'nightlife_level: 35 Suitable for: Best areas: Not a primary requirement for: Evening activities are better suited to: Honeymoon travelers should generally prefer: Romantic dinner / evening cultural experience over: Late-night party or club itinerary unless nightlife is explicitly requested.', 5278),
  ('madurai', 28, 'sample-itinerary-patterns', 'SAMPLE ITINERARY PATTERNS', '3 NIGHTS', NULL, '### Day 1 Arrival → Hotel → Meenakshi Amman Temple area → Evening temple visit → Local market / dinner ### Day 2 Morning: Meenakshi Amman Temple → Koodal Azhagar Temple Afternoon: Thirumalai Nayak Palace → Gandhi Memorial Museum Evening: Mariamman Teppakulam → Local food experience / relaxed dinner ### Day 3 Morning: Thirupparankundram Murugan Temple → Local sightseeing Afternoon: Azhagar Kovil → Pazhamudircholai / scenic hill area Evening: Temple-area shopping → Traditional Madurai dinner ### Day 4 Breakfast → Hotel checkout → Railway station / airport / road transfer → Departure', 5279),
  ('madurai', 29, 'six-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 1', NULL, 'Arrival at Coimbatore Airport / Railway Station → Private transfer to Ooty → Romantic hotel check-in → Relax and enjoy the hotel → Romantic dinner → Overnight at Ooty Intensity: LOW', 5280),
  ('madurai', 29, 'six-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 2', NULL, 'Morning: Private Ooty sightseeing → Doddabetta Peak → Botanical Garden Afternoon: Private lunch → Ooty Lake → Optional boating / horse riding → Hotel relaxation Evening: Free time → Romantic dinner Intensity: MEDIUM', 5281),
  ('madurai', 29, 'six-nights-honeymoon-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Day 3', NULL, 'Breakfast → Private chauffeur transfer from Ooty to Kodaikanal → Romantic hotel check-in → Relax → Leisure evening → Special dinner Intensity: LOW–MEDIUM', 5282),
