  ('chikkaballapur', 26, 'nightlife', 'NIGHTLIFE', NULL, NULL, 'nightlife_level: 40 Suitable for: weekend couple + bikers + family - resort bonfire + Adiyogi light show 7 PM + Nandi sunset + early sleep + sunrise prep 4 AM wake up Not a primary requirement for: party seekers wanting pubs + breweries till late - Go to Bengaluru 60km 1hr + Indiranagar + Koramangala + Toit + pubs + breweries + nightlife Travellers should generally prefer: Resort bonfire + valley view + Nandi Hills + Adiyogi light show 7 PM + Nandi sunset + early sleep + sunrise prep 4 AM wake up + Nandi dosa + filter coffee + Adiyogi meditation + resort pool + bonfire + valley + misty + romantic + weekend + Nandi + Adiyogi over: late-night pubs + clubs', 5404),
  ('chikkaballapur', 28, 'sample-itinerary-patterns', 'SAMPLE ITINERARY PATTERNS', '0 NIGHT BENGALURU BIKERS DAY TRIP - MOST POPULAR', NULL, '4 AM Bengaluru start: bike/car, 60km, 1.5hr via NH44 Bellary Road. 6 AM Nandi Hills sunrise + cloud bed winter Oct-Feb + Tipu Drop + Yoga Nandeeshwara Temple top + valley view + Bangalore view + cool + photo. 8 AM Nandi Hills breakfast dosa + filter coffee $1-$2. 9:30 AM Bhoga Nandeeshwara Temple 1000yr Chola Hoysala Vijayanagara + Arunachaleshwara + Uma Maheshwara + intricate + 15km from Nandi base. 11 AM Muddenahalli Sir M Visvesvaraya Museum + birthplace + 15km. 12:30 PM Back to Bengaluru 60 km 1.5 hr. 2 PM Reach Bengaluru with sunrise + temple + cloud bed memories.', 5405),
  ('chikkaballapur', 28, 'sample-itinerary-patterns', 'SAMPLE ITINERARY PATTERNS', '1 NIGHT WEEKEND + SKANDAGIRI NIGHT TREK PATTERN - IDEAL', 'adventure', 'Day 1 4 AM Bengaluru start -> 6 AM Nandi Hills sunrise + cloud bed + Tipu Drop + Yoga Nandeeshwara + 8 AM Nandi dosa + coffee + 9:30 AM Bhoga Nandeeshwara Temple 1000yr + 11 AM Muddenahalli Museum + 1 PM check-in Discovery Village Nandi Hills resort near Nandi base + valley view + pool + rest + 5 PM Gudibande Fort sunset monolith + 7 PM Adiyogi Isha 112ft light show Divya Darshanam + meditation + night stay resort + bonfire. Overnight: Chikkaballapur - Nandi Base Resort - Discovery Village / Q-Stays / Cicada Meals: Breakfast + Adiyogi cafe + Bonfire Day 2 2 AM wake up + 2:30 AM Skandagiri night trek start + 8km trek 4hr + forest + torch + guide + permit + 6 AM Skandagiri sunrise above clouds cloud bed + Papagni Temple ruins + valley + misty + 9 AM back base + breakfast + 11 AM Kalavara Durga short trek or Lepakshi Temple 30km hanging pillar + monolithic Nandi 27ft + frescoes + 2 PM drive back Bengaluru 60km 1.5hr with Nandi + Skandagiri + Adiyogi memories. Meals: Breakfast + Trek water + Lepakshi lunch', 5406),
  ('chikkaballapur', 29, 'two-night-trekkers-adventure-pattern', 'TWO-NIGHT TREKKERS + ADVENTURE PATTERN', NULL, NULL, 'Day 1 Nandi Hills sunrise + Bhoga Nandeeshwara + Muddenahalli + Adiyogi light show. Day 2 Skandagiri night trek + Kalavara Durga + Gudibande Fort + Nandi cycling + paragliding. Day 3 Lepakshi + Awanahalli + Amruth Sarovar + back Bengaluru.', 5407),
  ('chikkaballapur', 30, 'family-day-trip-pattern', 'FAMILY DAY TRIP PATTERN', NULL, NULL, '4 AM Bengaluru -> 6 AM Nandi Hills sunrise + cloud bed + Tipu Drop + Yoga Nandeeshwara + 8 AM Nandi dosa + coffee + 9:30 AM Bhoga Temple + 11 AM Muddenahalli + 12 PM Adiyogi (if time) + 2 PM back Bengaluru. No trek. Family car + kids-friendly.', 5408),
  ('chikkaballapur', 31, 'luxury-weekend-pattern', 'LUXURY WEEKEND PATTERN', NULL, NULL, 'Stay Discovery Village Nandi Hills private cottage valley view + private balcony + bonfire + private Nandi sunrise + private Bhoga Temple + private Adiyogi light show + private Skandagiri trek + private car + private guide + butler + pool + spa + bonfire + valley + Nandi view + weekend honeymoon.', 5409),
  ('chikkaballapur', 32, 'travel-agent-insights', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS', 'What inexperienced planners often do wrong', NULL, '', 5410),
  ('chikkaballapur', 32, 'travel-agent-insights', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS', 'What an experienced planner does differently', NULL, '1. Starts with purpose - Weekend sunrise = Nandi Hills sunrise + cloud bed winter + Bhoga Temple + Adiyogi light show + bikers 4 AM ride, Adventure = Skandagiri night trek + Kalavara Durga + Gudibande Fort + Nandi cycling + paragliding, Family = Nandi drive + Bhoga flat + Adiyogi flat + Muddenahalli + Gudibande easy + Lepakshi flat 2. Groups by geography: Nandi Hills + Bhoga Nandeeshwara + Muddenahalli together 15km circuit morning 4 AM-12 PM car/bike, Skandagiri + Kalavara Durga + Gudibande together trek circuit 10-30km night/morning jeep/guide, Adiyogi evening 7 PM light show + Lepakshi day 30km circuit car 3. Uses hotel location strategically: NANDI BASE RESORT - Discovery Village near Nandi base valley view for Nandi sunrise + Bhoga + Adiyogi + Skandagiri base + family + bikers + weekend, CHIKKABALLAPUR TOWN - Town hotels for budget + bus stand + market + near Skandagiri base + Gudibande road 4. Places Nandi Hills sunrise 6 AM + Bhoga Temple morning 9-11 AM + Muddenahalli 11 AM-12 PM + Adiyogi light show evening 7 PM + Skandagiri night trek 2 AM start + sunrise 6 AM + Gudibande Fort sunset + Lepakshi morning + Nandi dosa 8 AM + filter coffee 5. Treats Chikkaballapur as 0-1N weekend + Nandi + Bhoga + Adiyogi half day + Skandagiri night trek separate night + not checklist 6 areas same morning + trek separate full night 6. Always includes private car/bike + guide + permit for Skandagiri + Nandi entry + Bhoga Temple + Adiyogi + Gudibande + Lepakshi + trek shoes + torch + jacket + water + hat + raincoat monsoon + leech socks + early start 4 AM Bengaluru + 2 AM Skandagiri start + need experienced driver/biker + ghats + forest + night + leopard + need guide + permit', 5411),
  ('chikkaballapur', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', NULL, NULL, 'IF: `trip_length == 0 night day trip` THEN: Nandi Hills sunrise 6 AM cloud bed + Yoga Nandeeshwara + Tipu Drop + Nandi dosa + Bhoga Nandeeshwara Temple 1000yr + Muddenahalli Museum + back Bengaluru 2 PM. Core bikers + family day. Reason: No time for Skandagiri night trek + Gudibande + Lepakshi + Adiyogi light show. IF: `trip_length == 1 night` THEN: Day 1: Nandi sunrise + Bhoga + Muddenahalli + Gudibande sunset + evening Adiyogi light show at 7 PM; Night 2: Skandagiri night trek + sunrise cloud bed; Day 2: Lepakshi hanging pillar + back to Bengaluru. Ideal. Reason: Covers Nandi cloud bed + Bhoga history + Adiyogi pilgrimage + Skandagiri cloud trek + Lepakshi history. IF: `trip_length >= 2 nights` THEN: Add Kalavara Durga trek + Gudibande Fort + Nandi cycling + paragliding + Awanahalli + Amruth Sarovar + leisure resort + bonfire + pool. Reason: Complete adventure + trek + fort + cycling + paragliding + weekend + offbeat. IF: `traveler_type == FAMILY` THEN: Nandi Hills drive + top flat + Bhoga Temple flat + Muddenahalli flat + Adiyogi flat + Gudibande easy + Lepakshi flat + Nandi dosa + filter coffee + resort pool + bonfire. Avoid Skandagiri night trek with kids. Reason: Family Nandi + temple + museum + Adiyogi + fort easy + history + safe + flat. IF: `traveler_type == BIKERS` THEN: Bike $10/day + 4 AM Bengaluru to Nandi Hills sunrise ride + Nandi dosa + filter coffee + Bhoga Temple + Muddenahalli + Adiyogi + back + Skandagiri optional night trek + Gudibande + Lepakshi + group ride + group trek + bikers 1 ride South. Reason: 1 bikers sunrise ride near Bengaluru + Nandi + Bhoga + Adiyogi + Skandagiri + group. IF: `traveler_type == ADVENTURE` THEN: Skandagiri night trek 8km + Kalavara Durga 3km + Gudibande Fort trek 1hr + Nandi cycling + paragliding + zip-line + off-road jeep + guide + trek shoes + torch + jacket + water + hat + early start 2 AM + moderate hard + fitness. Reason: Best night trek near Bengaluru + above clouds + cloud bed + monolith fort + cycling + paragliding.', 5412),
  ('chikkaballapur', 34, 'destination-scoring', 'DESTINATION SCORING', NULL, NULL, '| Factor | Score | | ------------------ | ----: | Family | 84 Honeymoon | 68 Luxury | 60 Budget | 92 Adventure | 88 Culture | 78 Food | 65 Shopping | 50 Nightlife | 40 Relaxation | 72 Nature | 80 Accessibility | 72 Safety | 82 First-time visitor | 86 Photography | 86', 5413),
  ('chikkaballapur', 35, 'final-travel-agent-verdict', 'FINAL TRAVEL AGENT VERDICT', NULL, NULL, 'Best traveller profiles: 1. Bengaluru bikers + weekend sunrise + Nandi Hills sunrise cloud bed + Skandagiri night trek above clouds + Adiyogi + Bhoga Temple + #1 weekend getaway 60km + bike ride + dosa + filter coffee + adventure + photography 2. Family day trip + Nandi Hills drive + Bhoga Temple flat + Muddenahalli museum + Adiyogi light show + Gudibande easy + Lepakshi + Nandi dosa + filter coffee + family + kids + flat + safe 3. Adventure + Skandagiri night trek cloud bed + Kalavara Durga + Gudibande Fort monolith + Nandi cycling + paragliding + zip-line + trek + offroad + guide + torch + jacket + water + hat + fitness + night trek + cloud trek + #1 trek near Bengaluru 4. Pilgrimage + Adiyogi Isha 112ft + light show 7 PM + Bhoga Nandeeshwara 1000yr + Yoga Nandeeshwara top + Lepakshi Veerabhadra hanging pillar + monolithic Nandi + history + culture + temple + architecture + photo + must 5. Photographers + Nandi Hills sunrise cloud bed winter Oct-Feb + Skandagiri above clouds + Adiyogi night light show + Bhoga Temple architecture + Gudibande monolith view + Lepakshi frescoes + valley + misty + nature + photography best Best duration: 0N day trip (4 AM-2 PM) or 1N with Skandagiri night trek Best season: Oct-Feb winter best + cool + cloud bed + Nandi sunrise + Skandagiri cloud trek + clear + bikers best + family best + photography best. Jun-Sep monsoon green + misty + lush + Nandi green + Skandagiri green + offbeat + less crowd + but trek slippery + leeches + need raincoat + leech socks. Best hotel strategy: Best transportation: Bike $10/day best for bikers + private car $25/day for family + auto $2-$3 town + KSRTC bus Bengaluru->Chikkaballapur $2 2hr + Nandi ghats 8km steep need good brakes + experienced driver/biker + Skandagiri base 10km + Adiyogi 15km + Gudibande 30km + Lepakshi 30km + NH44 6 lane excellent. Must-do: Don''t-do: Biggest advantage: Bengaluru''s closest hill station 60km 1.5hr + cheapest weekend + Nandi Hills sunrise cloud bed + Skandagiri night trek above clouds #1 near Bengaluru + Adiyogi Isha 112ft light show + Bhoga Nandeeshwara Temple 1000yr + Gudibande Fort monolith + Muddenahalli + Lepakshi hanging pillar + bikers #1 sunrise ride + family day trip + adventure + photography + valley + misty + nature + pilgrimage + history + offbeat + weekend + bike + car + dosa + filter coffee + bonfire + resort + valley view. Biggest disadvantage: Weekend crowd VERY HIGH + traffic jam Nandi ghats 5-7 AM + no 5_ luxury + no long stay 3N boring + summer no cloud + limited food + no shopping + no nightlife + trek need fitness + forest + leopard + night + need guide + permit + leeches monsoon + slippery + need raincoat + trek shoes + torch + jacket + water + need early start 4 AM + 2 AM Skandagiri + no railway direct Nandi + bus limited + auto limited + far Lepakshi 30km + need car + bike + ghats steep + need good brakes. Overall destination score: 82/100 - Must 0N day trip or 1N weekend from Bengaluru + Nandi Hills sunrise cloud bed + Bhoga Temple 1000yr + Adiyogi light show + Skandagiri night trek + Gudibande Fort + Lepakshi + bikers + family + adventure + photography + weekend + bonfire + valley + misty.', 5414),
  ('chikkaballapur', 36, 'data-quality', 'DATA QUALITY', NULL, NULL, 'information_completeness: 88/100 last_updated: 2026-08-17 last_verified: PARTIALLY_LIVE_VERIFIED verified_by: INDIA_DESTINATION_KNOWLEDGE_DATASET sources: IMPORTANT: This Chikkaballapur file is suitable for itinerary design, traveller profiling, hotel-area strategy, and initial package planning. Nandi Hills sunrise 6 AM best + cloud bed Oct-Feb + valley view + Tipu Drop + Yoga Nandeeshwara + $2 + near Bengaluru 60km 1.5hr + walkable top + must sunrise + bikers #1 + family + photo + valley + sunrise + flat + easy + 1hr + must + crowded weekend sunrise + need early 4 AM Bengaluru + traffic jam 5-7 AM + parking issue. Skandagiri night trek 2 AM start + sunrise 6 AM cloud bed + 8km + $5 permit + $10 guide + must adventure + above clouds + Papagni Temple ruins + forest + leopard + need guide + permit + torch + jacket + water + moderate hard. Adiyogi Isha 112ft + light show 7 PM + free + must + Nandi foothills + 15km from Nandi + near Bengaluru 60km + #1 new attraction + crowd weekend evening + need early 6 PM + parking issue. Prices, hotel inventory, Skandagiri permit availability, and trek/cycling/paragliding timings must be live-verified before quotation.', 5415),
  ('shimla', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Summer', NULL, 'months: March-June weather: Pleasant to warm mountain weather, generally comfortable for sightseeing, heritage walks, photography, and nearby excursions. March and April are usually mild, while May and June can be warmer during the day, with cooler mornings and evenings. crowd_level: HIGH → VERY HIGH price_level: MEDIUM → HIGH overall_score: 84–90 recommended: true reason: One of the best periods for first-time visitors, families, and sightseeing because the weather is comfortable and most attractions and roads are accessible. Shimla is especially busy during school holidays and long weekends, so early booking is advisable.', 5416),
  ('shimla', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Monsoon', NULL, 'months: June–September weather: Cool, cloudy, and rainy, with lush green forests and misty mountain views. Heavy showers can make roads slippery and may cause traffic delays, reduced visibility, or temporary disruption to excursions and trekking plans. crowd_level: LOW → MEDIUM price_level: LOW → MEDIUM overall_score: 68–76 recommended: true reason: Suitable for budget travelers, photographers, and visitors who enjoy misty landscapes and quiet hill-station stays. It is less ideal for extensive sightseeing, long road excursions, trekking, or travelers with fixed outdoor plans because rainfall can disrupt movement.', 5417),
  ('shimla', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Autumn (Post-Monsoon)', NULL, 'months: October–November weather: Clearer skies, fresh mountain air, pleasant daytime temperatures, and cool mornings and evenings. Visibility usually improves after the monsoon, making this a strong period for Himalayan viewpoints, photography, heritage walks, and outdoor excursions. crowd_level: LOW → MEDIUM price_level: LOW → MEDIUM overall_score: 88–93 recommended: true reason: One of the best all-round seasons for Shimla, offering a strong balance of pleasant weather, clearer views, manageable crowds, and good value. It is particularly suitable for couples, first-time visitors, photographers, families, and travelers seeking relaxed sightseeing.', 5418),
  ('shimla', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Winter', NULL, 'months: December-February weather: Cold and generally dry, with freezing mornings and evenings. Snowfall is possible, especially around Shimla and Kufri, although timing and intensity vary; roads, walking paths, and outdoor activities may become difficult after heavy snow. crowd_level: HIGH → VERY HIGH price_level: HIGH → VERY HIGH overall_score: 86–94 recommended: true reason: Best for snowfall seekers, honeymooners, photographers, and travelers wanting a classic winter hill-station experience. Christmas, New Year, and snowfall periods bring peak demand, crowded roads, higher hotel prices, and possible travel delays, so advance booking and flexible plans are important.', 5419),
  ('shimla', 10, 'budget-strategy', 'BUDGET STRATEGY', NULL, NULL, '', 5420),
  ('shimla', 12, 'airport-transfer-logic', 'AIRPORT TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Family', 'family', 'Airport taxi or pre-booked private MPV / Innova-type vehicle from Chandigarh Airport; door-to-door, luggage-friendly, and more comfortable for Shimla’s winding mountain roads. The larger vehicle is especially useful for families carrying winter clothing, strollers, or multiple bags.', 5421),
  ('shimla', 12, 'airport-transfer-logic', 'AIRPORT TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Honeymoon', 'honeymoon', 'Pre-booked private sedan or comfortable SUV from Chandigarh Airport; best for privacy, scenic stops, comfort, and a relaxed first impression of the Himalayan journey. reason: The transfer from the airport to Shimla takes several hours on mountainous roads, so a private vehicle provides flexibility for rest breaks, viewpoints, luggage handling, and a comfortable start to the honeymoon.', 5422),
  ('shimla', 12, 'airport-transfer-logic', 'AIRPORT TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Luxury', 'luxury', 'Chauffeured premium sedan, Innova Crysta, or luxury MPV from Chandigarh Airport; ideal for enhanced comfort, privacy, professional service, flexible sightseeing stops, and seamless hotel drop-off. Shimla Airport may be used when a suitable flight is available, but Chandigarh generally offers more practical flight connectivity and transfer options.', 5423),
  ('shimla', 12, 'airport-transfer-logic', 'AIRPORT TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Budget', 'budget', 'Prepaid airport taxi, shared cab, or scheduled bus from Chandigarh Airport; the most economical option for cost-conscious travelers while still providing reliable access to Shimla. Shared transport is particularly suitable for solo travelers or small groups with limited luggage.', 5424),
  ('shimla', 18, 'family-travel', 'FAMILY TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'child_friendly_score: 85 best_ages: Rules: For young children: Prefer: Avoid:', 5425),
  ('shimla', 19, 'honeymoon-travel', 'HONEYMOON TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'honeymoon_score: 91 romance_score: 90 privacy_score: 85 luxury_score: 84 Recommended: **Honeymoon itinerary should NOT contain more than:** Prefer: over: Recommended hotel areas:', 5426),
  ('shimla', 20, 'luxury-travel', 'LUXURY TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'luxury_score: 84 Recommended: Luxury should primarily increase: Recommended hotel areas:', 5427),
  ('shimla', 21, 'adventure', 'ADVENTURE', NULL, NULL, 'adventure_score: 78 Shimla is a good light-to-moderate adventure destination, with the focus on Himalayan trekking, forest walks, seasonal snow activities, horse riding, cycling, and scenic outdoor excursions rather than extreme high-adrenaline sports. Shimla and nearby areas such as Kufri, Naldehra, Mashobra, and Tattapani offer a wider range of outdoor experiences than the city centre alone. **Adventure-like experiences should be interpreted as:** Recommended adventure-style areas: Best for:', 5428),
  ('shimla', 22, 'senior-travel', 'SENIOR TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'senior_suitability: 70 walking_intensity: MEDIUM_HIGH Rules: Recommended hotel areas: Chhota Shimla & Brockhurst – among the better choices for seniors because they are quieter than the central pedestrian zone and generally offer better road access, hotels, restaurants, and easier taxi drop-offs. Sanjauli – suitable for budget-conscious seniors who want local markets, more affordable accommodation, and road access toward Jakhoo and Kufri; verify the hotel’s slope, entrance, lift, and parking arrangements. Summer Hill – peaceful and green, with a quieter atmosphere and scenic surroundings; best for seniors who prioritise relaxation and stay at a property with dependable vehicle access. Viceregal Lodge–Observatory Hill side – convenient for a heritage-focused visit with private transport, although the grounds and approach may still involve walking, steps, or uneven surfaces.', 5429),
  ('shimla', 23, 'accessibility', 'ACCESSIBILITY', NULL, NULL, 'wheelchair_accessibility: PARTIAL_TO_GOOD depending on attraction and transport public_transport_accessibility: VARIABLE hotel_accessibility: MUST_BE_VERIFIED_PER_HOTEL attraction_accessibility: MUST_BE_VERIFIED_PER_ATTRACTION Rule: Never infer accessibility from destination-level accessibility. Each hotel and attraction must carry its own accessibility data.', 5430),
  ('shimla', 24, 'food', 'FOOD', NULL, NULL, 'Shimla is particularly strong for: Food experiences: Family: Prioritize clean, comfortable restaurants with familiar and flexible menus. North Indian meals, parathas, rice, dal, rajma-chawal, noodles, momos, sandwiches, pizzas, bakery items, and mild Himachali dishes usually work well for families. Hotels and restaurants with indoor seating, heating, early meal timings, and child-friendly options are especially convenient during winter. Honeymoon: At least one memorable mountain-view dinner is recommended—choose a heritage hotel restaurant, boutique resort, cosy café, or private dining setup with valley views. A relaxed café date with hot chocolate and pastries, followed by a warm Himachali dinner or in-room meal, suits Shimla’s romantic hill-station atmosphere better than a rushed food itinerary. Luxury: Fine dining in Shimla is strongest in setting, ambience, service, and presentation rather than in a large variety of specialised restaurants. Premium heritage hotels and valley-view resorts can offer curated Himachali menus, private balcony dining, chef-led meals, afternoon tea, personalised breakfast, fireplaces, and scenic mountain-view dinners. Budget: Mix local Himachali restaurants, simple North Indian eateries, bakeries, cafés, Tibetan food outlets, and selected hotel meals. Himachali thalis, rajma-chawal, chole bhature, momos, thukpa, parathas, bun snacks, and bakery items provide good value, while local restaurants around Mall Road, Lakkar Bazaar, and the main market areas are useful for quick and affordable meals.', 5431),
  ('shimla', 25, 'shopping', 'SHOPPING', NULL, NULL, 'Strong categories: Luxury shopping: Shimla is not a major luxury-shopping destination, but it offers quality handloom products, premium shawls, curated Himachali handicrafts, traditional jewellery, and high-end local food products. For more refined selections, compare products at Himachal Emporium or premium boutiques around The Mall; for designer fashion, luxury jewellery, and large-brand shopping, Chandigarh or Delhi is a better choice. Prefer:', 5432),
  ('shimla', 26, 'nightlife', 'NIGHTLIFE', NULL, NULL, 'nightlife_level: 45–50 Shimla is not a major nightlife destination; evenings are generally relaxed and low-key, with activity centred around Mall Road, The Ridge, cafés, bakeries, hotel lounges, restaurants, and scenic evening walks rather than late-night clubs. The city is best suited to travellers who enjoy cosy mountain evenings, colonial surroundings, warm drinks, and valley views over energetic partying. Suitable for: Not a primary requirement for: **Honeymoon travellers should generally prefer:**', 5433),
  ('shimla', 28, 'sample-itinerary-patterns', 'SAMPLE ITINERARY PATTERNS', NULL, NULL, 'Night 1 Arrive at Chandigarh Airport / Kalka Railway Station → Private transfer to Shimla → Check-in → Rest and acclimatise → Evening walk around The Ridge, Christ Church, and Mall Road → Café or bakery stop → Dinner. Night 2 Morning: The Ridge, Christ Church, Scandal Point, and Gaiety Heritage Cultural Complex. Afternoon: Mall Road and Lakkar Bazaar shopping → Local lunch → Hotel rest. Evening: Café time, colonial street photography, or relaxed walk around the central heritage zone → Dinner. Night 3 Morning: Jakhoo Temple and Jakhoo Hill by taxi or lift, depending on walking comfort. Afternoon: Green Valley viewpoint → Kufri → Himalayan Nature Park / seasonal snow activities / horse riding. Evening: Return to Shimla → Rest at hotel → Warm Himachali or Tibetan dinner. Night 4 Morning: Viceregal Lodge / Rashtrapati Niwas and Indian Institute of Advanced Study. Afternoon: Himachal State Museum → Summer Hill or nearby pine-forest surroundings. Evening: Quiet café, hotel balcony time, or valley-view relaxation → Dinner. Night 5 Option 1 (nature and relaxation): Mashobra forest drive → Naldehra Golf Course and cedar forests → Horse riding or scenic walk → Resort lunch → Return to Shimla. Option 2 (heritage and countryside): Naldehra → Chail excursion → Chail Palace / forest surroundings → Evening return to Shimla or overnight in Chail. Dinner and relaxed hotel evening. Flexible day: Kalka–Shimla Toy Train experience, Annandale and Army Heritage Museum, Tara Devi Temple, or a repeat visit to The Ridge and Mall Road. Afternoon: Leisure time for shopping, photography, café visits, spa treatment, or hotel balcony time. Evening: Special Himachali dinner or romantic mountain-view dinner → Overnight in Shimla. Day 7: Breakfast → Checkout → Departure transfer to Kalka Station.', 5434),
  ('shimla', 29, 'six-night-seven-day-honeymoon-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHT / SEVEN-DAY HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Night 1', NULL, 'Morning pickup from Chandigarh Railway Station or Chandigarh Airport → Scenic private transfer to Shimla through Himalayan valleys and mountain roads → Check-in at a romantic valley-view hotel → Rest and acclimatise. Late afternoon: Visit Jakhoo Hanuman Temple by private vehicle or lift → Continue to The Ridge, Shimla Kali Bari Temple, Wax Museum, Christ Church, Rani Jhansi Park, Scandal Point, Lakkar Bazaar, and The Mall by walk, subject to time and walking comfort. Evening: Couple walk around The Mall → Café or bakery stop → Romantic dinner at the hotel. **Overnight in Shimla.**', 5435),
  ('shimla', 29, 'six-night-seven-day-honeymoon-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHT / SEVEN-DAY HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Night 2', NULL, 'After breakfast, proceed for a private sightseeing excursion to Green Valley, Kufri, Fagu, Himalayan Adventure Park, and Chail. Optional: Horse riding or seasonal snow activities at Kufri, at an additional cost and subject to weather and local conditions. Enjoy scenic photography, forest views, and relaxed couple time around Fagu or Chail. Avoid packing too many activities into the day; select one main activity in addition to the scenic drive. Return to Shimla by late afternoon or evening → Free time for balcony relaxation, spa treatment, or a quiet café visit → Special dinner. **Overnight in Shimla.**', 5436),
  ('shimla', 29, 'six-night-seven-day-honeymoon-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHT / SEVEN-DAY HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Night 3', NULL, 'After breakfast, check out from the Shimla hotel and begin the private transfer to Manali. Enjoy the scenic mountain journey through valleys, forests, and riverside landscapes. En-route, stop at suitable viewpoints and Pandoh Dam, subject to road conditions and available time. Continue towards Manali → Check-in at the hotel → Rest after the long journey. Evening: Relaxed dinner at the hotel or a short couple walk near the property, depending on arrival time. **Overnight in Manali.**', 5437),
  ('shimla', 29, 'six-night-seven-day-honeymoon-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHT / SEVEN-DAY HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Night 4', NULL, 'After breakfast, visit Hadimba Devi Temple and the nearby Ghatotkach Temple amid cedar forests. Continue to the Beas River, Vashisht Temple and Vashisht Kund, Manu Temple, Manali Clubhouse, Van Vihar, Himalayan Nyinmapa Tibetan Buddhist Monastery, and Manali Mall, selecting the attractions according to available time and walking comfort. Return to the hotel by late afternoon or evening → Rest and enjoy private balcony time. Evening: Café date or relaxed walk at Manali Mall → Dinner at the hotel. **Overnight in Manali.**', 5438),
  ('shimla', 29, 'six-night-seven-day-honeymoon-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHT / SEVEN-DAY HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Night 5', NULL, 'After breakfast, proceed by private vehicle to Solang Valley. Enjoy mountain scenery, snow views, and optional activities such as snow play, cable-car rides, or other seasonal adventure activities, at an additional cost and subject to weather and operational conditions. Continue towards Atal Tunnel, Sissu Village, and Sissu Lake if the road, weather, and local regulations permit. Keep the excursion flexible during winter or adverse weather. Return to Manali by late afternoon → Rest at the hotel. Evening: Spend quiet couple time at Manali Mall, enjoy a warm café meal, or arrange a private dinner at the hotel. **Overnight in Manali.**', 5439),
  ('shimla', 29, 'six-night-seven-day-honeymoon-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHT / SEVEN-DAY HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Night 6', NULL, 'After breakfast, check out from the Manali hotel and proceed towards Kasol. En-route, stop at suitable viewpoints around Pandoh Dam, Sundar Nagar Lake, the rafting point, and Bhuntar, depending on the route and available time. Continue through the Parvati Valley to Kasol → Visit Manikaran Sahib Gurudwara and Manikaran Hot Springs. Since this is a long road journey, avoid adding too many stops. Check in to the Kasol hotel or resort by late afternoon or evening → Rest and enjoy the peaceful valley setting. Evening: Quiet riverside or balcony time, followed by a relaxed dinner. **Overnight in Kasol.**', 5440),
  ('shimla', 29, 'six-night-seven-day-honeymoon-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHT / SEVEN-DAY HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Night 7', NULL, 'After breakfast, check out from the Kasol hotel. Private transfer towards Chandigarh or Kalka Railway Station, depending on the departure arrangement. Because the journey from Kasol to the plains is long, keep the departure schedule comfortable and avoid booking an early train or flight. Depart with beautiful memories of Shimla’s colonial charm, Kufri’s mountain scenery, Manali’s valleys, Solang’s snow experiences, and Kasol’s peaceful riverside atmosphere.', 5441),
  ('shimla', 30, 'six-night-seven-day-family-itinerary', 'SIX-NIGHT / SEVEN-DAY FAMILY ITINERARY', 'Night 1', NULL, 'Pick up from Chandigarh Railway Station / Chandigarh Airport in the morning and transfer to Shimla by private vehicle. Enjoy the scenic valleys and mountain roads en route. Check in to the Shimla hotel and take some rest. In the late afternoon, proceed for local sightseeing: Jakhoo Hanuman Temple, The Ridge, Shimla Kali Bari Temple, Wax Museum, Christ Church, Rani Jhansi Park, Scandal Point, Lakkar Bazaar, and The Mall by walk. Return to the hotel by evening → Dinner at the hotel → Overnight stay in Shimla.', 5442),
  ('shimla', 30, 'six-night-seven-day-family-itinerary', 'SIX-NIGHT / SEVEN-DAY FAMILY ITINERARY', 'Night 2', NULL, 'After breakfast, proceed for a family excursion to Kufri, Fagu, Himalayan Nature Park, Himalayan Adventure Park, and Chail. At Kufri, enjoy the mountain scenery and optional horse riding or seasonal snow activities at an additional cost. Families may also enjoy the adventure park, subject to age, weather, and operating conditions. Continue towards Fagu for scenic views and photography, followed by Chail forest surroundings and optional Chail Palace visit. Return to Shimla by late afternoon / evening → Evening free for leisure → Dinner at the hotel → Overnight stay in Shimla.', 5443),
  ('shimla', 30, 'six-night-seven-day-family-itinerary', 'SIX-NIGHT / SEVEN-DAY FAMILY ITINERARY', 'Night 3', NULL, 'After breakfast, check out from the Shimla hotel and drive towards Manali through the scenic valleys of Himachal Pradesh. En route, enjoy views of Sundernagar, Mandi, Pandoh Dam, Hanogi Mata Temple, and the Kullu Valley. Depending on time, stop at a Kullu shawl outlet or local handicraft centre. Continue the journey to Manali and check in to the hotel on arrival. The rest of the evening is free for rest after the long mountain drive. Dinner at the hotel → Overnight stay in Manali.', 5444),
  ('shimla', 30, 'six-night-seven-day-family-itinerary', 'SIX-NIGHT / SEVEN-DAY FAMILY ITINERARY', 'Night 4', NULL, 'After breakfast, proceed for Manali local sightseeing. Visit Hadimba Devi Temple, Ghatotkach Temple, Beas River, Vashisht Temple, Vashisht Kund, Manu Temple, Manali Clubhouse, Van Vihar, and the Himalayan Nyinmapa Tibetan Buddhist Monastery. Later, enjoy a relaxed walk around Manali Mall Road for shopping, cafés, snacks, and family time. Return to the hotel by late afternoon / evening → Evening free for leisure → Dinner at the hotel → Overnight stay in Manali.', 5445),
  ('shimla', 30, 'six-night-seven-day-family-itinerary', 'SIX-NIGHT / SEVEN-DAY FAMILY ITINERARY', 'Night 5', NULL, 'After breakfast, start the excursion to Solang Valley. Enjoy the snow-covered landscapes or mountain scenery, depending on the season. Optional activities may include snow play, ropeway rides, snow tubing, or other adventure activities at an additional cost. Continue towards Atal Tunnel, subject to weather, road conditions, traffic, and local access regulations. If permitted, visit Sissu Village and Sissu Lake. Return to Manali by late afternoon / evening. Later, spend quality family time at Manali Mall by local transport. Dinner at the hotel → Overnight stay in Manali.', 5446),
  ('shimla', 30, 'six-night-seven-day-family-itinerary', 'SIX-NIGHT / SEVEN-DAY FAMILY ITINERARY', 'Night 6', NULL, 'After breakfast, check out from the Manali hotel and proceed towards Kasol / Manikaran. En route, enjoy scenic stops around Kullu Valley, including Pandoh Dam, Sundarnagar Lake, the Beas or Parvati Valley viewpoints, rafting point, Bhuntar, and local markets, depending on time and road conditions. Continue to Manikaran and visit Manikaran Sahib Gurudwara and the famous Manikaran hot springs. Guests may spend some peaceful time in the surrounding Parvati Valley. Proceed to Kasol and check in to the hotel by late afternoon / evening. Take rest after the journey. Evening free for leisure or a short riverside / market walk, subject to local conditions → Dinner at the hotel → Overnight stay in Kasol.', 5447),
  ('shimla', 30, 'six-night-seven-day-family-itinerary', 'SIX-NIGHT / SEVEN-DAY FAMILY ITINERARY', 'Night 7', NULL, 'After breakfast, check out from the Kasol hotel and transfer to Chandigarh Railway Station / Chandigarh Airport for your onward journey. The trip ends with happy memories of Shimla, Manali, Kullu, Kasol, and Manikaran.', 5448),
  ('shimla', 31, 'six-night-seven-day-luxury-itinerary', 'SIX-NIGHT / SEVEN-DAY LUXURY ITINERARY', 'Night 1', NULL, 'Private premium vehicle pickup from Chandigarh Airport or Railway Station → Scenic transfer through the Himalayan valleys with planned comfort stops → Check-in at a luxury heritage hotel, boutique property, or valley-view resort in Shimla / Mashobra → Welcome drink and rest. Late afternoon: Private guided sightseeing of Jakhoo Hanuman Temple, followed by The Ridge, Christ Church, Scandal Point, Rani Jhansi Park, and the colonial buildings around Mall Road. Continue with a relaxed walk through Lakkar Bazaar and the central heritage lanes. Evening: Return to the hotel → Private balcony tea, spa treatment, or time beside the fireplace → Curated Himachali dinner with valley views → Overnight stay in Shimla.', 5449),
  ('shimla', 31, 'six-night-seven-day-luxury-itinerary', 'SIX-NIGHT / SEVEN-DAY LUXURY ITINERARY', 'Night 2', NULL, 'After a leisurely breakfast, depart in a private chauffeur-driven SUV for Kufri and Fagu → Scenic drive through pine and cedar forests → Green Valley photography stop → Kufri sightseeing. Optional activities: Private nature walk, Himalayan Nature Park visit, horse riding, seasonal snow experience, or a curated adventure activity with local assistance. Continue towards Fagu for peaceful mountain views and a relaxed lunch at a premium resort or selected countryside restaurant → Proceed to Chail for forest scenery, Chail Palace surroundings, and quiet heritage photography. Return to Shimla by late afternoon / evening → High tea at the hotel → Spa, indoor relaxation, or private balcony time → Special dinner → Overnight stay in Shimla.', 5450),
  ('shimla', 31, 'six-night-seven-day-luxury-itinerary', 'SIX-NIGHT / SEVEN-DAY LUXURY ITINERARY', 'Night 3', NULL, 'After breakfast, visit Viceregal Lodge / Rashtrapati Niwas and the Indian Institute of Advanced Study with a private guide → Explore the heritage architecture and landscaped surroundings at an unhurried pace. Continue to the Himachal State Museum for regional art, history, sculptures, and traditional artefacts → Visit Summer Hill and enjoy a peaceful pine-forest drive. Afternoon: Return to the hotel for lunch and rest → Optional spa treatment, wellness session, or in-room relaxation. Evening: Private colonial heritage walk covering Gaiety Heritage Cultural Complex, The Ridge, Christ Church, and Mall Road → Afternoon tea or hot chocolate at a premium café → Fine-dining dinner at the hotel → Overnight stay in Shimla.', 5451),
  ('shimla', 31, 'six-night-seven-day-luxury-itinerary', 'SIX-NIGHT / SEVEN-DAY LUXURY ITINERARY', 'Night 4', NULL, 'After breakfast, check out from the Shimla hotel and transfer by private luxury vehicle to Mashobra or Naldehra → Scenic forest drive through pine and cedar landscapes → Check-in at a premium mountain resort or luxury retreat. Afternoon: Resort lunch followed by leisure time → Enjoy the property’s spa, private balcony, heated indoor facilities, or guided forest walk. Late afternoon: Visit Naldehra Golf Course and surrounding cedar forests → Optional horse riding or relaxed photography session → Return to the resort. Evening: Private mountain-view dinner, bonfire-style experience where available, or in-room dining → Overnight stay in Mashobra / Naldehra.', 5452),
  ('shimla', 31, 'six-night-seven-day-luxury-itinerary', 'SIX-NIGHT / SEVEN-DAY LUXURY ITINERARY', 'Night 5', NULL, 'Begin with a leisurely breakfast overlooking the hills → Guided nature walk through the forest surroundings or a gentle private excursion around Mashobra. Visit selected viewpoints and quiet countryside areas → Optional horse riding at Naldehra, golf-course visit, photography session, or private picnic-style lunch arranged by the resort. Afternoon: Return to the resort for spa therapy, wellness time, afternoon tea, or relaxed balcony time with mountain views. Evening: Sunset viewing from the property or a nearby scenic point → Chef-curated Himachali dinner featuring local specialties such as siddu, chana madra, rajma, kadhi, and regional breads → Overnight stay in Mashobra / Naldehra.', 5453),
  ('shimla', 31, 'six-night-seven-day-luxury-itinerary', 'SIX-NIGHT / SEVEN-DAY LUXURY ITINERARY', 'Night 6', NULL, 'After breakfast, choose one of the following luxury experiences: **Option 1 – Scenic railway experience:** Enjoy a reserved section of the Kalka–Shimla Toy Train on a suitable route → Scenic views of tunnels, bridges, forests, and mountain valleys → Private vehicle transfer back to the hotel. **Option 2 – Relaxed Shimla experience:** Visit Annandale and the Army Heritage Museum → Continue to Tara Devi Temple or Sankat Mochan Temple → Return to central Shimla for premium shopping at Himachal Emporium, Lakkar Bazaar, and selected local boutiques. Afternoon: Leisure lunch followed by rest at the hotel or resort → Optional spa treatment, private photography session, or curated café visit. Evening: Farewell sunset experience at The Ridge, Jakhoo Hill, or a private valley-view terrace → Celebration dinner with personalised service → Overnight stay in Mashobra / Naldehra or Shimla, depending on departure logistics.', 5454),
  ('shimla', 31, 'six-night-seven-day-luxury-itinerary', 'SIX-NIGHT / SEVEN-DAY LUXURY ITINERARY', 'Night 7', NULL, 'Enjoy a relaxed breakfast at the hotel → Final mountain-view tea or short property walk → Checkout with luggage assistance. Private chauffeur-driven transfer to Chandigarh Airport or Chandigarh Railway Station → Departure with scenic views of the Himalayan foothills and comfortable rest stops en route.', 5455),
  ('shimla', 32, 'travel-agent-insights', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS', 'What inexperienced planners often do wrong', NULL, '', 5456),
  ('shimla', 32, 'travel-agent-insights', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS', 'What an experienced planner does differently', NULL, '', 5457),
  ('shimla', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'IF:', NULL, '**trip_length <= 1 night**', 5458),
  ('shimla', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'THEN:', NULL, 'prefer The Ridge + Christ Church + Mall Road + one nearby viewpoint or temple. Reason: A one-night Shimla stay works best as a compact central experience. The Ridge, Christ Church, Mall Road, Scandal Point, and a short café or shopping stop provide a clear first impression without adding a tiring Kufri or Chail excursion.', 5459),
  ('shimla', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'IF:', NULL, '**trip_length == 2 nights**', 5460),
  ('shimla', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'THEN:', NULL, 'schedule one central heritage-and-shopping day AND: schedule one nearby excursion such as Kufri, Jakhoo Temple, or Viceregal Lodge. Reason: Two nights are enough for central Shimla plus one major mountain or heritage experience, but not for comfortably combining Kufri, Fagu, Chail, Naldehra, Mashobra, and multiple museums.', 5461),
  ('shimla', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'IF:', NULL, '**trip_length >= 3 nights**', 5462),
  ('shimla', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'THEN:', NULL, 'include one central walking cluster AND: include one scenic excursion AND: include one flexible half-day. Reason: Three nights are the practical sweet spot for balancing heritage, nature, shopping, cafés, and relaxed hill-station time without turning the itinerary into a checklist.', 5463),
  ('shimla', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'IF:', NULL, '**trip_length <= 3 nights**', 5464),
  ('shimla', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'THEN:', NULL, 'prefer_one_hotel AND: avoid changing accommodation between Shimla, Kufri, Mashobra, and Naldehra. Reason: Short stays lose valuable time through packing, checkout, luggage movement, and road transfers. One well-located base is usually more efficient.', 5465),
  ('shimla', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'IF:', NULL, '**trip_type == FIRST_TIME_VISITOR**', 5466),
  ('shimla', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'THEN:', NULL, 'anchor the itinerary around The Ridge, Mall Road, Christ Church, Jakhoo Temple, and one excursion to Kufri or Naldehra. Reason: These experiences provide the clearest introduction to Shimla’s colonial heritage, mountain scenery, temples, shopping, cafés, and family-friendly sightseeing.', 5467),
  ('shimla', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'IF:', NULL, '**traveler_type == FAMILY** AND: **children_age <= 6**', 5468),
  ('shimla', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'THEN:', NULL, 'reduce_walking_intensity_target by 25% AND: limit_major_activities_per_day to 2 AND: increase_downtime by 20% AND: prefer hotels with easy vehicle access. Reason: Steep roads, stairs, cold weather, traffic, and uneven paths can tire young children. Short sightseeing blocks, predictable meal breaks, open spaces, and hotel rest make the trip more comfortable.', 5469),
  ('shimla', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'IF:', NULL, '**trip_type == FAMILY**', 5470),
  ('shimla', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'THEN:', NULL, 'prefer The Ridge, Christ Church, Mall Road, toy-train experiences, Kufri, Himalayan Nature Park, Annandale, and easy viewpoints AND: avoid long uphill walks and multiple remote excursions on the same day. Reason: Shimla suits families particularly well when sightseeing is mixed with child-friendly outdoor time, short walks, snow play, and regular rest periods.', 5471),
  ('shimla', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'IF:', NULL, '**trip_type == HONEYMOON**', 5472),
  ('shimla', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'THEN:', NULL, 'increase romance_weight by 30% increase privacy_weight by 25% increase free_time_weight by 25% decrease activity_density by 25%. Reason: Shimla’s honeymoon value comes from valley-view accommodation, private drives, pine forests, snowfall possibilities, café dates, scenic walks, spa time, and romantic dinners rather than maximum attraction coverage.', 5473),
  ('shimla', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'IF:', NULL, '**trip_type == HONEYMOON**', 5474),
  ('shimla', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'THEN:', NULL, 'prefer Mashobra, Summer Hill, Naldehra, or a quiet valley-view property AND: schedule no more than 2 major activities per day AND: include one private dinner or scenic sunset experience. Reason: These areas provide greater privacy and slower mountain experiences, while central Shimla is better used for one relaxed heritage walk, café visit, or shopping session.', 5475),
  ('shimla', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'IF:', NULL, '**traveler_type == LUXURY**', 5476),
  ('shimla', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'THEN:', NULL, 'prefer_private_transfer AND: prefer_high_service_heritage_or_valley_view_hotel AND: prefer_curated_excursions AND: increase_service_and_rest_weight. Reason: Luxury value in Shimla is created through comfort, privacy, professional chauffeurs, premium rooms, spa services, personalised dining, and flexible pacing—not by adding more roadside stops.', 5477),
  ('shimla', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'IF:', NULL, '**traveler_type == LUXURY** AND: **trip_length >= 4 nights**', 5478),
  ('shimla', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'THEN:', NULL, 'consider a split stay between central Shimla and Mashobra / Naldehra OR: retain one luxury base and add a full-day private excursion. Reason: A longer stay can benefit from both central heritage access and a quieter forest-resort atmosphere, provided the hotel change does not create unnecessary logistical effort.', 5479),
  ('shimla', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'IF:', NULL, '**traveler_type == BUDGET**', 5480),
  ('shimla', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'THEN:', NULL, 'prefer a value hotel in Chhota Shimla, Sanjauli, or another area with practical road access AND: use walking for central sightseeing AND: mix free attractions with one or two paid excursions. Reason: The Ridge, Mall Road, Christ Church, Scandal Point, colonial streets, local markets, and viewpoints provide substantial low-cost sightseeing. Taxis should be reserved for spread-out attractions such as Kufri, Naldehra, and Mashobra.', 5481),
  ('shimla', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'IF:', NULL, 'hotel_is_far_from_central_shimla: AND: **hotel_saving < additional_transport_cost + value_of_lost_time**', 5482),
  ('shimla', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'THEN:', NULL, 'prefer_central_hotel_or_easy_road_access_hotel. Reason: A cheaper hotel may provide poor overall value if guests must repeatedly pay for taxis or climb long stairways to reach Mall Road, The Ridge, restaurants, and shopping areas.', 5483),
  ('shimla', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'IF:', NULL, 'hotel_is_near_mall_road:', 5484),
  ('shimla', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'THEN:', NULL, 'verify_vehicle_drop_point AND: verify_luggage_access AND: verify_stairs_and_lift AND: verify_actual_walking_distance. Reason: Many central Shimla streets are pedestrian-only, so “near Mall Road” does not necessarily mean that a vehicle can reach the hotel entrance or that luggage movement will be easy.', 5485),
  ('shimla', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'IF:', NULL, '**traveler_type == SENIOR**', 5486),
  ('shimla', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'THEN:', NULL, 'prefer Chhota Shimla, Brockhurst, Sanjauli, Summer Hill, or a hotel with direct road access AND: use private transport AND: avoid long uphill walks, steep shortcuts, and stair-heavy sightseeing. Reason: Shimla’s central attractions are rewarding but can involve slopes, stairs, narrow roads, uneven pavements, and heavy crowds. Hotel accessibility and vehicle access should be checked individually before booking.', 5487),
  ('shimla', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'IF:', NULL, '**traveler_type == SENIOR** OR: **mobility_level == LIMITED**', 5488),
  ('shimla', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'THEN:', NULL, 'limit_major_activities_per_day to 1–2 AND: schedule outdoor sightseeing during the warmer part of the day AND: include a rest period after every excursion. Reason: Shorter sightseeing blocks reduce fatigue and make it easier to manage cold weather, traffic, weather changes, and the physical demands of hill terrain.', 5489),
  ('shimla', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'IF:', NULL, '**traveler_interest == HISTORY OR traveler_interest == CULTURE**', 5490),
  ('shimla', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'THEN:', NULL, 'combine The Ridge, Christ Church, Gaiety Heritage Cultural Complex, Viceregal Lodge, Himachal State Museum, and one temple visit over adjacent days. Reason: These attractions create a coherent colonial, architectural, religious, and regional-heritage experience without requiring long road transfers.', 5491),
  ('shimla', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'IF:', NULL, '**traveler_interest == NATURE OR traveler_interest == PHOTOGRAPHY**', 5492),
  ('shimla', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'THEN:', NULL, 'prefer Green Valley, Kufri, Himalayan Nature Park, Mashobra, Naldehra, Summer Hill, and selected forest viewpoints AND: protect early-morning or late-afternoon photography time. Reason: Shimla is especially strong for pine forests, Himalayan scenery, colonial streets, seasonal snow, valley views, and changing mountain light.', 5493),
  ('shimla', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'IF:', NULL, '**traveler_interest == SNOW**', 5494),
  ('shimla', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'THEN:', NULL, 'prefer December–February AND: treat snowfall and snow activities as weather-dependent AND: keep road transfers and outdoor plans flexible. Reason: Winter can provide the classic snow experience, but snowfall timing and intensity vary. Heavy snow may also affect roads, walking paths, attraction access, and local transport.', 5495),
  ('shimla', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'IF:', NULL, '**weather == MONSOON**', 5496),
  ('shimla', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'THEN:', NULL, 'reduce_outdoor_walking AND: reduce_long_excursions AND: increase_indoor_or_flexible_time AND: keep Kufri, Chail, waterfalls, and forest visits weather-dependent. Reason: Rain can reduce visibility, make paths slippery, delay road journeys, and disrupt fixed outdoor plans. Museums, heritage buildings, cafés, shopping, hotel dining, and spa time provide useful alternatives.', 5497),
  ('shimla', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'IF:', NULL, '**weather == HEAVY_SNOWFALL**', 5498),
  ('shimla', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'THEN:', NULL, 'avoid_tight_itinerary AND: prioritise_nearby_or_walkable_attractions AND: keep_extra_transfer_buffer AND: confirm road and attraction conditions locally. Reason: Snow can create traffic delays, slippery walking conditions, vehicle restrictions, and temporary changes to sightseeing access. Flexibility is more valuable than attempting to preserve every scheduled stop.', 5499),
  ('shimla', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'IF:', NULL, '**trip_length >= 4 nights** AND: **traveler_interest == RELAXATION**', 5500),
  ('shimla', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'THEN:', NULL, 'add one resort-focused day AND: consider Mashobra, Naldehra, Summer Hill, or Chail AND: include spa, balcony, café, or forest time. Reason: Longer Shimla stays are more rewarding when they include quiet mountain experiences and recovery time instead of repeating central sightseeing.', 5501),
  ('shimla', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'IF:', NULL, '**trip_length >= 5 nights** AND: **traveler_interest == ADVENTURE**', 5502),
  ('shimla', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'THEN:', NULL, 'consider extending beyond central Shimla to Kufri, Naldehra, Mashobra, Chail, or Tattapani AND: reserve separate time for trekking, cycling, horse riding, snow activities, or rafting where seasonally suitable. Reason: Shimla offers light-to-moderate adventure, but the city centre itself is more suited to sightseeing and walking. Outdoor variety increases when nearby areas are included.', 5503),
  ('shimla', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'IF:', NULL, '**trip_type == FIRST_TIME_VISITOR** AND: **trip_length <= 2 nights**', 5504),
  ('shimla', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'THEN:', NULL, 'do_not_recommend Kufri + Fagu + Chail + Naldehra + Mashobra in one day. Reason: The destinations may appear close on a map, but mountain roads, traffic, stops, and sightseeing time make such a circuit tiring and low quality. Choose one excursion cluster instead.', 5505),
  ('shimla', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'IF:', NULL, '**traveler_interest == SHOPPING**', 5506),
  ('shimla', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'THEN:', NULL, 'include Lakkar Bazaar, Mall Road, Himachal Emporium, Tibetan Market, and Lower Bazaar AND: keep shopping time separate from a long excursion day. Reason: Woollens, wooden handicrafts, Himachali caps, shawls, souvenirs, local snacks, and handmade products are best explored without rushing between distant viewpoints.', 5507),
  ('shimla', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'IF:', NULL, '**trip_type == ROMANTIC**', 5508),
  ('shimla', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'THEN:', NULL, 'schedule a quiet forest walk, café date, mountain-view dinner, and one sunset or snowfall experience. Reason: Shimla’s strongest romantic moments come from atmosphere—pine forests, warm cafés, colonial streets, mountain views, and slow evenings—rather than from covering many attractions.', 5509),
  ('shimla', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'IF:', NULL, '**traveler_type == PARTY_TRAVELLER**', 5510),
  ('shimla', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'THEN:', NULL, 'set_low_nightlife_expectation AND: prioritise cafés, hotel lounges, restaurants, live-music venues, and evening walks. Reason: Shimla’s nightlife is generally low-key, with cosy cafés, restaurants, hotel lounges, and Mall Road evenings rather than a large clubbing or late-night entertainment scene.', 5511),
  ('shimla', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'IF:', NULL, '**arrival_mode == CHANDIGARH_AIRPORT_OR_RAILWAY_STATION**', 5512),
  ('shimla', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'THEN:', NULL, 'allow approximately half a day for the road transfer AND: prefer a private sedan, SUV, or MPV when comfort and flexibility matter. Reason: The Chandigarh–Shimla transfer is a lengthy mountain journey, so rest stops, luggage space, motion comfort, and a realistic arrival schedule should be built into the plan.', 5513),
  ('shimla', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'IF:', NULL, '**traveler_type == FAMILY OR traveler_type == LUXURY OR traveler_type == HONEYMOON**', 5514),
  ('shimla', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'THEN:', NULL, 'prefer_private_transfer_from_chandigarh AND: include comfort stops AND: avoid scheduling major sightseeing immediately after arrival. Reason: A private transfer improves door-to-door convenience, luggage handling, scenic flexibility, and comfort after the mountain journey.', 5515),
  ('shimla', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'IF:', NULL, '**traveler_type == BUDGET** AND: **central_sightseeing_required == true**', 5516),
  ('shimla', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'THEN:', NULL, 'use walking and local transport for The Ridge, Mall Road, Christ Church, Scandal Point, Gaiety Theatre, and Lakkar Bazaar AND: reserve taxis for attractions outside the central zone. Reason: Shimla’s central heritage and shopping areas are naturally suited to walking, while private transport is more valuable for Kufri, Naldehra, Mashobra, Chail, and other spread-out locations.', 5517),
  ('shimla', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'IF:', NULL, '**trip_length >= 4 nights**', 5518),
  ('shimla', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'THEN:', NULL, 'add one flexible half-day. Reason: A flexible block allows recovery after transfers, weather adjustments, extra photography, shopping, snowfall time, resort relaxation, or a repeat visit to a favourite café or viewpoint.', 5519),
  ('shimla', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'IF:', NULL, '**accessibility_requirement == HIGH**', 5520),
  ('shimla', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'THEN:', NULL, 'verify_each_hotel_and_attraction_individually AND: prefer direct vehicle access, lifts, ground-floor rooms, accessible bathrooms, and minimal-step routes AND: avoid assuming that central or “wheelchair-friendly” labels guarantee full accessibility. Reason: Shimla’s accessibility varies significantly by hotel, attraction, entrance, terrain, and transport arrangement. Destination-level accessibility should never replace property-level verification.', 5521),
  ('shimla', 34, 'destination-scoring', 'DESTINATION SCORING', NULL, NULL, '| Factor | Score | | ------------------ | ----- | | Family | 88 | | Honeymoon | 91 | | Luxury | 84 | | Budget | 82 | | Adventure | 78 | | Culture | 86 | | Food | 80 | | Shopping | 84 | | Nightlife | 48 | | Relaxation | 88 | | Nature | 92 | | Accessibility | 62 | | Safety | 82 | | First-time visitor | 93 | | Photography | 94 |', 5522),
  ('shimla', 35, 'final-travel-agent-verdict', 'FINAL TRAVEL AGENT VERDICT', NULL, NULL, 'Best traveler profiles: 1. Nature and mountain scenery lover 2. Honeymoon or romantic couple 3. First-time Himalayan visitor 4. Family seeking a comfortable hill-station holiday 6. Snowfall seeker Best duration: **2–3 nights for most travelers, with 3 nights as the sweet spot in Shimla.** Two nights allow central sightseeing, Mall Road, The Ridge, Christ Church, one heritage or temple visit, and one nearby excursion. Four or more nights are worthwhile for couples, photographers, relaxation-focused travelers, or those adding Mashobra, Naldehra, Chail, or a wider Himachal itinerary. Best season: **October–November** is the best all-round period for clear mountain views, pleasant weather, manageable crowds, photography, heritage walks, and nearby excursions. **December–February** is best for snowfall, honeymoon trips, and winter photography, but it also brings higher prices, traffic, crowds, and weather-related travel uncertainty. **March–June** is suitable for families, sightseeing, and escaping the heat of the plains. **July–September** is quieter and greener but less reliable for fixed outdoor itineraries because of rain, mist, slippery paths, and possible road delays. Best hotel strategy: Choose accommodation with easy vehicle access, heating, luggage assistance, and verified walking distance from the main attractions. Best transportation: Walk for compact central circuits AND: use taxis or private cars for Kufri, Naldehra, Mashobra, Chail, Jakhoo Temple, Viceregal Lodge, and other spread-out attractions. The Kalka–Shimla Toy Train is best treated as a scenic experience rather than the fastest transport option. Private transfer for: Must-do for first-time visitor: **Don’t-do:** Biggest advantage: Shimla combines Himalayan scenery, colonial heritage, temples, shopping, cafés, photography, seasonal snow, family-friendly activities, and nearby excursions in one accessible hill-station base. Biggest disadvantage: Steep terrain, stairs, uneven pavements, pedestrian-only areas, peak-season crowds, traffic congestion, high winter prices, and weather-sensitive road travel can reduce comfort if the trip is overplanned. Overall destination score: **88/100**', 5523),
  ('shimla', 36, 'data-quality', 'DATA QUALITY', NULL, NULL, 'information_completeness: 95/100 last_updated: 2026-08-17 last_verified: NOT_LIVE_VERIFIED verified_by: TRAVEL_ENGINE_INITIAL_DATASET sources: IMPORTANT: Prices, opening hours, schedules, visa requirements, availability, accessibility and operational conditions must NOT be treated as permanently valid from this document. These must be sourced from structured, refreshable data.', 5524),
  ('manali', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Summer', NULL, 'months: March-June weather: Cool to pleasantly warm mountain weather, with crisp mornings and evenings. March retains a late-winter feel at higher elevations, while April to June brings comfortable sightseeing conditions in Manali; June is generally the warmest period in the valley. crowd_level: HIGH → VERY HIGH price_level: MEDIUM → HIGH overall_score: 84–90 recommended: true reason: One of the strongest periods for first-time visitors, families, couples, sightseeing, Solang Valley activities, cafés, and local excursions. May and June are peak domestic-holiday months, so expect traffic, higher hotel prices, and advance-booking needs—especially on weekends and for Rohtang-related excursions.', 5525),
  ('manali', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Monsoon', NULL, 'months: June–September weather: Rainy, cool, humid, and intensely green, with cloud cover, misty forests, and occasional clearer intervals. July and August are typically the wettest months, while September gradually becomes more manageable as rainfall begins to ease. crowd_level: LOW → MEDIUM price_level: LOW → MEDIUM overall_score: 58–72 recommended: false reason: Best only for flexible budget travellers, quiet-stay seekers, and photographers who enjoy rain-washed landscapes. Heavy rain can bring slippery roads, landslide risk, reduced visibility, traffic disruption, and cancellations or restrictions for trekking, paragliding, Rohtang Pass, and other outdoor excursions.', 5526),
  ('manali', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Autumn (Post-Monsoon)', NULL, 'months: October–November weather: Mostly dry, clear, and cool, with fresh air, stronger Himalayan views, comfortable days, and increasingly cold mornings and nights. October is among the driest months, while November feels distinctly colder but usually remains favourable for sightseeing. crowd_level: LOW → MEDIUM price_level: LOW → MEDIUM overall_score: 88–93 recommended: true reason: The best all-round period for travellers seeking clear mountain scenery, photography, cafés, local sightseeing, relaxed stays, and good value without the major summer or New Year crowds. It is particularly suitable for couples, families, first-time visitors, and travellers who prefer pleasant conditions over guaranteed snow.', 5527),
  ('manali', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Winter', NULL, 'months: December-February weather: Cold to very cold, with freezing mornings and nights and seasonal snowfall in Manali’s surrounding higher areas, especially Solang Valley. Snow conditions and road access can change quickly; Rohtang Pass is generally snowbound, while routes and activities may face weather-related restrictions. crowd_level: HIGH → VERY HIGH price_level: HIGH → VERY HIGH overall_score: 86–94 recommended: true reason: Best for snow seekers, honeymooners, winter photographers, and travellers wanting cosy mountain stays, snow play, skiing, or snowboarding around Solang. Christmas, New Year, long weekends, and active snowfall periods create the highest demand, crowded roads, and premium hotel rates, so book early and retain flexibility in the itinerary.', 5528),
  ('manali', 10, 'budget-strategy', 'BUDGET STRATEGY', NULL, NULL, '', 5529),
  ('manali', 12, 'airport-transfer-logic', 'AIRPORT TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Family', 'family', 'Airport taxi or pre-booked private MPV / Innova-type vehicle from Airport taxi or pre-booked private MPV / Innova-type vehicle from Chandigardh Airport; door-to-door, luggage-friendly, and more comfortable for Manali’s winding mountain roads. The larger vehicle is especially useful for families carrying winter clothing, strollers, sports equipment.', 5530),
  ('manali', 12, 'airport-transfer-logic', 'AIRPORT TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Honeymoon', 'honeymoon', 'Pre-booked private sedan or comfortable SUV from Chandigardh Airport; best for privacy, scenic stops, comfort, and a relaxed first impression of the Himalayan journey. reason: The airport-to-Manali transfer follows a scenic but winding mountain route, so a private vehicle provides flexibility for rest breaks, viewpoints, luggage handling, and a comfortable start to the honeymoon. A private transfer also allows a direct drop-off at a riverside, valley-view, or Old Manali accommodation.', 5531),
  ('manali', 12, 'airport-transfer-logic', 'AIRPORT TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Luxury', 'luxury', 'Chauffeured premium sedan, Innova Crysta, or luxury MPV from Chandigardh Airport; ideal for enhanced comfort, privacy, professional service, luggage assistance, flexible scenic stops, and seamless hotel drop-off.', 5532),
  ('manali', 12, 'airport-transfer-logic', 'AIRPORT TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Budget', 'budget', 'Prepaid airport taxi, shared cab, or locally arranged shared transfer from Chandigardh Airport; the most economical option for cost-conscious travellers while still providing reliable access to Manali. Shared transport is particularly suitable for solo travellers or small groups with limited luggage, although availability may depend on the flight arrival time. Airport taxi fares vary by vehicle type, distance, season, and booking provider, so confirm the total fare and inclusions before travel.', 5533),
  ('manali', 18, 'family-travel', 'FAMILY TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'child_friendly_score: 85 best_ages: Rules: For young children: Prefer: Avoid:', 5534),
  ('manali', 19, 'honeymoon-travel', 'HONEYMOON TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'honeymoon_score: 94 romance_score: 92 privacy_score: 85 luxury_score: 84 Recommended: **Honeymoon itinerary should NOT contain more than:** Prefer: over: Recommended honeymoon experiences: Recommended hotel areas:', 5535),
  ('manali', 20, 'luxury-travel', 'LUXURY TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'luxury_score: 84 Recommended: Luxury should primarily increase: Recommended hotel areas:', 5536),
  ('manali', 21, 'adventure', 'ADVENTURE', NULL, NULL, 'adventure_score: 91 Manali is an excellent adventure destination, offering trekking, skiing, snowboarding, paragliding, river rafting, mountain biking, camping, snow activities and scenic high-altitude excursions. It suits both beginners seeking accessible outdoor activities and experienced travellers interested in demanding Himalayan treks, depending on season, weather, permits and operator safety standards. **Adventure-like experiences should be interpreted as:** Recommended adventure-style areas:', 5537),
  ('manali', 22, 'senior-travel', 'SENIOR TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'senior_suitability: 68 walking_intensity: MEDIUM_HIGH Rules: Recommended hotel areas: Aleo: – one of the better choices for seniors because it is comparatively peaceful, has road-accessible hotels, offers easier taxi drop-offs, and is convenient for central Manali and riverside areas. Prini: – suitable for seniors seeking a quiet stay, mountain views, apple orchards, and less congestion; verify the hotel entrance, slope, parking, heating, elevator, and distance from the main road. Simsa: – a practical option for budget-conscious seniors, with several hotels, road access, quieter surroundings, and convenient taxi connections toward central Manali. Shuru: – peaceful and scenic, with village surroundings, orchards, and open valley views; best for seniors who prioritise relaxation and stay at a property with dependable vehicle access. **Aleo–Beas River side** – convenient for relaxed riverside scenery and quieter accommodation, although the exact walking surface and distance to the river should be checked before booking. Vashisht: – suitable for seniors interested in the temple and hot springs, but many properties and approach roads involve slopes, steps, or narrow lanes; choose accommodation with confirmed vehicle access. Old Manali: – convenient for cafés, Manu Temple, and local atmosphere, but some lanes are uneven, steep, congested, or pedestrian-only; select a hotel close to a motorable road and avoid properties requiring long uphill walks. Solang Valley surroundings: – suitable only for a short scenic stay or snow-focused visit when road and weather conditions are favourable; confirm heating, medical support, vehicle access, and altitude comfort before booking.', 5538),
  ('manali', 23, 'accessibility', 'ACCESSIBILITY', NULL, NULL, 'wheelchair_accessibility: PARTIAL_TO_GOOD depending on attraction and transport public_transport_accessibility: VARIABLE hotel_accessibility: MUST_BE_VERIFIED_PER_HOTEL attraction_accessibility: MUST_BE_VERIFIED_PER_ATTRACTION Rule: Never infer accessibility from destination-level accessibility. Each hotel and attraction must carry its own accessibility data.', 5539),
  ('manali', 24, 'food', 'FOOD', NULL, NULL, 'Manali is particularly strong for: Food experiences: Family: Prioritize clean, comfortable restaurants with familiar and flexible menus. North Indian meals, parathas, rice, dal, rajma-chawal, noodles, momos, sandwiches, pizzas, bakery items, and mild Himachali dishes usually work well for families. Hotels and restaurants with indoor seating, heating, early meal timings, and child-friendly options are especially convenient during winter. Honeymoon: At least one memorable mountain-view dinner is recommended—choose a heritage hotel restaurant, boutique resort, cosy café, or private dining setup with valley views. A relaxed café date with hot chocolate and pastries, followed by a warm Himachali dinner or in-room meal, suits Shimla’s romantic hill-station atmosphere better than a rushed food itinerary. Luxury: Fine dining in Shimla is strongest in setting, ambience, service, and presentation rather than in a large variety of specialised restaurants. Premium heritage hotels and valley-view resorts can offer curated Himachali menus, private balcony dining, chef-led meals, afternoon tea, personalised breakfast, fireplaces, and scenic mountain-view dinners. Budget: Mix local Himachali restaurants, simple North Indian eateries, bakeries, cafés, Tibetan food outlets, and selected hotel meals. Himachali thalis, rajma-chawal, chole bhature, momos, thukpa, parathas, bun snacks, and bakery items provide good value, while local restaurants around Mall Road, Lakkar Bazaar, and the main market areas are useful for quick and affordable meals**FOOD** Manali is particularly strong for: Food experiences: Family: Prioritize clean, comfortable restaurants with familiar and flexible menus. North Indian meals, rice, dal, rajma-chawal, parathas, noodles, momos, sandwiches, pizzas, pasta, soups, bakery items, and mild Himachali dishes usually work well for families. Restaurants with indoor seating, heating, early meal timings, clean washrooms, child-friendly portions, and takeaway options are especially convenient during winter. Honeymoon: At least one memorable mountain-view dinner is recommended—choose a valley-view resort, boutique hotel, riverside restaurant, or cosy café with warm lighting and scenic surroundings. A relaxed café date with hot chocolate, pastries, pancakes, or Tibetan food followed by a private Himachali or North Indian dinner suits Manali’s romantic mountain atmosphere better than a rushed food itinerary. Luxury: Fine dining in Manali is strongest in setting, ambience, service, views, and personalised hospitality rather than in a large variety of specialised restaurants. Premium resorts and boutique hotels can offer curated Himachali menus, Kullu trout, private balcony dining, chef-led meals, personalised breakfasts, fireplace-style settings, spa refreshments, in-room dining, and mountain-view dinners. Budget: Mix local Himachali restaurants, simple North Indian eateries, Tibetan food outlets, bakeries, cafés, dhabas, and selected hotel meals. Siddu, thalis, rajma-chawal, parathas, momos, thukpa, noodles, samosas, pakoras, tea, and bakery items provide good value. Local restaurants around Manali Market, Mall Road, Old Manali, Vashisht, and nearby market areas are useful for quick and affordable meals.', 5540),
  ('manali', 25, 'shopping', 'SHOPPING', NULL, NULL, 'Strong categories: Luxury shopping: Manali is not a major luxury-shopping destination, but it offers quality handloom products, premium shawls, curated Himachali handicrafts, traditional jewellery, and high-end local food products. For more refined selections, compare products at Himachal Emporium or premium boutiques around The Mall; for designer fashion, luxury jewellery, and large-brand shopping, Chandigarh or Delhi is a better choice.', 5541),
  ('manali', 26, 'nightlife', 'NIGHTLIFE', NULL, NULL, 'nightlife_level: 55–60 Manali has a limited but reasonably active nightlife scene compared with many Himalayan hill stations. Evening activity is mainly concentrated in Old Manali, Mall Road, Manu Market, Vashisht, and selected hotel areas, with cafés, restaurants, pubs, live-music venues, lounges, riverside dining, and occasional dance-oriented venues rather than a large or highly organized clubbing district. Old Manali is generally the best area for relaxed evening entertainment, while most places become quieter late at night. Suitable for: Not a primary requirement for:', 5542),
  ('manali', 28, 'sample-itinerary-patterns', 'SAMPLE ITINERARY PATTERNS', NULL, NULL, 'Night 1 Arrive at Chandigarh Airport → Private transfer to Manali → Scenic drive through the Kullu Valley → Hotel check-in → Rest and acclimatise → Evening walk around Mall Road and Manali Market → Café or bakery stop → Dinner. Night 2 Morning: Hadimba Devi Temple → Dhungri Forest → Museum of Himachal Culture and Folk Art. Afternoon: Manu Temple → Old Manali lanes → Local lunch at a café or Tibetan restaurant → Hotel rest. Evening: Beas River walk → Café time or relaxed photography around Old Manali → Dinner. Night 3 Morning: Excursion to Solang Valley → Snow play / skiing / snowboarding / zorbing / paragliding / ropeway experience, depending on season and weather. Afternoon: Continue towards Atal Tunnel and Sissu, subject to road access and local conditions → Scenic mountain viewpoints and waterfall stops → Packed lunch or local lunch. Evening: Return to Manali → Rest at hotel → Warm Himachali or Tibetan dinner. Night 4 Morning: Vashisht Temple → Natural hot springs → Village lanes and mountain viewpoints. Afternoon: Jogini Waterfall walk, depending on walking comfort and weather → Lunch at Vashisht → Hotel rest. Evening: Relaxed riverside walk or quiet café time → Optional spa or wellness treatment → Dinner. Night 5 Option 1 (heritage and culture): Naggar Castle → Naggar Village → Roerich Art Gallery → Traditional Himachali lunch → Temple or orchard surroundings → Evening return to Manali. Option 2 (nature and relaxation): Kullu Valley drive → Riverside scenery → Kullu shawl shopping → Apple orchards and village photography → Relaxed lunch → Return to Manali. Dinner and relaxed hotel evening. Flexible day: Sethan Village for seasonal snow experiences, Kothi Village and mountain viewpoints, Van Vihar and Beas River walks, or a relaxed local Manali day. Afternoon: Leisure time for shopping, photography, café visits, spa treatment, local handicraft shopping, or hotel balcony time. Evening: Special Himachali dinner or romantic mountain-view dinner → Overnight in Manali. Breakfast → Checkout → Departure transfer from Manali to Chandigarh Airport / Railway Station.', 5543),
  ('manali', 29, 'six-night-seven-day-honeymoon-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHT / SEVEN-DAY HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Night 1', NULL, 'Morning pickup from Chandigarh Railway Station or Chandigarh Airport → Scenic private transfer to Shimla through Himalayan valleys and mountain roads → Check-in at a romantic valley-view hotel → Rest and acclimatise. Late afternoon: Visit Jakhoo Hanuman Temple by private vehicle or lift → Continue to The Ridge, Shimla Kali Bari Temple, Wax Museum, Christ Church, Rani Jhansi Park, Scandal Point, Lakkar Bazaar, and The Mall by walk, subject to time and walking comfort. Evening: Couple walk around The Mall → Café or bakery stop → Romantic dinner at the hotel. **Overnight in Shimla.**', 5544),
  ('manali', 29, 'six-night-seven-day-honeymoon-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHT / SEVEN-DAY HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Night 2', NULL, 'After breakfast, proceed for a private sightseeing excursion to Green Valley, Kufri, Fagu, Himalayan Adventure Park, and Chail. Optional: Horse riding or seasonal snow activities at Kufri, at an additional cost and subject to weather and local conditions. Enjoy scenic photography, forest views, and relaxed couple time around Fagu or Chail. Avoid packing too many activities into the day; select one main activity in addition to the scenic drive. Return to Shimla by late afternoon or evening → Free time for balcony relaxation, spa treatment, or a quiet café visit → Special dinner. **Overnight in Shimla.**', 5545),
  ('manali', 29, 'six-night-seven-day-honeymoon-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHT / SEVEN-DAY HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Night 3', NULL, 'After breakfast, check out from the Shimla hotel and begin the private transfer to Manali. Enjoy the scenic mountain journey through valleys, forests, and riverside landscapes. En-route, stop at suitable viewpoints and Pandoh Dam, subject to road conditions and available time. Continue towards Manali → Check-in at the hotel → Rest after the long journey. Evening: Relaxed dinner at the hotel or a short couple walk near the property, depending on arrival time. **Overnight in Manali.**', 5546),
  ('manali', 29, 'six-night-seven-day-honeymoon-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHT / SEVEN-DAY HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Night 4', NULL, 'After breakfast, visit Hadimba Devi Temple and the nearby Ghatotkach Temple amid cedar forests. Continue to the Beas River, Vashisht Temple and Vashisht Kund, Manu Temple, Manali Clubhouse, Van Vihar, Himalayan Nyinmapa Tibetan Buddhist Monastery, and Manali Mall, selecting the attractions according to available time and walking comfort. Return to the hotel by late afternoon or evening → Rest and enjoy private balcony time. Evening: Café date or relaxed walk at Manali Mall → Dinner at the hotel. **Overnight in Manali.**', 5547),
  ('manali', 29, 'six-night-seven-day-honeymoon-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHT / SEVEN-DAY HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Night 5', NULL, 'After breakfast, proceed by private vehicle to Solang Valley. Enjoy mountain scenery, snow views, and optional activities such as snow play, cable-car rides, or other seasonal adventure activities, at an additional cost and subject to weather and operational conditions. Continue towards Atal Tunnel, Sissu Village, and Sissu Lake if the road, weather, and local regulations permit. Keep the excursion flexible during winter or adverse weather. Return to Manali by late afternoon → Rest at the hotel. Evening: Spend quiet couple time at Manali Mall, enjoy a warm café meal, or arrange a private dinner at the hotel. **Overnight in Manali.**', 5548),
  ('manali', 29, 'six-night-seven-day-honeymoon-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHT / SEVEN-DAY HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Night 6', NULL, 'After breakfast, check out from the Manali hotel and proceed towards Kasol. En-route, stop at suitable viewpoints around Pandoh Dam, Sundar Nagar Lake, the rafting point, and Bhuntar, depending on the route and available time. Continue through the Parvati Valley to Kasol → Visit Manikaran Sahib Gurudwara and Manikaran Hot Springs. Since this is a long road journey, avoid adding too many stops. Check in to the Kasol hotel or resort by late afternoon or evening → Rest and enjoy the peaceful valley setting. Evening: Quiet riverside or balcony time, followed by a relaxed dinner. **Overnight in Kasol.**', 5549),
  ('manali', 29, 'six-night-seven-day-honeymoon-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHT / SEVEN-DAY HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Night 7', NULL, 'After breakfast, check out from the Kasol hotel. Private transfer towards Chandigarh or Kalka Railway Station, depending on the departure arrangement. Because the journey from Kasol to the plains is long, keep the departure schedule comfortable and avoid booking an early train or flight. Depart with beautiful memories of Shimla’s colonial charm, Kufri’s mountain scenery, Manali’s valleys, Solang’s snow experiences, and Kasol’s peaceful riverside atmosphere.', 5550),
  ('manali', 30, 'six-night-seven-day-family-itinerary', 'SIX-NIGHT / SEVEN-DAY FAMILY ITINERARY', 'Night 1', NULL, 'Pick up from Chandigarh Railway Station / Chandigarh Airport in the morning and transfer to Shimla by private vehicle. Enjoy the scenic valleys and mountain roads en route. Check in to the Shimla hotel and take some rest. In the late afternoon, proceed for local sightseeing: Jakhoo Hanuman Temple, The Ridge, Shimla Kali Bari Temple, Wax Museum, Christ Church, Rani Jhansi Park, Scandal Point, Lakkar Bazaar, and The Mall by walk. Return to the hotel by evening → Dinner at the hotel → Overnight stay in Shimla.', 5551),
  ('manali', 30, 'six-night-seven-day-family-itinerary', 'SIX-NIGHT / SEVEN-DAY FAMILY ITINERARY', 'Night 2', NULL, 'After breakfast, proceed for a family excursion to Kufri, Fagu, Himalayan Nature Park, Himalayan Adventure Park, and Chail. At Kufri, enjoy the mountain scenery and optional horse riding or seasonal snow activities at an additional cost. Families may also enjoy the adventure park, subject to age, weather, and operating conditions. Continue towards Fagu for scenic views and photography, followed by Chail forest surroundings and optional Chail Palace visit. Return to Shimla by late afternoon / evening → Evening free for leisure → Dinner at the hotel → Overnight stay in Shimla.', 5552),
  ('manali', 30, 'six-night-seven-day-family-itinerary', 'SIX-NIGHT / SEVEN-DAY FAMILY ITINERARY', 'Night 3', NULL, 'After breakfast, check out from the Shimla hotel and drive towards Manali through the scenic valleys of Himachal Pradesh. En route, enjoy views of Sundernagar, Mandi, Pandoh Dam, Hanogi Mata Temple, and the Kullu Valley. Depending on time, stop at a Kullu shawl outlet or local handicraft centre. Continue the journey to Manali and check in to the hotel on arrival. The rest of the evening is free for rest after the long mountain drive. Dinner at the hotel → Overnight stay in Manali.', 5553),
  ('manali', 30, 'six-night-seven-day-family-itinerary', 'SIX-NIGHT / SEVEN-DAY FAMILY ITINERARY', 'Night 4', NULL, 'After breakfast, proceed for Manali local sightseeing. Visit Hadimba Devi Temple, Ghatotkach Temple, Beas River, Vashisht Temple, Vashisht Kund, Manu Temple, Manali Clubhouse, Van Vihar, and the Himalayan Nyinmapa Tibetan Buddhist Monastery. Later, enjoy a relaxed walk around Manali Mall Road for shopping, cafés, snacks, and family time. Return to the hotel by late afternoon / evening → Evening free for leisure → Dinner at the hotel → Overnight stay in Manali.', 5554),
  ('manali', 30, 'six-night-seven-day-family-itinerary', 'SIX-NIGHT / SEVEN-DAY FAMILY ITINERARY', 'Night 5', NULL, 'After breakfast, start the excursion to Solang Valley. Enjoy the snow-covered landscapes or mountain scenery, depending on the season. Optional activities may include snow play, ropeway rides, snow tubing, or other adventure activities at an additional cost. Continue towards Atal Tunnel, subject to weather, road conditions, traffic, and local access regulations. If permitted, visit Sissu Village and Sissu Lake. Return to Manali by late afternoon / evening. Later, spend quality family time at Manali Mall by local transport. Dinner at the hotel → Overnight stay in Manali.', 5555),
  ('manali', 30, 'six-night-seven-day-family-itinerary', 'SIX-NIGHT / SEVEN-DAY FAMILY ITINERARY', 'Night 6', NULL, 'After breakfast, check out from the Manali hotel and proceed towards Kasol / Manikaran. En route, enjoy scenic stops around Kullu Valley, including Pandoh Dam, Sundarnagar Lake, the Beas or Parvati Valley viewpoints, rafting point, Bhuntar, and local markets, depending on time and road conditions. Continue to Manikaran and visit Manikaran Sahib Gurudwara and the famous Manikaran hot springs. Guests may spend some peaceful time in the surrounding Parvati Valley. Proceed to Kasol and check in to the hotel by late afternoon / evening. Take rest after the journey. Evening free for leisure or a short riverside / market walk, subject to local conditions → Dinner at the hotel → Overnight stay in Kasol.', 5556),
  ('manali', 30, 'six-night-seven-day-family-itinerary', 'SIX-NIGHT / SEVEN-DAY FAMILY ITINERARY', 'Night 7', NULL, 'After breakfast, check out from the Kasol hotel and transfer to Chandigarh Railway Station / Chandigarh Airport for your onward journey. The trip ends with happy memories of Shimla, Manali, Kullu, Kasol, and Manikaran.', 5557),
  ('manali', 31, 'six-night-seven-day-luxury-itinerary', 'SIX-NIGHT / SEVEN-DAY LUXURY ITINERARY', 'Night 1', NULL, 'Private premium vehicle pickup from Chandigarh Airport or Railway Station → Scenic transfer through the Himalayan valleys with planned comfort stops → Check-in at a luxury heritage hotel, boutique property, or valley-view resort in Shimla / Mashobra → Welcome drink and rest. Late afternoon: Private guided sightseeing of Jakhoo Hanuman Temple, followed by The Ridge, Christ Church, Scandal Point, Rani Jhansi Park, and the colonial buildings around Mall Road. Continue with a relaxed walk through Lakkar Bazaar and the central heritage lanes. Evening: Return to the hotel → Private balcony tea, spa treatment, or time beside the fireplace → Curated Himachali dinner with valley views → Overnight stay in Shimla.', 5558),
  ('manali', 31, 'six-night-seven-day-luxury-itinerary', 'SIX-NIGHT / SEVEN-DAY LUXURY ITINERARY', 'Night 2', NULL, 'After a leisurely breakfast, depart in a private chauffeur-driven SUV for Kufri and Fagu → Scenic drive through pine and cedar forests → Green Valley photography stop → Kufri sightseeing. Optional activities: Private nature walk, Himalayan Nature Park visit, horse riding, seasonal snow experience, or a curated adventure activity with local assistance. Continue towards Fagu for peaceful mountain views and a relaxed lunch at a premium resort or selected countryside restaurant → Proceed to Chail for forest scenery, Chail Palace surroundings, and quiet heritage photography. Return to Shimla by late afternoon / evening → High tea at the hotel → Spa, indoor relaxation, or private balcony time → Special dinner → Overnight stay in Shimla.', 5559),
  ('manali', 31, 'six-night-seven-day-luxury-itinerary', 'SIX-NIGHT / SEVEN-DAY LUXURY ITINERARY', 'Night 3', NULL, 'After breakfast, visit Viceregal Lodge / Rashtrapati Niwas and the Indian Institute of Advanced Study with a private guide → Explore the heritage architecture and landscaped surroundings at an unhurried pace. Continue to the Himachal State Museum for regional art, history, sculptures, and traditional artefacts → Visit Summer Hill and enjoy a peaceful pine-forest drive. Afternoon: Return to the hotel for lunch and rest → Optional spa treatment, wellness session, or in-room relaxation. Evening: Private colonial heritage walk covering Gaiety Heritage Cultural Complex, The Ridge, Christ Church, and Mall Road → Afternoon tea or hot chocolate at a premium café → Fine-dining dinner at the hotel → Overnight stay in Shimla.', 5560),
  ('manali', 31, 'six-night-seven-day-luxury-itinerary', 'SIX-NIGHT / SEVEN-DAY LUXURY ITINERARY', 'Night 4', NULL, 'After breakfast, check out from the Shimla hotel and transfer by private luxury vehicle to Mashobra or Naldehra → Scenic forest drive through pine and cedar landscapes → Check-in at a premium mountain resort or luxury retreat. Afternoon: Resort lunch followed by leisure time → Enjoy the property’s spa, private balcony, heated indoor facilities, or guided forest walk. Late afternoon: Visit Naldehra Golf Course and surrounding cedar forests → Optional horse riding or relaxed photography session → Return to the resort. Evening: Private mountain-view dinner, bonfire-style experience where available, or in-room dining → Overnight stay in Mashobra / Naldehra.', 5561),
  ('manali', 31, 'six-night-seven-day-luxury-itinerary', 'SIX-NIGHT / SEVEN-DAY LUXURY ITINERARY', 'Night 5', NULL, 'Begin with a leisurely breakfast overlooking the hills → Guided nature walk through the forest surroundings or a gentle private excursion around Mashobra. Visit selected viewpoints and quiet countryside areas → Optional horse riding at Naldehra, golf-course visit, photography session, or private picnic-style lunch arranged by the resort. Afternoon: Return to the resort for spa therapy, wellness time, afternoon tea, or relaxed balcony time with mountain views. Evening: Sunset viewing from the property or a nearby scenic point → Chef-curated Himachali dinner featuring local specialties such as siddu, chana madra, rajma, kadhi, and regional breads → Overnight stay in Mashobra / Naldehra.', 5562),
  ('manali', 31, 'six-night-seven-day-luxury-itinerary', 'SIX-NIGHT / SEVEN-DAY LUXURY ITINERARY', 'Night 6', NULL, 'After breakfast, choose one of the following luxury experiences: **Option 1 – Scenic railway experience:** Enjoy a reserved section of the Kalka–Shimla Toy Train on a suitable route → Scenic views of tunnels, bridges, forests, and mountain valleys → Private vehicle transfer back to the hotel. **Option 2 – Relaxed Shimla experience:** Visit Annandale and the Army Heritage Museum → Continue to Tara Devi Temple or Sankat Mochan Temple → Return to central Shimla for premium shopping at Himachal Emporium, Lakkar Bazaar, and selected local boutiques. Afternoon: Leisure lunch followed by rest at the hotel or resort → Optional spa treatment, private photography session, or curated café visit. Evening: Farewell sunset experience at The Ridge, Jakhoo Hill, or a private valley-view terrace → Celebration dinner with personalised service → Overnight stay in Mashobra / Naldehra or Shimla, depending on departure logistics.', 5563),
  ('manali', 31, 'six-night-seven-day-luxury-itinerary', 'SIX-NIGHT / SEVEN-DAY LUXURY ITINERARY', 'Night 7', NULL, 'Enjoy a relaxed breakfast at the hotel → Final mountain-view tea or short property walk → Checkout with luggage assistance. Private chauffeur-driven transfer to Chandigarh Airport or Chandigarh Railway Station → Departure with scenic views of the Himalayan foothills and comfortable rest stops en route.', 5564),
  ('manali', 32, 'travel-agent-insights-manali', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS — MANALI', 'What inexperienced planners often do wrong', NULL, '', 5565),
  ('manali', 32, 'travel-agent-insights-manali', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS — MANALI', 'What an experienced planner does differently', NULL, '', 5566),
  ('manali', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'IF:', NULL, '**trip_length <= 1 night**', 5567),
  ('manali', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'THEN:', NULL, 'prefer Hadimba Devi Temple + Dhungri Forest + Mall Road + one short Beas River or Old Manali experience. Reason: A one-night Manali stay works best as a compact local experience. Hadimba Temple, Dhungri Forest, Mall Road, Old Manali cafés, and a short riverside walk provide a clear introduction without adding a tiring Solang Valley or Atal Tunnel excursion.', 5568),
  ('manali', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'IF:', NULL, '**trip_length == 2 nights**', 5569),
  ('manali', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'THEN:', NULL, 'schedule one local culture-and-market day AND: schedule one scenic excursion such as Solang Valley, Vashisht, or Naggar. Reason: Two nights are enough for central Manali plus one major excursion, but not for comfortably combining Solang Valley, Atal Tunnel, Sissu, Rohtang-area viewpoints, Naggar, Kullu, and Kasol.', 5570),
  ('manali', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'IF:', NULL, '**trip_length >= 3 nights**', 5571),
  ('manali', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'THEN:', NULL, 'include one central sightseeing cluster AND: include one scenic mountain excursion AND: include one relaxed or flexible half-day. Reason: Three nights are the practical sweet spot for balancing temples, forests, cafés, markets, mountain scenery, and unhurried Manali time.', 5572),
  ('manali', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'IF:', NULL, '**trip_length <= 3 nights**', 5573),
  ('manali', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'THEN:', NULL, 'prefer_one_hotel AND: avoid changing accommodation between Manali, Solang Valley, Naggar, and Kasol. Reason: Short stays lose valuable time through packing, checkout, luggage movement, and mountain transfers. One well-located base is usually more efficient.', 5574),
  ('manali', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'IF:', NULL, '**trip_type == FIRST_TIME_VISITOR**', 5575),
  ('manali', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'THEN:', NULL, 'anchor the itinerary around Hadimba Devi Temple, Old Manali, Mall Road, Solang Valley, Vashisht, and one scenic route towards Atal Tunnel or Naggar. Reason: These experiences provide the clearest introduction to Manali’s temples, forests, cafés, markets, mountain scenery, local culture, and seasonal snow activities.', 5576),
  ('manali', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'IF:', NULL, '**traveler_type == FAMILY** AND: **children_age <= 6**', 5577),
  ('manali', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'THEN:', NULL, 'reduce_walking_intensity_target by 25% AND: limit_major_activities_per_day to 2 AND: increase_downtime by 20% AND: prefer hotels with easy vehicle access, heating, and an in-house restaurant. Reason: Winding roads, cold weather, uneven paths, slopes, stairs, traffic, and altitude can tire young children. Short sightseeing blocks, regular meal breaks, and hotel rest make the trip more comfortable.', 5578),
  ('manali', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'IF:', NULL, '**trip_type == FAMILY**', 5579),
  ('manali', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'THEN:', NULL, 'prefer Hadimba Devi Temple, Dhungri Forest, Van Vihar, Beas River, Old Manali, Solang Valley, Vashisht, and easy viewpoints AND: avoid long treks and multiple mountain excursions on the same day. Reason: Manali suits families best when sightseeing is mixed with gentle forest walks, seasonal snow play, child-friendly activities, regular rest, and flexible travel time.', 5580),
  ('manali', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'IF:', NULL, '**trip_type == HONEYMOON**', 5581),
  ('manali', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'THEN:', NULL, 'increase romance_weight by 30% AND: increase privacy_weight by 25% AND: increase free_time_weight by 25% AND: decrease activity_density by 25%. Reason: Manali’s honeymoon value comes from valley-view stays, private drives, pine forests, snowfall possibilities, café dates, riverside walks, spa time, and romantic dinners rather than maximum attraction coverage.', 5582),
  ('manali', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'IF:', NULL, '**trip_type == HONEYMOON**', 5583),
  ('manali', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'THEN:', NULL, 'prefer Old Manali, Aleo, Prini, Naggar, or a quiet valley-view property AND: schedule no more than 2 major activities per day AND: include one private dinner or scenic sunset experience. Reason: These areas offer greater privacy and slower mountain experiences, while central Manali can be used for one relaxed temple visit, café date, market walk, or riverside experience.', 5584),
  ('manali', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'IF:', NULL, '**traveler_type == LUXURY**', 5585),
  ('manali', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'THEN:', NULL, 'prefer_private_transfer AND: prefer_high_service_valley_view_or_boutique_hotel AND: prefer_curated_excursions AND: increase_service_and_rest_weight. Reason: Luxury value in Manali is created through comfort, privacy, professional chauffeurs, premium rooms, spa services, personalised dining, scenic drives, and flexible pacing—not by adding more roadside stops.', 5586),
  ('manali', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'IF:', NULL, '**traveler_type == LUXURY** AND: **trip_length >= 4 nights**', 5587),
  ('manali', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'THEN:', NULL, 'consider a split stay between central Manali and Naggar / Prini OR: retain one luxury base and add a full-day private excursion. Reason: A longer stay can combine central cafés and local sightseeing with a quieter forest, orchard, heritage, or valley-view atmosphere, provided the hotel change does not create unnecessary travel time.', 5588),
  ('manali', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'IF:', NULL, '**traveler_type == BUDGET**', 5589),
  ('manali', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'THEN:', NULL, 'prefer a value hotel in Vashisht, Simsa, Old Manali, or another area with practical road access AND: use walking for local sightseeing AND: mix free attractions with one or two paid excursions. Reason: Hadimba Temple, Manu Temple, Old Manali lanes, Beas River walks, Van Vihar, monasteries, and local markets provide substantial low-cost sightseeing. Taxis should be reserved for Solang Valley, Atal Tunnel, Naggar, and other spread-out attractions.', 5590),
  ('manali', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'IF:', NULL, 'hotel_is_far_from_central_manali: AND: **hotel_saving < additional_transport_cost + value_of_lost_time**', 5591),
  ('manali', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'THEN:', NULL, 'prefer_central_hotel_or_easy_road_access_hotel. Reason: A cheaper hotel may provide poor overall value if guests must repeatedly pay for taxis or walk steep uphill routes to reach markets, cafés, temples, restaurants, and transport points.', 5592),
  ('manali', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'IF:', NULL, 'hotel_is_in_old_manali_or_vashisht:', 5593),
  ('manali', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'THEN:', NULL, 'verify_vehicle_drop_point AND: verify_luggage_access AND: verify_stairs_and_slope AND: verify_actual_walking_distance. Reason: Some properties are located on narrow, steep, or pedestrian-only lanes. “Near Old Manali” or “near Vashisht” does not always mean that a vehicle can reach the hotel entrance.', 5594),
  ('manali', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'IF:', NULL, '**traveler_type == SENIOR**', 5595),
  ('manali', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'THEN:', NULL, 'prefer Aleo, Prini, Simsa, Shuru, or a hotel with direct road access AND: use private transport AND: avoid long uphill walks, steep village lanes, and stair-heavy sightseeing. Reason: Manali’s attractions may involve slopes, stairs, uneven paths, cold weather, traffic, and winding mountain roads. Hotel accessibility and vehicle access should be checked individually before booking.', 5596),
  ('manali', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'IF:', NULL, '**traveler_type == SENIOR** OR: **mobility_level == LIMITED**', 5597),
  ('manali', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'THEN:', NULL, 'limit_major_activities_per_day to 1–2 AND: schedule outdoor sightseeing during the warmer part of the day AND: include a rest period after every excursion. Reason: Shorter sightseeing blocks reduce fatigue and make it easier to manage altitude, cold weather, traffic, weather changes, and uneven mountain terrain.', 5598),
  ('manali', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'IF:', NULL, '**traveler_interest == HISTORY OR traveler_interest == CULTURE**', 5599);
INSERT INTO destination_guidance (place_id, section, topic, section_title, heading, audience, body, position) VALUES
  ('manali', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'THEN:', NULL, 'combine Hadimba Devi Temple, Manu Temple, Vashisht Temple, Tibetan monasteries, Museum of Himachal Culture and Folk Art, Naggar Castle, and Roerich Art Gallery over adjacent days. Reason: These attractions create a coherent experience of Himachali traditions, religious heritage, Buddhist culture, traditional architecture, regional art, and village life without requiring every site to be visited in one day.', 5600),
  ('manali', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'IF:', NULL, '**traveler_interest == NATURE OR traveler_interest == PHOTOGRAPHY**', 5601),
  ('manali', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'THEN:', NULL, 'prefer Dhungri Forest, Beas River, Solang Valley, Atal Tunnel–Sissu, Naggar, apple orchards, Kothi, and selected forest viewpoints AND: protect early-morning or late-afternoon photography time. Reason: Manali is especially strong for deodar forests, rivers, waterfalls, Himalayan peaks, villages, snow landscapes, orchards, and changing mountain light.', 5602),
  ('manali', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'IF:', NULL, '**traveler_interest == SNOW**', 5603),
  ('manali', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'THEN:', NULL, 'prefer December–February AND: treat snowfall and snow activities as weather-dependent AND: keep road transfers and outdoor plans flexible. Reason: Winter may provide snow around Solang Valley and higher areas, but snowfall timing, intensity, road access, activity availability, and local transport can change quickly.', 5604),
  ('manali', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'IF:', NULL, '**weather == MONSOON**', 5605),
  ('manali', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'THEN:', NULL, 'reduce_outdoor_walking AND: reduce_long_excursions AND: increase_indoor_or_flexible_time AND: keep trekking, rafting, paragliding, waterfalls, and high-altitude routes weather-dependent. Reason: Rain can reduce visibility, make paths slippery, delay road journeys, and increase landslide or cancellation risk. Cafés, monasteries, museums, shopping, hotel dining, spa time, and relaxed riverside stays provide useful alternatives.', 5606),
  ('manali', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'IF:', NULL, '**weather == HEAVY_SNOWFALL**', 5607),
  ('manali', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'THEN:', NULL, 'avoid_tight_itinerary AND: prioritise_nearby_or_walkable_attractions AND: keep_extra_transfer_buffer AND: confirm road and attraction conditions locally. Reason: Snow can create traffic delays, slippery walking conditions, vehicle restrictions, and temporary changes to sightseeing access. Flexibility is more valuable than attempting to preserve every scheduled stop.', 5608),
  ('manali', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'IF:', NULL, '**trip_length >= 4 nights** AND: **traveler_interest == RELAXATION**', 5609),
  ('manali', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'THEN:', NULL, 'add one resort-focused day AND: consider Naggar, Prini, Aleo, Vashisht, or a riverside property AND: include spa, balcony, café, hot-spring, or forest time. Reason: Longer Manali stays are more rewarding when they include quiet mountain experiences, wellness, and recovery time instead of repeating central sightseeing.', 5610),
  ('manali', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'IF:', NULL, '**trip_length >= 5 nights** AND: **traveler_interest == ADVENTURE**', 5611),
  ('manali', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'THEN:', NULL, 'consider Solang Valley, Sethan, Atal Tunnel–Sissu, Kullu, Hampta Valley, or a guided trek AND: reserve separate time for skiing, paragliding, rafting, trekking, mountain biking, camping, or snow activities where seasonally suitable. Reason: Manali offers light activities close to town as well as demanding Himalayan adventures. Outdoor variety increases when nearby mountain areas and separate activity days are included.', 5612),
  ('manali', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'IF:', NULL, '**trip_type == FIRST_TIME_VISITOR** AND: **trip_length <= 2 nights**', 5613),
  ('manali', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'THEN:', NULL, 'do_not_recommend Solang Valley + Atal Tunnel + Sissu + Rohtang-area viewpoints + Naggar in one day. Reason: These places may look close on a map, but mountain roads, traffic, weather, sightseeing time, and activity stops make such a circuit tiring and low quality. Choose one excursion cluster instead.', 5614),
  ('manali', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'IF:', NULL, '**traveler_interest == SHOPPING**', 5615),
  ('manali', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'THEN:', NULL, 'include Mall Road, Manali Market, Manu Market, Tibetan shops, Kullu shawl outlets, and local handicraft stores AND: keep shopping time separate from a long mountain excursion. Reason: Woollens, Kullu shawls, Himachali caps, wooden products, Tibetan items, outdoor clothing, souvenirs, and local food products are best explored without rushing between distant viewpoints.', 5616),
  ('manali', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'IF:', NULL, '**trip_type == ROMANTIC**', 5617),
  ('manali', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'THEN:', NULL, 'schedule a quiet forest walk, café date, mountain-view dinner, and one sunset or snowfall experience. Reason: Manali’s strongest romantic moments come from atmosphere—deodar forests, warm cafés, riverside scenery, mountain views, snowfall, and slow evenings—rather than from covering many attractions.', 5618),
  ('manali', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'IF:', NULL, '**traveler_type == PARTY_TRAVELLER**', 5619),
  ('manali', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'THEN:', NULL, 'set_low_nightlife_expectation AND: prioritise cafés, restaurants, live-music venues, hotel lounges, Old Manali evenings, and relaxed market walks. Reason: Manali offers a casual evening scene with cafés, restaurants, music venues, and hotel lounges, but it is not primarily a large-scale clubbing or late-night entertainment destination.', 5620),
  ('manali', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'IF:', NULL, '**arrival_mode == CHANDIGARH_AIRPORT_OR_RAILWAY_STATION**', 5621),
  ('manali', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'THEN:', NULL, 'allow approximately 8–10 hours for the road transfer AND: prefer a private sedan, SUV, or MPV when comfort and flexibility matter. Reason: The Chandigarh–Manali journey is a long mountain transfer. Rest stops, luggage space, motion comfort, road conditions, and a realistic arrival schedule should be built into the plan.', 5622),
  ('manali', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'IF:', NULL, '**traveler_type == FAMILY OR traveler_type == LUXURY OR traveler_type == HONEYMOON**', 5623),
  ('manali', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'THEN:', NULL, 'prefer_private_transfer_from_chandigarh AND: include comfort stops AND: avoid scheduling major sightseeing immediately after arrival. Reason: A private transfer improves door-to-door convenience, luggage handling, scenic flexibility, and comfort after the long mountain journey.', 5624),
  ('manali', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'IF:', NULL, '**traveler_type == BUDGET** AND: **central_sightseeing_required == true**', 5625),
  ('manali', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'THEN:', NULL, 'use walking and local transport for Mall Road, Manali Market, Old Manali, Hadimba Devi Temple, Manu Temple, Beas River, Van Vihar, and nearby monasteries AND: reserve taxis for Solang Valley, Atal Tunnel, Naggar, Vashisht, and other spread-out locations. Reason: Manali’s central attractions are suitable for walking and short local transfers, while private transport is more valuable for distant mountain excursions.', 5626),
  ('manali', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'IF:', NULL, '**trip_length >= 4 nights**', 5627),
  ('manali', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'THEN:', NULL, 'add one flexible half-day. Reason: A flexible block allows recovery after the Chandigarh transfer, weather adjustments, extra photography, shopping, snowfall time, spa treatment, resort relaxation, or a repeat visit to a favourite café or viewpoint.', 5628),
  ('manali', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'IF:', NULL, '**accessibility_requirement == HIGH**', 5629),
  ('manali', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'THEN:', NULL, 'verify_each_hotel_and_attraction_individually AND: prefer direct vehicle access, lifts, ground-floor rooms, accessible bathrooms, and minimal-step routes AND: avoid assuming that “wheelchair-friendly” labels guarantee full accessibility. Reason: Manali’s accessibility varies significantly by hotel, attraction, entrance, terrain, road surface, weather, and transport arrangement. Destination-level accessibility should never replace property-level verification.', 5630),
  ('manali', 34, 'destination-scoring', 'DESTINATION SCORING', NULL, NULL, '| Factor | Score | | -------------------------- | ----- | | Family | 90 | | Family with young children | 78 | | Honeymoon | 94 | | Romantic | 92 | | Luxury | 84 | | Budget | 84 | | Adventure | 91 | | Culture | 86 | | History | 78 | | Food | 84 | | Shopping | 82 | | Nightlife | 58 | | Relaxation | 91 | | Nature | 95 | | Photography | 96 | | Solo travel | 87 | | Senior travellers | 68 | | First-time visitor | 92 | | Repeat traveller | 90 | | Accessibility | 60 | | Safety | 82 |', 5631),
  ('manali', 35, 'final-travel-agent-verdict-manali', 'FINAL TRAVEL AGENT VERDICT — MANALI', NULL, NULL, '**Manali is a highly recommended 5–6-night Himalayan destination for nature lovers, honeymooners, families, photographers, first-time visitors, and adventure seekers.** It delivers exceptional mountain scenery, forests, snow experiences, cafés, culture, relaxation, and outdoor activities. Plan a relaxed itinerary with **one cultural experience, one scenic excursion, one optional adventure, and sufficient free time**. Best overall verdict: **Excellent destination — 86/100.** Ideal for: Nature, photography, romance, snow, sightseeing, and relaxation. Less suitable for: Nightlife-focused trips, clubbing, and travellers requiring easy step-free accessibility.', 5632),
  ('manali', 36, 'data-quality', 'DATA QUALITY', NULL, NULL, 'information_completeness: 90/100 last_updated: 2026-08-18 last_verified: NOT_LIVE_VERIFIED verified_by: TRAVEL_ENGINE_INITIAL_DATASET sources: IMPORTANT: Prices, opening hours, schedules, visa requirements, availability, accessibility and operational conditions must NOT be treated as permanently valid from this document. These must be sourced from structured, refreshable data.', 5633),
  ('dharamshala', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Spring', NULL, 'months: March-May weather: Pleasant and increasingly warm, with clear mountain views and comfortable sightseeing conditions. crowd_level: MEDIUM → HIGH price_level: MEDIUM → HIGH overall_score: 84-88 recommended: true reason: A strong shoulder season for Dharamshala, especially for monastery visits, viewpoints, photography, and relaxed outdoor time before the heaviest summer heat arrives.', 5634),
  ('dharamshala', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Summer', NULL, 'months: June-August weather: Warm to humid with monsoon influence; frequent rain, mist, and overcast skies. crowd_level: MEDIUM price_level: LOW → MEDIUM overall_score: 70-78 recommended: true reason: Good for travelers who want lower prices and greener scenery, but rain can reduce visibility and make outdoor plans less reliable.', 5635),
  ('dharamshala', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Autumn', NULL, 'months: September-November weather: Clear, pleasant, and generally one of the best times for mountain views and walking. crowd_level: LOW → MEDIUM price_level: MEDIUM overall_score: 90-94 recommended: true reason: One of the best all-around periods for Dharamshala, with excellent weather, strong photography conditions, and comfortable sightseeing.', 5636),
  ('dharamshala', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Winter', NULL, 'months: December-February weather: Cool to cold, dry, and crisp; higher areas can feel quite chilly. crowd_level: MEDIUM → HIGH price_level: HIGH overall_score: 82-87 recommended: true reason: Very good for a quiet hill-station feel, especially for cozy stays and clear views, though nights can be cold and peak holiday periods get busier. Dharamshala is best sold as an autumn and spring destination, with summer as a value season and winter as a cooler, quieter option.', 5637),
  ('dharamshala', 10, 'budget-strategy', 'BUDGET STRATEGY', NULL, NULL, 'Travel-agent rule: Dharamshala is best positioned as a good-value mountain destination, not an ultra-cheap one and not an expensive one. It offers strong experience quality for the money, especially when the trip is built around monasteries, viewpoints, food, and relaxed exploration.', 5638),
  ('dharamshala', 12, 'airport-transfer-logic', 'AIRPORT TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Family', 'family', 'Airport taxi or pre-booked private MPV/van; door-to-door, luggage-friendly, and easiest after arrival.', 5639),
  ('dharamshala', 12, 'airport-transfer-logic', 'AIRPORT TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Honeymoon', 'honeymoon', 'Pre-booked private car or SUV; best for privacy, comfort, and a smooth first impression. reason: The first impression of the trip matters and private transfer provides comfort and privacy.', 5640),
  ('dharamshala', 12, 'airport-transfer-logic', 'AIRPORT TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Luxury', 'luxury', 'Chauffeured sedan or luxury SUV; ideal for premium stays, added comfort, and seamless service.', 5641),
  ('dharamshala', 12, 'airport-transfer-logic', 'AIRPORT TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Budget', 'budget', 'Prepaid taxi from Kangra/Gaggal Airport to the town, then local transport if needed; best value for cost-conscious travelers.', 5642),
  ('dharamshala', 18, 'family-travel', 'FAMILY TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'child_friendly_score: 84 best_ages: Rules: For young children: Prefer: Avoid:', 5643),
  ('dharamshala', 19, 'honeymoon-travel', 'HONEYMOON TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'honeymoon_score: 96 romance_score: 98 privacy_score: 90 luxury_score: 95 Recommended: Honeymoon itinerary should NOT contain more than: 2 major activities/day. Prefer: One memorable experience + free time over: Three or four attractions. Recommended hotel areas: Dharamkot works best for romance and quiet atmosphere, while Naddi is better for privacy and mountain views.', 5644),
  ('dharamshala', 20, 'luxury-travel', 'LUXURY TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'luxury_score: 97 Recommended: Luxury travelers should not be given an itinerary that simply contains more activities. Luxury should primarily increase: Recommended hotel areas: Dharamkot works best for quiet romance and privacy, while Naddi is better for wider mountain views and a calmer premium feel.', 5645),
  ('dharamshala', 21, 'adventure', 'ADVENTURE', NULL, NULL, 'adventure_score: 72 Dharamshala is not a high-adrenaline adventure destination, but it is strong for **soft adventure** and scenic outdoor activities. The best fit is trekking, short nature walks, village exploration, and view-based outings rather than extreme sports. Adventure-like experiences should be interpreted as: Recommended adventure-style areas: Best for:', 5646),
  ('dharamshala', 22, 'senior-travel', 'SENIOR TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'senior_suitability: 78 walking_intensity: MEDIUM_HIGH unless Rules: Recommended hotel areas:', 5647),
  ('dharamshala', 23, 'accessibility', 'ACCESSIBILITY', NULL, NULL, 'wheelchair_accessibility: PARTIAL_TO_GOOD depending on attraction and transport public_transport_accessibility: VARIABLE hotel_accessibility: MUST_BE_VERIFIED_PER_HOTEL attraction_accessibility: MUST_BE_VERIFIED_PER_ATTRACTION Rule: Never infer accessibility from destination-level accessibility. Each hotel and attraction must carry its own accessibility data.', 5648),
  ('dharamshala', 24, 'food', 'FOOD', NULL, NULL, 'Dharamshala is particularly strong for: Food experiences: Family: Prioritize clean, convenient restaurants with familiar and flexible menus. Honeymoon: At least one memorable dinner, sunset café meal, or quiet mountain-view meal is recommended. Luxury: Focus on premium cafés, refined multi-course dining, and private or scenic dinner settings. Budget: Mix local Tibetan eateries, casual restaurants, and a few selected paid dining experiences.', 5649),
  ('dharamshala', 25, 'shopping', 'SHOPPING', NULL, NULL, 'Dharamshala is particularly strong for: Shopping experiences: Luxury shopping: Dharamshala is not a premium-mall destination, so luxury shopping is limited. For higher-end purchases, focus on curated handicraft boutiques, better-quality Tibetan art pieces, and select specialty stores rather than expecting large designer retail. Prefer:', 5650),
  ('dharamshala', 26, 'nightlife', 'NIGHTLIFE', NULL, NULL, 'nightlife_level: 58 Suitable for: Not a primary requirement for: Honeymoon travelers should generally prefer: romantic evening over: late-night club itinerary unless nightlife is explicitly requested.', 5651),
  ('dharamshala', 28, 'sample-itinerary-patterns', 'SAMPLE ITINERARY PATTERNS', '3 NIGHTS', NULL, 'Day 1 Arrival → Hotel → McLeod Ganj light exploration → Dinner Day 2 Morning: McLeod Ganj core Afternoon: Bhagsu / Bhagsunag Evening: Sunset at Naddi or a relaxed café dinner Day 3 Morning: One major attraction Afternoon: One relaxed activity or café stop Evening: Free time / romantic dinner Day 4 Breakfast → Airport transfer → Departure', 5652),
  ('dharamshala', 29, 'eight-night-nine-day-honeymoon-pattern', 'EIGHT-NIGHT NINE-DAY HONEYMOON PATTERN', NULL, NULL, 'Day 1 Arrival → Hotel → Light McLeod Ganj evening exploration → Dinner → Overnight stay in Dharamshala Day 2 Morning: McLeod Ganj core Afternoon: Bhagsu / Bhagsunag Evening: Sunset at Naddi or a relaxed café dinner → Overnight stay in Dharamshala Day 3 Morning: Dharamkot slow walk or monastery visit Afternoon: One scenic viewpoint or quiet café stop Evening: Free time / romantic dinner → Overnight stay in Dharamshala Day 4 Morning: One major attraction Afternoon: One relaxed activity or local market time Evening: Leisure time at hotel → Overnight stay in Dharamshala Day 5 Morning: Breakfast → Check out → Transfer to a nearby Himachal add-on destination or scenic halt Afternoon: Leisure sightseeing / rest Evening: Dinner → Overnight stay Day 6 Morning: Slow sightseeing Afternoon: Nature or culture stop Evening: Romantic dinner → Overnight stay Day 7 Morning: Short excursion or viewpoint visit Afternoon: Free time Evening: Private dinner or quiet evening walk → Overnight stay Day 8 Morning: Relaxed breakfast Afternoon: Shopping, café time, or spa/wellness time Evening: Farewell dinner → Overnight stay Day 9 Breakfast → Airport transfer → Departure', 5653),
  ('dharamshala', 30, 'eight-night-nine-day-family-itinerary', 'EIGHT-NIGHT NINE-DAY FAMILY ITINERARY', 'Day 1', NULL, 'Arrival → Pick up from airport / station → Transfer to Dharamshala → Check in hotel → Light evening at McLeod Ganj → Dinner at hotel or nearby café → Overnight stay in Dharamshala', 5654),
  ('dharamshala', 30, 'eight-night-nine-day-family-itinerary', 'EIGHT-NIGHT NINE-DAY FAMILY ITINERARY', 'Day 2', NULL, 'Morning: McLeod Ganj core Dalai Lama Temple Complex Namgyal Monastery Tibetan Museum Afternoon: McLeod Ganj market Relaxed lunch Short café break Evening: Sunset at Naddi Return to hotel Dinner Overnight stay in Dharamshala', 5655),
  ('dharamshala', 30, 'eight-night-nine-day-family-itinerary', 'EIGHT-NIGHT NINE-DAY FAMILY ITINERARY', 'Day 3', NULL, 'Morning: Bhagsu / Bhagsunag Bhagsu Waterfall Bhagsunag Temple Afternoon: Dharamkot slow walk Café stop Leisure time Evening: Free time with family Dinner Overnight stay in Dharamshala', 5656),
  ('dharamshala', 30, 'eight-night-nine-day-family-itinerary', 'EIGHT-NIGHT NINE-DAY FAMILY ITINERARY', 'Day 4', NULL, 'Morning: St. John in the Wilderness Church Library of Tibetan Works and Archives Afternoon: HPCA Cricket Stadium War Memorial Light local sightseeing Evening: Return to hotel Dinner Overnight stay in Dharamshala', 5657),
  ('dharamshala', 30, 'eight-night-nine-day-family-itinerary', 'EIGHT-NIGHT NINE-DAY FAMILY ITINERARY', 'Day 5', NULL, 'Morning: Breakfast → Scenic transfer day → Naddi / Dal Lake side exploration Afternoon: Relaxed viewpoints Short nature stops Family photo time Evening: Back to hotel Dinner Overnight stay in Dharamshala', 5658),
  ('dharamshala', 30, 'eight-night-nine-day-family-itinerary', 'EIGHT-NIGHT NINE-DAY FAMILY ITINERARY', 'Day 6', NULL, 'Morning: Kangra Valley side excursion Kangra Fort or nearby heritage stop Afternoon: Scenic drive back Lunch en route Rest at hotel Evening: Free time Dinner Overnight stay in Dharamshala', 5659),
  ('dharamshala', 30, 'eight-night-nine-day-family-itinerary', 'EIGHT-NIGHT NINE-DAY FAMILY ITINERARY', 'Day 7', NULL, 'Morning: Slow breakfast Optional revisit to favorite spot Afternoon: Shopping in McLeod Ganj Tibetan handicrafts Souvenirs Tea / snack break Evening: Leisure evening Family dinner Overnight stay in Dharamshala', 5660),
  ('dharamshala', 30, 'eight-night-nine-day-family-itinerary', 'EIGHT-NIGHT NINE-DAY FAMILY ITINERARY', 'Day 8', NULL, 'Morning: Relaxed outing One last attraction or viewpoint Afternoon: Pack and rest Family downtime Evening: Farewell dinner Overnight stay in Dharamshala', 5661),
  ('dharamshala', 30, 'eight-night-nine-day-family-itinerary', 'EIGHT-NIGHT NINE-DAY FAMILY ITINERARY', 'Day 9', NULL, 'Breakfast → Check out → Airport / station transfer → Departure', 5662),
  ('dharamshala', 31, 'eight-night-nine-day-luxury-pattern', 'EIGHT-NIGHT NINE-DAY LUXURY PATTERN', NULL, NULL, 'Day 1 Arrival → Pick up from airport → Transfer to Dharamshala luxury hotel → Check in → Relaxed evening tea / spa time → Dinner at hotel → Overnight stay in Dharamshala Day 2 Morning: McLeod Ganj core Afternoon: Bhagsu / Bhagsunag Evening: Sunset at Naddi or a premium café dinner → Overnight stay in Dharamshala Day 3 Morning: Dharamkot slow walk or monastery visit Afternoon: One scenic viewpoint or quiet café stop Evening: Free time / romantic dinner → Overnight stay in Dharamshala Day 4 Morning: One major attraction Afternoon: One relaxed activity or local market time Evening: Leisure time at hotel → Overnight stay in Dharamshala Day 5 Morning: Breakfast → Check out → Transfer to a nearby Himachal add-on destination or scenic halt Afternoon: Leisure sightseeing / rest Evening: Premium dinner → Overnight stay Day 6 Morning: Slow sightseeing Afternoon: Nature or culture stop Evening: Romantic dinner → Overnight stay Day 7 Morning: Short excursion or viewpoint visit Afternoon: Free time Evening: Private dinner or quiet evening walk → Overnight stay Day 8 Morning: Relaxed breakfast Afternoon: Shopping, café time, or spa / wellness time Evening: Farewell dinner → Overnight stay Day 9 Breakfast → Airport transfer → Departure', 5663),
  ('dharamshala', 32, 'travel-agent-insights', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS', 'What inexperienced planners often do wrong', NULL, '', 5664),
  ('dharamshala', 32, 'travel-agent-insights', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS', 'What an experienced planner does differently', NULL, '', 5665),
  ('dharamshala', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', NULL, NULL, 'IF: trip_length <= 3 nights THEN: do not recommend Triund trek or a Kangra Valley day trip by default. Reason: Short Dharamshala stays work best when time is concentrated around McLeod Ganj, Bhagsu, and Naddi rather than spread across distant or time-heavy add-ons. IF: trip_type == HONEYMOON THEN: increase romance_weight by 30% increase privacy_weight by 20% increase free_time_weight by 20% decrease activity_density by 20% Reason: Dharamshala honeymoon value comes from atmosphere, mountain views, quiet stays, and slow pacing rather than maximum sightseeing. IF: traveler_type == FAMILY AND: children_age <= 6 THEN: reduce walking_intensity_target by 20% increase downtime by 20% prefer short transfers and predictable meal breaks Reason: Young children handle Dharamshala better with compact sightseeing blocks and fewer long walks on hilly roads. IF: hotel_is_far_from_mcleod_ganj_and_core_areas AND: hotel_saving < additional_transport_cost + value_of_lost_time THEN: prefer_central_hotel Reason: A cheaper hotel outside the main visitor zone often creates worse overall trip value in Dharamshala. IF: trip_length <= 3 nights THEN: prefer_one_hotel Reason: Hotel changes consume valuable time on a short Dharamshala trip. IF: trip_length >= 5 nights AND: traveler_interest == RELAXATION THEN: consider_naddi_or_quieter_village_add_on Reason: Longer stays make a slower scenic extension more practical and more rewarding. IF: traveler_type == LUXURY THEN: prefer_private_transfer AND: prefer_high_service_hotel AND: prefer_exclusive_or_private_experiences Reason: Luxury value in Dharamshala is created through comfort, privacy, and service rather than through more sightseeing stops. IF: traveler_type == BUDGET THEN: prefer_public_transport_or_walkable_base AND: prefer_high_value_hotel_location AND: mix_free_and_paid_attractions Reason: Dharamshala offers strong value when the itinerary uses compact hill zones, local food, and fewer paid transfers. IF: trip_type == FIRST_TIME_VISITOR THEN: anchor the trip around McLeod Ganj AND: add Bhagsu / Bhagsunag AND: include one mountain-view or sunset experience Reason: These three elements give the clearest first impression of Dharamshala’s culture, scenery, and atmosphere. IF: trip_type == FAMILY THEN: limit_major_activities_per_day to 2 AND: include one leisure block daily Reason: Dharamshala family trips work best when the pace stays relaxed and manageable. IF: trip_type == HONEYMOON THEN: schedule premium dinner or sunset viewpoint in the evening Reason: Dharamshala is strongest at sunset, on the hillside, and during quiet evening experiences. IF: weather == MONSOON THEN: reduce outdoor_walking AND: increase indoor_culture_or_food_time Reason: Rain and mist make a slower, more flexible Dharamshala plan perform better. IF: traveler_interest == HISTORY OR traveler_interest == CULTURE THEN: combine McLeod Ganj and the monastery / museum cluster on the same day Reason: These areas cluster well and create a more coherent heritage experience. IF: traveler_type == SENIOR THEN: prefer_central_hotel AND: use_taxi_or_private_transfer_when_helpful AND: avoid_multiple_walking_heavy_stops Reason: Dharamshala’s hill areas are rewarding, but they are easier when movement and walking are controlled. IF: trip_length >= 4 nights THEN: add one flexible half-day Reason: Dharamshala benefits from breathing room, especially for cafés, shopping, spa time, or weather adjustments.', 5666),
  ('dharamshala', 34, 'destination-scoring', 'DESTINATION SCORING', NULL, NULL, '| Factor | Score | | ------------------ | ----- | | Family | 88 | | Honeymoon | 91 | | Luxury | 88 | | Budget | 91 | | Adventure | 72 | | Culture | 97 | | Food | 82 | | Shopping | 75 | | Nightlife | 58 | | Relaxation | 95 | | Nature | 96 | | Accessibility | 76 | | Safety | 82 | | First-time visitor | 90 | | Photography | 97 |', 5667),
  ('dharamshala', 35, 'final-travel-agent-verdict', 'FINAL TRAVEL AGENT VERDICT', NULL, NULL, 'Best traveler profiles: 1. Honeymoon 2. Romantic couple 3. Culture/first-time visitor 4. Luxury traveler 5. Food traveler 6. Family with appropriate pacing Best duration: 4–5 nights Best season: September–February Best hotel strategy: Central or highly connected location, ideally McLeod Ganj for atmosphere or Naddi / Dharamkot for privacy and premium stays. Best transportation: Taxi, private transfers, and short local drives depending on trip style. Private transfer for: Must-do for first-time visitor: Don''t-do: Biggest advantage: Extremely high concentration of culture, nature, food, romance, photography, and relaxed mountain experiences in a compact hill destination. Biggest disadvantage: Walking friction in hilly areas, seasonal weather changes, and crowd pressure in peak months. Overall destination score: 94/100', 5668),
  ('dharamshala', 36, 'data-quality', 'DATA QUALITY', NULL, NULL, 'information_completeness: 94/100 last_updated: 2026-08-18 last_verified: NOT_LIVE_VERIFIED verified_by: TRAVEL_ENGINE_INITIAL_DATASET sources: IMPORTANT: Prices, opening hours, schedules, visa requirements, availability, accessibility and operational conditions must NOT be treated as permanently valid from this document. These must be sourced from structured, refreshable data.', 5669),
  ('mcleod-ganj', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Summer', NULL, 'months: March–June weather: Pleasantly cool to mild mountain weather with sunny, clear skies and crisp air. Temperatures range from 15°C to 28°C. March retains a late-winter chill at higher elevations like Triund, while April to June provides optimal conditions for sightseeing, café hopping, and Himalayan trekking. crowd_level: HIGH → VERY HIGH price_level: HIGH → VERY HIGH overall_score: 82–88 recommended: true reason: Peak season for first-time visitors, families, backpackers, and trekkers escaping the Indian plains'' heat. Ideal for visiting the Tsuglagkhang Complex, trekking to Triund, and exploring Dharamkot cafés. Expect heavy traffic on narrow mountain roads, packed markets, and premium hotel rates, especially on May–June weekends.', 5670),
  ('mcleod-ganj', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Monsoon', NULL, 'months: July–September weather: Heavy downpours, high humidity, misty pine forests, and dramatic cloudscapes over the Kangra Valley. McLeod Ganj receives some of the highest rainfall in Himachal Pradesh during July and August, easing gradually in mid-to-late September. crowd_level: LOW → MEDIUM price_level: LOW → MEDIUM overall_score: 55–68 recommended: false reason: Best suited for long-term budget stays, yoga and meditation practitioners, and artists who enjoy quiet, rain-washed landscapes. Heavy rainfall leads to high landslide risks, slippery mountain paths, leach activity, and temporary bans on trekking trails like Triund and Indrahar Pass.', 5671),
  ('mcleod-ganj', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Autumn (Post-Monsoon)', NULL, 'months: October–November weather: Mostly dry, exceptionally clear skies, crisp mountain air, and crystal-clear panoramas of the snow-dusted Dhauladhar Range. Day temperatures range between 10°C and 22°C, with nights becoming increasingly cold. crowd_level: MEDIUM price_level: MEDIUM overall_score: 90–95 recommended: true reason: The prime season for trekkers, photographers, and culture seekers. Perfect weather for the Triund Trek, monastic visits, and café dates without the overwhelming summer rush. Moderate accommodation pricing and pleasant daytime weather offer the best balance across all traveler profiles.', 5672),
  ('mcleod-ganj', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Winter', NULL, 'months: December–February weather: Cold to freezing, with temperatures dropping between -2°C and 12°C. Snowfall typically occurs in late December, January, and February at upper elevations, blanketing McLeod Ganj, Naddi, and Dharamkot in scenic winter landscapes. crowd_level: MEDIUM → HIGH price_level: MEDIUM → HIGH overall_score: 78–84 recommended: true reason: Ideal for snow seekers, couples, and winter photographers looking for cozy fireplace stays and snow-covered pine vistas. Christmas and New Year bring a surge of domestic tourists, causing brief price hikes and road congestion, though mid-January to February remains relatively tranquil.', 5673),
  ('mcleod-ganj', 10, 'budget-strategy', 'BUDGET STRATEGY', NULL, NULL, '', 5674),
  ('mcleod-ganj', 12, 'airport-transfer-logic', 'AIRPORT TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Family', 'family', 'Pre-booked private **sedan / MPV / Innova-type vehicle** from Kangra Airport; best for luggage, children, elderly members and direct hotel drop-off.', 5675),
  ('mcleod-ganj', 12, 'airport-transfer-logic', 'AIRPORT TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Honeymoon', 'honeymoon', 'Pre-booked private sedan or comfortable SUV from Kangra Airport; ideal for privacy, scenic stops and direct transfer to a boutique or valley-view property. reason: McLeod Ganj involves steep hill roads and narrow local streets. A private transfer avoids unnecessary changes and makes luggage handling considerably easier.', 5676),
  ('mcleod-ganj', 12, 'airport-transfer-logic', 'AIRPORT TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Luxury', 'luxury', 'Premium SUV / Innova Crysta / chauffeur-driven vehicle from Kangra Airport with luggage assistance and direct hotel transfer.', 5677),
  ('mcleod-ganj', 12, 'airport-transfer-logic', 'AIRPORT TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Budget', 'budget', 'Shared taxi, public transport or locally arranged taxi from Kangra Airport to Dharamshala/McLeod Ganj. Confirm the total fare before departure, particularly for private airport transfers.', 5678),
  ('mcleod-ganj', 18, 'family-travel', 'FAMILY TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'child_friendly_score: 82 best_ages: Rules: Prefer: Avoid:', 5679),
  ('mcleod-ganj', 19, 'honeymoon-travel', 'HONEYMOON TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'honeymoon_score: 91 romance_score: 93 privacy_score: 80 luxury_score: 78 Recommended: **Honeymoon itinerary should NOT contain more than:** Prefer: over: Recommended honeymoon experiences:', 5680),
  ('mcleod-ganj', 20, 'luxury-travel', 'LUXURY TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'luxury_score: 78 Recommended: Luxury should primarily increase: Recommended hotel areas:', 5681),
  ('mcleod-ganj', 21, 'adventure', 'ADVENTURE', NULL, NULL, 'adventure_score: 89 McLeod Ganj is particularly strong for **trekking, hiking, camping, mountain photography and paragliding excursions**, rather than motorised adventure tourism. Triund is the signature experience, while Bir–Billing adds a major paragliding option. **Adventure-like experiences should be interpreted as:** Recommended adventure-style areas:', 5682),
  ('mcleod-ganj', 22, 'senior-travel', 'SENIOR TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'senior_suitability: 74 walking_intensity: MEDIUM Rules: Recommended hotel areas: Naddi: – best for quiet scenery and slower travel. McLeod Ganj central: – convenient for monasteries, restaurants and shops, but verify slope and vehicle access. Jogiwara Road: – useful balance of cafés and relatively convenient sightseeing. Lower Dharamshala: – practical for road access and local transport. Norbulingka surroundings: – peaceful option for travelers prioritising gardens and culture. Avoid as primary base: Dharamkot / upper Bhagsu: when mobility is limited because steep lanes and uneven paths can become tiring.', 5683),
  ('mcleod-ganj', 23, 'accessibility', 'ACCESSIBILITY', NULL, NULL, 'wheelchair_accessibility: PARTIAL public_transport_accessibility: VARIABLE hotel_accessibility: MUST_BE_VERIFIED_PER_HOTEL attraction_accessibility: MUST_BE_VERIFIED_PER_ATTRACTION Rule: Never infer accessibility from destination-level accessibility. McLeod Ganj''s hills, stairs, narrow lanes and uneven paths make accessibility highly property- and attraction-specific. Main roads and selected newer facilities can be easier, but Bhagsu, Dharamkot and trekking areas are considerably more challenging.', 5684),
  ('mcleod-ganj', 24, 'food', 'FOOD', NULL, NULL, 'McLeod Ganj is particularly strong for: Food experiences: Family: Choose restaurants with indoor seating, clean washrooms and flexible menus. Momos, noodles, rice, dal, parathas, pasta, pizza and soups are easy family choices. Honeymoon: Choose a mountain-view café breakfast, sunset coffee at Naddi and one private or premium dinner. Luxury: Focus on boutique-hotel dining, curated Tibetan/Himachali menus, private dining, mountain views and personalised service rather than expecting a large fine-dining ecosystem. Budget: Local Tibetan restaurants and simple cafés offer particularly good value. A 2026 budget guide estimates approximately ₹400–600/day for food when relying on local cafés and Tibetan meals.', 5685),
  ('mcleod-ganj', 25, 'shopping', 'SHOPPING', NULL, NULL, 'Strong categories: Luxury shopping: McLeod Ganj is **not a major luxury-shopping destination**. Its strength is authentic Tibetan and Himalayan handicrafts, spiritual products, handmade textiles and cultural souvenirs rather than international luxury brands.', 5686),
  ('mcleod-ganj', 26, 'nightlife', 'NIGHTLIFE', NULL, NULL, 'nightlife_level: 55–60 McLeod Ganj has a **relaxed café-and-social nightlife** rather than a major clubbing scene. Evening activity centres around cafés, bakeries, live music, restaurants, backpacker spaces and occasional cultural performances. Cafés are a major part of the destination''s identity. Suitable for: Not a primary requirement for:', 5687),
  ('mcleod-ganj', 28, 'sample-itinerary-patterns', 'SAMPLE ITINERARY PATTERNS', NULL, NULL, 'Night 1 Arrive at Chandigarh Airport → Private transfer to Manali → Scenic drive through the Kullu Valley → Hotel check-in → Rest and acclimatise → Evening walk around Mall Road and Manali Market → Café or bakery stop → Dinner. Night 2 Morning: Hadimba Devi Temple → Dhungri Forest → Museum of Himachal Culture and Folk Art. Afternoon: Manu Temple → Old Manali lanes → Local lunch at a café or Tibetan restaurant → Hotel rest. Evening: Beas River walk → Café time or relaxed photography around Old Manali → Dinner. Night 3 Morning: Excursion to Solang Valley → Snow play / skiing / snowboarding / zorbing / paragliding / ropeway experience, depending on season and weather. Afternoon: Continue towards Atal Tunnel and Sissu, subject to road access and local conditions → Scenic mountain viewpoints and waterfall stops → Packed lunch or local lunch. Evening: Return to Manali → Rest at hotel → Warm Himachali or Tibetan dinner. Night 4 Morning: Vashisht Temple → Natural hot springs → Village lanes and mountain viewpoints. Afternoon: Jogini Waterfall walk, depending on walking comfort and weather → Lunch at Vashisht → Hotel rest. Evening: Relaxed riverside walk or quiet café time → Optional spa or wellness treatment → Dinner. Night 5 Option 1 (heritage and culture): Naggar Castle → Naggar Village → Roerich Art Gallery → Traditional Himachali lunch → Temple or orchard surroundings → Evening return to Manali. Option 2 (nature and relaxation): Kullu Valley drive → Riverside scenery → Kullu shawl shopping → Apple orchards and village photography → Relaxed lunch → Return to Manali. Dinner and relaxed hotel evening. Flexible day: Sethan Village for seasonal snow experiences, Kothi Village and mountain viewpoints, Van Vihar and Beas River walks, or a relaxed local Manali day. Afternoon: Leisure time for shopping, photography, café visits, spa treatment, local handicraft shopping, or hotel balcony time. Evening: Special Himachali dinner or romantic mountain-view dinner → Overnight in Manali. Breakfast → Checkout → Departure transfer from Manali to Chandigarh Airport / Railway Station.', 5688),
  ('mcleod-ganj', 29, 'six-night-seven-day-honeymoon-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHT / SEVEN-DAY HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Night 1', NULL, 'Morning pickup from Chandigarh Railway Station or Chandigarh Airport → Scenic private transfer to Shimla through Himalayan valleys and mountain roads → Check-in at a romantic valley-view hotel → Rest and acclimatise. Late afternoon: Visit Jakhoo Hanuman Temple by private vehicle or lift → Continue to The Ridge, Shimla Kali Bari Temple, Wax Museum, Christ Church, Rani Jhansi Park, Scandal Point, Lakkar Bazaar, and The Mall by walk, subject to time and walking comfort. Evening: Couple walk around The Mall → Café or bakery stop → Romantic dinner at the hotel. **Overnight in Shimla.**', 5689),
  ('mcleod-ganj', 29, 'six-night-seven-day-honeymoon-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHT / SEVEN-DAY HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Night 2', NULL, 'After breakfast, proceed for a private sightseeing excursion to Green Valley, Kufri, Fagu, Himalayan Adventure Park, and Chail. Optional: Horse riding or seasonal snow activities at Kufri, at an additional cost and subject to weather and local conditions. Enjoy scenic photography, forest views, and relaxed couple time around Fagu or Chail. Avoid packing too many activities into the day; select one main activity in addition to the scenic drive. Return to Shimla by late afternoon or evening → Free time for balcony relaxation, spa treatment, or a quiet café visit → Special dinner. **Overnight in Shimla.**', 5690),
  ('mcleod-ganj', 29, 'six-night-seven-day-honeymoon-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHT / SEVEN-DAY HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Night 3', NULL, 'After breakfast, check out from the Shimla hotel and begin the private transfer to Manali. Enjoy the scenic mountain journey through valleys, forests, and riverside landscapes. En-route, stop at suitable viewpoints and Pandoh Dam, subject to road conditions and available time. Continue towards Manali → Check-in at the hotel → Rest after the long journey. Evening: Relaxed dinner at the hotel or a short couple walk near the property, depending on arrival time. **Overnight in Manali.**', 5691),
  ('mcleod-ganj', 29, 'six-night-seven-day-honeymoon-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHT / SEVEN-DAY HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Night 4', NULL, 'After breakfast, visit Hadimba Devi Temple and the nearby Ghatotkach Temple amid cedar forests. Continue to the Beas River, Vashisht Temple and Vashisht Kund, Manu Temple, Manali Clubhouse, Van Vihar, Himalayan Nyinmapa Tibetan Buddhist Monastery, and Manali Mall, selecting the attractions according to available time and walking comfort. Return to the hotel by late afternoon or evening → Rest and enjoy private balcony time. Evening: Café date or relaxed walk at Manali Mall → Dinner at the hotel. **Overnight in Manali.**', 5692),
  ('mcleod-ganj', 29, 'six-night-seven-day-honeymoon-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHT / SEVEN-DAY HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Night 5', NULL, 'After breakfast, proceed by private vehicle to Solang Valley. Enjoy mountain scenery, snow views, and optional activities such as snow play, cable-car rides, or other seasonal adventure activities, at an additional cost and subject to weather and operational conditions. Continue towards Atal Tunnel, Sissu Village, and Sissu Lake if the road, weather, and local regulations permit. Keep the excursion flexible during winter or adverse weather. Return to Manali by late afternoon → Rest at the hotel. Evening: Spend quiet couple time at Manali Mall, enjoy a warm café meal, or arrange a private dinner at the hotel. **Overnight in Manali.**', 5693),
  ('mcleod-ganj', 29, 'six-night-seven-day-honeymoon-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHT / SEVEN-DAY HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Night 6', NULL, 'After breakfast, check out from the Manali hotel and proceed towards Kasol. En-route, stop at suitable viewpoints around Pandoh Dam, Sundar Nagar Lake, the rafting point, and Bhuntar, depending on the route and available time. Continue through the Parvati Valley to Kasol → Visit Manikaran Sahib Gurudwara and Manikaran Hot Springs. Since this is a long road journey, avoid adding too many stops. Check in to the Kasol hotel or resort by late afternoon or evening → Rest and enjoy the peaceful valley setting. Evening: Quiet riverside or balcony time, followed by a relaxed dinner. **Overnight in Kasol.**', 5694),
  ('mcleod-ganj', 29, 'six-night-seven-day-honeymoon-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHT / SEVEN-DAY HONEYMOON PATTERN', 'Night 7', NULL, 'After breakfast, check out from the Kasol hotel. Private transfer towards Chandigarh or Kalka Railway Station, depending on the departure arrangement. Because the journey from Kasol to the plains is long, keep the departure schedule comfortable and avoid booking an early train or flight. Depart with beautiful memories of Shimla’s colonial charm, Kufri’s mountain scenery, Manali’s valleys, Solang’s snow experiences, and Kasol’s peaceful riverside atmosphere.', 5695),
  ('mcleod-ganj', 30, 'six-night-seven-day-family-itinerary', 'SIX-NIGHT / SEVEN-DAY FAMILY ITINERARY', 'Night 1', NULL, 'Pick up from Chandigarh Railway Station / Chandigarh Airport in the morning and transfer to Shimla by private vehicle. Enjoy the scenic valleys and mountain roads en route. Check in to the Shimla hotel and take some rest. In the late afternoon, proceed for local sightseeing: Jakhoo Hanuman Temple, The Ridge, Shimla Kali Bari Temple, Wax Museum, Christ Church, Rani Jhansi Park, Scandal Point, Lakkar Bazaar, and The Mall by walk. Return to the hotel by evening → Dinner at the hotel → Overnight stay in Shimla.', 5696),
  ('mcleod-ganj', 30, 'six-night-seven-day-family-itinerary', 'SIX-NIGHT / SEVEN-DAY FAMILY ITINERARY', 'Night 2', NULL, 'After breakfast, proceed for a family excursion to Kufri, Fagu, Himalayan Nature Park, Himalayan Adventure Park, and Chail. At Kufri, enjoy the mountain scenery and optional horse riding or seasonal snow activities at an additional cost. Families may also enjoy the adventure park, subject to age, weather, and operating conditions. Continue towards Fagu for scenic views and photography, followed by Chail forest surroundings and optional Chail Palace visit. Return to Shimla by late afternoon / evening → Evening free for leisure → Dinner at the hotel → Overnight stay in Shimla.', 5697),
  ('mcleod-ganj', 30, 'six-night-seven-day-family-itinerary', 'SIX-NIGHT / SEVEN-DAY FAMILY ITINERARY', 'Night 3', NULL, 'After breakfast, check out from the Shimla hotel and drive towards Manali through the scenic valleys of Himachal Pradesh. En route, enjoy views of Sundernagar, Mandi, Pandoh Dam, Hanogi Mata Temple, and the Kullu Valley. Depending on time, stop at a Kullu shawl outlet or local handicraft centre. Continue the journey to Manali and check in to the hotel on arrival. The rest of the evening is free for rest after the long mountain drive. Dinner at the hotel → Overnight stay in Manali.', 5698),
  ('mcleod-ganj', 30, 'six-night-seven-day-family-itinerary', 'SIX-NIGHT / SEVEN-DAY FAMILY ITINERARY', 'Night 4', NULL, 'After breakfast, proceed for Manali local sightseeing. Visit Hadimba Devi Temple, Ghatotkach Temple, Beas River, Vashisht Temple, Vashisht Kund, Manu Temple, Manali Clubhouse, Van Vihar, and the Himalayan Nyinmapa Tibetan Buddhist Monastery. Later, enjoy a relaxed walk around Manali Mall Road for shopping, cafés, snacks, and family time. Return to the hotel by late afternoon / evening → Evening free for leisure → Dinner at the hotel → Overnight stay in Manali.', 5699),
  ('mcleod-ganj', 30, 'six-night-seven-day-family-itinerary', 'SIX-NIGHT / SEVEN-DAY FAMILY ITINERARY', 'Night 5', NULL, 'After breakfast, start the excursion to Solang Valley. Enjoy the snow-covered landscapes or mountain scenery, depending on the season. Optional activities may include snow play, ropeway rides, snow tubing, or other adventure activities at an additional cost. Continue towards Atal Tunnel, subject to weather, road conditions, traffic, and local access regulations. If permitted, visit Sissu Village and Sissu Lake. Return to Manali by late afternoon / evening. Later, spend quality family time at Manali Mall by local transport. Dinner at the hotel → Overnight stay in Manali.', 5700),
  ('mcleod-ganj', 30, 'six-night-seven-day-family-itinerary', 'SIX-NIGHT / SEVEN-DAY FAMILY ITINERARY', 'Night 6', NULL, 'After breakfast, check out from the Manali hotel and proceed towards Kasol / Manikaran. En route, enjoy scenic stops around Kullu Valley, including Pandoh Dam, Sundarnagar Lake, the Beas or Parvati Valley viewpoints, rafting point, Bhuntar, and local markets, depending on time and road conditions. Continue to Manikaran and visit Manikaran Sahib Gurudwara and the famous Manikaran hot springs. Guests may spend some peaceful time in the surrounding Parvati Valley. Proceed to Kasol and check in to the hotel by late afternoon / evening. Take rest after the journey. Evening free for leisure or a short riverside / market walk, subject to local conditions → Dinner at the hotel → Overnight stay in Kasol.', 5701),
  ('mcleod-ganj', 30, 'six-night-seven-day-family-itinerary', 'SIX-NIGHT / SEVEN-DAY FAMILY ITINERARY', 'Night 7', NULL, 'After breakfast, check out from the Kasol hotel and transfer to Chandigarh Railway Station / Chandigarh Airport for your onward journey. The trip ends with happy memories of Shimla, Manali, Kullu, Kasol, and Manikaran.', 5702),
  ('mcleod-ganj', 31, 'six-night-seven-day-luxury-itinerary', 'SIX-NIGHT / SEVEN-DAY LUXURY ITINERARY', 'Night 1', NULL, 'Private premium vehicle pickup from Chandigarh Airport or Railway Station → Scenic transfer through the Himalayan valleys with planned comfort stops → Check-in at a luxury heritage hotel, boutique property, or valley-view resort in Shimla / Mashobra → Welcome drink and rest. Late afternoon: Private guided sightseeing of Jakhoo Hanuman Temple, followed by The Ridge, Christ Church, Scandal Point, Rani Jhansi Park, and the colonial buildings around Mall Road. Continue with a relaxed walk through Lakkar Bazaar and the central heritage lanes. Evening: Return to the hotel → Private balcony tea, spa treatment, or time beside the fireplace → Curated Himachali dinner with valley views → Overnight stay in Shimla.', 5703),
  ('mcleod-ganj', 31, 'six-night-seven-day-luxury-itinerary', 'SIX-NIGHT / SEVEN-DAY LUXURY ITINERARY', 'Night 2', NULL, 'After a leisurely breakfast, depart in a private chauffeur-driven SUV for Kufri and Fagu → Scenic drive through pine and cedar forests → Green Valley photography stop → Kufri sightseeing. Optional activities: Private nature walk, Himalayan Nature Park visit, horse riding, seasonal snow experience, or a curated adventure activity with local assistance. Continue towards Fagu for peaceful mountain views and a relaxed lunch at a premium resort or selected countryside restaurant → Proceed to Chail for forest scenery, Chail Palace surroundings, and quiet heritage photography. Return to Shimla by late afternoon / evening → High tea at the hotel → Spa, indoor relaxation, or private balcony time → Special dinner → Overnight stay in Shimla.', 5704),
  ('mcleod-ganj', 31, 'six-night-seven-day-luxury-itinerary', 'SIX-NIGHT / SEVEN-DAY LUXURY ITINERARY', 'Night 3', NULL, 'After breakfast, visit Viceregal Lodge / Rashtrapati Niwas and the Indian Institute of Advanced Study with a private guide → Explore the heritage architecture and landscaped surroundings at an unhurried pace. Continue to the Himachal State Museum for regional art, history, sculptures, and traditional artefacts → Visit Summer Hill and enjoy a peaceful pine-forest drive. Afternoon: Return to the hotel for lunch and rest → Optional spa treatment, wellness session, or in-room relaxation. Evening: Private colonial heritage walk covering Gaiety Heritage Cultural Complex, The Ridge, Christ Church, and Mall Road → Afternoon tea or hot chocolate at a premium café → Fine-dining dinner at the hotel → Overnight stay in Shimla.', 5705),
  ('mcleod-ganj', 31, 'six-night-seven-day-luxury-itinerary', 'SIX-NIGHT / SEVEN-DAY LUXURY ITINERARY', 'Night 4', NULL, 'After breakfast, check out from the Shimla hotel and transfer by private luxury vehicle to Mashobra or Naldehra → Scenic forest drive through pine and cedar landscapes → Check-in at a premium mountain resort or luxury retreat. Afternoon: Resort lunch followed by leisure time → Enjoy the property’s spa, private balcony, heated indoor facilities, or guided forest walk. Late afternoon: Visit Naldehra Golf Course and surrounding cedar forests → Optional horse riding or relaxed photography session → Return to the resort. Evening: Private mountain-view dinner, bonfire-style experience where available, or in-room dining → Overnight stay in Mashobra / Naldehra.', 5706),
  ('mcleod-ganj', 31, 'six-night-seven-day-luxury-itinerary', 'SIX-NIGHT / SEVEN-DAY LUXURY ITINERARY', 'Night 5', NULL, 'Begin with a leisurely breakfast overlooking the hills → Guided nature walk through the forest surroundings or a gentle private excursion around Mashobra. Visit selected viewpoints and quiet countryside areas → Optional horse riding at Naldehra, golf-course visit, photography session, or private picnic-style lunch arranged by the resort. Afternoon: Return to the resort for spa therapy, wellness time, afternoon tea, or relaxed balcony time with mountain views. Evening: Sunset viewing from the property or a nearby scenic point → Chef-curated Himachali dinner featuring local specialties such as siddu, chana madra, rajma, kadhi, and regional breads → Overnight stay in Mashobra / Naldehra.', 5707),
  ('mcleod-ganj', 31, 'six-night-seven-day-luxury-itinerary', 'SIX-NIGHT / SEVEN-DAY LUXURY ITINERARY', 'Night 6', NULL, 'After breakfast, choose one of the following luxury experiences: **Option 1 – Scenic railway experience:** Enjoy a reserved section of the Kalka–Shimla Toy Train on a suitable route → Scenic views of tunnels, bridges, forests, and mountain valleys → Private vehicle transfer back to the hotel. **Option 2 – Relaxed Shimla experience:** Visit Annandale and the Army Heritage Museum → Continue to Tara Devi Temple or Sankat Mochan Temple → Return to central Shimla for premium shopping at Himachal Emporium, Lakkar Bazaar, and selected local boutiques. Afternoon: Leisure lunch followed by rest at the hotel or resort → Optional spa treatment, private photography session, or curated café visit. Evening: Farewell sunset experience at The Ridge, Jakhoo Hill, or a private valley-view terrace → Celebration dinner with personalised service → Overnight stay in Mashobra / Naldehra or Shimla, depending on departure logistics.', 5708),
  ('mcleod-ganj', 31, 'six-night-seven-day-luxury-itinerary', 'SIX-NIGHT / SEVEN-DAY LUXURY ITINERARY', 'Night 7', NULL, 'Enjoy a relaxed breakfast at the hotel → Final mountain-view tea or short property walk → Checkout with luggage assistance. Private chauffeur-driven transfer to Chandigarh Airport or Chandigarh Railway Station → Departure with scenic views of the Himalayan foothills and comfortable rest stops en route.', 5709),
  ('mcleod-ganj', 32, 'travel-agent-insights', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS', 'What inexperienced planners often do wrong', NULL, '', 5710),
  ('mcleod-ganj', 32, 'travel-agent-insights', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS', 'What an experienced planner does differently', NULL, '', 5711),
  ('mcleod-ganj', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'IF:', NULL, '**trip_length <= 1 night**', 5712),
  ('mcleod-ganj', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'THEN:', NULL, 'prefer Hadimba Devi Temple + Dhungri Forest + Mall Road + one short Beas River or Old Manali experience. Reason: A one-night Manali stay works best as a compact local experience. Hadimba Temple, Dhungri Forest, Mall Road, Old Manali cafés, and a short riverside walk provide a clear introduction without adding a tiring Solang Valley or Atal Tunnel excursion.', 5713),
  ('mcleod-ganj', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'IF:', NULL, '**trip_length == 2 nights**', 5714),
  ('mcleod-ganj', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'THEN:', NULL, 'schedule one local culture-and-market day AND: schedule one scenic excursion such as Solang Valley, Vashisht, or Naggar. Reason: Two nights are enough for central Manali plus one major excursion, but not for comfortably combining Solang Valley, Atal Tunnel, Sissu, Rohtang-area viewpoints, Naggar, Kullu, and Kasol.', 5715),
  ('mcleod-ganj', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'IF:', NULL, '**trip_length >= 3 nights**', 5716),
  ('mcleod-ganj', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'THEN:', NULL, 'include one central sightseeing cluster AND: include one scenic mountain excursion AND: include one relaxed or flexible half-day. Reason: Three nights are the practical sweet spot for balancing temples, forests, cafés, markets, mountain scenery, and unhurried Manali time.', 5717),
  ('mcleod-ganj', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'IF:', NULL, '**trip_length <= 3 nights**', 5718),
  ('mcleod-ganj', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'THEN:', NULL, 'prefer_one_hotel AND: avoid changing accommodation between Manali, Solang Valley, Naggar, and Kasol. Reason: Short stays lose valuable time through packing, checkout, luggage movement, and mountain transfers. One well-located base is usually more efficient.', 5719),
  ('mcleod-ganj', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'IF:', NULL, '**trip_type == FIRST_TIME_VISITOR**', 5720),
  ('mcleod-ganj', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'THEN:', NULL, 'anchor the itinerary around Hadimba Devi Temple, Old Manali, Mall Road, Solang Valley, Vashisht, and one scenic route towards Atal Tunnel or Naggar. Reason: These experiences provide the clearest introduction to Manali’s temples, forests, cafés, markets, mountain scenery, local culture, and seasonal snow activities.', 5721),
  ('mcleod-ganj', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'IF:', NULL, '**traveler_type == FAMILY** AND: **children_age <= 6**', 5722),
  ('mcleod-ganj', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'THEN:', NULL, 'reduce_walking_intensity_target by 25% AND: limit_major_activities_per_day to 2 AND: increase_downtime by 20% AND: prefer hotels with easy vehicle access, heating, and an in-house restaurant. Reason: Winding roads, cold weather, uneven paths, slopes, stairs, traffic, and altitude can tire young children. Short sightseeing blocks, regular meal breaks, and hotel rest make the trip more comfortable.', 5723),
  ('mcleod-ganj', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'IF:', NULL, '**trip_type == FAMILY**', 5724),
  ('mcleod-ganj', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'THEN:', NULL, 'prefer Hadimba Devi Temple, Dhungri Forest, Van Vihar, Beas River, Old Manali, Solang Valley, Vashisht, and easy viewpoints AND: avoid long treks and multiple mountain excursions on the same day. Reason: Manali suits families best when sightseeing is mixed with gentle forest walks, seasonal snow play, child-friendly activities, regular rest, and flexible travel time.', 5725),
  ('mcleod-ganj', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'IF:', NULL, '**trip_type == HONEYMOON**', 5726),
  ('mcleod-ganj', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'THEN:', NULL, 'increase romance_weight by 30% AND: increase privacy_weight by 25% AND: increase free_time_weight by 25% AND: decrease activity_density by 25%. Reason: Manali’s honeymoon value comes from valley-view stays, private drives, pine forests, snowfall possibilities, café dates, riverside walks, spa time, and romantic dinners rather than maximum attraction coverage.', 5727),
  ('mcleod-ganj', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'IF:', NULL, '**trip_type == HONEYMOON**', 5728),
  ('mcleod-ganj', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'THEN:', NULL, 'prefer Old Manali, Aleo, Prini, Naggar, or a quiet valley-view property AND: schedule no more than 2 major activities per day AND: include one private dinner or scenic sunset experience. Reason: These areas offer greater privacy and slower mountain experiences, while central Manali can be used for one relaxed temple visit, café date, market walk, or riverside experience.', 5729),
  ('mcleod-ganj', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'IF:', NULL, '**traveler_type == LUXURY**', 5730),
  ('mcleod-ganj', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'THEN:', NULL, 'prefer_private_transfer AND: prefer_high_service_valley_view_or_boutique_hotel AND: prefer_curated_excursions AND: increase_service_and_rest_weight. Reason: Luxury value in Manali is created through comfort, privacy, professional chauffeurs, premium rooms, spa services, personalised dining, scenic drives, and flexible pacing—not by adding more roadside stops.', 5731),
  ('mcleod-ganj', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'IF:', NULL, '**traveler_type == LUXURY** AND: **trip_length >= 4 nights**', 5732),
  ('mcleod-ganj', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'THEN:', NULL, 'consider a split stay between central Manali and Naggar / Prini OR: retain one luxury base and add a full-day private excursion. Reason: A longer stay can combine central cafés and local sightseeing with a quieter forest, orchard, heritage, or valley-view atmosphere, provided the hotel change does not create unnecessary travel time.', 5733),
  ('mcleod-ganj', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'IF:', NULL, '**traveler_type == BUDGET**', 5734),
  ('mcleod-ganj', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'THEN:', NULL, 'prefer a value hotel in Vashisht, Simsa, Old Manali, or another area with practical road access AND: use walking for local sightseeing AND: mix free attractions with one or two paid excursions. Reason: Hadimba Temple, Manu Temple, Old Manali lanes, Beas River walks, Van Vihar, monasteries, and local markets provide substantial low-cost sightseeing. Taxis should be reserved for Solang Valley, Atal Tunnel, Naggar, and other spread-out attractions.', 5735),
  ('mcleod-ganj', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'IF:', NULL, 'hotel_is_far_from_central_manali: AND: **hotel_saving < additional_transport_cost + value_of_lost_time**', 5736),
  ('mcleod-ganj', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'THEN:', NULL, 'prefer_central_hotel_or_easy_road_access_hotel. Reason: A cheaper hotel may provide poor overall value if guests must repeatedly pay for taxis or walk steep uphill routes to reach markets, cafés, temples, restaurants, and transport points.', 5737),
  ('mcleod-ganj', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'IF:', NULL, 'hotel_is_in_old_manali_or_vashisht:', 5738),
  ('mcleod-ganj', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'THEN:', NULL, 'verify_vehicle_drop_point AND: verify_luggage_access AND: verify_stairs_and_slope AND: verify_actual_walking_distance. Reason: Some properties are located on narrow, steep, or pedestrian-only lanes. “Near Old Manali” or “near Vashisht” does not always mean that a vehicle can reach the hotel entrance.', 5739),
  ('mcleod-ganj', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'IF:', NULL, '**traveler_type == SENIOR**', 5740),
  ('mcleod-ganj', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'THEN:', NULL, 'prefer Aleo, Prini, Simsa, Shuru, or a hotel with direct road access AND: use private transport AND: avoid long uphill walks, steep village lanes, and stair-heavy sightseeing. Reason: Manali’s attractions may involve slopes, stairs, uneven paths, cold weather, traffic, and winding mountain roads. Hotel accessibility and vehicle access should be checked individually before booking.', 5741),
  ('mcleod-ganj', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'IF:', NULL, '**traveler_type == SENIOR** OR: **mobility_level == LIMITED**', 5742),
  ('mcleod-ganj', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'THEN:', NULL, 'limit_major_activities_per_day to 1–2 AND: schedule outdoor sightseeing during the warmer part of the day AND: include a rest period after every excursion. Reason: Shorter sightseeing blocks reduce fatigue and make it easier to manage altitude, cold weather, traffic, weather changes, and uneven mountain terrain.', 5743),
  ('mcleod-ganj', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'IF:', NULL, '**traveler_interest == HISTORY OR traveler_interest == CULTURE**', 5744),
  ('mcleod-ganj', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'THEN:', NULL, 'combine Hadimba Devi Temple, Manu Temple, Vashisht Temple, Tibetan monasteries, Museum of Himachal Culture and Folk Art, Naggar Castle, and Roerich Art Gallery over adjacent days. Reason: These attractions create a coherent experience of Himachali traditions, religious heritage, Buddhist culture, traditional architecture, regional art, and village life without requiring every site to be visited in one day.', 5745),
  ('mcleod-ganj', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'IF:', NULL, '**traveler_interest == NATURE OR traveler_interest == PHOTOGRAPHY**', 5746),
  ('mcleod-ganj', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'THEN:', NULL, 'prefer Dhungri Forest, Beas River, Solang Valley, Atal Tunnel–Sissu, Naggar, apple orchards, Kothi, and selected forest viewpoints AND: protect early-morning or late-afternoon photography time. Reason: Manali is especially strong for deodar forests, rivers, waterfalls, Himalayan peaks, villages, snow landscapes, orchards, and changing mountain light.', 5747),
  ('mcleod-ganj', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'IF:', NULL, '**traveler_interest == SNOW**', 5748),
  ('mcleod-ganj', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'THEN:', NULL, 'prefer December–February AND: treat snowfall and snow activities as weather-dependent AND: keep road transfers and outdoor plans flexible. Reason: Winter may provide snow around Solang Valley and higher areas, but snowfall timing, intensity, road access, activity availability, and local transport can change quickly.', 5749),
  ('mcleod-ganj', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'IF:', NULL, '**weather == MONSOON**', 5750),
  ('mcleod-ganj', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'THEN:', NULL, 'reduce_outdoor_walking AND: reduce_long_excursions AND: increase_indoor_or_flexible_time AND: keep trekking, rafting, paragliding, waterfalls, and high-altitude routes weather-dependent. Reason: Rain can reduce visibility, make paths slippery, delay road journeys, and increase landslide or cancellation risk. Cafés, monasteries, museums, shopping, hotel dining, spa time, and relaxed riverside stays provide useful alternatives.', 5751),
  ('mcleod-ganj', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'IF:', NULL, '**weather == HEAVY_SNOWFALL**', 5752),
  ('mcleod-ganj', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'THEN:', NULL, 'avoid_tight_itinerary AND: prioritise_nearby_or_walkable_attractions AND: keep_extra_transfer_buffer AND: confirm road and attraction conditions locally. Reason: Snow can create traffic delays, slippery walking conditions, vehicle restrictions, and temporary changes to sightseeing access. Flexibility is more valuable than attempting to preserve every scheduled stop.', 5753),
  ('mcleod-ganj', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'IF:', NULL, '**trip_length >= 4 nights** AND: **traveler_interest == RELAXATION**', 5754),
  ('mcleod-ganj', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'THEN:', NULL, 'add one resort-focused day AND: consider Naggar, Prini, Aleo, Vashisht, or a riverside property AND: include spa, balcony, café, hot-spring, or forest time. Reason: Longer Manali stays are more rewarding when they include quiet mountain experiences, wellness, and recovery time instead of repeating central sightseeing.', 5755),
  ('mcleod-ganj', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'IF:', NULL, '**trip_length >= 5 nights** AND: **traveler_interest == ADVENTURE**', 5756),
  ('mcleod-ganj', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'THEN:', NULL, 'consider Solang Valley, Sethan, Atal Tunnel–Sissu, Kullu, Hampta Valley, or a guided trek AND: reserve separate time for skiing, paragliding, rafting, trekking, mountain biking, camping, or snow activities where seasonally suitable. Reason: Manali offers light activities close to town as well as demanding Himalayan adventures. Outdoor variety increases when nearby mountain areas and separate activity days are included.', 5757),
  ('mcleod-ganj', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'IF:', NULL, '**trip_type == FIRST_TIME_VISITOR** AND: **trip_length <= 2 nights**', 5758),
  ('mcleod-ganj', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'THEN:', NULL, 'do_not_recommend Solang Valley + Atal Tunnel + Sissu + Rohtang-area viewpoints + Naggar in one day. Reason: These places may look close on a map, but mountain roads, traffic, weather, sightseeing time, and activity stops make such a circuit tiring and low quality. Choose one excursion cluster instead.', 5759),
  ('mcleod-ganj', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'IF:', NULL, '**traveler_interest == SHOPPING**', 5760),
  ('mcleod-ganj', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'THEN:', NULL, 'include Mall Road, Manali Market, Manu Market, Tibetan shops, Kullu shawl outlets, and local handicraft stores AND: keep shopping time separate from a long mountain excursion. Reason: Woollens, Kullu shawls, Himachali caps, wooden products, Tibetan items, outdoor clothing, souvenirs, and local food products are best explored without rushing between distant viewpoints.', 5761),
  ('mcleod-ganj', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'IF:', NULL, '**trip_type == ROMANTIC**', 5762),
  ('mcleod-ganj', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'THEN:', NULL, 'schedule a quiet forest walk, café date, mountain-view dinner, and one sunset or snowfall experience. Reason: Manali’s strongest romantic moments come from atmosphere—deodar forests, warm cafés, riverside scenery, mountain views, snowfall, and slow evenings—rather than from covering many attractions.', 5763),
  ('mcleod-ganj', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'IF:', NULL, '**traveler_type == PARTY_TRAVELLER**', 5764),
  ('mcleod-ganj', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'THEN:', NULL, 'set_low_nightlife_expectation AND: prioritise cafés, restaurants, live-music venues, hotel lounges, Old Manali evenings, and relaxed market walks. Reason: Manali offers a casual evening scene with cafés, restaurants, music venues, and hotel lounges, but it is not primarily a large-scale clubbing or late-night entertainment destination.', 5765),
  ('mcleod-ganj', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'IF:', NULL, '**arrival_mode == CHANDIGARH_AIRPORT_OR_RAILWAY_STATION**', 5766),
  ('mcleod-ganj', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'THEN:', NULL, 'allow approximately 8–10 hours for the road transfer AND: prefer a private sedan, SUV, or MPV when comfort and flexibility matter. Reason: The Chandigarh–Manali journey is a long mountain transfer. Rest stops, luggage space, motion comfort, road conditions, and a realistic arrival schedule should be built into the plan.', 5767),
  ('mcleod-ganj', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'IF:', NULL, '**traveler_type == FAMILY OR traveler_type == LUXURY OR traveler_type == HONEYMOON**', 5768),
  ('mcleod-ganj', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'THEN:', NULL, 'prefer_private_transfer_from_chandigarh AND: include comfort stops AND: avoid scheduling major sightseeing immediately after arrival. Reason: A private transfer improves door-to-door convenience, luggage handling, scenic flexibility, and comfort after the long mountain journey.', 5769),
  ('mcleod-ganj', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'IF:', NULL, '**traveler_type == BUDGET** AND: **central_sightseeing_required == true**', 5770),
  ('mcleod-ganj', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'THEN:', NULL, 'use walking and local transport for Mall Road, Manali Market, Old Manali, Hadimba Devi Temple, Manu Temple, Beas River, Van Vihar, and nearby monasteries AND: reserve taxis for Solang Valley, Atal Tunnel, Naggar, Vashisht, and other spread-out locations. Reason: Manali’s central attractions are suitable for walking and short local transfers, while private transport is more valuable for distant mountain excursions.', 5771),
  ('mcleod-ganj', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'IF:', NULL, '**trip_length >= 4 nights**', 5772),
  ('mcleod-ganj', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'THEN:', NULL, 'add one flexible half-day. Reason: A flexible block allows recovery after the Chandigarh transfer, weather adjustments, extra photography, shopping, snowfall time, spa treatment, resort relaxation, or a repeat visit to a favourite café or viewpoint.', 5773),
  ('mcleod-ganj', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'IF:', NULL, '**accessibility_requirement == HIGH**', 5774),
  ('mcleod-ganj', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', 'THEN:', NULL, 'verify_each_hotel_and_attraction_individually AND: prefer direct vehicle access, lifts, ground-floor rooms, accessible bathrooms, and minimal-step routes AND: avoid assuming that “wheelchair-friendly” labels guarantee full accessibility. Reason: Manali’s accessibility varies significantly by hotel, attraction, entrance, terrain, road surface, weather, and transport arrangement. Destination-level accessibility should never replace property-level verification.', 5775),
  ('mcleod-ganj', 34, 'destination-scoring', 'DESTINATION SCORING', NULL, NULL, '| Factor | Score | | -------------------------- | ----- | | Family | 80 | | Family with young children | 74 | | Honeymoon | 85 | | Romantic | 88 | | Luxury | 75 | | Budget | 95 | | Adventure | 93 | | Culture | 97 | | History | 89 | | Food | 91 | | Shopping | 84 | | Nightlife | 70 | | Relaxation | 92 | | Nature | 94 | | Photography | 96 | | Solo travel | 97 | | Senior travellers | 72 | | First-time visitor | 90 | | Repeat traveller | 88 | | Accessibility | 65 |', 5776),
  ('mcleod-ganj', 35, 'final-travel-agent-verdict', 'FINAL TRAVEL AGENT VERDICT', NULL, NULL, '**McLeod Ganj is a highly recommended 3–4-night Himalayan destination for culture lovers, nature lovers, honeymooners, photographers, spiritual travellers, backpackers, and adventure seekers.** It delivers a distinctive mix of **Tibetan culture, Himalayan scenery, monasteries, cafés, trekking, meditation, local markets, and peaceful mountain experiences**. Plan a balanced itinerary with **one cultural experience, one scenic excursion, one optional adventure, and sufficient free time**. Ideal for: Tibetan culture, nature, photography, spirituality, trekking, cafés, romance, and relaxation. Less suitable for: Clubbing-focused trips, travellers seeking a flat/easy-access destination, and those uncomfortable with steep roads, stairs, and walking. Best overall verdict: **Excellent destination — 88/100.**', 5777),
  ('mcleod-ganj', 36, 'data-quality', 'DATA QUALITY', NULL, NULL, 'information_completeness: 90/100 last_updated: 2026-09-06 last_verified: NOT_LIVE_VERIFIED verified_by: TRAVEL_ENGINE_INITIAL_DATASET sources: IMPORTANT: Prices, opening hours, schedules, visa requirements, availability, accessibility and operational conditions must NOT be treated as permanently valid from this document. These must be sourced from structured, refreshable data.', 5778),
  ('narkanda', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Winter Dec-Feb - SNOW PEAK + BEST FOR SNOW SKIING', NULL, 'weather: -5 to 10°C, snow 3-5ft + skiing + snowboarding + snow trek + Hatu Peak snow + Tani Jubbar frozen + best snow near Shimla. crowd_level: HIGH Jan-Feb snow season, MEDIUM Dec price_level: HIGH Jan-Feb overall_score: 92 recommended: true reason: Snow best + skiing Jan-Feb + snowboarding + Hatu Peak snow trek + Tani Jubbar snow + apple orchards snow + best snow near Shimla + cheaper than Manali Gulmarg + weekend Delhi + honeymoon snow.', 5779),
  ('narkanda', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Summer Mar-Jun - PLEASANT + APPLE BLOSSOM + GREEN', NULL, 'weather: 10-25°C, pleasant + apple blossom Mar-Apr + green meadows + deodar forest + Hatu Peak trek + Tani Jubbar + Kotgarh valley + clear Himalayan views. crowd_level: MEDIUM price_level: MEDIUM overall_score: 84 recommended: true reason: Pleasant + apple blossom + green + Hatu Peak trek + Tani Jubbar + Kotgarh + clear views + offbeat + less crowd than Shimla + family + honeymoon + meadows.', 5780),
  ('narkanda', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Monsoon Jul-Sep - APPLE SEASON + GREEN + OFFBEAT', NULL, 'weather: 12-22°C, rain + green + apple season Jul-Aug apple picking + Kotgarh apple valley + Hatu Peak misty + Tani Jubbar lush + rain + landslides risk + road slippery. crowd_level: LOW price_level: LOW overall_score: 78 recommended: true reason: Apple season Jul-Aug + apple picking + Kotgarh + green + misty + offbeat + less crowd + apple orchards + but rain + landslides + road slippery + need raincoat + avoid Hatu trek rain.', 5781),
  ('narkanda', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Autumn Oct-Nov - BEST VIEWS + CLEAR + PLEASANT', NULL, 'weather: 8-20°C, clear + pleasant + best Himalayan views + Hatu Peak clear 360 views + deodar forest + apple harvest end + pleasant + best for photography + trek. crowd_level: MEDIUM price_level: MEDIUM overall_score: 88 recommended: true reason: Clear + best views + Hatu Peak 360 Himalayan + pleasant + photography + trek + Tani Jubbar + Kotgarh + offbeat + family + honeymoon + clear views.', 5782),
  ('narkanda', 10, 'budget-strategy', 'BUDGET STRATEGY', NULL, NULL, 'Where money can be saved: Where saving money is usually NOT recommended:', 5783),
  ('narkanda', 12, 'airport-transfer-logic', 'AIRPORT TRANSFER LOGIC', NULL, NULL, 'Family: Shimla/Chandigarh/Delhi -> Narkanda by private AC car $40-$80 2-10hr + family hotel near Narkanda market + valley view + family cottage + Hatu + Tani Jubbar + Kotgarh. Honeymoon: Private car + Tethys Ski Resort / HPTDC Hotel Hatu / Kotgarh villas private cottage + valley view + apple orchard + bonfire + Hatu private + Tani Jubbar private + Kotgarh private + snow private Jan-Feb. Luxury: Private luxury car + Tethys Ski Resort + private cottage + valley view + bonfire + butler + private guide + Hatu private + Tani Jubbar private + Kotgarh private + skiing private Jan-Feb. Budget: HRTC bus Shimla->Narkanda $3 2hr + shared jeep Hatu $5 + homestay near market $20-$30 + bus to Tani Jubbar $1 + apple orchard free + dhaba $5. Senior: AC taxi door-to-door + hotel near Narkanda market flat + elevator + valley view + car for Hatu + Tani Jubbar + Kotgarh + Thanedar + avoid Hatu trek 7km + snow slippery + need car + chains Jan-Feb.', 5784),
  ('narkanda', 18, 'family-travel', 'FAMILY TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'child_friendly_score: 82 best_ages: 3-15 - Tani Jubbar Lake boating + Hatu Peak drive + apple orchards + Kotgarh flat + Thanedar flat + snow playing Jan-Feb + meadows Rules:', 5785),
  ('narkanda', 19, 'honeymoon-travel', 'HONEYMOON TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'honeymoon_score: 84 romance_score: 84 privacy_score: 86 luxury_score: 58 Recommended: Narkanda is best offbeat honeymoon near Shimla + snow + meadows + apple orchards + valley view + Hatu Peak + Tani Jubbar + Kotgarh + offbeat + quiet vs Shimla crowd:', 5786),
  ('narkanda', 20, 'luxury-travel', 'LUXURY TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'luxury_score: 58 Recommended:', 5787),
  ('narkanda', 21, 'adventure', 'ADVENTURE', NULL, NULL, 'adventure_score: 82 Adventure-like experiences should be interpreted as:', 5788),
  ('narkanda', 22, 'senior-travel', 'SENIOR TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'senior_suitability: 76 walking_intensity: LOW_TO_MEDIUM Rules:', 5789),
  ('narkanda', 23, 'accessibility', 'ACCESSIBILITY', NULL, NULL, 'wheelchair_accessibility: MODERATE public_transport_accessibility: MODERATE - Bus + shared jeep + but Hatu ghats + winding + limited + snow Jan-Feb Road closed hotel_accessibility: GOOD; 3-4 RESORTS HAVE ELEVATORS + ACCESSIBLE ROOMS + RAMPS + VALLEY VIEW attraction_accessibility: MODERATE; MUST_BE_VERIFIED_PER_ATTRACTION Rule: Verify accessible room + elevator + private car + chains Jan-Feb.', 5790),
  ('narkanda', 24, 'food', 'FOOD', NULL, NULL, 'Strong categories:', 5791),
  ('narkanda', 25, 'shopping', 'SHOPPING', NULL, NULL, 'Strong categories:', 5792),
  ('narkanda', 26, 'nightlife', 'NIGHTLIFE', NULL, NULL, 'nightlife_level: 35 Suitable for: honeymoon + romantic + snow cottage + valley view + apple orchard + meadows + bonfire + valley + snow + offbeat + quiet Not a primary requirement for: party seekers wanting pubs + breweries till late - Go to Shimla 60km 2hr + Mall Road + pubs + bars + nightlife + party Travellers should generally prefer: Resort bonfire + valley view + meadows + deodar forest + Hatu Peak sunset + Tani Jubbar Lake + Kotgarh + Thanedar + apple orchard + snow Jan-Feb + skiing + snowboarding + snow playing + bonfire + spa + resort + valley + meadows + snow + offbeat + quiet + early sleep 10 PM + bonfire + resort + valley + meadows + snow + offbeat + quiet over: late-night pubs + clubs', 5793),
  ('narkanda', 28, 'sample-itinerary-patterns', 'SAMPLE ITINERARY PATTERNS', '1 NIGHT NARKANDA SNOW + HATU PEAK - QUICK', NULL, 'Day 1: Arrive Narkanda from Shimla 60km 2hr. Transfer to Narkanda hotel/homestay + valley view + apple orchard. Afternoon Hatu Peak 3400m drive/trek 7km + Hatu Mata Temple + 360 Himalayan views + sunset best + deodar forest + meadows + valley view + skiing slopes Jan-Feb + snow playing + bonfire + apple orchard. Day 2 Morning Tani Jubbar Lake 10km boating + meadows + deodar + Nag Temple + Kotgarh apple valley 15km + Thanedar church 1915 + Stokes farm + apple picking Jul-Aug + apple blossom Mar-Apr + departure Shimla 60km 2hr with snow + Hatu + apple memories.', 5794),
  ('narkanda', 28, 'sample-itinerary-patterns', 'SAMPLE ITINERARY PATTERNS', '2 NIGHTS NARKANDA SNOW + APPLE + HATU - PERFECT', NULL, 'Day 1 Arrive Narkanda from Shimla 60km 2hr / Chandigarh 170km 6hr / Delhi 410km 9-10hr. Transfer to Tethys Ski Resort / HPTDC Hotel Hatu + valley view + apple orchard + check-in rest + valley view + meadows + deodar + apple orchard + snow Jan-Feb. Afternoon Hatu Peak 3400m drive/trek 7km + Hatu Mata Temple + 360 Himalayan views + sunset best + deodar forest + meadows + valley view + bonfire + apple orchard + snow Jan-Feb + skiing slopes + snow playing. Day 2 Morning Tani Jubbar Lake 10km boating + meadows + deodar + Nag Temple + Kotgarh apple valley 15km + Thanedar church 1915 + Stokes farm + apple history + apple picking Jul-Aug + apple blossom Mar-Apr + valley + meadows + deodar + apple orchard + afternoon leisure + bonfire + snow activities Jan-Feb skiing + snowboarding + snow playing + meadows + valley + apple orchard + offbeat + quiet. Day 3 Morning at leisure - Apple orchard walk + valley view + meadows + deodar forest + Hatu Peak sunrise + Tani Jubbar morning + shopping apple + apple jam + apple juice + Kinnauri shawl + woollens + check out and transfer to Shimla 60km 2hr or Kinnaur Sangla 90km 3hr for departure with snow + Hatu + apple + meadows + valley memories.', 5795),
  ('narkanda', 29, 'two-night-honeymoon-snow-apple-pattern-ideal', 'TWO-NIGHT HONEYMOON + SNOW + APPLE PATTERN (IDEAL)', NULL, NULL, 'Day 1 Arrive at Narkanda from Shimla 60 km 2 hr / Chandigarh 170 km 6 hr and private transfer to luxury cottage near Narkanda - Tethys Ski Resort / HPTDC Hotel Hatu / Kotgarh villas. Check-in, rest + private cottage valley view + apple orchard + meadows + deodar + valley + snow Jan-Feb + private balcony + bonfire. Afternoon Hatu Peak 3400m drive/trek 7km + Hatu Mata Temple + 360 Himalayan views + sunset best + deodar forest + meadows + valley view + bonfire + apple orchard + snow Jan-Feb + skiing slopes + snow playing. Overnight: Narkanda - Tethys Ski Resort / HPTDC Hotel Hatu / Kotgarh villas Meals: Breakfast + Himachali dinner Day 2 After breakfast, Tani Jubbar Lake 10km boating + meadows + deodar + Nag Temple + Kotgarh apple valley 15km + apple orchards + apple picking Jul-Aug + apple blossom Mar-Apr + Thanedar church 1915 + Stokes farm + apple history + British + church + farm + history + offbeat + valley + meadows + deodar + apple orchard + afternoon leisure + bonfire + snow activities Jan-Feb skiing + snowboarding + snow playing + meadows + valley + apple orchard + offbeat + quiet. Overnight: Narkanda - Tethys Ski Resort / HPTDC Hotel Hatu / Kotgarh villas Meals: Breakfast + Bonfire Day 3 Morning at leisure - Apple orchard walk + valley view + meadows + deodar forest + Hatu Peak sunrise + Tani Jubbar morning + shopping apple + apple jam + apple juice + Kinnauri shawl + woolens + check out and transfer to Shimla 60km 2hr or Kinnaur Sangla 90km 3hr for departure with snow + Hatu + apple + meadows + valley + honeymoon memories. Meals: Breakfast + Apple', 5796),
  ('narkanda', 30, 'three-night-snow-skiing-apple-kinnaur-gateway-pattern', 'THREE-NIGHT SNOW + SKIING + APPLE + KINNAUR GATEWAY PATTERN', NULL, NULL, 'Day 1 Arrive Narkanda + private car to Tethys Ski Resort + check-in + Hatu Peak 3400m + Hatu Mata Temple + 360 views + sunset + deodar + meadows + valley + bonfire + apple orchard + snow Jan-Feb + skiing slopes + snow playing + dinner bonfire + skiing briefing. Day 2 Breakfast. Early morning 9 AM jeep + guide to Hatu Peak snow trek Jan-Feb + Tani Jubbar Lake 10km boating + meadows + Kotgarh apple valley 15km + Thanedar church + Stokes farm + apple picking Jul-Aug + lunch packed + return 2 PM + rest + evening snow activities Jan-Feb skiing + snowboarding + snow playing + meadows + valley + bonfire + spa. Day 3 Breakfast. Morning Kotgarh apple valley + Thanedar + apple orchards + apple picking Jul-Aug + afternoon Kinnaur gateway Sangla 90km + Chitkul 100km + Kalpa 90km + Spiti circuit + gateway + valley + river + offbeat + Kinnaur + Spiti + gateway + 60-90km + 2-3hr car + offbeat + Kinnaur + Spiti + gateway + bonfire + farewell. Day 4 Breakfast. Morning apple orchard walk + valley view + meadows + deodar forest + Hatu Peak sunrise + Tani Jubbar morning + shopping apple + apple jam + apple juice + Kinnauri shawl + woolens + check out + transfer Shimla 60km 2hr or Chandigarh 170km 6hr with snow + skiing + apple + meadows + valley + gateway memories.', 5797),
  ('narkanda', 31, 'one-night-snow-weekend-pattern-delhi-shimla-weekend', 'ONE-NIGHT SNOW WEEKEND PATTERN - DELHI SHIMLA WEEKEND', NULL, NULL, 'Day 1 Shimla 60km 2hr -> Narkanda + Hatu Peak 3400m + Hatu Mata Temple + Tani Jubbar Lake 10km + Kotgarh apple valley 15km + Thanedar church + Stokes farm + apple orchards + snow Jan-Feb + skiing + snowboarding + snow playing + bonfire + Tethys Ski Resort + valley view + meadows + deodar + snow + valley + offbeat + quiet + less crowd than Shimla + snow + meadows. Day 2 Morning Hatu Peak sunrise + Tani Jubbar morning + Kotgarh morning + apple picking Jul-Aug + shopping apple + apple jam + apple juice + Kinnauri shawl + departure Shimla 60km 2hr / Delhi 410km 9-10hr with snow + Hatu + apple + meadows + valley + weekend memories.', 5798),
  ('narkanda', 32, 'travel-agent-insights', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS', 'What inexperienced planners often do wrong', NULL, '', 5799);
INSERT INTO destination_guidance (place_id, section, topic, section_title, heading, audience, body, position) VALUES
  ('narkanda', 32, 'travel-agent-insights', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS', 'What an experienced planner does differently', NULL, '1. Starts with purpose 2. Groups by geography: Narkanda market + Hatu Peak 7km + skiing slopes 2km together snow core 2-7km jeep/trek + car, Tani Jubbar Lake 10km + Kotgarh apple valley 15km + Thanedar church 15km + Stokes farm together apple + lake + 10-15km + car, Satluj Valley + Rampur 60km + Sarahan 60km + Kinnaur Sangla 90km + Chitkul 100km + Kalpa 90km together gateway + valley + river + 60-90km + car + bus + gateway + valley + river + offbeat + Kinnaur + Spiti. 3. Uses hotel location strategically: NARKANDA MARKET + TETHYS SKI RESORT VALLEY VIEW for honeymoon + family + snow + Hatu + Tani Jubbar + Kotgarh + valley view + meadows + deodar + snow + skiing + 2km from market + valley view + apple orchard + near Hatu + Tani Jubbar + Kotgarh + safe + view + meadows + valley + apple + snow + skiing + homestay + resort + valley + view + meadows + apple + snow + skiing. KOTGARH + THANEDAR + APPLE VALLEY for apple + valley + offbeat + apple + valley + quiet + honeymoon + offbeat + 15km from Narkanda + offbeat + apple + valley + quiet + honeymoon + offbeat. 4. Places Hatu Peak morning 9-11 AM + Tani Jubbar morning 11 AM-1 PM boating + Kotgarh morning + Thanedar morning + Skiing morning Jan-Feb + Hatu morning + sunset evening + snow playing morning + apple picking morning Jul-Aug + apple blossom morning Mar-Apr + valley views morning + meadows morning + deodar forest morning. 5. Treats Narkanda as 2-3 areas/day + Hatu Peak + Tani Jubbar + Kotgarh + Thanedar separate half days + not checklist 6 areas same day + trek + skiing + apple separate full day. 6. Always includes private car + jeep + guide for Hatu + Tani Jubbar + Kotgarh + Thanedar + skiing + snowboarding + snow playing + apple orchard tour + apple picking Jul-Aug + apple blossom Mar-Apr + apple shopping + shawl + woolens + honey + valley view + meadows + deodar + snow + skiing + valley + meadows + snow + offbeat + quiet + private car + jeep + guide + snow boots + jacket + water + hat + chains Jan-Feb + 4x4 + snow + road slippery + need experienced driver + snow + rain + apple + snow + skiing + valley + meadows + snow + offbeat + quiet.', 5800),
  ('narkanda', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', NULL, NULL, 'IF: `trip_length == 1 night` THEN: Narkanda market + Hatu Peak 3400m + Hatu Mata Temple + Tani Jubbar Lake 10km + Kotgarh apple valley quick + skiing Jan-Feb quick. Rushed + no Kinnaur. Reason: No time for Kinnaur Sangla 90km + Chitkul 100km + Kalpa 90km + Spiti. IF: `trip_length == 2 nights` THEN: Day 1 Narkanda + Hatu Peak 3400m + Hatu Mata Temple + sunset + skiing Jan-Feb, Day 2 Tani Jubbar Lake + Kotgarh apple valley + Thanedar church + Stokes farm + apple picking Jul-Aug + snow activities Jan-Feb. Core. Reason: Covers snow + Hatu + lake + apple valley + church + farm + valley. IF: `trip_length >= 3 nights` THEN: Add skiing lessons Jan-Feb + snowboarding + Hatu snow trek + Tani Jubbar trek + Kotgarh trek + mountain biking + Kinnaur Sangla 90km + Chitkul + Kalpa + Spiti circuit + Rampur + Sarahan + bonfire + snow + apple + meadows + valley. Reason: Complete honeymoon + family + adventure + trek + skiing + apple + snow + gateway + Kinnaur Spiti. IF: `traveler_type == FAMILY` THEN: Hatu Peak drive + Hatu Mata Temple + Tani Jubbar Lake boating + Kotgarh apple valley + Thanedar church + Stokes farm + apple picking Jul-Aug + snow playing Jan-Feb + deodar forest + meadows + Satluj valley + apple orchards + valley + meadows + snow + apple + family. Reason: Family snow + Hatu + lake + apple valley + church + farm + apple picking + snow playing + meadows + valley + snow + apple. IF: `traveler_type == HONEYMOON` THEN: Tethys Ski Resort / HPTDC Hatu / Kotgarh villas private cottage valley view + apple orchard + meadows + deodar + valley + snow Jan-Feb + private balcony + bonfire + Hatu private + Tani Jubbar private + Kotgarh private + Thanedar private + apple private + skiing private Jan-Feb + snow private + meadows private + valley + honeymoon + romantic + quiet + offbeat + snow + meadows. Reason: 1 offbeat honeymoon near Shimla + snow + meadows + apple orchard + valley view + Hatu + Tani Jubbar + Kotgarh + offbeat + quiet vs Shimla crowd + snow + meadows. IF: `traveler_type == ADVENTURE` THEN: Skiing Jan-Feb + snowboarding + Hatu Peak trek 7km + snow trek Jan-Feb + Tani Jubbar trek + Kotgarh trek + mountain biking + snow playing + deodar forest trek + meadows trek + Kinnaur Spiti trek + offroad + jeep + guide + snow boots + jacket + water + hat + early start 9 AM + moderate + hard + need fitness + offbeat + valley + meadows + snow + apple. Reason: Best skiing near Shimla + Hatu trek + snow trek + Tani Jubbar + Kotgarh + biking + snow + meadows + valley + offbeat.', 5801),
