  ('kausani', 23, 'accessibility', 'ACCESSIBILITY', NULL, NULL, 'wheelchair_accessibility: PARTIAL: public_transport_accessibility: VARIABLE: hotel_accessibility: MUST_BE_VERIFIED_PER_HOTEL: attraction_accessibility: MUST_BE_VERIFIED_PER_ATTRACTION: Rule: Never assume hill-destination accessibility from the destination score. Check:', 6132),
  ('kausani', 24, 'food', 'FOOD', NULL, NULL, 'Kausani is particularly strong for: Food experiences: Family: Choose clean restaurants, familiar North Indian options, simple meals, and predictable meal timings. Honeymoon: Prioritize one scenic mountain-view dinner with privacy and relaxed service. Luxury: Focus on curated Kumaoni cuisine, premium presentation, scenic dining, and private meals. Budget: Use local restaurants, homestays, simple thalis, tea stalls, and regional food for strong value.', 6133),
  ('kausani', 25, 'shopping', 'SHOPPING', NULL, NULL, 'Strong categories: Prefer: Kausani is better for **local products and handicrafts** than large-scale branded shopping.', 6134),
  ('kausani', 26, 'nightlife', 'NIGHTLIFE', NULL, NULL, 'nightlife_level: **38** Kausani is primarily a **quiet mountain destination**. Evening experiences focus on sunsets, stargazing, resort dining, bonfires, and peaceful walks rather than clubs and bars. Suitable for: Night experiences: Best areas: Not a primary requirement for: Family: Prefer early dinner, stargazing, resort activities, and quiet evenings. Honeymoon travelers should generally prefer: romantic mountain evening: over: late-night nightlife itinerary:', 6135),
  ('kausani', 28, 'sample-itinerary-patterns', 'SAMPLE ITINERARY PATTERNS', 'HALF-DAY – EXPRESS LAKE PROMENADE & MAA NAINA DEVI DARSHAN', NULL, 'Morning / Afternoon: Pickup from your hotel or meet near the Tallital Bus Stand → Begin with a peaceful stroll along the pedestrianized Mall Road promenade running alongside the emerald waters of Naini Lake → Visit the historic Shree Maa Naina Devi Temple on the northern shore of the lake to offer prayers and explore the sacred Shakti Peeth courtyard → Browse through the adjacent Tibetan Market (Bhotia Bazaar) to inspect hand-knitted winterwear, silver trinkets, and traditional Himalayan crafts → Conclude with a warm cup of Kumaoni tea and fresh steaming momos at a lakeside café in Mallital before returning to your hotel', 6136),
  ('kausani', 28, 'sample-itinerary-patterns', 'SAMPLE ITINERARY PATTERNS', '1 DAY – LAKESIDE HERITAGE, ROPEWAY & VIEWPOINT HIGHLIGHTS', NULL, 'Morning: Morning pickup from your hotel to experience Nainital’s iconic natural landmarks and alpine vistas → Head to the Mallital Ropeway Station and ride the Aerial Ropeway cable car up to Snow View Point (2,270 m) for sweeping panoramic views of Nanda Devi and Trishul peaks → Descend back to Mallital and walk to the iconic Naini Lake jetty to board a traditional wooden rowboat or paddleboat for a scenic ride across the water Afternoon: Board a local union taxi at Bara Pathar for a short drive up to Tiffin Top (Dorothy’s Seat) at 2,292 meters for 360-degree views of Nainital town and surrounding Kumaon hills → Continue to the family-friendly Eco Cave Gardens in Mallital to crawl through interconnected rocky, natural animal-shaped cave formations → Drive past the colonial-era Church of St. John in the Wilderness tucked away beneath towering pine trees Evening: Transfer to Mall Road during evening pedestrian-only hours when vehicular traffic is restricted → Stroll past heritage storefronts and specialty shops to purchase signature hand-poured decorative candles and local fruit preserves → Settle down for a authentic Kumaoni dinner featuring *Bhatt Ki Churkani* and *Aloo Ke Gutke* at an established restaurant along the lakefront', 6137),
  ('kausani', 28, 'sample-itinerary-patterns', 'SAMPLE ITINERARY PATTERNS', '2 DAYS – NAINITAL HERITAGE & THE GREAT LAKES CIRCUIT', NULL, 'Day 1: Full-day exploration of Nainital’s main attractions including the Maa Naina Devi Temple, Naini Lake rowboat ride, Aerial Ropeway to Snow View Point, and Eco Cave Gardens → Spend the late afternoon taking a guided tour of the colonial-era Raj Bhavan (Governor''s House), built in a Scottish Gothic castle style → Enjoy fine dining and a cozy evening bonfire at a heritage resort nestled on the Ayarpatta slopes Day 2: Early morning departure for a day-trip circuit exploring the surrounding Kumaon lakes and spiritual ashrams (~30 to 45-minute drive) → Drive to Bhimtal Lake, the largest lake in the district, to visit the unique island aquarium temple sitting in the middle of the water → Continue to Sattal (Seven Lakes) for a peaceful nature walk through pine woods and spot native Himalayan birds around the interconnected freshwater basins → Head to Naukuchiatal (Nine-Cornered Lake) for adventurous water sports or quiet lakeside relaxation → Visit the nearby Neem Karoli Baba Ashram at Kainchi Dham for quiet spiritual reflection before returning to Nainital in the late afternoon for departure transfers', 6138),
  ('kausani', 29, '6-days-and-5-nights-honeymoon-itinerary', '6 DAYS & 5 NIGHTS HONEYMOON ITINERARY', 'DAY 1 – ARRIVAL IN CORBETT & PRIVATE JUNGLE RESORT ESCAPE', NULL, 'Morning / Afternoon: Arrive at **Ramnagar Railway Station** or reach Corbett by private road transfer from Delhi → Meet your private chauffeur and proceed toward your luxury jungle resort around **Dhikuli/Dhela** → Complete check-in and settle into your private room or forest-view accommodation → Enjoy a relaxed lunch followed by private leisure time at the resort Evening: Take a peaceful walk around the resort''s landscaped surroundings → Enjoy a romantic sunset tea overlooking the forest landscape → Celebrate your first evening with a private candlelit dinner or intimate outdoor dining experience arranged by the resort', 6139),
  ('kausani', 29, '6-days-and-5-nights-honeymoon-itinerary', '6 DAYS & 5 NIGHTS HONEYMOON ITINERARY', 'DAY 2 – SUNRISE JEEP SAFARI & ROMANTIC FOREST RETREAT', 'honeymoon', 'Early Morning: Wake before sunrise and depart for a **private Jeep Safari** in an available zone such as Bijrani, Garjia, Jhirna or Dhela → Travel through dense Sal forests, grasslands and riverine habitats while searching for tiger, elephant, deer and other wildlife → Return to the resort for breakfast Afternoon: Spend the afternoon completely at leisure → Enjoy a couple''s spa treatment, private pool time or a relaxed forest-view lunch Evening: Head toward the **Kosi River/Garjiya landscape** for a scenic sunset experience → Return to the resort for a private dinner under the forest sky', 6140),
  ('kausani', 29, '6-days-and-5-nights-honeymoon-itinerary', '6 DAYS & 5 NIGHTS HONEYMOON ITINERARY', 'DAY 3 – TRANSFER TO DHIKALA & DEEP WILDERNESS EXPERIENCE', NULL, 'Morning: After breakfast, proceed toward **Dhangari Gate** for your Dhikala experience, subject to seasonal opening and confirmed accommodation/permit → Enter the reserve through the dramatic forest corridor leading toward **Dhikala** → Travel through Sal forests, open grasslands and river channels with panoramic views of the wilderness Lunch: Enjoy lunch at the Dhikala accommodation/restaurant facilities Afternoon: Explore the Dhikala landscape through the permitted safari experience → Spend time around **Dhikala Chaur**, where elephants, spotted deer and other wildlife are frequently encountered Evening: Return to your forest accommodation → Enjoy a quiet dinner and experience the atmosphere of staying inside the wilderness Dhikala currently operates seasonally and does not offer ordinary day-safari permits; visitors use the permitted canter or night-stay system.', 6141),
  ('kausani', 29, '6-days-and-5-nights-honeymoon-itinerary', '6 DAYS & 5 NIGHTS HONEYMOON ITINERARY', 'DAY 4 – DHIKALA WILDERNESS & RAMGANGA LANDSCAPES', NULL, 'Early Morning: Wake early for the day''s permitted wildlife experience around Dhikala → Explore the changing forest habitats around **Ramganga River**, grasslands and Sal forests → Keep the morning focused on wildlife photography and quiet observation Lunch: Return to the accommodation for lunch and rest Afternoon / Evening: Enjoy a slow afternoon within the Dhikala complex → Walk only along designated permitted areas and enjoy the forest surroundings → Watch the changing light over the grasslands before dinner → Overnight at Dhikala or transfer back according to your confirmed itinerary', 6142),
  ('kausani', 29, '6-days-and-5-nights-honeymoon-itinerary', '6 DAYS & 5 NIGHTS HONEYMOON ITINERARY', 'DAY 5 – GARJIYA TEMPLE, KOSI RIVER & COUPLE''S RELAXATION', 'honeymoon', 'Morning: Return toward the Dhikuli/Ramnagar resort area after breakfast → Visit **Garjiya Devi Temple** beside the Kosi River for blessings together → Spend quiet time photographing the riverside forest landscape Lunch: Return to your resort for a relaxed private lunch Afternoon: Enjoy the rest of the day without a fixed sightseeing schedule → Optional couple''s spa session, private pool, nature walk where permitted or in-resort activities Evening: Celebrate your final night with a specially arranged **private candlelit dinner** → Enjoy a quiet bonfire or stargazing experience where permitted by the property', 6143),
  ('kausani', 29, '6-days-and-5-nights-honeymoon-itinerary', '6 DAYS & 5 NIGHTS HONEYMOON ITINERARY', 'DAY 6 – CORBETT WATERFALLS & DEPARTURE', NULL, 'Morning: Enjoy a leisurely breakfast and complete checkout → Drive toward **Corbett Waterfalls** for a short forest excursion and photography stop → Continue toward **Kaladhungi** if departure timing permits → Optional visit to the **Corbett Museum** for a final glimpse into Jim Corbett''s conservation legacy Afternoon: Meet your private chauffeur for the transfer to **Ramnagar Railway Station** or onward road journey toward Delhi → Depart Corbett with a final view of the Himalayan foothills and forest landscape', 6144),
  ('kausani', 30, '6-days-and-5-nights-pilgrim-and-family-itinerary', '6 DAYS & 5 NIGHTS PILGRIM & FAMILY ITINERARY', 'DAY 1 – ARRIVAL IN RAMNAGAR & GARJIYA DEVI DARSHAN', NULL, 'Morning / Afternoon: Arrive at **Ramnagar Railway Station** and meet your private family vehicle → Transfer to your family-friendly resort around Dhikuli/Ramnagar → Complete check-in and enjoy lunch Evening: Visit **Garjiya Devi Temple**, situated beside the Kosi River → Offer family prayers and enjoy the peaceful riverside surroundings → Return to the resort for an early dinner and rest Uttarakhand Tourism specifically includes Garjiya Devi Temple as an early Corbett experience and identifies Ramnagar as the nearest railway station.', 6145),
  ('kausani', 30, '6-days-and-5-nights-pilgrim-and-family-itinerary', '6 DAYS & 5 NIGHTS PILGRIM & FAMILY ITINERARY', 'DAY 2 – FAMILY JEEP SAFARI & RESORT LEISURE', 'family', 'Early Morning: Depart for a family-friendly **Jeep Safari** in an available zone such as Bijrani, Garjia, Jhirna or Dhela → Explore the forest while looking for elephants, deer, birds, crocodiles and the elusive Bengal tiger → Return to the resort for breakfast and rest Lunch: Enjoy lunch at the resort Afternoon: Keep the afternoon relaxed for children and senior family members → Enjoy swimming, indoor games, nature activities or supervised resort experiences Evening: Family dinner followed by a quiet forest-themed evening', 6146),
  ('kausani', 30, '6-days-and-5-nights-pilgrim-and-family-itinerary', '6 DAYS & 5 NIGHTS PILGRIM & FAMILY ITINERARY', 'DAY 3 – CORBETT MUSEUM, WATERFALLS & LOCAL HERITAGE', NULL, 'Morning: After breakfast, drive toward **Kaladhungi** → Visit the **Corbett Museum** and learn about Jim Corbett''s life and his connection with the region Lunch: Enjoy lunch at a family-friendly restaurant or resort en route Afternoon: Continue toward **Corbett Waterfalls** → Take a short nature walk to the waterfall area and enjoy family photography → Return toward Ramnagar/Dhikuli before sunset Evening: Relax at the resort and enjoy an early family dinner Uttarakhand Tourism''s Corbett itinerary also combines safari, the Corbett Museum, birdwatching and Corbett Waterfall/Sitabani experiences.', 6147),
  ('kausani', 30, '6-days-and-5-nights-pilgrim-and-family-itinerary', '6 DAYS & 5 NIGHTS PILGRIM & FAMILY ITINERARY', 'DAY 4 – DHIKALA WILDERNESS EXPERIENCE', NULL, 'Morning: After an early breakfast, proceed toward **Dhangari Gate** for a Dhikala experience, subject to seasonal operation and confirmed booking → Enter the forest corridor toward Dhikala → Enjoy the spectacular combination of grasslands, Sal forests and Ramganga landscapes Afternoon: Have lunch at the forest accommodation/restaurant → Continue with the permitted **Dhikala canter or night-stay wildlife experience** → Observe elephants, spotted deer and other wildlife from designated safari areas Evening: Return to your accommodation or continue with the booked Dhikala night stay → Early dinner and rest Dhikala is currently listed by the reserve as open from **15 November to 15 June**, while its ordinary day safari is not available; seasonal rules should be checked for the exact travel date.', 6148),
  ('kausani', 30, '6-days-and-5-nights-pilgrim-and-family-itinerary', '6 DAYS & 5 NIGHTS PILGRIM & FAMILY ITINERARY', 'DAY 5 – BIRDWATCHING, KOSI RIVER & FAMILY LEISURE', 'family', 'Morning: Return toward the Dhikuli/Ramnagar area if staying inside Dhikala → Enjoy a gentle **Kosi River birdwatching** experience around suitable forest-edge areas → Dhikuli and the Kosi landscape are particularly suitable for relaxed birding and nature photography Lunch: Return to the resort for lunch Afternoon: Spend the afternoon at leisure → Optional supervised nature activities, swimming, indoor games and family recreation Evening: Enjoy a final family dinner and relaxed evening at the resort', 6149),
  ('kausani', 30, '6-days-and-5-nights-pilgrim-and-family-itinerary', '6 DAYS & 5 NIGHTS PILGRIM & FAMILY ITINERARY', 'DAY 6 – OPTIONAL SAFARI & DEPARTURE', NULL, 'Early Morning: Optional final **Jeep Safari** in Jhirna/Dhela or another zone operating on the travel date → Return to the resort for breakfast and checkout Late Morning: Spend remaining time shopping for permitted local handicrafts and souvenirs in the Ramnagar area → Meet your private vehicle for transfer to **Ramnagar Railway Station** or onward road journey Departure: Continue toward Delhi or your next Uttarakhand destination', 6150),
  ('kausani', 31, '6-days-and-5-nights-luxury-itinerary', '6 DAYS & 5 NIGHTS LUXURY ITINERARY', 'DAY 1 – VIP ARRIVAL & LUXURY JUNGLE RETREAT', 'luxury', 'Morning / Afternoon: Arrive at **Ramnagar Railway Station** or travel by premium private SUV from Delhi → Meet your dedicated chauffeur and transfer to an upscale jungle resort around **Dhikuli/Dhela/Kosi** → Complete a private check-in with welcome refreshments → Settle into your premium forest-view room, suite or private villa Lunch: Enjoy a curated lunch featuring North Indian and Kumaoni-inspired cuisine Evening: Relax beside the pool or enjoy a private spa session → Watch the sunset over the forest landscape → Conclude the evening with an exclusive candlelit dinner surrounded by the jungle atmosphere', 6151),
  ('kausani', 31, '6-days-and-5-nights-luxury-itinerary', '6 DAYS & 5 NIGHTS LUXURY ITINERARY', 'DAY 2 – PRIVATE JEEP SAFARI & FOREST FINE DINING', NULL, 'Early Morning: Depart in an authorized **private Jeep Safari** in the best available zone according to season and permit availability → Explore Sal forests, open grasslands and riverine habitats with a trained guide → Focus on wildlife photography and naturalist-led interpretation Breakfast: Return to the resort for a leisurely gourmet breakfast Afternoon: Enjoy a private wellness session, swimming or relaxation at the resort → Optional guided birdwatching around suitable forest-edge habitats Evening: Enjoy a private **forest-view sundowner** where permitted → Follow with a multi-course dinner featuring regional Kumaoni and North Indian flavours', 6152),
  ('kausani', 31, '6-days-and-5-nights-luxury-itinerary', '6 DAYS & 5 NIGHTS LUXURY ITINERARY', 'DAY 3 – PRIVATE TRANSFER TO DHIKALA WILDERNESS', NULL, 'Morning: After breakfast, travel by private vehicle toward **Dhangari Gate** → Enter the reserve for a confirmed **Dhikala night-stay experience**, subject to seasonal availability → Travel through one of Corbett''s most dramatic forest landscapes → Arrive at **Dhikala Forest Rest House** and complete check-in Dhikala''s historic forest rest house dates back to 1890 and overlooks the Ramganga landscape with the Kanda ridge in the background. Lunch: Enjoy lunch at the Dhikala restaurant facilities Afternoon: Take the permitted wildlife experience through the Dhikala landscape → Explore grasslands, Sal forests and river channels → Spend time photographing wildlife around Dhikala Chaur Evening: Return to the forest accommodation → Enjoy a quiet dinner and an immersive wilderness evening', 6153),
  ('kausani', 31, '6-days-and-5-nights-luxury-itinerary', '6 DAYS & 5 NIGHTS LUXURY ITINERARY', 'DAY 4 – EXCLUSIVE WILDERNESS & RAMGANGA LANDSCAPE', NULL, 'Early Morning: Wake before sunrise for the permitted Dhikala wildlife experience → Explore the forest corridors and open grasslands around the Ramganga landscape → Focus on wildlife photography, birdwatching and naturalist interpretation Breakfast / Lunch: Return to the forest accommodation for breakfast → Enjoy lunch followed by a slow afternoon within the Dhikala complex Evening: Spend the final evening inside the wilderness → Enjoy a quiet forest dinner and photography session from designated safe areas → Overnight at Dhikala or transfer according to the confirmed booking structure', 6154),
  ('kausani', 31, '6-days-and-5-nights-luxury-itinerary', '6 DAYS & 5 NIGHTS LUXURY ITINERARY', 'DAY 5 – GARJIYA TEMPLE, KOSI RIVER & PRIVATE RESORT INDULGENCE', NULL, 'Morning: Depart Dhikala after the permitted morning program and return toward Dhikuli → Visit **Garjiya Devi Temple** for a peaceful spiritual stop beside the Kosi River → Continue along the Kosi landscape for photography and scenic relaxation Lunch: Check back into your luxury resort and enjoy a private gourmet lunch Afternoon: Reserve the afternoon exclusively for relaxation → Private spa treatment → Poolside leisure → Forest-view tea → Optional guided birdwatching Evening: Enjoy a bespoke **private dining experience** with a curated Kumaoni-inspired menu → End the evening with a private bonfire or stargazing arrangement where permitted', 6155),
  ('kausani', 31, '6-days-and-5-nights-luxury-itinerary', '6 DAYS & 5 NIGHTS LUXURY ITINERARY', 'DAY 6 – CORBETT HERITAGE, WATERFALLS & VIP DEPARTURE', NULL, 'Morning: Enjoy a final leisurely breakfast → Check out and proceed toward **Kaladhungi** → Visit the **Corbett Museum** for a final heritage experience connected with Jim Corbett → Continue to **Corbett Waterfalls** for a short scenic nature stop if departure timing allows Lunch: Enjoy a final regional lunch en route Afternoon: Board your premium private SUV for the onward journey → Transfer to **Ramnagar Railway Station**, Delhi, or your next Uttarakhand destination → Depart Corbett after completing your luxury wildlife and wilderness retreat', 6156),
