  ('guwahati', 19, 'honeymoon-travel', 'HONEYMOON TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, '***honeymoon_score:*** ***86*** ***privacy_score:*** ***84*** ***luxury_score:*** ***78*** ***Recommended:*** ***Honeymoon itinerary should NOT contain more than:*** ***2–3 major activities/day.*** Prefer: ***River + culture + dining*** over: ***Continuous city sightseeing.***', 6851),
  ('guwahati', 20, 'luxury-travel', 'LUXURY TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, '***luxury_score:*** ***78*** ***Recommended:*** Luxury here primarily means:', 6852),
  ('guwahati', 21, 'adventure', 'ADVENTURE', NULL, NULL, '***adventure_score:*** ***76*** Guwahati is a ***soft-adventure and gateway destination*** rather than a dedicated adventure base. ***Adventure experiences:*** ***Strongest adventure zones:*** ***Brahmaputra + Deepor Beel + Pobitora + wider Assam***', 6853),
  ('guwahati', 22, 'senior-travel', 'SENIOR TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, '***senior_suitability:*** ***84*** ***walking_intensity:*** ***LOW → MEDIUM*** ***Rules:*** ***Easier options:*** ***Avoid:***', 6854),
  ('guwahati', 23, 'accessibility', 'ACCESSIBILITY', NULL, NULL, '***wheelchair_accessibility:*** ***LIMITED → MODERATE*** ***public_transport_accessibility:*** ***VARIABLE*** ***hotel_accessibility:*** ***VERIFY_PER_HOTEL*** ***attraction_accessibility:*** ***VERIFY_PER_ATTRACTION*** ***Rule:*** Do not assume accessibility at ***temples, river islands, wetlands or older heritage buildings***. ***Check:***', 6855),
  ('guwahati', 24, 'food', 'FOOD', NULL, NULL, 'Guwahati is strongest for: ***Food experiences:*** ***Budget:*** Local eateries. ***Premium:*** Hotel dining.', 6856),
  ('guwahati', 25, 'shopping', 'SHOPPING', NULL, NULL, '***Strong categories:*** ***Prefer:*** Shopping is ***moderate-to-strong***, particularly for Assamese textiles, silk, handicrafts and tea.', 6857),
  ('guwahati', 26, 'nightlife', 'NIGHTLIFE', NULL, NULL, '***nightlife_level:*** ***55*** Guwahati has ***moderate urban nightlife***, stronger than most Northeast gateway towns but not comparable with India''s major metropolitan nightlife hubs. ***Suitable for:*** ***Night experiences:*** ***Best for:*** ***Relaxed urban evenings*** rather than: ***Major club-focused nightlife.***', 6858),
  ('guwahati', 28, 'sample-itinerary-patterns', 'SAMPLE ITINERARY PATTERNS', 'HALF-DAY – BHALUKPONG NATURE & ORCHID ESCAPE', NULL, 'Morning / Afternoon: Pickup from Tezpur/Guwahati and drive toward **Bhalukpong** → Explore the **Kameng River** and enjoy the scenic foothill landscape → Visit **Bhalukpong Fort ruins**, associated with King Bhaluka → Continue to **Tipi Orchid Research Centre**, approximately 5 km from Bhalukpong → Explore the orchid museum and surrounding botanical landscape → Continue toward Bomdila or return to Bhalukpong for overnight stay', 6859),
  ('guwahati', 28, 'sample-itinerary-patterns', 'SAMPLE ITINERARY PATTERNS', '1 DAY – BHALUKPONG, TIPI & KAMENG HIGHLIGHTS', NULL, 'Morning: Arrive at Bhalukpong → Complete Arunachal entry formalities → Visit **Bhalukpong Fort ruins** → Spend time beside the **Kameng River** Afternoon: Drive to **Tipi Orchid Research Centre** → Explore orchids, museum and natural surroundings → Enjoy lunch at a local restaurant Evening: Relax at the hotel → Prepare for the onward **Bomdila–Dirang–Tawang** journey', 6860),
  ('guwahati', 28, 'sample-itinerary-patterns', 'SAMPLE ITINERARY PATTERNS', '2 DAYS – BHALUKPONG & WEST KAMENG INTRODUCTION', NULL, 'Day 1: → Arrive at Bhalukpong → Kameng River → Bhalukpong Fort → Tipi Orchid Research Centre → Overnight in Bhalukpong Day 2: → Drive toward **Bomdila** → Stop at scenic viewpoints and forest landscapes → Explore **Bomdila Monastery, craft centres and local cultural areas** → Continue toward Dirang if road and weather conditions permit', 6861),
  ('guwahati', 28, 'sample-itinerary-patterns', 'SAMPLE ITINERARY PATTERNS', '3 DAYS – BHALUKPONG–BOMDILA–DIRANG CIRCUIT', NULL, 'Day 1: → Tezpur/Guwahati → Bhalukpong → Kameng River → Bhalukpong Fort → Tipi Orchid Centre Day 2: → Bhalukpong → Bomdila → Bomdila Monastery → Craft Centre and local cultural exploration Day 3: → Bomdila → Dirang → Dirang Dzong → Hot Water Spring → Sangti Valley / orchard landscapes → Overnight in Dirang Official Arunachal Tourism identifies **hot springs, apple and kiwi orchards, Sangti Valley and the Yak Research Centre** among Dirang''s major attractions.', 6862),
  ('guwahati', 28, 'sample-itinerary-patterns', 'SAMPLE ITINERARY PATTERNS', '5 DAYS – BHALUKPONG–DIRANG–TAWANG EXPRESS CIRCUIT', NULL, 'Day 1: Guwahati → Kamakhya Temple → Bhalukpong Day 2: Bhalukpong → Tipi → Bomdila → Dirang Day 3: Dirang → Sela Pass → Tawang Day 4: Full-day Tawang sightseeing Day 5: Tawang → Dirang/Bomdila onward Travel-agent note: This is an **express mountain circuit**. A longer trip is preferable because the road journey between destinations is substantial and high-altitude conditions can affect travel times.', 6863),
  ('guwahati', 29, '6-days-and-5-nights-honeymoon-itinerary', '6 DAYS & 5 NIGHTS HONEYMOON ITINERARY', 'DAY 1 – GUWAHATI PILGRIMAGE & BHALUKPONG ARRIVAL', NULL, 'Morning: Arrive at **Guwahati** → Visit **Kamakhya Temple** for a spiritual beginning to the journey Afternoon: Private chauffeur-driven transfer toward **Bhalukpong** → Enjoy scenic Assam-to-Arunachal landscapes Evening: Check into a comfortable riverside/nature-oriented stay → Relax beside the **Kameng River** → Private dinner and overnight stay in Bhalukpong', 6864),
  ('guwahati', 29, '6-days-and-5-nights-honeymoon-itinerary', '6 DAYS & 5 NIGHTS HONEYMOON ITINERARY', 'DAY 2 – BHALUKPONG NATURE & BOMDILA ROMANCE', NULL, 'Morning: Breakfast and visit **Bhalukpong Fort ruins** → Continue to **Tipi Orchid Research Centre** → Enjoy couple photography among the orchid gardens Afternoon: Drive toward **Bomdila** → Scenic Himalayan road journey → Check into a comfortable mountain hotel Evening: Visit **Bomdila Monastery** → Enjoy sunset mountain views → Romantic dinner and overnight stay Bomdila is recognised by Arunachal Tourism for its monasteries, craft centres, ethnographic attractions and Himalayan views.', 6865),
  ('guwahati', 29, '6-days-and-5-nights-honeymoon-itinerary', '6 DAYS & 5 NIGHTS HONEYMOON ITINERARY', 'DAY 3 – BOMDILA, DIRANG & VALLEY ROMANCE', NULL, 'Morning: Drive from Bomdila to **Dirang** → Stop at scenic mountain viewpoints → Visit **Dirang Dzong** Afternoon: Explore **Dirang Valley** → Visit the **hot water springs** → Continue toward **Sangti Valley** → Enjoy a relaxed lunch surrounded by mountain scenery Evening: Return to your hotel → Private couple''s dinner → Quiet mountain evening and overnight stay', 6866),
  ('guwahati', 29, '6-days-and-5-nights-honeymoon-itinerary', '6 DAYS & 5 NIGHTS HONEYMOON ITINERARY', 'DAY 4 – DIRANG TO TAWANG HIGH-ALTITUDE JOURNEY', NULL, 'Early Morning: Depart Dirang for **Tawang** → Cross the spectacular **Sela Pass** → Stop at **Sela Lake** for photography → Continue through dramatic Himalayan landscapes Afternoon: Arrive in **Tawang** → Check into your hotel → Rest and acclimatise Evening: Enjoy a quiet dinner → Avoid excessive sightseeing after the high-altitude ascent Tawang is situated at approximately **3,500 metres**, making a slower first evening after arrival particularly sensible.', 6867),
  ('guwahati', 29, '6-days-and-5-nights-honeymoon-itinerary', '6 DAYS & 5 NIGHTS HONEYMOON ITINERARY', 'DAY 5 – TAWANG MONASTERY & ROMANTIC HIMALAYAN DAY', 'honeymoon', 'Morning: Visit **Tawang Monastery** → Explore its Buddhist architecture, prayer halls and cultural atmosphere Afternoon: Visit selected nearby viewpoints and lakes depending on road/weather conditions → Enjoy lunch in Tawang → Return to the hotel for rest Evening: Enjoy a private mountain-view dinner → Couple photography → Relaxed final Himalayan evening', 6868),
  ('guwahati', 29, '6-days-and-5-nights-honeymoon-itinerary', '6 DAYS & 5 NIGHTS HONEYMOON ITINERARY', 'DAY 6 – TAWANG → DIRANG/BOMDILA & DEPARTURE', NULL, 'Early Morning: Begin the return journey from Tawang → Drive through the Himalayan mountain corridor toward **Dirang/Bomdila** Afternoon: Continue toward the Assam side → Depending on road conditions and onward connection, proceed toward **Guwahati/Tezpur** Evening: Continue to your onward destination → Departure Honeymoon style: Keep the trip focused on **scenery + privacy + mountain experiences**, rather than attempting too many attractions each day.', 6869),
  ('guwahati', 30, '6-days-and-5-nights-family-itinerary', '6 DAYS & 5 NIGHTS FAMILY ITINERARY', 'DAY 1 – GUWAHATI, KAMAKHYA & BHALUKPONG', NULL, 'Morning: Arrive at **Guwahati** → Visit **Kamakhya Temple** Afternoon: Begin private family transfer toward **Bhalukpong** → Stop for refreshments during the journey Evening: Check into hotel → Relax beside the **Kameng River** → Family dinner and overnight stay', 6870),
  ('guwahati', 30, '6-days-and-5-nights-family-itinerary', '6 DAYS & 5 NIGHTS FAMILY ITINERARY', 'DAY 2 – BHALUKPONG & TIPI ORCHIDS', NULL, 'Morning: Visit **Bhalukpong Fort ruins** → Explore the surrounding foothill landscape → Continue to **Tipi Orchid Research Centre** Afternoon: Explore the orchid museum and botanical surroundings → Family lunch → Enjoy relaxed time around the Kameng River Evening: Return to hotel → Indoor/family leisure → Early dinner and overnight stay Tipi is approximately **5 km from Bhalukpong** and is one of the principal attractions on the official Bhalukpong circuit.', 6871),
  ('guwahati', 30, '6-days-and-5-nights-family-itinerary', '6 DAYS & 5 NIGHTS FAMILY ITINERARY', 'DAY 3 – BHALUKPONG → BOMDILA → DIRANG', NULL, 'Morning: Depart Bhalukpong after breakfast → Drive toward **Bomdila** → Visit **Bomdila Monastery** → Explore local craft and cultural areas Afternoon: Continue toward **Dirang** → Check into family accommodation → Visit **Dirang Valley** Evening: Relax at the hotel → Family dinner → Overnight in Dirang', 6872),
  ('guwahati', 30, '6-days-and-5-nights-family-itinerary', '6 DAYS & 5 NIGHTS FAMILY ITINERARY', 'DAY 4 – DIRANG → TAWANG', NULL, 'Early Morning: Depart Dirang → Cross **Sela Pass** → Stop at Sela Lake for photographs → Continue toward Tawang Afternoon: Arrive in **Tawang** → Check into hotel → Lunch and rest Evening: Short local walk if the family feels comfortable → Early dinner → Overnight in Tawang Family rule: Do not overload the first Tawang evening because of the significant elevation change.', 6873),
  ('guwahati', 30, '6-days-and-5-nights-family-itinerary', '6 DAYS & 5 NIGHTS FAMILY ITINERARY', 'DAY 5 – TAWANG FAMILY SIGHTSEEING', 'family', 'Morning: Visit **Tawang Monastery** → Explore the monastery complex at a comfortable pace Afternoon: Visit selected accessible local viewpoints → Lunch in Tawang → Return to hotel for rest Evening: Family dinner → Enjoy the mountain atmosphere → Pack for the return journey', 6874),
  ('guwahati', 30, '6-days-and-5-nights-family-itinerary', '6 DAYS & 5 NIGHTS FAMILY ITINERARY', 'DAY 6 – TAWANG → BOMDILA/DIRANG → ASSAM', NULL, 'Early Morning: Begin return journey → Drive through **Dirang–Bomdila–Bhalukpong** Afternoon: Continue toward **Tezpur/Guwahati** → Meal and rest stop en route Evening: Arrive in Guwahati/Tezpur according to onward connection → Departure Family style: Prioritise **comfortable road travel + fewer stops + adequate rest** rather than trying to cover every attraction.', 6875),
  ('guwahati', 31, '6-days-and-5-nights-luxury-itinerary', '6 DAYS & 5 NIGHTS LUXURY ITINERARY', 'DAY 1 – VIP GUWAHATI ARRIVAL & BHALUKPONG RETREAT', NULL, 'Morning: VIP arrival at **Guwahati** → Private chauffeur-driven premium SUV → Visit **Kamakhya Temple** Afternoon: Private transfer toward Bhalukpong → Curated roadside lunch → Continue through the Assam–Arunachal foothills Evening: Private check-in at a premium nature-oriented property → Welcome refreshments → Riverside relaxation beside the **Kameng River** → Private dinner', 6876),
  ('guwahati', 31, '6-days-and-5-nights-luxury-itinerary', '6 DAYS & 5 NIGHTS LUXURY ITINERARY', 'DAY 2 – PRIVATE BHALUKPONG & BOMDILA EXPERIENCE', NULL, 'Morning: Private guided visit to **Bhalukpong Fort** → Continue to **Tipi Orchid Research Centre** → Dedicated nature and photography experience Afternoon: Private chauffeur transfer toward **Bomdila** → Scenic mountain lunch → Check into premium mountain accommodation Evening: Private visit to **Bomdila Monastery** → Sunset Himalayan photography → Curated regional dinner', 6877),
  ('guwahati', 31, '6-days-and-5-nights-luxury-itinerary', '6 DAYS & 5 NIGHTS LUXURY ITINERARY', 'DAY 3 – BOMDILA → DIRANG PRIVATE VALLEY EXPERIENCE', NULL, 'Morning: Leisurely breakfast → Private drive toward **Dirang** → Scenic stops along the mountain route Afternoon: Explore **Dirang Dzong** → Visit the **Dirang Hot Water Spring** → Continue toward **Sangti Valley** → Private lunch overlooking the valley Evening: Return to premium accommodation → Spa/wellness or private relaxation → Curated Arunachali dinner', 6878),
  ('guwahati', 31, '6-days-and-5-nights-luxury-itinerary', '6 DAYS & 5 NIGHTS LUXURY ITINERARY', 'DAY 4 – PRIVATE SELA PASS & TAWANG ARRIVAL', NULL, 'Early Morning: Premium SUV departure from Dirang → Drive toward **Sela Pass** → Private photography stops at **Sela Lake** → Continue through the high-altitude Himalayan landscape Afternoon: Arrive in **Tawang** → Premium hotel check-in → Lunch and extended acclimatisation Evening: Private in-hotel dinner → Mountain-view relaxation Luxury rule: Keep Day 4 intentionally light after the major elevation gain.', 6879),
  ('guwahati', 31, '6-days-and-5-nights-luxury-itinerary', '6 DAYS & 5 NIGHTS LUXURY ITINERARY', 'DAY 5 – PRIVATE TAWANG CULTURAL EXPERIENCE', NULL, 'Morning: Private guided visit to **Tawang Monastery** → Explore Buddhist architecture and Monpa cultural heritage Afternoon: Private sightseeing around selected Tawang viewpoints and natural attractions → Curated lunch → Return to hotel → Spa/wellness or suite relaxation Evening: Private farewell dinner → Mountain-view setting → Optional cultural experience', 6880),
  ('guwahati', 31, '6-days-and-5-nights-luxury-itinerary', '6 DAYS & 5 NIGHTS LUXURY ITINERARY', 'DAY 6 – PRIVATE RETURN & VIP DEPARTURE', NULL, 'Early Morning: Private SUV departure from Tawang → Scenic return through **Dirang → Bomdila → Bhalukpong** Afternoon: Continue toward **Tezpur/Guwahati** → Premium lunch stop → Arrive in Guwahati according to onward flight schedule Evening: Private airport transfer → VIP departure Luxury positioning: The emphasis should be on **premium vehicle + quality accommodation + private guiding + slower pacing**, rather than adding excessive sightseeing. Planning note: The official Arunachal Tourism circuit itself covers **Tezpur–Bhalukpong–Bomdila–Tawang** and describes it as a roughly **350 km circuit**. Because this is mountainous terrain, these 6-day versions are intentionally structured as an **express circuit**; for a genuinely relaxed honeymoon, family or luxury experience, adding 1–2 nights is preferable.', 6881),
  ('guwahati', 32, 'travel-agent-insights', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS', 'What inexperienced planners often do wrong', NULL, '', 6882),
  ('guwahati', 32, 'travel-agent-insights', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS', 'What an experienced planner does differently', NULL, '', 6883),
  ('guwahati', 32, 'travel-agent-insights', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS', 'Best planning rule', NULL, '', 6884),
  ('guwahati', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', NULL, NULL, '***IF:*** `trip_length <= 1 day` ***THEN:*** Treat Guwahati as a **gateway city + culture + riverfront express**: prioritise **Kamakhya Temple, Umananda Temple, Assam State Museum and Brahmaputra River cruise**; add **Navagraha Temple** if time permits. ***Reason:*** Guwahati''s strongest short-visit combination is **spiritual heritage + Assamese culture + Brahmaputra scenery**, with several major attractions accessible from the city. ***IF:*** `trip_length == 3 days` ***THEN:*** Build a classic **Guwahati culture + spirituality + nature circuit** with **Kamakhya Temple, Umananda Temple, Assam State Museum, Assam State Zoo, Navagraha Temple and Brahmaputra River cruise**, keeping one flexible period for local exploration. ***Reason:*** Three days allow travellers to experience Guwahati''s **temples, museums, river landscape, wildlife and Assamese urban culture** without excessive rushing. ***IF:*** `trip_length >= 5 days` ***THEN:*** Expand Guwahati into an **Assam gateway circuit**, combining **Guwahati, Sualkuchi, Hajo, Pobitora Wildlife Sanctuary and selected destinations toward Kaziranga or Shillong**, rather than keeping the entire stay inside the city. ***Reason:*** Guwahati works best as a **regional gateway and base** for exploring Lower Assam, the Brahmaputra Valley and nearby Northeast destinations. ***IF:*** `trip_type == FIRST_TIME_VISITOR` ***THEN:*** Build the itinerary around **Kamakhya Temple, Brahmaputra River cruise, Umananda Temple, Assam State Museum and Navagraha Temple**, adding **Assam State Zoo** if time allows. ***Reason:*** These provide the strongest introduction to Guwahati''s **spiritual identity, Assamese heritage, river landscape and urban culture**. ***IF:*** `trip_type == HONEYMOON` ***THEN:*** Choose a **comfortable riverside or premium city stay**, arrange **private transport**, and prioritise **Brahmaputra sunset cruise, Umananda Island, Kamakhya Temple, scenic dining and relaxed evenings**. ***Reason:*** Guwahati''s romantic appeal comes from **river views, sunsets, private experiences and convenient premium hospitality**, rather than traditional hill-station scenery. ***IF:*** `traveler_type == FAMILY` ***THEN:*** Base the family in a **comfortable city hotel**, use **private transport**, and prioritise **Assam State Zoo, Brahmaputra cruise, Kamakhya Temple, Umananda Temple and regional museums**. ***Reason:*** Guwahati offers a useful combination of **education, wildlife, spirituality, sightseeing and easy urban access** for families. ***IF:*** `traveler_type == LUXURY` ***THEN:*** Select the **best available premium hotel**, arrange a **chauffeur-driven vehicle and curated guide**, and emphasise **private river experiences, premium Assamese dining, heritage sightseeing and seamless airport/rail transfers**. ***Reason:*** Guwahati has the Northeast''s stronger urban hospitality infrastructure, making it more suitable for **business-class and premium travel** than many smaller regional destinations. ***IF:*** `traveler_type == BUDGET` ***THEN:*** Stay around **Paltan Bazaar, Pan Bazaar or central Guwahati**, choose **budget hotels/guesthouses**, use public transport or app-based taxis where practical, and prioritise **Kamakhya Temple, Umananda Temple, museums and riverfront experiences**. ***Reason:*** Guwahati''s core attractions can be explored relatively economically; the main budget pressure comes from **private vehicles and longer excursions outside the city**. ***IF:*** `traveler_interest == NATURE` ***THEN:*** Prioritise **Brahmaputra riverfront, Deepor Beel, Assam State Zoo and nearby nature destinations**, adding **Pobitora Wildlife Sanctuary** for a dedicated wildlife excursion. ***Reason:*** Guwahati combines **riverine landscapes, wetlands, forested surroundings and accessible wildlife areas** within and around the city. ***IF:*** `traveler_interest == ADVENTURE` ***THEN:*** Add **river cruises, nearby trekking/hiking, cycling, wildlife safaris and day excursions to surrounding natural areas**, depending on season and operating conditions. ***Reason:*** Guwahati itself is primarily a **gateway and cultural city**, while its surrounding region provides stronger opportunities for outdoor adventure. ***IF:*** `traveler_type == SENIOR` ***THEN:*** Choose a **centrally located comfortable hotel**, use **private transport**, prioritise **Kamakhya Temple, museums, Umananda Temple, river views and easy sightseeing**, and avoid unnecessarily long day excursions. ***Reason:*** Guwahati is relatively accessible, but **temple steps, heat, traffic and long regional drives** should be considered when pacing the itinerary. ***IF:*** `traveler_type == TRANSIT` ***THEN:*** Use Guwahati as a **1-night gateway stop**, prioritising **Kamakhya Temple + Brahmaputra riverfront/cruise** or **Umananda Temple**, then continue toward the next Northeast destination. ***Reason:*** Guwahati is one of the Northeast''s principal **air, rail and road gateways**, making short stays particularly practical. ***IF:*** `traveler_interest == HISTORY` ***THEN:*** Prioritise **Assam State Museum, Kamakhya Temple, Umananda Temple, Navagraha Temple and regional heritage sites**, adding **Sualkuchi or Hajo** for a wider historical-cultural excursion. ***Reason:*** Guwahati combines **ancient temple traditions, Ahom-era heritage, Assamese culture and the historical importance of the Brahmaputra Valley**. ***IF:*** `traveler_interest == WELLNESS` ***THEN:*** Choose a **quiet premium or riverside stay**, reduce daily transfers and focus on **river views, temple visits, wellness facilities, Assamese cuisine and relaxed evenings**. ***Reason:*** Guwahati''s wellness strength is primarily based on **comfortable hospitality, river ambience and slower cultural experiences**, rather than mountain-style wellness retreats. ***IF:*** `season == SUMMER` ***THEN:*** Prioritise **early-morning temples, museums, indoor cultural attractions and evening Brahmaputra experiences**, keeping the hottest afternoon hours flexible. ***Reason:*** Guwahati can become **hot and humid during the warmer months**, so sightseeing is more comfortable in the morning and late afternoon. ***IF:*** `season == MONSOON` ***THEN:*** Treat Guwahati as a **flexible city-and-culture destination**, keep **rain and traffic buffers**, and confirm conditions before planning excursions to wetlands or wildlife areas. ***Reason:*** Heavy rainfall can affect **road travel, river activities and surrounding low-lying areas**, making flexible scheduling important. ***IF:*** `traveler_interest == FOOD` ***THEN:*** Build an **Assamese food experience** around **khar, tenga, pitha, duck preparations, freshwater fish, pork dishes, Assamese thali and local tea**, using established local restaurants and traditional eateries. ***Reason:*** Guwahati is one of the best places to experience **Assamese cuisine alongside broader Northeast Indian food traditions**. ***IF:*** `traveler_interest == SHOPPING` ***THEN:*** Prioritise **Assamese silk, especially Muga and Paat silk, traditional textiles, bamboo/cane crafts, tea and local handicrafts**, with **Sualkuchi** added for a dedicated silk experience. ***Reason:*** Shopping is a **strong supporting attraction** in Guwahati, particularly for **Assamese textiles, tea and handicrafts**. ***IF:*** `traveler_interest == PHOTOGRAPHY` ***THEN:*** Prioritise **Brahmaputra River, Umananda Island, Kamakhya Temple, Deepor Beel, sunset river cruises, Assamese markets and traditional architecture**. ***Reason:*** Guwahati provides strong photographic variety through **river landscapes, temples, wetlands, culture, markets and dramatic evening light**. ***IF:*** `trip_type == CULTURAL` ***THEN:*** Combine **Kamakhya Temple + Umananda Temple + Assam State Museum + Navagraha Temple** with **Sualkuchi, Hajo or local Assamese cultural experiences**. ***Reason:*** Guwahati provides a strong introduction to **Assamese religious traditions, textiles, crafts, history and Brahmaputra Valley culture**. ***IF:*** `trip_type == WILDLIFE_EXPERIENCE` ***THEN:*** Use Guwahati as a **wildlife gateway**, prioritising **Deepor Beel and Assam State Zoo**, then add **Pobitora Wildlife Sanctuary** or continue toward **Kaziranga National Park** for a dedicated safari itinerary. ***Reason:*** Guwahati offers accessible nature experiences, while **Pobitora and Kaziranga provide substantially stronger dedicated wildlife and safari experiences**. ***IF:*** `trip_type == ASSAM_CIRCUIT` ***THEN:*** Allocate **2–3 days around Guwahati** before continuing toward **Sualkuchi → Hajo → Pobitora → Kaziranga**, depending on the overall trip length. ***Reason:*** Guwahati functions naturally as the **principal gateway for an Assam itinerary**, allowing travellers to combine urban culture with wildlife, heritage and rural experiences. ***IF:*** `permit_required == TRUE` ***THEN:*** Confirm the applicable **entry, wildlife-sanctuary and protected-area requirements** before travelling, particularly when adding destinations outside Guwahati. ***Reason:*** Requirements can vary by **destination and activity**, especially for protected wildlife areas, so advance verification prevents disruptions. ***IF:*** `route_to_other_northeast == TRUE` ***THEN:*** Treat Guwahati as the **major Northeast gateway**, allowing sufficient time for **airport/rail transfers, traffic, weather and regional road conditions** before onward travel to Assam, Meghalaya, Arunachal Pradesh or other Northeast destinations. ***Reason:*** Guwahati is strategically positioned as a **transport hub**, but onward mountain and regional journeys can take substantially longer than expected.', 6885),
  ('guwahati', 34, 'destination-scoring', 'DESTINATION SCORING', NULL, NULL, '| Factor | Score | | ------------------ | ----: | | Family | 91 | | Honeymoon | 86 | | Luxury | 89 | | Budget | 88 | | Adventure | 76 | | Culture | 95 | | Food | 94 | | Shopping | 86 | | Nightlife | 73 | | Relaxation | 79 | | Nature | 89 | | Accessibility | 92 | | Safety | 86 | | First-time visitor | 96 | | Photography | 94 |', 6886),
  ('guwahati', 35, 'final-travel-agent-verdict', 'FINAL TRAVEL AGENT VERDICT', NULL, NULL, '****Best for:**** Families, couples, honeymooners, culture enthusiasts, food lovers, history seekers, photographers, spiritual travellers, business travellers, budget travellers, and first-time visitors to Assam looking for a ****convenient gateway to Northeast India with strong cultural, religious, riverfront and urban experiences****. Guwahati is particularly strong for travellers who want a combination of ****Kamakhya Temple, Brahmaputra River experiences, Assamese culture, wildlife gateways, local food, shopping and easy onward connectivity****. ****Best duration:**** ****2–3 days**** for a focused Guwahati experience covering ****Kamakhya Temple, Umananda Temple, Brahmaputra River cruise, Assam State Museum and local markets****; ****4–5 days**** for a deeper experience adding ****Deepor Beel, Basistha Ashram, Srimanta Sankardev Kalakshetra and nearby nature experiences****. For a broader ****Assam/Northeast circuit****, allow ****7–12 days**** to combine Guwahati with destinations such as ****Kaziranga, Shillong, Cherrapunji or Majuli****. ****Best season:**** ****October–April**** for the strongest overall combination of comfortable weather, sightseeing, river experiences and onward Northeast travel. ****October–November**** is particularly good for clear-weather sightseeing and cultural exploration. ****December–February**** offers cooler conditions and is excellent for combining Guwahati with wildlife destinations. ****March–April**** brings pleasant weather and spring landscapes. The ****monsoon period (June–September)**** can bring heavy rainfall and occasional flooding, so flexible planning is advisable. ****Best stay:**** A combination of ****business hotels, boutique hotels, luxury properties, mid-range hotels and budget guesthouses**** depending on travel style. Guwahati has a considerably stronger accommodation base than smaller destinations in Assam, making it suitable for ****budget through premium travel****. For convenience, choose accommodation around ****Paltan Bazaar, Pan Bazaar, GS Road, Dispur or central Guwahati**** according to sightseeing and transport requirements. ****Best transport:**** ****Private car/taxi**** is the most convenient option for families, honeymooners and travellers combining Guwahati with nearby destinations. ****App-based taxis, auto-rickshaws and city buses**** are useful for local movement, while ****trains and buses**** provide economical onward connectivity. Guwahati''s major advantage is its role as a ****transport gateway to Assam and the wider Northeast****, with railway, road and air connections. ****Must-do:**** ****Avoid:**** ****Biggest advantage:**** An exceptional combination of ****spiritual heritage, Brahmaputra River experiences, Assamese culture, food, shopping, urban convenience and Northeast connectivity****. Guwahati''s greatest strength is its position as the ****principal gateway to Assam and one of the most important access points to Northeast India****, while still offering substantial experiences through ****Kamakhya Temple, Umananda, the Brahmaputra, museums, cultural centres and wetlands****. ****Biggest disadvantage:**** Guwahati''s ****traffic congestion, humid climate, urban character and relatively limited traditional sightseeing compared with destinations such as Kaziranga or Shillong**** can make it less appealing for travellers seeking a purely scenic or resort-style holiday. The city can also feel busy and commercial, particularly around central markets and major transport corridors. Guwahati therefore works best as a ****culture + spirituality + river + food + Northeast gateway destination**** rather than a long-stay nature resort. ****Overall destination score:**** ****89/100****', 6887),
  ('guwahati', 36, 'data-quality', 'DATA QUALITY', NULL, NULL, 'information_completeness: 92/100 last_updated: 2026-09-05 last_verified: NOT_LIVE_VERIFIED verified_by: TRAVEL_ENGINE_INITIAL_DATASET sources: IMPORTANT: Prices, opening hours, schedules, visa requirements, availability, accessibility and operational conditions must NOT be treated as permanently valid from this document. These must be sourced from structured, refreshable data.', 6888),
  ('lucknow', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Spring', NULL, 'months: March April May weather: March is warm and highly suitable for sightseeing, while April becomes increasingly hot and May is frequently very hot with intense afternoon conditions. crowd_level: MEDIUM → LOW price_level: MEDIUM → LOW overall_score: 70.00–75.33 recommended: true_with_heat_planning reason: March provides one of the strongest sightseeing balances, while April and especially May gain crowd and price value but lose weather points because of rising temperatures. Best for:', 6889),
  ('lucknow', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Summer', NULL, 'months: June July August weather: June is generally extremely hot before the monsoon becomes established. July and August bring monsoon rainfall, high humidity, cloud cover and occasional disruption from intense rain. crowd_level: LOW price_level: LOW → VERY_LOW overall_score: 65.33–73.67 recommended: true_with_careful_planning reason: Summer and monsoon months benefit from lower visitor pressure and strong hotel value, but heat, humidity and rainfall substantially reduce outdoor sightseeing comfort. Best for:', 6890),
  ('lucknow', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Autumn', NULL, 'months: September October November weather: September remains humid after the monsoon, while October becomes considerably drier and more comfortable. November is one of Lucknow''s most pleasant months with warm days and cooler evenings. crowd_level: MEDIUM → HIGH price_level: MEDIUM overall_score: 71.67–77.33 recommended: true reason: Post-monsoon conditions steadily improve, making October and November especially attractive for heritage sightseeing, walking, food exploration and photography despite stronger seasonal demand. Best for:', 6891),
  ('lucknow', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Winter', NULL, 'months: December January February weather: Cool to mild days and cold nights create the strongest overall sightseeing conditions, although December and January can experience fog, low morning visibility and occasional transport disruption. crowd_level: MEDIUM → HIGH price_level: MEDIUM overall_score: 68.67–76.00 recommended: true reason: Winter is generally Lucknow''s strongest tourism season because outdoor sightseeing becomes comfortable, food culture is particularly rewarding and seasonal specialties are available, although fog can affect early-morning travel. Best for:', 6892),
  ('lucknow', 10, 'budget-strategy', 'BUDGET STRATEGY', NULL, NULL, 'Where money can be saved: Where saving money is usually NOT recommended: Travel-agent rule: In Lucknow, **METRO + SHORT_AUTO_OR_E_RICKSHAW + LOCAL_FOOD + GEOGRAPHICAL_HERITAGE_CLUSTERING** should be evaluated together. For short stays, prioritize: **BARA_IMAMBARA + RUMI_DARWAZA + CHOTA_IMAMBARA + RESIDENCY + CHOWK + HAZRATGANJ**. For longer stays, add: **QAISERBAGH + LA_MARTINIERE + DILKUSHA + GOMTI_NAGAR + AMBEDKAR_MEMORIAL_JANESHWAR_PARK + KUKRAIL**. Operational note: Lucknow Metro fares, monument ticket prices, attraction opening hours, guided-tour costs and airport transfer charges should be rechecked through official operators before travel because operational pricing can change.', 6893),
  ('lucknow', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Family', 'family', 'Chaudhary Charan Singh International Airport is Lucknow''s principal air gateway and is located in the Amausi area south of central Lucknow. Families can use: LUCKNOW_METRO + APP_BASED_CAB + PRIVATE_CAR depending on luggage, child age and hotel location. For families with young children and substantial luggage: PRIVATE_AC_CAB + DIRECT_HOTEL_TRANSFER is generally the easiest solution. For moderate budgets: AIRPORT_METRO + SHORT_AUTO_OR_CAB_TO_HOTEL can provide strong value when accommodation is near the operational metro corridor.', 6894),
  ('lucknow', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Honeymoon', 'honeymoon', 'Prefer: PRIVATE_AIRPORT_CAR + PREMIUM_HOTEL_TRANSFER + DIRECT_CHECK_IN rather than multiple public-transport changes with luggage. Suitable honeymoon bases include: HAZRATGANJ GOMTI_NAGAR PREMIUM_CENTRAL_LUCKNOW For premium trips, combine the arrival transfer with an evening Awadhi dining experience rather than immediate heavy sightseeing.', 6895),
  ('lucknow', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Luxury', 'luxury', 'Use: AIRPORT_MEET_AND_GREET + PRIVATE_PREMIUM_SEDAN_OR_SUV + DIRECT_HOTEL_TRANSFER + LUGGAGE_ASSISTANCE Luxury travelers generally benefit more from chauffeured road transport than public transit because heritage attractions are spread across multiple districts.', 6896),
  ('lucknow', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Budget', 'budget', 'Primary options: Metro becomes particularly useful for airport–Charbagh–Hazratganj corridor movements.', 6897),
  ('lucknow', 12, 'arrival-transfer-logic', 'ARRIVAL TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Senior', 'senior', 'Prefer: PRIVATE_AC_CAB or METRO + SHORT_CAB_CONNECTION depending on mobility. Avoid unnecessary walking with luggage around railway-station or Old Lucknow traffic zones. Hotel access, elevators and bathroom accessibility should be verified individually.', 6898),
  ('lucknow', 18, 'family-travel', 'FAMILY TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'child_friendly_score: 87 best_ages: Rules: For young children: Prefer: Avoid:', 6899),
  ('lucknow', 19, 'honeymoon-travel', 'HONEYMOON TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'honeymoon_score: 82 romance_score: 81 privacy_score: 75 luxury_score: 84 Recommended: Honeymoon itineraries should generally stay at: 2–3 major experiences/day. Prefer: PREMIUM_CITY_HOTEL + PRIVATE_CAR + HERITAGE_ARCHITECTURE + AWADHI_FINE_DINING + EVENING_CITY_EXPERIENCE + FREE_TIME over: Continuous monument scheduling and crowded market hopping.', 6900),
  ('lucknow', 20, 'luxury-travel', 'LUXURY TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'luxury_score: 84 Recommended: Lucknow is particularly strong for: URBAN_LUXURY + PRIVATE_HERITAGE_GUIDING + AWADHI_FINE_DINING + BESPOKE_CRAFT_SHOPPING + CHAUFFEURED_CITY_EXPLORATION.', 6901),
  ('lucknow', 21, 'adventure', 'ADVENTURE', NULL, NULL, 'adventure_score: 51 Lucknow offers primarily soft urban and nature-oriented activity rather than high-adrenaline adventure. Adventure experiences: Best regions: OLD_LUCKNOW + JANESHWAR_MISHRA_PARK + KUKRAIL + GOMTI_NAGAR + OUTER_LUCKNOW Travel-agent positioning: Lucknow should be treated as: SOFT_URBAN_EXPLORATION + WALKING + CYCLING + CULTURAL_DISCOVERY rather than a high-adrenaline destination.', 6902),
  ('lucknow', 22, 'senior-travel', 'SENIOR TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'senior_suitability: 81 walking_intensity: LOW–MEDIUM for chauffeured sightseeing, Hazratganj, Gomti Nagar, parks and selected heritage compounds. MEDIUM–HIGH for Bhul Bhulaiya stairs, large monument complexes, Chowk lanes, congested markets and extended Residency walking. Rules: Lucknow works best for seniors as a: CULTURAL_HERITAGE + AWADHI_GASTRONOMY + CHAUFFEURED_SIGHTSEEING + SHOPPING + RELAXED_CITY_BREAK destination.', 6903),
  ('lucknow', 23, 'accessibility', 'ACCESSIBILITY', NULL, NULL, 'wheelchair_accessibility: MODERATE IN MODERN DISTRICTS, METRO-BASED ROUTES, AIRPORT, PARKS AND SELECTED HERITAGE GROUNDS LIMITED OR VARIABLE IN HISTORIC MONUMENT INTERIORS, OLD_MARKET_LANES, STAIRS_AND_UNEVEN_SURFACES public_transport_accessibility: MODERATE → HIGH ON MODERN METRO INFRASTRUCTURE, SUBJECT TO STATION FACILITY STATUS hotel_accessibility: MUST_BE_VERIFIED_PER_HOTEL attraction_accessibility: MUST_BE_VERIFIED_PER_ATTRACTION Rule: Never assume that every historic monument in Lucknow is step-free simply because vehicle access reaches the entrance. Additional notes: Lucknow accessibility should therefore be classified as: MODERN_INFRASTRUCTURE_SUPPORTED_BUT_HERITAGE_SITE_DEPENDENT.', 6904),
  ('lucknow', 24, 'food', 'FOOD', NULL, NULL, 'Lucknow is particularly strong for: Food experiences: Family: Prioritize biryani, mild kebabs, breads, chaat, kulfi, sweets and familiar vegetarian North Indian dishes. Honeymoon: Choose premium Awadhi restaurants, tasting menus, refined kebab platters and heritage-inspired dining. Luxury: Include chef-led Awadhi menus, private dining, premium kebab tasting and curated regional cuisine. Budget: Use local kebab shops, biryani outlets, chaat stalls, vegetarian eateries and traditional sweet shops with appropriate hygiene standards. Travel-agent rule: Avoid treating Lucknow cuisine as generic North Indian cuisine. Position it around: AWADHI_DUM_COOKING + KEBABS + BIRYANI + NIHARI_AND_KORMA + TRADITIONAL_BREADS + CHAAT_AND_SEASONAL_SWEETS.', 6905),
  ('lucknow', 25, 'shopping', 'SHOPPING', NULL, NULL, 'Strong categories: Luxury shopping: Prefer: Artisan shopping: Prefer: Budget: Prefer: Travel-agent rule: Use: CHOWK for TRADITIONAL_CHIKANKARI_AND_CRAFT, AMINABAD for VALUE_SHOPPING, HAZRATGANJ for ORGANIZED_RETAIL, GOMTI_NAGAR for MODERN_PREMIUM_SHOPPING. Avoid assuming every embroidered garment is fully handmade.', 6906),
  ('lucknow', 26, 'nightlife', 'NIGHTLIFE', NULL, NULL, 'nightlife_level: 74 Suitable for: Best areas: Evening activities: Lucknow nightlife is strongest for: DINING + CAFES + LOUNGES + EVENING_SHOPPING + RELAXED_SOCIAL_NIGHTLIFE rather than: LARGE_SCALE_CLUBBING. Honeymoon travelers should generally prefer: AWADHI_FINE_DINING + EVENING_CITY_DRIVE + PREMIUM_HOTEL_LOUNGE + HAZRATGANJ_WALK + DESSERT_EXPERIENCE over: Crowded late-night entertainment districts.', 6907),
  ('lucknow', 28, 'sample-itinerary-patterns', 'SAMPLE ITINERARY PATTERNS', '3 NIGHTS', NULL, '### Day 1 Arrival at Chaudhary Charan Singh International Airport (LKO) → Airport Metro / taxi / private AC car transfer to central Lucknow hotel → Hotel check-in & relax after arrival Afternoon: → Begin exploring Lucknow''s monumental Husainabad heritage precinct → Visit Bara Imambara, one of the city''s signature Nawabi-era landmarks → Explore the famous Bhul Bhulaiya labyrinth → Visit the historic Shahi Baoli → Continue towards the monumental Rumi Darwaza → Walk through the surrounding Old Lucknow heritage area Evening: → Explore the illuminated Husainabad precinct → Traditional Awadhi dinner featuring Lucknow''s celebrated culinary heritage → Optional Gomti Riverfront / relaxed city drive → Hotel LKO is Lucknow''s principal domestic and international aviation gateway and is connected with the city by road and Lucknow Metro. As the capital of Uttar Pradesh, Lucknow also provides useful road and rail connections towards Ayodhya, Varanasi and other major destinations across the state. ### Day 2 Morning: Breakfast → Continue Lucknow''s Nawabi heritage exploration → Visit Chota Imambara → See the Husainabad Clock Tower → Explore the surrounding historic architecture → Continue towards the British Residency → Walk through the ruins and landscaped grounds associated with Lucknow''s colonial-era history Afternoon: → Traditional Awadhi lunch → Explore Hazratganj → Browse Lucknow''s famous Chikankari embroidery & handicrafts → Explore Chowk and the historic market lanes of Old Lucknow → Sample local sweets / street-food specialties according to preference Evening: → Gomti Riverfront OR Janeshwar Mishra Park → Relaxed sunset experience → Awadhi kebab / biryani / vegetarian regional dinner → Hotel Optional alternative instead of central Lucknow sightseeing: AYODHYA: → Early road / rail journey from Lucknow to Ayodhya → Shri Ram Janmabhoomi Mandir → Hanuman Garhi → Kanak Bhawan → Ram Ki Paidi → Sarayu riverfront & evening Aarti → Return to Lucknow ### Day 3 Recommended first-time option: → Breakfast → Explore Lucknow''s broader cultural and lifestyle heritage → Visit La Martinière heritage precinct / exterior → Continue through historic central Lucknow → Visit Lucknow Zoo OR additional museum / cultural attraction according to interest Afternoon: → Lunch featuring regional Awadhi cuisine → Chikankari & artisan shopping → Hazratganj café experience → Leisure at Janeshwar Mishra Park / Gomti riverfront Evening: → Final Old Lucknow food experience → Heritage photography → Farewell dinner → Hotel Optional alternative instead of a full third day within Lucknow: AYODHYA_DAY_TRIP: → Shri Ram Janmabhoomi Mandir → Hanuman Garhi → Kanak Bhawan → Ram Ki Paidi → Sarayu Aarti NAIMISHARANYA: → Day excursion from Lucknow → Sacred pilgrimage landscape → Chakra Tirth → Major temples & religious sites → Relaxed spiritual exploration NATURE: → Kukrail forest / nature experience → Janeshwar Mishra Park → Gomti riverfront → Outdoor leisure & photography CULTURE & HISTORY: → Bara Imambara → Chota Imambara → British Residency → Husainabad heritage precinct → Old Lucknow heritage walk FAMILY: → Bhul Bhulaiya exploration → Lucknow Zoo → Janeshwar Mishra Park → Chikankari shopping → Family food experience HONEYMOON: → Heritage couple photography → Gomti riverfront sunset → Luxury hotel spa → Hazratganj café experience → Romantic Awadhi dinner LUXURY: → Chauffeured private sightseeing → Privately guided Nawabi heritage tour → Curated Chikankari shopping → Premium spa & wellness → Fine-dining Awadhi experience FOOD: → Traditional Awadhi kebabs → Lucknow biryani → Sheermal & traditional breads → Old Lucknow street-food exploration → Regional sweets & desserts For only 3 nights, prioritize: BARA_IMAMBARA_AND_RUMI_DARWAZA + OLD_LUCKNOW_AND_BRITISH_RESIDENCY + AYODHYA_OR_LUCKNOW_CULTURAL_DAY OR NAWABI_LUCKNOW_HERITAGE + CHOWK_AND_AWADHI_CUISINE + GOMTI_AND_MODERN_LUCKNOW rather than trying to include Varanasi, Prayagraj, Agra and multiple distant Uttar Pradesh destinations within the same short stay. ### Day 4 Breakfast → Leisurely morning around Hazratganj / hotel relaxation → Final Chikankari, handicraft & souvenir shopping → Hotel checkout → Private transfer / taxi / Metro connection towards Chaudhary Charan Singh International Airport (LKO) → Departure', 6908),
