  ('ayodhya', 31, 'six-nights-luxury-pattern', 'SIX-NIGHTS LUXURY PATTERN', 'Day 7', NULL, 'Breakfast → Leisure morning → Hotel checkout → Private luxury transfer to Ayodhya Airport (AYJ) → Departure', 7070),
  ('ayodhya', 32, 'travel-agent-insights', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS', 'What inexperienced planners often do wrong', NULL, '', 7071),
  ('ayodhya', 32, 'travel-agent-insights', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS', 'What an experienced planner does differently', NULL, 'RAM_JANMABHOOMI_AND_RAMKOT_HERITAGE + HANUMAN_GARHI_AND_KANAK_BHAWAN + SARYU_RIVERFRONT_AARTI_AND_AWADHI_SATVIK_CUISINE rather than maximum destination count.', 7072),
  ('ayodhya', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', NULL, NULL, 'IF: trip_length <= 3 nights THEN: prioritize_RAM_JANMABHOOMI_MANDIR + HANUMAN_GARHI_MANDIR + SARYU_RIVER_AARTI_AND_RAM_KI_PAIDI Reason: Very short stays gain more value from properly experiencing core temple darshan, spiritual riverfront lighting, and authentic satvik culinary heritage than losing time to distant regional day excursions. IF: trip_length >= 5 nights AND: traveler_interest == FIRST_TIME_AYODHYA THEN: prioritize_RAM_JANMABHOOMI_CORE + HANUMAN_GARHI_AND_KANAK_BHAWAN + GUPTAR_GHAT_PROMENADE + FAIZABAD_NAWABI_HERITAGE_DAY_TRIP Reason: This gives a balanced introduction to Vedic spiritual heritage, grand temple architecture, peaceful riverfront promenades, and 18th-century Nawabi garden history. IF: trip_length >= 7 nights AND: traveler_interest == FIRST_TIME_AYODHYA THEN: prefer_AYODHYA_DHAM_CENTRAL_CORE + SARYU_RIVERFRONT_RETREAT + DAY_TRIPS_TO_NAIMISHARANYA_OR_VARANASI_VIA_RAIL_OR_HIGHWAY AND: use_E_RICSKSHAWS_ELECTRIC_BUSES_AND_PRIVATE_AC_TAXIS Reason: Central heritage havelis, riverside eco-parks, historical monuments, and regional pilgrimage connections via expressways offer distinct insights into northern India''s spiritual belt. IF: trip_type == HONEYMOON THEN: prioritize_SARYU_RIVERFRONT_LUXURY_HOTELS + CENTRAL_HERITAGE_HAVELI_STAYS + PRIVATE_SUNSET_SARYU_BOAT_CRUISE AND: increase_BOUTIQUE_STAYS + ROOFTOP_SARYU_VIEW_DINING + LUXURY_SPA + SATVIK_FINE_DINING + COUPLE_EXPERIENCES Reason: Ayodhya''s romantic routes mix luxury river-view suites, fine satvik Awadhi thali dining, rooftop tea sessions overlooking illuminated temple spires, and quiet evening walks along Guptar Ghat. IF: traveler_type == FAMILY THEN: prioritize_RAM_KI_PAIDI_LASER_SHOW + SARYU_BOAT_RIDE_FISH_FEEDING + LATA_MANGESHKAR_CHOWK_VEENA AND: include_TULSI_SMARAK_BHAWAN_RAMLILA + GOLF_CART_RIDES_JANMABHOOMI_PATH + LOCAL_SWEET_TASTING AND: reduce_STEEP_TEMPLE_STAIR_CLIMBS + LONG_CONTINUOUS_PEDESTRIAN_QUEUES Reason: Ayodhya has exceptional family sights, including 3D light and sound shows, river boat rides, electric golf cart transport, puppet shows, and interactive Ramayana museums. IF: traveler_type == LUXURY THEN: prefer_SARYU_RIVERFRONT_LUXURY_HOTELS + HERITAGE_HAVELI_SUITES + VIP_TENTED_CITIES_DEEPOTSAV AND: increase_PRIVATE_VIP_DARSHAN_GUIDES + SATVIK_FINE_DINING + PRIVATE_SUV_TRANSFERS + PRIVATE_BOAT_CHARTERS + AYURVEDIC_SPA Reason: Ayodhya high-end travel relies on boutique heritage suites, multi-course chef-curated Satvik thalis, private chauffeured SUV transfers, fast-track temple assistance, and private riverfront cruises. IF: traveler_type == BUDGET THEN: prefer_ELECTRIC_BUSES + E_RICSKSHAWS + WALKING + TEMPLE_ANNAKSHETRA_COMMUNITY_KITCHENS AND: book_FREE_TEMPLE_DARSHAN_SLOTS_EARLY AND: balance_PAID_ATTRACTIONS_WITH_FREE_RAM_KI_PAIDI_STROLLS + SARYU_AARTI_VIEWS + GUPTAR_GHAT_PROMENADE Reason: Ayodhya can be accessed affordably using local e-rickshaws, temple community feast halls (*annakshetras*), free public ghat parks, and free open-air laser light shows. IF: traveler_interest == CULTURE_AND_HERITAGE THEN: prioritize_RAM_JANMABHOOMI_MANDIR + GULAB_BARI + BAHU_BEGUM_KA_MAQBARA + TULSI_SMARAK_BHAWAN AND: include_VAGHELA_AWADHI_ARCHITECTURE + RAMAYANA_LITERARY_HERITAGE + LOCAL_FESTIVALS_DEEPOTSAV Reason: These sights showcase Ayodhya''s unique multi-layered history, mixing ancient Suryavanshi heritage, Ramayana literary traditions, and 18th-century Awadhi Nawabi architecture. IF: traveler_interest == ART_AND_ARCHITECTURE THEN: prefer_RAM_JANMABHOOMI_NAGARA_STYLE + KANAK_BHAWAN_ORLI_WORK + BAHU_BEGUM_MAQBARA_NAWABI_DOMES + LATA_MANGESHKAR_CHOWK_VEENA AND: include_ANCIENT_STONE_CARVINGS + HERITAGE_HAVELI_COURTYARDS + MODERN_PLAZA_DESIGN Reason: This route contrasts ancient and modern Nagara temple architecture with grand Nawabi Mughal domes and contemporary civic bronze installations. IF: traveler_interest == GASTRONOMY THEN: prefer_AWADHI_SATVIK_THALI + BEDMI_PURI_ALOO_KACHORI + DAHI_JALEBI_AND_RABRI + AYODHYA_PEDA AND: include_HANUMAN_GARHI_SWEET_LANE + KULHAD_CHAI_STALLS + MAKHAN_MALAI_WINTER_SPECIAL Reason: Ayodhya dining spans pure-vegetarian satvik feasts prepared without onion or garlic, crispy morning kachoris, winter milk foam desserts, and historical peda sweet traditions. IF: traveler_interest == NATURE_AND_WILDLIFE THEN: prioritize_SARYU_RIVER_WETLANDS + GUPTAR_GHAT_TREE_PROMENADE + SARYU_ECO_PARK + SURAJ_KUND_GARDENS AND: do_not_treat_MANICURED_TEMPLE_GARDENS_AND_RIVERFRONT_CONSERVATION_TRAILS_AS_IDENTICAL Reason: Temple gardens offer manicured lawns and fountains, while Saryu riverfront conservation zones feature migratory water birds, natural wetlands, and riverine flora. IF: traveler_interest == SHOPPING THEN: prioritize_HANUMAN_GARHI_MARKET_LANE + RAM_PATH_HERITAGE_STORES + GITA_PRESS_BOOK_DEPOT + FAIZABAD_TEXTILE_BAZAARS AND: include_BRASS_IDOLS + WOODEN_RAM_MANDIR_REPLICAS + CHIKANKARI_TEXTILES + TULSI_MALAS Reason: Hanuman Garhi lane supplies brass idols and devotional souvenirs, Ram Path houses book depots and handicraft stores, and Faizabad markets supply traditional textiles and embroidery. IF: traveler_interest == SAUNA_AND_WELLNESS THEN: choose_RIVERSIDE_AYURVEDIC_RETREATS + TRADITIONAL_VEDIC_HERBAL_MASSAGE + RIVERSIDE_YOGA_PAVILIONS AND: do_not_treat_LOCAL_HOLISTIC_MASSAGES_AND_LUXURY_RESORT_SPAS_AS_IDENTICAL Reason: Ayodhya wellness ranges from quiet riverfront yoga sessions and Vedic Ayurvedic centers to luxury resort spa treatments overlooking the Saryu. IF: traveler_interest == PHOTOGRAPHY THEN: prioritize_RAM_KI_PAIDI_ILLUMINATIONS + BAHU_BEGUM_MAQBARA_LOOKOUT + SARYU_RIVER_SUNSET_BOATS + GUPTAR_GHAT_PROMENADE AND: prioritize_GOLDEN_HOUR + BLUE_HOUR + EVENING_AARTI_LIGHTING Reason: These sites produce stunning visual contrasts between glowing temple spires, reflective river waters, historic Nawabi domes, and vibrant evening aarti flames. IF: trip_length <= 5 nights THEN: prefer_MAXIMUM_ONE_OR_TWO_BASES AND: avoid_EXCESSIVE_HOTEL_CHANGES Reason: Inner-city traffic, pedestrian security zones, and airport/rail transfers consume valuable sightseeing hours. IF: route == AYODHYA_DHAM_TO_FAIZABAD_OR_LUCKNOW THEN: prefer_DIRECT_E_BUSES_PRIVATE_TRANSFERS_OR_EXPRESS_TRAINS_OVER_MULTIPLE_LOCAL_TRANSITS Reason: Direct transfers eliminate transit confusion and save energy for exploring temple complexes and historical monuments. IF: traveler_type == SENIOR OR: traveler_mobility == LIMITED THEN: prefer_ACCESSIBLE_HOTELS + FLAT_GHAT_PROMENADES + ELECTRIC_GOLF_CARTS + JANMABHOOMI_PATH_RAMPS AND: reduce_HANUMAN_GARHI_STEEP_STEPS + LONG_UNSHADED_WALKS + EXTREME_SUMMER_HEAT_EXPOSURE Reason: Steep temple staircases and long pedestrian walking corridors cause fatigue; ramps, battery golf carts, and flat promenades ease travel. IF: traveler_uses_WHEELCHAIR THEN: prefer_JANMABHOOMI_PATH_RAMPS + MAHARISHI_VALMIKI_AIRPORT + GUPTAR_GHAT_FLAT_PROMENADE + MODERN_HOTELS AND: do_not_assume_ANCIENT_TEMPLE_STEPS + HISTORIC_GHAT_STAIRS + OLD_CITY_HAVELIS_ARE_STEP_FREE Reason: Major modern infrastructure (Ram Janmabhoomi complex, Ayodhya Airport) is accessible, but ancient temple staircases and historic river ghat steps present physical barriers. IF: weather == EXTREME_SUMMER_HEAT AND: region == AYODHYA_TERRITORY THEN: prioritize_EARLY_MORNING_DARSHAN + AIR_CONDITIONED_MUSEUMS_AND_HOTELS + EVENING_RIVER_AARTI AND: reduce_MIDDAY_UNSHADED_TEMPLE_QUEUE_EXPOSURE Reason: Ayodhya summer temps routinely exceed 40°C with intense solar radiation; early morning starts and shaded/indoor breaks maintain comfort. IF: weather == HEAVY_SMOG_OR_RAIN THEN: increase_RAM_KATHA_MUSEUM + TULSI_SMARAK_BHAWAN + INDOOR_BHOJANALAYAS + COVERED_BAZAARS AND: reduce_SARYU_BOAT_CRUISES + OUTDOOR_GHAT_PROMENADES Reason: Indoor history museums, cultural centers, covered sweet bazaars, and traditional bhojanalayas remain excellent regardless of outdoor rain or smog. IF: traveler_interest == FIRST_TIME_AYODHYA THEN: prioritize_RAM_JANMABHOOMI_MANDIR + HANUMAN_GARHI + KANAK_BHAWAN + SARYU_RIVER_AARTI AND: add_ONE_OF_RAM_KI_PAIDI_LASER_SHOW_GUPTAR_GHAT_OR_GULAB_BARI AND: include_ONE_SIGNATURE_AWADHI_SATVIK_THALI_OR_BEDMI_PURI_EXPERIENCE Reason: This structure provides a comprehensive introduction to Ayodhya''s premier spiritual heritage and historic sights alongside authentic local food culture. IF: traveler_interest == CULTURE_AND_RELAXATION_BALANCE THEN: allocate_60_TO_70_PERCENT_TO_CORE_SIGHTSEEING AND: allocate_REMAINING_TIME_TO_TEA_HOUSES + RIVERSIDE_CAFES + SPAS + SUNSET_BOATS + SHOPPING + FREE_TIME', 7073),
  ('ayodhya', 34, 'destination-scoring', 'DESTINATION SCORING', NULL, NULL, '| Factor | Score | | ------------------ | ----: | | Family | 94 | | Honeymoon | 82 | | Luxury | 84 | | Budget | 95 | | Adventure | 68 | | Culture | 99 | | Food | 90 | | Shopping | 80 | | Nightlife | 62 | | Relaxation | 92 | | Nature | 84 | | Accessibility | 85 | | Safety | 92 | | First-time visitor | 95 | | Photography | 96 |', 7074),
  ('ayodhya', 35, 'final-travel-agent-verdict', 'FINAL TRAVEL AGENT VERDICT', NULL, NULL, 'Best traveler profiles: 1. Spiritual / Ramayan heritage pilgrim (Shri Ram Janmabhoomi Mandir, Hanuman Garhi, Kanak Bhawan, Treta Ke Thakur, Nageshwarnath Temple) 2. First-time North India / Uttar Pradesh spiritual circuit traveler 3. Heritage / sacred history traveler (Surya Kund, Guptar Ghat, Mani Parvat, Ram ki Paidi, Chhoti Devkali Temple) 4. Awadhi & Temple architecture traveler (Nagara-style Shri Ram Mandir, Awadh Rajasthani Kanak Bhawan, Heritage Sarayu Ghats, Badi Devkali) 5. Modern pilgrimage / urban infrastructure traveler (Ram Path, Bhakti Path, Dharma Path, Maharishi Valmiki Airport Terminal, Ayodhya Dham Junction) 6. Photography & drone traveler (Sarayu River Aarti at Ram ki Paidi, Deepotsav illumination, Guptar Ghat sunset, Surya Kund water reflections) 7. Sacred Awadhi / vegetarian gastronomy traveler (Ayodhya Pedha, Ram Prasadam, Bedmi Puri & Aloo, Makhan Malai, Samosa-Kachori, Pure Veg Sattvik Dining) 8. Family & multi-generational pilgrim (Sarayu River Cruise, Ram Katha Park light shows, Dashrath Mahal, Botanical Solar Park, Eco-battery car corridor tours) 9. Cultural art & festival lifestyle traveler (Lathmar & Deepotsav celebrations, Ram Navami melas, Ram Leela performances, Bhajan Sandhya Pavilion) 10. Budget / independent pilgrim (UPSRTC Electric Bus Network, Free Janmabhoomi Luggage Counters, Coastal Sarayu Walking Paths, Pilgrims'' Rain Basera & Community Bhojanalayas) Best duration: 2–3 nights 1 night: Best for ONE primary focus such as Ram Janmabhoomi Mandir express darshan + Hanuman Garhi + Evening Sarayu Aarti at Ram ki Paidi. 2–3 nights: Best for TWO major bases/focuses such as Central Sacred Corridor (Ram Janmabhoomi, Kanak Bhawan, Hanuman Garhi) + River Ghats & Heritage Parks (Guptar Ghat, Surya Kund, Ram Katha Park). 4–5 nights: Excellent for Ayodhya Dham Core + Extended Panchkoshi Parikrama sites + Day trips to Naimisharanya, Lucknow Awadh Heritage, or Prayagraj Sangam. 6–7 nights: Best for deep regional Ramayan Circuit travel, including Chitrakoot, Janakpur border connections, Prayagraj, and Varanasi spiritual heritage trail. Best season: YEAR-ROUND Peak / Winter Window (October – March): PLEASANT_WEATHER + DEEPOTSAV_CELEBRATIONS + COMFORTABLE_WALKING_TEMPERATURES + OPTIMAL_GHAT_SIGHTSEEING + RAM_NAVAMI_FESTIVALS. Summer / Hot Season (April – June): MORNING_DARSHAN + BUDGET_ACCOMMODATION + EARLY_EVENING_AARTI + FEWER_CROWDS. Monsoon / Wet Season (July – September): LUSH_GREEN_SARAYU_BANKS + REFRESHING_RAIN_SHOWERS + COVERED_TEMPLE_CORRIDORS + SERENE_GHAT_VIEWS. Festive Season (Oct – Nov & Mar – Apr): DEEPOTSAV_WORLD_RECORD_DIYAS + RAM_NAVAMI_GRAND_RATH_YATRA + CULTURAL_RAMLEELA + SPIRITUAL_DISCOURSES. Uttar Pradesh Tourism guidance treats the holy city as year-round: October through March are world-famous for cool winter days, grand festival illuminations, and comfortable walking conditions; April through June for early-morning peaceful darshans; July through September for lush green riverbank scenery; and festival windows for massive spiritual celebrations and vibrant street culture. Best hotel strategy: Choose accommodation according to transit convenience, atmosphere, and trip purpose. For first-time pilgrims: RAM_PATH_OR_NAGAR_PALIKA_CIRCLE (Central Ayodhya corridor) for direct walking and e-rickshaw access to top temples, eateries, and sacred ghats. For quiet heritage / riverbank charm: GUPTAR_GHAT_OR_SARYU_RIVERFRONT (Boutique homestays near Guptar Ghat or Laxman Ghat) for serene river views, peaceful morning walks, and contemplative retreat. For modern design & business convenience: LUCKNOW_GORAKHPUR_HIGHWAY / AIRPORT_BELT selectively according to luxury star stays, family resorts, direct parking facilities, and smooth highway transit. Avoid unnecessary hotel changes within Ayodhya; e-rickshaws, golf carts, battery buses, and auto-rickshaws serve Ram Path, Bhakti Path, and Sarayu Ghats efficiently without relocating. Best transportation: Use: HAWS for Ram Path, Bhakti Path, Janmabhoomi Path, and central temple precincts HAWS selectively for airport transfers, outer circuit sites (Surya Kund, Bharat Kund), and heavy luggage transfers Ayodhya transportation should primarily be treated as: PEDESTRIAN_PATHS_AND_ELECTRIC_RICKSHAWS_FOR_TEMPLE_ZONES + WALKING_FOR_RAM_PATH_AND_SARAYU_GHATS + UPSRTC_ELECTRIC_BUSES_FOR_AIRPORT_AND_RAILWAY_STATION_TRANSIT + SARAYU_BOATS_FOR_RIVERFRONT_EXCURSIONS Must-do for first-time visitor: Ayodhya should not be reduced to single-temple visits alone; official tourism positions SACRED_RIVER_GHATS + PEDESTRIAN_HERITAGE_CORRIDORS + HISTORIC_RAMAYAN_SITES + AWADHI_SATTVIK_GASTRONOMY + MODEL_SOLAR_INFRASTRUCTURE as core city pillars. Don''t-do: Biggest advantage: Unrivaled concentration of ancient Ramayan heritage, grand Nagara temple architecture, modernized smart pedestrian corridors, and seamless regional air and rail integration. Ayodhya combines a 5th-century historical legacy, iconic vibrant riverfronts (Ram ki Paidi & Guptar Ghat), preserved sacred Kunds, and dynamic modern infrastructure (Maharishi Valmiki Airport & Model Solar City) within a compact, easily navigable holy precinct. Official tourism highlights the unique Ramayan cultural legacy, rich Sarayu marine ecosystem, accessible electric transit links, and vibrant local Sattvik culinary culture, catering to diverse spiritual travel styles. Biggest disadvantage: Massive festival crowd surges, strict security locker procedures, and severe summer heat extremes. Navigating intense crowd flows during Ram Navami or Deepotsav requires patience and advance planning, hot summer monsoons bring high humidity while strict security protocols require locker check-ins for electronics before temple entry. Overall destination score: 95/100', 7075),
  ('ayodhya', 36, 'data-quality', 'DATA QUALITY', NULL, NULL, 'information_completeness: 97/100 last_updated: 2026-09-03 last_verified: WEB_VERIFIED verified_by: UP TOURISM (UPTOURISM.GOV.IN) / AYODHYA DEVELOPMENT AUTHORITY (ADA) / SRI RAM JANMABHOOMI TEERTH KSHETRA / UTTAR PRADESH STATE ROAD TRANSPORT CORPORATION (UPSRTC) / AIRPORTS AUTHORITY OF INDIA (AAI) sources: IMPORTANT: Ram Janmabhoomi VIP Darshan passes, Aarti booking tokens, Ayodhya Dham rail tickets, museum entries, and special Deepotsav seating must NOT be treated as permanently valid. Major shrines and river transit platforms have seasonal crowd capacity limits and advance timed-entry rules; current slot availability must be verified online. Electric Rickshaws, Battery Buses, and Self-Drive Taxis are the standard transport choices, but real-time schedules and festival road diversions should be verified on official municipal platforms for actual travel dates. Ayodhya''s climate varies significantly by season: PEAK WINTER WINDOW (OCTOBER – MARCH) brings pleasant, cool days ideal for temple darshans, Sarayu boat rides, heritage walks, and festival events. SUMMER SEASON (APRIL – JUNE) brings high heat (exceeding 40°C/104°F) and high sun exposure, requiring early morning darshans, afternoon rest, and hydration break planning. MONSOON SEASON (JULY – SEPTEMBER) brings refreshing rains and high humidity, requiring caution along wet river ghat steps and outdoor walking paths. Accessible tourism infrastructure is available across redeveloped Ayodhya Dham Junction, Maharishi Valmiki Airport, Ram Path pedestrian walks, and major hotel complexes, but historic temple staircases, steep ghat steps, and ancient stepwells are rarely fully step-free. Ayodhya should primarily be treated as: PEAK WINTER WINDOW (OCTOBER – MARCH): RAM_JANMABHOOMI + HANUMAN_GARHI + SARAYU_AARTI + GU PTAR_GHAT + DEEPOTSAV_HERITAGE_TOURS SUMMER SEASON (APRIL – JUNE): EARLY_MORNING_DARSHAN + COVERED_KUND_SITES + SATTVIK_DINING + EVENING_GHAT_STROLLS + INDOOR_EXHIBITIONS MONSOON SEASON (JULY – SEPTEMBER): SARYU_RIVER_BOATING + RAM_KATHA_PARK + SURYA_KUND + TEMPLE_CORRIDOR_WALKS + CULTURAL_SHOWS Uptourism.gov.in, Ayodhya.nic.in, UPSRTC Official, and individual temple trust booking portals should be treated as primary sources for operational information. This dataset should be refreshed regularly before production use.', 7076),
