  ('jaipur', 28, 'sample-itinerary-patterns', 'SAMPLE ITINERARY PATTERNS', 'HALF-DAY – PINK CITY HERITAGE & HAWA MAHAL', NULL, 'Morning / Afternoon: Pickup from your hotel in Jaipur → Begin in the historic walled city with **Hawa Mahal**, Jaipur''s iconic five-storey honeycomb façade and one of the city''s signature landmarks → Walk through the surrounding **Johari Bazaar** and old-city streets for traditional jewellery, textiles and handicrafts → Continue to **City Palace** to explore royal courtyards, museums, costumes and Rajput-Mughal architecture → Visit **Jantar Mantar**, the UNESCO-listed astronomical observatory containing monumental geometric instruments → End with traditional **Rajasthani snacks and chai** before returning to your hotel', 7167),
  ('jaipur', 28, 'sample-itinerary-patterns', 'SAMPLE ITINERARY PATTERNS', '1 DAY – AMER FORT, CITY PALACE & PINK CITY HIGHLIGHTS', NULL, 'Morning: Morning pickup from your hotel for Jaipur''s principal heritage circuit → Drive to **Amber Fort**, approximately 11 km from central Jaipur, and explore its courtyards, Sheesh Mahal, royal quarters and restored tunnel section → Continue to **Jaigarh Fort** for panoramic Aravalli views and its historic fortifications Afternoon: Return toward the walled city → Visit **City Palace** and explore the Mubarak Mahal, Maharani''s Palace and royal museum collections → Continue to **Jantar Mantar** for an introduction to Jaipur''s historic astronomical instruments Evening: Walk around **Hawa Mahal** and the surrounding old-city bazaars → Continue toward **Jal Mahal** for an evening photography stop beside Man Sagar Lake; the palace is primarily viewed from the lakeside because it is not generally open to the public → Finish with a Rajasthani dinner featuring **Dal Baati Churma, Gatte Ki Sabzi and Ghevar**', 7168),
  ('jaipur', 28, 'sample-itinerary-patterns', 'SAMPLE ITINERARY PATTERNS', '2 DAYS – JAIPUR ROYAL HERITAGE & ARAVALLI CIRCUIT', NULL, 'Day 1: Full-day exploration of Jaipur''s principal heritage attractions → Begin at **Amber Fort** and continue to **Jaigarh Fort** → Return to the walled city for **City Palace, Jantar Mantar and Hawa Mahal** → Spend the evening exploring **Johari Bazaar and Bapu Bazaar** → Enjoy an authentic Rajasthani dinner with traditional sweets Day 2: Begin with **Albert Hall Museum** and its historic collections → Continue to **Birla Temple** for a peaceful cultural stop → Visit **Galtaji** and its historic temple complex in the surrounding hills → Proceed to **Sisodia Rani Garden** for landscaped Mughal-Rajput gardens → End at **Nahargarh Fort** for sunset views over Jaipur; Rajasthan Tourism recommends a taxi or car because there is no convenient public transport directly to the fort ([Rajasthan Tourism][6]) → Return to Jaipur for dinner and departure preparations', 7169),
  ('jaipur', 29, '6-days-and-5-nights-honeymoon-itinerary', '6 DAYS & 5 NIGHTS HONEYMOON ITINERARY', 'DAY 1 – ROYAL ARRIVAL & PINK CITY ROMANCE', NULL, 'Morning / Afternoon: Arrive at **Jaipur International Airport**, **Jaipur Railway Station**, or reach Jaipur by private road transfer → Meet your private chauffeur and transfer to your romantic boutique, heritage or luxury hotel → Complete check-in and relax in your room Lunch: Enjoy a relaxed lunch featuring traditional Rajasthani cuisine Evening: Take a private sightseeing drive through the **Pink City** → Stop at **Hawa Mahal** for couple photography → Continue through the illuminated old-city streets and bazaars → Enjoy a romantic rooftop dinner overlooking the historic cityscape', 7170),
  ('jaipur', 29, '6-days-and-5-nights-honeymoon-itinerary', '6 DAYS & 5 NIGHTS HONEYMOON ITINERARY', 'DAY 2 – AMBER FORT, JAIGARH & PRIVATE SUNSET', NULL, 'Morning: After breakfast, depart for **Amber Fort** → Explore the royal courtyards, Sheesh Mahal, palace gardens and historic architecture → Continue to **Jaigarh Fort** for Aravalli panoramas and a quieter heritage experience Afternoon: Return to the hotel for lunch and couple''s leisure → Enjoy private spa time, poolside relaxation or an in-room afternoon Evening: Drive to **Nahargarh Fort** for panoramic sunset views across Jaipur → Return to the hotel for a private candlelit dinner', 7171),
  ('jaipur', 29, '6-days-and-5-nights-honeymoon-itinerary', '6 DAYS & 5 NIGHTS HONEYMOON ITINERARY', 'DAY 3 – ROYAL PALACES, OBSERVATORY & OLD CITY', NULL, 'Morning: Visit **City Palace** and explore its royal courtyards, museums and historic collections → Continue to **Jantar Mantar**, Jaipur''s UNESCO World Heritage astronomical observatory Lunch: Enjoy a leisurely lunch at a heritage-style restaurant Afternoon: Walk through **Johari Bazaar** → Browse traditional jewellery, gemstones, textiles and handicrafts → Return to the hotel for rest Evening: Enjoy a romantic rooftop dinner overlooking **Hawa Mahal and the Pink City**', 7172),
  ('jaipur', 29, '6-days-and-5-nights-honeymoon-itinerary', '6 DAYS & 5 NIGHTS HONEYMOON ITINERARY', 'DAY 4 – JAL MAHAL, GALTAJI & COUPLE''S LEISURE', 'honeymoon', 'Morning: Enjoy a relaxed breakfast and depart toward **Jal Mahal** → Photograph the Water Palace from the banks of Man Sagar Lake → Continue to **Galtaji** for a peaceful temple and hillside experience Lunch: Enjoy lunch at a traditional Rajasthani restaurant Afternoon: Return to the hotel → Private couple''s spa treatment → Poolside relaxation → Optional in-room romantic setup Evening: Enjoy a private sunset experience followed by a specially arranged couple''s dinner', 7173),
  ('jaipur', 29, '6-days-and-5-nights-honeymoon-itinerary', '6 DAYS & 5 NIGHTS HONEYMOON ITINERARY', 'DAY 5 – HERITAGE GARDENS, CULTURE & ROMANTIC FINALE', 'honeymoon', 'Morning: Visit **Albert Hall Museum** for a cultural and architectural experience → Continue to **Birla Temple** → Explore **Sisodia Rani Garden** for landscaped gardens, pavilions and peaceful couple photography Lunch: Enjoy a relaxed lunch and traditional dessert Afternoon: Return to the hotel for leisure → Optional shopping session for Jaipur jewellery, blue pottery, block prints and handicrafts Evening: Celebrate your final night with a **private candlelit dinner** → Optional live Rajasthani folk music and cultural performance → Return to your hotel for overnight stay', 7174),
  ('jaipur', 29, '6-days-and-5-nights-honeymoon-itinerary', '6 DAYS & 5 NIGHTS HONEYMOON ITINERARY', 'DAY 6 – LEISURE BREAKFAST & DEPARTURE', NULL, 'Morning: Enjoy a slow breakfast and complete checkout → Take a final short walk through the nearby heritage streets or hotel gardens → Optional last-minute shopping for souvenirs Late Morning / Afternoon: Meet your private chauffeur → Transfer to **Jaipur International Airport**, **Jaipur Railway Station** or your onward destination → Depart Jaipur with the final views of the Pink City', 7175),
  ('jaipur', 30, '6-days-and-5-nights-family-itinerary', '6 DAYS & 5 NIGHTS FAMILY ITINERARY', 'DAY 1 – FAMILY ARRIVAL & PINK CITY INTRODUCTION', 'family', 'Morning / Afternoon: Arrive at **Jaipur International Airport** or **Jaipur Railway Station** → Meet your private family vehicle and transfer to your hotel → Complete check-in and enjoy lunch Evening: Visit **Hawa Mahal** for family photography → Explore the surrounding old-city streets at an easy pace → Enjoy an early Rajasthani dinner → Return to the hotel for family rest', 7176),
  ('jaipur', 30, '6-days-and-5-nights-family-itinerary', '6 DAYS & 5 NIGHTS FAMILY ITINERARY', 'DAY 2 – AMBER FORT, JAIGARH & JAL MAHAL', NULL, 'Morning: Depart after breakfast for **Amber Fort** → Explore the palace courtyards, Sheesh Mahal and historic sections at a comfortable family pace → Continue to **Jaigarh Fort** for panoramic views Lunch: Enjoy lunch at a family-friendly restaurant Afternoon: Drive toward **Jal Mahal** → Stop beside Man Sagar Lake for photography and refreshments Evening: Return to the hotel → Swimming, indoor games or family leisure → Early dinner and overnight stay', 7177),
  ('jaipur', 30, '6-days-and-5-nights-family-itinerary', '6 DAYS & 5 NIGHTS FAMILY ITINERARY', 'DAY 3 – CITY PALACE, JANTAR MANTAR & HAWA MAHAL', NULL, 'Morning: Visit **City Palace** → Explore the royal museum collections, courtyards and historic architecture → Continue to **Jantar Mantar** and introduce children to Jaipur''s historic astronomical instruments Lunch: Enjoy a family lunch in the walled city Afternoon: Visit **Hawa Mahal** → Explore nearby bazaars for souvenirs and traditional crafts Evening: Return to the hotel for rest → Enjoy a relaxed family dinner', 7178),
  ('jaipur', 30, '6-days-and-5-nights-family-itinerary', '6 DAYS & 5 NIGHTS FAMILY ITINERARY', 'DAY 4 – ALBERT HALL, BIRLA TEMPLE & GARDENS', NULL, 'Morning: Visit **Albert Hall Museum** → Explore its historical collections and Indo-Saracenic architecture → Continue to **Birla Temple** for a peaceful cultural visit Lunch: Enjoy lunch at a family-friendly restaurant Afternoon: Visit **Sisodia Rani Garden** → Enjoy a gentle walk through the landscaped gardens → Continue to **Galtaji** if the family is comfortable with the steps and walking Evening: Return to the hotel → Family leisure and dinner', 7179),
  ('jaipur', 30, '6-days-and-5-nights-family-itinerary', '6 DAYS & 5 NIGHTS FAMILY ITINERARY', 'DAY 5 – NAHARGARH, SHOPPING & CULTURAL EVENING', NULL, 'Morning: After breakfast, drive to **Nahargarh Fort** → Explore the fort and enjoy panoramic views over Jaipur ([Rajasthan Tourism][6]) Lunch: Return toward the city for lunch Afternoon: Enjoy family shopping at **Bapu Bazaar / Johari Bazaar** → Purchase textiles, handicrafts, jewellery, blue pottery and local sweets Evening: Attend a **Rajasthani cultural dinner experience** → Enjoy folk music, traditional performances and regional cuisine → Return to hotel', 7180),
  ('jaipur', 30, '6-days-and-5-nights-family-itinerary', '6 DAYS & 5 NIGHTS FAMILY ITINERARY', 'DAY 6 – RELAXED MORNING & DEPARTURE', NULL, 'Morning: Enjoy breakfast at the hotel → Complete checkout → Optional final visit to a nearby market for souvenirs Late Morning / Afternoon: Transfer by private family vehicle to **Jaipur International Airport** or **Jaipur Railway Station** → Continue to your next destination', 7181),
  ('jaipur', 31, '6-days-and-5-nights-luxury-itinerary', '6 DAYS & 5 NIGHTS LUXURY ITINERARY', 'DAY 1 – VIP ARRIVAL & HERITAGE PALACE RETREAT', NULL, 'Morning / Afternoon: Arrive at **Jaipur International Airport** → Meet your dedicated luxury chauffeur and premium vehicle → Transfer to an exclusive **heritage palace or luxury hotel** Rajasthan Tourism maintains a dedicated heritage-property programme featuring properties designed to recreate the experience of staying in former royal structures. → Private check-in with welcome refreshments → Settle into your luxury suite or palace accommodation Lunch: Enjoy a curated multi-course Rajasthani lunch Evening: Relax at the property → Private spa or pool experience → Sunset drinks and private terrace leisure → Finish with an exclusive candlelit dinner', 7182),
  ('jaipur', 31, '6-days-and-5-nights-luxury-itinerary', '6 DAYS & 5 NIGHTS LUXURY ITINERARY', 'DAY 2 – PRIVATE AMBER FORT & ROYAL ARAVALLI EXPERIENCE', NULL, 'Early Morning: Depart with your private chauffeur for **Amber Fort** → Enjoy a quieter early visit to the palace complex → Explore the royal courtyards, Sheesh Mahal, gardens and historic architecture → Continue to **Jaigarh Fort** for spectacular Aravalli views Lunch: Return to a luxury hotel or heritage property for an elaborate lunch Afternoon: Return to your suite for private relaxation → Spa treatment → Poolside leisure → Optional curated shopping consultation Evening: Private sunset drive toward **Nahargarh Fort** → Enjoy panoramic views across Jaipur → Return for a fine-dining experience', 7183),
  ('jaipur', 31, '6-days-and-5-nights-luxury-itinerary', '6 DAYS & 5 NIGHTS LUXURY ITINERARY', 'DAY 3 – PRIVATE ROYAL CITY PALACE & JANTAR MANTAR', NULL, 'Morning: Private guided visit to **City Palace** → Explore royal courtyards, museum galleries, costumes, weaponry and palace architecture → Continue to **Jantar Mantar** with a knowledgeable heritage guide Lunch: Enjoy a refined Rajasthani thali or chef-curated regional menu Afternoon: Private walking tour through the **Pink City''s historic bazaars** → Explore jewellery, gemstones, textiles and artisanal crafts → Optional private shopping assistance Evening: Return to your palace hotel → Enjoy a private rooftop or courtyard dinner with traditional Rajasthani music', 7184),
  ('jaipur', 31, '6-days-and-5-nights-luxury-itinerary', '6 DAYS & 5 NIGHTS LUXURY ITINERARY', 'DAY 4 – JAL MAHAL, GALTAJI & PRIVATE WELLNESS', NULL, 'Morning: Enjoy a leisurely palace breakfast → Drive to **Jal Mahal** → Private photography stop overlooking Man Sagar Lake; the palace itself is generally viewed from the lakeshore rather than entered by ordinary visitors → Continue toward **Galtaji** for a heritage and spiritual experience Lunch: Enjoy a private lunch at your luxury property Afternoon: Reserve the afternoon for exclusive wellness → Couples'' spa treatment → Private pool → Afternoon tea → Suite leisure Evening: Enjoy a private **sunset and fine-dining experience** → Optional curated Rajasthani folk performance at the property', 7185),
  ('jaipur', 31, '6-days-and-5-nights-luxury-itinerary', '6 DAYS & 5 NIGHTS LUXURY ITINERARY', 'DAY 5 – CULTURAL HERITAGE, GARDENS & ROYAL FINALE', NULL, 'Morning: Visit **Albert Hall Museum** with a private guide → Continue to **Birla Temple** → Explore **Sisodia Rani Garden** for a relaxed heritage-garden experience Lunch: Enjoy an elegant regional lunch Afternoon: Return to the palace hotel → Rest and prepare for the final evening → Optional luxury shopping for Jaipur jewellery, blue pottery, textiles and handcrafted products Evening: Celebrate the final night with an **exclusive royal dinner** → Private courtyard or rooftop setting → Curated Rajasthani menu → Traditional folk music and cultural performance → Return to your luxury suite', 7186),
  ('jaipur', 31, '6-days-and-5-nights-luxury-itinerary', '6 DAYS & 5 NIGHTS LUXURY ITINERARY', 'DAY 6 – ROYAL BREAKFAST & VIP DEPARTURE', NULL, 'Morning: Enjoy a leisurely final breakfast at the palace hotel → Complete checkout → Optional final private shopping stop Late Morning / Afternoon: Meet your dedicated chauffeur → Transfer in a premium vehicle to **Jaipur International Airport** or **Jaipur Railway Station** → Continue onward to your next Rajasthan destination Departure: Depart Jaipur after a carefully paced combination of **royal heritage, luxury hospitality, private sightseeing, cultural experiences and fine dining**.', 7187),
  ('jaipur', 32, 'travel-agent-insights', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS', 'What inexperienced planners often do wrong', NULL, '', 7188),
  ('jaipur', 32, 'travel-agent-insights', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS', 'What an experienced planner does differently', NULL, '', 7189),
  ('jaipur', 32, 'travel-agent-insights', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS', 'Best planning rule', NULL, '', 7190),
  ('jaipur', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', NULL, NULL, '****IF:**** `trip_length <= 1 day` ****THEN:**** Treat Jaipur as a ****Pink City heritage express****: prioritise ****Amber Fort, City Palace, Hawa Mahal and Jantar Mantar****; add ****Jal Mahal**** for a quick photography stop if timing permits. ****Reason:**** Jaipur''s core heritage is concentrated around the historic walled city and Amber area. A one-day visit should focus on its signature forts, palaces and UNESCO-listed heritage rather than attempting distant or secondary attractions. ****IF:**** `trip_length == 3 days` ****THEN:**** Build a classic ****Jaipur royal heritage circuit**** covering ****Amber Fort, Jaigarh Fort, City Palace, Jantar Mantar, Hawa Mahal, Nahargarh Fort, Jal Mahal, and Albert Hall Museum****, with time for traditional food and bazaar shopping. ****Reason:**** Three days provide enough time to experience Jaipur''s major architectural, historical, cultural, photographic and shopping highlights without turning the itinerary into continuous monument-hopping. ****IF:**** `trip_length >= 5 days` ****THEN:**** Expand Jaipur into a ****Rajasthan heritage gateway****, combining Jaipur with nearby destinations such as ****Ajmer & Pushkar, Ranthambore, or other Rajasthan cities**** depending on traveller interests and onward route. ****Reason:**** Jaipur itself can comfortably fill 3–4 days of focused sightseeing; longer stays are better used for nearby Rajasthan experiences while keeping additional time for shopping, food, leisure and cultural activities. Jaipur is also a key part of Rajasthan''s wider tourism circuit. ****IF:**** `trip_type == FIRST_TIME_VISITOR` ****THEN:**** Build a balanced first-timer itinerary around ****Amber Fort, City Palace, Hawa Mahal, Jantar Mantar, Nahargarh Fort and Jal Mahal****, supplemented by ****Albert Hall Museum and Pink City bazaars****. ****Reason:**** These experiences provide the strongest introduction to Jaipur''s royal history, planned urban heritage, architecture, panoramic views, museums, markets and local culture. Jaipur''s walled city itself is UNESCO-listed, while Jantar Mantar is separately inscribed as a World Heritage property. ****IF:**** `trip_type == HONEYMOON` ****THEN:**** Choose a ****heritage palace or luxury boutique hotel****, request a private balcony/terrace, schedule ****Nahargarh sunset, Amber Fort, Jal Mahal photography and rooftop dining****, and include spa and leisure time. ****Reason:**** Jaipur''s romantic appeal comes from royal architecture, illuminated monuments, heritage accommodation, rooftop dining and curated experiences rather than nightlife alone. ****IF:**** `traveler_type == FAMILY` ****THEN:**** Base the family in a centrally located hotel, use a ****private vehicle****, prioritise ****Amber Fort, City Palace, Jantar Mantar, Hawa Mahal, Albert Hall and Jal Mahal****, and keep walking-heavy heritage exploration flexible. ****Reason:**** Jaipur offers a strong combination of educational heritage, architecture, museums, photography and family-friendly sightseeing, while private transport makes the fort circuit considerably easier for children and older family members. ****IF:**** `traveler_type == LUXURY` ****THEN:**** Select an exclusive ****heritage palace or luxury hotel**** with premium dining, spa and personalised service; arrange a dedicated chauffeur, private guide, curated shopping and exclusive cultural experiences. ****Reason:**** Jaipur''s luxury proposition is built around ****royal heritage, palace hospitality, private experiences, fine dining and personalised service****, making it one of Rajasthan''s strongest luxury destinations. ****IF:**** `traveler_type == BUDGET` ****THEN:**** Stay around ****Bani Park, MI Road or the Old City****, use autos/metro where practical, eat at local restaurants, and prioritise ****Hawa Mahal, Pink City walks, bazaars and selected low-cost attractions****. ****Reason:**** Jaipur has accommodation and food options across multiple price levels, while several major experiences can be combined efficiently within the historic city without requiring private transport throughout the trip. ****IF:**** `traveler_interest == NATURE` ****THEN:**** Prioritise ****Nahargarh Fort, Jal Mahal, Man Sagar Lake, Galtaji, Sisodia Rani Garden and Aravalli viewpoints****, while adding relaxed outdoor photography. ****Reason:**** Jaipur is primarily a heritage destination, but its surrounding Aravalli hills, lakes, gardens and elevated forts provide useful nature and landscape experiences. ****IF:**** `traveler_interest == ADVENTURE` ****THEN:**** Add ****hot-air ballooning, cycling, hiking around the Aravallis, fort exploration and outdoor experiences****, while keeping activities weather-appropriate. ****Reason:**** Adventure is supplementary rather than Jaipur''s principal tourism strength; the destination works best when outdoor activities are combined with its major heritage attractions. ****IF:**** `traveler_type == SENIOR` ****THEN:**** Choose an easily accessible hotel, use a ****private vehicle****, prioritise ****City Palace, Hawa Mahal, Albert Hall, Jantar Mantar and Jal Mahal****, and limit strenuous fort walking. ****Reason:**** Jaipur''s main heritage circuit can be experienced comfortably with private transport and planned rest periods, although Amber, Jaigarh and Nahargarh involve more walking and uneven surfaces. ****IF:**** `traveler_type == TRANSIT` ****THEN:**** Use Jaipur as a ****1-night heritage stopover****, with ****Hawa Mahal, City Palace and Jantar Mantar**** in the main circuit and ****Amber Fort or Jal Mahal**** depending on arrival/departure timing. ****Reason:**** Jaipur''s compact historic core allows several major landmarks to be combined efficiently, making it particularly suitable for a short Rajasthan stopover. ****IF:**** `traveler_interest == HISTORY` ****THEN:**** Prioritise ****Amber Fort, City Palace, Jaigarh Fort, Nahargarh Fort, Jantar Mantar and Jaipur''s historic walled city****. ****Reason:**** Jaipur combines Rajput royal architecture, fortified hill landscapes, planned urban heritage and scientific history. The historic walled city was founded in 1727 by Sawai Jai Singh II, while Jantar Mantar preserves one of India''s most significant historic astronomical observatories. ****IF:**** `traveler_interest == WELLNESS` ****THEN:**** Choose a premium heritage hotel or resort, minimise daily transfers, incorporate ****spa treatments, yoga, pool time, leisurely breakfasts and sunset experiences****, and keep sightseeing to selected highlights. ****Reason:**** Jaipur works well for ****heritage-based wellness and luxury leisure**** when the itinerary balances sightseeing with palace-hotel relaxation, spa experiences and slow cultural exploration. ****IF:**** `season == SUMMER` ****THEN:**** Schedule ****Amber Fort, City Palace and outdoor sightseeing in the morning****, keep midday for museums, restaurants or hotel leisure, and reserve bazaars and viewpoints for late afternoon/evening. ****Reason:**** Jaipur''s summer temperatures can become very high, making prolonged midday outdoor sightseeing uncomfortable. A split-day itinerary substantially improves traveller comfort. ****IF:**** `season == MONSOON` ****THEN:**** Keep outdoor schedules flexible, prioritise ****City Palace, Jantar Mantar, Albert Hall and indoor cultural experiences**** during rainy periods, and use clear-weather windows for forts and viewpoints. ****Reason:**** Monsoon rain can interrupt outdoor sightseeing, but Jaipur''s major architectural and museum attractions allow itineraries to remain productive even during wet periods. ****IF:**** `traveler_interest == FOOD` ****THEN:**** Build a dedicated ****Rajasthani food circuit**** featuring ****Dal Baati Churma, Gatte Ki Sabzi, Laal Maas, Pyaaz Kachori, Mirchi Bada, Ghevar and Mawa Kachori****. ****Reason:**** Jaipur is one of Rajasthan''s strongest destinations for experiencing regional cuisine, from traditional thalis and savoury snacks to distinctive Rajasthani sweets. ****IF:**** `traveler_interest == SHOPPING` ****THEN:**** Allocate dedicated time for ****Johari Bazaar, Bapu Bazaar, Tripolia Bazaar, MI Road and Nehru Bazaar****, focusing on jewellery, gemstones, textiles, blue pottery, block prints and handicrafts. ****Reason:**** Jaipur''s historic commercial identity is deeply connected with its bazaars and artisan traditions; UNESCO specifically recognises the walled city''s historic market streets and commercial character. ****IF:**** `traveler_interest == PHOTOGRAPHY` ****THEN:**** Prioritise ****Hawa Mahal, Amber Fort, City Palace, Jal Mahal, Nahargarh Fort and Pink City bazaars****, with sunrise/sunset sessions and blue-hour photography. ****Reason:**** Jaipur offers exceptional visual variety through pink sandstone architecture, royal courtyards, geometric façades, Aravalli landscapes, lake reflections and colourful bazaars. Hawa Mahal is officially described as Jaipur''s iconic landmark. ****IF:**** `trip_type == CULTURAL` ****THEN:**** Combine ****City Palace, Jantar Mantar, Govind Dev Ji Temple, Hawa Mahal, Pink City bazaars and a Rajasthani cultural performance****. ****Reason:**** Jaipur''s cultural identity is strongly embedded in its planned historic city, royal institutions, temples, markets, crafts and performing traditions. ****IF:**** `trip_type == GOLDEN_TRIANGLE` ****THEN:**** Allocate ****3–4 days to Jaipur**** and connect it with ****Delhi and Agra****, using Jaipur for the principal Rajput heritage, palace, fort, shopping and Rajasthani cultural experiences. ****Reason:**** Jaipur is one of the defining destinations of India''s ****Golden Triangle**** and works particularly well as the Rajasthan heritage component of the circuit.', 7191),
  ('jaipur', 34, 'destination-scoring', 'DESTINATION SCORING', NULL, NULL, '| Category | Score | | --- | --- | | Family | 92 | | Young children | 84 | | Honeymoon | 93 | | Romantic | 91 | | Luxury | 96 | | Budget | 86 | | Adventure | 72 | | Culture | 97 | | History | 97 | | Food | 94 | | Shopping | 96 | | Nightlife | 68 | | Relaxation | 82 | | Nature | 72 | | Photography | 97 | | Solo travel | 89 | | Senior travelers | 82 | | First-time travelers | 96 | | Repeat travelers | 91 | | Accessibility | 76 |', 7192),
  ('jaipur', 35, 'final-travel-agent-verdict', 'FINAL TRAVEL AGENT VERDICT', NULL, NULL, 'Best for: Families, honeymooners, couples, senior travellers, history lovers, culture enthusiasts, photographers, food lovers, luxury travellers, shopping enthusiasts, wildlife lovers, spiritual travellers, and first-time Rajasthan visitors looking for a **royal, culturally rich and visually spectacular journey through forts, palaces, deserts, lakes, temples, wildlife and historic cities**. Rajasthan is particularly strong for travellers who want a combination of **heritage, architecture, local culture, cuisine, shopping, photography and distinctive regional experiences**. Best duration: **10–14 days** for a classic Rajasthan circuit covering **Jaipur, Jodhpur, Udaipur, Jaisalmer, Bikaner and Ajmer & Pushkar**; **14–18 days** for a deeper journey adding **Ranthambore, Chittorgarh, Bharatpur and Mount Abu**. Shorter **5–7 day** trips work well when focused on 2–3 destinations rather than attempting the entire state. Best season: **October–March** for the strongest overall combination of comfortable weather, sightseeing conditions, desert experiences and outdoor activities. **November–February** is particularly strong for a classic Rajasthan circuit, although it is also the peak tourism period with higher demand and prices. **April–June** can be extremely hot, while **July–September** brings monsoon conditions but can offer greener landscapes, fewer crowds and better value in many areas. Best stay: A combination of **heritage hotels, palace hotels, luxury resorts, boutique properties, desert camps and comfortable city hotels**, depending on the destination. Rajasthan is particularly well suited to experiential accommodation—from **heritage havelis and former royal residences to luxury desert camps in Jaisalmer and lakeside properties in Udaipur**. Best transport: **Private car/SUV with an experienced driver** is the most convenient option for a multi-city Rajasthan circuit, providing flexibility between forts, villages, heritage sites and rural areas. **Trains** are excellent for selected intercity connections, while flights are useful for longer distances such as **Jaipur–Udaipur or Delhi–Jaisalmer/Jodhpur** when available and convenient. Local autos, taxis and walking work well within individual cities. Must-do: Avoid: Biggest advantage: An exceptional combination of **royal heritage, magnificent forts and palaces, desert landscapes, lakes, wildlife, spirituality, colourful bazaars, regional cuisine, traditional arts, luxury hospitality and diverse cultural experiences**. Rajasthan''s greatest strength is its **destination diversity**: travellers can move from the planned Pink City of Jaipur to Jodhpur''s blue lanes, Udaipur''s lakes, Jaisalmer''s Thar Desert, Ranthambore''s wildlife and Mount Abu''s hills within the same state. Biggest disadvantage: Rajasthan''s **large geographic scale and long intercity travel times** can make poorly planned itineraries tiring. Summer heat can be severe, peak winter brings higher prices and crowds, and attempting too many cities in one journey can turn a culturally rich holiday into a rushed road trip. Rajasthan therefore rewards **slower, regionally clustered itineraries** rather than trying to collect every major destination. Overall destination score: **96/100**', 7193),
  ('jaipur', 36, 'data-quality', 'DATA QUALITY', NULL, NULL, 'information_completeness: 95/100 last_updated: 2026-09-04 last_verified: NOT_LIVE_VERIFIED verified_by: TRAVEL_ENGINE_INITIAL_DATASET sources: IMPORTANT: Prices, opening hours, schedules, visa requirements, availability, accessibility and operational conditions must NOT be treated as permanently valid from this document. These must be sourced from structured, refreshable data.', 7194),
