  ('jodhpur', 19, 'honeymoon-travel', 'HONEYMOON TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'honeymoon_score: ****92**** privacy_score: ****89**** luxury_score: ****90**** Recommended: **Honeymoon itinerary should NOT contain more than:** ****2–3 major activities/day.**** Prefer: ****Royal experience + private time**** over: ****Continuous sightseeing.****', 7205),
  ('jodhpur', 20, 'luxury-travel', 'LUXURY TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'luxury_score: ****92**** Recommended: Luxury should primarily increase: Jodhpur is one of Rajasthan''s stronger choices for **heritage luxury**, particularly because of its royal architecture and palace-hotel ecosystem.', 7206),
  ('jodhpur', 21, 'adventure', 'ADVENTURE', NULL, NULL, 'adventure_score: ****73**** Jodhpur is primarily a **heritage-and-desert adventure destination**, rather than an extreme-adventure hub. Adventure experiences: Rajasthan Tourism specifically lists **Flying Fox** around Mehrangarh and Bishnoi Village Tours among Jodhpur''s activities. Best for:', 7207),
  ('jodhpur', 22, 'senior-travel', 'SENIOR TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, 'senior_suitability: ****84**** walking_intensity: ****MEDIUM**** Rules: Easier options:', 7208),
  ('jodhpur', 23, 'accessibility', 'ACCESSIBILITY', NULL, NULL, 'wheelchair_accessibility: ****PARTIAL**** public_transport_accessibility: ****VARIABLE**** hotel_accessibility: ****VERIFY_PER_HOTEL**** attraction_accessibility: ****VERIFY_PER_ATTRACTION**** Rule: Never assume historic-fort accessibility. Check: Mehrangarh and other historic attractions can involve slopes, stairs and uneven heritage surfaces, so accessibility needs to be assessed attraction-by-attraction.', 7209),
  ('jodhpur', 24, 'food', 'FOOD', NULL, NULL, 'Jodhpur is particularly strong for: Food experiences: Family: Choose hygienic restaurants and milder Rajasthani dishes. Honeymoon: Prioritize one private heritage dining experience. Luxury: Choose curated regional menus and palace-style dining. Budget: Old City eateries provide excellent value.', 7210),
  ('jodhpur', 25, 'shopping', 'SHOPPING', NULL, NULL, 'Strong categories: Prefer: Jodhpur''s traditional market culture is particularly strong around the Clock Tower/Sardar Market area, while Salawas provides a more craft-focused rural experience.', 7211),
  ('jodhpur', 26, 'nightlife', 'NIGHTLIFE', NULL, NULL, 'nightlife_level: ****62**** Jodhpur has a **moderate evening scene**, focused more on rooftop restaurants, heritage properties, live music and illuminated monuments than large-scale clubs. Suitable for: Night experiences: Best for: ****Cultural evenings + rooftop dining**** rather than: ****Club-focused nightlife****', 7212),
  ('jodhpur', 28, 'sample-itinerary-patterns', 'SAMPLE ITINERARY PATTERNS', 'HALF-DAY – PINK CITY HERITAGE & HAWA MAHAL', NULL, 'Morning / Afternoon: Pickup from your hotel in Jaipur → Begin in the historic walled city with **Hawa Mahal**, Jaipur''s iconic five-storey honeycomb façade and one of the city''s signature landmarks → Walk through the surrounding **Johari Bazaar** and old-city streets for traditional jewellery, textiles and handicrafts → Continue to **City Palace** to explore royal courtyards, museums, costumes and Rajput-Mughal architecture → Visit **Jantar Mantar**, the UNESCO-listed astronomical observatory containing monumental geometric instruments → End with traditional **Rajasthani snacks and chai** before returning to your hotel', 7213),
  ('jodhpur', 28, 'sample-itinerary-patterns', 'SAMPLE ITINERARY PATTERNS', '1 DAY – AMER FORT, CITY PALACE & PINK CITY HIGHLIGHTS', NULL, 'Morning: Morning pickup from your hotel for Jaipur''s principal heritage circuit → Drive to **Amber Fort**, approximately 11 km from central Jaipur, and explore its courtyards, Sheesh Mahal, royal quarters and restored tunnel section → Continue to **Jaigarh Fort** for panoramic Aravalli views and its historic fortifications Afternoon: Return toward the walled city → Visit **City Palace** and explore the Mubarak Mahal, Maharani''s Palace and royal museum collections → Continue to **Jantar Mantar** for an introduction to Jaipur''s historic astronomical instruments Evening: Walk around **Hawa Mahal** and the surrounding old-city bazaars → Continue toward **Jal Mahal** for an evening photography stop beside Man Sagar Lake; the palace is primarily viewed from the lakeside because it is not generally open to the public → Finish with a Rajasthani dinner featuring **Dal Baati Churma, Gatte Ki Sabzi and Ghevar**', 7214),
  ('jodhpur', 28, 'sample-itinerary-patterns', 'SAMPLE ITINERARY PATTERNS', '2 DAYS – JAIPUR ROYAL HERITAGE & ARAVALLI CIRCUIT', NULL, 'Day 1: Full-day exploration of Jaipur''s principal heritage attractions → Begin at **Amber Fort** and continue to **Jaigarh Fort** → Return to the walled city for **City Palace, Jantar Mantar and Hawa Mahal** → Spend the evening exploring **Johari Bazaar and Bapu Bazaar** → Enjoy an authentic Rajasthani dinner with traditional sweets Day 2: Begin with **Albert Hall Museum** and its historic collections → Continue to **Birla Temple** for a peaceful cultural stop → Visit **Galtaji** and its historic temple complex in the surrounding hills → Proceed to **Sisodia Rani Garden** for landscaped Mughal-Rajput gardens → End at **Nahargarh Fort** for sunset views over Jaipur; Rajasthan Tourism recommends a taxi or car because there is no convenient public transport directly to the fort ([Rajasthan Tourism][6]) → Return to Jaipur for dinner and departure preparations', 7215),
  ('jodhpur', 29, '6-days-and-5-nights-honeymoon-itinerary', '6 DAYS & 5 NIGHTS HONEYMOON ITINERARY', 'DAY 1 – ROYAL ARRIVAL & PINK CITY ROMANCE', NULL, 'Morning / Afternoon: Arrive at **Jaipur International Airport**, **Jaipur Railway Station**, or reach Jaipur by private road transfer → Meet your private chauffeur and transfer to your romantic boutique, heritage or luxury hotel → Complete check-in and relax in your room Lunch: Enjoy a relaxed lunch featuring traditional Rajasthani cuisine Evening: Take a private sightseeing drive through the **Pink City** → Stop at **Hawa Mahal** for couple photography → Continue through the illuminated old-city streets and bazaars → Enjoy a romantic rooftop dinner overlooking the historic cityscape', 7216),
  ('jodhpur', 29, '6-days-and-5-nights-honeymoon-itinerary', '6 DAYS & 5 NIGHTS HONEYMOON ITINERARY', 'DAY 2 – AMBER FORT, JAIGARH & PRIVATE SUNSET', NULL, 'Morning: After breakfast, depart for **Amber Fort** → Explore the royal courtyards, Sheesh Mahal, palace gardens and historic architecture → Continue to **Jaigarh Fort** for Aravalli panoramas and a quieter heritage experience Afternoon: Return to the hotel for lunch and couple''s leisure → Enjoy private spa time, poolside relaxation or an in-room afternoon Evening: Drive to **Nahargarh Fort** for panoramic sunset views across Jaipur → Return to the hotel for a private candlelit dinner', 7217),
  ('jodhpur', 29, '6-days-and-5-nights-honeymoon-itinerary', '6 DAYS & 5 NIGHTS HONEYMOON ITINERARY', 'DAY 3 – ROYAL PALACES, OBSERVATORY & OLD CITY', NULL, 'Morning: Visit **City Palace** and explore its royal courtyards, museums and historic collections → Continue to **Jantar Mantar**, Jaipur''s UNESCO World Heritage astronomical observatory Lunch: Enjoy a leisurely lunch at a heritage-style restaurant Afternoon: Walk through **Johari Bazaar** → Browse traditional jewellery, gemstones, textiles and handicrafts → Return to the hotel for rest Evening: Enjoy a romantic rooftop dinner overlooking **Hawa Mahal and the Pink City**', 7218),
  ('jodhpur', 29, '6-days-and-5-nights-honeymoon-itinerary', '6 DAYS & 5 NIGHTS HONEYMOON ITINERARY', 'DAY 4 – JAL MAHAL, GALTAJI & COUPLE''S LEISURE', 'honeymoon', 'Morning: Enjoy a relaxed breakfast and depart toward **Jal Mahal** → Photograph the Water Palace from the banks of Man Sagar Lake → Continue to **Galtaji** for a peaceful temple and hillside experience Lunch: Enjoy lunch at a traditional Rajasthani restaurant Afternoon: Return to the hotel → Private couple''s spa treatment → Poolside relaxation → Optional in-room romantic setup Evening: Enjoy a private sunset experience followed by a specially arranged couple''s dinner', 7219),
  ('jodhpur', 29, '6-days-and-5-nights-honeymoon-itinerary', '6 DAYS & 5 NIGHTS HONEYMOON ITINERARY', 'DAY 5 – HERITAGE GARDENS, CULTURE & ROMANTIC FINALE', 'honeymoon', 'Morning: Visit **Albert Hall Museum** for a cultural and architectural experience → Continue to **Birla Temple** → Explore **Sisodia Rani Garden** for landscaped gardens, pavilions and peaceful couple photography Lunch: Enjoy a relaxed lunch and traditional dessert Afternoon: Return to the hotel for leisure → Optional shopping session for Jaipur jewellery, blue pottery, block prints and handicrafts Evening: Celebrate your final night with a **private candlelit dinner** → Optional live Rajasthani folk music and cultural performance → Return to your hotel for overnight stay', 7220),
  ('jodhpur', 29, '6-days-and-5-nights-honeymoon-itinerary', '6 DAYS & 5 NIGHTS HONEYMOON ITINERARY', 'DAY 6 – LEISURE BREAKFAST & DEPARTURE', NULL, 'Morning: Enjoy a slow breakfast and complete checkout → Take a final short walk through the nearby heritage streets or hotel gardens → Optional last-minute shopping for souvenirs Late Morning / Afternoon: Meet your private chauffeur → Transfer to **Jaipur International Airport**, **Jaipur Railway Station** or your onward destination → Depart Jaipur with the final views of the Pink City', 7221),
  ('jodhpur', 30, '6-days-and-5-nights-family-itinerary', '6 DAYS & 5 NIGHTS FAMILY ITINERARY', 'DAY 1 – FAMILY ARRIVAL & PINK CITY INTRODUCTION', 'family', 'Morning / Afternoon: Arrive at **Jaipur International Airport** or **Jaipur Railway Station** → Meet your private family vehicle and transfer to your hotel → Complete check-in and enjoy lunch Evening: Visit **Hawa Mahal** for family photography → Explore the surrounding old-city streets at an easy pace → Enjoy an early Rajasthani dinner → Return to the hotel for family rest', 7222),
  ('jodhpur', 30, '6-days-and-5-nights-family-itinerary', '6 DAYS & 5 NIGHTS FAMILY ITINERARY', 'DAY 2 – AMBER FORT, JAIGARH & JAL MAHAL', NULL, 'Morning: Depart after breakfast for **Amber Fort** → Explore the palace courtyards, Sheesh Mahal and historic sections at a comfortable family pace → Continue to **Jaigarh Fort** for panoramic views Lunch: Enjoy lunch at a family-friendly restaurant Afternoon: Drive toward **Jal Mahal** → Stop beside Man Sagar Lake for photography and refreshments Evening: Return to the hotel → Swimming, indoor games or family leisure → Early dinner and overnight stay', 7223),
  ('jodhpur', 30, '6-days-and-5-nights-family-itinerary', '6 DAYS & 5 NIGHTS FAMILY ITINERARY', 'DAY 3 – CITY PALACE, JANTAR MANTAR & HAWA MAHAL', NULL, 'Morning: Visit **City Palace** → Explore the royal museum collections, courtyards and historic architecture → Continue to **Jantar Mantar** and introduce children to Jaipur''s historic astronomical instruments Lunch: Enjoy a family lunch in the walled city Afternoon: Visit **Hawa Mahal** → Explore nearby bazaars for souvenirs and traditional crafts Evening: Return to the hotel for rest → Enjoy a relaxed family dinner', 7224),
  ('jodhpur', 30, '6-days-and-5-nights-family-itinerary', '6 DAYS & 5 NIGHTS FAMILY ITINERARY', 'DAY 4 – ALBERT HALL, BIRLA TEMPLE & GARDENS', NULL, 'Morning: Visit **Albert Hall Museum** → Explore its historical collections and Indo-Saracenic architecture → Continue to **Birla Temple** for a peaceful cultural visit Lunch: Enjoy lunch at a family-friendly restaurant Afternoon: Visit **Sisodia Rani Garden** → Enjoy a gentle walk through the landscaped gardens → Continue to **Galtaji** if the family is comfortable with the steps and walking Evening: Return to the hotel → Family leisure and dinner', 7225),
  ('jodhpur', 30, '6-days-and-5-nights-family-itinerary', '6 DAYS & 5 NIGHTS FAMILY ITINERARY', 'DAY 5 – NAHARGARH, SHOPPING & CULTURAL EVENING', NULL, 'Morning: After breakfast, drive to **Nahargarh Fort** → Explore the fort and enjoy panoramic views over Jaipur ([Rajasthan Tourism][6]) Lunch: Return toward the city for lunch Afternoon: Enjoy family shopping at **Bapu Bazaar / Johari Bazaar** → Purchase textiles, handicrafts, jewellery, blue pottery and local sweets Evening: Attend a **Rajasthani cultural dinner experience** → Enjoy folk music, traditional performances and regional cuisine → Return to hotel', 7226),
  ('jodhpur', 30, '6-days-and-5-nights-family-itinerary', '6 DAYS & 5 NIGHTS FAMILY ITINERARY', 'DAY 6 – RELAXED MORNING & DEPARTURE', NULL, 'Morning: Enjoy breakfast at the hotel → Complete checkout → Optional final visit to a nearby market for souvenirs Late Morning / Afternoon: Transfer by private family vehicle to **Jaipur International Airport** or **Jaipur Railway Station** → Continue to your next destination', 7227),
  ('jodhpur', 31, '6-days-and-5-nights-luxury-itinerary', '6 DAYS & 5 NIGHTS LUXURY ITINERARY', 'DAY 1 – VIP ARRIVAL & HERITAGE PALACE RETREAT', NULL, 'Morning / Afternoon: Arrive at **Jaipur International Airport** → Meet your dedicated luxury chauffeur and premium vehicle → Transfer to an exclusive **heritage palace or luxury hotel** Rajasthan Tourism maintains a dedicated heritage-property programme featuring properties designed to recreate the experience of staying in former royal structures. → Private check-in with welcome refreshments → Settle into your luxury suite or palace accommodation Lunch: Enjoy a curated multi-course Rajasthani lunch Evening: Relax at the property → Private spa or pool experience → Sunset drinks and private terrace leisure → Finish with an exclusive candlelit dinner', 7228),
  ('jodhpur', 31, '6-days-and-5-nights-luxury-itinerary', '6 DAYS & 5 NIGHTS LUXURY ITINERARY', 'DAY 2 – PRIVATE AMBER FORT & ROYAL ARAVALLI EXPERIENCE', NULL, 'Early Morning: Depart with your private chauffeur for **Amber Fort** → Enjoy a quieter early visit to the palace complex → Explore the royal courtyards, Sheesh Mahal, gardens and historic architecture → Continue to **Jaigarh Fort** for spectacular Aravalli views Lunch: Return to a luxury hotel or heritage property for an elaborate lunch Afternoon: Return to your suite for private relaxation → Spa treatment → Poolside leisure → Optional curated shopping consultation Evening: Private sunset drive toward **Nahargarh Fort** → Enjoy panoramic views across Jaipur → Return for a fine-dining experience', 7229),
  ('jodhpur', 31, '6-days-and-5-nights-luxury-itinerary', '6 DAYS & 5 NIGHTS LUXURY ITINERARY', 'DAY 3 – PRIVATE ROYAL CITY PALACE & JANTAR MANTAR', NULL, 'Morning: Private guided visit to **City Palace** → Explore royal courtyards, museum galleries, costumes, weaponry and palace architecture → Continue to **Jantar Mantar** with a knowledgeable heritage guide Lunch: Enjoy a refined Rajasthani thali or chef-curated regional menu Afternoon: Private walking tour through the **Pink City''s historic bazaars** → Explore jewellery, gemstones, textiles and artisanal crafts → Optional private shopping assistance Evening: Return to your palace hotel → Enjoy a private rooftop or courtyard dinner with traditional Rajasthani music', 7230),
  ('jodhpur', 31, '6-days-and-5-nights-luxury-itinerary', '6 DAYS & 5 NIGHTS LUXURY ITINERARY', 'DAY 4 – JAL MAHAL, GALTAJI & PRIVATE WELLNESS', NULL, 'Morning: Enjoy a leisurely palace breakfast → Drive to **Jal Mahal** → Private photography stop overlooking Man Sagar Lake; the palace itself is generally viewed from the lakeshore rather than entered by ordinary visitors → Continue toward **Galtaji** for a heritage and spiritual experience Lunch: Enjoy a private lunch at your luxury property Afternoon: Reserve the afternoon for exclusive wellness → Couples'' spa treatment → Private pool → Afternoon tea → Suite leisure Evening: Enjoy a private **sunset and fine-dining experience** → Optional curated Rajasthani folk performance at the property', 7231),
  ('jodhpur', 31, '6-days-and-5-nights-luxury-itinerary', '6 DAYS & 5 NIGHTS LUXURY ITINERARY', 'DAY 5 – CULTURAL HERITAGE, GARDENS & ROYAL FINALE', NULL, 'Morning: Visit **Albert Hall Museum** with a private guide → Continue to **Birla Temple** → Explore **Sisodia Rani Garden** for a relaxed heritage-garden experience Lunch: Enjoy an elegant regional lunch Afternoon: Return to the palace hotel → Rest and prepare for the final evening → Optional luxury shopping for Jaipur jewellery, blue pottery, textiles and handcrafted products Evening: Celebrate the final night with an **exclusive royal dinner** → Private courtyard or rooftop setting → Curated Rajasthani menu → Traditional folk music and cultural performance → Return to your luxury suite', 7232),
  ('jodhpur', 31, '6-days-and-5-nights-luxury-itinerary', '6 DAYS & 5 NIGHTS LUXURY ITINERARY', 'DAY 6 – ROYAL BREAKFAST & VIP DEPARTURE', NULL, 'Morning: Enjoy a leisurely final breakfast at the palace hotel → Complete checkout → Optional final private shopping stop Late Morning / Afternoon: Meet your dedicated chauffeur → Transfer in a premium vehicle to **Jaipur International Airport** or **Jaipur Railway Station** → Continue onward to your next Rajasthan destination Departure: Depart Jaipur after a carefully paced combination of **royal heritage, luxury hospitality, private sightseeing, cultural experiences and fine dining**.', 7233),
  ('jodhpur', 32, 'travel-agent-insights', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS', 'What inexperienced planners often do wrong', NULL, '', 7234),
  ('jodhpur', 32, 'travel-agent-insights', 'TRAVEL AGENT INSIGHTS', 'What an experienced planner does differently', NULL, '', 7235),
