  ('pachmarhi', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', NULL, NULL, '***IF:** `trip_length <= 1 day` ***THEN:** Treat Pachmarhi as a **Satpura hill + waterfall + cave express**: prioritise **Bee Falls, Pandava Caves, Jata Shankar Cave and Dhoopgarh sunset**. ***Reason:** Pachmarhi''s strongest short-visit combination is **waterfall swimming + mythological cave heritage + highest peak sunset**. ***IF:** `trip_length == 3 days` ***THEN:** Build a classic **Pachmarhi nature + heritage + spiritual circuit** with **Dhoopgarh, Bee Falls, Apsara Vihar, Rajat Prapat, Jata Shankar, Pandava Caves, Handi Khoh and Reechgarh**. ***Reason:** Three days allow a comfortable mix of **waterfalls, viewpoint drives, natural caves, local heritage and pine forest walks** without excessive rushing. ***IF:** `trip_length >= 5 days` ***THEN:** Expand Pachmarhi into a **regional Biosphere Reserve and eco-adventure circuit**, combining **Pachmarhi hill sightseeing + Chauragarh trek + Satpura National Park safaris (Madai/Panaarpani)**. ***Reason:** Pachmarhi works well as a base for exploring **Satpura Tiger Reserve, deep wilderness treks, and regional waterfalls**. ***IF:** `trip_type == FIRST_TIME_VISITOR` ***THEN:** Prioritise **Dhoopgarh, Bee Falls, Jata Shankar Cave, Pandava Caves and Handi Khoh**. ***Reason:** These provide the strongest introduction to Pachmarhi''s **natural, mythological, geological and high-altitude identity**. ***IF:** `trip_type == HONEYMOON` ***THEN:** Choose an **MP Tourism heritage bungalow or quiet forest resort**, arrange a **private 4x4 Gypsy**, and prioritise **Dhoopgarh sunsets, Rajendragiri gardens, pine forest walks and relaxed resort leisure**. ***Reason:** Pachmarhi''s romantic appeal comes from **misty landscapes, quiet forest trails, dramatic sunsets and peaceful hill climate** rather than nightlife. ***IF:** `traveler_type == FAMILY` ***THEN:** Rent a **private 4x4 Gypsy** and prioritise **Apsara Vihar, Bee Falls, Pandava Caves, Pachmarhi Lake boating and Rajendragiri**. ***Reason:** Pachmarhi offers a useful combination of **gentle nature pools, boating, garden walks and child-friendly cave exploration** for families. ***IF:** `traveler_type == LUXURY` ***THEN:** Select the **best MP Tourism heritage bungalow or boutique forest resort**, arrange a **private chauffeur-driven 4x4 Gypsy and naturalist guide**, and emphasise **custom forest tours, private safaris and heritage resort dining**. ***Reason:** Pachmarhi has a **moderate luxury fit**, strongest for colonial heritage charm and private forest experiences rather than 5-star mega-resorts. ***IF:** `traveler_type == BUDGET` ***THEN:** Stay near **Pachmarhi main market**, use budget guesthouses and shared Gypsies, and prioritise **Jata Shankar, Pandava Caves, Handi Khoh, Bee Falls and Dhoopgarh**. ***Reason:** Core attraction entry fees are minimal; the main budget increase comes from **private Gypsy rentals and deep forest permits**. ***IF:** `traveler_interest == NATURE` ***THEN:** Prioritise **Bee Falls, Rajat Prapat, Handi Khoh, Dhoopgarh and Satpura Tiger Reserve**. ***Reason:** Pachmarhi combines **Satpura biosphere forests, deep ravines, perennial waterfalls and highest peak vistas**. ***IF:** `traveler_interest == ADVENTURE` ***THEN:** Add **Chauragarh mountain trek, Duchess Falls steep forest hike, Reechgarh boulder scrambling and Satpura jeep/boat safaris**. ***Reason:** Pachmarhi is exceptionally strong for **eco-trekking, mountain climbs and jungle wilderness adventures**. ***IF:** `traveler_type == SENIOR` ***THEN:** Choose a **comfortable cantonment hotel**, use **private 4x4 Gypsy transfers**, and prioritise **Pandava Caves gardens, Rajendragiri, Bison Lodge Museum and Pachmarhi Lake**; avoid steep waterfall descents and Chauragarh stairs. ***Reason:** **Steep stairs at Bee Falls (400+ steps), Chauragarh (1,300+ steps) and slippery cave approaches** should be considered when pacing the itinerary. ***IF:** `traveler_interest == HISTORY` ***THEN:** Prioritise **Pandava Caves, Bison Lodge Museum, Christ Church and colonial British-era cantonment architecture**. ***Reason:** Pachmarhi offers a unique mix of **ancient rock-cut cave heritage, tribal history and 19th-century British cantonment legacy**. ***IF:** `traveler_interest == WELLNESS` ***THEN:** Choose a **quiet forest retreat**, reduce daily transfers, and focus on **pine forest walks, mountain air, spa/leisure facilities and peaceful nature spots**. ***Reason:** Pachmarhi''s wellness strength is based on **pine-scented air, serene nature, altitude and slow-paced hill living**. ***IF:** `season == SUMMER` ***THEN:** Prioritise **early-morning waterfall visits and evening sunset drives to Dhoopgarh**, keeping hot afternoon hours flexible. ***Reason:** Pachmarhi experiences **warm daytime temperatures during peak summer**, making midday step-climbing tiring. ***IF:** `season == MONSOON` ***THEN:** Prioritise **Bee Falls, Apsara Vihar, Rajat Prapat and misty viewpoints** while checking trail safety and road conditions. ***Reason:** Monsoon transforms Pachmarhi into a **misty, verdant waterfall paradise**, though Satpura National Park core safaris remain closed. ***IF:** `traveler_interest == FOOD` ***THEN:** Build a local food experience around **poha-jalebi, dal bafti, sabudana dishes, Central Indian thalis and market street snacks**. ***Reason:** Pachmarhi offers a simple, comforting **Central Indian hill station food experience**. ***IF:** `traveler_interest == SHOPPING` ***THEN:** Prioritise **pure forest honey, herbal oils, wooden handicrafts, tribal Gond art and local souvenirs at the town bazaar**. ***Reason:** **Organic forest products and indigenous handicrafts** are Pachmarhi''s most distinctive shopping items. ***IF:** `traveler_interest == PHOTOGRAPHY` ***THEN:** Prioritise **Dhoopgarh sunset, Handi Khoh canyon, Rajat Prapat Silver Falls, Bee Falls stream and Reechgarh rock formations**. ***Reason:** Pachmarhi provides strong photographic variety through **dramatic ravines, cascading waterfalls, ancient rocks and sunset peak panoramas**. ***IF:** `trip_type == CULTURAL` ***THEN:** Combine **Jata Shankar Cave, Gupt Mahadev, Pandava Caves, Bison Lodge and local tribal art shops**. ***Reason:** This creates a balanced introduction to **Pachmarhi''s Shaivite mythology, Mahabharata legends and regional forest culture**. ***IF:** `trip_type == WILDLIFE_EXPERIENCE` ***THEN:** Combine Pachmarhi hill visits with a dedicated safari at **Satpura National Park (Madai or Panaarpani gates)** for tiger, leopard, and sloth bear tracking. ***Reason:** Pachmarhi sits within the **Satpura Biosphere Reserve**, offering direct access to one of Central India''s finest tiger reserves. ***IF:** `trip_type == MADHYA_PRADESH_CIRCUIT` ***THEN:** Combine **Pachmarhi** with onward travel toward **Bhopal, Bhimbetka, Sanchi, Jabalpur or Kanha National Park**. ***Reason:** Pachmarhi is strategically positioned as a **central hill and nature anchor** on wider Madhya Pradesh travel routes. ***IF:** `route_to_other_destinations == TRUE` ***THEN:** Allow sufficient time for **winding mountain roads, Pipariya railway transfers, and forest checkpost buffers** before onward travel. ***Reason:** Ghat roads leading down from the plateau can take longer than expected, especially when connecting to **trains at Pipariya or flights at Bhopal/Jabalpur**.', 7564),
  ('pachmarhi', 34, 'destination-scoring', 'DESTINATION SCORING', NULL, NULL, '| Factor | Score | | --- | --- | | Family | 92 | | Honeymoon | 89 | | Luxury | 74 | | Budget | 91 | | Adventure | 87 | | Culture | 86 | | Food | 78 | | Shopping | 72 | | Nightlife | 60 | | Relaxation | 93 | | Nature | 96 | | Accessibility | 76 | | Safety | 94 | | First-time visitor | 93 | | Photography | 94 |', 7565),
  ('pachmarhi', 35, 'final-travel-agent-verdict', 'FINAL TRAVEL AGENT VERDICT', NULL, NULL, 'Best for: Families, nature lovers, wildlife enthusiasts, history seekers, photographers, spiritual travellers, and first-time visitors to Madhya Pradesh looking for a **convenient gateway to Central India''s tiger reserves with strong geological, historical, and riverfront experiences**. Jabalpur is particularly strong for travellers who want a combination of **Bhedaghat''s Marble Rocks, Narmada River boat rides, Gond and Kalachuri heritage, wildlife gateways, local food, and nature reserves**. Best duration: **2–3 days** for a focused Jabalpur experience covering **Bhedaghat (Marble Rocks and Dhuandhar Falls), Chausath Yogini Temple, Madan Mahal Fort, and Bargi Dam**; **4–5 days** for a deeper experience adding **Dumna Nature Reserve, Lamheta Ghat fossil site, and local historical museums**. For a broader **Central India wildlife circuit**, allow **7–10 days** to combine Jabalpur with major destinations such as **Kanha National Park, Bandhavgarh National Park, Pench, or Amarkantak**. Best season: **October–March** for the strongest overall combination of comfortable weather, sightseeing, river boating, and onward wildlife travel. **October–November** is particularly good for post-monsoon greenery and pleasant temperatures. **December–February** offers cooler conditions and is excellent for combining Jabalpur with tiger safaris. The **monsoon period (July–September)** brings magnificent, roaring views of Dhuandhar Falls, but flexible planning is advisable as **boat rides through the Marble Rocks are usually suspended during this time** due to high water levels and safety concerns. Best stay: A combination of **business hotels, heritage properties, mid-range city hotels, budget guesthouses, and nature resorts** depending on travel style. Jabalpur offers excellent accommodation bases; for convenience and dining, choose accommodation around **Civil Lines, Napier Town, South Avenue Mall area, or central Jabalpur**. For a more scenic, relaxed stay, consider **nature resorts near Bhedaghat or Bargi Dam**. Best transport: Private car/taxi: is the most convenient option for families and travellers combining Jabalpur with nearby wildlife reserves or Bhedaghat. **App-based taxis, auto-rickshaws, and cycle-rickshaws** are useful for local city movement, while **trains and buses** provide highly economical onward connectivity. Jabalpur''s major advantage is its role as a **transport gateway to Madhya Pradesh''s national parks**, with excellent railway connectivity (WCR headquarters) and a well-connected airport (Dumna Airport). Must-do: Avoid: Biggest advantage: An exceptional combination of **geological wonders, Narmada River spiritual experiences, historical forts, local cuisine, and unmatched wildlife connectivity**. Jabalpur''s greatest strength is its position as the **principal gateway to Central India''s finest tiger reserves (Kanha and Bandhavgarh)**, while simultaneously offering substantial and unique natural sights like the **Marble Rocks, Dhuandhar Falls, and Bargi Dam**. Biggest disadvantage: Jabalpur''s **extreme summer heat, seasonal suspension of its most famous boating activity during the monsoon, and occasionally congested urban center** can make it challenging for travellers expecting a year-round, seamless resort holiday. The city can feel quite commercial in the older hubs. Jabalpur therefore works best as a **geology + history + river + wildlife gateway destination** rather than a standalone long-stay leisure retreat. Overall destination score: **90/100**', 7566),
  ('pachmarhi', 36, 'data-quality', 'DATA QUALITY', NULL, NULL, 'information_completeness: 92/100 last_updated: 2026-09-05 last_verified: NOT_LIVE_VERIFIED verified_by: TRAVEL_ENGINE_INITIAL_DATASET sources: IMPORTANT: Prices, opening hours, schedules, visa requirements, availability, accessibility and operational conditions must NOT be treated as permanently valid from this document. These must be sourced from structured, refreshable data.', 7567),
  ('bandhavgarh-and-kanha', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Winter & Peak Safari Season', NULL, '***months:*** December–February ***weather:*** Chilly, crisp mornings with mist rising over sal forests and meadows, followed by pleasant, sunny afternoons ideal for **morning and afternoon tiger safaris, birdwatching, and forest photography**. ***crowd_level:*** HIGH ***price_level:*** HIGH ***overall_score:*** ***74–77*** ***recommended:*** true ***reason:*** Winter is the most comfortable and popular time for exploring both Bandhavgarh and Kanha National Parks. The lush, post-monsoon foliage and crisp weather offer a scenic jungle experience. Early morning safari temperatures can drop near freezing, requiring heavy winter gear. While demand, permit competition, and resort prices reach peak levels during Christmas, New Year, and winter holidays, the overall travel experience remains exceptional.', 7568),
  ('bandhavgarh-and-kanha', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Spring & Shoulder Season', NULL, '***months:*** March–April ***weather:*** Pleasantly warm transitioning to hot afternoons, dry forest canopy, and ideal visibility for **tracking Royal Bengal Tigers, Barasingha in Kanha, and general wildlife around expanding clearings**. ***crowd_level:*** MEDIUM → HIGH ***price_level:*** MEDIUM → HIGH ***overall_score:*** ***80–84*** ***recommended:*** true ***reason:*** Spring is widely regarded as one of the best balanced windows for wildlife enthusiasts in the Central Indian tiger circuit. As water sources begin to shrink and trees shed leaves, tiger sightings and photography conditions improve significantly compared to early winter. Temperatures are warm but manageable, and crowd levels drop slightly outside festival breaks like Holi, offering strong value before the extreme summer heat arrives.', 7569),
  ('bandhavgarh-and-kanha', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Summer & Prime Tiger Sighting Season', NULL, '***months:*** May–June ***weather:*** Very hot and dry with temperatures frequently exceeding 40°C–44°C, but offering the **highest probability for tiger sightings around active waterholes**. ***crowd_level:*** MEDIUM ***price_level:*** MEDIUM ***overall_score:*** ***75–78*** ***recommended:*** true ***reason:*** Extreme heat makes daytime safaris intense and physically demanding, but May and June are legendary among wildlife photographers and tiger chasers. Tigers spend hours soaking in waterholes and shady nullahs to beat the heat, leading to frequent and prolonged sightings. Resort rates ease off slightly and general tourist footfall drops, though dedicated naturalists keep key core safari zones steadily booked.', 7570),
  ('bandhavgarh-and-kanha', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Monsoon & Park Closure Season', NULL, '***months:*** July–September ***weather:*** Heavy monsoon rainfall, lush green revival of the jungle, closed core safari zones, and high humidity across the region. ***crowd_level:*** VERY LOW ***price_level:*** LOW ***overall_score:*** ***85–88*** ***recommended:*** false ***reason:*** All core safari zones in both Bandhavgarh and Kanha remain strictly closed to tourists from July 1st to September 30th for monsoon regeneration and wildlife breeding. While select buffer zones or peripheral nature drives may stay accessible depending on weather and mud conditions, primary tiger safaris are impossible. However, low resort pricing and high availability create very favorable conditions for budget travelers interested purely in monsoon stays, local nature walks, and resort relaxation.', 7571),
  ('bandhavgarh-and-kanha', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Post-Monsoon Reopening Season', NULL, '***months:*** October–November ***weather:*** Clear skies, vibrant green landscapes, fresh forest air, and pleasant weather perfect for **exploring newly reopened core safari tracks and birdwatching**. ***crowd_level:*** MEDIUM → HIGH ***price_level:*** MEDIUM → HIGH ***overall_score:*** ***81–84*** ***recommended:*** true ***reason:*** The core gates of Bandhavgarh and Kanha reopen in October (typically October 1st to 15th). The forests are at their visual peak—dense, emerald green, and filled with vibrant post-monsoon life. Early tiger sightings require patient tracking through dense vegetation, but comfortable daytime temperatures, clear air, and enthusiasm around park reopening make this a prime time for general nature lovers and safari goers.', 7572),
  ('bandhavgarh-and-kanha', 10, 'budget-strategy', 'BUDGET STRATEGY', NULL, NULL, '***Where saving money is usually not recommended:*** Bandhavgarh and Kanha can be budget-managed with advance planning, though fixed permit prices make safari travel inherently higher in cost than general city tourism.', 7573),
  ('bandhavgarh-and-kanha', 12, 'airport-transfer-logic', 'AIRPORT TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Family', 'family', 'Pre-booked ***SUV/MPV*** from Jabalpur Airport or Umaria Railway Station for direct park transfers.', 7574),
  ('bandhavgarh-and-kanha', 12, 'airport-transfer-logic', 'AIRPORT TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Honeymoon', 'honeymoon', 'Private ***sedan/SUV*** with pre-arranged resort pickup for seamless jungle resort arrivals.', 7575),
  ('bandhavgarh-and-kanha', 12, 'airport-transfer-logic', 'AIRPORT TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Luxury', 'luxury', 'Chauffeur-driven ***luxury SUV*** with private transfer directly to high-end wilderness lodges.', 7576),
  ('bandhavgarh-and-kanha', 12, 'airport-transfer-logic', 'AIRPORT TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Budget', 'budget', 'Train to ***Umaria (Bandhavgarh) or Jabalpur/Gondia (Kanha)***, followed by local shared taxis or buses. ***reason:*** Both parks sit within the ***Sal forests of Central India***, connected via scenic road transfers from Jabalpur Airport (160–170 km) or regional railheads like Umaria and Katni.', 7577),
  ('bandhavgarh-and-kanha', 18, 'family-travel', 'FAMILY TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, '***child_friendly_score:*** ***86*** ***best_ages:*** ***Rules:*** ***Prefer:*** ***Avoid:***', 7578),
  ('bandhavgarh-and-kanha', 19, 'honeymoon-travel', 'HONEYMOON TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, '***honeymoon_score:*** ***92*** ***privacy_score:*** ***91*** ***luxury_score:*** ***95*** ***Recommended:*** ***Honeymoon itinerary should NOT contain more than:*** ***1–2 safaris per day.*** Prefer: ***Resort luxury + wildlife safaris + private dining*** over: ***Exhaustive 4-safari daily marathons.***', 7579),
  ('bandhavgarh-and-kanha', 20, 'luxury-travel', 'LUXURY TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, '***luxury_score:*** ***95*** ***Recommended:*** Luxury here primarily means:', 7580),
  ('bandhavgarh-and-kanha', 21, 'adventure', 'ADVENTURE', NULL, NULL, '***adventure_score:*** ***94*** Bandhavgarh & Kanha represent a ***premier Indian tiger safari and eco-adventure destination***. ***Adventure experiences:*** ***Strongest adventure zones:*** ***Tala Zone + Kanha Zone + Dhamokhar Night Buffer + Mukki Zone***', 7581),
  ('bandhavgarh-and-kanha', 22, 'senior-travel', 'SENIOR TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, '***senior_suitability:*** ***82*** ***walking_intensity:*** ***LOW*** ***Rules:*** ***Easier options:*** ***Avoid:***', 7582),
  ('bandhavgarh-and-kanha', 23, 'accessibility', 'ACCESSIBILITY', NULL, NULL, '***wheelchair_accessibility:*** ***LIMITED*** ***public_transport_accessibility:*** ***LOW*** ***hotel_accessibility:*** ***VERIFY_PER_HOTEL*** ***attraction_accessibility:*** ***VERIFY_PER_ATTRACTION*** ***Rule:*** Do not assume accessibility on ***unpaved jungle tracks, open 4x4 Gypsies, or historic rock carvings***. ***Check:***', 7583),
  ('bandhavgarh-and-kanha', 24, 'food', 'FOOD', NULL, NULL, 'Bandhavgarh & Kanha are strongest for: ***Food experiences:*** ***Budget:*** Local gate dhabas & homestays. ***Premium:*** Luxury safari lodge dining.', 7584),
  ('bandhavgarh-and-kanha', 25, 'shopping', 'SHOPPING', NULL, NULL, '***Strong categories:*** ***Prefer:*** Village markets around Tala and Khatia offer authentic Gond tribal paintings directly from local artisans.', 7585),
  ('bandhavgarh-and-kanha', 26, 'nightlife', 'NIGHTLIFE', NULL, NULL, '***nightlife_level:*** ***30*** Bandhavgarh & Kanha feature ***zero commercial urban nightlife***, focusing entirely on quiet jungle evenings, stargazing, and wildlife documentaries. ***Suitable for:*** ***Night experiences:*** ***Best for:*** ***Early nights & quiet nature*** rather than: ***Late-night partying.***', 7586),
  ('bandhavgarh-and-kanha', 28, 'sample-itinerary-patterns', 'SAMPLE ITINERARY PATTERNS', 'HALF-DAY – BHEDAGHAT MARBLE ROCKS & DHUANDHAR FALLS', NULL, '****Morning / Afternoon**** Pickup from your hotel in Jabalpur → Drive to ****Bhedaghat Marble Rocks**** and experience the towering marble cliffs along the Narmada River → Enjoy a ****Narmada River boat ride**** through the marble gorge → Continue to ****Dhuandhar Falls**** to see the Narmada cascading dramatically through the rocky landscape → Visit the nearby ****Chausath Yogini Temple**** if time and mobility permit → Browse local ****marble and soapstone handicrafts**** before returning to Jabalpur', 7587),
  ('bandhavgarh-and-kanha', 28, 'sample-itinerary-patterns', 'SAMPLE ITINERARY PATTERNS', '1 DAY – BHEDAGHAT, DHUANDHAR & CHAUSATH YOGINI', NULL, '****Morning**** Morning pickup from your hotel for Jabalpur''s principal nature circuit → Drive to ****Bhedaghat Marble Rocks**** → Enjoy a ****Narmada boat ride**** between the dramatic marble cliffs → Continue to ****Chausath Yogini Temple**** for its historic temple complex and panoramic views ****Afternoon**** Lunch near Bhedaghat → Visit ****Dhuandhar Falls**** and explore the viewing areas around the waterfall → Browse the nearby ****marble handicraft markets**** ****Evening**** Return toward Jabalpur → Stop at ****Gwarighat**** for a peaceful Narmada riverside experience and evening aarti → Return to your hotel for dinner', 7588),
  ('bandhavgarh-and-kanha', 28, 'sample-itinerary-patterns', 'SAMPLE ITINERARY PATTERNS', '2 DAYS – JABALPUR NARMADA, NATURE & HERITAGE CIRCUIT', NULL, '****Day 1**** Full-day exploration of the Bhedaghat region → Begin at ****Bhedaghat Marble Rocks**** and enjoy the Narmada boat ride → Visit ****Chausath Yogini Temple**** → Continue to ****Dhuandhar Falls**** for waterfall views and photography → Explore local marble and soapstone handicrafts → Return to Jabalpur for an evening visit to ****Gwarighat**** ****Day 2**** Begin with ****Madan Mahal Fort**** and explore its historic hilltop ruins associated with Jabalpur''s Gond heritage → Continue to ****Balancing Rock**** near Madan Mahal → Visit ****Rani Durgavati Museum**** for regional history, tribal culture and archaeological collections → Proceed to ****Dumna Nature Reserve**** for a relaxed nature and birdwatching experience → Return to Jabalpur for dinner', 7589),
  ('bandhavgarh-and-kanha', 29, '6-days-and-5-nights-honeymoon-itinerary', '6 DAYS & 5 NIGHTS HONEYMOON ITINERARY', 'DAY 1 – ROMANTIC ARRIVAL & NARMADA EVENING', 'honeymoon', '****Morning / Afternoon**** Arrive at ****Jabalpur Airport**** or ****Jabalpur Railway Station**** → Meet your private chauffeur and transfer to your romantic hotel or boutique property → Complete check-in and relax ****Lunch**** Enjoy a relaxed lunch featuring Central Indian and local Jabalpur specialities ****Evening**** Drive to ****Gwarighat**** → Spend a peaceful evening beside the Narmada River → Experience the evening ****Narmada aarti**** → Return to the hotel for a romantic dinner', 7590),
  ('bandhavgarh-and-kanha', 29, '6-days-and-5-nights-honeymoon-itinerary', '6 DAYS & 5 NIGHTS HONEYMOON ITINERARY', 'DAY 2 – BHEDAGHAT MARBLE ROCKS & DHUANDHAR ROMANCE', NULL, '****Morning**** After breakfast, depart for ****Bhedaghat Marble Rocks**** → Enjoy a scenic ****Narmada boat ride**** through the marble gorge → Take couple photographs beside the dramatic marble cliffs ****Afternoon**** Enjoy lunch near Bhedaghat → Visit ****Chausath Yogini Temple**** for its historic setting and panoramic surroundings ****Evening**** Continue to ****Dhuandhar Falls**** → Enjoy the waterfall views and surrounding landscape → Return to Jabalpur for a relaxed romantic dinner', 7591),
  ('bandhavgarh-and-kanha', 29, '6-days-and-5-nights-honeymoon-itinerary', '6 DAYS & 5 NIGHTS HONEYMOON ITINERARY', 'DAY 3 – MADAN MAHAL, BALANCING ROCK & COUPLE''S LEISURE', 'honeymoon', '****Morning**** Visit ****Madan Mahal Fort**** → Explore the historic hilltop fort and its panoramic surroundings → Continue to ****Balancing Rock**** for photographs ****Lunch**** Enjoy lunch at a comfortable city restaurant ****Afternoon**** Return to the hotel → Private couple''s spa or wellness session → Poolside relaxation and leisure ****Evening**** Enjoy a private dinner at the hotel → Optional romantic room or terrace setup', 7592),
  ('bandhavgarh-and-kanha', 29, '6-days-and-5-nights-honeymoon-itinerary', '6 DAYS & 5 NIGHTS HONEYMOON ITINERARY', 'DAY 4 – DUMNA NATURE & PEACEFUL JABALPUR', NULL, '****Morning**** Enjoy a relaxed breakfast → Visit ****Dumna Nature Reserve**** for a peaceful forest and wildlife experience → Enjoy nature photography and birdwatching ****Lunch**** Return toward the city for lunch ****Afternoon**** Relax at the hotel → Enjoy private leisure time → Optional couple''s massage or pool session ****Evening**** Take a relaxed drive through Jabalpur → Enjoy dinner at a refined local restaurant', 7593),
  ('bandhavgarh-and-kanha', 29, '6-days-and-5-nights-honeymoon-itinerary', '6 DAYS & 5 NIGHTS HONEYMOON ITINERARY', 'DAY 5 – BARGI DAM & ROMANTIC NARMADA ESCAPE', 'honeymoon', '****Morning**** After breakfast, drive toward ****Bargi Dam**** → Enjoy views of the Narmada reservoir → Take a scenic ****boat ride**** or other available water-based experience → Spend relaxed couple time beside the reservoir ****Lunch**** Enjoy lunch near the Bargi Dam area ****Afternoon**** Return to Jabalpur → Rest at the hotel ****Evening**** Celebrate the final night with a ****private candlelit dinner**** → Optional couple photography and romantic hotel setup', 7594),
  ('bandhavgarh-and-kanha', 29, '6-days-and-5-nights-honeymoon-itinerary', '6 DAYS & 5 NIGHTS HONEYMOON ITINERARY', 'DAY 6 – LEISURE BREAKFAST & DEPARTURE', NULL, '****Morning**** Enjoy a slow breakfast → Complete checkout → Optional last-minute shopping for ****marble handicrafts and local souvenirs**** ****Late Morning / Afternoon**** Meet your private chauffeur → Transfer to ****Jabalpur Airport**** or ****Jabalpur Railway Station**** → Depart Jabalpur for your onward destination', 7595),
  ('bandhavgarh-and-kanha', 30, '6-days-and-5-nights-family-itinerary', '6 DAYS & 5 NIGHTS FAMILY ITINERARY', 'DAY 1 – FAMILY ARRIVAL & GWARIGHAT EVENING', 'family', '****Morning / Afternoon**** Arrive at ****Jabalpur Airport**** or ****Jabalpur Railway Station**** → Meet your family vehicle and transfer to your hotel → Complete check-in and enjoy lunch ****Evening**** Visit ****Gwarighat**** → Enjoy a relaxed riverside family experience → Experience the evening ****Narmada aarti**** → Return to the hotel for dinner and rest', 7596),
  ('bandhavgarh-and-kanha', 30, '6-days-and-5-nights-family-itinerary', '6 DAYS & 5 NIGHTS FAMILY ITINERARY', 'DAY 2 – BHEDAGHAT, BOATING & DHUANDHAR FALLS', NULL, '****Morning**** Depart after breakfast for ****Bhedaghat Marble Rocks**** → Enjoy the ****Narmada boat ride**** through the marble cliffs → Explore the riverside scenery and photography points ****Lunch**** Enjoy lunch near Bhedaghat ****Afternoon**** Visit ****Dhuandhar Falls**** → Explore the designated viewing areas → Continue to nearby ****marble handicraft markets**** for family shopping ****Evening**** Return to Jabalpur → Family dinner and overnight stay', 7597),
  ('bandhavgarh-and-kanha', 30, '6-days-and-5-nights-family-itinerary', '6 DAYS & 5 NIGHTS FAMILY ITINERARY', 'DAY 3 – CHAUSATH YOGINI, MADAN MAHAL & BALANCING ROCK', NULL, '****Morning**** Visit ****Chausath Yogini Temple**** → Explore the historic temple and surrounding views → Continue to ****Madan Mahal Fort**** → Introduce children to Jabalpur''s Gond and regional history ****Lunch**** Enjoy a family-friendly lunch ****Afternoon**** Visit ****Balancing Rock**** → Stop for family photographs → Return to the hotel for rest ****Evening**** Enjoy a relaxed family dinner', 7598),
  ('bandhavgarh-and-kanha', 30, '6-days-and-5-nights-family-itinerary', '6 DAYS & 5 NIGHTS FAMILY ITINERARY', 'DAY 4 – RANI DURGAVATI MUSEUM & DUMNA NATURE', NULL, '****Morning**** Visit ****Rani Durgavati Museum**** → Explore regional archaeological, tribal and cultural collections ****Lunch**** Enjoy lunch in Jabalpur ****Afternoon**** Proceed to ****Dumna Nature Reserve**** → Enjoy a gentle nature outing → Look for birds and wildlife in the forested surroundings → Allow children time for relaxed outdoor activities ****Evening**** Return to the hotel → Family leisure and dinner', 7599);
