  ('bandhavgarh-and-kanha', 33, 'destination-decision-rules', 'DESTINATION DECISION RULES', NULL, NULL, '***IF:** `trip_length <= 2 days` ***THEN:** Pick **ONE park only** (either Bandhavgarh or Kanha) and focus strictly on **3–4 core zone safaris** (e.g., Tala/Magadhi in Bandhavgarh OR Kanha/Mukki in Kanha). ***Reason:** Splitting 2 days between both parks results in **excessive transit time (5–6 hours driving)** and missed morning safari gates. ***IF:** `trip_length == 5 to 6 days` ***THEN:** Build a classic **Bandhavgarh + Kanha Tiger Reserve Circuit** (2–3 nights Bandhavgarh + 2–3 nights Kanha) with **6–8 total safaris**. ***Reason:** Five to six days allow a complete **Central Indian wildlife odyssey**, balancing Bandhavgarh''s high tiger density with Kanha''s Sal forests and Barasingha meadows. ***IF:** `trip_length >= 7 days` ***THEN:** Expand the circuit into a **Grand Central Indian Wilderness Experience** combining **Bandhavgarh + Kanha + Pench National Park** or adding buffer night safaris and village cultural walks. ***Reason:** Extended trips allow full multi-zone coverage, **night buffer tracking**, and relaxed downtime without safari fatigue. ***IF:** `trip_type == FIRST_TIME_VISITOR` ***THEN:** Combine **Bandhavgarh (Tala / Magadhi zones)** and **Kanha (Kanha / Mukki zones)** using registered open 4x4 Gypsies and expert naturalists. ***Reason:** Delivers the highest probability of **tiger sightings, varied landscapes, and iconic Central Indian wildlife** for first-timers. ***IF:** `trip_type == HONEYMOON` ***THEN:** Book **private high-end luxury wilderness lodges** (e.g., Taj Safaris, Pugdundee Safaris), reserve **exclusive private Gypsies**, and arrange private bush dinners, nature walks, and infinity pool downtime. ***Reason:** The circuit offers **secluded wilderness, colonial-style tented camps, and intimate outdoor luxury** away from crowded tourist centers. ***IF:** `traveler_type == FAMILY` ***THEN:** Select **resorts with large lawns, swimming pools, and in-house naturalists**, alternate morning core safaris with afternoon buffer drives/nature walks, and book contiguous resort rooms. ***Reason:** Keeps children engaged while managing the physical demands of **4-hour pre-dawn open-Gypsy safari drives**. ***IF:** `traveler_type == LUXURY` ***THEN:** Stay at **ultra-luxury lodges near Tala Gate (Bandhavgarh) and Mukki/Khatia Gates (Kanha)**, book **private Gypsies with senior naturalists**, and charter private air/road transfers from Jabalpur or Raipur. ***Reason:** Both parks host world-class **luxury eco-lodges offering bespoke safari hosting and gourmet dining**. ***IF:** `traveler_type == BUDGET` ***THEN:** Stay in **MP Tourism resorts or local homestays near Khatia (Kanha) and Tala (Bandhavgarh)**, utilize **single-seat / shared Gypsy permits**, and opt for buffer zone drives. ***Reason:** Main costs are driven by **permit fees and private Gypsy rentals**; shared options and budget stays keep costs manageable. ***IF:** `traveler_interest == TIGER_PHOTOGRAPHY` ***THEN:** Spend **at least 3 nights in Bandhavgarh (Tala & Magadhi zones)** with a **dedicated private Gypsy and custom camera lens mounts**. ***Reason:** Bandhavgarh''s **rugged terrain and high predator density** provide exceptional close-range tiger photography opportunities. ***IF:** `traveler_interest == BIODIVERSITY_AND_BIRDS` ***THEN:** Prioritize **Kanha National Park (Mukki and Sarhi zones)** and add a **guided nature walk along the park periphery**. ***Reason:** Kanha''s vast **Sal forests, wetlands, and open meadows** host over 300 bird species and the rare Hard Ground Barasingha. ***IF:** `traveler_type == SENIOR` ***THEN:** Request **Gypsies with backrest cushions and step-stools**, choose lodges within **10 minutes of safari gates**, and limit to **one safari per day** with rest afternoons. ***Reason:** Open-Gypsy rides over **bumpy forest tracks for 4+ hours** can cause physical strain and fatigue. ***IF:** `traveler_interest == HISTORY_AND_HERITAGE` ***THEN:** Prioritize **Bandhavgarh National Park** and include viewpoints of **Bandhavgarh Fort, Shesh Shaiya (reclining Vishnu statue), and ancient rock-cut caves**. ***Reason:** Bandhavgarh uniquely integrates **ancient 2,000-year-old archaeological heritage directly within a active tiger reserve**. ***IF:** `traveler_interest == NIGHT_WILDLIFE` ***THEN:** Book **Night Buffer Safaris** in Bandhavgarh (Dhamokhar/Panpatha) or Kanha (Khatia buffer). ***Reason:** Core zones close at sunset; buffer night drives offer chances to spot **nocturnal predators, sloth bears, Indian civets, and owls**. ***IF:** `season == WINTER (NOV - FEB)` ***THEN:** Advise **heavy thermal layering, windcheaters, gloves, and caps** for pre-dawn open-Gypsy drives, transitioning to lighter clothes by midday. ***Reason:** Temperatures in open jungle meadows can plunge to **2°C–5°C during early morning drives**. ***IF:** `season == SUMMER (MAR - JUN)` ***THEN:** Book **morning core safaris**, carry heavy dust protection (scarves/masks), stay hydrated, and focus on **waterhole animal tracking**. ***Reason:** Rising heat (38°C–44°C) forces wildlife to **frequent open waterholes**, dramatically increasing sighting probability despite dust and warmth. ***IF:** `season == MONSOON (JUL - SEP)` ***THEN:** Restrict itinerary to **Buffer Zone Safaris only** or pivot to non-wildlife destinations. ***Reason:** All **core safari gates across Bandhavgarh and Kanha remain strictly closed** from July 1 to September 30 for animal breeding and forest regeneration. ***IF:** `traveler_interest == LOCAL_CULTURE` ***THEN:** Add a **guided Baiga or Gond tribal village walk**, visit local weekly haat markets near Kanha, and purchase authentic Gond paintings. ***Reason:** The regions surrounding Kanha and Bandhavgarh are rich in **indigenous tribal heritage, art, and traditional forest lifestyles**. ***IF:** `traveler_interest == PHOTOGRAPHY` ***THEN:** Secure **private Gypsies for full mobility**, carry dust-proof camera covers, and focus on **Kanha''s misty golden morning meadows and Bandhavgarh''s sandstone cliffs**. ***Reason:** Combines **dramatic landscape geometry with diverse wildlife portrait opportunities**. ***IF:** `trip_type == MADHYA_PRADESH_CIRCUIT` ***THEN:** Route travel seamlessly as **Jabalpur → Bandhavgarh → Kanha → Pench / Nagpur** or reverse. ***Reason:** Optimizes **ground transfer logistics along clean highway corridors** without backtracking. ***IF:** `route_to_other_destinations == TRUE` ***THEN:** Pre-book **reliable private AC cabs** and allow **5–6 hours for Bandhavgarh to Kanha** and **4–5 hours for Kanha to Jabalpur/Nagpur**. ***Reason:** Highway conditions vary and **pre-dawn or late-night forest drives require experienced drivers**.', 7611),
  ('bandhavgarh-and-kanha', 34, 'destination-scoring', 'DESTINATION SCORING', NULL, NULL, '| Factor | Score | | --- | --- | | Family | 91 | | Honeymoon | 92 | | Luxury | 94 | | Budget | 68 | | Adventure | 95 | | Culture | 82 | | Food | 76 | | Shopping | 62 | | Nightlife | 35 | | Relaxation | 88 | | Nature | 97 | | Accessibility | 65 | | Safety | 94 | | First-time visitor | 93 | | Photography | 97 |', 7612),
  ('bandhavgarh-and-kanha', 35, 'final-travel-agent-verdict', 'FINAL TRAVEL AGENT VERDICT', NULL, NULL, 'Best for: Wildlife enthusiasts, wildlife photographers, nature lovers, adventure travellers, families, luxury eco-tourists, and first-time visitors to India looking for **Central India''s premier tiger reserves with exceptionally high predator density, Kipling-inspired Sal forest landscapes, and rich tribal heritage**. This iconic circuit is particularly strong for travellers who want a combination of **Bandhavgarh''s high-density tiger tracking and ancient fort ruins, Kanha''s legendary Hard Ground Barasingha meadows, open 4x4 Gypsies, luxury safari lodges, and authentic Gond and Baiga culture**. Best duration: **5–6 days** for a classic, high-value Bandhavgarh & Kanha circuit (split evenly with **2–3 nights in Bandhavgarh and 3 nights in Kanha** covering 6–8 total safaris); **7–10 days** for a comprehensive Central Indian wildlife odyssey adding **Pench National Park, buffer night safaris, and tribal cultural excursions**. A rushed **1–2 day trip to either park is strongly discouraged** due to permit constraints, gate logistics, and travel distances. Best season: **October–June** when core safari gates are fully open. **November–February (Winter)** offers the most comfortable weather, crisp mornings (2°C–5°C), misty golden landscapes, and excellent birdwatching. **March–June (Summer)** brings intense heat (38°C–44°C) and dusty conditions, but delivers **unrivaled tiger tracking and wildlife sighting density** as animals gather predictably around shrinking waterholes. **July–September (Monsoon) must be avoided for core safaris**, as all core gates across both parks remain strictly closed for animal breeding and forest regeneration. Best stay: A combination of **ultra-luxury wilderness lodges, boutique eco-camps, heritage properties, MP Tourism resorts, and local jungle homestays** depending on budget and preference. For optimal logistics, select accommodations located within **10–15 minutes of your assigned safari gate** (e.g., Tala or Magadhi area for Bandhavgarh; Mukki or Khatia/Kisli area for Kanha) to minimize pre-dawn transit delays. High-end lodges around Mukki (Kanha) and Tala (Bandhavgarh) offer world-class naturalists and bespoke wilderness dining. Best transport: Private chauffeur-driven AC cabs: are the most efficient option for ground transfers between airports, railway stations, and national parks. The circuit is best accessed via **Jabalpur (JBP)**, **Nagpur (NAG)**, or **Raipur (RPR)** airports and major railway hubs like **Jabalpur, Katni, or Umaria**. For inside the reserves, **registered open 4x4 Gypsies with licensed park drivers and certified forest department guides** are mandatory; self-driving private vehicles inside core zones is strictly prohibited. Must-do: Avoid: Biggest advantage: An unparalleled combination of **world-class predator tracking, rich biodiversity, ancient archaeological heritage, and exceptional wilderness conservation**. Bandhavgarh provides unrivaled tiger density and dramatic landscape geometry, while Kanha complements it with expansive Sal meadows, rare endemic species, and sublime eco-luxe hospitality—making this circuit the indisputable gold standard for African-style safaris in India. Biggest disadvantage: The circuit''s **strict permit availability, 120-day advance booking pressure, rigid zone entry regulations, and significant transit times** between parks (5–6 hours) require meticulous long-term planning. Additionally, extreme winter cold, summer heat, and the complete closure of core zones during the 3-month monsoon limit spontaneous year-round travel. Overall destination score: **96/100**', 7613),
  ('bandhavgarh-and-kanha', 36, 'data-quality', 'DATA QUALITY', NULL, NULL, 'information_completeness: 95/100 last_updated: 2026-09-05 last_verified: NOT_LIVE_VERIFIED verified_by: TRAVEL_ENGINE_INITIAL_DATASET sources: IMPORTANT: Prices, opening hours, schedules, visa requirements, availability, accessibility and operational conditions must NOT be treated as permanently valid from this document. These must be sourced from structured, refreshable data.', 7614),
  ('omkareshwar', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Winter & Peak Pilgrimage Season', NULL, '***months:*** October–February ***weather:*** Pleasant, cool days and crisp mornings with temperatures ranging between 12°C and 28°C, making conditions comfortable for **temple darshan, river ghat visits, island parikrama walks, and Narmada boat rides**. ***crowd_level:*** HIGH ***price_level:*** HIGH ***overall_score:*** ***75–78*** ***recommended:*** true ***reason:*** Winter is the most comfortable and popular time for visiting Omkareshwar. Clear skies and mild temperatures make navigating temple stairs, crossing suspension bridges, and completing the 7 km Omkareshwar Parvat Parikrama pleasant. Major religious celebrations like Kartik Purnima, Diwali, and Mahashivratri draw massive crowds of devotees, leading to longer temple queues and peak hotel pricing. Despite higher footfalls, the overall spiritual atmosphere and pleasant weather offer an exceptional experience.', 7615),
  ('omkareshwar', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Spring & Transition Season', NULL, '***months:*** March–April ***weather:*** Warm transitioning to hot afternoons, with daytime temperatures rising from 32°C to 38°C, requiring morning and evening hours for **comfortable temple visits and scenic riverfront strolls**. ***crowd_level:*** MEDIUM ***price_level:*** MEDIUM ***overall_score:*** ***80–83*** ***recommended:*** true ***reason:*** Spring offers a balanced window for pilgrims and heritage travellers looking to avoid winter peak holiday crowds. While afternoon temperatures become warm, early morning darshan and evening Narmada Aarti remain pleasant. Tourist footfall drops slightly outside major festival days, leading to moderate accommodation rates and shorter queue waiting times at both Omkareshwar and Mamleshwar Jyotirlingas.', 7616),
  ('omkareshwar', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Summer Season', NULL, '***months:*** May–June ***weather:*** Hot and dry conditions with peak afternoon temperatures exceeding 39°C to 42°C, though **early morning and late evening river breezes offer relief for boat rides and temple visits**. ***crowd_level:*** MEDIUM ***price_level:*** MEDIUM ***overall_score:*** ***74–77*** ***recommended:*** true ***reason:*** Summer brings intense heat across Central India, making daytime walking along open stone ghats and island trails physically demanding. However, the town remains functional with steady streams of pilgrims. Late afternoons and evenings bring cooler river breezes, making sunset boat rides across the Narmada and night Aarti enjoyable. Hotel rates remain reasonable and booking availability is high.', 7617),
  ('omkareshwar', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Monsoon & Sacred Shravan Season', NULL, '***months:*** July–September ***weather:*** Moderate to heavy rainfall bringing lush green landscapes along the Satpura hills and surging Narmada river waters. ***crowd_level:*** HIGH → VERY HIGH (during Shravan) / LOW (non-Shravan days) ***price_level:*** MEDIUM → HIGH ***overall_score:*** ***82–86*** ***recommended:*** true ***reason:*** Monsoon transforms the Satpura hills and Narmada river valley into a picturesque green sanctuary. The holy month of Shravan (July–August) brings a massive influx of Kanwar yatris and Shiva devotees, filling the ghats and temples. While heavy rain can occasionally disrupt boat rides or slippery island trails, monsoon pilgrimage holds deep spiritual significance. Outside peak Shravan festival days, low crowds and discounted hotel tariffs make it an attractive time for quiet retreats.', 7618),
  ('omkareshwar', 7, 'seasonality', 'SEASONALITY', 'Post-Monsoon Season', NULL, '***months:*** October–November ***weather:*** Clear skies, refreshed green surroundings, pleasant post-rain weather, and full Narmada river levels ideal for **photography, river cruises, and heritage sightseeing**. ***crowd_level:*** MEDIUM → HIGH ***price_level:*** MEDIUM → HIGH ***overall_score:*** ***81–84*** ***recommended:*** true ***reason:*** Post-monsoon brings ideal weather to Omkareshwar as rainfall subsides and humidity drops. The Narmada River flows in full majesty, creating spectacular backdrops for boat rides and photographic vistas across Mamleshwar Setu. With comfortable temperatures returning, this period marks the opening of peak travel season, offering an excellent combination of clear weather and vibrant spiritual activity.', 7619),
  ('omkareshwar', 10, 'budget-strategy', 'BUDGET STRATEGY', NULL, NULL, '***Where saving money is usually not recommended:***', 7620),
  ('omkareshwar', 12, 'airport-transfer-logic', 'AIRPORT TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Family', 'family', 'Pre-booked ***SUV/MPV*** from Indore Airport for comfortable direct transfer.', 7621),
  ('omkareshwar', 12, 'airport-transfer-logic', 'AIRPORT TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Honeymoon', 'honeymoon', 'Private ***sedan/SUV*** with hotel pickup and flexible sightseeing.', 7622),
  ('omkareshwar', 12, 'airport-transfer-logic', 'AIRPORT TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Luxury', 'luxury', 'Chauffeur-driven ***premium SUV*** with private temple and heritage circuit.', 7623),
  ('omkareshwar', 12, 'airport-transfer-logic', 'AIRPORT TRANSFER LOGIC', 'Budget', 'budget', 'Bus/shared taxi from ***Indore or Khandwa*** followed by local autos. ***reason:*** Omkareshwar is a compact pilgrimage destination, so a private transfer is most useful for ***airport/railway access and nearby excursions*** rather than local sightseeing.', 7624),
  ('omkareshwar', 18, 'family-travel', 'FAMILY TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, '***child_friendly_score:*** ***84*** ***best_ages:*** ***Rules:*** ***Prefer:*** ***Avoid:***', 7625),
  ('omkareshwar', 19, 'honeymoon-travel', 'HONEYMOON TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, '***honeymoon_score:*** ***80*** ***privacy_score:*** ***75*** ***luxury_score:*** ***68*** ***Recommended:*** ***Honeymoon itinerary should NOT contain more than:*** ***2–3 major temple circuits per day.*** Prefer: ***Spiritual experiences + river scenery + relaxed hotel time*** over: ***continuous temple-hopping and long walking circuits.***', 7626),
  ('omkareshwar', 20, 'luxury-travel', 'LUXURY TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, '***luxury_score:*** ***68*** ***Recommended:*** Luxury here primarily means: rather than:', 7627),
  ('omkareshwar', 21, 'adventure', 'ADVENTURE', NULL, NULL, '***adventure_score:*** ***58*** Omkareshwar is primarily a ***spiritual and cultural destination***, with adventure playing a secondary role. ***Adventure / outdoor experiences:*** ***Strongest outdoor areas:*** ***Narmada–Kaveri Sangam + Kajal Rani Cave + Omkareshwar Parikrama***', 7628),
  ('omkareshwar', 22, 'senior-travel', 'SENIOR TRAVEL', NULL, NULL, '***senior_suitability:*** ***78*** ***walking_intensity:*** ***MEDIUM*** ***Rules:*** ***Easier options:*** ***Avoid:***', 7629),
  ('omkareshwar', 23, 'accessibility', 'ACCESSIBILITY', NULL, NULL, '***wheelchair_accessibility:*** ***LIMITED → MODERATE*** ***public_transport_accessibility:*** ***LOW → MODERATE*** ***hotel_accessibility:*** ***VERIFY_PER_HOTEL*** ***attraction_accessibility:*** ***VERIFY_PER_ATTRACTION***', 7630),
  ('omkareshwar', 24, 'food', 'FOOD', NULL, NULL, 'Omkareshwar is strongest for ***vegetarian pilgrimage food and simple Madhya Pradesh cuisine***. ***Strong categories:*** ***Food experiences:*** ***Budget:*** Local eateries and temple-area food. ***Premium:*** Hotel and MPSTDC dining. The destination is ***more pilgrimage-food oriented than gourmet-food oriented***.', 7631),
  ('omkareshwar', 25, 'shopping', 'SHOPPING', NULL, NULL, '***Strong categories:*** ***Prefer:*** ***Shopping strength:*** ***LOW → MEDIUM*** Omkareshwar is better for ***religious and devotional shopping*** than branded retail.', 7632),
  ('omkareshwar', 26, 'nightlife', 'NIGHTLIFE', NULL, NULL, '***nightlife_level:*** ***18*** Omkareshwar has ***virtually no commercial nightlife*** and is oriented toward spiritual evenings. ***Suitable for:*** ***Night experiences:*** ***Best for:*** ***Peaceful spiritual evenings*** rather than: ***Late-night entertainment.***', 7633),
  ('omkareshwar', 28, 'sample-itinerary-patterns', 'SAMPLE ITINERARY PATTERNS', 'HALF-DAY – BHEDAGHAT MARBLE ROCKS & DHUANDHAR FALLS', NULL, '****Morning / Afternoon**** Pickup from your hotel in Jabalpur → Drive to ****Bhedaghat Marble Rocks**** and experience the towering marble cliffs along the Narmada River → Enjoy a ****Narmada River boat ride**** through the marble gorge → Continue to ****Dhuandhar Falls**** to see the Narmada cascading dramatically through the rocky landscape → Visit the nearby ****Chausath Yogini Temple**** if time and mobility permit → Browse local ****marble and soapstone handicrafts**** before returning to Jabalpur', 7634),
  ('omkareshwar', 28, 'sample-itinerary-patterns', 'SAMPLE ITINERARY PATTERNS', '1 DAY – BHEDAGHAT, DHUANDHAR & CHAUSATH YOGINI', NULL, '****Morning**** Morning pickup from your hotel for Jabalpur''s principal nature circuit → Drive to ****Bhedaghat Marble Rocks**** → Enjoy a ****Narmada boat ride**** between the dramatic marble cliffs → Continue to ****Chausath Yogini Temple**** for its historic temple complex and panoramic views ****Afternoon**** Lunch near Bhedaghat → Visit ****Dhuandhar Falls**** and explore the viewing areas around the waterfall → Browse the nearby ****marble handicraft markets**** ****Evening**** Return toward Jabalpur → Stop at ****Gwarighat**** for a peaceful Narmada riverside experience and evening aarti → Return to your hotel for dinner', 7635),
  ('omkareshwar', 28, 'sample-itinerary-patterns', 'SAMPLE ITINERARY PATTERNS', '2 DAYS – JABALPUR NARMADA, NATURE & HERITAGE CIRCUIT', NULL, '****Day 1**** Full-day exploration of the Bhedaghat region → Begin at ****Bhedaghat Marble Rocks**** and enjoy the Narmada boat ride → Visit ****Chausath Yogini Temple**** → Continue to ****Dhuandhar Falls**** for waterfall views and photography → Explore local marble and soapstone handicrafts → Return to Jabalpur for an evening visit to ****Gwarighat**** ****Day 2**** Begin with ****Madan Mahal Fort**** and explore its historic hilltop ruins associated with Jabalpur''s Gond heritage → Continue to ****Balancing Rock**** near Madan Mahal → Visit ****Rani Durgavati Museum**** for regional history, tribal culture and archaeological collections → Proceed to ****Dumna Nature Reserve**** for a relaxed nature and birdwatching experience → Return to Jabalpur for dinner', 7636),
  ('omkareshwar', 29, '6-days-and-5-nights-honeymoon-itinerary', '6 DAYS & 5 NIGHTS HONEYMOON ITINERARY', 'DAY 1 – ROMANTIC ARRIVAL & NARMADA EVENING', 'honeymoon', '****Morning / Afternoon**** Arrive at ****Jabalpur Airport**** or ****Jabalpur Railway Station**** → Meet your private chauffeur and transfer to your romantic hotel or boutique property → Complete check-in and relax ****Lunch**** Enjoy a relaxed lunch featuring Central Indian and local Jabalpur specialities ****Evening**** Drive to ****Gwarighat**** → Spend a peaceful evening beside the Narmada River → Experience the evening ****Narmada aarti**** → Return to the hotel for a romantic dinner', 7637),
