  ('cairo', 20, 2, '**Honeymoon Touch:** Relax together after your flight with a quiet, romantic evening enjoying views of the Nile or the Pyramids from your hotel balcony.'),
  ('cairo', 21, 0, '**Activities:** Guided Pyramids of Giza & Sphinx Tour, Egyptian Museum, Khan El Khalili Bazaars'),
  ('cairo', 21, 1, '**Meals:** Breakfast (B)'),
  ('cairo', 21, 2, '**Morning:** Enjoy an early breakfast before embarking on a guided tour of the **Great Pyramids of Giza** (Cheops, Chephren, and Mycerinus) and the iconic **Great Sphinx**. Optionally visit a local papyrus institute or essential oils perfume boutique to sample lotus and jasmine fragrances used since pharaonic times.'),
  ('cairo', 21, 3, '**Afternoon:** Head into the city center to explore the classic **Egyptian Museum** housing thousands of antiquities, royal treasures, and ancient statues *(Note: You can also opt to request your guide to take you to the newly fully-opened Grand Egyptian Museum in Giza)*.'),
  ('cairo', 21, 4, '**Late Afternoon:** Stroll hand-in-hand through the narrow, vibrant alleyways of **Khan El Khalili Bazaar**.'),
  ('cairo', 21, 5, '**Honeymoon Touch:** Stop for an authentic Egyptian mint tea or fresh mango juice at the historic *El Fishawy Cafe* in the heart of the bazaar.'),
  ('cairo', 22, 0, '**Activities:** Flight to Aswan, High Dam, Philae Temple, Cruise Boarding'),
  ('cairo', 22, 1, '**Meals:** Breakfast, Lunch, Dinner (B, L, D)'),
  ('cairo', 22, 2, '**Morning:** Breakfast at the hotel, check out, and transfer to Cairo Airport for your domestic flight to Aswan.'),
  ('cairo', 22, 3, '**11:00 AM:** Meet your transfer upon arrival at Aswan Airport and check into your Nile Cruise ship.');
INSERT INTO destination_guidance_bullet (place_id, position, bullet_index, text) VALUES
  ('cairo', 22, 4, '**12:30 PM:** Enjoy your first lunch together on board as you settle into your cabin.'),
  ('cairo', 22, 5, '**01:30 PM:** Depart for a afternoon guided tour visiting the **Aswan High Dam** and the island-based **Temple of Philae**, dedicated to Isis, the ancient goddess of love and magic.'),
  ('cairo', 22, 6, '**07:30 PM:** Dinner on board.'),
  ('cairo', 23, 0, '**Activities:** Optional Abu Simbel, Kom Ombo Temple, Sailing the Nile'),
  ('cairo', 23, 1, '**Meals:** Breakfast, Lunch, Dinner (B, L, D)'),
  ('cairo', 23, 2, '**07:00 AM:** Breakfast on board.'),
  ('cairo', 23, 3, '*Optional Tour:* Early morning trip to the colossal temples of **Abu Simbel** carved into the mountainside.'),
  ('cairo', 23, 4, '**12:30 PM:** Lunch on board while the cruise sails toward Kom Ombo.'),
  ('cairo', 23, 5, '**05:00 PM:** Visit the **Temple of Kom Ombo**, uniquely dedicated to two gods: Sobek the crocodile god and Haeroris the falcon-headed god.'),
  ('cairo', 23, 6, '**06:30 PM:** Sail on toward Edfu.'),
  ('cairo', 23, 7, '**07:30 PM:** Dinner on board.'),
  ('cairo', 24, 0, '**Activities:** Temple of Horus, Nile Sailing, Optional Luxor East Bank'),
  ('cairo', 24, 1, '**Meals:** Breakfast, Lunch, Dinner (B, L, D)'),
  ('cairo', 24, 2, '**06:00 AM:** Morning tea and coffee before embarking.'),
  ('cairo', 24, 3, '**06:30 AM:** Take a horse-drawn carriage to visit the remarkably preserved **Temple of Horus** in Edfu.'),
  ('cairo', 24, 4, '**08:00 AM:** Return for breakfast on board while sailing toward Luxor via the Esna Lock.'),
  ('cairo', 24, 5, '**01:00 PM:** Lunch on board.'),
  ('cairo', 24, 6, '**Afternoon:** Free time at leisure on the sundeck as you dock in Luxor, or opt for an afternoon tour of the **Karnak & Luxor Temples** on the East Bank.'),
  ('cairo', 24, 7, '**08:00 PM:** Dinner on board.'),
  ('cairo', 25, 0, '**Activities:** Valley of the Kings, Hatshepsut Temple, Transfer to Hurghada'),
  ('cairo', 25, 1, '**Meals:** Breakfast, Lunch, Dinner (B, L, D)'),
  ('cairo', 25, 2, '**07:00 AM:** Breakfast on board and cruise check-out.'),
  ('cairo', 25, 3, '**08:00 AM:** Explore the famous **West Bank of Luxor**, touring the **Valley of the Kings** (pharaonic royal tombs) and the mortuary **Temple of Queen Hatshepsut**.'),
  ('cairo', 25, 4, '**Afternoon:** Disembark and enjoy a private overland transfer across the desert hills to the resort town of **Hurghada** on the Red Sea coast. Check into your seaside hotel and enjoy the rest of the day at leisure.'),
  ('cairo', 26, 0, '**Activities:** Beach Leisure, Water Sports, Desert Safari Options'),
  ('cairo', 26, 1, '**Meals:** Breakfast, Lunch, Dinner (B, L, D) *(As provided by hotel plan)*'),
  ('cairo', 26, 2, '**Island & Marine Escapes:** Book a private boat trip or snorkeling excursion to **Giftun Island** or **Mahmya Island** to swim among coral reefs. Alternatively, explore the underwater marine life aboard the **Sindbad Submarine**.'),
  ('cairo', 26, 3, '**Desert Adventure:** Take a 4x4 Jeep or Quad Bike safari into the desert mountains, visit a Bedouin village, enjoy camel rides, and end the evening with a traditional **Bedouin Barbecue Dinner** under a starry sky.'),
  ('cairo', 26, 4, '**City & Leisure:** Stroll through **Hurghada Marina** or the **El Sakala** area for waterside dining, shopping bazaars, and vibrant seaside lounges.'),
  ('cairo', 27, 0, '**Activities:** Airport Transfer & Flight Home'),
  ('cairo', 27, 1, '**Meals:** Breakfast (B)'),
  ('cairo', 27, 2, '**Morning:** Breakfast at the hotel and check-out.'),
  ('cairo', 27, 3, 'Transfer to Hurghada Airport for your return flight home, bringing back unforgettable honeymoon memories of Egypt.'),
  ('cairo', 28, 0, '**Activities:** Meet & assist upon arrival at Cairo International Airport by your Excel Travel representative. Private, air-conditioned transfer directly to your hotel for check-in.'),
  ('cairo', 28, 1, '**Family Tip:** Take the evening to relax, unpack, and recover from jet lag. If traveling with young children, request a ground-floor room or a room close to the hotel’s main amenities for convenience.'),
  ('cairo', 28, 2, '**Overnight:** Cairo'),
  ('cairo', 29, 0, '**08:00 AM – Giza Pyramids & Great Sphinx:** Early start to explore the Giza Plateau (Cheops, Chephren, and Mycerinus).'),
  ('cairo', 29, 1, '*Family Activity:* Take a family photo at the Panorama Viewpoint. Optional camel or horse-drawn carriage ride for the kids (agree on the fare in advance).'),
  ('cairo', 29, 2, '*Notes:* Going inside the Great Pyramid involves steep, narrow tunnels; if anyone in the family is claustrophobic or traveling with toddlers, stick to exploring the outside terraces.'),
  ('cairo', 29, 3, '**11:30 AM – Quick Cultural Stop:** Brief stop at a certified Papyrus Institute or Perfume Shop to learn ancient Egyptian craft techniques (interactive for kids).'),
  ('cairo', 29, 4, '**01:00 PM – Lunch:** Lunch break at a family-friendly local restaurant (optional/at own expense).'),
  ('cairo', 29, 5, '**02:30 PM – Egyptian Museum (Tahrir Square) & Grand Egyptian Museum (GEM):** Discover over 120,000 artifacts spanning thousands of years, including royal statues, ancient jewelry, and mummies.'),
  ('cairo', 29, 6, '*Museum Update:* The **Grand Egyptian Museum (GEM)** near the Giza Pyramids is fully open. Depending on your preference, you can visit the classic Egyptian Museum in Tahrir or the modern, family-accessible GEM with interactive displays.'),
  ('cairo', 29, 7, '**05:00 PM – Khan El-Khalili Bazaar:** Walk through the historic, colorful alleyways of medieval Cairo. Enjoy a family pit stop for fresh juice or mint tea at the historic *El Fishawy Cafe*.'),
  ('cairo', 29, 8, '**Overnight:** Cairo'),
  ('cairo', 30, 0, '**Morning:** Hotel breakfast, check-out, and private transfer to Cairo Airport for your short domestic flight to Aswan.'),
  ('cairo', 30, 1, '**11:00 AM:** Meet at Aswan Airport and transfer to your Nile Cruise ship for check-in.'),
  ('cairo', 30, 2, '**12:30 PM:** Lunch served on board.'),
  ('cairo', 30, 3, '**01:30 PM – Aswan Highlights:**'),
  ('cairo', 30, 4, 'Visit the **Aswan High Dam**, an impressive modern engineering marvel.'),
  ('cairo', 30, 5, 'Take a short motorboat ride to Agilkia Island to visit the **Temple of Philae**, dedicated to the goddess Isis (kids will love the boat ride over the Nile).'),
  ('cairo', 30, 6, '**07:30 PM:** Welcome dinner on board.'),
  ('cairo', 30, 7, '**Overnight:** Aswan (On board cruise)'),
  ('cairo', 31, 0, '**07:00 AM:** Breakfast on board.'),
  ('cairo', 31, 1, '*Optional Tour:* Early morning excursion to the **Abu Simbel Temples** (by air or private road transfer) to view the colossal rock-cut statues of Ramses II.'),
  ('cairo', 31, 2, '**12:30 PM:** Lunch on board as the cruise begins sailing downstream toward Kom Ombo.'),
  ('cairo', 31, 3, '**05:00 PM – Kom Ombo Temple:** Disembark to visit the unique double temple dedicated to **Sobek** (the Crocodile God) and **Haroeris** (the Falcon God).'),
  ('cairo', 31, 4, '*Kid Highlight:* Visit the adjacent **Crocodile Museum** at Kom Ombo to see ancient mummified crocodiles.'),
  ('cairo', 31, 5, '**06:30 PM:** Continue sailing toward Edfu.'),
  ('cairo', 31, 6, '**07:30 PM:** Dinner on board.'),
  ('cairo', 31, 7, '**Overnight:** Edfu (On board cruise)'),
  ('cairo', 32, 0, '**06:00 AM:** Morning coffee/tea served before early departure.'),
  ('cairo', 32, 1, '**06:30 AM – Temple of Horus at Edfu:** Visit one of the best-preserved ancient temples in Egypt via horse-drawn carriage (*caleche*).'),
  ('cairo', 32, 2, '**08:00 AM:** Return to the ship for breakfast.'),
  ('cairo', 32, 3, '**08:30 AM:** Sail toward Luxor, passing through the historic **Esna Lock**.'),
  ('cairo', 32, 4, '*Family Activity:* Gather on the sun deck to watch the ship pass through the lock mechanism and see local boat traders selling colorful Egyptian scarves from below.'),
  ('cairo', 32, 5, '**01:00 PM:** Lunch on board.'),
  ('cairo', 32, 6, '**Afternoon:** Free time at leisure on the sun deck.'),
  ('cairo', 32, 7, '*Optional Excursion:* Visit the illuminated **Luxor Temple** or **Karnak Temple** on the East Bank in the late afternoon/evening.'),
  ('cairo', 32, 8, '**08:00 PM:** Dinner on board (often featuring an optional Galabeya Egyptian theme night).'),
  ('cairo', 32, 9, '**Overnight:** Luxor (On board cruise)'),
  ('cairo', 33, 0, '**07:00 AM:** Breakfast on board and final cruise check-out.'),
  ('cairo', 33, 1, '**08:00 AM – Luxor West Bank Excursion:**'),
  ('cairo', 33, 2, 'Explore the **Valley of the Kings**, descending into ancient pharaonic tombs.'),
  ('cairo', 33, 3, 'Visit the terraced **Mortuary Temple of Queen Hatshepsut** at Deir el-Bahari.'),
  ('cairo', 33, 4, 'Stop for photos at the massive **Colossi of Memnon**.'),
  ('cairo', 33, 5, '**12:30 PM:** Disembark and board a private air-conditioned vehicle for your scenic drive across the Eastern Desert to **Hurghada** on the Red Sea coast (~3.5 to 4 hours).'),
  ('cairo', 33, 6, '**Late Afternoon:** Arrival and check-in at your Hurghada beach resort.'),
  ('cairo', 33, 7, '**Overnight:** Hurghada'),
  ('cairo', 34, 0, '**Water & Coral Reef Activities:**'),
  ('cairo', 34, 1, '**Giftun & Mahmya Islands:** Full-day boat excursion with shallow-water snorkeling, white sand beaches, and coral garden viewing.'),
  ('cairo', 34, 2, '**Sindbad Submarine:** A 20-meter dive aboard a real passenger submarine—ideal for younger children to see marine life without swimming.'),
  ('cairo', 34, 3, '**Glass-Bottom Boat Tours:** Easy reef viewing for non-swimmers and toddlers.'),
  ('cairo', 34, 4, '**Desert & Cultural Safaris:**'),
  ('cairo', 34, 5, '**4x4 Jeep or Quad Bike Desert Tour:** Journey into the Red Sea mountains to visit a Bedouin village, take camel rides, enjoy a Bedouin barbecue dinner, and end with guided stargazing through telescopes.'),
  ('cairo', 34, 6, '**Resort Relaxation:** Enjoy hotel water parks, swimming pools, and beach recreation along the Touristic Promenade or Hurghada Marina.'),
  ('cairo', 34, 7, '**Overnight:** Hurghada'),
  ('cairo', 35, 0, '**Morning:** Hotel breakfast and check-out.'),
  ('cairo', 35, 1, '**Transfer:** Private transfer to Hurghada International Airport for your domestic flight to Cairo to connect with your international departure flight home.'),
  ('cairo', 37, 0, '**Airport Welcome:** Meet your dedicated travel representative at Cairo International Airport (CAI) for expedited VIP fast-track customs and immigration clearance.'),
  ('cairo', 37, 1, '**Private Transfer:** Private transfer via luxury, air-conditioned vehicle to your hotel.'),
  ('cairo', 37, 2, '**Check-in & Rest:** Settle into your room overlooking the Nile or the Pyramids.'),
  ('cairo', 37, 3, '**Overnight:** Cairo.'),
  ('cairo', 38, 0, '**Giza Plateau Private Tour:** Meet your private Egyptologist guide for an early departure to the Giza Plateau.'),
  ('cairo', 38, 1, '**Great Pyramids of Giza:** Explore the Pyramids of Khufu (Cheops), Khafre (Chephren), and Menkaure (Mycerinus). Includes entry inside the burial chambers of the Great Pyramid of Khufu.'),
  ('cairo', 38, 2, '**The Great Sphinx & Valley Temple:** Visit the monolithic limestone Sphinx dating to 2620 BC and the adjacent Valley Temple.'),
  ('cairo', 38, 3, '**Artisanal Visit:** Optional curated stop at a traditional papyrus institute or perfume atelier.'),
  ('cairo', 38, 4, '**Egyptian Museum / Grand Egyptian Museum:** Visit the Egyptian Museum, established in 1835 and designed in neoclassical style by Marcel Dourgnon, housing over 120,000 antiquities.'),
  ('cairo', 38, 5, '*Note:* The Royal Mummies were permanently relocated to the National Museum of Egyptian Civilization (NMEC) in Fustat, while King Tutankhamun’s complete treasures have moved to the newly opened Grand Egyptian Museum (GEM) in Giza. You may choose to customize this visit to the GEM or NMEC depending on your specific exhibit preferences.'),
  ('cairo', 38, 6, '**Downtown Drive & Khan El Khalili:** Drive through historic downtown Cairo to the 14th-century Khan El Khalili Bazaar. Private guided walk through its narrow alleys, spice stalls, and brassware workshops.'),
  ('cairo', 38, 7, '**Return Transfer:** Private transfer back to your hotel.'),
  ('cairo', 38, 8, '**Overnight:** Cairo.'),
  ('cairo', 39, 0, '**Flight to Aswan:** Breakfast, check out, and private transfer to Cairo Airport for your domestic flight to Aswan.'),
  ('cairo', 39, 1, '**Embarkation:** Met upon arrival at Aswan Airport (ASW) and transferred to board your luxury Nile Cruise ship.'),
  ('cairo', 39, 2, '**11:00 AM:** Cruise Check-In.'),
  ('cairo', 39, 3, '**12:30 PM:** Buffet lunch on board.'),
  ('cairo', 39, 4, '**01:30 PM:** Guided excursion to the **Aswan High Dam** and the island-bound **Temple of Philae**, dedicated to the goddess Isis.'),
  ('cairo', 39, 5, '**07:30 PM:** Welcome Dinner on board.'),
  ('cairo', 39, 6, '**Overnight:** Aswan (on board).'),
  ('cairo', 40, 0, '**07:00 AM:** Breakfast on board.'),
  ('cairo', 40, 1, '*Optional Tour:* Early morning excursion (by private flight or road) to the temples of **Abu Simbel** built by Ramesses II.'),
  ('cairo', 40, 2, '**12:30 PM:** Lunch on board as the ship begins sailing downriver toward Kom Ombo.'),
  ('cairo', 40, 3, '**01:00 PM:** Sailing to Kom Ombo.'),
  ('cairo', 40, 4, '**05:00 PM:** Shore visit to the **Temple of Kom Ombo**, a dual-entry temple dedicated symmetrically to Sobek (the crocodile god) and Haeroris (Falcon-headed Horus).'),
  ('cairo', 40, 5, '**06:30 PM:** Sailing to Edfu.'),
  ('cairo', 40, 6, '**07:30 PM:** Dinner on board.'),
  ('cairo', 40, 7, '**Overnight:** Edfu (on board).'),
  ('cairo', 41, 0, '**06:00 AM:** Morning coffee/tea served prior to tour departure.'),
  ('cairo', 41, 1, '**06:30 AM:** Visit the **Temple of Horus at Edfu**, the most intact ancient temple complex in Egypt.'),
  ('cairo', 41, 2, '**08:00 AM:** Return for breakfast on board.'),
  ('cairo', 41, 3, '**08:30 AM:** Sailing toward Luxor via the Esna Lock.'),
  ('cairo', 41, 4, '**01:00 PM:** Lunch on board.'),
  ('cairo', 41, 5, '**Afternoon:** Free time at leisure as you sail. Optional afternoon tour to the **Luxor East Bank** (Karnak Temple & Luxor Temple).'),
  ('cairo', 41, 6, '**08:00 PM:** Dinner on board.'),
  ('cairo', 41, 7, '**Overnight:** Luxor (on board).'),
  ('cairo', 42, 0, '**07:00 AM:** Breakfast on board.'),
  ('cairo', 42, 1, '**08:00 AM:** Check out and disembark.'),
  ('cairo', 42, 2, '**West Bank Tour:** Visit the **Valley of the Kings** (including entry to royal rock-cut tombs) and the mortuary **Temple of Queen Hatshepsut** at Deir el-Bahari.'),
  ('cairo', 42, 3, '**Overland Transfer:** Private transfer by air-conditioned vehicle from Luxor through the Eastern Desert to Hurghada on the Red Sea coast (~3.5–4 hours).'),
  ('cairo', 42, 4, '**Check-in:** Arrive at your Red Sea luxury resort. Rest of the day at leisure.'),
  ('cairo', 42, 5, '**Overnight:** Hurghada.'),
  ('cairo', 43, 0, '**Marine & Island Excursions:**'),
  ('cairo', 43, 1, 'Day-boat charters or private yacht cruises to **Giftun Island** or **Mahmya Island** national parks for snorkeling and diving along coral reefs.'),
  ('cairo', 43, 2, 'Deep-sea exploration via the **Sindbad Submarine** (diving 20 meters below the surface).'),
  ('cairo', 43, 3, 'Watersports including kitesurfing, windsurfing, and waterskiing.'),
  ('cairo', 43, 4, '**Desert & Cultural Excursions:**'),
  ('cairo', 43, 5, '4x4 Jeep or Quad Bike safari into the Eastern Desert.'),
  ('cairo', 43, 6, 'Camel treks, Bedouin village visits, and traditional Bedouin BBQ dinners with evening stargazing via high-powered telescopes.'),
  ('cairo', 43, 7, '**Overnight:** Hurghada.'),
  ('cairo', 44, 0, '**Checkout:** Breakfast at the resort, followed by check-out.'),
  ('cairo', 44, 1, '**Airport Transfer:** Private transfer to Hurghada International Airport (HRG) for your short domestic flight back to Cairo Airport (CAI) to connect with your international departure flight home.'),
  ('cairo', 45, 0, 'Try to cover the Pyramids, Saqqara, museums, Islamic Cairo, Coptic Cairo, and shopping in one or two rushed days.'),
  ('cairo', 45, 1, 'Treat Cairo, Aswan, and Luxor as if they are close together instead of allowing time for flights, airport procedures, transfers, and check-in.'),
  ('cairo', 45, 2, 'Schedule the Pyramids, Saqqara, and other outdoor archaeological sites during the hottest part of the day.'),
  ('cairo', 45, 3, 'Book domestic flights or a Nile cruise without checking how the flight timings connect with cruise embarkation and sightseeing schedules.'),
  ('cairo', 45, 4, 'Include too many temples and museums without allowing time for rest, meals, and hotel relaxation.'),
  ('cairo', 45, 5, 'Ignore Cairo’s traffic when planning airport transfers, museum visits, and return flights.'),
  ('cairo', 45, 6, 'Stay near the airport for the entire trip, creating long daily journeys to the main historical attractions.'),
  ('cairo', 45, 7, 'Choose a Nile cruise based only on the ship’s appearance without checking cabin quality, sailing dates, embarkation arrangements, and onboard service.'),
  ('cairo', 45, 8, 'Plan Luxor’s West Bank as a casual afternoon visit, even though it involves early starts, outdoor walking, uneven surfaces, and heat exposure.'),
  ('cairo', 45, 9, 'Add a late-night dinner or entertainment experience before an early domestic flight or full sightseeing day.'),
  ('cairo', 46, 0, 'Builds the itinerary around the traveler’s purpose, comfort level, interests, and preferred pace.'),
  ('cairo', 46, 1, 'Uses Cairo as the arrival and departure gateway, while arranging Aswan and Luxor as a logical Nile-cruise sequence.'),
  ('cairo', 46, 2, 'Groups nearby attractions together, such as Giza and Saqqara, the Egyptian Museum and Downtown Cairo, or the Citadel and Islamic Cairo.'),
  ('cairo', 46, 3, 'Places outdoor sightseeing early in the morning, especially at the Pyramids, Saqqara, Luxor’s West Bank, and other exposed archaeological sites.'),
  ('cairo', 46, 4, 'Protects travel buffers for Cairo traffic, airport procedures, domestic flights, cruise embarkation, and hotel check-in.'),
  ('cairo', 46, 5, 'Chooses a well-located Cairo hotel in Giza, Zamalek, Garden City, Downtown, or the Nile Corniche according to the traveler’s priorities.'),
  ('cairo', 46, 6, 'Selects the Nile cruise based on sailing dates, cabin comfort, food quality, service standards, itinerary reliability, and embarkation convenience.'),
  ('cairo', 46, 7, 'Uses private air-conditioned vehicles and professional guides for major sightseeing days, airport transfers, and multi-site excursions.'),
  ('cairo', 46, 8, 'Limits each day to one major sightseeing block plus one lighter experience whenever possible.'),
  ('cairo', 46, 9, 'Balances ancient monuments with hotel downtime, spa treatments, pool time, relaxed meals, and Nile-based evenings.'),
  ('cairo', 46, 10, 'Keeps the Pyramids and Sphinx visit focused, comfortable, and flexible rather than extending it into an exhausting full-day schedule.'),
  ('cairo', 46, 11, 'Combines Luxor’s East Bank temples on one day and the West Bank monuments on another to reduce unnecessary backtracking.'),
  ('cairo', 46, 12, 'Arranges selected tombs and temples according to the traveler’s interests instead of attempting to visit every available site.'),
  ('cairo', 47, 0, 'Pyramids of Giza and the Great Sphinx.'),
  ('cairo', 47, 1, 'One major museum.'),
  ('cairo', 47, 2, 'One Nile-side evening experience.'),
  ('cairo', 47, 3, 'Islamic Cairo or Khan el-Khalili.'),
  ('cairo', 47, 4, 'Saladin Citadel and Muhammad Ali Mosque.'),
  ('cairo', 47, 5, 'One flexible or relaxed evening.'),
