  ('alexandria', 150, 13, 'Qaitbay Citadel / Eastern Harbour for harbour walks, sea views, photography, and boat outings.'),
  ('alexandria', 150, 14, 'Alexandria Corniche for coastal walks, sunset views, cafés, and waterfront exploration.'),
  ('alexandria', 150, 15, 'Stanley / Eastern Corniche for Stanley Bridge viewpoints, sea views, photography, and evening walks.'),
  ('alexandria', 150, 16, 'Montaza / Palace Gardens area for garden walks, coastal scenery, beach access, and relaxed outdoor activities.'),
  ('alexandria', 150, 17, 'Anfushi / Western Harbour for traditional harbour life, seafood, photography, and local exploration.'),
  ('alexandria', 150, 18, 'Central Alexandria / Raml Station for tram rides, historic streets, markets, cafés, and urban discovery.'),
  ('alexandria', 150, 19, 'Kom El-Shoqafa / Pompey’s Pillar area for archaeological exploration and cultural discovery.'),
  ('alexandria', 150, 20, 'Eastern beach districts for swimming, beach activities, and local summer experiences.'),
  ('alexandria', 150, 21, 'Leisurely explorers.'),
  ('alexandria', 150, 22, 'Couples.'),
  ('alexandria', 150, 23, 'Families with older children.'),
  ('alexandria', 150, 24, 'Teenagers.'),
  ('alexandria', 150, 25, 'History and archaeology enthusiasts.'),
  ('alexandria', 150, 26, 'Photography travelers.'),
  ('alexandria', 150, 27, 'Coastal and harbour explorers.'),
  ('alexandria', 150, 28, 'Food and urban-exploration travelers.'),
  ('alexandria', 150, 29, 'Soft-adventure travelers.'),
  ('alexandria', 150, 30, 'Visitors who prefer cultural exploration with light physical activity.'),
  ('alexandria', 151, 0, 'Prefer a centrally located hotel around the Central Corniche, Bibliotheca Alexandrina, Stanley, or Qaitbay area for easier access to major attractions, restaurants, cafés, and transport. The Central Corniche and Bibliotheca area are particularly practical for a short sightseeing stay.'),
  ('alexandria', 151, 1, 'Use private transfers, hotel-arranged taxis, Uber, or Careem for multi-stop sightseeing, longer journeys, airport transfers, and visits to attractions outside the immediate hotel area; avoid relying heavily on buses or microbuses.'),
  ('alexandria', 151, 2, 'Avoid changing hotels during a short 2–4-night visit. Keeping one accommodation base reduces luggage handling, traffic-related delays, and unnecessary transfers.'),
  ('alexandria', 151, 3, 'Group attractions geographically to reduce time in Alexandria traffic: visit the Bibliotheca Alexandrina, Corniche, and Qaitbay Citadel together; visit the Catacombs of Kom El Shoqafa, Pompey’s Pillar, and one central museum on another day.'),
  ('alexandria', 151, 4, 'Limit sightseeing to one major area per day, with no more than two substantial attractions. A relaxed coastal day could include the Bibliotheca Alexandrina and Qaitbay Citadel, while a heritage day could focus on the Catacombs and Pompey’s Pillar.'),
  ('alexandria', 151, 5, 'Visit outdoor attractions such as Qaitbay Citadel, Montaza Palace Gardens, Stanley Bridge, and the Corniche early in the morning or during the late afternoon, especially in warmer months.'),
  ('alexandria', 151, 6, 'Include regular seating, shade, cafés, hotel breaks, and air-conditioned rest periods between attractions. Plan a midday break at the hotel or a comfortable restaurant rather than continuing sightseeing continuously.'),
  ('alexandria', 151, 7, 'Choose attractions according to mobility. The Bibliotheca Alexandrina, museums, selected Corniche viewpoints, and carefully planned Qaitbay visits may be more manageable than long walks through crowded archaeological areas.'),
  ('alexandria', 151, 8, 'Check accessibility, vehicle drop-off points, toilets, lifts, ramps, handrails, stairs, and entrance conditions before visiting each attraction. Accessibility varies considerably between modern facilities, historic buildings, archaeological sites, pavements, and transport options.'),
  ('alexandria', 151, 9, 'Avoid unnecessary stairs, crowded pavements, uneven historic streets, difficult road crossings, and long walking routes around busy markets unless mobility is good.'),
  ('alexandria', 151, 10, 'Treat the Catacombs of Kom El Shoqafa cautiously because underground access, stairs, narrow passages, and uneven surfaces may be tiring or unsuitable for some seniors. Skip the interior if the descent or confined spaces are uncomfortable.'),
  ('alexandria', 151, 11, 'Allow generous travel buffers between central Alexandria, Qaitbay, Montaza, Stanley, and the western archaeological sites because traffic and busy roads can make journeys unpredictable.'),
  ('alexandria', 151, 12, 'Use a licensed local guide or private Egyptologist for Qaitbay Citadel, the Catacombs of Kom El Shoqafa, Pompey’s Pillar, Kom El-Dikka, and the Bibliotheca Alexandrina. A guide can reduce confusion, unnecessary walking, vendor pressure, and transport stress.'),
  ('alexandria', 151, 13, 'Prefer a private car with an experienced driver for full sightseeing days instead of self-driving, as traffic, parking, road crossings, and urban congestion can be challenging.'),
  ('alexandria', 151, 14, 'Select a hotel with lifts, reliable air-conditioning, comfortable bathrooms, good seating areas, a convenient restaurant, and easy vehicle access. Confirm accessibility directly with the hotel before booking rather than relying only on general online descriptions.'),
  ('alexandria', 151, 15, 'Carry bottled water, sun protection, comfortable supportive shoes, required medication, a small medical kit, copies of prescriptions, identification, and a mobile phone with emergency contacts. Senior-travel guidance also recommends travel insurance covering medical care, evacuation, and pre-existing conditions where applicable.'),
  ('alexandria', 151, 16, 'Prefer cooler travel periods, particularly October–April, with March–April and October–November offering especially comfortable conditions for sightseeing and waterfront walks.'),
  ('alexandria', 151, 17, 'Avoid the hottest part of the day for outdoor attractions. In summer, keep archaeological visits short and schedule museums, lunch, and hotel rest during the afternoon.'),
  ('alexandria', 151, 18, 'Enjoy low-effort experiences such as a short Corniche walk, a seated seafood lunch, a museum visit, a gentle harbour viewpoint stop, or a sunset drive rather than building every day around extensive walking.'),
  ('alexandria', 151, 19, 'Consider Montaza Palace Gardens only as a separate, slower visit. The area offers gardens and coastal scenery but is farther from central Alexandria, so it may involve longer transfers in traffic.'),
  ('alexandria', 151, 20, 'Avoid staying in distant eastern beach districts if the main purpose is historical sightseeing, since repeated journeys to the Bibliotheca, Qaitbay Citadel, and western archaeological sites may become tiring.'),
  ('alexandria', 151, 21, 'Plan one main sightseeing experience followed by a relaxed meal or waterfront activity, such as a seated seafood dinner, a quiet Corniche café, or a short sunset harbour outing.'),
  ('alexandria', 151, 22, 'Recommended daily structure: one major attraction in the morning, lunch and hotel rest at midday, then one short museum, garden, or waterfront visit in the late afternoon.'),
  ('alexandria', 151, 23, 'Do not overload the itinerary with the Bibliotheca Alexandrina, Qaitbay Citadel, Catacombs, Pompey’s Pillar, Montaza, museums, and markets in a single day; Alexandria’s traffic, crowds, stairs, and uneven surfaces can make an ambitious schedule exhausting.'),
