  ('alexandria', 184, 0, '**Valley of the Kings:** The burial place of many New Kingdom pharaohs, including selected royal tombs open to visitors.'),
  ('alexandria', 184, 1, '**Valley of the Queens:** The burial area of royal wives and children, including the tomb associated with Queen Nefertari, subject to opening arrangements.'),
  ('alexandria', 184, 2, '**Temple of Hatshepsut:** A dramatic temple built against the cliffs at Deir el-Bahari.'),
  ('alexandria', 184, 3, '**Colossi of Memnon:** Two enormous seated statues of Pharaoh Amenhotep III.'),
