  ('gori', 739, 0, 'Treat Gori only as a quick Stalin Museum stop and miss Gori Fortress, the Old Town, Ethnographic Museum, local heritage, and surrounding historical sites.'),
  ('gori', 739, 1, 'Try to cover Gori Fortress, Stalin Museum, Uplistsikhe, Ateni Valley, Ateni Sioni, waterfalls, fortresses, and other Shida Kartli attractions in a very short trip.'),
  ('gori', 739, 2, 'Schedule Gori city sightseeing, Uplistsikhe, and Ateni Valley together without allowing enough time for museums, walking, archaeological exploration, meals, and transfers.'),
  ('gori', 739, 3, 'Underestimate the time required for excursions outside central Gori, particularly when combining Uplistsikhe, Ateni Valley, rural villages, and other regional sites.'),
  ('gori', 739, 4, 'Treat Uplistsikhe as a simple photo stop despite the amount of walking and uneven rocky terrain involved.'),
  ('gori', 739, 5, 'Plan outdoor excursions such as Uplistsikhe, Ateni Sioni, and Damchkeri Waterfall without considering heat, rain, slippery terrain, visibility, or trail conditions.'),
  ('gori', 739, 6, 'Assume every attraction can be visited at any time without checking museum opening hours, seasonal schedules, local access conditions, or religious-site considerations.'),
  ('gori', 739, 7, 'Plan too much sightseeing on arrival or departure day, particularly when transferring between Tbilisi and Gori.'),
  ('gori', 739, 8, 'Spend too much itinerary time on Stalin-related attractions while ignoring Gori''s broader medieval, archaeological, ethnographic, religious, and natural heritage.'),
  ('gori', 739, 9, 'Ignore the traveler''s actual purpose, especially when the trip is primarily for history, archaeology, culture, food and wine, nature, photography, family travel, or a short stop between Tbilisi and western Georgia.'),
  ('gori', 739, 10, 'Attempt difficult rural or hiking excursions with travelers who have significant mobility limitations without checking terrain and access beforehand.'),
  ('gori', 740, 0, 'Builds the trip around the traveler''s purpose rather than treating Gori as a single-attraction destination.'),
  ('gori', 740, 1, 'Groups Gori Fortress, Old Town, Stalin Museum, Ethnographic Museum, central monuments, cafés, and restaurants into an efficient central-Gori sightseeing circuit.'),
  ('gori', 740, 2, 'Uses Gori''s location strategically as a base for nearby Uplistsikhe and the Ateni Valley rather than repeatedly backtracking from another destination.'),
  ('gori', 740, 3, 'Gives Uplistsikhe sufficient time for the archaeological reserve, rock-cut streets, chambers, temples, wine presses, tunnels, and viewpoints. Uplistsikhe is only around 10 km from Gori but involves outdoor walking over uneven terrain.'),
  ('gori', 740, 4, 'Treats Ateni Valley as a separate half-day or full-day experience when travelers are interested in churches, wine, rural landscapes, hiking, or waterfalls. The valley begins roughly 10 km from Gori and includes Ateni Sioni, Ateni Fortress and Biisi Waterfall.'),
  ('gori', 740, 5, 'Uses taxis, private cars, or organized tours selectively for Uplistsikhe, Ateni Valley, Gorisjvari, Tsedisi Fortress, waterfalls, and other sites outside the central city.'),
  ('gori', 740, 6, 'Keeps the main city attractions walkable and clustered where possible. Gori Fortress, Stalin Museum and several central sights can be combined efficiently, with the fortress and Stalin Museum roughly a 15-minute walk apart.'),
  ('gori', 740, 7, 'Protects free time for Georgian dining, local cafés, wine experiences, photography, relaxed walks, and exploring Gori''s smaller streets rather than filling every hour with monuments.'),
  ('gori', 740, 8, 'Checks weather and terrain before scheduling Uplistsikhe, Ateni Valley, and waterfall excursions, particularly during periods of rain or extreme summer heat.'),
  ('gori', 740, 9, 'Treats hiking separately from standard sightseeing. The Ateni Sioni–Damchkeri Waterfall route passes through forest and follows the Tana River, making it more suitable for travelers who are comfortable with outdoor walking.'),
  ('gori', 740, 10, 'Allows additional time for religious sites such as Ateni Sioni and Gorisjvari and avoids treating them like rapid photo stops.'),
  ('gori', 740, 11, 'Uses the Shida Kartli region''s food and wine identity to enrich the itinerary, particularly with Chinuri, Goruli Mtsvane, Shavkapito and other regional wines.'),
  ('gori', 740, 12, 'Avoids unnecessary hotel changes on short Gori stays because the central attractions and nearby excursions can be handled efficiently from one base.'),
  ('gori', 740, 13, 'Keeps at least one relaxed period in the itinerary for Georgian food, cafés, local markets, photography, or simply enjoying central Gori.'),
  ('gori', 740, 14, 'Places Uplistsikhe and Ateni Valley on separate days for travelers staying 2–3 nights when a relaxed pace is preferred.'),
  ('gori', 740, 15, 'Uses Gori primarily as a **history, archaeology, culture, food-and-wine, and regional-exploration destination**, rather than trying to position it as a major nightlife or resort destination.'),
  ('gori', 740, 16, 'For short stays, prioritizes **Gori Fortress + central Gori + one major excursion such as Uplistsikhe** instead of attempting every surrounding attraction.'),
  ('gori', 740, 17, 'For longer stays, adds Ateni Valley, Gorisjvari, Tsedisi Fortress, waterfall hikes, rural food and wine experiences, and wider Shida Kartli excursions according to traveler interest.'),
  ('gori', 740, 18, 'Leaves a practical buffer for transfers because Gori is approximately 1 hour 10 minutes from Tbilisi by road, while Uplistsikhe is a short excursion from the city.'),
  ('gori', 740, 19, 'Uses the Gori Tourist Information Center when travelers need current local information on attractions, access, and regional travel conditions.'),
