  ('uplistsikhe', 758, 16, 'Uplistsikhe is best positioned as light-to-moderate archaeological adventure rather than a high-intensity adventure destination.'),
  ('uplistsikhe', 758, 17, 'The archaeological complex occupies a rocky cliff landscape of almost 8 hectares, with surviving areas connected by footways.'),
  ('uplistsikhe', 758, 18, 'Visitors explore ancient streets, squares, caves, halls, temples, wine facilities, and other rock-cut structures on foot.'),
  ('uplistsikhe', 758, 19, 'The Secret Tunnel provides one of the site''s most distinctive exploration experiences and historically connected the cave city with the Mtkvari River.'),
  ('uplistsikhe', 758, 20, 'Uneven natural rock, slopes, steps, and exposed areas add a moderate physical element to sightseeing.'),
  ('uplistsikhe', 758, 21, 'Photography is one of the strongest outdoor activities because the site combines archaeological structures with open views across the surrounding landscape.'),
  ('uplistsikhe', 758, 22, 'Suitable walking shoes, water, sun protection, and weather-appropriate clothing are important.'),
  ('uplistsikhe', 758, 23, 'Hot summer afternoons can make exploration more demanding because much of the archaeological landscape is exposed.'),
  ('uplistsikhe', 758, 24, 'Wet, icy, or otherwise slippery conditions can increase difficulty on natural rock surfaces.'),
  ('uplistsikhe', 758, 25, 'Visitors with mobility or balance limitations should treat the archaeological terrain cautiously.'),
  ('uplistsikhe', 758, 26, 'Do not position Uplistsikhe as a destination for technical climbing, mountaineering, extreme cave exploration, rafting, or other high-intensity adventure sports.'),
  ('uplistsikhe', 758, 27, 'Travelers wanting substantial hiking, mountain sports, or wilderness adventure should combine Uplistsikhe with other destinations in Georgia.'),
  ('uplistsikhe', 759, 0, 'Treat Uplistsikhe as a walking-intensive archaeological attraction rather than an easy sightseeing site.'),
  ('uplistsikhe', 759, 1, 'Prefer private car, taxi, or organized transport from Gori or Tbilisi to minimize unnecessary walking and transfers.'),
  ('uplistsikhe', 759, 2, 'Allow approximately 1.5–3 hours depending on walking ability, weather, and sightseeing depth.'),
  ('uplistsikhe', 759, 3, 'Use comfortable, supportive, non-slip footwear.'),
  ('uplistsikhe', 759, 4, 'Include regular rest and hydration breaks.'),
  ('uplistsikhe', 759, 5, 'Avoid rushing through the archaeological complex.'),
  ('uplistsikhe', 759, 6, 'Prioritize the museum, lower/easier sections, main archaeological structures, and accessible viewpoints for travelers with reduced stamina.'),
  ('uplistsikhe', 759, 7, 'Consider a shorter partial visit rather than attempting the entire complex when mobility is limited.'),
  ('uplistsikhe', 759, 8, 'Avoid combining Uplistsikhe with several other physically demanding heritage attractions on the same day.'),
  ('uplistsikhe', 759, 9, 'Schedule visits during comfortable morning or late-afternoon temperatures in summer.'),
  ('uplistsikhe', 759, 10, 'Avoid exposed archaeological walking during extreme heat, heavy rain, snow, frost, or icy conditions.'),
  ('uplistsikhe', 759, 11, 'Use extra caution on smooth, worn, steep, or uneven rock surfaces.'),
  ('uplistsikhe', 759, 12, 'Allow additional time for steps, slopes, narrow passages, and natural-rock walking areas.'),
  ('uplistsikhe', 759, 13, 'Carry sufficient drinking water, particularly during warmer months.'),
  ('uplistsikhe', 759, 14, 'Seniors using walking aids should assess the archaeological terrain carefully before attempting the upper sections.'),
  ('uplistsikhe', 759, 15, 'Wheelchair users should distinguish between accessibility of the museum and accessibility of the wider cave-city complex.'),
  ('uplistsikhe', 759, 16, 'Do not assume that vehicle access close to the visitor area eliminates walking requirements inside Uplistsikhe.'),
  ('uplistsikhe', 759, 17, 'Travelers with significant mobility or balance limitations should consider enjoying only accessible sections rather than the complete archaeological route.'),
  ('uplistsikhe', 759, 18, 'Combine Uplistsikhe with a relaxed meal or scenic drive rather than another demanding walking attraction.'),
  ('uplistsikhe', 760, 0, 'The Uplistsikhe Museum is officially listed by Georgia Travel as having a ramp.'),
  ('uplistsikhe', 760, 1, 'The wider archaeological complex contains natural rock surfaces, slopes, steps, historic footways, caves, tunnels, and elevation changes.'),
  ('uplistsikhe', 760, 2, 'Full independent wheelchair exploration of the archaeological cave city should not be assumed.'),
  ('uplistsikhe', 760, 3, 'Visitors using wheelchairs, mobility scooters, walkers, or other mobility aids should confirm current conditions before visiting.'),
  ('uplistsikhe', 760, 4, 'Some lower or visitor-facility areas may be considerably easier to access than elevated archaeological sections.'),
  ('uplistsikhe', 760, 5, 'The Secret Tunnel, steep rock sections, and upper archaeological areas may be unsuitable for visitors with significant mobility limitations.'),
  ('uplistsikhe', 760, 6, 'Wet, icy, or snowy conditions can further reduce practical accessibility because natural rock can become slippery.'),
  ('uplistsikhe', 760, 7, 'Summer heat can also increase physical difficulty because much of the archaeological landscape is exposed.'),
  ('uplistsikhe', 760, 8, 'Private vehicles or taxis provide greater transport flexibility than multi-stage public-transport journeys.'),
  ('uplistsikhe', 760, 9, 'Accessible vehicle requirements should be confirmed with the transport provider before travel.'),
  ('uplistsikhe', 760, 10, 'Travelers requiring step-free access should prioritize the museum and any currently verified accessible visitor areas.'),
  ('uplistsikhe', 760, 11, 'Do not market Uplistsikhe as a fully accessible attraction.'),
  ('uplistsikhe', 760, 12, 'Families using strollers should expect similar difficulties on uneven archaeological terrain.'),
  ('uplistsikhe', 760, 13, 'Travelers with significant mobility requirements should consider a shortened or partially accessible visit.'),
  ('uplistsikhe', 760, 14, 'Current accessibility should be reconfirmed with official tourism or site authorities before travel.'),
