  ('gudauri', 821, 0, 'Treat Gudauri as a conventional sightseeing destination and fill the itinerary with attractions instead of allowing enough time for skiing, snowboarding, mountain scenery, après-ski, and relaxation.'),
  ('gudauri', 821, 1, 'Try to combine Gudauri skiing, Russia–Georgia Friendship Monument, Jvari Pass, Kobi, Stepantsminda / Kazbegi, Gergeti Trinity Church, paragliding, snow activities, and multiple Georgian Military Road stops in a very short trip.'),
  ('gudauri', 821, 2, 'Schedule full-day skiing immediately after a long arrival transfer without allowing sufficient time for hotel check-in, equipment rental, ski-pass arrangements, instructor coordination, meals, and rest.'),
  ('gudauri', 821, 3, 'Assume ski lifts, gondolas, upper slopes, paragliding, and other mountain activities will operate regardless of weather, wind, visibility, snow conditions, or operational restrictions.'),
  ('gudauri', 821, 4, 'Plan Stepantsminda / Kazbegi as a guaranteed winter excursion without considering changing road conditions around the Gudauri–Kobi corridor. Snowfall, ice, strong winds, and avalanche risk can cause temporary traffic restrictions.'),
  ('gudauri', 821, 5, 'Underestimate Gudauri''s altitude and mountain environment. The resort is around 2,000–2,200 m above sea level, while lift access reaches approximately 3,276 m.'),
  ('gudauri', 821, 6, 'Assume every traveler should ski from the first day without considering experience level, fitness, confidence, suitable slopes, equipment, or the need for professional instruction.'),
  ('gudauri', 821, 7, 'Send beginners onto unsuitable slopes instead of starting with beginner terrain and professional ski / snowboard lessons. Gudauri has pistes across different difficulty levels and ski schools for beginners.'),
  ('gudauri', 821, 8, 'Treat freeriding, heli-skiing, ski touring, and off-piste skiing as normal sightseeing activities rather than specialist mountain activities requiring appropriate experience, equipment, guides, and avalanche-risk assessment.'),
  ('gudauri', 821, 9, 'Ignore avalanche warnings, weather information, slope signage, helmets, and other mountain-safety requirements. Official tourism guidance specifically emphasizes weather monitoring and avalanche warnings during winter.'),
  ('gudauri', 821, 10, 'Choose accommodation solely because it is cheaper without considering proximity to the appropriate ski lift, ski school, equipment rental, restaurants, or the specific Gudauri area required by the traveler.'),
  ('gudauri', 821, 11, 'Assume Gudauri has the same extensive shopping, cultural sightseeing, entertainment, and nightlife ecosystem as Tbilisi or Batumi.'),
  ('gudauri', 821, 12, 'Overload departure day with skiing or distant excursions without allowing sufficient time for equipment return, checkout, winter-road delays, and the transfer back to Tbilisi.'),
  ('gudauri', 821, 13, 'Plan paragliding as a guaranteed activity. Flights depend strongly on suitable weather conditions, and different Gudauri launch areas have different preferred seasons and access requirements.'),
  ('gudauri', 821, 14, 'Ignore the traveler''s actual purpose, especially when the trip is primarily for skiing, snowboarding, family snow experiences, honeymoon, adventure, photography, relaxation, summer mountains, or a first-time snow holiday.'),
  ('gudauri', 822, 0, 'Builds the Gudauri itinerary around the traveler''s main purpose, skiing ability, season, fitness, preferred activity level, and comfort requirements.'),
  ('gudauri', 822, 1, 'Treats skiing and snowboarding as the core winter experiences rather than trying to fill every day with conventional sightseeing. Gudauri''s ski season generally runs from December to around mid-April.'),
  ('gudauri', 822, 2, 'Matches ski areas and slopes to traveler ability, using beginner lessons and easier pistes for first-time skiers while reserving advanced terrain and specialist activities for appropriately experienced travelers.'),
  ('gudauri', 822, 3, 'Gives beginners sufficient time for equipment fitting, ski-school orientation, instruction, practice, breaks, and gradual progression instead of treating a ski lesson as a short sightseeing activity.'),
  ('gudauri', 822, 4, 'Uses hotel location strategically according to the traveler''s preferred lift access, ski-school arrangements, restaurants, equipment rental, nightlife requirements, and overall convenience.'),
  ('gudauri', 822, 5, 'Protects substantial time for skiing / snowboarding while also allowing mountain lunches, cafés, photography, après-ski, spa, hotel relaxation, and scenic experiences.'),
  ('gudauri', 822, 6, 'Keeps Russia–Georgia Friendship Monument, Jvari Pass, Kobi, Stepantsminda / Kazbegi, and other Georgian Military Road experiences geographically and operationally logical rather than repeatedly backtracking.'),
  ('gudauri', 822, 7, 'Treats Stepantsminda / Kazbegi as a weather- and road-dependent extension from Gudauri during winter rather than an unconditional itinerary component.');
INSERT INTO destination_guidance_bullet (place_id, position, bullet_index, text) VALUES
  ('gudauri', 822, 8, 'Checks current road restrictions before Gudauri–Kobi–Stepantsminda travel because snow, ice, blizzards, and avalanche conditions can temporarily affect the Georgian Military Road.'),
  ('gudauri', 822, 9, 'Leaves flexibility for lift closures, strong winds, snowfall, poor visibility, changing snow quality, road restrictions, and other mountain conditions.'),
  ('gudauri', 822, 10, 'Uses professional instructors for beginners and qualified guides for advanced mountain activities rather than relying solely on independent exploration.'),
  ('gudauri', 822, 11, 'Treats freeriding, ski touring, heli-skiing, and advanced off-piste skiing as specialist adventure products requiring substantially more safety planning than ordinary groomed-piste skiing.'),
  ('gudauri', 822, 12, 'Uses the Gudauri–Kobi cable-car connection strategically when appropriate and operational, particularly for scenery and onward access toward the Stepantsminda side.'),
  ('gudauri', 822, 13, 'Treats paragliding as a conditional experience rather than a fixed itinerary item. Gudauri has several established paragliding areas, but flights require suitable weather and certified operators.'),
  ('gudauri', 822, 14, 'Keeps at least one lower-intensity period in a 3–4 night itinerary for spa, hotel relaxation, cafés, mountain photography, scenic viewpoints, or a relaxed New Gudauri evening.'),
  ('gudauri', 822, 15, 'Adjusts the itinerary substantially by season: winter focuses on skiing and snow activities, while warmer months are better suited to mountain scenery, hiking, biking, paragliding, and outdoor exploration.'),
  ('gudauri', 822, 16, 'Uses private transfers or suitable mountain-road vehicles when greater comfort, luggage capacity, ski equipment, family convenience, or winter-road reliability is important.'),
  ('gudauri', 822, 17, 'Avoids unnecessary hotel changes because Gudauri works best when travelers establish one convenient mountain base and organize skiing and nearby excursions from it.'),
  ('gudauri', 822, 18, 'Allows additional departure-day buffer during winter because road conditions between Gudauri and Tbilisi can change and mountain weather can affect journey times.'),
  ('gudauri', 822, 19, 'For short stays, prioritizes **SKIING / SNOWBOARDING + GUDAURI MOUNTAIN EXPERIENCE + ONE SCENIC EXPERIENCE** rather than attempting Gudauri, Kazbegi, multiple adventure activities, and numerous road stops.'),
  ('gudauri', 822, 20, 'For longer stays, adds **KOBI / KAZBEGI EXCURSION + PARAGLIDING + SPA / RELAXATION + ADDITIONAL SKI DAYS + SCENIC GEORGIAN MILITARY ROAD EXPERIENCES** according to weather, season, traveler ability, and interests.'),
  ('gudauri', 822, 21, 'Uses Gudauri primarily as a **SKI, SNOW, MOUNTAIN, ADVENTURE, SCENIC, PHOTOGRAPHY, AND ALPINE-RELAXATION DESTINATION**, rather than positioning it as a culture-heavy city break, shopping destination, or major urban nightlife destination.'),
