  ('baku', 868, 0, 'Treat Baku as only a quick Old City stop and miss the Boulevard, Highland Park, Flame Towers, Heydar Aliyev Center, food, shopping, nightlife, and wider Absheron experiences.'),
  ('baku', 868, 1, 'Try to cover Icherisheher, Maiden Tower, Palace of the Shirvanshahs, Baku Boulevard, Highland Park, Heydar Aliyev Center, Gobustan, mud volcanoes, Ateshgah, Yanar Dag, shopping, and nightlife in a very short trip.'),
  ('baku', 868, 2, 'Schedule Gobustan, mud volcanoes, Ateshgah, Yanar Dag, and central Baku sightseeing together without allowing enough time for road travel, meals, walking, photography, and rest.'),
  ('baku', 868, 3, 'Underestimate Baku''s geography. Central attractions are relatively easy to combine, but Gobustan and Absheron attractions require separate road-based planning.'),
  ('baku', 868, 4, 'Rush Icherisheher as a photo stop instead of allowing enough time for Maiden Tower, Palace of the Shirvanshahs, historic streets, caravanserais, mosques, cafés, crafts, and architectural details.'),
  ('baku', 868, 5, 'Plan long Old City, Boulevard, Gobustan, or Absheron sightseeing periods during the hottest summer hours without considering heat and sun exposure.'),
  ('baku', 868, 6, 'Ignore Baku''s strong winds when planning long waterfront walks, elevated viewpoints, boat experiences, or exposed regional excursions.'),
  ('baku', 868, 7, 'Choose accommodation solely because it is cheaper without considering access to Icherisheher, Fountain Square, Nizami Street, Baku Boulevard, metro stations, restaurants, and evening activities.'),
  ('baku', 868, 8, 'Plan every day as a full sightseeing day without leaving enough time for Azerbaijani dining, traditional tea, cafés, shopping, spa experiences, Baku Boulevard, nightlife, or relaxed city exploration.'),
  ('baku', 868, 9, 'Treat Gobustan and the mud volcanoes as the same attraction instead of allowing separate travel, viewing, and terrain considerations.'),
  ('baku', 868, 10, 'Assume every vehicle is suitable for mud-volcano routes regardless of road and surface conditions.'),
  ('baku', 868, 11, 'Assume all Old City streets and historical attractions are completely step-free despite cobblestones, slopes, stairs, and historic building layouts.'),
  ('baku', 868, 12, 'Focus only on modern landmarks such as Flame Towers and Heydar Aliyev Center while missing Baku''s UNESCO-listed historical core.'),
  ('baku', 868, 13, 'Focus only on historical sightseeing and miss Baku''s strong modern architecture, food, shopping, nightlife, and Caspian waterfront identity.'),
  ('baku', 868, 14, 'Overload departure day with regional excursions without allowing sufficient time for traffic, hotel checkout, shopping, and the transfer to Heydar Aliyev International Airport.'),
  ('baku', 868, 15, 'Ignore major events when selecting dates. Events such as the Azerbaijan Grand Prix can significantly affect central traffic, road access, accommodation demand, and pricing. The 2026 Azerbaijan Grand Prix is scheduled for September 24–26.'),
  ('baku', 868, 16, 'Ignore the traveler''s actual purpose, especially when the trip is primarily for honeymoon, family, heritage, architecture, gastronomy, shopping, nightlife, luxury, photography, or regional day trips.'),
  ('baku', 869, 0, 'Builds the Baku itinerary around the traveler''s primary purpose rather than treating every visitor as a standard sightseeing client.'),
  ('baku', 869, 1, 'Groups Icherisheher, Maiden Tower, Palace of the Shirvanshahs, Fountain Square, Nizami Street, and nearby central attractions into geographically efficient sightseeing circuits.'),
  ('baku', 869, 2, 'Gives Icherisheher sufficient time because it is Baku''s UNESCO-listed historic core and contains far more than the Maiden Tower alone.'),
  ('baku', 869, 3, 'Separates central Baku sightseeing from major regional excursions when the traveler prefers a relaxed pace.'),
  ('baku', 869, 4, 'Treats Gobustan as a major archaeology / UNESCO excursion rather than a brief roadside stop.');
INSERT INTO destination_guidance_bullet (place_id, position, bullet_index, text) VALUES
  ('baku', 869, 5, 'Combines Ateshgah + Yanar Dag as a logical Absheron fire-heritage circuit instead of repeatedly traveling between central Baku and the peninsula.'),
  ('baku', 869, 6, 'Uses Gobustan + mud volcanoes as a coordinated excursion when road conditions, transport, weather, and traveler ability make the combination practical.'),
  ('baku', 869, 7, 'Keeps Gobustan and the full Absheron fire circuit on separate days for families, seniors, honeymooners, or travelers who prefer a slower itinerary.'),
  ('baku', 869, 8, 'Uses hotel location strategically around Icherisheher, Fountain Square, Nizami Street, Sahil, Baku Boulevard, 28 May, or another well-connected central area.'),
  ('baku', 869, 9, 'Uses walking for compact central clusters, metro and buses for economical urban travel, taxis for convenience, and private drivers for Gobustan and Absheron excursions.'),
  ('baku', 869, 10, 'Protects free time for Azerbaijani food, traditional tea, cafés, shopping, Baku Boulevard, spa experiences, rooftop dining, nightlife, and relaxed city exploration.'),
  ('baku', 869, 11, 'Places outdoor sightseeing during morning or later-afternoon periods in hot summer weather and uses museums, malls, restaurants, or hotel relaxation during the hottest hours.'),
  ('baku', 869, 12, 'Treats Baku''s wind as a real itinerary factor, particularly for Boulevard walks, Highland Park, Caspian boat experiences, and exposed Absheron locations.'),
  ('baku', 869, 13, 'Uses Highland Park and Flame Towers strategically around sunset or evening rather than treating them only as daytime checklist stops.'),
  ('baku', 869, 14, 'Uses Heydar Aliyev Center as the principal modern-architecture contrast to Icherisheher rather than filling the itinerary with too many separate architecture stops.'),
  ('baku', 869, 15, 'Allows sufficient time for Azerbaijani cuisine because food is one of Baku''s stronger tourism products rather than merely a meal between attractions.'),
  ('baku', 869, 16, 'Uses Yashil Bazaar, Nizami Street, Icherisheher, and modern malls according to the traveler''s shopping purpose instead of recommending the same shopping area to everyone.'),
  ('baku', 869, 17, 'Treats nightlife by traveler type: Fountain Square / Nizami Street for lively evenings, Boulevard for relaxed waterfront time, and premium hotels / rooftops for luxury or honeymoon travelers.'),
  ('baku', 869, 18, 'Uses private transfers and chauffeured vehicles selectively for luxury travelers, families, seniors, airport journeys, and regional excursions.'),
  ('baku', 869, 19, 'Keeps accessibility attraction-specific because modern Baku and historic Icherisheher can provide very different walking and mobility conditions.'),
  ('baku', 869, 20, 'Allows extra time for Gobustan and mud-volcano excursions because terrain, access routes, heat, and transport can materially affect the visit.'),
  ('baku', 869, 21, 'Checks opening hours, museum schedules, attraction tickets, road conditions, event calendars, and operating conditions before finalizing the itinerary.'),
  ('baku', 869, 22, 'Checks the Formula 1 calendar and other major events before confirming central accommodation. In 2026, the Azerbaijan Grand Prix runs September 24–26 on the Baku City Circuit, which passes through central parts of the city and the Icherisheher area.'),
  ('baku', 869, 23, 'Avoids unnecessary hotel changes on short Baku stays because most central sightseeing and regional excursions can be managed efficiently from one well-located base.'),
  ('baku', 869, 24, 'Keeps at least one lower-intensity period in a 3–4 night itinerary for Baku Boulevard, cafés, traditional tea, shopping, spa, hotel relaxation, or an unhurried dinner.'),
  ('baku', 869, 25, 'For short stays, prioritizes **ICHERISHEHER + BAKU BOULEVARD + HIGHLAND PARK / FLAME TOWERS + ONE MODERN OR CULINARY EXPERIENCE** rather than attempting every regional excursion.'),
  ('baku', 869, 26, 'For 3–4 night stays, adds **HEYDAR ALIYEV CENTER + GOBUSTAN OR ABSHERON FIRE-HERITAGE EXCURSION + SHOPPING / FOOD / EVENING EXPERIENCES** according to traveler interests.'),
  ('baku', 869, 27, 'For longer stays, adds **GOBUSTAN + MUD VOLCANOES + ATESHGAH + YANAR DAG + ABSHERON COAST + DEEPER MUSEUM / SHOPPING / FOOD EXPERIENCES** without overloading individual days.'),
  ('baku', 869, 28, 'Uses Baku primarily as a **CITY, CULTURE, HERITAGE, ARCHITECTURE, FOOD, SHOPPING, NIGHTLIFE, LUXURY, PHOTOGRAPHY, AND CASPIAN-WATERFRONT DESTINATION**, with Gobustan and Absheron providing the strongest regional extensions.'),
