  ('kok-tobe', 1056, 0, 'Treat Kok Tobe only as a quick viewpoint and miss that it is a hilltop leisure complex combining panoramic city views, the cable-car journey, restaurants, cafés, family entertainment, walking areas, and an evening atmosphere.'),
  ('kok-tobe', 1056, 1, 'Schedule Kok Tobe as a rushed 30-minute stop without allowing time for transport to the lower station, ticketing, possible queues, the cable-car ride, walking around the park, photographs, food, and the return journey.'),
  ('kok-tobe', 1056, 2, 'Assume Kok Tobe is interchangeable with Medeu or Shymbulak. Kok Tobe is an urban hilltop attraction close to central Almaty, while Medeu and Shymbulak are separate mountain products requiring different transport, time, weather planning, and expectations.'),
  ('kok-tobe', 1056, 3, 'Plan Kok Tobe together with multiple distant attractions such as Medeu, Shymbulak, Big Almaty Lake, Charyn Canyon, or Kolsay Lakes on the same day.'),
  ('kok-tobe', 1056, 4, 'Visit only at midday and miss one of Kok Tobe’s strongest uses: late-afternoon, sunset, and evening city views, followed by dinner, cafés, or entertainment.'),
  ('kok-tobe', 1056, 5, 'Assume the cable car always operates normally. The official Kok Tobe site periodically announces temporary cableway closures and individual attraction closures, so current operating status must be checked before confirming the visit.'),
  ('kok-tobe', 1056, 6, 'Assume the cable-car ride is merely transport rather than part of the experience. The route links central Almaty with the hilltop park, runs for approximately 1,620 metres, and takes about six minutes over the city.'),
  ('kok-tobe', 1056, 7, 'Fail to distinguish between the lower cable-car station and the hilltop park. The cableway departs from Dostyk Avenue in central Almaty, while the upper station is inside Kok Tobe Park.'),
  ('kok-tobe', 1056, 8, 'Underestimate the importance of timing during weekends, holidays, school breaks, summer evenings, and good-weather periods, when demand can increase for tickets, restaurants, and family attractions.'),
  ('kok-tobe', 1056, 9, 'Ignore weather and visibility. Kok Tobe is best known for wide views over Almaty, so haze, rain, snow, wind, or low cloud can materially affect the experience and photography.'),
  ('kok-tobe', 1056, 10, 'Treat Kok Tobe as a purely adult sightseeing stop and overlook its relevance for families. The park includes attractions and leisure facilities in addition to viewpoints and dining.'),
  ('kok-tobe', 1056, 11, 'Treat Kok Tobe as a purely family amusement park and overlook its appeal for couples, honeymooners, photographers, food-focused travelers, and luxury clients seeking a scenic dinner or private-feeling evening.'),
  ('kok-tobe', 1056, 12, 'Assume all attractions, restaurants, cafés, and entertainment facilities have identical operating hours. Individual operations, maintenance schedules, seasonal conditions, and special events can affect availability.'),
  ('kok-tobe', 1056, 13, 'Ignore the elevation difference. Kok Tobe is located at approximately 1,100 metres above sea level, making it higher than central Almaty but much lower and generally less demanding than the major high-mountain products around Medeu and Shymbulak.'),
  ('kok-tobe', 1056, 14, 'Plan a formal dinner at Kok Tobe without checking restaurant reservations, opening times, dress expectations, weather comfort, and transport arrangements after dark.'),
  ('kok-tobe', 1056, 15, 'Choose a return by cable car without considering whether the last descent time works with dinner, sunset, children’s routines, or onward evening plans.'),
  ('kok-tobe', 1056, 16, 'Focus only on the hilltop and overlook the practical city connection. Kok Tobe works well with nearby central-Almaty sightseeing, especially the Dostyk Avenue, Republic Palace, Abay-area, and central cultural districts.'),
  ('kok-tobe', 1056, 17, 'Overload departure day with Kok Tobe when luggage, hotel checkout, traffic, airport transfer, weather risk, and cableway operating conditions make timing uncertain.'),
  ('kok-tobe', 1056, 18, 'Ignore the traveler’s actual purpose, especially whether Kok Tobe is intended primarily for family leisure, photography, a scenic cable-car ride, sunset, dining, romance, city orientation, or a relaxed evening.'),
  ('kok-tobe', 1057, 0, 'Positions Kok Tobe as a flexible **CITY VIEW + CABLE CAR + DINING + FAMILY LEISURE + EVENING** product rather than as a substitute for Almaty’s major mountain excursions.'),
  ('kok-tobe', 1057, 1, 'Uses Kok Tobe strategically on the first or second day to provide a visual orientation to Almaty, its urban scale, green districts, and mountain setting.'),
  ('kok-tobe', 1057, 2, 'Schedules the visit for late afternoon where possible, allowing time for daylight views, sunset photography, illuminated city views, and dinner or cafés afterward.'),
  ('kok-tobe', 1057, 3, 'Allows approximately two to three hours for a basic Kok Tobe visit, and longer when adding a sit-down meal, children’s attractions, photography, or a relaxed evening.'),
  ('kok-tobe', 1057, 4, 'Uses the cable car as the preferred experience-led arrival when operating, because it connects central Almaty with Kok Tobe and provides aerial views during the approximately six-minute journey.'),
  ('kok-tobe', 1057, 5, 'Keeps a flexible alternative for access and descent, especially for travelers with mobility needs, young children, weather sensitivity, strict schedules, or late-evening reservations.'),
  ('kok-tobe', 1057, 6, 'Checks the official Kok Tobe website or current park communications shortly before the visit for cable-car availability, maintenance announcements, attraction closures, event activity, and updated pricing.'),
  ('kok-tobe', 1057, 7, 'Confirms the return cable-car operating time before booking a sunset dinner, arranging a guided evening, or committing to an onward nightlife plan.'),
  ('kok-tobe', 1057, 8, 'Combines Kok Tobe efficiently with nearby central-Almaty experiences rather than with distant mountain or regional nature excursions.'),
  ('kok-tobe', 1057, 9, 'Uses Kok Tobe as an evening anchor after a lighter central city programme, such as museums, Panfilov Park, Ascension Cathedral, Green Bazaar, cafés, or shopping.'),
  ('kok-tobe', 1057, 10, 'Treats the park as family-friendly but avoids assuming every attraction suits every age, height, mobility level, weather condition, or personal comfort level.'),
  ('kok-tobe', 1057, 11, 'Uses restaurants according to traveler profile: Kazakh dining for cultural travelers, refined dining for luxury and honeymoon clients, cafés for relaxed city-break visitors, and flexible casual options for families.'),
  ('kok-tobe', 1057, 12, 'Builds in weather flexibility. On clear days, Kok Tobe can be prioritized for panoramas and photography; in poor visibility, the visit can be shortened, shifted, or replaced by indoor city experiences.'),
  ('kok-tobe', 1057, 13, 'Advises travelers to bring layers, particularly for sunset and evening visits, because hilltop conditions can feel cooler or windier than central Almaty.'),
  ('kok-tobe', 1057, 14, 'Uses Kok Tobe especially well for couples, honeymooners, families, first-time visitors, photographers, food-focused travelers, and clients with limited time who still want a mountain-adjacent visual experience without a full mountain day.'),
  ('kok-tobe', 1057, 15, 'Avoids presenting Kok Tobe as an adventure or alpine excursion. It is better marketed as an accessible scenic and leisure experience, while Medeu, Shymbulak, Ile-Alatau, Charyn, Kolsay, and Kaindy serve different outdoor and nature-travel purposes.'),
  ('kok-tobe', 1057, 16, 'For short stays, prioritizes **CENTRAL ALMATY + KOK TOBE SUNSET / EVENING + ONE FOOD OR CULTURAL EXPERIENCE**.'),
  ('kok-tobe', 1057, 17, 'For family itineraries, combines **KOK TOBE CABLE CAR + VIEWPOINTS + AGE-APPROPRIATE ATTRACTIONS + FLEXIBLE DINING**, without adding excessive same-day sightseeing.'),
  ('kok-tobe', 1057, 18, 'For honeymoon and luxury itineraries, combines **PRIVATE OR PREMIUM TRANSFERS + SUNSET VIEWS + RESERVATION-LED DINING + A RELAXED CITY EVENING**.'),
  ('kok-tobe', 1057, 19, 'For photography-led itineraries, checks visibility and sunset timing, arrives before golden hour, allows time for both daylight and dusk images, and avoids scheduling a rigid immediate commitment afterward.'),
  ('kok-tobe', 1057, 20, 'For 3–4 night Almaty stays, uses Kok Tobe as a lighter urban-evening experience alongside one separate Medeu / Shymbulak mountain day and central city sightseeing.'),
  ('kok-tobe', 1057, 21, 'For longer stays, uses Kok Tobe as part of the urban programme while keeping major regional products—Big Almaty Lake / Ile-Alatau, Charyn Canyon, Kolsay Lakes, and Kaindy Lake—on separate dedicated days or overnight circuits.'),
  ('kok-tobe', 1057, 22, 'Positions Kok Tobe primarily as a **CITY PANORAMA, CABLE CAR, DINING, CAFÉ, FAMILY LEISURE, PHOTOGRAPHY, SUNSET, ROMANCE, AND EVENING ALMATY EXPERIENCE**, rather than only as a viewpoint or a mountain attraction.'),
