  ('samarkand', 1097, 0, 'Treat Samarkand only as a Registan photo stop and miss Bibi-Khanum, Siab Bazaar, Shah-i-Zinda, Gur-e-Amir, Afrasiab, Ulugh Beg Observatory, local food, crafts, and the wider Silk Road heritage.'),
  ('samarkand', 1097, 1, 'Try to cover Registan, Gur-e-Amir, Bibi-Khanum, Siab Bazaar, Shah-i-Zinda, Afrasiab, Ulugh Beg Observatory, Konigil, Silk Road Samarkand, and Shakhrisabz in one short stay.'),
  ('samarkand', 1097, 2, 'Underestimate Samarkand''s historical depth. The destination combines ancient Afrasiab, medieval / Timurid Samarkand, traditional neighbourhoods, and later urban development rather than one single monument zone.'),
  ('samarkand', 1097, 3, 'Schedule Registan + Bibi-Khanum + Shah-i-Zinda + Gur-e-Amir + museums + markets in one rushed day without allowing enough time for interiors, walking, photography, meals, heat, and rest.'),
  ('samarkand', 1097, 4, 'Treat Shah-i-Zinda as a quick photo stop without allowing time for its architecture, religious significance, steps, slopes, and detailed tilework.'),
  ('samarkand', 1097, 5, 'Ignore Afrasiab and Ulugh Beg Observatory even though they add ancient Sogdian and medieval scientific history beyond Samarkand''s better-known Timurid monuments.'),
  ('samarkand', 1097, 6, 'Treat Siab Bazaar only as shopping rather than combining it with Samarkand bread, dried fruits, nuts, sweets, spices, local food, and everyday market atmosphere.'),
  ('samarkand', 1097, 7, 'Ignore summer heat when designing long walking programmes around Registan, Bibi-Khanum, Shah-i-Zinda, and other exposed heritage sites.'),
  ('samarkand', 1097, 8, 'Assume every historic monument is easily accessible. Steps, thresholds, historic paving, uneven surfaces, and large monument complexes require traveler-specific planning.'),
  ('samarkand', 1097, 9, 'Choose accommodation only by price without considering access to Registan, restaurants, evening sightseeing, railway transfers, and the planned heritage circuit.'),
  ('samarkand', 1097, 10, 'Treat Konigil, Imam Al-Bukhari Memorial Complex, Urgut, Ohalik, and Shakhrisabz as if they were part of the compact central walking zone.'),
  ('samarkand', 1097, 11, 'Add Shakhrisabz to an already full Samarkand sightseeing day instead of treating it as a separate regional heritage excursion.'),
  ('samarkand', 1097, 12, 'Focus exclusively on monuments and miss Uzbek cuisine, Samarkand bread, markets, traditional crafts, paper-making, cafés, and local cultural experiences.'),
  ('samarkand', 1097, 13, 'Assume Samarkand offers the same nightlife and modern entertainment depth as a major metropolitan destination; its strongest evening products are illuminated heritage, dining, cafés, cultural experiences, and relaxed leisure.'),
  ('samarkand', 1097, 14, 'Ignore Silk Road Samarkand / Eternal City for honeymoon, luxury, family, wellness, conference, or modern-resort clients.'),
  ('samarkand', 1097, 15, 'Overload departure day with distant attractions without allowing enough time for hotel checkout, railway-station / airport transfer, traffic, and luggage.'),
  ('samarkand', 1097, 16, 'Ignore the traveler''s actual purpose, especially when the trip is primarily for culture, history, architecture, photography, family, honeymoon, pilgrimage, food, luxury, crafts, or Silk Road exploration.'),
  ('samarkand', 1098, 0, 'Builds the itinerary around Samarkand''s strongest identity: SILK ROAD + TIMURID HERITAGE + ARCHITECTURE + HISTORY + FOOD + PHOTOGRAPHY.'),
  ('samarkand', 1098, 1, 'Uses Registan / Central Historic Samarkand as the core first-time sightseeing area and allows time for both daytime architectural detail and evening illumination.'),
  ('samarkand', 1098, 2, 'Groups Bibi-Khanum + Siab Bazaar + Hazrat Khizr logically into one heritage, market, food, and photography circuit.'),
  ('samarkand', 1098, 3, 'Groups Shah-i-Zinda + Afrasiab as a deeper historical corridor while allowing additional time for steps, walking, archaeology, and photography.'),
  ('samarkand', 1098, 4, 'Combines Gur-e-Amir + Rukhabad with the central Timurid circuit instead of creating unnecessary vehicle movements.'),
  ('samarkand', 1098, 5, 'Uses Ulugh Beg Observatory + Afrasiab Museum for travelers interested in astronomy, archaeology, education, science, and deeper historical interpretation.'),
  ('samarkand', 1098, 6, 'Keeps Konigil as a secondary craft experience for 3+ night stays rather than sacrificing major monuments during a very short first visit.'),
  ('samarkand', 1098, 7, 'Uses Silk Road Samarkand / Eternal City strategically for luxury, honeymoon, family, wellness, dining, and premium leisure travelers.'),
  ('samarkand', 1098, 8, 'Treats Imam Al-Bukhari Memorial Complex as a dedicated religious / pilgrimage excursion rather than normal central sightseeing.'),
  ('samarkand', 1098, 9, 'Uses Ohalik / Ok Buyro / Mirankul for countryside relaxation when travelers want a break from monument-heavy days.'),
  ('samarkand', 1098, 10, 'Uses Urgut for travelers specifically interested in markets, crafts, local culture, shopping, and regional photography.'),
  ('samarkand', 1098, 11, 'Treats Shakhrisabz as a separate half-day / full-day regional heritage excursion, particularly for travelers with 4+ nights.'),
  ('samarkand', 1098, 12, 'Protects time for Uzbek food, Samarkand bread, plov, samsa, kebabs, tea, dried fruits, local sweets, and market experiences.'),
  ('samarkand', 1098, 13, 'Uses early morning and late afternoon strategically during hot months and avoids unnecessarily long exposed walking around midday.'),
  ('samarkand', 1098, 14, 'Keeps at least one lower-intensity period for cafés, shopping, hotel relaxation, Silk Road Samarkand, crafts, or an unhurried dinner.'),
  ('samarkand', 1098, 15, 'Checks current monument hours, ticket arrangements, restoration work, religious access, railway schedules, road conditions, and special events before finalizing the itinerary.'),
  ('samarkand', 1098, 16, 'Adjusts the itinerary by traveler type: Registan + Siab Bazaar + easier heritage stops for families; Registan evening + Gur-e-Amir + premium dining + Silk Road Samarkand for honeymoon travelers; private guides, premium hotels, chauffeured transport, and curated heritage experiences for luxury travelers.'),
  ('samarkand', 1098, 17, 'For short stays, prioritizes **REGISTAN + GUR_E_AMIR + BIBI_KHANUM / SIAB_BAZAAR + SHAH_I_ZINDA**.'),
  ('samarkand', 1098, 18, 'For 3–4 night stays, adds **AFRASIAB + ULUGH_BEG_OBSERVATORY + KONIGIL OR SILK_ROAD_SAMARKAND** according to traveler profile.'),
  ('samarkand', 1098, 19, 'For longer stays, adds **IMAM_AL_BUKHARI + URGUT / COUNTRYSIDE + SHAKHRISABZ + DEEPER FOOD / CRAFT EXPERIENCES** without sacrificing the central heritage core.'),
  ('samarkand', 1098, 20, 'Uses Samarkand primarily as a **CULTURE, SILK_ROAD, HISTORY, ARCHITECTURE, PHOTOGRAPHY, FOOD, FAMILY, HONEYMOON, RELIGIOUS_HERITAGE, CRAFT, AND LUXURY DESTINATION**, rather than positioning it as only a Registan stop.'),
