  ('tashkent', 1138, 0, 'Treat Tashkent only as an arrival point for Samarkand, Bukhara, Khiva, or nearby mountains and miss Khast Imam, Chorsu Bazaar, Tashkent Metro architecture, museums, Uzbek food, cafés, shopping, parks, nightlife, and the capital''s wider urban identity.'),
  ('tashkent', 1138, 1, 'Try to cover Khast Imam, Chorsu Bazaar, Tashkent Metro, Amir Timur Square, Independence Square, Tashkent TV Tower, museums, shopping, Chimgan, Amirsoy, Charvak Reservoir, and the Fergana Valley in one short stay.'),
  ('tashkent', 1138, 2, 'Underestimate Tashkent''s geography. Central attractions can be combined efficiently, but Chimgan, Beldersay, Amirsoy, Charvak Reservoir, Ugam-Chatkal National Park, and the Fergana Valley require separate planning and substantial transfer time.'),
  ('tashkent', 1138, 3, 'Schedule Khast Imam + Chorsu Bazaar + several museums + Tashkent TV Tower + multiple shopping districts together without allowing enough time for traffic, metro transfers, meals, prayer-time considerations, photography, heat, and relaxation.'),
  ('tashkent', 1138, 4, 'Treat Chimgan, Amirsoy, Beldersay, and Charvak as quick additions to a city-sightseeing day instead of a dedicated mountain / reservoir excursion.'),
  ('tashkent', 1138, 5, 'Attempt Amirsoy + Chimgan + Beldersay + Charvak + Ugam-Chatkal hiking in one day without considering driving time, resort operations, walking, daylight, weather, road conditions, and traveler fatigue.'),
  ('tashkent', 1138, 6, 'Assume every mountain activity operates throughout the year. Skiing, snowboarding, gondolas, hiking, water recreation, and mountain leisure depend on season, weather, snow, wind, visibility, road conditions, and resort operations.'),
  ('tashkent', 1138, 7, 'Plan skiing or snowboarding without considering ability, equipment rental, instructor availability, appropriate clothing, snow conditions, lift operations, and mountain-weather changes. Uzbekistan''s official tourism platform identifies Chimgan, Beldersay, and Amirsoy as the region''s principal winter-sports resorts. [web:166]'),
  ('tashkent', 1138, 8, 'Plan long mountain hikes without considering fitness, weather, trail conditions, water, sun exposure, appropriate equipment, daylight, guide requirements, or whether access restrictions apply.'),
  ('tashkent', 1138, 9, 'Assume Charvak Reservoir always has easy vehicle access to every shoreline, beach, viewpoint, or recreation facility. Specific access, seasonal operations, road conditions, and visitor arrangements should be checked before travel.'),
  ('tashkent', 1138, 10, 'Ignore the contrast between hot urban Tashkent and cooler mountain environments. Summer mountain visits can be far more comfortable than city sightseeing, while winter mountain travel can involve snow, ice, fog, and reduced visibility.'),
  ('tashkent', 1138, 11, 'Choose accommodation only by price without considering proximity to a metro station, restaurants, central attractions, evening options, airport transfers, and practical mountain-excursion pickup routes.'),
  ('tashkent', 1138, 12, 'Focus only on Uzbek heritage and miss Tashkent''s major urban strengths: metro architecture, Soviet and modern cityscapes, parks, museums, cafés, restaurants, shopping, theatre, and nightlife.'),
  ('tashkent', 1138, 13, 'Focus only on city sightseeing and underestimate Tashkent''s access to the Western Tian Shan / Chatkal foothills, including Chimgan, Beldersay, Amirsoy, Charvak, and Ugam-Chatkal landscapes.'),
  ('tashkent', 1138, 14, 'Treat food merely as a meal stop despite Tashkent''s strong Uzbek gastronomy. Chorsu Bazaar, osh centres, bakeries, tea culture, plov, shashlik, samsa, lagman, non, and modern Uzbek restaurants should form part of the itinerary.'),
  ('tashkent', 1138, 15, 'Assume Tashkent offers limited shopping because Uzbekistan is often marketed around Silk Road heritage. In reality, the capital combines Chorsu''s market economy with substantial malls, international brands, local designers, crafts, and food-product shopping.'),
  ('tashkent', 1138, 16, 'Plan every evening around sightseeing and miss Tashkent''s restaurants, cafés, lounges, bars, rooftop venues, theatre, live music, shopping centres, and relaxed urban evening atmosphere.'),
  ('tashkent', 1138, 17, 'Overload departure day with a Chimgan, Amirsoy, Charvak, or Fergana Valley excursion without allowing for traffic, luggage, checkout, airport-transfer timing, and possible road delays.'),
  ('tashkent', 1138, 18, 'Ignore seasonal differences. Spring and autumn are strongest for city walking and general sightseeing; summer favors morning/evening city activity plus mountain and reservoir escapes; winter increases demand for ski and snow experiences.'),
  ('tashkent', 1138, 19, 'Treat the Fergana Valley as a simple same-day extension without recognizing its scale. Several daily trains connect Tashkent with main valley cities, but journeys commonly take about 5–6 hours each way, so a multi-day plan is normally more realistic. [web:165]'),
  ('tashkent', 1138, 20, 'Ignore the traveler''s actual purpose, especially when the trip is primarily for culture, food, shopping, nightlife, family travel, honeymoon, skiing, mountain scenery, photography, luxury, business, or wider Uzbekistan travel.'),
  ('tashkent', 1139, 0, 'Builds the Tashkent itinerary around the traveler''s primary purpose, available nights, and season rather than treating every visitor as a standard city-and-mountain client.'),
  ('tashkent', 1139, 1, 'Groups Khast Imam + Chorsu Bazaar + Kukeldash Madrasah + nearby old-city streets into one efficient cultural and food circuit. Khast Imam is one of Tashkent''s principal sightseeing places and works naturally with the broader old-city area. [web:164]'),
  ('tashkent', 1139, 2, 'Gives central Tashkent enough time because the city itself is a major tourism product, not merely a transfer point for Uzbekistan''s other destinations.'),
  ('tashkent', 1139, 3, 'Uses Tashkent Metro architecture strategically as a practical cultural activity, especially when heat, rain, or a low-walking itinerary makes long outdoor sightseeing less desirable.'),
  ('tashkent', 1139, 4, 'Treats the Tashkent TV Tower as a strategic sunset / evening experience rather than simply another daytime attraction.'),
  ('tashkent', 1139, 5, 'Groups Amir Timur Square, Independence Square, museums, central boulevards, selected metro stations, cafés, and evening dining into a logical central-city circuit.'),
  ('tashkent', 1139, 6, 'Groups Chimgan + Beldersay + Amirsoy + Charvak carefully according to the traveler''s purpose, season, departure time, traffic, road conditions, and confirmed resort operations.'),
  ('tashkent', 1139, 7, 'Uses Amirsoy differently by season: skiing and snowboarding during winter; gondola rides, mountain views, dining, hiking, and outdoor leisure during warmer conditions.'),
  ('tashkent', 1139, 8, 'Treats Charvak as a separate mountain-and-reservoir product, often combined selectively with Chimgan or Amirsoy rather than treated as a quick city add-on. Uzbekistan Tourism identifies Charvak as about 30 kilometres from Chimgan and highlights its recreation areas, boating, water activities, and mountain scenery. [web:167]'),
  ('tashkent', 1139, 9, 'Keeps Ugam-Chatkal National Park and longer hiking routes as separate active-nature products, with current route access, guide needs, weather, and physical requirements checked before confirmation.'),
  ('tashkent', 1139, 10, 'Treats the Fergana Valley as a major cultural extension. Use rail, private transport, or domestic flights strategically, but for comfort-focused itineraries prioritize at least one overnight rather than attempting a rushed return journey.'),
  ('tashkent', 1139, 11, 'Uses private transport or organized excursions for mountain, reservoir, national-park, and regional journeys while relying on walking, metro, buses, and reputable ride-hailing for Tashkent city sightseeing.'),
  ('tashkent', 1139, 12, 'Uses hotel location strategically. Central or metro-connected accommodation works best for city-heavy itineraries, while premium central-south properties suit luxury, business, dining, shopping, and private-driver itineraries.'),
  ('tashkent', 1139, 13, 'Protects substantial time for Uzbek food, Chorsu Bazaar, plov, samsa, non, shashlik, local tea, cafés, and contemporary restaurants because gastronomy is one of Tashkent''s strongest urban products.'),
  ('tashkent', 1139, 14, 'Uses shopping according to traveler type: Chorsu Bazaar for food, spices, dried fruit, everyday market energy, and traditional products; central malls for mainstream retail; premium hotels and modern districts for international brands and luxury shopping.'),
  ('tashkent', 1139, 15, 'Treats nightlife as a meaningful urban strength rather than an afterthought, particularly for couples, solo travelers, younger visitors, business travelers, luxury travelers, and food-focused clients.'),
  ('tashkent', 1139, 16, 'Keeps at least one lower-intensity period for cafés, spa, parks, shopping, hotel relaxation, theatre, or an unhurried Uzbek dinner.'),
  ('tashkent', 1139, 17, 'Adjusts the itinerary substantially by traveler type: Khast Imam + Chorsu + parks + TV Tower for families; TV Tower + premium dining + spa + private Charvak / Amirsoy experience for honeymoon travelers; private guides, chauffeur service, luxury hotels, fine dining, and flexible mountain excursions for luxury travelers; Chimgan / Ugam-Chatkal hiking and resort activities for active travelers.'),
  ('tashkent', 1139, 18, 'Checks museum hours, mosque visiting etiquette and access, metro conditions, event schedules, mountain weather, snow depth, road conditions, lift operations, trail conditions, and excursion-provider inclusions before finalizing the itinerary.'),
  ('tashkent', 1139, 19, 'Uses seasonal logic carefully: spring prioritizes culture, parks, food, and improving mountain access; summer prioritizes early / late city sightseeing plus Charvak and mountain escapes; autumn prioritizes walking, gastronomy, photography, and mountain scenery; winter combines indoor culture with Amirsoy, Chimgan, or Beldersay snow experiences.'),
  ('tashkent', 1139, 20, 'Avoids unnecessary hotel changes during short Tashkent stays because the city works effectively as a single base for cultural sightseeing and selected mountain-day excursions.'),
  ('tashkent', 1139, 21, 'For short stays, prioritizes **KHAST_IMAM + CHORSU_BAZAAR + TASHKENT_METRO + CENTRAL_TASHKENT + ONE_SIGNATURE_UZBEK_FOOD_EXPERIENCE**.'),
  ('tashkent', 1139, 22, 'For 3–4 night stays, adds **TASHKENT_TV_TOWER + MUSEUMS / SHOPPING / NIGHTLIFE + ONE_MOUNTAIN_OR_RESERVOIR_EXCURSION such as CHIMGAN, AMIRSOY, or CHARVAK** according to season and interests.'),
  ('tashkent', 1139, 23, 'For longer stays, adds **UGAM_CHATKAL + DEEPER_MOUNTAIN_EXPLORATION + FERGANA_VALLEY + SHOPPING + GASTRONOMY + NIGHTLIFE** without sacrificing central-city time.'),
  ('tashkent', 1139, 24, 'Uses Tashkent primarily as a **CITY, CULTURE, HERITAGE, FOOD, SHOPPING, NIGHTLIFE, BUSINESS, WELLNESS, MOUNTAIN, NATURE, SKI, ADVENTURE, PHOTOGRAPHY, FAMILY, HONEYMOON, AND GATEWAY-TO-UZBEKISTAN DESTINATION**, rather than positioning it only as a transit hub.'),
