  ('beijing', 1966, 0, 'Use the Beijing Subway network for almost all inner-city transit instead of taxis; rides start at just ¥3–¥8 ($0.40–$1.10 USD) and avoid heavy surface traffic jams.'),
  ('beijing', 1966, 1, 'Dine at local neighborhood noodle houses, dumpling stalls, and food courts (*xiaochi*) instead of tourist-oriented restaurants near major sights, dropping meal costs dramatically.'),
  ('beijing', 1966, 2, 'Visit major sights using standard advance online ticket reservations directly, avoiding secondary third-party agency markups for Forbidden City, Summer Palace, and Temple of Heaven entry.'),
  ('beijing', 1966, 3, 'Stay in boutique hotels or hostels located 2–3 subway stops outside the immediate Tiananmen or Wangfujing radius to enjoy significantly lower room rates with minimal added travel time.'),
  ('beijing', 1966, 4, 'Take public express buses or shared high-speed rail connections to Mutianyu or Badaling Great Wall sections instead of booking expensive private tour packages.'),
  ('beijing', 1966, 5, 'Explore Beijing''s vibrant public parks (Jingshan, Beihai, Temple of Heaven park grounds) and historic hutong alleyways on self-guided walking or cycling tours using shared city bikes.'),
  ('beijing', 1966, 6, 'Booking accommodations far from any subway station to save on nightly rates, leading to heavy transit delays, excessive walking in extreme weather, or high taxi reliance.'),
  ('beijing', 1966, 7, 'Skipping a reliable eSIM, VPN, or data roaming solution to save minor costs, which leaves you unable to navigate, use digital translation, or pay via mobile payment apps (Alipay / WeChat Pay).'),
  ('beijing', 1966, 8, 'Opting for unlicensed "black cabs" (*heiche*) at airports, train stations, or Great Wall parking lots instead of official metered taxis or ride-hailing apps (DiDi).'),
  ('beijing', 1966, 9, 'Cutting out a authentic Peking Duck dinner or a trip to scenic Great Wall sections (like Mutianyu or Simatai) purely for budget reasons when visiting the capital.'),
  ('beijing', 1970, 0, 'CAPITAL AIRPORT (PEK): Capital Airport Express train running directly from T2/T3 to Dongzhimen and Beixinqiao metro transfer hubs.'),
  ('beijing', 1970, 1, 'DAXING AIRPORT (PKX): Daxing Airport Express subway running directly to Caoqiao Station (Line 10/19), or high-speed rail to Beijing West.'),
  ('beijing', 1970, 2, 'MAIN RAIL STATIONS: Beijing Railway Station (Line 2), Beijing South (Line 4/14), and Beijing West (Line 7/9) connect seamlessly to the citywide subway grid.'),
