  ('shanghai', 2019, 0, 'Use the extensive Shanghai Metro network for nearly all city transit instead of taxis; single rides start at just ¥3–¥10 ($0.40–$1.40 USD) and completely bypass surface road congestion.'),
  ('shanghai', 2019, 1, 'Dine at local neighborhood dumpling houses, pan-fried bun stalls (*shengjianbao*), and basement mall food courts instead of high-end Western cafes or Bund-side restaurants to cut food costs dramatically.'),
  ('shanghai', 2019, 2, 'Book tickets for Shanghai Disneyland, the Shanghai Tower observation deck, and Huangpu River cruises online in advance directly or through official partner platforms to secure early-bird discounts and avoid long lines.'),
  ('shanghai', 2019, 3, 'Choose accommodations located 2–4 metro stops away from major hubs like The Bund, East Nanjing Road, or Lujiazui to enjoy substantially lower nightly rates with minimal added commute time.'),
  ('shanghai', 2019, 4, 'Take standard metro lines (Line 11 for Disneyland, Line 17 for Zhujiajiao Water Town) or regular high-speed trains to Suzhou/Hangzhou instead of booking costly private day tours.'),
  ('shanghai', 2019, 5, 'Explore Shanghai''s vibrant, free-to-visit urban zones, including The Bund promenade, the leafy streetscapes of the Former French Concession, West Bund riverside parks, and public museums (like the Shanghai Museum).'),
  ('shanghai', 2019, 6, 'Booking a hotel far from any Shanghai Metro line to save on room costs, resulting in long transit times, high taxi dependency, or navigation hassles in city traffic.'),
  ('shanghai', 2019, 7, 'Foregoing a reliable eSIM, VPN, or international data roaming option to save small amounts, leaving you without mobile maps, translation tools, or digital payment access (Alipay / WeChat Pay).'),
  ('shanghai', 2019, 8, 'Using unregistered drivers or "black cabs" (*heiche*) at Pudong (PVG) or Hongqiao (SHA) airports and train stations instead of official metered taxis, ride-hailing apps (DiDi), or the Maglev train.'),
  ('shanghai', 2019, 9, 'Skipping iconic Shanghai experiences—such as a plate of authentic Xiaolongbao, a skyline viewing deck, or an evening Huangpu River light-show walk—purely for budget restrictions when visiting the city.'),
  ('shanghai', 2023, 0, 'PUDONG AIRPORT (PVG): High-speed Shanghai Maglev Train running directly to Longyang Road Station (8 minutes to Metro Lines 2/7/16/18), Airport Inter-Terminal Link Express, or Metro Line 2 direct to central hubs like People''s Square and East Nanjing Road.'),
  ('shanghai', 2023, 1, 'HONGQIAO AIRPORT / RAILWAY STATION (SHA): Metro Line 2 and Line 10 connecting T1/T2 directly to Jing''an Temple, Xintiandi, and The Bund.'),
  ('shanghai', 2023, 2, 'MAIN RAIL STATIONS: Shanghai Station (Lines 1/3/4), Shanghai South (Lines 1/3/15), and Hongqiao Railway Station (Lines 2/10/17) connect seamlessly to the citywide metro grid.'),
