  ('hong-kong', 2066, 0, 'Ride the MTR Disneyland Resort Line from any part of Hong Kong using an Octopus Card instead of taking point-to-point taxis or private ride-shares.'),
  ('hong-kong', 2066, 1, 'Purchase pre-booked official Disney Meal Vouchers online (e.g., 2-in-1 or 3-in-1 combo vouchers) to save significantly on quick-service lunch, dinner, and snacks inside the park.'),
  ('hong-kong', 2066, 2, 'Book 2-Day Park Tickets or multi-day room-and-ticket bundle offers directly on official channels or authorized platforms (like Klook) for a substantially lower per-day rate compared to single-day tickets.'),
  ('hong-kong', 2066, 3, 'Choose off-site accommodation in nearby Tung Chung (1 stop away via MTR) or Tsing Yi/Tsuen Wan instead of staying inside the resort to reduce nightly hotel expenses drastically.'),
  ('hong-kong', 2066, 4, 'Bring allowed personal snacks and an empty reusable water bottle into the park to refill at free drinking fountains located throughout all 8 themed lands.'),
  ('hong-kong', 2066, 5, 'Buy Disney merchandise and character headbands ahead of time or at town outlets if traveling with young children, saving inside-park retail budgets for resort-exclusive items.'),
  ('hong-kong', 2066, 6, 'Staying at an off-site hotel with poor public transit connectivity to save a small amount, resulting in expensive late-night taxi rides back after the *Momentous* fireworks show.'),
  ('hong-kong', 2066, 7, 'Skipping a 2-Day ticket or early entry pass when visiting during peak periods, which forces you to rush through major lands like World of Frozen and face extreme queue wait times.'),
  ('hong-kong', 2066, 8, 'Foregoing a reliable local SIM, eSIM, or mobile roaming service, leaving you unable to use the official Hong Kong Disneyland App for live wait times, mobile food ordering, and standby passes.'),
  ('hong-kong', 2066, 9, 'Skipping iconic resort experiences—such as watching the *Momentous* nighttime spectacular, riding Mystic Manor, or trying character-themed dim sum—purely for budget restrictions.'),
  ('hong-kong', 2070, 0, 'HONG KONG INTERNATIONAL AIRPORT (HKG): Board public franchised Airport Bus Route A21, A22, or A29 to Lantau Link Bus Interchange, then switch to Bus R8 directly into Hong Kong Disneyland Resort (total cost approx. HK$15–$25 per person).'),
  ('hong-kong', 2070, 1, 'MTR SUBWAY NETWORK: Take the MTR Tung Chung Line from Central/Hong Kong Station or Kowloon Station to Sunny Bay Station, then cross the platform to the iconic Disney-themed MTR Disneyland Resort Line (trains feature Mickey-shaped windows and bronze character statues).'),
  ('hong-kong', 2070, 2, 'WEST KOWLOON HIGH-SPEED RAIL STATION: Take MTR from Austin/Kowloon Station to Sunny Bay Station, or take a direct 25-minute taxi.'),
  ('hong-kong', 2070, 3, 'HZMB HONG KONG PORT: Take local feeder buses (e.g., B5) connecting the border bridge terminal directly to Sunny Bay MTR Station or the resort.'),
  ('hong-kong', 2072, 0, 'TODDLERS'),
  ('hong-kong', 2072, 1, '3+'),
  ('hong-kong', 2072, 2, '6+'),
  ('hong-kong', 2072, 3, 'TEENAGERS'),
  ('hong-kong', 2072, 4, 'Leverage the compact park layout—all lands radiate from the central Castle hub, allowing easy mid-day hotel nap breaks.'),
  ('hong-kong', 2072, 5, 'Prioritize indoor air-conditioned shows (*Festival of the Lion King*, *Mickey and the Wondrous Book*) during hot afternoon hours.'),
  ('hong-kong', 2072, 6, 'Download the official Hong Kong Disneyland App for live queue wait times, mobile food ordering, and Disney Standby Pass reservations.'),
  ('hong-kong', 2072, 7, 'Use the Baby Care Center on Main Street, U.S.A., equipped with nursing rooms, changing tables, micro-waves, and high chairs.'),
  ('hong-kong', 2072, 8, 'Verify ride height requirements early (e.g., RC Racer: 120cm, Big Grizzly Mountain: 112cm, Hyperspace Mountain: 102cm).'),
  ('hong-kong', 2072, 9, 'Pre-rent strollers at the park entrance or bring your own foldable stroller for infants and toddlers.'),
