  ('macau', 2113, 0, 'Take advantage of the extensive, free casino and hotel shuttle bus network connecting ferry terminals, border gates, airport, and major Cotai/Peninsula resorts to cover major transfer corridors at zero cost.'),
  ('macau', 2113, 1, 'Use public buses for secondary routes (flattish fare around 6 MOP / ~$0.75 USD per ride, or discounted with a Macau Pass) and the Macau LRT for Cotai-to-Taipa transit instead of taking taxis.'),
  ('macau', 2113, 2, 'Dine at local neighborhood soup noodle shops, Macanese bakery stalls (*pork chop buns*, *Portuguese egg tarts*), and street food alleys around San Ma Lo and Taipa Village rather than high-end resort dining rooms.'),
  ('macau', 2113, 3, 'Book tickets for the Macau Tower Observation Deck, zip-line experiences, and resort performance shows online in advance to catch early-bird rates and direct promotion packages.'),
  ('macau', 2113, 4, 'Base your hotel stay on the Macau Peninsula or in non-resort areas of Taipa for significantly lower nightly rates compared to central Cotai Strip integrated mega-resorts.'),
  ('macau', 2113, 5, 'Explore Macau''s rich, free-to-visit UNESCO World Heritage sites, including the Ruins of St. Paul''s, Senado Square, A-Ma Temple, Mount Fortress, and the scenic villages of Taipa and Coloane.'),
  ('macau', 2113, 6, 'Staying in distant border-adjacent properties far from bus routes or shuttle hubs to save on room rates, resulting in long waiting times and high taxi fares.'),
  ('macau', 2113, 7, 'Skipping localized data roaming, an eSIM, or portable Wi-Fi, leaving you without live navigation maps, transport route apps, or mobile translation assistance.'),
  ('macau', 2113, 8, 'Using unmetered private transfers or unauthorized taxi offers at ferry ports, border gates, or the airport instead of official metered taxis or free hotel shuttle buses.'),
  ('macau', 2113, 9, 'Passing up iconic culinary and cultural experiences—such as fresh Portuguese egg tarts, authentic Macanese African Chicken, or a night walk along the illuminated Cotai Strip—solely due to tight budget caps.'),
  ('macau', 2117, 0, 'MACAU INTERNATIONAL AIRPORT (MFM) / TAIPA FERRY TERMINAL: Complimentary casino shuttles directly to Cotai Strip and Peninsula integrated resorts, or Macau Light Rapid Transit (LRT) Taipa Line connecting directly to Cotai, Lotus/Hengqin transfer points, and Barra (Peninsula).'),
  ('macau', 2117, 1, 'OUTER HARBOUR FERRY TERMINAL / BORDER GATE: Free casino express shuttles running to major Peninsula and Cotai hotel hubs, or public buses (e.g., Routes 3, 10, 25B, 101X).'),
  ('macau', 2117, 2, 'HZMB MACAU PORT: Public bus routes 101X (to Macau Peninsula) and 102X (to Taipa/Cotai), or shuttle transfers connecting to major ferry terminal transport hubs.'),
