  ('france', 2247, 0, 'Treat France as only Paris and miss Normandy, Loire Valley, Champagne, Burgundy, Alsace, Provence, Côte d''Azur, Alps, Atlantic coast, and other major regions.'),
  ('france', 2247, 1, 'Try to cover Paris + Normandy + Loire + Bordeaux + Provence + Riviera + Alps in one short trip.'),
  ('france', 2247, 2, 'Underestimate France''s geography. Major regions are well connected, but excessive city changes still create luggage handling, station time, transfers, and rushed sightseeing.'),
  ('france', 2247, 3, 'Schedule Eiffel Tower + Louvre + Versailles + Montmartre + Seine cruise + shopping in one overloaded Paris day.'),
  ('france', 2247, 4, 'Treat Versailles as a quick central-Paris attraction instead of a substantial half-day / full-day excursion.'),
  ('france', 2247, 5, 'Focus only on monuments and miss French food, bakeries, cafés, markets, wine, neighbourhoods, gardens, shopping, and evening culture.'),
  ('france', 2247, 6, 'Assume a rental car is necessary everywhere. Paris and many major cities work better by walking and public transport, while cars are more useful for countryside and village routes.'),
  ('france', 2247, 7, 'Choose hotels only by price without considering rail stations, metro access, central sightseeing, restaurants, and regional-transfer logistics.'),
  ('france', 2247, 8, 'Underestimate peak-season demand in Paris, the Riviera, Alpine resorts, Provence, and other major leisure destinations.'),
  ('france', 2247, 9, 'Add too many museum visits for families or couples without protecting parks, meals, shopping, cruises, spa, and free time.'),
  ('france', 2247, 10, 'Treat Provence, Burgundy, Champagne, and Bordeaux only as sightseeing regions instead of food, wine, countryside, and slow-travel experiences.'),
  ('france', 2247, 11, 'Ignore seasonal differences between Mediterranean France, Atlantic regions, cities, Alps, Pyrenees, and Corsica.'),
  ('france', 2247, 12, 'Assume all historic centres, castles, beaches, and mountain attractions have uniform accessibility.'),
  ('france', 2247, 13, 'Ignore the traveler''s actual purpose, especially when the trip is primarily for honeymoon, family, luxury, gastronomy, wine, culture, coast, skiing, shopping, or relaxation.'),
  ('france', 2248, 0, 'Builds the itinerary around France''s strongest identity: CULTURE + HERITAGE + FOOD + WINE + CITIES + COAST + COUNTRYSIDE + MOUNTAINS + LUXURY.'),
  ('france', 2248, 1, 'Uses Paris as the main first-time gateway but does not automatically make the entire trip Paris-only.'),
  ('france', 2248, 2, 'Gives Paris at least 3–4 nights when major museums, neighbourhoods, shopping, Versailles, gastronomy, and evening experiences are important.'),
  ('france', 2248, 3, 'Groups central Paris attractions geographically instead of repeatedly crossing the city.'),
  ('france', 2248, 4, 'Uses Versailles as a dedicated excursion and keeps sufficient time for the palace and gardens.'),
  ('france', 2248, 5, 'Selects ONE_OR_TWO_REGIONS after Paris according to traveler purpose rather than collecting destinations.'),
  ('france', 2248, 6, 'Uses Champagne for wine / honeymoon / luxury, Loire Valley for castles / family / romance, and Normandy for history / coast.'),
  ('france', 2248, 7, 'Uses Provence and Côte d''Azur differently: Provence for villages, markets, countryside and wine; Riviera for coast, luxury, nightlife and Mediterranean leisure.'),
  ('france', 2248, 8, 'Uses Burgundy and Bordeaux strategically for wine and gastronomy travelers rather than inserting them into every first itinerary.'),
  ('france', 2248, 9, 'Uses French Alps / Pyrenees primarily for ski, hiking, mountain, adventure, and wellness travel.'),
  ('france', 2248, 10, 'Uses TGV / regional rail for major intercity travel and rental cars / private drivers selectively for countryside, vineyards, villages, and remote coastal areas.'),
  ('france', 2248, 11, 'Protects substantial time for French cuisine, bakeries, markets, cafés, wine, and regional food because gastronomy is a core destination product.'),
  ('france', 2248, 12, 'Uses hotel location strategically, especially in Paris and short multi-city itineraries.'),
  ('france', 2248, 13, 'Keeps at least one lower-intensity period for cafés, parks, shopping, spa, wine tasting, beach time, or relaxed dining.'),
  ('france', 2248, 14, 'Checks attraction reservations, rail schedules, seasonal operations, strikes / disruptions, weather, and accessibility before finalizing.'),
  ('france', 2248, 15, 'For short stays, prioritizes **PARIS + ONE_NEARBY_EXCURSION**.'),
  ('france', 2248, 16, 'For 7–10 nights, prioritizes **PARIS + ONE_OR_TWO_CONTRASTING_REGIONS**.'),
  ('france', 2248, 17, 'For 12–14 nights, adds **TWO_OR_THREE_REGIONS + DEEPER_GASTRONOMY / WINE / COAST / COUNTRYSIDE EXPERIENCES** without excessive hotel changes.'),
  ('france', 2248, 18, 'Uses France primarily as a **CULTURE, HISTORY, FOOD, WINE, ROMANCE, FAMILY, LUXURY, SHOPPING, COAST, NATURE, SKI, PHOTOGRAPHY, AND SLOW-TRAVEL DESTINATION**.'),
