  ('switzerland', 2291, 0, 'Treat Switzerland as only Zurich + Lucerne and miss Interlaken / Jungfrau Region, Zermatt, Montreux, St. Moritz, Ticino, Bern, Rhine Falls, and the major panoramic rail routes.'),
  ('switzerland', 2291, 1, 'Try to cover Zurich + Lucerne + Interlaken + Jungfraujoch + Zermatt + Montreux + St. Moritz in one short trip.'),
  ('switzerland', 2291, 2, 'Underestimate transfer time even though Swiss transport is excellent. Frequent hotel changes still create luggage handling, station time, check-in, and lost sightseeing hours.'),
  ('switzerland', 2291, 3, 'Schedule Mt. Titlis + Pilatus + Rigi together instead of choosing one signature Lucerne mountain excursion.'),
  ('switzerland', 2291, 4, 'Treat Interlaken as the final attraction rather than the gateway to Grindelwald, Lauterbrunnen, Jungfraujoch, Wengen, and the wider Bernese Oberland.'),
  ('switzerland', 2291, 5, 'Plan Jungfraujoch, Titlis, Gornergrat, and other high-altitude excursions on consecutive days without allowing for weather, altitude, fatigue, or poor visibility.'),
  ('switzerland', 2291, 6, 'Assume every mountain excursion operates identically year-round. Cable cars, hiking routes, snow activities, and some mountain facilities vary by season.'),
  ('switzerland', 2291, 7, 'Ignore scenic rail as a core attraction. Glacier Express, Bernina Express, GoldenPass Express, and Lucerne–Interlaken Express are experiences, not simply transport. Switzerland Tourism''s Grand Train Tour covers 1,280 km across eight sections and links major destinations through these panoramic routes.'),
  ('switzerland', 2291, 8, 'Rent a car automatically even though trains, buses, boats, mountain railways, and cable cars cover most standard first-time itineraries extremely well.'),
  ('switzerland', 2291, 9, 'Choose hotels only by room price without considering railway-station access, mountain connections, luggage movement, and time saved.'),
  ('switzerland', 2291, 10, 'Spend too many nights in Zurich while reducing time in Lucerne, Jungfrau Region, or Zermatt on a nature-focused first trip.'),
  ('switzerland', 2291, 11, 'Treat Zermatt as a roadside destination despite its car-free structure and rail-based arrival logic.'),
  ('switzerland', 2291, 12, 'Overload families with high-altitude excursions and long train days instead of mixing lakes, villages, snow play, scenic rail, and easy outdoor experiences. Switzerland Tourism specifically promotes family resorts, lakes, themed trails, cable cars, snow parks, and family-friendly outdoor activities.'),
  ('switzerland', 2291, 13, 'Assume Switzerland is only winter-focused. Summer and early autumn are major seasons for hiking, lakes, villages, scenic railways, cycling, and mountain sightseeing.'),
  ('switzerland', 2291, 14, 'Underestimate Switzerland''s prices and buy multiple summit excursions without comparing passes, discounts, and itinerary value.'),
  ('switzerland', 2291, 15, 'Ignore weather flexibility. A cloudy mountain day can severely reduce the value of Jungfraujoch, Matterhorn, Titlis, or other panoramic excursions.'),
  ('switzerland', 2291, 16, 'Ignore the traveler''s actual purpose, especially when the trip is primarily for honeymoon, family, skiing, hiking, luxury, scenic rail, photography, wellness, or relaxed lake travel.'),
  ('switzerland', 2292, 0, 'Builds the itinerary around Switzerland''s strongest identity: **MOUNTAINS + LAKES + SCENIC_RAIL + VILLAGES + SKIING + HIKING + LUXURY + WELLNESS + PHOTOGRAPHY**.'),
  ('switzerland', 2292, 1, 'Uses Zurich mainly as an international gateway, city experience, shopping base, or final-night stop unless urban travel is a major priority.'),
  ('switzerland', 2292, 2, 'Uses Lucerne strategically for **OLD_TOWN + LAKE_LUCERNE + ONE_OF_TITLIS_OR_PILATUS_OR_RIGI**.'),
  ('switzerland', 2292, 3, 'Treats Interlaken as the base for the wider **JUNGFRAU + GRINDELWALD + LAUTERBRUNNEN** cluster.'),
  ('switzerland', 2292, 4, 'Uses Zermatt when Matterhorn, romance, skiing, hiking, luxury, or iconic mountain photography are important.'),
  ('switzerland', 2292, 5, 'Uses Montreux / Lake Geneva for lakefront romance, Chillon, Lavaux, and GoldenPass connectivity.'),
  ('switzerland', 2292, 6, 'Uses St. Moritz / Engadin primarily for luxury, skiing, Alpine wellness, and Bernina / Glacier Express itineraries.'),
  ('switzerland', 2292, 7, 'Uses Ticino for a warmer, Italian-speaking contrast with lakes, food, palms, and slower travel.'),
  ('switzerland', 2292, 8, 'Treats panoramic trains as dedicated tourism products and protects enough time to enjoy them rather than stacking sightseeing immediately before and after long rail sectors.'),
  ('switzerland', 2292, 9, 'Uses public transport as the default and adds private transfers only when luggage, privacy, mobility, luxury, or specialist routing justifies them.'),
  ('switzerland', 2292, 10, 'Minimizes hotel changes. For 5–7 nights, two or three bases normally provide a better experience than four or five one-night stops.'),
  ('switzerland', 2292, 11, 'Keeps major high-altitude excursions flexible by weather and avoids pre-building every day around a summit.'),
  ('switzerland', 2292, 12, 'Keeps at least one lower-intensity period for lake cruises, village walks, spa, cafés, chocolate, shopping, or hotel relaxation.'),
  ('switzerland', 2292, 13, 'Adjusts by traveler type: Lucerne + easy mountain rail for families; Lucerne + Jungfrau + Zermatt for honeymoon; St. Moritz / Zermatt + first-class rail for luxury; Jungfrau + Zermatt + outdoor activities for adventure.'),
  ('switzerland', 2292, 14, 'Uses Switzerland Tourism''s Grand Train Tour logic for longer itineraries rather than inventing inefficient cross-country routes. Its official tours connect destinations such as Zurich, Interlaken, Montreux, Zermatt, St. Moritz, Lugano, Lucerne, and Schaffhausen.'),
  ('switzerland', 2292, 15, 'Checks railway schedules, panoramic-train reservations, mountain operations, weather, trail status, ski conditions, and accessibility before finalizing.'),
  ('switzerland', 2292, 16, 'For short stays, prioritizes **LUCERNE + ONE_SIGNATURE_MOUNTAIN + INTERLAKEN / JUNGFRAU**.'),
  ('switzerland', 2292, 17, 'For 5–7 nights, prioritizes **LUCERNE + JUNGFRAU_REGION + ZERMATT_OR_ZURICH**.'),
  ('switzerland', 2292, 18, 'For 8–10 nights, adds **MONTREUX / ST_MORITZ / TICINO + ONE_MAJOR_PANORAMIC_RAIL_ROUTE** according to interests.'),
  ('switzerland', 2292, 19, 'Uses Switzerland primarily as a **NATURE, MOUNTAIN, SCENIC_RAIL, HONEYMOON, FAMILY, LUXURY, SKI, ADVENTURE, PHOTOGRAPHY, WELLNESS, LAKE, AND SLOW-TRAVEL DESTINATION**.'),
  ('switzerland', 2295, 0, 'luxury'),
  ('switzerland', 2295, 1, 'honeymoon convenience'),
  ('switzerland', 2295, 2, 'senior travelers'),
  ('switzerland', 2295, 3, 'substantial luggage'),
  ('switzerland', 2295, 4, 'specialist rural excursions'),
  ('switzerland', 2295, 5, 'private photography tours'),
  ('switzerland', 2295, 6, 'selected airport transfers'),
  ('switzerland', 2295, 7, 'travelers requiring maximum schedule flexibility'),
  ('switzerland', 2295, 8, 'Lucerne'),
  ('switzerland', 2295, 9, 'Chapel Bridge'),
  ('switzerland', 2295, 10, 'Lake Lucerne experience'),
  ('switzerland', 2295, 11, 'One of Titlis / Pilatus / Rigi'),
  ('switzerland', 2295, 12, 'Interlaken'),
  ('switzerland', 2295, 13, 'Jungfrau Region'),
  ('switzerland', 2295, 14, 'Grindelwald or Lauterbrunnen'),
  ('switzerland', 2295, 15, 'Zermatt / Matterhorn when time allows'),
  ('switzerland', 2295, 16, 'One scenic railway experience'),
  ('switzerland', 2295, 17, 'One Swiss chocolate / cheese experience');
INSERT INTO destination_guidance_bullet (place_id, position, bullet_index, text) VALUES
  ('switzerland', 2295, 18, 'One relaxed lake or Alpine-village experience'),
  ('switzerland', 2295, 19, 'Do not try to cover Lucerne, Jungfrau, Zermatt, Montreux, St. Moritz, Ticino, and Zurich in a short stay.'),
  ('switzerland', 2295, 20, 'Do not schedule multiple expensive summit excursions every day.'),
  ('switzerland', 2295, 21, 'Do not assume Titlis, Jungfraujoch, Matterhorn, or other high-Alpine views are guaranteed in poor visibility.'),
  ('switzerland', 2295, 22, 'Do not underestimate altitude, mountain weather, snow, or trail difficulty.'),
  ('switzerland', 2295, 23, 'Do not ignore scenic trains by treating them only as transportation.'),
  ('switzerland', 2295, 24, 'Do not rent a car automatically when rail already serves the itinerary efficiently.'),
  ('switzerland', 2295, 25, 'Do not choose accommodation only by room price without considering station access.'),
  ('switzerland', 2295, 26, 'Do not overload families with consecutive high-altitude days.'),
  ('switzerland', 2295, 27, 'Do not assume all cable cars, mountain railways, and hiking routes operate year-round.'),
  ('switzerland', 2295, 28, 'Do not underestimate peak summer and ski-season prices.'),
  ('switzerland', 2295, 29, 'Do not assume mountain trails, snow areas, historic streets, or every station are uniformly wheelchair accessible.'),
  ('switzerland', 2295, 30, 'Do not sacrifice lake cruises, village walks, spa, dining, and free time simply to increase destination count.'),
  ('switzerland', 2296, 0, 'Switzerland Tourism — Official information on Lucerne, Interlaken, Jungfrau Region, Zermatt, Matterhorn, Montreux, Ticino, St. Moritz, Zurich, family travel, mountain activities, scenic rail, and national destination planning.'),
  ('switzerland', 2296, 1, 'Switzerland Tourism / Grand Train Tour — Information on the 1,280-km panoramic network, eight sections, major scenic routes, lakes, UNESCO sites, and recommended multi-day itineraries.'),
  ('switzerland', 2296, 2, 'Switzerland Tourism / Family Destinations — Information on child-friendly resorts, hiking, lakes, cable cars, themed trails, snow activities, and family travel.'),
  ('switzerland', 2296, 3, 'SBB — Official information on Swiss rail transport, reduced-mobility travel, accessible connections, station assistance, and train accessibility.'),
  ('luxembourg', 2301, 0, 'Use free nationwide trains, buses, and trams instead of taxis or rental cars for most sightseeing.'),
  ('luxembourg', 2301, 1, 'Choose hostels, guesthouses, apartments, or well-reviewed regional hotels rather than premium central properties.'),
  ('luxembourg', 2301, 2, 'Stay in Luxembourg City or another well-connected base and make day trips instead of changing hotels frequently.'),
  ('luxembourg', 2301, 3, 'Eat at bakeries, supermarkets, cafés, markets, and casual restaurants rather than premium dining for every meal.'),
  ('luxembourg', 2301, 4, 'Prioritize free or low-cost experiences such as Luxembourg City walks, viewpoints, forests, hiking trails, cycling, villages, and countryside scenery.'),
  ('luxembourg', 2301, 5, 'Group Vianden, Mullerthal, Moselle, Éislek, or Minett excursions according to transport connections.'),
  ('luxembourg', 2301, 6, 'Travel in March, April, October, or November when interests suit the season and accommodation demand is generally lower.'),
  ('luxembourg', 2301, 7, 'Use regional trains and buses for castle, hiking, and countryside excursions instead of automatically booking private tours.'),
  ('luxembourg', 2301, 8, 'Very cheap accommodation with poor public-transport access.'),
  ('luxembourg', 2301, 9, 'Using taxis unnecessarily without checking the fare first; Luxembourg taxi fares are not nationally fixed.'),
  ('luxembourg', 2301, 10, 'Booking the cheapest hiking, cycling, kayaking, or specialist outdoor service without checking safety and inclusions.'),
  ('luxembourg', 2301, 11, 'Sacrificing convenient accommodation for a very small saving on a short stay.'),
  ('luxembourg', 2301, 12, 'Renting a car simply because the itinerary includes countryside attractions.'),
