  ('venice', 2909, 0, 'Treat Venice as only Piazza San Marco + Rialto Bridge + gondola ride and miss Dorsoduro art heritage, Cannaregio and the Jewish Ghetto, Castello and the Arsenale, San Polo churches, Giudecca viewpoints, and the wider lagoon islands.'),
  ('venice', 2909, 1, 'Overload Day 1 with St. Mark''s Basilica, Doge''s Palace, Rialto Bridge, Dorsoduro, Murano, Burano, and an evening gondola ride within a single sightseeing day.'),
  ('venice', 2909, 2, 'Try to combine SAN_MARCO + MURANO + BURANO + TORCELLO + LIDO in one short itinerary simply because the islands appear geographically close on a map.'),
  ('venice', 2909, 3, 'Treat Venice like a normal road-based European city and rely on taxis, private cars, or ride-hailing instead of understanding that the historic city functions primarily through WALKING + VAPORETTI + WATER_TAXIS.'),
  ('venice', 2909, 4, 'Underestimate bridge crossings, narrow calli, uneven paving, waterbus boarding, luggage handling, and the physical effort involved in navigating Venice on foot.'),
  ('venice', 2909, 5, 'Choose a hotel only by straight-line map distance without checking how many stepped bridges lie between the nearest vaporetto stop and the property.'),
  ('venice', 2909, 6, 'Stay only around San Marco throughout the trip and miss quieter evening atmosphere, local bacari, residential canals, and authentic neighborhoods in Cannaregio, Castello and Dorsoduro.'),
  ('venice', 2909, 7, 'Rush Murano as a generic souvenir stop rather than distinguishing the island''s centuries-old glassmaking heritage, Museo del Vetro, artisan furnaces, Basilica dei Santi Maria e Donato, and reputable glass workshops.'),
  ('venice', 2909, 8, 'Treat Burano only as an Instagram photography location and ignore its lace tradition, fishing-island history, lagoon food culture, and the possibility of combining it intelligently with Torcello.');
INSERT INTO destination_guidance_bullet (place_id, position, bullet_index, text) VALUES
  ('venice', 2909, 9, 'Assume that Murano + Burano + Torcello can always be covered properly in only two or three hours despite waterbus travel and waiting time.'),
  ('venice', 2909, 10, 'Schedule San Marco and Rialto only during the busiest middle-of-day periods instead of using early mornings and evenings when the historic centre becomes significantly more atmospheric.'),
  ('venice', 2909, 11, 'Ignore Venice''s serious visitor-pressure problem and design itineraries around maximum attraction count rather than slower, geographically grouped sightseeing.'),
  ('venice', 2909, 12, 'Use repeated individual vaporetto journeys without comparing them against time-limited ACTV passes when several water trips or lagoon islands are planned.'),
  ('venice', 2909, 13, 'Treat every gondola journey as essential transportation rather than primarily an experiential sightseeing activity.'),
  ('venice', 2909, 14, 'Assume all Venetian cuisine is generic Italian pasta and pizza instead of scheduling cicchetti, bàcari, baccalà mantecato, sarde in saor, lagoon seafood, risotto, bigoli and Veneto wines.'),
  ('venice', 2909, 15, 'Book restaurants exclusively beside Piazza San Marco and the busiest Rialto routes, where pricing and tourist orientation can be significantly stronger than in neighborhood dining areas.'),
  ('venice', 2909, 16, 'Schedule excessive hotel moves between Venice Historic Centre, Mestre, Lido and lagoon islands during a short stay.'),
  ('venice', 2909, 17, 'Assume every bridge, church, vaporetto landing, heritage hotel and museum is automatically wheelchair-accessible or stroller-friendly.'),
  ('venice', 2909, 18, 'Ignore the possibility of acqua alta, heavy rain, strong wind, summer humidity or temporary transport disruption when planning tightly timed outdoor and lagoon itineraries.'),
  ('venice', 2909, 19, 'Treat the Venice Access Fee as a permanent daily entrance charge without checking the current municipal calendar and rules. The 2026 experimental application operated on 60 selected days between 3 April and 26 July and concluded on 26 July 2026.'),
  ('venice', 2910, 0, 'Builds first-time itineraries around SAN_MARCO_AND_DOGES_PALACE + GRAND_CANAL_AND_RIALTO + DORSODURO_ART_DISTRICT + ONE_AUTHENTIC_NEIGHBORHOOD_OR_LAGOON_EXPERIENCE.'),
  ('venice', 2910, 1, 'Gives San Marco enough time for Piazza San Marco, St. Mark''s Basilica, Doge''s Palace, Bridge of Sighs, Museo Correr and waterfront photography without treating the entire district as a one-hour photo stop.'),
  ('venice', 2910, 2, 'Uses the Grand Canal deliberately as both TRANSPORT_CORRIDOR + ARCHITECTURAL_SIGHTSEEING_ROUTE through ACTV Line 1 or Line 2 rather than viewing it only from bridges.'),
  ('venice', 2910, 3, 'Gives Dorsoduro enough time for GALLERIE_DELL_ACCADEMIA + PEGGY_GUGGENHEIM + SALUTE + ZATTERE + PUNTA_DELLA_DOGANA when art and romantic walking are priorities.'),
  ('venice', 2910, 4, 'Uses CANNAREGIO_AND_JEWISH_GHETTO for local atmosphere, Gothic and Renaissance churches, bacari, evening food experiences and quieter canal photography.'),
  ('venice', 2910, 5, 'Uses CASTELLO_AND_ARSENALE for Venetian naval history, Biennale venues, gardens, Via Garibaldi and more residential Venetian atmosphere.'),
  ('venice', 2910, 6, 'Uses SAN_POLO_AND_RIALTO for market heritage, cicchetti, Frari, Scuola Grande di San Rocco and Grand Canal architecture rather than only photographing Rialto Bridge.'),
  ('venice', 2910, 7, 'Treats MURANO as a dedicated GLASS_HERITAGE destination and selects reputable workshops, Museo del Vetro and historic churches instead of generic souvenir demonstrations.'),
  ('venice', 2910, 8, 'Combines BURANO + TORCELLO intelligently when a full or substantial lagoon-island block is available.'),
  ('venice', 2910, 9, 'Uses GIUDECCA_AND_SAN_GIORGIO_MAGGIORE for lagoon panoramas, quieter evenings, architecture, honeymoon itineraries and San Marco skyline photography.'),
  ('venice', 2910, 10, 'Uses LIDO_DI_VENEZIA selectively for beaches, cycling, relaxation, Film Festival interests and summer family itineraries.'),
  ('venice', 2910, 11, 'Uses ACTV_VAPORETTI for long movements and island connections, WALKING inside individual sestieri, and PRIVATE_WATER_TAXIS selectively for airport transfers, luxury itineraries, heavy luggage or difficult hotel access.'),
  ('venice', 2910, 12, 'Checks the exact hotel-to-vaporetto route before booking, including bridge count and luggage practicality.'),
  ('venice', 2910, 13, 'Keeps time for café breaks, bacari, quiet campi, waterfront sitting, spontaneous photography and getting pleasantly lost rather than turning Venice into a continuous museum checklist.'),
  ('venice', 2910, 14, 'Matches lagoon excursions, gondola rides, San Marco photography and island visits to weather, daylight and visitor-pressure conditions.'),
  ('venice', 2910, 15, 'Uses early morning and evening for SAN_MARCO + RIALTO + GRAND_CANAL_PHOTOGRAPHY whenever possible.'),
  ('venice', 2910, 16, 'Uses indoor art museums, churches and palaces strategically during rain or oppressive summer midday heat.'),
  ('venice', 2910, 17, 'For first-time visits, prioritize:'),
  ('venice', 2913, 0, 'WALKING for Pantheon, Piazza Navona, Trevi Fountain, Spanish Steps, Jewish Ghetto, Campo de'' Fiori, Monti and compact historic-centre circuits'),
  ('venice', 2913, 1, 'METRO_LINES_A_B_B1_C for longer urban movements and connections toward Vatican, Colosseum, Termini and outer districts'),
  ('venice', 2913, 2, 'ATAC_BUSES_AND_TRAMS for areas not directly connected by metro'),
  ('venice', 2913, 3, 'TAXI_OR_PRIVATE_NCC selectively for luggage, mobility limitations, late evenings and difficult cross-city transfers'),
  ('venice', 2913, 4, 'LEONARDO_EXPRESS / REGIONAL_RAIL for Fiumicino Airport and selected regional connections'),
  ('venice', 2913, 5, 'URBAN_OR_REGIONAL_RAIL for Ostia Antica and other suitable excursions'),
  ('venice', 2913, 6, 'Colosseum + Roman Forum + Palatine Hill archaeological circuit'),
  ('venice', 2913, 7, 'Vatican Museums + Sistine Chapel + St. Peter''s Basilica'),
  ('venice', 2913, 8, 'Pantheon + Piazza Navona historic-centre walk'),
  ('venice', 2913, 9, 'Trevi Fountain + Spanish Steps early-morning or evening circuit'),
  ('venice', 2913, 10, 'Authentic Roman pasta experience including Carbonara / Cacio e Pepe / Amatriciana'),
  ('venice', 2913, 11, 'Trastevere evening walk and traditional trattoria dinner'),
  ('venice', 2913, 12, 'Villa Borghese + Pincian Terrace relaxation and panorama'),
  ('venice', 2913, 13, 'Capitoline Hill + Jewish Ghetto cultural walk'),
  ('venice', 2913, 14, 'Appian Way + Catacombs archaeological extension'),
  ('venice', 2913, 15, 'Gianicolo or Aventine sunset viewpoint'),
  ('venice', 2913, 16, 'Do not treat Rome as only Colosseum + Vatican while skipping Pantheon, Piazza Navona, Trastevere, Villa Borghese, Appian Way and neighborhood food culture.'),
  ('venice', 2913, 17, 'Do not force Colosseum + Roman Forum + Vatican Museums + Trevi + Spanish Steps + Trastevere into a single rushed day.'),
  ('venice', 2913, 18, 'Do not underestimate compulsory or high-demand advance booking for headline attractions.'),
  ('venice', 2913, 19, 'Do not buy major attraction tickets through lookalike unofficial websites without checking the official portal.'),
  ('venice', 2913, 20, 'Do not schedule the Roman Forum, Palatine Hill or Appian Way during the hottest summer afternoon hours when early morning or evening alternatives are available.'),
  ('venice', 2913, 21, 'Do not rely exclusively on taxis for central sightseeing when many of Rome''s most important monuments form efficient walking circuits.'),
  ('venice', 2913, 22, 'Do not choose very distant accommodation solely for a lower nightly rate without considering commuting time.'),
  ('venice', 2913, 23, 'Do not treat Roman food as generic Italian cuisine and miss Testaccio, Jewish-Roman dishes, Roman pasta traditions, supplì and seasonal artichokes.'),
  ('venice', 2913, 24, 'Do not assume cobblestone streets, archaeological surfaces, historic stairways and every metro station are fully step-free.'),
  ('venice', 2913, 25, 'Do not underestimate walking intensity; Rome''s archaeological zones, hills, uneven paving and large historic centre require reasonable physical stamina.'),
  ('venice', 2913, 26, 'Do not add Tivoli, Florence, Naples or other regional excursions to very short Rome stays before allocating enough time to the city itself.'),
