  ('sweden', 3063, 0, 'Book a self-catering log cabin (*stuga*) with a built-in kitchen and sauna to cook meals using supermarket groceries (ICA, Coop, Willys), sharply dropping daily food costs compared to eating out.'),
  ('sweden', 3063, 1, 'Travel in late winter (March–April) or early autumn (September–October) for excellent Northern Lights viewing, snow activities, or autumn foliage (*höstglöd*) at significantly lower accommodation and train/flight rates than peak December.'),
  ('sweden', 3063, 2, 'Chase the Northern Lights independently by staying outside light-polluted town centers (like Abisko or Jukkasjärvi) and monitoring Aurora forecast apps, avoiding costly daily guided minibus tours.'),
  ('sweden', 3063, 3, 'Reserve the Vy / SJ overnight Arctic night train (*Nattåget*) from Stockholm to Kiruna or Abisko months in advance, saving both on day travel time and one night''s hotel accommodation.'),
  ('sweden', 3063, 4, 'Limit Icehotel or design hotel stays (like Treehotel or Arctic Bath) to a single bucket-list night, spending the remaining nights in traditional timber cabins or standard regional hotels.'),
  ('sweden', 3063, 5, 'Rent cross-country skis or snowshoes for low-cost, full-day self-guided exploration of national park trail networks (such as Abisko National Park) instead of motorized tours every day.'),
  ('sweden', 3063, 6, 'Booking accommodations far away from key activity hubs without renting a winter-equipped car, leading to exorbitant local taxi fares and strict regional bus timing constraints in sub-zero conditions.'),
  ('sweden', 3063, 7, 'Skipping proper thermal outer gear (heavy-duty snowsuits, insulated sub-zero boots, thermal gloves), which can ruin outdoor experiences or cost significantly more to buy last-minute.'),
  ('sweden', 3063, 8, 'Opting for unaccredited, ultra-cheap safari operators with poor safety standards, inadequate winter gear, or poor animal welfare practices on husky and reindeer farms.'),
  ('sweden', 3063, 9, 'Cutting out core bucket-list activities (like one genuine husky safari or an Icehotel experience) purely for budget reasons when visiting for a once-in-a-lifetime Arctic trip.'),
  ('sweden', 3067, 0, 'KIRUNA: Falcks Omnibus airport bus running directly from KRN Airport to Kiruna city center hotels and the central bus/train station.'),
  ('sweden', 3067, 1, 'ABISKO / BJÖRKLIDEN: Vy / SJ trains running directly along the historic Iron Ore Line (*Malmbanan*) from Kiruna C to Abisko Turiststation.'),
  ('sweden', 3067, 2, 'LULEÅ / HARADS: Länstrafiken Norrbotten regional express buses connecting Luleå Airport and central bus terminals to Bodens, Harads, and Jokkmokk.'),
