  ('iceland', 3157, 0, 'Book self-catering accommodations or campervans with kitchen facilities to cook meals using discount supermarkets (Bónus, Krónan, Nettó), drastically lowering daily food expenses compared to dining out.'),
  ('iceland', 3157, 1, 'Travel during the shoulder seasons (September–October or April–May) for ideal road conditions, puffin watching, autumn colors, or late/early Northern Lights viewing at much lower car rental and hotel rates than peak summer.'),
  ('iceland', 3157, 2, 'Purchase all alcoholic beverages at the Keflavík Airport Duty-Free store upon arrival to avoid high alcohol taxes at state-run Ávrtenbúðin (Vínbúðin) stores or bars.'),
  ('iceland', 3157, 3, 'Drink pure Icelandic tap water using a refillable bottle rather than purchasing bottled water at convenience stores.'),
  ('iceland', 3157, 4, 'Visit municipal public thermal pools (Sundlaug) in Reykjavík and local towns for an authentic geothermal bath experience at a fraction of the cost of luxury lagoons.'),
  ('iceland', 3157, 5, 'Self-drive the Ring Road or Golden Circle in a rental car or campervan to explore natural attractions (waterfalls, black sand beaches, volcanic craters) without paying for group bus tours.'),
  ('iceland', 3157, 6, 'Renting a 2WD compact car when visiting in winter or attempting to drive on unpaved Highland F-roads in summer, which risks severe vehicle damage, stranded calls, and illegal insurance violations.'),
  ('iceland', 3157, 7, 'Skipping mandatory gravel protection, sand and ash protection (SADW), or full collision damage waiver (CDW) insurance on rental vehicles, as flying gravel and high coastal winds frequently damage car doors and paintwork.'),
  ('iceland', 3157, 8, 'Attempting self-guided glacier hikes or entering ice caves without certified local mountain guides and safety equipment, which presents extreme life-threatening hazards.'),
  ('iceland', 3157, 9, 'Cutting out iconic bucket-list experiences (such as a guided glacier walk, a snowmobile tour on Langjökull, or a zodiac boat trip among Jökulsárlón icebergs) purely for budget reasons during a once-in-a-lifetime trip.'),
  ('iceland', 3161, 0, 'FLYBUS / AIRPORT DIRECT: Direct scheduled coaches from KEF to BSÍ Terminal or Skógarhlíð Bus Terminal in Reykjavík.'),
  ('iceland', 3161, 1, 'STRÆTÓ PUBLIC BUS: Bus 55 offering cheap, scheduled transit between KEF Airport and central Reykjavík.'),
  ('iceland', 3161, 2, 'DOMESTIC BUSES: Strætó intercity buses linking Reykjavík to North, East, and South Iceland routes.'),
