  ('london', 3239, 0, '**Tap via contactless or Oyster Card** for all public transport. Never buy single cash paper tickets; automated fare capping ensures you never pay more than the daily maximum limit across the Underground and bus networks.'),
  ('london', 3239, 1, '**Take advantage of free world-class museums** like the British Museum, Natural History Museum, Victoria and Albert Museum, and Tate Modern, which offer complete entry to permanent collections without charging admission.'),
  ('london', 3239, 2, '**Grab supermarket "Meal Deals"** from chains like Tesco, Sainsbury''s, or Boots (sandwich, side, and drink for £3.50–£5.00) or explore street food markets like Borough Market or Camden Market for cheap, high-quality lunches.'),
  ('london', 3239, 3, '**Score discounted West End theatre tickets** by booking same-day tickets via the official TKTS booth in Leicester Square, using apps like TodayTix, or snagging £5 standing tickets for Shakespeare''s Globe.'),
  ('london', 3239, 4, '**Book major attraction tickets online in advance** (such as the London Eye or Tower of London) to secure advance-purchase discounts compared to walk-up gate prices.'),
  ('london', 3239, 5, '**Relying solely on black cabs or ride-share apps for cross-city transit;** heavy London traffic quickly escalates taxi meters, making the Underground or walking vastly faster and cheaper.'),
  ('london', 3239, 6, '**Skipping paid entry for top historic institutions** like Westminster Abbey or the Tower of London; while expensive, their unique architectural and national history cannot be replicated by viewing them strictly from the outside.'),
  ('london', 3239, 7, '**Choosing low-cost accommodation outside Travel Zones 1–3 without accounting for transit costs;** staying in distant suburbs can consume excessive time and offset hotel savings with high daily train fares.'),
  ('london', 3239, 8, '**Opting for cheap, unaccredited street tours** instead of official Yeoman Warder ("Beefeater") tours at the Tower of London, which are included in standard entry and deliver unmatched historical insight.'),
