  ('london', 3246, 5, '**Families:** Vibrant street-food markets like Borough Market and Seven Dials Market, family-friendly gastropubs with dedicated children''s menus, and casual dining halls across Covent Garden.'),
  ('london', 3246, 6, '**Honeymooners:** Intimate candlelit dining in cozy West End bistros, romantic skyline dinners at 20 Stories-style rooftop spots like Duck & Waffle or Clos Maggiore, and luxury afternoon tea experiences.'),
  ('london', 3246, 7, '**Luxury travelers:** Multi-course tasting menus at three-Michelin-starred institutions (such as Restaurant Gordon Ramsay or Alain Ducasse at The Connaught), private chef''s tables, and historic hotel dining rooms.'),
  ('london', 3246, 8, '**Budget travelers:** Historic covered food halls, takeaway fish-and-chip shops, Asian noodle houses in Chinatown, and supermarket "meal deals" for quick park picnics.'),
  ('london', 3246, 9, '**Foodies:** Exploring the artisan stalls of Borough Market, hunting for international street eats at Maltby Street Market, and booking cutting-edge tasting menus across Soho and Shoreditch.'),
