  ('liverpool', 3283, 3, '**High-Street & Luxury Designer Wear:** High-end cosmetics, luxury accessories, and premium British and international fashion from Peter''s Lane boutiques and department stores.'),
  ('liverpool', 3283, 4, '**Antiques & Salvage Goods:** Mid-century furniture, retro homewares, industrial salvage, and rare curiosities from warehouse markets like Red Brick Vintage in the Baltic Triangle.'),
  ('liverpool', 3283, 5, '**Bold Street & The Ropewalks:** Best for independent boutiques, retro fashion, vintage record shops, alternative lifestyle goods, and quirky bookshops.'),
  ('liverpool', 3283, 6, '**Peter''s Lane (Liverpool ONE):** Preferred for luxury fashion, high-end beauty, designer tailoring, and premium international retail brands.'),
  ('liverpool', 3283, 7, '**South John Street & Paradise Street (Liverpool ONE):** Ideal for major high-street fashion flagships, sports apparel, electronics, and department stores.'),
  ('liverpool', 3283, 8, '**The Baltic Triangle (Red Brick Vintage):** Preferred for massive warehouse browsing, vintage furniture, retro homewares, and artisan crafts.'),
  ('liverpool', 3283, 9, 'Buying unofficial football merchandise or cheap knock-offs from unlicensed street vendors outside stadium gates or matchday pubs.'),
  ('liverpool', 3283, 10, 'Navigating the busy open-air thoroughfares of Liverpool ONE during peak Saturday afternoon hours if you want to avoid dense crowds.'),
  ('liverpool', 3283, 11, 'Assuming small independent arcade traders or pop-up market stalls accept card only; while digital payments are common, carrying a bit of cash is helpful for antique haggling.'),
  ('liverpool', 3283, 12, '**Vintage & Retro Bargain Hunters:** Shoppers looking to dig through curated retro rails, warehouse markets, and vintage clothing arcades.'),
  ('liverpool', 3283, 13, '**High-Street & Designer Shoppers:** Visitors seeking major global fashion brands, luxury beauty halls, and comprehensive outdoor retail centers.'),
  ('liverpool', 3283, 14, '**Music & Football Enthusiasts:** Fans searching for vinyl records, Beatles memorabilia, and official Premier League team merchandise.'),
  ('liverpool', 3284, 0, '**Live music & rock fans** hunting for legendary heritage venues, Beatles cover acts, indie basement gigs, and multi-floor music halls.'),
  ('liverpool', 3284, 1, '**High-energy partygoers & stag/hen groups** seeking massive open-air party squares, cheap drink deals, and non-stop late-night dance floors.'),
  ('liverpool', 3284, 2, '**Underground electronic & rave heads** looking for converted warehouses, industrial taprooms, and late-night techno/house events.'),
  ('liverpool', 3284, 3, '**LGBTQ+ revellers** looking for a compact, welcoming Pride Quarter packed with high-energy drag shows, pop anthems, and late-night clubs.'),
  ('liverpool', 3284, 4, 'Starting your night with refined cocktails along **Berry Street and Wood Street**, dipping into hidden speakeasies like *Berry & Rye* or secret hideouts before the main rush.'),
  ('liverpool', 3284, 5, 'Experiencing the high-voltage atmosphere of **Concert Square**, enjoying outdoor drinks under heated canopies before hitting multi-room spots like *Modo*, *Soho*, or *Heebie Jeebies* on Seel Street.'),
  ('liverpool', 3284, 6, 'Exploring the warehouse scene in the **Baltic Triangle (Cains Brewery Village)** for street food, craft beer taprooms, and large-scale alternative events like *Bongo''s Bingo* at *Camp & Furnace*.'),
  ('liverpool', 3284, 7, 'Soaking in pop-music history along **Mathew Street (The Cavern Quarter)**, catching live bands inside *The Cavern Club* and classic pubs.'),
  ('liverpool', 3284, 8, 'Attempting to enter higher-end venues or dressy cocktail lounges in sports gear, scuffed trainers, or casual shorts; keep to a smart-casual dress code.'),
  ('liverpool', 3284, 9, 'Getting caught off-guard on matchdays—city-center bars and sports venues around Concert Square overflow early, so plan extra time or book ahead.'),
  ('liverpool', 3284, 10, 'Expecting a quiet night out anywhere near Concert Square on a Saturday evening; head to the Georgian Quarter or Baltic taprooms if you want a relaxed pint.'),
  ('liverpool', 3284, 11, '**Concert Square & Ropewalks:** The high-octane central heart of Liverpool’s nightlife, packed with outdoor terraces, student bars, dive spots, and late-night clubs (*Level*, *Heebie Jeebies*, *Modo*).'),
  ('liverpool', 3284, 12, '**Baltic Triangle & Cains Brewery:** The city''s converted industrial hub, ideal for craft breweries, retro arcade bars (*NQ64*), street food halls, and massive warehouse rave spaces (*24 Kitchen Street*, *Camp & Furnace*).'),
  ('liverpool', 3284, 13, '**Mathew Street (Cavern Quarter):** Iconic, bustling alleyways filled with historic pubs, live Beatles tribute acts, and classic pop/rock party bars.'),
  ('liverpool', 3284, 14, '**Pride Quarter (Stanley Street & Eberle Street):** A vibrant, inclusive district known for top-tier drag performances, fun pop bars, and multi-story late-night clubs.'),
  ('liverpool', 3292, 0, 'Treat Liverpool as just a quick 1-day Beatles or matchday excursion, missing out on its world-class maritime heritage, vibrant art galleries, and thriving food halls.'),
  ('liverpool', 3292, 1, 'Over-pack matchdays at Anfield or Goodison Park by trying to fit in heavy full-day museum tours right before kickoff, getting caught in massive transport bottlenecks across the city.'),
  ('liverpool', 3292, 2, 'Attempt to walk everywhere between districts during heavy Mersey sea breezes, underestimating wet weather spells and the distance up to elevated neighborhoods like the Knowledge Quarter.'),
  ('liverpool', 3292, 3, 'Rely strictly on hailing street taxis during peak weekend events or football matches instead of using pre-booked private transfers or the Merseyrail network.'),
  ('liverpool', 3292, 4, 'Fail to pre-book timed entry for major attractions like The Beatles Story, stadium tours, or Cavern Club entry, resulting in sold-out time slots and long queues.'),
  ('liverpool', 3293, 0, 'Distributes stadium tours and major Beatles heritage visits on non-matchdays to ensure relaxed pacing and seamless access.'),
  ('liverpool', 3293, 1, 'Leverages direct First Class rail connections into Liverpool Lime Street and arranges private executive transfers for effortless hotel check-ins along Castle Street or the Waterfront.'),
  ('liverpool', 3293, 2, 'Schedules morning cultural visits to the Royal Albert Dock museums paired with relaxed afternoon dining along Castle Street or the Baltic Market.'),
  ('liverpool', 3293, 3, 'Incorporates scenic coastal excursions, such as a trip out to Crosby Beach or the Formby Pinewoods, to offer clients a balanced contrast to the energetic city core.'),
  ('liverpool', 3293, 4, 'Secures VIP matchday hospitality packages well in advance to guarantee prime seating, private lounge access, and dedicated transport routing.'),
  ('liverpool', 3294, 0, 'For **Matchday Pacing**, clear all major itineraries at least 4 hours prior to match start times, reserving pre-game hours exclusively for stadium navigation and hospitality lounges.'),
  ('liverpool', 3294, 1, 'For **Transit & Urban Mobility**, utilize the efficient Merseyrail underground network for quick central jumps, and rely on pre-booked chauffeured vehicles during peak rainy weather or matchday departures.'),
  ('liverpool', 3294, 2, 'For **Excursion & Regional Balance**, dedicate at least 3 nights to Liverpool to combine waterfront heritage, music history, and regional dining before connecting onward to North Wales, Manchester, or London.'),
  ('liverpool', 3297, 0, 'Take an executive VIP stadium tour of Anfield to explore the home dressing room, walk under the famous "This Is Anfield" sign, and view the club''s European trophies.'),
  ('liverpool', 3297, 1, 'Stroll through the historic cobbled colonnades of the Royal Albert Dock and visit the Museum of Liverpool alongside the world''s premier Beatles Story museum.'),
  ('liverpool', 3297, 2, 'Make a musical pilgrimage to The Cavern Club on Mathew Street and catch live music where pop history was made.'),
  ('liverpool', 3297, 3, 'Experience cutting-edge gastronomy, artisan street food, and independent nightlife across the Baltic Triangle and food halls like Baltic Market.'),
  ('liverpool', 3297, 4, 'Take a scenic river cruise aboard the iconic Mersey Ferry to capture panoramic skyline views of the Three Graces at Pier Head.'),
  ('liverpool', 3297, 5, 'Treating Liverpool strictly as a 1-day Beatles or football transit stop, missing out on its grand Neoclassical architecture, rich maritime heritage, and dynamic culinary scene.'),
  ('liverpool', 3297, 6, 'Underestimating matchday crowd congestion around Anfield or Goodison Park by failing to pre-book private transport or allow ample transit buffer time.'),
  ('liverpool', 3297, 7, 'Skipping out on advance reservations for popular waterfront dining spots, rooftop lounges, or timed museum entries during peak weekend travel.'),
  ('liverpool', 3297, 8, 'Sticking strictly to the commercial shopping core and missing out on the indie culture, vintage shops, and local cafes along Bold Street.'),
  ('liverpool', 3298, 0, 'To be populated with authoritative tourism/transport/attraction sources before production use.'),
