  ('sydney', 3742, 0, 'Tap on and off with contactless cards or mobile wallets on public transit—taking advantage of Sydney''s daily and weekly fare capping system ($19.30 AUD weekday daily cap, $9.65 AUD weekend/holiday daily cap, and $50.00 AUD weekly cap).'),
  ('sydney', 3742, 1, 'Plan major regional travel, such as the train ride to Katoomba in the Blue Mountains or a scenic ferry ride to Manly, on weekends to utilize the discounted $9.65 AUD daily cap.'),
  ('sydney', 3742, 2, 'Book accommodations in inner-ring neighborhoods (such as Surry Hills, Haymarket, or Pyrmont) within short walking distance or direct light-rail/metro connection to Circular Quay, reducing ride-hailing expenses.'),
  ('sydney', 3742, 3, 'Dine at Asian food courts in Haymarket/Chinatown, local pub specials, or RSL clubs for generous, high-quality meals at a fraction of waterfront restaurant pricing.'),
  ('sydney', 3742, 4, 'Enjoy iconic views for free by walking across the Sydney Harbour Bridge pedestrian walkway, hiking the Bondi to Coogee Coastal Walk, or lounging at Mrs Macquarie''s Chair instead of paying for costly observation decks.'),
  ('sydney', 3742, 5, 'Skip the expensive direct Airport Link train surcharge ($17.92 AUD extra) by taking public Bus 420 from the airport terminal to Mascot Station before connecting to the regular train network.'),
  ('sydney', 3742, 6, 'Choosing distant accommodations in outer western suburbs without rapid train or metro access, resulting in excessive commute times that cut into limited sightseeing hours.'),
  ('sydney', 3742, 7, 'Renting a car for inner-city exploration, which incurs heavy traffic delays, high toll charges (such as the Sydney Harbour Bridge and Tunnel tolls), and exorbitant CBD parking fees.'),
  ('sydney', 3742, 8, 'Skipping the iconic F1 Manly Ferry ride from Circular Quay to cut costs, missing one of the world''s most scenic urban harbor commutes.'),
  ('sydney', 3742, 9, 'Relying exclusively on peak-period taxi hailing or rideshare surcharges across major event evenings instead of utilizing the 24-hour metro and late-night bus network.'),
  ('sydney', 3742, 10, 'Skipping premier regional highlights—such as a dedicated trip to the World Heritage Blue Mountains National Park or Taronga Zoo—solely due to tight daily transit budget limits.'),
  ('sydney', 3746, 0, 'AIRPORT LINK TRAIN (T8 LINE): Connects Sydney Airport directly to Central, Town Hall, Wynyard, and Circular Quay stations in under 20 minutes using contactless payment (credit/debit card or Opal).'),
  ('sydney', 3746, 1, 'CHEAPEST AIRPORT TRANSIT (BUS 420 + TRAIN ROUTE): To avoid the direct airport station access fee ($17.92 AUD surcharge), budget travelers take local Bus 420 from Terminal 1 or 3 to Mascot Station and transfer to the regular train or metro network for standard fares (~$4–$6 AUD total).'),
  ('sydney', 3746, 2, 'METRO & LIGHT RAIL CONNECTIONS: Sydney Metro M1 and Light Rail lines (L2/L3) connect Central Station to inner-city budget hubs, Haymarket, and Surry Hills.'),
  ('sydney', 3748, 0, '5+'),
  ('sydney', 3748, 1, '8+'),
  ('sydney', 3748, 2, 'TEENAGERS'),
  ('sydney', 3748, 3, 'Maximum 2 major attractions/sightseeing regions per day due to widespread city geography and walking terrain.'),
  ('sydney', 3748, 4, 'Balance outdoor coastal walks with indoor air-conditioned museums, aquariums, or transit breaks.'),
  ('sydney', 3748, 5, 'Avoid peak midday sun exposure (11:30 AM – 3:30 PM); schedule lunch, indoor aquariums, or hotel rest.'),
  ('sydney', 3748, 6, 'Plan downtime during ferry transit or intercity day trip travel.'),
  ('sydney', 3748, 7, 'Use public Opal ferries, light rail, or pre-booked private minivans.'),
  ('sydney', 3748, 8, 'Verify pram and stroller accessibility before visiting hilly or stepped sites like coastal walks or historic Rocks staircases.'),
