  ('langkawi', 4365, 0, 'Feast on **Fresh Charcoal-Grilled Seafood & Sambal**, including live tiger prawns (*udang galah*), squid, and banana leaf-wrapped stingray (*ikan pari bakar*) brushed with spicy sambal.'),
  ('langkawi', 4365, 1, 'Taste regional **Kedah-Style Gulai Ikan & Asam Pedas**, featuring red snapper or sea bass simmered in fragrant turmeric-coconut gravy or sour-spicy tamarind stew.'),
  ('langkawi', 4365, 2, 'Sample island-favorite **Nasi Tomato & Nasi Campur**, where fragrant tomato-infused or coconut rice is paired with beef rendang, spiced chicken, and sweet-sour pineapple curry (*pajeri nenas*).'),
  ('langkawi', 4365, 3, 'Slurp a bowl of **Laksa Kedah**, featuring thick rice noodles in a tangy, spiced, fish-based broth unique to northern Peninsular Malaysia.'),
  ('langkawi', 4365, 4, 'Snack on **Rotating Night Market Street Eats**, such as folded peanut-and-corn pancakes (*apam balik*), coconut rice treats (*dangai*), skewered satay, and savory stuffed *murtabak*.'),
  ('langkawi', 4365, 5, '**Families:** Casual beachfront seafood houses in Pantai Cenang and interactive night markets offering quick, varied street snacks for all ages.'),
  ('langkawi', 4365, 6, '**Honeymooners:** Romantic sunset dinner cruises, cliffside fine dining with ocean views, and private candlelit meals amidst lush paddy fields.'),
  ('langkawi', 4365, 7, '**Luxury travelers:** Refined multi-course Malay-Western fusion dinners and fresh catch dining at upscale resorts in Datai Bay and Tanjung Rhu.'),
  ('langkawi', 4365, 8, '**Budget travelers:** No-frills local *warungs*, Malay *nasi campur* lunch spots, and inexpensive night market food stalls across the island.'),
  ('langkawi', 4365, 9, '**Foodies:** Hunting down authentic island-exclusive dishes like *Laksa Kedah*, fresh grilled stingray, and traditional Malay home-cooked curries in local villages.'),
  ('langkawi', 4365, 10, '**Pantai Cenang & Pantai Tengah:** Best for lively beachfront dining, seafood display restaurants, international cafes, and bustling evening strip eats.'),
  ('langkawi', 4365, 11, '**Kuah Town:** Best for authentic local Malay eateries, affordable Chinese seafood spots, and historical island food markets.'),
  ('langkawi', 4365, 12, '**Padang Matsirat:** Best for local inland street food, traditional morning market stalls, and village-style Malay cooking near the airport.'),
  ('langkawi', 4365, 13, '**Tanjung Rhu & Datai Bay:** Best for tranquil seaside dining, fresh fish and chips, and high-end luxury resort culinary experiences.'),
  ('langkawi', 4365, 14, '**Langkawi Night Market (Daily Rotating Locations):** Best for affordable evening food tours across various locations like Temoyong, Kuah, and Padang Matsirat.'),
  ('langkawi', 4366, 0, '**Duty-Free Chocolates & Confectionery:** Massive selections of international chocolates (Toblerone, Ferrero Rocher, Lindt, Hershey''s) sold at significantly lower prices than mainland Malaysia.'),
  ('langkawi', 4366, 1, '**Duty-Free Spirits, Wines & Cigarettes:** Heavily discounted international liquor, fine wines, craft beers, and tobacco products under official tax-exempt allowances.'),
  ('langkawi', 4366, 2, '**Perfumes, Cosmetics & Designer Apparel:** Duty-free fragrance collections, skincare brands, luggage, sunglasses, and activewear available in major commercial shopping malls.'),
  ('langkawi', 4366, 3, '**Handmade Batik Textiles & Local Crafts:** Hand-dyed silk batik sarongs, wooden carvings, traditional woven bags, and regional crafts directly from local artisan workshops.'),
  ('langkawi', 4366, 4, '**Kitchenware & Crystal:** High-end imported tableware, cookware, porcelain, and crystal sets sold at tax-free commercial complexes in Kuah Town.'),
  ('langkawi', 4366, 5, '**Jetty Point Complex & Kuah Town Outlets:** The island''s primary hub for duty-free shopping, featuring major centers like Oriental Village, HIG (Haji Ismail Group Complex), and Teow Soon Huat Duty Free.'),
  ('langkawi', 4366, 6, '**Pantai Cenang Shopping Strip:** Ideal for casual resort wear, beach accessories, duty-free snack shops (such as Zon Duty Free), and evening market browsing right by the ocean.'),
  ('langkawi', 4366, 7, '**Atma Alam Batik Art Village:** Best for authentic, high-quality hand-painted Malaysian batik fabric, artwork, clothing, and cultural souvenirs crafted by local artisans.'),
  ('langkawi', 4366, 8, '**Langkawi Craft Complex (Kompleks Kraf Langkawi):** Located on the northern coast; excellent for viewing traditional Malaysian craft demonstrations and purchasing high-end heritage items.'),
  ('langkawi', 4366, 9, '**Langkawi Night Markets (Pasar Malam):** Perfect for picking up inexpensive accessories, summer clothes, beachwear, and street snacks at rotating daily locations across the island.'),
  ('langkawi', 4366, 10, 'Exceeding personal duty-free customs allowances when departing Langkawi for mainland Malaysia or international destinations, especially regarding alcohol and tobacco limits.'),
  ('langkawi', 4366, 11, 'Buying duty-free items without carrying your original passport and boarding pass/flight ticket, as official verification is required for tax-free clearance.'),
  ('langkawi', 4366, 12, 'Expecting high-end high-fashion designer boutiques (like Chanel or Gucci); shopping here focuses primarily on commercial duty-free goods, chocolates, spirits, cosmetics, and resort apparel.'),
  ('langkawi', 4366, 13, '**Duty-Free Bargain Hunters:** Travelers looking to stock up on imported chocolates, perfumes, liquor, and luggage at unmatched tax-free prices.'),
  ('langkawi', 4366, 14, '**Souvenir & Gift Buyers:** Visitors seeking batik clothing, local snacks, sea-salt products, and handcrafted island trinkets.'),
  ('langkawi', 4366, 15, '**Culture & Art Collectors:** Enthusiasts looking for authentic hand-dyed batik paintings, traditional textiles, and wood carvings.'),
  ('langkawi', 4366, 16, '**Resort & Beach Shoppers:** Vacationers needing stylish swimsuits, sun hats, flip-flops, and coastal accessories right along Pantai Cenang.'),
  ('langkawi', 4367, 0, '**Couples & honeymooners** seeking romantic sunset cocktails, candlelit oceanfront dining, and relaxed seaside lounges with soft background music.'),
  ('langkawi', 4367, 1, '**Solo travelers & backpackers** looking for lively beachfront bars, social hostel pub crawls, and interactive beach fire shows along Pantai Cenang.'),
  ('langkawi', 4367, 2, '**Families & foodies** wanting relaxed late-night seafood dining, duty-free shopping strolls, and vibrant local night markets.'),
  ('langkawi', 4367, 3, 'Unwinding with sunset cocktails and cold beers at beachfront bars along Pantai Cenang and Pantai Tengah as fire spinners perform along the shoreline.'),
  ('langkawi', 4367, 4, 'Taking advantage of Langkawi''s duty-free island status to enjoy significantly cheaper spirits, wines, and craft beers at oceanfront lounges and pubs.'),
  ('langkawi', 4367, 5, 'Hunting for late-night street food, grilled satay, fresh fruit juices, and local handicrafts at the daily rotating Langkawi Night Markets (Pasar Malam).'),
  ('langkawi', 4367, 6, 'Enjoying live acoustic sets, reggae bands, or sports broadcasts at casual pubs and beach lounges along the central coastal strips.'),
  ('langkawi', 4367, 7, 'Expecting multi-story mega-clubs, all-night mega-festivals, or intense electronic dance music venues; the vibe is strictly coastal, casual, and island-style.'),
  ('langkawi', 4367, 8, 'Driving along unlit rural roads or mountain passes late at night on rented scooters after consuming alcohol.'),
  ('langkawi', 4367, 9, 'Expecting late-night commercial activity or nightlife in quiet northern resort enclaves like Tanjung Rhu or Datai Bay, which wind down early.'),
  ('langkawi', 4367, 10, '**Pantai Cenang Main Strip & Beachfront:** Best for vibrant beach bars, live fire performances, casual sports pubs, duty-free snack shopping, and late-night dining.'),
  ('langkawi', 4367, 11, '**Pantai Tengah:** Best for chic, upscale sunset lounges, laid-back cocktail bars, and romantic seaside dining away from dense crowds.'),
  ('langkawi', 4367, 12, '**Telaga Harbour Boardwalk (Pantai Kok):** Best for quiet marina-side dining, Spanish tapas bars, and relaxed wine lounges overlooking yachts.'),
  ('langkawi', 4367, 13, '**Kuah Town Center:** Best for local Malay night market food stalls, late-night Indian *mamak* spots, and cheap duty-free beverage shops.'),
  ('langkawi', 4375, 0, 'Route clients to **Langkawi** without warning them about extreme seasonal weather shifts, booking open-air boat excursions during the peak monsoon season (September–October) when heavy swells can cancel tours.'),
  ('langkawi', 4375, 1, 'Assume public transport or train systems exist on the island, leaving clients stranded without arranging rental vehicles, scooters, or pre-booking ride-hailing services for late-night resort transfers.'),
  ('langkawi', 4375, 2, 'Book short 1- to 2-hour layovers for ferry transfers from Thailand (Koh Lipe) or mainland Malaysia, ignoring lengthy customs clearance queues at Kuah Jetty during peak travel periods.'),
  ('langkawi', 4375, 3, 'Expect quiet beach relaxation at Pantai Cenang for luxury or honeymoon clients, placing them in noisy nightlife zones instead of secluded northern sanctuaries like Datai Bay or Tanjung Rhu Beach.'),
  ('langkawi', 4375, 4, 'Advise clients to purchase duty-free goods right before airport check-in without checking official customs allowances or warning them about original passport verification requirements at tax-free counters.'),
  ('langkawi', 4376, 0, 'Secures **Express Lane tickets** for the Langkawi Skybridge Cable Car and schedules visits for 8:30 AM openings, ensuring clients avoid 2+ hour queues under the tropical sun.'),
  ('langkawi', 4376, 1, 'Arranges private or small-group motorboat charters for Kilim Geoforest Park mangrove tours departing from less-crowded jetties to ensure intimate wildlife viewing before main tour barges arrive.'),
  ('langkawi', 4376, 2, 'Pairs morning water sports or high-energy island hopping with air-conditioned afternoon spa treatments or resort lounging, matching outdoor activities to clear morning weather windows before peak afternoon heat.'),
  ('langkawi', 4376, 3, 'Curates accommodation strictly by persona—placing high-net-worth travelers and honeymooners in ultra-private enclaves like The Datai Langkawi or Four Seasons Resort Langkawi, families near calm swimming bays, and budget travelers along walkable Cenang.'),
  ('langkawi', 4376, 4, 'Coordinates luxury sunset catamaran cruises with reputable operators that provide licensed crew, guaranteed safety equipment, and proper hotel transfers.'),
  ('langkawi', 4377, 0, 'For **Island Mobility & Logistics**, pre-arrange rental cars for families or confirm Grab availability in advance, avoiding unaccredited roadside vehicle hires that lack proper insurance coverage.'),
  ('langkawi', 4377, 1, 'For **Attraction & Tour Timing**, enforce early-morning starts (8:30 AM–11:00 AM) for cable cars, mangrove tours, and island-hopping trips to maximize clear weather, beat crowd surges, and avoid extreme midday heat.'),
  ('langkawi', 4377, 2, 'For **Duty-Free & Departure**, advise clients to complete duty-free purchases in Kuah Town or Cenang at least 24 hours before departure, ensuring all items comply with export limits and customs verification rules.'),
  ('langkawi', 4380, 0, 'Ride the steep Langkawi Skybridge Cable Car up Gunung Machinchang and walk across the spectacular curved Langkawi Sky Bridge for panoramic archipelago views.'),
  ('langkawi', 4380, 1, 'Take an early-morning private boat or kayak tour through Kilim Geoforest Park to explore ancient limestone karst formations, bat caves, and mangrove rivers.'),
  ('langkawi', 4380, 2, 'Enjoy an island-hopping boat trip to Pulau Dayang Bunting to swim in the legendary freshwater Lake of the Pregnant Maiden.'),
  ('langkawi', 4380, 3, 'Set sail on an evening sunset dinner catamaran cruise across the Andaman Sea, featuring a saltwater jacuzzi net and free-flowing drinks.'),
  ('langkawi', 4380, 4, 'Capture photos at the iconic 12-meter eagle sculpture at Dataran Lang (Eagle Square) overlooking the Kuah harbor.'),
  ('langkawi', 4380, 5, 'Stock up on tax-free chocolates, perfumes, and kitchenware at major duty-free complexes in Kuah Town or Pantai Cenang.'),
  ('langkawi', 4380, 6, 'Graze through the rotating local night market (Pasar Malam) to sample *ikan bakar* (sambal grilled fish), *nasi tomato*, and fresh *apam balik* pancakes.'),
  ('langkawi', 4380, 7, 'Booking open-water boat tours during peak monsoon months (September–October) due to rough ocean swells and unpredictable tropical downpours.'),
  ('langkawi', 4380, 8, 'Staying along the central Pantai Cenang main strip if you are seeking a quiet, secluded, or high-end romantic honeymoon environment.'),
  ('langkawi', 4380, 9, 'Arriving at major high-volume attractions like the SkyCab after 10:30 AM without Express Lane passes, as general queues can exceed 2 hours during peak travel periods.'),
  ('langkawi', 4380, 10, 'Purchasing high-value duty-free goods right before your flight without bringing your original passport or checking international customs allowance limits.'),
  ('langkawi', 4380, 11, 'Renting unaccredited roadside vehicles or scooters without verifying proper insurance coverages and local driver''s license requirements.'),
  ('langkawi', 4380, 12, 'Relying on public buses or train networks, as no public rail or scheduled transit routes exist across the island.'),
  ('langkawi', 4381, 0, 'To be populated with authoritative tourism/transport/attraction sources before production use.'),
  ('batu-cave', 4385, 0, 'Take the KTM Komuter train directly from KL Sentral to Batu Caves station for the cheapest, most efficient transit option (MYR 2.60 each way), dropping you off directly at the temple complex entrance.'),
  ('batu-cave', 4385, 1, 'Prioritize visiting the main Cathedral Cave (Temple Cave), which is 100% free to enter, avoiding unnecessary tour guide add-ons or organized day trips if you are comfortable navigating basic public transit.'),
  ('batu-cave', 4385, 2, 'Dine at the authentic South Indian *mamak* stalls and banana leaf restaurants surrounding the base of the complex for affordable, filling meals (MYR 8–MYR 15 per person) featuring *dosas*, *thalis*, and fresh coconut water.'),
  ('batu-cave', 4385, 3, 'Bring your own modest clothing (sarong or pants covering knees, and shirts covering shoulders) to avoid paying mandatory sarong rental fees (MYR 5–MYR 10) enforced at the base of the steps.'),
  ('batu-cave', 4385, 4, 'Purchase small temple offerings, fresh flower garlands, or souvenirs from ground-level market stalls where prices are negotiable, rather than high-priced tourist shops inside transit stations.'),
  ('batu-cave', 4385, 5, 'Purchasing cheap food or drinks to consume on the 272 steps while holding them in plastic bags, which aggressively attracts wild macaques and risks bites, scratches, or stolen personal belongings.'),
  ('batu-cave', 4385, 6, 'Skipping the small entry fee (MYR 5–MYR 15) for the Ramayana Cave near the giant green Hanuman statue if you want a quiet, less-crowded experience with colorful mythological light displays.'),
  ('batu-cave', 4385, 7, 'Relying strictly on public transit if traveling with elderly family members or young children; opting for a direct Grab or private car (MYR 25–MYR 40 each way) saves considerable energy and heat stress.'),
  ('batu-cave', 4385, 8, 'Buying cheap, unsealed bottled water from unlicensed vendors in the scorching sun; opt for sealed cold drinks from established shops to ensure safety and hygiene.'),
  ('batu-cave', 4386, 0, '4+'),
  ('batu-cave', 4386, 1, '6+'),
  ('batu-cave', 4386, 2, '8+'),
  ('batu-cave', 4386, 3, 'Teenagers'),
  ('batu-cave', 4386, 4, 'Leave strollers behind and opt for an ergonomic baby carrier instead; while the base plaza is paved, the 272 steep, narrow concrete steps to the main Cathedral Cave are completely impossible to navigate with a stroller.');
INSERT INTO destination_guidance_bullet (place_id, position, bullet_index, text) VALUES
  ('batu-cave', 4386, 5, 'Keep all snacks, food containers, juice boxes, and plastic bags completely hidden inside securely zipped backpacks; the resident long-tailed macaques on the staircase aggressively target visible food or plastic bags held by children.'),
  ('batu-cave', 4386, 6, 'Arrive early in the morning (between 7:30 AM and 8:30 AM) to tackle the heavy staircase climb before the intense tropical mid-day heat sets in and before large tour bus crowds congestion the steps.'),
  ('batu-cave', 4386, 7, 'Ensure parents and older children are wearing modest clothing covering knees and shoulders (or bring light swaddles/sarongs) to adhere to active Hindu temple dress codes and avoid mandatory sarong rental hassles at the base.'),
  ('batu-cave', 4386, 8, 'Keep toddlers and young children on the inner side of the staircase handrails, holding hands firmly at all times, as the steps are steep, high, and narrow with constant foot traffic.'),
  ('batu-cave', 4386, 9, 'Ensure everyone uses the public restrooms located at the base plaza before beginning the ascent, as there are no active toilet facilities inside the upper Cathedral Cave.'),
  ('batu-cave', 4387, 0, 'honeymoon_score: 62'),
  ('batu-cave', 4387, 1, 'romance_score: 60'),
  ('batu-cave', 4387, 2, 'privacy_score: 35'),
  ('batu-cave', 4387, 3, 'luxury_score: 45'),
  ('batu-cave', 4389, 0, 'Tackling sport rock climbing on natural limestone crags at **Gua Damai Extreme Park**, featuring over 120 bolted routes catering to beginner (Grade 5) and advanced (Grade 7) climbers.'),
  ('batu-cave', 4389, 1, 'Conquering the rapid, cardio-intensive ascent of the **272 colorful concrete steps** while navigating steep inclines and tropical heat.'),
  ('batu-cave', 4389, 2, 'Embarking on guided abseiling and zip-lining sessions down the vertical limestone cliff faces on the backside of the mountain massif.'),
  ('batu-cave', 4389, 3, 'Participating in specialized eco-caving and spelunking tours through the **Dark Cave** network to observe endemic trapdoor spiders, cave fruit bats, and ancient stalactite formations.'),
  ('batu-cave', 4389, 4, 'Trail hiking and nature trekking along the rugged karst slopes and jungle fringes of the neighboring Selangor State Park.'),
  ('batu-cave', 4389, 5, '**Gua Damai Extreme Park (Damai Wall)** — best for rock climbing, abseiling, multi-pitch training, and eco-adventure activities on the northern face of the hill.'),
  ('batu-cave', 4389, 6, '**Cathedral Cave Staircase** — best for stair-climbing workouts, high-incline cardio, and urban adventure photography.'),
  ('batu-cave', 4389, 7, '**Dark Cave Complex** — best for subterranean spelunking, bat colony tracking, and cave ecology tours.'),
  ('batu-cave', 4389, 8, '**Selayang Karst Fringes & Hot Springs** — best for post-climb muscle recovery, jungle trail walks, and natural thermal soak pools nearby.'),
  ('batu-cave', 4389, 9, 'Rock climbers, sport crag enthusiasts, and bouldering practitioners.'),
  ('batu-cave', 4389, 10, 'Spelunkers, cavern explorers, and cave ecology enthusiasts.'),
  ('batu-cave', 4389, 11, 'Fitness enthusiasts, stair-climbers, and urban trail runners.'),
  ('batu-cave', 4389, 12, 'Outdoor thrill-seekers, zip-liners, and abseilers.'),
  ('batu-cave', 4389, 13, 'Active day-trippers seeking high-energy outdoor activities close to Kuala Lumpur.'),
  ('batu-cave', 4390, 0, 'Arrive early in the morning (7:30 AM–9:00 AM) to avoid the intense midday sun, high humidity, and heavy tour bus crowds on the main plaza and walkways.'),
  ('batu-cave', 4390, 1, 'Use direct door-to-door transport via a private chauffeured car or ride-hailing app (Grab) to drop off near the main entrance plaza, eliminating long walks from outer parking areas or transit stops.'),
  ('batu-cave', 4390, 2, 'Assess physical capability before attempting the 272-step climb; the concrete steps are high, uneven in sections, and lack mid-way resting platforms or shaded coverage.'),
  ('batu-cave', 4390, 3, 'Keep all personal belongings, eyeglasses, hat brim accessories, and bags securely zipped and held close to deter macaque monkeys from snatching items along the lower plaza and staircase.'),
  ('batu-cave', 4390, 4, 'Wear comfortable, non-slip supportive walking shoes with good traction, as smooth stone and concrete paths can become slippery if wet.'),
  ('batu-cave', 4390, 5, 'Plan for accessible ground-level rest breaks at shaded South Indian cafes around the main plaza, enjoying fresh coconut water or tea to stay hydrated.'),
  ('batu-cave', 4390, 6, 'Bring pre-arranged modest attire (lightweight long pants or mid-calf skirts and covered shoulders) to stay cool while adhering to temple dress codes without needing step-side sarong rentals.'),
  ('batu-cave', 4390, 7, 'Exploring the ground-level **Ramayana Cave**, which features flat footpaths, colorful illuminated dioramas, and stalactites without requiring a steep climb (low admission fee).'),
  ('batu-cave', 4390, 8, 'Marveling at the colossal 42.7-meter golden Lord Murugan statue and capturing photos from the spacious, level plaza ground base.'),
  ('batu-cave', 4390, 9, 'Visiting the lower **Sri Venkatachalapathi Temple** and ground-level shrines to observe authentic Hindu morning devotions in a comfortable, step-free setting.'),
  ('batu-cave', 4390, 10, 'Taking a leisurely stroll through the shaded garden paths, koi ponds, and flat pathways around the **Cave Villa** grounds at the foot of the limestone cliff.'),
  ('batu-cave', 4390, 11, 'Relaxed South Indian vegetarian dining at ground-level *mamak* and banana leaf restaurants surrounding the complex.'),
  ('batu-cave', 4390, 12, 'Attempting to climb the 272 steps if dealing with heart conditions, knee/joint pain, severe asthma, or mobility limitations.'),
  ('batu-cave', 4390, 13, 'Visiting during the peak annual **Thaipusam festival** (late January/February) unless explicitly seeking intense crowd experiences, as extreme congestion makes walking and navigation difficult.'),
  ('batu-cave', 4390, 14, 'Carrying visible food items, plastic shopping bags, or open drink containers near the staircase and cliff base due to monkey activity.'),
  ('batu-cave', 4390, 15, 'Visiting during mid-afternoon peak heat hours (12:00 PM–3:00 PM) when humidity is highest and direct sun covers the staircase.'),
  ('batu-cave', 4390, 16, 'Relying on public commuter trains if traveling with mobility aids, as connecting transfers and platform navigation can add extra physical fatigue compared to direct door-to-door taxis.'),
  ('batu-cave', 4392, 0, 'Savor an authentic **South Indian Banana Leaf Rice Thali**, featuring steamed rice served on a fresh banana leaf with an array of vegetable curries, *rasam*, *sambar*, papadums, and spicy mango pickles.'),
  ('batu-cave', 4392, 1, 'Indulge in crisp, freshly made **Dosas & Uttapams**, paired with freshly ground coconut chutney, tomato chutney, and lentil-based vegetable stew.'),
  ('batu-cave', 4392, 2, 'Snack on warm ground-level **Indian Street Savories**, such as freshly fried *medu vada* (savory lentil donuts), vegetable samosas, and piping-hot *poori bhaji*.'),
  ('batu-cave', 4392, 3, 'Cool down after climbing the steps with **Chilled Fresh Coconuts & Sugarcane Juice**, hacked open to order at ground-level refreshment kiosks.'),
  ('batu-cave', 4392, 4, 'Slurp a plate of **Sang Har Wat Tan Hor** (Giant River Prawn Egg-Drop Noodles) or **Curry Laksa** at legendary non-vegetarian eateries located just minutes away in the surrounding Batu Caves township.'),
  ('batu-cave', 4392, 5, '**Families:** Casual ground-level vegetarian restaurants offering mild, accessible dishes like *ghee dosa*, sweet lassi, and fresh coconut water.'),
  ('batu-cave', 4392, 6, '**Honeymooners:** Scenic post-climb breakfasts at authentic banana leaf cafes before heading to central Kuala Lumpur for high-end dining.'),
  ('batu-cave', 4392, 7, '**Luxury travelers:** Experiencing authentic South Indian cultural dining at ground level as a brief culinary stop before returning to 5-star fine dining in KLCC.'),
  ('batu-cave', 4392, 8, '**Budget travelers:** Ultra-affordable *mamak* stalls and vegetarian eateries where full, filling meals cost under MYR 10–15 per person.'),
  ('batu-cave', 4392, 9, '**Foodies:** Sampling authentic South Indian Tamil breakfast items at the base plaza, then heading nearby to try famous Chinese river prawn noodles (*Sang Har Hor Fun*) in Medan Batu Caves.'),
  ('batu-cave', 4392, 10, '**Temple Base Concourse (Ground Plaza):** Best for 100% vegetarian Indian dining, fresh banana leaf thalis, dosas, and quick coconut water stands right at the foot of the rainbow stairs.'),
  ('batu-cave', 4392, 11, '**KTM Station Promenade:** Best for quick street-food snacks, fried samosas, sweet Indian sweets (*laddu*, *jalebi*), and grab-and-go beverages.'),
  ('batu-cave', 4392, 12, '**Medan Batu Caves Commercial Center:** Best for famous local Chinese noodle shops (such as Restoran Pan Heong) serving Cantonese egg-drop prawn noodles and century egg porridge.'),
  ('batu-cave', 4392, 13, '**Taman Sri Gombak (1–2 km away):** Best for local Malay *nasi campur*, Thai seafood eateries, and regional Malaysian curry laksa joints.'),
  ('batu-cave', 4393, 0, '**Hindu Religious Artifacts & Brassware:** Detailed brass statues of Lord Murugan, Ganesh, and Lakshmi, alongside traditional oil lamps (*kuthuvilakku*), incense burners, and prayer altars.'),
  ('batu-cave', 4393, 1, '**Fresh Flower Garlands & Offering Supplies:** Vibrant, freshly woven marigold, jasmine, and rose garlands, alongside camphor, coconuts, and prayer powders (*kumkum* and *vibhuti*).'),
  ('batu-cave', 4393, 2, '**Indian Traditional Wear & Textiles:** Colorful saris, *dhoti* cloths, embroidered scarves, bangles, and lightweight cotton tunics sold at ground-level market stalls.'),
  ('batu-cave', 4393, 3, '**Traditional Indian Sweets & Snacks:** Freshly packed boxes of Tamil delicacies like *laddu*, *jalebi*, *murukku*, and sweet *mysore pak*.'),
  ('batu-cave', 4393, 4, '**Batu Caves Souvenirs & Photography Gifts:** Rainbow-stair mini replicas, fridge magnets, keychains, printed graphic t-shirts, and Postcards depicting the golden Lord Murugan statue.'),
  ('batu-cave', 4393, 5, '**Ground Plaza Bazaar:** Best for browsing dozens of open-air stalls selling flower garlands, religious art, brass items, and colorful festival souvenirs right in front of the limestone cliff.'),
  ('batu-cave', 4393, 6, '**KTM Batu Caves Station Concourse:** Ideal for quick-grab items, small souvenir keychains, bottled cold drinks, and packaged snacks before boarding the train back to central Kuala Lumpur.'),
  ('batu-cave', 4393, 7, '**Little India (Brikfields, Central KL):** Prefer heading to Brickfields in downtown KL if looking for higher-quality Indian gold jewelry, tailor-made traditional attire, and extensive spice shops, using Batu Caves primarily for site-specific souvenirs.'),
  ('batu-cave', 4393, 8, '**Royal Selangor Visitor Centre (15 mins away):** Prefer pairing your trip with a visit to nearby Royal Selangor for high-end Malaysian pewter crafts, custom tableware, and luxury souvenirs.'),
  ('batu-cave', 4393, 9, 'Buying heavy, fragile brassware or delicate framed artwork right before climbing the 272 steps; purchase all heavy items *after* coming down to avoid carrying unnecessary weight up the stairs.'),
  ('batu-cave', 4393, 10, 'Leaving purchased food items or edible souvenirs in open plastic bags while shopping near the staircase base, as resident macaque monkeys will aggressively try to snatch them.'),
  ('batu-cave', 4393, 11, 'Expecting high-end air-conditioned shopping malls or fixed-price department stores; most shops at the base are open-air bazaar stalls where modest, polite price negotiation is acceptable for non-edible goods.'),
  ('batu-cave', 4393, 12, '**Cultural & Religious Seekers:** Devotees and visitors looking for authentic Hindu ritual offerings, brass deity figures, and sacred items.'),
  ('batu-cave', 4393, 13, '**Souvenir Collectors:** Travelers wanting site-specific mementos like rainbow-stair miniatures, magnet keepsakes, and photo prints of the giant Murugan statue.'),
  ('batu-cave', 4393, 14, '**Budget Shoppers:** Visitors looking for low-cost accessories, traditional bangles, incense sticks, and inexpensive cotton scarves.'),
  ('batu-cave', 4393, 15, '**Food & Sweet Lovers:** Travelers eager to sample and purchase authentic packed Tamil sweets, savory *murukku* snacks, and fresh coconut products.'),
  ('batu-cave', 4394, 0, '**Culture enthusiasts & photographers** seeking dramatic night views of the lit-up 42.7-meter golden Lord Murugan statue and illuminated rainbow stairs without daytime heat.'),
  ('batu-cave', 4394, 1, '**Foodies & budget travelers** looking for late-night *mamak* food culture, hot *teh tarik*, crisp *dosas*, and authentic street snacks around the ground plaza.'),
  ('batu-cave', 4394, 2, '**Night owls basing in Central KL** who prefer taking a brief evening photo stop before heading into central Kuala Lumpur’s vibrant bar and nightlife districts.'),
  ('batu-cave', 4394, 3, 'Visiting the ground plaza during early evening hours (6:30 PM–8:00 PM) to watch the sunset against the limestone karst, observe evening temple *pooja* (prayer) rituals, and photograph the illuminated golden statue.'),
  ('batu-cave', 4394, 4, 'Experiencing authentic 24-hour South Indian *mamak* dining culture at the ground-level eateries surrounding the station and plaza, sampling hot *roti canai*, *murtabak*, and fresh tea late into the night.'),
  ('batu-cave', 4394, 5, 'Heading south into Central Kuala Lumpur (Bukit Bintang, Changkat, or KLCC) via Grab or taxi for high-energy cocktail lounges, rooftop bars, and live music venues.'),
  ('batu-cave', 4394, 6, 'Checking the local calendar for special religious occasions, such as the annual **Thaipusam festival** (late January/February), during which the entire Batu Caves complex transforms into a massive, 24-hour festival area filled with millions of lights, midnight processions, and overnight food bazaars.'),
  ('batu-cave', 4394, 7, 'Expecting night clubs, beach-style bars, alcohol-serving lounges, or high-decibel music venues inside or directly around the temple grounds.'),
  ('batu-cave', 4394, 8, 'Attempting to climb the main 272 steps deep into the night after the main Cathedral Cave gates lock and inner lights are turned off (around 8:30 PM).'),
  ('batu-cave', 4394, 9, 'Wandering around unlit areas, rear limestone rock faces, or quiet transit edges late at night, as lighting is concentrated mainly on the central plaza base.'),
  ('batu-cave', 4394, 10, '**Batu Caves Main Plaza Base:** Best for early evening photography of the illuminated golden Lord Murugan statue, evening prayer atmosphere, and peaceful plaza walks.'),
  ('batu-cave', 4394, 11, '**Medan Batu Caves & Gombak Commercial Strips:** Best for late-night local dining at 24-hour Indian *mamak* restaurants, Malay burger stalls, and casual juice shops.'),
  ('batu-cave', 4394, 12, '**Changkat Bukit Bintang (Central KL, 20 mins away):** Best for high-energy nightlife, international pubs, cocktail lounges, and dance clubs.'),
  ('batu-cave', 4394, 13, '**KLCC & Petronas Towers Area (Central KL, 25 mins away):** Best for sophisticated rooftop cocktail bars (such as Marini''s on 57 or SkyBar) offering views over the illuminated city skyline.'),
  ('batu-cave', 4402, 0, 'Route clients to **Batu Caves** during the mid-afternoon peak hours (11:00 AM–3:00 PM), exposing them to scorching tropical heat, intense humidity, and massive crowds on the unshaded 272-step climb.'),
  ('batu-cave', 4402, 1, 'Schedule client visits during or immediately surrounding the annual **Thaipusam Festival** (January/February) without explicit warning, subjecting regular sightseers to extreme crowd congestion, road closures, and restricted temple access.'),
  ('batu-cave', 4402, 2, 'Fail to brief female clients on the strict **modesty dress code** (covered knees and shoulders), leaving them forced to buy overpriced cover-ups or get turned away at the base of the staircase.'),
  ('batu-cave', 4402, 3, 'Advise clients to carry open food, sweet drinks, or loose plastic bags while climbing, making them target practice for the aggressive long-tailed macaque monkeys along the stairs.'),
  ('batu-cave', 4402, 4, 'Allocate only 30 to 45 minutes for the entire site, underestimating the time required to climb the steps, navigate crowds, explore the massive inner Cathedral Cave, and visit ground-level sites like Ramayana Cave.'),
  ('batu-cave', 4403, 0, 'Schedules visits for sharp **7:30 AM to 8:30 AM arrivals**, allowing clients to climb in cool morning temperatures, capture clear photos without crowd clutter, and observe peaceful morning Hindu prayer rituals (*pooja*).'),
  ('batu-cave', 4403, 1, 'Pairs a Batu Caves morning excursion with nearby complementary experiences—such as the **Gua Damai Extreme Park** for adventure seekers or a trip to **Kuala Selangor** for evening firefly watching—maximizing the day''s travel logistics.'),
  ('batu-cave', 4403, 2, 'Pre-books comfortable private transfers or advises clients to take the **KTM Komuter train directly from KL Sentral to Batu Caves station**, avoiding unpredictable peak-hour highway traffic out of central Kuala Lumpur.'),
  ('batu-cave', 4403, 3, 'Guides clients to explore the often-overlooked **Ramayana Cave** at the base of the limestone hill, ensuring they buy tickets for its immersive lighting and epic statues rather than focusing only on the main staircase.'),
  ('batu-cave', 4403, 4, 'Directs clients to authentic South Indian vegetarian eateries around the plaza for genuine **banana leaf rice** and freshly brewed *masala chai*, elevating a standard sightseeing trip into a cultural culinary stop.'),
  ('batu-cave', 4404, 0, 'For **Attraction & Step Timing**, enforce an early morning arrival (before 8:30 AM) to beat both the extreme midday heat and tour bus surges, ensuring a safer and far more comfortable 272-step ascent.'),
  ('batu-cave', 4404, 1, 'For **Dress Code & Cultural Respect**, instruct all travelers (especially women) to wear clothing covering knees and shoulders, or pack a sarong in their daypack to pass gate checks seamlessly.'),
  ('batu-cave', 4404, 2, 'For **Safety & Wildlife Awareness**, advise clients to secure all personal belongings (sunglasses, phones, snacks) inside zipped backpacks before reaching the steps to avoid aggressive interactions with local macaques.'),
  ('batu-cave', 4407, 0, 'Ascend the iconic 272 colorful rainbow steps while taking in views of the 42.7-meter golden Lord Murugan statue.'),
  ('batu-cave', 4407, 1, 'Explore the lofty ceilings, natural rock formations, and Hindu shrines inside Cathedral Cave (Temple Cave).'),
  ('batu-cave', 4407, 2, 'Visit Ramayana Cave at the base to view colorful dioramas depicting ancient Indian epics.'),
  ('batu-cave', 4407, 3, 'Enjoy a South Indian vegetarian meal (*dosa* or banana leaf rice) with hot *masala chai* at base plaza eateries.'),
  ('batu-cave', 4407, 4, 'Book a rock-climbing session at Gua Damai Extreme Park on the backside of the limestone massif.'),
  ('batu-cave', 4407, 5, 'Visiting between 11:00 AM and 3:00 PM to avoid extreme heat, unshaded stair climbing, and tour bus crowds.'),
  ('batu-cave', 4407, 6, 'Wearing short skirts, short shorts, or sleeveless tops—strict modesty rules require covered knees and shoulders.'),
  ('batu-cave', 4407, 7, 'Carrying open food, sweet drinks, or plastic bags that attract aggressive long-tailed macaque monkeys.'),
  ('batu-cave', 4407, 8, 'Spending money on uncredited tour guides at the entrance; entering the main Cathedral Cave is free.'),
  ('batu-cave', 4408, 0, 'To be populated with authoritative tourism/transport/attraction sources before production use.'),
  ('penang', 4412, 0, 'Utilize the cheap and efficient CAT (Central Area Transit) free shuttle bus service within George Town to navigate major heritage landmarks, or use the Rapid Penang bus network for low-cost routes across the island.'),
  ('penang', 4412, 1, 'Focus your dining on famous hawker centers like Gurney Drive, Chulia Street, and Presgrave Street, where world-class local dishes like Char Kway Teow, Asam Laksa, and Hokkien Mee cost just MYR 6 to MYR 12 ($1.30–$2.80 USD) per plate.'),
  ('penang', 4412, 2, 'Take advantage of Penang''s abundance of free cultural sights, including self-guided street art mural hunting in George Town, visiting the Clan Jetties, and walking around historical sites like Fort Cornwallis'' exterior grounds.'),
  ('penang', 4412, 3, 'Book heritage guesthouses or boutique hostels within the core UNESCO zone of George Town to keep accommodation costs down while remaining within easy walking distance of major attractions and street food hubs.'),
  ('penang', 4412, 4, 'Rent a bicycle or motor scooter for MYR 15 to MYR 40 per day if exploring outside the immediate walking zone to save on multiple short ride-hailing fares.'),
  ('penang', 4412, 5, 'Skipping the Express Lane or standard ticket for the Penang Hill Funicular Railway to hike up in extreme heat and humidity, which can lead to severe heat exhaustion for unprepared travelers.'),
  ('penang', 4412, 6, 'Choosing extremely low-budget accommodation lacking air conditioning; Penang’s tropical humidity makes AC essential for adequate rest and recovery after long walking days.'),
  ('penang', 4412, 7, 'Passing on authentic Peranakan (Nyonya) dining experiences at established heritage restaurants like Kebaya or Auntie Gaik Lean''s to strictly eat hawker food, as Nyonya cuisine represents a crucial, unique cultural highlight of the island.'),
  ('penang', 4412, 8, 'Skimping on accredited local guides when visiting intricate clan houses like Khoo Kongsi or Cheong Fatt Tze Mansion (The Blue Mansion), where deep historical context transforms the experience from a simple photo stop into a meaningful journey.'),
  ('penang', 4413, 0, '2+'),
  ('penang', 4413, 1, '4+'),
  ('penang', 4413, 2, '6+'),
  ('penang', 4413, 3, '8+'),
  ('penang', 4413, 4, 'Teenagers'),
  ('penang', 4413, 5, 'Bring an all-terrain stroller or an ergonomic baby carrier depending on your plans; while George Town''s narrow, broken, and high-kerbed historic shophouse sidewalks are difficult for strollers, modern spaces like Gurney Bay, Entopia, and beach resorts are highly stroller-accessible.'),
  ('penang', 4413, 6, 'Book Penang Hill Funicular Railway Express Fast-Track passes online in advance to avoid long, exhausting wait times in high heat and humidity with impatient young children.'),
  ('penang', 4413, 7, 'Pack lightweight, breathable clothing, sun hats, water bottles, and child-safe mosquito repellent, as tropical humidity and sudden afternoon sun can drain kids'' energy during outdoor heritage walks.'),
  ('penang', 4413, 8, 'Start outdoor activities early in the morning (between 8:00 AM and 10:30 AM) to complete street art hunts or temple visits before peak mid-day heat, reserving hot afternoons for air-conditioned indoor destinations like Entopia, Wonderfood Museum, or hotel pool breaks.'),
  ('penang', 4413, 9, 'Exercise close supervision around wildlife; keep kids at a safe distance from wild macaques at Penang Hill, Penang Botanical Gardens, and Penang National Park, keeping food and snacks packed away out of sight.'),
  ('penang', 4413, 10, 'Introduce street food gradually at clean, well-established open-air hawker centers (such as Gurney Drive or Long Beach Cafe), ordering mild dishes like Hainanese chicken rice or satay first before introducing spicier options.'),
  ('penang', 4414, 0, 'honeymoon_score: 82'),
  ('penang', 4414, 1, 'romance_score: 85'),
  ('penang', 4414, 2, 'privacy_score: 75'),
  ('penang', 4414, 3, 'luxury_score: 88'),
  ('penang', 4416, 0, 'Tackling high-adrenaline obstacle rope courses, zip-lining, and riding the world''s longest tube water slide at ESCAPE Penang.'),
  ('penang', 4416, 1, 'Trekking through dense jungle trails to reach secluded coastal spots like Pantai Keracut to view its seasonal meromictic lake and turtle conservation sanctuary.'),
  ('penang', 4416, 2, 'Walking among ancient rainforest canopies via the Curtis Crest Treetop Walk and zip-lining over virgin jungle at The Habitat Penang Hill.'),
  ('penang', 4416, 3, 'Enduring the grueling cardio hike up the steep Heritage Trail from the foot of Air Itam all the way to the summit of Penang Hill.'),
  ('penang', 4416, 4, 'Engaging in high-speed water sports, including parasailing, jet skiing, and sea kayaking along the northern coast of Batu Ferringhi.'),
  ('penang', 4416, 5, '**Teluk Bahang & ESCAPE Park** — best for extreme adventure sports, high rope obstacle courses, zip-lining, and water park thrill rides.'),
  ('penang', 4416, 6, '**Penang National Park (Teluk Bahang Entry)** — best for jungle trail trekking, coastal wildlife spotting, forest canopy walks, and remote beach hiking.'),
  ('penang', 4416, 7, '**Penang Hill Highlands & The Habitat** — best for canopy treetop walks, rainforest zip-line eco-tours, and high-altitude mountain hikes.'),
  ('penang', 4416, 8, '**Batu Ferringhi Coastline** — best for motorized and non-motorized water sports, parasailing, and ocean kayaking.'),
  ('penang', 4416, 9, 'Thrill-seekers, zip-liners, and obstacle park enthusiasts.'),
  ('penang', 4416, 10, 'Rainforest trekkers, jungle hikers, and eco-explorers.'),
  ('penang', 4416, 11, 'Water sports enthusiasts and coastal kayakers.'),
  ('penang', 4416, 12, 'Trail runners and high-incline endurance walkers.'),
  ('penang', 4416, 13, 'Active families and adventure-minded solo travelers."'),
  ('penang', 4417, 0, 'Schedule outdoor walks and street art tours during early morning hours (8:00 AM–10:00 AM) or late afternoons to avoid peak mid-day heat and high tropical humidity.'),
  ('penang', 4417, 1, 'Use direct door-to-door transit via ride-hailing apps (Grab) or private chauffeured transfers to drop off directly at attraction gates, minimizing long walks across exposed pavements.'),
  ('penang', 4417, 2, 'Purchase Express Fast-Track tickets for the Penang Hill Funicular Train Station to bypass long standing queues at the lower station base.'),
  ('penang', 4417, 3, 'Wear comfortable, non-slip supportive walking shoes with extra cushioning to comfortably navigate uneven shophouse kerbs and historic cobblestone alleys.'),
  ('penang', 4417, 4, 'Stay hydrated by stopping frequently at shaded traditional coffee shops (*kopitiams*) or air-conditioned cafes for cold beverages and local snacks.'),
  ('penang', 4417, 5, 'Exercise caution when walking along narrow shophouse corridors in George Town, taking care with step height variations and motor scooter traffic on narrow streets.'),
  ('penang', 4417, 6, 'Plan afternoon rest breaks at hotel amenities, spas, or cool indoor spaces like Gurney Plaza or the Pinang Peranakan Mansion.'),
  ('penang', 4417, 7, 'Exploring historic George Town via traditional pedal-powered trishaw tours for a relaxed, step-free perspective of shophouse architecture and street art.'),
  ('penang', 4417, 8, 'Riding the comfortable Penang Hill Funicular Train Station up to the summit to enjoy sweeping island vistas and cooler mountain breezes from flat viewing decks.'),
  ('penang', 4417, 9, 'Taking guided architectural walking tours of flat, ground-level heritage landmarks such as Cheong Fatt Tze - The Blue Mansion and the Pinang Peranakan Mansion.'),
  ('penang', 4417, 10, 'Strolling along the flat wooden walkways of the Clan Jetties of Penang (such as Chew Jetty) during low-crowd morning hours.'),
  ('penang', 4417, 11, 'Enjoying seated hawker dining at organized, well-ventilated open-air food courts or air-conditioned local restaurants.'),
  ('penang', 4417, 12, 'Attempting to climb the upper multi-tiered pagoda stairs at Kek Lok Si Temple in steep heat without utilizing the available incline lifts.'),
  ('penang', 4417, 13, 'Undertaking self-guided walking tours during peak mid-day hours (12:00 PM–3:00 PM) when sun exposure and temperatures are at their highest.'),
  ('penang', 4417, 14, 'Long jungle hikes in Penang National Park without proper physical preparation and guide support.'),
  ('penang', 4417, 15, 'Carrying visible snacks or plastic food bags near wild monkey habitats at Penang Hill or the Botanic Gardens.'),
  ('penang', 4417, 16, 'Relying strictly on public buses during peak commuting traffic hours, which can extend travel times and require standing at bus stops.'),
  ('penang', 4419, 0, 'Savor a plate of **Char Kway Teow**, stir-fried over high heat in a charcoal wok with flat rice noodles, prawns, blood cockles, eggs, bean sprouts, and smoky *wok hei*.'),
  ('penang', 4419, 1, 'Slurp a bowl of tangy **Penang Asam Laksa**, a rich fish-based sour noodle soup infused with tamarind, shredded mackerel, torch ginger flower, and sweet shrimp paste (*petis udang*).'),
  ('penang', 4419, 2, 'Indulge in authentic **Peranakan (Nyonya) Cuisine**, sampling complex traditional dishes like *Otak-Otak*, *Ayam Buah Keluak*, and colorful handmade *Nyonya Kuih*.'),
  ('penang', 4419, 3, 'Enjoy a late-night plate of **Nasi Kandar**, choosing from vast spreads of spicy curries, fried chicken, beef rendang, and okra poured over steamed rice (*kuah banjir*).'),
  ('penang', 4419, 4, 'Refresh yourself with traditional local desserts like **Cendol**—shaved ice layered with green rice flour jelly, coconut milk, and gula melaka palm sugar—or a hot cup of white coffee at a local *kopitiam*.'),
  ('penang', 4419, 5, '**Families:** Lively open-air hawker food courts (like Gurney Drive or Long Beach Cafe) where everyone can order different dishes—from mild satay and chicken rice to fresh fruit juices—all in one place.'),
  ('penang', 4419, 6, '**Honeymooners:** Romantic fine-dining dinners at heritage Nyonya spots like Kebaya Dining Room or upscale beachfront seafood meals in Batu Ferringhi.'),
  ('penang', 4419, 7, '**Luxury travelers:** Experiencing Michelin-starred or Michelin-selected fine dining, chef-led private culinary tours, and high tea at the historic Eastern & Oriental Hotel.'),
  ('penang', 4419, 8, '**Budget travelers:** Ultra-affordable hawker centers where world-class noodle dishes, rice plates, and snacks cost between MYR 6 to MYR 12 ($1.30–$2.80 USD).'),
  ('penang', 4419, 9, '**Foodies:** Following the Penang Michelin Guide trail to hunt down famous hawker stalls like Siam Road Char Kway Teow, 888 Hokkien Mee, and Sister Yao''s Char Koay Kak.'),
  ('penang', 4419, 10, '**George Town Heritage Core (Chulia St & Kimberley St):** Best for legendary evening street food stalls, night markets, historic *kopitiams*, and traditional Nyonya kuih shops.'),
  ('penang', 4419, 11, '**Gurney Drive Promenade:** Best for massive seafront hawker centers featuring vast spreads of local seafood, Char Kway Teow, and local desserts all under one roof.'),
  ('penang', 4419, 12, '**Air Itam Market Precinct:** Best for iconic morning food runs, including famous Assam Laksa stalls and Hokkien mee near Kek Lok Si Temple.'),
  ('penang', 4419, 13, '**Little India (Lebuh Pasar):** Best for aromatic South Indian banana leaf thalis, fresh dosas, samosas, and spicy *mamak* food.'),
  ('penang', 4420, 0, '**Traditional Penang Pastries & Sweets:** Flaky *Tau Sar Pneah* (mung bean biscuits), *Beh Teh Saw* (maltose pastry), and sweet peanut candy freshly baked at century-old heritage bakeries.'),
  ('penang', 4420, 1, '**Nutmeg Products & Local Preserves:** Dried nutmeg slices, nutmeg syrup, massage oils, balms, and pickled fruits (*jeruk*) sourced straight from Balik Pulau plantations.'),
  ('penang', 4420, 2, '**Authentic Malaysian Batik & Textiles:** Hand-painted batik sarongs, silk scarves, shirts, and decorative tapestries produced using traditional wax-resist dyeing techniques.'),
  ('penang', 4420, 3, '**Peranakan Crafts & Nyonya Kebayas:** Intricately beaded slippers, hand-stitched Nyonya *kebaya* blouses, traditional batik bags, and ornate Peranakan jewelry.'),
  ('penang', 4420, 4, '**Penang White Coffee & Local Spices:** Pre-packed roasted 3-in-1 Penang white coffee, artisan sesame oil, vacuum-packed *belacan* (shrimp paste), and sealed Assam Laksa pastes.'),
  ('penang', 4420, 5, '**Chowrasta Market & George Town Heritage Streets:** Best for authentic local edible souvenirs, traditional pastries, nutmeg balms, and vintage shophouse browsing.'),
  ('penang', 4420, 6, '**Gurney Paragon & Gurney Plaza:** Ideal for luxury international brands, mid-to-high fashion, beauty boutiques, and modern air-conditioned retail convenience.'),
  ('penang', 4420, 7, '**Hin Bus Depot & Art Markets:** Prefer visiting on weekends for indie artisan crafts, hand-drawn street art prints, eco-friendly totes, and locally designed jewelry.'),
  ('penang', 4420, 8, '**Batu Ferringhi Night Market:** Perfect for late-night casual browsing, generic resort wear, beach accessories, and inexpensive souvenir keepsakes.'),
  ('penang', 4420, 9, 'Purchasing unpackaged, non-vacuum-sealed edible items (like fresh *belacan* or liquid sauces) right before an international flight; opt for sealed, airport-friendly travel packaging.'),
  ('penang', 4420, 10, 'Accepting the first quoted price at tourist-heavy street bazaars (such as Batu Ferringhi Night Market); polite bargaining is expected, whereas prices in heritage shophouses and malls are strictly fixed.'),
  ('penang', 4420, 11, 'Buying mass-produced, commercially printed fabrics sold as "handmade batik"; verify authenticity by checking if the pattern bleeds clearly through both sides of the fabric.'),
  ('penang', 4420, 12, '**Culture & Craft Lovers:** Travelers seeking genuine handmade Malaysian batik, Peranakan beadwork, and street-art-inspired local art prints.'),
  ('penang', 4420, 13, '**Foodie Shoppers:** Visitors looking to take home Penang''s iconic culinary heritage through fresh pastries, local white coffee, and traditional spice pastes.'),
  ('penang', 4420, 14, '**Luxury & High-Street Shoppers:** Mall-goers wanting international designer brands, high-end electronics, and premier retail experiences along Gurney Drive.'),
  ('penang', 4420, 15, '**Bargain & Souvenir Hunters:** Travelers hunting for budget-friendly beachwear, trinkets, magnets, and traditional accessories at local night markets.'),
  ('penang', 4421, 0, '**Cocktail enthusiasts & speakeasy hunters** seeking world-class mixology, hidden shophouse bars, and heritage-themed cocktail lounges.'),
  ('penang', 4421, 1, '**Backpackers & casual drinkers** looking for affordable beer, high-energy pub crawling, and outdoor street-side seating.'),
  ('penang', 4421, 2, '**Night-owl foodies** wanting to pair late-night drinks with iconic Penang street food from bustling hawker stalls open until the early hours.'),
  ('penang', 4421, 3, '**Live music & jazz lovers** looking for acoustic sessions, Chinese opera-themed performances, and live bands inside intimate heritage spaces.'),
  ('penang', 4421, 4, 'Bar-hopping between **Chulia Street and Love Lane** in George Town, moving from open-air pub tables to cozy live music joints within easy walking distance.'),
  ('penang', 4421, 5, 'Hunting down hidden **heritage speakeasies** like *Backdoor Bodega*, *Magazine 63*, or *Manchu Bar* for bespoke craft cocktails inspired by local spices and Chinese teas.'),
  ('penang', 4421, 6, 'Enjoying late-night hawker dining at **Kimberley Street or Chulia Street Night Markets** to grab hot bowls of *Lok-Lok* or *Kway Chap* after a round of drinks.'),
  ('penang', 4421, 7, 'Heading to beachfront lounges or sunset bars in **Batu Ferringhi** for casual seaside cocktails and ocean breezes before the midnight crowds roll in.');
INSERT INTO destination_guidance_bullet (place_id, position, bullet_index, text) VALUES
  ('penang', 4421, 8, 'Expecting a dense metropolis-style superclub district; Penang’s nightlife is predominantly bar-, pub-, and lounge-focused rather than focused on multi-story electronic dance clubs.'),
  ('penang', 4421, 9, 'Driving yourself between night spots after drinking; local ride-hailing app Grab is widely available, cheap, and safe for late-night transportation around the island.'),
  ('penang', 4421, 10, 'Waiting past midnight to find open kitchens at standard restaurants; transition to 24-hour *mamak* stalls or late-night street vendors for food after 11:00 PM.'),
  ('penang', 4421, 11, '**Love Lane (George Town):** The vibrant center of Penang’s nightlife, packed with open-fronted shophouse bars, live acoustic music venues, craft beer joints, and a lively international crowd.'),
  ('penang', 4421, 12, '**Chulia Street (Lebuh Chulia):** Best for high-energy pub culture, budget-friendly draft beer, and seamless transitions between street-food hawker stalls and roadside bars.'),
  ('penang', 4421, 13, '**Nagore Square & Hin Bus Depot Area:** Best for chic craft cocktail spots, creative art spaces, local microbreweries, and hipster speakeasies.'),
  ('penang', 4421, 14, '**Batu Ferringhi Beach Strip:** Best for relaxing beachfront bars, resort lounges, and sunset drinks right along the coast.'),
  ('penang', 4429, 0, 'Attempt to explore the **George Town Heritage Core** during midday peak hours (11:00 AM–3:00 PM) on foot, exposing clients to intense tropical heat and humidity while navigating narrow, unshaded shophouse sidewalks.'),
  ('penang', 4429, 1, 'Book clients for the **Penang Hill Funicular Railway** on weekend afternoons or public holidays without pre-purchasing Express Fast-Lane passes, stranding them in non-air-conditioned queue lines for up to two to three hours.'),
  ('penang', 4429, 2, 'Treat Penang purely as a beach resort destination by housing clients exclusively in **Batu Ferringhi**, underestimating the 45-to-60-minute daily traffic commute into George Town for dining and cultural sightseeing.'),
  ('penang', 4429, 3, 'Schedule visits to **Kek Lok Si Temple** as a brief 30-minute photo stop, failing to realize the massive scale of the complex, which requires multiple incline lifts and significant walking to reach the colossal Kuan Yin statue.'),
  ('penang', 4429, 4, 'Under-budget time for Penang’s famous street food culture, expecting quick sit-down service at popular hawker hubs like **Gurney Drive** or **Jalan Chulia** during peak evening dinner hours (7:00 PM–9:00 PM).'),
  ('penang', 4430, 0, 'Splits client itineraries strategically between two bases—booking heritage boutique hotels in **George Town** for culture and food, followed by luxury beachfront resorts in **Batu Ferringhi** for relaxation.'),
  ('penang', 4430, 1, 'Schedules **Penang Hill** visits for early morning arrivals (8:00 AM–8:30 AM) to enjoy crisp highland temperatures and clear morning vistas, or books afternoon visits paired with sunset dining at David Brown''s.'),
  ('penang', 4430, 2, 'Secures advance tickets or private guided heritage tours for restricted-entry attractions like **Cheong Fatt Tze (The Blue Mansion)** and **Pinang Peranakan Mansion** to avoid missed entrance slots.'),
  ('penang', 4430, 3, 'Directs food-enthusiast clients beyond generic tourist food courts toward authentic, localized hawker precincts in **Air Itam**, **Carnarvon Street**, and **Kimberley Street** for famous dishes like Asam Laksa and Char Kway Teow.'),
  ('penang', 4430, 4, 'Pre-arranges private SUV transfers or instructs clients on using e-hailing apps (Grab) for cross-island journeys, avoiding long waits for local public buses along narrow coastal roads.'),
  ('penang', 4431, 0, 'For **Geographic & Accommodation Strategy**, enforce a dual-base split (2–3 nights in George Town Heritage Core + 3–4 nights in Batu Ferringhi Beach) to eliminate tedious daily cross-island commute times.'),
  ('penang', 4431, 1, 'For **Penang Hill & Kek Lok Si Logistics**, combine both Air Itam attractions into a single morning circuit and always upgrade clients to Fast-Lane Express funicular tickets to bypass massive tour group queues.'),
  ('penang', 4431, 2, 'For **Culinary & Walking Tours**, schedule heritage street art walks for early mornings (7:30 AM–10:00 AM) or late afternoons (4:30 PM–6:30 PM), reserving the hottest hours of the day for air-conditioned museums, heritage mansion tours, or colonial high tea.'),
  ('penang', 4434, 0, 'Hunt for iconic street art murals along Armenian Street and explore the floating stilted village of Chew Jetty.'),
  ('penang', 4434, 1, 'Take the Penang Hill Funicular Railway up to the summit and walk the Curtis Crest Treetop Walk inside The Habitat UNESCO Biosphere Reserve.'),
  ('penang', 4434, 2, 'Explore Kek Lok Si Temple to admire the multi-tiered pagoda and the colossal bronze Kuan Yin statue.'),
  ('penang', 4434, 3, 'Feast on legendary street food—including Char Kway Teow, Asam Laksa, Nasi Kandar, and Cendol—at historic *kopitiams* and lively night markets.'),
  ('penang', 4434, 4, 'Visit opulent heritage mansions, including Cheong Fatt Tze (The Blue Mansion) and the Pinang Peranakan Mansion.'),
  ('penang', 4434, 5, 'Walking the George Town Heritage Core during peak midday heat hours (11:00 AM–3:00 PM) without air-conditioned museum or cafe breaks.'),
  ('penang', 4434, 6, 'Visiting Penang Hill on weekend afternoons without pre-purchased Express Fast-Track tickets, leading to long standing queues.'),
  ('penang', 4434, 7, 'Staying exclusively in Batu Ferringhi if your main goal is historical sightseeing and daily dining in George Town, due to cross-island commuting traffic.'),
  ('penang', 4434, 8, 'Carrying open snacks or plastic food bags near wild monkey habitats at Penang Hill, Botanic Gardens, or Penang National Park.'),
  ('penang', 4435, 0, 'To be populated with authoritative tourism/transport/attraction sources before production use.'),
