  ('sumatra', 4530, 0, 'Take advantage of shared tourist minibuses (approx. 210,000–270,000 IDR / ~$13–$17 USD) or local public buses (*angkot*) to cover major transit routes between Medan, Bukit Lawang, Berastagi, and Lake Toba.'),
  ('sumatra', 4530, 1, 'Focus daily dining on local roadside *warungs*, where classic Indonesian staples like *Nasi Goreng*, *Mie Goreng*, and *Nasi Padang* cost just 20,000 to 45,000 IDR ($1.30–$2.90 USD) per dish.'),
  ('sumatra', 4530, 2, 'Book authentic, family-run guesthouses or eco-lodges along the Bohorok River in Bukit Lawang or over the volcanic waters on Samosir Island (Lake Toba), which offer clean, scenic private rooms for $10 to $25 USD per night.'),
  ('sumatra', 4530, 3, 'Stock up on fresh tropical fruits (such as passionfruit, mangos, and local bananas) at traditional highland markets in Berastagi for cheap, high-energy snacks during overland transit days.'),
  ('sumatra', 4530, 4, 'Rent a motor scooter on Samosir Island (approx. 70,000–100,000 IDR / ~$4.50–$6.50 USD per day) to independently explore ancient Batak villages, hot springs, and scenic viewpoints at your own pace without paying for private drivers.'),
  ('sumatra', 4530, 5, 'Skimping on licensed, ethical guides for orangutan trekking in Gunung Leuser National Park; bargain uncertified guides often violate conservation rules by feeding or touching wildlife, threatening the habitat.'),
  ('sumatra', 4530, 6, 'Relying exclusively on local public transportation when operating on a tight timeframe, as unannounced delays, multiple vehicle transfers, and lack of air conditioning can turn a 4-hour drive into an exhausting 8-hour journey.'),
  ('sumatra', 4530, 7, 'Traveling into remote regions like Bukit Lawang, Tangkahan, or the Mentawai Islands without sufficient cash; local ATMs are non-existent or unreliable, and international card processing incurs hefty surcharges.'),
  ('sumatra', 4530, 8, 'Drinking cheap, unverified local home-brewed alcohol (*arak*), as adulterated spirits carry severe health risks; stick to sealed commercial beers like Bintang or reputable bottled beverages.'),
  ('sumatra', 4531, 0, '4+'),
  ('sumatra', 4531, 1, '6+'),
  ('sumatra', 4531, 2, '8+'),
  ('sumatra', 4531, 3, 'Teenagers'),
  ('sumatra', 4531, 4, 'Leave traditional strollers at home and rely on an ergonomic, heavy-duty baby/toddler carrier; Sumatra’s unpaved jungle paths, mud trails, broken city sidewalks, and steep stairs make wheels unusable outside major airport terminals.'),
  ('sumatra', 4531, 5, 'Book private air-conditioned MPV transfers (such as a Toyota Innova) for long overland journeys; transit between Medan, Bukit Lawang, and Lake Toba can take 4 to 6 hours over bumpy mountain roads, so having a private driver allows for flexible bathroom and motion-sickness breaks.'),
  ('sumatra', 4531, 6, 'Hire certified, kid-friendly park guides for jungle trekking in Gunung Leuser National Park; experienced naturalists tailor trail lengths to little legs, assist kids across slippery riverbeds, and ensure safe wildlife distance.'),
  ('sumatra', 4531, 7, 'Enforce strict rules around wild animals; instruct children never to hold food out, touch, or make direct eye contact with macaques or semi-wild orangutans, as monkeys can grab unsecured snacks quickly.'),
  ('sumatra', 4531, 8, 'Pack a family health kit containing child-safe DEET mosquito repellent, lightweight long-sleeve clothing to prevent insect bites, rehydration salts, antidiarrheal medication, and motion-sickness remedies for winding highland passes.'),
  ('sumatra', 4531, 9, 'Introduce local cuisine gradually, opting for non-spicy Indonesian staples like *Nasi Goreng* (fried rice), *Mie Goreng* (fried noodles), or *Sate Ayam* (chicken skewers) with peanut sauce served on the side before trying fiery regional dishes.'),
  ('sumatra', 4532, 0, 'honeymoon_score: 82'),
  ('sumatra', 4532, 1, 'romance_score: 85'),
  ('sumatra', 4532, 2, 'privacy_score: 75'),
  ('sumatra', 4532, 3, 'luxury_score: 88'),
  ('sumatra', 4534, 0, 'Multi-day deep rainforest trekking in Gunung Leuser National Park to track wild orangutans, Thomas''s leaf monkeys, and exotic wildlife before river tubing down the Bohorok River.'),
  ('sumatra', 4534, 1, 'Conquering the predawn climb up active Mount Sibayak or Mount Sinabung in Berastagi to witness steaming fumaroles and sunrise over the volcanic highlands.'),
  ('sumatra', 4534, 2, 'Surfing world-famous, pristine ocean reef breaks and barrel waves across the remote Mentawai Islands and Nias Island.'),
  ('sumatra', 4534, 3, 'Scuba diving through underwater volcanic hydrothermal vents, deep ocean drop-offs, and thriving marine sanctuaries off Pulau Weh.'),
  ('sumatra', 4534, 4, 'Summiting Mount Kerinci—Indonesia''s tallest active volcano at 3,805 meters—on a grueling multi-day mountain expedition through Kerinci Seblat National Park.'),
  ('sumatra', 4534, 5, '**Bukit Lawang & Gunung Leuser** — best for deep jungle wilderness trekking, wild orangutan encounters, overnight rainforest camping, and white-water river tubing.'),
  ('sumatra', 4534, 6, '**Berastagi & Karo Highlands** — best for active volcano hiking, crater rim climbs, geothermal hot springs, and rugged mountain trekking.'),
  ('sumatra', 4534, 7, '**Mentawai & Nias Islands** — best for world-class ocean surfing expeditions, remote island exploration, and off-the-grid coastal wilderness.'),
  ('sumatra', 4534, 8, '**Pulau Weh (Aceh)** — best for deep-sea scuba diving, marine cave exploration, volcanic reef snorkeling, and coastal kayaking.'),
  ('sumatra', 4534, 9, 'Wilderness jungle trekkers, wildlife trackers, and eco-adventurers.'),
  ('sumatra', 4534, 10, 'Mountain climbers, volcano hikers, and high-altitude trail expeditioners.'),
  ('sumatra', 4534, 11, 'World-class ocean surfers and big-wave riders.'),
  ('sumatra', 4534, 12, 'Advanced scuba divers and marine nature photographers.'),
  ('sumatra', 4534, 13, 'Off-the-beaten-path backpackers and extreme thrill-seekers.'),
  ('sumatra', 4535, 0, 'Schedule scenic drives and outdoor visits during early morning hours (8:00 AM–10:30 AM) to secure cooler temperatures, smoother road conditions, and calm lake waters.'),
  ('sumatra', 4535, 1, 'Book private air-conditioned vehicles (like Toyota Innova) with professional local drivers for long overland legs (such as Medan to Parapat) to ensure flexible rest breaks.'),
  ('sumatra', 4535, 2, 'Choose luxury lakefront accommodations on Samosir Island (such as Marianna Resort) equipped with elevators and step-free access to avoid steep lakeside staircases.');
INSERT INTO destination_guidance_bullet (place_id, position, bullet_index, text) VALUES
  ('sumatra', 4535, 3, 'Opt for private chartered speedboats or wooden passenger ferries from Parapat to Tuktuk for seamless, level embarkation onto island docks.'),
  ('sumatra', 4535, 4, 'Wear sturdy, non-slip supportive walking shoes with good ankle support when visiting traditional villages with uneven stone pathways or grassy clearings.'),
  ('sumatra', 4535, 5, 'Keep emergency cash in Indonesian Rupiah (IDR) and travel with necessary prescription medications, as pharmacy access is limited outside major cities like Medan.'),
  ('sumatra', 4535, 6, 'Plan midday rest periods at air-conditioned resort lounges or scenic lakeside dining spots during peak equatorial heat and humidity hours (12:00 PM–3:00 PM).'),
  ('sumatra', 4535, 7, 'Exploring Samosir Island''s Batak culture via private car or gentle walk around flat, paved heritage areas like Tomok and Ambarita.'),
  ('sumatra', 4535, 8, 'Taking relaxed boat cruises on Lake Toba to view high waterfalls (like Sipiso-Piso) from the comfort of the water rather than climbing steep canyon stairs.'),
  ('sumatra', 4535, 9, 'Visiting the historic Batak Museum at Balige and the TB Silalahi Center, which offer flat, modern, air-conditioned access to rich local history.'),
  ('sumatra', 4535, 10, 'Enjoying panoramic vistas of the Sianok Canyon and Lake Maninjau in West Sumatra from flat, paved roadside viewing platforms and shaded cafes.'),
  ('sumatra', 4535, 11, 'Dining on gentle, non-spiced traditional Sumatran cuisine or fresh lake fish at well-ventilated, sit-down lakeside restaurants.'),
  ('sumatra', 4535, 12, 'Attempting the long, steep flight of stairs down to the base of Sipiso-Piso Waterfall or hiking up active volcanoes like Mount Sibayak.'),
  ('sumatra', 4535, 13, 'Undertaking self-guided jungle treks in Bukit Lawang to see orangutans, which require negotiating steep, muddy, and root-filled rainforest paths.'),
  ('sumatra', 4535, 14, 'Taking public mini-buses (*sudako* or *becak*) for long cross-island transit due to tight seating, high vibration, and lack of air conditioning.'),
  ('sumatra', 4535, 15, 'Traveling long road distances across mountain passes after dark due to poor road lighting, sudden downpours, and limited roadside assistance.'),
  ('sumatra', 4535, 16, 'Walking on unpaved village tracks immediately following heavy tropical rainstorms when surfaces become slippery and uneven.'),
  ('sumatra', 4537, 0, 'Savor authentic **Rendang**, the globally famous slow-cooked beef dish simmered for hours in coconut milk and a complex spice paste until tender and caramelized.'),
  ('sumatra', 4537, 1, 'Experience a traditional **Nasi Padang** feast, where dozens of small plates filled with spicy curries, fried fish, sambals, and stewed meats are stacked high at your table (*hidang* style).'),
  ('sumatra', 4537, 2, 'Feast on Batak highland specialties near Lake Toba, such as **Saksang** or **Ikan Mas Arsik**, a fragrant carp dish stewed with torch ginger and vibrant Andaliman pepper (the Sumatran Sichuan pepper).'),
  ('sumatra', 4537, 3, 'Slurp a steaming bowl of **Mie Gompa** or **Mie Aceh**, thick yellow noodles cooked in a curry-like spice paste loaded with meat, seafood, and aromatic local herbs.'),
  ('sumatra', 4537, 4, 'Sip world-famous **Sumatran Arabica Coffee** (such as Mandheling or Gayo) at local street cafes (*warkop*) alongside crispy **Pisang Goreng** (fried bananas) or sweet durian treats.'),
  ('sumatra', 4537, 5, '**Families:** Friendly local *warungs* and casual lakeside eateries around Lake Toba serving mild fried rice (*Nasi Goreng*), chicken satay, fresh fruit smoothies, and grilled lake fish.'),
  ('sumatra', 4537, 6, '**Honeymooners:** Romantic candlelit lakeside dinners on Samosir Island or private beach barbecues featuring fresh-caught grilled seafood in the Mentawai Islands.'),
  ('sumatra', 4537, 7, '**Luxury travelers:** Chef-led private dining experiences inside secluded eco-lodges, custom Batak tasting menus, and private tasting tours of high-altitude coffee estates in the highlands.'),
  ('sumatra', 4537, 8, '**Budget travelers:** Ultra-affordable roadside food stalls and *warungs* where filling plates of *Nasi Padang*, *Mie Goreng*, or *Soto Medan* cost just 20,000 to 45,000 IDR ($1.30–$2.90 USD).'),
  ('sumatra', 4537, 9, '**Foodies:** Culinary pilgrimages through Padang and Bukittinggi in West Sumatra to taste authentic Minangkabau recipes and fiery sambals at their original source.'),
  ('sumatra', 4537, 10, '**Bukittinggi & Padang (West Sumatra):** Best for the ultimate *Nasi Padang* immersion, rich beef rendang, *Sate Padang*, and traditional Minangkabau spice markets.'),
  ('sumatra', 4537, 11, '**Medan City Center:** Best for multi-cultural street food, combining iconic North Sumatran *Soto Medan*, Chinese-Indonesian noodle dishes, and famed durian stalls.'),
  ('sumatra', 4537, 12, '**Samosir Island (Lake Toba):** Best for traditional Batak cuisine, grilled lake tilapia (*Ikan Bakar*), dishes seasoned with native Andaliman pepper, and cozy lakeside dining.'),
  ('sumatra', 4537, 13, '**Banda Aceh:** Best for fiery, spice-heavy *Mie Aceh*, aromatic chicken dish *Ayam Tangkap*, and historic coffee house culture (*kopi sanger*).'),
  ('sumatra', 4538, 0, '**Ulos & Songket Textiles:** Intricately hand-woven traditional Batak *Ulos* cloths from Lake Toba and rich Minangkabau *Songket* woven with metallic threads from West Sumatra.'),
  ('sumatra', 4538, 1, '**Single-Origin Sumatran Coffee:** Freshly roasted Mandheling, Gayo, and Lintong Arabica coffee beans sourced directly from highland plantations.'),
  ('sumatra', 4538, 2, '**Batak Woodcarvings & Antiques:** Hand-carved wooden sculptures, traditional masks, Batak calendar staffs (*Pustaha*), and ornamental home decor from Samosir Island.'),
  ('sumatra', 4538, 3, '**Passionfruit & Highland Produce:** Fresh passionfruit (*markisa*) syrup, jams, dried tropical fruits, and local spices from the agricultural markets of Berastagi.'),
  ('sumatra', 4538, 4, '**Minangkabau Silverwork & Crafts:** Filigree silverware, traditional horn-shaped brass decor, and embroidered textiles from Bukittinggi.'),
  ('sumatra', 4538, 5, '**Tomok & Ambarita Markets (Samosir Island):** Best for Batak hand-woven *Ulos*, wooden carvings, traditional musical instruments, and lakeside souvenirs.'),
  ('sumatra', 4538, 6, '**Pasar Atsiri & Highland Markets (Berastagi):** Ideal for fresh passionfruit products, regional spices, tropical fruits, and highland flowers.'),
  ('sumatra', 4538, 7, '**Pasar Atas & Bukittinggi Souvenir Shops:** Preferred for authentic West Sumatran *Songket*, Minangkabau silver jewelry, embroidered goods, and local snacks like *Keripik Sanjai*.'),
  ('sumatra', 4538, 8, '**Pajak Ikan Lama (Medan):** Perfect for browsing traditional textiles, fabrics, batik, and local garments in a historic city market environment.'),
  ('sumatra', 4538, 9, 'Purchasing items made from endangered wildlife, including coral, sea turtle shells, or unverified animal products, which strictly violate international conservation laws.'),
  ('sumatra', 4538, 10, 'Buying antique Batak artifacts without verifying authenticity, as many items sold in tourist centers are newly aged, mass-produced replicas.'),
  ('sumatra', 4538, 11, 'Paying the initial asking price at informal markets and street stalls; friendly bargaining is expected, whereas prices in established boutiques and modern stores in Medan are fixed.'),
  ('sumatra', 4538, 12, '**Culture & Craft Lovers:** Travelers seeking rare indigenous textiles, hand-carved wooden art, and traditional tribal handicrafts.'),
  ('sumatra', 4538, 13, '**Coffee Enthusiasts:** Visitors wanting to purchase world-class single-origin Sumatran Arabica beans directly from highland source regions.'),
  ('sumatra', 4538, 14, '**Bargain Hunters & Souvenir Collectors:** Travelers hunting for handmade wooden trinkets, woven bags, and regional snacks at local village markets.'),
  ('sumatra', 4539, 0, '**Coffee lovers & cultural night-owls** seeking late-night conversations over traditional *Kopi Sanger* or *Kopi Luwak* at bustling local *warungs* open past midnight.'),
  ('sumatra', 4539, 1, '**Live music & Batak folk enthusiasts** wanting to hear acoustic guitar performances and soul-stirring harmony singing along the shores of Lake Toba.'),
  ('sumatra', 4539, 2, '**Backpackers & jungle trekkers** looking for relaxed, riverside Bintang beers and campfire acoustic jams in Bukit Lawang or Tuktuk.'),
  ('sumatra', 4539, 3, '**Urban lounge-goers** looking for modern craft cocktails, hotel bars, and live band venues in central Medan.'),
  ('sumatra', 4539, 4, 'Gathering at lakeside bars along the **Tuktuk Peninsula on Samosir Island (Lake Toba)** like *Bagus Bay* or *Juwita Cafe* for cold beers, lakeside bonfires, and traditional Batak folk music.'),
  ('sumatra', 4539, 5, 'Immersing yourself in local coffee culture at late-night **warung kopi in Medan, Padang, or Banda Aceh**, where locals gather late into the evening for coffee and sweet rotis.'),
  ('sumatra', 4539, 6, 'Visiting upscale hotel lounges and modern beer houses in **Medan City Center** (such as *The Tavern*, *Cava Lounge*, or *SoHo*) for live band sets, imported beers, and dining.'),
  ('sumatra', 4539, 7, 'Unwinding after a jungle trek in **Bukit Lawang** at open-air riverside guesthouse restaurants that feature local acoustic jams and quiet social atmospheres.'),
  ('sumatra', 4539, 8, 'Expecting alcohol, bars, or nightclubs in **Banda Aceh and broader Aceh province**, where strict Sharia law prohibits alcohol consumption and public nightlife venues strictly do not exist.'),
  ('sumatra', 4539, 9, 'Searching for multi-story electronic dance mega-clubs; nightlife outside Medan is predominantly acoustic, quiet, and ends around 11:00 PM.'),
  ('sumatra', 4539, 10, 'Drinking unverified or unlabelled local home-brewed spirits (*arak*); stick strictly to commercial bottled beers like Bintang or drinks from established hotel bars.'),
  ('sumatra', 4539, 11, '**Tuktuk Peninsula (Samosir Island, Lake Toba):** The primary social hub for travelers, lined with relaxed waterfront cafes, live Batak music venues, and cozy guesthouse bars.'),
  ('sumatra', 4539, 12, '**Central Medan (Jalan Putri Hijau & Jalan Imam Bonjol):** Best for modern city nightlife, upscale hotel lounges, live music bars, and international dining spots.'),
  ('sumatra', 4539, 13, '**Bukit Lawang Riverside:** Best for low-key social evenings along the riverbank with cold Bintang beers and acoustic guitar circles among trekking guides and travelers.'),
  ('sumatra', 4539, 14, '**Iboih & Gapang Bays (Pulau Weh):** Best for quiet, starry-night oceanfront dining, fish BBQs, and diving debriefs (without commercial bars or alcohol).'),
  ('sumatra', 4547, 0, 'Treat Sumatra like a small, easy-to-navigate resort island, severely underestimating the massive geographical scale, winding mountain roads, and long overland transfer times between key destinations (e.g., 4 hours between Medan and Bukit Lawang, or up to 8–10 hours across mountain passes).'),
  ('sumatra', 4547, 1, 'Schedule tight, single-day transit connections between **Bukit Lawang** and **Lake Toba**, forcing clients into exhausting 8-to-10-hour road journeys on bumpy roads without adequate rest stops or flight cushions.'),
  ('sumatra', 4547, 2, 'Over-pack itineraries with too many regions (e.g., combining North Sumatra, West Sumatra, and Belitung in a short 7-to-8-day window), keeping clients trapped in vehicles for the majority of their trip.'),
  ('sumatra', 4547, 3, 'Fail to account for variable road conditions and traffic bottlenecks around **Medan** and **Berastagi**, missing domestic flight departures from Silangit (DTB) or Medan (KNO) due to under-budgeted drive times.'),
  ('sumatra', 4547, 4, 'Book clients on jungle treks in **Gunung Leuser National Park** without vetting local eco-guides, exposing travelers to unaccredited operators who disregard safety protocols, lack child-appropriate gear, or engage in unethical wildlife interactions.'),
  ('sumatra', 4548, 0, 'Structures regional trips around logical flight gateways—using **Medan (KNO)** and **Silangit (DTB)** for North Sumatra (Bukit Lawang & Lake Toba), and **Padang (PDG)** for West Sumatra (Bukittinggi, Harau Valley, & Mentawai coast).'),
  ('sumatra', 4548, 1, 'Books private, high-clearance executive air-conditioned vehicles (SUVs or private minivans) with seasoned local drivers who know mountain passes and alternative routes to navigate Sumatra''s complex terrain safely.'),
  ('sumatra', 4548, 2, 'Schedules jungle treks in **Bukit Lawang** during early morning hours to maximize orangutan sightings in cooler temperatures, ensuring all river tubing activities use safety helmets and accredited eco-guides.'),
  ('sumatra', 4548, 3, 'Arranges private speedboat charters or express ferries across Lake Toba directly to hotel private piers in **Samosir Island (Tuktuk)**, bypassing crowded public ferry terminals at Parapat.'),
  ('sumatra', 4548, 4, 'Pairs active jungle and highland exploration with relaxing stays at luxury resorts or high-end eco-lodges along Lake Toba or West Sumatra''s private coastal islands to ensure client comfort.'),
  ('sumatra', 4549, 0, 'For **Geographic & Logistics Strategy**, focus itineraries on a single region (either North Sumatra OR West Sumatra) for trips under 8 days, utilizing regional airports like Silangit (DTB) to eliminate long return drives to Medan.'),
  ('sumatra', 4549, 1, 'For **Jungle & Wildlife Logistics**, always partner with accredited local eco-guides for Gunung Leuser National Park, and reserve afternoons for river tubing or downtime to avoid sudden tropical downpours.'),
  ('sumatra', 4549, 2, 'For **Overland Transfers & Comfort**, limit continuous road transit to a maximum of 4–5 hours per day, inserting strategic stops at scenic highlands like Berastagi or Sipiso-Piso Waterfall to break up long mountain drives.'),
  ('sumatra', 4552, 0, 'Track semi-wild Sumatran orangutans on a guided eco-trek through Gunung Leuser National Park in Bukit Lawang and tube down the Bohorok River.'),
  ('sumatra', 4552, 1, 'Cross the massive waters of Lake Toba to Samosir Island, exploring King Siallagan''s stone chair courtyard and ancient Batak villages.'),
  ('sumatra', 4552, 2, 'Marvel at the 120-meter drop of Sipiso-Piso Waterfall plunging directly into the volcanic Lake Toba crater basin.'),
  ('sumatra', 4552, 3, 'Feast on legendary Sumatran cuisine—including authentic *Rendang*, *Ayam Pop*, *Soto Medan*, and fresh lake-caught grilled tilapia (*Ikan Bakar*).'),
  ('sumatra', 4552, 4, 'Explore the dramatic granite cliffs of Harau Valley and the grand horn-roofed architecture of Istano Basa Pagaruyung in West Sumatra.'),
  ('sumatra', 4552, 5, 'Attempting to cover both North and West Sumatra in less than 7 days purely via long overland road drives without domestic flights.'),
  ('sumatra', 4552, 6, 'Underestimating long mountain transit times between destinations (e.g., Medan to Bukit Lawang or Lake Toba) and booking tight flight connections.'),
  ('sumatra', 4552, 7, 'Hiring unaccredited or independent guides for jungle trekking in Gunung Leuser National Park who do not enforce ethical wildlife safety standards.'),
  ('sumatra', 4552, 8, 'Expecting fast-paced urban transit or continuous highway driving; island infrastructure requires patient, flexible travel planning.'),
  ('sumatra', 4553, 0, 'To be populated with authoritative tourism/transport/attraction sources before production use.'),
  ('jawa', 4557, 0, 'Utilize Java’s comfortable and punctual executive passenger train network (approx. 150,000–380,000 IDR / ~$10–$25 USD per leg) or the Whoosh High-Speed Rail to travel efficiently between major hubs like Jakarta, Bandung, Yogyakarta, Surabaya, and Malang.'),
  ('jawa', 4557, 1, 'Eat like a local at roadside *warungs*, *angkrangan* street stalls, or night markets, where Javanese staples like *Gudeg*, *Nasi Goreng*, *Soto Ayam*, and *Sate* cost between 15,000 and 40,000 IDR ($1.00–$2.60 USD) per plate.'),
  ('jawa', 4557, 2, 'Stay at boutique guesthouses, private homestays, or budget heritage hotels around Yogyakarta’s Malioboro district or near Mount Bromo’s Cemoro Lawang village, offering comfortable private rooms for $12 to $30 USD per night.'),
  ('jawa', 4557, 3, 'Take advantage of Gojek and Grab super-apps for cheap motorcycle taxis (*GoRide* / *GrabBike*) or car hires in urban centers, avoiding overpriced unmetered street taxis.'),
  ('jawa', 4557, 4, 'Rent a motor scooter in cultural or highland regions like Yogyakarta or Solo (approx. 70,000–100,000 IDR / ~$4.50–$6.50 USD per day) for independent day trips to nearby villages, waterfalls, and lesser-known temples.'),
  ('jawa', 4557, 5, 'Skipping the official climb-up entry ticket allocation or local guide for Borobudur Temple; standard ground-only access misses the historic relief panels and upper stupa terraces, making the dedicated climb permit (~455,000 IDR / ~$30 USD) well worth the investment.'),
  ('jawa', 4557, 6, 'Bargaining down to uncertified or unlicensed 4x4 Jeep operators for Mount Bromo sunrise tours; non-standard vehicles can break down in the sandy volcanic caldera or lack proper safety gear during early morning mountain runs.'),
  ('jawa', 4557, 7, 'Choosing basic economy class trains on long-distance, multi-hour overland routes (e.g., Jakarta to Yogyakarta or Malang to Banyuwangi) to save a few dollars; the slight upgrade to Executive class provides critical air conditioning, plush reclining seats, and quiet cars.'),
  ('jawa', 4557, 8, 'Skimping on proper safety equipment (gas masks and headlamps) or certified guides when trekking to witness Mount Ijen''s blue sulfur flames in the middle of the night.'),
  ('jawa', 4558, 0, '4+'),
  ('jawa', 4558, 1, '6+'),
  ('jawa', 4558, 2, '8+'),
  ('jawa', 4558, 3, 'Teenagers'),
  ('jawa', 4558, 4, 'Leave traditional strollers at home and rely on an ergonomic baby/toddler carrier; Java’s uneven sidewalks, high curbs, crowded street markets, and steep temple stairs at Borobudur and Prambanan make stroller wheels highly impractical.'),
  ('jawa', 4558, 5, 'Utilize Java''s modern executive train network for long distances between cities like Jakarta, Yogyakarta, and Malang; trains offer comfortable seating, air conditioning, and clean restrooms, avoiding congested highway traffic and bumpy mountain roads.'),
  ('jawa', 4558, 6, 'Hire certified, family-friendly private drivers or tour guides for early morning volcano excursions to Mount Bromo; local drivers ensure safe 4x4 Jeep transit across the Sea of Sand and assist kids through chilly pre-dawn temperatures.'),
  ('jawa', 4558, 7, 'Exercise caution at active volcanic craters and thermal vents; keep children on marked observation paths at Mount Bromo, Tangkuban Perahu, or Kawah Putih to prevent exposure to sulfur fumes and steep drops.'),
  ('jawa', 4558, 8, 'Pack a family health kit containing child-safe mosquito repellent, lightweight long-sleeve clothing for humid conditions, warm layers for high-altitude mountain nights, rehydration salts, and motion-sickness remedies for winding mountain drives.'),
  ('jawa', 4558, 9, 'Introduce local cuisine gradually by ordering kid-friendly, non-spicy Javanese staples like *Nasi Goreng* (fried rice), *Mie Goreng* (fried noodles), *Sate Ayam* (chicken skewers), or *Soto Ayam* (mild chicken soup) before introducing spicier regional sambals.'),
  ('jawa', 4559, 0, 'honeymoon_score: 88'),
  ('jawa', 4559, 1, 'romance_score: 90'),
  ('jawa', 4559, 2, 'privacy_score: 82'),
  ('jawa', 4559, 3, 'luxury_score: 92'),
  ('jawa', 4561, 0, 'Climbing to the crater rim of Mount Bromo at sunrise after traversing the vast volcanic Sea of Sand in a 4x4 Jeep.'),
  ('jawa', 4561, 1, 'Descending into Mount Ijen’s active crater under the cover of darkness to behold electric-blue sulfur flames and the turquoise acid lake.'),
  ('jawa', 4561, 2, 'Abseiling 60 meters down into Jomblang Cave (*Gua Jomblang*) near Yogyakarta to witness the spectacular "Light of Heaven" ray illuminating the subterranean forest.'),
  ('jawa', 4561, 3, 'Trekking through the multi-tiered cascades of Tumpak Sewu Waterfall under the towering shadow of Mount Semeru.'),
  ('jawa', 4561, 4, 'Surfing world-famous reef and point breaks at G-Land (Grajagan Bay) in East Java or along the wild coast of Pangandaran.'),
  ('jawa', 4561, 5, '**East Java Volcanic Belt (Bromo, Ijen, Semeru)** — best for high-altitude volcano hiking, crater rim treks, blue flame nocturnal expeditions, and 4x4 caldera crossings.'),
  ('jawa', 4561, 6, '**Yogyakarta Outer Region (Jomblang, Merapi, Pindul)** — best for underground cave abseiling, subterranean river tubing, and off-road Mount Merapi lava Jeep safaris.'),
  ('jawa', 4561, 7, '**Lumajang & Malang Highlands (Tumpak Sewu, Batu)** — best for multi-tiered waterfall canyoning, river rafting, and mountain trail trekking.'),
  ('jawa', 4561, 8, '**Alu Purwo & Grajagan (G-Land)** — best for world-class ocean surfing, coastal rainforest expeditions, and remote wilderness tracking.'),
  ('jawa', 4561, 9, 'Volcano hikers, high-altitude trail runners, and crater climbers.'),
  ('jawa', 4561, 10, 'Caving enthusiasts, subterranean explorers, and canyoners.'),
  ('jawa', 4561, 11, 'Experienced ocean surfers and big-wave riders.'),
  ('jawa', 4561, 12, 'Thrill-seekers, off-road Jeep expeditioners, and outdoor photographers.'),
  ('jawa', 4561, 13, 'Overland backpackers seeking intense natural landscapes and geothermal wonders.'),
  ('jawa', 4562, 0, 'Book executive class or panoramic train seats for long-distance travel between Jakarta, Yogyakarta, Solo, and Malang for spacious, air-conditioned comfort and smooth scenic travel.'),
  ('jawa', 4562, 1, 'Schedule outdoor temple visits at Borobudur and Prambanan during early morning hours (6:30 AM–9:00 AM) to avoid high equatorial heat, humidity, and peak afternoon tourist crowds.'),
  ('jawa', 4562, 2, 'Hire private air-conditioned MPVs (such as a Toyota Innova or Alphard) with professional local drivers for comfortable transfers and flexible rest breaks.'),
  ('jawa', 4562, 3, 'Request ground-floor rooms or properties with modern elevator access, as historic Javanese heritage hotels and boutique lodges often feature multi-level layouts without lifts.'),
  ('jawa', 4562, 4, 'Wear comfortable, non-slip supportive walking shoes with cushioned soles when navigating stone temple courtyards, cobblestone paths, and uneven city sidewalks.'),
  ('jawa', 4562, 5, 'Keep emergency cash in Indonesian Rupiah (IDR) and carry sufficient prescription medications, as comprehensive medical facilities and international pharmacies are concentrated primarily in major urban centers.'),
  ('jawa', 4562, 6, 'Plan midday rest periods at air-conditioned hotel lounges, shaded cafes, or spa facilities during the hottest hours of the day (11:30 AM–2:30 PM).'),
  ('jawa', 4562, 7, 'Exploring the ground-level courtyards of Borobudur and Prambanan, utilizing accessible electric cart shuttles available within the main park grounds.'),
  ('jawa', 4562, 8, 'Enjoying private sunrise viewpoints over Mount Bromo from paved, drive-up observation platforms like King Kong Hill via private 4x4 Jeep, avoiding steep hiking paths.'),
  ('jawa', 4562, 9, 'Attending evening Shadow Puppet (*Wayang Kulit*) or Ramayana Ballet performances seated comfortably at the open-air theater near Prambanan with temple backdrops.'),
  ('jawa', 4562, 10, 'Taking private chauffeured day trips through the cool tea plantations and mountain air of Bandung, Solo, or Malang.'),
  ('jawa', 4562, 11, 'Dining on gentle, non-spicy Javanese specialties like mild *Soto Ayam* (chicken soup), *Gudeg* (jackfruit stew), or fresh seafood at established sit-down restaurants.'),
  ('jawa', 4562, 12, 'Attempting the steep, narrow, and high-step stone staircases leading to the upper terraces of ancient temples without assistance.'),
  ('jawa', 4562, 13, 'Undertaking midnight sulfur crater treks at Mount Ijen, which involve steep uphill climbs, loose gravel, and exposure to sulfur gas fumes.'),
  ('jawa', 4562, 14, 'Relying on public city buses (*Angkot*) or unmetered road transport for transit due to high step entries, sudden stops, and lack of air conditioning.'),
  ('jawa', 4562, 15, 'Walking through dense street markets (*Pasar*) during peak midday hours when narrow walkways become crowded and hot.'),
  ('jawa', 4562, 16, 'Traveling by road across mountain passes at night during the monsoon season due to reduced visibility and heavy rain delays.'),
  ('jawa', 4564, 0, 'Feast on authentic **Gudeg**, Yogyakarta''s legendary signature dish of young jackfruit slow-simmered for hours in coconut milk and palm sugar, served with braised chicken, hard-boiled eggs, and spicy cattle-skin stew (*krecek*).'),
  ('jawa', 4564, 1, 'Savor authentic **Sate Madura** or **Sate Tangkar**, tender skewered meats grilled over open charcoal braziers and coated in rich, velvety peanut sauce or aromatic spiced broth.'),
  ('jawa', 4564, 2, 'Indulge in Sundanese-style **Lalapan and Ikan Bakar**, featuring fresh grilled freshwater fish served alongside raw tropical vegetables, sweet-and-spicy *sambal terasi*, and warm steamed rice wrapped in banana leaves.'),
  ('jawa', 4564, 3, 'Slurp a comforting bowl of **Soto Ayam** or **Bakso**, fragrant turmeric-infused chicken noodle soup or savory beef meatball soup topped with crispy shallots, celery, and fresh lime juice.'),
  ('jawa', 4564, 4, 'Sip authentic **Javanese Heritage Coffee** (such as West Java Preanger or Mount Bromo Arabica) alongside traditional sweet treats like **Roti Bakar**, **Klepon**, or warm herbal **Jamu** tonic infusions.'),
  ('jawa', 4564, 5, '**Families:** Friendly local street markets, casual family restaurants, and heritage eateries serving mild, non-spicy staples like fried rice (*Nasi Goreng*), chicken satay, and sweet corn fritters (*Perkedel Jagung*).'),
  ('jawa', 4564, 6, '**Honeymooners:** Romantic candlelit dining overlooking illuminated ancient temples, fine-dining Javanese rijsttafel experiences in Yogyakarta, or private sunset dinners in the Bandung highlands.'),
  ('jawa', 4564, 7, '**Luxury travelers:** Exclusive chef-curated royal Javanese banquets inside restored palaces (*Kraton*), private farm-to-table dining overlooking rice terraces, and high-end fusion restaurants in Jakarta and Surakarta (Solo).'),
  ('jawa', 4564, 8, '**Budget travelers:** Bustling street food lanes and roadside *lesehan* stalls (floor-seating eateries) where filling plates of *Gudeg*, *Nasi Liwet*, or *Mie Jawa* cost just 15,000 to 35,000 IDR ($1.00–$2.30 USD).'),
  ('jawa', 4564, 9, '**Foodies:** Culinary walking tours through Yogyakarta, Solo, and Semarang to sample heritage street recipes, traditional night markets, and iconic Chinese-Javanese fusion dishes.'),
  ('jawa', 4564, 10, '**Yogyakarta & Solo (Central Java):** Best for classic sweet Javanese culinary traditions, authentic *Gudeg*, *Nasi Liwet*, *Sate Buntel*, and vibrant evening *lesehan* street dining.'),
  ('jawa', 4564, 11, '**Semarang (Central Java Coast):** Best for historic Chinese-Javanese heritage dishes, including authentic *Lumpia Semarang* (spring rolls), *Tahu Gimbal*, and fresh coastal seafood.'),
  ('jawa', 4564, 12, '**Bandung & West Java Highlands:** Best for fresh Sundanese cuisine, *Sunda Lalapan*, *Batagor* (fried fish dumplings), *Siomay*, and trendy highland cafes with cooler mountain climates.'),
  ('jawa', 4564, 13, '**Surabaya & East Java:** Best for bold, savory flavors such as dark beef soup (*Rawon* sweetened with keluak nuts), *Rujak Cingur*, and East Javanese style satay.'),
  ('jawa', 4565, 0, '**Authentic Batik Textiles:** Hand-drawn (*Batik Tulis*) and hand-stamped (*Batik Cap*) fabrics, sarongs, and apparel from the historic textile centers of Yogyakarta, Solo, and Pekalongan.'),
  ('jawa', 4565, 1, '**Wayang Leather & Wooden Puppets:** Intricately carved and hand-painted Shadow Puppets (*Wayang Kulit*) and wooden rod puppets (*Wayang Golek*), representing classical Javanese epics.'),
  ('jawa', 4565, 2, '**Javanese Silverware & Jewelry:** Fine silver filigree jewelry, tea sets, and ornamental crafts from the historic Kota Gede district in Yogyakarta.'),
  ('jawa', 4565, 3, '**Single-Origin Javanese Coffee:** Premium Arabica and Robusta coffee beans, including Mount Malabar, Preanger, Mount Bromo, and West Java specialty roasts.'),
  ('jawa', 4565, 4, '**Traditional Antiques & Crafts:** Vintage Javanese woodcarvings, brass oil lamps, Gamelan instruments, and handmade ceramic pottery from Kasongan.'),
  ('jawa', 4565, 5, '**Malioboro Street & Pasar Beringharjo (Yogyakarta):** Best for affordable Javanese Batik, leather goods, Wayang puppets, local handicrafts, and traditional street snacks.'),
  ('jawa', 4565, 6, '**Kota Gede District (Yogyakarta):** Preferred for authentic, high-quality silver filigree workshops, custom jewelry, and artisan silversmith demonstrations.'),
  ('jawa', 4565, 7, '**Pasar Triwindu (Solo / Surakarta):** Ideal for antique hunting, vintage Javanese homeware, brass artifacts, retro curios, and rare heritage collectibles.'),
  ('jawa', 4565, 8, '**Grand Indonesia & Plaza Indonesia (Jakarta):** Premier destinations for high-end luxury fashion, modern Indonesian designer boutiques, and upscale Batik galleries like Danar Hadi and Batik Keris.'),
  ('jawa', 4565, 9, 'Purchasing low-quality printed fabric marketed as authentic "Batik Tulis"; real hand-waxed Batik shows visible design patterns on both sides of the cloth and commands higher prices.'),
  ('jawa', 4565, 10, 'Buying antique artifacts or historical items without proper authentication certificates, as export restrictions apply to genuine Indonesian national heritage objects.'),
  ('jawa', 4565, 11, 'Transporting fragile Kasongan ceramics or heavy wooden carvings without arranging professional bubble-wrap packing and insured international shipping services.'),
  ('jawa', 4565, 12, '**Textile & Art Collectors:** Enthusiasts seeking museum-quality hand-drawn Batik textiles, fine silverwork, and authentic Javanese folk art.'),
  ('jawa', 4565, 13, '**Souvenir & Craft Enthusiasts:** Travelers looking for unique, budget-friendly handmade gifts like wooden puppets, Batik accessories, and local snacks.'),
  ('jawa', 4565, 14, '**Modern Luxury Shoppers:** Visitors seeking upscale shopping malls, luxury international brands, and contemporary Indonesian fashion designers in Jakarta.'),
  ('jawa', 4566, 0, '**Urban partygoers & clubbers** looking for world-class DJs, high-end rooftop cocktail bars, and multi-level dance clubs in Jakarta and Bandung.'),
  ('jawa', 4566, 1, '**Culture enthusiasts & indie music lovers** seeking late-night acoustic sessions, jazz clubs, shadow puppet shows, and traditional art performances in Yogyakarta and Solo.'),
  ('jawa', 4566, 2, '**Coffee lovers & night-owl students** wanting to socialize at late-night street stalls (*Angkringan*) and trendy 24-hour cafes over local coffee and cheap skewers.'),
  ('jawa', 4566, 3, '**Foodies & night market explorers** looking to sample famous midnight street food specialties like *Nasi Kucing* and *Soto* across Java’s historic city centers.'),
  ('jawa', 4566, 4, 'Enjoying sky-high views and craft cocktails at premier rooftop lounges in **Central Jakarta (SCBD & Menteng)** such as *Skye*, *Henshin*, or *Lucy in the Sky*, followed by high-end nightlife in the mega-club district.'),
  ('jawa', 4566, 5, 'Immersing in Yogyakarta''s relaxed student vibe along **Prawirotaman and Jalan Bergerak**, enjoying live indie bands, craft beer bars, and cozy acoustic cafes.'),
  ('jawa', 4566, 6, 'Experiencing late-night Javanese street culture at an **Angkringan in Yogyakarta or Solo**, sipping *Kopi Joss* (charcoal coffee) while chatting with locals into the early morning hours.'),
  ('jawa', 4566, 7, 'Exploring **Bandung’s hip lounge and bar scene** along *Jalan Riau* and *Jalan Braga*, featuring craft beer houses, speakeasies, and cool mountain-air rooftops.'),
  ('jawa', 4566, 8, 'Drinking unverified or unlabelled local home-brewed spirits (*arak*); stick strictly to commercial bottled beers like Bintang, imported spirits, or drinks from reputable bars and hotel lounges.'),
  ('jawa', 4566, 9, 'Overlooking dress codes at Jakarta’s high-end SCBD and Mega Kuningan clubs, where flip-flops, shorts, and singlets are strictly prohibited at entry.'),
  ('jawa', 4566, 10, 'Expecting late-night alcohol-driven nightlife during the holy month of Ramadan, when nightlife operating hours across Javanese cities are strictly regulated or altered.'),
  ('jawa', 4566, 11, '**SCBD & Mega Kuningan (Jakarta):** The ultimate epicenter of Javanese luxury nightlife, packed with upscale rooftop bars, speakeasies, and premier nightclubs.'),
  ('jawa', 4566, 12, '**Prawirotaman & Tirtodipuran (Yogyakarta):** The main social enclave for international travelers and local creatives, featuring lively bars, live music venues, and cozy cafes.'),
  ('jawa', 4566, 13, '**Jalan Braga & Dago Upper (Bandung):** Best for atmospheric colonial street bars, trendy night lounges, and scenic mountain-view rooftop venues.'),
  ('jawa', 4566, 14, '**Kota Tua & Pantai Indah Kapuk (Jakarta):** Best for vibrant night markets, waterfront dining hubs, late-night dessert cafes, and bustling craft beer bars.'),
  ('jawa', 4574, 0, 'Treat Java like a quick island getaway, severely underestimating its massive 1,000-kilometer length, intense highway congestion, and complex logistics between major hubs like Jakarta, Yogyakarta, Mount Bromo, and Ijen.'),
  ('jawa', 4574, 1, 'Schedule tight overland drives across East Java (e.g., trying to drive directly from Yogyakarta to Mount Bromo in a single afternoon), trapping clients in 10-to-12-hour traffic jams instead of utilizing high-speed Executive Trains.'),
  ('jawa', 4574, 2, 'Over-pack itineraries by squeezing West, Central, and East Java into a brief 7-to-8-day window, resulting in clients spending more time in vans and train stations than exploring UNESCO sites or volcanoes.'),
  ('jawa', 4574, 3, 'Fail to account for peak morning crowds and strict entry slot restrictions at **Borobudur Temple**, leaving clients stuck with standard ground tickets instead of reserved temple-structure ascension passes.'),
  ('jawa', 4574, 4, 'Book clients on Mount Bromo or Ijen volcano tours without arranging private 4x4 Jeeps, proper cold-weather gear, or safety briefings, exposing travelers to chaotic public transport and unsafe crater scrambles.'),
  ('jawa', 4575, 0, 'Connects key regions seamlessly using Java’s premier **Executive Trains** (such as the *Argo Wilis* or *Sancaka* routes) to bypass unpredictable highway traffic between Jakarta, Yogyakarta, and Surabaya.'),
  ('jawa', 4575, 1, 'Secures advance VIP ascension tickets for **Borobudur Temple** to ensure clients walk the upper monument terraces alongside expert heritage guides during low-density time slots.'),
  ('jawa', 4575, 2, 'Partners with professional private 4x4 Jeep operators and local rangers in **Mount Bromo** and **Ijen**, ensuring private sunrise viewpoints away from peak tour-bus crowds and providing high-quality safety gear.'),
  ('jawa', 4575, 3, 'Organizes private high-clearance executive MPVs or SUVs with experienced local drivers for smooth highland transfers in Batu, Malang, and the Bromo caldera.'),
  ('jawa', 4575, 4, 'Pairs demanding early-morning volcano treks with relaxing stays at luxury heritage hotels or high-end highland resorts to balance physical activity with client rest and comfort.'),
  ('jawa', 4576, 0, 'For **Geographic & Logistics Strategy**, use Executive Trains for long inter-city legs (Jakarta → Yogyakarta → East Java) and reserve flights into Surabaya (SUB) or Yogyakarta (YIA) to maximize sightseeing time.'),
  ('jawa', 4576, 1, 'For **Heritage & Monument Access**, book Borobudur ascension passes weeks in advance and schedule visits during early morning hours to beat the tropical heat and large student tour groups.'),
  ('jawa', 4576, 2, 'For **Volcano & Highland Logistics**, limit early-morning wakeup calls to non-consecutive days, ensuring dedicated afternoon downtime or spa sessions after pre-dawn Bromo or Ijen excursions.'),
  ('jawa', 4579, 0, 'Observe semi-wild orangutans, sun bears, and proboscis monkeys in Sepilok, Labuk Bay, and along the Kinabatangan River safaris.'),
  ('jawa', 4579, 1, 'Immerse yourself in the primary rainforest of Danum Valley or Maliau Basin with canopy walks and night 4x4 wildlife safaris.'),
  ('jawa', 4579, 2, 'Snorkel or dive the crystal-clear marine sanctuaries of Tunku Abdul Rahman Marine Park or world-famous Sipadan Island.'),
  ('jawa', 4579, 3, 'Explore the rich indigenous cultures and historic riverfronts of Kuching, tasting authentic Sarawak Laksa and Dayak *Tuak*.'),
  ('jawa', 4579, 4, 'Marvel at the grand granite peaks of Mount Kinabalu or explore the colossal karst cave passages in Gunung Mulu National Park.'),
  ('jawa', 4579, 5, 'Attempting to cover both Sabah and Sarawak in under 7 days using only long overland road journeys without leveraging short domestic flights.'),
  ('jawa', 4579, 6, 'Underestimating transfer times and boat schedules between coastal towns, river lodges, and deep jungle reserves.'),
  ('jawa', 4579, 7, 'Booking unaccredited guides or unethical wildlife operators that disregard conservation standards and animal welfare protocols.');
INSERT INTO destination_guidance_bullet (place_id, position, bullet_index, text) VALUES
  ('jawa', 4579, 8, 'Forgetting high-quality tropical rain gear, leech socks, and insect repellent for rainforest treks.'),
  ('jawa', 4580, 0, 'To be populated with authoritative tourism/transport/attraction sources before production use.'),
  ('bornea-island', 4584, 0, 'Take advantage of shared express minivans or public express buses (approx. 30–50 MYR / ~$7–$12 USD in Malaysia or 150,000–250,000 IDR / ~$8–$14 USD in Kalimantan) to navigate major transit routes between cities like Kota Kinabalu, Sandakan, Kuching, and Pontianak.'),
  ('bornea-island', 4584, 1, 'Focus daily dining on local hawker stalls and roadside *kopitiam* or *warungs*, where classic regional dishes like *Sarawak Laksa*, *Kolo Mee*, *Nasi Goreng*, and fresh seafood stir-fries cost just 8 to 18 MYR ($2.00–$4.50 USD) or 25,000 to 50,000 IDR ($1.40–$2.80 USD) per plate.'),
  ('bornea-island', 4584, 2, 'Book authentic, family-run eco-guesthouses or traditional longhouse stays along the Kinabatangan River, near Sepilok, or in Bako National Park, which offer clean, scenic private accommodations for $12 to $30 USD per night.'),
  ('bornea-island', 4584, 3, 'Stock up on regional snacks, local fruits, and bottled water at night markets like Kuching’s Siniawan or Kota Kinabalu’s Waterfront Night Market for affordable, high-energy fuel during long overland transit days.'),
  ('bornea-island', 4584, 4, 'Rent a scooter in main regional hubs like Kuching or Kota Kinabalu (approx. 40–60 MYR / ~$10–$15 USD per day) to independently explore nearby beaches, national park entrances, and cultural villages without paying for expensive private taxi hires.'),
  ('bornea-island', 4584, 5, 'Skimping on licensed, accredited wildlife guides or official park permits when trekking in deep rainforest sanctuaries like Danum Valley, Deramakot, or Tanjung Puting; uncertified operators endanger native habitats and compromise safety during wildlife encounters.'),
  ('bornea-island', 4584, 6, 'Relying solely on local public transit when adhering to tight itineraries, as regional bus schedules can be infrequent, and riverboat transfers in interior jungle regions are strictly subject to weather and water level delays.'),
  ('bornea-island', 4584, 7, 'Venturing into remote national parks or deep interior Dayak settlements without carrying sufficient physical cash (MYR or IDR); local ATMs are non-existent outside main towns, and electronic payment systems are not accepted in remote lodges.'),
  ('bornea-island', 4584, 8, 'Skipping comprehensive travel and adventure insurance, especially when undertaking high-risk outdoor activities like climbing Mount Kinabalu, deep cave explorations in Mulu, or scuba diving in remote archipelago reefs.'),
  ('bornea-island', 4585, 0, '4+'),
  ('bornea-island', 4585, 1, '6+'),
  ('bornea-island', 4585, 2, '8+'),
  ('bornea-island', 4585, 3, 'Teenagers'),
  ('bornea-island', 4585, 4, 'Leave strollers behind and pack an ergonomic, breathable toddler carrier; unpaved jungle trails, wooden boardwalks, steep boat gangways, and uneven city sidewalks render wheeled strollers completely impractical across national parks and island docks.'),
  ('bornea-island', 4585, 5, 'Book private air-conditioned MPV transfers (such as a Toyota Innova) for long overland transit; regional drives between Kota Kinabalu, Sandakan, Sepilok, and Kuching involve multi-hour winding mountain roads where private drivers can accommodate essential bathroom, meal, and motion-sickness stops.'),
  ('bornea-island', 4585, 6, 'Select kid-friendly wildlife sanctuaries and structured eco-lodges for animal encounters; controlled environments like the Sepilok Orangutan Rehabilitation Centre, Bornean Sun Bear Conservation Centre, and guided Kinabatangan River boat cruises offer safe, high-visibility wildlife viewing without strenuous multi-day jungle marches.'),
  ('bornea-island', 4585, 7, 'Maintain strict safety protocols around wild animals; teach children never to display open snacks, reach out to touch, or make direct eye contact with macaque monkeys or wild primates, as inquisitive animals can quickly snatch loose items or act defensively.'),
  ('bornea-island', 4585, 8, 'Pack a dedicated tropical health kit containing child-safe insect repellent, lightweight long-sleeve rash guards and trekking clothes, rehydration salts, waterproof sun protection, and motion-sickness medication for choppy riverboat transfers and winding highland drives.'),
  ('bornea-island', 4585, 9, 'Ease kids into regional food with popular, non-spicy Bornean staples like *Chicken Kolo Mee* (tossed noodles), *Nasi Goreng* (fried rice), *Sate Ayam* (grilled chicken skewers), and fresh tropical fruit juices before introducing heavily spiced dishes or hawker specialties.'),
  ('bornea-island', 4586, 0, 'honeymoon_score: 88'),
  ('bornea-island', 4586, 1, 'romance_score: 90'),
  ('bornea-island', 4586, 2, 'privacy_score: 86'),
  ('bornea-island', 4586, 3, 'luxury_score: 85'),
  ('bornea-island', 4588, 0, 'Summiting Mount Kinabalu (4,095 meters)—Southeast Asia''s iconic alpine peak—to catch the sunrise above the clouds and tackle the world''s highest via ferrata route.'),
  ('bornea-island', 4588, 1, 'Trekking deep into the primary rainforest of Danum Valley and Deramakot Conservation Area to spot wild orangutans, clouded leopards, and pygmy elephants on night safaris.'),
  ('bornea-island', 4588, 2, 'Exploring the massive subterranean chambers of Gunung Mulu National Park, watching millions of bats emerge from Deer Cave, and climbing the razor-sharp karst limestone Pinnacles.'),
  ('bornea-island', 4588, 3, 'Scuba diving the world-renowned oceanic drop-offs, barracuda points, and rich coral walls off Sipadan Island and the Derawan Archipelago.'),
  ('bornea-island', 4588, 4, 'Embarking on multi-day jungle river expeditions along the Kinabatangan and Rajang Rivers to reach remote indigenous Dayak longhouses and interior wildlife habitats.'),
  ('bornea-island', 4588, 5, '**Gunung Mulu National Park (Sarawak)** — best for world-class cave exploration, technical karst Pinnacle climbing, bat exodus spectacles, and deep jungle canopy walks.'),
  ('bornea-island', 4588, 6, '**Kinabatangan River & Danum Valley (Sabah)** — best for primary rainforest trekking, river safari wildlife tracking, night jungle walks, and rare mammal spotting.'),
  ('bornea-island', 4588, 7, '**Mount Kinabalu & Crocker Range (Sabah)** — best for high-altitude alpine mountain climbing, via ferrata thrill routes, and mountain ridge trekking.'),
  ('bornea-island', 4588, 8, '**Sipadan & Mabul Islands (Sabah)** — best for world-class oceanic wall diving, marine turtle encounters, and pelagic fish photography.'),
  ('bornea-island', 4588, 9, 'Mountain climbers, high-altitude trekkers, and alpine thrill-seekers.'),
  ('bornea-island', 4588, 10, 'Wildlife trackers, jungle expeditioners, and rainforest eco-adventurers.'),
  ('bornea-island', 4588, 11, 'Cavers, speleologists, and karst terrain hikers.'),
  ('bornea-island', 4588, 12, 'Advanced scuba divers and marine wildlife photographers.'),
  ('bornea-island', 4588, 13, 'Intrepid travelers and off-the-beaten-path river explorers.'),
  ('bornea-island', 4589, 0, 'Schedule wildlife cruises, sanctuary visits, and light walks during early morning hours (6:30 AM–9:30 AM) to enjoy cooler temperatures and active wildlife before midday heat sets in.'),
  ('bornea-island', 4589, 1, 'Book private air-conditioned multi-purpose vehicles (MPVs, such as a Toyota Innova) with experienced local driver-guides for overland transfers between airports, Sepilok, and river lodges.'),
  ('bornea-island', 4589, 2, 'Select eco-lodges along the Kinabatangan River or near Sepilok that feature ground-floor chalets, flat wooden walkways, and handrails for easy access to dining areas and boat docks.'),
  ('bornea-island', 4589, 3, 'Utilize gentle, flat river cruises along the Kinabatangan River or Sarawak River rather than strenuous foot treks for wildlife viewing and sightseeing.'),
  ('bornea-island', 4589, 4, 'Wear sturdy, lightweight walking shoes or non-slip hiking sandals with good ankle support when navigating wooden boardwalks, boat docks, and village paths.'),
  ('bornea-island', 4589, 5, 'Carry a comprehensive health kit with daily prescription medications, child-safe insect repellent, rehydration salts, and basic antidiarrheal remedies, as specialized pharmacies are scarce outside major urban hubs.'),
  ('bornea-island', 4589, 6, 'Plan midday rest periods in air-conditioned rooms or shaded riverfront lounges during peak equatorial heat hours (12:00 PM–3:00 PM).'),
  ('bornea-island', 4589, 7, 'Visiting Sepilok Orangutan Rehabilitation Centre, Bornean Sun Bear Conservation Centre, and Labuk Bay Proboscis Monkey Sanctuary via paved, level boardwalks with shaded viewing platforms.'),
  ('bornea-island', 4589, 8, 'Exploring Kuching’s historic waterfront promenade, riverfront heritage sites, and flat indoor museums like the Borneo Cultures Museum, which features full elevator accessibility.'),
  ('bornea-island', 4589, 9, 'Taking guided electric buggies or private vehicle tours through the Sarawak Cultural Village to learn about Dayak longhouses and traditional crafts without excessive walking.'),
  ('bornea-island', 4589, 10, 'Enjoying scenic, flat boat safaris along the Kinabatangan River to spot wild pygmy elephants, proboscis monkeys, and hornbills directly from comfortable boat seating.'),
  ('bornea-island', 4589, 11, 'Dining on gentle, non-spicy regional specialties, fresh seafood, and tropical fruits at clean, well-ventilated sit-down restaurants in Kota Kinabalu or Kuching.'),
  ('bornea-island', 4589, 12, 'Attempting the strenuous, multi-day high-altitude ascent of Mount Kinabalu or the technical, steep climb up the razor-sharp karst Pinnacles at Gunung Mulu National Park.'),
  ('bornea-island', 4589, 13, 'Undertaking off-grid, unpaved deep jungle treks in Danum Valley or Deramakot that require negotiating steep mud inclines, river crossings, and heavy leech activity.'),
  ('bornea-island', 4589, 14, 'Using local public buses or unmetered minivans for long inter-city journeys due to irregular schedules, tight seating, and limited air conditioning.'),
  ('bornea-island', 4589, 15, 'Walking on wet wooden boardwalks or unpaved forest trails immediately following heavy tropical downpours when surfaces become hazardous and slippery.'),
  ('bornea-island', 4589, 16, 'Scheduling tight overland transfers after dark across winding mountain highways between Kota Kinabalu and Sandakan due to limited road lighting and frequent fog.'),
  ('bornea-island', 4591, 0, 'Slurp a steaming bowl of **Sarawak Laksa**, the iconic regional specialty praised for its complex, aromatic broth of coconut milk, sambal belacan, tamarind, garlic, galangal, and lemongrass, topped with prawns and shredded chicken.'),
  ('bornea-island', 4591, 1, 'Feast on **Midim** (or *Midin*), a wild, crunchy jungle fern indigenous to Borneo, flash-fried with garlic or spicy shrimp paste (*belacan*).'),
  ('bornea-island', 4591, 2, 'Sample authentic Dayak longhouse dishes like **Manok Pansoh**, tender chicken marinated with lemongrass and ginger, then slow-cooked inside a sealed bamboo stalk over an open fire.'),
  ('bornea-island', 4591, 3, 'Relish a bowl of **Kolo Mee**, springy egg noodles tossed in a savory shallot and lard dressing, topped with minced pork, char siu, and fresh green onions.'),
  ('bornea-island', 4591, 4, 'Indulge in ultra-fresh, affordable **Coastal Seafood** at night markets in Kota Kinabalu or Semporna, choosing live butter prawns, chili crab, and grilled red snapper straight from the tanks.'),
  ('bornea-island', 4591, 5, '**Families:** Lively riverfront night markets and casual hawker centers serving universally loved dishes like satay skewers, mild fried rice (*Nasi Goreng*), fresh tropical fruit juices, and sweet coconut shaved ice (*ABC/Cendol*).'),
  ('bornea-island', 4591, 6, '**Honeymooners:** Romantic waterfront dining overlooking the South China Sea in Kota Kinabalu or private seafood barbecues under the stars at eco-resorts on Gaya Island.'),
  ('bornea-island', 4591, 7, '**Luxury travelers:** Exclusive chef-curated tasting menus inside wilderness eco-lodges in Danum Valley and private sunset champagne and seafood cruises along the Sarawak River.'),
  ('bornea-island', 4591, 8, '**Budget travelers:** Highly affordable hawker stalls and local *kopitiams* where hearty bowls of Sarawak Laksa, Kolo Mee, or Tuaran Mee cost just 8 to 18 MYR ($2.00–$4.50 USD) or 25,000 to 50,000 IDR ($1.40–$2.80 USD).'),
  ('bornea-island', 4591, 9, '**Foodies:** Culinary walking tours through Kuching and Kota Kinabalu to uncover secret hawker stalls, indigenous rainforest herbs, and regional coffee house customs.'),
  ('bornea-island', 4591, 10, '**Kuching (Sarawak):** Best for the ultimate food capital experience, renowned worldwide for Sarawak Laksa, Kolo Mee, wild jungle ferns, and historic riverfront hawker centers.'),
  ('bornea-island', 4591, 11, '**Kota Kinabalu (Sabah):** Best for bustling night markets, waterfront dining, live seafood markets, Tuaran noodles, and Sabah pork sang nyuk mee.'),
  ('bornea-island', 4591, 12, '**Sandakan (Sabah):** Best for heritage seafood, famous UFO tarts, coconut puddings, and historic coffee shops reflecting strong Cantonese culinary roots.'),
  ('bornea-island', 4591, 13, '**Pontianak & Samarinda (Kalimantan):** Best for Indonesian-Bornean fusion, rich *Soto Banjar* chicken soup, seafood dishes cooked in bamboo, and riverfront night stalls.'),
  ('bornea-island', 4592, 0, '**Sarawak Pepper & Spices:** World-renowned, high-grade white and black peppercorns, pepper sauces, and wild jungle spice blends sourced directly from Sarawak plantations.'),
  ('bornea-island', 4592, 1, '**Indigenous Dayak Beadwork & Rattan:** Intricately woven rattan backpacks (*pasa*), woven floor mats, beaded accessories, and traditional Dayak sunhats (*sa''ong*).'),
  ('bornea-island', 4592, 2, '**Pua Kumbu Textiles:** Hand-woven, natural-dyed sacred ceremonial cotton textiles created by indigenous Iban weavers featuring traditional tribal motifs.'),
  ('bornea-island', 4592, 3, '**Bornean Woodcarvings & Shields:** Hand-carved hardwood tribal masks, ornamental Dayak warrior shields, parang swords, and traditional wooden blowpipes.'),
  ('bornea-island', 4592, 4, '**Local Pearls & Artisanal Crafts:** Cultured South Sea pearls, mother-of-pearl jewelry, and seashell handicrafts from coastal markets in Sabah (Kota Kinabalu and Semporna).'),
  ('bornea-island', 4592, 5, '**Main Bazaar & Carpenter Street (Kuching):** Best for authentic Sarawak antiques, Pua Kumbu textiles, tribal woodcarvings, pepper products, and local pottery along historic shopfronts.'),
  ('bornea-island', 4592, 6, '**Kota Kinabalu Handicraft Market (Sabah):** Ideal for cultured pearls, beaded jewelry, woven basketry, traditional instruments, and seaside souvenirs.'),
  ('bornea-island', 4592, 7, '**Sarawak Cultural Village & Craft Council Outlets:** Preferred for certified authentic, high-quality indigenous handicrafts and fair-trade Dayak artisan goods.'),
  ('bornea-island', 4592, 8, '**Gaya Street Sunday Market (Kota Kinabalu):** Perfect for browsing local crafts, regional snacks, tropical plants, and street souvenirs in a vibrant weekly market setting.'),
  ('bornea-island', 4592, 9, 'Purchasing items made from protected or endangered wildlife, including turtle shells, shark teeth, bird feathers, or unverified animal parts, which violate international conservation laws (CITES).'),
  ('bornea-island', 4592, 10, 'Buying mass-produced resin or plastic replicas labeled as authentic Dayak tribal antiques; always buy from reputable craft councils or established heritage shops.'),
  ('bornea-island', 4592, 11, 'Expecting fixed prices at informal night markets and craft stalls; polite, friendly bargaining is customary, whereas prices in official government craft centers and city boutiques are fixed.'),
  ('bornea-island', 4592, 12, '**Culture & Craft Lovers:** Travelers seeking rare tribal textiles, authentic Dayak beadwork, and hand-carved wood art directly from indigenous artisans.'),
  ('bornea-island', 4592, 13, '**Culinary Enthusiasts:** Visitors wanting to purchase world-famous Sarawak pepper, local coffee, and regional jungle condiments.'),
  ('bornea-island', 4592, 14, '**Souvenir Collectors & Bargain Hunters:** Travelers hunting for handmade pearls, woven rattan goods, and traditional handicrafts in atmospheric waterfront bazaars.'),
  ('bornea-island', 4593, 0, '**Sunset lovers & waterfront socializers** seeking cold sunset beers and craft cocktails along the South China Sea in Kota Kinabalu or the Sarawak River in Kuching.'),
  ('bornea-island', 4593, 1, '**Foodies & night-market explorers** wanting to graze through bustling night bazaars past midnight for fresh seafood, local satay, and regional desserts.'),
  ('bornea-island', 4593, 2, '**Backpackers & jungle adventurers** looking to swap trekking stories over cold Bintang or Tuak (local rice wine) at cozy guesthouse bars in Sepilok or Kuching.'),
  ('bornea-island', 4593, 3, '**Urban lounge-goers** looking for modern pub venues, live cover bands, and rooftop bars in major hubs like Kota Kinabalu, Kuching, or Balikpapan.'),
  ('bornea-island', 4593, 4, 'Gathering at the waterfront bars along **Waterfront Esplanade in Kota Kinabalu** and **Jalan Waterfront in Kuching** for live band sets, craft drinks, and refreshing river breezes.'),
  ('bornea-island', 4593, 5, 'Exploring vibrant evening markets like **Siniawan Night Market** near Kuching or the **KK Waterfront Night Market** for late-night street dining and local social atmospheres.'),
  ('bornea-island', 4593, 6, 'Sampling traditional Dayak rice wine (*Tuak*) at cultural craft bars and heritage venues in Kuching.'),
  ('bornea-island', 4593, 7, 'Unwinding at cozy hotel bars, live sports pubs, and rooftop lounges in central city districts across Kota Kinabalu, Kuching, and Balikpapan.'),
  ('bornea-island', 4593, 8, 'Expecting public bars, alcohol sales, or late-night clubbing in **Brunei (Bandar Seri Begawan)**, where alcohol is not sold publicly and nightlife centers around alcohol-free night markets and royal landmarks.'),
  ('bornea-island', 4593, 9, 'Searching for multi-story electronic dance mega-clubs; nightlife outside major regional capitals is predominantly low-key, acoustic, and winds down around 11:00 PM.'),
  ('bornea-island', 4593, 10, 'Consuming unverified local home-brewed spirits (*langkau* or unregulated moonshine); stick to commercial beers, reputable wine, or certified craft *tuak* from established venues.'),
  ('bornea-island', 4593, 11, '**Kota Kinabalu Waterfront & Waterfront Promenade (Sabah):** The primary nightlife hub for travelers in Borneo, packed with seaside pubs, live music venues, seafood markets, and cocktail lounges.'),
  ('bornea-island', 4593, 12, '**Kuching Riverfront & Carpenter Street (Sarawak):** Best for atmospheric heritage dining, cozy craft bars, historic *kopitiams*, and live acoustic music along the river.'),
  ('bornea-island', 4593, 13, '**Siniawan Night Market (Sarawak):** Best for a festive weekend night market experience under lit lanterns, surrounded by historic wooden shop-houses and street food stalls.'),
  ('bornea-island', 4593, 14, '**Balikpapan & Pontianak Riverfronts (Kalimantan):** Best for bustling Indonesian-style night markets, riverfront cafe gatherings, and lively local coffee shop culture (*kopitiam/warung kopi*).'),
  ('bornea-island', 4601, 0, 'Treat Borneo like a single unified island, failing to realize it is split between Malaysia (Sabah and Sarawak), Indonesia (Kalimantan), and Brunei, leading to impossible overland logisitics across international borders.'),
  ('bornea-island', 4601, 1, 'Underestimate internal transfer times between primary rainforests and coastal hubs, assuming quick road connections between **Kota Kinabalu**, **Danum Valley**, and **Kuching** without utilizing essential domestic flight connections.'),
  ('bornea-island', 4601, 2, 'Over-pack itineraries by attempting to cover Sabah''s wildlife reserves and Sarawak''s cultural heritage in less than a week, leaving travelers constantly in transit via regional airports and long river transfers.'),
  ('bornea-island', 4601, 3, 'Fail to account for unpredictable rainforest weather patterns and high humidity, scheduling strenuous canopy walks or wildlife treks during peak midday heat rather than early morning hours.'),
  ('bornea-island', 4601, 4, 'Book unaccredited jungle guides in sensitive eco-zones like **Kinabatangan River** or **Sepilok**, exposing clients to poor safety standards, lack of leech protection/child gear, or irresponsible wildlife feeding practices.'),
  ('bornea-island', 4602, 0, 'Structures Borneo itineraries around logical aviation hubs—using **Kota Kinabalu (BKI)** for Sabah''s islands and Kinabalu Park, **Sandakan (SDK)** or **Lahad Datu (LDU)** for wildlife/Danum Valley, and **Kuching (KCH)** for Sarawak''s culture and Bako National Park.'),
  ('bornea-island', 4602, 1, 'Reserves luxury eco-lodges like **Borneo Rainforest Lodge** or **Gaya Island Resort** months in advance to secure limited villa inventory and private naturalist-guided excursions in primary reserves.'),
  ('bornea-island', 4602, 2, 'Schedules river safaris and canopy walks during early dawn (6:00 AM) or dusk hours to maximize sightings of endemic wild proboscis monkeys, pygmy elephants, and hornbills while avoiding mid-afternoon heat.'),
  ('bornea-island', 4602, 3, 'Arranges private speedboat charters for Marine Park island transfers and Bako National Park sea stack excursions, allowing clients to bypass crowded public ferry terminals.'),
  ('bornea-island', 4602, 4, 'Incorporates built-in downtime and buffer days between intense rainforest treks and coastal resort stays, ensuring clients enjoy spa wellness and beachfront relaxation without feeling rushed.'),
  ('bornea-island', 4603, 0, 'For **Geographic & Aviation Strategy**, group destinations strictly by state (Sabah OR Sarawak) for trips under 8 days, utilizing short domestic flights between Kota Kinabalu, Sandakan/Lahad Datu, and Kuching to eliminate 10+ hour overland drives.'),
  ('bornea-island', 4603, 1, 'For **Wildlife & Eco-Trekking Logistics**, always secure certified senior park rangers or lodge naturalists for Danum Valley and Bako National Park, scheduling all major outdoor treks for dawn or late afternoon.'),
  ('bornea-island', 4603, 2, 'For **Comfort & Transit Balance**, pair immersive primary rainforest stays with luxury beachfront or island resorts, limiting continuous road/river transfers to under 3 hours per segment to manage humidity and energy levels.'),
  ('bornea-island', 4606, 0, 'Track wild and semi-wild Bornean orangutans, pygmy elephants, and proboscis monkeys in Danum Valley Conservation Area, Sepilok, or along the Kinabatangan River.'),
  ('bornea-island', 4606, 1, 'Experience the treetop canopy walkways and ancient rainforest mist in Danum Valley or witness the spectacular bat exodus at Mulu National Park.'),
  ('bornea-island', 4606, 2, 'Snorkel or dive in the turquoise marine sanctuaries of Tunku Abdul Rahman Marine Park or Sipadan Island.'),
  ('bornea-island', 4606, 3, 'Sample authentic Bornean cuisine—including fresh Sabah butter prawns, iconic Sarawak Laksa, Kolo Mee, and traditional Dayak rice wine (*Tuak*).'),
  ('bornea-island', 4606, 4, 'Marvel at the towering granite peaks of Mount Kinabalu in Kinabalu Park and walk the coastal trails of Bako National Park to spot bearded pigs and silvered langurs.'),
  ('bornea-island', 4606, 5, 'Attempting to cover both Sabah and Sarawak entirely via long overland road drives in under 7 days without utilizing regional domestic flights.'),
  ('bornea-island', 4606, 6, 'Underestimating transfer times into deep rainforest reserves like Danum Valley or Maliau Basin, which require high-clearance 4WD vehicles over gravel tracks.'),
  ('bornea-island', 4606, 7, 'Hiring unaccredited or independent guides for primary rainforest trekking who lack proper safety protocols, leech protection gear, or wildlife safety standards.'),
  ('bornea-island', 4606, 8, 'Expecting fast-paced urban highways; Borneo’s natural beauty relies on remote wilderness logistics that require flexible, patient trip planning.'),
  ('bornea-island', 4607, 0, 'To be populated with authoritative tourism/transport/attraction sources before production use.'),
  ('angkor-wat', 4611, 0, 'Opt for multi-day official Angkor Passes ($62 USD for a 3-day pass or $72 USD for a 7-day pass) rather than single-day tickets ($37 USD), as multi-day passes offer significantly lower daily entry costs and allow flexible non-consecutive temple visits.'),
  ('angkor-wat', 4611, 1, 'Hire a local tuk-tuk for the entire day (approx. $15–$25 USD) directly via ride-hailing apps like PassApp or Grab or through your hotel, and split the cost with fellow travelers to easily cover the vast temple circuits.'),
  ('angkor-wat', 4611, 2, 'Dine at local family-run eateries and food stalls located just outside the main temple gates or around Siem Reap''s local markets, where traditional Cambodian meals like *Bai Sach Chrouk* or *Lort Cha* cost just $2.50 to $4.50 USD per dish.'),
  ('angkor-wat', 4611, 3, 'Stay in Siem Reap’s budget-friendly guesthouses or social hostels ($8–$18 USD per night for private or dorm options) equipped with free bicycle rentals, which can be used for zero-cost transit into Siem Reap town and nearby countryside villages.'),
  ('angkor-wat', 4611, 4, 'Refill reusable water bottles at filtration stations offered by hostels and restaurants, or purchase multi-packs of bottled water in Siem Reap town, avoiding the inflated price markup on cold drinks inside the temple park.'),
  ('angkor-wat', 4611, 5, 'Purchasing the 3-Day or 7-Day Angkor Pass ($62–$72 USD) is a mandatory government requirement; attempting to skip or buy unauthorized, discounted passes from unofficial street vendors will lead to entry denial, heavy fines, or confiscation at park checkpoints.'),
  ('angkor-wat', 4611, 6, 'Skipping a licensed local temple guide (approx. $30–$45 USD per day) for key sites like Angkor Wat, Bayon, and Ta Prohm, as their expertise is essential for understanding complex Khmer history, Hindu-Buddhist iconography, and hidden architectural details.'),
  ('angkor-wat', 4611, 7, 'Sacrificing proper hydration, sun protection, and sturdy walking footwear during intense midday heat; skipping water or wearing improper shoes can lead to heat exhaustion and injuries on steep, uneven ancient stone stairways.'),
  ('angkor-wat', 4611, 8, 'Skimping on accredited transportation during sunrise or sunset excursions; relying on unverified drivers in the dark can result in missed early morning entry times or being stranded at outer temple ruins like Banteay Srei or Beng Mealea.'),
  ('angkor-wat', 4612, 0, '6+'),
  ('angkor-wat', 4612, 1, '8+'),
  ('angkor-wat', 4612, 2, '10+'),
  ('angkor-wat', 4612, 3, 'Teenagers'),
  ('angkor-wat', 4612, 4, 'Leave traditional strollers behind and rely on an ergonomic baby/toddler carrier; uneven stone pathways, high door thresholds, crumbling ruins, and steep wooden staircases make strollers virtually unusable inside the temples.'),
  ('angkor-wat', 4612, 5, 'Hire a dedicated tuk-tuk driver or private air-conditioned vehicle for the entire day; having accessible transport allows families to quickly retreat to their hotel for afternoon pool breaks and naps during peak midday heat.'),
  ('angkor-wat', 4612, 6, 'Note age and safety restrictions at upper temple levels; children under 12 are prohibited from climbing the steep stairs to the central upper sanctuary (Bakan) of Angkor Wat, and narrow unguarded drop-offs require constant supervision.'),
  ('angkor-wat', 4612, 7, 'Plan sight visits during early morning hours starting at 5:30–6:00 AM; early starts allow kids to explore under cooler conditions before tropical humidity and crowds peak.'),
  ('angkor-wat', 4612, 8, 'Pack a family day kit stocked with high-factor sunscreen, wide-brim hats, child-safe insect repellent, rehydration salts, plenty of bottled water, and familiar snacks to sustain energy across large temple grounds.'),
  ('angkor-wat', 4612, 9, 'Stick to child-friendly, non-spicy Cambodian dishes like *Bai Sach Chrouk* (grilled pork over rice), mild *Fish Amok* with coconut milk, or local fried noodles before introducing stronger regional spices.'),
  ('angkor-wat', 4613, 0, 'honeymoon_score: 92'),
  ('angkor-wat', 4613, 1, 'romance_score: 94'),
  ('angkor-wat', 4613, 2, 'privacy_score: 88'),
  ('angkor-wat', 4613, 3, 'luxury_score: 95'),
  ('angkor-wat', 4615, 0, 'Mountain biking and cycling along shaded jungle trails, ancient moat embankments, and hidden earthen tracks connecting outer temple ruins.'),
  ('angkor-wat', 4615, 1, 'Trekking through the dense forest trails of Phnom Kulen National Park to discover ancient riverbed carvings (Kbal Spean) and sacred jungle waterfalls.'),
  ('angkor-wat', 4615, 2, 'Embarking on off-road quad bike or dirt bike tours across the countryside to navigate dusty paths, rice paddies, and remote rural villages.'),
  ('angkor-wat', 4615, 3, 'Kayaking through the submerged mangrove forests and stilted floating villages of Kompong Phluk on Tonle Sap Lake.'),
  ('angkor-wat', 4615, 4, 'Exploring the heavily overgrown, partially unrestored jungle ruins of Beng Mealea and the sprawling, remote pyramid temple complex of Koh Ker.'),
  ('angkor-wat', 4615, 5, '**Central Angkor Archaeological Park** — best for jungle cycling loops, earthen rampart treks, and multi-day temple exploration.'),
  ('angkor-wat', 4615, 6, '**Phnom Kulen National Park** — best for jungle hiking, riverbed carving discoveries, waterfall swimming, and sacred mountain sights.'),
  ('angkor-wat', 4615, 7, '**Tonle Sap Lake & Mangroves** — best for open-water kayaking, floating village boat expeditions, and bird-watching in flooded forests.'),
  ('angkor-wat', 4615, 8, '**Koh Ker & Beng Mealea (Outer Siem Reap)** — best for remote expeditionary ruin exploration, off-the-beaten-path day trips, and jungle trekking.'),
  ('angkor-wat', 4615, 9, 'Cultural adventurers, temple explorers, and history enthusiasts.'),
  ('angkor-wat', 4615, 10, 'Active cyclists, trail riders, and countryside biking travelers.'),
  ('angkor-wat', 4615, 11, 'Off-road riders, quad bike enthusiasts, and rural explorers.'),
  ('angkor-wat', 4615, 12, 'Kayakers, river boaters, and wetland nature explorers.'),
  ('angkor-wat', 4615, 13, 'Photographers and travelers seeking atmospheric, jungle-entangled ruins.'),
  ('angkor-wat', 4616, 0, 'Schedule outdoor temple visits during early morning hours (6:00 AM–9:30 AM) or late afternoons (4:00 PM–6:00 PM) to avoid intense equatorial heat, high humidity, and peak tour bus crowds.'),
  ('angkor-wat', 4616, 1, 'Hire private air-conditioned vehicles (such as a Toyota Innova or SUV) with professional local driver-guides for seamless temple transfers, cold bottled water, and air-conditioned rest stops between ruins.'),
  ('angkor-wat', 4616, 2, 'Reserve accommodations at heritage hotels or boutique resorts featuring ground-floor suites or modern elevator access, as many traditional properties feature multi-level layouts without lifts.'),
  ('angkor-wat', 4616, 3, 'Wear sturdy, non-slip supportive walking shoes with cushioned soles to navigate ancient sandstone pathways, tree roots, and cobblestone courtyards safely.'),
  ('angkor-wat', 4616, 4, 'Carry sufficient prescription medications, sun protection, insect repellent, and emergency cash in US Dollars (USD) or Cambodian Riel (KHR), as medical facilities within the park grounds are basic.'),
  ('angkor-wat', 4616, 5, 'Plan dedicated midday rest periods at hotel lounges, shaded cafes, or spa facilities during the hottest hours of the day (11:30 AM–3:00 PM).'),
  ('angkor-wat', 4616, 6, 'Exploring flat, ground-level stone causeways and accessible outer galleries at Angkor Wat, Bayon, and Banteay Srei.'),
  ('angkor-wat', 4616, 7, 'Taking relaxing remork (tuk-tuk) rides through shaded jungle avenues between the Grand and Small Circuit temple ruins.'),
  ('angkor-wat', 4616, 8, 'Attending evening cultural performances, such as traditional Apsara dance dinners or the Phare Cambodian Circus, seated comfortably in climate-controlled or well-ventilated venues.'),
  ('angkor-wat', 4616, 9, 'Enjoying private boat excursions on Tonle Sap Lake to view floating villages from comfortable, shaded wooden watercraft.'),
  ('angkor-wat', 4616, 10, 'Dining on gentle, non-spicy Khmer culinary classics such as *Fish Amok* (steamed coconut fish curry), *Chicken Lok Lak*, or fresh tropical fruit at established sit-down restaurants.'),
  ('angkor-wat', 4616, 11, 'Attempting steep, narrow, and high-step stone staircases leading to upper temple sanctuaries (such as the Bakan sanctuary at Angkor Wat or the upper tiers of Baphuon) without assistance.'),
  ('angkor-wat', 4616, 12, 'Walking across unshaded stone courtyards during peak midday hours when heat absorption off sandstone surfaces reaches extreme levels.'),
  ('angkor-wat', 4616, 13, 'Relying on unverified street transport or walking long distances along rural roads lacking paved footpaths.'),
  ('angkor-wat', 4616, 14, 'Rushing through multiple major temple complexes in a single day, which leads to physical exhaustion and heat fatigue.'),
  ('angkor-wat', 4616, 15, 'Exploring remote, off-the-beaten-path ruins without an accredited local guide who knows safe pathways and terrain hazards.'),
  ('angkor-wat', 4618, 0, 'Feast on authentic **Fish Amok** (*Amok Trey*), Cambodia''s national signature dish featuring freshwater fish fillets steamed in banana leaf cups with a delicate, soufflé-like coconut cream curry flavored with fresh *kroeung* paste.'),
  ('angkor-wat', 4618, 1, 'Savor authentic **Beef Lok Lak**, tender wok-marinated beef stir-fried with onions and served over crisp lettuce, fresh tomatoes, and a tangy lime-and-black-pepper dipping sauce.'),
  ('angkor-wat', 4618, 2, 'Indulge in a warm bowl of **Nom Banh Chok**, traditional Khmer noodles topped with a fragrant fish-based green curry sauce made from lemongrass, kaffir lime leaves, and turmeric, garnished with fresh wild herbs and raw banana flowers.'),
  ('angkor-wat', 4618, 3, 'Slurp a comforting bowl of **Kuy Teav**, a classic Cambodian breakfast noodle soup featuring flat rice noodles in a rich pork broth topped with minced meat, fish balls, crispy garlic, and fresh herbs.'),
  ('angkor-wat', 4618, 4, 'Sip authentic **Cambodian Iced Coffee** with sweet condensed milk alongside local sweet snacks like **Kralan** (sticky rice, beans, and coconut milk roasted inside bamboo tubes) or **Nom Krok** (crispy coconut rice cakes).'),
  ('angkor-wat', 4618, 5, '**Families:** Friendly street food hubs, open-air garden venues, and casual sit-down restaurants serving non-spicy favorites like chicken *Lok Lak*, fried rice (*Bai Cha*), stir-fried noodles (*Lort Cha*), and fresh fruit smoothies.'),
  ('angkor-wat', 4618, 6, '**Honeymooners:** Romantic candlelit dining in restored French colonial courtyards, private dinners set amid lush garden rice paddies, and intimate riverfront tasting experiences.'),
  ('angkor-wat', 4618, 7, '**Luxury travelers:** Exclusive multi-course royal Khmer tasting menus inside heritage estates, private chef-led cooking masterclasses, and elevated modern Khmer fusion restaurants in Siem Reap''s Wat Bo district.'),
  ('angkor-wat', 4618, 8, '**Budget travelers:** Bustling night market stalls, street-side carts along Pub Street, and local market eateries near Phsar Chas where filling plates of *Lort Cha*, *Bai Sach Chrouk*, or stir-fried noodles cost just $1.50 to $3.50 USD.'),
  ('angkor-wat', 4618, 9, '**Foodies:** Guided night-time tuk-tuk food tours through local neighborhood night markets to sample authentic street recipes, roasted insects, seasonal tropical fruits, and herbal rice wines.'),
  ('angkor-wat', 4618, 10, '**Wat Bo District & Riverfront (Siem Reap):** Best for stylish boutique dining, high-end French-Khmer fusion bistros, upscale cafes, and peaceful riverfront cocktail lounges.'),
  ('angkor-wat', 4618, 11, '**Old Market (Phsar Chas) & Pub Street:** Best for vibrant street food stalls, budget-friendly local eateries, bustling night market lanes, and casual international dining options.'),
  ('angkor-wat', 4618, 12, '**Psar Leu & Outer Siem Reap Markets:** Best for authentic local Cambodian street food, fresh produce markets, traditional breakfast noodle stalls, and local culinary discoveries.'),
  ('angkor-wat', 4618, 13, '**Rural Siem Reap Countryside & Angkor Road:** Best for farm-to-table dining experiences set inside traditional wooden stilt houses, surrounded by lotus ponds and organic rice fields.'),
  ('angkor-wat', 4619, 0, '**Cambodian Silk & Krama Scarves:** Luxurious, hand-loomed raw silk textiles, shawls, and traditional checkered cotton *krama* scarves woven in countryside villages.'),
  ('angkor-wat', 4619, 1, '**Hand-Carved Stone & Wood Sculptures:** Exquisite replicas of Angkorian bas-reliefs, Buddha statues, and celestial *apsara* dancers carved by local master artisans using sandstone and native hardwoods.'),
  ('angkor-wat', 4619, 2, '**Kampot Pepper & Palm Sugar:** World-famous, geographical-indication-certified Kampot peppercorns (black, red, and white) alongside organic Kampong Speu palm sugar and aromatic local spice blends.'),
  ('angkor-wat', 4619, 3, '**Silverware & Brass Handicrafts:** Intricately stamped silver-plated boxes, animal-shaped betel nut containers, brass ornaments, and handcrafted jewelry made using centuries-old techniques.'),
  ('angkor-wat', 4619, 4, '**Artisanal Soaps & Botanical Spices:** Handcrafted natural cosmetics, herbal tea blends, lemongrass essential oils, and herbal massage compresses sourced from local Cambodian botanicals.'),
  ('angkor-wat', 4619, 5, '**Made in Cambodia Market:** Best for certified authentic, high-quality artisanal goods, fair-trade handicrafts, fine jewelry, and live traditional craft demonstrations in an open-air plaza.'),
  ('angkor-wat', 4619, 6, '**Angkor Artisans (Artisans d''Angkor):** Preferred for ethically produced master-quality silk textiles, stone statues, lacquered woodware, and guided workshop tours supporting rural craft training.'),
  ('angkor-wat', 4619, 7, '**Psar Chaa (Old Market):** Ideal for browsing vibrant stalls packed with local spices, Kampot pepper, dried fruits, tea, copperware, and budget-friendly street souvenirs near Pub Street.'),
  ('angkor-wat', 4619, 8, '**Siem Reap Art Center Night Market:** Perfect for late-afternoon and evening browsing across the river, offering a wide selection of cotton clothing, silver crafts, paintings, and handmade accessories.'),
  ('angkor-wat', 4619, 9, 'Purchasing genuine antique Khmer artifacts or unverified archaeological items, which is strictly illegal under Cambodian law and international heritage protection regulations.');
INSERT INTO destination_guidance_bullet (place_id, position, bullet_index, text) VALUES
  ('angkor-wat', 4619, 10, 'Buying cheap, mass-produced plastic or resin temple replicas imported from neighboring countries when authentic local social enterprises directly support Cambodian artisans.'),
  ('angkor-wat', 4619, 11, 'Expecting fixed prices in informal market stalls; polite, lighthearted bargaining is expected, whereas prices in government-certified workshops, boutique stores, and social enterprises are fixed.'),
  ('angkor-wat', 4619, 12, '**Culture & Craft Lovers:** Travelers seeking hand-carved stone reliefs, woven raw silk, and authentic lacquered art directly supporting local social enterprises.'),
  ('angkor-wat', 4619, 13, '**Culinary Enthusiasts:** Food lovers looking to take home world-renowned Kampot pepper, artisan palm sugar, and local Khmer curry spice blends.'),
  ('angkor-wat', 4619, 14, '**Ethical & Fair-Trade Shoppers:** Visitors eager to support rural community development, disability employment initiatives, and traditional heritage preservation programs through conscious purchases.'),
  ('angkor-wat', 4620, 0, '**Backpackers & partygoers** seeking cheap draft beers ($0.50–$1.00 USD), multi-story dance clubs, open-air bar street parties, and late-night music venues.'),
  ('angkor-wat', 4620, 1, '**Cocktail enthusiasts & speakeasy lovers** looking for inventive craft drinks infused with local Cambodian botanicals, Kampot pepper, and rice spirits in stylish, hidden lounges.'),
  ('angkor-wat', 4620, 2, '**Culture seekers & families** wanting to experience evening classical Apsara dance dinners, live traditional shadow puppet theater, or the acclaimed Phare Cambodian Circus performance.'),
  ('angkor-wat', 4620, 3, '**Night owls & market strolling** visitors wanting to explore bustling night bazaars, enjoy cheap outdoor foot massages, or sample street food snacks like grilled skewers and rolled ice cream.'),
  ('angkor-wat', 4620, 4, 'Diving into the legendary high-energy atmosphere of **Pub Street (Street 8)**, hopping between iconic dance venues like *Street 08*, *The Red Piano*, and *Temple Club*.'),
  ('angkor-wat', 4620, 5, 'Discovering the chic, upscale cocktail scene along **Sok San Road and Wat Bo Road**, sampling handcrafted botanical cocktails at famous speakeasies like *Miss Wong* or *Sok San Street Bar*.'),
  ('angkor-wat', 4620, 6, 'Attending an evening show at **Phare, The Cambodian Circus**, an inspiring non-profit performance blending theatrical storytelling, high-energy acrobatics, and live traditional music.'),
  ('angkor-wat', 4620, 7, 'Unwinding along **Kandal Village**, a trendy European-style alley featuring quiet wine bars, indie cafes, craft beer taps, and cozy outdoor dining spots.'),
  ('angkor-wat', 4620, 8, 'Accepting unmetered tuk-tuk rides late at night from drivers waiting outside major clubs; always use ride-hailing apps like PassApp or Grab for safe, fixed-rate transport back to your hotel.'),
  ('angkor-wat', 4620, 9, 'Engaging in confrontation or buying illicit substances from street touts around Pub Street; local authorities strictly enforce drug and public safety laws.'),
  ('angkor-wat', 4620, 10, 'Leaving personal belongings unattended on street-side tables or open tuk-tuks during late-night hours in high-density bar districts.'),
  ('angkor-wat', 4620, 11, '**Pub Street & Alley West:** The absolute epicenter of Siem Reap’s nightlife, packed with loud bar venues, dance clubs, neon signs, and street performers.'),
  ('angkor-wat', 4620, 12, '**Wat Bo Road & Kandal Village:** Best for a sophisticated evening out, featuring fine dining options, boutique wine lounges, craft cocktail bars, and art cafes.'),
  ('angkor-wat', 4620, 13, '**Sok San Road:** Popular with long-term travelers and expats, offering a mix of casual pubs, cheap sports bars, live music joints, and hostel bars.'),
  ('angkor-wat', 4620, 14, '**Siem Reap Night Market Riverfront:** Ideal for late-night strolls, outdoor foot massages, craft souvenir browsing, and casual street-side beer drinking.'),
  ('angkor-wat', 4628, 0, 'Treat the 400-square-kilometer **Angkor Archaeological Park** like a single self-contained monument, packing daily schedules with back-to-back ruin visits that trigger acute "temple fatigue" and physical exhaustion.'),
  ('angkor-wat', 4628, 1, 'Follow standard counter-clockwise tour routes starting with **Angkor Wat** at sunrise, pushing clients straight into massive tour bus bottlenecks at the lotus reflection ponds and eastern galleries.'),
  ('angkor-wat', 4628, 2, 'Underestimate midday temperatures and high humidity by attempting midday treks through exposed sites like **Pre Rup** or the **Terrace of the Elephants**, leaving clients dehydrated and overheated.'),
  ('angkor-wat', 4628, 3, 'Fail to enforce the strict official dress code (covered shoulders and knees required for entry into upper tiers like **Bakan Sanctuary**), leading to clients being turned away at checkpoint stairs.'),
  ('angkor-wat', 4628, 4, 'Book uncertified tuk-tuk or vehicle drivers to act as historical guides, failing to recognize that official site narration requires a ministry-licensed guide in a distinct yellow uniform.'),
  ('angkor-wat', 4629, 0, 'Reverses standard crowd flows by sending clients to **Ta Prohm** or **Bayon** at dawn''s light, visiting **Angkor Wat** in the late afternoon when backlight conditions are superior for photography and big groups have cleared.'),
  ('angkor-wat', 4629, 1, 'Builds a mandatory midday "siesta block" (11:30 AM to 2:30 PM) into multi-day passes, returning clients to hotel pools in **Siem Reap** to escape oppressive tropical heat.'),
  ('angkor-wat', 4629, 2, 'Secures 3-Day Angkor Passes in advance online or at the official ticket center, distributing site visits over a 5-to-7 day window for a balanced pace.'),
  ('angkor-wat', 4629, 3, 'Pairs a dedicated private driver with a certified ministry guide—allowing the driver to handle ice water drops and exit pickups while the guide navigates interior galleries.'),
  ('angkor-wat', 4629, 4, 'Balances heavy stone ruin tours with countryside excursions like boat trips to **Kampong Phluk** on **Tonle Sap Lake** or visits to pink sandstone carvings at **Banteay Srei**.'),
  ('angkor-wat', 4630, 0, 'For **Crowd & Route Strategy**, run the Small and Grand Circuits in reverse order, scheduling heavy stone exploration for early morning (6:00 AM – 11:00 AM) and late afternoon (3:00 PM – 6:00 PM).'),
  ('angkor-wat', 4630, 1, 'For **Guiding & Transit Logistics**, always separate the driver and expert guide roles, utilizing air-conditioned vehicles for outer sites like **Banteay Srei** or **Phnom Kulen** while relying on tuk-tuks for inner park loops.'),
  ('angkor-wat', 4630, 2, 'For **Pacing & Comfort Balance**, enforce a maximum of 3 major temple complexes per day with a built-in midday rest break, pairing temple days with cultural and culinary experiences in **Siem Reap**.'),
  ('angkor-wat', 4633, 0, 'Experience the iconic dawn light behind the five lotus towers of Angkor Wat, followed by an immediate inner sanctuary tour before the mid-morning tour groups arrive.'),
  ('angkor-wat', 4633, 1, 'Explore the serene, giant stone face towers of the Bayon Temple at the center of ancient Angkor Thom.'),
  ('angkor-wat', 4633, 2, 'Wander the jungle-entangled stone corridors of Ta Prohm, where massive strangler fig and silk-cotton tree roots wrap directly over ancient lintels.'),
  ('angkor-wat', 4633, 3, 'Drive into the rural countryside to admire the intricate, rose-pink sandstone bas-reliefs at Banteay Srei.'),
  ('angkor-wat', 4633, 4, 'Take a private golden-hour gondola cruise along the ancient moat of Angkor Thom or enjoy a tethered helium balloon ride for a 360-degree aerial view of the temple complex.'),
  ('angkor-wat', 4633, 5, 'Attempting to visit back-to-back temples during the intense midday heat (11:30 AM – 2:30 PM) without returning to your hotel for a rest or pool break.'),
  ('angkor-wat', 4633, 6, 'Wearing clothing that violates the official sacred dress code (shoulders and knees must be fully covered to access upper tiers like the Bakan Sanctuary in Angkor Wat).'),
  ('angkor-wat', 4633, 7, 'Buying a 1-Day pass for the 400-square-kilometer park; always opt for a 3-Day pass spread across a 5-day window to avoid severe "temple fatigue."'),
  ('angkor-wat', 4633, 8, 'Hiring uncertified drivers as guides who lack official licensing from the Cambodian Ministry of Tourism to explain complex Hindu and Buddhist bas-relief history.'),
  ('angkor-wat', 4634, 0, 'To be populated with authoritative tourism/transport/attraction sources before production use.'),
  ('phnom-penh', 4638, 0, 'Book rides via local app-based services like PassApp or Grab instead of flagging street tuk-tuks, securing transparent, fixed fare rates ($1.00–$2.50 USD per trip) across central neighborhoods without the need for manual price haggling.'),
  ('phnom-penh', 4638, 1, 'Eat at local markets like Psar Tapang or night markets along the Sisowath Quay riverfront, where staple dishes like *Bai Sach Chrouk* (pork and rice), *Nom Banh Chok* (Khmer noodles), or fried noodles cost only $1.50 to $3.50 USD per portion.'),
  ('phnom-penh', 4638, 2, 'Stay at budget-friendly boutique guesthouses or highly rated hostels in the BKK3 or Riverside districts, where air-conditioned private rooms run from $12 to $25 USD per night and dormitory beds cost under $8 USD.'),
  ('phnom-penh', 4638, 3, 'Combine your trips to Tuol Sleng (S-21) and the Choeung Ek Killing Fields into a single half-day tuk-tuk charter ($12–$18 USD round trip) to split transit costs and avoid multiple individual taxi fares.'),
  ('phnom-penh', 4638, 4, 'Carry small USD bills ($1, $5, and $10) in pristine condition with no tears or marks, as physical change under $1 USD is routinely given back in Cambodian Riel (typically at a standard $1 USD = 4,000 KHR rate) to use for small street-side snacks and water purchases.'),
  ('phnom-penh', 4638, 5, 'Skipping the official audio guides at Tuol Sleng Genocide Museum ($5 USD) or Choeung Ek Killing Fields ($3 USD); the audio commentary provides critical historical context, eyewitness testimony, and educational depth essential to understanding Cambodia''s tragic Khmer Rouge era.'),
  ('phnom-penh', 4638, 6, 'Choosing unaccredited or unlicensed local boats along Sisowath Quay for sunset cruises on the Tonle Sap and Mekong rivers, as safety standards, life jacket availability, and boat maintenance vary widely compared to reputable operators ($10–$15 USD).'),
  ('phnom-penh', 4638, 7, 'Buying cheap, unverified alcohol or unsealed spirits in late-night nightlife zones, where counterfeit alcohol or unhygienic ice sources can pose serious health risks.'),
  ('phnom-penh', 4638, 8, 'Refusing to hire accredited, licensed guides at the Royal Palace and National Museum, where complex Khmer architectural symbols, Buddhist iconography, and royal artifacts require expert interpretation to be fully appreciated.'),
  ('phnom-penh', 4639, 0, '4+'),
  ('phnom-penh', 4639, 1, '6+'),
  ('phnom-penh', 4639, 2, '8+'),
  ('phnom-penh', 4639, 3, 'Teenagers'),
  ('phnom-penh', 4639, 4, 'Leave traditional strollers at home and rely on an ergonomic baby or toddler carrier; Phnom Penh’s uneven or missing sidewalks, broken concrete, high curb drops, and parked motorcycles make stroller wheels highly impractical.'),
  ('phnom-penh', 4639, 5, 'Use ride-hailing apps like PassApp or Grab to book private tuk-tuks or air-conditioned cars; booking digitally secures upfront fixed pricing, eliminates language barriers, and avoids negotiating fares on hot street corners with tired kids.'),
  ('phnom-penh', 4639, 6, 'Hire private, air-conditioned vehicle transfers for day trips and travel between major hubs like Siem Reap or Kampot; private drivers offer flexible stopovers, working seatbelts, and a cooler environment than crowded shared minivans.'),
  ('phnom-penh', 4639, 7, 'Schedule outdoor sightseeing—such as the Royal Palace, Wat Phnom, or Silk Island—early in the morning or late in the afternoon; escape midday heat and humidity by taking air-conditioned breaks at modern malls like AEON or hotel swimming pools.'),
  ('phnom-penh', 4639, 8, 'Exercise extra caution with personal belongings on public streets and open-air tuk-tuks; hold onto bags and smartphones tightly toward the inside of vehicles to prevent opportunistic bag-snatching in busy market districts.'),
  ('phnom-penh', 4639, 9, 'Practice strict food and water safety by drinking bottled water, refusing ice from street stalls, and sticking to thoroughly cooked local meals like *Lok Lak* (mild beef stir-fry), fresh fruit smoothies, or noodle soups from reputable establishments.'),
  ('phnom-penh', 4640, 0, 'honeymoon_score: 82'),
  ('phnom-penh', 4640, 1, 'romance_score: 84'),
  ('phnom-penh', 4640, 2, 'privacy_score: 80'),
  ('phnom-penh', 4640, 3, 'luxury_score: 82'),
  ('phnom-penh', 4642, 0, 'Embarking on a full-day cross-country bicycle or quad bike expedition through the quiet dirt tracks, lotus farms, and rural villages of Koh Dach.'),
  ('phnom-penh', 4642, 1, 'Navigating the busy waters of the Mekong and Tonle Sap river confluence on long-distance riverboat excursions or evening sunset kayak trips.'),
  ('phnom-penh', 4642, 2, 'Climbing the steep stairways of the ancient royal mountain of Udong to explore hilltop stupas and sweeping countryside vistas.'),
  ('phnom-penh', 4642, 3, 'Taking a thrilling open-air tuk-tuk or motorbike trip through chaotic urban traffic and rural tracks out to the Choeung Ek Genocidal Center.'),
  ('phnom-penh', 4642, 4, 'Attending energetic live Kun Khmer martial arts matches inside local stadiums alongside passionate local crowds.'),
  ('phnom-penh', 4642, 5, '**Koh Dach (Silk Island)** — best for rural cross-country cycling, riverboat crossings, fruit orchard walks, and eco-island exploring.'),
  ('phnom-penh', 4642, 6, '**Mekong & Tonle Sap Riverfront** — best for sunset riverboat cruises, river kayaking, and scenic waterborne sightseeing.'),
  ('phnom-penh', 4642, 7, '**Udong Mountain Region** — best for day hikes, ancient stupa exploring, and countryside panoramic photography.'),
  ('phnom-penh', 4642, 8, '**Outskirts & Countryside Trails** — best for quad bike adventures, off-road dirt track riding, and local village visits.'),
  ('phnom-penh', 4642, 9, 'Urban explorers and active city cyclists.'),
  ('phnom-penh', 4642, 10, 'Off-the-beaten-path day trippers and rural sightseers.'),
  ('phnom-penh', 4642, 11, 'Culture-focused adventurers and local sports enthusiasts.'),
  ('phnom-penh', 4642, 12, 'River cruisers, kayakers, and outdoor photography hobbyists.'),
  ('phnom-penh', 4642, 13, 'Backpackers seeking budget-friendly outdoor activities near the capital.'),
  ('phnom-penh', 4643, 0, 'Book private, air-conditioned MPVs or cars (such as a Lexus RX or Toyota Alphard) with dedicated local drivers for city transit, avoiding long walks along hot, broken sidewalks.'),
  ('phnom-penh', 4643, 1, 'Schedule outdoor sightseeing at the Royal Palace, Wat Phnom, and Choeung Ek during early morning hours (7:30 AM–10:00 AM) to avoid peak equatorial heat, humidity, and afternoon sun exposure.'),
  ('phnom-penh', 4643, 2, 'Hire private, English-speaking local guides for historical sites like Tuol Sleng (S-21) and the Choeung Ek Killing Fields to ensure a paced, educational tour tailored to your mobility level.'),
  ('phnom-penh', 4643, 3, 'Request ground-floor suites or properties with reliable, modern elevator access, as French colonial boutique hotels across the city often feature multi-level layouts without lifts.'),
  ('phnom-penh', 4643, 4, 'Wear comfortable, supportive walking shoes with non-slip cushioned soles when navigating uneven brick plazas, market floors, and high temple steps.'),
  ('phnom-penh', 4643, 5, 'Keep emergency cash in US Dollars (USD) or Cambodian Riel (KHR) and carry sufficient prescription medications, as specialized international medical centers are limited primarily to central urban districts.'),
  ('phnom-penh', 4643, 6, 'Plan midday rest periods at air-conditioned hotel lounges, shaded riverfront cafes, or luxury spa facilities during the hottest hours of the day (11:30 AM–2:30 PM).'),
  ('phnom-penh', 4643, 7, 'Exploring flat, easily accessible grounds like the Sisowath Quay riverfront promenade, the National Museum courtyards, and the Royal Palace gardens.'),
  ('phnom-penh', 4643, 8, 'Enjoying private sunset river cruises along the confluence of the Mekong and Tonle Sap rivers aboard comfortable, covered wooden boats.'),
  ('phnom-penh', 4643, 9, 'Attending evening traditional Khmer dance and shadow theatre performances hosted by Cambodian Living Arts while seated in covered venue settings.'),
  ('phnom-penh', 4643, 10, 'Taking private chauffeured day trips across the river to Silk Island (Koh Dach) for quiet rural scenery and shade-covered silk weaving demonstrations.'),
  ('phnom-penh', 4643, 11, 'Dining on gentle, non-spicy Khmer specialties like Fish Amok, *Lok Lak* (beef stir-fry), or fresh tropical fruits at established sit-down restaurants.'),
  ('phnom-penh', 4643, 12, 'Attempting to navigate long stretches of urban street curbs on foot, as parked motorbikes and missing pavement slabs force pedestrians into traffic.'),
  ('phnom-penh', 4643, 13, 'Taking open-air motorbike taxis (*motodops*) or unmetered road transport for long trips due to lack of seating support, high step entries, and exposure to dust.'),
  ('phnom-penh', 4643, 14, 'Visiting overcrowded, narrow market aisles inside the Central Market or Russian Market during peak midday heat.'),
  ('phnom-penh', 4643, 15, 'Walking through high-density urban traffic zones without a guide or driver during peak rush-hour periods.'),
  ('phnom-penh', 4643, 16, 'Traveling by boat along river waterways during sudden heavy monsoon downpours due to choppy waters and low visibility.'),
  ('phnom-penh', 4645, 0, 'Feast on national favorite **Fish Amok**, a silken freshwater fish mousse steamed in banana leaves with coconut cream, lemongrass, kaffir lime, and aromatic yellow *kroeung*.'),
  ('phnom-penh', 4645, 1, 'Savor classic **Beef Lok Lak**, tender stir-fried beef cubes served over fresh lettuce, tomatoes, and red onions, accompanied by the signature tangy lime and Kampot black pepper dipping sauce.'),
  ('phnom-penh', 4645, 2, 'Enjoy a traditional morning bowl of **Nom Banh Chok**, delicate rice noodles topped with a cold, fish-based green curry sauce and fresh local herbs, cucumber, and banana flower slices.'),
  ('phnom-penh', 4645, 3, 'Indulge in savory **Bai Sach Chrouk**, thinly sliced pork marinated in garlic and palm sugar, grilled over charcoal and served over warm rice with pickled vegetables and a bowl of clear broth.'),
  ('phnom-penh', 4645, 4, 'Sip iced **Iced Coffee with Sweetened Condensed Milk** (*Café Tuek Dok Tey*) alongside fresh French baguettes (*Nom Pang*) filled with savory paté, cold cuts, and pickled papaya from street vendors.'),
  ('phnom-penh', 4645, 5, '**Families:** Casual riverfront eateries, modern mall dining halls, and established sit-down restaurants serving mild, non-spicy favorites like beef *Lok Lak*, stir-fried noodles (*Lort Cha*), and fresh fruit smoothies.'),
  ('phnom-penh', 4645, 6, '**Honeymooners:** Romantic candlelit courtyards inside French colonial villas across BKK1, sunset cocktail cruises along the Mekong River, and intimate courtyard dining with elevated French-Khmer fusion menus.'),
  ('phnom-penh', 4645, 7, '**Luxury travelers:** High-end fine dining at Rosewood Phnom Penh, exclusive master-chef royal Khmer tasting menus, and private riverboat dining charters.'),
  ('phnom-penh', 4645, 8, '**Budget travelers:** Bustling central markets and street food stalls around Night Market (Phsar Reatrey) where filling plates of *Nom Banh Chok*, fried noodles, or pork rice cost just $1.50 to $3.50 USD.'),
  ('phnom-penh', 4645, 9, '**Foodies:** Self-guided tuk-tuk street food tours through hidden alleyways, wet market tasting walks at Russian Market, and craft cocktail bars incorporating local botanical spirits.'),
  ('phnom-penh', 4645, 10, '**Sisowath Quay & Riverfront:** Best for scenic outdoor dining, French-style bistros, international cafes, and sunset views over the Tonle Sap and Mekong confluence.'),
  ('phnom-penh', 4645, 11, '**BKK1 (Boeng Keng Kang 1):** Best for upscale dining, stylish third-wave cafes, trendy fusion restaurants, international cuisines, and leafy courtyard dining setups.'),
  ('phnom-penh', 4645, 12, '**Bassac Lane & Tonle Bassac:** Best for atmospheric nightlife, hidden cocktail lounges, craft beer bars, and small, high-concept tapas and fusion kitchens.'),
  ('phnom-penh', 4645, 13, '**Central & Russian Markets (Phsar Thmei & Phsar Tuol Tom Poung):** Best for authentic, budget-friendly street food stalls, fresh noodle soups, grilled meats, and local desserts.'),
  ('phnom-penh', 4646, 0, '**Kampot Pepper & Spices:** World-renowned, PDO-certified black, white, and red pepper vacuum-sealed from coastal plantations, alongside custom Khmer curry and *amok* spice blends.'),
  ('phnom-penh', 4646, 1, '**Krama Scarves & Khmer Silk:** Traditional checkered cotton *krama* scarves—extremely versatile and authentically Cambodian—plus raw hand-loomed silk garments, sarongs, and accessories.'),
  ('phnom-penh', 4646, 2, '**Cambodian Silverwork & Jewelry:** Hand-pounded sterling silver bowls, boxes shaped like sacred animals, and fine jewelry set with locally mined Cambodian gemstones (rubies, zircons, and sapphires).'),
  ('phnom-penh', 4646, 3, '**Stone Carvings & Lacquerware:** High-quality sandstone and bronze Angkorian replica sculptures, alongside hand-painted wooden lacquerware trays and decorative bowls.'),
  ('phnom-penh', 4646, 4, '**Ethical Crafts & Natural Wellness:** Handwoven bags, lotus-fiber products, and organic natural soaps, massage oils, and candles infused with lemongrass and kaffir lime.'),
  ('phnom-penh', 4646, 5, '**Russian Market (Phsar Toul Tom Poung):** Best all-around market for boutique handicrafts, silk scarves, carved silverwork, factory overruns, and sealed Kampot pepper.'),
  ('phnom-penh', 4646, 6, '**Street 178 & Street 240 (Near Royal Palace):** Preferred for upscale artisan boutiques, social enterprise craft stores (like Daughters of Cambodia), and high-end ethical fashion.'),
  ('phnom-penh', 4646, 7, '**Central Market (Phsar Thmei):** Ideal for viewing 1937 Art Deco architecture while browsing gold and silver jewelry under the central dome, textiles, and everyday local goods.'),
  ('phnom-penh', 4646, 8, '**Artisans d''Angkor Phnom Penh Outlet:** Preferred for certified, premium-quality sandstone carvings, silk garments, and luxury Khmer home decor.'),
  ('phnom-penh', 4646, 9, 'Buying unverified loose gemstones from street stalls or inner market aisles without proper authenticity certification; purchase only from established jewelry houses.'),
  ('phnom-penh', 4646, 10, 'Purchasing genuine antiquities or protected wildlife items; ancient relics are strictly prohibited from export by law, and wildlife products violate CITES conventions.'),
  ('phnom-penh', 4646, 11, 'Expecting fixed prices in open-air markets like Russian or Central Market; polite, good-natured bargaining is standard practice, while social enterprises and brick-and-mortar boutiques maintain fixed pricing.'),
  ('phnom-penh', 4646, 12, '**Culture & Craft Lovers:** Travelers seeking hand-carved stone statues, authentic raw silk textiles, and hand-hammered silver artifacts.'),
  ('phnom-penh', 4646, 13, '**Ethical & Conscious Shoppers:** Visitors wanting to support fair-trade NGOs, disability cooperatives, and local artisan empowerment initiatives.'),
  ('phnom-penh', 4646, 14, '**Gourmet Foodies:** Culinary travelers looking to bring home world-famous Kampot pepper, palm sugar disks, and specialty Khmer coffee beans.'),
  ('phnom-penh', 4647, 0, '**Cocktail enthusiasts & trendsetters** seeking hidden speakeasies, artisanal mixology bars, and atmospheric micro-bars tucked into leafy side alleys.'),
  ('phnom-penh', 4647, 1, '**Rooftop & view lovers** wanting sky-high views, sunset cocktails, and sleek outdoor lounge settings overlooking the confluence of the Mekong and Tonle Sap rivers.'),
  ('phnom-penh', 4647, 2, '**Partygoers & late-night clubbers** looking for international guest DJs, craft beer venues, and high-energy dance floors open into the early morning hours.'),
  ('phnom-penh', 4647, 3, '**Budget travelers & social backpackers** hunting for cheap local draft beer, lively hostel bars, and informal night markets with affordable street food.'),
  ('phnom-penh', 4647, 4, 'Exploring the micro-bar ecosystem of **Bassac Lane & Street 308**, sipping craft cocktails and local botanical spirits at cozy, open-air alleyway bars.'),
  ('phnom-penh', 4647, 5, 'Taking in panoramic 360-degree views of the city skyline from **high-altitude sky bars** like *Sora Bar* at Rosewood, *Rukkha Sky Bar*, or *HighGround*.'),
  ('phnom-penh', 4647, 6, 'Catching vibrant weekend drag performances and friendly community night events at local LGBTQ+ institutions like **Blue Chilli** near the Royal Palace area.'),
  ('phnom-penh', 4647, 7, 'Experiencing late-night street food stalls and casual beer drinking along **Sisowath Quay and Phnom Penh Night Market** for a relaxed, breeze-filled evening.'),
  ('phnom-penh', 4647, 8, 'Walking alone late at night along dark, unlit side streets near the riverfront or Street 51; use trusted ride-hailing apps (PassApp or Grab) for door-to-door tuk-tuk transport.'),
  ('phnom-penh', 4647, 9, 'Leaving personal belongings, phones, or bags unattended on outdoor bar tables or while riding in open-air tuk-tuks.'),
  ('phnom-penh', 4647, 10, 'Entering unverified late-night venues or hostess bars around Street 104 and Street 136 without checking drink prices upfront.'),
  ('phnom-penh', 4647, 11, '**Bassac Lane & Street 308 (Tonle Bassac):** The epicenter of trendy nightlife, packed with micro-bars, tapas spots, speakeasies, and vibrant social alleys.'),
  ('phnom-penh', 4647, 12, '**BKK1 & Langka Lane:** Best for stylish craft beer gardens, upscale wine bars, chic coffee lounges, and relaxed expat-friendly venues.'),
  ('phnom-penh', 4647, 13, '**Sisowath Quay (Riverside):** Ideal for sunset views, casual open-air pubs, international dining, and vibrant night market street snacks.'),
  ('phnom-penh', 4647, 14, '**Tuol Tom Poung (Russian Market area):** Best for bohemian dive bars, laid-back rooftop hangs, craft brewery taprooms, and affordable neighborhood watering holes.'),
  ('phnom-penh', 4655, 0, 'Treat Phnom Penh as a mere 1-day transit stop between Siem Reap and the southern islands, missing the city''s complex modern history, thriving food scene, and riverfront culture.'),
  ('phnom-penh', 4655, 1, 'Over-pack the first day with heavy dark-tourism sites, scheduling both **Tuol Sleng Genocide Museum (S-21)** and the **Choeung Ek Killing Fields** back-to-back immediately after landing.'),
  ('phnom-penh', 4655, 2, 'Attempt to walk everywhere between district hubs, underestimating Phnom Penh''s intense humidity, lack of pedestrian-friendly sidewalks, and chaotic traffic patterns.'),
  ('phnom-penh', 4655, 3, 'Rely strictly on unmetered roadside tuk-tuks or large US dollar bills ($20/$50), leading to price negotiations and issues with drivers lacking small change or USD/Riel conversion.'),
  ('phnom-penh', 4655, 4, 'Fail to prepare clients for curbside opportunistic bag-snatching along crowded areas like **Sisowath Quay** or near open tuk-tuks, putting phones and loose bags at risk from passing motorbikes.'),
  ('phnom-penh', 4656, 0, 'Distributes dark-tourism visits across separate half-days or pairs them with lighter cultural experiences, providing appropriate pacing and emotional balance.'),
  ('phnom-penh', 4656, 1, 'Books app-based transport (such as Grab or PassApp) or arranges private chauffeured cars for day tours, ensuring fixed pricing, air-conditioned transfers, and seamless door-to-door transit.'),
  ('phnom-penh', 4656, 2, 'Schedules visits to **The Royal Palace** and **National Museum** for early morning hours to beat peak midday heat, large tour groups, and sudden ceremonial closures.'),
  ('phnom-penh', 4656, 3, 'Incorporates sunset wooden-boat river cruises along the confluence of the **Tonle Sap** and **Mekong** rivers as a relaxing, high-value evening transition activity.'),
  ('phnom-penh', 4656, 4, 'Curates day trips to rural retreats like **Koh Dach (Silk Island)** or the ancient royal capital of **Udong**, offering clients a peaceful contrast to the bustling city center.'),
  ('phnom-penh', 4657, 0, 'For **Historical & Cultural Pacing**, limit visits to heavy historical sites to one per day, pairing morning reflections with lighter afternoon activities like riverboat cruises or market visits.'),
  ('phnom-penh', 4657, 1, 'For **Transit & Urban Mobility**, rely on digital ride-hailing apps or private drivers for distances over 10 minutes walk, while advising clients to keep phone usage away from open tuk-tuk edges and curbsides.'),
  ('phnom-penh', 4657, 2, 'For **Excursion & Regional Balance**, dedicate at least 2 to 3 nights to Phnom Penh, combining central capital landmarks with a rural day trip (Silk Island or Udong) before connecting to Siem Reap or the southern coast.'),
  ('phnom-penh', 4660, 0, 'Explore the gilded spires of the Royal Palace, the Silver Pagoda, and the ancient masterworks inside the National Museum of Cambodia.'),
  ('phnom-penh', 4660, 1, 'Pay meaningful respects to Cambodia’s history with a private guided tour of the Tuol Sleng Genocide Museum (S-21) and the Choeung Ek Killing Fields.'),
  ('phnom-penh', 4660, 2, 'Experience a sunset boat cruise along the confluence of the Mekong and Tonle Sap rivers taking in skyline views.'),
  ('phnom-penh', 4660, 3, 'Stroll along Sisowath Quay Riverfront Promenade and discover local cafes, street-food stalls, and hidden lane bars.'),
  ('phnom-penh', 4660, 4, 'Shop for hand-woven silks, vintage goods, and local crafts inside the Art Deco dome of Central Market (*Phsar Thmei*) and the bustling Russian Market (*Phsar Tuol Tom Poung*).'),
  ('phnom-penh', 4660, 5, 'Treating Phnom Penh strictly as a 1-day transit stop on the way to Siem Reap, missing out on its world-class culinary and historical sites.'),
  ('phnom-penh', 4660, 6, 'Trying to pack heavy historical visits (S-21 and Choeung Ek) into the same half-day as lightweight shopping and fine dining without built-in downtime.'),
  ('phnom-penh', 4660, 7, 'Walking along unlit street corners at night carrying loose valuables or unzipped bags near high-traffic tourist strips.'),
  ('phnom-penh', 4660, 8, 'Visiting outdoor sites like Wat Phnom or market halls during the peak midday heat (12:00 PM – 2:30 PM) without adequate hydration.'),
  ('phnom-penh', 4661, 0, 'To be populated with authoritative tourism/transport/attraction sources before production use.'),
  ('el-nido', 4666, 0, 'Withdraw sufficient Philippine Pesos (PHP) in Manila or Puerto Princesa before traveling to El Nido, as local ATMs frequently experience network outages, run out of cash during peak season, or impose steep international transaction fees (₱250 plus independent ATM surcharges up to 10%).'),
  ('el-nido', 4666, 1, 'Eat at local *carinderias* (Filipino eateries) or small local beach shacks, where authentic local meals (such as adobo, local grilled fish, or rice plates) cost between ₱150 and ₱250 ($2.50–$4.50 USD), compared to tourist-oriented international restaurants that charge ₱400 to ₱800 per dish.'),
  ('el-nido', 4666, 2, 'Rent a scooter for ₱400 to ₱600 ($7–$11 USD) per day for inland exploration to Nacpan Beach or Duli Beach, which is significantly cheaper than hiring a private tricycle round-trip (₱1,200 to ₱1,500).'),
  ('el-nido', 4666, 3, 'Combine group island-hopping tours (Tour A or Tour C) instead of booking private boats if traveling solo or as a couple; standard joiner boat tours cost ₱1,200 to ₱1,500 per person and include a full buffet lunch on the beach.'),
  ('el-nido', 4666, 4, 'Purchase essential water gear—such as a waterproof dry bag (₱300–₱500) and water shoes (₱300–₱400)—at local shops in El Nido town or ahead of time, rather than paying daily rental fees at every boat launch point.'),
  ('el-nido', 4666, 5, 'Skipping the rental of a sea kayak inside the Big Lagoon or Small Lagoon (₱300–₱350 per kayak), as swimming long distances into the shallow lagoon entrances is exhausting, restricted in certain zones, and deprives you of the core experience.'),
  ('el-nido', 4666, 6, 'Buying unverified or discounted island-hopping packages from unofficial street hawkers who omit mandatory extra charges, such as the Eco-Tourism Development Fee (ETDF, ₱400 valid for 10 days) or specific lagoon entrance permits (₱200).'),
  ('el-nido', 4666, 7, 'Booking cheap, isolated accommodation far outside town or away from main transport corridors (like remote parts of San Fernando) purely for low night rates, as extra tricycle fares or private transfers will quickly wipe out your savings.'),
  ('el-nido', 4666, 8, 'Opting out of basic travel insurance coverage for medical emergencies or motor scooter accidents, as El Nido has basic medical clinics, and major injuries require expensive emergency air or land evacuation to Puerto Princesa or Manila.'),
  ('el-nido', 4667, 0, '4+'),
  ('el-nido', 4667, 1, '6+'),
  ('el-nido', 4667, 2, '8+'),
  ('el-nido', 4667, 3, 'Teenagers'),
  ('el-nido', 4667, 4, 'Consider chartering a private bangka boat instead of joining group island-hopping tours when traveling with young children; private charters allow you to adjust the schedule for naps, skip deep-water swims, and return to shore early if kids get tired.'),
  ('el-nido', 4667, 5, 'Bring fitted child-sized life jackets and sturdy aqua shoes for the entire family; shared tour boats often only carry adult life vests, and sharp limestone rocks or sea urchins pose hazards at lagoon entrances.'),
  ('el-nido', 4667, 6, 'Choose mainland beach options like Lio Beach or Nacpan Beach for dedicated rest days; Lio Beach offers flat, paved walking paths, shallow entry, shaded seating, and quick access to family-friendly restaurants.'),
  ('el-nido', 4667, 7, 'Check the physical requirements of specific island-hopping stops beforehand—such as crawling through the narrow gap at Secret Lagoon or swimming through underwater holes at Secret Beach—and opt for gentle alternatives like Tour D or Snake Island for easier shore access.'),
  ('el-nido', 4667, 8, 'Pack waterproof dry bags, reef-safe sunscreen, insect repellent, and sufficient snacks and bottled water before boarding; remote islands lack shops, shaded facilities, and basic restrooms.'),
  ('el-nido', 4667, 9, 'Keep a baby carrier handy instead of a stroller, as sandy shorelines, unpaved roads, and wet boat landings make wheeled transport impractical throughout El Nido.'),
  ('el-nido', 4668, 0, 'honeymoon_score: 94'),
  ('el-nido', 4668, 1, 'romance_score: 96'),
  ('el-nido', 4668, 2, 'privacy_score: 92'),
  ('el-nido', 4668, 3, 'luxury_score: 90'),
  ('el-nido', 4670, 0, 'Kayaking through hidden rock passageways into the clear, towering walls of the Big Lagoon and Small Lagoon.'),
  ('el-nido', 4670, 1, 'Scuba diving through underwater caverns and deep tunnels like the famous Dilumacad Tunnel and South Miniloc reef walls.'),
  ('el-nido', 4670, 2, 'Climbing the Via Ferrata Canopy Walk up Taraw Cliff for safer, panoramic aerial views overlooking El Nido Town and Bacuit Bay.'),
  ('el-nido', 4670, 3, 'Riding the inter-island zipline from Las Cabañas Beach high over the ocean to Depeldet Island.'),
  ('el-nido', 4670, 4, 'Motorbiking north to Duli Beach for open-ocean surfing, bodyboarding, and uncrowded coastal exploration.'),
  ('el-nido', 4670, 5, '**Bacuit Bay & Outer Islands** — best for sea kayaking, lagoon exploration, cliff jumping, and world-class scuba diving.'),
  ('el-nido', 4670, 6, '**Las Cabañas & Marimegmeg Beach** — best for inter-island ziplining, water sports, and coastal sunset adrenaline.'),
  ('el-nido', 4670, 7, '**Taraw Cliff & Poblacion Backdrops** — best for via-ferrata ridge climbing and high-elevation panoramic views.'),
  ('el-nido', 4670, 8, '**Northern El Nido (Duli & Nacpan)** — best for surfing, off-road motorbike riding, and jungle-to-beach trekking.'),
  ('el-nido', 4670, 9, 'Ocean adventurers, scuba divers, and sea kayakers.'),
  ('el-nido', 4670, 10, 'Adrenaline seekers wanting ziplining and rock-climbing challenges.'),
  ('el-nido', 4670, 11, 'Surfers and off-grid explorers renting scooters for rural coastal trails.'),
  ('el-nido', 4670, 12, 'Active travelers who love marine wildlife, snorkeling, and cave exploration.');
INSERT INTO destination_guidance_bullet (place_id, position, bullet_index, text) VALUES
  ('el-nido', 4670, 13, 'Backcountry hikers and tropical nature enthusiasts.'),
  ('el-nido', 4671, 0, 'Fly directly into El Nido''s Lio Airport (LIO) to bypass the exhausting 5- to 6-hour van drive from Puerto Princesa over winding roads.'),
  ('el-nido', 4671, 1, 'Book private outrigger boat charters (*bangkas*) instead of crowded group tours, enabling custom schedules, dedicated crew assistance with boat boarding, and easy opt-outs for strenuous swimming stops.'),
  ('el-nido', 4671, 2, 'Choose accommodation with guaranteed ground-floor rooms, step-free access, reliable air conditioning, and on-site dining—such as properties in Lio Beach or luxury island resorts—to avoid steep staircases.'),
  ('el-nido', 4671, 3, 'Pack supportive, non-slip water shoes for stepping onto wet boat ladders, shallow coral reef beds, and slippery limestone shores.'),
  ('el-nido', 4671, 4, 'Plan visits during the dry season (November to February) to ensure milder temperatures, lower humidity, and calm sea conditions for island hopping.'),
  ('el-nido', 4671, 5, 'Carry a comprehensive supply of personal prescription medications, basic first-aid items, and travel insurance covering medical evacuation, as local medical clinics handle basic needs only.'),
  ('el-nido', 4671, 6, 'Stay continuously hydrated and avoid direct sun exposure during peak heat hours (11:00 AM to 2:00 PM) by utilizing shaded boat decks and beach lounges.'),
  ('el-nido', 4671, 7, 'Booking gentle island-hopping routes (such as Tour D or sheltered stops on Tour A) that feature calm lagoons, short distances, and shallow boat-side snorkeling.'),
  ('el-nido', 4671, 8, 'Taking private catamaran or sailing yacht sunset cruises across Bacuit Bay for broad, stable deck seating and smooth sea travel.'),
  ('el-nido', 4671, 9, 'Spending relaxed beach days at Lio Beach or Nacpan Beach, where flat shorelines, shaded loungers, and easy road access eliminate the need for boat transfers.'),
  ('el-nido', 4671, 10, 'Utilizing local tricycles for short, low-cost transit across town zones rather than walking long distances on uneven or unpaved roads.'),
  ('el-nido', 4671, 11, 'Dining at flat, beachfront sit-down restaurants in Lio or Corong-Corong for scenic sunset views without climbing steep cliffside stairs.'),
  ('el-nido', 4671, 12, 'Attempting physically demanding stops like Secret Beach or Secret Lagoon that require swimming through narrow underwater portals or crawling through tight limestone gaps.'),
  ('el-nido', 4671, 13, 'Climbing the steep, sharp limestone paths of Taraw Cliff or taking fast-paced trekking tours.'),
  ('el-nido', 4671, 14, 'Relying on shared van shuttles over long distances, which lack supportive seating and make frequent unassisted stops.'),
  ('el-nido', 4671, 15, 'Staying in cliffside resorts or multi-story boutique hotels that lack elevators or paved access roads.'),
  ('el-nido', 4671, 16, 'Traveling during the monsoon season (June to October) when rough seas make boat landings unstable and walking paths slippery.'),
  ('el-nido', 4673, 0, 'Savor fresh **Kinilaw**, the signature raw fish dish of the island cured in native coconut vinegar and calamansi lime, mixed with fresh ginger, onions, and red chilies.'),
  ('el-nido', 4673, 1, 'Feast on a traditional **Island-Hopping Boat Buffet**, featuring charcoal-grilled entire fish, pork belly, sweet Philippine mangoes, and garlic rice served right on white-sand beaches.'),
  ('el-nido', 4673, 2, 'Order **Inihaw na Pusit** (whole stuffed grilled squid) or fresh snapper by the weight at beachside night market stalls, cooked directly over coconut charcoal.'),
  ('el-nido', 4673, 3, 'Try comforting **Sinigang na Isda**, a deeply savory and sour tamarind-based broth simmered with local fish and fresh water spinach (*kangkong*).'),
  ('el-nido', 4673, 4, 'Cool off with a tall glass of **Halo-Halo**, a refreshing shaved-ice sundae layered with purple yam (*ube*) ice cream, sweet beans, coconut jellies, and creamy *leche flan*.'),
  ('el-nido', 4673, 5, '**Families:** Relaxed beachfront dining along Lio Beach, child-friendly pizzerias, and freshly blended tropical fruit smoothies served all over town.'),
  ('el-nido', 4673, 6, '**Honeymooners:** Candlelit seafood dinners on the sand at Corong-Corong Beach, romantic sunset craft cocktails, and intimate open-air dining in Bacuit Bay.'),
  ('el-nido', 4673, 7, '**Luxury travelers:** Private chef island beach picnics, multi-course seafood tasting menus at private island resorts, and upscale eco-luxury dining on Lio Estate.'),
  ('el-nido', 4673, 8, '**Budget travelers:** Local *carinderia* eateries serving home-cooked rice plates, fresh fruit stands, and budget-friendly fish grills around the El Nido Public Market.'),
  ('el-nido', 4673, 9, '**Foodies:** Artisanal Filipino bean-to-cup coffee shops, natural wine and Mediterranean tapas lounges, and fresh market-to-table seafood tasting crawls.'),
  ('el-nido', 4673, 10, '**Calle Hama & Serena Street (Poblacion):** Best for bustling pedestrian streets lined with Italian pizzerias, international cafes, gelato shops, and lively beachfront seafood restaurants.'),
  ('el-nido', 4673, 11, '**Corong-Corong Beach:** Best for open-air sunset bars, Spanish tapas, fresh seafood grills, and chic relaxed beachfront dining right on the water.'),
  ('el-nido', 4673, 12, '**Lio Beach:** Best for a spacious, eco-friendly dining strip featuring upscale bistros, specialty coffee shops, craft beer bars, and family-friendly outdoor seating.'),
  ('el-nido', 4673, 13, '**Real Street & Public Market Zone:** Best for authentic local *carinderias*, affordable night market seafood grills, and budget Filipino comfort food.'),
  ('el-nido', 4674, 0, '**Palawan Roasted Cashews (*Kasoy*):** Locally harvested cashews sold in various flavors like roasted, fried, salted, garlic, or caramelized—a staple regional edible souvenir.'),
  ('el-nido', 4674, 1, '**Palawan Wild Honey & Local Jams:** Pure, raw harvested wild honey and artisanal coconut jams or cashew butter packed in travel-friendly jars.'),
  ('el-nido', 4674, 2, '**Handmade Woven Goods & Baskets:** Eco-friendly handwoven *nito* baskets, *buri* bags, mats, and woven bamboo crafts made by local island artisans.'),
  ('el-nido', 4674, 3, '**Island Wear & Waterproof Accessories:** Locally printed t-shirts, breezy sarongs, linen beachwear, sun hats, heavy-duty dry bags, and ocean-ready aqua shoes.'),
  ('el-nido', 4674, 4, '**Pearl & Shell Jewelry:** Cultivated Palawan South Sea pearl accessories, capiz shell crafts, and carved wooden souvenirs.'),
  ('el-nido', 4674, 5, '**Serena Street & Calle Hama (Poblacion):** Best for walkable boutique hopping, locally screen-printed resort wear, eco-friendly souvenirs, dry bags, and artisanal cafes.'),
  ('el-nido', 4674, 6, '**The Shoppes at Vanilla Beach (Las Cabañas):** Preferred for a modern open-air beachfront shopping strip featuring stylish swim boutiques, lifestyle brands, and sunset souvenir shops.'),
  ('el-nido', 4674, 7, '**El Nido Boutique ArtCafe:** Ideal for high-quality island apparel, local handicrafts, organic farm products, dive gear, and reliable travel essentials.'),
  ('el-nido', 4674, 8, '**El Nido Public Market (Corong-Corong):** Preferred for affordable bulk purchases of fresh local tropical fruits, Palawan cashews, dried fish (*daing*), and budget souvenirs.'),
  ('el-nido', 4674, 9, 'Buying products made from endangered marine life, such as real sea turtle shells or protected giant clam shells, which are strictly illegal to export.'),
  ('el-nido', 4674, 10, 'Expecting large automated teller coverage; carry sufficient cash (Philippine Pesos) when shopping at local street stalls and public markets as card readers can lose signal.'),
  ('el-nido', 4674, 11, 'Purchasing high-priced "South Sea pearls" from unverified street hawkers on the beach without authentic certificates of authenticity.'),
  ('el-nido', 4674, 12, '**Beach & Resort Shoppers:** Travelers needing last-minute swimwear, dry bags, snorkeling accessories, and breezy island clothing.'),
  ('el-nido', 4674, 13, '**Souvenir & Craft Collectors:** Visitors seeking handwoven Philippine baskets, pearl jewelry, wooden carvings, and local artisan keepsakes.'),
  ('el-nido', 4674, 14, '**Foodie Keepsake Hunters:** Travelers wanting to pack authentic Palawan cashews, wild honey, and local sweet delicacies to bring home.'),
  ('el-nido', 4675, 0, '**Sunset worshipers & cocktail lovers** looking for cliffside vantage points, beachfront happy hours, and artisan rum cocktails.'),
  ('el-nido', 4675, 1, '**Backpackers & solo travelers** seeking social hostel bars, fire-spinning beach shows, and lively pub-crawl crowds along narrow island streets.'),
  ('el-nido', 4675, 2, '**Live music & acoustic fans** hunting for cozy reggae venues, open-mic nights, and local jam sessions in rustic timber bars.'),
  ('el-nido', 4675, 3, '**Chilled-out beachgoers** wanting to sip cold San Miguel beers barefoot in the sand while listening to ambient reggae or low-fi beats.'),
  ('el-nido', 4675, 4, 'Catching breathtaking Bacuit Bay views over pre-dinner drinks at cliffside or beachfront venues like *Republica Sunset Bar* or *Las Cabañas Beach Club*.'),
  ('el-nido', 4675, 5, 'Hopping between bohemian, sand-floored drinking spots along **Calle Hama** in El Nido Town Proper, where the late-night action concentrates.'),
  ('el-nido', 4675, 6, 'Enjoying live reggae, acoustic covers, and OPM (Original Pilipino Music) at cozy island staples like *Pukka Bar* or *Happiness Beach Bar*.'),
  ('el-nido', 4675, 7, 'Lounging on beach mats and beanbags in **Corong-Corong** for a quieter, romantic evening of wine and seafood by the shore.'),
  ('el-nido', 4675, 8, 'Expecting massive, high-tech dance clubs with dress codes; El Nido is strictly casual—flip-flops and beachwear are standard almost everywhere.'),
  ('el-nido', 4675, 9, 'Walking back along unlit beaches or dark coastal stretches late at night; hire a tricycle or stick to well-traveled main paths in town.'),
  ('el-nido', 4675, 10, 'Relying exclusively on credit cards or mobile wallets for late-night bar tabs; cash is essential as card readers and internet connections can be unreliable.'),
  ('el-nido', 4675, 11, '**Poblacion (El Nido Town Proper):** The dense main hub featuring the *Calle Hama* and *Rizal Street* strip, packed with dive bars, open-air reggae spots, rooftop lounges, and night-market eats.'),
  ('el-nido', 4675, 12, '**Las Cabañas (Maremegmeg Beach):** The premier sunset party zone, ideal for golden-hour beach bars, zipline views, and casual music under palm trees.'),
  ('el-nido', 4675, 13, '**Corong-Corong Beach:** A slightly more relaxed alternative to town, perfect for romantic sunset lounges, Italian trattorias, and seaside cocktail spots.'),
  ('el-nido', 4680, 0, '**Gilutongan Island:** Snorkeling paradise with vibrant corals and rich marine life.'),
  ('el-nido', 4680, 1, '**Caohagan Island:** Peaceful island with local charm and relaxing shoreline vibes.'),
  ('el-nido', 4680, 2, '**Nalusuan Island:** Famous boardwalk and marine sanctuary—perfect for photos and swimming.'),
  ('el-nido', 4680, 3, '**Blood Compact Shrine:** Historical site commemorating the first treaty between Filipinos and Spaniards.'),
  ('el-nido', 4680, 4, '**Baclayon Church:** One of the oldest stone churches in the Philippines, rich in heritage.'),
  ('el-nido', 4680, 5, '**Man-Made Forest:** Picturesque stretch of mahogany trees creating a natural canopy.'),
  ('el-nido', 4680, 6, '**Exotic Wildlife Encounter:** Visit a sanctuary with pythons and butterflies.'),
  ('el-nido', 4680, 7, '**Tarsier Conservation Area:** See the world’s smallest primates up close in their natural habitat.'),
  ('el-nido', 4680, 8, '**Chocolate Hills:** Bohol’s iconic geological wonder offering panoramic viewing deck vistas.'),
  ('el-nido', 4681, 0, 'Arrival at El Nido Airport (ENI) and warm family meet-and-greet'),
  ('el-nido', 4681, 1, 'Private transfer to hotel, seamless check-in, and time for the family to unwind after traveling'),
  ('el-nido', 4681, 2, 'Evening free for leisure to explore nearby local cafes or relax at the hotel'),
  ('el-nido', 4681, 3, 'Overnight stay at **BEST WESTERN PLUS HOTEL** (or similar) in Puerto Princesa'),
  ('el-nido', 4681, 4, 'Family breakfast at the hotel'),
  ('el-nido', 4681, 5, 'Pick up for the iconic UNESCO World Heritage Underground River Tour with an included picnic lunch'),
  ('el-nido', 4681, 6, 'Arrive at Sabang Wharf and embark on the Underground River Cave Exploration Experience, marveling at thousand-year-old stalagmites and stalactites with child-friendly audio guides'),
  ('el-nido', 4681, 7, 'Enjoy a scenic picnic lunch by Sabang Beach'),
  ('el-nido', 4681, 8, 'Proceed to El Nido by private comfortable van (approx. 6 hours journey through Palawan''s lush countryside)'),
  ('el-nido', 4681, 9, '*Note: Arrival in El Nido is typically around 10:00 PM – 11:00 PM following the tour and transit from PPS*'),
  ('el-nido', 4681, 10, 'Check-in and late night rest'),
  ('el-nido', 4681, 11, 'Overnight stay at **El Nido Garden Resort** (or similar) in El Nido'),
  ('el-nido', 4681, 12, 'Breakfast at the resort with beachfront views'),
  ('el-nido', 4681, 13, 'Proceed for Island Hopping Tour A aboard a private outrigger boat with a local grilled lunch included'),
  ('el-nido', 4681, 14, 'Visit the iconic **Big Lagoon** (family kayaking through crystal turquoise waters), **Small Lagoon**, and the hidden passage of **Secret Lagoon**'),
  ('el-nido', 4681, 15, 'Stop at **Shimizu Island** for world-class snorkeling among colorful fish and sea turtles'),
  ('el-nido', 4681, 16, 'Relax along the white coconut palm shores of **Seven Commandos Beach**'),
  ('el-nido', 4681, 17, 'Return to El Nido town center for an evening stroll'),
  ('el-nido', 4681, 18, 'Overnight stay at **El Nido Garden Resort** (or similar) in El Nido'),
  ('el-nido', 4681, 19, 'Breakfast at the resort'),
  ('el-nido', 4681, 20, 'Embark on El Nido Island Hopping Tour C, famous for dramatic limestone formations and secluded beaches, with local lunch included'),
  ('el-nido', 4681, 21, 'Crawl through a natural rock opening to discover **Secret Beach** and explore the secluded shores of **Hidden Beach**'),
  ('el-nido', 4681, 22, 'Admire the distinct shape of **Helicopter Island** (Dilumacad Island) and swim along **Talisay Beach**'),
  ('el-nido', 4681, 23, 'Snorkel in pristine marine protection areas teeming with vibrant coral reefs'),
  ('el-nido', 4681, 24, 'Return to the hotel in the late afternoon for relaxed family dining along Corong-Corong or town proper'),
  ('el-nido', 4681, 25, 'Overnight stay at **El Nido Garden Resort** (or similar) in El Nido'),
  ('el-nido', 4681, 26, 'Breakfast at the hotel'),
  ('el-nido', 4681, 27, 'Check out and transfer to Lio Airport (ENI) or Puerto Princesa Airport for your domestic flight to Caticlan (Boracay)'),
  ('el-nido', 4681, 28, 'Transfer via land and boat to Boracay Island, followed by smooth check-in at your beachfront resort'),
  ('el-nido', 4681, 29, 'Evening free for the family to stroll along the famous soft sands of White Beach and catch a tropical sunset'),
  ('el-nido', 4681, 30, 'Overnight stay at **Boracay Mandarin Bay Resort and Spa** (or similar) in Boracay'),
  ('el-nido', 4681, 31, 'Breakfast at the resort'),
  ('el-nido', 4681, 32, 'Board your boat for a fun-filled family Island Hopping Tour across Boracay’s outer coves (SIC Basis)'),
  ('el-nido', 4681, 33, 'Explore **Puka Shell Beach** for family swimming, shelling, photo opportunities, and souvenir shopping'),
  ('el-nido', 4681, 34, 'Visit **Crystal Cove Island** to explore its natural sea caves and private viewpoints'),
  ('el-nido', 4681, 35, 'Enjoy an included beachside lunch buffet during the tour'),
  ('el-nido', 4681, 36, 'Return to Station 2/3 and spend the evening at leisure along the vibrant beachfront D''Mall'),
  ('el-nido', 4681, 37, 'Overnight stay at **Boracay Mandarin Bay Resort and Spa** (or similar) in Boracay'),
  ('el-nido', 4681, 38, 'Breakfast at the resort'),
  ('el-nido', 4681, 39, 'Morning completely free for leisure—enjoy the resort pool, build sandcastles, or try gentle family water sports'),
  ('el-nido', 4681, 40, 'Around 3:00 PM, meet for a breathtaking **Boracay Sunset Paraw Cruise**, sailing into the golden hour aboard a traditional outrigger sailboat'),
  ('el-nido', 4681, 41, 'Return to the resort for an evening of beachside dining and live acoustic entertainment'),
  ('el-nido', 4681, 42, 'Overnight stay at **Boracay Mandarin Bay Resort and Spa** (or similar) in Boracay'),
  ('el-nido', 4681, 43, 'Breakfast at the hotel'),
  ('el-nido', 4681, 44, 'Check out of the resort and transfer to Caticlan Airport (MPH)'),
  ('el-nido', 4681, 45, 'Domestic flight to Cebu (Mactan-Cebu International Airport)'),
  ('el-nido', 4681, 46, 'Meet-and-greet upon arrival in Cebu and private transfer to hotel'),
  ('el-nido', 4681, 47, 'Check in and spend the evening relaxing or exploring nearby dining hubs'),
  ('el-nido', 4681, 48, 'Overnight stay at **BAI Hotel** (or similar) in Cebu'),
  ('el-nido', 4681, 49, 'Breakfast at the hotel'),
  ('el-nido', 4681, 50, 'Embark on a comprehensive family Cebu City & Highland Tour covering major cultural and modern highlights:'),
  ('el-nido', 4681, 51, 'Visit the grand Roman-inspired **Temple of Leah** overlooking the city skyline'),
  ('el-nido', 4681, 52, 'Stop at the charming French bakery hub **La Vie Parisienne**'),
  ('el-nido', 4681, 53, 'Explore historic sites: **Heritage Park**, **Yap-San Diego Ancestral House**, and **Fort San Pedro**'),
  ('el-nido', 4681, 54, 'Visit **Magellan''s Cross** and the revered **Santo Niño Church**'),
  ('el-nido', 4681, 55, 'Drive up to **Tops Lookout** for stunning nighttime views of Metropolitan Cebu'),
  ('el-nido', 4681, 56, 'Cross the impressive **CCLEX Bridge** (Cebu–Cordova Link Expressway)'),
  ('el-nido', 4681, 57, 'Visit the romantic illuminated garden of **10,000 Roses** in Cordova'),
  ('el-nido', 4681, 58, 'Return to hotel late evening'),
  ('el-nido', 4681, 59, 'Overnight stay at **BAI Hotel** (or similar) in Cebu'),
  ('el-nido', 4681, 60, 'Early morning departure (approx. 3:00 AM) heading south to Tan-awan, Oslob *(packed breakfast provided by the hotel)*'),
  ('el-nido', 4681, 61, '**Oslob Whale Shark Watching**: An unforgettable experience swimming and snorkeling near gentle whale shark giants under strict eco-guides'),
  ('el-nido', 4681, 62, 'Proceed to Badian for the famous **Kawasan Waterfalls**, marveling at its legendary turquoise river waters'),
  ('el-nido', 4681, 63, 'Enjoy family-friendly river trekking and the **Kawasan Canyoneering** activity (tailored for safety and fun with certified local guides)'),
  ('el-nido', 4681, 64, 'Scenic drive back to Cebu City in the afternoon'),
  ('el-nido', 4681, 65, 'Overnight stay at **BAI Hotel** (or similar) in Cebu'),
  ('el-nido', 4681, 66, 'Breakfast at the hotel'),
  ('el-nido', 4681, 67, 'Morning pick-up around 7:00 AM and transfer to Mactan wharf for an island-hopping marine sanctuary adventure:'),
  ('el-nido', 4681, 68, '**Gilutongan Island**: Snorkeling paradise filled with rich marine life and colorful coral gardens'),
  ('el-nido', 4681, 69, '**Caohagan Island**: Peaceful island village offering authentic local charm and relaxing sandy shorelines'),
  ('el-nido', 4681, 70, '**Nalusuan Island**: Famous for its scenic wooden boardwalk and protected marine sanctuary, ideal for fish feeding and swimming'),
  ('el-nido', 4681, 71, 'Enjoy a fresh seafood and island lunch before cruising back to Mactan'),
  ('el-nido', 4681, 72, 'Return transfer to hotel and evening at leisure'),
  ('el-nido', 4681, 73, 'Overnight stay at **BAI Hotel** (or similar) in Cebu'),
  ('el-nido', 4681, 74, 'Breakfast at the hotel'),
  ('el-nido', 4681, 75, 'Early morning ferry transfer across the Cebu Strait to Tagbilaran, Bohol, for a full-day countryside excursion:'),
  ('el-nido', 4681, 76, '**Blood Compact Shrine**: Historical monument commemorating the first treaty of friendship between Spain and the Philippines'),
  ('el-nido', 4681, 77, '**Baclayon Church**: One of the oldest stone churches in the country with a rich heritage museum'),
  ('el-nido', 4681, 78, '**Bohol Man-Made Forest**: Ride through a dense, picturesque green canopy stretch of mahogany trees'),
  ('el-nido', 4681, 79, '**Exotic Wildlife Encounter**: Visit a local sanctuary featuring native pythons and butterflies'),
  ('el-nido', 4681, 80, '**Tarsier Conservation Area**: Get up close with the world’s smallest primates in their natural forested habitat'),
  ('el-nido', 4681, 81, '**Chocolate Hills**: Marvel at Bohol''s world-famous geological wonder from the main viewing deck'),
  ('el-nido', 4681, 82, 'Afternoon return ferry to Cebu and transfer back to hotel'),
  ('el-nido', 4681, 83, 'Overnight stay at **BAI Hotel** (or similar) in Cebu'),
  ('el-nido', 4681, 84, 'Breakfast at the hotel'),
  ('el-nido', 4681, 85, 'Check out of the hotel and private transfer to Mactan-Cebu International Airport (CEB) for your international departure flight home'),
  ('el-nido', 4683, 0, 'Treat El Nido as a quick 1-day island-hopping stop, underestimating the travel time required to reach northern Palawan and missing out on inland beaches, cultural sites, and outer islands.'),
  ('el-nido', 4683, 1, 'Over-schedule multiple group tours back-to-back without accounting for physical exhaustion, sun exposure, and unpredictable ocean swells in Bacuit Bay.'),
  ('el-nido', 4683, 2, 'Attempt to navigate the area using only credit cards or digital payments, failing to realize that cash is essential for island environmental fees, small boat operators, and local tricycles.'),
  ('el-nido', 4683, 3, 'Book mainland accommodations far from central boat departure points without arranging reliable daily transfers, leading to missed morning tour departures.'),
  ('el-nido', 4683, 4, 'Expect high-speed, seamless internet connectivity and uninterrupted electrical power everywhere on the island, causing frustration during remote stays.'),
  ('el-nido', 4684, 0, 'Allocates at least 3 to 4 full days in El Nido to balance core island-hopping routes (Tour A and Tour C) with relaxed land-based beach days at Nacpan or Lio Beach.'),
  ('el-nido', 4684, 1, 'Arranges private outrigger boat charters to allow clients to customize schedules, depart earlier than standard group tours, and reach popular lagoons before the crowds arrive.'),
  ('el-nido', 4684, 2, 'Coordinates smooth multi-modal transit by booking direct flights into Lio Airport (ENI) or arranging private executive van transfers from Puerto Princesa (PPS).'),
  ('el-nido', 4684, 3, 'Incorporates a mix of eco-luxury island resorts and mainland boutique hotels to give clients both exclusive overwater experiences and easy access to Poblacion''s dining scene.'),
  ('el-nido', 4684, 4, 'Pre-registers client permits and environment fees for restricted destinations like the Big Lagoon and Small Lagoon well in advance to ensure guaranteed access.'),
  ('el-nido', 4685, 0, 'For **Island-Hopping Pacing**, schedule heavy water activity days on alternating days, leaving open afternoons for sunset dining or land-based relaxation to prevent burnout.'),
  ('el-nido', 4685, 1, 'For **Arrival Logistics**, book direct flights to El Nido''s Lio Airport whenever possible; if flying via Puerto Princesa, always secure a private air-conditioned vehicle for the 5- to 6-hour land transfer.'),
  ('el-nido', 4685, 2, 'For **Itinerary Balance**, dedicate a minimum of 4 nights to El Nido to cover Bacuit Bay''s signature marine sights while leaving room for unexpected weather shifts or coast guard itinerary adjustments.'),
  ('el-nido', 4688, 0, 'Charter a private early-morning boat for Island Hopping Tour A to kayak through the tranquil waters of the Big Lagoon before public tour groups arrive.'),
  ('el-nido', 4688, 1, 'Swim through the narrow cliff opening into the Secret Lagoon and explore the hidden beach alcoves of Shimizu Island and Seven Commandos Beach.'),
  ('el-nido', 4688, 2, 'Take Island Hopping Tour C to discover Secret Beach, wade onto Hidden Beach, and snorkel around the vibrant coral gardens off Helicopter Island and Talisay Beach.'),
  ('el-nido', 4688, 3, 'Catch world-famous tropical sunsets over cocktails along Las Cabañas Beach or Nacpan Beach.'),
  ('el-nido', 4688, 4, 'Enjoy a fresh seafood barbecue lunch prepared island-style directly on the white sand beaches during your boat excursion.'),
  ('el-nido', 4688, 5, 'Relying solely on public group boat tours, which can feel crowded and strictly follow standard timed itineraries at popular lagoon spots.'),
  ('el-nido', 4688, 6, 'Underestimating cash requirements—while luxury resorts accept cards, island environmental fees, local tricycles, and small beach vendors operate almost strictly on cash.'),
  ('el-nido', 4688, 7, 'Scheduling direct international flight connections on the same day as your El Nido departure without buffering for weather or domestic flight delays.'),
  ('el-nido', 4688, 8, 'Forgetting water shoes, dry bags, and reef-safe sunscreen—sharp limestone rocks, sea urchins, and splashing ocean spray are part of daily island exploration.'),
  ('el-nido', 4689, 0, 'To be populated with authoritative tourism/transport/attraction sources before production use.'),
  ('boracay', 4697, 0, 'Withdraw sufficient Philippine Pesos (PHP) at Caticlan Airport or major bank ATMs in Station 2 before venturing to smaller beach vendors, as local ATMs on the island occasionally go offline, run out of cash during high-volume holiday weekends, or charge international cash advance fees (₱250 plus bank surcharges).'),
  ('boracay', 4697, 1, 'Eat at local *carinderias* (Filipino eateries), local bakeries, or non-beachfront eateries along the main road behind Station 2 and Station 3, where authentic local meals cost between ₱120 and ₱220 ($2.00–$4.00 USD), compared to upscale beachfront resorts and D''Mall international restaurants that charge ₱400 to ₱900 per dish.'),
  ('boracay', 4697, 2, 'Take shared Hop-On Hop-Off (HOHO) buses or public e-trikes along the main road for ₱15 to ₱50 ($0.25–$0.90 USD) per ride instead of chartering private e-trikes, which can charge ₱150 to ₱350+ for short point-to-point trips.'),
  ('boracay', 4697, 3, 'Join a group island-hopping boat tour (₱800–₱1,200 per person) including stops at Puka Shell Beach, Crocodile Island, and a buffet lunch, rather than hiring a private outrigger boat charter (₱3,500–₱6,000) if traveling solo or as a couple.'),
  ('boracay', 4697, 4, 'Purchase basic beach equipment—such as a waterproof dry bag (₱250–₱450) and your own snorkel mask—at D''Mall or local shops in town to avoid paying recurring daily rental fees at activity boat hubs.'),
  ('boracay', 4697, 5, 'Skipping the advance payment or official payment window for mandatory government entry fees (₱300 Environmental Fee, ₱150 Caticlan Terminal Fee, and ₱50 Boat Fare), as skipping or attempting to bypass official port ticketing can lead to denied entry onto the island.'),
  ('boracay', 4697, 6, 'Buying unverified or steeply discounted water sports vouchers (such as parasailing, jet skiing, or helmet diving) from unlicensed beach hawkers on White Beach, who often omit mandatory safety gear, use uncertified equipment, or lack proper insurance coverage.'),
  ('boracay', 4697, 7, 'Booking cheap accommodation on extreme off-road locations or far-flung hillsides purely for low night rates, as difficult accessibility, lack of direct road access, and constant e-trike fares back to the beach will quickly offset any initial savings.'),
  ('boracay', 4697, 8, 'Opting out of comprehensive travel insurance covering emergency medical treatment or water sports injuries, as Boracay has basic medical clinics and urgent, complex trauma care requires emergency air or sea transport to Panay or Manila.'),
  ('boracay', 4698, 0, '2+'),
  ('boracay', 4698, 1, '4+'),
  ('boracay', 4698, 2, '6+'),
  ('boracay', 4698, 3, '8+'),
  ('boracay', 4698, 4, 'Teenagers'),
  ('boracay', 4698, 5, 'Stay in Station 1 or Station 2 directly on White Beach for easy, flat access to the sand and calm waters, minimizing long e-trike rides with small kids.'),
  ('boracay', 4698, 6, 'Bring fitted child-sized life jackets and floating arm bands for island-hopping boat tours, as local outrigger boats (*bangkas*) primarily carry standard adult-sized vests.'),
  ('boracay', 4698, 7, 'Pack sturdy water shoes for the whole family when joining island-hopping tours to protect young feet from coral fragments and sea urchins at shallow reef stops like Crocodile Island.'),
  ('boracay', 4698, 8, 'Hire a private boat charter for family island hopping instead of shared joiner tours to customize stop lengths, manage nap schedules, and return to shore if children get tired or seasick.'),
  ('boracay', 4698, 9, 'Utilize baby carriers or slings rather than strollers, as soft sand along White Beach and narrow, uneven alleyways make wheeled pushchairs nearly impossible to roll.'),
  ('boracay', 4698, 10, 'Keep children hydrated and protected from intense sun by applying reef-safe sunscreen, wearing UV-protective rash guards, and staying shaded during peak afternoon heat (11 AM to 3 PM).'),
  ('boracay', 4699, 0, 'honeymoon_score: 96');
INSERT INTO destination_guidance_bullet (place_id, position, bullet_index, text) VALUES
  ('boracay', 4699, 1, 'romance_score: 95'),
  ('boracay', 4699, 2, 'privacy_score: 88'),
  ('boracay', 4699, 3, 'luxury_score: 92'),
  ('boracay', 4701, 0, 'Kitesurfing and windsurfing across the shallow, wind-swept waters of Bulabog Beach.'),
  ('boracay', 4701, 1, 'Taking the leap with cliff jumping from platforms ranging up to 15 meters at Ariel’s Point or Magic Island.'),
  ('boracay', 4701, 2, 'Parasailing high above White Beach for panoramic aerial views of the entire island and coral reefs.'),
  ('boracay', 4701, 3, 'Riding high-speed water crafts including jet skis, wakeboards, and towed flyfish or banana boats in designated offshore activity zones.'),
  ('boracay', 4701, 4, 'Scuba diving deep wreck and wall sites such as the Camia Wreck, Yapak Drop-Off, and Friday''s Rock.'),
  ('boracay', 4701, 5, '**Bulabog Beach (East Coast)** — best for kitesurfing, windsurfing, and wind-powered adrenaline sports.'),
  ('boracay', 4701, 6, '**Offshore Activity Platforms & Water Sports Zone** — best for jet skiing, parasailing, flyfish, and helmet diving.'),
  ('boracay', 4701, 7, '**Ariel’s Point & Magic Island** — best for open-ocean cliff jumping, sea kayaking, and snorkeling day trips.'),
  ('boracay', 4701, 8, '**Mount Luho & Inland Trails** — best for ATV quad biking, mainland buggy tours, and elevated ziplining.'),
  ('boracay', 4701, 9, 'Kitesurfers, windsurfers, and water-sports enthusiasts.'),
  ('boracay', 4701, 10, 'Thrill-seekers looking for cliff jumping, parasailing, and jet skiing.'),
  ('boracay', 4701, 11, 'Certified scuba divers eager to explore offshore wrecks and wall drop-offs.'),
  ('boracay', 4701, 12, 'Active travelers who enjoy high-speed ocean activities and aerial island views.'),
  ('boracay', 4701, 13, 'Off-road ATV riders and land-adventure lovers.'),
  ('boracay', 4702, 0, 'Book private, seamless airport transfers (such as resort-managed VIP speedboats) from Caticlan Airport (MPH) to avoid waiting in crowded public ferry lines and navigating steep boat ramps with heavy luggage.'),
  ('boracay', 4702, 1, 'Choose beachfront accommodations with ground-floor rooms or elevator access, level beach paths, on-site dining, and private lounger zones—particularly in Station 1 or Station 0—to eliminate stair climbing and road traffic.'),
  ('boracay', 4702, 2, 'Pack supportive water shoes and non-slip sandals for walking along wet boat ramps, soft sand, and tiled resort walkways.'),
  ('boracay', 4702, 3, 'Travel during the dry season (*Amihan*, December to April) when White Beach enjoys glassy, calm waters, flat boat landings, and clear sunny weather.'),
  ('boracay', 4702, 4, 'Carry an adequate supply of personal prescription medications, as island pharmacies may have limited stock for specialized healthcare needs.'),
  ('boracay', 4702, 5, 'Stay continuously hydrated and seek shade or air-conditioned spaces during peak afternoon heat (11:00 AM to 2:00 PM).'),
  ('boracay', 4702, 6, 'Confirm that hotel bathrooms feature walk-in showers or grab rails, as some older boutique properties only offer deep bathtubs or stepped shower entries.'),
  ('boracay', 4702, 7, 'Chartering a private *paraw* sailboat for a gentle, scenic sunset cruise along White Beach with personalized assistance for stepping on and off the vessel.'),
  ('boracay', 4702, 8, 'Staying in Station 1 or Station 0 for wider beachfronts, peaceful surroundings, flat sand entry, and low foot-traffic density.'),
  ('boracay', 4702, 9, 'Taking shared e-trikes or hop-on hop-off (HOHO) tourist buses for effortless transport along the paved main inland road.'),
  ('boracay', 4702, 10, 'Relaxing at flat, open-air beachfront cafés and restaurants in Station 1 or Station 2 for sunset dining right on the sand.'),
  ('boracay', 4702, 11, 'Enjoying gentle wellness treatments, beachfront massages, or leisurely strolls along the firm, packed sand near the water''s edge during low tide.'),
  ('boracay', 4702, 12, 'Participating in high-impact or jerky water sports like Flyfish rides, banana boats, jet skiing, or ATV land tours over bumpy terrain.'),
  ('boracay', 4702, 13, 'Joining crowded group island-hopping boats with high gunwales that require climbing vertical metal ladders from deep water.'),
  ('boracay', 4702, 14, 'Flying into Kalibo Airport (KLO) if possible, as it adds an exhausting 1.5-to-2-hour land van transfer before reaching the ferry port.'),
  ('boracay', 4702, 15, 'Staying in hilltop resorts or cliffside accommodations around Mount Luho or Diniwid that rely heavily on steep stairways or lack elevator access.'),
  ('boracay', 4702, 16, 'Visiting during the peak *Habagat* monsoon season (July to October) when strong winds cause waves and shifts in boat landing sites to the windward side of the island.'),
  ('boracay', 4704, 0, 'Savor authentic **Calamansi Muffins**, a legendary island pastry that balances sweet, crumbly cake with a tart, citrusy local lime punch.'),
  ('boracay', 4704, 1, 'Indulge in a classic **D''Talipapa Seafood Feast**, where you select fresh live lobsters, crabs, and prawns directly from the wet market and have nearby restaurants cook them to order (e.g., butter garlic or sweet chili).'),
  ('boracay', 4704, 2, 'Try **Choriburger**, Boracay’s iconic street food staple consisting of grilled sweet Filipino chorizo patties brushed with spicy banana ketchup inside a toasted bun.'),
  ('boracay', 4704, 3, 'Refresh with a rich **Mango Milkshake**, blended fresh daily using sweet Philippine Carabao mangoes along the White Beach promenade.'),
  ('boracay', 4704, 4, 'Feast on authentic **Cebuano Lechon** and **Inasal**, featuring spit-roasted pork with crispy skin and charcoal-grilled chicken marinated in calamansi, lemongrass, and annatto oil.'),
  ('boracay', 4704, 5, '**Families:** Relaxed beachfront dining at D''Mall, kid-friendly pizzerias, all-day breakfast cafes, and dessert stalls with shaved ice treats.'),
  ('boracay', 4704, 6, '**Honeymooners:** Candlelit multi-course seafood dinners right on White Beach in Station 1, private cove dining, and sunset craft cocktail lounges.'),
  ('boracay', 4704, 7, '**Luxury travelers:** Upscale oceanfront fine dining at Station Zero resorts, chef-driven tasting menus, private yacht catering, and wine pairing experiences.'),
  ('boracay', 4704, 8, '**Budget travelers:** Local *carinderia* eateries along the main road, affordable street food skewers, fast-casual grill chains, and bakeries in Station 3.'),
  ('boracay', 4704, 9, '**Foodies:** Fusion Filipino-Mediterranean tapas bars, artisanal specialty coffee shops, Korean barbecue spots, and vibrant beachfront buffet crawls.'),
  ('boracay', 4704, 10, '**D''Mall & Station 2:** Best for the central dining epicenter featuring international restaurants, burger shacks, cafes, gelato spots, and lively open-air bars.'),
  ('boracay', 4704, 11, '**Station 1 Beachfront:** Best for high-end beachfront dining, romantic sunset cocktail lounges, upscale brunch cafes, and refined international cuisine.'),
  ('boracay', 4704, 12, '**Station 3 & Main Road:** Best for budget-friendly local *carinderias*, authentic Filipino eateries, affordable seafood grills, and cozy, quiet beachfront cafes.'),
  ('boracay', 4704, 13, '**Station Zero (Yapak):** Best for private, luxury resort fine dining, exclusive seafood tasting menus, and peaceful clifftop culinary experiences.'),
  ('boracay', 4705, 0, '**Boracay Beachwear & Resort Fashion:** Locally designed linen shirts, breezy dresses, bamboo sunglasses, sun hats, swimwear, and island-branded apparel.'),
  ('boracay', 4705, 1, '**Handmade Shell & Coconut Crafts:** Intricately carved coconut crafts, capiz shell home decor, woven tote bags, and locally crafted costume jewelry.'),
  ('boracay', 4705, 2, '**South Sea & Freshwater Pearl Accessories:** Locally strung pearl necklaces, earrings, and bracelets sourced from Philippine waters.'),
  ('boracay', 4705, 3, '**Waterproof Gear & Beach Essentials:** Ocean-ready dry bags, rash guards, water shoes, reef-safe sunscreen, and UV-protection swimwear.'),
  ('boracay', 4705, 4, '**Local Edible Souvenirs (*Pasalubong*):** Crispy banana chips, dried mangoes, calamansi muffins, coconut jam, and local artisanal sweets packed for travel.'),
  ('boracay', 4705, 5, '**D''Mall Boracay (Station 2):** The central open-air shopping, dining, and retail hub of the island, best for boutique clothing stores, beach gear, souvenir stalls, and money changers.'),
  ('boracay', 4705, 6, '**D''Talipapa Market (Station 2/3):** Preferred for traditional market shopping, handwoven crafts, affordable souvenir t-shirts, pearls, and fresh seafood markets.'),
  ('boracay', 4705, 7, '**CityMall Boracay (Yapak):** Ideal for an air-conditioned modern shopping experience featuring a full supermarket, pharmacy, local retail shops, and essential services.'),
  ('boracay', 4705, 8, '**Station 1 Beachfront Boutiques:** Preferred for high-end resort wear, artisanal jewelry, designer swimwear, and premium organic skincare products.'),
  ('boracay', 4705, 9, 'Purchasing items made from protected marine species, such as real sea turtle shells, corals, or giant clam shells, which are strictly illegal to buy or export.'),
  ('boracay', 4705, 10, 'Buying high-priced "genuine pearls" from unverified roving hawkers on the sand without proper certificates or authenticity tests.'),
  ('boracay', 4705, 11, 'Relying exclusively on credit cards when browsing smaller stalls at D''Talipapa; carry Philippine Pesos in small denominations for easier transactions.'),
  ('boracay', 4705, 12, '**Resort Wear & Fashion Enthusiasts:** Travelers looking to update their tropical wardrobe with stylish swimwear, linen clothing, and handmade island accessories.'),
  ('boracay', 4705, 13, '**Souvenir & Craft Collectors:** Visitors wanting authentic Philippine keepsakes, handwoven totes, shell crafts, and personalized Boracay mementos.'),
  ('boracay', 4705, 14, '**Pasalubong Hunters:** Travelers seeking popular local food gifts like banana chips, mango delicacies, and regional sweets to bring back home.'),
  ('boracay', 4706, 0, '**Party enthusiasts & nightclubbers** looking for world-class DJ sets, pumping basslines, and high-energy dance floors that go until dawn.'),
  ('boracay', 4706, 1, '**Sunset socializers & cocktail fans** seeking prime happy hour spots, beachfront beanbags, and signature rum cocktails.'),
  ('boracay', 4706, 2, '**Live music & performance lovers** hunting for energetic reggae bands, acoustic jams, and dramatic beachfront fire-dancing shows.'),
  ('boracay', 4706, 3, '**Pub crawlers & group travelers** wanting an easy, walkable strip of diverse bars, speakeasies, and social drinking spots.'),
  ('boracay', 4706, 4, 'Starting the evening with sunset cocktails at iconic beachfront spots like *Aplaya Beach Bar*, *Hello, Sailor*, or *Paraw Beach Club*.'),
  ('boracay', 4706, 5, 'Transitioning to high-energy dance clubs like *Epic Boracay*, *OM Bar*, or *Summer Place* as DJ sets kick off after 11 PM.'),
  ('boracay', 4706, 6, 'Catching authentic island vibes with live reggae, cold beers, and a local crowd at rustic spots like *Exit Bar*.'),
  ('boracay', 4706, 7, 'Experiencing specialized nightlife options like the *Boracay PubCrawl* or sunset party yachts cruising along the coastline.'),
  ('boracay', 4706, 8, 'Drinking alcohol or smoking directly on the open sand within the designated White Beach beachfront protection zone; keep all consumption inside licensed venue borders to avoid strict fines.'),
  ('boracay', 4706, 9, 'Forgetting to carry cash or small peso bills for cover charges and quick bar tabs, though major venues increasingly take cards.'),
  ('boracay', 4706, 10, 'Wearing delicate footwear; flip-flops, sandals, or stylish island flats are ideal for navigating the sandy paths between venues.'),
  ('boracay', 4706, 11, '**Station 2 (White Beach):** The hyper-energetic epicenter of Boracay nightlife, anchored around D''Mall and featuring the island''s biggest nightclubs, dance bars, and late-night eats.'),
  ('boracay', 4706, 12, '**Station 1 (White Beach):** Offers a slightly more upscale and stylish bar scene, known for chic beachfront lounges, craft cocktail spots, and high-end resort bars.'),
  ('boracay', 4706, 13, '**Station 3 & Bulabog Beach:** Preferred for a laid-back, bohemian atmosphere filled with reggae lounges, craft beer spots, sports bars, and cozy neighborhood watering holes.'),
  ('boracay', 4711, 0, '**Gilutongan Island:** Snorkeling paradise with vibrant corals and rich marine life.'),
  ('boracay', 4711, 1, '**Caohagan Island:** Peaceful island with local charm and relaxing shoreline vibes.'),
  ('boracay', 4711, 2, '**Nalusuan Island:** Famous boardwalk and marine sanctuary—perfect for photos and swimming.'),
  ('boracay', 4711, 3, '**Blood Compact Shrine:** Historical site commemorating the first treaty between Filipinos and Spaniards.'),
  ('boracay', 4711, 4, '**Baclayon Church:** One of the oldest stone churches in the Philippines, rich in heritage.'),
  ('boracay', 4711, 5, '**Man-Made Forest:** Picturesque stretch of mahogany trees creating a natural canopy.'),
  ('boracay', 4711, 6, '**Exotic Wildlife Encounter:** Visit a sanctuary with pythons and butterflies.'),
  ('boracay', 4711, 7, '**Tarsier Conservation Area:** See the world’s smallest primates up close in their natural habitat.'),
  ('boracay', 4711, 8, '**Chocolate Hills:** Bohol’s iconic geological wonder offering panoramic viewing deck vistas.'),
  ('boracay', 4712, 0, 'Arrival at El Nido Airport (ENI) and warm family meet-and-greet'),
  ('boracay', 4712, 1, 'Private transfer to hotel, seamless check-in, and time for the family to unwind after traveling'),
  ('boracay', 4712, 2, 'Evening free for leisure to explore nearby local cafes or relax at the hotel'),
  ('boracay', 4712, 3, 'Overnight stay at **BEST WESTERN PLUS HOTEL** (or similar) in Puerto Princesa'),
  ('boracay', 4712, 4, 'Family breakfast at the hotel'),
  ('boracay', 4712, 5, 'Pick up for the iconic UNESCO World Heritage Underground River Tour with an included picnic lunch'),
  ('boracay', 4712, 6, 'Arrive at Sabang Wharf and embark on the Underground River Cave Exploration Experience, marveling at thousand-year-old stalagmites and stalactites with child-friendly audio guides'),
  ('boracay', 4712, 7, 'Enjoy a scenic picnic lunch by Sabang Beach'),
  ('boracay', 4712, 8, 'Proceed to El Nido by private comfortable van (approx. 6 hours journey through Palawan''s lush countryside)'),
  ('boracay', 4712, 9, '*Note: Arrival in El Nido is typically around 10:00 PM – 11:00 PM following the tour and transit from PPS*'),
  ('boracay', 4712, 10, 'Check-in and late night rest'),
  ('boracay', 4712, 11, 'Overnight stay at **El Nido Garden Resort** (or similar) in El Nido'),
  ('boracay', 4712, 12, 'Breakfast at the resort with beachfront views'),
  ('boracay', 4712, 13, 'Proceed for Island Hopping Tour A aboard a private outrigger boat with a local grilled lunch included'),
  ('boracay', 4712, 14, 'Visit the iconic **Big Lagoon** (family kayaking through crystal turquoise waters), **Small Lagoon**, and the hidden passage of **Secret Lagoon**'),
  ('boracay', 4712, 15, 'Stop at **Shimizu Island** for world-class snorkeling among colorful fish and sea turtles'),
  ('boracay', 4712, 16, 'Relax along the white coconut palm shores of **Seven Commandos Beach**'),
  ('boracay', 4712, 17, 'Return to El Nido town center for an evening stroll'),
  ('boracay', 4712, 18, 'Overnight stay at **El Nido Garden Resort** (or similar) in El Nido'),
  ('boracay', 4712, 19, 'Breakfast at the resort'),
  ('boracay', 4712, 20, 'Embark on El Nido Island Hopping Tour C, famous for dramatic limestone formations and secluded beaches, with local lunch included'),
  ('boracay', 4712, 21, 'Crawl through a natural rock opening to discover **Secret Beach** and explore the secluded shores of **Hidden Beach**'),
  ('boracay', 4712, 22, 'Admire the distinct shape of **Helicopter Island** (Dilumacad Island) and swim along **Talisay Beach**'),
  ('boracay', 4712, 23, 'Snorkel in pristine marine protection areas teeming with vibrant coral reefs'),
