  ('boracay', 4712, 37, 'Overnight stay at **Boracay Mandarin Bay Resort and Spa** (or similar) in Boracay'),
  ('boracay', 4712, 38, 'Breakfast at the resort'),
  ('boracay', 4712, 39, 'Morning completely free for leisure—enjoy the resort pool, build sandcastles, or try gentle family water sports'),
  ('boracay', 4712, 40, 'Around 3:00 PM, meet for a breathtaking **Boracay Sunset Paraw Cruise**, sailing into the golden hour aboard a traditional outrigger sailboat'),
  ('boracay', 4712, 41, 'Return to the resort for an evening of beachside dining and live acoustic entertainment'),
  ('boracay', 4712, 42, 'Overnight stay at **Boracay Mandarin Bay Resort and Spa** (or similar) in Boracay'),
  ('boracay', 4712, 43, 'Breakfast at the hotel'),
  ('boracay', 4712, 44, 'Check out of the resort and transfer to Caticlan Airport (MPH)'),
  ('boracay', 4712, 45, 'Domestic flight to Cebu (Mactan-Cebu International Airport)'),
  ('boracay', 4712, 46, 'Meet-and-greet upon arrival in Cebu and private transfer to hotel'),
  ('boracay', 4712, 47, 'Check in and spend the evening relaxing or exploring nearby dining hubs'),
  ('boracay', 4712, 48, 'Overnight stay at **BAI Hotel** (or similar) in Cebu'),
  ('boracay', 4712, 49, 'Breakfast at the hotel'),
  ('boracay', 4712, 50, 'Embark on a comprehensive family Cebu City & Highland Tour covering major cultural and modern highlights:'),
  ('boracay', 4712, 51, 'Visit the grand Roman-inspired **Temple of Leah** overlooking the city skyline'),
  ('boracay', 4712, 52, 'Stop at the charming French bakery hub **La Vie Parisienne**'),
  ('boracay', 4712, 53, 'Explore historic sites: **Heritage Park**, **Yap-San Diego Ancestral House**, and **Fort San Pedro**'),
  ('boracay', 4712, 54, 'Visit **Magellan''s Cross** and the revered **Santo Niño Church**'),
  ('boracay', 4712, 55, 'Drive up to **Tops Lookout** for stunning nighttime views of Metropolitan Cebu'),
  ('boracay', 4712, 56, 'Cross the impressive **CCLEX Bridge** (Cebu–Cordova Link Expressway)'),
  ('boracay', 4712, 57, 'Visit the romantic illuminated garden of **10,000 Roses** in Cordova'),
  ('boracay', 4712, 58, 'Return to hotel late evening'),
  ('boracay', 4712, 59, 'Overnight stay at **BAI Hotel** (or similar) in Cebu'),
  ('boracay', 4712, 60, 'Early morning departure (approx. 3:00 AM) heading south to Tan-awan, Oslob *(packed breakfast provided by the hotel)*'),
  ('boracay', 4712, 61, '**Oslob Whale Shark Watching**: An unforgettable experience swimming and snorkeling near gentle whale shark giants under strict eco-guides'),
  ('boracay', 4712, 62, 'Proceed to Badian for the famous **Kawasan Waterfalls**, marveling at its legendary turquoise river waters'),
  ('boracay', 4712, 63, 'Enjoy family-friendly river trekking and the **Kawasan Canyoneering** activity (tailored for safety and fun with certified local guides)'),
  ('boracay', 4712, 64, 'Scenic drive back to Cebu City in the afternoon'),
  ('boracay', 4712, 65, 'Overnight stay at **BAI Hotel** (or similar) in Cebu'),
  ('boracay', 4712, 66, 'Breakfast at the hotel'),
  ('boracay', 4712, 67, 'Morning pick-up around 7:00 AM and transfer to Mactan wharf for an island-hopping marine sanctuary adventure:'),
  ('boracay', 4712, 68, '**Gilutongan Island**: Snorkeling paradise filled with rich marine life and colorful coral gardens'),
  ('boracay', 4712, 69, '**Caohagan Island**: Peaceful island village offering authentic local charm and relaxing sandy shorelines'),
  ('boracay', 4712, 70, '**Nalusuan Island**: Famous for its scenic wooden boardwalk and protected marine sanctuary, ideal for fish feeding and swimming'),
  ('boracay', 4712, 71, 'Enjoy a fresh seafood and island lunch before cruising back to Mactan'),
  ('boracay', 4712, 72, 'Return transfer to hotel and evening at leisure'),
  ('boracay', 4712, 73, 'Overnight stay at **BAI Hotel** (or similar) in Cebu'),
  ('boracay', 4712, 74, 'Breakfast at the hotel'),
  ('boracay', 4712, 75, 'Early morning ferry transfer across the Cebu Strait to Tagbilaran, Bohol, for a full-day countryside excursion:'),
  ('boracay', 4712, 76, '**Blood Compact Shrine**: Historical monument commemorating the first treaty of friendship between Spain and the Philippines'),
  ('boracay', 4712, 77, '**Baclayon Church**: One of the oldest stone churches in the country with a rich heritage museum'),
  ('boracay', 4712, 78, '**Bohol Man-Made Forest**: Ride through a dense, picturesque green canopy stretch of mahogany trees'),
  ('boracay', 4712, 79, '**Exotic Wildlife Encounter**: Visit a local sanctuary featuring native pythons and butterflies'),
  ('boracay', 4712, 80, '**Tarsier Conservation Area**: Get up close with the world’s smallest primates in their natural forested habitat'),
  ('boracay', 4712, 81, '**Chocolate Hills**: Marvel at Bohol''s world-famous geological wonder from the main viewing deck'),
  ('boracay', 4712, 82, 'Afternoon return ferry to Cebu and transfer back to hotel'),
  ('boracay', 4712, 83, 'Overnight stay at **BAI Hotel** (or similar) in Cebu'),
  ('boracay', 4712, 84, 'Breakfast at the hotel'),
  ('boracay', 4712, 85, 'Check out of the hotel and private transfer to Mactan-Cebu International Airport (CEB) for your international departure flight home'),
  ('boracay', 4714, 0, 'Treat Boracay as a single homogenous beach, underestimating the distinct vibe, noise level, and crowd density between Station 1, Station 2, Station 3, and Bulabog Beach.'),
  ('boracay', 4714, 1, 'Over-pack itineraries with back-to-back water sports without factoring in seasonal wind changes, such as the *Amihan* (northeast monsoon) vs. *Habagat* (southwest monsoon) shifts that dictate which side of the island is swimmable.'),
  ('boracay', 4714, 2, 'Rely entirely on card payments or digital wallets, failing to keep sufficient Philippine Peso cash for local e-trikes, small market stalls, and tipping.'),
  ('boracay', 4714, 3, 'Miscalculate arrival logistics by underestimating the multi-step transit required from Caticlan Airport (MPH) to the island, including jetty port processing, terminal fees, environmental taxes, and boat transfers.'),
  ('boracay', 4714, 4, 'Book accommodations along Bulabog Beach expecting quiet swimming, unaware that it serves as the island’s high-energy kitesurfing and windsurfing hub during the primary tourist season.'),
  ('boracay', 4715, 0, 'Tailors resort selection directly to client personality—recommending Station 1 or Boracay Newcoast for luxury and tranquility, Station 2 for nightlife and dining proximity, and Station 3 for a relaxed, old-school Boracay feel.'),
  ('boracay', 4715, 1, 'Pre-arranges seamless door-to-door airport transfer packages that handle luggage, speedboat transfers, and e-trikes directly to the resort lobby to eliminate arrival stress.'),
  ('boracay', 4715, 2, 'Plans water activities around monsoon seasons, scheduling diving, parasailing, and paddleboarding on White Beach during *Amihan* months (November–April) and shifting activities to Bulabog during *Habagat* months (May–October).'),
  ('boracay', 4715, 3, 'Builds in dedicated downtime for sunset paraw sailing and beachfront dining rather than over-scheduling daytime tours, allowing clients to experience the island’s natural rhythms.'),
  ('boracay', 4715, 4, 'Advises clients to pre-book environmental clearance and official hotel vouchers in advance, which are strictly verified by port authorities prior to boarding island ferries.'),
  ('boracay', 4716, 0, 'For **Resort Selection**, match the station to the traveler''s lifestyle—Station 1 for luxury and quiet, Station 2 for central action and dining, and Station 3 or Yapak for seclusion and nature.'),
  ('boracay', 4716, 1, 'For **Transit Logistics**, always book a verified all-inclusive transfer service from Caticlan Airport to avoid long queues at the jetty port and navigate environmental fee payments seamlessly.'),
  ('boracay', 4716, 2, 'For **Seasonal Pacing**, monitor the seasonal monsoon transition dates so water activities and boat departures are set on the correct, calm side of the island.'),
  ('boracay', 4719, 0, 'Take a classic afternoon sunset ride on a traditional *paraw* double-outrigger sailboat off White Beach.'),
  ('boracay', 4719, 1, 'Stroll along the ultra-fine sand of Station 1 and snap photos near the iconic Willy''s Rock formation.'),
  ('boracay', 4719, 2, 'Book an island-hopping boat tour to snorkel around Crocodile Island, visit Coral Garden, and relax on the coarse shell shores of Puka Shell Beach.'),
  ('boracay', 4719, 3, 'Explore Bulabog Beach to watch or try windsurfing and kitesurfing during high-wind mornings.'),
  ('boracay', 4719, 4, 'Dine along the Station 2 promenade and browse through the open-air retail arcades of D’Mall.'),
  ('boracay', 4719, 5, 'Eating, drinking, or smoking directly on the primary White Beach sand zone, as strict environmental conservation ordinances enforce heavy fines.'),
  ('boracay', 4719, 6, 'Arriving at Caticlan Jetty Port without a confirmed booking at an accredited hotel, as port entry verification strictly requires hotel confirmation documents.'),
  ('boracay', 4719, 7, 'Expecting beach loungers, umbrellas, or permanent structures directly on the public White Beach sand, which are prohibited to keep the shoreline natural and open.'),
  ('boracay', 4719, 8, 'Relying exclusively on credit cards at small souvenir stalls, local fruit stands, and e-trikes where cash (Philippine Peso) remains required.'),
  ('boracay', 4720, 0, 'To be populated with authoritative tourism/transport/attraction sources before production use.'),
  ('cebu', 4725, 0, 'Withdraw cash at major bank branch ATMs (such as BPI, BDO, or Metrobank) inside Cebu City shopping malls or Mactan-Cebu International Airport, where transaction limits are higher and reliability is guaranteed; most Philippine ATMs charge a flat fee of ₱250 ($4.50 USD) for foreign card withdrawals.'),
  ('cebu', 4725, 1, 'Dine at local *carinderias* (Filipino eateries), street-side *lechon* stalls, or food night markets like Sugbo Mercado in IT Park, where full local meals cost between ₱100 and ₱250 ($1.80–$4.50 USD), compared to tourist resort restaurants that charge ₱450 to ₱900+ per dish.'),
  ('cebu', 4725, 2, 'Utilize Ceres Liner public buses or MyBus routes to travel long distances across Cebu province (such as traveling south to Moalboal or Badian for ₱150 to ₱250 / $2.70–$4.50 USD), which is drastically cheaper than private van transfers or taxi charters (₱2,500 to ₱4,000).'),
  ('cebu', 4725, 3, 'Join shared group canyoneering tours at Kawasan Falls (₱1,500 to ₱2,100 / $27–$38 USD per person, including safety gear, guides, and entrance fees) rather than hiring exclusive private guides, which carry heavy markups for small groups.'),
  ('cebu', 4725, 4, 'Purchase basic water gear—such as a dry bag (₱300–₱500) and snorkel mask (₱400–₱700)—in Cebu City''s commercial malls (SM Seaside or Ayala Center) prior to traveling south or north, rather than paying inflated daily rental rates at coastal tourist hubs.');
INSERT INTO destination_guidance_bullet (place_id, position, bullet_index, text) VALUES
  ('cebu', 4725, 5, 'Skipping certified local guides or safety gear for Badian/Kawasan Falls canyoneering, as navigating steep gorges and waterfalls without proper helmets, life vests, and experienced guides presents severe safety risks.'),
  ('cebu', 4725, 6, 'Booking accommodation in isolated rural locations away from main highway transit routes purely for cheap night rates, as private tricycle or motorcycle-taxi (*habal-habal*) transport to attractions will quickly outweigh room savings.'),
  ('cebu', 4725, 7, 'Attempting long-distance scooter journeys across major highways (such as Cebu City to Oslob or Moalboal) if you lack extensive riding experience, due to intense highway truck traffic, steep mountain roads, and heavy coastal rain bursts.'),
  ('cebu', 4725, 8, 'Opting out of comprehensive travel and medical insurance, as specialized emergency care and medical evacuations from remote coastal districts (like Malapascua or Moalboal) back to Cebu City''s main hospitals are extremely costly.'),
  ('cebu', 4726, 0, '4+'),
  ('cebu', 4726, 1, '6+'),
  ('cebu', 4726, 2, '8+'),
  ('cebu', 4726, 3, 'Teenagers'),
  ('cebu', 4726, 4, 'Consider chartering a private bangka boat instead of joining shared group island-hopping tours when traveling with young kids; private charters allow you to adjust the schedule for naps, skip deep-water swimming stops, and return to shore early if children tire out.'),
  ('cebu', 4726, 5, 'Bring fitted child-sized life jackets and sturdy aqua shoes for the entire family; public tour boats often only provide adult-sized life vests, and sharp coral or sea urchins pose hazards at shallow beach landings.'),
  ('cebu', 4726, 6, 'Choose self-contained resort hubs like Mactan Island or flat beach towns like Santa Fe on Bantayan Island for dedicated rest days; these offer calm, shallow water entries, shaded seating, and quick access to kid-friendly dining.'),
  ('cebu', 4726, 7, 'Verify the physical requirements of adventure stops beforehand—such as age restrictions for Badian canyoneering at Kawasan Falls (typically ages 6+ or 12+ depending on the jump level)—and opt for gentle river floating or shallow waterfall pools for younger children.'),
  ('cebu', 4726, 8, 'Pack waterproof dry bags, reef-safe sunscreen, insect repellent, rehydration salts, and sufficient snacks and bottled water before embarking on day trips; rural beach hubs and boat landings often lack well-stocked convenience stores.'),
  ('cebu', 4726, 9, 'Rely on a sturdy baby carrier rather than a stroller, as sandy beaches, uneven cobblestone heritage paths, and wet outrigger boat entries make wheeled transport impractical across Cebu''s nature sites and island spots.'),
  ('cebu', 4727, 0, 'honeymoon_score: 91'),
  ('cebu', 4727, 1, 'romance_score: 93'),
  ('cebu', 4727, 2, 'privacy_score: 88'),
  ('cebu', 4727, 3, 'luxury_score: 92'),
  ('cebu', 4729, 0, 'Canyoneering through the striking turquoise river canyons, natural rock slides, and cliff jumps of Kawasan Falls in Badian.'),
  ('cebu', 4729, 1, 'Scuba diving or snorkeling directly off the shoreline in Moalboal to immerse yourself in the world-famous Million Sardine Run.'),
  ('cebu', 4729, 2, 'Scuba diving at Monad Shoal off Malapascua Island to encounter pelagic thresher sharks emerging from deep-water cleaning stations.'),
  ('cebu', 4729, 3, 'Trekking across the unique, jagged rock formations and ridge trails of Osmeña Peak or Casino Peak for panoramic views of Cebu''s central range.'),
  ('cebu', 4729, 4, 'Riding high-speed ziplines and tackling ATV mountain trails through the lush interior hills and waterfall valleys of South Cebu.'),
  ('cebu', 4729, 5, '**Badian & Kawasan Falls** — best for river canyoneering, cliff jumping, and jungle trekking.'),
  ('cebu', 4729, 6, '**Moalboal (Panagsama Coast)** — best for wall-reef scuba diving, sea turtle encounters, and the sardine run.'),
  ('cebu', 4729, 7, '**Southern Mountains (Dalaguete & Alegria)** — best for high-altitude ridge trekking, peak scaling, and cave exploration.'),
  ('cebu', 4729, 8, '**Malapascua Island (Northern Tip)** — best for world-class pelagic shark diving, reef exploration, and deep-water scuba.'),
  ('cebu', 4729, 9, 'High-adrenaline thrill-seekers, cliff jumpers, and river canyoneers.'),
  ('cebu', 4729, 10, 'Scuba divers, snorkelers, and underwater marine photo enthusiasts.'),
  ('cebu', 4729, 11, 'Mountain hikers, trail runners, and off-road ATV explorers.'),
  ('cebu', 4729, 12, 'Ocean adventurers wanting close encounters with pelagic marine life.'),
  ('cebu', 4729, 13, 'Active travelers who love combining rugged mountain treks with tropical ocean sports.'),
  ('cebu', 4730, 0, 'Fly directly into Mactan-Cebu International Airport (CEB) to avoid multi-leg transit and enjoy seamless access to city hotels and Mactan beach resorts.'),
  ('cebu', 4730, 1, 'Book private air-conditioned van charters with dedicated drivers for day trips to Cebu City''s heritage spots or coastal regions like Moalboal, ensuring customized rest breaks and flexible departure times.'),
  ('cebu', 4730, 2, 'Choose accommodations featuring elevators, step-free access, on-site dining, and accessible facilities—such as luxury resorts on Mactan Island or international chain hotels in Metro Cebu—to avoid navigating steep staircases.'),
  ('cebu', 4730, 3, 'Reserve private outrigger boat charters (*bangkas*) or motor yachts for island hopping around Mactan or Sumilon Island, allowing dedicated crew assistance with boat boarding and customized, unhurried itineraries.'),
  ('cebu', 4730, 4, 'Pack supportive, non-slip water shoes or sturdy sandals for walking on wet boat decks, sandy shores, and uneven historic cobblestone paths.'),
  ('cebu', 4730, 5, 'Ensure an ample supply of personal prescription medications, basic first-aid items, and travel insurance covering medical emergencies, as advanced specialized hospitals are concentrated in Metro Cebu.'),
  ('cebu', 4730, 6, 'Plan activities for the early morning or late afternoon to avoid direct sun exposure and heavy humidity during peak heat hours (11:00 AM to 2:00 PM).'),
  ('cebu', 4730, 7, 'Exploring historical and cultural landmarks in Cebu City with step-free or low-impact access, such as Magellan''s Cross, Fort San Pedro, Basilica Minore del Santo Niño, and the Yap-San Diego Ancestral House.'),
  ('cebu', 4730, 8, 'Staying at self-contained 5-star beachfront resorts on Mactan Island (e.g., Shangri-La or Crimson) offering private beaches, flat paved walking paths, golf cart shuttles, and luxury spa services.'),
  ('cebu', 4730, 9, 'Enjoying private sunset dining or scenic drives to hillside venues like Tops Lookout or Sirao Garden with comfortable private transport.'),
  ('cebu', 4730, 10, 'Taking calm, private boat excursions to shallow marine sanctuaries like Gilutungan or Nalusuan for easy boat-side snorkeling and fish viewing.'),
  ('cebu', 4730, 11, 'Dining at flat, beachfront or city-view sit-down establishments offering accessible seating and full-service dining.'),
  ('cebu', 4730, 12, 'Attempting high-adrenaline or physically demanding activities such as Kawasan Falls river canyoneering, cliff jumping, or steep ridge trekking at Osmeña Peak.'),
  ('cebu', 4730, 13, 'Relying on public jeepneys or long-distance public buses for travel across the province, which can involve cramped seating and frequent unassisted stops.'),
  ('cebu', 4730, 14, 'Staying in multi-story budget guesthouses or hill-perched lodges that lack elevators, paved roads, or accessible entrances.'),
  ('cebu', 4730, 15, 'Walking long distances through dense urban traffic in central Cebu City without pre-arranged transport.'),
  ('cebu', 4730, 16, 'Traveling during the monsoon and typhoon-prone months (July to October) when heavy rain makes walking surfaces slippery and rough seas disrupt boat excursions.'),
  ('cebu', 4732, 0, 'Feast on iconic **Cebuano Lechon**, whole pig slow-roasted over charcoal stuffed with lemongrass, garlic, scallions, and sea salt, resulting in impossibly crispy skin and tender, savory meat without needing sauce.'),
  ('cebu', 4732, 1, 'Try authentic **Puso** (hanging rice), rice wrapped and boiled inside woven coconut palm leaves, serving as the quintessential portable accompaniment to street-side grills and roasted meats.'),
  ('cebu', 4732, 2, 'Indulge in fresh **SuTuKil** (Sugba, Tuwa, Kilaw), a three-in-one seafood dining experience where you pick fresh fish to be charcoal-grilled (*Sugba*), simmered in a light ginger broth (*Tuwa*), and cured raw in vinegar and citrus (*Kilaw*).'),
  ('cebu', 4732, 3, 'Savor a steaming bowl of **Pochero**, a comforting Cebuano beef shank soup slow-cooked with bone marrow, cabbage, sweet corn, and saba bananas until deeply rich and savory.'),
  ('cebu', 4732, 4, 'Snack on sweet **Dried Mangoes** or cool down with creamy **Ube and Mango Halo-Halo**, highlighting Cebu’s world-famous tropical produce.'),
  ('cebu', 4732, 5, '**Families:** Casual feast-style *lechon* halls, lively night market dining at Sugbo Mercado, and spacious beachfront resort buffets on Mactan Island.'),
  ('cebu', 4732, 6, '**Honeymooners:** Romantic cliffside dining in Busay, candlelit oceanfront seafood tables in Cordova, and intimate craft cocktail lounges in IT Park.'),
  ('cebu', 4732, 7, '**Luxury travelers:** Multi-course executive seafood tasting menus at 5-star Mactan resorts, private yacht dining, and upscale modern Cebuano gastronomy in Cebu City.'),
  ('cebu', 4732, 8, '**Budget travelers:** Bustling street-side *Pungko-Pungko* stalls (serving deep-fried meats with onions and vinegar), local *carinderias*, and affordable public market seafood grills.'),
  ('cebu', 4732, 9, '**Foodies:** Heritage food crawls through Carcar and Cebu City, artisanal Visayan coffee houses, and market-to-table *SuTuKil* seafood explorations.'),
  ('cebu', 4732, 10, '**Cebu IT Park & Lahug:** Best for vibrant night markets (Sugbo Mercado), trendy international cafes, late-night craft beer spots, and modern dining concepts.'),
  ('cebu', 4732, 11, '**Busay (Central Mountains):** Best for scenic, high-elevation dining with sweeping views over Metro Cebu, offering romantic Spanish-Filipino restaurants and cozy cafes.'),
  ('cebu', 4732, 12, '**Mactan Island & Cordova:** Best for high-end resort dining, oceanfront seafood halls, authentic *SuTuKil* coastal spots, and relaxed beach clubs.'),
  ('cebu', 4732, 13, '**Carcar City & Central Cebu City:** Best for traditional heritage food hubs, historic street food stalls, and sampling the province''s most famous roasted *lechon*.'),
  ('cebu', 4733, 0, '**Cebuano Hand-Crafted Guitars & Ukuleles:** Internationally acclaimed acoustic guitars, ukuleles, and mandolins hand-crafted from premium local woods in Lapu-Lapu City workshops.'),
  ('cebu', 4733, 1, '**Cebu Dried Mangoes & Mango Chocolates:** World-famous, naturally sweet dried Philippine mangoes, chocolate-dipped mango slices, and mango preserves—the ultimate edible souvenir.'),
  ('cebu', 4733, 2, '**Hand-Woven Crafts & Fashion Accessories:** Intricately woven *rattan*, *abaca*, and *buri* bags, home decor, and costume jewelry crafted by famous Visayan designers and local artisans.'),
  ('cebu', 4733, 3, '**Otap & Local Delicacies:** Crisp, flaky, sugar-encrusted oval puff pastries (*Otap*), *Rosquillos* biscuits, and dried seafood (*daing*) packed for travel.'),
  ('cebu', 4733, 4, '**South Sea Pearls & Shell Crafts:** Locally sourced pearl jewelry, mother-of-pearl home accessories, and capiz shell handicrafts.'),
  ('cebu', 4733, 5, '**Ayala Center Cebu & Ayala Malls Central Bloc:** Preferred for upscale international retail, local designer boutiques, department stores, and modern indoor-outdoor lifestyle shopping.'),
  ('cebu', 4733, 6, '**SM Seaside City Cebu:** Preferred for a massive oceanfront mega-mall experience featuring global fashion brands, entertainment hubs, ice skating, and sweeping sea views.'),
  ('cebu', 4733, 7, '**Guitar Factories in Lapu-Lapu City (Alegre & Lilang):** Ideal for touring authentic guitar workshop floors and purchasing custom-made, high-quality string instruments directly from master craftsmen.'),
  ('cebu', 4733, 8, '**Carbon Market & Taboan Public Market:** Best for adventurous travelers seeking deep discounts on dried mangoes by the kilo, fresh tropical fruits, local basketry, and authentic Cebuano street market culture.'),
  ('cebu', 4733, 9, 'Expecting credit cards to be accepted everywhere; always carry Philippine Pesos (PHP) when shopping at Taboan Market, Carbon Market, or small street-side souvenir stalls.'),
  ('cebu', 4733, 10, 'Purchasing unpackaged dried fish (*danggit*) to carry on flights without requesting airtight, sealed "flight-ready" packaging at the market to prevent odor issues.'),
  ('cebu', 4733, 11, 'Buying pearl accessories or coral items from unverified beach hawkers on Mactan beaches without verifying quality or authenticity.'),
  ('cebu', 4733, 12, '**Mall & Fashion Shoppers:** Visitors looking for large air-conditioned retail complexes with international high-street brands and lifestyle shopping.'),
  ('cebu', 4733, 13, '**Artisan & Craft Collectors:** Travelers seeking world-class hand-crafted acoustic guitars, hand-woven home accessories, and designer Visayan handicrafts.'),
  ('cebu', 4733, 14, '**Foodie Keepsake Hunters:** Travelers wanting to stock up on bulk packs of dried mangoes, local pastries, and regional delicacies to take home.'),
  ('cebu', 4734, 0, '**Clubbers & dance enthusiasts** looking for high-capacity DJ venues, EDM laser shows, and upbeat dance floors that stay packed until dawn.'),
  ('cebu', 4734, 1, '**Craft cocktail & rooftop lovers** seeking ambient mountain-top views overlooking the city skyline or refined, speakeasy-style lounge drinks.'),
  ('cebu', 4734, 2, '**Karaoke fans & groups** hunting for private KTV rooms, live acoustic cover bands, and social gastropubs stocked with local food.'),
  ('cebu', 4734, 3, '**Bustling urban explorers** wanting 24/7 dining options, lit-up night markets, and vibrant open-air bar hubs in modern commercial districts.'),
  ('cebu', 4734, 4, 'Dancing the night away at high-energy party hubs and dance clubs like *Club Icon* or modern mega-clubs in Mandaue and City Time Square.'),
  ('cebu', 4734, 5, 'Soaking in sweeping, multi-level city skyline views over evening drinks at elevated Busay mountain bars like *Tops*, *Scape ''N Skydeck*, or *La Vie in the Sky*.'),
  ('cebu', 4734, 6, 'Enjoying craft beer, speakeasy cocktails, and trendy dining in modern lifestyle hubs like **Cebu IT Park**, **Crossroads**, and **Streetscape**.'),
  ('cebu', 4734, 7, 'Singing your heart out with friends at popular private KTV lounges like *Red Box* or local videoke hubs along A.S. Fortuna.'),
  ('cebu', 4734, 8, 'Walking alone late at night along dimly lit side streets around older downtown districts; stick to well-lit main strips and use ride-hailing apps like Grab.'),
  ('cebu', 4734, 9, 'Haggling with unmetered street taxis outside major nightclubs; insist on meter usage or book through official apps to ensure fair fares.'),
  ('cebu', 4734, 10, 'Flashy displays of high-value electronics or unwatched belongings in densely packed bar quarters.'),
  ('cebu', 4734, 11, '**Cebu IT Park (Lahug):** A safe, bustling 24/7 commercial lifestyle district packed with open-air gastropubs, night markets (Sugbo Mercado), wine bars, and al-fresco lounges.'),
  ('cebu', 4734, 12, '**Mandaue & City Time Square:** Home to large-scale modern nightclubs, KTV complexes, and hip-hop bars favored by local partygoers and visitors.'),
  ('cebu', 4734, 13, '**Busay Hills:** The premier upland scenic strip overlooking Metro Cebu, perfect for high-altitude sunset dining, romantic wine bars, and cool mountain-breeze drinks.'),
  ('cebu', 4739, 0, '**Gilutongan Island:** Snorkeling paradise with vibrant corals and rich marine life.'),
  ('cebu', 4739, 1, '**Caohagan Island:** Peaceful island with local charm and relaxing shoreline vibes.'),
  ('cebu', 4739, 2, '**Nalusuan Island:** Famous boardwalk and marine sanctuary—perfect for photos and swimming.'),
  ('cebu', 4739, 3, '**Blood Compact Shrine:** Historical site commemorating the first treaty between Filipinos and Spaniards.'),
  ('cebu', 4739, 4, '**Baclayon Church:** One of the oldest stone churches in the Philippines, rich in heritage.'),
  ('cebu', 4739, 5, '**Man-Made Forest:** Picturesque stretch of mahogany trees creating a natural canopy.'),
  ('cebu', 4739, 6, '**Exotic Wildlife Encounter:** Visit a sanctuary with pythons and butterflies.'),
  ('cebu', 4739, 7, '**Tarsier Conservation Area:** See the world’s smallest primates up close in their natural habitat.'),
  ('cebu', 4739, 8, '**Chocolate Hills:** Bohol’s iconic geological wonder offering panoramic viewing deck vistas.'),
  ('cebu', 4740, 0, 'Arrival at El Nido Airport (ENI) and warm family meet-and-greet'),
  ('cebu', 4740, 1, 'Private transfer to hotel, seamless check-in, and time for the family to unwind after traveling'),
  ('cebu', 4740, 2, 'Evening free for leisure to explore nearby local cafes or relax at the hotel'),
  ('cebu', 4740, 3, 'Overnight stay at **BEST WESTERN PLUS HOTEL** (or similar) in Puerto Princesa'),
  ('cebu', 4740, 4, 'Family breakfast at the hotel'),
  ('cebu', 4740, 5, 'Pick up for the iconic UNESCO World Heritage Underground River Tour with an included picnic lunch'),
  ('cebu', 4740, 6, 'Arrive at Sabang Wharf and embark on the Underground River Cave Exploration Experience, marveling at thousand-year-old stalagmites and stalactites with child-friendly audio guides'),
  ('cebu', 4740, 7, 'Enjoy a scenic picnic lunch by Sabang Beach'),
  ('cebu', 4740, 8, 'Proceed to El Nido by private comfortable van (approx. 6 hours journey through Palawan''s lush countryside)'),
  ('cebu', 4740, 9, '*Note: Arrival in El Nido is typically around 10:00 PM – 11:00 PM following the tour and transit from PPS*'),
  ('cebu', 4740, 10, 'Check-in and late night rest'),
  ('cebu', 4740, 11, 'Overnight stay at **El Nido Garden Resort** (or similar) in El Nido'),
  ('cebu', 4740, 12, 'Breakfast at the resort with beachfront views'),
  ('cebu', 4740, 13, 'Proceed for Island Hopping Tour A aboard a private outrigger boat with a local grilled lunch included'),
  ('cebu', 4740, 14, 'Visit the iconic **Big Lagoon** (family kayaking through crystal turquoise waters), **Small Lagoon**, and the hidden passage of **Secret Lagoon**'),
  ('cebu', 4740, 15, 'Stop at **Shimizu Island** for world-class snorkeling among colorful fish and sea turtles'),
  ('cebu', 4740, 16, 'Relax along the white coconut palm shores of **Seven Commandos Beach**'),
  ('cebu', 4740, 17, 'Return to El Nido town center for an evening stroll'),
  ('cebu', 4740, 18, 'Overnight stay at **El Nido Garden Resort** (or similar) in El Nido'),
  ('cebu', 4740, 19, 'Breakfast at the resort'),
  ('cebu', 4740, 20, 'Embark on El Nido Island Hopping Tour C, famous for dramatic limestone formations and secluded beaches, with local lunch included'),
  ('cebu', 4740, 21, 'Crawl through a natural rock opening to discover **Secret Beach** and explore the secluded shores of **Hidden Beach**'),
  ('cebu', 4740, 22, 'Admire the distinct shape of **Helicopter Island** (Dilumacad Island) and swim along **Talisay Beach**'),
  ('cebu', 4740, 23, 'Snorkel in pristine marine protection areas teeming with vibrant coral reefs'),
  ('cebu', 4740, 24, 'Return to the hotel in the late afternoon for relaxed family dining along Corong-Corong or town proper'),
  ('cebu', 4740, 25, 'Overnight stay at **El Nido Garden Resort** (or similar) in El Nido'),
  ('cebu', 4740, 26, 'Breakfast at the hotel'),
  ('cebu', 4740, 27, 'Check out and transfer to Lio Airport (ENI) or Puerto Princesa Airport for your domestic flight to Caticlan (Boracay)'),
  ('cebu', 4740, 28, 'Transfer via land and boat to Boracay Island, followed by smooth check-in at your beachfront resort'),
  ('cebu', 4740, 29, 'Evening free for the family to stroll along the famous soft sands of White Beach and catch a tropical sunset'),
  ('cebu', 4740, 30, 'Overnight stay at **Boracay Mandarin Bay Resort and Spa** (or similar) in Boracay'),
  ('cebu', 4740, 31, 'Breakfast at the resort'),
  ('cebu', 4740, 32, 'Board your boat for a fun-filled family Island Hopping Tour across Boracay’s outer coves (SIC Basis)'),
  ('cebu', 4740, 33, 'Explore **Puka Shell Beach** for family swimming, shelling, photo opportunities, and souvenir shopping'),
  ('cebu', 4740, 34, 'Visit **Crystal Cove Island** to explore its natural sea caves and private viewpoints'),
  ('cebu', 4740, 35, 'Enjoy an included beachside lunch buffet during the tour'),
  ('cebu', 4740, 36, 'Return to Station 2/3 and spend the evening at leisure along the vibrant beachfront D''Mall'),
  ('cebu', 4740, 37, 'Overnight stay at **Boracay Mandarin Bay Resort and Spa** (or similar) in Boracay'),
  ('cebu', 4740, 38, 'Breakfast at the resort'),
  ('cebu', 4740, 39, 'Morning completely free for leisure—enjoy the resort pool, build sandcastles, or try gentle family water sports'),
  ('cebu', 4740, 40, 'Around 3:00 PM, meet for a breathtaking **Boracay Sunset Paraw Cruise**, sailing into the golden hour aboard a traditional outrigger sailboat'),
  ('cebu', 4740, 41, 'Return to the resort for an evening of beachside dining and live acoustic entertainment'),
  ('cebu', 4740, 42, 'Overnight stay at **Boracay Mandarin Bay Resort and Spa** (or similar) in Boracay'),
  ('cebu', 4740, 43, 'Breakfast at the hotel'),
  ('cebu', 4740, 44, 'Check out of the resort and transfer to Caticlan Airport (MPH)'),
  ('cebu', 4740, 45, 'Domestic flight to Cebu (Mactan-Cebu International Airport)'),
  ('cebu', 4740, 46, 'Meet-and-greet upon arrival in Cebu and private transfer to hotel'),
  ('cebu', 4740, 47, 'Check in and spend the evening relaxing or exploring nearby dining hubs'),
  ('cebu', 4740, 48, 'Overnight stay at **BAI Hotel** (or similar) in Cebu'),
  ('cebu', 4740, 49, 'Breakfast at the hotel'),
  ('cebu', 4740, 50, 'Embark on a comprehensive family Cebu City & Highland Tour covering major cultural and modern highlights:'),
  ('cebu', 4740, 51, 'Visit the grand Roman-inspired **Temple of Leah** overlooking the city skyline'),
  ('cebu', 4740, 52, 'Stop at the charming French bakery hub **La Vie Parisienne**'),
  ('cebu', 4740, 53, 'Explore historic sites: **Heritage Park**, **Yap-San Diego Ancestral House**, and **Fort San Pedro**'),
  ('cebu', 4740, 54, 'Visit **Magellan''s Cross** and the revered **Santo Niño Church**'),
  ('cebu', 4740, 55, 'Drive up to **Tops Lookout** for stunning nighttime views of Metropolitan Cebu'),
  ('cebu', 4740, 56, 'Cross the impressive **CCLEX Bridge** (Cebu–Cordova Link Expressway)'),
  ('cebu', 4740, 57, 'Visit the romantic illuminated garden of **10,000 Roses** in Cordova'),
  ('cebu', 4740, 58, 'Return to hotel late evening'),
  ('cebu', 4740, 59, 'Overnight stay at **BAI Hotel** (or similar) in Cebu'),
  ('cebu', 4740, 60, 'Early morning departure (approx. 3:00 AM) heading south to Tan-awan, Oslob *(packed breakfast provided by the hotel)*'),
  ('cebu', 4740, 61, '**Oslob Whale Shark Watching**: An unforgettable experience swimming and snorkeling near gentle whale shark giants under strict eco-guides'),
  ('cebu', 4740, 62, 'Proceed to Badian for the famous **Kawasan Waterfalls**, marveling at its legendary turquoise river waters'),
  ('cebu', 4740, 63, 'Enjoy family-friendly river trekking and the **Kawasan Canyoneering** activity (tailored for safety and fun with certified local guides)'),
  ('cebu', 4740, 64, 'Scenic drive back to Cebu City in the afternoon'),
  ('cebu', 4740, 65, 'Overnight stay at **BAI Hotel** (or similar) in Cebu'),
  ('cebu', 4740, 66, 'Breakfast at the hotel'),
  ('cebu', 4740, 67, 'Morning pick-up around 7:00 AM and transfer to Mactan wharf for an island-hopping marine sanctuary adventure:'),
  ('cebu', 4740, 68, '**Gilutongan Island**: Snorkeling paradise filled with rich marine life and colorful coral gardens'),
  ('cebu', 4740, 69, '**Caohagan Island**: Peaceful island village offering authentic local charm and relaxing sandy shorelines'),
  ('cebu', 4740, 70, '**Nalusuan Island**: Famous for its scenic wooden boardwalk and protected marine sanctuary, ideal for fish feeding and swimming'),
  ('cebu', 4740, 71, 'Enjoy a fresh seafood and island lunch before cruising back to Mactan'),
  ('cebu', 4740, 72, 'Return transfer to hotel and evening at leisure'),
  ('cebu', 4740, 73, 'Overnight stay at **BAI Hotel** (or similar) in Cebu'),
  ('cebu', 4740, 74, 'Breakfast at the hotel'),
  ('cebu', 4740, 75, 'Early morning ferry transfer across the Cebu Strait to Tagbilaran, Bohol, for a full-day countryside excursion:'),
  ('cebu', 4740, 76, '**Blood Compact Shrine**: Historical monument commemorating the first treaty of friendship between Spain and the Philippines'),
  ('cebu', 4740, 77, '**Baclayon Church**: One of the oldest stone churches in the country with a rich heritage museum'),
  ('cebu', 4740, 78, '**Bohol Man-Made Forest**: Ride through a dense, picturesque green canopy stretch of mahogany trees'),
  ('cebu', 4740, 79, '**Exotic Wildlife Encounter**: Visit a local sanctuary featuring native pythons and butterflies'),
  ('cebu', 4740, 80, '**Tarsier Conservation Area**: Get up close with the world’s smallest primates in their natural forested habitat'),
  ('cebu', 4740, 81, '**Chocolate Hills**: Marvel at Bohol''s world-famous geological wonder from the main viewing deck'),
  ('cebu', 4740, 82, 'Afternoon return ferry to Cebu and transfer back to hotel'),
  ('cebu', 4740, 83, 'Overnight stay at **BAI Hotel** (or similar) in Cebu'),
  ('cebu', 4740, 84, 'Breakfast at the hotel'),
  ('cebu', 4740, 85, 'Check out of the hotel and private transfer to Mactan-Cebu International Airport (CEB) for your international departure flight home'),
  ('cebu', 4742, 0, 'Treat Cebu purely as a brief airport transit hub for other island destinations, completely skipping its world-class marine ecosystems, historic landmarks, and dramatic mountain highlands.'),
  ('cebu', 4742, 1, 'Underestimate the heavy traffic and transit times within Metro Cebu, scheduling tight transfers between mainland city tours and south Cebu water adventures like Kawasan Falls or Moalboal.'),
  ('cebu', 4742, 2, 'Over-pack a single day with both northern and southern island destinations, underestimating that driving from Cebu City to Oslob or Bantayan Island takes 3 to 4 hours each way.'),
  ('cebu', 4742, 3, 'Expect all adventure tours, like river canyoneering or boat rentals, to accept credit cards or mobile payments, failing to bring sufficient Philippine Pesos for local municipal fees and guides.'),
  ('cebu', 4742, 4, 'Book mainland city accommodations when their main goal is relaxing on powdery beaches, missing out on the beachfront resort strips of Mactan Island or Bantayan.'),
  ('cebu', 4743, 0, 'Bases clients strategically depending on their main focus—booking Mactan Island for beach luxury and water sports, Cebu City core for historical and culinary exploration, or Moalboal/Bantayan for dedicated nature adventures.'),
  ('cebu', 4743, 1, 'Schedules high-adrenaline early-morning excursions (like the Moalboal Sardine Run or Kawasan Falls Canyoneering) with 4:00 AM departures to beat both peak tourist crowds and highway traffic.'),
  ('cebu', 4743, 2, 'Pre-books certified local guides and official municipal permits for regulated activities like river canyoneering, ensuring full safety gear and seamless entry.'),
  ('cebu', 4743, 3, 'Combines urban cultural heritage walks with cool mountain highland escapes in Busay to showcase Cebu''s dual identity as both a historical trade hub and a scenic island retreat.'),
  ('cebu', 4743, 4, 'Arranges private air-conditioned van transfers or express ferry tickets in advance to eliminate transit friction between island clusters.'),
  ('cebu', 4744, 0, 'For **Geographical Pacing**, divide Cebu into distinct zones (Metro/Mactan, South Cebu, and North Islands) and never attempt to switch bases on back-to-back days.'),
  ('cebu', 4744, 1, 'For **Transit Management**, always allocate a minimum of 3 to 4 hours of travel time when moving between Metro Cebu and major regional adventure hubs like Moalboal or Hagnaya Port.'),
  ('cebu', 4744, 2, 'For **Itinerary Balance**, plan a minimum of 4 to 5 nights in Cebu—allocating 1–2 days for historical and highland city sights, 1–2 days for southern aquatic adventures, and 2 days for northern beach relaxation.');
INSERT INTO destination_guidance_bullet (place_id, position, bullet_index, text) VALUES
  ('cebu', 4747, 0, 'Experience high-adrenaline river canyoneering through the turquoise waters, natural slides, and cliff jumps of Kawasan Falls in Badian.'),
  ('cebu', 4747, 1, 'Snorkel or scuba dive right off the shore in Moalboal to witness the world-famous Million Sardine Run and swim alongside resident sea turtles.'),
  ('cebu', 4747, 2, 'Feast on legendary, crispy-skinned Cebuano *Lechon* at iconic local roast houses or night markets like Sugbo Mercado.'),
  ('cebu', 4747, 3, 'Explore historic Cebu City landmarks including Magellan''s Cross, Basilica Minore del Santo Niño, and Fort San Pedro.'),
  ('cebu', 4747, 4, 'Head up to Busay in the evening to take in 180-degree panoramic sunset and night views over Metro Cebu from Tops Lookout or La Vie in the Sky.'),
  ('cebu', 4747, 5, 'Underestimating road travel times across the main island—coastal highways south to Moalboal, Badian, or Oslob can take 3 to 4 hours depending on city traffic.'),
  ('cebu', 4747, 6, 'Attempting Badian canyoneering without licensed guides, proper helmet and vest safety gear, and sturdy closed-toe water shoes.'),
  ('cebu', 4747, 7, 'Relying solely on credit cards outside major hotels and malls; cash (Philippine Pesos) is essential for street food, public transport, local guides, and rural beach spots.'),
  ('cebu', 4747, 8, 'Booking tight flight connections immediately after returning from long land excursions across the province due to potential highway traffic bottlenecks.'),
  ('cebu', 4748, 0, 'To be populated with authoritative tourism/transport/attraction sources before production use.'),
  ('bohol', 4753, 0, 'Withdraw cash at major bank branch ATMs (such as BPI, BDO, or Metrobank) inside Cebu City shopping malls or Mactan-Cebu International Airport, where transaction limits are higher and reliability is guaranteed; most Philippine ATMs charge a flat fee of ₱250 ($4.50 USD) for foreign card withdrawals.'),
  ('bohol', 4753, 1, 'Dine at local *carinderias* (Filipino eateries), street-side *lechon* stalls, or food night markets like Sugbo Mercado in IT Park, where full local meals cost between ₱100 and ₱250 ($1.80–$4.50 USD), compared to tourist resort restaurants that charge ₱450 to ₱900+ per dish.'),
  ('bohol', 4753, 2, 'Utilize Ceres Liner public buses or MyBus routes to travel long distances across Cebu province (such as traveling south to Moalboal or Badian for ₱150 to ₱250 / $2.70–$4.50 USD), which is drastically cheaper than private van transfers or taxi charters (₱2,500 to ₱4,000).'),
  ('bohol', 4753, 3, 'Join shared group canyoneering tours at Kawasan Falls (₱1,500 to ₱2,100 / $27–$38 USD per person, including safety gear, guides, and entrance fees) rather than hiring exclusive private guides, which carry heavy markups for small groups.'),
  ('bohol', 4753, 4, 'Purchase basic water gear—such as a dry bag (₱300–₱500) and snorkel mask (₱400–₱700)—in Cebu City''s commercial malls (SM Seaside or Ayala Center) prior to traveling south or north, rather than paying inflated daily rental rates at coastal tourist hubs.'),
  ('bohol', 4753, 5, 'Skipping certified local guides or safety gear for Badian/Kawasan Falls canyoneering, as navigating steep gorges and waterfalls without proper helmets, life vests, and experienced guides presents severe safety risks.'),
  ('bohol', 4753, 6, 'Booking accommodation in isolated rural locations away from main highway transit routes purely for cheap night rates, as private tricycle or motorcycle-taxi (*habal-habal*) transport to attractions will quickly outweigh room savings.'),
  ('bohol', 4753, 7, 'Attempting long-distance scooter journeys across major highways (such as Cebu City to Oslob or Moalboal) if you lack extensive riding experience, due to intense highway truck traffic, steep mountain roads, and heavy coastal rain bursts.'),
  ('bohol', 4753, 8, 'Opting out of comprehensive travel and medical insurance, as specialized emergency care and medical evacuations from remote coastal districts (like Malapascua or Moalboal) back to Cebu City''s main hospitals are extremely costly.'),
  ('bohol', 4754, 0, '4+'),
  ('bohol', 4754, 1, '6+'),
  ('bohol', 4754, 2, '8+'),
  ('bohol', 4754, 3, 'Teenagers'),
  ('bohol', 4754, 4, 'Consider chartering a private bangka boat instead of joining shared group island-hopping tours when traveling with young kids; private charters allow you to adjust the schedule for naps, skip deep-water swimming stops, and return to shore early if children tire out.'),
  ('bohol', 4754, 5, 'Bring fitted child-sized life jackets and sturdy aqua shoes for the entire family; public tour boats and local operators often only provide adult-sized life vests, and sharp coral, rocks, or sea urchins pose hazards during shallow beach landings.'),
  ('bohol', 4754, 6, 'Choose self-contained resort hubs along Panglao Island (such as Dumaluan Beach or Alona Beach) or quiet, flat beach zones like Anda for dedicated rest days; these offer calm, shallow water entries, shaded seating, and quick access to kid-friendly dining.'),
  ('bohol', 4754, 7, 'Verify the physical requirements of adventure stops beforehand—such as age, height, and weight restrictions for ATV rides near the Chocolate Hills or ziplining at Danao Adventure Park—and opt for gentle river cruises or shallow eco-park trails for younger children.'),
  ('bohol', 4754, 8, 'Brief children beforehand on strict animal interaction rules before visiting tarsier sanctuaries; remind kids to keep voices down to a whisper and avoid flash photography or attempting to touch the tarsiers, as loud noises cause severe distress to these sensitive primates.'),
  ('bohol', 4754, 9, 'Pack waterproof dry bags, reef-safe sunscreen, child-friendly insect repellent, rehydration salts, and sufficient snacks and bottled water before embarking on inland countryside tours or boat trips; rural attractions often lack well-stocked convenience stores.'),
  ('bohol', 4754, 10, 'Rely on a sturdy baby carrier rather than a stroller, as sandy beaches, steep observation staircases (like the Chocolate Hills viewing deck), and wet outrigger boat boarding ladders make wheeled transport impractical across Bohol''s nature sites and island spots.'),
  ('bohol', 4755, 0, 'honeymoon_score: 93'),
  ('bohol', 4755, 1, 'romance_score: 95'),
  ('bohol', 4755, 2, 'privacy_score: 90'),
  ('bohol', 4755, 3, 'luxury_score: 92'),
  ('bohol', 4757, 0, 'Ziplining, gorge-swinging, and cable-car traversing across deep river canyons at Danao Adventure Park.'),
  ('bohol', 4757, 1, 'Scuba diving along the dramatic marine drop-offs and protected coral walls of Balicasag Island Marine Sanctuary.'),
  ('bohol', 4757, 2, 'Riding ATVs (all-terrain vehicles) through off-road dirt trails and muddy tracks around the base of the Chocolate Hills.'),
  ('bohol', 4757, 3, 'Cliff jumping into the crystal-clear subterranean basin of Cabagnow Cave Pool and exploring the limestone caverns of Anda.'),
  ('bohol', 4757, 4, 'Stand-up paddleboarding or night kayaking along the serene, emerald stretches of the Loboc River system.'),
  ('bohol', 4757, 5, '**Danao (Northern Bohol)** — best for high-adrenaline adventure sports, extreme gorge swinging, ziplines, and rappelling.'),
  ('bohol', 4757, 6, '**Carmen & Chocolate Hills Foothills** — best for off-road ATV quad biking, trail riding, and countryside exploration.'),
  ('bohol', 4757, 7, '**Balicasag Island (Panglao Marine Zone)** — best for world-class reef diving, wall-drop snorkeling, and sea turtle encounters.'),
  ('bohol', 4757, 8, '**Anda Peninsula** — best for limestone sinkhole cliff jumping, cave pool swimming, and uncrowded coastal diving.'),
  ('bohol', 4757, 9, 'Eco-adventure enthusiasts, off-road ATV riders, and outdoor trail explorers.'),
  ('bohol', 4757, 10, 'Scuba divers, wall-reef snorkelers, and underwater marine photography lovers.'),
  ('bohol', 4757, 11, 'Zipliners, cliff jumpers, and water sports lovers seeking river and cave adventures.'),
  ('bohol', 4757, 12, 'Active travelers wanting to pair geological wonders with high-energy physical activities.'),
  ('bohol', 4757, 13, 'Nature seekers looking for a balance between lush jungle terrain and marine sanctuaries.'),
  ('bohol', 4758, 0, 'Fly directly into Bohol-Panglao International Airport (TAG) to minimize land travel times and enjoy immediate access to Panglao''s flat, accessible beach resorts.'),
  ('bohol', 4758, 1, 'Hire private air-conditioned cars or vans with dedicated drivers for countryside excursions to ensure flexible schedules, comfortable climate control, and customized rest stops.'),
  ('bohol', 4758, 2, 'Select resorts with step-free access, elevators, on-site dining, and flat paved garden paths—such as premier properties along Dumaluan or Alona Beach—to avoid steep inclines or staircases.'),
  ('bohol', 4758, 3, 'Opt for gentle, private outrigger boat charters (*bangkas*) for island-hopping to Balicasag or Virgin Island, ensuring dedicated crew support when boarding and unhurried schedules.'),
  ('bohol', 4758, 4, 'Pack comfortable, non-slip footwear or aqua shoes to maintain stable footing on wet boat ramps, sandy beaches, and stone heritage pathways.'),
  ('bohol', 4758, 5, 'Carry a sufficient supply of personal prescription medications and comprehensive travel insurance, noting that major medical facilities are concentrated around Tagbilaran City.'),
  ('bohol', 4758, 6, 'Schedule outdoor sightseeing for the early morning or late afternoon to avoid the intense midday sun and humidity (11:00 AM to 2:00 PM).'),
  ('bohol', 4758, 7, 'Enjoying a leisurely scenic lunch cruise along the Loboc River aboard a flat, accessible floating restaurant barge with live musical entertainment.'),
  ('bohol', 4758, 8, 'Visiting the protected Philippine Tarsier Sanctuary in Corella along flat, shaded forest walking paths for easy wildlife viewing.'),
  ('bohol', 4758, 9, 'Seeing the iconic Chocolate Hills from accessible ground-level viewing areas or main resort vantage points if stairways present a challenge.'),
  ('bohol', 4758, 10, 'Exploring historical and heritage landmarks with step-free or low-impact access, such as the Baclayon Church & Museum and the Sandugo Blood Compact Shrine.'),
  ('bohol', 4758, 11, 'Relaxing at flat, full-service beachfront resorts offering gentle water entry, poolside lounges, and holistic spa treatments.'),
  ('bohol', 4758, 12, 'Attempting physically strenuous or high-impact adventure sports like ATV quad biking, Danao Adventure Park gorge swinging, ziplining, or limestone cave pool cliff jumping in Anda.'),
  ('bohol', 4758, 13, 'Climbing the steep, 200+ step staircase to the main viewing deck at the Chocolate Hills Complex if mobility or endurance is limited.'),
  ('bohol', 4758, 14, 'Relying on public tricycles or open-air jeepneys for long-distance transit across the island, which lack suspension support and climate control.'),
  ('bohol', 4758, 15, 'Staying in multi-story hillside eco-lodges or remote rustic guesthouses that lack elevators and accessible walkways.'),
  ('bohol', 4758, 16, 'Taking public boat transfers during rough sea conditions or during peak monsoon months (September to November) when boarding can be unsteady.'),
  ('bohol', 4760, 0, 'Sample authentic **Calamay**, Bohol''s iconic sweet treat made from ground glutinous rice, coconut milk, and brown sugar, traditionally packed and sealed inside smooth coconut shells.'),
  ('bohol', 4760, 1, 'Indulge in a **Floating River Cruise Buffet** along the Loboc River, enjoying a spread of grilled pork belly, chicken inasal, pancit, and fresh tropical fruit while cruising through lush jungle scenery.'),
  ('bohol', 4760, 2, 'Savor a fresh **Seafood Boodle Fight** along Alona Beach, where fresh crabs, prawns, squid, and grilled fish are served over banana leaves with garlic rice and fresh calamansi.'),
  ('bohol', 4760, 3, 'Taste **Chicken Halang-Halang**, a comforting Visayan chicken soup cooked in rich coconut milk with ginger, chili, and lemongrass for a soothing, spicy kick.'),
  ('bohol', 4760, 4, 'Try **Takla** (local pistol shrimp) or fresh **Lato** (sea grapes salad tossed with tomatoes, onions, and local vinegar) at coastal eateries in Tagbilaran and Panglao.'),
  ('bohol', 4760, 5, '**Families:** Scenic floating restaurant buffets on the Loboc River, spacious beachfront dining along Panglao, and sweet snack-tasting tours in Tagbilaran.'),
  ('bohol', 4760, 6, '**Honeymooners:** Romantic cliffside dining in Panglao, private beachfront candlelit dinners, and organic farm-to-table dining overlooking the Bohol Sea.'),
  ('bohol', 4760, 7, '**Luxury travelers:** Upscale multi-course resort dining at 5-star properties in Panglao, private yacht chef catering, and organic gastronomy pairings.'),
  ('bohol', 4760, 8, '**Budget travelers:** Local *carinderia* eateries, night market food stalls in Tagbilaran City, and affordable roadside fruit stands serving fresh mangoes and young coconuts.'),
  ('bohol', 4760, 9, '**Foodies:** Organic farm tours, artisanal peanut kiss and *calamay* workshops, and fresh seafood crawls along Panglao and Anda.'),
  ('bohol', 4760, 10, '**Panglao Island (Alona & Dumaluan):** Best for lively beachfront seafood grills, international cafes, craft cocktail lounges, and high-end resort dining.'),
  ('bohol', 4760, 11, '**Loboc Riverbanks:** Best for traditional Visayan buffet cruises, eco-lodge dining, and riverside native cuisine.'),
  ('bohol', 4760, 12, '**Tagbilaran City:** Best for local night markets, authentic *calamay* specialty shops, affordable bakeries, and heritage Filipino restaurants.'),
  ('bohol', 4760, 13, '**Bee Farm & Dauis Coast:** Best for organic farm-to-table dining, homemade tropical ice creams, cassava cones, and panoramic sea-view meals.'),
  ('bohol', 4761, 0, '**Boholano Calamay:** The island''s signature sweet delicacy made from glutinous rice, coconut milk, and brown sugar, traditionally presented and sealed inside smooth coconut shells.'),
  ('bohol', 4761, 1, '**Peanut Kisses:** Crisp, dome-shaped peanut and egg-white confections inspired by the shape of the iconic Chocolate Hills, making them a quintessential Bohol souvenir.'),
  ('bohol', 4761, 2, '**Woven Raffia & Abaca Crafts:** Handwoven bags, hats, mats, and baskets crafted by local weaving cooperatives in towns like Tubigon, renowned for high-quality natural fibers.'),
  ('bohol', 4761, 3, '**Tarsier-Themed Souvenirs & Handicrafts:** Plush toys, keychains, wood-carved statues, and apparel supporting wildlife conservation initiatives and local artisan livelihoods.'),
  ('bohol', 4761, 4, '**Artisanal Sea Salt (Asin Tibuok):** A rare, heritage Philippine sea salt handcrafted in Alburquerque using ancient, labor-intensive coconut-husk filtering and clay-pot firing methods.'),
  ('bohol', 4761, 5, '**Island City Mall (ICM) & Alturas Mall in Tagbilaran:** Preferred for modern air-conditioned retail, department store shopping, supermarkets stocked with boxed local treats, and ATM/currency exchange services.'),
  ('bohol', 4761, 6, '**Bohol Bee Farm Shop (Dauis & Alona Outlets):** Preferred for organic honey, cassava chips, natural skincare products, homemade jams, and eco-friendly handicrafts.'),
  ('bohol', 4761, 7, '**Tubigon Loomweaving Center:** Preferred for purchasing authentic, high-quality handwoven raffia and abaca fashion items directly from master local weavers.'),
  ('bohol', 4761, 8, '**Tagbilaran City Public Market:** Best for purchasing fresh tropical fruits, sweet mangoes, regional dried fish, and bulk packages of local sweets at local prices.'),
  ('bohol', 4761, 9, 'Expecting large luxury designer malls or international high-street fashion brands; complete major commercial shopping prior to arriving on the island.'),
  ('bohol', 4761, 10, 'Purchasing prohibited wildlife items, coral jewelry, or uncertified shell crafts from unverified beach hawkers along Alona Beach.'),
  ('bohol', 4761, 11, 'Relying solely on credit cards when shopping in local artisan village workshops, roadside souvenir stalls, or public markets where cash in small denominations (PHP) is required.'),
  ('bohol', 4761, 12, '**Delicacy & Culinary Collectors:** Travelers wanting to stock up on authentic *calamay*, Peanut Kisses, organic honey products, and rare heritage *Asin Tibuok* salt.'),
  ('bohol', 4761, 13, '**Handicraft & Textile Lovers:** Visitors seeking eco-friendly handwoven raffia bags, natural woven home decor, and authentic Visayan artisan crafts.'),
  ('bohol', 4761, 14, '**Souvenir & Gift Hunters:** Travelers looking for memorable, lightweight gifts like tarsier merchandise, wood carvings, and local coconut treats to share back home.'),
  ('bohol', 4762, 0, '**Beach lovers & social travelers** looking for open-air, barefoot sand bars, live acoustic sets, and fire-dancing shows along the shore.'),
  ('bohol', 4762, 1, '**Cocktail & sunset enthusiasts** seeking relaxing beachfront lounges, craft beer spots, and prime golden-hour views over the Bohol Sea.'),
  ('bohol', 4762, 2, '**Divers & backpackers** wanting to swap travel stories over cold local beers in casual, bohemian seaside pubs.'),
  ('bohol', 4762, 3, '**Casual partygoers** hunting for lively beach parties, reggae nights, and friendly, unpretentious dance floors.'),
  ('bohol', 4762, 4, 'Enjoying live acoustic music, fire dancers, and cold local beers directly on the sand along **Alona Beach**.'),
  ('bohol', 4762, 5, 'Sipping craft cocktails or imported wines at ambient beachfront lounges and cliffside resort bars like *Amorita Resort''s Treetops* or *MIST*.'),
  ('bohol', 4762, 6, 'Soaking in laid-back, bohemian island vibes with reggae beats and craft brews in cozy Panglao hideaways.'),
  ('bohol', 4762, 7, 'Joining social hostel bar crawls and evening beach bonfires in central Alona or Panglao town.'),
  ('bohol', 4762, 8, 'Expecting late-night urban mega-clubs or 24/7 party districts outside of Alona Beach; most inland countryside towns quiet down significantly by 9:00 PM.'),
  ('bohol', 4762, 9, 'Leaving personal belongings unattended on the beach while swimming or dancing at night.'),
  ('bohol', 4762, 10, 'Driving scooters back to your hotel late at night after drinking, as poorly lit rural roads and sharp turns present major safety hazards.'),
  ('bohol', 4762, 11, '**Alona Beach Strip (Panglao):** The undisputed center of Bohol’s nightlife, densely packed with beachfront bars, live music venues, seafood grills, and late-night lounges.'),
  ('bohol', 4762, 12, '**Dumaluan & Danao Beach Areas:** Ideal for a more relaxed, upscale evening with tranquil resort lounges, romantic cliffside cocktails, and quiet beachfront dining.'),
  ('bohol', 4762, 13, '**Tagbilaran City Center:** Best for local videoke/KTV bars, casual sports pubs, and night market snacks for travelers staying near the main port.'),
  ('bohol', 4767, 0, '**Gilutongan Island:** Snorkeling paradise with vibrant corals and rich marine life.'),
  ('bohol', 4767, 1, '**Caohagan Island:** Peaceful island with local charm and relaxing shoreline vibes.'),
  ('bohol', 4767, 2, '**Nalusuan Island:** Famous boardwalk and marine sanctuary—perfect for photos and swimming.'),
  ('bohol', 4767, 3, '**Blood Compact Shrine:** Historical site commemorating the first treaty between Filipinos and Spaniards.'),
  ('bohol', 4767, 4, '**Baclayon Church:** One of the oldest stone churches in the Philippines, rich in heritage.'),
  ('bohol', 4767, 5, '**Man-Made Forest:** Picturesque stretch of mahogany trees creating a natural canopy.'),
  ('bohol', 4767, 6, '**Exotic Wildlife Encounter:** Visit a sanctuary with pythons and butterflies.'),
  ('bohol', 4767, 7, '**Tarsier Conservation Area:** See the world’s smallest primates up close in their natural habitat.'),
  ('bohol', 4767, 8, '**Chocolate Hills:** Bohol’s iconic geological wonder offering panoramic viewing deck vistas.'),
