  ('ranthambore', 7326, 0, 'Treat Ranthambore as only a **tiger-safari destination**, missing its **fort, temples, lakes, ruins and local culture**.'),
  ('ranthambore', 7326, 1, 'Pack **multiple safaris + Ranthambore Fort + other sightseeing** into one day, creating fatigue and rushed travel.'),
  ('ranthambore', 7326, 2, 'Assume a **tiger sighting is guaranteed** instead of understanding that wildlife sightings are unpredictable.'),
  ('ranthambore', 7326, 3, 'Choose safari timing only by convenience instead of considering **early-morning and late-afternoon wildlife activity**. Rajasthan Tourism specifically recommends these periods for game drives.'),
  ('ranthambore', 7326, 4, 'Book only one safari and expect the complete wildlife experience. Experienced planners generally keep **2–3 safari drives** for a first visit.'),
  ('ranthambore', 7326, 5, 'Ignore **October–June park operating season** and accidentally plan a main safari-focused trip during the July–September closure period.'),
  ('ranthambore', 7326, 6, 'Underestimate **summer heat**, especially in April–June, when daytime conditions become harsh.'),
  ('ranthambore', 7326, 7, 'Choose accommodation based only on price without considering **distance from safari gates, transfer arrangements and safari pickup logistics**.'),
  ('ranthambore', 7326, 8, 'Spend the entire trip inside the resort and miss **Ranthambore Fort, Trinetra Ganesh Temple, Padam Talao and the historic ruins**.'),
  ('ranthambore', 7327, 0, 'Positions Ranthambore as a **wildlife + heritage + luxury wilderness destination**, rather than simply a tiger-safari stop.'),
  ('ranthambore', 7327, 1, 'Prioritizes **Ranthambore National Park, Ranthambore Fort, Trinetra Ganesh Temple, Padam Talao and Raj Bagh Ruins** for first-time visitors.'),
  ('ranthambore', 7327, 2, 'Plans **2–3 safari drives** across suitable morning/afternoon slots rather than relying on a single game drive.'),
  ('ranthambore', 7327, 3, 'Combines **safari + Fort + temple + resort leisure** instead of continuously adding distant sightseeing.'),
  ('ranthambore', 7327, 4, 'Uses **early morning and late afternoon** for outdoor activities and keeps midday for lunch, rest and resort time.'),
  ('ranthambore', 7327, 5, 'Treats **October–March** as the most comfortable broad period for sightseeing, while recognizing that March–June can offer strong wildlife-viewing opportunities around water sources.'),
  ('ranthambore', 7327, 6, 'Builds in **wildlife photography, birdwatching, local crafts and Rajasthani dining** to diversify the trip.'),
  ('ranthambore', 7327, 7, 'Chooses accommodation according to the travel purpose: **central/budget stay for value, quality resort for families, and luxury jungle lodge for honeymoon/premium travel**.'),
  ('ranthambore', 7328, 0, '**Wildlife Strategy:** Sell Ranthambore as a **tiger + wilderness + heritage experience**, not simply a safari destination.'),
  ('ranthambore', 7328, 1, '**Safari Strategy:** For a first visit, plan **2–3 safaris**, preferably combining morning and afternoon drives rather than depending on one attempt.'),
  ('ranthambore', 7328, 2, '**Heritage Strategy:** Combine **Ranthambore Fort + Trinetra Ganesh Temple** as the principal non-safari heritage experience. The Fort is part of UNESCO''s **Hill Forts of Rajasthan** World Heritage property.'),
  ('ranthambore', 7328, 3, '**Heat Strategy:** During **April–June**, prioritize early starts, safari timings and midday resort rest.'),
  ('ranthambore', 7328, 4, '**Route Logistics:** Cluster **Fort–Ganesh Temple** separately from **Shilpgram–local craft/cultural experiences**, while keeping forest lakes and ruins within the safari plan.'),
  ('ranthambore', 7328, 5, '**Itinerary Balance:** **2–3 safaris + 2–4 heritage/nature attractions + resort leisure + local food** works better than continuous sightseeing.'),
  ('ranthambore', 7328, 6, '**Experience Strategy:** For couples and families, combine **wildlife + comfortable resort stay + Fort + photography + relaxed evenings**.'),
  ('ranthambore', 7328, 7, '**Luxury Strategy:** For premium travellers, emphasize **luxury jungle lodge + private Gypsy safari + expert naturalist + private chauffeur + curated dining + spa/wellness**.'),
  ('ranthambore', 7331, 0, 'Explore **Amber Fort, City Palace, Hawa Mahal and Jantar Mantar** in Jaipur.'),
  ('ranthambore', 7331, 1, 'Experience the magnificent **Mehrangarh Fort and Blue City** of Jodhpur.'),
  ('ranthambore', 7331, 2, 'Enjoy the lakes, palaces and romantic atmosphere of **Udaipur**, particularly around Lake Pichola.'),
  ('ranthambore', 7331, 3, 'Experience a **Thar Desert sunset, camel safari and desert camp** around Jaisalmer.'),
  ('ranthambore', 7331, 4, 'Explore **Jaisalmer Fort**, one of Rajasthan''s most distinctive living forts.'),
  ('ranthambore', 7331, 5, 'Visit **Bikaner''s Junagarh Fort** and experience its traditional food and desert culture.'),
  ('ranthambore', 7331, 6, 'Combine the spiritual atmosphere of **Ajmer Sharif and Pushkar** with Pushkar Lake and its historic temples.'),
  ('ranthambore', 7331, 7, 'Go on a **wildlife safari in Ranthambore** for the possibility of seeing Bengal tigers and other wildlife.'),
  ('ranthambore', 7331, 8, 'Explore **Chittorgarh Fort** for one of Rajasthan''s most important Rajput historical experiences.'),
  ('ranthambore', 7331, 9, 'Visit **Keoladeo National Park in Bharatpur** for birdwatching and wetland wildlife.'),
  ('ranthambore', 7331, 10, 'Experience the hill-station character and forests of **Mount Abu**, including Nakki Lake and the Dilwara Temples.'),
  ('ranthambore', 7331, 11, 'Taste regional specialties including **dal baati churma, laal maas, gatte ki sabzi, ker sangri, pyaaz kachori, mirchi bada and ghevar**.'),
  ('ranthambore', 7331, 12, 'Allocate dedicated time for **textiles, jewellery, handicrafts, blue pottery, block prints, leather goods and traditional Rajasthani products**.'),
  ('ranthambore', 7331, 13, 'Include at least one **Rajasthani cultural performance, folk-music evening or traditional dining experience**.'),
  ('ranthambore', 7331, 14, 'Trying to cover **all 11 destinations** in one short trip.'),
  ('ranthambore', 7331, 15, 'Treating Rajasthan as a single homogeneous destination—**Jaipur, Jodhpur, Udaipur, Jaisalmer, Ranthambore and Mount Abu offer very different experiences**.'),
  ('ranthambore', 7331, 16, 'Planning long outdoor sightseeing schedules during **April–June**, when daytime temperatures can become extremely uncomfortable.'),
  ('ranthambore', 7331, 17, 'Underestimating the **distance and travel time between cities**, particularly on road-based itineraries.'),
  ('ranthambore', 7331, 18, 'Spending only a few hours in Jaisalmer while trying to include the desert experience.'),
  ('ranthambore', 7331, 19, 'Visiting multiple forts and palaces consecutively without balancing the itinerary with **food, markets, cultural experiences and leisure**.'),
  ('ranthambore', 7331, 20, 'Assuming every desert or wildlife activity is available year-round or under identical weather conditions.'),
  ('ranthambore', 7331, 21, 'Booking winter accommodation and desert camps too late during **November–February**, when demand is strongest.'),
  ('ranthambore', 7331, 22, 'Overpacking the itinerary with distant destinations instead of allowing sufficient time to experience each city.'),
  ('ranthambore', 7331, 23, 'Ignoring **early-morning starts** for major forts, wildlife safaris and desert activities.'),
