  ('queenstown:rule:75', 'queenstown', 'verify_CURRENT_EVENT_DATES + VENUE + TRANSPORT + HOTEL_DEMAND + ROAD_CONTROLS AND: reduce_NORMAL_SIGHTSEEING_DENSITY_WHERE_REQUIRED', 'Queenstown''s major winter, sporting and seasonal events can materially change accommodation demand, nightlife and transport conditions. ---'),
  ('queenstown:rule:76', 'queenstown', 'prioritize_MOKE_LAKE + BEN_LOMOND_OR_ADVANCED_HIKE + DEEPER_GLENORCHY + QUEENSTOWN_TRAIL + SPECIALIST_WINE_OR_ADVENTURE AND: reduce_REPEAT_ONLY_SKYLINE_AND_STANDARD_CBD_SIGHTSEEING', 'Queenstown becomes substantially richer for repeat visitors when itineraries move beyond the headline resort attractions into trails, valleys and specialist regional experiences. ---'),
  ('melbourne:rule:0', 'melbourne', 'prioritize_MCG_SUNRISE + ROYAL_EXHIBITION_HERITAGE + GREAT_OCEAN_ROAD_AND_WEST_MELBOURNE', 'Very short stays gain more value from properly experiencing core Victorian heritage, world-famous sports and cultural sites, and dramatic coastal landscapes than losing time to exhausting multi-city transit schedules. ---'),
  ('melbourne:rule:1', 'melbourne', 'prioritize_MELBOURNE_ARTS_PRECINCT + SOUTHBANK_RESORT_ATTRACTIONS + GREAT_OCEAN_ROAD_AND_SANCTUARY + YARRA_VALLEY_AND_MORNINGTON_DAY_TRIP', 'This gives a balanced introduction to Victorian cultural heritage, world-class city entertainment, preserved native wildlife sanctuaries, and seamless regional cool-climate wine day excursions. ---'),
  ('melbourne:rule:2', 'melbourne', 'prefer_CENTRAL_MELBOURNE_CORE + DANDENONGS_AND_HEALESVILLE_RETREAT + DAY_TRIPS_TO_PHILLIP_ISLAND_AND_BALLARAT_VIA_REGIONAL_EXPRESSWAYS AND: use_PRIVATE_AC_CARS_V_LINE_EXPRESS_AND_INTER_CITY_TAXIS', 'Luxury urban stays, riverfront cultural precincts, protected native wildlife sanctuaries, and express rail connections to regional historic goldfields offer distinct insights into South Eastern Australia''s premier state. ---'),
  ('melbourne:rule:3', 'melbourne', 'prioritize_RITZ_CARLTON_LUXURY_SUITES + CROWN_METROPOL_HERITAGE_STAYS + PRIVATE_YARRA_RIVER_SUNSET_CRUISE AND: increase_BOUTIQUE_STAYS + ROOFTOP_SKYLINE_DINING + LUXURY_URBAN_SPA + MODERN_AUSTRALIAN_TASTING + COUPLE_EXPERIENCES', 'Melbourne''s romantic routes mix ultra-luxury skyline balcony sanctuaries, multi-course chef-hatted dining, rooftop lounges overlooking glowing city skyscrapers, and quiet walks along Yarra riverfront garden estates. ---'),
  ('melbourne:rule:4', 'melbourne', 'prioritize_HEALESVILLE_SANCTUARY_WILDLIFE + FREE_CITY_TRAMS + PUFFING_BILLY_STEAM_TRAIN AND: include_BOTANIC_GARDENS_GARDEN_RUNS + ARTISAN_CHOCOLATE_WORKSHOPS_AT_YARRA_VALLEY + DISTRICT_DOCKLANDS_PLAY_PARK AND: reduce_STEEP_COASTAL_HIGH_CLIFFS + LONG_CONTINUOUS_TRANSFERS', 'Melbourne has exceptional family sights, including native wildlife sanctuary visits, historic steam train rides through fern gullies, interactive chocolate craft workshops, and colorful immersive play parks. ---'),
  ('melbourne:rule:5', 'melbourne', 'prefer_RITZ_CARLTON_MELBOURNE + PARK_HYATT_MELBOURNE + THE_LANYGON_HOTEL_MELBOURNE AND: increase_PRIVATE_GUIDES + MODERN_AUSTRALIAN_FINE_DINING + PRIVATE_MPV_TRANSFERS + VIP_MCG_ENTRY + SPA', 'Melbourne high-end travel relies on world-famous skyline-view luxury suites, multi-course chef-hatted dining, private MPV transfers via expressways, and high-end heritage hotel estates. ---'),
  ('melbourne:rule:6', 'melbourne', 'prefer_FREE_CITY_CIRCLE_TRAMS_AND_BUSES + SELF_GUIDED_LANEWAY_WALKS + LOCAL_TAKEAWAY_LANEWAY_CAFES AND: book_FREE_GARDEN_VIEW_POINTS_EARLY AND: balance_PAID_ATTRACTIONS_WITH_FREE_ST_KILDA_PIER_PROMENADE_STROLLS + HOSIER_LANE_MARKET_WALKS + YARRA_RIVER_LOOKOUT_VIEWS', 'Melbourne can be accessed affordably using local free tram zone networks, authentic lane coffee stalls, free St Kilda pier promenade walkways, and scenic riverbank garden viewpoints across the Yarra. ---'),
  ('melbourne:rule:7', 'melbourne', 'prioritize_ROYAL_EXHIBITION_BUILDING + STATE_LIBRARY_VICTORIA + OLD_MELBOURNE_GAOL + NGV_INTERNATIONAL AND: include_VICTORIAN_ARCHITECTURE + FIRST_NATIONS_HERITAGE + LOCAL_FESTIVALS', 'These sights showcase Melbourne''s unique Victorian history, mixing 19th-century boomtown elegance, Kulin Nation indigenous culture, and 170 years of Australian civic heritage. ---'),
  ('melbourne:rule:8', 'melbourne', 'prioritize_HOSIER_LANE_STREET_ART + NGV_AUSTRALIA + STATE_LIBRARY_READING_ROOM + FLINDERS_STREET_STATION AND: include_CONTEMPORARY_CITY_GALLERIES + HISTORIC_VICTORIAN_RENEWAL + ECO_RESORT_DESIGN', 'This route contrasts intricate bluestone laneway graffiti art with grand Victorian arches, geometric modern architectural squares, and historic gold rush design. ---'),
  ('melbourne:rule:9', 'melbourne', 'prefer_SPECIALTY_FLAT_WHITE_COFFEE + SMASHED_AVOCADO_TOAST + LOCAL_YARRA_VALLEY_PINOT_NOIR + LYGON_STREET_PASTA AND: include_CHINATOWN_DUMPLING_STALLS + DEGRAVES_STREET_BISTROS + SEAFOOD_FINE_DINING', 'Melbourne dining spans world-famous artisanal espresso coffee, avocado brunch fare, unique regional cool-climate wines, and world-class multicultural dining. ---'),
  ('melbourne:rule:10', 'melbourne', 'prioritize_HEALESVILLE_SANCTUARY + PHILLIP_ISLAND_PENGUINS + ROYAL_BOTANIC_GARDENS + GRAMPIANS_NATIONAL_PARK AND: do_not_treat_MANICURED_RESORT_GARDENS_AND_NATIONAL_PARK_BUSH_TRAILS_AS_IDENTICAL', 'Resort lawns offer manicured lawns and pools, while Victoria''s surrounding national parks and wildlife sanctuaries feature native migratory penguins, wild kangaroos, and protected eucalyptus ecosystems. ---'),
  ('melbourne:rule:11', 'melbourne', 'prioritize_QUEEN_VICTORIA_MARKET + BLOCK_ARCADE_OLD_CITY + EMPORIUM_MELBOURNE + CHAPEL_STREET_FASHION_MARKET AND: include_LOCAL_WINE_STORES + ARTISAN_COFFEE_SHOPS + INDIGENOUS_HANDICRAFTS', 'Queen Victoria Market offers high-end artisan goods and souvenirs, Block Arcade supplies luxury boutiques and historic tea rooms, and Chapel Street features authentic local fashion designer shops. ---'),
  ('melbourne:rule:12', 'melbourne', 'choose_PENINSULA_HOT_SPRINGS + TRADITIONAL_THERMAL_MINERAL_BATHS + HYDROTHERAPY_SANCTUARIES AND: do_not_treat_LOCAL_HOLISTIC_MASSAGE_AND_MODERN_RESORT_HOTEL_SPAS_AS_IDENTICAL', 'Melbourne wellness ranges from heritage city hotel holistic massages to award-winning geothermal hot springs in the surrounding coastal countryside. ---'),
  ('melbourne:rule:13', 'melbourne', 'prioritize_FLINDERS_STREET_STATION_SUNRISE + ST_KILDA_PIER_SUNSET + EUREKA_SKYDECK_VIEWPOINT + HOSIER_LANE_LANES AND: prioritize_GOLDEN_HOUR + BLUE_HOUR + CLEAR_AIR_DAYS', 'These sites produce stunning visual contrasts between historic yellow domed stations, modern glass skyscraper skylines, and emerald Yarra riverbank gardens. ---'),
  ('melbourne:rule:14', 'melbourne', 'prefer_MAXIMUM_ONE_OR_TWO_BASES AND: avoid_EXCESSIVE_HOTEL_CHANGES', 'City transit, freeway traffic navigation, and regional rail transfers consume valuable sightseeing hours. ---'),
  ('melbourne:rule:15', 'melbourne', 'prefer_DIRECT_CAR_RENTALS_PRIVATE_TRANSFERS_OR_V_LINE_EXPRESS_TRAINS_OVER_MULTIPLE_LOCAL_BUS_TRANSFERS', 'Direct express trains and private car transfers eliminate transit confusion and save energy for exploring coastal drive routes and historic goldfields. ---'),
  ('melbourne:rule:16', 'melbourne', 'prefer_ACCESSIBLE_RESORT_HOTELS + FLAT_SOUTHBANK_PROMENADE + PRIVATE_MPV + ROYAL_BOTANIC_GARDENS_ACCESSIBLE_PATHWAYS AND: reduce_EXCESSIVE_BUSH_STEPS + DANDENONG_RANGES_INCLINES + EXTREME_COLD_WIND_WALKS', 'High heritage stairs and steep forest tracks cause fatigue; low-floor trams, private MPVs, and flat garden pathways ease travel. ---'),
  ('melbourne:rule:17', 'melbourne', 'prioritize_EARLY_MORNING_HERITAGE_VISITS + AIR_CONDITIONED_GALLERIES_AND_STORES + EVENING_RIVERFRONT_DINING AND: reduce_MIDDAY_UNSHADED_BEACH_EXPOSURE', 'Melbourne summer temps routinely spike during heatwave conditions (over 40°C); early starts and air-conditioned indoor gallery breaks maintain comfort. ---'),
  ('melbourne:rule:18', 'melbourne', 'increase_NGV_INTERNATIONAL + STATE_LIBRARY_VICTORIA + INDOOR_RESORT_ENTERTAINMENT + COVERED_LANEWAY_ARCADES AND: reduce_DANDENONG_OUTDOOR_DECKS + OUTDOOR_BEACH_PROMENADES', 'Indoor art galleries, historical libraries, covered heritage arcades, and luxury lounges remain excellent regardless of outdoor rain or sudden cool fronts. ---'),
  ('melbourne:rule:19', 'melbourne', 'prioritize_MCG + ROYAL_EXHIBITION_BUILDING + GREAT_OCEAN_ROAD + ROYAL_BOTANIC_GARDENS AND: add_ONE_OF_HEALESVILLE_SANCTUARY_PUFFING_BILLY_OR_PENINSULA_HOT_SPRINGS AND: include_ONE_SIGNATURE_FLAT_WHITE_COFFEE_OR_TAKEAWAY_LANWAY_PARMA_EXPERIENCE', 'This structure provides a comprehensive introduction to Melbourne''s premier architectural and sporting heritage alongside authentic local cafe culture. ---'),
  ('melbourne:rule:20', 'melbourne', 'allocate_60_TO_70_PERCENT_TO_CORE_SIGHTSEEING AND: allocate_REMAINING_TIME_TO_COFFEE_LANEWAYS + RIVER_CAFES + SPAS + ROOFTOP_LOUNGES + SHOPPING + FREE_TIME ---', NULL),
  ('sydney:rule:0', 'sydney', 'prioritize_OPERA_HOUSE_SUNRISE + HARBOUR_BRIDGE_HERITAGE + BLUE_MOUNTAINS_AND_WEST_SYDNEY', 'Very short stays gain more value from properly experiencing core Australian heritage, world-famous harbour monuments, and charm-filled mountain eucalyptus wilderness than losing time to exhausting multi-state transit schedules. ---'),
  ('sydney:rule:1', 'sydney', 'prioritize_SYDNEY_HARBOUR_CENTRE + BARANGAROO_RESORT_ATTRACTIONS + BLUE_MOUNTAINS_AND_SANCTUARY + HUNTER_VALLEY_DAY_TRIP', 'This gives a balanced introduction to harbour heritage, world-class waterfront entertainment, preserved national park wilderness, and seamless regional wine country day excursions. ---'),
  ('sydney:rule:2', 'sydney', 'prefer_CENTRAL_SYDNEY_CORE + MANLY_AND_NORTHERN_BEACHES_RETREAT + DAY_TRIPS_TO_BLUE_MOUNTAINS_AND_CANBERRA_VIA_EXPRESS_TRAIN AND: use_PRIVATE_AC_CARS_EXPRESS_TRAINS_AND_HARBOUR_FERRIES', 'Luxury harbour resorts, coastal marine reserves, protected national park wilderness, and express rail connections to regional hubs offer distinct insights into Southeast Australia''s premier coastal corridor. ---'),
  ('sydney:rule:3', 'sydney', 'prioritize_CROWN_TOWERS_LUXURY_HARBOUR_RESORTS + CIRCULAR_QUAY_HERITAGE_STAYS + PRIVATE_HARBOUR_SUNSET_CHARTER AND: increase_BOUTIQUE_STAYS + ROOFTOP_OPERA_VIEW_DINING + LUXURY_URBAN_SPA + MODERN_AUSTRALIAN_TASTING + COUPLE_EXPERIENCES', 'Sydney''s romantic routes mix ultra-luxury harbour-view suites, Pacific-rim multi-course fine dining, rooftop lounges overlooking glowing sails, and quiet walks along secluded harbor coves. ---'),
  ('sydney:rule:4', 'sydney', 'prioritize_TARONGA_ZOO_FERRIES + CIRCULAR_QUAY_LIGHT_RAIL + SYDNEY_OPERA_HOUSE_FAMILY_SHOWS AND: include_ROYAL_BOTANIC_GARDEN_RUNS + INDIGENOUS_CULTURAL_WORKSHOPS_AT_BARANGAROO + DARLING_HARBOUR_PLAYGROUNDS AND: reduce_STEEP_CLIFF_STEPS + LONG_CONTINUOUS_TRANSFERS', 'Sydney has exceptional family sights, including native wildlife harbour zoos, ferry rides across Port Jackson, interactive First Nations craft workshops, and vibrant waterfront play precincts. ---'),
  ('sydney:rule:5', 'sydney', 'prefer_PARK_HYATT_SYDNEY + CROWN_TOWERS_SYDNEY + THE_LANGHAM_SYDNEY AND: increase_PRIVATE_GUIDES + FINE_DINING_AT_QUAY_AND_BENNELONG + PRIVATE_MPV_TRANSFERS + VIP_OPERA_HOUSE_ENTRY + SPA', 'Sydney high-end travel relies on world-famous harbour-view luxury suites, multi-course modern Australian dining, private MPV transfers, and high-end waterfront hotel estates. ---'),
  ('sydney:rule:6', 'sydney', 'prefer_OPAL_LIGHT_RAIL_AND_PUBLIC_FERRIES + SELF_GUIDED_WALKS + LOCAL_BAKERY_AND_TAKEAWAY_STALLS AND: book_FREE_HARBOUR_VIEW_POINTS_EARLY AND: balance_PAID_ATTRACTIONS_WITH_FREE_BOTANIC_GARDEN_STROLLS + THE_ROCKS_MARKET_WALKS + BONDI_TO_COOGEE_LOOKOUT_VIEWS', 'Sydney can be accessed affordably using capped daily public transport, authentic suburban cafes, free botanical park walkways, and scenic coastal cliff viewpoints across Port Jackson. ---'),
  ('sydney:rule:7', 'sydney', 'prioritize_SYDNEY_OPERA_HOUSE + THE_ROCKS_HISTORIC_PRECINCT + QUEEN_VICTORIA_BUILDING + FIRST_NATIONS_BARANGAROO AND: include_COLONIAL_ARCHITECTURE + INDIGENOUS_HERITAGE + LOCAL_ARTS_FESTIVALS', 'These sights showcase Sydney''s unique history, mixing thousands of years of Indigenous Gadigal heritage with colonial sandstone architecture and iconic modern design. ---'),
  ('sydney:rule:8', 'sydney', 'prioritize_ART_GALLERY_OF_NSW + MCA_AUSTRALIA + OPERA_HOUSE_ARCHITECTURE_TOURS + QVB_STAINED_GLASS AND: include_CONTEMPORARY_WATERFRONT_GALLERIES + HISTORIC_SANDSTONE_RENEWAL + ECO_RESORT_DESIGN', 'This route contrasts modern architectural masterpieces with colonial sandstone arches, contemporary visual art spaces, and historic Australian craftsmanship. ---'),
  ('sydney:rule:9', 'sydney', 'prefer_SYDNEY_ROCK_OYSTERS + MODERN_AUSTRALIAN_SEAFOOD + PACIFIC_RIM_FUSION + ARTISANAL_SPECIALTY_COFFEE AND: include_FISH_MARKET_STALLS + SURRY_HILLS_BISTROS + WATERFRONT_FINE_DINING', 'Sydney dining spans iconic harbour seafood markets, specialty third-wave coffee, vibrant Asian hawker markets, and world-class fine dining overlooking the water. ---'),
  ('sydney:rule:10', 'sydney', 'prioritize_BLUE_MOUNTAINS_NATIONAL_PARK + TARONGA_ZOO_CONSERVATION + FEATHERDALE_WILDLIFE_PARK + ROYAL_BOTANIC_GARDEN AND: do_not_treat_MANICURED_CITY_GARDENS_AND_NATIONAL_PARK_BUSH_TRAILS_AS_IDENTICAL', 'City gardens offer manicured lawns and harbour views, while surrounding national parks and wildlife sanctuaries feature wild eucalyptus forests, native koalas, and coastal marine ecosystems. ---'),
  ('sydney:rule:11', 'sydney', 'prioritize_QUEEN_VICTORIA_BUILDING + PADDINGTON_OXFORD_STREET + THE_ROCKS_MARKETS + WESTFIELD_SYDNEY AND: include_OPAL_BOUTIQUES + INDIGENOUS_ART_GALLERIES + LOCAL_DESIGNER_FASHION', 'QVB offers high-end heritage architecture shopping, Oxford Street supplies boutique Australian designer fashion, and The Rocks features authentic artisan crafts and opals. ---'),
  ('sydney:rule:12', 'sydney', 'choose_LUXURY_URBAN_SPAS + TRADITIONAL_OCEAN_BATHS_SWIMMING + HYDROTHERAPY_SANCTUARIES AND: do_not_treat_LOCAL_OCEAN_POOLS_AND_MODERN_RESORT_HOTEL_SPAS_AS_IDENTICAL', 'Sydney wellness ranges from historic ocean rockpools and beach swimming to world-class luxury hotel spa retreats overlooking the harbour. ---'),
  ('sydney:rule:13', 'sydney', 'prioritize_OPERA_HOUSE_SUNRISE + MRS_MACQUARIES_CHAIR_SUNSET + BRIDGE_CLIMB_LOOKOUT + OBSERVATORY_HILL_VIEWPOINT AND: prioritize_GOLDEN_HOUR + BLUE_HOUR + CLEAR_AIR_DAYS', 'These sites produce stunning visual contrasts between glowing white architectural sails, dark blue ocean waters, and golden sandstone headlands. ---'),
  ('sydney:rule:14', 'sydney', 'prefer_MAXIMUM_ONE_OR_TWO_BASES AND: avoid_EXCESSIVE_HOTEL_CHANGES', 'City traffic navigation, ferry boarding schedules, and regional road transfers consume valuable sightseeing hours. ---'),
  ('sydney:rule:15', 'sydney', 'prefer_DIRECT_CAR_RENTALS_PRIVATE_TRANSFERS_OR_EXPRESS_TRAINS_OVER_MULTIPLE_LOCAL_BUS_TRANSFERS', 'Direct express trains and private car transfers eliminate transit confusion and save energy for exploring national parks and cellar doors. ---'),
  ('sydney:rule:16', 'sydney', 'prefer_ACCESSIBLE_HARBOUR_HOTELS + FLAT_BARANGAROO_FORESHORE_PROMENADE + PRIVATE_MPV + BOTANIC_GARDEN_ACCESSIBLE_PATHWAYS AND: reduce_EXCESSIVE_CLIFF_STEPS + BLUE_MOUNTAINS_INCLINES + EXTREME_SUMMER_HEAT_WALKS', 'Steep coastal stairs and cliffside trails cause fatigue; harbour ferries, light rail, private MPVs, and flat foreshore pathways ease travel. ---'),
  ('sydney:rule:17', 'sydney', 'prioritize_EARLY_MORNING_HARBOUR_VISITS + AIR_CONDITIONED_MUSEUMS_AND_STORES + EVENING_WATERFRONT_DINING AND: reduce_MIDDAY_UNSHADED_BEACH_EXPOSURE', 'Sydney summer temps routinely exceed high heat (over 35°C); early starts and air-conditioned indoor breaks maintain comfort. ---'),
  ('sydney:rule:18', 'sydney', 'increase_ART_GALLERY_OF_NSW + CAPITOL_THEATRE + INDOOR_RESORT_ENTERTAINMENT + QUEEN_VICTORIA_BUILDING_STORES AND: reduce_CLIFFTOP_OUTDOOR_DECKS + OUTDOOR_BEACH_PROMENADES', 'Indoor art museums, theatrical shows, covered shopping arcades, and harbour lounges remain excellent regardless of outdoor downpours or heavy swell. ---'),
  ('sydney:rule:19', 'sydney', 'prioritize_SYDNEY_OPERA_HOUSE + HARBOUR_BRIDGE + BLUE_MOUNTAINS + MANLY_BEACH AND: add_ONE_OF_TARONGA_ZOO_BARANGAROO_OR_BONDI_COASTAL_WALK AND: include_ONE_SIGNATURE_PACIFIC_SEAFOOD_OR_SPECIALTY_COFFEE_EXPERIENCE', 'This structure provides a comprehensive introduction to Sydney''s premier architectural heritage alongside authentic local food and beach culture. ---'),
  ('sydney:rule:20', 'sydney', 'allocate_60_TO_70_PERCENT_TO_CORE_SIGHTSEEING AND: allocate_REMAINING_TIME_TO_HARBOUR_CAFES + BEACH_LOUNGES + SPAS + SUNSET_BARS + SHOPPING + FREE_TIME ---', NULL),
  ('suva:rule:0', 'suva', 'prioritize_FIJI_MUSEUM + THURSTON_GARDENS + ALBERT_PARK AND: choose_ONE_OF_SUVA_MARKET_CUMMING_STREET_OR_WATERFRONT', 'A very short Suva visit gains more value from concentrated culture, heritage and local-life sightseeing than from attempting distant outer-city attractions. ---'),
  ('suva:rule:1', 'suva', 'prioritize_FIJI_MUSEUM + THURSTON_GARDENS + ALBERT_PARK + SUVA_MARKET_CUMMING_STREET AND: retain_ONE_HALF_DAY_FOR_COLO_I_SUVA_OR_DEEPER_CITY_EXPLORATION', 'Two to three nights provide Suva''s strongest first-time balance of national history, multicultural urban life, markets, food, rainforest and evening culture. ---'),
  ('suva:rule:2', 'suva', 'add_COLO_I_SUVA + WATERFRONT_NASESE + USP_LAUCALA_BAY + LOCAL_NEIGHBORHOODS', 'Longer stays allow Suva''s rainforest, educational institutions, waterfront, restaurants and wider neighborhoods to be explored without excessive rushing. ---'),
  ('suva:rule:3', 'suva', 'consider_ONE_OF_PACIFIC_HARBOUR + NAVUA + MOUNT_KOROBABA + NAUSORI_SURROUNDS', 'Suva becomes a stronger extended base when city culture is combined with rainforest, river, adventure or surrounding Viti Levu experiences. ---'),
  ('suva:rule:4', 'suva', 'consider_SUVA_BASE + ONE_SECONDARY_FIJI_REGION AND: avoid_USING_SUVA_AS_BASE_FOR_REPEATED_LONG_WESTERN_VITI_LEVU_DAY_TRIPS', 'Suva is an excellent eastern Viti Levu cultural base, but repeated long-distance road travel to Coral Coast, Nadi, Denarau or western regions can reduce itinerary quality. ---'),
  ('suva:rule:5', 'suva', 'prefer_PREMIUM_HOTEL + WATERFRONT_EVENING + FINE_DINING + SPA + ONE_CULTURAL_EXPERIENCE AND: combine_WITH_RESORT_OR_ISLAND_DESTINATION_IF_TIME_ALLOWS', 'Suva''s romantic strength comes from culture, dining, greenery and city atmosphere, while Fiji''s strongest classic honeymoon experiences remain concentrated in resort and island regions. ---'),
  ('suva:rule:6', 'suva', 'prioritize_FIJI_MUSEUM + THURSTON_GARDENS + MY_SUVA_PARK + SHORT_COLO_I_SUVA_VISIT_WHEN_SAFE AND: include_INDOOR_OR_CAFE_BREAKS', 'Families benefit from balancing educational culture with gardens, recreation and manageable nature experiences rather than continuous city walking. ---'),
  ('suva:rule:7', 'suva', 'reduce_LONG_MARKET_WALKS + DIFFICULT_RAINFOREST_TRAILS + MOUNT_KOROBABA AND: increase_GARDENS + MUSEUM + WATERFRONT_PARK + SHORT_TRANSPORT_SEGMENTS', 'Heat, humidity, rain, busy urban environments and slippery natural terrain can quickly reduce comfort for younger children. ---'),
  ('suva:rule:8', 'suva', 'prefer_PREMIUM_HOTEL + PRIVATE_GUIDE + CHAUFFEURED_TRANSFER + PREMIUM_DINING AND: add_PRIVATE_COLO_I_SUVA_OR_PACIFIC_HARBOUR_EXCURSION_IF_RELEVANT', 'Suva''s strongest luxury positioning combines premium city accommodation, private cultural interpretation, Pacific gastronomy and chauffeured regional touring rather than resort isolation. ---'),
  ('suva:rule:9', 'suva', 'prefer_CENTRAL_VALUE_HOTEL + WALKING + LOCAL_BUS + MARKET_AND_LOCAL_RESTAURANT_FOOD AND: limit_PRIVATE_TRANSFERS + PREMIUM_HOTELS + EXCESSIVE_TAXI_USAGE', 'Suva offers unusually strong value through local buses, markets, inexpensive restaurants, public parks and low-cost cultural experiences. ---'),
  ('suva:rule:10', 'suva', 'prioritize_FIJI_MUSEUM + THURSTON_GARDENS + ALBERT_PARK + GOVERNMENT_PRECINCT + CITY_HERITAGE_WALK', 'Suva concentrates archaeological interpretation, colonial history, national political development and multicultural heritage within a compact urban area. ---'),
  ('suva:rule:11', 'suva', 'allocate_APPROXIMATELY_2_TO_3_HOURS_BASED_ON_INTEREST AND: combine_WITH_THURSTON_GARDENS + ALBERT_PARK', 'The Fiji Museum is the country''s principal national museum and preserves archaeological material dating back approximately 3,700 years alongside collections documenting Fiji''s Indigenous and later communities. ---'),
  ('suva:rule:12', 'suva', 'verify_CURRENT_OPENING_HOURS + ADMISSION + HOLIDAY_STATUS', 'Museum hours, admission rates, guided-tour arrangements and holiday closures are operational information that should be reconfirmed before travel. ---'),
  ('suva:rule:13', 'suva', 'prioritize_ALBERT_PARK + GOVERNMENT_BUILDINGS_PRECINCT + GRAND_PACIFIC_HOTEL_EXTERIOR + CENTRAL_HERITAGE_STREETS', 'Suva''s rise as Fiji''s colonial administrative centre after the capital moved from Levuka in 1882 remains visible through its civic landscape and surviving historic architecture. ---'),
  ('suva:rule:14', 'suva', 'prioritize_FIJI_MUSEUM + CULTURAL_INTERPRETATION + MARKET + FIJIAN_FOOD + APPROPRIATE_COMMUNITY_EXPERIENCE', 'Understanding Suva requires Indigenous iTaukei history and contemporary culture rather than treating the capital purely through colonial-era architecture. ---'),
  ('suva:rule:15', 'suva', 'prioritize_MULTICULTURAL_FOOD + RELIGIOUS_HERITAGE + SAMABULA_OR_RELEVANT_NEIGHBORHOOD + MARKET_CONTEXT', 'Indo-Fijian communities form a major part of Fiji''s cultural, religious, culinary and commercial history and are essential to understanding contemporary Suva. ---'),
  ('suva:rule:16', 'suva', 'prioritize_SUVA_MUNICIPAL_MARKET + CUMMING_STREET + LOCAL_BUS_EXPERIENCE + LOCAL_RESTAURANTS + COMMUNITY_MARKET_IF_AVAILABLE', 'Suva is one of Fiji''s strongest destinations for experiencing everyday urban culture outside the country''s resort-oriented tourism zones. ---'),
  ('suva:rule:17', 'suva', 'combine_MUNICIPAL_MARKET + CUMMING_STREET + LOCAL_FOOD + HANDICRAFT_OR_RETAIL_EXPLORATION', 'Suva Market is most valuable when treated as part of a wider local-life and commercial district rather than only a produce-photo stop. ---'),
  ('suva:rule:18', 'suva', 'verify_CURRENT_MARKET_DATE_AND_LOCATION AND: combine_WITH_LOCAL_FOOD + ARTISANS + CONTEMPORARY_SUVA', 'RoC Market is a periodic community event rather than a permanently operating daily attraction. ---'),
  ('suva:rule:19', 'suva', 'include_FIJIAN_CUISINE + INDO_FIJIAN_CUISINE + SEAFOOD + MARKET_FOOD + CONTEMPORARY_PACIFIC_DINING AND: retain_ONE_QUALITY_RESTAURANT_EXPERIENCE', 'Suva''s food scene reflects Fiji''s multicultural population and extends well beyond simplified resort interpretations of traditional Fijian cuisine. ---'),
  ('suva:rule:20', 'suva', 'include_MARKET_OR_CULTURALLY_INTERPRETED_KAVA_EXPERIENCE AND: avoid_TREATING_KAVA_AS_SIMPLE_ALCOHOL_STYLE_NIGHTLIFE', 'Kava has important cultural and ceremonial meaning in Fiji and is best presented with appropriate context and etiquette. ---'),
  ('suva:rule:21', 'suva', 'combine_SUVA_MARKET + HANDICRAFT_RETAIL + CUMMING_STREET + CBD_MALL_OR_DEPARTMENT_STORE', 'Suva provides both traditional local shopping and modern retail, giving travelers greater variety than a single market or resort shop. ---'),
  ('suva:rule:22', 'suva', 'prioritize_LOCAL_MARKETS + REPUTABLE_HANDICRAFT_RETAILERS + ROC_MARKET_IF_OPERATING AND: check_HOME_COUNTRY_CUSTOMS_RULES_FOR_PLANT_OR_WOOD_PRODUCTS', 'Fijian handicrafts include woven pandanus products, wood carvings, masi and other natural-material goods that may be subject to import controls at the traveler''s destination. ---'),
  ('suva:rule:23', 'suva', 'combine_DINNER + LIVE_MUSIC_OR_BAR + CENTRAL_SUVA_OR_TOORAK_VENUE AND: use_TAXI_FOR_LATE_NIGHT_MOVEMENT_WHERE_APPROPRIATE', 'Suva has one of Fiji''s strongest urban nightlife scenes, centered on restaurants, bars, bands and a smaller number of nightclubs rather than beach-club nightlife. ---'),
  ('suva:rule:24', 'suva', 'prioritize_NASESE + QUEEN_ELIZABETH_DRIVE + MY_SUVA_PARK AND: position_AS_WALKING_AND_RECREATION_NOT_CLASSIC_BEACH_RESORT', 'Suva''s waterfront is valuable for harbor views, local recreation and evening atmosphere but should not be confused with Fiji''s famous white-sand resort beaches. ---'),
  ('suva:rule:25', 'suva', 'do_NOT_POSITION_CENTRAL_SUVA_AS_PRIMARY_BEACH_DESTINATION AND: consider_PACIFIC_HARBOUR + CORAL_COAST + ISLAND_REGION_BASED_ON_TRIP', 'Suva''s primary destination strengths are cultural and urban, while Fiji''s major classic beach experiences are stronger elsewhere. ---'),
  ('suva:rule:26', 'suva', 'prioritize_COLO_I_SUVA + WATERFRONT_GREEN_SPACE AND: consider_MOUNT_KOROBABA_IF_FIT_AND_WEATHER_SUITABLE', 'Suva provides unusually strong urban access to tropical rainforest, freshwater pools, birdlife and hiking despite being Fiji''s largest city. ---'),
  ('suva:rule:27', 'suva', 'allocate_HALF_DAY AND: prepare_FOR_RAINFOREST_TRAILS + NATURAL_POOLS + BIRDWATCHING + WEATHER_VARIABILITY', 'Tourism Fiji identifies Colo-i-Suva as a major rainforest attraction where the popular loop alone requires roughly 1.5_TO_2_HOURS and longer exploration can fill half a day. ---');
INSERT INTO decision_rule (id, place_id, action, reason) VALUES
  ('suva:rule:28', 'suva', 'verify_TRAIL_CONDITIONS_BEFORE_DEPARTURE AND: replace_WITH_CITY_CULTURE_IF_CONDITIONS_ARE_UNSUITABLE', 'Tropical rainforest trails, roots and pool approaches can become considerably more slippery and difficult after substantial rainfall. ---'),
  ('suva:rule:29', 'suva', 'prioritize_COLO_I_SUVA AND: consider_LOCAL_GUIDE_OR_RANGER_INTERPRETATION', 'Tourism Fiji identifies Colo-i-Suva as an important birdwatching location within Viti Levu''s rainforest environment. ---'),
  ('suva:rule:30', 'suva', 'check_WEATHER + FITNESS + FOOTWEAR + TRAIL_CONDITIONS AND: allocate_APPROXIMATELY_HALF_DAY', 'Mount Korobaba is a genuine hiking experience with steep natural terrain rather than a conventional road-accessible city viewpoint. ---'),
  ('suva:rule:31', 'suva', 'replace_WITH_COLO_I_SUVA_IF_SAFE_OR_INDOOR_CITY_SIGHTSEEING', 'Steep tropical terrain becomes significantly less suitable when saturated or during severe weather. ---'),
  ('suva:rule:32', 'suva', 'prioritize_THURSTON_GARDENS + MY_SUVA_PARK + SHORT_COLO_I_SUVA_PROGRAM_WHEN_SUITABLE OVER: MOUNT_KOROBABA', 'These options deliver greenery and tropical landscape with substantially lower physical intensity than the Korobaba hike. ---'),
  ('suva:rule:33', 'suva', 'prioritize_SUVA_MARKET_EARLY + THURSTON_GARDENS + ALBERT_PARK + COLONIAL_STREETSCAPES + WATERFRONT_LATE AND: add_COLO_I_SUVA_FOR_NATURE_PHOTOGRAPHY', 'Suva''s strongest photographic diversity comes from combining people, markets, civic architecture, tropical gardens, rainforest and harbor scenery. ---'),
  ('suva:rule:34', 'suva', 'prioritize_MARKET + CUMMING_STREET + CBD + COMMUNITY_AREAS AND: respect_PERSONAL_PRIVACY + REQUEST_PERMISSION_WHERE_APPROPRIATE', 'Suva''s busy multicultural streets provide strong photographic material, but everyday residents and vendors should not be treated as anonymous tourism props. ---'),
  ('suva:rule:35', 'suva', 'prioritize_FIJI_MUSEUM + USP_LAUCALA_BAY + CITY_HISTORY + MULTICULTURAL_CONTEXT', 'Suva is one of the South Pacific''s major educational and institutional hubs and offers unusually strong opportunities for history, anthropology, politics and Pacific-studies travel. ---'),
  ('suva:rule:36', 'suva', 'prioritize_CIVIC_SUVA + USP + GOVERNMENT_DISTRICT + RELEVANT_PUBLIC_INSTITUTIONS', 'Suva''s role as an economic, educational and diplomatic hub gives it unusual importance within the wider South Pacific. ---'),
  ('suva:rule:37', 'suva', 'verify_CURRENT_EVENT_DATES + VENUE + ROAD_RESTRICTIONS + ACCOMMODATION_DEMAND AND: reduce_NORMAL_SIGHTSEEING_DENSITY', 'Large Suva events can significantly change traffic, park access, hotel demand and realistic city movement. ---'),
  ('suva:rule:38', 'suva', 'prefer_CENTRAL_HOTEL + DOOR_TO_DOOR_TAXI + SHORT_WALKING_CLUSTERS AND: reduce_LONG_MARKET_WALKS + SLIPPERY_RAINFOREST_TRAILS + MOUNT_KOROBABA', 'Suva can work well for seniors, but tropical heat, humidity, rain, variable footpaths and natural terrain require pacing and transport support. ---'),
  ('suva:rule:39', 'suva', 'increase_CITY_WALKING + COLO_I_SUVA + WATERFRONT + PHOTOGRAPHY + OUTDOOR_PROGRAMS AND: retain_RAIN_PROTECTION', 'Fiji''s May-to-October period is generally the cooler and drier season, but Suva''s location on wetter eastern Viti Levu means rainfall remains possible year-round. ---'),
  ('suva:rule:40', 'suva', 'increase_FLEXIBLE_INDOOR_CULTURE + FOOD + SHOPPING AND: retain_SHORT_WEATHER_DEPENDENT_OUTDOOR_BLOCKS', 'November through April is Fiji''s warmer and wetter season with higher humidity and more frequent rainfall. ---'),
  ('suva:rule:41', 'suva', 'check_TROPICAL_CYCLONE_OUTLOOK + CURRENT_WEATHER_ALERTS AND: avoid_GUARANTEEING_WEATHER_SENSITIVE_EXCURSIONS', 'Tropical cyclones in the southwest Pacific are most likely during Fiji''s warmer November-to-April season. ---'),
  ('suva:rule:42', 'suva', 'retain_FLEXIBLE_CITY_PROGRAM AND: move_BETWEEN_INDOOR_AND_OUTDOOR_ATTRACTIONS_AS_CONDITIONS_CHANGE', 'Short tropical showers do not automatically require cancelling an entire Suva sightseeing day. ---'),
  ('suva:rule:43', 'suva', 'replace_EXTENDED_WALKING_AND_HIKING_WITH_FIJI_MUSEUM + SHOPPING + CAFES + FOOD + OTHER_INDOOR_EXPERIENCES AND: use_TAXIS_MORE_SELECTIVELY', 'Suva''s cultural, shopping and dining inventory provides useful all-weather alternatives when prolonged rain reduces walking comfort. ---'),
  ('suva:rule:44', 'suva', 'suspend_NONESSENTIAL_OUTDOOR_EXCURSIONS + FOREST_HIKES + LONG_ROAD_TRIPS AND: follow_OFFICIAL_LOCAL_EMERGENCY_AND_WEATHER_GUIDANCE', 'Cyclones can bring destructive winds, flooding and severe rainfall, so normal tourism scheduling must become secondary to official safety instructions. ---'),
  ('suva:rule:45', 'suva', 'schedule_WALKING_EARLIER + INDOOR_MIDDAY + WATERFRONT_OR_DINING_LATER AND: increase_HYDRATION_AND_REST_BREAKS', 'Suva''s tropical climate can create significant humidity even when absolute temperatures are not extreme by continental standards. ---'),
  ('suva:rule:46', 'suva', 'prefer_PREBOOKED_TRANSFER_OR_TAXI_FOR_STANDARD_VISITOR_COMFORT AND: consider_PUBLIC_TRANSPORT_FOR_BUDGET_TRAVEL_WHEN_PRACTICAL', 'Nausori International Airport is Suva''s principal air gateway and lies outside the central city, making a dedicated road transfer necessary after arrival. ---'),
  ('suva:rule:47', 'suva', 'compare_DOMESTIC_FLIGHT_TO_NAUSORI + INTERCITY_BUS + PRIVATE_ROAD_TRANSFER AND: choose_BASED_ON_TIME + BUDGET + LUGGAGE + ITINERARY', 'Nadi remains Fiji''s principal international gateway while Suva is on the opposite side of Viti Levu, so the onward connection materially affects itinerary design. ---'),
  ('suva:rule:48', 'suva', 'allocate_APPROXIMATELY_HALF_DAY_WITH_TRAFFIC_AND_STOPS AND: avoid_SCHEDULING_MAJOR_FIXED_TIME_SUVA_SIGHTSEEING_IMMEDIATELY_AFTER_ARRIVAL', 'Tourism Fiji positions Suva roughly 3.5_TO_4_HOURS from Nadi by road under standard travel conditions, making the transfer a meaningful itinerary component. ---'),
  ('suva:rule:49', 'suva', 'prefer_TAXI + PRIVATE_TRANSFER + LOCAL_BUS_WHERE_PRACTICAL', 'Colo-i-Suva lies outside the compact central sightseeing core and is more efficiently treated as a dedicated road-accessed nature excursion. ---'),
  ('suva:rule:50', 'suva', 'prefer_PRIVATE_TRANSFER_OR_INTERCITY_BUS_BASED_ON_TRAVELER_STYLE', 'Pacific Harbour is a separate adventure destination south-west of Suva and Tourism Fiji positions it at approximately a 45-minute drive from the capital under suitable conditions. ---'),
  ('suva:rule:51', 'suva', 'prefer_WALKING AND: use_LOCAL_BUS + SELECTIVE_TAXI_FOR_LONGER_MOVEMENTS', 'Suva''s museum, civic, market and CBD areas can be combined efficiently on foot, while outer districts are better connected by road transport. ---'),
  ('suva:rule:52', 'suva', 'prefer_LOCAL_BUS_OR_TAXI AND: use_PRIVATE_VEHICLE_FOR_MULTI_STOP_PROGRAMS', 'Laucala Bay, Colo-i-Suva, Samabula, Lami and other outer areas are too dispersed for efficient all-day walking. ---'),
  ('suva:rule:53', 'suva', 'verify_CURRENT_ELECTRONIC_TICKETING_REQUIREMENTS AND: carry_APPROPRIATE_PAYMENT_METHOD', 'Fiji''s bus network uses electronic-ticketing arrangements that should be confirmed before relying on buses for timed sightseeing movements. ---'),
  ('suva:rule:54', 'suva', 'carry_FIJI_DOLLARS AND: confirm_METER_OR_LONG_DISTANCE_FARE_BEFORE_TRAVEL', 'Tourism Fiji advises travelers to carry cash for taxis and to confirm correct meter or fare use rather than assuming card-based rideshare-style operation. ---'),
  ('suva:rule:55', 'suva', 'avoid_RENTAL_CAR_FOR_PRIMARY_CENTRAL_SUVA_ITINERARY AND: use_WALKING + BUS + TAXI + SELECTIVE_PRIVATE_TRANSFER', 'A short Suva city break generally does not require the added parking, navigation and driving friction of a rental car. ---'),
  ('suva:rule:56', 'suva', 'consider_PRIVATE_CAR_OR_RENTAL_CAR AND: account_FOR_LEFT_SIDE_DRIVING + ROAD_CONDITIONS + PARKING + WEATHER', 'A vehicle becomes more useful when Suva is combined with repeated outer-city or regional touring rather than central sightseeing alone. ---'),
  ('suva:rule:57', 'suva', 'consider_SEPARATE_HALF_DAY_OR_FULL_DAY_EXCURSION AND: do_NOT_LABEL_ACTIVITY_AS_CENTRAL_SUVA', 'Pacific Harbour substantially expands the region''s rafting, diving and adventure inventory but is geographically distinct from Suva city. ---'),
  ('suva:rule:58', 'suva', 'do_NOT_LABEL_SUVA_AS_UNESCO_WORLD_HERITAGE_SITE AND: consider_LEVUKA_HISTORICAL_PORT_TOWN_IF_TIME_AND_LOGISTICS_ALLOW', 'Levuka Historical Port Town on Ovalau, rather than Suva, is Fiji''s UNESCO World Heritage property. ---'),
  ('suva:rule:59', 'suva', 'treat_AS_SEPARATE_OVALAU_EXCURSION_OR_OVERNIGHT_COMPONENT AND: verify_CURRENT_AIR_OR_FERRY_LOGISTICS', 'Levuka is Fiji''s former capital and a UNESCO World Heritage destination but should not be represented as part of central Suva sightseeing. ---'),
  ('suva:rule:60', 'suva', 'use_SUVA_FOR_CULTURE + HISTORY + FOOD + LOCAL_LIFE AND: combine_WITH_BEACH_OR_ISLAND_REGION_IF_CLASSIC_FIJI_EXPERIENCE_IS_REQUIRED', 'Suva provides one of Fiji''s strongest introductions to contemporary national life, but it does not independently represent the country''s full beach, reef and island-resort tourism identity. ---'),
  ('suva:rule:61', 'suva', 'prioritize_FIJI_MUSEUM + THURSTON_GARDENS_ALBERT_PARK + SUVA_MARKET_CUMMING_STREET AND: add_COLO_I_SUVA_OR_WATERFRONT_IF_TIME_ALLOWS', 'These experiences provide Suva''s strongest first introduction to Fijian history, multicultural culture, everyday urban life, tropical greenery and the capital''s distinctive South Pacific identity. ---'),
  ('ha-noi:rule:0', 'ha-noi', 'Max 1 major attraction/day + afternoon pool/AC break.', 'Heat and walking are heavy for kids. ---'),
  ('ha-long-bay:rule:0', 'ha-long-bay', 'Choose an express 2D1N cruise departing from Tuan Chau Marina or stay in Ha Long City/Cat Ba Town with a 4-hour day-boat tour.', 'Overnights under 24 hours require tight logistics; a structured 2D1N itinerary minimizes transit gaps and maximizes time on the water.'),
  ('ha-long-bay:rule:1', 'ha-long-bay', 'Book a 3D2N luxury cruise covering deep Lan Ha Bay or Bai Tu Long Bay, or pair a 2D1N cruise with 1 night in Hanoi/Cat Ba Island.', 'Two full nights on the bay allow access to uncrowded outer lagoons, floating villages, and off-the-beaten-path sea caves without daily packing.'),
  ('ha-long-bay:rule:2', 'ha-long-bay', 'Combine a 2D1N/3D2N luxury cruise with a 2-night land stay on Cat Ba Island or in Ha Long City/Bãi Cháy.', 'Three or more nights allow you to combine marine karst navigation with inland jungle trekking, cave exploring, and mainland market dining.'),
  ('ha-long-bay:rule:3', 'ha-long-bay', 'Prioritize Central Ha Long Bay highlights including Sung Sot (Surprise) Cave, Titov Island peak viewpoint, and Luon Cave.', 'These classic UNESCO heritage landmarks provide the most iconic, quintessential postcard images of Ha Long Bay.'),
  ('ha-long-bay:rule:4', 'ha-long-bay', 'Book a private oceanfront balcony suite on a boutique vessel sailing Lan Ha Bay or Bai Tu Long Bay, paired with a private seaplane flight.', 'Lan Ha and Bai Tu Long offer far quieter anchorages, secluded sea lagoons, and elevated privacy compared to the busier central routes.'),
  ('ha-long-bay:rule:5', 'ha-long-bay', 'Select a large, high-safety 5-star cruise ship featuring family interconnecting suites, sun deck swimming pools, and guided bamboo boat transfers.', 'Modern 5-star ships provide high deck safety railings, kid-friendly cooking masterclasses, and gentle water activities suitable for all ages.'),
  ('ha-long-bay:rule:6', 'ha-long-bay', 'Fly via private Hai Au Aviation seaplane from Hanoi to Tuan Chau Marina, chartering a executive suite or private yacht with dedicated butler service.', 'Seaplane arrival eliminates highway transit and provides dramatic aerial views, paired with bespoke fine dining and private tender excursions.'),
  ('ha-long-bay:rule:7', 'ha-long-bay', 'Base in Cat Ba Town, book local day-boat tours from Ben Beo Harbor, and use public ferries or direct Hanoi tourist buses.', 'Cat Ba Island offers abundant affordable hostels, cheap harbor-front seafood, and low-cost kayaking rentals without luxury cruise surcharges.'),
  ('ha-long-bay:rule:8', 'ha-long-bay', 'Combine a Bai Tu Long Bay eco-cruise with multi-day trekking in Cat Ba National Park (Ngu Lam Peak & Viet Hai Village).', 'The northern wilderness sector of Bai Tu Long and the terrestrial biosphere reserve of Cat Ba contain the region’s highest ecological diversity.'),
  ('ha-long-bay:rule:9', 'ha-long-bay', 'Sample hand-pounded squid patties (Chả Mực) at Bãi Cháy Night Market and enjoy onboard seafood banquets and cooking masterclasses.', 'Regional cuisine centers on world-class fresh catches, artisanal squid preparations, and interactive culinary demonstrations.'),
  ('ha-long-bay:rule:10', 'ha-long-bay', 'Focus on certified floating pearl farms in Lan Ha Bay and Bãi Cháy/Hon Gai local markets.', 'Ha Long shopping centers around cultured marine pearls, vacuum-sealed seafood specialties, and traditional wooden vessel handicrafts.'),
  ('ha-long-bay:rule:11', 'ha-long-bay', 'Book high-end vessels with ground-level suite access, private expressway limousine transfers, and local bamboo rowboat cave excursions.', 'Bamboo rowboats and stable luxury vessels eliminate strenuous cavern stairs and physical kayaking demands.'),
  ('ha-long-bay:rule:12', 'ha-long-bay', 'Stay in Tuan Chau Marina or Ha Long City near the expressway interchange for easy access to Cat Bi (HPH) or Hanoi (HAN) airports.', 'Close proximity to major highway arteries ensures rapid harbor-to-airport transfers for tight flight schedules.'),
  ('ha-long-bay:rule:13', 'ha-long-bay', 'Split your stay between Ha Long Bay/Lan Ha Bay marine cruising and land-based regional hubs like Cat Ba Island, Hanoi, or Ninh Binh. ---', NULL),
  ('mekong-delta:rule:0', 'mekong-delta', 'Choose Can Tho + Cai Rang Floating Market or My Tho + Ben Tre depending on the arrival point.', 'A short stay should minimise road transfers and focus on one compact river region rather than attempting multiple Delta destinations.'),
  ('mekong-delta:rule:1', 'mekong-delta', 'Base in Can Tho and combine Cai Rang, local canals and countryside, or pair Ben Tre + Can Tho.', 'Two nights allow an early floating-market experience plus slower village, orchard and river activities without excessive hotel changes.'),
  ('mekong-delta:rule:2', 'mekong-delta', 'Combine Ben Tre/Cai Be → Can Tho → Chau Doc with private road transfers and selected boat excursions.', 'Three or more nights allow the traveller to experience different Delta landscapes, markets, wetlands, cultural communities and rural waterways.'),
  ('mekong-delta:rule:3', 'mekong-delta', 'Prioritize Cai Rang Floating Market, Can Tho, Ben Tre, Mekong canals and a countryside/orchard experience.', 'These provide the clearest introduction to the Delta''s floating-market culture, waterways, tropical agriculture and everyday river life.'),
  ('mekong-delta:rule:4', 'mekong-delta', 'Choose a private riverside stay in Ben Tre, Cai Be or Can Tho outskirts, with private sampan rides, sunset cruises and couple''s dining.', 'Quiet canals, tropical gardens and intimate riverside accommodation provide a more peaceful experience than crowded group tours.'),
  ('mekong-delta:rule:5', 'mekong-delta', 'Base in Can Tho or Ben Tre and use private vehicles, short boat rides, orchards, cycling and hands-on local experiences.', 'These areas offer manageable travel distances and a mix of educational and gentle outdoor activities suitable for families.'),
  ('mekong-delta:rule:6', 'mekong-delta', 'Combine a luxury riverside resort or boutique hotel with private chauffeur service, private boats, personal guides and a premium Mekong river-cruise experience.', 'Luxury in the Delta is best created through privacy, personalised guiding, comfortable transfers and exclusive river experiences rather than relying only on hotel category.'),
  ('mekong-delta:rule:7', 'mekong-delta', 'Base in Can Tho, Ben Tre or My Tho, using local buses, homestays, bicycles, shared boat tours and local restaurants.', 'The Mekong Delta is relatively budget-friendly, with inexpensive local transport, accommodation and food compared with major Vietnamese resort destinations.'),
  ('mekong-delta:rule:8', 'mekong-delta', 'Prioritize Tra Su Cajuput Forest, Ca Mau, U Minh wetlands, Ben Tre waterways and rural orchards.', 'High-water and wet-season conditions can create especially lush waterways and rewarding wetland scenery; Tra Su is particularly suited to boat-based nature exploration.'),
  ('mekong-delta:rule:9', 'mekong-delta', 'Focus on Can Tho, Chau Doc and Soc Trang, sampling floating-market breakfasts, tropical fruits, bun nuoc leo, elephant-ear fish, hu tieu and other regional dishes.', 'Delta cuisine is strongly shaped by river fish, tropical agriculture and distinct Khmer and southern Vietnamese culinary traditions.'),
  ('mekong-delta:rule:10', 'mekong-delta', 'Focus on Can Tho, Ben Tre, Sa Dec and Chau Doc for coconut products, tropical fruit products, local handicrafts, flowers, textiles and regional foods.', 'Shopping in the Delta is more about agricultural products, handmade goods and regional specialties than conventional luxury retail.'),
  ('mekong-delta:rule:11', 'mekong-delta', 'Choose Can Tho or Ben Tre as a base with private transfers, short boat journeys, comfortable riverside accommodation and limited walking.', 'A private vehicle and carefully selected boat operators reduce unnecessary transfers, while early-morning sightseeing avoids the strongest daytime heat.'),
  ('mekong-delta:rule:12', 'mekong-delta', 'Stay around Can Tho when using Can Tho International Airport, or choose My Tho/Ben Tre when connecting directly from Ho Chi Minh City.', 'Keeping the overnight base close to the arrival/departure corridor reduces unnecessary backtracking and protects tight onward travel schedules. Can Tho Airport is approximately 20 minutes from central Can Tho.'),
  ('mekong-delta:rule:13', 'mekong-delta', 'Split the stay between Ben Tre/Cai Be, Can Tho and Chau Doc, with optional extensions toward Sa Dec, Tra Vinh or Ca Mau.', 'Four or more nights make it practical to combine the Delta''s major river, orchard, floating-market, wetland and cultural zones without turning the trip into a continuous series of long transfers. ---'),
  ('sapa:rule:0', 'sapa', 'Sapa Town + Fansipan only. Skip trekking', 'Travel time eats day'),
  ('sapa:rule:1', 'sapa', 'Town 1N + Trek 1N + Fansipan 1N', 'Minimum culture + nature'),
  ('sapa:rule:2', 'sapa', 'Sapa Town 4★. Cable Car + Cat Cat', 'Easy, safe, no long treks'),
  ('sapa:rule:3', 'sapa', 'Muong Hoa Valley 5★. Private villa', 'Romance + views + privacy'),
  ('sapa:rule:4', 'sapa', 'Sapa Town 3★ + Group trek + Homestay 1N', 'Cheapest mountain experience ---'),
  ('bangkok:rule:0', 'bangkok', 'Choose an express 2D1N city stay staying near Siam or Rattanakosin, focusing on early morning major temples (Wat Pho, Wat Arun) and an evening street food crawl in Chinatown (Yaowarat).', 'Overnights under 24 hours require tight logistics; staying along key mass transit corridors (BTS/MRT) or the river minimizes transit bottlenecks and maximizes sightseeing efficiency.'),
  ('bangkok:rule:1', 'bangkok', 'Book a 3D2N stay based along the Chao Phraya Riverside or Sukhumvit, pairing historic Old City sightseeing with a luxury rooftop lounge experience and ICONSIAM shopping.', 'Two full nights allow you to balance historic temple heritage and canal tours with modern skyline dining and upscale shopping without rushing.'),
  ('bangkok:rule:2', 'bangkok', 'Combine a 3-night urban stay in Bangkok with a full-day excursion to the UNESCO World Heritage ruins of Ayutthaya or a jungle cycling day trip to Bang Krachao.', 'Three or more nights allow you to venture beyond the main commercial core into ancient regional capitals or mangrove oases while keeping your urban hotel base.'),
  ('bangkok:rule:3', 'bangkok', 'Prioritize Rattanakosin Island (Old City) landmarks including the Grand Palace, Wat Phra Kaew, Wat Pho (Reclining Buddha), Wat Arun, and Yaowarat Road street food.', 'These iconic royal and cultural landmarks form the essential spiritual and historical foundation of Bangkok.'),
  ('bangkok:rule:4', 'bangkok', 'Book a riverfront balcony suite at a flagship 5-star resort (Mandarin Oriental, Capella, or The Siam), paired with a private teak barge dinner cruise and high-altitude rooftop cocktails.', 'Riverside sanctuaries offer world-class privacy, serene water views, and romantic fine dining away from dense urban noise.'),
  ('bangkok:rule:5', 'bangkok', 'Select central luxury hotels in Siam or Sukhumvit with direct BTS skywalk access, swimming pools, and proximity to indoor attractions like SEA LIFE Bangkok Ocean World.', 'Direct skywalk and transit connectivity avoids long street walks in intense heat and allows easy midday rest breaks.'),
  ('bangkok:rule:6', 'bangkok', 'Arrange VIP Airport Fast-Track arrival clearance, chauffeured executive transfers (Mercedes S-Class or Toyota Alphard), private longtail boat canal charters, and Michelin-starred tasting menus (Sorn, Gaggan Anand).', 'Fast-track services and private transfers eliminate airport queues, heavy traffic gridlock, and crowded public transport lines.'),
  ('bangkok:rule:7', 'bangkok', 'Base around Khao San Road / Rambuttri Village or along the MRT Blue Line, using Chao Phraya Express Boats, public mass transit, and street food stalls under ฿100.', 'These zones offer abundant low-cost hostels, cheap street dining, and direct access to affordable river transport without expensive taxi fares.'),
  ('bangkok:rule:8', 'bangkok', 'Plan an active day trip to Bang Krachao ("Green Lung") for elevated path cycling, combined with morning strolls through Lumphini Park or Benjakitti Forest Park.', 'These protected green reserves and urban forest parks feature wild Asian water monitor lizards, tropical flora, and car-free nature trails.'),
  ('bangkok:rule:9', 'bangkok', 'Take night street food crawls through Yaowarat (Chinatown), Charoenkrung, and Ban Tad Thong Road, paired with Michelin bib gourmand noodle shops.', 'Bangkok is a world culinary capital famous for fiery stir-fries, heritage roast duck, boat noodles, and night market culinary culture.'),
  ('bangkok:rule:10', 'bangkok', 'Focus on Chatuchak Weekend Market for authentic handicrafts, alongside Siam Paragon, ICONSIAM, and Platinum Fashion Mall for wholesale fashion and luxury labels.', 'Bangkok seamlessly combines the world''s largest open-air market with ultra-modern air-conditioned retail complexes.'),
  ('bangkok:rule:11', 'bangkok', 'Book accessible riverside hotels, utilize chauffeured air-conditioned cars or express boats, schedule early morning temple visits, and reserve afternoon spa downtime.', 'Guided private transport and early morning itineraries prevent heat exhaustion and eliminate long walks on uneven city sidewalks.'),
  ('bangkok:rule:12', 'bangkok', 'Choose a hotel along the Airport Rail Link (ARL) corridor (such as Phaya Thai or Makkasan) or near Suvarnabhumi (BKK) / Don Mueang (DMK) airports.', 'Direct rail link connectivity ensures reliable, traffic-proof transfers to terminal departure gates.'),
  ('bangkok:rule:13', 'bangkok', 'Multi-center your trip by combining 2 nights in central Bangkok (shopping/nightlife) with 2 nights in Pattaya/Phuket or a deep heritage extension in Ayutthaya. ---', NULL),
  ('pattaya:rule:0', 'pattaya', 'Choose an express 2D1N coastal stay in Central Pattaya or Wong Amat, prioritizing an early morning visit to the Sanctuary of Truth and an evening stroll through Walking Street or Jomtien Night Market.', 'Short overnights require tight logistics; staying in central or northern coastal hubs keeps highway transit from Bangkok under 2 hours and maximizes beach and temple access.'),
  ('pattaya:rule:1', 'pattaya', 'Book a 3D2N stay in North Pattaya (Wong Amat) or Jomtien, combining iconic sightseeing (Sanctuary of Truth, Big Buddha Temple) with a day trip to Koh Larn (Coral Island) and sunset rooftop drinks at Horizon.', 'Two full nights allow you to balance cultural heritage and island water sports with oceanfront dining without rushing your itinerary.'),
  ('pattaya:rule:2', 'pattaya', 'Combine a 3-night coastal stay in Pattaya with a full-day hinterland excursion to Nong Nooch Tropical Botanical Garden, Khao Chi Chan (Buddha Mountain), and Ramayana Water Park or Columbia Pictures Aquaverse.', 'Three or more nights allow you to explore beyond the central beach strip into expansive botanical gardens, water parks, and vineyard countryside while maintaining your resort base.'),
  ('pattaya:rule:3', 'pattaya', 'Prioritize iconic landmarks including the Sanctuary of Truth, Koh Larn (Coral Island) speedboat trip, Wat Phra Yai (Big Buddha Temple), Pattaya Viewpoint, and an evening cabaret show (Tiffany’s or Alcazar).', 'These signature coastal and cultural attractions represent the essential highlights and architectural wonders of Pattaya.'),
  ('pattaya:rule:4', 'pattaya', 'Book a luxury ocean-view suite or private pool villa in Wong Amat or Na Jomtien (e.g., InterContinental Pattaya or Royal Wing Suites), paired with a private luxury yacht charter from Ocean Marina and cliffside sunset dining.', 'Quiet coastal enclaves offer romantic privacy, pristine ocean vistas, and exclusive dining away from noisy central nightlife strips.'),
  ('pattaya:rule:5', 'pattaya', 'Select family-friendly resorts in Na Jomtien, Jomtien, or Wong Amat featuring expansive pools and kids'' clubs, paired with visits to Ramayana Water Park, Underwater World, and Nong Nooch Botanical Garden.', 'Quiet beach zones avoid adult nightlife strips while providing immediate access to world-class water parks and interactive marine attractions.'),
  ('pattaya:rule:6', 'pattaya', 'Arrange VIP Airport Fast-Track arrival clearance at BKK/DMK, chauffeured executive transfers (Mercedes S-Class or Toyota Alphard) down Motorway 7, private catamaran charters to outer islands (Koh Pai), and oceanfront fine dining.', 'Private chauffeured transfers and custom marine charters eliminate airport queues, highway travel stress, and crowded public ferry lines.'),
  ('pattaya:rule:7', 'pattaya', 'Base along Jomtien Beach or Soi Buakhao, using public ฿10–฿20 songthaews ("baht buses"), ฿30 public ferries to Koh Larn from Bali Hai Pier, and night market street food stalls under ฿100.', 'These zones offer abundant low-cost guesthouses, cheap seafood night markets, and direct access to affordable shared transport.'),
  ('pattaya:rule:8', 'pattaya', 'Plan a day trip to Nong Nooch Tropical Botanical Garden, combined with off-road hinterland trails near Mabprachan Reservoir or snorkeling in the pristine waters of Koh Rin and Koh Pai.', 'Pattaya’s surrounding region features vast botanical collections, protected island reefs, and scenic countryside eco-trails.'),
  ('pattaya:rule:9', 'pattaya', 'Take evening seafood crawls through the Naklua Lan Pho Seafood Market, Thepprasit Night Market, and Jomtien Night Market, paired with beachfront salt-baked fish (Pla Pao) and local Isan specialties.', 'Pattaya is a major coastal culinary destination famous for ultra-fresh Gulf seafood, spicy papaya salads, charcoal-grilled squid, and night market snacks.'),
  ('pattaya:rule:10', 'pattaya', 'Focus on Terminal 21 Pattaya and Central Pattaya for air-conditioned global retail, alongside Thepprasit Night Market and Pattaya Floating Market for local handicrafts and beachwear.', 'Pattaya seamlessly combines modern themed oceanfront mega-malls with bustling open-air evening markets.'),
  ('pattaya:rule:11', 'pattaya', 'Book step-free beachfront resorts in Wong Amat or Jomtien, utilize private air-conditioned cars via Bolt/Grab, schedule early morning visits to Wat Phra Yai, and reserve afternoon spa downtime.', 'Private chauffeured transport and early morning itineraries prevent heat exhaustion and eliminate long walks on uneven street pavements.'),
  ('pattaya:rule:12', 'pattaya', 'Choose a resort near Motorway 7 entry points or North Pattaya, utilizing pre-booked private chauffeured transfers for direct airport access to Suvarnabhumi (BKK) or Don Mueang (DMK).', 'Proximity to the main highway ensures reliable, traffic-controlled transfers to airport departure gates (~1.5 hours to BKK).'),
  ('pattaya:rule:13', 'pattaya', 'Multi-center your trip by combining 2 nights in Central Pattaya (shopping/nightlife/Koh Larn) with 2 nights in a quiet Na Jomtien luxury resort or a city extension in Bangkok. ---', NULL),
  ('phuket:rule:0', 'phuket', 'Choose an express 2D1N coastal stay in Patong or Kata Beach, prioritizing an early morning heritage walk in Old Phuket Town and a sunset visit to Promthep Cape or the Big Buddha.', 'Short overnights require tight logistics; staying in central west-coast hubs keeps airport transit efficient and maximizes access to top cultural landmarks and beach views.'),
  ('phuket:rule:1', 'phuket', 'Book a 3D2N stay in Patong, Kata, or Karon, combining iconic cultural heritage (Big Buddha, Wat Chalong) with a full-day speedboat excursion to the Phi Phi Islands or Coral Island.', 'Two full nights allow you to balance historic island sights and offshore island hopping with oceanfront dining without rushing your itinerary.'),
  ('phuket:rule:2', 'phuket', 'Combine a 3-night coastal stay in Phuket with a full-day hinterland excursion to the Phuket Elephant Sanctuary, Hanuman World ziplining, and a day trip to Phang Nga Bay or James Bond Island.', 'Three or more nights allow you to explore beyond the main beach strip into lush rainforest hinterlands, ethical wildlife reserves, and dramatic limestone sea caves while keeping your resort base.'),
  ('phuket:rule:3', 'phuket', 'Prioritize iconic landmarks including the Phuket Big Buddha, Wat Chalong, Old Phuket Town Sino-Portuguese architecture, a Phi Phi Islands speedboat tour, Promthep Cape sunset, and a cultural show (Phuket FantaSea or Carnival Magic).', 'These signature coastal, cultural, and island highlights represent the essential attractions and historical identity of Phuket.'),
  ('phuket:rule:4', 'phuket', 'Book a luxury ocean-view suite or private pool villa in Bang Tao, Surin, or Kamala (e.g., Banyan Tree Phuket, Amanpuri, or Keemala), paired with a private motor yacht charter through Phang Nga Bay and cliffside sunset cocktails at Baba Nest.', 'Quiet upscale enclaves offer high-end privacy, breathtaking Andaman sunsets, and world-class fine dining away from commercial party corridors.'),
  ('phuket:rule:5', 'phuket', 'Select family-friendly resorts in Laguna/Bang Tao, Kata, or Karon featuring expansive pool complexes and kids'' clubs, paired with visits to Andamanda Water Park, Phuket Elephant Sanctuary, and Splash Jungle.', 'Tranquil beach zones steer clear of adult nightlife strips while providing fast access to top-tier water parks, calm swimming waters, and educational nature reserves.'),
  ('phuket:rule:6', 'phuket', 'Arrange VIP Airport Fast-Track arrival clearance at HKT, chauffeured luxury executive transfers (Toyota Alphard or Mercedes S-Class), private catamaran charters to outer islands (Racha or Similan), and fine-dining experiences at Michelin-recognized venues.', 'Private chauffeured transit and custom yacht charters eliminate airport arrival queues, local taxi negotiation stress, and crowded public ferry terminals.'),
  ('phuket:rule:7', 'phuket', 'Base along Kata, Karon, or Old Phuket Town, utilizing local Smart Buses or songthaews (฿40–฿100), longtail boat runs to Coral Island, and night market street food stalls under ฿100.', 'These areas offer budget guesthouses, affordable local night markets, and cheap public coastal transport links across the island.'),
  ('phuket:rule:8', 'phuket', 'Plan an ethical visit to the Phuket Elephant Sanctuary, combined with jungle trekking in Khao Phra Thaeo National Park, snorkeling in the Similan Islands, or kayaking through the mangroves of Phang Nga Bay.', 'Phuket’s surrounding marine and mainland ecosystems feature dense virgin rainforests, protected coral reefs, and ethical wildlife conservation zones.'),
  ('phuket:rule:9', 'phuket', 'Take evening street food crawls through the Sunday Walking Street Market (Lard Yai) and Naka Weekend Market, paired with authentic Southern Thai curry (Gaeng Som), slow-braised pork belly (Moo Hong), and fresh seafood at Rawai Seafood Market.', 'Phuket is a UNESCO City of Gastronomy celebrated for its fiery Southern Thai cuisine, Hokkien Chinese culinary heritage, and ultra-fresh Andaman seafood.'),
  ('phuket:rule:10', 'phuket', 'Focus on Central Phuket (Festival & Floresta) for air-conditioned high-end global retail, alongside Lard Yai Sunday Market and Chillva Market for handmade crafts, local art, and trendy beachwear.', 'Phuket offers a versatile shopping environment blending luxury multi-concept mega-malls with vibrant night markets set against historic architecture.'),
  ('phuket:rule:11', 'phuket', 'Book step-free beachfront resorts in Bang Tao, Kamala, or Karon, utilize private air-conditioned cars via Grab/Bolt or private drivers, schedule early morning visits to Wat Chalong, and reserve afternoon spa downtime.', 'Dedicated chauffeured transport and early morning scheduling avoid peak midday heat, steep hill climbs, and long walks on crowded pavements.'),
  ('phuket:rule:12', 'phuket', 'Choose a resort near Nai Yang or Mai Khao Beach, utilizing pre-booked private chauffeured transfers for quick 10-to-15-minute access to Phuket International Airport (HKT).', 'Proximity to the northern beach strip ensures zero risk of coastal traffic jams and easy access to airport departure terminals.'),
  ('phuket:rule:13', 'phuket', 'Multi-center your stay by combining 2 nights in a vibrant beach hub like Kata or Patong (for island tours, dining, and shopping) with 2 nights in a quiet Bang Tao pool villa or a nature extension in Khao Sok National Park. ---', NULL),
  ('krabi:rule:0', 'krabi', 'Choose an express 2D1N coastal stay in Ao Nang Beach, prioritizing an early longtail boat hop to Railay Beach (Phra Nang Cave Beach) and a morning climb up Tiger Cave Temple (Wat Tham Suea).', 'Short overnights require tight logistics; basing in Ao Nang keeps airport transit simple while giving instant longtail access to Railay''s iconic limestone scenery and top cultural lookouts.'),
  ('krabi:rule:1', 'krabi', 'Book a 3D2N stay in Ao Nang or Railay, combining iconic karst landscapes (Phra Nang Beach, Railay West) with a full-day 4 Islands or Hong Islands speedboat excursion and an evening night market tour.', 'Two full nights let you balance dramatic mainland cliff walks, island hopping across turquoise lagoons, and fresh street food without rushing your transit schedule.'),
  ('krabi:rule:2', 'krabi', 'Combine a coastal stay in Ao Nang or Railay with a full-day jungle inland excursion to the Emerald Pool (Sa Morakot), Krabi Hot Springs, and a mangrove kayaking tour through the canyons of Ao Thalane.', 'Three or more nights allow you to venture past the coastline into thermal jungle springs, sacred high-altitude summits, and prehistoric mangrove sea caves while maintaining a seaside base.'),
  ('krabi:rule:3', 'krabi', 'Prioritize signature highlights including Tiger Cave Temple, Railay West & Phra Nang Cave Beach, an early-morning 4 Islands or Hong Islands boat tour, Ao Nang Night Market, and sunset beachfront drinks.', 'These quintessential limestone cliffs, sacred summits, emerald lagoons, and night markets showcase the definitive scenery and culture of Krabi.'),
  ('krabi:rule:4', 'krabi', 'Book a luxury oceanfront villa or suite in Tubkaek Beach or Klong Muang (e.g., Phulay Bay a Ritz-Carlton Reserve, Rayavadee, or Banyan Tree Krabi), paired with a private speed-catamaran charter to Hong Lagoon and sunset dining on the sand.', 'Serene upscale enclaves offer high-end privacy, dramatic views of the Hong Archipelago, and romantic candlelit beachfront dining far from tourist crowds.'),
  ('krabi:rule:5', 'krabi', 'Select family-friendly resorts along Noppharat Thara or Klong Muang featuring shallow pool complexes and direct beach access, paired with a private longtail boat to 4 Islands, easy kayak trips, and visits to Ao Nang Landmark Night Market.', 'Calm, shallow beach zones keep kids safe while avoiding steep cliff stairs, keeping transit simple for island excursions and evening meals.'),
  ('krabi:rule:6', 'krabi', 'Arrange VIP Airport Fast-Track arrival clearance at KBV, chauffeured private transfers, private luxury yacht charters to Hong Islands or Phi Phi, and multi-hour hydrotherapy spa treatments at Wareerak Hot Springs.', 'Private watercraft and dedicated luxury vehicles eliminate waiting in longtail boat queues, crowded pier transfers, and standard group tour schedules.'),
  ('krabi:rule:7', 'krabi', 'Base in Krabi Town or back-street Ao Nang, utilizing shared songthaews (฿50–฿100), public longtail boat runs to Railay (฿100–฿150), and street food meals under ฿100 at Chao Fah or Krabi Town Walking Street Market.', 'Krabi Town offers affordable guesthouses, rich night market food culture, and cheap public transit connecting directly to coastal piers and inland attractions.'),
  ('krabi:rule:8', 'krabi', 'Plan a trek up Dragon Crest Mountain (Khao Ngon Nak), paired with kayaking through Ao Thalane mangrove canyons, swimming in the Emerald Pool, and exploring the sea caves at Ban Bor Thor.', 'Krabi boasts exceptional biodiversity across virgin rainforests, thermal mineral springs, mangrove ecosystems, and dramatic karst mountain trails.'),
  ('krabi:rule:9', 'krabi', 'Take evening street food crawls through Krabi Town Weekend Walking Street and Ao Nang Landmark Night Market, sampling Southern Thai massaman curry, fresh grilled seafood, Khao Yam (rice salad), and crispy Thai rotis.', 'Krabi is famous for its rich Southern Thai culinary traditions, characterized by aromatic curry pastes, fresh seafood, and lively street market culture.'),
  ('krabi:rule:10', 'krabi', 'Focus on world-class rock climbing on the limestone cliffs of Railay East and Tonsai Beach, deep-water soloing, jungle trekking, and high-intensity kayaking through mangrove canyons.', 'Krabi''s towering vertical limestone karsts and jungle terrain make it one of the world''s premier destinations for rock climbing and active eco-adventures.'),
  ('krabi:rule:11', 'krabi', 'Book step-free beachfront resorts in Klong Muang or Noppharat Thara, utilize private air-conditioned cars or longtail boats with low-tide boarding platforms, schedule early morning visits, and plan midday resort downtime.', 'Accessible transport and careful timing avoid steep climbs like Tiger Cave Temple, long wading transfers through sea surf, and oppressive midday heat.'),
  ('krabi:rule:12', 'krabi', 'Choose a hotel base in Krabi Town, leveraging pre-booked private chauffeured transfers or taxis for swift 15-to-20-minute access to Krabi International Airport (KBV).', 'Proximity to the central riverfront district avoids coastal beach traffic bottlenecks and ensures effortless, stress-free access to airport departure terminals.'),
  ('krabi:rule:13', 'krabi', 'Multi-center your stay by combining 2 nights in an active beach hub like Ao Nang or Railay (for climbing and island hopping) with 2 nights in a peaceful sanctuary like Tubkaek Beach or an island jump to Koh Lanta or Koh Yao Noi. ---', NULL),
  ('sentosa-island:rule:0', 'sentosa-island', 'prioritise Marina Bay, Gardens by the Bay, and one signature evening experience.', 'A very short stay should focus on Singapore’s strongest first-impression experiences, not on covering multiple distant zones. ---'),
  ('sentosa-island:rule:1', 'sentosa-island', 'include only one major full-day attraction zone: Sentosa or Mandai Wildlife Reserve.', 'Both areas require substantial travel time and activity time; combining them with a compact city-break schedule creates an exhausting itinerary. ---'),
  ('sentosa-island:rule:2', 'sentosa-island', 'add either a Sentosa full day, Mandai wildlife day, or a relaxed cultural-and-food day.', 'Four or more nights allow core Marina Bay sightseeing plus one interest-led experience without rushing. ---'),
  ('sentosa-island:rule:3', 'sentosa-island', 'include two themed days from Sentosa, Universal Studios, Mandai Wildlife Reserve, Orchard/Botanic Gardens, or East Coast.', 'A five-night stay gives enough time to combine iconic sightseeing, attractions, leisure, and recovery time. ---'),
  ('sentosa-island:rule:4', 'sentosa-island', 'consider a slower Singapore programme, regional add-ons, or a Singapore–Malaysia itinerary.', 'Most first-time Singapore highlights can be covered comfortably in 4–5 nights; extra days work best with a slower pace or multi-destination routing. ---'),
  ('sentosa-island:rule:5', 'sentosa-island', 'schedule a maximum of one major attraction per day and include afternoon hotel, pool, or beach downtime.', 'Heat, walking, queues, and long attraction days reduce practical capacity for young children. ---'),
  ('sentosa-island:rule:6', 'sentosa-island', 'limit the itinerary to two major activities per day and increase free-time allocation.', 'Singapore honeymoon value comes from atmosphere, privacy, dining, skyline views, gardens, and relaxed shared experiences—not maximum attraction count. ---'),
  ('sentosa-island:rule:7', 'sentosa-island', 'use MRT and buses as the default transport, select a well-connected mid-range or budget hotel, and mix paid attractions with free experiences.', 'Singapore can be expensive, but transport, hawker food, public spaces, waterfront walks, Jewel Changi, and selected free light shows help protect the budget without reducing trip quality. ---'),
  ('sentosa-island:rule:8', 'sentosa-island', 'prioritise Marina Bay, Sentosa Island, or Orchard Road for hotel selection.', 'These areas offer Singapore’s strongest concentration of five-star hotels, premium shopping, skyline views, resort facilities, fine dining, and high-touch service. ---'),
  ('kuala-lumpur:rule:0', 'kuala-lumpur', 'Choose an express 2D1N central stay in KLCC or Bukit Bintang, prioritizing an early morning visit to Batu Caves, an afternoon walk around Suria KLCC and KLCC Park, photo ops at the Petronas Twin Towers, and evening street food on Jalan Alor.', 'Short overnights require tight transit logistics; staying in the city core allows fast access via the KLIA Ekspres while putting the city''s most famous landmarks and dining hubs within walking distance.'),
  ('kuala-lumpur:rule:1', 'kuala-lumpur', 'Book a 3D2N stay in KLCC or Bukit Bintang, combining iconic skyline views (Petronas Twin Towers, rooftop lounges) with a morning trip to Batu Caves, historic heritage walks around Merdeka Square and Chinatown, and shopping at Pavilion Kuala Lumpur.', 'Two nights allow a seamless blend of modern architectural marvels, sacred cultural monuments, high-end shopping, and vibrant street food lanes without feeling rushed.'),
  ('kuala-lumpur:rule:2', 'kuala-lumpur', 'Base in Kuala Lumpur and add full-day excursions—such as a mountain retreat to Genting Highlands via the Awana SkyWay cable car, a day trip to the UNESCO-listed historic city of Malacca (Melaka), or an eco-adventure day at Sunway Lagoon Theme Park.', 'Three or more nights enable exploring beyond the city center into cool mountain highlands, historic colonial river towns, or theme parks while maintaining a single luxury city base.'),
  ('kuala-lumpur:rule:3', 'kuala-lumpur', 'Prioritize signature highlights including the Petronas Twin Towers, the 272 colorful steps of Batu Caves, Merdeka Square, Central Market (Pasar Seni), Chinatown (Petaling Street Market, and an evening food feast on Jalan Alor.', 'These quintessential landmarks, historic bazaars, sacred temples, and street food lanes showcase the definitive skyline, multi-ethnic culture, and culinary richness of Kuala Lumpur.'),
  ('kuala-lumpur:rule:4', 'kuala-lumpur', 'Book a high-floor luxury suite in KLCC (e.g., Four Seasons Hotel Kuala Lumpur, Banyan Tree Kuala Lumpur, The RuMa Hotel & Residences, or Mandarin Oriental KL), paired with pre-booked sunset Skybridge tickets, private fine dining overlooking the glowing Twin Towers, and high-altitude rooftop cocktails.', 'Sophisticated urban enclaves offer romantic high-rise skyline views, world-class luxury spas, elevated dining options, and glamorous nightlife away from street-level crowds.'),
  ('kuala-lumpur:rule:5', 'kuala-lumpur', 'Select family-friendly hotels near KLCC Park featuring splash pools and playground access, paired with visits to Aquaria KLCC, Petrosains Discovery Centre, a full day at Sunway Lagoon Theme Park, and interactive cable car rides at Genting Highlands.', 'Proximity to pedestrian parks, indoor science centers, aquariums, and world-class theme parks keeps children entertained safely while minimizing long transit times.'),
  ('kuala-lumpur:rule:6', 'kuala-lumpur', 'Arrange VIP Airport Fast-Track clearance at KLIA, private chauffeured luxury sedan transfers, pre-booked private observation deck experiences, high tea at The Majestic Hotel, and fine dining at Troika Sky Dining or Marini''s on 57.', 'Dedicated private vehicles and executive privileges eliminate long airport queues, traffic delays, and crowded public tourist tours.'),
  ('kuala-lumpur:rule:7', 'kuala-lumpur', 'Base in Chinatown or Bukit Bintang backstreets, utilizing the free Go KL City Bus routes, LRT/MRT rail networks, and eating meals under RM 15 at local mamak stalls (Roti Canai), market halls (ICC Pudu), or street stalls along Petaling Street Market.', 'Central Kuala Lumpur offers an abundance of affordable boutique guesthouses, clean public rail transit, and legendary cheap street food.'),
  ('kuala-lumpur:rule:8', 'kuala-lumpur', 'Plan a visit to the KL Forest Eco Park (canopy walk inside a virgin rainforest), Perdana Botanical Garden (Lake Gardens), KL Bird Park (world''s largest free-flight walk-in aviary), and an excursion to Kanching Falls or the Cameron Highlands tea plantations.', 'KL is uniquely situated around lush tropical rainforest reserves, botanical sanctuaries, mountain tea estates, and expansive aviary gardens.'),
  ('kuala-lumpur:rule:9', 'kuala-lumpur', 'Take evening street food crawls through Jalan Alor and Chinatown, explore ICC Pudu for authentic morning breakfasts, sample Nasi Lemak in Kampung Baru, and enjoy banana leaf rice in Little India (Brickfields).', 'Kuala Lumpur is one of Asia''s premier culinary capitals, celebrated for its unique blend of Malay, Chinese, and Indian flavors, vibrant hawker centers, and 24-hour mamak food culture.'),
  ('kuala-lumpur:rule:10', 'kuala-lumpur', 'Focus on outdoor rock climbing at Gua Damai Extreme Park near Batu Caves, canopy walks at KL Forest Eco Park, high-altitude coaster rides at Genting SkyWorlds Theme Park, or white-water rafting in nearby Kuala Kubu Bharu.', 'Beyond modern shopping malls, the limestone karsts, mountain ridges, and rivers surrounding KL provide world-class outdoor thrills.'),
  ('kuala-lumpur:rule:11', 'kuala-lumpur', 'Book step-free hotels in KLCC connected via covered, air-conditioned skywalks (KLCC-to-Bukit Bintang Walkway), utilize Grab rides or private drivers, schedule early morning visits to outdoor sites like Batu Caves, and plan air-conditioned museum or high tea breaks in the afternoon.', 'Accessible indoor walkways and private door-to-door transit help avoid steep climbs, uneven pavements, and oppressive tropical midday heat.'),
  ('kuala-lumpur:rule:12', 'kuala-lumpur', 'Choose a hotel base near KL Sentral, leveraging direct access to the 28-minute nonstop KLIA Ekspres airport train for seamless transit to KLIA T1/T2.', 'Basing at the primary transit hub completely bypasses unpredictable city highway traffic gridlock, ensuring fast, stress-free access to departure terminals.'),
  ('kuala-lumpur:rule:13', 'kuala-lumpur', 'Multi-center your stay by combining 2 or 3 nights in modern, bustling Kuala Lumpur (for culture, shopping, and nightlife) with 2 nights in a mountain tea retreat in Cameron Highlands or an island beach escape to Langkawi or Penang.', 'A multi-center approach balances the high-energy metropolitan skyline of KL with cool highland tea plantations or relaxing tropical island beaches. ---'),
  ('cameron-highlands:rule:0', 'cameron-highlands', 'Choose an express overnight stay in Tanah Rata, prioritizing a morning drive to the Sungei Palas BOH Tea Estate, a quick walk through the Mossy Forest boardwalk, self-pick strawberries at Big Red Strawberry Farm, and an evening steamboat dinner in Brinchang.', 'Short overnights require efficient routing along the main road trunk; staying in central Tanah Rata provides quick access to transport hubs while putting iconic tea plantations, farms, and dining options within easy reach.'),
  ('cameron-highlands:rule:1', 'cameron-highlands', 'Book a 3D2N stay in Tanah Rata or Brinchang, combining early morning 4WD trips to Sungei Palas BOH Tea Estate and Mossy Forest with afternoon English high tea at a colonial hotel, farm visits (strawberries, sheep, cactus), and browsing the Golden Hills Night Market.', 'Two nights allow a complete highland experience, balancing early morning cloud forest views, agricultural farm tours, classic colonial heritage tea breaks, and evening night market street food without rushing.'),
  ('cameron-highlands:rule:2', 'cameron-highlands', 'Base in the highlands and add immersive nature excursions—such as full-day active jungle hikes (Trail 10 to Gunung Batu Brinchang), guided deep-jungle Rafflesia flower tracking treks, visits to indigenous Orang Asli villages, and relaxed spa days at Spa Village Cameron Highlands.', 'Three or more nights enable exploring beyond the main tourist strip into dense montane rainforests, remote jungle trails, indigenous cultural sites, and luxury wellness retreats.'),
  ('cameron-highlands:rule:3', 'cameron-highlands', 'Prioritize signature highlights including the Sungei Palas BOH Tea Centre, Mossy Forest cloud forest boardwalk, Kea Farm Market, self-pick strawberry harvesting, traditional English high tea, and a hot steaming Highland Steamboat dinner.', 'These quintessential sights, tea estate panoramas, fresh agro-tourism farms, and culinary experiences showcase the iconic cool-climate appeal of Cameron Highlands.'),
  ('cameron-highlands:rule:4', 'cameron-highlands', 'Book a heritage suite at a boutique colonial resort (e.g., Cameron Highlands Resort or The Lakehouse), paired with private garden high tea, a signature tea-infused spa treatment at Spa Village, private candlelit dining by an open fireplace, and sunrise tea plantation photography sessions.', 'Romantic colonial estates offer intimate hillside settings, cozy fireplace lounges, indulgent wellness therapies, and scenic vistas far removed from busy town centers.'),
  ('cameron-highlands:rule:5', 'cameron-highlands', 'Select family-friendly hotels or apartments in Brinchang or Golden Hills, paired with interactive animal feeding at The Sheep Sanctuary, self-pick fruit harvesting at Big Red Strawberry Farm, vibrant flower displays at Cameron Flora Park, and evening snacks at the Golden Hills Night Market.', 'Proximity to hands-on farm activities, flower gardens, animal encounters, and night markets keeps children engaged safely while keeping intra-highland drive times short.'),
  ('cameron-highlands:rule:6', 'cameron-highlands', 'Arrange private executive MPV transfers from KLIA or Penang, stays at Cameron Highlands Resort or The Lakehouse, private 4WD tours to Sungei Palas BOH Tea Estate and Mossy Forest, private English high tea on manicured lawns, and multi-course dining.', 'Dedicated private transport and heritage resort privileges eliminate crowded tour coaches, mountain driving stress, and long queues at narrow roadside spots.'),
  ('cameron-highlands:rule:7', 'cameron-highlands', 'Base in guesthouses or hostels in central Tanah Rata, utilizing local bus connections, walking self-guided trails (e.g., Trail 4 to Parit Falls), eating affordable meals under RM 15 at local mamak stalls or Indian banana leaf joints, and joining shared 4WD half-day tours.', 'Tanah Rata is the primary budget hub, offering abundant low-cost accommodation, cheap local dining options, accessible walking trails, and budget-friendly group tours.'),
  ('cameron-highlands:rule:8', 'cameron-highlands', 'Plan an early morning excursion to the Mossy Forest (Gunung Brinchang cloud forest reserve), jungle hikes along Trail 10, visits to MARDI Agro Technology Park, botanical walks through Cameron Flora Park, and seasonal guided Rafflesia flower tracking.', 'The region is renowned for rare montane cloud forests, unique moss-draped flora, wild pitcher plants, orchids, and endemic jungle biodiversity.'),
  ('cameron-highlands:rule:9', 'cameron-highlands', 'Indulge in an evening communal Highland Steamboat (Hot Pot) dinner featuring fresh mountain vegetables, sample freshly baked scones with clotted cream and strawberry jam, try fresh strawberry desserts, and graze through street food stalls at the Golden Hills Night Market.', 'The cool mountain climate makes piping-hot steamboat meals, freshly harvested berries, farm-fresh produce, and British colonial high tea traditions central to the destination''s culinary identity.'),
  ('cameron-highlands:rule:10', 'cameron-highlands', 'Focus on full-day jungle trekking along high-altitude mountain ridge trails (Trail 1 and Trail 10), steep climbs up Gunung Batu Brinchang, multi-hour Rafflesia tracking deep in the rainforest, and 4WD off-road mountain drives.', 'Beyond peaceful tea gardens, the rugged mountain ridges, dense mossy forests, and surrounding rainforest valleys offer challenging outdoor trekking opportunities.'),
  ('cameron-highlands:rule:11', 'cameron-highlands', 'Book heritage hotels with step-free ground options or elevators, utilize private chauffeured vehicles, schedule easy walks along flat wooden boardwalks at Mossy Forest and BOH Tea Centre, and incorporate relaxed afternoon tea breaks and gentle garden visits (MARDI or Flora Park).', 'Private door-to-door transit and accessible wooden boardwalks allow seniors to enjoy panoramic mountain scenery and flora without tackling steep, uneven jungle tracks.'),
  ('cameron-highlands:rule:12', 'cameron-highlands', 'Choose a central hotel base near Tanah Rata Bus Terminal, leveraging direct access to long-distance express coaches connecting to Kuala Lumpur, Penang, or Ipoh.', 'Staying near the main bus terminal ensures seamless connections to intercity coaches without needing local taxi transfers along congested mountain roads.'),
  ('cameron-highlands:rule:13', 'cameron-highlands', 'Multi-center your trip by combining 2 nights in the cool tea plantations of Cameron Highlands with 2 nights exploring the UNESCO-listed culinary city of Ipoh or the historic heritage streets and street food scene of Penang.', 'A multi-center approach pairs the serene mountain landscapes and cool weather of the highlands with the rich heritage, limestone caves, and world-class food hubs of nearby West Malaysia destinations. ---'),
  ('langkawi:rule:0', 'langkawi', 'Choose an express overnight stay in Pantai Cenang, prioritizing a morning ride on the Langkawi Skybridge Cable Car, a quick walk across the Langkawi Sky Bridge, a photo stop at Dataran Lang (Eagle Square), and an evening beachfront seafood dinner.', 'Short overnights require efficient routing along the main coastal corridors; staying in central Pantai Cenang provides quick access to transport hubs while keeping top attractions, watersports, and dining within easy reach.'),
  ('langkawi:rule:1', 'langkawi', 'Book a 3D2N stay in Pantai Cenang or Tengah Beach, Langkawi, Kedah, combining an early morning Cable Car trip up Gunung Machinchang with a half-day island-hopping boat tour to Pulau Dayang Bunting, duty-free shopping in Kuah, and browsing local night markets.', 'Two nights allow a complete island experience, balancing spectacular high-altitude mountain views, island-hopping marine excursions, tax-free retail, and relaxed evening street food without rushing.'),
  ('langkawi:rule:2', 'langkawi', 'Base on the island and add immersive eco-adventures—such as a guided mangrove boat tour through Kilim Geoforest Park, a day trip to Pulau Payar Marine Park for coral snorkeling, a sunset catamaran dinner cruise, and natural infinity pool swims at Seven Wells Waterfall.', 'Three or more nights enable exploring beyond the commercial beach strips into UNESCO Global Geopark mangroves, offshore marine reserves, secluded northern bays, and luxury wellness offerings.'),
  ('langkawi:rule:3', 'langkawi', 'Prioritize signature highlights including the Langkawi SkyCab and SkyBridge, Dataran Lang (Eagle Square), Pantai Cenang beach strip, a Kilim Geoforest mangrove tour, duty-free shopping in Kuah, and a sunset dinner cruise.', 'These quintessential sights, iconic landmarks, mangrove ecosystems, and island watersports showcase the primary tropical and geological appeal of Langkawi.'),
  ('langkawi:rule:4', 'langkawi', 'Book a luxury pool villa in Datai Bay or Tanjung Rhu Beach, paired with a romantic private sunset catamaran cruise, couples'' traditional Malay spa treatments, private candlelit beach dining, and secluded coastal walks.', 'Secluded northern enclaves offer exclusive private beaches, pristine rainforest canopy settings, high-end wellness therapies, and intimate dining far removed from crowded tourist strips.'),
  ('langkawi:rule:5', 'langkawi', 'Select family-friendly resorts or serviced apartments along Pantai Cenang or Pantai Tengah, paired with interactive visits to 3D Art in Paradise Museum, Underwater World Langkawi, calm island-hopping boat tours, and evening snacks at rotating night markets.', 'Proximity to gentle beach areas, interactive indoor attractions, animal encounters, and walkable dining keeps children engaged safely while keeping intra-island drive times short.'),
  ('langkawi:rule:6', 'langkawi', 'Arrange private luxury MPV island transfers, stays at top-tier resorts (e.g., The Datai Langkawi or Four Seasons Resort), private motorboat charters through Kilim Geoforest Park, exclusive sunset yacht charters, and fine-dining experiences.', 'Dedicated private transport and luxury resort privileges eliminate crowded tour boats, rental vehicle hassle, and long queues at major cable car attractions.'),
  ('langkawi:rule:7', 'langkawi', 'Base in guesthouses or hostels near Pantai Cenang or Kuah Town, utilizing scooter rentals or Grab, enjoying affordable meals under RM 15 at local Malay warungs or Indian mamak stalls, and joining shared half-day island-hopping boat tours.', 'Pantai Cenang and Kuah offer abundant low-cost accommodation, cheap local dining options, accessible public beach access, and budget-friendly group excursion rates.'),
  ('langkawi:rule:8', 'langkawi', 'Plan an early morning mangrove tour through Kilim Geoforest Park, rainforest canopy wildlife walks, birdwatching near Gunung Raya, natural pool swims at Seven Wells Waterfall, and eco-kayaking along pristine river estuaries.', 'The island is Southeast Asia''s first UNESCO Global Geopark, featuring 500-million-year-old limestone formations, ancient rainforests, and diverse coastal ecosystems.'),
  ('langkawi:rule:9', 'langkawi', 'Indulge in fresh ikan bakar (sambal grilled fish) at beachfront seafood restaurants, sample authentic Laksa Kedah, browse rotating local night markets (Pasar Malam) for nasi tomato and apam balik, and enjoy tropical sunset cocktail lounges.', 'Langkawi’s culinary identity fuses fresh Andaman seafood, authentic northern Malay flavors, vibrant night market street snacks, and beachside international dining.'),
  ('langkawi:rule:10', 'langkawi', 'Focus on open-water jet ski island tours, treetop ziplining at Skytrex Adventure, hiking up to the peak of Gunung Raya or Machinchang ridge, scuba diving at Pulau Payar, and sea kayaking through mangrove caves.', 'Beyond relaxing beaches, the archipelago offers adrenaline-fueled marine sports, rugged mountain trekking trails, and dynamic water-based eco-expeditions.'),
  ('langkawi:rule:11', 'langkawi', 'Book oceanfront resorts with step-free access and elevators, utilize private chauffeured vehicles, opt for Express Lane passes at the SkyCab, schedule flat boardwalk strolls at Oriental Village and Kuah waterfront, and select gentle mangrove boat cruises.', 'Private door-to-door transit and accessible cable car options allow seniors to enjoy panoramic archipelago views and tropical nature without navigating steep, uneven jungle tracks.'),
  ('langkawi:rule:12', 'langkawi', 'Choose a central hotel base in Kuah Town near the Jetty Point Ferry Terminal or near Langkawi International Airport (LGK), leveraging direct access to fast ferries to Thailand/mainland Malaysia or flight departures.', 'Staying near transport hubs ensures seamless travel connections for early morning flights or ferry departures without risking delays from island traffic.'),
  ('langkawi:rule:13', 'langkawi', 'Multi-center your trip by combining 3 nights on the tropical beaches and mangrove forests of Langkawi with 2 nights exploring the UNESCO World Heritage street art, colonial culture, and famous street food scene of Penang.', 'A multi-center approach pairs the serene island landscapes and duty-free beach relaxation of Langkawi with the rich urban culture, historic architecture, and world-renowned street food hubs of neighboring Penang. ---'),
  ('batu-cave:rule:0', 'batu-cave', 'Choose an express half-day excursion to Batu Caves, prioritizing an early morning climb up the 272 rainbow steps, a quick visit inside the Cathedral Cave (Temple Cave), photos with the 42.7-meter golden Lord Murugan statue, and a fresh coconut water at the base plaza before returning to central Kuala Lumpur.', 'Half-day transit visits require strict time management; focusing purely on the main staircase and primary cavern allows travelers to capture iconic photos and experience the limestone scale without burning out on secondary ground-level attractions.'),
  ('batu-cave:rule:1', 'batu-cave', 'Combine an early morning Batu Caves visit with a cultural tour of central Kuala Lumpur, pairing the rainbow steps and Cathedral Cave with ground-level sites like Ramayana Cave, an authentic South Indian vegetarian lunch in Brickfields (Little India), and an afternoon walk around historic Merdeka Square and Sri Mahamariamman Temple.', 'A full day provides enough time to explore both the main limestone cavern and ground-level cave temples, followed by a logical progression into KL''s Indian cultural enclaves and colonial heritage sites.'),
  ('batu-cave:rule:2', 'batu-cave', 'Base in central Kuala Lumpur and expand your itinerary beyond standard temple viewing—adding outdoor rock climbing at Gua Damai Extreme Park on the backside of the Batu Caves limestone massif, jungle trekking at Kanching Waterfalls, or an evening trip to Kuala Selangor for riverside seafood and mangrove firefly watching.', 'Multi-day stays in the region enable pairing the spiritual and cultural primary site with active eco-adventures across the surrounding Selangor limestone Karst landscapes and coastal sanctuaries.'),
  ('batu-cave:rule:3', 'batu-cave', 'Prioritize signature highlights including early morning arrival to beat crowds, taking photos in front of the Lord Murugan statue, climbing the 272 colorful stairs, exploring Cathedral Cave, visiting Ramayana Cave, and enjoying a traditional banana leaf rice or dosa breakfast at the base plaza.', 'These core architectural, natural, and culinary elements capture the classic Batu Caves experience while hitting every visually famous landmark.'),
  ('batu-cave:rule:4', 'batu-cave', 'Schedule a private early-morning chauffeured visit to Batu Caves before 8:00 AM for quiet photo opportunities, followed by a high-end Indian fine-dining lunch in KL, a luxury spa treatment, and sunset drinks at a rooftop bar overlooking the Petronas Twin Towers.', 'Early arrivals avoid chaotic tour groups and heat, turning a busy pilgrimage site into an intimate morning cultural stop before transitioning to high-end city romance.'),
  ('batu-cave:rule:5', 'batu-cave', 'Take the direct KTM Komuter train from KL Sentral, explore the ground-level Ramayana Cave with its colorful dioramas and giant Hanuman statue, take slow breaks while climbing the 272 steps, and strictly secure all snacks and personal items inside zipped bags to keep children safe from monkeys.', 'Direct rail transit avoids traffic delays with children, while ground-level diorama caves provide easy visual storytelling before tackling the staircase climb.'),
  ('batu-cave:rule:6', 'batu-cave', 'Arrange a private air-conditioned vehicle with a professional driver, visit early in the morning to bypass heat and crowd surges, hire a private cultural guide to explain Hindu iconography, and return to central KL for fine dining at top-tier hotel venues.', 'Door-to-door private transport eliminates navigation stress, while expert guided commentary deepens the cultural value of the temple complex.'),
  ('batu-cave:rule:7', 'batu-cave', 'Travel using the KTM Komuter train line directly to Batu Caves station for RM 2.60 each way, skip paid base attractions to focus on the free Cathedral Cave climb, and eat affordable South Indian snacks (thosai or vada) under RM 10 at local courtyard eateries.', 'Direct rail transport and free access to the main temple cave make Batu Caves one of the cheapest yet most spectacular world-class day trips in Southeast Asia.'),
  ('batu-cave:rule:8', 'batu-cave', 'Combine your Cathedral Cave visit with a guided eco-tour or rock-climbing session at Gua Damai Extreme Park, observe the natural cave limestone formations and roosting bats, and continue northward to Kanching Rainforest Waterfall Reserve.', 'Batu Caves is a massive 400-million-year-old limestone Karst outcrop with unique subterranean ecosystems, outdoor rock walls, and surrounding rainforest pockets.'),
  ('batu-cave:rule:9', 'batu-cave', 'Focus your visit around the base plaza’s South Indian culinary scene, sampling authentic banana leaf rice with vegetable curries, freshly baked roti canai, hot masala chai, and Indian sweets like laddu and jalebi from temple stalls.', 'Batu Caves hosts one of Malaysia''s densest concentrations of traditional South Indian vegetarian eateries, offering a genuine culinary glimpse into Tamil food culture.'),
  ('batu-cave:rule:10', 'batu-cave', 'Head to the northern face of the limestone outcrop at Gua Damai Extreme Park for rock climbing, abseiling, or zip-lining across natural rock walls, followed by hiking the steep stairs and exploring deep caverns.', 'The limestone cliffs around Batu Caves feature over 160 established rock-climbing routes, making it the premier urban crag and adventure hub in Malaysia.'),
  ('batu-cave:rule:11', 'batu-cave', 'Utilize private door-to-door driver transfers, prioritize ground-level flat attractions like the main plaza and Ramayana Cave, take frequent rests on stair landings if climbing, and ensure visit timing stays strictly within cool early-morning hours.', 'The steep 272-step ascent can be challenging under tropical humidity; focusing on flat base areas and early morning timings protects mobility and comfort.'),
  ('batu-cave:rule:12', 'batu-cave', 'Book a luggage storage service at KL Sentral station, hop on the 30-minute KTM Komuter train directly to Batu Caves, spend 1.5 to 2 hours exploring the site, and take the train directly back to connect with the KLIA Express airport rail line.', 'Direct rail connectivity between Batu Caves and KL Sentral makes it the ideal half-day layover destination for travelers passing through Kuala Lumpur.'),
  ('batu-cave:rule:13', 'batu-cave', 'Multi-center your itinerary by spending 2 nights exploring Kuala Lumpur’s urban sights and Batu Caves, combined with 2 nights in the Cameron Highlands for cool mountain tea plantations or Malacca for UNESCO heritage architecture and Peranakan culture.', 'Pairing central KL and Batu Caves with nearby highland or historical destinations creates a balanced contrast between urban culture, ancient limestone temples, and cool natural landscapes. ---'),
  ('penang:rule:0', 'penang', 'Choose an express half-day excursion to inner George Town, focusing on a self-guided walking loop along Armenian Street for iconic murals like "Kids on Bicycle", a quick visit to Chew Jetty, and a plate of smoky Char Kway Teow at a traditional street-side kopitiam before departing.', 'Half-day transit stops require maximum efficiency; limiting exploration to the dense heritage core near Armenian Street guarantees iconic photography, cultural exposure, and legendary street food without transit delays.'),
  ('penang:rule:1', 'penang', 'Combine an early morning ascent of Penang Hill via the funicular railway and a visit to Kek Lok Si Temple with an afternoon heritage street walk in George Town, visiting the Pinang Peranakan Mansion and finishing with an evening street-food crawl along Kimberley Street or Chulia Street.', 'A full day allows for a clear split between Penang''s cool highland ecosystem/spiritual monuments in the morning and its vibrant urban UNESCO Heritage streetscapes and night bazaars in the afternoon and evening.'),
  ('penang:rule:2', 'penang', 'Base your trip with a multi-area focus—spending day one immersing yourself in George Town''s street art, heritage mansions, and food stalls, and day two exploring the northern coastline with nature hikes at Penang National Park, high-adrenaline adventures at ESCAPE Park, or relaxation along Batu Ferringhi beach.', 'Multi-day stays provide the opportunity to experience Penang''s dual identity: historic urban heritage and culture paired with coastal beaches, outdoor thrill parks, and tropical rainforest reserves.'),
  ('penang:rule:3', 'penang', 'Focus on signature island highlights including riding the Penang Hill Funicular, visiting Kek Lok Si Temple, hunting for street art murals in George Town, exploring Khoo Kongsi or Cheong Fatt Tze Mansion, and eating Char Kway Teow, Asam Laksa, and Cendol at local hawker stalls.', 'Combining the island’s top historical landmarks, iconic nature viewpoints, and world-famous street food hits all classic elements of a first-time Penang itinerary.'),
  ('penang:rule:4', 'penang', 'Split your stay between a romantic boutique heritage hotel in George Town (such as the historic E&O Hotel or Cheong Fatt Tze Mansion) and a luxury beachfront resort in Batu Ferringhi, scheduling private morning street art tours, colonial high tea, and private sunset beach dinners.', 'Combining boutique historic luxury with quiet beachfront indulgence creates a romantic balance between rich cultural exploration and relaxing seaside intimacy.'),
  ('penang:rule:5', 'penang', 'Base in a kid-friendly resort along Batu Ferringhi or Tanjung Tokong, spend full days at ESCAPE Penang Theme Park and Entopia Butterfly Farm, take the funicular up Penang Hill to cross the Curtis Crest Treetop Walk, and enjoy interactive fun at the Wonderfood Museum.', 'High-energy outdoor thrill parks, immersive butterfly enclosures, and interactive museums keep children engaged while avoiding lengthy walking fatigue in peak heat.'),
  ('penang:rule:6', 'penang', 'Arrange private executive vehicle charters with dedicated heritage specialists, stay in luxury oceanfront suites at the Eastern & Oriental Hotel or Shangri-La Rasa Sayang, book VIP express passes for Penang Hill, and dine on fine-dining Peranakan tasting menus at Kebaya Dining Room.', 'VIP door-to-door transport eliminates heat and traffic friction, while exclusive heritage access and chef-led fine dining showcase Penang''s culture with maximum comfort.'),
  ('penang:rule:7', 'penang', 'Stay in historic guesthouses along Chulia Street or Love Lane, explore free open-air heritage sites, street art murals, and clan jetties on foot, take public Rapid Penang buses across the island, and feast at affordable local hawker centers where world-class meals cost under MYR 10–12.', 'Penang is a budget paradise where top attractions (street art, jetties, colonial architecture) and world-renowned hawker cuisine require minimal spending.'),
  ('penang:rule:8', 'penang', 'Head directly to the UNESCO Biosphere Reserve at Penang Hill and The Habitat for treetop canopy walks, hike the jungle trails of Penang National Park to pristine Pantai Kerachut and the meromictic lake, and explore the flora at Tropical Spice Garden.', 'Penang houses ancient coastal virgin rainforests, unique meromictic marine ecosystems, and rich island flora tucked right alongside its historic urban centers.'),
  ('penang:rule:9', 'penang', 'Map out a food-centric itinerary following the Penang Michelin Guide and local hawker spots, sampling Char Kway Teow on Siam Road, Asam Laksa in Air Itam, Nasi Kandar on Line Clear, Nyonya Kuih at Moh Teng Pheow, and late-night Lok-Lok on Kimberley Street.', 'Penang is globally recognized as Malaysia’s street food capital, offering an unparalleled density of Chinese, Malay, South Indian, and Peranakan hawker heritage.'),
  ('penang:rule:10', 'penang', 'Spend a full day at ESCAPE Penang conquering extreme rope courses, zip-lines, and the world''s longest tube water slide, followed by jungle trekking from Teluk Bahang to Monkey Beach or water sports along Batu Ferringhi.', 'The northwestern tip of Penang features top-tier outdoor obstacle parks, steep jungle trails, and coastal water sports hubs for active thrill-seekers.');
INSERT INTO decision_rule (id, place_id, action, reason) VALUES
  ('penang:rule:11', 'penang', 'Utilize e-hailing transport (Grab) for door-to-door drop-offs, explore the flat George Town heritage core via traditional pedal-powered trishaws, buy Express Fast-Track passes for the Penang Hill funicular, and schedule indoor museum or kopitiam rest breaks during peak mid-day heat.', 'Trishaw rides, funicular incline access, and strategic afternoon cooling breaks eliminate long walking fatigue and shield mature travelers from tropical sun exposure.'),
  ('penang:rule:12', 'penang', 'Drop luggage at Penang International Airport or Butterwick transit hubs, take a quick 30-minute Grab ride straight into inner George Town, spend 2 to 3 hours completing a street art and hawker food loop around Armenian Street, and return directly for your departure.', 'George Town’s compact heritage core is located just 25 to 35 minutes from the airport, making it an accessible layover stop for quick sightseeing and street-food sampling.'),
  ('penang:rule:13', 'penang', 'Divide your stay with 2 nights in the George Town UNESCO Heritage Core for cultural walking tours and night markets, followed by 2 to 3 nights in Batu Ferringhi or Teluk Bahang for resort relaxation, nature parks, and coastal beach activities.', 'A dual-base strategy eliminates tedious daily cross-island traffic commutes, delivering a seamless split between urban heritage exploration and seaside resort downtime. ---'),
  ('bali:rule:0', 'bali', 'do not recommend Nusa Penida as a default day trip.', 'The boat transfer and travel time can make a short Bali stay unnecessarily rushed. ---'),
  ('bali:rule:1', 'bali', 'increase romance_weight by 30% increase privacy_weight by 20% increase free_time_weight by 20% decrease activity_density by 20%', 'The objective is a romantic and relaxing Bali experience rather than maximum sightseeing. ---'),
  ('bali:rule:2', 'bali', 'reduce travel_intensity_target by 20% increase downtime by 20% prefer beach/resort-based activities', 'Young children reduce practical daily activity capacity and long road journeys can be tiring. ---'),
  ('bali:rule:3', 'bali', 'prefer_hotel_in_preferred_area', 'A cheaper hotel may not provide better total value once transport costs and travel time are considered. ---'),
  ('bali:rule:4', 'bali', 'prefer_one_hotel', 'Hotel changes consume valuable short-trip time. ---'),
  ('bali:rule:5', 'bali', 'consider_ubud + SOUTH_BALI_COMBINATION', 'A longer stay makes it practical to experience both Ubud''s cultural/natural attractions and South Bali''s beaches and coastal experiences. ---'),
  ('bali:rule:6', 'bali', 'prefer_private_transfer AND: prefer_high_service_hotel_or_resort AND: prefer_private_or_exclusive_experiences', 'Luxury value in Bali is strongly supported by convenience, privacy, service and resort quality. ---'),
  ('bali:rule:7', 'bali', 'prefer_efficient_hotel_location AND: use_shared_or_app_based_transport_where_practical AND: mix_free_and_paid_attractions', 'Maintain experience quality while reducing unnecessary transportation and activity costs. ---'),
  ('bali:rule:8', 'bali', 'prefer_sanur_or_nusa_dua_or_SEMINYAK AND: reduce_daily_sightseeing_density', 'These areas provide convenient access to beaches, hotels, restaurants and leisure experiences. ---'),
  ('bali:rule:9', 'bali', 'prefer_UBUD AND: group_rice_terraces + temples + cultural_experiences', 'Ubud is particularly suited to Bali''s cultural, artistic and natural experiences. ---'),
  ('bali:rule:10', 'bali', 'prefer_SEMINYAK_or_CANGGU', 'These areas offer strong concentrations of restaurants, cafés, nightlife and lifestyle experiences. ---'),
  ('bali:rule:11', 'bali', 'consider_split_stay BETWEEN: UBUD + SOUTH_BALI', 'A split stay can reduce repeated long-distance travel while allowing both inland and coastal Bali experiences. ---'),
  ('yogyakarta:rule:0', 'yogyakarta', 'do not recommend Borobudur, Prambanan, Merapi, and southern beaches together.', 'The travel time and activity density are too high for a short Yogyakarta stay. ---'),
  ('yogyakarta:rule:1', 'yogyakarta', 'increase romance_weight by 30% increase privacy_weight by 20% increase free_time_weight by 20% decrease activity_density by 20%', 'The objective is a romantic cultural experience rather than maximum sightseeing. ---'),
  ('yogyakarta:rule:2', 'yogyakarta', 'reduce walking_intensity_target by 20% increase downtime by 20% prefer_child_friendly_activity', 'Young children have limited tolerance for heat, stairs, long transfers, and full-day temple visits. ---'),
  ('yogyakarta:rule:3', 'yogyakarta', 'prefer_central_hotel AND: prefer_private_transfers AND: reduce_major_attractions_per_day AND: verify_accessibility_per_attraction', 'Yogyakarta’s temples and historic areas may include stairs, uneven surfaces, heat, and long walking distances. ---'),
  ('yogyakarta:rule:4', 'yogyakarta', 'prefer_central_hotel', 'The cheaper hotel may not provide better total value after transport costs and lost sightseeing time. ---'),
  ('yogyakarta:rule:5', 'yogyakarta', 'prefer_one_hotel', 'Hotel changes consume valuable time on a short trip. ---'),
  ('yogyakarta:rule:6', 'yogyakarta', 'consider_Borobudur_area_overnight OR: add_Kotagede_or_Merapi', 'A longer stay allows deeper heritage exploration without overcrowding the itinerary. ---'),
  ('yogyakarta:rule:7', 'yogyakarta', 'prioritize_Borobudur AND: prioritize_Prambanan AND: include_Kraton_or_Taman_Sari AND: add_one_living_culture_experience', 'Yogyakarta’s strongest travel value comes from temples, royal heritage, arts, and living Javanese traditions. ---'),
  ('yogyakarta:rule:8', 'yogyakarta', 'prefer_Borobudur_sunrise AND: prefer_Prambanan_sunset AND: prefer_private_or_premium_dinner AND: protect_free_time', 'Atmosphere, timing, privacy, and relaxed pacing create more romantic value than adding extra attractions. ---'),
  ('yogyakarta:rule:9', 'yogyakarta', 'prefer_private_transfer AND: prefer_high_service_hotel AND: prefer_private_guide AND: prefer_exclusive_or_curated_experiences', 'Luxury value is primarily created through comfort, convenience, privacy, service, and personalization. ---'),
  ('yogyakarta:rule:10', 'yogyakarta', 'prefer_high_value_hotel_location AND: prefer_local_warungs AND: use_public_transport_for_city_travel AND: mix_free_and_paid_attractions', 'Yogyakarta offers strong cultural experiences at low cost, but a poor hotel location can erase transport savings. ---'),
  ('yogyakarta:rule:11', 'yogyakarta', 'consider_Merapi OR: consider_Goa_Jomblang OR: consider_village_cycling', 'Adventure sites are generally outside the city and require additional travel time. ---'),
  ('yogyakarta:rule:12', 'yogyakarta', 'include_gudeg AND: include_angkringan AND: include_local_warung AND: include_one_curated_food_experience', 'Yogyakarta’s food identity is strongest in Javanese cuisine, street food, markets, and informal local dining. ---'),
  ('yogyakarta:rule:13', 'yogyakarta', 'prioritize_museums AND: prioritize_workshops AND: prioritize_cafes AND: keep_outdoor_schedule_flexible', 'Temple, beach, volcano, and village experiences are less comfortable and may require schedule changes during heavy rain. ---'),
  ('yogyakarta:rule:14', 'yogyakarta', 'schedule_hotel_check_in AND: schedule_light_neighborhood_exploration AND: avoid_major_temple_visit', 'A light arrival day reduces fatigue and protects the quality of the main sightseeing days. ---'),
  ('yogyakarta:rule:15', 'yogyakarta', 'do_not_add_southern_beaches_or_Goa_Jomblang_by_default', 'Long-distance nature and adventure excursions have a high opportunity cost on a short cultural trip. ---'),
  ('yogyakarta:rule:16', 'yogyakarta', 'do_not_schedule_Borobudur_and_Prambanan_on_same_day', 'The combination creates excessive heat exposure, walking, and transfer time. ---'),
  ('yogyakarta:rule:17', 'yogyakarta', 'prefer_one_major_experience_plus_free_time OVER: three_or_four_attractions', 'The desired experience is memorable and unhurried rather than densely scheduled. ---'),
  ('yogyakarta:rule:18', 'yogyakarta', 'schedule_breakfast → checkout → airport_transfer AND: avoid_major_attraction', 'Yogyakarta International Airport is outside central Yogyakarta, so departure transfers require a reliable time buffer. ---'),
  ('sumatra:rule:0', 'sumatra', 'Choose a quick heritage loop in central Medan, visiting the historic Tjong A Fie Mansion, taking photos at Istana Maimun, and enjoying a traditional cup of Sumatran coffee alongside mild Soto Medan or Roti Canai at Tip Top Restaurant before departing.', 'Half-day layovers require maximum efficiency near Kualanamu transit routes; focusing on Medan''s compact city center provides rich Dutch-Malay heritage and iconic Sumatran cuisine without risking delayed connections.'),
  ('sumatra:rule:1', 'sumatra', 'Spend the morning exploring Medan’s cultural heritage landmarks (Tjong A Fie Mansion and Istana Maimun), followed by an afternoon journey to Berastagi to visit the colorful fruit market and view the active Mount Sinabung/Sibayak peaks, returning in the evening for a Medan street-food tour along Jalan Semarang.', 'A full day enables a seamless split between North Sumatra’s royal Malay/Chinese heritage architecture in the city and the cool, volcanic Karo Highland vistas.'),
  ('sumatra:rule:2', 'sumatra', 'Base your journey with a dual-focus itinerary—spending day one tracking semi-wild Sumatran orangutans on a guided eco-trek in Bukit Lawang (Gunung Leuser National Park), and day two traveling into the Karo Highlands to witness Sipiso-Piso Waterfall and gaze over Lake Toba.', 'Multi-day stays allow travelers to sample Sumatra''s iconic highlights: ancient tropical rainforest wildlife paired with dramatic crater-lake highland scenery.'),
  ('sumatra:rule:3', 'sumatra', 'Focus on the classic North Sumatra circuit—visiting Medan’s historic mansions, trekking to see orangutans in Bukit Lawang, marveling at Sipiso-Piso Waterfall, and taking a ferry to Samosir Island in Lake Toba to experience Batak culture.', 'Combining Sumatra''s world-famous primate species, magnificent volcanic landscapes, and unique indigenous heritage covers all quintessential first-time Sumatran experiences.'),
  ('sumatra:rule:4', 'sumatra', 'Split your stay between a cozy riverside eco-lodge in Bukit Lawang and a premier luxury lakefront resort or private villa on Samosir Island (Lake Toba) or a secluded island resort off West Sumatra, featuring private boat charters, lakeside candlelit dinners, and couples spa treatments.', 'Blending serene rainforest nature with the peaceful, romantic expanse of Lake Toba or pristine island beaches creates the ideal balance between adventure and intimate tropical luxury.'),
  ('sumatra:rule:5', 'sumatra', 'Stay at kid-friendly eco-lodges and lakeside resorts, take gentle half-day jungle walks in Bukit Lawang with fun river tubing down the Bohorok River, visit the Berastagi Fruit Market to feed horses, and enjoy safe swimming and cycling along Lake Toba''s Tuktuk peninsula.', 'Exciting wildlife encounters, safe water tubing, and flat cycling routes keep children entertained while avoiding overly strenuous trekking routes in hot conditions.'),
  ('sumatra:rule:6', 'sumatra', 'Arrange chauffeured private SUV transfers, stay in high-end lakefront suites at Marianna Resort on Samosir Island or luxury beach resorts in West Sumatra, charter private speedboats across Lake Toba, and secure accredited private naturalists for eco-treks in Gunung Leuser National Park.', 'Dedicated private transport and speedboat charters eliminate long transit friction, while exclusive lakefront resorts and private naturalists ensure maximum comfort in rugged environments.'),
  ('sumatra:rule:7', 'sumatra', 'Stay in charming riverside guesthouses in Bukit Lawang and local Batak homestays in Tuktuk, travel via shared local sutra buses or shared tourist minivans, explore ancient Batak villages and waterfalls independently, and feast at local warungs where delicious meals cost under IDR 25,000–40,000 ($2–$3 USD).', 'Sumatra is an incredible budget paradise where world-class rainforest trekking, stunning crater lakes, and authentic regional dishes are accessible at minimal cost.'),
  ('sumatra:rule:8', 'sumatra', 'Head directly into Gunung Leuser National Park (Bukit Lawang or Ketambe) for multi-day wildlife tracking to spot orangutans, Thomas''s leaf monkeys, and hornbills, followed by exploring the volcanic geology of Lake Toba and the dramatic granite formations of Harau Valley.', 'Sumatra houses some of the planet''s oldest primary rainforests, mega-biodiverse national parks, and earth''s largest volcanic crater lake.'),
  ('sumatra:rule:9', 'sumatra', 'Map out a culinary route across North and West Sumatra, sampling Soto Medan and Durian Ucok in Medan, fresh lake tilapia (Ikan Bakar) in Lake Toba, and authentic Nasi Padang feasts featuring Rendang, Ayam Pop, and Sate Padang in Bukittinggi and Padang.', 'Sumatra is world-famous for its bold, aromatic spice profiles, yielding legendary dishes like Rendang alongside unique regional Batak and Malay culinary traditions.'),
  ('sumatra:rule:10', 'sumatra', 'Combine multi-day wilderness treks through deep primary jungle in Gunung Leuser National Park, climb active volcanoes like Mount Sibayak or Mount Marapi, tube down fast-flowing jungle rivers, and surf world-class waves off the Mentawai Islands.', 'The island offers rugged, untamed terrain ideal for high-adrenaline jungle expeditions, volcanic peak ascents, and world-renowned ocean surfing.'),
  ('sumatra:rule:11', 'sumatra', 'Utilize private chauffeured vehicles for overland transfers, opt for flat, gentle nature walks near Bukit Lawang rather than steep jungle treks, take scenic passenger ferries or private speedboats across Lake Toba, and stay at full-service lakefront resorts with accessible ground-floor rooms.', 'Comfortable private transportation and flat, scenic walking routes eliminate strenuous mountain hiking while preserving full access to Sumatra’s serene landscapes.'),
  ('sumatra:rule:12', 'sumatra', 'Store luggage at Kualanamu International Airport (KNO) or a city hotel, take the airport train (Railink) directly into central Medan, spend 2 to 3 hours touring Tjong A Fie Mansion and Istana Maimun, and enjoy lunch at Tip Top Restaurant before taking the train back for your flight.', 'Medan’s dedicated airport Railink connects Kualanamu Airport to the city center in under 45 minutes, making short layover excursions convenient and stress-free.'),
  ('sumatra:rule:13', 'sumatra', 'Divide your stay between 2 nights in Bukit Lawang for rainforest eco-trekking and river tubing, followed by 2 to 3 nights on Samosir Island in Lake Toba for Batak cultural exploration, lakeside relaxation, and highland waterfall visits.', 'A dual-base strategy pairs Sumatra''s top wild rainforest ecosystem with its iconic crater lake, delivering a well-paced balance between active adventure and tranquil scenic downtime. ---'),
  ('jawa:rule:0', 'jawa', 'Choose a quick heritage loop in central Jakarta, visiting National Monument (Monas), taking photos outside Istana Merdeka, and enjoying a traditional cup of Javanese coffee alongside mild Soto Betawi or Gado-Gado at a historic establishment in Old Batavia (Kota Tua) before departing.', 'Half-day layovers require maximum efficiency near airport and rail routes; focusing on Jakarta''s central heritage core provides iconic landmarks and traditional Betawi cuisine without risking delayed connections.'),
  ('jawa:rule:1', 'jawa', 'Spend the morning exploring Old Batavia''s Fatahillah Square and Sunda Kelapa Harbor in Jakarta, followed by an afternoon high-speed train (Whoosh) ride to Bandung to view colonial Art Deco architecture and crater views at Tangkuban Perahu, returning in the evening for dinner.', 'A single full day leverages Java’s high-speed rail network to seamlessly combine national capital history with cool highland volcanic crater vistas.'),
  ('jawa:rule:2', 'jawa', 'Base your journey in Central Java—spending day one exploring the massive stone stupas of Borobudur Temple and heritage lanes of Yogyakarta, and day two visiting Prambanan Hindu Temple followed by an evening Ramayana Ballet performance.', 'Multi-day stays allow travelers to experience Java''s premier cultural highlight: ancient UNESCO World Heritage monument architecture paired with classic Javanese royal arts.'),
  ('jawa:rule:3', 'jawa', 'Focus on the classic Java overland route—exploring Old Batavia in Jakarta, visiting Borobudur and Prambanan temples in Yogyakarta, taking an Executive Train into East Java, and witnessing sunrise over Mount Bromo''s volcanic caldera.', 'Combining Java''s vibrant capital, UNESCO cultural treasures, scenic high-speed rail journeys, and world-famous volcanic landscapes covers all quintessential first-time Javanese experiences.'),
  ('jawa:rule:4', 'jawa', 'Split your stay between a private luxury resort villa amidst the rice terraces near Borobudur and a secluded highland lodge overlooking Mount Bromo, featuring private 4x4 sunrise tours, private temple picnics, and traditional Javanese couples spa treatments.', 'Blending tranquil heritage luxury with dramatic, misty volcanic sunrise landscapes creates an exceptionally romantic and memorable Javanese getaway.'),
  ('jawa:rule:5', 'jawa', 'Stay at kid-friendly garden resorts in Yogyakarta and Malang, take comfortable Executive Train rides, explore Batu Secret Zoo and Museum Angkut, embark on a gentle sunrise Jeep tour at Mount Bromo, and join hands-on Batik-making workshops.', 'Interactive animal parks, thrilling Jeep rides, hands-on craft activities, and smooth train travel keep children engaged while avoiding overly exhausting road journeys.'),
  ('jawa:rule:6', 'jawa', 'Book luxury heritage resorts like Amanjiwo near Borobudur, reserve VIP ascension passes for temple terraces, travel via luxury private train compartments or chauffeured SUVs, and charter private 4x4 Jeeps for exclusive Mount Bromo sunrise access.', 'Private door-to-door transport and exclusive temple access eliminate crowd friction, while iconic luxury properties provide world-class service in majestic settings.'),
  ('jawa:rule:7', 'jawa', 'Stay in charming homestays in Yogyakarta''s Prawirotaman district and guesthouses in Cemorolawang, travel using affordable Executive Trains and public minibuses, explore heritage neighborhoods independently, and dine at local warungs where delicious meals cost under IDR 20,000–35,000 ($1.30–$2.30 USD).', 'Java boasts an exceptional train network and vibrant street-food culture, making world-class historical sites and volcanic peaks accessible at very low costs.'),
  ('jawa:rule:8', 'jawa', 'Head into East Java to trek across Mount Bromo''s volcanic sea of sand, witness the rare blue flames and turquoise crater lake of Ijen Crater, and explore the lush tropical rainforests of Ujung Kulon National Park or Meru Betiri.', 'Java hosts some of the world''s most impressive active volcanoes, dramatic crater lakes, and bio-diverse national parks protecting endangered endemic wildlife.'),
  ('jawa:rule:9', 'jawa', 'Map out a regional culinary route across Java, sampling Soto Betawi in Jakarta, sweet Gudeg and Bakpia in Yogyakarta, Nasi Liwet in Solo, Bakso Malang in East Java, and rich Rawon (black nut beef soup) in Surabaya.', 'Java features incredibly diverse regional food traditions, balancing sweet Central Javanese flavors with rich, savory, and aromatic East Javanese spice profiles.'),
  ('jawa:rule:10', 'jawa', 'Combine night treks to see Ijen''s blue fire, 4x4 off-road expeditions on Mount Merapi and Bromo, white-water rafting on the Elo or Progo Rivers, and caving down the vertical sinkhole of Jomblang Cave.', 'Java offers high-adrenaline outdoor pursuits ranging from subterranean cave rappelling and river rafting to pre-dawn volcano peak climbs.'),
  ('jawa:rule:11', 'jawa', 'Utilize comfortable Executive Class trains for long transfers, book ground-floor suites at full-service resorts in Yogyakarta and Malang, take private golf cart tours around Prambanan, and view Mount Bromo from accessible caldera lookouts.', 'Java''s excellent rail infrastructure and well-developed tour services allow seniors to experience UNESCO sites and volcanic scenery without grueling physical strain.'),
  ('jawa:rule:12', 'jawa', 'Take the dedicated Railink airport train from Soekarno-Hatta Airport (CGK) into central Jakarta, spend 2 to 3 hours visiting Monas and National Museum or Old Batavia, enjoy a meal at Cafe Batavia, and return via Railink for your flight.', 'Jakarta''s direct airport rail link avoids severe city traffic, allowing layover travelers to sample central monuments and dining safely on schedule.'),
  ('jawa:rule:13', 'jawa', 'Divide your stay between 2 nights in Yogyakarta for Borobudur, Prambanan, and royal heritage, followed by 1 to 2 nights in East Java near Mount Bromo for scenic volcano exploration via Executive Train connections.', 'A dual-region itinerary efficiently bridges Java’s major cultural heartland with its spectacular volcanic landscapes via smooth rail logistics. ---'),
  ('bornea-island:rule:0', 'bornea-island', 'Choose a quick heritage loop in central Kota Kinabalu, visiting the Sabah State Museum, taking photos at the floating City Mosque (Masjid Bandaraya), and enjoying fresh coconut water alongside grilled seafood at the waterfront night market before departing.', 'Short layovers require high efficiency near Kota Kinabalu Airport (BKI); focusing on the compact city center provides rich Bornean heritage and iconic local flavors without risking delayed connections.'),
  ('bornea-island:rule:1', 'bornea-island', 'Spend the morning taking a short speedboat ride to Sapi or Manukan Island in Tunku Abdul Rahman Marine Park for snorkeling and beach relaxation, returning by mid-afternoon for a scenic coastal drive to Signal Hill Observatory Platform and a Bornean seafood dinner along the Kota Kinabalu Waterfront.', 'A full day enables a seamless split between Sabah’s vibrant marine life right off the coast and Kota Kinabalu’s scenic urban and sunset vantage points.'),
  ('bornea-island:rule:2', 'bornea-island', 'Base your journey with a dual-focus itinerary—spending day one exploring the coastal islands and coral reefs of Tunku Abdul Rahman Marine Park, and day two traveling inland through the Crocker Range to Kinabalu Park to witness Mount Kinabalu’s granite peaks and canopy walkways.', 'Multi-day stays allow travelers to sample Borneo''s iconic highlights: pristine marine ecosystems paired with ancient mountain rainforest scenery.'),
  ('bornea-island:rule:3', 'bornea-island', 'Focus on the classic Sabah circuit—visiting Kota Kinabalu’s coastal islands, trekking near Mount Kinabalu, flying to Sandakan to see orangutans and sun bears at Sepilok, and taking a river cruise along the Kinabatangan River to spot proboscis monkeys and pygmy elephants.', 'Combining Borneo’s world-famous primate species, magnificent mountain peaks, and wild river safari ecosystems covers all quintessential first-time Bornean experiences.'),
  ('bornea-island:rule:4', 'bornea-island', 'Split your stay between an exclusive oceanfront resort off Gaya Island or the Damai Peninsula and a luxury eco-lodge deep in the primary rainforest of Danum Valley or along the Kinabatangan River, featuring private yacht charters, romantic beachside dining, and couples spa treatments.', 'Blending pristine rainforest wilderness with the peaceful luxury of secluded oceanfront villas creates the ideal balance between adventure and intimate tropical luxury.'),
  ('bornea-island:rule:5', 'bornea-island', 'Stay at kid-friendly beach resorts and eco-lodges, take gentle wildlife walks at Sepilok Orangutan Rehabilitation Centre and Bornean Sun Bear Conservation Centre, enjoy safe snorkeling trips in Tunku Abdul Rahman Marine Park, and go on guided river safaris along the Kinabatangan River.', 'Exciting wildlife encounters, safe snorkeling waters, and effortless boat safaris keep children entertained while avoiding overly strenuous trekking routes in hot jungle conditions.'),
  ('bornea-island:rule:6', 'bornea-island', 'Arrange chauffeured SUV transfers and private flight connections, stay in high-end villas at Gaya Island Resort or Borneo Rainforest Lodge in Danum Valley, charter private yachts for island hopping, and secure accredited lead naturalists for wildlife treks.', 'Dedicated private transport and helicopter/charter flights eliminate long overland transit friction, while elite rainforest lodges and private naturalists ensure maximum comfort in wild environments.'),
  ('bornea-island:rule:7', 'bornea-island', 'Stay in cozy heritage guesthouses in Kota Kinabalu or Kuching, travel via shared local buses or express boats, explore national parks like Bako or Kinabalu Park independently, and dine at local kopitiams and night markets where delicious meals cost under MYR 10–20 ($2–$4 USD).', 'Borneo is an incredible budget destination where world-class rainforest tracking, stunning marine parks, and rich regional culinary traditions are accessible at minimal cost.'),
  ('bornea-island:rule:8', 'bornea-island', 'Head directly into primary rainforest sanctuaries like Danum Valley, Maliau Basin, or Gunung Mulu National Park for multi-day wildlife tracking and cave exploration, followed by wildlife boat safaris along the Kinabatangan River.', 'Borneo houses some of the planet''s oldest primary rainforests, mega-biodiverse river ecosystems, and earth''s most massive karst cave networks.'),
  ('bornea-island:rule:9', 'bornea-island', 'Map out a culinary route across Sabah and Sarawak, sampling fresh butter prawns and Hinava in Kota Kinabalu, world-famous Sarawak Laksa and Kolo Mee in Kuching, authentic Dayak rice wine (Tuak), and night-market seafood spreads along the waterfront.', 'Borneo is celebrated for its unique fusion of indigenous tribal traditions, Chinese heritage, and fresh coastal seafood, yielding legendary local dishes found nowhere else.'),
  ('bornea-island:rule:10', 'bornea-island', 'Combine multi-day mountain climbs up Mount Kinabalu, deep jungle treks through Danum Valley, cave exploration and canopy walks in Mulu National Park, and scuba diving off world-renowned sites like Sipadan Island.', 'The island offers rugged, biodiversity-rich terrain ideal for high-adrenaline mountain ascents, deep wilderness expeditions, and top-tier ocean diving.'),
  ('bornea-island:rule:11', 'bornea-island', 'Utilize private chauffeured vehicles for transfers, opt for flat boardwalk trails at Sepilok and botanical garden walks in Kinabalu Park, take relaxing river cruise safaris on the Kinabatangan River, and stay at full-service resorts with ground-floor access and elevator amenities.', 'Comfortable private transportation and smooth river safaris eliminate strenuous jungle hiking while preserving full access to Borneo’s remarkable wildlife and scenery.'),
  ('bornea-island:rule:12', 'bornea-island', 'Store luggage at Kota Kinabalu International Airport (BKI), take a private taxi or ride-share directly into central KK, spend 2 to 3 hours visiting the Kota Kinabalu City Mosque and Signal Hill Observatory, and enjoy local seafood or white coffee before returning for your flight.', 'Kota Kinabalu Airport is located just 15 minutes from the city center, making short layover excursions simple, flexible, and stress-free.'),
  ('bornea-island:rule:13', 'bornea-island', 'Divide your stay between 2 nights in Kota Kinabalu (for marine park snorkeling and Kinabalu Park highland visits) and 2 to 3 nights in Sandakan or along the Kinabatangan River for rainforest wildlife tracking and river safaris.', 'A dual-base strategy pairs Borneo''s premier coastal marine life and mountain ecosystems with its world-renowned jungle wildlife sanctuaries. ---'),
  ('angkor-wat:rule:0', 'angkor-wat', 'Choose a focused short loop in Siem Reap, taking a private tuk-tuk to Angkor Wat for a 2-hour guided walkthrough of the central enclosure and main bas-relief galleries, followed by a quick iced Khmer coffee at a nearby shade pavilion before returning to the airport or hotel.', 'Half-day layovers or ultra-short visits require absolute efficiency; focusing strictly on Angkor Wat''s central core delivers the destination''s primary iconic landmark without risking delayed departures.'),
  ('angkor-wat:rule:1', 'angkor-wat', 'Purchase a 1-Day Angkor Pass and execute a targeted Small Circuit loop—starting with a 5:30 AM sunrise at Angkor Wat, heading to the faces of Bayon in Angkor Thom by mid-morning, visiting tree-strangled Ta Prohm before noon, and enjoying a traditional Khmer lunch in Siem Reap before evening departure.', 'A single full day maximizes time by hitting the "Big Three" temples (Angkor Wat, Bayon, Ta Prohm) during optimal daylight hours while keeping transit times short around the central park core.'),
  ('angkor-wat:rule:2', 'angkor-wat', 'Base your journey in Siem Reap—spending Day 1 on the core temples (Angkor Wat, Bayon, Ta Prohm, and Banteay Kdei) with a midday pool siesta, and Day 2 venturing out to the intricate pink sandstone carvings of Banteay Srei, the jungle ruins of Beng Mealea, and a sunset boat cruise along Tonle Sap Lake.', 'Multi-day stays prevent severe "temple fatigue," allowing travelers to combine the primary monument core with outer jungle sites and authentic floating village ecology on the lake.'),
  ('angkor-wat:rule:3', 'angkor-wat', 'Follow the classic 3-Day Angkor Circuit—covering the sunrise at Angkor Wat and inner Angkor Thom on Day 1, outer circuit sites like Preah Khan, Neak Pean, and Banteay Srei on Day 2, and a scenic rural day trip to Phnom Kulen waterfall and Beng Mealea on Day 3, paired with evening Pub Street food walks and Phare Circus shows.', 'Distributing visits across three days guarantees first-timers see all primary architectural styles, stunning jungle-invaded ruins, and vibrant Siem Reap cultural performances without physical burnout.'),
  ('angkor-wat:rule:4', 'angkor-wat', 'Stay at a luxury boutique villa resort in Siem Reap (e.g., Amansara or Phum Baitang), book private early-dawn temple tours before public gates open, enjoy a private sunset champagne boat charter on the Angkor Thom moat, and schedule couples'' traditional Khmer spa treatments alongside private candlelit temple precinct dinners.', 'Combining secluded heritage luxury with private, crowd-free access and romantic moat cruises creates an unforgettably intimate Cambodian getaway.'),
  ('angkor-wat:rule:5', 'angkor-wat', 'Base at a resort with a large swimming pool, take open-air tuk-tuks between temples, focus visits on interactive "explorer" temples like Ta Prohm and Beng Mealea where kids can see giant tree roots, take a pottery-making class at the Khmer Ceramics Centre, and attend an energetic Phare Cambodian Circus show.', 'Open tuk-tuk rides, dramatic "Tomb Raider" jungle ruins, hands-on craft workshops, and high-flying acrobatics keep children thrilled without overburdening them with heavy historical lectures.'),
  ('angkor-wat:rule:6', 'angkor-wat', 'Reserve private suites at premier Siem Reap luxury heritage properties, travel via private air-conditioned SUV with a dedicated driver and lead senior historian guide, secure VIP sunrise entry permits, charter private helicopters for aerial views over Angkor Wat and remote jungle temples, and dine at fine-dining Khmer gastronomy venues.', 'Door-to-door private transport and expert-led storytelling eliminate heat and crowd friction, while helicopter flights reveal the true colossal scale of the ancient Khmer empire.'),
  ('angkor-wat:rule:7', 'angkor-wat', 'Stay in charming boutique guesthouses in Siem Reap''s Wat Bo district, hire a reliable private tuk-tuk driver for $25–$35/day, buy a 3-Day Angkor Pass ($62 USD), explore central temples independently, and dine at local street stalls or night markets where delicious dishes like Lort Cha and Amok cost $2–$5 USD.', 'Siem Reap offers world-class tourist infrastructure with exceptionally affordable tuk-tuk transport, guesthouses, and street food, making ancient UNESCO sites highly accessible on modest budgets.'),
  ('angkor-wat:rule:8', 'angkor-wat', 'Combine morning visits to jungle-enveloped temples like Ta Prohm and Ta Som with an afternoon expedition to Phnom Kulen National Park to swim in tropical waterfalls, visit the River of a Thousand Lingas, and embark on a private birdwatching excursion at the Prek Toal Core Bird Reserve on Tonle Sap Lake.', 'Beyond stone monuments, the Angkor region features lush tropical national parks, sacred highland waterfalls, and Southeast Asia''s most significant freshwater bird sanctuary.'),
  ('angkor-wat:rule:9', 'angkor-wat', 'Map out an authentic Cambodian culinary route—sampling street-side Nom Banh Chok (Khmer noodles) for breakfast, taking a hands-on rural cooking class in a stilt house village, tasting mild Fish Amok cooked in banana leaves, and indulging in modern elevated Khmer tasting menus paired with craft cocktails in Siem Reap''s French Quarter.', 'Khmer cuisine offers a subtle, aromatic food tradition balancing lemongrass, galangal, kaffir lime, and coconut milk, distinct from neighboring Thai or Vietnamese flavor profiles.'),
  ('angkor-wat:rule:10', 'angkor-wat', 'Take a sunrise quad bike (ATV) tour through rural red-dirt villages, ride the Flight of the Gibbon zipline through the Angkor rainforest canopy, trek through the dense overgrown jungle around Beng Mealea and Koh Ker, and kayak through the flooded mangrove forests of Tonle Sap Lake.', 'Siem Reap offers exhilarating outdoor action ranging from forest canopy ziplining and dirt-track quad biking to backcountry trekking around unrestored remote ruins.'),
  ('angkor-wat:rule:11', 'angkor-wat', 'Utilize air-conditioned private cars instead of tuk-tuks to manage humidity, select flat-terrain temples like Angkor Wat (ground level), Bayon, and Banteay Srei while skipping steep pyramid climbs like Ta Keo or Phnom Bakheng, enforce strict midday hotel pool rests (11:30 AM – 2:30 PM), and rent electric golf carts at larger sites where available.', 'Tailoring temple selections to flat terrain and incorporating air-conditioned transport and midday breaks allows seniors to experience world-class architecture without physical exhaustion or heat illness.'),
  ('angkor-wat:rule:12', 'angkor-wat', 'Take a direct pre-arranged taxi from Siem Reap-Angkor International Airport (SAI) to the Angkor Ticket Center, hire a tuk-tuk for a 3-hour highlight loop covering Angkor Wat and Bayon, enjoy a quick lunch at a riverfront cafe in town, and return to SAI Airport for your onward connection.', 'Having a dedicated driver ready ensures seamless timing between airport arrivals and departures, allowing layover travelers to view UNESCO landmarks safely within time limits.'),
  ('angkor-wat:rule:13', 'angkor-wat', 'Dedicate 2 days to the central and outer Angkor Archaeological Park monuments (Angkor Wat, Bayon, Ta Prohm, Banteay Srei, and Beng Mealea) with built-in midday siestas, and devote Day 3 to a full-day countryside excursion to the sacred mountain waterfalls of Phnom Kulen and a sunset boat cruise at Kampong Phluk floating village.', 'A 3-plus day timeframe balances stone temple immersion with natural landscapes and living Khmer cultural traditions across the broader Siem Reap province. ---'),
  ('phnom-penh:rule:0', 'phnom-penh', 'Choose a focused city center loop in central Phnom Penh, visiting Wat Phnom, taking exterior photos of the Royal Palace, and enjoying a traditional cup of Cambodian iced coffee alongside mild Lort Cha (stir-fried pin noodles) or Kuy Teav at a riverside establishment along Sisowath Quay before departing.', 'Half-day layovers require maximum transit efficiency near the airport; focusing on the central riverfront district provides iconic landmarks and traditional Khmer food without risking delayed connections.'),
  ('phnom-penh:rule:1', 'phnom-penh', 'Spend the morning exploring the Royal Palace and Silver Pagoda followed by the National Museum of Cambodia, take a midday break along Sisowath Quay, and spend the afternoon visiting Wat Phnom and Central Market (Phsar Thmei), concluding with a sunset river cruise on the Mekong.', 'A single full day allows travelers to efficiently experience Phnom Penh''s premier royal architecture, ancient Khmer art, vibrant markets, and scenic riverways in a compact geographic zone.'),
  ('phnom-penh:rule:2', 'phnom-penh', 'Spend day one focusing on Cambodia''s royal history and riverside culture at the Royal Palace, National Museum, Wat Phnom, and Sisowath Quay; spend day two exploring sobering recent history at Tuol Sleng Genocide Museum (S-21) and Choeung Ek (Killing Fields), followed by souvenir shopping at the Russian Market (Phsar Tuol Tom Poung).', 'Multi-day stays allow travelers to balance Phnom Penh''s majestic royal heritage with a meaningful understanding of 20th-century history and vibrant modern market life.'),
  ('phnom-penh:rule:3', 'phnom-penh', 'Focus on the core capital highlights—visiting the Royal Palace and Silver Pagoda, National Museum, Tuol Sleng Genocide Museum (S-21), Choeung Ek Killing Fields, Central Market, and taking a sunset cruise along the confluence of the Tonle Sap and Mekong rivers.', 'Combining Phnom Penh''s iconic royal complexes, World War II/Khmer Rouge historical sites, architectural markets, and river vistas delivers a comprehensive first-time overview of the nation''s capital.'),
  ('phnom-penh:rule:4', 'phnom-penh', 'Book an executive river-view suite at a 5-star heritage property like Raffles Hotel Le Royal or Rosewood Phnom Penh, featuring private sunset wooden boat charters along the Mekong, couples spa treatments using traditional Khmer botanicals, and romantic multi-course fine dining overlooking the city skyline.', 'Pairing classic French colonial heritage luxury with scenic sunset river cruises and refined Khmer gastronomy creates a deeply romantic and sophisticated urban escape.'),
  ('phnom-penh:rule:5', 'phnom-penh', 'Stay at kid-friendly hotels with large swimming pools near Sisowath Quay, take fun open-air tuk-tuk rides between Wat Phnom and the Royal Palace, embark on a Mekong River sunset boat tour, take a day trip to the silk farms on Koh Dach (Silk Island), and visit the Phnom Tamao Wildlife Rescue Centre.', 'Open-air tuk-tuk rides, interactive animal rescue sanctuaries, riverboat trips, and hands-on silk-weaving demonstrations keep children engaged while avoiding overly rigid schedules.'),
  ('phnom-penh:rule:6', 'phnom-penh', 'Book premier suites at 5-star luxury hotels, reserve private historian-guided tours of the National Museum and Royal Palace, hire VIP chauffeured SUVs for transfers, charter private speedboats or wooden yachts for Mekong excursions, and enjoy fine-dining French-Khmer tasting menus.', 'Private door-to-door luxury transport, expert local historians, and exclusive river charters eliminate urban friction while delivering world-class service in historic settings.'),
  ('phnom-penh:rule:7', 'phnom-penh', 'Stay in boutique guesthouses around the Riverside or BKK1 districts, travel using local PassApp tuk-tuks, explore street markets and Wat Phnom independently, and dine at local Phsar eateries and street stalls where delicious meals cost under $2.00–$4.00 USD.', 'Phnom Penh offers highly affordable tuk-tuk transport, low-cost entry fees, and vibrant street-food hubs, making rich cultural and historical sightseeing accessible on a modest budget.'),
  ('phnom-penh:rule:8', 'phnom-penh', 'Take day excursions out of the concrete city to the lush rural orchards and silk-weaving villages of Koh Dach (Silk Island), explore the wildlife rehabilitation enclosures at Phnom Tamao Wildlife Rescue Centre, and take eco-cruises along the Mekong and Tonle Sap rivers.', 'The immediate countryside surrounding Phnom Penh features peaceful river islands, protected tropical forests, and rescued native wildlife sanctuaries.'),
  ('phnom-penh:rule:9', 'phnom-penh', 'Map out an authentic culinary exploration of the capital, sampling traditional Nom Banh Chok (Khmer noodles), rich Fish Amok, mild Lort Cha, grilled pork and rice (Bai Sach Chrouk), fresh seafood at local night markets, and elevated French-Khmer fusion at upscale bistros.', 'Phnom Penh features a dynamic food landscape, seamlessly blending ancient Khmer royal culinary heritage, vibrant street-stall cultures, and French colonial culinary influences.'),
  ('phnom-penh:rule:10', 'phnom-penh', 'Combine off-road quad biking or cycling tours through rural villages on Silk Island (Koh Dach), boat expeditions along the Mekong River, self-guided exploration of ancient hilltop stupas at Udong, and evening street-food tuk-tuk rallies through busy night markets.', 'Capital-adjacent regions offer exciting active outdoor pursuits, ranging from rural dirt-track cycling to off-the-beaten-path ancient capital hill climbs.'),
  ('phnom-penh:rule:11', 'phnom-penh', 'Stay at full-service luxury heritage hotels with elevators, utilize comfortable private air-conditioned cars for site transfers, explore the flat garden grounds of the Royal Palace and National Museum at a relaxed pace, and enjoy calm sunset river cruises along Sisowath Quay.', 'Accessible city-center attractions, flat walking surfaces in major museums, private air-conditioned vehicles, and gentle riverboat cruises allow senior travelers to experience the capital comfortably without physical strain.'),
  ('phnom-penh:rule:12', 'phnom-penh', 'Take an airport taxi or private car into central Phnom Penh, spend 2 to 3 hours touring Wat Phnom and browsing the central dome of Central Market (Phsar Thmei), enjoy a relaxed meal or coffee along Sisowath Quay, and return directly to Phnom Penh International Airport (PNH).', 'Direct road access between the city center and the airport allows layover travelers to comfortably take in iconic monuments, shopping, and riverside dining within a short timeframe.'),
  ('phnom-penh:rule:13', 'phnom-penh', 'Divide your stay between 2 days exploring Phnom Penh''s royal, historical, and market highlights, paired with a full-day excursion to the ancient royal capital of Udong and the wildlife enclosures at Phnom Tamao Wildlife Rescue Centre.', 'A three-day itinerary bridges Phnom Penh''s essential urban cultural sites with countryside heritage and wildlife conservation hubs. ---'),
  ('el-nido:rule:0', 'el-nido', 'Choose a focused coastal loop in El Nido Town Proper (Poblacion), taking exterior photos of the dramatic limestone backdrop of Taraw Cliff, grabbing a fresh mango smoothie along Calle Hama, doing a brief walk to Seven Commandos Beach or Corong-Corong Beach, and enjoying a beachfront seafood lunch before departing toward Lio Airport or Puerto Princesa.', 'Half-day layovers require maximum transit efficiency near town; focusing on the compact Poblacion strip delivers vibrant beach views, fresh island cuisine, and iconic karst landscapes without risking missed boat or flight transfers.'),
  ('el-nido:rule:1', 'el-nido', 'Spend the morning kayak-exploring Big Lagoon and Secret Lagoon via Tour A, take a beachside buffet lunch break at Shimizu Island, return to shore by mid-afternoon to take a tricycle south to Las Cabañas Beach, and spend the evening watching the sunset with cocktails at a beachfront lounge.', 'A single full day allows travelers to efficiently experience Bacuit Bay''s signature limestone lagoons, turquoise marine waters, and world-class Palawan sunsets in one seamless sequence.'),
  ('el-nido:rule:2', 'el-nido', 'Spend day one focusing on Bacuit Bay''s essential lagoon hopping via Tour A (Big Lagoon, Secret Lagoon, 7 Commandos Beach) followed by a sunset at Las Cabañas Beach; spend day two discovering outer island hidden beaches via Tour C (Secret Beach, Hidden Beach, Matinloc Shrine) before returning to town for dinner along Calle Hama.', 'Multi-day stays allow travelers to balance El Nido''s main lagoon highlights with outer-island marine sanctuaries, hidden cove swimming, and vibrant coastal dining.'),
  ('el-nido:rule:3', 'el-nido', 'Focus on the core island highlights—taking Tour A to paddle through Big Lagoon, embarking on Tour C for Hidden Beach, spending a relaxing land-based afternoon at Nacpan Beach, catching the sunset at Las Cabañas Beach, and enjoying evening seafood dining in El Nido Town Proper.', 'Combining Bacuit Bay''s world-famous lagoon waterways, outer hidden coves, expansive coconut-lined beaches, and bustling town center nightlife delivers a comprehensive first-time overview of northern Palawan.'),
  ('el-nido:rule:4', 'el-nido', 'Book a private villa at an exclusive luxury island resort like El Nido Resorts Pangulasian Island or Lagen Island, featuring private outrigger boat charters, candlelit beach picnics, couples'' hilot massages in open-air cabanas, and champagne sunset sails across Bacuit Bay.', 'Pairing remote tropical island luxury with dramatic limestone backdrops, private beaches, and elevated sea-to-table dining creates an unforgettable, intimate island romantic getaway.'),
  ('el-nido:rule:5', 'el-nido', 'Stay at family-friendly beach resorts near Lio Beach or Corong-Corong, charter private outrigger boats for island hopping to customize swimming stops and rest periods, explore gentle shallow waters at Nacpan Beach, and take a safe, guided walk along the paved boardwalks of Lio Estate.', 'Flat beach access, shallow swimmable waters, customizable private boat schedules, and family-oriented resort spaces keep children safe and engaged while avoiding travel fatigue.'),
  ('el-nido:rule:6', 'el-nido', 'Book premier overwater bungalows or luxury beachfront villas at 5-star private island eco-resorts, charter private speedboats or yachts for island hopping, arrange private helicopter transfers from Manila or direct flights into Lio Airport (ENI), and enjoy private chef beach barbecues on secluded coves.', 'Private aerial transport, exclusive boat charters, and dedicated island host services eliminate transit friction while delivering world-class privacy in dynamic marine settings.'),
  ('el-nido:rule:7', 'el-nido', 'Stay in social hostels or guesthouses around Poblacion or Corong-Corong, join standard shared group tours (Tour A or Tour C), ride local tricycles or rent a scooter for land transit, visit swimmable public stretches like Nacpan Beach and Las Cabañas, and dine at affordable local carinderias and public market food stalls.', 'El Nido offers easily accessible shared island-hopping tours, low-cost street stalls, cheap public beaches, and budget hostel networks, making iconic island hopping accessible on a modest budget.'),
  ('el-nido:rule:8', 'el-nido', 'Explore the marine biodiversity of Bacuit Bay by snorkeling around Shimizu Island, trek to the prehistoric archaeological site of Ille Cave, take a guided excursion to the quiet mangroves and eco-sanctuaries of Sibaltan, and hike the Via Ferrata Canopy Walk up Taraw Cliff.', 'Northern Palawan features exceptional marine life, untouched mangrove ecosystems, ancient limestone cave formations, and panoramic coastal ridges.'),
  ('el-nido:rule:9', 'el-nido', 'Map out a dynamic coastal culinary exploration, sampling fresh ocean Kinilaw and traditional island-hopping boat buffets, enjoying wood-fired pizzas on Serena Street, trying authentic Filipino dishes at local carinderias, and indulging in seaside tapas and craft cocktails along Corong-Corong Beach.', 'El Nido boasts a vibrant ocean-to-table dining scene, seamlessly blending traditional Filipino flavors, fresh charcoal-grilled seafood, international expat bistros, and chic beachfront sunset lounges.'),
  ('el-nido:rule:10', 'el-nido', 'Combine sea kayaking through narrow rock openings at Small Lagoon, scuba diving through the deep underwater cavern at Dilumacad Tunnel, riding the inter-island zipline at Las Cabañas, motorbiking north to surf waves at Duli Beach, and climbing the sharp limestone faces of Taraw Cliff.', 'El Nido and its surrounding marine archipelago offer world-class ocean sports, underwater cave diving, surf breaks, and high-altitude ridge climbing.'),
  ('el-nido:rule:11', 'el-nido', 'Stay at accessible, full-service beachfront resorts in Lio Beach or Corong-Corong, hire private outrigger boats with easy-boarding ladders and dedicated crew assistance, enjoy flat seaside strolls, and spend relaxing afternoons sipping fresh juices at calm beachfront cafes.', 'Flat beach resorts, dedicated private boat crews, step-free dining strips like Lio Beach, and gentle coastal pacing allow senior travelers to experience Palawan comfortably without physical strain.'),
  ('el-nido:rule:12', 'el-nido', 'Take a short 15-minute tricycle ride from Lio Airport (ENI) to Lio Beach, spend 2 to 3 hours swimming along the wide sandy shore, enjoy a relaxed lunch at an eco-boutique beachfront cafe, browse local handicraft shops, and return directly to the airport.', 'Rapid proximity connecting Lio Airport directly to Lio Beach allows layover travelers to comfortably take in tropical scenery, ocean swimming, and dining within a short timeframe.'),
  ('el-nido:rule:13', 'el-nido', 'Divide your stay between 2 days of Bacuit Bay island hopping (Tour A and Tour C), paired with a full land-based exploration day north to Nacpan Beach, Duli Beach, and the Taraw Cliff Canopy Walk.', 'A three-day itinerary bridges El Nido''s world-famous marine lagoons and outer reefs with surrounding northern beach coastlines, surfing coves, and aerial viewpoints. ---'),
  ('boracay:rule:0', 'boracay', 'Choose a focused walking loop along White Beach Station 2, taking photos at Willy''s Rock in Station 1, grabbing a fresh mango shake along the beachfront path, browsing through D''Mall Boracay, and enjoying a seaside lunch before heading to the jetty port or Caticlan Airport.', 'Half-day layovers require high transit efficiency; concentrating on central White Beach provides iconic island views, fresh tropical drinks, and easy souvenir shopping without risking missed boat or flight departures.'),
  ('boracay:rule:1', 'boracay', 'Spend the morning on an outrigger boat tour snorkeling around Crocodile Island and visiting Puka Shell Beach, return to White Beach Station 2 for lunch at D''Mall, spend the afternoon swimming in the calm Station 1 waters, and end the day with a paraw sailboat sunset ride and cocktails on the beach.', 'A single day allows travelers to efficiently experience Boracay''s pristine outer reefs, iconic powdery white sands, and world-famous sailboat sunsets in one seamless flow.'),
  ('boracay:rule:2', 'boracay', 'Spend day one exploring White Beach (Stations 1 to 3), visiting Willy''s Rock, trying water activities like helmet diving or paddleboarding, and taking a sunset paraw sail; spend day two visiting northern beaches like Puka Shell Beach and Diniwid Beach, going up Mount Luho Viewpoint, and enjoying seafood dining at D''Talipapa Market.', 'Multi-day stays allow travelers to balance White Beach''s central lifestyle and water sports with the island''s quieter northern coves, panoramic viewpoints, and local culinary markets.'),
  ('boracay:rule:3', 'boracay', 'Focus on core island highlights—strolling the powdery sand of White Beach Station 1, taking photos at Willy''s Rock, shopping and dining in D''Mall, taking an island-hopping boat tour to Puka Shell Beach and Magic Island, watching the sunset via a local paraw sailboat, and dining along the Station 2 beach promenade.', 'Combining the island''s signature white sand beaches, central retail arcades, offshore reef snorkeling, and iconic sailboat sunsets provides a comprehensive introduction to Boracay.'),
  ('boracay:rule:4', 'boracay', 'Book a private villa at an exclusive cliffside or northern luxury resort like Shangri-La Boracay or Crimson Resort, schedule private sunset paraw cruises, book couples'' hilot massage treatments at an oceanfront spa, and arrange private candlelit dinners on the quiet sands of Puka Beach or Diniwid Beach.', 'Combining secluded luxury resorts, quiet northern coves, private sea excursions, and fine oceanfront dining creates an intimate and romantic island escape.'),
  ('boracay:rule:5', 'boracay', 'Stay at beachfront resorts with direct access in Station 1 or Station 3, enjoy gentle shallow swimming in front of Station 1, take a glass-bottom boat tour or banana boat ride, visit Puka Shell Beach for shell hunting, and dine at family-friendly restaurants around D''Mall.', 'Step-free beach access, shallow swimmable waters, fun group water activities, and pedestrian-friendly dining zones keep children safe and entertained while minimizing travel stress.'),
  ('boracay:rule:6', 'boracay', 'Book high-end ocean-view suites or private pool villas at 5-star resorts in Station 1 or Boracay Newcoast, arrange private speedboat transfers directly from Caticlan Jetty Port, charter private yachts for sunset sailing, and indulge in beachfront fine dining and private spa treatments.', 'Private water transit, exclusive cliffside accommodations, custom yacht charters, and personalized resort services eliminate travel friction while ensuring top-tier privacy and comfort.'),
  ('boracay:rule:7', 'boracay', 'Stay in social hostels or budget guesthouses around Station 3 or Bulabog Beach, join shared group island-hopping boat tours, walk along the beachfront promenade, swim at public access beaches, and eat at local carinderias or budget-friendly stalls near D''Talipapa.', 'Boracay offers accessible shared boat tours, affordable guesthouses near Station 3, cheap street eats, and free public beach access, making the island enjoyable on a modest budget.'),
  ('boracay:rule:8', 'boracay', 'Explore the marine life by snorkeling at Crocodile Island and Coral Garden, take a peaceful walk along the coarse, shell-filled shores of Puka Shell Beach, visit the tranquil mangroves at Lugutan Mangrove Park, and take in 360-degree island views from Mount Luho.', 'Beyond White Beach''s commercial core, Boracay features marine sanctuaries, protected mangrove ecosystems, natural shell beaches, and elevated forest viewpoints.'),
  ('boracay:rule:9', 'boracay', 'Map out a dynamic island food tour, sampling fresh grilled seafood at D''Talipapa Market, enjoying calamansi muffins at local bakery staples, trying beachfront mango soft-serve shakes, dining at international expat bistros in D''Mall, and enjoying seafood tapas with craft cocktails during sunset happy hours in Station 1.', 'Boracay offers an impressive culinary mix, ranging from local Filipino seafood markets and beach snacks to upscale international restaurants and trendy sunset bars.'),
  ('boracay:rule:10', 'boracay', 'Go kitesurfing or windsurfing on the high-wind shores of Bulabog Beach, jump into the ocean at Magic Island cliff jumping spot, try scuba diving or helmet diving off Station 2, ride ATVs or mainland zorb courses, and try parasailing over the island''s turquoise waters.', 'Boracay is a major center for water sports, offering world-class wind sports, high-flying parasailing, cliff jumping, and scuba diving opportunities.'),
  ('boracay:rule:11', 'boracay', 'Stay at flat, accessible beachfront resorts in Station 1, utilize electric tricycles (e-trikes) for island transit, take gentle sunset paraw sailboat rides, enjoy flat walks along the paved paths of D''Mall, and relax at quiet beachfront cafes overlooking calm waters.', 'Step-free beach access in Station 1, smooth e-trike transport, flat pedestrian walkways, and gentle boat options allow senior travelers to experience the island comfortably and safely.'),
  ('boracay:rule:12', 'boracay', 'Take a quick 10-minute boat ride from Caticlan Jetty Port to Tambisaan Beach or Station 3, spend 2 to 3 hours relaxing on the beach, grab a quick seafood lunch along the promenade, buy local souvenirs at D''Mall, and return directly to the port.', 'Close proximity to Caticlan''s entry ports allows layover travelers to enjoy beach views, ocean swimming, and quick shopping within a tight schedule.'),
  ('boracay:rule:13', 'boracay', 'Divide your stay between 1 day of White Beach activities and sunset sailing, 1 day of offshore island hopping (Crocodile Island, Puka Beach, Magic Island), and 1 day exploring northern beaches (Diniwid, Ilig-Iligan), wind sports at Bulabog Beach, and mountain views from Mount Luho.', 'A three-day itinerary balances Boracay''s world-famous main beach lifestyle with outer reef boat tours, quiet northern coves, high-wind sports, and panoramic inland viewpoints. ---'),
  ('cebu:rule:0', 'cebu', 'Choose a focused historic walking loop in Cebu City''s Parian and Plaza Sugbo district, taking photos at Magellan''s Cross, stepping inside the ancient Basilica Minore del Santo Niño, taking a brief walk to Fort San Pedro, and enjoying a plate of authentic Cebuano lechon at a nearby restaurant before departing toward Mactan-Cebu International Airport.', 'Half-day layovers require maximum transit efficiency near the city center; focusing on the compact historic core delivers centuries of Filipino heritage, iconic religious landmarks, and celebrated local cuisine without risking missed flight connections.'),
  ('cebu:rule:1', 'cebu', 'Take an early-morning transfer southwest to Moalboal to snorkel alongside the world-famous Sardine Run and sea turtles off Panagsama Beach, head to Badian for a full afternoon of adrenaline-fueled river canyoneering through Kawasan Falls, and return to Metro Cebu in the evening for street food at Sugbo Mercado in IT Park.', 'A single full day allows energetic travelers to experience Cebu''s most famous natural water adventures—massive sardine bait balls and turquoise river canyoneering—in one action-packed loop.'),
  ('cebu:rule:2', 'cebu', 'Spend day one exploring the natural marine wall at Moalboal (Sardine Run) and river canyoneering at Kawasan Falls, followed by a scenic evening drive; spend day two discovering Cebu''s urban highlights (Magellan''s Cross, Basilica del Santo Niño) before ascending into the cool Busay Hills for Temple of Leah, Sirao Flower Garden, and sunset skyline views at Tops Lookout.', 'Multi-day stays allow travelers to balance Cebu''s world-class marine and river adventures in the south with its rich cultural heritage and scenic mountain highland views overlooking the city.'),
  ('cebu:rule:3', 'cebu', 'Focus on the ultimate island highlights—swimming with the Moalboal Sardine Run, canyoneering down Kawasan Falls, touring historic landmarks (Magellan''s Cross, Basilica Minore del Santo Niño), exploring the mountain sights of Busay (Temple of Leah, Sirao Garden), and dining on authentic Cebu lechon.', 'Combining Cebu''s iconic marine ecosystems, thrill-seeker river canyons, colonial Spanish heritage, and mountain panoramic viewpoints delivers a complete first-time overview of the province.'),
  ('cebu:rule:4', 'cebu', 'Book a private oceanfront villa at a luxury resort on Mactan Island or Bantayan Island, arrange private sunset yacht charters across the Mactan Channel, indulge in couples'' spa treatments in open-air garden pavilions, and enjoy romantic mountain-top dinners at La Vie in the Sky in Busay.', 'Pairing coastal beach resort luxury with private island charters, elevated mountain skyline dining, and secluded tropical sandbars creates an unforgettable romantic getaway.'),
  ('cebu:rule:5', 'cebu', 'Stay at family-friendly beach resorts along Mactan Island with private lagoons and kids'' clubs, take accessible day trips to Sirao Flower Garden and Temple of Leah in Busay, enjoy gentle boat rides and shallow snorkeling at Hilutungan Marine Sanctuary, and dine at family-friendly food halls like Sugbo Mercado.', 'Gentle beach access, resort amenities, child-friendly mountain gardens, and easily accessible marine sanctuaries keep children safe and entertained without physical strain.'),
  ('cebu:rule:6', 'cebu', 'Book 5-star oceanfront suites at top-tier Mactan resorts like Shangri-La Mactan or Jpark Island Resort, charter private speedboats or luxury yachts for island hopping around the Olango Reef Flat, arrange helicopter transfers to island resorts, and enjoy private chef dining overlooking the Visayan Sea.', 'Exclusive resort amenities, private maritime transport, and dedicated concierge services eliminate travel friction while delivering high-end comfort across island and marine settings.'),
  ('cebu:rule:7', 'cebu', 'Stay in central hostels or budget guesthouses around Cebu IT Park or Moalboal (Panagsama Beach), take local Ceres buses or shared vans across the island, join shared group tours for Kawasan Canyoneering, visit swimmable public stretches like Kota Beach in Bantayan, and dine at local carinderias and night markets.', 'Cebu offers an extensive network of affordable public buses, cheap street-food markets, budget guesthouses, and accessible shore-entry snorkeling spots suitable for modest budgets.'),
  ('cebu:rule:8', 'cebu', 'Explore the marine biodiversity at Moalboal Reef Wall and Hilutungan Marine Sanctuary, hike the dramatic jagged limestone peaks of Osmeña Peak in Dalaguete, explore subterranean waters in Ogtong Cave, and stroll through the Obo-ob Mangrove Eco-Park on Bantayan Island.', 'Cebu features diverse natural eco-systems ranging from high-altitude karst mountain peaks and underground caves to dense mangrove forests and thriving coral reef walls.'),
  ('cebu:rule:9', 'cebu', 'Map out an iconic Cebuano culinary trail, sampling world-famous roasted Cebu Lechon (at Rico''s or House of Lechon), fresh seafood Kinilaw, sweet Carcar chicharon, herbal Pochero stew, and local street stalls at Sugbo Mercado in IT Park.', 'Cebu is celebrated as the culinary capital of the Visayas, famous for producing the Philippines'' best roasted pig, fresh seafood ceviche, and a bustling 24/7 street food culture.'),
  ('cebu:rule:10', 'cebu', 'Combine high-intensity river canyoneering through the limestone canyons of Kawasan Falls, scuba diving with thresher sharks off Malapascua Island, freediving alongside the Moalboal Sardine Run, and trekking across the rugged ridgelines of Osmeña Peak and Casino Peak.', 'Cebu is a premier adventure hub, offering world-class shark diving, extreme river jumping, freediving, and high-ridge mountain trekking.'),
  ('cebu:rule:11', 'cebu', 'Stay at accessible, full-service beachfront resorts in Mactan Island, take private air-conditioned vehicle tours to historic city landmarks (Magellan''s Cross, Basilica del Santo Niño) and Busay mountain viewdecks, and enjoy flat seaside strolls along Kota Beach on Bantayan Island.', 'Step-free heritage sights, private vehicle transit, accessible beachfront resorts, and gentle mountain gardens allow senior travelers to experience Cebu comfortably without strenuous hiking.'),
  ('cebu:rule:12', 'cebu', 'Take a 10-to-15 minute taxi from Mactan-Cebu International Airport (CEB) to Mactan Marina Mall or Mactan Newtown, enjoy a relaxed meal of fresh seafood or Cebuano lechon, grab a coffee at an open-air plaza, and return directly to the terminal.', 'Proximity between Mactan-Cebu International Airport and adjacent Mactan commercial hubs allows layover travelers to sample local cuisine and tropical atmosphere efficiently without city traffic risks.'),
  ('cebu:rule:13', 'cebu', 'Divide your stay between 1 day of historic city sights and Busay mountain escapes, 1 day of south Cebu adventures (Moalboal Sardine Run and Kawasan Falls Canyoneering), and 1-2 days relaxing on the pristine white sandbars of Bantayan Island or Malapascua Island in the north.', 'A multi-day itinerary smoothly bridges Cebu''s urban cultural heritage and mountain outlooks with its high-adrenaline southern river canyons and peaceful northern island beaches. ---'),
  ('bohol:rule:0', 'bohol', 'Choose a focused transit loop from Tagbilaran Port or Bohol-Panglao International Airport (TAG) to Panglao Island, enjoying a relaxed seaside lunch at Alona Beach, taking photos along the powder-white shoreline, sipping fresh coconut water at an open-air beachfront lounge, and returning directly for your departure connection.', 'Half-day layovers demand quick, frictionless transit; Panglao Island''s immediate proximity to the airport (~10 minutes) provides a stress-free taste of Bohol''s coastal charm without risking missed connections.'),
  ('bohol:rule:1', 'bohol', 'Embark on an early-morning Bohol Countryside Tour, taking photos at the iconic Chocolate Hills in Carmen, walking through the lush canopy of the Bilar Man-Made Forest, viewing rescued primates at the Corella Tarsier Sanctuary, taking a scenic buffet lunch cruise down the Loboc River, and stopping at the historic Baclayon Church before heading back.', 'A single full day allows travelers to efficiently cover Bohol''s core geographic highlights—geological wonders, endemic wildlife, river scenery, and Spanish colonial heritage—in one cohesive inland circuit.'),
  ('bohol:rule:2', 'bohol', 'Spend day one discovering the central countryside highlights (Chocolate Hills, Tarsier Sanctuary, and Loboc River Cruise); spend day two taking a early-morning outrigger boat trip to Balicasag Island Marine Sanctuary for dolphin watching and sea turtle snorkeling, followed by a walk across the shifting sandbar of Virgin Island (Pungtud Reef) and an afternoon relaxing on Dumaluan Beach.', 'Multi-day stays allow visitors to seamlessly balance Bohol''s world-famous inland eco-wonders with its thriving marine ecosystems and white-sand beaches.'),
  ('bohol:rule:3', 'bohol', 'Focus on the quintessential Bohol combination—touring the Chocolate Hills, spotting Philippine tarsiers at the Corella Tarsier Sanctuary, taking the Loboc River Cruise, snorkeling with sea turtles at Balicasag Island, strolling across Virgin Island Sandbar, and enjoying sunset drinks along Alona Beach.', 'Combining the island''s iconic geological monuments, rare endemic wildlife, scenic riverways, and premier marine sanctuaries delivers the ultimate first-timer overview of Bohol.'),
  ('bohol:rule:4', 'bohol', 'Book a private oceanfront pool villa at an exclusive cliffside resort on Panglao (such as Amorita Resort or South Palms), arrange a private sunset sailboat charter across the Bohol Sea, indulge in couples'' spa treatments over the ocean, and book a romantic private dinner cruise down the tranquil Loboc River.', 'Pairing secluded luxury resort accommodations with private maritime charters, serene riverways, and tranquil white-sand beaches creates an unhurried, intimate romantic retreat.'),
  ('bohol:rule:5', 'bohol', 'Stay at family-friendly beachfront resorts along Dumaluan Beach with shallow swimming waters, visit the Chocolate Hills Complex via easy paved viewing decks, observe tarsiers at the Corella Sanctuary, take a gentle boat ride down the Loboc River, and go dolphin watching off Balicasag Island.', 'Calm, shallow beach waters, accessible viewing platforms, educational wildlife encounters, and smooth river cruises keep children engaged and safe without physical exhaustion.'),
  ('bohol:rule:6', 'bohol', 'Stay in top-tier suites or private villas at luxury boutique resorts on Panglao Island, charter private speedboats for island-hopping around Balicasag Island with private marine guides, arrange private helicopter tours over the Chocolate Hills, and enjoy fine dining at high-end venues like MIST or Treetops.', 'High-end boutique accommodations, tailored private charters, and exclusive aerial viewpoints eliminate travel friction while providing personalized comfort across Bohol''s natural settings.'),
  ('bohol:rule:7', 'bohol', 'Stay in budget hostels or guesthouses around Tawala/Alona Beach or Tagbilaran City, rent a motor scooter to explore the inland countryside independently, join shared group tours for the Countryside Circuit and Balicasag Island, and dine at local carinderias and casual night markets.', 'Bohol offers affordable scooter rentals, cheap shared outrigger tours, budget hostel networks, and low-cost local eateries that make its major attractions accessible on a modest budget.'),
  ('bohol:rule:8', 'bohol', 'Explore the limestone formations of the Chocolate Hills, walk through the quiet Bilar Man-Made Mahogany Forest, observe primates at the Corella Tarsier Sanctuary, snorkel the coral walls of Balicasag Island Sanctuary, paddleboard through the Loboc-Anding River System, and trek to hidden falls in Anda.', 'Bohol features exceptionally diverse natural ecosystems ranging from ancient coral karst hills and tropical rainforests to riverine jungles and marine biodiversity hotspots.'),
  ('bohol:rule:9', 'bohol', 'Sample local Boholano specialties including Kalamay (sweet sticky rice treat in coconut shells), fresh farm-to-table organic dishes at Bohol Bee Farm, fresh seafood grills along Alona Beach, traditional peanut kisses, and local riverfront buffets serving native Filipino dishes.', 'Bohol offers a distinct regional culinary identity centered on traditional coconut-based sweets, farm-fresh organic produce, and vibrant oceanfront seafood dining.'),
  ('bohol:rule:10', 'bohol', 'Experience ziplining and sky-biking across river canyons at Chocolate Hills Adventure Park (CHAP), stand-up paddleboarding or night firefly kayaking down the Loboc River, scuba diving along the deep drop-offs of Balicasag Reef, and cave-swimming at Cabagnow Cave Pool in Anda.', 'Beyond quiet sightseeing, Bohol provides adrenaline-packed aerial ziplines, river paddle sports, deep-wall scuba diving, and subterranean cave exploration.'),
  ('bohol:rule:11', 'bohol', 'Stay at accessible beachfront resorts on Dumaluan Beach, take private air-conditioned van tours to the Chocolate Hills (utilizing the accessible ramp areas) and Baclayon Church, enjoy a comfortable, seated lunch cruise on the Loboc River, and take gentle strolls through the Corella Tarsier Sanctuary.', 'Smooth private vehicle transportation, step-conscious viewing areas, and relaxing seated river cruises allow senior travelers to experience Bohol''s highlights with ease and comfort.'),
  ('bohol:rule:12', 'bohol', 'Take a 10-minute taxi from Bohol-Panglao International Airport (TAG) to Dumaluan Beach or Alona Beach, enjoy a relaxed beachfront seafood meal, take a quiet stroll along the shore, and return smoothly to the departure terminal.', 'The extreme proximity of Bohol''s international airport to Panglao''s primary beach strips allows layover passengers to enjoy authentic coastal hospitality without transit delays.'),
  ('bohol:rule:13', 'bohol', 'Divide your itinerary into 1 day for the inland Countryside Circuit (Chocolate Hills, Tarsier Sanctuary, Loboc River), 1 day for Panglao & Balicasag Island Hopping (dolphins, sea turtles, Virgin Island sandbar), and 1–2 days heading east to Anda for quiet white-sand beaches, cave pools, and tranquil eco-resort relaxation.', 'A multi-day stay balances Bohol''s essential inland sights and Panglao island-hopping with the serene, uncrowded coastal landscapes of eastern Bohol. ---'),
  ('manila:rule:0', 'manila', 'Choose a focused historic walking loop inside Intramuros, exploring Fort Santiago, walking past San Agustin Church and Manila Cathedral, and enjoying a traditional meal or halo-halo at Barbara''s or Bambike Ecotours before departing back toward Ninoy Aquino International Airport (NAIA).', 'Half-day layovers require maximum transit efficiency near the city center; focusing on the compact historic core delivers centuries of Spanish colonial heritage, iconic religious landmarks, and celebrated local cuisine without risking missed flight connections.'),
  ('manila:rule:1', 'manila', 'Tour the historic sights of Intramuros and the National Museum of Fine Arts in the morning, embark on an authentic Chinatown food crawl down Ongpin Street in Binondo for lunch, and head to Bonifacio Global City (BGC) in the evening for high-street shopping, dinner, and craft cocktails.', 'A single full day allows energetic travelers to experience Metro Manila''s contrast between its rich 16th-century colonial past, vibrant culinary trade history, and sleek, modern modern urban lifestyle.'),
  ('manila:rule:2', 'manila', 'Spend day one exploring historic Intramuros, Rizal Park, the National Museum Complex, and Binondo Chinatown; spend day two taking a scenic day trip south to Tagaytay to view Taal Volcano and Lake before returning to Entertainment City in Manila for dinner and the Okada Manila water fountain show.', 'Multi-day stays allow travelers to balance Metro Manila''s rich urban heritage and culinary districts with scenic highland escapes overlooking active volcanic landscapes.'),
  ('manila:rule:3', 'manila', 'Focus on the quintessential city highlights—exploring Spanish heritage in Intramuros (Fort Santiago, San Agustin Church), viewing Juan Luna''s Spoliarium at the National Museum of Fine Arts, eating street food in Binondo, catching the golden-hour sunset along Manila Bay, and dining in BGC or Makati.', 'Combining Manila''s iconic colonial monuments, national art treasures, culinary trade roots, world-famous bay sunsets, and modern commercial centers delivers a complete first-time overview of the Philippine capital.'),
  ('manila:rule:4', 'manila', 'Book a luxury suite at top-tier heritage or bayfront properties like The Manila Hotel, Okada Manila, or Raffles Makati, indulge in private fine-dining dinners in Poblacion or BGC, arrange private sunset yacht charters across Manila Bay, and take a day trip to Tagaytay for romantic ridge-side dining.', 'Pairing colonial elegance and modern bayfront luxury with private yacht charters, fine-dining gastronomy, and scenic mountain viewports creates a memorable romantic getaway.'),
  ('manila:rule:5', 'manila', 'Visit Manila Ocean Park along the bayfront, explore hands-on interactive exhibits at The Mind Museum in BGC, ride the MOA Eye ferris wheel at SM Mall of Asia, take a child-friendly Bambike (bamboo bicycle) tour through Intramuros, and enjoy the musical fountain show at Okada Manila.', 'Accessible marine exhibits, interactive science centers, safe pedestrianized plazas, and colorful entertainment shows keep children engaged and entertained without physical strain.'),
  ('manila:rule:6', 'manila', 'Book 5-star suites at luxury integrated resorts like Okada Manila, Solaire Resort, or Raffles Makati, shop international designer boutiques at Greenbelt or Shangri-La Plaza, hire private chauffeur transfers, and enjoy multi-course tasting menus at fine-dining establishments in BGC and Makati.', 'World-class integrated resort casinos, private luxury transport, designer shopping precincts, and acclaimed culinary venues provide high-end comfort and seamless service.'),
  ('manila:rule:7', 'manila', 'Stay in central hostels or budget guesthouses around Poblacion (Makati) or Ermita, navigate the city using LRT/MRT lines, Grab, and jeepneys, take self-guided walking tours through Intramuros and Rizal Park, visit free-admission venues like the National Museum Complex, and feast on cheap street food in Binondo.', 'Manila provides an extensive network of affordable street markets, free national museum galleries, budget hostels, and low-cost public transit suitable for price-conscious travelers.'),
  ('manila:rule:8', 'manila', 'Take day trips out of the urban center to trek the crater lake of Mount Pinatubo, view active volcanic islands at Taal Volcano Viewpoint (Tagaytay), shoot rapids at Pagsanjan Falls, or explore the open-air art installations and terraced gardens at Pinto Art Museum in Antipolo.', 'While Metro Manila is an urban metropolis, its surrounding provinces offer rapid access to active volcanoes, roaring waterfalls, lush mountain ridges, and eco-art sanctuaries.'),
  ('manila:rule:9', 'manila', 'Embark on an epic culinary journey—sampling street food and dim sum in Binondo (the world''s oldest Chinatown), tasting traditional Filipino staples like Adobo, Sinigang, and Sizzling Sisig, exploring modern Filipino fusion in BGC, and hopping between craft cocktail bars and hipster bistros in Poblacion, Makati.', 'Manila is the ultimate melting pot of Philippine gastronomy, offering centuries-old Chinese-Filipino street eats alongside cutting-edge culinary fusion and world-class mixology.'),
  ('manila:rule:10', 'manila', 'Head on outdoor day trips outside the city perimeter—taking 4x4 off-road rides and trekking to the crater lake of Mount Pinatubo, river rafting and canoeing through Pagsanjan Falls, or mountain hiking in the nearby Sierra Madre range (like Mount Daraitan).', 'Adrenaline seekers can easily use Manila as a launching pad for thrilling off-road volcano treks, white-water river navigation, and rugged mountain trail hikes.'),
  ('manila:rule:11', 'manila', 'Stay at full-service luxury hotels in Makati or BGC, take private air-conditioned vehicle tours through Intramuros with horse-drawn kalesa rides, explore flat museum halls at the Ayala Museum, and enjoy scenic, low-effort ridge dining in Tagaytay.', 'Accessible cultural museums, private vehicular transport, step-free shopping complexes, and gentle highland dining allow senior travelers to experience Manila comfortably.'),
  ('manila:rule:12', 'manila', 'Take a 10-to-15 minute taxi from Ninoy Aquino International Airport (NAIA) to Resorts World Manila (Newport World Resorts) or SM Mall of Asia, enjoy a relaxed meal of authentic Filipino cuisine, browse shop concourses, and return directly to the terminal.', 'Immediate proximity between NAIA and adjacent Newport or bayfront commercial hubs allows layover passengers to sample local food and modern Filipino atmosphere safely without city traffic delays.'),
  ('manila:rule:13', 'manila', 'Divide your stay between 1 full day of historic heritage and museums (Intramuros, National Museum, Binondo), 1 full day exploring modern lifestyle and nightlife hubs (BGC, Makati, Manila Bay), and 1-2 days taking highland and natural day trips to Tagaytay, Antipolo, or Pagsanjan Falls.', 'A comprehensive multi-day itinerary seamlessly bridges Manila''s urban historic roots and high-energy modern districts with scenic volcanic lakes and lush outdoor attractions nearby. ---'),
  ('cochin:rule:0', 'cochin', 'do not recommend Cherai Beach or a backwater day trip by default.', 'Short Kochi stays work best when time is concentrated around Fort Kochi and Mattancherry rather than spread across multiple outlying experiences.'),
  ('cochin:rule:1', 'cochin', 'increase romance_weight by 30% increase privacy_weight by 20% increase free_time_weight by 20% decrease activity_density by 20%', 'Kochi honeymoon value comes from atmosphere, waterfront experiences, and slow pacing rather than maximum sightseeing.'),
  ('cochin:rule:2', 'cochin', 'reduce walking_intensity_target by 20% increase downtime by 20% prefer short transfers and predictable meal breaks', 'Young children handle Kochi better with compact sightseeing blocks and fewer long walks.'),
  ('cochin:rule:3', 'cochin', 'prefer_central_hotel', 'A cheaper hotel outside the main visitor zone often creates worse overall trip value in Kochi.'),
