  ('sarahan:rule:3', 'sarahan', 'Bhimakali Temple 51 Shakti Peeth + wooden architecture + 800 years old + Bhimakali Palace + museum + Rampur Bushahr history + Bird Pheasantry + Jujurana + monal + Western Tragopan + HPTDC Srikhand + Shrikhand Mahadev view 5155m + apple orchards + Sutlej Valley + deodar + small market + woolens + Kinnauri cap + evening aarti + HPTDC lawn + Shrikhand view + bonfire + stars + quiet + offbeat + temple + Shrikhand + apple orchards.', '1 temple town Kinnaur gateway + 51 Shakti Peeth + wooden architecture + 800 years old + Rampur Bushahr capital + heritage + culture + birding + apple orchards + Shrikhand view + Sutlej Valley + deodar + offbeat + quiet + silence + temple town. ---'),
  ('kasol:rule:0', 'kasol', 'Kasol Market + Parvati River + Nature Park + Chalal bridge 2km + Chalal Village + flea market + Israeli cafes + Manikaran 5km Gurudwara + hot springs + langar + evening party + riverside + bonfire + stars + backpacker + solo + offbeat + cafe + riverside.', '1N quick + Parvati River + Nature Park + Chalal + Manikaran + cafe + flea + party + riverside + bonfire + stars + backpacker + solo + offbeat.'),
  ('kasol:rule:1', 'kasol', 'Day1 Kasol Market + Parvati River + Nature Park + Chalal + Manikaran + cafe + flea + party + riverside, Day2 Tosh 20km 2400m or Kheerganga trek 12km 2960m hot springs + camping + meadows + cafe + party + offbeat + trek base.', '2N perfect + Kasol core + trek + Tosh/Kheerganga + cafe + party + riverside + backpacker + solo + offbeat + budget + best.'),
  ('kasol:rule:2', 'kasol', 'Day1 Kasol core, Day2 Tosh 20km + meadows + cafe + party or Kheerganga trek 12km + hot springs + camping, Day3 Malana 21km ancient + Rasol 5km + Grahan 8km + offbeat + ancient + culture + party + trek base + adventure + backpacker + solo.', 'Complete Kasol + Parvati Valley + trek + village + cafe + party + riverside + backpacker + solo + offbeat + budget + best.'),
  ('kasol:rule:3', 'kasol', 'Parvati Riverside flat + Nature Park flat + Chalal flat with help + Manikaran Gurudwara flat + flea market flat + Israeli cafe + riverside cottage family room + safe + flat + easy + offbeat + riverside + nature + offbeat + family + safe + flat + easy + offbeat + riverside + nature + but hippie + party crowd + not typical Shimla type family + if family offbeat only.', 'Family Parvati River + Nature Park + Chalal + Manikaran + safe + flat + easy + offbeat + riverside + nature + offbeat + family + safe + flat + easy + offbeat + riverside + nature + but hippie + party crowd + not typical Shimla type family + if family offbeat only + backpacker + solo + offbeat.'),
  ('kasol:rule:4', 'kasol', 'Kasol Market + Parvati River + Nature Park + Chalal + Manikaran + Barshaini + Kheerganga trek + Tosh + Malana + Rasol + Grahan + Sar Pass + Pin Parvati + Israeli cafes + flea market + hostels + cottages + shared jeep + party + trance + riverside + bonfire + stars + backpacker + solo + offbeat + budget + best.', '1 backpacker hub HP + hostel $8-$15 + cafe $4-$6 + shared jeep $2-$5 + beer $3 + trek base + party + trance + riverside + bonfire + stars + backpacker + solo + offbeat + budget + best + Parvati Valley + Kheerganga + Tosh + Malana + offbeat + party + trance + riverside + bonfire + stars + backpacker + solo + offbeat + budget + best. ---'),
  ('jispa:rule:0', 'jispa', 'Jispa village last green Lahaul + green meadows + Bhaga Riverside + riverside premium + basic camps + bonfire + Milky Way + Star Gazing + zero light pollution + Padmasambhava statue 10km + village walk + green meadows + Bhaga River + valley + photography + riverside camping + bonfire + Milky Way + Star Gazing + zero light pollution + offbeat + quiet + silence + riverside + camping + bonfire + stars + Milky Way + last green + offbeat + quiet + silence + acclimatization 3200m for Baralacha La 4850m + Sarchu 4290m + Leh 3500m + need 1N rest + water 3-4L + Diamox + need rest + must + biking hub + mechanic + fuel + repair + overnight stop Manali-Leh + Sarchu-Leh + Leh-Manali.', '1N enough + overnight + acclimatisation + riverside + camping + last green + green meadows + Bhaga River + valley + offbeat + quiet + silence + riverside + camping + bonfire + stars + Milky Way + biking hub + mechanic + fuel + repair + overnight stop Manali-Leh + Sarchu-Leh + Leh-Manali + must + 1N.'),
  ('jispa:rule:1', 'jispa', 'Too much for Jispa alone unless adding biking + acclimatisation + rest + Baralacha La day trip 90km + Darcha 22km + Keylong 20km + Suraj Tal 60km + Deepak Tal 50km + village walk + green meadows + offbeat + quiet + acclimatisation + rest + water + Diamox.', '1N enough for overnight + acclimatisation + riverside + camping + last green + green meadows + Bhaga River + valley + offbeat + quiet + silence + riverside + camping + bonfire + stars + Milky Way + biking hub + overnight stop.'),
  ('jispa:rule:2', 'jispa', 'Jispa village flat + Bhaga Riverside flat + green meadows flat + riverside camping flat + Padmasambhava statue flat with help + village walk flat + green meadows flat + Bhaga River flat + bonfire flat + Milky Way flat + Star Gazing flat + safe + family + offbeat + riverside + green meadows + last green + acclimatization 3200m for Baralacha La 4850m + Sarchu 4290m + Leh 3500m + need 1N rest + water 3-4L + Diamox + need rest + must + family + safe + flat + easy + offbeat + riverside + green meadows + last green.', 'Family Jispa village + Bhaga River + green meadows + camping + Padmasambhava + safe + flat + easy + offbeat + riverside + green meadows + last green.'),
  ('jispa:rule:3', 'jispa', 'Jispa village last green Lahaul + green meadows + Bhaga Riverside + riverside premium + basic camps + bonfire + Milky Way + Star Gazing + zero light pollution + Padmasambhava statue 10km + village walk + green meadows + Bhaga River + valley + photography + riverside camping + bonfire + Milky Way + Star Gazing + zero light pollution + offbeat + quiet + silence + riverside + camping + bonfire + stars + Milky Way + last green + offbeat + quiet + silence + biking + Manali-Leh highway + acclimatization 3200m for Baralacha La 4850m + Sarchu 4290m + Leh 3500m + need 1N rest + water 3-4L + Diamox + need rest + must + biking hub + mechanic + fuel + repair + overnight stop Manali-Leh + Sarchu-Leh + Leh-Manali + must + 1N.', '1 overnight stop Manali-Leh + last green Lahaul + green meadows + Bhaga River + riverside + camping + bonfire + Milky Way + acclimatization 3200m for Baralacha La 4850m + Sarchu 4290m + Leh 3500m + need 1N rest + water 3-4L + Diamox + need rest + must + biking hub + mechanic + fuel + repair + overnight stop Manali-Leh + Sarchu-Leh + Leh-Manali + must + 1N. ---'),
  ('corbett:rule:0', 'corbett', 'Stay around Ramnagar, Garjiya Devi Temple, Kosi River, and take one Jeep Safari in the best available zone.', 'Short trips should focus on one quality safari plus nearby attractions rather than long transfers. ---'),
  ('corbett:rule:1', 'corbett', 'Plan 2 nights around Dhikuli/Ramnagar and add 2–3 safaris across suitable zones such as Bijrani, Jhirna, Dhela or Garjia; include Corbett Museum and Garjiya.', 'Four days allow a balanced mix of wildlife, sightseeing and resort relaxation. ---'),
  ('corbett:rule:2', 'corbett', 'Build a deeper Corbett circuit with 2–3 nights around Dhikuli/Ramnagar, a Dhikala wilderness stay when seasonally available, multiple safari zones, Sitabani, Kaladhungi and Corbett Waterfalls.', 'Longer stays justify multiple habitats and a dedicated wilderness experience without rushing. ---'),
  ('corbett:rule:3', 'corbett', 'Choose a classic Corbett safari circuit with Bijrani/Garjia, Jhirna/Dhela, Garjiya Devi Temple, Corbett Museum and, if seasonally open, Dhikala.', 'This combines Corbett''s signature wildlife, forest landscapes, heritage and riverside experiences. ---'),
  ('corbett:rule:4', 'corbett', 'Choose a premium jungle resort around Dhikuli/Kosi or Dhela, private transfers, 1–2 private Jeep Safaris, riverside experiences and dedicated couple time.', 'Corbett works best for honeymooners when wildlife experiences are balanced with privacy and resort relaxation. ---'),
  ('corbett:rule:5', 'corbett', 'Choose family-friendly resorts around Ramnagar/Dhikuli, use private transfers, schedule 1–2 safaris, and add Corbett Museum, Garjiya and Corbett Waterfalls.', 'A mixed activity schedule prevents children from becoming fatigued by repeated rough safari drives. ---'),
  ('corbett:rule:6', 'corbett', 'Book premium jungle accommodation, private chauffeur-driven transfers, authorized private safari vehicles, experienced guides/naturalists, spa facilities and curated dining.', 'Luxury Corbett is primarily about comfort, privacy, service quality and immersive wilderness experiences. ---'),
  ('corbett:rule:7', 'corbett', 'Stay around Ramnagar, use economical accommodation and local dining, choose carefully selected safari zones, and prioritize one or two safaris.', 'Accommodation and sightseeing can be economical, but authorized safari costs should not be compromised. ---'),
  ('corbett:rule:8', 'corbett', 'Choose comfortable accommodation near Ramnagar/Dhikuli, use private vehicles, limit rough safari drives, avoid overloaded schedules and allow substantial afternoon rest.', 'Safari roads can be bumpy and early departures physically demanding for senior travellers. ---'),
  ('corbett:rule:9', 'corbett', 'Prioritize Bijrani, Dhikala, Jhirna, Dhela and Garjia according to season and permit availability.', 'Different zones provide varied forest, grassland and riverine habitats. ---'),
  ('corbett:rule:10', 'corbett', 'Combine Kosi River, Sitabani Forest, Corbett Waterfalls, birdwatching and relaxed forest-edge experiences.', 'These provide Corbett''s quieter side beyond conventional tiger-focused safaris. ---'),
  ('corbett:rule:11', 'corbett', 'Focus on Jeep Safaris, Canter Safaris, guided nature activities, birdwatching and wilderness drives.', 'Corbett''s adventure appeal is primarily wildlife and forest exploration rather than extreme adventure sports. ---'),
  ('corbett:rule:12', 'corbett', 'Stay around Ramnagar/Dhikuli and combine resort dining with local Kumaoni and North Indian cuisine.', 'Corbett offers good regional dining but is not primarily a culinary destination. ---'),
  ('corbett:rule:13', 'corbett', 'Prioritize Garjiya Devi Temple and combine it with peaceful Kosi River surroundings and nearby forest experiences.', 'Garjiya provides Corbett''s strongest combination of pilgrimage, river scenery and natural surroundings. ---'),
  ('corbett:rule:14', 'corbett', 'For a short stop, restrict the program to Ramnagar, Garjiya Devi Temple or one nearby safari if the timing and permit allow.', 'Safari gates operate on fixed schedules, making multiple attractions impractical during short transits. ---');
INSERT INTO decision_rule (id, place_id, action, reason) VALUES
  ('corbett:rule:15', 'corbett', 'Treat Dhikala as a dedicated wilderness experience requiring the applicable seasonal booking/stay or canter arrangement rather than a standard day-jeep safari.', 'Dhikala follows a different tourism and booking structure from ordinary day-safari zones. ---'),
  ('corbett:rule:16', 'corbett', 'Do not promise a specific zone, safari timing or tiger sighting; verify official availability before finalizing the itinerary.', 'Safari access is permit-based, seasonal and subject to operational availability. ---'),
  ('corbett:rule:17', 'corbett', 'Reframe the trip around wildlife diversity, forest landscapes and safari experience rather than guaranteed tiger sightings.', 'Tigers are wild animals and sightings can never be guaranteed. ---'),
  ('corbett:rule:18', 'corbett', 'Verify each tourism zone''s current operating status before booking and emphasize Dhela/Jhirna or other currently open options only when officially available.', 'Corbett tourism zones have different seasonal operating schedules and conditions. ---'),
  ('ranikhet:rule:0', 'ranikhet', 'Stay around Ranikhet town, and prioritize Jhula Devi Temple, Chaubatia Garden, Mankameshwar Temple and 1–2 nearby scenic viewpoints.', 'Short trips should focus on Ranikhet''s core attractions rather than spending excessive time on mountain-road transfers. ---'),
  ('ranikhet:rule:1', 'ranikhet', 'Plan 3 nights in Ranikhet and combine Chaubatia Garden, Jhula Devi Temple, Mankameshwar Temple, Kumaon Regimental Centre Museum, Majhkhali and a relaxed nature/forest experience.', 'Four days provide enough time for major sightseeing while retaining the slow, peaceful character of Ranikhet. ---'),
  ('ranikhet:rule:2', 'ranikhet', 'Build a deeper Kumaon circuit with 3–4 nights in Ranikhet, adding Dwarahat, Binsar Mahadev, Jageshwar or other suitable nearby Kumaon destinations, depending on road conditions and traveller interests.', 'Longer stays justify exploring beyond Ranikhet itself rather than repeating similar sightseeing within the town. ---'),
  ('ranikhet:rule:3', 'ranikhet', 'Choose a classic Ranikhet circuit covering Chaubatia Garden, Jhula Devi Temple, Mankameshwar Temple, Kumaon Regimental Centre Museum, Majhkhali and major Himalayan viewpoints.', 'This combines Ranikhet''s strongest mix of nature, heritage, spirituality and mountain scenery. ---'),
  ('ranikhet:rule:4', 'ranikhet', 'Choose a premium hillside resort/hotel, preferably with valley or Himalayan views, private transfers, relaxed sightseeing, Chaubatia, scenic viewpoints, forest walks and substantial couple time.', 'Ranikhet works best for honeymooners as a peaceful mountain retreat, where privacy and slow experiences matter more than a packed attraction list. ---'),
  ('ranikhet:rule:5', 'ranikhet', 'Choose comfortable family-friendly accommodation around Ranikhet town, use private transfers, schedule Chaubatia Garden, Jhula Devi Temple, Mankameshwar Temple, Kumaon Regimental Centre Museum and easy scenic stops.', 'A combination of gardens, temples, heritage and short sightseeing drives is more comfortable for families than long mountain excursions every day. ---'),
  ('ranikhet:rule:6', 'ranikhet', 'Book premium hillside accommodation, private chauffeur-driven transfers, upgraded rooms with mountain views, curated dining, nature walks and personalized sightseeing.', 'Luxury Ranikhet is primarily about privacy, scenery, service, comfort and slow Himalayan living rather than expensive attractions. ---'),
  ('ranikhet:rule:7', 'ranikhet', 'Stay near Ranikhet town, choose economical hotels/homestays, use shared or economical transport where practical, and prioritize Chaubatia Garden, Jhula Devi Temple, Mankameshwar Temple and accessible viewpoints.', 'Ranikhet can be experienced economically because many of its attractions are relatively low-cost; the main budget pressure is transportation. ---'),
  ('ranikhet:rule:8', 'ranikhet', 'Choose comfortable accommodation with easy road access, use private vehicles, minimize steep walking, avoid excessive daily driving and allow generous afternoon rest.', 'Mountain roads, uneven paths and altitude-related fatigue can make an overloaded Ranikhet itinerary uncomfortable for senior travellers. ---'),
  ('ranikhet:rule:9', 'ranikhet', 'Prioritize Chaubatia Garden, Majhkhali, forest walks, Himalayan viewpoints, birdwatching and relaxed scenic drives.', 'Ranikhet''s strongest appeal is its quiet forests, mountain landscapes, gardens and peaceful natural surroundings. ---'),
  ('ranikhet:rule:10', 'ranikhet', 'Prioritize Kumaon Regimental Centre Museum, Mankameshwar Temple, Jhula Devi Temple and traditional Kumaoni surroundings.', 'Ranikhet offers a strong combination of colonial-era hill heritage, military history and Kumaoni culture. ---'),
  ('ranikhet:rule:11', 'ranikhet', 'Focus on trekking, nature walks, hiking, birdwatching, forest exploration and suitable nearby outdoor activities, depending on season and local conditions.', 'Ranikhet''s adventure appeal is primarily soft adventure and nature exploration, rather than extreme adventure sports. ---'),
  ('ranikhet:rule:12', 'ranikhet', 'Stay around Ranikhet town and combine hotel/resort dining with local Kumaoni dishes and North Indian cuisine.', 'Ranikhet has a pleasant regional food experience, but food is a supporting attraction rather than the primary reason to visit. ---'),
  ('ranikhet:rule:13', 'ranikhet', 'Prioritize Jhula Devi Temple, Mankameshwar Temple, Binsar Mahadev and other suitable nearby temples.', 'Ranikhet and the surrounding Kumaon region offer a strong combination of mountain scenery, peaceful temples and traditional Kumaoni spirituality. ---'),
  ('ranikhet:rule:14', 'ranikhet', 'Prioritize Chaubatia, Majhkhali, Himalayan viewpoints, forest roads, sunrise/sunset locations and traditional townscapes.', 'Ranikhet''s forests, mountain panoramas, gardens and changing seasonal landscapes make it particularly suitable for landscape and travel photography. ---'),
  ('ranikhet:rule:15', 'ranikhet', 'For a short stop, restrict the program to Ranikhet town, Jhula Devi Temple or Chaubatia Garden, depending on arrival/departure timing.', 'Mountain-road travel can consume significant time, making multiple distant attractions impractical during a short transit. ---'),
  ('ranikhet:rule:16', 'ranikhet', 'Prioritize Chaubatia Garden, nature walks, scenic viewpoints and comfortable outdoor sightseeing.', 'Spring provides pleasant conditions and is particularly attractive for flowers, greenery and outdoor exploration. ---'),
  ('ranikhet:rule:17', 'ranikhet', 'Use Ranikhet as a cooler Himalayan escape, schedule outdoor sightseeing during comfortable hours and reserve afternoons for resort/café relaxation.', 'Summer is popular because Ranikhet offers relief from the heat of the plains, but higher demand can increase accommodation pressure. ---'),
  ('ranikhet:rule:18', 'ranikhet', 'Keep the itinerary flexible, verify current road conditions, avoid unnecessary long mountain drives and prioritize nearby attractions when rainfall is heavy.', 'Heavy monsoon rainfall can cause road disruption, landslide risk, poor visibility and cancellation of outdoor plans. ---'),
  ('ranikhet:rule:19', 'ranikhet', 'Prioritize long scenic drives, Himalayan viewpoints, nature walks, photography and outdoor sightseeing.', 'Post-monsoon Ranikhet generally offers clearer skies, pleasant temperatures and excellent visibility, making this one of the strongest travel periods. ---'),
  ('ranikhet:rule:20', 'ranikhet', 'Choose warm, comfortable accommodation, keep sightseeing flexible and treat snowfall as a bonus rather than a guaranteed experience.', 'Winter brings cold temperatures and occasional snowfall, but snowfall conditions vary from year to year. ---'),
  ('ranikhet:rule:21', 'ranikhet', 'Reframe the trip around winter landscapes, cold-weather experiences, Himalayan views and peaceful mountain stays, rather than promising snowfall.', 'Snowfall in Ranikhet is weather-dependent and cannot be guaranteed. ---'),
  ('ranikhet:rule:22', 'ranikhet', 'Confirm weather, road and local sightseeing conditions before finalizing the itinerary and keep alternative nearby attractions available.', 'Ranikhet''s mountain-road accessibility can be affected by heavy rainfall, making flexibility essential during July–September. ---'),
  ('ranikhet:rule:23', 'ranikhet', 'Reduce the number of distant attractions, use a reliable local/private driver and maintain buffer time between activities.', 'Mountain travel times can vary considerably because of road conditions, traffic, weather and terrain. ---'),
  ('ranikhet:rule:24', 'ranikhet', 'Spend more time at the hotel/resort, add forest walks, photography, cafés, viewpoints and relaxed local exploration, and limit the daily attraction count.', 'Ranikhet''s greatest strength is its peaceful atmosphere and scenic environment, which are best experienced without rushing. ---'),
  ('ranikhet:rule:25', 'ranikhet', 'Remove lower-priority attractions and retain 3–5 key experiences per full day with adequate road and rest buffers.', 'Overloading a hill-station itinerary reduces the very relaxation and scenic enjoyment that makes Ranikhet attractive. ---'),
  ('kausani:rule:0', 'kausani', 'Treat Kausani as a scenic Kumaon stopover: prioritise the main Himalayan viewpoint, Anasakti Ashram, Kausani Tea Estate, and a sunset/sunrise experience; add Baijnath Temple only if road timing permits.', 'Kausani''s core appeal is its Himalayan panorama and peaceful atmosphere, so a one-day visit should concentrate on its signature experiences rather than attempting every nearby attraction. ---'),
  ('kausani:rule:1', 'kausani', 'Build a classic Kausani nature-and-culture circuit covering the Himalayan viewpoints, Anasakti Ashram, Kausani Tea Estate, Sumitranandan Pant Museum, Rudradhari Falls & Caves, and Baijnath Temple.', 'Three days provide enough time to experience Kausani''s landscape, cultural heritage, tea gardens, and nearby natural attractions without turning the trip into a rushed checklist. ---'),
  ('kausani:rule:2', 'kausani', 'Expand Kausani into a Kumaon slow-travel circuit, combining Kausani with nearby destinations such as Baijnath, Bageshwar, Ranikhet, Almora, or Gwaldam, depending on the route and road conditions.', 'Kausani itself does not require a week of intensive sightseeing; longer stays are better used to explore the surrounding Kumaon region while maintaining Kausani as a peaceful base. Bageshwar District Administration lists Kausani as well connected by road to destinations including Almora, Ranikhet, Gwaldam, and Bageshwar. ---'),
  ('kausani:rule:3', 'kausani', 'Build a balanced first-timer itinerary around Himalayan sunrise/sunset, Anasakti Ashram, Kausani Tea Estate, Rudradhari Falls & Caves, Baijnath Temple, and Sumitranandan Pant Museum.', 'These experiences collectively represent Kausani''s strongest combination of Himalayan scenery, spirituality, nature, tea culture, history, and literary heritage. ---'),
  ('kausani:rule:4', 'kausani', 'Choose a Himalayan-view boutique resort, request a private balcony or valley-facing room, schedule sunrise and sunset together, and add a private tea-estate/forest excursion with a relaxed Kumaoni dinner.', 'Kausani''s greatest romantic asset is its quiet atmosphere and uninterrupted Himalayan scenery rather than nightlife or dense tourist entertainment. Its accommodation market includes resorts specifically positioned for honeymooners and scenic stays. ---'),
  ('kausani:rule:5', 'kausani', 'Base the family in Kausani town, use a private vehicle, prioritise Anasakti Ashram, Tea Estate, Baijnath Temple, Himalayan viewpoints, and easy nature walks, and keep longer treks optional.', 'Kausani''s road-accessible attractions and relaxed environment work well for multigenerational travel, while longer trekking routes can impose unnecessary physical demands. ---'),
  ('kausani:rule:6', 'kausani', 'Select the best available Himalayan-facing premium resort, preferably with private balconies/terraces, high-quality in-house dining, wellness facilities, and personalised service; arrange a dedicated chauffeur and private sightseeing.', 'Kausani''s luxury proposition is based on privacy, panoramic views, nature, personalised hospitality, and exclusivity, rather than extensive five-star urban infrastructure. Current accommodation listings show multiple upscale/luxury options, including Himalayan-view properties. ---'),
  ('kausani:rule:7', 'kausani', 'Stay in a local guesthouse, homestay, or economical hotel, use local eateries where convenient, and focus on free viewpoints, Anasakti Ashram, tea gardens, village walks, and accessible nature experiences.', 'Kausani has accommodation across luxury, mid-range, budget, homestay, and eco-lodge categories, allowing travellers to control costs without sacrificing the destination''s principal scenic experiences. ---'),
  ('kausani:rule:8', 'kausani', 'Prioritise Kausani Tea Estate, Rudradhari Falls & Caves, forest walks, Himalayan viewpoints, birdwatching, and village trails.', 'Kausani is fundamentally a nature destination, with pine forests, valleys, streams, tea gardens, birdlife, and expansive Himalayan views forming its core appeal. ---'),
  ('kausani:rule:9', 'kausani', 'Add Pinnath trekking, Rudradhari trekking, mountain biking, cycling, rock climbing, or other locally available adventure activities, while reserving additional time for weather and trail-condition changes.', 'Official Incredible India information highlights trekking, rock climbing, mountain biking, cycling, and zorbing around Kausani, while more demanding glacier treks require significantly greater preparation. ---'),
  ('kausani:rule:10', 'kausani', 'Choose a centrally located or easily accessible hotel, use a private vehicle, focus on Himalayan viewpoints, Anasakti Ashram, Tea Estate, Pant Museum, and Baijnath Temple, and avoid strenuous treks unless mobility and weather conditions are suitable.', 'Kausani can be enjoyed through scenic road-accessible attractions and relaxed sightseeing without requiring strenuous mountain trekking. ---'),
  ('kausani:rule:11', 'kausani', 'Use Kausani as a 1-night scenic break between other Kumaon destinations, with the evening reserved for sunset and the following morning for sunrise before continuing the road journey.', 'Kausani is best suited to slow scenic travel rather than a rushed stop; its principal attraction can be experienced effectively around the sunrise/sunset cycle. ---'),
  ('kausani:rule:12', 'kausani', 'Prioritise Anasakti Ashram, Sumitranandan Pant Museum, and Baijnath Temple, supplemented by local Kumaoni cultural experiences.', 'Kausani''s historical identity is closely connected with Mahatma Gandhi''s 1929 stay and Anasakti Yoga, while the town is also the birthplace of poet Sumitranandan Pant; nearby Baijnath adds an important temple-heritage component. ---'),
  ('kausani:rule:13', 'kausani', 'Choose a quiet Himalayan-view resort, minimise daily transfers, incorporate meditation/yoga, nature walks, spa or wellness treatments where available, and dedicate unstructured time to Himalayan sunrise and sunset.', 'Kausani''s low-key environment, forests, mountain views, and spiritual heritage make it more suitable for slow wellness and restorative travel than activity-heavy itineraries. Uttarakhand Tourism also positions the state broadly as a wellness destination. ---'),
  ('kausani:rule:14', 'kausani', 'Reduce trekking dependence, maintain flexible road schedules, and prioritise accommodation-based experiences, viewpoints when visibility permits, tea gardens, cultural attractions, and shorter excursions.', 'Kausani receives substantial rainfall, making mountain-road and outdoor activity planning more weather-sensitive during the monsoon. ---'),
  ('kausani:rule:15', 'kausani', 'Include an evening stargazing/astronomy experience and keep the night schedule free from unnecessary transfers.', 'Kausani''s relatively clear mountain skies and low-light surroundings make astronomy an increasingly notable part of its tourism offering; Incredible India specifically highlights the Starscapes Observatory and Kausani''s appeal to stargazers and astrophotographers. ---'),
  ('nainital:rule:0', 'nainital', 'Focus on a compact lakeside loop in Nainital’s core town center by strolling along Mall Road, taking a peaceful boat ride on Naini Lake, visiting the sacred Naina Devi Temple, and enjoying local snacks or tea at the historic Boat House Club or The Flatts before departing.', 'Half-day layovers or passing visits require minimal internal transit; restricting your stay to the central lakefront provides iconic Himalayan scenery, spiritual heritage, and walkable dining without risking vehicle delays or mountain traffic gridlock.'),
  ('nainital:rule:1', 'nainital', 'Take an early morning aerial cable car to Snow View Point for panoramic views of the Nanda Devi peak range, explore the natural rock formations at Eco Cave Gardens in the late morning, enjoy a traditional afternoon rowboat ride on Naini Lake paired with a walk around Mall Road, and savor Kumaoni fine dining at an upper-slope heritage property like The Manor House or Gurney House.', 'A single full day allows energetic travelers to experience Nainital''s iconic high-ridge Himalayan viewpoints, unique eco-cave trails, and historic colonial lakefront culture within a balanced daytime structure.'),
  ('nainital:rule:2', 'nainital', 'Spend day one exploring core Nainital highlights (Naini Lake, Naina Devi Temple, Snow View Point, Mall Road, and Tiffin Top); spend day two taking a scenic day trip out to the broader Greater Lake District (Bhimtal, Sattal, and Naukuchiatal) for water sports and kayaking, or make a spiritual pilgrimage to Kainchi Dham Ashram before returning for a evening dinner.', 'Multi-day stays allow travelers to bridge Nainital’s bustling colonial hill-station charm with the quieter, eco-rich lakes and renowned spiritual sanctuaries of the surrounding Kumaon region.'),
  ('nainital:rule:3', 'nainital', 'Focus on quintessential hill-station highlights—boating across Naini Lake, visiting the revered Naina Devi Temple, walking the full stretch of Mall Road, riding the Nainital Ropeway to Snow View Point, walking up to Tiffin Top (Dorothy''s Seat), and shopping for handcrafted candles and woolens at the Bara Bazaar.', 'Combining Nainital''s foundational lakefront monuments, panoramic Himalayan viewpoints, colonial heritage trails, and bustling hill-market bazaars delivers a complete first-time overview of the town''s timeless charm.'),
  ('nainital:rule:4', 'nainital', 'Book a luxury lake-view suite or private colonial estate like The Naini Retreat or Manu Maharani, arrange private sunset yachting or private rowboat rides on Naini Lake, take quiet walks along Lover’s Lane toward Lands End, arrange a private day tour to the tranquil waters of Naukuchiatal, and enjoy candlelit fireside dining overlooking the illuminated valley.', 'Pairing secluded hillside estate luxury and panoramic lake-view sunsets with intimate walks, private boating, and fine Kumaoni gastronomy creates an idyllic mountain romantic getaway.'),
  ('nainital:rule:5', 'nainital', 'Explore the fun subterranean tunnels at Eco Cave Gardens, take the exciting Nainital Ropeway up to Snow View Point for rides and games, enjoy family pedal boating on Naini Lake, visit the high-altitude animals at High Altitude Zoo (Pt. G.B. Pant High Altitude Zoo), and go horse riding near Bara Pathar.', 'Interactive cave trails, scenic cable car rides, gentle pony rides, and high-altitude wildlife parks keep children engaged across all age groups in a safe environment.'),
  ('nainital:rule:6', 'nainital', 'Book luxury suites at historic heritage properties like The Naini Retreat, Welcomheritage Ashdale, or The Metropole, hire private luxury SUVs with accredited local drivers, arrange private traditional wooden boat charters on Naini Lake, shop for high-end local silk woolens, and enjoy multi-course Kumaoni gourmet dining in private hotel gardens.', 'Historic British-era estates, private vehicular transport, exclusive boat charters, and refined regional culinary experiences provide maximum mountain comfort and personalized service.'),
  ('nainital:rule:7', 'nainital', 'Stay in central guesthouses or homestays around Sukhatal or Tallital, explore the city on foot using the scenic Thandi Sadak walking path, use shared local green taxis for ridge viewpoints, visit free or low-cost sites like Naina Devi Temple and Nainital Lakefront, and savor local street food like Aloo Gutuk and Bhatt Ki Churdkani near The Flatts Market.', 'Nainital offers a robust network of affordable homestays, scenic free walking promenades, low-cost shared transit, and authentic budget street-food stalls suitable for price-conscious travelers.'),
  ('nainital:rule:8', 'nainital', 'Hike the oak and rhododendron forest trails up to Naina Peak (China Peak) for panoramic Himalayan views, go birdwatching in the dense pine forests of Pangot and Kilbury Bird Sanctuary, explore the pristine seven inter-connected lakes at Sattal, or walk through the Himalayan Botanical Garden.', 'Beyond the main urban lakefront, Nainital’s surrounding ridges host dense Himalayan biospheres, world-class birdwatching habitats, pristine forest hiking trails, and undisturbed mountain lakes.'),
  ('nainital:rule:9', 'nainital', 'Sample regional Kumaoni delicacies—tasting Ras (lentil broth), Bhatt Ki Churdkani, and Gahat Ki Dal at authentic local eateries, trying sweet local treats like Bal Mithai and Singori at historic sweet shops in Bara Bazaar, enjoying fresh lakefront snacks near The Flatts, and savoring heritage colonial dining at the Boat House Club.', 'Nainital offers a distinct culinary identity blending rustic Kumaoni mountain flavors with British colonial heritage dishes and vibrant street-food culture.'),
  ('nainital:rule:10', 'nainital', 'Go paragliding over the valley at Bhimtal or Naukuchiatal, tackle the steep trekking trail to the summit of Naina Peak, rent kayaks or water-zorbing spheres at Naukuchiatal Lake, and embark on mountain biking trails through the dense woods of Pangot.', 'Adventure seekers can use Nainital as a base for high-altitude paragliding, multi-hour peak treks, lake kayaking, and forest off-road cycling.'),
  ('nainital:rule:11', 'nainital', 'Stay at flat, easily accessible full-service hotels near Tallital or Mall Road, take gentle scenic rowboat rides on Naini Lake, use the Nainital Ropeway for effortless access to high viewpoints, enjoy flat evening strolls along Thandi Sadak, and relax over high-tea at historic heritage estates like The Naini Retreat.', 'Cable-car ridge transport, step-free lakefront walking paths, gentle boat rides, and accessible heritage hotel gardens allow senior travelers to experience Nainital''s natural beauty in complete ease and safety.'),
  ('nainital:rule:12', 'nainital', 'Take a short private cab transfer from Kathgodam Railway Station (or Pantnagar Airport) up to Mall Road, enjoy a 1-hour rowboat tour across Naini Lake, visit Naina Devi Temple, pick up local Bal Mithai sweets from Bara Bazaar, and head back down to the plains or onward to your next Himalayan destination.', 'Direct road access between Kathgodam railhead and central Naini Lake allows layover travelers to sample iconic mountain views, temple culture, and regional sweets without detailed stays.'),
  ('nainital:rule:13', 'nainital', 'Divide your stay between 1 full day of central lake highlights and mountain viewpoints (Naini Lake, Naina Devi Temple, Snow View Point, Tiffin Top), 1 full day exploring regional nature and birding hubs (Pangot, Kilbury, Naina Peak hike), and 1 full day taking a lake-hopping circuit (Bhimtal, Sattal, Naukuchiatal) paired with a morning visit to Kainchi Dham Ashram.', 'A comprehensive multi-day itinerary seamlessly balances Nainital''s vibrant central town atmosphere and historic sights with high-altitude forest sanctuaries, spiritual retreats, and peaceful outer mountain lakes. ---'),
  ('adi-kailash:rule:0', 'adi-kailash', 'Limit your journey to the lower Kumaon foothills and lake region (Nainital, Bhimtal, or Pithoragarh town) for local temple heritage and scenic lake views, skipping the high-altitude inner-line expedition.', 'The Adi Kailash yatra requires a minimum of 5 to 6 days due to long inner-Himalayan mountain transit, high-altitude acclimatization protocols at Gunji, and official Inner Line Permit (ILP) verification near international borders.'),
  ('adi-kailash:rule:1', 'adi-kailash', 'Book a streamlined high-altitude itinerary—fly via private or shared charter helicopter directly from Pithoragarh to Gunji/Napalchu, dedicate day three to Adi Kailash, Parvati Sarovar, and Gauri Kund, devote day four to Om Parvat and Kalapani Temple, and return via helicopter to Pithoragarh on day five.', 'A 5-day duration is only viable when using helicopter sorties to bypass the grueling 2-day road journey along the Dharchula-Lipulekh mountain highway.'),
  ('adi-kailash:rule:2', 'adi-kailash', 'Complete the full overland expedition starting from Kathgodam/Pithoragarh, driving through Dharchula to Gunji, spending 3 full days exploring sacred sites (Adi Kailash, Parvati Sarovar, Gauri Kund, Om Parvat, Nabhidhang, and Kalapani Temple), and returning via Chaukori or Jageshwar Dham.', 'Multi-day overland travel provides essential altitude acclimatization, accommodates potential weather delays on alpine passes, and permits rich cultural integration with local Bhotiya villages along the Vyas Valley.'),
  ('adi-kailash:rule:3', 'adi-kailash', 'Book a fully guided package through government-approved operators (like KMVN) or specialized high-altitude outfitters that handle all Inner Line Permits (ILP), medical checkups, 4x4 mountain transportation, high-altitude stay arrangements in Gunji, and sacred Darshan at Adi Kailash and Om Parvat.', 'First-time travelers face complex border security clearances, rugged terrain, and steep elevation gains (~4,400 m), making accredited local guides and pre-arranged logistics essential for safety and permit compliance.'),
  ('adi-kailash:rule:4', 'adi-kailash', 'Upgrade to a VIP Heli-Yatra package staying in premium private wooden huts at Gunji, arrange private 4x4 SUV transfers, include personalized Vedic prayer ceremonies at Parvati Sarovar, and extend the trip with a luxury wilderness retreat in Pithoragarh or Binsar.', 'Replacing long overland road journeys with helicopter transfers and private high-altitude wooden huts transforms a rugged alpine pilgrimage into a comfortable, exclusive spiritual getaway amidst Himalayan views.'),
  ('adi-kailash:rule:5', 'adi-kailash', 'Opt for a comfortable 6- to 7-day paced itinerary with proper intermediate stopovers at Dharchula (~915 m) and Gunji (~3,200 m), ensure children meet the minimum age/fitness guidelines, utilize 4x4 SUVs for all road legs, and hire ponies for the trek section between Jolingkong and Parvati Sarovar.', 'Gradual elevation shifts protect younger family members from Acute Mountain Sickness (AMS), while pony services ease physical exertion on high-altitude walking tracks.'),
  ('adi-kailash:rule:6', 'adi-kailash', 'Reserve chartered helicopter transfers between Pithoragarh and Gunji, secure private heated eco-huts with dedicated butler and chef services, travel in private 4x4 luxury SUVs across high-altitude roads, and incorporate luxury heritage stays in Pithoragarh pre- and post-expedition.', 'Combining air sorties, private heated accommodations, customized organic meals, and dedicated support staff mitigates high-altitude discomfort without sacrificing VIP luxury.'),
  ('adi-kailash:rule:7', 'adi-kailash', 'Join a group overland tour or travel via shared local 4x4 jeeps from Dharchula, stay in authentic village homestays or standard KMVN dormitories in Gunji and Kuti, trek on foot from Jolingkong to Parvati Sarovar, and eat local Kumaoni vegetarian meals at village dhabas.', 'Utilizing shared mountain jeeps, local homestays, and self-guided trekking drastically lowers costs while supporting rural Himalayan village economies.'),
  ('adi-kailash:rule:8', 'adi-kailash', 'Focus on the pristine alpine ecosystems of the Vyas Valley—photographing snow-capped peaks at Jolingkong, exploring glacial lakes like Parvati Sarovar and Gauri Kund, witnessing the rare snow pattern of Om Parvat at Nabhidhang, and observing high-altitude flora along the Kali River.', 'The Adi Kailash circuit showcases rare glacial landscapes, alpine lakes, high-altitude meadows, and miraculous natural snow formations within the Remote Eastern Kumaon Himalaya.'),
  ('adi-kailash:rule:9', 'adi-kailash', 'Savor traditional high-altitude Kumaoni and Bhotiya culinary staples—sampling Bhang ki Chutney, Madua (Finger Millet) Roti, Aloo ke Gutke, warm Gahat Dal (Horsegram), Phaanu, and hot butter tea in remote border villages like Gunji and Kuti.', 'Mountain cuisine in the Vyas Valley uses nutrient-dense local grains, wild herbs, and warming spices engineered specifically for mountain endurance and high-altitude digestion.'),
  ('adi-kailash:rule:10', 'adi-kailash', 'Choose a combined trekking-expedition route—hiking the high-altitude trail up to Gauri Kund (~4,500 m) right under the face of Adi Kailash, exploring high mountain passes near the Indo-Tibet border, and combining the yatra with a side trek to Sin La Pass or Kuti Village.', 'High elevations, rugged terrain, steep glacial hikes, and remote border landscapes offer world-class challenge and thrill for experienced trekkers and mountaineers.'),
  ('adi-kailash:rule:11', 'adi-kailash', 'Strictly require a comprehensive pre-yatra medical check (BP and ECG), choose the helicopter yatra option to bypass rough mountain roads, hire ponies or doli services for the high-altitude walking stretches at Jolingkong, and carry portable medical oxygen cylinders throughout the journey.', 'High altitudes above 4,000 meters present severe hypoxia risks for older travelers; helicopter transfers, pony assistance, and portable oxygen ensure spiritual fulfillment without physical overexertion.'),
  ('adi-kailash:rule:12', 'adi-kailash', 'Do not attempt the Adi Kailash trek on a short layover or quick transit stop; instead, take a day excursion to Jageshwar Dham or Pithoragarh Fort from Kathgodam/Pantnagar.', 'Adi Kailash is located in a restricted border zone requiring multi-day permits and high-altitude travel that cannot be compressed into a short transit window.'),
  ('adi-kailash:rule:13', 'adi-kailash', 'Dedicate extended time for silent meditation and Vedic rituals at Parvati Sarovar, offer prayers at the sacred Kalapani Temple (source of the Kali River), perform Darshan of the divine snow "ॐ" at Om Parvat, and visit the ancient Pandava-linked heritage structures in Kuti Village.', 'Adi Kailash (Chota Kailash) and Om Parvat are among the most revered cosmic energy centers in Hinduism, deeply connected to Lord Shiva, Goddess Parvati, and Mahabharata lore. ---'),
  ('om-parvat:rule:0', 'om-parvat', 'Limit your visit to the central ghats and hilltop shrines of Har Ki Pauri, Brahma Kund, and Mansa Devi Temple via the Udan Khatoola ropeway, concluding with the evening Ganga Aarti before departure.', 'A single-day visit requires absolute focus on central landmarks to avoid getting trapped in regional traffic while ensuring you experience the city''s primary spiritual ritual.'),
  ('om-parvat:rule:1', 'om-parvat', 'Combine the core central ghats with the southern heritage cluster of Kankhal (Daksha Mahadev Temple, Ma Anandamayi Ashram), the northern ashram corridor (Bharat Mata Mandir, Shanti Kunj), and an early morning wildlife safari at Rajaji National Park (Motichur Gate).', 'A 3-day window allows a complete overview of Haridwar''s four major geographic clusters without feeling rushed, blending spirituality, heritage, and nature.'),
  ('om-parvat:rule:2', 'om-parvat', 'Complete a comprehensive spiritual and wellness circuit by combining Haridwar''s sacred sites, wildlife zones, and ashrams over 2 to 3 days, then extending your stay north along the Ganges corridor to Rishikesh (Ram Jhula, Beatles Ashram, Parmarth Niketan).', 'Multi-day itineraries provide sufficient time to pair Haridwar''s traditional river rituals and ancient temples with Rishikesh''s yoga, Ayurvedic wellness, and adventure offerings.'),
  ('om-parvat:rule:3', 'om-parvat', 'Book a structured itinerary covering the iconic twin Siddha Peeths (Mansa Devi and Chandi Devi via cable car), historic market walks through Bara Bazaar, heritage visits to Daksha Mahadev Temple, and pre-arranged early access or VIP platform seating for the evening Ganga Aarti at Har Ki Pauri.', 'First-time visitors benefit from clear geographic routing and pre-arranged Aarti seating to easily navigate dense crowds and complex temple queues.'),
  ('om-parvat:rule:4', 'om-parvat', 'Stay at an upscale riverfront resort along the quiet Motichur or Ganges canal corridor, schedule private evening Ganga Aarti viewing or private boat experiences, enjoy couple''s Ayurvedic spa treatments, and take day trips to serene spots in nearby Rishikesh.', 'Escaping the crowded central market hotels for secluded riverfront luxury turns a hectic pilgrimage hub into a romantic, rejuvenating getaway.'),
  ('om-parvat:rule:5', 'om-parvat', 'Plan a balanced, relaxed itinerary using low-emission e-rickshaws for short transfers, include the Udan Khatoola ropeways to Mansa Devi and Chandi Devi, take an open-top jeep safari in Rajaji National Park, and visit the multi-story Bharat Mata Mandir.', 'Cable car rides, wildlife safaris, and colorful multi-story exhibits keep children engaged while avoiding excessive walking for all family members.'),
  ('om-parvat:rule:6', 'om-parvat', 'Reserve a private suite at a high-end wellness resort along the river corridor, arrange climate-controlled private SUV transfers, secure reserved VIP platform passes at Malviya Dip for the Ganga Aarti, and book personalized Ayurvedic consultations and private yoga sessions.', 'High-end accommodations and VIP access bypass heavy crowds, long lines, and local traffic, delivering an exclusive and comfortable experience.'),
  ('om-parvat:rule:7', 'om-parvat', 'Stay in a clean ashram or budget hotel along Ashram Road in Bhupatwala, travel using shared e-rickshaws and local buses, eat wholesome Sattvik meals at ashram bhojanalayas, and participate in free public bathing ghat rituals and open Aarti viewings at Har Ki Pauri.', 'Haridwar offers extensive low-cost infrastructure, allowing budget travelers to experience all primary spiritual sites at minimal expense.'),
  ('om-parvat:rule:8', 'om-parvat', 'Focus on the biodiversity of the Shivalik foothills by taking a morning 4x4 jeep safari at Rajaji National Park (Motichur Gate), walking along the peaceful channels of Saptrishi Ashram and Sapt Sarovar, and exploring the riverbanks near Raiwala.', 'The forested fringes and river splits around Haridwar host wild Asian elephants, leopards, migratory birds, and serene riparian landscapes away from urban crowds.'),
  ('om-parvat:rule:9', 'om-parvat', 'Take a curated street food walk through Bara Bazaar, Moti Bazaar, and Upper Road—sampling hot Bedmi Poori with spicy Aloo Subzi, fresh Kachoris, thick clay-cup (kulhad) Lassi, and hot Rabri-Jalebi from legacy sweet shops.', 'Haridwar''s historic market lanes feature decades-old culinary traditions specializing in rich, authentic North Indian vegetarian street food.'),
  ('om-parvat:rule:10', 'om-parvat', 'Use Haridwar as a launching pad to head 30 km north toward Rishikesh and Shivpuri for white-water rafting on the Ganges, cliff jumping, ziplining, and trekking to nearby jungle waterfalls like Neer Garh.', 'While Haridwar focuses primarily on traditional pilgrimage and culture, its immediate neighbor Rishikesh provides world-class adventure sports and outdoor activities.'),
  ('om-parvat:rule:11', 'om-parvat', 'Select flat-access hotels or quiet ashrams, utilize round-trip cable cars (Udan Khatoola) for hilltop temples, arrange e-rickshaws directly to ghat entry points, and secure reserved seated spots at Har Ki Pauri well before the evening Aarti begins.', 'Seniors need to minimize steep stair climbing and long periods of standing in crowded lines, making comfortable transport and reserved seating essential.'),
  ('om-parvat:rule:12', 'om-parvat', 'If stopping for 3 to 4 hours near Haridwar Junction, take a quick e-rickshaw straight to Har Ki Pauri for a short riverside walk, visit Bara Bazaar for a quick local breakfast, and return directly to the station.', 'Central ghats and historic markets are located within 2 km of the railway station, making short layover visits simple and efficient.'),
  ('om-parvat:rule:13', 'om-parvat', 'Dedicate time for early morning holy dips at Brahma Kund, meditate at Ma Anandamayi Ashram in Kankhal, explore the Vedic philosophy archives at Shanti Kunj, offer prayers at Daksha Mahadev Temple, and attend the evening Ganga Aarti.', 'Haridwar is one of India''s seven sacred Sapta Puri cities, offering deep connections to Vedic mythology, ancient ashrams, and sacred river rituals. ---'),
  ('haridwar:rule:0', 'haridwar', 'Focus exclusively on central Har Ki Pauri, the hilltop Mansa Devi Temple, and the local Bara Bazaar and Moti Bazaar markets for sacred baths, ropeway rides, and the evening Ganga Aarti, skipping outer ashram corridors and southern heritage zones.', 'Short weekend visits require tight geographical containment around the central ghat precinct to prevent getting caught in town traffic and missing evening ritual seating windows.'),
  ('haridwar:rule:1', 'haridwar', 'Book a classic 3-day spiritual circuit—covering Har Ki Pauri, Mansa Devi, and Chandi Devi Siddha Peeths via the Udan Khatoola ropeway, exploring the northern ashram corridor (Bharat Mata Mandir, Shanti Kunj, Pawan Dham), and taking a heritage afternoon tour of Kankhal (Daksha Mahadev Temple, Ma Anandamayi Ashram).', 'A 3-day duration provides the perfect timeframe to comfortably experience all four primary geographical clusters of Haridwar without rushing rituals or daily transfers.'),
  ('haridwar:rule:2', 'haridwar', 'Complete a broad regional circuit combining Haridwar’s core sacred highlights (Har Ki Pauri, Siddha Peeths, Kankhal) with a morning jeep safari at Rajaji National Park (Motichur Gate), followed by a 2-day wellness and yoga extension in nearby Rishikesh (Ram Jhula, Beatles Ashram, Parmarth Niketan).', 'Extended stays beyond 4 days are best spent expanding into nearby natural and wellness hubs, avoiding repetitive city stays while deepening the overall regional experience.'),
  ('haridwar:rule:3', 'haridwar', 'Choose a guided heritage and pilgrimage package that includes priority express ropeway passes for Mansa Devi and Chandi Devi, reserved VIP platform seating at Har Ki Pauri (Malviya Dip) for the evening Ganga Aarti, and pre-arranged low-emission e-rickshaw transfers through narrow market lanes.', 'First-time visitors frequently get overwhelmed by massive riverfront crowds, vehicle restrictions, and long cable car queues; pre-arranged VIP access ensures a smooth, stress-free intro.'),
  ('haridwar:rule:4', 'haridwar', 'Reserve a high-end luxury riverfront resort along the quiet Bhupatwala or Motichur-Rishikesh highway corridor, book private VIP escort for the evening Ganga Aarti at Har Ki Pauri, schedule private Ayurvedic couples'' spa treatments, and take a private day excursion to Rishikesh.', 'Standard hotels in central Haridwar can be noisy and crowded; luxury highway resorts offer serene private Ganges views, fine dining, and spa wellness tailored for couples.'),
  ('haridwar:rule:5', 'haridwar', 'Opt for a relaxed 3-day pace using private climate-controlled vehicles for transit, utilize express cable car tickets for Mansa Devi and Chandi Devi, include an exciting open-top jeep safari at Rajaji National Park for children, and stay in hotels with spacious family suites along Ashram Road.', 'Multi-generational families benefit from minimal walking friction, engaging wildlife activities for kids, and quiet accommodations with easy dietary customizations.'),
  ('haridwar:rule:6', 'haridwar', 'Book a private villa or riverfront suite at a luxury wellness resort along the Motichur corridor, arrange a private chauffeur-driven SUV (Toyota Innova Crysta), secure VIP platform seating for the Har Ki Pauri evening Ganga Aarti, and incorporate personalized Ayurvedic therapies and private yoga sessions.', 'High-end travelers require insulated, premium accommodations, private transfers, and VIP access to bypass public crowd surges while enjoying authentic spiritual traditions.'),
  ('haridwar:rule:7', 'haridwar', 'Stay in comfortable, well-maintained ashram guest houses or budget hotels in Bhupatwala or near the Haridwar Railway Station, utilize shared electric rickshaws for local transit, eat at authentic ashram bhojanalayas or traditional market sweet shops, and walk the riverfront ghats on foot.', 'Haridwar offers an extensive network of affordable ashram accommodations, low-cost public transport, and clean, wholesome vegetarian dining that keeps costs exceptionally low.'),
  ('haridwar:rule:8', 'haridwar', 'Focus on the green fringes of the Shivalik hills—booking a morning 4x4 wildlife safari at Rajaji National Park (Motichur Gate), exploring the serene Sapt Sarovar river channels, taking scenic cable car rides up Bilwa and Neel Parvat, and walking along the uncrowded banks of the Ganges Canal.', 'Haridwar sits at the intersection of the Gangetic plains and the Shivalik foothills, offering rich forested birding zones, elephant corridors, and pristine riverways.'),
  ('haridwar:rule:9', 'haridwar', 'Take a curated heritage street food tour through Bara Bazaar, Moti Bazaar, and Upper Road—sampling famous local specialties like Bedmi Poori with spicy Aloo Subzi, crisp Kachoris, Kulhad Lassi, fresh Rabri-Jalebi, and warm Gulab Jamuns from legacy sweet shops.', 'Haridwar’s old city markets feature decades-old culinary institutions specializing in iconic, pure-vegetarian North Indian breakfast items and milk-based desserts cooked in pure ghee.'),
  ('haridwar:rule:10', 'haridwar', 'Combine Haridwar''s sacred city highlights with outdoor mountain activities—adding a 4x4 jeep safari in Rajaji National Park, hiking up the steep forest walking tracks to Mansa Devi and Chandi Devi, and taking a short drive to Rishikesh for white-water rafting on the Ganges River and cliff jumping.', 'Positioning Haridwar as an entry gateway allows adventure enthusiasts to quickly transition from cultural rituals to high-energy river rafting and forest trekking in the Shivalik region.'),
  ('haridwar:rule:11', 'haridwar', 'Prioritize accessible, low-friction sightseeing—utilizing flat e-rickshaw transit to ghats, booking express cable car passes with elevator access for hilltop temples, reserving VIP seated platforms for the Har Ki Pauri Ganga Aarti, and staying in peaceful ashrams or quiet resorts with elevator facilities.', 'Older travelers require protection from steep stairs, extreme midday heat, and long standing periods in dense crowds during riverfront rituals and temple visits.'),
  ('haridwar:rule:12', 'haridwar', 'For travelers with a short 4- to 6-hour layover at Haridwar Junction, take an e-rickshaw directly to Har Ki Pauri (~2 km) for a quick riverbank view, visit the nearby market for breakfast or snacks, and return smoothly to the railway station.', 'Central Har Ki Pauri is situated just 10 minutes from the primary rail station, making it easy to experience the core sacred atmosphere without risking missed train connections.'),
  ('haridwar:rule:13', 'haridwar', 'Spend dedicated time meditating at Ma Anandamayi Ashram in Kankhal, attend both early morning and evening Ganga Aarti rituals at Har Ki Pauri, take sacred baths at Brahma Kund, explore the global spiritual center of Shanti Kunj, and offer prayers at the ancient Daksha Mahadev Temple.', 'Haridwar is one of the four legendary Kumbh Mela sites and a principal Vedic energy center, offering rich opportunities for quiet meditation, temple rituals, and spiritual learning. ---'),
  ('srinagar:rule:0', 'srinagar', 'Focus exclusively on central lake and garden highlights by taking an early morning visit to Shankaracharya Temple, exploring Nishat Bagh and Shalimar Bagh, and concluding with a 2-hour sunset Shikara ride on Dal Lake visiting Char Chinar.', 'A single-day itinerary requires prioritizing iconic landmarks along the lakefront corridor to minimize city transit and maximize scenery.'),
  ('srinagar:rule:1', 'srinagar', 'Combine central lake highlights (Mughal Gardens, Shankaracharya Temple) with an early morning Floating Vegetable Market Shikara tour, a guided Old City heritage walk (Jamia Masjid, Khanqah-e-Moula), and a full-day excursion to either Gulmarg or Pahalgam.', 'A 3-day stay allows a balanced introduction to Srinagar''s cultural heritage, water-based lifestyle, and nearby alpine mountain passes.'),
  ('srinagar:rule:2', 'srinagar', 'Execute a complete Kashmir circuit using Srinagar as the central hub: spend 2 days exploring Srinagar’s lakes, Mughal gardens, and Old City bazaars, followed by overnight stays in Pahalgam (Lidder Valley, Betaab Valley) and Gulmarg (Gondola Phase 2), with an optional day excursion to Sonmarg or Yusmarg.', 'Multi-day itineraries provide sufficient time to experience both Srinagar''s urban heritage and Kashmir''s major alpine valleys without rushing long mountain drives.'),
  ('srinagar:rule:3', 'srinagar', 'Book a structured itinerary covering an early morning Shikara ride on Dal Lake, visits to Nishat Bagh and Shalimar Bagh, sunrise darshan at Shankaracharya Temple, shopping at Polo View Market, and an authentic Kashmiri Wazwan meal.', 'First-time visitors benefit from experiencing the core signature elements that define Kashmir''s cultural and natural identity.'),
  ('srinagar:rule:4', 'srinagar', 'Reserve a private luxury houseboat on the tranquil waters of Nigeen Lake, schedule private sunset Shikara rides, enjoy private candlelit dinners with saffron Kahwa, take romantic walks through Pari Mahal at dusk, and take a private day trip to Aru Valley in Pahalgam.', 'Staying on quieter lake stretches away from commercial piers provides the privacy, atmosphere, and cinematic views ideal for couples.'),
  ('srinagar:rule:5', 'srinagar', 'Stay in a lakefront resort along Boulevard Road, explore the broad, flat lawns of Nishat Bagh and Shalimar Bagh, visit the seasonal Indira Gandhi Memorial Tulip Garden (March–April), take child-friendly Shikara rides with life jackets, and take a day excursion to Gulmarg for snow sports.', 'Flat garden paths, gentle water transport, and high-altitude cable cars keep children and elders comfortable and engaged.'),
  ('srinagar:rule:6', 'srinagar', 'Book a premier luxury houseboat on Nigeen Lake or a 5-star mountain resort on Boulevard Road, arrange private chauffeured Innova Crysta transfers, charter private upholstered Shikaras, book VIP Gulmarg Gondola access, and reserve chef-curated private Wazwan dining.', 'Dedicated private transport, VIP ticketing, and high-end lakeside accommodations eliminate logistics friction and elevate comfort.'),
  ('srinagar:rule:7', 'srinagar', 'Stay in locally managed guest houses in Dalgate or budget houseboats on inner Dal Lake channels, travel using shared union taxis and auto-rickshaws, eat at local dhabas along Lal Chowk and Khayam Chowk, and enjoy self-guided walks through public Mughal gardens and Old City bazaars.', 'Srinagar offers extensive affordable accommodation and public transport options, allowing budget travelers to access all major attractions economically.'),
  ('srinagar:rule:8', 'srinagar', 'Focus on the natural ecosystems of the Zabarwan range by visiting the Botanical Gardens, taking early morning bird-watching Shikara trips through Anchar Lake or Hokersar wetlands, exploring Badamwari Park during spring almond blooms, and taking an excursion to Sonmarg''s Thajiwas Glacier.', 'Srinagar''s lakes, wetlands, and mountain foothills host diverse flora, migratory birdlife, and dramatic alpine scenery away from urban centers.'),
  ('srinagar:rule:9', 'srinagar', 'Embark on a Kashmiri culinary journey—sampling street-side mutton kebabs at Khayam Chowk, trying fresh Girda bread at local Kandur bakeries, enjoying a full multi-course Wazwan feast at legacy eateries like Ahdoos, and sipping Nun Chai and saffron Kahwa in Old City tea shops.', 'Srinagar is the culinary capital of Kashmiri cuisine, renowned for its complex meat preparations, unique bakeries, and traditional tea culture.'),
  ('srinagar:rule:10', 'srinagar', 'Use Srinagar as a base to access high-altitude adventure hubs: head to Gulmarg for skiing and snowboard terrain via Apharwat Peak, travel to Pahalgam for Level 3 white-water rafting on the Lidder River, or launch multi-day alpine lake treks toward Tarsar-Marsar or Great Lakes.', 'While Srinagar itself offers relaxed lake activities, it serves as the primary gateway to Kashmir''s world-class trekking, skiing, and river rafting routes.'),
  ('srinagar:rule:11', 'srinagar', 'Choose ground-floor hotel rooms along Boulevard Road or stable houseboats on Nigeen Lake, use private covered Shikaras with cushioned seating and ramp access, drive directly to the base gates of Mughal Gardens, and view Shankaracharya Temple from lower vehicle viewpoints to avoid steep stone stairs.', 'Senior travelers require low-impact walking options, clear access paths, and comfortable transit to enjoy mountain and lake environments without physical strain.'),
  ('srinagar:rule:12', 'srinagar', 'If layover time allows 3 to 4 hours near Sheikh ul-Alam International Airport, hire a private cab straight to Dal Lake for a short 1-hour Shikara ride, visit Polo View Market for quick handicraft or saffron shopping, and return directly to the airport.', 'The main lake and market corridors are accessible within a short drive from the airport, making brief layover excursions feasible.'),
  ('srinagar:rule:13', 'srinagar', 'Visit the sacred white-marble Hazratbal Shrine on Nigeen Lake, ascend to the ancient 6th-century Shankaracharya Temple on Bilwa Parvat, explore the 14th-century Deodar wooden architecture of Jamia Masjid and Khanqah-e-Moula, and offer prayers at Sharika Devi Temple on Hari Parvat.', 'Srinagar represents a rich tapestry of Kashmiri spiritual heritage, encompassing ancient Hindu stone temples, historical Sufi shrines, and grand Islamic architectural monuments. ---'),
  ('pahalgam:rule:0', 'pahalgam', 'Focus exclusively on central Pahalgam by exploring the banks of the Lidder River, visiting the historic 12th-century Mamleshwar Temple, and taking a short local pony ride or hike up to the pine-framed meadows of Baisaran ("Mini Switzerland").', 'A single-day visit requires absolute focus on central landmarks and immediate trailheads to avoid getting caught in inter-valley transit delays or union taxi queues.'),
  ('pahalgam:rule:1', 'pahalgam', 'Combine central Pahalgam and Baisaran on Day 1, take a local union taxi tour of the complete "ABC" valley circuit (Aru Valley, Betaab Valley, and Chandanwari) on Day 2, and spend Day 3 enjoying river rafting near Yenner or angling on the Lidder River before departure.', 'A 3-day window allows an unhurried, comprehensive tour of Pahalgam''s three major alpine valleys while incorporating signature outdoor activities along the river.'),
  ('pahalgam:rule:2', 'pahalgam', 'Complete a comprehensive alpine immersion covering central Pahalgam, the full "ABC" valley circuit, and Baisaran, then launch a high-altitude day hike or overnight trek to Tulian Lake, Tarsar-Marsar Lakes, or Lidderwat from Aru Valley.', 'Multi-day stays provide the necessary buffer to experience Pahalgam''s pristine backcountry wilderness, glacial lakes, and multi-day trekking trails beyond the main vehicle routes.'),
  ('pahalgam:rule:3', 'pahalgam', 'Book a structured itinerary covering the iconic scenery of Betaab Valley, the snow points of Chandanwari, the rolling meadows of Aru Valley, a pony excursion to Baisaran, and a stroll through the Pahalgam Main Market.', 'First-time visitors benefit from experiencing Pahalgam''s most famous cinematic landscapes and accessible alpine meadows without needing intensive trekking gear.'),
  ('pahalgam:rule:4', 'pahalgam', 'Stay at an upscale riverfront wooden chalet in Laripora or along the Upper Lidder River, schedule private evening bonfires, arrange a secluded riverside Kahwa picnic in Aru Valley, and take early morning strolls through Betaab Valley.', 'Escaping central market noise for secluded pine-framed chalets and tranquil alpine valleys delivers an intimate, romantic, and breathtaking mountain getaway.'),
  ('pahalgam:rule:5', 'pahalgam', 'Plan a balanced itinerary using local union taxis for comfortable day trips to Betaab Valley and Aru Valley, enjoy trout feeding at Lidder Amusement Park, and take gentle pony rides through the open lawns of Baisaran.', 'Well-paved garden paths, river parks, and supervised pony rides keep children and elders entertained without strenuous physical exertion.'),
  ('pahalgam:rule:6', 'pahalgam', 'Reserve a private suite or chalet at top-tier resorts like ITC Pine N Peak, arrange private chauffeured transfers, hire dedicated union taxis for private valley excursions, play golf at the Pahalgam Golf Course, and book customized multi-course Wazwan dining experiences.', 'Premium accommodations and personalized service ensure high-end comfort, heated luxury, and exclusive access to fine mountain dining amidst pine wilderness.'),
  ('pahalgam:rule:7', 'pahalgam', 'Stay in a locally run family homestay or wooden guest house in Aru Village or outer Laripora, use shared union taxis for valley transfers, dine on local mutton kebab rolls and Girda bakery items near the bus stand, and take self-guided day walks along free forest trails.', 'Pahalgam offers accessible local homestays and public trail networks, allowing budget travelers to enjoy world-class alpine scenery at low costs.'),
  ('pahalgam:rule:8', 'pahalgam', 'Explore the untouched wilderness of the Overa-Aru Wildlife Sanctuary, photograph pine forests and rushing mountain streams in Aru Valley, and hike along the glacial waters of the Sheshnag River corridor toward Chandanwari.', 'The upper Lidder basin hosts rich alpine flora, pristine pine canopies, wildlife habitats, and crystalline mountain streams far removed from commercial hubs.'),
  ('pahalgam:rule:9', 'pahalgam', 'Embark on a regional culinary journey sampling fresh butter-fried Himalayan Trout along Laripora Road, savor authentic multi-course Wazwan at legacy market eateries, and pair warm Girda bread with salted Nun Chai at local village bakeries.', 'Pahalgam is Kashmir''s premier trout destination and offers an authentic taste of traditional mountain baking, tea culture, and royal feasts.'),
  ('pahalgam:rule:10', 'pahalgam', 'Tackle Grade II to IV white-water rafting on the Lidder River near Yenner, trek up steep pine ridges to high-altitude Tulian Lake, or launch a multi-day backcountry expedition toward Kolahoi Glacier or Tarsar Lake.', 'The Lidder Valley serves as Kashmir''s premier adventure hub, offering world-class river rafting, alpine lake trekking, and glacier expeditions.'),
  ('pahalgam:rule:11', 'pahalgam', 'Select flat ground-floor rooms or resorts with easy river access, utilize private union cabs directly to the paved walking paths of Betaab Valley, enjoy flat strolls around the Pahalgam Golf Course, and avoid steep horse rides to Baisaran.', 'Minimizing rough horseback trails and steep climbs ensures mature travelers can comfortably enjoy Pahalgam''s scenery via paved paths and covered vehicles.'),
  ('pahalgam:rule:12', 'pahalgam', 'If passing through Pahalgam for 3 to 4 hours on a regional circuit, take a quick drive to Betaab Valley for scenic photos, enjoy a fresh trout lunch along Main Market Road, and take a short walk along the Lidder Riverbank.', 'Central riverfronts and Betaab Valley are easily accessible from the main entry road, making short layover visits highly rewarding.'),
  ('pahalgam:rule:13', 'pahalgam', 'Visit the ancient 12th-century stone Mamleshwar Temple dedicated to Lord Shiva, climb the steps to the historic Aishmuqam Shrine (Hazrat Zain-ud-din Wali Dargah) in the lower valley, and explore the Chandanwari base camp gateway of the holy Amarnath Yatra.', 'The Lidder Valley holds ancient spiritual significance spanning sacred Hindu Shiva shrines, historic Yatra routes, and revered Kashmiri Sufi dargahs. ---'),
  ('amarnath:rule:0', 'amarnath', 'Choose the direct Baltal route for a high-intensity express same-day trek or take a Baltal-Panjtarni helicopter service, trek/pony the final 6 km to the Holy Amarnath Cave, obtain Darshan, and return to Baltal base camp by evening.', 'A single-day pilgrimage is physically impossible via Pahalgam and requires the shortest direct mountain trail (14 km) or helicopter transfer to complete Darshan within operational hours.'),
  ('amarnath:rule:1', 'amarnath', 'Execute a fast 3-day pilgrimage via the Baltal route or Neelgrath helicopter hub, incorporating 1 full day for transit and mandatory SASB RFID biometric verification in Srinagar/Baltal, 1 day for the Yatra and Holy Cave Darshan, and 1 buffer/recovery day visiting Sonamarg''s Thajiwas Glacier or Srinagar''s Dal Lake.', 'A 3-day itinerary provides enough time for high-altitude biometric checks and safety clearances while keeping transit tight via the northern corridor.'),
  ('amarnath:rule:2', 'amarnath', 'Embark on the complete traditional pilgrimage along the Pahalgam route—trekking over 3 to 4 days across Chandanwari, Pissu Top, Sheshnag Lake, Mahagunas Pass (14,000 ft), and Panjtarni, visiting the Holy Cave, and descending via Baltal or Pahalgam with a final relaxing day in Srinagar.', 'Multi-day itineraries allow for proper stage-by-stage acclimatization across high mountain passes, drastically reducing the risk of Acute Mountain Sickness (AMS) while experiencing the full traditional Yatra corridor.'),
  ('amarnath:rule:3', 'amarnath', 'Route through the traditional Pahalgam circuit, pre-booking official Shrine Board (SASB) registered ponies or palkis, spending an acclimatization night at Nunwan Base Camp, obtaining RFID Yatra passes early, and completing the trek over 3 days with structured halts at Sheshnag and Panjtarni.', 'First-time yatris benefit from Pahalgam''s gradual altitude gain and wide trails compared to Baltal''s steep, grueling inclines.'),
  ('amarnath:rule:4', 'amarnath', 'Opt for a hybrid itinerary using the Pahalgam route up to Chandanwari, hire pre-verified Palkis (palanquins) or dandis for children and elders, utilize Helicopter services from Pahalgam/Neelgrath to Panjtarni, and stay in managed Shrine Board camp huts with proper heating and medical facilities.', 'Family groups require low-impact ascent options, secure accommodation, and immediate access to emergency medical posts during high-altitude travel.'),
  ('amarnath:rule:5', 'amarnath', 'Secure VIP Helicopter tickets from Srinagar/Neelgrath to Panjtarni, arrange stay at premium private Swiss tents or luxury hotel suites in Sonamarg/Pahalgam, charter private chauffeured Innova Crysta transfers, and book dedicated Palki/Pony services for the final 6 km Panjtarni-to-Cave stretch.', 'Direct helicopter transfers and high-end base camp hospitality eliminate physical trek exhaustion and streamline security and transit logistics.'),
  ('amarnath:rule:6', 'amarnath', 'Register independently via official SASB bank branches, stay in shared Shrine Board Langer/Camp Tents at Baltal or Panjtarni, trek on foot via the short Baltal route (14 km), and eat at free non-profit community Langers operating along the route.', 'SASB registration, public camp tents, and volunteer langers enable devotees to complete the holy pilgrimage at minimal cost.'),
  ('amarnath:rule:7', 'amarnath', 'Undertake a full high-altitude trek crossing both routes: ascend via the rugged Pahalgam traditional trail over Mahagunas Pass (14,000 ft) to the Holy Cave, and descend via the steep, narrow precipices of the Baltal route, taking in views of the Amravati River and Zojila range.', 'Combining both corridors offers the ultimate Himalayan endurance trek, covering alpine glacial lakes, high passes, and dramatic vertical mountain terrain.'),
  ('amarnath:rule:8', 'amarnath', 'Require a strict SASB Compulsory Health Certificate (CHC) clearance (must be under 70/75 years age limit), use Helicopter transfers from Neelgrath or Pahalgam to Panjtarni, pre-book a 4-person Palki (palanquin) for the remaining 6 km to the Cave, and avoid overnight stays at high-altitude Cave/Panjtarni camps.', 'Senior pilgrims face extreme AMS risks at altitudes above 12,000 ft; minimizing physical exertion and sleeping at lower altitudes ensures medical safety.'),
  ('amarnath:rule:9', 'amarnath', 'If stopping in Srinagar or Jammu for 1 day en route to/from base camps, obtain mandatory RFID Yatra tracking cards at local airport/railway counter hubs, complete biometric scanning, and proceed directly via private cab to Baltal Base Camp (Sonamarg).', 'Biometric RFID verification is strictly compulsory before entering base camp checkposts, making transit halts necessary for permit collection.'),
  ('amarnath:rule:10', 'amarnath', 'Follow the complete traditional pilgrimage path starting at Pahalgam, performing ritual bathings at Chandanwari and Sheshnag Lake, chanting Shiva stotrams along Pissu Top, offering prayers at the Holy Ice Shivling during morning Aarti, and visiting the Bhairav Temple near the Cave.', 'Following the sacred Vedic trail walked by sages and devotees honors the traditional spiritual significance of the holy Yatra. ---'),
  ('katra-vaishno-devi:rule:0', 'katra-vaishno-devi', 'Focus exclusively on central lake and garden highlights by taking an early morning visit to Shankaracharya Temple, exploring Nishat Bagh and Shalimar Bagh, and concluding with a 2-hour sunset Shikara ride on Dal Lake visiting Char Chinar.', 'A single-day itinerary requires prioritizing iconic landmarks along the lakefront corridor to minimize city transit and maximize scenery.'),
  ('katra-vaishno-devi:rule:1', 'katra-vaishno-devi', 'Combine central lake highlights (Mughal Gardens, Shankaracharya Temple) with an early morning Floating Vegetable Market Shikara tour, a guided Old City heritage walk (Jamia Masjid, Khanqah-e-Moula), and a full-day excursion to either Gulmarg or Pahalgam.', 'A 3-day stay allows a balanced introduction to Srinagar''s cultural heritage, water-based lifestyle, and nearby alpine mountain passes.'),
  ('katra-vaishno-devi:rule:2', 'katra-vaishno-devi', 'Execute a complete Kashmir circuit using Srinagar as the central hub: spend 2 days exploring Srinagar’s lakes, Mughal gardens, and Old City bazaars, followed by overnight stays in Pahalgam (Lidder Valley, Betaab Valley) and Gulmarg (Gondola Phase 2), with an optional day excursion to Sonmarg or Yusmarg.', 'Multi-day itineraries provide sufficient time to experience both Srinagar''s urban heritage and Kashmir''s major alpine valleys without rushing long mountain drives.'),
  ('katra-vaishno-devi:rule:3', 'katra-vaishno-devi', 'Book a structured itinerary covering an early morning Shikara ride on Dal Lake, visits to Nishat Bagh and Shalimar Bagh, sunrise darshan at Shankaracharya Temple, shopping at Polo View Market, and an authentic Kashmiri Wazwan meal.', 'First-time visitors benefit from experiencing the core signature elements that define Kashmir''s cultural and natural identity.'),
  ('katra-vaishno-devi:rule:4', 'katra-vaishno-devi', 'Reserve a private luxury houseboat on the tranquil waters of Nigeen Lake, schedule private sunset Shikara rides, enjoy private candlelit dinners with saffron Kahwa, take romantic walks through Pari Mahal at dusk, and take a private day trip to Aru Valley in Pahalgam.', 'Staying on quieter lake stretches away from commercial piers provides the privacy, atmosphere, and cinematic views ideal for couples.'),
  ('katra-vaishno-devi:rule:5', 'katra-vaishno-devi', 'Stay in a lakefront resort along Boulevard Road, explore the broad, flat lawns of Nishat Bagh and Shalimar Bagh, visit the seasonal Indira Gandhi Memorial Tulip Garden (March–April), take child-friendly Shikara rides with life jackets, and take a day excursion to Gulmarg for snow sports.', 'Flat garden paths, gentle water transport, and high-altitude cable cars keep children and elders comfortable and engaged.'),
  ('katra-vaishno-devi:rule:6', 'katra-vaishno-devi', 'Book a premier luxury houseboat on Nigeen Lake or a 5-star mountain resort on Boulevard Road, arrange private chauffeured Innova Crysta transfers, charter private upholstered Shikaras, book VIP Gulmarg Gondola access, and reserve chef-curated private Wazwan dining.', 'Dedicated private transport, VIP ticketing, and high-end lakeside accommodations eliminate logistics friction and elevate comfort.'),
  ('katra-vaishno-devi:rule:7', 'katra-vaishno-devi', 'Stay in locally managed guest houses in Dalgate or budget houseboats on inner Dal Lake channels, travel using shared union taxis and auto-rickshaws, eat at local dhabas along Lal Chowk and Khayam Chowk, and enjoy self-guided walks through public Mughal gardens and Old City bazaars.', 'Srinagar offers extensive affordable accommodation and public transport options, allowing budget travelers to access all major attractions economically.'),
  ('katra-vaishno-devi:rule:8', 'katra-vaishno-devi', 'Focus on the natural ecosystems of the Zabarwan range by visiting the Botanical Gardens, taking early morning bird-watching Shikara trips through Anchar Lake or Hokersar wetlands, exploring Badamwari Park during spring almond blooms, and taking an excursion to Sonmarg''s Thajiwas Glacier.', 'Srinagar''s lakes, wetlands, and mountain foothills host diverse flora, migratory birdlife, and dramatic alpine scenery away from urban centers.'),
  ('katra-vaishno-devi:rule:9', 'katra-vaishno-devi', 'Embark on a Kashmiri culinary journey—sampling street-side mutton kebabs at Khayam Chowk, trying fresh Girda bread at local Kandur bakeries, enjoying a full multi-course Wazwan feast at legacy eateries like Ahdoos, and sipping Nun Chai and saffron Kahwa in Old City tea shops.', 'Srinagar is the culinary capital of Kashmiri cuisine, renowned for its complex meat preparations, unique bakeries, and traditional tea culture.'),
  ('katra-vaishno-devi:rule:10', 'katra-vaishno-devi', 'Use Srinagar as a base to access high-altitude adventure hubs: head to Gulmarg for skiing and snowboard terrain via Apharwat Peak, travel to Pahalgam for Level 3 white-water rafting on the Lidder River, or launch multi-day alpine lake treks toward Tarsar-Marsar or Great Lakes.', 'While Srinagar itself offers relaxed lake activities, it serves as the primary gateway to Kashmir''s world-class trekking, skiing, and river rafting routes.'),
  ('katra-vaishno-devi:rule:11', 'katra-vaishno-devi', 'Choose ground-floor hotel rooms along Boulevard Road or stable houseboats on Nigeen Lake, use private covered Shikaras with cushioned seating and ramp access, drive directly to the base gates of Mughal Gardens, and view Shankaracharya Temple from lower vehicle viewpoints to avoid steep stone stairs.', 'Senior travelers require low-impact walking options, clear access paths, and comfortable transit to enjoy mountain and lake environments without physical strain.'),
  ('katra-vaishno-devi:rule:12', 'katra-vaishno-devi', 'If layover time allows 3 to 4 hours near Sheikh ul-Alam International Airport, hire a private cab straight to Dal Lake for a short 1-hour Shikara ride, visit Polo View Market for quick handicraft or saffron shopping, and return directly to the airport.', 'The main lake and market corridors are accessible within a short drive from the airport, making brief layover excursions feasible.'),
  ('katra-vaishno-devi:rule:13', 'katra-vaishno-devi', 'Visit the sacred white-marble Hazratbal Shrine on Nigeen Lake, ascend to the ancient 6th-century Shankaracharya Temple on Bilwa Parvat, explore the 14th-century Deodar wooden architecture of Jamia Masjid and Khanqah-e-Moula, and offer prayers at Sharika Devi Temple on Hari Parvat.', 'Srinagar represents a rich tapestry of Kashmiri spiritual heritage, encompassing ancient Hindu stone temples, historical Sufi shrines, and grand Islamic architectural monuments. ---'),
  ('yusmarg:rule:0', 'yusmarg', 'Focus exclusively on central Yusmarg Meadow, descend via foot or pony to the foaming glacial stream of Doodh Ganga River, and make a brief stop at the historic Charar-e-Sharief Shrine during the return journey.', 'A single-day visit requires concentrating on the immediate meadow and river corridor to maximize time amidst nature without incurring long wilderness trail delays.'),
  ('yusmarg:rule:1', 'yusmarg', 'Dedicate Day 1 to exploring central Yusmarg Meadow and Doodh Ganga River, take a guided day trek or pony ride to the forest-enclosed Nilnag Lake on Day 2, and visit nearby pastoral Gujjar settlements and Charar-e-Sharief on Day 3.', 'A 3-day window provides a balanced mix of meadow relaxation, an offbeat alpine lake excursion, and cultural interaction with local pastoral communities.'),
  ('yusmarg:rule:2', 'yusmarg', 'Complete a deep alpine immersion covering Yusmarg Meadow, Doodh Ganga, and Nilnag Lake, then launch multi-day wilderness treks or camping expeditions toward Sang-e-Safed Valley, Tatakooti Peak base, or cross-country trails toward Tosamaidan.', 'Extended stays allow adventurous travelers to venture beyond day-use trails and experience untouched Pir Panjal backcountry wilderness, alpine passes, and glacial valleys.'),
  ('yusmarg:rule:3', 'yusmarg', 'Book a structured itinerary incorporating a scenic drive from Srinagar, a stop at Charar-e-Sharief, a walk or pony ride across Yusmarg Meadow, a picnic along the Doodh Ganga River, and an evening tasting of Kashmiri Kahwa at local tea stalls.', 'First-time visitors experience Yusmarg''s core highlights—its iconic green pastures, roaring glacial streams, and Sufi heritage—without needing heavy trekking logistics.'),
  ('yusmarg:rule:4', 'yusmarg', 'Reserve a secluded JKTDC pine cottage, schedule private riverside picnics along Doodh Ganga, arrange a peaceful guided pony excursion to Nilnag Lake, and enjoy cozy evening bonfires with views of Sunset Peak.', 'Escaping crowded tourist hubs for quiet pine-framed cottages and undisturbed mountain glades delivers an intimate, serene, and romantic alpine retreat.'),
  ('yusmarg:rule:5', 'yusmarg', 'Plan a relaxed itinerary centered on open-air activities in Yusmarg Meadow, organize safe guided pony rides down to Doodh Ganga River, enjoy family picnics on flat grassy lawns, and stay in spacious JKTDC family huts.', 'Expansive grassy pastures, easy pony tracks, and quiet riverbanks offer a safe, open environment for children and elders to relax together.'),
  ('yusmarg:rule:6', 'yusmarg', 'Combine luxury hotel stays in Srinagar with private chauffeured SUV transfers to Yusmarg, reserve private executive JKTDC chalets, hire dedicated local guides for customized day trips to Nilnag Lake, and arrange private chef-curated outdoor luncheons along Doodh Ganga.', 'While Yusmarg offers rustic wilderness accommodations, combining private transfers, personal guides, and curated outdoor setups maintains high comfort levels.'),
  ('yusmarg:rule:7', 'yusmarg', 'Utilize local shared taxis from Srinagar via Chadoora and Charar-e-Sharief, stay in basic local eco-homestays or budget JKTDC rooms, take self-guided hikes to Doodh Ganga River and Nilnag Lake, and dine at local meadow dhabas serving Noon Chai and local bread.', 'Direct public trail access and affordable government accommodation make Yusmarg one of the most cost-effective offbeat destinations in Kashmir.'),
  ('yusmarg:rule:8', 'yusmarg', 'Walk through pristine pine and fir forests, observe wildflower blooms across the pastures, photograph the snow-capped summits of Tatakooti Peak and Sunset Peak, and explore the alpine ecology around Nilnag Lake.', 'Situated in the Pir Panjal range, Yusmarg features undisturbed forest canopies, alpine glades, and crystalline water bodies free from commercial urban sprawl.'),
  ('yusmarg:rule:9', 'yusmarg', 'Sample authentic mountain tea culture with salted Noon Chai and Girda bread at meadow stalls, savor home-cooked Kashmiri farm meals at local homestays, and enjoy traditional Kashmiri Kahwa infused with saffron and almonds by the river.', 'Yusmarg offers a genuine taste of rustic Kashmiri tea stall culture and traditional village-style culinary hospitality.'),
  ('yusmarg:rule:10', 'yusmarg', 'Embark on challenging multi-day treks through the pine forests to Sang-e-Safed Valley, set up alpine wilderness camps near Nilnag Lake, or undertake high-altitude summit treks toward Tatakooti Peak.', 'The surrounding Pir Panjal range provides rugged, uncrowded terrain ideal for serious wilderness trekking, alpine camping, and mountain exploration.'),
  ('yusmarg:rule:11', 'yusmarg', 'Utilize private vehicles directly to the main meadow parking area, enjoy leisurely walks on flat grassy pastures near the tourist complex, take short, gentle pony rides, and avoid steep, unpaved hikes down to Doodh Ganga.', 'Keeping activities confined to flat meadow terrain and comfortable vehicle access ensures mature travelers enjoy Yusmarg''s scenery without physical strain.'),
  ('yusmarg:rule:12', 'yusmarg', 'If stopping in Yusmarg for 2 to 3 hours while exploring Budgam district, take a quick walk onto the central meadow, photograph Tatakooti Peak, enjoy a hot cup of Kahwa at a meadow stall, and visit Charar-e-Sharief en route.', 'Central Yusmarg Meadow is immediately accessible from the main parking area, allowing quick layover visitors to take in panoramic views efficiently.'),
  ('yusmarg:rule:13', 'yusmarg', 'Visit the revered 14th-century Charar-e-Sharief Shrine dedicated to Sheikh Noor-ud-Din Wali (Nund Reshi) in the lower hills, and spend quiet time reflecting amidst the peaceful, natural surroundings of the "Meadow of Jesus."', 'The region combines profound Kashmiri Sufi heritage with local traditions of spiritual sanctuary in the surrounding mountain wilderness. ---'),
  ('leh:rule:0', 'leh', 'Stay within the Leh local circuit: Shanti Stupa, Leh Palace, Namgyal Tsemo, Main Bazaar, Hall of Fame, and nearby monasteries such as Shey, Thiksey, and Hemis.', 'Leh itself sits at about 3,500 m, so short stays should prioritize acclimatization and low-exertion local sightseeing rather than immediate high-pass travel.'),
  ('leh:rule:1', 'leh', 'Reserve the first two days for Leh acclimatization and local heritage; add an overnight trip to Nubra Valley via Khardung La, including Diskit Monastery and the Hunder sand dunes.', 'This gives clients the recommended minimum 48 hours in Leh before moving to higher or remote mountain circuits.'),
  ('leh:rule:2', 'leh', 'Plan a balanced Ladakh circuit: 2 nights in Leh, 1–2 nights in Nubra Valley, 1 night near Pangong Tso, then return to Leh; add Tso Moriri, Hanle, or Turtuk only with extra nights.', 'Nubra, Pangong, Tso Moriri, and Hanle require long mountain drives and careful pacing, while Pangong stands at roughly 4,350 m.'),
  ('leh:rule:3', 'leh', 'Book a classic Leh–Nubra–Pangong itinerary with Shanti Stupa, Leh Palace, Thiksey Monastery, Diskit, Hunder, Khardung La, and an overnight at Pangong Tso.', 'This route combines Ladakh’s signature monasteries, high passes, desert landscapes, and lake scenery without overcomplicating the first visit.'),
  ('leh:rule:4', 'leh', 'Choose boutique Leh accommodation, a private vehicle with an experienced mountain driver, a premium Hunder camp, and a quieter Pangong stay; include sunset at Shanti Stupa and a stargazing evening near Pangong.', 'Private transfers and fewer hotel changes create a more comfortable, intimate experience in a destination where drives are long and altitude is demanding.'),
  ('leh:rule:5', 'leh', 'Stay 3 nights in Leh before any major circuit, use private SUVs, select heated family rooms or fixed camps, and limit the itinerary to Leh local sights, Nubra, and one Pangong overnight.', 'Children need a slow altitude adjustment, and the mandatory 48-hour acclimatization period is especially important before higher-altitude excursions.'),
  ('leh:rule:6', 'leh', 'Book high-end Leh hotels, private chauffeur-driven 4x4 transfers, premium fixed camps at Hunder and Pangong, private monastery guides, and curated Ladakhi dining experiences.', 'Luxury planning in Ladakh is primarily about insulation from harsh road, weather, and accommodation variability through reliable transport, comfort-led stays, and flexible pacing.'),
  ('leh:rule:7', 'leh', 'Use locally run guesthouses in Leh, shared taxis where suitable, economical homestays in Hunder or Spangmik, and focus on Leh’s free or low-cost heritage sights and monasteries.', 'Leh town can be explored economically, but clients should not cut costs on acclimatization, permits, verified transport, or safe overnight stays.'),
  ('leh:rule:8', 'leh', 'Keep the trip Leh-focused for the first 3 days, book ground-floor heated rooms with oxygen support on request, use private vehicles for monastery visits, and avoid same-day excursions over Khardung La or Chang La.', 'Leh’s high elevation and pass crossings can be physically demanding; a conservative itinerary reduces altitude and fatigue risks.'),
  ('leh:rule:9', 'leh', 'Prioritize Leh Palace, Namgyal Tsemo Gompa, Shanti Stupa, Thiksey Monastery, Hemis Monastery, Shey Palace, and the traditional Ladakhi market around Main Bazaar.', 'These places provide the strongest introduction to Ladakh’s royal history, Tibetan Buddhist heritage, architecture, and local life.'),
  ('leh:rule:10', 'leh', 'Combine Nubra Valley’s cold desert and dunes with Pangong Tso; extend to Tso Moriri or Hanle only when the itinerary has at least 8–9 days.', 'These remote landscapes are spectacular but involve protected-area formalities, high elevations, and substantial travel time.'),
  ('leh:rule:11', 'leh', 'Plan rafting on the Zanskar River, a guided Markha Valley trek, mountain biking around Leh, or a road-based circuit through Khardung La, Chang La, and Nubra—only after acclimatization.', 'Adventure activity at Ladakh’s elevation should begin after the recommended 48-hour rest period, not immediately upon arriving by flight.'),
  ('leh:rule:12', 'leh', 'Arrange a Ladakhi food walk in Leh Main Bazaar, focusing on thukpa, momos, skyū, chutagi, butter tea, apricot products, and local cafés.', 'Leh is the most convenient base for sampling Ladakhi cuisine, shopping for apricot-based products, and finding a wider range of restaurants.'),
  ('leh:rule:13', 'leh', 'Build a monastery circuit covering Thiksey, Hemis, Shey, Spituk, Sankar Gompa, and Shanti Stupa, with time for morning prayers where visitor access is permitted.', 'Leh and its Indus Valley surroundings concentrate some of Ladakh’s most important Buddhist monasteries within manageable driving distance.'),
  ('leh:rule:14', 'leh', 'For a 4–6 hour layover, restrict plans to Shanti Stupa, Leh Palace, and Main Bazaar; do not attempt Nubra, Pangong, or high-pass excursions.', 'Remote circuits require permits, long return drives, and altitude-sensitive pacing, making them unsuitable for short transits.'),
  ('leh:rule:15', 'leh', 'Arrange required permits before departure, carry printed or digital copies as required at checkpoints, and confirm the applicable permit type based on the traveller’s nationality.', 'Protected circuits including Nubra, Pangong, Tso Moriri, Hanle, and Turtuk have permit and checkpoint requirements; foreign visitors commonly require a Protected Area Permit. ---'),
  ('kargil:rule:0', 'kargil', 'Treat Kargil as a focused stopover: visit the Kargil War Memorial at Drass, explore Kargil town and its market, and add a short scenic drive into the nearby Suru Valley if road conditions allow.', 'A single day is insufficient for deep Suru Valley or Zanskar exploration; prioritizing the war memorial and close-by scenery avoids exhausting mountain-road travel.'),
  ('kargil:rule:1', 'kargil', 'Combine Drass War Memorial with a 2-day Suru Valley circuit covering Sankoo, Karpokhar, Parkachik Glacier, and views of the Nun-Kun peaks; stay one night in Kargil and one in the valley.', 'Suru Valley’s principal viewpoints, villages, and glacier landscapes are best covered over 2–3 days rather than as a rushed day trip.'),
  ('kargil:rule:2', 'kargil', 'Plan an extended Kargil–Suru–Zanskar route: include Drass, Suru Valley, Parkachik, Rangdum Monastery, and—if roads and weather permit—Pensi La and the Drang Drung Glacier.', 'Rangdum and Pensi La require substantial mountain-road time; a 4–5-day itinerary enables meaningful exploration with weather buffers.'),
  ('kargil:rule:3', 'kargil', 'Build a balanced itinerary with the Kargil War Memorial, Kargil town, Mulbekh Maitreya Buddha, and a scenic Suru Valley drive.', 'These stops represent Kargil’s defining mix of 1999-war remembrance, frontier landscapes, and Buddhist cultural heritage.'),
  ('kargil:rule:4', 'kargil', 'Choose a quiet boutique stay in Suru Valley, arrange a private car for Sankoo and Parkachik Glacier, and schedule sunset views of the Nun-Kun massif.', 'Suru Valley offers more privacy, greenery, and dramatic mountain scenery than Kargil town’s transit-oriented environment.'),
  ('kargil:rule:5', 'kargil', 'Base the family in Kargil town, visit the War Memorial and nearby Suru Valley viewpoints, use a private SUV, and avoid long drives toward Rangdum or Pensi La with young children.', 'Kargil provides practical services, while the longer interior-valley routes are remote and physically demanding.'),
  ('kargil:rule:6', 'kargil', 'Book the best available premium hotel or eco-resort in Kargil/Suru Valley, use a dedicated private SUV with an experienced mountain driver, and add curated picnic or photography stops near Parkachik.', 'Luxury in Kargil is defined more by private logistics, scenic exclusivity, and comfortable mountain stays than by large resort infrastructure.'),
  ('kargil:rule:7', 'kargil', 'Stay in local guesthouses in Kargil town, eat at local cafés and dhabas, use shared taxis where practical, and concentrate on free-access viewpoints, markets, and the Suru Valley road corridor.', 'Kargil has lower-cost guesthouse options, while independent road-based sightseeing keeps overall expenses controlled.'),
  ('kargil:rule:8', 'kargil', 'Prioritize Suru Valley, Sankoo, Parkachik Glacier, Nun-Kun views, and—on a longer trip—Rangdum and Drang Drung Glacier.', 'This corridor combines green river valleys, high Himalayan peaks, glacier views, and remote mountain landscapes.'),
  ('kargil:rule:9', 'kargil', 'Arrange guided trekking, camping, or mountaineering-oriented excursions around Parkachik, the Nun-Kun region, and Suru Valley; reserve extra acclimatization and weather-buffer days.', 'Suru Valley is a gateway to high-altitude trekking and mountain terrain, where professional local guidance and flexible logistics are essential.'),
  ('kargil:rule:10', 'kargil', 'Stay in Kargil town, use a private vehicle for the War Memorial, Mulbekh, and short Suru Valley drives, and avoid strenuous walks, long unbroken journeys, and high-pass excursions.', 'Road-accessible heritage and landscape stops offer Kargil’s highlights with lower physical strain than remote trekking and high-altitude routes.'),
  ('kargil:rule:11', 'kargil', 'On the Srinagar–Leh road journey, schedule a Kargil overnight rather than forcing a same-day crossing; use the stop for local rest, meals, and a short town visit.', 'Kargil is a natural break on the trans-Himalayan route, while extended detours into Suru Valley require additional nights.'),
  ('kargil:rule:12', 'kargil', 'Prioritize the Kargil War Memorial at Drass, including its memorial galleries and the names of soldiers commemorated for the 1999 conflict; add Mulbekh Monastery for Buddhist heritage.', 'The Drass memorial is Kargil’s principal site of national remembrance, while Mulbekh contributes a distinct historical and religious layer through its rock-cut Maitreya image. ---'),
  ('hanle:rule:0', 'hanle', 'Treat Kargil as a focused stopover: visit the Kargil War Memorial at Drass, explore Kargil town and its market, and add a short scenic drive into the nearby Suru Valley if road conditions allow.', 'A single day is insufficient for deep Suru Valley or Zanskar exploration; prioritizing the war memorial and close-by scenery avoids exhausting mountain-road travel.'),
  ('hanle:rule:1', 'hanle', 'Combine Drass War Memorial with a 2-day Suru Valley circuit covering Sankoo, Karpokhar, Parkachik Glacier, and views of the Nun-Kun peaks; stay one night in Kargil and one in the valley.', 'Suru Valley’s principal viewpoints, villages, and glacier landscapes are best covered over 2–3 days rather than as a rushed day trip.');
